{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire","id":818754,"title":"Ask a simple question, get a simple answer: Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-28T14:51:12-08:00","id":818754,"title":"Ask a simple question, get a simple answer: Vampire","content":"I can't believe no one's created one of these for Vampire yet, of all games. Well, I know <i>I'm</i> constantly flooded with simple questions, so let's do this! I'm creating this thread with the assumption that questions will be about VtR2e unless otherwise noted.<br /> <br /> 1)The Strix's Breath Drinking ability says that soulless victims create no Vitae - is that in general, or just related to the Breath Drinking?<br /> <br /> 2) Just to fully clarify, if a character wants to Lash Out to break an effect like Awe or Dread Presence , how exactly does it work? Do you need to pick a Kindred target that you think is doing it and run through the normal rules, or do you somehow lash out at the effect itself?<br /> <br /> I could have sworn I had more questions for this outing. Oh well, I'll probably remember them in time and post them here later. In the meantime, ask and answer any questions you see fit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:07:07-08:00","id":818816,"title":"","content":"You can lash out against another kindred or their effect. You don't need to guess who you need to lash out against to break awe, the power broadcasts to everyone in radius <i>pay attention to me because I'm the most important person here</i>. If they're using dread presence to have people deliberately avoid the user, once again it's a situation where the power's usage tells you who to target. It's also questionable as to whether or not you could target them directly in that scenario since you can't spend willpower to attack them, only defend. Ditto with higher level Majesty effects (Then you get into whether or not initiating a predatory aura showdown constitutes an attack when it's specifically listed as a defense mechanism against discipline use.) You can also target the aura in order to be immune, or lash out and break all the obfuscate effects on a vampire if you find yourself in a scenario where you suspect obfuscate is being used because you're tracking the obfuscated person or forced to interact with another obfuscated object or place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:26:45-08:00","id":818826,"title":"","content":"What is the general agreement about different powers that grant Damage Bonuses? I once saw a house rule that said the following:<br /> <br /> &quot;Every point of Damage Bonus above 5 becomes one point of Armor Piercing. Every 1/1 of Armor above 5/5 becomes one point of Anti-Armor Piercing.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's also the notion that only the highest among the Damage Bonuses is applied.<br /> <br /> Let's suppose I use Protean to get claws with +2L and Armor Piercing 2, and then I spend 1 Vitae to add my Vigor 5. If I followed the first rule, my claws would have +5L and Armor Piercing 4. If I followed the second rule, my claws would have +5L and Armor Piercing 2.<br /> <br /> Now let's suppose I also have the Claws Of The Unholy Merit. My claws deal +0A and bypass all Armor that isn't Resilience. Should I fight a vampire with Resilience, do I still have the Armor Piercing 2 that Protean gives? Can I spend 1 Vitae to add my Vigor 5 on top of that, resulting in claws with +5A and Armor Piercing 2? What about supernatural Armors that aren't Resilience? A Mage with Death 2 in 2ED can downgrade damage as if he was a vampire. Would a Werewolf in Gauru form downgrade the Claws Of The Unholy into lethal?<br /> <br /> Do the Demonic Form abilities and Gadgets of the Unchained deal lethal or bashing damage to vampires? How about a changeling with the Lethal Mien Merit? Is Gauru the only werewolf form that deals lethal to vampires? What criteria do people use to detetmine if a vampire will downgrade a supernatural attack that is normally lethal into bashing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T16:33:03-08:00","id":818830,"title":"","content":"Would it be in-character for the Ordo Dracul to develop a Coil that gives benefits for drinking the blood or equivalent of other supernaturals? The Unnatural Affinity Merit simply lets you get Vitae from the blood of other supernaturals, so it might be a pre-requisite for that Coil.<br /> <br /> For example, drinking Beast blood could give bonuses to Protean, Nightmare and Lashing Out with the Monstrous Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T18:11:15-08:00","id":818893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire#post818754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)The Strix's Breath Drinking ability says that soulless victims create no Vitae - is that in general, or just related to the Breath Drinking?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's just for Breath Drinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire#post818754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Just to fully clarify, if a character wants to Lash Out to break an effect like Awe or Dread Presence , how exactly does it work? Do you need to pick a Kindred target that you think is doing it and run through the normal rules, or do you somehow lash out at the effect itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have reason to suspect you're being affected by a power like Awe or Dread Presence (opinions differ on exactly how easy this should be to figure out, but let's say you notice that the Daeva's rivals are treating him more respectfully than usual, or you find yourself unnerved by a Nos and no one else seems disturbed by the fact that the walls are melting), you just Lash Out against the person you suspect is responsible using the normal rules, and if you win, the power stops affecting you. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=818826#post818826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the general agreement about different powers that grant Damage Bonuses? I once saw a house rule that said the following:<br /> <br /> &quot;Every point of Damage Bonus above 5 becomes one point of Armor Piercing. Every 1/1 of Armor above 5/5 becomes one point of Anti-Armor Piercing.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's also the notion that only the highest among the Damage Bonuses is applied.<br /> <br /> Let's suppose I use Protean to get claws with +2L and Armor Piercing 2, and then I spend 1 Vitae to add my Vigor 5. If I followed the first rule, my claws would have +5L and Armor Piercing 4. If I followed the second rule, my claws would have +5L and Armor Piercing 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are definitely both house rules. By RAW, damage bonuses stack, and there is no cap on them. But if your group finds that to be a problem, either of these house rules seem like decent alternatives to RAW.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=818826#post818826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now let's suppose I also have the Claws Of The Unholy Merit. My claws deal +0A and bypass all Armor that isn't Resilience. Should I fight a vampire with Resilience, do I still have the Armor Piercing 2 that Protean gives? Can I spend 1 Vitae to add my Vigor 5 on top of that, resulting in claws with +5A and Armor Piercing 2? What about supernatural Armors that aren't Resilience? A Mage with Death 2 in 2ED can downgrade damage as if he was a vampire. Would a Werewolf in Gauru form downgrade the Claws Of The Unholy into lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Resilience isn't armor, it reduces damage &quot;like armor&quot;, so the AP2 is redundant with the fact that Claws of the Unholy bypass all armor. If you spend a Vitae to add Vigor to damage, yes, the full amount will be dealt as Aggravated. Supernatural armor other than Resilience is getting into crossover territory, so you'll probably have to answer that for yourself. I would say that Death mage armor works like vampire damage reduction, it would not reduce damage from Claws of the Unholy because it's a supernatural source of damage. As for werewolf damage reduction, I'd personally use David H.'s rule of thumb and say if the player spent experience to be able to do agg, it shouldn't be reduced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=818826#post818826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Demonic Form abilities and Gadgets of the Unchained deal lethal or bashing damage to vampires? How about a changeling with the Lethal Mien Merit? Is Gauru the only werewolf form that deals lethal to vampires? What criteria do people use to detetmine if a vampire will downgrade a supernatural attack that is normally lethal into bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>My rules for vampire damage reduction are:<ul><li>If it's a mundane source of damage, it gets downgraded.</li> <li>If it's a supernatural power that creates a mundane source of damage like a weapon (Protean 2 is a good example), it gets downgraded.</li> <li>If it's a supernatural power that creates a mundane source of damage like a weapon and it says that it bypasses supernatural resistances or that it does a certain kind of damage to vampires, it does not get downgraded (Protean 4 and werewolf bites are both good examples).</li> <li>If it's a supernatural power that does direct damage, it does not get downgraded (Nightmare 5 is a good example)</li> <li>If it's a supernatural power in a vampire book, it does not get downgraded, because it's written with the assumption that it'll primarily be used against other vampires.</li> <li>If it's an ability that a player spent experience on, it probably shouldn't get downgraded unless there's a very good reason for it to be.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T05:43:54-08:00","id":819146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=818830#post818830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be in-character for the Ordo Dracul to develop a Coil that gives benefits for drinking the blood or equivalent of other supernaturals? The Unnatural Affinity Merit simply lets you get Vitae from the blood of other supernaturals, so it might be a pre-requisite for that Coil.<br /> <br /> For example, drinking Beast blood could give bonuses to Protean, Nightmare and Lashing Out with the Monstrous Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis seems like something that a custom Scales from the Mystery of the Voivode(or Zinirtra) can do.<br /> I don't know how hard is to create a new Coil in 2nd edition, maybe Secrets of the Covenants can help with this, but on my point of view, creating an entirely new Coil is something really hard and time consuming. (Too much tests and stuff)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:21:03-08:00","id":819170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=818826#post818826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Gauru the only werewolf form that deals lethal to vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell no. The book says they deal lethal to vamps in <i>hishu</i>, when their bites should only do bashing to anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:53:36-08:00","id":819192,"title":"","content":"Do you allow modifiers such as Striking Looks to play a roll in Hunting Rolls? As I recall they're abstractions anyway.<br /> <br /> What modifiers do you use most often on Hunting Rolls? Do you incentivize merits like Hunting Grounds or Herd at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:13:00-08:00","id":819203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire#post818754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe no one's created one of these for Vampire yet, of all games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never really needed them before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire#post818754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)The Strix's Breath Drinking ability says that soulless victims create no Vitae - is that in general, or just related to the Breath Drinking?</div> </div> </div> </div> Breath Drinking. It ties into the whole idea that your breath contains your soul. So, if you're soulless, there's nothing for the breath to carry out, and for the Strix to tap into to drink. Blood born vitae taps directly into life energy in a different way - its actually a more stable way of draining life energy that even other supernaturals can deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Just to fully clarify, if a character wants to Lash Out to break an effect like Awe or Dread Presence , how exactly does it work? Do you need to pick a Kindred target that you think is doing it and run through the normal rules, or do you somehow lash out at the effect itself? </div> </div> </div> You have to target the vampire in question. When you Lash Out, its not an entirely internal, psychic ability you can use while sitting down sipping a mandrake wine and watching something on your phone. There's accompanying physical actions. &quot;To lash out, the vampire must take a simple action appropriate to the aspect of predator used. A monstrous Beast growls, threatens, gnashes teeth, or calls to action. A seductive Beast sidles up to the prey, whispers beautiful lies, or gives a telling gaze from across the crowd. A competitive Beast draws a line in the sand, announces terms, or takes the role of mouse in a chase.&quot;<br /> <br /> You kind of need someone to do that growling, whispering, and daring to. There might be exceptions that make sense story wise, but generally speaking you need to have a target in mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=818826#post818826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My claws deal +0A and bypass all Armor that isn't Resilience. Should I fight a vampire with Resilience, do I still have the Armor Piercing 2 that Protean gives?</div> </div> </div> </div> Resilience isn't actually armor. Armor Piercing does not apply to Resilience. In some ways Resilience does act like armor, but in other ways, it doesn't. The wording in the book isnt' the best. <br /> <br /> In general, from the sounds of it, you have mundane armor that works like normal. You get 2/2 (or whatever), which doesn't stack with other sources that grant armor (unless the ability specifically says it does). So, you can wear a flak jacket and have Iron Body as a vampire, but only the higher rating applies. This is the only kind of armor that Armor Piercing works against. Then, you have magical &quot;armors&quot; that work like damage reduction - a vampire unliving body and Resilience are two kinds. One downgrades damage, and one reduces damage taken. You need specific abilities that bypass them, or they work as normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about supernatural Armors that aren't Resilience? A Mage with Death 2 in 2ED can downgrade damage as if he was a vampire. Would a Werewolf in Gauru form downgrade the Claws Of The Unholy into lethal? </div> </div> </div> As with all other crossover questions, you have to ask your ST. There's no definitive answer. Personally, I allow swapping out power-equivalents. Werewolves can't downgrade damage naturally, even from regular Protean claws. If there's a power that can, then that would be a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the Demonic Form abilities and Gadgets of the Unchained deal lethal or bashing damage to vampires? How about a changeling with the Lethal Mien Merit? </div> </div> </div> Bashing. Touched by magic doesn't automatically bypass the damage reduction trait of vampries. Of course, that's assuming that CtL will have a Lethal Mien merit in 2e - given how kiths work now, I'm actually more inclined to think that there won't be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is Gauru the only werewolf form that deals lethal to vampires? </div> </div> </div> Any form's <i>bite attack</i> deals lethal to vampires, even the Hishu / human form. Claw attacks from all five forms still deal bashing, even in Gauru.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What criteria do people use to detetmine if a vampire will downgrade a supernatural attack that is normally lethal into bashing? </div> </div> </div> I ask the following question - &quot;Is it similar to vampire abilities that deal lethal damage to vampires?&quot; Vampires can deal lethal to each other using bite attacks and pure magic attacks (some blood rituals). They can also deal lethal damage with abilities that are specifically designed to deal lethal to each other (Kindred Dueling FS, blood scourge, Protean 4 claws).<br /> <br /> This is actually consistant with how werewolves deal damage to vampires. Bite attacks bypass the damage reduction, natural claws don't, and direct attack Gifts are deadly. Rare, but deadly.<br /> <br /> So, if you have a predator-themed changeling or Beast that happens to use a bite attack on a vampire? I would totally say lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-29-2016, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:15:35-08:00","id":819206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819192#post819192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you allow modifiers such as Striking Looks to play a roll in Hunting Rolls? As I recall they're abstractions anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the approach and the nature of the Striking Looks merit, but if it feels appropriate, yes. Same for other Merit based modifiers and even equipment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819192#post819192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What modifiers do you use most often on Hunting Rolls? Do you incentivize merits like Hunting Grounds or Herd at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I use Districts and Sites from Damnation City, and apply modifiers to feeding rolls based on the District. I absolutely encourage Hunting Grounds and Herd. Herd is especially useful because the free Vitae allowance means you don't have to hunt as often just to stay active. The dice bonus from Hunting Grounds is often not needed, but adding your Hunting Grounds dots to starting Vitae rolls is well worth the exp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-29-2016, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:35:36-08:00","id":819227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819192#post819192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you allow modifiers such as Striking Looks to play a roll in Hunting Rolls? As I recall they're abstractions anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, as well as any other appropriate equipment modifier. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What modifiers do you use most often on Hunting Rolls? </div> </div> </div> Other than the suggested modifier table? Whatever the players come up with. I reward creativity. Also, Majesty is popular for the daeva. Since it directly increases Presence, I don't consider it to need a vitae to &quot;activate&quot; and consider it part of the usual roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you incentivize merits like Hunting Grounds or Herd at all? </div> </div> </div> Hunting Grounds is highly useful for &quot;starting vitae&quot; rolls, which I use fairly frequently. Herd is pretty popular as well, considering that hunting rolls tend to take up a significant amount of time. Hunting takes an hour by default. Maybe two, after travel time and everything. My games tend to be a bit rushed in the early evening, then more relaxed as the night progresses. So, you don't have time for leisurely feeding in the beginning all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T09:30:56-08:00","id":819321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819203#post819203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> sipping a mandrake wine</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me- have Mandragoa explicitly survived the edition change, or are they in &quot;old rules &amp; fluff that aren't directly contradicted are fair game to re-implement&quot; territory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:08:38-08:00","id":819347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819321#post819321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me- have Mandragoa explicitly survived the edition change, or are they in &quot;old rules &amp; fluff that aren't directly contradicted are fair game to re-implement&quot; territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe they made the jump in the Secrets of the Covenants Merits for the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1eJz_HsiLvwF8e4okeCDF-FzV-japjrLxmd9bx4diVSc/edit#heading=h.sm15y6807i79\" target=\"_blank\">Circle of the Crone</a>.<br /> <br /> ex:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Secrets of the Covenants Open Development, Circle of the Crone</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mandragora Garden (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Safe Place (same level), Cr\u00faac \u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your character maintains a garden of ghouled plants. They behave </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[RB4] </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">on their own in slow, almost imperceptible fashion. As well, they act as a vector for your character\u2019s Cr\u00faac.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Your character\u2019s rating in Mandragora Garden determines the rough size, which must correspond with an equal or greater Safe Place. An Acolyte can use mandragora she\u2019s created herself as if they were her own hands and eyes for the purposes of Cr\u00faac rituals. This allows her to use her rituals at a distance. If she\u2019s standing amidst her garden, she may add her Mandragora Garden dots to any Cr\u00faac ritual rolls. Additionally, the Acolyte may cast rituals on her garden that would normally last a scene. The magic of the garden sustains these rituals indefinitely. She may have a number of such rituals active equal to her dots in this Merit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While she must feed her garden one Vitae per month equal to her dots in Mandragora Garden, the garden will produce twice that quantity in sap, nectar, or other fluids which serve as animal blood, on which Kindred may feed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lastly, because of the intimate association a vampire must keep with such a garden, it becomes an extension of her body. Anyone attacking or otherwise harming the garden provokes her to frenzy as if they attacked her directly.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Note:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A vampire\u2019s mandragora take on qualities of her blood. They will bear fruit symbolic of her clan, for example.</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[RB5] </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> If the character has a Cr\u00faac style (see p. XX), this will show up in her plants.</span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Now, whether one considers this the only application of Mandragora is really up to you. I imagine that anybody can ghoul plants, but that this merit represents the special connection/training required for one to use them in this fashion for blood sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 01-29-2016, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:41:18-08:00","id":819364,"title":"","content":"Do ghouls count as human for the purpose of the nosferatu clan curse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T11:56:18-08:00","id":819402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819347#post819347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, whether one considers this the only application of Mandragora is really up to you. I imagine that anybody can ghoul plants, but that this merit represents the special connection/training required for one to use them in this fashion for blood sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div> The merit includes making sap, wine, etc that can be drank. Isn't that pretty much the main use of a mandrake garden? What else is there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819364#post819364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do ghouls count as human for the purpose of the nosferatu clan curse?</div> </div> </div> </div> Ghouls are neither Kindred, nor are they necessarily Touchstones. They're still human enough that they have the same human cues that vamipres are detached about reading. So, I would say yes. Seems like the kind of thing they would include in that list if not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-29-2016, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T12:30:48-08:00","id":819418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819402#post819402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The merit includes making sap, wine, etc that can be drank. Isn't that pretty much the main use of a mandrake garden? What else is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>And maybe anyone who ghouls a plant can get those parts. What I was talking about being the unique benefit of this merit was that the mandragora augment Cruac in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T14:15:50-08:00","id":819501,"title":"","content":"I might be missing it in the book, but how does feeding off ghouls work? Do they lose 1L per Vitae drained like normal and just have a few extra points to pull from their (now almost certainly dead) bodies, or do they lose their stored Vitae like Kindred and only take damage once their own blood starts getting drained?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T14:38:52-08:00","id":819513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819501#post819501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might be missing it in the book, but how does feeding off ghouls work? Do they lose 1L per Vitae drained like normal and just have a few extra points to pull from their (now almost certainly dead) bodies, or do they lose their stored Vitae like Kindred and only take damage once their own blood starts getting drained?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's ever stated explicitly, so I would assume they're just humans for the purposes of feeding, i.e., they lose Health boxes, but their stored blood is separate. Vitae isn't (quite) literally blood, after all. Otherwise ghouls would be like stored Vitae bloodbags for elders...which would be a cool plot hook, come to think of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T14:39:47-08:00","id":819515,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine if they had vitae left they'd reflexively spend it to stay alive when they got drained low enough. Strix take it first though. That's made very clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T15:20:56-08:00","id":819533,"title":"","content":"Ghouls are drained via health levels, like a normal person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T10:32:01-08:00","id":819871,"title":"","content":"Going back to one of my past questions, for those who say you have to lash out at a specific vampire to break their effect, how does that work when Stealth/Obfuscate is involved, like the classic Obfuscate/Dread Presence combo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T11:58:11-08:00","id":819906,"title":"","content":"Can someone please give me some example of how an Idealist and Perfectionist vampire can regain willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T12:52:28-08:00","id":819927,"title":"","content":"Getting an exceptional success on something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T12:56:17-08:00","id":819929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819906#post819906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone please give me some example of how an Idealist and Perfectionist vampire can regain willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Letting their idealism restrict them from making what would be, from a metagaming perspective, a smarter choice. Trusting a certain individual because you believe they can be redeemed, for instance, rather than killing them because they're a diablerist. For a full fill-up, have your idealism rewarded, maybe see that the diablerist did turn a new leaf. For a Perfectionist, refusing to do something until you believe you have it perfectly planned out, which may require constant investigation into the facts surrounding a situation rather than the ones you know now. For a fill-up, perhaps have your plans go so well that with the modifiers you get, as Elfive said, an exceptional success or manage to let your plan go off without getting hurt or extra effort on your behalf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:17:39-08:00","id":819938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819871#post819871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to one of my past questions, for those who say you have to lash out at a specific vampire to break their effect, how does that work when Stealth/Obfuscate is involved, like the classic Obfuscate/Dread Presence combo?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not a whole lot you can do unless you have a way to see past the Obfuscate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T16:13:28-08:00","id":820024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819938#post819938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not a whole lot you can do unless you have a way to see past the Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the game of Paper, Scissors, Obfuscate, always bring Auspex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:14:13-08:00","id":821238,"title":"","content":"Another Protean question: If a ghoul is taught to use this Discipline, what happens when they use Unmarked Grave? Breaking Point issues aside, does a living subject merge with the object in question and stay there as per the general description, or do they have to worry about asphyxiation since they're part of (or inside?) a solid object?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:28:27-08:00","id":821247,"title":"","content":"The first edition ghouls book had them last 15 minutes per dot of stamina (+resilience, I guess) before they died of suffocation. The power seems to work more or less the same in second edition (sans being a dot lower on the pole) so you could say the same happens here, <i>but </i> you also have to consider that the power is now how you shuffle traits and animal forms for shapeshifting, which requires staying like that for a whole day, so you might want to let ghouls use the power fully. On the other hand maybe you figure being stuck with the initial set up is a logical restriction for a ghoul. I mean, you need to drain an animal of blood to get animal forms now, so how a ghoul would manage that at all is a question in itself.<br /> <br /> Devs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:33:10-08:00","id":821252,"title":"","content":"First edition's Ghouls book covered it, though the Discipline has changed a bit and obviously we don't have the same systems for mortals it should give you some ideas for what to do.<br /> <br /> 'A ghoul with this power cannot use it indefinitely. He can remain interred for 15 minutes per Stamina dot he possesses, after which he dies. When that happens, his body congeals back into its normal shape at the surface of the material with which he has blended, but it remains composed of that material and part of that material thereafter. While he\u2019s blended (and still alive), Morality is the trait rolled to determine his awareness of his surroundings.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:45:26-08:00","id":821264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=821252#post821252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First edition's Ghouls book covered it, though the Discipline has changed a bit and obviously we don't have the same systems for mortals it should give you some ideas for what to do.<br /> <br /> 'A ghoul with this power cannot use it indefinitely. He can remain interred for 15 minutes per Stamina dot he possesses, after which he dies. When that happens, his body congeals back into its normal shape at the surface of the material with which he has blended, but it remains composed of that material and part of that material thereafter. While he\u2019s blended (and still alive), Morality is the trait rolled to determine his awareness of his surroundings.'</div> </div> </div> </div>That works easily enough\u2014and someone who's met their demise this way makes for a hellish frescoe or bas-relief <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=821247#post821247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first edition ghouls book had them last 15 minutes per dot of stamina (+resilience, I guess) before they died of suffocation. The power seems to work more or less the same in second edition (sans being a dot lower on the pole) so you could say the same happens here, <i>but </i> you also have to consider that the power is now how you shuffle traits and animal forms for shapeshifting, which requires staying like that for a whole day, so you might want to let ghouls use the power fully. On the other hand maybe you figure being stuck with the initial set up is a logical restriction for a ghoul. I mean, you need to drain an animal of blood to get animal forms now, so how a ghoul would manage that at all is a question in itself.<br /> <br /> Devs?</div> </div> </div> </div>This does raise a couple of interesting conundrums. (conundra?)<br /> <br /> For the animal blood aspect, perhaps you consume the animal blood yourself as a ghoul (one of the Scales of the Dragon, for example, does impart a thirst for blood to a mortal as a side-effect\u2014albeit without actually counting as Vitae, making the imbiber sick, and threatening an Integrity roll. Maybe this is a similar case?). Alternatively, can you have your Domitor immediately feed you a point of Vitae after they consume the animal's blood in the same scene, perhaps?<br /> <br /> As for the using Unmarked Grave to shift traits from Feral Aspect or Unnatural Aspect, either they have to basically . . . spend a day using it over and over? Or just sleep like a normal person, undisturbed, in complete silence and darkness (the 'human' equivalent to staying in an Unmarked Grave) and let the changes happen then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 02-01-2016, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:57:57-08:00","id":821272,"title":"","content":"Admittedly there's nothing in the power that says you need to get <i>vitae </i>from the blood of the animal you drain, presumably to maintain ease of use for elder vamps, so theoretically you do just need to drink the blood. That's not going to be <i>easy </i>for a ghoul to do, but it's an option. <br /> <br /> Another thing to consider is that protean 5 also lets you shift the traits, and the Ghouls book says nothing about a time limit on that one, so it could be read that ghouls simply need full mastery of the power to shift traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:58:40-08:00","id":821273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=821264#post821264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the animal blood aspect, perhaps you consume the animal blood yourself as a ghoul (one of the Scales of the Dragon, for example, does impart a thirst for blood to a mortal as a side-effect\u2014albeit without actually counting as Vitae, making the imbiber sick, and threatening an Integrity roll. Maybe this is a similar case?). Alternatively, can you have your Domitor immediately feed you a point of Vitae after they consume the animal's blood in the same scene, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div> Or just eat the animal. That's a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the using Unmarked Grave to shift traits from Feral Aspect or Unnatural Aspect, either they have to basically . . . spend a day using it over and over? Or just sleep like a normal person, undisturbed, in complete silence and darkness (the 'human' equivalent to staying in an Unmarked Grave) and let the changes happen then? </div> </div> </div> Unmarked Grave might work differently in 2e than 1e. We're getting a ghoul book pretty soon, so I would personally just wait to see what it says.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T08:35:45-08:00","id":821640,"title":"","content":"Hey, speaking of ghouls, I've been wondering this for a while: If a strix possess a ghoul, can they use their disciplines? And can they spend a vitae a month to keep them from ageing, or does it not work because it's strix vitae and they just end up in a regular living host?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T10:48:21-08:00","id":821727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=821247#post821247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first edition ghouls book had them last 15 minutes per dot of stamina (+resilience, I guess) before they died of suffocation. The power seems to work more or less the same in second edition (sans being a dot lower on the pole) so you could say the same happens here, <i>but </i> you also have to consider that the power is now how you shuffle traits and animal forms for shapeshifting, which requires staying like that for a whole day, so you might want to let ghouls use the power fully. On the other hand maybe you figure being stuck with the initial set up is a logical restriction for a ghoul. I mean, you need to drain an animal of blood to get animal forms now, so how a ghoul would manage that at all is a question in itself.<br /> <br /> Devs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unmarked grave does not state that it works any differently on a ghoul than it does a vampire, We shouldn't use the 1st edition ghoul book, because the power changed, it's requirements changed. If we change it by using old rules so they can only stay in there part of a night, then ghouls wouldn't have access to the rest of the discipline because much of it requires you to be in the unmarked grave for a full day to use some of the benefits or change things.<br /> <br /> For the other protean powers it says you just need to kill it by consuming it.. if that means blood or body or whatever is not specified. It doesnt say anything about Vitae. so an elder doing it wouldnt have any issues.<br /> <br /> Why would we look for different rules on this and not just do what the book says?<br /> <br /> ( in other threads) The book specifically states that Riding the wave is for when you are pushed into frenzy, but some suggest we use obscure rules for that too.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am not sure why we do this sort of thing here. Forgive me for pointing it out. it seems that sometimes we take RAW for what they are and what the book states, and sometimes ... we don't.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Originally posted by <b>Kirby Jerusalem</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819871#post819871\">View Post</a></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Going back to one of my past questions, for those who say you have to lash out at a specific vampire to break their effect, how does that work when Stealth/Obfuscate is involved, like the classic Obfuscate/Dread Presence combo?</span></span></i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=819938#post819938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not a whole lot you can do unless you have a way to see past the Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> *** The book specifically states you can lash out against an obfucated vampire to break the effect... same as dread presense and awe<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T14:26:50-08:00","id":821879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=821727#post821727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*** The book specifically states you can lash out against an obfucated vampire to break the effect... same as dread presense and awe</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. But you can't exactly Lash Out against someone you don't even know is there. If you find them, either through Auspex or through incidental signs of their presence, then you can Lash Out against them to end the effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T07:19:28-08:00","id":826796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=821727#post821727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unmarked grave does not state that it works any differently on a ghoul than it does a vampire, We shouldn't use the 1st edition ghoul book, because the power changed, it's requirements changed. If we change it by using old rules so they can only stay in there part of a night, then ghouls wouldn't have access to the rest of the discipline because much of it requires you to be in the unmarked grave for a full day to use some of the benefits or change things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Logic dictates it does. Ghouls still breathe. The old Ghoul book also I think stated protean did damage as ghoul shifted. I don't have either book in front of me.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:25:34-08:00","id":826879,"title":"","content":"I do have the book on me, and as far as shapeshifting goes it apparently works just fine. The only notes the book makes are that the ghoul becomes a living animal and that animalism won't work on them because they still have a human mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:28:20-08:00","id":826881,"title":"","content":"When do you roll for Humanity, when the Breaking Point occurs, or at the end of the scene? The Changeling Clarity draft has prompted this question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:00:03-08:00","id":826901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=826796#post826796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Logic dictates it does. Ghouls still breathe. The old Ghoul book also I think stated protean did damage as ghoul shifted. I don't have either book in front of me.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me, but logic dictates it would be impossible for the earth to open up and swallow someone without leaving any traces of the event either. And a humanoild ( vampire or ghoul ) can't logically transform into a cat.. or a bat.. either, but they do. It's magic and I think magic throws logic out the window. I do not think we should look into the 1edition books for reference here, because protean was completely reworked.<br /> <br /> Why would the developers say ghouls can have any 2 dots of clan disciplines, if they couldn't use Protean? not being able to use the first dot of this discipline, means they wouldnt be able to really use the rest of it either. To me that is illogical. Perhaps we do need Rose or someone else to clarify this one. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a> I have them roll at the time it happens. The point in time in which they break and give the condition that goes with it right away, though I have seen in other threads that people wait until combat or the scene is over as not to slow down the story. I believe it was determined it is up to the Story teller and the flow of the game. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T10:40:48-08:00","id":826932,"title":"","content":"Are vampires who commit diablerie called diabolists? Because I've been calling them diablerists this whole time and looking over my Masquerade books I just realized that diabolists seems to be the term they call them there. Also I could be wrong but I don't think I've seen the term diabolist in the Requiem books.<br /> <br /> What would be the term for 'one who commits Amaranth?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-09-2016, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:00:15-08:00","id":826947,"title":"","content":"Is there any way for either party to end an Invictus Oath before its duration expires? Is it possible for an outside party to do so? Is there a procedure for... annulment, or a mutual cessation clause, or for a Covenant superior shutting down a non-legal Oath without killing those involved, or anything, or do you just ride that train to the end of the line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:39:21-08:00","id":827104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=826932#post826932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are vampires who commit diablerie called diabolists? Because I've been calling them diablerists this whole time and looking over my Masquerade books I just realized that diabolists seems to be the term they call them there. Also I could be wrong but I don't think I've seen the term diabolist in the Requiem books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always said diablerists. I think diabolist means one who practices diabolism, which is a form of satanism. It's often just used to mean devil worshiper, and might refer to the Baali in Masquerade or Belial's Brood in Requiem. I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=826932#post826932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the term for 'one who commits Amaranth?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... Amaranthist, I guess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T18:31:00-08:00","id":827237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=826932#post826932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the term for 'one who commits Amaranth?'</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, but we really need to stop institutionalizing plant life.<br /> <br /> Thank you, I'll be here all week.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T19:05:24-08:00","id":827263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=826901#post826901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"159\" data-vbnamecard=\"159\">Leetsepeak</a> I have them roll at the time it happens. The point in time in which they break and give the condition that goes with it right away, though I have seen in other threads that people wait until combat or the scene is over as not to slow down the story. I believe it was determined it is up to the Story teller and the flow of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ask chiefly because it seems hard to hit some breaking points (like say, mass murder) if you're rolling every time you commit the act of murdering somebody, unless you make an additional roll for it at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> I'm sort of inclined to do it at the end of a scene at this point, but it being up to the storyteller makes good sense.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T01:16:13-08:00","id":827353,"title":"","content":"Strix are known for their patience. I'm sure the Beast would be willing to wait after one opportunity to pull the vampire down if it meant a better one could arise later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:30:44-08:00","id":827411,"title":"","content":"About sunlight damage, when a low Blood Potency(1~2) vampire is exposed to sunlight, he suffers damage immediately or just after 10 minutes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T04:45:16-08:00","id":827417,"title":"","content":"10 mins, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T05:08:03-08:00","id":827423,"title":"","content":"If I'm the centre of attention and I want to use Face in the Crowd without modifying it with Cloak of Night, how does that work? Does it automatically fail to work against those paying attention to me, does it immediately work and they stop really noticing me, or does each person get a Wits+Composure-Obfuscate roll as if I had done something to draw notice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:05:00-08:00","id":829996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=826901#post826901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forgive me, but logic dictates it would be impossible for the earth to open up and swallow someone without leaving any traces of the event either. And a humanoild ( vampire or ghoul ) can't logically transform into a cat.. or a bat.. either, but they do. It's magic and I think magic throws logic out the window. I do not think we should look into the 1edition books for reference here, because protean was completely reworked.<br /> <br /> Why would the developers say ghouls can have any 2 dots of clan disciplines, if they couldn't use Protean? not being able to use the first dot of this discipline, means they wouldnt be able to really use the rest of it either. To me that is illogical. Perhaps we do need Rose or someone else to clarify this one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Setting says shapeshifting is possible and earth melding is possible but they have their own rules and logic,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's magic and I think magic throws logic out the window. </div> </div> </div>Nonsense the best fictional worlds including those with magic have their own internal logic. It is basic storytelling 101<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not think we should look into the 1edition books for reference here, because protean was completely reworked. </div> </div> </div>BOLLOCKS! You have a most of the same powers. reinterpreted but still there. <br /> Unmarked Grave is still Earthmeld functionally. It is just the first dot now and is used to modify forms giving by other levels.<br /> It doesn't state it lets ghouls breathe underground.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T20:07:37-08:00","id":829997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=827411#post827411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About sunlight damage, when a low Blood Potency(1~2) vampire is exposed to sunlight, he suffers damage immediately or just after 10 minutes?</div> </div> </div> </div>not canon but you could divide the damage and parcel it out over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T21:39:26-08:00","id":830030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=829997#post829997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not canon but you could divide the damage and parcel it out over time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a table for exactly this way back when 2e first came out (under the name Blood and Smoke at the time). <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19F1RVRp-kuhDApl_eP1Z_y8FPT1jar5gOnU9VJtYUF8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the link</a> if anyone wants to check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T00:21:08-08:00","id":830072,"title":"","content":"For sunlight damage, I actually inflict damage upon first contact, and then a second time after 10 minutes. For the simple reason of: A vampire shouldn't be able to walk around for 9 minutes, hide for a minute somewhere and move again unharmed. <br /> <br /> But I'm not sure what the RAW here is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T02:19:14-08:00","id":830108,"title":"","content":"See, I don't really like that idea, because it just generates the same problem in the opposite direction. If it takes ten minutes to gain 1 lethal damage, you shouldn't get it for a 30 second trip. What if the vampire walks under a series of bridges? <br /> <br /> I'd probably have it be a scene by scene basis. If you expose yourself for nine minutes and then later in the same scene you go out again, the clock keeps going from where it left off. If there's been a scene change, it resets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:10:27-08:00","id":830119,"title":"","content":"I don't see the problem in the opposite direction. Your skin and blood payed the price of strolling down the street, you received the damage - tata. <br /> <br /> Of course, for damage better dividable, it could be 1 lethal every 5 minutes. <br /> <br /> I'm more concerned with vampires having a price for walking down in the sun, than on trying to avoid them overpaying for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:29:08-08:00","id":830126,"title":"","content":"It devalues the cost of raising blood potency or losing humanity. As you have it it's possible for a blood potency 1 vampire and a blood potency 5 vampire to stand in the sun for the same amount of time and get the same amount of damage. That ain't right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:53:05-08:00","id":830136,"title":"","content":"Having it the other way around does the same <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If you only deal damage after the set amount of time, you can have both blood potency 1 vampire and blood potency 5 vampire to stand in the sun for the same amount of time and get the same amount of damage. That is not right either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T03:55:59-08:00","id":830137,"title":"","content":"No you can't. Blood potency 5 gets it every turn. They <i>do</i> get hit as soon as they walk out the door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T04:01:02-08:00","id":830138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=830137#post830137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No you can't. Blood potency 5 gets it every turn. They <i>do</i> get hit as soon as they walk out the door.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not necessarily. What if I jump between two dark spots, which happen to have a window of light within a turn? I spent less than a turn in the sun, and under your way of doing it - I should get no damage, since I didn't end my turn in sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T04:05:42-08:00","id":830140,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, in that situation they would be fine, because otherwise there's no distinction between bp 5 and bp 10, who should be hit 5 times as fast and thus probably couldn't make the crossing without taking at least a lethal.<br /> <br /> Although a vampire at that level would probably know at least a dot of celerity, which complicates matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T04:20:50-08:00","id":830149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=830140#post830140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, in that situation they would be fine, because otherwise there's no distinction between bp 5 and bp 10, who should be hit 5 times as fast and thus probably couldn't make the crossing without taking at least a lethal.<br /> <br /> Although a vampire at that level would probably know at least a dot of celerity, which complicates matters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> or he wouldn't? Anyways, for those suffering more than one damage, or more than once a time interval, it's easy enough to subdivide the damage throughout the time. <br /> <br /> But at least in my games - get out in the sun - get damage. In character, characters don't count damage levels, and they don't know how many minutes they can take without damage. They just know that older more inhumane vampires die faster. So it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> All in all, it's a preference thing, I guess. But I find it more important to preserve the themes which come with vampire and in one part are shown as &quot;you can no longer touch the sun easily&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T04:28:45-08:00","id":830154,"title":"","content":"Vampires can't count damage, but they <i>can</i> tell the difference between &quot;some&quot; and &quot;none&quot;. So it would be very obvious that the amount of time all vampires could go without damage is &quot;none at all&quot;, but then it takes a variable amount of time to get notably worse. Which is not what the fluff presents as happening at all. I like my grace periods. If you haven't earned insta-damage, you don't get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T05:37:40-08:00","id":830171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=830154#post830154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can't count damage, but they <i>can</i> tell the difference between &quot;some&quot; and &quot;none&quot;. So it would be very obvious that the amount of time all vampires could go without damage is &quot;none at all&quot;, but then it takes a variable amount of time to get notably worse. Which is not what the fluff presents as happening at all. I like my grace periods. If you haven't earned insta-damage, you don't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's also fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As I said, I put emphasis on the fact that sun burns, so for me, all sun visits deal damage. For you that's not the case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So let's move on..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T05:43:36-08:00","id":830175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=830030#post830030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a table for exactly this way back when 2e first came out (under the name Blood and Smoke at the time). <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19F1RVRp-kuhDApl_eP1Z_y8FPT1jar5gOnU9VJtYUF8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the link</a> if anyone wants to check it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking Splitting the lethal out as bashing ay Humanity 7-10 for bp 1. say after 3 minutes a bashing per minute? Yeah you could spend blood to keep looking bruised or sickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:47:24-08:00","id":830988,"title":"","content":"Can revenants be diablerized? Do normal rules apply?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What to call someone who commits 'Amaranth.' </div> </div> </div>We use <i>Amaranthine </i>as the formal noun/adjective for a diablerist, but I'm not sure if we nabbed it from somewhere or it came up organically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:03:15-08:00","id":830994,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly sure the answer is no, they can't. But I can't quite remember where I saw the ruling. Might have been in the FAQ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:08:16-08:00","id":831153,"title":"","content":"Why would you want to Diablerie a Revenant? They'll always have lower Blood Potency than you, and it's pretty unlikely they'll have any Disciplines you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T12:08:59-08:00","id":831203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=831153#post831153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you want to Diablerie a Revenant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because sometimes thirsty won't wait<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T13:27:01-08:00","id":831250,"title":"","content":"To be fair the way diablerie works now relative blood potency is irrelevant. A bp 5 vamp will always get you one dot of blood potency, regardless of whether you're at 1 dot or 9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T14:00:16-08:00","id":831280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=831153#post831153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you want to Diablerie a Revenant? They'll always have lower Blood Potency than you, and it's pretty unlikely they'll have any Disciplines you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly for story reasons. In terms of mechanics, you would still in theory get 1 XP toward Blood Potency and either a level-one basic discipline you don't have, or a skill point. Not a great bargain for the humanity loss + addiction potential, but I was also curious if an existing diablerie addict would see a revenant as a tempting fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T14:26:16-08:00","id":831290,"title":"","content":"It is possible for a revenant to have expertise in disciplines. That's probably how the longer-lasting ones manage to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T14:29:48-08:00","id":831292,"title":"","content":"I'd probably allow it as a method to get access to the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lonely-together/\" target=\"_blank\">Agah</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T11:31:47-08:00","id":832625,"title":"","content":"I think it would be fantastic if we could get a developer in here to answer questions about first edition to second edition. On if we should use first edition rules for second edition things, when the second edition does not agree with what our thoughts think it should mean. <br /> <br /> If ghouls can not use Unmarked Grave it would mean that they can not use the rest of protean to it's fullest. Though, no where in the book does it say that they can't use it or that there are different rules for disciplines for a ghoul's use of a discipline.<br /> <br /> Unmarked grave is as much Earth melding as Idol is Sovereignty. Or Auspex is.. Auspex .. I am not trying to bring up a dead argument, but I Am trying to get some outside ruling. <br /> <br /> Should we use 1st edition rules for 2nd edition problems ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T12:11:07-08:00","id":832648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=832625#post832625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If ghouls can not use Unmarked Grave it would mean that they can not use the rest of protean to it's fullest. Though, no where in the book does it say that they can't use it or that there are different rules for disciplines for a ghoul's use of a discipline.<br /> <br /> Unmarked grave is as much Earth melding as Idol is Sovereignty. Or Auspex is.. Auspex .. I am not trying to bring up a dead argument, but I Am trying to get some outside ruling. <br /> <br /> Should we use 1st edition rules for 2nd edition problems ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean this is definitely a YMMV question, but I think the general philosophy is that you shouldn't use 1e mechanics for 2e stuff, no.<br /> <br /> It's a decision you need to make for your own table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T12:49:41-08:00","id":832684,"title":"","content":"I have a question that's been bugging me, and I've gotten conflicting information on it. A lot of powers talk about having Auspex active giving bonuses to things, or being active and then causing a Clash of Wills. But Auspex isn't something that IS left on anymore. The first 3 levels are all instant rolls that let you ask specific questions. So:<br /> 1) How does Auspex give a benefit to A Taste of Blood? Is it assumed that if you have it you get the bonus if you want it, without activating it, or do you need to activate it and ask something liek &quot;What does this blood taste like?&quot; or the like?<br /> 2) The first level doesn't give an example question for piercing obfuscate; do you need to use a specific question for it, or when you activate the power does it let you get a Clash even if the potentially Obfuscated (or otherwise hidden) character wasn't your target or focus? Or can you activate it once and then can Clash with obfuscate/etc for the rest of the scene even without spending vitae and asking more questions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T13:34:05-08:00","id":832721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=832684#post832684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) How does Auspex give a benefit to A Taste of Blood? Is it assumed that if you have it you get the bonus if you want it, without activating it, or do you need to activate it and ask something liek &quot;What does this blood taste like?&quot; or the like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you would have to want to know something about it. You are set with the scenario where there is blood and you would activate auspex and drink it to get the +2<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=832684#post832684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The first level doesn't give an example question for piercing obfuscate; do you need to use a specific question for it, or when you activate the power does it let you get a Clash even if the potentially Obfuscated (or otherwise hidden) character wasn't your target or focus? Or can you activate it once and then can Clash with obfuscate/etc for the rest of the scene even without spending vitae and asking more questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again I would think it would be something like you know that there is someone here, or that there should be some one there. You saw them or have a good reason to feel it. Then you would activate auspex to target the beast giving you the clash of wills.<br /> <br /> Or even if you dont have a good reason to believe something is there... You could go into every place and pop your auspex looking for the danger provoking the clash of wills. Also Lashing out Stops some of the powers as well. (3rd dot of obfuscate )<br /> <br /> Something to keep in mind: The book states &quot;(when)<i>Auspex is turned against a vampire hidden by Obfuscate, there is a Clash of Wills.&quot; </i> You would need to target them.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: Auspex is not my forte.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=831280#post831280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly for story reasons. In terms of mechanics, you would still in theory get 1 XP toward Blood Potency and either a level-one basic discipline you don't have, or a skill point. Not a great bargain for the humanity loss + addiction potential, but I was also curious if an existing diablerie addict would see a revenant as a tempting fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no potential for diablerie addiction. You are addicted. The end. ( however there is the vitae addiction potential which you could maybe pass. Resolve composure - how much vitae you drank )<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=831153#post831153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you want to Diablerie a Revenant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that a diablerie addict wont care that their fix isnt a good fix... it's still a fix. They need to roll resolve+composure not to do it any time they are tempted with it. Your drug is your drug, most dont really care if its watered down a little ...<br /> <br /> \u200b Also Is there a way to tell a Revenant from a real vampire just by looking at them? Waking up with them, sure, but bumping into one on the streets? I am not sure if you could see the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-18-2016, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T23:16:07-08:00","id":833065,"title":"","content":"How I run Auspex? <br /> Auspex 1 question: Is anything hidden from my sight? / is anyone obfuscated here? / how many people are in this room? <br /> Etc provokes a clash of wills against the obfuscated people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:28:45-08:00","id":833371,"title":"","content":"The character asks the question, but he doesn't gets a literal answer, he gets shown. If they win the clash of wills they see darkness and fog part away to reveal the obfuscated object or person, they don't get a psychic voice in their head that spells the things out for them. So always assume it defaults to &quot;As far as you can tell...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:28:32-08:00","id":838500,"title":"","content":"Mechanically, how would you create a trap that would stake a vampire? Obviously the Crafts skill should be involved, but what does it take to make a device that upon activation, stabs a stake through a vampire's heart?<br /> <br /> For clarity's sake, by the rules a staking brings a -3 penalty to attack rolls to the table. I always figured this was part of being a targeted attack, as the penalty is the same as making a specified attack on the heart. After that, it's required to do 5 points of Lethal damage. And be wooden.<br /> <br /> Lets try to keep this solely about the mechanics of Crafting a device to remotely shove a stake through a vampire's heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Removed sections about a possible seat that were so distracting no one could read any part of the post but that. 02-28-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:43:08-08:00","id":838507,"title":"","content":"Hiding a mechanism powerful and accurate enough to put a piece of wood through someone's rib cage and pierce the heart inside the back of a chair sounds incredibly difficult if not impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:05:26-08:00","id":838604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=838507#post838507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hiding a mechanism powerful and accurate enough to put a piece of wood through someone's rib cage and pierce the heart inside the back of a chair sounds incredibly difficult if not impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make it something like a booth, or a sofa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T08:57:44-08:00","id":838665,"title":"","content":"Since mentioning the seat made the simple question impossible to answer, I removed it.<br /> <br /> So, again, mechanics of a device to stake vampires through the heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:35:30-08:00","id":838677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=838665#post838665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, again, mechanics of a device to stake vampires through the heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would use a Build Equipment action for this. It's a physical object, so the dice pool will be Wits + Crafts. You need it to do at least 5 damage, so that's a +5 equipment bonus, translating to a -5 penalty to the roll. You also want the stake to be hidden and to trigger the attack when the vampire does something to set it off, such as sitting in the chair. That'd be an extra modification to the equipment, which would normally add another -1 penalty to the roll, but we've already reached the cap of -5. Personally, I would rule that exceeding the -5 dice maximum means this equipment is too complex to craft in a single roll, so it has to be done as an extended action. On extended crafting actions, the target number is equal to the equipment bonus + the number of non-bonus-adding modifications, + 1. So, we're left with an extended Wits + Crafts roll with a target number of 7 to build this device. I'd also say you need some simple tools and materials to build a complex machine like this. Probably an Availability 1 purchase for each, if the character doesn't already have them. Though, if the character is big on crafting I'd say they probably have what they need lying around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-28-2016, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:39:47-08:00","id":838682,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Charlaquin. I've only glossed over the Chronicles books' crafting stuff, but our characters are great on Crafting and good on Resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T11:37:03-08:00","id":838727,"title":"","content":"If you want to go cheap, just fit a bunch of long wooden spikes on a wooden board or sheetrock/drywall roughly the size and length of a mattress. Attach it to the ceiling with hinges on one side to swing down and slam into someone's back when triggered. It you want to conceal the spikes, you can affix the spiked board to another board or section of drywall and allow it to pivot down before striking the target. Someone with the relevant carpentry or tile installing skills could probably throw together a decent working one in about a day's work. If you want it concealed in furniture, get somebody who can do furniture reupholstery, someone with a passing knowledge to fix small electric/hydraulic engines, buy a shiatsu massage chair, install spikes onto the internal massage wheels and reupholster the chair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-28-2016, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T18:31:08-08:00","id":838893,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't allow it except for a specific vampire. Where exactly the heart is depends on body size and shape and height and all manner of factors that differ from one vampire to the next. You could maybe make a trap for a specific vampire if you knew their dimensions, but you really can't one-size-fits-all that sort of thing. Even then it'd be hard to pack enough force into small enough space to hide it as a trap. Except in a rule-of-cool campaign, that's just way to silly. In that kind of campaign, then yeah, just use normal crafting rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T19:08:28-08:00","id":838914,"title":"","content":"Can a vampire use dominate and majesty on Ghost/spirit/angels without special devotion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T19:19:01-08:00","id":838916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=838914#post838914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a vampire use dominate and majesty on Ghost/spirit/angels without special devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2nd edition, nothing stops that, so long as you have some way to perceive them, communicate, and make eye contact if needed. For angels, though, you might want to follow the same advice as for the Mage interim rules; if you try to command it to go against its programming, you fail, because you effectively end up in a Clash of Wills with the godmachine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 02-28-2016, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T19:35:49-08:00","id":838922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=838500#post838500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For clarity's sake, by the rules a staking brings a -3 penalty to attack rolls to the table. I always figured this was part of being a targeted attack, as the penalty is the same as making a specified attack on the heart. After that, it's required to do 5 points of Lethal damage. And be wooden.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Jumping in on this. This actually came up in my game last night. Stakes are a 0L weapon. Vampires downgrade Lethal to Bashing. So a stake does Bashing to a vampire or am I wrong on that? and the book says you need to do &quot;5 damage&quot; to stake them... it doesnt say lethal or bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T19:42:30-08:00","id":838926,"title":"","content":"Yes, the book says 5 points of damage and it doesn't say Lethal or Bashing. That was a mistake on my part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T19:54:47-08:00","id":838931,"title":"","content":"Yeah we went with Bashing, but we werent entirely sure since a stake is kind of a special case thing. Maybe it still did lethal..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T02:51:55-08:00","id":839034,"title":"","content":"The special case is that it leaves vampires torpid. No need to double-dip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T06:36:19-08:00","id":839122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=838914#post838914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a vampire use dominate and majesty on Ghost/spirit/angels without special devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not a problem. Nothing stops you from doing that in 1e either. The only caveat was that they had to qualify like a normal being - spirits without eyes couldn't be Dominated, for instance. Ephemeral beings of human intellect can't be affected by Animalism. Etc. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T06:38:53-08:00","id":839124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=838931#post838931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah we went with Bashing, but we werent entirely sure since a stake is kind of a special case thing. Maybe it still did lethal..</div> </div> </div> </div> The only special cases are 1) magic powers / enhancements that specifically deal lethal damage, 2) the teeth of supernatural predators (vampires and werewolves), and 3) Kindred Dueling FS. Someone who uses a Theban spell to enchant a stake or has Kindred Dueling 3 can cause lethal with a stake, but those are the only exceptions I'm aware of.<br /> <br /> Some writers have suggested that weapons that would normally deal aggravated damage (woodchipper!) would deal lethal damage to Kindred, but that's not an official rule, merely a suggested rule of thumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:10:43-08:00","id":839138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=839124#post839124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2) the teeth of supernatural predators (vampires and werewolves)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is only in these two cases. It isn't the teeth of all supernaturals, it doesn't say that in the book. It says vampires fangs, and the werewolf book specifies werewolf bites bypass supernatural resistance and specifically mentions vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:54:23-08:00","id":839173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=839138#post839138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is only in these two cases. It isn't the teeth of all supernaturals, it doesn't say that in the book. It says vampires fangs, and the werewolf book specifies werewolf bites bypass supernatural resistance and specifically mentions vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is why I listed vampires and werewolves? Are vampires and werewolves suddenly not supernatural predators? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:02:59-08:00","id":839179,"title":"","content":"I think it was simply being clarified because, for example, Demons are supernatural and could be considered predators. Less likely, but maybe a changeling too, a beast one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-29-2016, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:03:16-08:00","id":839181,"title":"","content":"Spirits are supernatural predators, and have no special ability to do Lethal damage to vampires with their teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:15:23-08:00","id":839185,"title":"","content":"Most of them are predators, but they're not all <i>symbolically resonant</i> with predation. I do have to wonder how the ones that <i>are</i> fare in this situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:22:57-08:00","id":839191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=839185#post839185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of them are predators, but they're not all <i>symbolically resonant</i> with predation. I do have to wonder how the ones that <i>are</i> fare in this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>'The spirit\u2019s attacks inflict bashing damage unless its nature (a spirit with metal fists, for example) indicates that it should inflict lethal wounds instead.'<br /> <br /> No indication that it pierces through supernatural resistance. And since vampires are not called out as having a weakness to the teeth of predators it's not in their book either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:21:28-08:00","id":839241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=839191#post839191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'The spirit\u2019s attacks inflict bashing damage unless its nature (a spirit with metal fists, for example) indicates that it should inflict lethal wounds instead.'<br /> <br /> No indication that it pierces through supernatural resistance. And since vampires are not called out as having a weakness to the teeth of predators it's not in their book either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't forget that vampires downgrade Lethal to bashing. Even a dagger which is indicated as Lethal... still only does bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:21:31-08:00","id":839357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=839124#post839124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some writers have suggested that weapons that would normally deal aggravated damage (woodchipper!) would deal lethal damage to Kindred, but that's not an official rule, merely a suggested rule of thumb.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire the Requiem 2e pg 90</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those few terrible things that cause aggravated wounds<br /> to mortals cause only lethal harm to vampires. This mostly<br /> includes terrible harm from chemicals, certain supernatural<br /> punishment, and the skills of utmost masters in certain fighting<br /> styles meant to maximize debilitating bodily harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's official and it's in the book. Not really a suggested rule of thumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:25:52-08:00","id":839360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=839357#post839357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's official and it's in the book. Not really a suggested rule of thumb.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh, missed that one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:31:26-08:00","id":839363,"title":"","content":"deleted for duplicate reasons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T13:01:52-08:00","id":840121,"title":"","content":"3 Questions:<br /> Which Mystery from the Ordo Dracul is mostly like to make Mad Science devices?<br /> Is there any Mad Science merits for 2nd edition?<br /> I'm having some trouble understanding Night Doctor Surgery merit to be Cartians exclusive. Ordo Dracul members don't experiment with this kind of stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T14:26:03-08:00","id":840172,"title":"","content":"First question No one mystery is more likely than another to use or create mad science devices. The Oath of the Dying Light would the the greater oath most likely to do so, since that's their purpose.<br /> 2nd question: Not specifically in that category no.<br /> 3rd question: Not really. Night Surgery would be a series of routine surgical techniques that benefits the patient undergoing the surgery. Vivisection, which is what the Ordo Dracul engages in (also reflected by the numerous Humanity checks that go along with their practice) is neither routine nor conducted with the benefit of the patient in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-01-2016, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T02:27:26-08:00","id":840497,"title":"","content":"What is best mechanical way to reflect character relying on artificially stored blood to supply herself? Resources (and if yes, then what is proposed cost of a vitae point) or simply refluffing one of the other Merits? Refluffed Herd?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:12:10-08:00","id":840521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=840497#post840497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is best mechanical way to reflect character relying on artificially stored blood to supply herself? Resources (and if yes, then what is proposed cost of a vitae point) or simply refluffing one of the other Merits? Refluffed Herd?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say Herd. It's perfectly written for the thing, you have a constant stream of vitae, and you need to maintain it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:18:47-08:00","id":840527,"title":"","content":"Status (Hospital)? Contacts? Allies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:45:07-08:00","id":840533,"title":"","content":"I like Herd because it provides fast and hard &quot;here is how much extra vitae can you get, no rolls involved&quot;. For Status and other Merits, I kinda like them, but they would need a way to check if and how much of blood you get. I can see Status as something that allows you something &quot;roll X+Y, you gain Z vitae&quot;, basically alternate feeding method. Suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T03:59:06-08:00","id":840539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=840497#post840497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is best mechanical way to reflect character relying on artificially stored blood to supply herself? Resources (and if yes, then what is proposed cost of a vitae point) or simply refluffing one of the other Merits? Refluffed Herd?</div> </div> </div> </div>Treat it like any acquisition. Any of those merits can afford them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T04:20:25-08:00","id":840545,"title":"","content":"I'm a dumb person. I forgot about Feeding Grounds and how standard feeding rules worked in general, instead of specific situations I've seen in play. <br /> I think that Herd for &quot;stored at home&quot; artificial blood, Status+Feeding Ground (Hospital) should get me covered for &quot;feed yourself indirectly without having to hurt a human personally&quot; angle. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T21:11:16-08:00","id":846424,"title":"","content":"Got two question for you guys?<br /> there is a Ordo Dracul coil that allows the Dragon to gain supernatural merits and minor template merits. <br /> So with that in mind, the Dragon can acquire the &quot;A Wolf's Meat&quot; to gain a werewolf's Primal Urge 1 regeneration. <br /> Following that, the Dragon then takes &quot;Biokinesis&quot; to heal in half the time. <br /> So my first question is, would this combo allow him to heal 2 bashing a turn, 1lethal in 8 minutes, and 1 aggravated in 2 day? <br /> <br /> My secondary question is, werewolf regeneration has special rules for taking aggravated damage.<br /> &quot;Only silver and supernatural powers (including Gifts, mage spells, and vampiric Disciplines) can cause aggravated damage to Uratha directly. Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a human.&quot;<br /> So would the Dragon be able to reduce the damage by two steps. Example of being hit by a grenade would normally do 4 aggravated, so would the vampire take 4 lethal or 4 bashing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T21:18:32-08:00","id":846429,"title":"","content":"Does anything exciting happen to Kindred at high Blood Potency, other than raising their Attribute caps, letting them spend extra Vitae/turn, and requiring them to feed on Kindred blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T21:19:55-08:00","id":846430,"title":"","content":"A Wolf's Meat is a Tell, not a Merit.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> That will probably be answered in 1000 Years of Night. The big thing is they're established, and will be following in Danse Macabre's 'elder as conspiracy' theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-13-2016, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T21:43:55-08:00","id":846436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846429#post846429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anything exciting happen to Kindred at high Blood Potency, other than raising their Attribute caps, letting them spend extra Vitae/turn, and requiring them to feed on Kindred blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. They just get better at doing what they've already been doing, maybe branch out more with experience or Diablerie or whatever.<br /> <br /> That's pretty terrifying already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:26:24-08:00","id":846455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846424#post846424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got two question for you guys?<br /> there is a Ordo Dracul coil that allows the Dragon to gain supernatural merits and minor template merits.<br /> So with that in mind, the Dragon can acquire the &quot;A Wolf's Meat&quot; to gain a werewolf's Primal Urge 1 regeneration.<br /> Following that, the Dragon then takes &quot;Biokinesis&quot; to heal in half the time.<br /> So my first question is, would this combo allow him to heal 2 bashing a turn, 1lethal in 8 minutes, and 1 aggravated in 2 day?<br /> <br /> My secondary question is, werewolf regeneration has special rules for taking aggravated damage.<br /> &quot;Only silver and supernatural powers (including Gifts, mage spells, and vampiric Disciplines) can cause aggravated damage to Uratha directly. Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a human.&quot;<br /> So would the Dragon be able to reduce the damage by two steps. Example of being hit by a grenade would normally do 4 aggravated, so would the vampire take 4 lethal or 4 bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't heal without spending blood, so no to the first one.<br /> <br /> And assuming the grenade is an incediary, 4 Aggravated. It's still a Bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:32:29-08:00","id":846457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846430#post846430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Wolf's Meat is a Tell, not a Merit.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> That will probably be answered in 1000 Years of Night. The big thing is they're established, and will be following in Danse Macabre's 'elder as conspiracy' theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extra Tell is a 3 dot merit that gives a Tell, so thats how a Dragon can get Wolf's Meat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:42:26-08:00","id":846458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846457#post846457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extra Tell is a 3 dot merit that gives a Tell, so thats how a Dragon can get Wolf's Meat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks like Luna or Father Wolf decides whether it works or not so even then I'd doubt the ability works with the Tell. We'll have to see the finished ability.<br /> <br /> A better way to go about it would just to be an Embraced Wolf-blooded, as they keep their Tell in the first place. Though there's probably better ones for a vampire to have, like Bite.<br /> <br /> But still, Elfive would be right, since they don't heal without spending blood they would not gain any benefit from it. I think there is an ability somewhere that lets them heal as normal but I may be wrong. If so, it would work during there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-13-2016, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:48:05-08:00","id":846462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846455#post846455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires don't heal without spending blood, so no to the first one.<br /> <br /> And assuming the grenade is an incediary, 4 Aggravated. It's still a Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the Tell would be a supernatural healing of sorts and last I checked vampires can still be healed through such means. Because im not sure if werewolf healing is described as rejecting wound that would weaken the hunter or their innate hyper healing.<br /> While the grenade was just an example of something that does aggravated damage but not the main point. Would the Dragon be able to reduce the damage by two steps or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T00:33:28-08:00","id":846480,"title":"","content":"The Coil's fluff implies merits like wolf-blooded's tell and similar are meant to be included, the initial wording was likely decided upon before the wolf blooded template was done. But yeah, the final product will likely give you your answer there.<br /> <br /> As for gaining regeneration, I'd say no offhand, as a werewolf's regeneration is meant to be a speeding up of and enhancing of normal living tissue regeneration. Vampires lack that, so I'd personally say neither of those actually give them any benefit to healing. They'd need something that specifically provides magical healing, rather than speeding up natural healing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:44:45-07:00","id":846539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846424#post846424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there is a Ordo Dracul coil that allows the Dragon to gain supernatural merits and minor template merits.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a highly controversial playtest Coil that's had a lot of feedback and is going to be revised. The final product could change a lot. <br /> <br /> And you are heavily into crossover territory here, to the point this isn't even really a Vampire question anymore. Its a question about what happens when you mix a werewolf and a mortal psychic ability. And, with all things crossover, this is going to be entirely up to individual STs and how they run things. I personally wouldn't let you halve the time with Biokinesis. I always round up, so 1 Bashing / half round rounds up to 1 bashing / round. Others will say different things. And all of them will be right, because there is no way we'll ever have an official answer for this entirely niche section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So would the Dragon be able to reduce the damage by two steps. Example of being hit by a grenade would normally do 4 aggravated, so would the vampire take 4 lethal or 4 bashing? </div> </div> </div> Vampires aren't Uratha. They're still vampires. If you are allowed to take &quot;A Wolf's Meat,&quot; you only gain what is specifically in that Tell. You become vulnerable to silver, take agg, and break out into a burn/rash from touching it, and you regenerate 1 bashing/1 lethal per turn. <br /> <br /> At no point do you gain the ability to shrug off damage. Silver allergy and flesh regeneration is it. There is no Tell for changing what kind of damage you take besides gaining silver as a bane.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:20:57-07:00","id":846597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846480#post846480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Coil's fluff implies merits like wolf-blooded's tell and similar are meant to be included, the initial wording was likely decided upon before the wolf blooded template was done. But yeah, the final product will likely give you your answer there.<br /> <br /> As for gaining regeneration, I'd say no offhand, as a werewolf's regeneration is meant to be a speeding up of and enhancing of normal living tissue regeneration. Vampires lack that, so I'd personally say neither of those actually give them any benefit to healing. They'd need something that specifically provides magical healing, rather than speeding up natural healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:46:12-07:00","id":846610,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the coil is fluffed as being about regaining the abilities you had in life. A Tell naturally sticks around anyway, so they'd already have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T10:50:14-07:00","id":846632,"title":"","content":"Alright thank you all for your guys input on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T20:40:08-07:00","id":846904,"title":"","content":"Can I make a person do a Killing Blow with a pistol to their own head using Dominate? Do I need Dominate 1 or Dominate 2 to make that happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T20:52:26-07:00","id":846907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846904#post846904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I make a person do a Killing Blow with a pistol to their own head using Dominate? Do I need Dominate 1 or Dominate 2 to make that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, Dominate 1 and 2 explicitly forbade suicidal commands for the enthralled. While 2e has no equivalent statement, I doubt that intent would've changed between editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T21:02:35-07:00","id":846912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846907#post846907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 1e, Dominate 1 and 2 explicitly forbade suicidal commands for the enthralled. While 2e has no equivalent statement, I doubt that intent would've changed between editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue clan description explicitly has that as an example of why you should be afraid of them in their opening paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T21:44:09-07:00","id":846930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846904#post846904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I make a person do a Killing Blow with a pistol to their own head using Dominate? Do I need Dominate 1 or Dominate 2 to make that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Kill yourself with this&quot; or &quot;shoot your own head&quot; both fit in the four word limit for Dominate 1. Though an argument could be made that attempted suicide should trigger a Breaking Point, which would resolve the Mesmerized Condition. With Dominate 2, the character has to succeed the Breaking Point roll to resolve Dominated. So my ruling would be that you can give the command with Dominate 1, but they'll come back to their senses before they can pull the trigger. With Dominate 2, they'll go through with it if they fail the Breaking Point roll, but if they succeed they'll snap out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T02:29:17-07:00","id":846983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846930#post846930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Kill yourself with this&quot; or &quot;shoot your own head&quot; both fit in the four word limit for Dominate 1. Though an argument could be made that attempted suicide should trigger a Breaking Point, which would resolve the Mesmerized Condition. With Dominate 2, the character has to succeed the Breaking Point roll to resolve Dominated. So my ruling would be that you can give the command with Dominate 1, but they'll come back to their senses before they can pull the trigger. With Dominate 2, they'll go through with it if they fail the Breaking Point roll, but if they succeed they'll snap out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It's worth nothing that it would taken at least 3 turns to implant a Dominated command on someone, making it extremely impractical in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T03:49:56-07:00","id":846998,"title":"","content":"Actually &quot;shoot your husband&quot; is one of the examples given in Dominate 1. and if the breaking point happens before the trigger is pulled the action would never happen, the breaking point needs to happen after the action is taken or dominate 1 is invalid as it stands, becouse most commands would be breaking points for mortals. And so &quot;shoot your own head&quot; is truely a breakingpoint for most and an overtly self-destructive action that presumably are breaking points for most, it would trigger after the trigger was pulled( no pun). The command is given, the command is executed, and in by doing so a breaking point occur and removes the condition. However, a killing blow for most &quot;normal&quot; mortals is still only 3-4 lethal damage, so whilst shot in their own head, their hand was most likely shaky and full of survival instinct, enough to not litterly blow their brains out but maybe just through the jawbone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":".  wrong example. 03-14-2016, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T05:05:51-07:00","id":847016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=846983#post846983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. It's worth nothing that it would taken at least 3 turns to implant a Dominated command on someone, making it extremely impractical in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure it's completely right. In 1v1 combat, imposing rhe mesmerized condition, is enough to stop him to attacks or make anithing else. He becomes quite and ready to recive command.<br /> With more opponents the situation may change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T05:27:32-07:00","id":847022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=847016#post847016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure it's completely right. In 1v1 combat, imposing rhe mesmerized condition, is enough to stop him to attacks or make anithing else. He becomes quite and ready to recive command.<br /> With more opponents the situation may change.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not the ruling everyone takes. And personally, imo, that's the whole reason why Exceptional allows you to command someone right now. Dominate should not be I win button in combat. it should be the thing used to avoid combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T06:38:17-07:00","id":847044,"title":"","content":"It's not the win button....not more then other power as obfuscate or nightmare for example. Someone can always resist the domination effect rolling more successes. Anyway this is my interpretation of the mesmerized condition but it's not specifically written so it's open to other interpretations. But if someone become quieter and reserved as in the official description, how could him going on to fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-14-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:04:19-07:00","id":847075,"title":"","content":"If someone stops screaming while they try to hack you to bits with a machete that technically counts as &quot;quieter and more reserved&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:23:42-07:00","id":847091,"title":"","content":"&quot;Quieter and reserved&quot; can translate to acting detached when using a weapon. Holds a gun at someone with eyes glazed over, not really seeing their target, no emtion on their face, no responce to words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T20:57:03-07:00","id":847520,"title":"","content":"Yeah, &quot;quieter and more reserved&quot; does not mean &quot;automaton standing still awaiting programming&quot;. Otherwise it would be very obvious if someone was under the Mesmerised condition which the condition itself specifies is not the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T08:04:22-07:00","id":847688,"title":"","content":"Probably it's my fault but it's hard for me to figure out someone attacking someone else in a quiet and reserved way. I know that while he is mesmerized he don't seems ipnotized, but in my opinion this simply means that in a dinner he going on to eat (probably without speaking if not directly interpellated). Probably the mesmerized go on in his ways if bumped by someone as nothing happened. I would like to see the answers to this question in a FAQ :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T08:13:00-07:00","id":847693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=847688#post847688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's hard for me to figure out someone attacking someone else in a quiet and reserved way.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing a key word here. They're not &quot;quiet and reserved&quot;, they're &quot;<i>more</i> quiet and reserved&quot; the volume and emotion are dialed back, but if they were previously swinging a chainsaw around whilst screaming like a lunatic there's a lot of room to spare that still involves murdering you.<br /> <br /> Alternately, think samurai. Their stereotypical demeanour is totally &quot;quiet and reserved&quot; even when they're stabbing people in the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T08:16:51-07:00","id":847698,"title":"","content":"If you can attack during that period, wouldn't you be able to Lash Out and break the mesmerization?<br /> <br /> Providing it was used against a vampire, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-15-2016, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T15:05:46-07:00","id":847883,"title":"","content":"As a benchmark, I think that a Mesmerized person should not be able to flip out and start punching the Vampire, or themselves... unless they were already flipping out. In that case, they carry on while staring at the Kindred dumbly.<br /> <br /> I don't think Lashing out is supposed to work against Dominate. There isn't anything about it at all in the whole book.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T15:49:25-07:00","id":847896,"title":"","content":"Not saying it's right or wrong here, but the way I play it out is.. they do the command ... and then do whatever they normally do. If there was a big brawl going on and the command was &quot;dont attack me&quot;, he would keep on attacking the next best target. Or the command was &quot;protect my friends&quot;.. he would start attacking his friends. That is. Until one of his friends clocked him back and broke the dominate. If the command was &quot;Follow me&quot; the person could have a conversation or babble or whine about going along. <br /> <br /> Ophion is correct: You can not lash out against dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T16:29:33-07:00","id":847913,"title":"","content":"Yes, yes, we all know what the book says.<br /> <br /> But since Dominate is just an extension of the the Predatory Aura, it would make sense that, if you were aware of another vampire's attempt to manipulate you with their Predatory Aura, you could Lash Out with yours to break it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T16:33:57-07:00","id":847915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=847913#post847913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, yes, we all know what the book says.<br /> <br /> But since Dominate is just an extension of the the Predatory Aura, it would make sense that, if you were aware of another vampire's attempt to manipulate you with their Predatory Aura, you could Lash Out with yours to break it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same for Majesty but in that case it is specifcally written you can lash out against awe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T17:51:24-07:00","id":847943,"title":"","content":"I would not allow you to lash out against any of the abilities except the 3 that allow it ( majesty, nightmare, and obfuscate ) That is what we have a resistance roll for....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T06:44:29-07:00","id":848124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=847913#post847913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, yes, we all know what the book says.<br /> <br /> But since Dominate is just an extension of the the Predatory Aura, it would make sense that, if you were aware of another vampire's attempt to manipulate you with their Predatory Aura, you could Lash Out with yours to break it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if that worked you don't know IC that you're being Mesmerised without some sort of ability that lets you automatically detect the use of a mental discipline on yourself. I suppose you could establish that, if the ability to lash out against Dominate is house-ruled into your game, your character always uses their action to lash out against anyone who made eye contact with them if they suspect they have Dominate, which would be hilarious. Personally, if I think someone's dominating me I'd rather just punch myself for 1 bashing than try to lash out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:04:48-07:00","id":848402,"title":"","content":"What is the Ventrue clanbook for Requiem second edition? Alternatively what are some of the bloodlines for Ventrue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T14:13:08-07:00","id":848404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xizzicks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848402#post848402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Ventrue clanbook for Requiem second edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is none, though <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/55241/Lords-Over-the-Damned-Ventrue\" target=\"_blank\">you can use the first edition one.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively what are some of the bloodlines for Ventrue? </div> </div> </div>Adrestoi, Apollinaire, Architects of the Monolith, Bron. There's a list <a href=\"http://wodindex.wikispaces.com/Complete+Vampire+the+Requiem\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> that includes which book they're mentioned in. And some of them have <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Bloodline_(VTR)\" target=\"_blank\">wiki entries</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-16-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T17:25:58-07:00","id":848500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xizzicks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848402#post848402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the Ventrue clanbook for Requiem second edition? Alternatively what are some of the bloodlines for Ventrue?</div> </div> </div> </div>To reiterate what was already said in, perhaps, a little more straightforward manner:<br /> <br /> There are zero official Ventrue bloodlines for 2nd edition. If you want any, you will have to use other poster's homebrews or translate the 1st edition bloodlines to 2nd edition yourself. The above poster gave you a great resource for finding 1st edition bloodlines, but you will need to do your own work to use them in 2nd (not that it's hard or anything, just, be aware).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:32:09-07:00","id":848780,"title":"","content":"OK thanks a lot! That link was really helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:59:53-07:00","id":848824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=847883#post847883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Lashing out is supposed to work against Dominate. There isn't anything about it at all in the whole book.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, think about it this way. If the Dominate power fails, there's nothing to Lash Out against. If it succeeds? You're already Mesmerized, and so won't Lash Out. Lashing Out is an agressive action, and when you're hypnotized, you're pliable and docile. There's just no point when it makes sense for you to Lash Out against Dominate.<br /> <br /> Same with Nightmare - you can't Lash Out against Face of the Beast because the Frightened Condition says you're not thinking rationally or able to act against the target of your fear; you're just fleeing, and once you're out of sight, nothing to Lash Out against is around . You can, however, Lash Out against Dread Presence, since its an ongoing effect that doesn't remove your free will. Higher levels of Nightmare can be used without the vampire as a source of the dread- how are you Lashing Out against it? If Dread Presence is active, the vampire is obvious as the source of fear, and can be Lashed Out against.<br /> <br /> Technically, only Awe can be Lashed Out against with Majesty. That's usually enough to stop everything else, since they build on each other. That said, a vampire who's Charmed or Enthralled likely won't want to Lash Out, since its agressive action against someone you like. That is why only Awe is Lash Out-able. The other abilities simply aren't viable targets to fight against.<br /> <br /> Both Majesty and Nightmare can be lashed out against because they are both obvious targets and the victims retain their free will. Dominate's victims... don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:27:56-07:00","id":848832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848824#post848824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, think about it this way. If the Dominate power fails, there's nothing to Lash Out against. If it succeeds? You're already Mesmerized, and so won't Lash Out. Lashing Out is an agressive action, and when you're hypnotized, you're pliable and docile. There's just no point when it makes sense for you to Lash Out against Dominate.<br /> <br /> Same with Nightmare - you can't Lash Out against Face of the Beast because the Frightened Condition says you're not thinking rationally or able to act against the target of your fear; you're just fleeing, and once you're out of sight, nothing to Lash Out against is around . You can, however, Lash Out against Dread Presence, since its an ongoing effect that doesn't remove your free will. Higher levels of Nightmare can be used without the vampire as a source of the dread- how are you Lashing Out against it? If Dread Presence is active, the vampire is obvious as the source of fear, and can be Lashed Out against.<br /> <br /> Technically, only Awe can be Lashed Out against with Majesty. That's usually enough to stop everything else, since they build on each other. That said, a vampire who's Charmed or Enthralled likely won't want to Lash Out, since its agressive action against someone you like. That is why only Awe is Lash Out-able. The other abilities simply aren't viable targets to fight against.<br /> <br /> Both Majesty and Nightmare can be lashed out against because they are both obvious targets and the victims retain their free will. Dominate's victims... don't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perfect <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I would just like to add, that even if you did lash against Charm or Enthrall fro some crazy reason. I dont think it would break the effect. You'd need to stop awe.. which is subtle and you'd have to have a good reason to think that someone is using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:36:44-07:00","id":848840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848824#post848824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, think about it this way. If the Dominate power fails, there's nothing to Lash Out against. If it succeeds? You're already Mesmerized, and so won't Lash Out. Lashing Out is an agressive action, and when you're hypnotized, you're pliable and docile. There's just no point when it makes sense for you to Lash Out against Dominate.<br /> <br /> Same with Nightmare - you can't Lash Out against Face of the Beast because the Frightened Condition says you're not thinking rationally or able to act against the target of your fear; you're just fleeing, and once you're out of sight, nothing to Lash Out against is around . You can, however, Lash Out against Dread Presence, since its an ongoing effect that doesn't remove your free will. Higher levels of Nightmare can be used without the vampire as a source of the dread- how are you Lashing Out against it? If Dread Presence is active, the vampire is obvious as the source of fear, and can be Lashed Out against.<br /> <br /> Technically, only Awe can be Lashed Out against with Majesty. That's usually enough to stop everything else, since they build on each other. That said, a vampire who's Charmed or Enthralled likely won't want to Lash Out, since its agressive action against someone you like. That is why only Awe is Lash Out-able. The other abilities simply aren't viable targets to fight against.<br /> <br /> Both Majesty and Nightmare can be lashed out against because they are both obvious targets and the victims retain their free will. Dominate's victims... don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but what if you lashed out instead of rolling resistance, technically before you got completely hypnotized?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:07:52-07:00","id":848851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848840#post848840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, but what if you lashed out instead of rolling resistance, technically before you got completely hypnotized?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> not possibly under RAW (Or RAI, as far as I can tell).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:17:56-07:00","id":848855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848840#post848840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, but what if you lashed out instead of rolling resistance, technically before you got completely hypnotized?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're lashing out against a nonexistent effect, therefore it fails. However, if you're lashing out against the vampire in anticipation of him trying to mesmerize you, I'd say that might constitute a valid attempt to interrupt action. Unless he opts to respond by lashing out to accept your challenge and turn it into a contest of wills where you just forfeited your resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:47:56-07:00","id":848872,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I would have no problem handling two vampires attempting to use two supernatural powers against each other like that as opposing Lashing Out. I think that it's pretty evocative for a Ventrue and Daeva struggling against each other's Auras in a battle of supremecy, Dominate versus Majesty. But we're entering the world of homebrew. Unlike Nightmare versus Majesty, where you could actually have a Clash to see who's the stronger, Dominate kind of bypasses that step.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:51:56-07:00","id":848874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848855#post848855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're lashing out against a nonexistent effect, therefore it fails. However, if you're lashing out against the vampire in anticipation of him trying to mesmerize you, I'd say that might constitute a valid attempt to interrupt action. Unless he opts to respond by lashing out to accept your challenge and turn it into a contest of wills where you just forfeited your resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're lashing out against a beast trying to hackle yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:18:41-07:00","id":848889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848855#post848855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're lashing out against a nonexistent effect, therefore it fails. However, if you're lashing out against the vampire in anticipation of him trying to mesmerize you, I'd say that might constitute a valid attempt to interrupt action. Unless he opts to respond by lashing out to accept your challenge and turn it into a contest of wills where you just forfeited your resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848874#post848874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're lashing out against a beast trying to hackle yours.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Let me ask you, If Lashing out was intended to be used to counter every discipline, why would they go through all the time in putting in resistance rolls to it? Lashing out is Violent and rough and people know you are doing it. If you did it in front of humans, they would know you are... weird at least. If you lost you get a really nasty condition.<br /> <br /> Also to lash to interrupt someone's action, you would need celerity to interrupt an action. Lashing takes your turn and if it's not your turn, then.. you dont get to do it. It is an instant action. Dominating is an Instant action. If they are first, then get to dominate, and you get to reflexively resist it. You cant instant action in response because it's not your turn. You could certainly Celerity to go first, lash out, but then that doesnt stop them from dominating on their turn...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-17-2016, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:40:36-07:00","id":848923,"title":"","content":"Lashing Out doesn't need to be violent or rough, it can just be done with a gesture or word. Nothing requires it to look weird in front of humans.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/41372-unhappy-with-b-s-assassination-by-obfuscate?p=41557#post41557\">Rose suggested</a> if you went with the house rule just use it instead of Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:55:56-07:00","id":848934,"title":"","content":"Well, I wouldn't say humans would pick it up, but I think vampires can tell if you do it. Its a rough scrape, compared to more practiced disciplines. <br /> <br /> And I think Lashing Out is different from resistance rolls for a number of reasons. Primarily, because Lashing Out is a concsious choice; you can't Lash Out if you don't realize what's going on. Resistance is reflexive and automatic. <br /> <br /> Actually, here's a question from me. If Majesty, Nightmare, and Dominate are &quot;pushing out&quot; with your Aura, like upgraded versions of Predator Auras... Auspex is an enhancement to Kindred Senses, Obfuscate is twisting your aura inwards and hiding it, and the physicals are like enhancements to Physical Intensity/healing... what's Animalism and Protean? How would you describe them? They don't feel like Aura manipulations, and I don't think there's a base vampire ability they corresond to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:03:38-07:00","id":848940,"title":"","content":"Animalism wrapping the Predatory Aura around the base parts of your brain or tongue, or letting it flow in your blood, depending on the discipline. Animalism really seems like getting the Beast to act as a medium. Protean is sheathing yourself in it, your Aura is what warps your otherwise dead, human flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:11:23-07:00","id":848944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848923#post848923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lashing Out doesn't need to be violent or rough, it can just be done with a gesture or word. Nothing requires it to look weird in front of humans.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/41372-unhappy-with-b-s-assassination-by-obfuscate?p=41557#post41557\">Rose suggested</a> if you went with the house rule just use it instead of Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>&quot; To lash out, the vampire must take a simple action appropriate<br /> to the aspect of predator used. A monstrous Beast growls,<br /> threatens, gnashes teeth, or calls to action. A seductive Beast<br /> sidles up to the prey, whispers beautiful lies, or gives a telling<br /> gaze from across the crowd. A competitive Beast draws a line in<br /> the sand, announces terms, or takes the role of mouse in a chase. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps I am too used to the monstrous beast, but they are all noticeable actions. If someone uses the seductive beast on you by giving you a naughty look, and you respond with the competitive, you don't just give a naughty look back you get up and draw that line, you tell them what's what. &quot;growling, gnashing your teeth&quot; or even giving a call to action all seem like violent actions to me, Drawing the line in the sand, or giving terms of the fight, dont seem to subtle and polite. Seductive is not so violent, but how you respond just might be.<br /> <br /> If someone (dominates) looks into your eyes and you respond with growling and snapping your teeth.... I would say that would be pretty darn weird....<br /> <br /> <br /> Just like to point out that lashing out costs a willpower if done against a vampire, and resistance roll is free. You are going to be running into some serious WP issues if your response to everything is to lash out.<br /> <br /> Like MCN said, &quot; Lashing Out is a concsious choice; you can't Lash Out if you don't realize what's going on. Resistance is reflexive and automatic. &quot;<br /> ^ totes agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-17-2016, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:39:38-07:00","id":848957,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hey, you. Fuck off mate.&quot; Works for me. A dirty look works, as well. Or wolf-whistling the cute ventrue gal because she thought she was hot enough to bewitch you. Totally hawt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:54:38-07:00","id":849002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848957#post848957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hey, you. Fuck off mate.&quot; Works for me. A dirty look works, as well. Or wolf-whistling the cute ventrue gal because she thought she was hot enough to bewitch you. Totally hawt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dont think telling someone to bugger off would fall under Monster or Beast. that's just me though. It's not drawing a line, or setting terms, or .. well doing anything monstrous. Though I can see the whistling working for your seductive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T14:59:22-07:00","id":849003,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://youtu.be/Gt5xBpmHS5Q?t=87\" target=\"_blank\">It all depends on how you say it.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T15:33:51-07:00","id":849011,"title":"","content":"Protean is the fangs, which can retract supercharged further? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's one base ability of vampires where they shift their bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T18:47:17-07:00","id":849068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=848934#post848934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, here's a question from me. If Majesty, Nightmare, and Dominate are &quot;pushing out&quot; with your Aura, like upgraded versions of Predator Auras... Auspex is an enhancement to Kindred Senses, Obfuscate is twisting your aura inwards and hiding it, and the physicals are like enhancements to Physical Intensity/healing... what's Animalism and Protean? How would you describe them? They don't feel like Aura manipulations, and I don't think there's a base vampire ability they corresond to?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that Animalism is Aura manipulation. You're using your aura to communicate with animals, essentially using your Beast to act as an interpreter between yourself and other beasts. You could also look at it as an enhancement to the properties of your Vitae, imbuing it with a small amount of your Predatory Aura to allow it to communicate your commands to the animals that smell or taste it.<br /> <br /> Protean is a bit more of a stretch, but vampires have some minor shapeshifting abilities in the base template. The fangs are an obvious example, but also arguably The Cleansing - returning the vampire's body to the form it was in at the time of embrace. Protean enhances this inherent shapeshifting ability and uses it to make the vampire's body more closely resemble her Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T19:30:29-07:00","id":849079,"title":"","content":"It's possible the fangs and other 'base template' shapeshifting are things they only have due to their Predatory Aura. Protean is just an exploration of that.<br /> <br /> That's sort of how the Wamphyri did it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T20:49:28-07:00","id":849113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849003#post849003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/Gt5xBpmHS5Q?t=87&amp;quot;]It</a> all depends on how you say it.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>I do love that example, but if a normal human saw that... It would be weird. It would make you weird. That was a super visible indicator he isn't human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T05:01:36-07:00","id":849198,"title":"","content":"I can't really see Animalism as Predatory Aura manipulation for a few reasons. I mean, Raise the Familiar isn't really anything related to one's Predatory Aura. I have trouble seeing Summon the Hunt as aura manipulation either. You're not mind controlling anything...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T06:07:45-07:00","id":849213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849198#post849198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not mind controlling anything...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're summoning animals and imprinting them with commands that they follow for a night per success, how is it not mind control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T06:26:18-07:00","id":849217,"title":"","content":"Is it going too far for a Malkovian Prince with compulsive behaviour regarding omens, taboos, and similar superstitious ritual, to order his sheriff to slice off the arm of a vampire who tried to participate in a ritual that requires members of a rank to participate, to prevent them from contaminating the ritual chalice with their blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T06:37:20-07:00","id":849219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849198#post849198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really see Animalism as Predatory Aura manipulation for a few reasons. I mean, Raise the Familiar isn't really anything related to one's Predatory Aura. I have trouble seeing Summon the Hunt as aura manipulation either. You're not mind controlling anything...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Raise the Familiar is the odd power out in that set. It doesn't really follow the rest of the Discipline's progression. And summon the hunt is definitely mind control, every animal that tastes the blood is forced to carry out the command you imprinted on it. But both do fall under the &quot;enhancement to the natural properties of Vitae&quot; explanation (the only power in the set that doesn't is Feral Whispers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T06:37:44-07:00","id":849220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849217#post849217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it going too far for a Malkovian Prince with compulsive behaviour regarding omens, taboos, and similar superstitious ritual, to order his sheriff to slice off the arm of a vampire who tried to participate in a ritual that requires members of a rank to participate, to prevent them from contaminating the ritual chalice with their blood?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems fine to me, for a particulary despotic prince. Question is, why is he still in charge? Why are his allies still backing him? If not, how close are we to the coup?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T06:56:29-07:00","id":849230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849217#post849217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it going too far for a Malkovian Prince with compulsive behaviour regarding omens, taboos, and similar superstitious ritual, to order his sheriff to slice off the arm of a vampire who tried to participate in a ritual that requires members of a rank to participate, to prevent them from contaminating the ritual chalice with their blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something that could happen. It probably wouldn't endear others to the Prince, if they were fond of their arms. But that depends on what the goal of the contamination was, or rather, what the rest of the All Night's Society thinks of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T07:33:49-07:00","id":849246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849219#post849219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Raise the Familiar is the odd power out in that set. It doesn't really follow the rest of the Discipline's progression. And summon the hunt is definitely mind control, every animal that tastes the blood is forced to carry out the command you imprinted on it. But both do fall under the &quot;enhancement to the natural properties of Vitae&quot; explanation (the only power in the set that doesn't is Feral Whispers).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've actually always thought that Raise the Familiar was a hint that Vampires could also develop necromantic powers similar to Strix possessing dead bodies or that their auras could affect the dead too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T07:35:45-07:00","id":849248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849220#post849220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems fine to me, for a particulary despotic prince. Question is, why is he still in charge? Why are his allies still backing him? If not, how close are we to the coup?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer is, the alternative is worse. The longer answer is that three of the now six families that run the city - Syrah, Murmure, and Stylo - thoroughly oppose the only other real contender for the throne, and of the remaining three, one of them - the Marinaio - is at least more inclined to the current Prince than the opposition. Of the two that support the alternative, one just lost a huge number of its members.<br /> <br /> The city's history is one dominated by five families. For most of that time, the ruling elite have been the Lucerna, a Nosferatu bloodline cursed with extreme albinism, who see their pallor as a sign of God's favour among the Damned. The Murmure, meanwhile, are a Gangrel bloodline that's been confined to the foothills beyond the city's limits, a lifestyle that grew increasingly less viable with the rise of urbanization.<br /> <br /> In the 1860s, at the peak of the Industrial Revolution, amid rising urbanization, one of the Marinaio by the name of Ghyslain believed he'd been chosen by the gods of oceans and rivers to take the role of Prince, a belief confirmed by the Murmure's matriarch, Grandmother Whispers. With the Syrah already indulging in the heresies of the Ordo Dracul, and a coven of Stylo scribes willing to break faith, a coup was enacted and the Mad Prince Ghyslain ascended the throne.<br /> <br /> Since then, Ghyslain's basically turned the world upside down by giving his Sheriff extreme leeway to punish any members of the Lancea, while offering extreme leniency to anyone who supports him.<br /> <br /> What's also helped is that Ghyslain might very well be actually touched by the gods. The man has a compulsion forcing him to obey prophecies, omens, ritual taboos, etc., and yet it seems to help him. By accident or design, he's managed to avoid most every assassin thus far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849230#post849230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something that could happen. It probably wouldn't endear others to the Prince, if they were fond of their arms. But that depends on what the goal of the contamination was, or rather, what the rest of the All Night's Society thinks of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The goal, in this case, was to fill in for a superior who'd gone missing without the good sense to tell the Prince that he was going to unexpectedly disappear. Ghyslain just... Cannot stand when procedure is not followed for these sorts of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:02:17-07:00","id":849268,"title":"","content":"Having an arm cut off is really a minor inconvenience to a vampire anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:03:53-07:00","id":849271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849217#post849217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it going too far for a Malkovian Prince with compulsive behaviour regarding omens, taboos, and similar superstitious ritual, to order his sheriff to slice off the arm of a vampire who tried to participate in a ritual that requires members of a rank to participate, to prevent them from contaminating the ritual chalice with their blood?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. Cutting off arms to prevent contamination when the arms themselves will likely splatter blood and contaminate things? It makes no sense what-so-ever.<br /> <br /> Not my type of game, either. Some people love that kind of game, others find it too over the top and, believe it or not, unrealistic. I'm in the latter group. But the only voices that matter are the ones at your table. Is this the kind thing they enjoy? That is your answer right there. Individual tables have different standards and playstyles, and no one knows what those are better than you. So... yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T08:31:21-07:00","id":849286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849248#post849248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The short answer is, the alternative is worse. The longer answer is that three of the now six families that run the city - Syrah, Murmure, and Stylo - thoroughly oppose the only other real contender for the throne, and of the remaining three, one of them - the Marinaio - is at least more inclined to the current Prince than the opposition. Of the two that support the alternative, one just lost a huge number of its members.<br /> <br /> The city's history is one dominated by five families. For most of that time, the ruling elite have been the Lucerna, a Nosferatu bloodline cursed with extreme albinism, who see their pallor as a sign of God's favour among the Damned. The Murmure, meanwhile, are a Gangrel bloodline that's been confined to the foothills beyond the city's limits, a lifestyle that grew increasingly less viable with the rise of urbanization.<br /> <br /> In the 1860s, at the peak of the Industrial Revolution, amid rising urbanization, one of the Marinaio by the name of Ghyslain believed he'd been chosen by the gods of oceans and rivers to take the role of Prince, a belief confirmed by the Murmure's matriarch, Grandmother Whispers. With the Syrah already indulging in the heresies of the Ordo Dracul, and a coven of Stylo scribes willing to break faith, a coup was enacted and the Mad Prince Ghyslain ascended the throne.<br /> <br /> Since then, Ghyslain's basically turned the world upside down by giving his Sheriff extreme leeway to punish any members of the Lancea, while offering extreme leniency to anyone who supports him.<br /> <br /> What's also helped is that Ghyslain might very well be actually touched by the gods. The man has a compulsion forcing him to obey prophecies, omens, ritual taboos, etc., and yet it seems to help him. By accident or design, he's managed to avoid most every assassin thus far.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The goal, in this case, was to fill in for a superior who'd gone missing without the good sense to tell the Prince that he was going to unexpectedly disappear. Ghyslain just... Cannot stand when procedure is not followed for these sorts of things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you got your background covered - of course then the answer is it could happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:56:35-07:00","id":849379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849271#post849271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes. Cutting off arms to prevent contamination when the arms themselves will likely splatter blood and contaminate things? It makes no sense what-so-ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't splatter blood unless they're doing the whole &quot;Blush of Life&quot; thing. It's too precious to lose and is drained away from wounds jealously.<br /> <br /> That being said, breaking immersion is sort of my chief worry. Would you mind explaining your distaste?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T12:42:24-07:00","id":849399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849217#post849217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it going too far for a Malkovian Prince with compulsive behaviour regarding omens, taboos, and similar superstitious ritual, to order his sheriff to slice off the arm of a vampire who tried to participate in a ritual that requires members of a rank to participate, to prevent them from contaminating the ritual chalice with their blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems excessive and unnecessary. Why chop the guy's arms off? Physically dragging him away should be fine. Or just Dominating him not to participate. The arm chop just feels pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:25:51-07:00","id":849424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849399#post849399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems excessive and unnecessary. Why chop the guy's arms off? Physically dragging him away should be fine. Or just Dominating him not to participate.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as the Prince knows, the vampire already knew he wasn't supposed to be there and wasn't supposed to participate. While it hasn't been said where this ritual is taking place, it doesn't seem to be in the middle of a mall or someplace the vampire would just stumble upon accidentally. They were there on purpose, when they weren't supposed to be.<br /> <br /> It's disrespectful, possibly sacrilegious, and strangers in the place of the known is certainly a bad omen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-18-2016, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:41:01-07:00","id":849436,"title":"","content":"It's taking place in the middle of the Cathedral of St. Maximilien Kolbe, which is the local Elysium (and a massive sore point for the local Lancea).<br /> <br /> Prince Ghyslain has what amounts to a compulsive disorder as regards adherence to occult tradition. No-one was there by accident, and the absence of the master of the family present is a pretty grievous insult; something that would inevitably warrant punishment upon the entire family in question. The vamp who suffered the spontaneous dismembering was of said family, trying to offer their own blood in place of their elder's. This was not a neonate, either.<br /> <br /> I s'pose I'll need to ponder this. It does feel over the top, but more important is the need to be careful not to make Ghyslain <i>too</i> draconian or else he becomes too easy to manipulate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:49:37-07:00","id":849439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849436#post849436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's taking place in the middle of the Cathedral of St. Maximilien Kolbe, which is the local Elysium</div> </div> </div> </div>The Elysium part could be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T14:04:19-07:00","id":849441,"title":"","content":"Prince Maxwell had Solomon Birch beaten and stabbed ten times with a white-hot sword for punching someone in Elysium. And Solomon was a very high-ranking fellow. The Tyrant Prince in one of my games also severed a vampire's arm, though that was for more disrespect, as well as poor aim. Plotting to overthrow her began that night.<br /> <br /> It's all passion and politics, predators posturing. Fun stuff. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/15961-vampire-punishments\">We had a thread about it.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-18-2016, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T15:10:03-07:00","id":849475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849379#post849379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires don't splatter blood unless they're doing the whole &quot;Blush of Life&quot; thing. It's too precious to lose and is drained away from wounds jealously.</div> </div> </div> </div> Many neonates use Blush of Life almost instictively, notably due to their Humanity. And they tend to relfexively spill blood, simply because they're too human to think otherwise. Its tied into the whole Masquerade, seeming human aspect.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, cutting off limbs is MESSY. Its not a clean slice, even with a Vigor. Bone and meat go flying everywhere. So, yeah. Contamination everywhere.<br /> <br /> My distaste stems from the idea that its all completely unnecessary. Vampires are generally practical. Even Malkavian ones. Cutting off an entire limb is simply going over the top simply for the sake of trying to be horrorific, but moves into the realm of splatter-gore-fests, especially if it just regrows. That's not horrific. That's just driving one's humanity down for the sake of trying to look like a monster and abandoning all pretence of Humanity, which is kind of against the themes of the game. <br /> <br /> If the Prince was really pissed and wanted to make an example, there are far more effective ways than this. It just feels like its an attempt to be EVULZ OLD VAMPIRE! Which feels just like a mustash twirling cartoon villain from the 70s and 80s. Over the top evil brutality without purpose isn't my thing, and that's my impression.<br /> <br /> But, like I said, that's my personal taste. Your table might like that kind of thing. Mine doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T15:17:06-07:00","id":849477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849475#post849475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Many neonates use Blush of Life almost instictively, notably due to their Humanity. And they tend to relfexively spill blood, simply because they're too human to think otherwise. Its tied into the whole Masquerade, seeming human aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you tell me where it says this? Because if that's accurate, since Blush of Life only lasts a scene, neonates must be tearing through a ton of people for blood and I've really been underestimating how often they drink people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, cutting off limbs is MESSY. Its not a clean slice, even with a Vigor. Bone and meat go flying everywhere. So, yeah. Contamination everywhere. </div> </div> </div>I don't think they were cutting it off over the chalice but I could be mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T16:46:05-07:00","id":849508,"title":"","content":"It sounds <i>very </i>tied into the Masquerade. 20th Anniversary edition, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:29:10-07:00","id":849524,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, it says they can use it for free at high Humanity. This explains a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:41:42-07:00","id":849535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849436#post849436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's taking place in the middle of the Cathedral of St. Maximilien Kolbe, which is the local Elysium (and a massive sore point for the local Lancea).<br /> <br /> Prince Ghyslain has what amounts to a compulsive disorder as regards adherence to occult tradition. No-one was there by accident, and the absence of the master of the family present is a pretty grievous insult; something that would inevitably warrant punishment upon the entire family in question. The vamp who suffered the spontaneous dismembering was of said family, trying to offer their own blood in place of their elder's. This was not a neonate, either.<br /> <br /> I s'pose I'll need to ponder this. It does feel over the top, but more important is the need to be careful not to make Ghyslain <i>too</i> draconian or else he becomes too easy to manipulate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a lot of context missing at this point where its hard to give an answer.<br /> <br /> My impression from the original post was that this prince was doing some ritual around a chalice in public, probably during some kind of elysium. He must have called for the &quot;vampires of rank&quot; or whatever, this one vampire came up, obviously thinking too highly of themselves, and before said vampire could touch the cup, the prince ordered his arm chopped off, which I imagined just basically flopping to the floor right then and there, in the middle of elysium, inches from the the Prince and the chalice.<br /> <br /> In that imagined scenario, it comes across totally unnecessary, uncalled for, and almost cartoonishly despotic and crazy.<br /> <br /> More detail, though, different circumstances, etc., could certainly change that opinion, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:44:02-07:00","id":849536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=849475#post849475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Many neonates use Blush of Life almost instictively, notably due to their Humanity. And they tend to relfexively spill blood, simply because they're too human to think otherwise. Its tied into the whole Masquerade, seeming human aspect.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, cutting off limbs is MESSY. Its not a clean slice, even with a Vigor. Bone and meat go flying everywhere. So, yeah. Contamination everywhere.<br /> <br /> My distaste stems from the idea that its all completely unnecessary. Vampires are generally practical. Even Malkavian ones. Cutting off an entire limb is simply going over the top simply for the sake of trying to be horrorific, but moves into the realm of splatter-gore-fests, especially if it just regrows. That's not horrific. That's just driving one's humanity down for the sake of trying to look like a monster and abandoning all pretence of Humanity, which is kind of against the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> If the Prince was really pissed and wanted to make an example, there are far more effective ways than this. It just feels like its an attempt to be EVULZ OLD VAMPIRE! Which feels just like a mustash twirling cartoon villain from the 70s and 80s. Over the top evil brutality without purpose isn't my thing, and that's my impression.<br /> <br /> But, like I said, that's my personal taste. Your table might like that kind of thing. Mine doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before I say anything else, I'm gonna say I agree with you on the mood it generates. I brought this up here precisely because I was worried it felt over-the-top; violence for its own sake, so your commentary is appreciated. The mood I want for Elysium is that it's a thin veneer of civility over a gathering of predators, but that thin veneer shouldn't be so thin as to be naught but vapour. I've since gone and retconned the scene; the Sheriff merely grabbed the raised arm and squeezed hard enough to prevent any release of blood; a forceful and aggressive gesture, but not more than necessary.<br /> <br /> None of it was intended to give a sense of evil or even brutality, though, at least not on the Prince's part; merely to emphasize that Ghyslain has a panic attack when someone threatens to break &quot;the rules&quot;.<br /> <br /> That all out the way, I'm not sure where you get the Blush of Life thing, and I'll natter and dicker over the messiness of slicing through a limb. Not really the point of it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T13:29:20-07:00","id":851323,"title":"","content":"Hello VtR community!<br /> I've got a simple question, sorry if it was already answered in some other topic (i've googled hard before asking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> The question is regarding the Charmed Condition wording:<br /> It's description consists of two paragraphs. The first one is pretty clear and states that vampire can add his Majesty dots to any Manipulation rolls against the victim. <br /> The second one explains how the victim should act when suffering the Charmed Condition effects. The question is does the second paragraph have anything to do with game mechanics? Does the vampire require to roll the dice or it is assumed that the victim acts literally like &quot;If he asks, you\u2019ll do favors for him like he was one of your best friends&quot; with no game mechanics like social skills or social maneuvering rolls needed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11508-gorin","name":"Gorin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T14:07:27-07:00","id":851345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gorin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=851323#post851323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello VtR community!<br /> I've got a simple question, sorry if it was already answered in some other topic (i've googled hard before asking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> The question is regarding the Charmed Condition wording:<br /> It's description consists of two paragraphs. The first one is pretty clear and states that vampire can add his Majesty dots to any Manipulation rolls against the victim.<br /> The second one explains how the victim should act when suffering the Charmed Condition effects. The question is does the second paragraph have anything to do with game mechanics? Does the vampire require to roll the dice or it is assumed that the victim acts literally like &quot;If he asks, you\u2019ll do favors for him like he was one of your best friends&quot; with no game mechanics like social skills or social maneuvering rolls needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they just literally act like you are their best friend, so, they require no further game mechanics to get favors from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T14:19:50-07:00","id":851355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gorin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=851323#post851323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello VtR community!<br /> I've got a simple question, sorry if it was already answered in some other topic (i've googled hard before asking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> The question is regarding the Charmed Condition wording:<br /> It's description consists of two paragraphs. The first one is pretty clear and states that vampire can add his Majesty dots to any Manipulation rolls against the victim.<br /> The second one explains how the victim should act when suffering the Charmed Condition effects. The question is does the second paragraph have anything to do with game mechanics? Does the vampire require to roll the dice or it is assumed that the victim acts literally like &quot;If he asks, you\u2019ll do favors for him like he was one of your best friends&quot; with no game mechanics like social skills or social maneuvering rolls needed?</div> </div> </div> </div> The latter. This is mind control. There are limits on what you can ask for without a roll, thus the bonus dice, but it absolutely has parts that are automatic victories.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:20:37-07:00","id":851430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gorin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=851323#post851323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello VtR community!<br /> I've got a simple question, sorry if it was already answered in some other topic (i've googled hard before asking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> The question is regarding the Charmed Condition wording:<br /> It's description consists of two paragraphs. The first one is pretty clear and states that vampire can add his Majesty dots to any Manipulation rolls against the victim.<br /> The second one explains how the victim should act when suffering the Charmed Condition effects. The question is does the second paragraph have anything to do with game mechanics? Does the vampire require to roll the dice or it is assumed that the victim acts literally like &quot;If he asks, you\u2019ll do favors for him like he was one of your best friends&quot; with no game mechanics like social skills or social maneuvering rolls needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It helps to keep in mind that the majority of the developers for the CofD/nWoD game lines fall into the &quot;there is no fluff/crunch division&quot; camp of game design. The description of how a character under the Charmed Condition should act is just as much a rule as the part about adding Majesty dots to Manipulation rolls. It doesn't directly interact with any subsystems, but it is a game rule, just one that pertains to roleplaying.The player (or the storyteller if it's an NPC) should roleplay as though the vampire was the character's close friend, for whom they wouldn't be likely to refuse requests for minor favors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T01:21:07-07:00","id":851624,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers! <br /> It will take some time for me to get used to this &quot;no crunch lines&quot; rule though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11508-gorin","name":"Gorin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T07:35:56-07:00","id":866823,"title":"","content":"So...Diablerie. I have a really soft spot for Diablerie, as it's a very creepy thing that can be used to make truly terrific stories. What are most important things to remember about it, and where they can be found? I'm usually following a stance that I'm not going to buy anything from 1ed, but I might get my hands on some 1st ed materials for limited period of time, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T08:21:05-07:00","id":866844,"title":"","content":"I think the 2e core is perfectly good.<br /> <br /> Things to remember about Diablerie: Even if you hide the body, everyone with strong enough blood sympathy or was close by to the site of what happened is going to feel that it was done. It's an exceedingly hard crime to actually conceal because of Blood Sympathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T08:50:23-07:00","id":866861,"title":"","content":"Not to mention the fact that anyone with Auspex can easily tell if someone is a Diablerist.<br /> <br /> This fact actually opens up some cool story potential though. When a subset of the local population has the power to identify members of the community as something everyone hates and fears, but the rest of the population has no reliable means of confirming or disproving their accusations, you've got yourself a perfect recipie for a good ol' fashioned witch hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:22:26-07:00","id":866908,"title":"","content":"I don't think Auspex and Blood Sympathy are as reliable detection methods here as they're made out to be, I think. With Auspex, you have to specifically <i>look</i> for diablarie veins after specifically targetting someone to use Auspex 2 on, and hope they don't have the Plausible Deniability Law or an updated Love Lies Bleeding ritual. Some people claim that they'd have their PC check for diablarie stains on every vampire they see, but I personally have my doubts that's something everyone would do, every day for years and get no answer. Especially given the strix. Strix register as diablerie stains in the aura, and they wouldn't be able to infiltrate vampire society (which they do) if it was common to check for veins so often.<br /> <br /> And Blood Sympathy? You need an exceptional success to merely tell the difference between torpor and Final Death - diablarie isn't even on the table. Given that you have to beat someone into torpor before diablarizing them, its more than possible that you'd register torpor, and then final death, but no clues between the two steps?<br /> <br /> As well, some versions of VII are notorious diablarists, as are the strix. So, even if you somehow know that diablarie happened, you can't even tell if it was Kindred or an outsider who did it.<br /> <br /> Individual STs will run things how they see fit, but I don't see as diablarie as being instantly known in the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Anyways, to answer the poster directly....<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=866823#post866823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...Diablerie. I have a really soft spot for Diablerie, as it's a very creepy thing that can be used to make truly terrific stories. What are most important things to remember about it, and where they can be found? I'm usually following a stance that I'm not going to buy anything from 1ed, but I might get my hands on some 1st ed materials for limited period of time, so...</div> </div> </div> </div> The most important things to remember is that even vampires tend to look at Diablerie as something horrific. I run it as common knowledge that, while this act is a power up, you're driven insane by it. You hear voices in your head as the soul is digested. That bit is found in the new core book. <br /> <br /> After that? There's actually not a lot of material. The only stuff from 1e that I remember is the Loves Lies Bleeding ritual (tiny mention in CotC book) and in Ancient Bloodlines, we have a Daeva bloodline that specializes in diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-17-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:26:53-07:00","id":866911,"title":"","content":"I believe you can reduce the amount of time you are Tainted by taking Aggravated damage; I could see a <i>very careful</i> Vampire dealing with the Condition by taking a branding iron to themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:58:31-07:00","id":866929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=866823#post866823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...Diablerie. I have a really soft spot for Diablerie, as it's a very creepy thing that can be used to make truly terrific stories. What are most important things to remember about it, and where they can be found? I'm usually following a stance that I'm not going to buy anything from 1ed, but I might get my hands on some 1st ed materials for limited period of time, so...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As the others mentioned. You hear voices in your head. You can get found out with Auspex 2. There is a question listed for it in the suggested questions. Blood Sympathy, their relatives will feel final death, but I am sure it doesnt tell you HOW they died. You will be tainted for 1 month per blood potency of your victim. 1 aggravated downs that by 1 month. <br /> <br /> What wasnt mentioned.. Is that you do it and you're addicted to it. No save. Addicted. and you MUST roll a resolve+ comp -the new victim's BP to NOT try to do it. This is any time you have an opportunity to do it. That's probably the nastiest part. The voices telling you to eat your best friend as you are chilling together.. alone. It is a humanity 1 check so you spiral really fast.. and try to eat people you really shouldnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:14:06-07:00","id":866938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=866823#post866823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...Diablerie. I have a really soft spot for Diablerie, as it's a very creepy thing that can be used to make truly terrific stories. What are most important things to remember about it, and where they can be found? I'm usually following a stance that I'm not going to buy anything from 1ed, but I might get my hands on some 1st ed materials for limited period of time, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the heavy Humanity toll you want to save it for vampires with higher Blood Potency. My group was heavy diablerists, and after draining a bunch of 1 Blood Potency neonates they realized they weren't getting much out of it except addiction, Taint and lower Humanity. Even the Skills were for the most part not really worth it, considering how cheap they are in Experience.<br /> <br /> Obviously due to the addiction you can't always choose who you're going to do it to, so you'll either want to blood bond to each other or sleep far away from one another so someone doesn't decide to stay up and drain everyone else.<br /> <br /> It's great for games with lots of older vampires in torpor, where the diablerists have to search for them and hide the fact that they're searching. I also find it's a fun way to introduce unique but leading Disciplines that could be used for plot hooks later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-17-2016, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:28:39-07:00","id":866945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=866908#post866908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Auspex and Blood Sympathy are as reliable detection methods here as they're made out to be, I think. With Auspex, you have to specifically <i>look</i> for diablarie veins after specifically targetting someone to use Auspex 2 on, and hope they don't have the Plausible Deniability Law or an updated Love Lies Bleeding ritual. Some people claim that they'd have their PC check for diablarie stains on every vampire they see, but I personally have my doubts that's something everyone would do, every day for years and get no answer. Especially given the strix. Strix register as diablerie stains in the aura, and they wouldn't be able to infiltrate vampire society (which they do) if it was common to check for veins so often.<br /> <br /> And Blood Sympathy? You need an exceptional success to merely tell the difference between torpor and Final Death - diablarie isn't even on the table. Given that you have to beat someone into torpor before diablarizing them, its more than possible that you'd register torpor, and then final death, but no clues between the two steps?<br /> <br /> As well, some versions of VII are notorious diablarists, as are the strix. So, even if you somehow know that diablarie happened, you can't even tell if it was Kindred or an outsider who did it.<br /> <br /> Individual STs will run things how they see fit, but I don't see as diablarie as being instantly known in the All Night Society.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the more fuel for the Salem Diablerist Trials!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T11:58:55-07:00","id":866968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=866911#post866911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe you can reduce the amount of time you are Tainted by taking Aggravated damage; I could see a <i>very careful</i> Vampire dealing with the Condition by taking a branding iron to themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting note:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR 2e pg 91 under Healing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aggravated damage is the only<br /> type of wound that leaves a scar on Kindred. The scar appears<br /> natural, unlike the original damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that could be an interesting way to out a Diablerist. Theyr'e going to have far more scars than innocent vampires. And probably getting more fairly regularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:43:49-07:00","id":866996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=866945#post866945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the more fuel for the Salem Diablerist Trials!</div> </div> </div> </div> Definitly! I notice there's definitely a lot more effort into make the game, as a whole, harder to just have the instant truth of the matter out of everyone. I think that's deliberate, so that you can have things like a diablarist walking around, and no one being sure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T13:49:48-07:00","id":867033,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all the responses! I think I'll make a new thread for this later, because these answers definitely got my head working. This is very informative and inspiring.<br /> Gangrel thread and &quot;BP 10 is easy, just Diablerize 40 vampires&quot; thread gave me a neat idea I want to write down and archivize for next time I can play a Vampire or GM it. Basically, a following character concept: a random human who got kidnapped and embraced for a sole purpose of getting diablerized by their captor, who, well, was in the middle of conducting the diablerie-to-power scheme. Central idea is that Diablerie went terribly wrong (Dramatic Failure, intervention, Or It's A Part of My Plan, dunno yet), and after some soul sucking grappling, we end up in a following scenario: one diablerized serial killer, one newly embraced kindred whose first act of their unlife was unwilling amaranth. For whatever reason, character is allowed to live by local kindred, but with all expected consequences (which sound like a blast to roleplay).<br /> <br /> Which is why I'm looking for all relevant rules, tidbits and stuff. For example, a specific question: I remember that Strix can raise their Shadow Stuff by being inside a Vampire who is diablerizing someone else. Was it ever said what happens to a Vampire who was used in this way? Do they get any benefits of Diablerie? This obviously is connected to the possible explanation of the incident as &quot;Strix saved the character and ate the agressor&quot;, though I really like idea of the dude getting fucked over because his all of his Tainted conditions triggered in synch during the diablerie and reduced his pool to a chance die, while boosting the poor victim to the point of Ex!Success :V.<br /> <br /> Question 2: I haven't looked at the Blood Sympathy yet (can't do that right now), but...is this &quot;hereditary&quot;? Should I &quot;inherit&quot; all of the Blood Sympathies of the captor, including sympathy he got from his victims? That would one fucked up scenario (which means it would be great).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-17-2016, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:46:31-07:00","id":867165,"title":"","content":"Blood Sympathy is simply you feel the blood of those related to you. Your sire, his sires, other &quot;siblings&quot; and &quot;cousins&quot; you might have, the closer in the &quot;family tree&quot; you are the stronger the feeling, and the wider the range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:09:12-07:00","id":867236,"title":"","content":"Just to give context to what I said about Blood Sympathy: Final Death and Amaranth seem to be very keenly felt judging by the fiction. In fact, short of seeing a diablerized corpse (which is also obvious to Kindred) it's one of the only ways Kindred even know somebody was diablerized/killed.<br /> <br /> This isn't the same as knowing who did it, which is excellent fodder for the concept of the Salem Diablerie Trials being discussed here! It's hard to hide that someone was diablerized in a domain where they have lineage or roots, and given that most assume vampires of a given clan to be relatives, it boosts the chance of people feeling it.<br /> <br /> I think it's a great little thing that adds to the familial sense of Requiem, and to its tensions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:25:43-07:00","id":867249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=867236#post867236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, short of seeing a diablerized corpse (which is also obvious to Kindred)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that accurate? Don't they die like the rest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:15:28-07:00","id":867285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=867249#post867249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that accurate? Don't they die like the rest?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only time diablerie has ever been discussed in terms of what kind of corpse it leaves behind is in the 1st Edition SAS called <i>Blood Red + Ash Grey</i>, where a character was killed but not diablerized, and the SAS explains that Diablerie does more than just leave a regular Kindred Corpse behind.<br /> <br /> <br /> In <i>Blood Red + Ash Grey</i>, a Final Death'd corpse is described, and then these facts are given about dead Kindred:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blood Red + Ash Grey, page 36</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Diablerie does more than just \u201ckill\u201d a vampire. A diablerized corpse leaves remains that are unnatural \u2014 a skull but otherwise ashes, or a heat-blackened patch of asphalt, or a papery sheath of hands around burnt bone \u2014 and unpredictable. Though no two diablerized corpses are necessarily the same, a diablerized corpse and one that is simply Finally Dead are difficult to confuse. [Thus, in this story, it should be clear that the Victim was not diablerized.]</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Of course, this is a 1e book and an SAS to boot, so it's not as if it's 'firmly canon' if there is such a metric. If an ST needs something to refer back to, it is the only reference I have found to what Diablerie does to a corpse in the line.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-18-2016, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T05:19:16-07:00","id":867498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=867236#post867236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to give context to what I said about Blood Sympathy: Final Death and Amaranth seem to be very keenly felt judging by the fiction. In fact, short of seeing a diablerized corpse (which is also obvious to Kindred) it's one of the only ways Kindred even know somebody was diablerized/killed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that's not what the rules say. Further, diablarized corpses aren't obvious to Kindred - there's nothing anywhere to differentiate a regular Final Death from a diablerie victim in 2e. Also, if you're going to quote something, you're going to have to quote something from 2e, not 1e. Hells, BR+AG looks like a SAS from before Requiem for Rome, which is when Requiem got a new staff and began changing direction, so its really old in terms of 1e as well.<br /> <br /> Where exactly is this supposed fiction, if you're going to quote it? Because, frankly, it sounds more like you've decided to use this fiction as a houserule. And you can't do that - you're giving out outdated or outright false information here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-18-2016, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:39:45-07:00","id":867555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=867498#post867498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except that's not what the rules say. Further, diablarized corpses aren't obvious to Kindred - there's nothing anywhere to differentiate a regular Final Death from a diablerie victim in 2e. Also, if you're going to quote something, you're going to have to quote something from 2e, not 1e. Hells, BR+AG looks like a SAS from before Requiem for Rome, which is when Requiem got a new staff and began changing direction, so its really old in terms of 1e as well.<br /> <br /> Where exactly is this supposed fiction, if you're going to quote it? Because, frankly, it sounds more like you've decided to use this fiction as a houserule. And you can't do that - you're giving out outdated or outright false information here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in a few of them, but if you're looking for the most notable example, it's in the Daeva Clanbook, when a member of the Carthians describes the consequences of Hurricane Katrina for Kindred throughout the United States. All those deaths are felt keenly through Blood Sympathy, and if that's not an indicator of how powerful it can be, I don't know what is. (Though, another obvious one is that you can feel it from your sire from anywhere, no matter the distance). If it has to be called out, the Clanbooks are one of the explicitly called out products to use with the 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire The Requiem Second Edition, pg. 99</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sympathy comes into effect automatically any time a vampire\u2019s relative enters torpor or <b>suffers Final Death</b>. The feeling washes over the vampire and she <b>senses her relative\u2019s state in vague, often symbolic terms</b>. As well, characters can initiate sympathy to communicate their states of being to their relatives once or twice removed. To do so, they must spend a Willpower point and make a Blood Potency roll. Each success allows them to contact a single relative; the relative must still make the roll to detect sympathy. <b>Any particularly powerful emotion can trigger sympathy, at Storyteller discretion.</b> This is less a foolproof detective tool, and a more dramatic device. A<b>ny time a relative suffers a horrible fate</b>, sympathy may cause frenzies.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can observe that Final Death factually causes Blood Sympathy to trigger automatically. So there's no debate to be had about that. I'll bold above the things that lend itself to the conclusion that they can almost certainly sense when someone has been diablerized, but I'll stress that I doubt it'll tell them who did it, because as the last sentence states, this is less of a foolproof detective tool, and more of a dramatic device.<br /> <br /> (The last sentence also probably explains what happened as a result of Katrina, mind!)<br /> <br /> Separate from that, there's a point to be made about the nebulousness of actual canon in the <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> and Vampire's ambiguous status as the <i>most </i>permeable of the lines in that regard. Check out references to 1e content such as the Icarian Bloodline or the Sanctified Creeds in <i>Requiem for Regina</i>. I think it's deliberate that both in 1e and in 2e, that the core does <i>not </i>state anything like what is said in Blood Red + Ash Grey to allow people to make that decision at their table. I think it contributes to the drama and interest of the game, and that the way Diablerie is discussed, it follows that one should be able to identify diablerie as something that actually occured. There isn't much of a witch hunt to be had if the only way to tell diablerie even occurred (that is, absent the answer of <i>who did it</i>) is to look at the person who did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-18-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:10:30-07:00","id":867569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=866938#post866938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the heavy Humanity toll you want to save it for vampires with higher Blood Potency. My group was heavy diablerists, and after draining a bunch of 1 Blood Potency neonates they realized they weren't getting much out of it except addiction, Taint and lower Humanity. Even the Skills were for the most part not really worth it, considering how cheap they are in Experience.<br /> <br /> Obviously due to the addiction you can't always choose who you're going to do it to, so you'll either want to blood bond to each other or sleep far away from one another so someone doesn't decide to stay up and drain everyone else.<br /> <br /> It's great for games with lots of older vampires in torpor, where the diablerists have to search for them and hide the fact that they're searching. I also find it's a fun way to introduce unique but leading Disciplines that could be used for plot hooks later.</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple of things. You get disciplines not skills unless ALL of your disciplines are higher than theirs, only then do you get skills. Out of clan disciplines are expensive in exp terms compared to skills. <br /> <br /> Also a blood bond would not save you from the addiction roll. I would definitely force the resolve+composure-BP roll for an opportunity to diablerize if you are alone with another vampire. Addicted people often hurt the ones they love the most... And I would probably make you roll 2 breaking points. 1 for diablerie and 1 for hurting your thrall. Because that's extra bad. However positive note to that, should you Hurt your thrall and not diablerize them... Addicted would be kicked.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=867498#post867498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except that's not what the rules say. Further, diablarized corpses aren't obvious to Kindred - there's nothing anywhere to differentiate a regular Final Death from a diablerie victim in 2e. Also, if you're going to quote something, you're going to have to quote something from 2e, not 1e. Hells, BR+AG looks like a SAS from before Requiem for Rome, which is when Requiem got a new staff and began changing direction, so its really old in terms of 1e as well.<br /> <br /> Where exactly is this supposed fiction, if you're going to quote it? Because, frankly, it sounds more like you've decided to use this fiction as a houserule. And you can't do that - you're giving out outdated or outright false information here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed on this. You shouldnt quote 1E stuff in a 2E thread. It's not helpful. Though one could offer it up as a house roll or flavor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:29:25-07:00","id":867580,"title":"","content":"I'll concede that it needn't be quoted in the context of some kind of canonical ruling, but it's absolutely ludicrous to declare carte blanche to ignore those books. Quoting information like that in Blood Red + Ash Gray is not about deciding what is right or wrong, it's about providing tools for Storytellers to make calls. I'll edit my post to clarify that it's one of the <i>only examples of this issue being discussed in the gameline</i> such that if someone needs fodder for ideas, they should look at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:07:49-07:00","id":867602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=867555#post867555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't much of a witch hunt to be had if the only way to tell diablerie even occurred (that is, absent the answer of <i>who did it</i>) is to look at the person who did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... The whole point of comparing a diablerist hunt to a witch hunt is to point out that there might not even be a diablerist <i>at all</i>, just like there might not have been any actual witches executed at witch trials. It doesn't much matter if a Diablerie has actually occurred or not if roughly a fifth of your population has the power to accuse anyone in the community of a heinous crime based on evidence that the other four fifths of the population can't verify.<br /> <br /> All it took in Salem was a couple of girls who didn't like their babysitter saying they saw her doing magic. Whether or not it was true, it was the spark that ignited a powder keg of paranoia and hatred. Likewise, all it would take in a vampiric domain is one Mekhet telling the authorities that she saw the stains of Diablerie on her rival's aura. Sure, you could get another Auspex user to verify the accusations, but you're still relying on one person's word against another. Then what happens when one claims the other is in league with the Diablerist? What if she pays off another Auspex user to &quot;confirm&quot; her claims? What about when other Auspex users decide to take advantage of the situation and start accusing people they don't like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T09:26:40-07:00","id":867613,"title":"","content":"It says something about me that all I can think when reading this debate is &quot;Now, why do diablerists burn?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T15:13:21-07:00","id":867850,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't force a roll to resist diablerie addiction just for being alone with another vampire, it isn't really an opportunity to diablerise just yet. Now if you beat them into torpor, had them in a grapple and are able to bite them, or otherwise had almost complete control of the situation, that's when I'd force the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T22:02:21-07:00","id":868182,"title":"","content":"There is a roll to resist vitae, crack, cocaine, heroine alcohol. There are only 2 things ( that I can think of ) that there is no roll to resist. That is just how addictive they are. Kiss of the Succubus and Diablerie. Now Think about it like this if an alcoholic was sitting alone in a room with Booze. Would there be an internal debate to drink it or not?<br /> <br /> A bag of heroine on your best friend, steal it or not?<br /> <br /> A sex addict alone with someone, ... Well you get my drift. Why would being alone in a room with a vampire not be classified as &quot;an opportunity to indulge &quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T22:07:02-07:00","id":868185,"title":"","content":"Because alcoholic left alone with booze may and can try to resist it. Please, drop the analogy, as it's something I have to deal with at daily basis in my family and it rubs me wrong way. <br /> Other than that, thanks a lot for these diablerie insights! They really helped me flesh out the character idea, which got it's own thread if anyone is interested in continuing the conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T01:26:25-07:00","id":868266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=868182#post868182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a roll to resist vitae, crack, cocaine, heroine alcohol. There are only 2 things ( that I can think of ) that there is no roll to resist. That is just how addictive they are. Kiss of the Succubus and Diablerie. Now Think about it like this if an alcoholic was sitting alone in a room with Booze. Would there be an internal debate to drink it or not?<br /> <br /> A bag of heroine on your best friend, steal it or not?<br /> <br /> A sex addict alone with someone, ... Well you get my drift. Why would being alone in a room with a vampire not be classified as &quot;an opportunity to indulge &quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>While there isn't a roll to resist gaining the Addicted condition there's a Resolve + Composure - would-be victim's BP roll to resist a reasonable opportunity to commit diablerie.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's never a roll being alone with another vamp, I'm saying there needs to be more to it than that. How reasonable it is that you could get away with it. Is the vampire you're alone with important enough that Mekhet and/or Ventrue will be checking the court to see who killed them? Are you certain you can win a fight to the death with them? Do they have Obfuscate, Celerity or just plain fast enough reflexes to escape?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T06:52:16-07:00","id":868389,"title":"","content":"While I certainly don't mean to offend anyone but we are talking about addictions and what happens while addicted to things. The roll to resist the addicted condition is resolve composure -BP. As I mentioned and was additionally pointed out. <br /> <br /> That roll is to not do it, to not fall to your temptations. Say you are alone with the vampire. You have the opportunity, you roll, you pass, and you say to yourself &quot;That's a really bad idea. They are going to know I did it and I am going to get in trouble and I don't want that. &quot;<br /> <br /> You roll, you fail, and for a moment, like an addict, you just don't care about what happens next, you need your fix.<br /> <br /> Side note: until BP 6 you are probably addicted to vitae too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-19-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T08:40:37-07:00","id":870229,"title":"","content":"A fast question for you.<br /> You can't quite remember what happened during Mesmerized Condition. Does it affect just the brief moment while you fallow a specific command or include the whole duration of the condition (a Scene)?<br /> For example: A vampire sees the character do something wrong, she try to stops them but a PC mesmerizes her commanding to &quot;keep still&quot;. So the vampire stop to make any movment. Now can the mesmerized talk to the character? And after the end of the scene, does she remember what she sees during the mesmerized condition (I know before the condition she would remember what she saw, I mean what happens after) and what they talk about? In the case of multiple commands, does she remember what happens between a command and the other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T09:19:04-07:00","id":870265,"title":"","content":"The latter. You have a foggy time remembering the entire time you're under the Mesmerized Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T09:51:22-07:00","id":870294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=870265#post870265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter. You have a foggy time remembering the entire time you're under the Mesmerized Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For my games I usually have it as missing time, like a black out. or like when you are feverish. when you only have a vague concept of what happened. <br /> My players have suggested like it is black out drunk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:37:22-07:00","id":870469,"title":"","content":"I run it as a vague, nonspecific recollection, so that the lost time isn't conspicuous. Like you remember where you were and generally what you were up to, but you can't recall any precise details - more of an &quot;I don't really remember, I wasn't paying attention&quot; feeling than a &quot;I have no idea, I must have blacked out&quot; feeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T19:53:01-07:00","id":870863,"title":"","content":"Yeah, unless you have Mind of the Unblinking Serpent you shouldn't be able to realise you've been dominated that easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T02:40:52-07:00","id":871072,"title":"","content":"I see. And during the mesmerized condition, if the command impressed is: keep still and silent, can the mesmerized uses powers like nightmare that don't need to speak or move? Or should she be simply in trance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T06:02:24-07:00","id":871137,"title":"","content":"Trance. You're &quot;quiet and reserved&quot; here in a hypnotic state. This isn't like 1e, where you can mess around with the wording of the power while otherwise fully in control. You are passive, and yes, using Nightmare is not a passive action. <br /> <br /> Heck, unlike 1e, you don't even need to speak to Mesmerize someone. You just meet the eyes, and the target falls victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T07:57:41-07:00","id":871228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871137#post871137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trance. You're &amp;quot;quiet and reserved&amp;quot; here in a hypnotic state. This isn't like 1e, where you can mess around with the wording of the power while otherwise fully in control. You are passive, and yes, using Nightmare is not a passive action. <br /> <br /> Heck, unlike 1e, you don't even need to speak to Mesmerize someone. You just meet the eyes, and the target falls victim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although you do need to speak to give commands. But if all you plan to command them to do is sit still and keep quiet there's really no need, since that's how a Mesmerized character is likely to behave without a command.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:07:33-07:00","id":871240,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... actually, that's a good question. Do you have to speak to give commands? Will a written one work? There's definitely the assumption of spoken, but I don't see anything that suggests you can't do written as well. It would take more time, but I can think of ways it would be still thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:25:12-07:00","id":871258,"title":"","content":"There is an argument for it having to be directly spoken, as Dominate works by manipulating the way you speak, and that modification is the reason for whatever happens to your victim. It's in the description of Dominate, before any of the dots. That's probably why Expression is the skill associated with it, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:00:48-07:00","id":871323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871228#post871228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although you do need to speak to give commands. But if all you plan to command them to do is sit still and keep quiet there's really no need, since that's how a Mesmerized character is likely to behave without a command.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there was a topic in wich we discussed about the behavior of a mesmerized subject. While what you saying is right in a normal situation, is it still valid during a heat moment or a fight? I mean, mesmerizing an enemy during a combat (without the vocal command of the next turn) would stop him? <br /> And in the case of a combat can someone mesmerized understand to be under domination effect and try to use nightmare even if subject to the command: keep still?<br /> I agree that after the end of the scene he would not remember, but what about during the condition?<br /> Because, otherwise, whatever command would you implant, when accomplished (like: trhow the gun), the mesmerized come back to attack you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:06:45-07:00","id":871329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871240#post871240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm.... actually, that's a good question. Do you have to speak to give commands? Will a written one work? There's definitely the assumption of spoken, but I don't see anything that suggests you can't do written as well. It would take more time, but I can think of ways it would be still thematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't have it work that way. I see Dominate as working very much like the cartoony, Curse of the Jade Scorpion type hypnosis, and voice is a big part of that. I just don't see the mesmeric villain passing commands to their hypnotized victims with a note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T09:54:02-07:00","id":871389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871258#post871258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an argument for it having to be directly spoken, as Dominate works by manipulating the way you speak, and that modification is the reason for whatever happens to your victim. It's in the description of Dominate, before any of the dots. That's probably why Expression is the skill associated with it, too.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dominate works as an expression of the Competative Beast aura. Generally, that's through your voice, but the Beast is part of your every action, and I can see that argument being used through commanding gestures and the like.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871329#post871329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't have it work that way. I see Dominate as working very much like the cartoony, Curse of the Jade Scorpion type hypnosis, and voice is a big part of that. I just don't see the mesmeric villain passing commands to their hypnotized victims with a note.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not perfect, but I can see some situations in which it could work. In either case, its generally going to be silly to pass notes when speaking is much faster and reliable. More of a thought experiement than something I ever expect to see outside of someone using Dominate 3 to plan through sleeper-agents.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871323#post871323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there was a topic in wich we discussed about the behavior of a mesmerized subject. While what you saying is right in a normal situation, is it still valid during a heat moment or a fight? I mean, mesmerizing an enemy during a combat (without the vocal command of the next turn) would stop him?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. Any amount of damage breaks Mesmerize, even a slap from an ally, however, making it unreliable in a fight. But you can try to Mesmerize and have them run away, or something to that effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in the case of a combat can someone mesmerized understand to be under domination effect and try to use nightmare even if subject to the command: keep still? </div> </div> </div> No. You are under a hypnotic trance until you take damage or a breaking point. You are docile, not violent or agressive. You can't use Nightmare, you can't Lash Out, you can't fight back. You are under the Dominate user's thrall until the Condition is resolved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree that after the end of the scene he would not remember, but what about during the condition? </div> </div> </div> During the Condition, you don't really need to remember anything, because its meaningless. You can't fight back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because, otherwise, whatever command would you implant, when accomplished (like: trhow the gun), the mesmerized come back to attack you. </div> </div> </div> No, because the mesmerized victim won't be agressive. They're passive. This is not like 1e Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:35:02-07:00","id":871435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871389#post871389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. You are under a hypnotic trance until you take damage or a breaking point. You are docile, not violent or agressive. You can't use Nightmare, you can't Lash Out, you can't fight back. You are under the Dominate user's thrall until the Condition is resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's nice to hear. So you don't need two turns to stop someone from attacking you. Is enough to inflict the mesmerized condition in the first turn and does he stops to attack?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871389#post871389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the Condition, you don't really need to remember anything, because its meaningless. You can't fight back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I didn't mean if the mesmerized remember the things during the condition. I just wanted to know if he can act against you if these actions don't go against a specific command. But ok, you answered me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:46:53-07:00","id":871550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871435#post871435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's nice to hear. So you don't need two turns to stop someone from attacking you. Is enough to inflict the mesmerized condition in the first turn and does he stops to attack?</div> </div> </div> </div> When you get the Mesmerized Condition, you become &quot;quiet and reserved.&quot; Being aggressive of your own will is clearly not being quiet nor reserved. Pretty much the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T16:26:19-07:00","id":871859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=871550#post871550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When you get the Mesmerized Condition, you become &quot;quiet and reserved.&quot; Being aggressive of your own will is clearly not being quiet nor reserved. Pretty much the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, this was my point of view in a previous topic on this matter but the most part of this comunity disagree with me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> As I said, this has always been my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T18:00:39-07:00","id":871931,"title":"","content":"Mesmerised states: &quot;You\u2019re not obviously hypnotized \u2014 you\u2019re a bit quiet and reserved compared to normal, but nothing out of the ordinary.&quot;<br /> You can absolutely continue to beat someone to death in a slightly more reserved fashion than normal if you've been Mesmerised. If you suddenly stopped fighting and became calm and passive in the middle of a heated combat that would absolutely be out of the ordinary and reveal you as obviously hypnotised.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that the memory muddling of Mesmerise only happens when the condition is resolved. If it simply fades at the end of the scene you don't get a +3 against further Mesmerise attempts and your memory remains intact (beyond any actual memory-altering commands given to you). You still probably won't realise you've been Mesmerised though, unless you did something really unusual for your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T18:20:05-07:00","id":871949,"title":"","content":"&quot;Not obviously hypnotized&quot; means that you're hypnotized, but it doesn't seem obvious that you are. You're in a hypnotic state, but the power is subtle enough that observers can't instantly tell. And there are plenty of reasons to stop fighting besides hypnotism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T19:45:00-07:00","id":872004,"title":"","content":"This is one of those things that we're probably never going to come to a consensus on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T19:57:31-07:00","id":872015,"title":"","content":"We've got the 'Ask a simple question' part down, but the 'get a simple answer' part needs a lot of work.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/14/149111/3053379-6467146350-on-le.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T20:31:11-07:00","id":872046,"title":"","content":"Best we can do is just agree that they are two equally valid interpretations, and work out what are their consequences, so next time someone asks, they can get &quot;You have Route A and Route B, Route A is best suited for games Z because it emphasizes aspects Y, while Route B is best suited for games C because of K. What kind of gameplay you aim to achieve?&quot; in the face.<br /> I don't care about someone not playing like I do (unless it's my table! :P), but I do care about helping people make informed choices that will maximize their joy of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T22:30:31-07:00","id":872898,"title":"","content":"When did the Burakumin Bloodline get its start? I feel like it was sometime in the mid to late-Tokugawa Shogunate when reading between the lines on how their elders dress. Were they ever mentioned again after the original core rulebook?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T12:29:59-07:00","id":873219,"title":"","content":"How vampiric is an animal raised with Animalism 2: Raise the Familiar, and what is the point of the power? It says they take bashing damage as a vampire, gain intelligence equivalent to an exceptional success on a Feral Whispers roll, and blood sympathy with long distance feral whispers but is that it?<br /> It requires far more vitae to sustain than a ghoul but does it take damage from banes like a vampire? Do its retractable fangs deal lethal damage to vampires? Can it learn disciplines with its newfound intelligence? Does it heal damage like a mortal or can it only heal by spending vitae? Does it gain enhanced vampiric senses?<br /> <br /> I understand there is a devotion that can increase the duration per vitae but I'm not seeing the utility of the base power. Is it so you can just quick raise a corpse and ask it a question?<br /> Also, I would think that a larger, more powerful animal(more stamina) would require more vitae to sustain than a smaller one, but the small scouting type animals are actually much more costly to fuel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-24-2016, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T12:38:28-07:00","id":873230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=873219#post873219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How vampiric is an animal raised with Animalism 2: Raise the Familiar, and what is the point of the power? It says they take bashing damage as a vampire and gain intelligence equivalent to an exceptional success on a Feral Whispers roll but is that it?<br /> It requires far more vitae to sustain but does it take damage from banes like a vampire? Do its retractable fangs deal lethal damage to other vampires? Can it learn disciplines with its newfound intelligence?<br /> <br /> I understand there is a devotion that can increase the duration per vitae but I'm not seeing the utility of the base power. Is it so you can just quick raise a corpse and ask it a question?<br /> Also, I would think that a larger, more powerful animal(more stamina) would require more vitae to sustain than a smaller one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are basically turning the animal into a Ghoul. More powerful than a regular animal without a lot of the drawbacks of being a Vampire.<br /> <br /> I could swear I read that ghouled animals could get physical disciplines, but I can't find it anywhere. I would assume that if it's not in the Disciplines description, they don't have it. Whether advantage or disadvantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T13:01:56-07:00","id":873239,"title":"","content":"Oh so animals can't be ghouled normally in 2E? It doesn't appear to say specifically in the corebook(the only one I have so far) but if that's the case, then it makes much more sense.<br /> <br /> Edit: I found it pg. 298 it saying they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-24-2016, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T13:13:57-07:00","id":873245,"title":"","content":"Animals can be ghouled normally. Raise the Familiar makes the animal in question into something more like a revenant - the familar takes bashing from weapons like a vampire, and can be targetted by Feral Whispers through a sympathetic connection. <br /> <br /> The big advantage of Rasie the Familar is that 1) it rises from the dead, 2) harder to kill, and 3) act as the master's long range control method for Summon the Hunt and other methods of long range manipulation. These three things taken together are rather powerful when taken together. The big advantage for RtF is when you combine it with other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-24-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T16:59:27-07:00","id":874104,"title":"","content":"I forget if this has been answered before (and I tried a simple search just before posting this to no avail), but is it possible for a Kindred who has used a mental/social discipline to dismiss its effect on the target? For example, if you've Mesmerized someone with Dominate, or if you've inflicted the Delusional condition with Nightmare, or you've left someone Charmed with Majesty, as the original cause of the condition, can you end it in some way, or does it have to run its course?<br /> <br /> (This is, of course, barring counter-application of a discipline like Dominating someone who's already Dominated, in which case Clash of Wills comes up instead.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T00:28:53-07:00","id":874324,"title":"","content":"Could an ordo dracul member benefiting from both of the first two dots of the mystery of the ascendant stay awake indefinitely? Since they can resist the day sleep with no ill effects as long as they benefit from the blush of life and they can benefit from the blush of life for 24hrs could they always be active? <br /> <br /> As a part b to this question since a vampire needs only spend a vitae to wake would this vampire only need to spend a vitae to maintain the blush of life but not to remain active?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T01:40:04-07:00","id":874349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=874324#post874324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could an ordo dracul member benefiting from both of the first two dots of the mystery of the ascendant stay awake indefinitely? Since they can resist the day sleep with no ill effects as long as they benefit from the blush of life and they can benefit from the blush of life for 24hrs could they always be active?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the intention behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T01:45:35-07:00","id":874351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=874349#post874349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's the intention behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought so but had to make sure I wasn't missing something obvious. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T02:18:24-07:00","id":874361,"title":"","content":"You'd still need to spend that a vitae each day at around when you'd normally be waking up, just as a &quot;well this is you staying alive&quot; cost. But otherwise yes, you're correct, you can stay awake constantly with no need to sleep with ascendant 2 only having to sleep if they want to heal aggravated wounds only it costs 2 vitae per day rather than 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:16:33-07:00","id":874596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=874361#post874361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd still need to spend that a vitae each day at around when you'd normally be waking up, just as a &amp;quot;well this is you staying alive&amp;quot; cost. But otherwise yes, you're correct, you can stay awake constantly with no need to sleep with ascendant 2 only having to sleep if they want to heal aggravated wounds only it costs 2 vitae per day rather than 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you have to pay vitae to awaken if your already awake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:24:57-07:00","id":874605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=874104#post874104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget if this has been answered before (and I tried a simple search just before posting this to no avail), but is it possible for a Kindred who has used a mental/social discipline to dismiss its effect on the target? For example, if you've Mesmerized someone with Dominate, or if you've inflicted the Delusional condition with Nightmare, or you've left someone Charmed with Majesty, as the original cause of the condition, can you end it in some way, or does it have to run its course?<br /> <br /> (This is, of course, barring counter-application of a discipline like Dominating someone who's already Dominated, in which case Clash of Wills comes up instead.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No you can not end the Charmed, Enthralled, Mesmerized.. ect conditions if you want to, They are stuck there until they wear off or resolve. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:05:00-07:00","id":874861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=874596#post874596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would you have to pay vitae to awaken if your already awake?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Vitae is not to awake, is to maintain the animation of your undead body and not fall into Torpor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:55:15-07:00","id":874912,"title":"","content":"I'm actually surprised that you don't have to spend an additional vitae on top of the blush to stay active during the day. I always looked at it as 1BP was how much vitae it takes to just fuel and animate the body and conscious mind for normal tasks over the course of a night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:05:32-07:00","id":874925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=874861#post874861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the Vitae is not to awake, is to maintain the animation of your undead body and not fall into Torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the case in 1st edition, but that's not what the 2e core book says.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once the sun rises, the vampire\u2019s soul drags her toward slumber. This isn\u2019t a certain thing, but difficult to resist. Unless she\u2019s at risk of facing the sun, she sleeps. To resist sleep, make a Stamina + Resolve roll. If successful, the vampire remains alert and active, but she gains the Lethargic Condition (see p. 305). With an exceptional success, she does not gain the Condition.<br /> <br /> Any time Kindred sleep, they stay asleep. Waking is difficult at best. Only direct threats like fire, sunlight, or a collapsing building will wake a vampire. The act of waking is hard, fast, and disconcerting. <br /> <br /> The blood snaps her to brief consciousness, and allows her to take immediate actions to defend herself. The dead heart shoves Vitae through the body once, hard.<br /> <br /> When something disturbs the vampire\u2019s slumber or puts her at risk, make a Humanity roll. Success allows her to remain awake for a number of turns equal to her Humanity. Failure means she remains asleep. Once those turns are over, she falls back to sleep without an additional Humanity roll. Once she\u2019s exceeded 5 + her Blood Potency successes during her waking turns, she can remain awake indefinitely, as if she never went to sleep in the first place.<br /> <b>Any time a vampire wakes from slumber, she immediately expends a point of Vitae.</b> Normal waking happens shortly after the sun goes down. Waking is like a fatal heart attack in reverse; the body hurts and does not work. The heart slowly begins pulsing, and the body slowly fights back to life. The limbs begin paralyzed, but then tingle and grow flush.</div> </div> </div> </div>(I bolded the most important bit). From my reading, if you don't sleep, you don't need to spend Vitae to wake up. Conversely, if you are woken up several times throughout the day, you reflexively spend 1 Vitae each time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-26-2016, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T13:37:00-07:00","id":875927,"title":"","content":"Huh. I'd really like a Word of God on whether they actually intended the Coil to work like that and in that case what is supposed to happen if a vampire who's awake just because she's been keeping the blush on for days suddenly turns it off*.<br /> <br /> *because with the blush on she has a pulse and bad things capable to hear a pulse go bump in the night, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T00:38:25-07:00","id":876332,"title":"","content":"Would ghouling someone halt the spread of a disease like cancer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T03:22:49-07:00","id":876423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=876332#post876332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would ghouling someone halt the spread of a disease like cancer?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the actually ghouling didn't, they could just spend vitae to heal themselves of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T03:49:51-07:00","id":876445,"title":"","content":"Yes, ghouling someone halts the spread of cancer, no they can't cure them-self of pre-existing diseases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T04:13:49-07:00","id":876463,"title":"","content":"2E Pg: 297: &quot;Even better, any disease they suffer from stops in its tracks, progressing no further from the point the character becomes a ghoul.&quot;<br /> <br /> So they aren't cured but the cancer stops growing, the syphilis stops spreading etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:15:47-07:00","id":876798,"title":"","content":"Hi guys! I didn't find anything about this subject so, i would like to know your opinion about this<br /> <br /> Can a ghoul have more than one dot on a discipline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7761,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","user":"Glauber","date":". 04-28-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:20:37-07:00","id":876800,"title":"","content":"Yes. For example, the Ghoul retainer sidebar mentions that Ghouls taken as Retainers have one Discipline dot at one Merit dot, two dots for three, and three for five, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:25:29-07:00","id":876806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=876800#post876800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. For example, the Ghoul retainer sidebar mentions that Ghouls taken as Retainers have one Discipline dot at one Merit dot, two dots for three, and three for five, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant, to rise one discipline to level two, three or beyond<br /> <br /> E.g. Can a ghoul have protean 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:28:39-07:00","id":876810,"title":"","content":"They could in first edition. Nothing seems to have suggested that has changed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blood &amp; Smoke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Learning Disciplines: Ghouls may learn Disciplines under the same rules as Kindred. They may not learn Coils or Scales of the Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-28-2016, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:32:53-07:00","id":876814,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:32:57-07:00","id":876816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=876810#post876810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They could in first edition. Nothing seems to have suggested that has changed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ha! I was just about to post that when you edited it in. Ghouls can learn disciplines the same as vampires, So they can have 1-5 and it costs 3 or 4 exp to raise it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T07:28:11-07:00","id":877660,"title":"","content":"Important to note that while ghoul can learn disciplines like a vampire, they have additional limitations. Animalism is hit particularly hard by this. Dot 2, 3 and 5 are useless to ghouls. Obfuscate 5 is also useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T08:33:50-07:00","id":877725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=877660#post877660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important to note that while ghoul can learn disciplines like a vampire, they have additional limitations. Animalism is hit particularly hard by this. Dot 2, 3 and 5 are useless to ghouls. Obfuscate 5 is also useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I always nix that in house rules, myself, when I have a say in it. I mean, I kinda get it, since their spilled blood isn't pure Vitae, but I think it'd have been better if they just said ghouls take lethal damage AND lose the vitae in the process, as they have to force the Vitae through with their normal blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T03:17:32-07:00","id":879416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=877725#post877725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I always nix that in house rules, myself, when I have a say in it. I mean, I kinda get it, since their spilled blood isn't pure Vitae, but I think it'd have been better if they just said ghouls take lethal damage AND lose the vitae in the process, as they have to force the Vitae through with their normal blood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly I think this is exactly what the developer wanted. Ghouls are not as powerful as vampires and they are limited in some way in their use of disciplines. Simply some effect go outside their condition. So if you want to house rule that in your chronicles it's ok but I personally prefer to keep this limitation for ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T00:12:11-07:00","id":897620,"title":"","content":"Hello, tried using the search but couldn't find the answers to these:<br /> <br /> How bestial is a vampire in frenzy? It's described as an animal, but also described as knowing how to throw things. Does it know how to balance on a ledge so as to not fall off, to get to its prey faster (if its prey was the frenzy's goal)? Does it know how to use most Disciplines? Does it know how to use firearms? (I'm guessing it would drop any firearms or weapons it's holding and use its claws instead)<br /> <br /> Also, can one use Physical Intensity while frenzying? Do the benefits stack?<br /> <br /> Edit: Can one Ride the Wave and change the Frenzy's desire from &quot;kill the target&quot; to something a bit contrarian, like &quot;shoot the target&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","user":"Captain Shoe","date":". 05-24-2016, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T04:24:31-07:00","id":897683,"title":"","content":"An inability to use physical intensity would severely weaken the character, so hell fucking yes they can use it in frenzy. Same with disciplines. I'd say a gun was fair game too, provided you were sufficiently brutal with it. If you shoot someone dead you'll probably keep going at the corpse until you run out of bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T05:06:31-07:00","id":897694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=897620#post897620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How bestial is a vampire in frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sorta 100% but still 100% sentient. There is no sign there is a decrease in intelligence. Bestial does not mean dumb (the book actually specifically says the beast is not dumb).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it know how to balance on a ledge so as to not fall off, to get to its prey faster </div> </div> </div>You can actually do that better in frenzy than you can out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it know how to use most Disciplines? </div> </div> </div>There is no sign the vampire loses it's vampiric powers, especially since it specifically says they do things like use things their predatory aura.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it know how to use firearms? </div> </div> </div>No reason to assume they wouldn't know how. Though, I'd imagine they'd probably prefer throwing a truck at you or ripping off your head if they have the choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I'm guessing it would drop any firearms or weapons it's holding and use its claws instead) </div> </div> </div>Most vampires don't have claws, though while in frenzy &quot;She can grab and bite as a single instant action, as she ravenously mauls her victim. Apply the successes on her Strength + Brawl roll to establish a grapple as lethal damage, and she takes an immediate point of Vitae from the victim.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, can one use Physical Intensity while frenzying? </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do the benefits stack? </div> </div> </div>Think so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Can one Ride the Wave and change the Frenzy's desire from &quot;kill the target&quot; to something a bit contrarian, like &quot;shoot the target&quot;? </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, but maybe. Shoot the target sounds less like a desire, and more like a method to me personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T05:22:26-07:00","id":897701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=897620#post897620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How bestial is a vampire in frenzy? It's described as an animal, but also described as knowing how to throw things.<br /> <br /> Does it know how to balance on a ledge so as to not fall off, to get to its prey faster (if its prey was the frenzy's goal)? Does it know how to use most Disciplines? Does it know how to use firearms? (I'm guessing it would drop any firearms or weapons it's holding and use its claws instead)<br /> <br /> Also, can one use Physical Intensity while frenzying? Do the benefits stack?<br /> <br /> Edit: Can one Ride the Wave and change the Frenzy's desire from &quot;kill the target&quot; to something a bit contrarian, like &quot;shoot the target&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> For the most part, I say &quot;yes&quot; to all the above. &quot;Beastial&quot; is a very thematic way of describing things, but its not exactly accurate. Beastial and animal-like*, in this case, is a reference to the loss of the ability to reason and think rationally, to plan ahead or care about consequences. I think this particular line from the core book section on frenzy sums up my take on the situation. &quot;End the problem by any means necessary.&quot; If shooting a gun or using a Discipline is the best way to acomplish that goal, then yes, it absolutely will use those.<br /> <br /> Though, it should be noted that some Disciplines and tactics are ill suited for the state of frenzy. Frenzies are &quot;immediate, forceful and destructive abandon.&quot; Calm and collected Dominate uses tend to be inappropriate, for instance, as is a carefully constructed Nightmare illusion. Using Obfuscate during a fear frenzy or Majesty for a hunger frenzy wouldn't be amiss, I imagine. Auspex to track prey would likely as well. Protean and the three Physicals are naturally a given. Frenzy is all about losing control over your emotions and lashing out at the world to satisfy a pressing need. If its something that doesn't rely on human ability to plan ahead or avoid violence, then its allowed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * The only reference to animal behavior is the single line that a Kindred is capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator is, and that is actually meant to imply a certain level of cunning, not a restriction on behaviors. Especially given the previous line, &quot;the Beast isn't stupid.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T06:28:54-07:00","id":897740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=879416#post879416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly I think this is exactly what the developer wanted. Ghouls are not as powerful as vampires and they are limited in some way in their use of disciplines. Simply some effect go outside their condition. So if you want to house rule that in your chronicles it's ok but I personally prefer to keep this limitation for ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think that rule is to reflect on Ghouls having mostly human blood in their system and any spilled is unlikely to contain a sufficient amount of Vitae to fuel the desired effect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T06:36:33-07:00","id":897746,"title":"","content":"Personally, I do not let vampires shoot guns while in a frenzy. If they had it in their hand and the intent was to kill, then maybe they beat the target to death. I think that frenzy, since it is bestial, should only include Feed, run, kill. Shooting (with any accuracy) is beyond the scope of many animals.<br /> <br /> I do agree that Some disciplines, as mentioned, require some thought and finesse too, like Majesty and Dominate, so I wouldnt allow those either.<br /> <br /> I do always allow the physical ones, protean, physical intensity and lashing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 05-24-2016, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:33:39-07:00","id":897785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=897620#post897620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can one Ride the Wave and change the Frenzy's desire from &quot;kill the target&quot; to something a bit contrarian, like &quot;shoot the target&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>One cannot ride the wave to change the goal of a frenzy unless one has Coil of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:43:24-07:00","id":897795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=897785#post897785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One cannot ride the wave to change the goal of a frenzy unless one has Coil of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book says &quot;..., she rides the wave. This functions identical to a normal frenzy, with all the normal benefits. However you may choose the Beast's desire and specific target. This desire does not have to align with the provocation.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the whole purpose of Riding the Wave is to change the goal. Which level of coil are you referring to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:48:36-07:00","id":897797,"title":"","content":"It says: the beast will try to achieve its goal in the most direct way but it's not stupid. So, for example, a frenzy vampire closed in a cage, if he cannot break the door, could use majesty or domination (in a more bestial or depravated way) to escape in my opinion. Not just growl and shake the iron bars if it is useless.<br /> Probably he shouldn't uses complicate command and even the majesty uses should be direct and instinctive. Seductive aura is an example of what a frenzy kindred can do so why he couldn't use majesty that is an enhancement of that kind of aura?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 05-24-2016, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T07:57:51-07:00","id":897803,"title":"","content":"I'd say anything that meets dominate 1's four word limit is probably simple enough to be used in frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T09:08:45-07:00","id":897869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=897797#post897797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says: the beast will try to achieve its goal in the most direct way but it's not stupid. So, for example, a frenzy vampire closed in a cage, if he cannot break the door, could use majesty or domination (in a more bestial or depravated way) to escape in my opinion. Not just growl and shake the iron bars if it is useless.<br /> Probably he shouldn't uses complicate command and even the majesty uses should be direct and instinctive. Seductive aura is an example of what a frenzy kindred can do so why he couldn't use majesty that is an enhancement of that kind of aura?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>&quot; While frenzied, the vampire does everything in her power<br /> to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires. She does so with immediate,<br /> forceful, and destructive abandon. If there\u2019s someone in the<br /> way, she throws him or decks him. If she\u2019s hungry, she bites the<br /> closest thing to her mouth. That said, the Beast isn\u2019t stupid.<br /> It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified,<br /> or starving animal predator is, and it will lash out with the<br /> predatory aura if that will help sate it. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> Majesty is not immediate, forceful or destructive. An enraged tiger does not stop attacking the bars of their cage long enough to convince the handler to let them out. They attack until they calm down.<br /> <br /> Lashing out even the seductive one plays to the primal urges. it is forceful and can be quite destructive.<br /> <br /> The beast isnt stupid yes, but it does seem to imply that it is not capable of plotting. &gt; It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator is.<br /> <br /> Even using Dominate to tell someone to get out of your way, seems out of the question, because it says you simply toss that person out of the way. That is what a beast would do. It is forceful and destructive.<br /> <br /> Perhaps we could get a developer to say what was intended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T09:25:06-07:00","id":897884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=897869#post897869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even using Dominate to tell someone to get out of your way, seems out of the question, because it says you simply toss that person out of the way. That is what a beast would do. It is forceful and destructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Dominate at least, I could see really simple and direct commands working: &quot;Be Quiet!&quot; &quot;Go Away!&quot; &quot;Leave Me Alone!&quot;, stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T09:49:50-07:00","id":897904,"title":"","content":"Which part of feed, kill, or Run. Does that help accomplish?<br /> <br /> You wouldnt tell someone you were feeding on to be quiet or go away. You just bite the first thing closest to your mouth.<br /> You wouldnt stop long enough to tell someone to be quiet or go away. if you were running away.<br /> And I dont think you would stop long enough to tell someone to be quiet or go away. if you were killing them.<br /> <br /> You dont ask bystandards around you to do those things either if you were killing or feeding off someone else.. You just do it. You dont care the consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 05-24-2016, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:03:01-07:00","id":897917,"title":"","content":"It's a reference to the &quot;Something / Someone in the way of your Goal&quot; part. If the Sheriff is between me and the Vampire who killed my Touchstone, and the a-hole taunts me about the slow death they inflicted triggering me to frenzy - my goal is to humiliate, hurt or kill the a-hole. Getting the Sheriff out of the way is my first priority. What will get him out of my way more immediately? If I'm a Ventrue without Vigor or Celerity, Dominate could very well be the most direct method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:42:43-07:00","id":897971,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for fleeing, if there is someone standing in your way taunting you or attacking you that provoked the frenzy then Dominating them to go away seems to be pretty on the nose for escaping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:59:44-07:00","id":897998,"title":"","content":"Personally I always felt it depended on the character, the situation and how you want to run it in your chronicle.<br /> <br /> I can see a scene were my character is behind a bar and someone insults him. He loses his Frenzy check and:<br /> 1. Jumps across the bar, fangs out and starts biting the guys neck, the guy struggles to get out of the grab but the Frenzied character just keeps gnawing away until the rude man falls into torpor. He then comes to his senses, looks around, wipes the blood from his face and asks &quot;Does anyone else have any anything to say?&quot;<br /> or.<br /> 2. Reaches under the bar, grabs a shotgun and shoots the guy the face. Then he jumps onto the bar and continues to unload on the now prone opponent until his gun is out of bullets, cursing and snarling the entire time. Then when he is out of bullets, he bludgeons the guy with the shotgun until the Beast is satiated. He then comes to his senses, looks around, wipes the blood from his face and asks &quot;Does anyone else have any anything to say?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean a situation like #2 is pretty cool and I wouldn't want to not have that possibility in the game, but at the same time, I can see how its a slippery slope to Frenzy being &quot;what I would have done in combat anyhow.&quot; Also if you limit options to #1, you run out of new and interesting ways to describe the Frenzy over time and it loses its impact.<br /> <br /> If you trust your players and your ST, it all works out. Just keep it loose, go with the cooler option and have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:33:59-07:00","id":898092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=897904#post897904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which part of feed, kill, or Run. Does that help accomplish?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feed, kill, or run aren't the only options for the goal of Frenzy anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:46:51-07:00","id":898110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=898092#post898092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feed, kill, or run aren't the only options for the goal of Frenzy anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book references those. twice: Pg 103-104<br /> <br /> &quot; When faced with a strong enough stimulus, the vampire<br /> risks losing control of her Beast. She can temporarily hold the<br /> monster inside, but eventually she must face her monstrosity.<br /> Either she\u2019ll force it down, or the Beast overwhelms her to<br /> <b>fight, feed, or flee. &quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an <b>enraged,</b>(fight)<b> terrified,</b>(flee)<br /> <b>or starving </b>(feed) animal predator is, &quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> What are the other options?<br /> <br /> Also remember the point where it says it does it with: &quot;immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon&quot; Frenzy isn't quiet, subtle, or thoughtful. Which dominate is all those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 05-24-2016, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T12:55:05-07:00","id":898124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=897998#post897998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I always felt it depended on the character, the situation and how you want to run it in your chronicle.<br /> <br /> I can see a scene were my character is behind a bar and someone insults him. He loses his Frenzy check and:<br /> 1. Jumps across the bar, fangs out and starts biting the guys neck, the guy struggles to get out of the grab but the Frenzied character just keeps gnawing away until the rude man falls into torpor. He then comes to his senses, looks around, wipes the blood from his face and asks &quot;Does anyone else have any anything to say?&quot;<br /> or.<br /> 2. Reaches under the bar, grabs a shotgun and shoots the guy the face. Then he jumps onto the bar and continues to unload on the now prone opponent until his gun is out of bullets, cursing and snarling the entire time. Then when he is out of bullets, he bludgeons the guy with the shotgun until the Beast is satiated. He then comes to his senses, looks around, wipes the blood from his face and asks &quot;Does anyone else have any anything to say?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean a situation like #2 is pretty cool and I wouldn't want to not have that possibility in the game, but at the same time, I can see how its a slippery slope to Frenzy being &quot;what I would have done in combat anyhow.&quot; Also if you limit options to #1, you run out of new and interesting ways to describe the Frenzy over time and it loses its impact.<br /> <br /> If you trust your players and your ST, it all works out. Just keep it loose, go with the cooler option and have fun.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My opinion: <br /> <br /> Option 1 is more of a frenzied vampire is suppose to be like. I also dont think that you would run out of ways to describe your rage. <br /> <br /> Option 2 is a conscious choice... or maybe you frenzied when you ran out of bullets..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T13:17:07-07:00","id":898144,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm of the opinion that how one acts most of the time greatly influences the frenzy. So if one is a frail, evasive gun-user they would use their guns first and use celerity and such to dodge or even take cover (before running up to them and emptying the clip once the prey is already dead, as many have mentioned). Or if one uses Dominate for everything, they would tell their prey to walk off a building (and then maybe push them off impatiently with their next action)<br /> <br /> However, it is also implied the Beast's actions are somewhat universal, as Vitalis believes. The main line from the book that argues this to me is the one stating that vampires do not inherently commit diablerie while frenzying. This would make them a bit more werewolf-like, except less suicidal.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the answers! As I thought, frenzying is a little murky and the answer seems as always is: one should ask one's ST to see how they do it. <br /> <br /> Perhaps a fun concept, even if the ST runs with &quot;universal frenzy vampires,&quot; would be an Ordu Dracul vampire trying to change the nature of the beast, like creating a personalized version of Coil of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T13:30:42-07:00","id":898158,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wouldn't have a vampire in frenzy <i>pull out</i> a gun, but if they were already holding one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T13:39:43-07:00","id":898171,"title":"","content":"An enraged predator will snarl and roar to scare others to get out of the way. Nightmare 2 does similar. I see no reason why a frenzied vampire wouldn't use Nightmare in this situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T14:05:16-07:00","id":898197,"title":"","content":"For sure. That would help you fight/kill your target. Beasts often use tactics to make themselves more ferocious looking. I would say Nightmare 1 and 2 would fly. <br /> <br /> The reason diablerie doesnt work is because that takes an act of will. A thoughtful conscious act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T22:39:01-07:00","id":898656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=897795#post897795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book says &quot;..., she rides the wave. This functions identical to a normal frenzy, with all the normal benefits. However you may choose the Beast's desire and specific target. This desire does not have to align with the provocation.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think the whole purpose of Riding the Wave is to change the goal. Which level of coil are you referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>The purpose of riding the wave is so you can gain the benefits of frenzying on your own terms. It is actually impossible to ride the wave to redirect a frenzy as you'd need to spend willpower to delay the frenzy while also spending willpower to ride the wave, breaking the one willpower per turn rule.<br /> I'm referring to the first dot of Coil of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T00:14:06-07:00","id":898727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=898656#post898656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The purpose of riding the wave is so you can gain the benefits of frenzying on your own terms. It is actually impossible to ride the wave to redirect a frenzy as you'd need to spend willpower to delay the frenzy while also spending willpower to ride the wave, breaking the one willpower per turn rule.<br /> I'm referring to the first dot of Coil of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>To ride the wave you don't have to delay the frenzy. You ride the frenzy. So you spend just one willpower to ride it not one to delay it and then another one to ride it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T05:29:20-07:00","id":898835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=898656#post898656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The purpose of riding the wave is so you can gain the benefits of frenzying on your own terms. It is actually impossible to ride the wave to redirect a frenzy as you'd need to spend willpower to delay the frenzy while also spending willpower to ride the wave, breaking the one willpower per turn rule.<br /> I'm referring to the first dot of Coil of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you are right here.<br /> <br /> 1. Riding the Wave: When you encounter a frenzy trigger, instead of resisting it, you can change the target and the focus of your Beast. (eg. you can change it from tearing Larry's throat out to running away from Larry). Page 105.<br /> <br /> 2. Stir the Beast allows you to enter Frenzy unprovoked, choosing your target and focus by spending a willpower. Page 157<br /> <br /> The differences is that #1 requires a frenzy trigger to go off and #2 is a sure thing.<br /> <br /> Delaying a frenzy is a third option and not required to Ride the Wave. Page 104<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T05:52:54-07:00","id":898842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=898144#post898144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'm of the opinion that how one acts most of the time greatly influences the frenzy. So if one is a frail, evasive gun-user they would use their guns first and use celerity and such to dodge or even take cover (before running up to them and emptying the clip once the prey is already dead, as many have mentioned). Or if one uses Dominate for everything, they would tell their prey to walk off a building (and then maybe push them off impatiently with their next action)<br /> <br /> However, it is also implied the Beast's actions are somewhat universal, as Vitalis believes. The main line from the book that argues this to me is the one stating that vampires do not inherently commit diablerie while frenzying. This would make them a bit more werewolf-like, except less suicidal.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the answers! As I thought, frenzying is a little murky and the answer seems as always is: one should ask one's ST to see how they do it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a fun concept, even if the ST runs with &quot;universal frenzy vampires,&quot; would be an Ordu Dracul vampire trying to change the nature of the beast, like creating a personalized version of Coil of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't go with a vampire in frenzy taking cover, the beast needs that guy to die NOW, not 3 seconds from now and its okay if he gets hurt doing it.<br /> <br /> That being said, if that works for your group, that's how you should do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T07:55:42-07:00","id":898921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=898835#post898835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you are right here.<br /> <br /> 1. Riding the Wave: When you encounter a frenzy trigger, instead of resisting it, you can change the target and the focus of your Beast. (eg. you can change it from tearing Larry's throat out to running away from Larry). Page 105.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing we're reading different editions? I'm looking at VtR 2nd ed. and this quote doesn't appear. Looking over it again and reading between the lines it seems you're correct and that riding the wave is intended to be in response to a frenzy trigger, I got entirely the opposite impression when I previously read the Riding the Wave rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T08:07:38-07:00","id":898930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=898921#post898921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing we're reading different editions? I'm looking at VtR 2nd ed. and this quote doesn't appear. Looking over it again and reading between the lines it seems you're correct and that riding the wave is intended to be in response to a frenzy trigger, I got entirely the opposite impression when I previously read the Riding the Wave rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>VtR 2nd edition as well. I didn't mean to imply its a quote, I was just summarizing and pointing our where it is detailed. I should have been clearer there using the phrase detailed on page 105.<br /> <br /> I know in 1st edition, riding the wave was something you worked yourself up to outside of the normal frenzy triggers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T20:13:19-07:00","id":936882,"title":"","content":"Does Ghouling someone with a nasty disease stop or heal it? What about the Embrace?<br /> <br /> I'm mostly curious about cancer and leprosy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T20:20:17-07:00","id":936891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=936882#post936882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Ghouling someone with a nasty disease stop or heal it? What about the Embrace?<br /> <br /> I'm mostly curious about cancer and leprosy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Says right in the book it stops the disease. Not heal, just stasis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T20:23:14-07:00","id":936893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=936891#post936891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Says right in the book it stops the disease. Not heal, just stasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Nothing quite like an eternity of pain from your tumors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T20:48:14-07:00","id":936905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=936893#post936893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Nothing quite like an eternity of pain from your tumors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing says you can't cut all the tumors out and let the vitae put you back to prime condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T22:50:19-07:00","id":936943,"title":"","content":"Ghouling someone effectively puts diseases like cancer into remission, but embracing someone keeps their body in exactly the same condition it was in at the moment of embrace. One of the reasons it's a good idea to ghoul someone before embracing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T00:21:30-07:00","id":936968,"title":"","content":"Embracing will cause any disease that wouldn't affect a vampire to, you know, no longer affect them, and thus it'd die off or cease, but their body wouldn't change. In the case of the aforementioned tumors, if they're big enough to be painful or awkward, that's what a Night Doctor and some willpower is for. If they're not, who cares that there's a lump in the lung you don't use anymore? It wouldn't cause you any actual trouble in that case, it'd just kinda be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T06:13:24-07:00","id":940597,"title":"","content":"New question: What is in your experience the best way to find other players to form a group? Do you mostly play offline or are there good online resources? (Ok, that's two questions but still...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T09:30:42-07:00","id":940653,"title":"","content":"There are several ways. Post here, Post Roll20 or Giantip. Finding players is as hard as finding a storyteller. offline, might check your local game stores, if you are lucky enough to have one. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T11:26:41-07:00","id":941285,"title":"","content":"Is there a Devotion that lets you extend the benefits of Obfuscate to observers on the other side of cameras, without resorting to outright technopathy? CCTV is a drag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T18:53:35-07:00","id":941587,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate works on all observers while the power is active, the only thing you have to worry about is the recording being reviewed after the scene. An exceptional success on Touch of Night continues to blur out whatever you used it on even on a recording but otherwise you're best of sneaking in to erase the footage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T19:28:39-07:00","id":941611,"title":"","content":"But making one would be pretty easy. Something like Vigor and Obfuscation perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T03:06:31-07:00","id":941792,"title":"","content":"Remember that vampires are categorically immune to being identified via mirror or cameras unless they want to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:25:55-07:00","id":941898,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=941587#post941587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obfuscate works on all observers while the power is active, the only thing you have to worry about is the recording being reviewed after the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I thought the consensus was that it only worked... line of effect, I guess, for lack of a better phrase. You had to be part of the immediate Scene, it didn't work on observers who weren't directly exposed to you. Also security observation comes perilously close to direct, active guarding, to my mind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=941792#post941792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">vampires are categorically immune to being identified via mirror or cameras unless they want to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hadn't forgotten. I'm less concerned with specific identification than general alarms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:13:08-07:00","id":942140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=941898#post941898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I thought the consensus was that it only worked... line of effect, I guess, for lack of a better phrase. You had to be part of the immediate Scene, it didn't work on observers who weren't directly exposed to you. Also security observation comes perilously close to direct, active guarding, to my mind.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am thinking that it works on anyone using eyeballs or ears to try to observe you. Someone who was looking at security cameras in a security room would see the blur or body but they cant see the face.. but they would know someone is there, but when they went to go look for that person.. they wouldnt find them. You would probably think they just moved on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T01:22:46-07:00","id":942567,"title":"","content":"Eyeballs, ears, noses, ampullae of lorenzini... If it has a brain and is trying to observe you in any way Obfuscate works. Assuming we're talking Cloak of Night, the camera picks you up, but the person looking at the live feed cannot see you. If you want to see someone using Cloak of Night you have to use some sort of supernatual power of perception.<br /> <br /> Personally I would straight up not buy Obfuscate in a game where it's been ruled that simply finding a way to observe someone indirectly can cancel out the effect of Obfuscate. Especially if it's set in modern times and everyone has a camera phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T03:51:02-07:00","id":942622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942567#post942567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eyeballs, ears, noses, ampullae of lorenzini... If it has a brain and is trying to observe you in any way Obfuscate works. Assuming we're talking Cloak of Night, the camera picks you up, but the person looking at the live feed cannot see you. If you want to see someone using Cloak of Night you have to use some sort of supernatual power of perception.<br /> <br /> Personally I would straight up not buy Obfuscate in a game where it's been ruled that simply finding a way to observe someone indirectly can cancel out the effect of Obfuscate. Especially if it's set in modern times and everyone has a camera phone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you shouldn't buy Obfuscate because throwing a bag of flour on the floor or simply not dusting makes it possible to cancel Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T06:21:58-07:00","id":942670,"title":"","content":"I apologize, my intent wasn't to restart one of ^these discussions. Amusingly, the whole point of the Devotion was to cut through some of Obfuscate's contextual murk. That and I prefer to cover my bases; ST interpretation tends to bite me in the ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T06:50:13-07:00","id":942678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942567#post942567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would straight up not buy Obfuscate in a game where it's been ruled that simply finding a way to observe someone indirectly can cancel out the effect of Obfuscate. Especially if it's set in modern times and everyone has a camera phone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure no one's said it would be cancelled. But sensing Obfuscated vampires through indirect means have always been a thing. 'He leaves no scent and makes no sound, though his passing leaves incidental signs, like drifting smoke or creaking floorboards.'<br /> <br /> Simple fact is, your vampire can carry around a sack of flour wherever they go, ready to spread it across the ground when they hear something that might have been movement. Just like they're allowed to never make eye contact, or gouge out their own eyes and use sonar. Or only join covenants that grant the most killing power and blood bond every living thing they come across or never take any risk or displease any other vampire or supernatural. They're all choices you can make for a character, just like in real life you can choose to never leave your apartment and never talk to anyone.<br /> <br /> They're just a series of choices that don't really embrace the game, or gaming in general. Or at least, they're embracing a very specific form of the game where they want their character to be a paranoiac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-03-2016, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T08:19:24-07:00","id":942722,"title":"","content":"I have no problem with a perceptive and well prepared character being given the opportunity to spend their entire turn making an opposed check to potentially get an idea of the rough location of an Obfuscated vampire. My problem is &quot;Oh Miss Mekhet the Obfuscate specialist just turned invisible? I look around the room staring through my phone to find her and make all those Obfuscate dots worthless against me.&quot; Not even Dominate is that easy to counter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","user":"PrinceRaven","date":". 08-03-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T08:24:10-07:00","id":942725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942678#post942678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure no one's said it would be cancelled. But sensing Obfuscated vampires through indirect means have always been a thing. 'He leaves no scent and makes no sound, though his passing leaves incidental signs, like drifting smoke or creaking floorboards.'<br /> <br /> Simple fact is, your vampire can carry around a sack of flour wherever they go, ready to spread it across the ground when they hear something that might have been movement. Just like they're allowed to never make eye contact, or gouge out their own eyes and use sonar. Or only join covenants that grant the most killing power and blood bond every living thing they come across or never take any risk or displease any other vampire or supernatural. They're all choices you can make for a character, just like in real life you can choose to never leave your apartment and never talk to anyone.<br /> <br /> They're just a series of choices that don't really embrace the game, or gaming in general. Or at least, they're embracing a very specific form of the game where they want their character to be a paranoiac.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. RAW it even says that you can be detected through indirect means. So. Princeraven, that would be most games where STs rule that. It doesnt exactly &quot;cancel&quot; the effect, but now you know they are there, and lashing out can break it.<br /> <br /> Though after reading this thread I am curious on the camera thing... I always thought it would be like a horror movie, You know, when you take a picture and someone is in it, blurry, but then you look and no one is there, so you snap another picture and they are closer. you look again. No one is there. Or video footage after the fact, You walk into a busy store, you fill your pockets with whatever and walk right out, when they are looking over the video footage later, they see this blurred person taking everything and leave. Cant Identify him anyway... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:26:18-07:00","id":942758,"title":"","content":"People seem to forget that there are two forms of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> One is mental invisibility. If cameras work on a form of Obfuscate, it works on this level. There's no indication that indirect methods like flour do work on this level. You have to cause a ruckus to be seen.<br /> <br /> The other is literal invisibility. You are invisible, and it isn't all in everyone's head. Indirect methods like the flour work on this form. It isn't broken by causing a ruckus, but people can perceive you if you stab them. Or if you're kicking around flour, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:57:49-07:00","id":942777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942758#post942758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People seem to forget that there are two forms of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> One is mental invisibility. If cameras work on a form of Obfuscate, it works on this level. There's no indication that indirect methods like flour do work on this level. You have to cause a ruckus to be seen.<br /> <br /> The other is literal invisibility. You are invisible, and it isn't all in everyone's head. Indirect methods like the flour work on this form. It isn't broken by causing a ruckus, but people can perceive you if you stab them. Or if you're kicking around flour, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>All forms of Obfuscate are mental invisibility. One works by making observers percieve you as nobody important. The other works by making observers completely ignore sensory information about you. But no form of obfuscate works by bending light. You're never &quot;actually invisible&quot;, you just may as well be for all intents and purposes because people who percieve you ignore what they percieve about you.<br /> <br /> As for cameras, I personally rule that both forms work on people viewing you through cameras. With Face in the Crowd, people viewing the camera feed see &quot;some guy&quot; on the feed. Depending on where you are and what you do while on camera, &quot;some guy&quot; being in a place no one is supposed to be or doing something illegal may still raise alarms. With Cloak of Night, you're there, the camera records you, anyone watching the feed sees you, but they ignore that sensory information. They &quot;missed that detail&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:13:18-07:00","id":942822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942777#post942777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All forms of Obfuscate are mental invisibility. One works by making observers percieve you as nobody important. The other works by making observers completely ignore sensory information about you. But no form of obfuscate works by bending light. You're never &quot;actually invisible&quot;, you just may as well be for all intents and purposes because people who percieve you ignore what they percieve about you.<br /> <br /> As for cameras, I personally rule that both forms work on people viewing you through cameras. With Face in the Crowd, people viewing the camera feed see &quot;some guy&quot; on the feed. Depending on where you are and what you do while on camera, &quot;some guy&quot; being in a place no one is supposed to be or doing something illegal may still raise alarms. With Cloak of Night, you're there, the camera records you, anyone watching the feed sees you, but they ignore that sensory information. They &quot;missed that detail&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Totally valid point of view. It does pose a question though.. Does Majesty then Work through cameras? The guy in the back security room watching over the bank and one vampire pops Majesty to have everyone look at him and ignore everything else.. while his friends go off and rob the bank? ( granted stupid scenario, but.. yeah )<br /> <br /> Then can you dominate through Cameras and video feed? Or even nightmare?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:21:24-07:00","id":942829,"title":"","content":"I would also advocate for not differentiating between attempts to perceive obfuscated characters with a camera or through biological vision. Essentially eyes are nothing else than cameras that are attached to your brain. The fact that they happen to be organic and a bit more directly connected does not change how they work.<br /> <br /> I would also rule out the flour method. It seems munchkin-y to the max and does not fit the tone of the game. Obfuscate is a form of mental manipulation that makes its victims do unreasonable things, such as ignoring the floury footprints.<br /> <br /> <b>On to my question</b>: Is there any clarification somewhere on what would happen if a Strix were to possess a werewolf (corpse?). Would it also gain the supernatural abilities of its host? Or are those tied to its spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:23:46-07:00","id":942831,"title":"","content":"There's no clarification on it, but coming from werewolf it seems like it would keep most of its abilities, though not be able to gain new Gifts and Renown. Providing it were alive. Claiming a werewolf corpse probably wouldn't give it any particular abilities, it would just be possessing a human corpse at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-03-2016, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:50:31-07:00","id":942864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lepaca</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942829#post942829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also advocate for not differentiating between attempts to perceive obfuscated characters with a camera or through biological vision. Essentially eyes are nothing else than cameras that are attached to your brain. The fact that they happen to be organic and a bit more directly connected does not change how they work.<br /> <br /> I would also rule out the flour method. It seems munchkin-y to the max and does not fit the tone of the game. Obfuscate is a form of mental manipulation that makes its victims do unreasonable things, such as ignoring the floury footprints.<br /> <br /> <b>On to my question</b>: Is there any clarification somewhere on what would happen if a Strix were to possess a werewolf (corpse?). Would it also gain the supernatural abilities of its host? Or are those tied to its spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not want to put words in your mouth, but Are you saying then that you could Dominate and Majesty through a camera/video feed? <br /> <br /> Because I am thinking a Ventrue with a Dominate on a TV so anyone who walks in and looks into the vampire's eyes through a screen.. Would be pretty beast... Business guy maybe selling something. &quot;Buy this Product&quot; <br /> <br /> A Daeva who Idol's on National TV for something. Oh they would be a god.. Every time someone viewed that clip, a god all over again. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also I Don't know if you would Ignore floury footprints, because it literally says (in dot 3) &quot;Leaves incidental signs, like drifting smoke or creaking floor boards&quot; I think that leaving foot prints in the sand, dust or flour would be completely valid. If it fits the tone or not, it's irrelevant if the RAW says it's possible. Somethings dont fit the box/stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:55:00-07:00","id":942870,"title":"","content":"In one of the Vampire the Masquerade adventures there was a vampire who dominated a guard through a security camera.<br /> <br /> Second edition Requiem is rather clear on the matter, though. 'Dominate requires a vampire make eye contact with her victims in order to issue commands. That contact is one-way \u2014 the victim needs to see the vampire\u2019s eyes, but not vice versa. This contact is possible through simple barriers like sunglasses (even mirrored) or tinted windows, but does not work when looking at a video feed rather than the vampire herself.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:03:30-07:00","id":942883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942870#post942870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of the Vampire the Masquerade adventures there was a vampire who dominated a guard through a security camera.<br /> <br /> Second edition Requiem is rather clear on the matter, though. 'Dominate requires a vampire make eye contact with her victims in order to issue commands. That contact is one-way \u2014 the victim needs to see the vampire\u2019s eyes, but not vice versa. This contact is possible through simple barriers like sunglasses (even mirrored) or tinted windows, but does not work when looking at a video feed rather than the vampire herself.'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Tell me you have never looked at the persons eyes while they were speaking on TV or watching a commercial or something? especially when they do that light strip over someone's eyes and shadow everything out. That's all you look at...<br /> But that's sort of my point.. If It can work for 1 power. It should work for them all.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: My personal thoughts are that powers don't work through cameras, photo or video footage. Those thoughts could be wrong, but I much rather that the vampires have to be there to use their powers and the person has to be there to physically witness it. Awe and Dread Presence couldn't work over a video feed or skype. I doubt you could talk to Animals over facetime... Dominate cant work that way... why should obfuscate?<br /> <br /> For example: I was just telling my friend about the Pictures and the ghost in Insidious. H<span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">e took pictures of that ghost... he couldnt see the ghost but the camera kept picking it up... and the ghost kept getting closer and closer, but he couldnt see it.</span></span><br /> <br /> and this example; <span style=\"color:#263238\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> The security guy sees you on the camera... he goes to look for that person who was oddly not quite right on the camera. Shadowy, looking away or whatever. but then he cant find you.. he goes back to his office.. and there you are.. standing in the same spot he just looked in.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-03-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:09:01-07:00","id":942890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942883#post942883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell me you have never looked at the persons eyes while they were speaking on TV or watching a commercial or something? especially when they do that light strip over someone's eyes and shadow everything out. That's all you look at...</div> </div> </div> </div>I have. And if that's all you look at, it's because it's the only thing on the tv to look at.<br /> <br /> Can you tell me you've been mind controlled by it? Because I can honestly say I haven't.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate and Dominate are both mind affecting abilities, but but both work differently, just like Majesty and Nightmare. You can make a Devotion that allows you to perform Dominate through video feeds, but the ability doesn't allow it as is.<br /> <br /> Even if you did allow it to work through video feeds, I wouldn't allow it to work through recorded video, which most shows you would see on tv are, without some sort of other Devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:09:18-07:00","id":942891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942822#post942822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally valid point of view. It does pose a question though.. Does Majesty then Work through cameras? The guy in the back security room watching over the bank and one vampire pops Majesty to have everyone look at him and ignore everything else.. while his friends go off and rob the bank? ( granted stupid scenario, but.. yeah )<br /> <br /> Then can you dominate through Cameras and video feed? Or even nightmare?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes to Majesty. Maybe to Nightmare? Might depend on the scenario. No to Dominate because it explicitly states that it has to be direct eye contact and doesn't work through cameras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:22:40-07:00","id":942914,"title":"","content":"I do not let anything, including obfuscate, work through a camera or image without a specific Devotion. <br /> <br /> However, I interpret the Lost Visage to work on all recording / reflecting media. So all Kindred naturally avoid cameras unless they willingly focus their visage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:22:11-07:00","id":943087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=942864#post942864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do not want to put words in your mouth, but Are you saying then that you could Dominate and Majesty through a camera/video feed?<br /> <br /> Because I am thinking a Ventrue with a Dominate on a TV so anyone who walks in and looks into the vampire's eyes through a screen.. Would be pretty beast... Business guy maybe selling something. &quot;Buy this Product&quot;<br /> <br /> A Daeva who Idol's on National TV for something. Oh they would be a god.. Every time someone viewed that clip, a god all over again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also I Don't know if you would Ignore floury footprints, because it literally says (in dot 3) &quot;Leaves incidental signs, like drifting smoke or creaking floor boards&quot; I think that leaving foot prints in the sand, dust or flour would be completely valid. If it fits the tone or not, it's irrelevant if the RAW says it's possible. Somethings dont fit the box/stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The rules specifically state that Dominate does not work through cameras.<br /> For Majesty (and Nightmare I might allow it) depending on the power and situation. I can see Awe working like this, maybe with a slight rule adjustment. Also, any Kindred pulling off a stunt like this will probably face a blood hunt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> thanks for the Werewolf clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T02:24:56-07:00","id":943495,"title":"","content":"I know VtM Presence specified that its powers (apart from Summoning of course) only work on those in the presence of the vampire, but Majesty does not. Majesty has a lot of &quot;in the room&quot; &quot;part of the crowd&quot; etc. wording so it does seem to imply it would not work via camera, but I wouldn't categorically state it wouldn't. However, many Majesty powers require you to specify a target and I don't think &quot;whoever's watching me from that camera over there&quot; is a valid target. The same holds true for Nightmare.<br /> <br /> As for a Strix possessing a werewolf corpse, the book has this to say: &quot;Strix inside supernatural hosts cannot access any powers held in the soul \u2014 they can\u2019t use a mage-host\u2019s powers, a mummy-host immediately dies and becomes a corpse-host, a werewolf-host can\u2019t use Gifts \u2014 but purely physical powers such as a werewolf\u2019s shapechanging may still be accessible at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. Advantages like Mana, Glamour, and Essence don\u2019t convert to Vitae, but living hosts can still be farmed as described under Possess Living.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T03:30:56-07:00","id":943521,"title":"","content":"A vampire can establish eye contact through a camera by focusing it on their eyes so saying they can't use their powers through electronic equipment but allowing majesty and obfuscate to work reeks of clan favoritism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:12:24-07:00","id":943529,"title":"","content":"Dominate is the only power that is directly stated in the rulebook to not work over a video feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:43:52-07:00","id":943540,"title":"","content":"What about a grapple 1 vs. 2-3 or more? Does the successes of the group sum in order to surclass the successes of the single enemy? How can I count tge damages???<br /> Can you clarify me this aspect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T05:20:08-07:00","id":943556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943540#post943540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a grapple 1 vs. 2-3 or more? Does the successes of the group sum in order to surclass the successes of the single enemy? How can I count tge damages???<br /> Can you clarify me this aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suspect this is getting expanded on in Hurt Locker, but in Requiem since everyone tags to the same initiative in a grapple, I let all involved choose if they are attempting to <i>control </i>the grapple, or if they want to <i>support </i>someone else's attempt. The supporters use teamwork rules as normal, rolling first and adding their successes as a bonus to another character's roll. All the non-supporters then make their rolls, and the highest wins.<br /> <br /> It gets a little messy from there, but I let the winning roll choose who on their team (they, or someone who supported them) makes a maneuver using their successes against anyone else in the grapple.<br /> <br /> So - for example - one of your supporters might have a shiv and be doing lethal, so you give them the Damage maneuver. Or - you're in a moshpit trying to rescue someone, so you let your boyfriend take the Break Grapple maneuver and GTFO. You have to think a little creatively when it comes to immobilization (sans cuffs) and going prone, though.<br /> <br /> When someone new attempts to enter the group-grapple, I use the highest defense rating out of everyone in the mass to oppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:30:37-07:00","id":943580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943529#post943529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate is the only power that is directly stated in the rulebook to not work over a video feed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing says any of those powers works directly over a video feed either. And the same claptrap explanation about why Dominate doesn't work over a camera is equally applicable to every other power. Any excuse to the contrary just betrays your obvious clan favoritism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T06:53:27-07:00","id":943586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943580#post943580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing says any of those powers works directly over a video feed either. And the same claptrap explanation about why Dominate doesn't work over a camera is equally applicable to every other power. Any excuse to the contrary just betrays your obvious clan favoritism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really why I don't have any powers work over video or a camera. The Daeva charming someone over the phone. The Nosferatu terrifying someone over FaceTime. Mekhet using Auspex to find out more someone they saw on on something they saw on TV. It doesnt make sense it seems silly. I look at electronic devices as a filter...It dilutes to the power so it's not potent. Also if they work through cameras, they would have to be able to be recorded, ( as there is very little difference between live and recorded ) which I dont feel vampires record well...<br /> <br /> That said... Dominate is the only one that says you can't so... RAW without considering Intent. have at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T07:47:44-07:00","id":943616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943586#post943586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really why I don't have any powers work over video or a camera.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I think that's a perfectly reasonable call to make, and a valid interpretation of the text, even if it's not the way I personally run it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943586#post943586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva charming someone over the phone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't allow that. Charming someone with Confidant or Loyalty requires them to first be affected by Awe, and Awe relies so heavily on visuals that I wouldn't allow it to work over the phone. But, I would allow Awe to work over a camera feed because it affects everyone who sees the Daeva. You look at the vampire and he's too good to be true. You have trouble paying attention to anything else because he's just that gorgeous. You view everything he does in the best possible light because he's too perfect for you to see his flaws. Nothing about that seems to me like it would require the observer's physical presence to notice. That said, the Daeva would have to spend the Willpower to suppress The Lost Visage for this to work, otherwise the people watching on camera won't be able to get a good enough look at him to notice his beauty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943586#post943586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nosferatu terrifying someone over FaceTime.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one I'm iffy on. I would certainly allow the Nos to activate Dread Presence, and for someone seeing her over FaceTime to be affected by the global effect of Dread Presence - her Intimidate pools would be bolstered against them, and they wouldn't be able to spend Willpower to attack her (not they can really attack her from the other side of a FaceTime call anyway). Because they can clearly see that she's fucking scary. I would not allow her to specifically designate them as a target for her illusions, or to create illusions on their side of the screen. But, if she creates an illusion that anyone can see on her side, and it's in full view of the camera, they would be able to see it just fine. Again, this all assumes the Nos is dropping The Loat Visage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943586#post943586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mekhet using Auspex to find out more someone they saw on on something they saw on TV.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another case where I think it depends on what exactly the Mekhet is trying to learn using Auspex. Beast's Hackles only gives the user pertinent information about immediate potential danger, and people on TV can't hurt you. Spirit's Touch gives the user information about the thing they're touching, so you could find out more about the TV, but you can't actually touch the people on the screen. However, Uncanny Perception gives you information about people based on observations of subtle details about them. I could certainly see using Uncanny Perception to find out if an actor is a vampire by watching him on TV, or to figure out an actor's true emotional state at the time of recording.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943586#post943586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesnt make sense it seems silly. I look at electronic devices as a filter...It dilutes to the power so it's not potent. Also if they work through cameras, they would have to be able to be recorded, ( as there is very little difference between live and recorded ) which I dont feel vampires record well...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm cool with the powers I mentioned above working through recordings. But I can also totally see why you wouldn't want to allow that. Personally, the most compelling argument for me is that these powers are all manipulations of the Predatory Aura, and how the heck is the Predatory Aura supposed to travel through a recording? I'll totally buy that that seems silly and doesn't make sense to people. For me though, I see The Lost Visage as an example of the Predatory Aura working through recordings, strange though it may seem. And I look at Rose's way of explaining the Predatory Aura as not a literal halo of vampiric energy, but as purely phenomenal. Vampires recognize each other by the palor of their skin, the hungry look in their eyes, their inhuman stillness, not by psychic impressions. The Lost Visage works by the Beast instinctively knowing just where to stand or just when to move, so that her face is always just out of frame, or obscured by glare, or movement blur, not by magically distorting the recorded image itself. Majesty works by the Beast instinctively knowing just how to move, when to smile, when to be assertive, and when to be winsome, to perfectly capture observers' attention, not by putting magical instigram filters in observers' brains. All those things, in my opinion, would be captured on video, whether live or recorded. But, that's just my take, and I've got no problem with other ST's interpreting it differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943586#post943586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said... Dominate is the only one that says you can't so... RAW without considering Intent. have at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it's a direct application of RAW without considering intent, nor would I say it's indicative of Clan favoritism (Ventrue is my favorite Clan, so...) As I explained above, based on statements from Rose I believe the intent is that aura-based powers work on purely sensual phenomena, and therefore any medium that carries that sensual information carries the power as well. I look at The Lost Visage of evidence of a power working in a way that is consistent with my interpretation. If others find that interpretation silly, that's cool. I wouldn't try to argue if I was playing in one of their games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:01:20-07:00","id":943624,"title":"","content":"I guess a better way to put it would be, if the power affects the vampire or the way she is perceived, those effects can be recorded and perceived by people who view the recording. If the power affects other people that the vampire designates, they have to actually be in the vampire's presence for her to designate and affect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-04-2016, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T08:32:44-07:00","id":943648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943616#post943616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm cool with the powers I mentioned above working through recordings. But I can also totally see why you wouldn't want to allow that. Personally, the most compelling argument for me is that these powers are all manipulations of the Predatory Aura, and how the heck is the Predatory Aura supposed to travel through a recording? I'll totally buy that that seems silly and doesn't make sense to people. For me though, I see The Lost Visage as an example of the Predatory Aura working through recordings, strange though it may seem. And I look at Rose's way of explaining the Predatory Aura as not a literal halo of vampiric energy, but as purely phenomenal. Vampires recognize each other by the palor of their skin, the hungry look in their eyes, their inhuman stillness, not by psychic impressions. The Lost Visage works by the Beast instinctively knowing just where to stand or just when to move, so that her face is always just out of frame, or obscured by glare, or movement blur, not by magically distorting the recorded image itself. Majesty works by the Beast instinctively knowing just how to move, when to smile, when to be assertive, and when to be winsome, to perfectly capture observers' attention, not by putting magical instigram filters in observers' brains. All those things, in my opinion, would be captured on video, whether live or recorded. But, that's just my take, and I've got no problem with other ST's interpreting it differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>While we have agreed to disagree and that's cool. I do see what you mean. I am going to add something little, maybe I am still trying to convince you of my point and I dont know why because we have agreed to see it differently ^.^<br /> <br /> Have you ever been to a concert? I saw Dir en Grey in concert twice and it was amazing. everything was fantastic. The energy in the room and Kyo was incredible.. but watching it later was like.. nothing compared to actually being there. I have watched some of their Japanese performances and it's just not as amazing as actually being there.<br /> <br /> or if there was a ghost in the room I would probably be scared, but seeing a ghost on TV is just.. a ghost on TV. If the Nosferatu was scary on Facetime, I would just hang up. It's just not as scary as they cant hurt me as they arent actually there.<br /> <br /> Or if I saw Johnny Depp on TV it would be cool, but holy hell if I met him in person I would be a puddle.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe distance, the screen it takes away from it. I think the aura is a combination of things, Sight, touch, smell, hearing. When done through something you're limited to the sound the speakers make which might be good or bad and isnt actually the person's voice just an electronic imitation of it and you're limited to the quality of the screen you're being presented on.<br /> <img src=\"http://funnyppl.com/uploads/fufu/1/wtm_fu_55cf3fae99614.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":"08-04-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:01:57-07:00","id":943662,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that definitely puts the &quot;powers don't work through recorded media&quot; perspective in the context of my interpretation of the metaphysics of the Predatory Aura, which I appreciate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T09:05:29-07:00","id":943664,"title":"","content":"You aren't seeing the Daeva on the camera, you're seeing a digitized image created, electronically transmitted, and reproduced on another screen that is a partial visual representation of the Daeva. You have to do a second reproduction transmitted the same way to get an audio copy of what the Daeva says. Unless of course, you have your cameras that work like Wonkavision. But if that's the case then power functionality is equally applicable across the board for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-04-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:30:29-07:00","id":943822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943495#post943495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a Strix possessing a werewolf corpse, the book has this to say: &quot;Strix inside supernatural hosts cannot access any powers held in the soul \u2014 they can\u2019t use a mage-host\u2019s powers, a mummy-host immediately dies and becomes a corpse-host, a werewolf-host can\u2019t use Gifts \u2014 but purely physical powers such as a werewolf\u2019s shapechanging may still be accessible at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. Advantages like Mana, Glamour, and Essence don\u2019t convert to Vitae, but living hosts can still be farmed as described under Possess Living.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for pointing that out, I must have somehow completely missed that when reading through the chapter.<br /> <br /> And thanks everyone for the (mostly) productive and respectful discussion on the use of powers when not in face2face contact. <br /> While I can see both sides of the argument, I would still be in favor of allowing (certain) powers to work like this. Physical proximity will often enhance the effect people have on each other but plenty of people have been scared by someone over the phone, or seduced in an online video chat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:26:12-07:00","id":944045,"title":"","content":"Or commanded by a phone call.<br /> I'm against any of these working over mediums other than raw presence but if one works, then there's no reason any others shouldn't","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T20:00:09-07:00","id":944087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943580#post943580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing says any of those powers works directly over a video feed either. And the same claptrap explanation about why Dominate doesn't work over a camera is equally applicable to every other power. Any excuse to the contrary just betrays your obvious clan favoritism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touch of Shadows explicitly does work over a camera, with an exceptional success it even continues working after the scene the power was used. As all Obfuscate powers operate the same way, I am firmly in the camp that all Obfuscate powers will work over a video feed for the duration the discipline is active.<br /> <br /> And if you must know about my favouritism, Dominate is easily my favourite discipline across the editions. It's got to the point where people just expect my characters to have it regardless of their clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T00:31:44-07:00","id":944177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=944087#post944087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touch of Shadows explicitly does work over a camera, with an exceptional success it even continues working after the scene the power was used. As all Obfuscate powers operate the same way, I am firmly in the camp that all Obfuscate powers will work over a video feed for the duration the discipline is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corollary being that it's far easier to disregard, miss, or plainly not care about what is happening over a screen because it is a screen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:53:20-07:00","id":944412,"title":"","content":"So I have a few questions based on changes between 1e and 2e:<br /> <br /> 1. Do vampires have normal reflections now and do they show up in video/photographs normally? The text seems to imply it but I couldn't find it spelled out anywhere.<br /> <br /> 2. Are fangs retractable or permanent? I remember it being spelled out that they were retractable in 1e, but it no longer specifies in 2e. That and the art seems to imply they are always there. <br /> <br /> 3. Do you still have to spend willpower in order to make changes to your appearance permanent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12028-questerr","name":"Questerr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:57:58-07:00","id":944415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Questerr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=944412#post944412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have a few questions based on changes between 1e and 2e:<br /> <br /> 1. Do vampires have normal reflections now and do they show up in video/photographs normally? The text seems to imply it but I couldn't find it spelled out anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they do not. Check out the Lost Visage. It is more that they are never in the right spot for the camera or whatever to record them perfectly. ( Unless they want them to be )<br /> <br /> &quot;The Beast knows precisely where to stand. A<br /> vampire is not a blurred mess in a photograph, but for some<br /> reason, never seems to look at the camera, or the flash smears<br /> the image, or it goes over- or under-exposed.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Questerr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=944412#post944412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Are fangs retractable or permanent? I remember it being spelled out that they were retractable in 1e, but it no longer specifies in 2e. That and the art seems to imply they are always there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Retractable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Questerr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=944412#post944412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Do you still have to spend willpower in order to make changes to your appearance permanent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. &gt; &gt; Assuming you mean tattoos, Piercings, scars ect..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-05-2016, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T10:58:17-07:00","id":944416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Questerr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=944412#post944412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have a few questions based on changes between 1e and 2e:<br /> <br /> 1. Do vampires have normal reflections now and do they show up in video/photographs normally? The text seems to imply it but I couldn't find it spelled out anywhere.<br /> <br /> 2. Are fangs retractable or permanent? I remember it being spelled out that they were retractable in 1e, but it no longer specifies in 2e. That and the art seems to imply they are always there.<br /> <br /> 3. Do you still have to spend willpower in order to make changes to your appearance permanent?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1.&amp;3. The Lost Visage is more of a boon than a hindrance this time around. Vampires can basically decide to have it affect them or not without expending willpower. I think the same holds for making permanent images.<br /> <br /> 2. I think the fangs are present in the art as a visual clue only. Permanently visible fangs would be pretty terrible for the Masquerade, so I cannot imagine them being a thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T12:59:49-07:00","id":944475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Questerr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=944412#post944412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Do vampires have normal reflections now and do they show up in video/photographs normally? The text seems to imply it but I couldn't find it spelled out anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The way it works now is that they just always happen to be standing in a spot where their face is out-of-frame, or blocked by something else, or they turn just as you're snapping the picture, or there's a problem with the exposure and the glare obscures their face, or what ever other weird coincidence needs to happen to make them not show up in the picture, video, or reflection. So no, their images aren't always distorted or blurred like in 1e, but they don't show up in reflections or recordings for reasons that are less suspicious. They can also choose to appear normally in reflections and recordings with no cost if they want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Questerr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=944412#post944412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Are fangs retractable or permanent? I remember it being spelled out that they were retractable in 1e, but it no longer specifies in 2e. That and the art seems to imply they are always there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Retractable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Questerr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=944412#post944412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Do you still have to spend willpower in order to make changes to your appearance permanent?</div> </div> </div> </div>You only have to spend a point of Willpower to make changes permanent in 2e, not a dot like in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-05-2016, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T13:07:39-07:00","id":944483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=943662#post943662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that definitely puts the &quot;powers don't work through recorded media&quot; perspective in the context of my interpretation of the metaphysics of the Predatory Aura, which I appreciate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like your interpretation but will probably say that going through a device causes a penalty to activation rolls to preserve that feeling that it is just not quite the same as being there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:44:04-07:00","id":944571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=944483#post944483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your interpretation but will probably say that going through a device causes a penalty to activation rolls to preserve that feeling that it is just not quite the same as being there.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good compromise between the two stances, I might do the same next time I run vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T11:56:34-07:00","id":945584,"title":"","content":"Can the 2 dot protean claws do lethal damage to kindred, or is it downgraded to bashing like a mundane weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T12:21:08-07:00","id":945591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=945584#post945584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the 2 dot protean claws do lethal damage to kindred, or is it downgraded to bashing like a mundane weapon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Downgraded to bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:11:22-07:00","id":947442,"title":"","content":"What about vampires and disease? It makes sense that they are immune to most things, but what about when using Blush of Life? Example, rabies. What if a kindred under the effects of Blush of Life is bitten by an infected animal? Would the vampire become infected as it courses through their bloodstream?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:27:57-07:00","id":947451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=947442#post947442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about vampires and disease? It makes sense that they are immune to most things, but what about when using Blush of Life? Example, rabies. What if a kindred under the effects of Blush of Life is bitten by an infected animal? Would the vampire become infected as it courses through their bloodstream?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blush of Life only works for the scene. Even if the disease did survive contact, rabies has an incubation period lasting weeks and would die out well before any symptoms could appear.<br /> <br /> But Blush of Life isn't actually turning alive, it's just faking it. Your downgrading of Lethal to Bashing damage doesn't turn off when it's active, it doesn't seem like most diseases would bother you either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-09-2016, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:36:09-07:00","id":947455,"title":"","content":"Alright, I can accept that. But what about Dragon's who have the coil that makes Blush of Life last the entire night? What if they didn't know the creature was infected and continues to use Blush of Life daily. For simplicity, let's say zombie virus. Most lore says that people who are bitten turn within either minutes or hours. Curious if anyone has ever played with the idea of diseased kindred (other than the Morbus).<br /> <br /> Edit: Kindred feel effects from drinking from intoxicated mortals. What about diseased?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":". 08-09-2016, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:50:52-07:00","id":947461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=947455#post947455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I can accept that. But what about Dragon's who have the coil that makes Blush of Life last the entire night? What if they didn't know the creature was infected and continues to use Blush of Life daily. For simplicity, let's say zombie virus. Most lore says that people who are bitten turn within either minutes or hours. Curious if anyone has ever played with the idea of diseased kindred (other than the Morbus).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in some cases they can be carriers, but the vampire isn't just a corpse, just like one with Blush of Life isn't a living human. You would need more than the standard coils, I think, to be susceptible to a mundane disease.<br /> <br /> However, it's the World of Darkness and when you talk about things like zombie viruses, you're talking about the supernatural. And when you get into supernatural, normal resistances can fade. There are strange diseases that can affect the dead, and vampires. I believe Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead has a disease borne by vampires, and possibly Mythologies. The Malkavian curse is an affliction that spreads <i>like </i>a disease, something similar could easily be behind a zombie virus. I had a disease that could affect vampires in one of my games, it was particularly lethal but mostly because the vampires never really thought it was a disease, instead believing it to be some sort of assassin or supernatural curse. It was created by a hunter assisted by a werewolf in a previous one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-09-2016, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T09:09:12-07:00","id":948640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=947455#post947455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: Kindred feel effects from drinking from intoxicated mortals. What about diseased?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 215<br /> &quot;Vampires do not tire, do not age, do not falter to disease or poison, hunting the night where none but the greatest of predators tread.&quot;<br /> <br /> They are immune to disease and poison, but if there is a type of disease or poison that affects them for some reason... Then they should be able to spend a vitae to burn the disease/poison out of their system. ( unless it is supernatural and has other requirements.. like NoFather said, that's a different ballgame ) <br /> <br /> I am in the camp where vampires are not carriers either. If they carried say. HIV and gave it to people they bit... then it would spread like wildfire. If a Daeva got it and fed on a different person each night. Suddenly 365 + (whoever they share it with ) have HIV in this one town... People would start looking, It might break the masquerade and it doesn't make sense to me. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T09:34:11-07:00","id":948646,"title":"","content":"I imagine we'll get more details on how diseases interact with vampire biology in Dark Eras Companion, with the Black Plague era coming out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T19:20:34-07:00","id":949019,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't really have blood, the only way I could see them acting as carriers for blood-borne diseases is if they have terrible hygiene, biting someone with HIV then going on to bite someone else with blood still in/around their mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T05:12:06-07:00","id":949246,"title":"","content":"That wouldnt work the HIV would die on their teeth. You basically need the fluid transfer to happen inside the body (bloody finger in mouth, intercourse) or like bloody wound to wound.<br /> <br /> Hep C could be transfered that way, but only if you bit a bunch of people in the same night.<br /> <br /> Without sneezing or relieving oneself, most vamps are going to be remarkably safe. Spreading germs via contact or sexual contact would be the big way. Smearing ornfeeding vitae could spread germs. Biting could spread some germs if they go from saliva to blood and they lick the wound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-12-2016, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:53:20-07:00","id":950143,"title":"","content":"Also, diseases that reproduce inside living cells don't usually do too well in dead cells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T12:32:23-07:00","id":950177,"title":"","content":"Vitae can preserve life when it would otherwise die out. Trying to throw biology into this supernatural mix is hardly productive.<br /> <br /> Even if you insist on using science? Bacteria can form cists that protect them in harsh conditions, and viruses can go dormant until they attach to living cells while suspended in the vitae-blood mixture within the vampire's body. That blood may be sluggish, but its still enough of an environment for both to survive in until better conditions result.<br /> <br /> Vampires use saliva to cover up the feedings, so there is absolutely transfer of bodily fluids.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, however. Plague Angel. We have cannon NPCs that are based around being disease carriers. While its possible that its no longer viable in 2e, there are examples of non-Morbus vampires becoming disease vectors in 1e's lore.<br /> <br /> So, yeah.<br /> <br /> My personal belief is that vampires can become carriers, but the diesease get wiped out by the day-sleep reset every sunset. If you somehow internalize the disease by accident (or on purpose), then it will stay with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:54:28-07:00","id":950232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950177#post950177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires use saliva to cover up the feedings, so there is absolutely transfer of bodily fluids.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with you that vampires are possible disease vectors on the initial night of exposure if it's possible at all, there is absolutely no reference to vampires having the ability to lick puncture wounds closed in second edition. But if you are transporting that detail over from first edition, the saliva would be used as a healing salve to instantly close puncture wounds. It kind of defeats the Masquerade preserving purpose to lick a puncture wound closed if it's still likely to become a festering leprosy scab or weeping abcess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:57:56-07:00","id":950235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950232#post950232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with you that vampires are possible disease vectors on the initial night of exposure if it's possible at all, there is absolutely no reference to vampires having the ability to lick puncture wounds closed in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood &amp; Smoke, p95 'With a subtle bite, the vampire can take one Vitae per turn, and may lick the wound afterwards, leaving no trace of her feeding.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T16:14:25-07:00","id":950290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950177#post950177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae can preserve life when it would otherwise die out. Trying to throw biology into this supernatural mix is hardly productive.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about ghouling microbial life, then vampires become MUCH bigger disease vectors than even you are suggesting here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:06:52-07:00","id":950319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950232#post950232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with you that vampires are possible disease vectors on the initial night of exposure if it's possible at all, there is absolutely no reference to vampires having the ability to lick puncture wounds closed in second edition. But if you are transporting that detail over from first edition, the saliva would be used as a healing salve to instantly close puncture wounds. It kind of defeats the Masquerade preserving purpose to lick a puncture wound closed if it's still likely to become a festering leprosy scab or weeping abcess.</div> </div> </div> </div> Irregardless if the licking actually happens in 2e, there's still going to be exchange of saliva from the fangs puncturing skin and entering the blood. Because vampire's mouths aren't dry. They breath, they spit, etc. So, that's a moot point. As for the festering scab bit? The healing completely seals the skin to new - there's no scab or abcess to fester. Anything that you come up as an argument for how it can't work, there's another for how it can. Its circular logic - trying to science the argument either way is only something you can believe if you buy into the entire premise at once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950290#post950290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're talking about ghouling microbial life, then vampires become MUCH bigger disease vectors than even you are suggesting here.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe? Maybe not? The point is that we have no idea of how this works, and you can't say that vampires can or cannot become disease vectors because of some science. All we can do is point to NPCs and story hooks and themes. Vampires deny all other kinds of logic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T22:10:16-07:00","id":950438,"title":"","content":"&quot;With a subtle bite, the vampire can take one Vitae per turn, and may lick the wound afterwards, leaving no trace of her feeding&quot;<br /> page 95<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I've always found the idea of vampires transferring any disease they come into contact with rather silly and clearly not thought out, statistically speaking (Barring certain named bloodlines). So, if 2e doesn't blatantly say they're carriers in all situations (I don't believe it does), I'd say they don't. But that's just me, lacking an official answer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:21:12-07:00","id":950623,"title":"","content":"It would be a fantastic plot hook though. For as long as anyone has known there hasn't been an issue with feeding, but in the last couple months any mortal that has been fed from has become terrible ill. They either end up in the hospital for a while, or end up succumbing to the disease. What are the kindred to do if they can't safely feed? Question is, do the victims stay dead afterwards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:35:12-07:00","id":950629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950623#post950623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be a fantastic plot hook though. For as long as anyone has known there hasn't been an issue with feeding, but in the last couple months any mortal that has been fed from has become terrible ill. They either end up in the hospital for a while, or end up succumbing to the disease. What are the kindred to do if they can't safely feed? Question is, do the victims stay dead afterwards?</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree with that. I've always been a proponent of &quot;It works X way unless a plot hook says otherwise&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:55:37-07:00","id":950730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950629#post950629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely agree with that. I've always been a proponent of &quot;It works X way unless a plot hook says otherwise&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This brings a question to mind. Story tellers.. How do you deal with players who call your bullshit on things like that? You have a great plot hook. We will just roll with the example with the disease and mortals getting sick and then your players say something like, &quot;you cant do that pg 215 says they are immune to disease&quot; And thus get upset? <br /> Or whatever else plot hook that you use that's a tish out of the box?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:11:52-07:00","id":950739,"title":"","content":"For me that depends on the reason behind the 'calling out on bullshit'. I play only with friends so usually we work together so that everything make sense for everyone. But sometimes, it happens when a player is either bored or not interested in the storyline (when everybody have fun, people care less about minor nonsense).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:13:53-07:00","id":950742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950730#post950730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This brings a question to mind. Story tellers.. How do you deal with players who call your bullshit on things like that? You have a great plot hook. We will just roll with the example with the disease and mortals getting sick and then your players say something like, &quot;you cant do that pg 215 says they are immune to disease&quot; And thus get upset? <br /> Or whatever else plot hook that you use that's a tish out of the box?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Yes, and as far as your character knows, this shouldn't be possible. And yet, it's happening. Don't you want to figure out how?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-14-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:16:57-07:00","id":950743,"title":"","content":"1. I make sure there's a reason that things are working differently for the plot hook.<br /> 2. I don't make the rules work differently for PCs without their direct involvement, as a general rule. PCs aren't the ones transferring disease with a bit, some NPC is. People are more upset if they're the one it's going wrong for without obvious cause.<br /> 3. ST has final say. Period. Especially mid-session. I'm very open to feedback between sessions, but one too many PCs who liked to debate the finer points of the setting for literal hours on end and I just had to make it the rule. If a player can't handle this rule, then they aren't a good fit for the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:58:25-07:00","id":950762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950730#post950730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> This brings a question to mind. Story tellers.. How do you deal with players who call your bullshit on things like that? You have a great plot hook. We will just roll with the example with the disease and mortals getting sick and then your players say something like, &quot;you cant do that pg 215 says they are immune to disease&quot; And thus get upset?<br /> Or whatever else plot hook that you use that's a tish out of the box?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any players Ive had will accept &quot;That's normally true, and your character knows that to be the case, even, but it still happened&quot; or something along those lines. Basically make it clear you know the normal rule but it's still happening and they'll usually pick up on the fact that it's a plot hook of some kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:21:13-07:00","id":950809,"title":"","content":"Confrim/Deny: When a Kindred loses (not just detaches from) their last Touchstone, gaining the Languid Condition, then falling into Torpor - once they emerge from Torpor after the appropriate time, the only ongoing mechanical effects will be the (-2: No Touchstones) penalty to Detachment. Assuming the PC is willing to eat that penalty, and I adjust dramatic conflicts to come in from other vectors, there's no other mechanical effects from being active with zero Touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:22:54-07:00","id":950810,"title":"","content":"That's how I read it, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T17:36:11-07:00","id":950816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950762#post950762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any players Ive had will accept &quot;That's normally true, and your character knows that to be the case, even, but it still happened&quot; or something along those lines. Basically make it clear you know the normal rule but it's still happening and they'll usually pick up on the fact that it's a plot hook of some kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think when something weird happens like that, providing it's an individual example like a special vampire and not a rule that changes across the board, like all vampires being infested with disease, the storyteller should at least let them know it's a stand-out situation. 'None of your coterie has ever heard of such a thing,' in the face of evidence of that thing lets them know it's not just the storyteller fumbling. The player characters aren't in a white room, they have access to sources of information, even if they don't have the book.<br /> <br /> It should be prompted by the players, though, and not just come out of nowhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-14-2016, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:21:19-07:00","id":950859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=950809#post950809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Confrim/Deny: When a Kindred loses (not just detaches from) their last Touchstone, gaining the Languid Condition, then falling into Torpor - once they emerge from Torpor after the appropriate time, the only ongoing mechanical effects will be the (-2: No Touchstones) penalty to <br /> Detachment. Assuming the PC is willing to eat that penalty, and I adjust dramatic conflicts to come in from other vectors, there's no other mechanical effects from being active with zero Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I have always read it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for the advice on plot hooks. Really appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T22:01:59-07:00","id":952304,"title":"","content":"The K9 fighting style merit. What happens if you have more than one dog? For example, the 3rd dot gives a +2 to attack for one and a +1 to defence for the other (from the subject of the maneuver). What happens if you have 3 dogs? Would that just be two sets of each bonus to be split between all involved? If so, then what happens when you have an uneven amount of participants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:48:34-07:00","id":952479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=952304#post952304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The K9 fighting style merit. What happens if you have more than one dog? For example, the 3rd dot gives a +2 to attack for one and a +1 to defence for the other (from the subject of the maneuver). What happens if you have 3 dogs? Would that just be two sets of each bonus to be split between all involved? If so, then what happens when you have an uneven amount of participants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a Hurt Locker preview Merit you're talking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:25:48-07:00","id":952871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=952479#post952479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this a Hurt Locker preview Merit you're talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, yes, I'm pretty sure it is. Someone linked to it in a different thread (along with others like various archery combat styles, falconry, and many more).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T17:52:45-07:00","id":952885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=952871#post952871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, yes, I'm pretty sure it is. Someone linked to it in a different thread (along with others like various archery combat styles, falconry, and many more).</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. <br /> Keep in mind, this is from a draft, so things may change between now and release. But, I would rule that the human gains either +1 defense or +2 to attack rolls (against the targeted opponent) and all of the dogs get the other bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T01:15:47-07:00","id":955471,"title":"","content":"Question: In 2nd edition Vampire: the Requiem, does a Kindred automatically detect it if someone else is Kindred too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7279-ichneumon","name":"Ichneumon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7279_6.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T02:28:07-07:00","id":955484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ichneumon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=955471#post955471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: In 2nd edition Vampire: the Requiem, does a Kindred automatically detect it if someone else is Kindred too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, she can perceive a set of clues like no breath, no heartbeat etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T03:45:13-07:00","id":955505,"title":"","content":"I run it the other way around: after sensing another Predatory Aura, other cues (breath, heartbeat) just pop out as obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T04:46:10-07:00","id":955521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ichneumon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=955471#post955471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: In 2nd edition Vampire: the Requiem, does a Kindred automatically detect it if someone else is Kindred too?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Without a Discipline or other ability to mask or suppress the predatory aura, Kindred perceive other vampires as their own kind. If they can smell the vampire, they know it\u2019s a vampire. If they touch a vampire, they know it\u2019s a vampire. Note that this is one-sided: One character may not notice the other. It\u2019s not just the aura, it\u2019s all the right cues. Kindred notice the shallow or nonexistent breathing of their kind. They notice the subtle, predatory tones in a voice. They smell multiple victims\u2019 blood on another.&quot; - Page 92","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T18:37:19-07:00","id":957977,"title":"","content":"Are there any official rulings on how Ride the Wave style and coil of the wyrm interact?<br /> <br /> Specifically RtW 3 and 4<br /> And Wyrm 3?<br /> <br /> Wyrm 3 seems to almost make RtW 3 and 4 really useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:25:22-07:00","id":958025,"title":"","content":"It does indeed make Ride the Wave 3 and 4 pretty useless, don't buy them, go 2 dots of Ride the Wave then buy more Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T21:31:58-07:00","id":958046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=957977#post957977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any official rulings on how Ride the Wave style and coil of the wyrm interact?<br /> <br /> Specifically RtW 3 and 4<br /> And Wyrm 3?<br /> <br /> Wyrm 3 seems to almost make RtW 3 and 4 really useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Recap:<br /> There is a 7 page <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave\">thread</a> about people arguing about this very thing. <br /> <br /> This is my take, and please dont start another giant fight, but I personally think that The coil allows you to do it voluntarily and the ride you have to be provoked first.<br /> <br /> But some people think that Ride is any time you want to, so it does mostly the same thing. <br /> <br /> We have asked for developer( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a>) help on this to clarify.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T21:45:31-07:00","id":958050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=958046#post958046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recap:<br /> There is a 7 page <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave\">thread</a> about people arguing about this very thing.<br /> <br /> This is my take, and please dont start another giant fight, but I personally think that The coil allows you to do it voluntarily and the ride you have to be provoked first.<br /> <br /> But some people think that Ride is any time you want to, so it does mostly the same thing.<br /> <br /> We have asked for developer( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a>) help on this to clarify.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the same thing at first, Vitalis, but they're asking about another ability. The Coil allows you to Ride without spending Willpower, while the Ride the Wave Fighting Style offers a Willpower refund or bonus to Willpower spent while Riding the Wave, which is pointless when you're not spending Willpower on it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T04:54:36-07:00","id":958146,"title":"","content":"It's not pointless. It's an option to make a character with Ride the Wave as an effective tactic who is NOT A DRAGON a viable concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T07:36:20-07:00","id":958223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=958046#post958046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Recap:<br /> There is a 7 page <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/939230-ride-the-wave&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">thread</a> about people arguing about this very thing. <br /> <br /> This is my take, and please dont start another giant fight, but I personally think that The coil allows you to do it voluntarily and the ride you have to be provoked first.<br /> <br /> But some people think that Ride is any time you want to, so it does mostly the same thing. <br /> <br /> We have asked for developer( <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>) help on this to clarify.</div> </div> </div> </div>That argument is about something completely different than what overload asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T08:29:10-07:00","id":958241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=958050#post958050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the same thing at first, Vitalis, but they're asking about another ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> skimmed too quickly. My apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T19:50:36-07:00","id":958570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=958146#post958146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not pointless. It's an option to make a character with Ride the Wave as an effective tactic who is NOT A DRAGON a viable concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, each dot is also a third or quarter the price of each Coil of the Wyrm dot. In fact having thought about it even if I was playing a Dragon and wanted to weaponise my frenzies, if Wyrm wasn't my primary mystery I'd go for 5 dots of the Ride the Wave style for 5 XP rather than a dot of Wyrm for 4 xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","user":"PrinceRaven","date":". 08-27-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:28:54-07:00","id":959103,"title":"","content":"I noticed the animal stats list had no aquatic animals. Why no love for sharks lol.<br /> <br /> Anybody stated up sharks, dolphins, kraken, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T06:02:11-07:00","id":964250,"title":"","content":"Curious question - can Telepathy be used to inflict Conditions other than Guilty, Inspired, or Shaken? I always just used those three, but I have a player that wants to use it to inflict the Swooning Condition. The power does say &quot;like&quot; the three listed Conditions, but what does that mean? What's &quot;like?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:39:02-07:00","id":964382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=964250#post964250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious question - can Telepathy be used to inflict Conditions other than Guilty, Inspired, or Shaken? I always just used those three, but I have a player that wants to use it to inflict the Swooning Condition. The power does say &quot;like&quot; the three listed Conditions, but what does that mean? What's &quot;like?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading is it means conditions of equivalent 'potency' and memory connection, things that represent momentary emotional shifts. Swooning's likely fine, if they have an appropriate memory, but you're certainly not going to make someone Delusional with their own memory, as an example. Well, maybe if they also have False Memories...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:04:57-07:00","id":964403,"title":"","content":"Well, I was thinking of one's that could result from breaking points or exceptional successes/dramatic failureso on mundane skill","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T17:07:00-07:00","id":964641,"title":"","content":"Obsessed seems like a condition that could easily arise from bringing up the right memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T00:06:26-07:00","id":966658,"title":"","content":"Do ghouls have the ability to ID vampires or vampires ID ghouls? I mean like vampires always know that someone else is a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T01:17:29-07:00","id":966673,"title":"","content":"Not by RAW, no. Though maybe you could smell Vitae on them if they'd fed relatively recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T04:13:01-07:00","id":966697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=966658#post966658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do ghouls have the ability to ID vampires or vampires ID ghouls? I mean like vampires always know that someone else is a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sort of? Ghoul families apprently qualify for the Unseen Sense merit, as per the ghoul Apendix, page 296. <br /> <br /> &quot;Like so many secrets about the Kindred condition, vampires are conflicted on exactly what a ghoul family is, how they come to be, and what keeps them going. <br /> <br /> There are some things that are largely agreed upon. They age more slowly even without the benefit of Vitae. Normally, ghouls have great difficulty having children; this seems to be less extreme in the case of ghoul family members. Similarly, they tend to be very good at \u201cfinding\u201d Kindred. (See the Unseen Sense Merit on page 124.)&quot;<br /> <br /> I would argue that such a merit can be purchased by any ghoul to represent the sensitivity to vampires that is developed over time. Meanwhile, on the reverse side, its entirely possible that vampires can sense ghouls through the Predator's Aura. We know that becoming a ghoul does alter a person's aura in some way. It has to in order to allow one to use Majesty, Nightmare, Dominate and Obfuscate. It changed in 1e, and carried around a stunted Beast inside their body. And Predator's Aura is sensitive to mroe than <br /> <br /> The simple fact of the matter is that this issue isn't really covered in any detail in the Appendix and, as I'm fond of saying, absense of evidence is different from evidence of absense. Last time, a lot of the details behind ghouls were left for the 1e ghoul book. There's a 2e ghoul book coming out soon, and I'm sure that will have all the answers you want. But, right now, its primarily an ST call on how they want to handle this. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T07:05:49-07:00","id":966739,"title":"","content":"Thanks both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:30:45-07:00","id":971357,"title":"","content":"Ok, I just had a thought about something I was wondering before, but never really bothered to think about hard because I never had to depict it/had players do it : What happens exactly when you fall into voluntary torpor ? Not in general, in the exact moment you do it. How do you do it and do you have to follow certain steps ? What does it look like ?<br /> <br /> The first big question is obviously, do you need to wait until the morning comes or can you just fall into torpor whenever you feel like it ? Can you (theoretically) just decide to go to sleep like you flip a switch in the middle of a conversation, fall face first on the ground and wake up ten years later ? Do you need to lie down or something, does it take a while to concentrate about it ?<br /> <br /> I mean, it's a technicality, but the book says nothing about it (and neither does E1 as far as I remember), so the natural guess would be that you can just drop asleep if you want to like C3PO, but, I mean, it's kinda comical in a way.<br /> <br /> Simple question, but I guess the answer might not be, unless a E1 supplement touched upon it and I haven't read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:50:58-07:00","id":971402,"title":"","content":"I think it would just be like going to sleep. Some people need to lay down in a particular position to fall asleep, others can sleep while sitting or even standing as long as their weight is supported. Some people need it to be dark, others need a bit of light. Some people can only fall asleep at certain times, others can do it when ever they want. I imagine vampires aren't much different. I see voluntary Torpor more as a case of deciding <i>not to get up</i> than deciding when to go down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:29:46-07:00","id":971422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=971357#post971357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I just had a thought about something I was wondering before, but never really bothered to think about hard because I never had to depict it/had players do it : What happens exactly when you fall into voluntary torpor ? Not in general, in the exact moment you do it. How do you do it and do you have to follow certain steps ? What does it look like ?</div> </div> </div> </div> In 1e, it was a conscious decision to not wake from your daysleep. You have complete control over your vitae, and that includes choosing to spend the vitae to wake up.<br /> <br /> Waking up as a vampire is like a heart attack in reverse. So, the vampire... simply chooses to not wake. To stay asleep. Its that half moment when you feel groggy and you don't want to get up, so you just turn over and fall back asleep, choosing to not spend the vitae to get your body moving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first big question is obviously, do you need to wait until the morning comes or can you just fall into torpor whenever you feel like it ? </div> </div> </div> In 1e, it was the former. Well, actually dusk, but similar idea. In 2e, I haven't seen anything to contradict that, so I'm going with it. Granted, I don't see any reason you can't fall into daysleep earlier either. I wouldn't allow it in mid-sentence, but chosing to curl up and drift off in the middle of the night is little different than trying to take a mid-day nap in my mind, so I'm for it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> unless a E1 supplement touched upon it and I haven't read it. </div> </div> </div> The Blood: Player's Guide to the Requiem. Granted, that was before the game switched gears, prior to Requiem for Rome, so the validity of that book in 2e is highly questionable. Still, its something I think makes sense, so I keep using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:46:36-07:00","id":971576,"title":"","content":"Do Kindred recover Willpower from sleeping like mortals do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:47:29-07:00","id":971577,"title":"","content":"Not in 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T04:14:47-07:00","id":986669,"title":"","content":"A very fast one. Dominate states <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Beast demands obedience from lesser creatures. It slips into the Kindred\u2019s voice, modulating his tone and his words to express absolute authority. It progresses from the simple barked commands of a drill sergeant to creating false memories of whatever the vampire desires \u2014 or letting her steal her victim\u2019s body to walk in the sunlight once again.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> the &quot;eye contact&quot; blurb states<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Eye Contact Dominate requires a vampire make eye contact with her victims in order to issue commands. That contact is one-way \u2014 the victim needs to see the vampire\u2019s eyes, but not vice versa. This contact is possible through simple barriers like sunglasses (even mirrored) or tinted windows, but does not work when looking at a video feed rather than the vampire herself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> The question is . Can a blind person get dominated? <br /> <br /> The logical thing would be a no but it is a discipline so although the Blind tilt is very punishing it feels somewhat ... unfair <br /> <br /> opinions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:23:15-07:00","id":986715,"title":"","content":"There's at least one devotion that works around the eye contact restriction that would let you Dominate a blind person but otherwise yes a blind person is practically immune to Dominate as they cannot see a vampire's eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:26:20-07:00","id":986716,"title":"","content":"Not unless they have a devotion or established method like a telepathic or empathic link which let's them use Dominate without needing eye contact. There's nothing unfair about it. Just chalk it up as one of those scenarios where tossing around superpowers isn't a solution to your problem. It's not like you can't take a ball peen hammer to the back of their head until they're unconscious so their recollection of whatever you want to make them forget, if it exists, is going to be spotty at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T02:33:47-07:00","id":987683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=986715#post986715\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=986715#post986715\"> Ask a simple question, get a simple answer: Vampire - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=986715#post986715\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=986715#post986715 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I can't believe no one's created one of these for Vampire yet, of all games. Well, I know I'm constantly flooded with simple questions, so let's do this! I'm creating this thread with the assumption that questions will be about VtR2e unless otherwise noted. 1)The Strix's Breath Drinking ability says that soulless victims create no Vitae - is that in general, or just related to the Breath Drinking? 2) Just to fully clarify, if a character wants to Lash Out to break an effect like Awe or Dread Presence , how exactly does it work? Do you need to pick a Kindred target that you think is doing it and run </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I looked through the devotions and the most close i found is the Summoning one. Maybe first edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T06:31:52-07:00","id":987720,"title":"","content":"In the Carthian book, if memory serves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:56:58-07:00","id":988176,"title":"","content":"In 2nd ed. there's Touch of Deprivation which requires touching rather than eye contact but it's less mind control more sensory deprivation.<br /> <br /> In 1st ed. there's Whispers in the Dark, The Command Bottle and Shout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T12:39:48-07:00","id":988340,"title":"","content":"In 2e, Conditioning can eventually inflict the Enslaved Condition, which allows you to give the subject commands without eye contact and without having to inflict Mesmerized first. But, it's a long, involved process that requires Mezmerizing the victim over and over again, so it doesn't really work on someone you can't already establish eye contact with.<br /> <br /> Of course, the Baddacelli were a 1e Bloodline of blind Nosferatu, and their writeup included a sidebar about how them being blind interacted with Dominate. In effect, simply looking into their eyes or the place where their eyes should be worked, albeit with a -2 penalty. So, that's a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T12:48:25-07:00","id":988346,"title":"","content":"I don't have any COD books yet,(planning to get them this Christmas.), would a campaign ranging almost 600 years be possible? (1760-2350+)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T13:18:28-07:00","id":988356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=988346#post988346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any COD books yet,(planning to get them this Christmas.), would a campaign ranging almost 600 years be possible? (1760-2350+)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes sure, why not? &quot;Fall of the camarilla&quot; crhonicle last centuries <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:06:36-07:00","id":988383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=988346#post988346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any COD books yet,(planning to get them this Christmas.), would a campaign ranging almost 600 years be possible? (1760-2350+)</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. These kinds of history-spanning games are some of the most fun, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:28:35-07:00","id":988499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=988346#post988346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any COD books yet,(planning to get them this Christmas.), would a campaign ranging almost 600 years be possible? (1760-2350+)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. And as a matter of fact, OPP is working on a book right now that offers more tools for games about elder vampires.<br /> <br /> The game includes rules for torpor, which more or less necessitate vampires creeping into their coffins and sleeping for a few decades everyone once in a while. That creates a good device for pushing the timeline along. And <i>Damnation City</i> includes new systems that accommodate high level political play. It's designed for the modern nights, but it could be adapted pretty easily to accommodate a game a few hundred years in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:43:05-07:00","id":988508,"title":"","content":"That probably won't be out before Christmas, mind. It's been in production for a very, very long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:47:23-07:00","id":988662,"title":"","content":"Does Touch of the Morrigan (Cr\u00faac spell) adds to an attack made with your bare hands (like Protean's Claws) or is it, somehow, intrinsically tied to a 'touch' rather than a bare-handed attack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T23:54:59-07:00","id":988718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=988662#post988662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Touch of the Morrigan (Cr\u00faac spell) adds to an attack made with your bare hands (like Protean's Claws) or is it, somehow, intrinsically tied to a 'touch' rather than a bare-handed attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure you could do it either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T12:49:50-07:00","id":991493,"title":"","content":"Do vampire Organs still work. I wanted to know because I have a character who wants to use brain surgery to make a vampire talk by stimulating different parts of the brain.<br /> <br /> Also I wanted to create a vampire NPC that would have their brain replaced with a few pounds of C4 and In the location were their liver was. <br /> <br /> So I wanted to know are these things possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:14:19-07:00","id":991498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991493#post991493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do vampire Organs still work. I wanted to know because I have a character who wants to use brain surgery to make a vampire talk by stimulating different parts of the brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>They work more or less normally while the Blush of Life is active, but otherwise are dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991493#post991493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I wanted to create a vampire NPC that would have their brain replaced with a few pounds of C4 and In the location were their liver was.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would really only work if the vampire was cooperating. Otherwise they could just spend Vitae to repair the damage to their body. Also the daysleep returns the body to its state at the time of death, so it wouldn't last more than about 16 hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:19:49-07:00","id":991501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991498#post991498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They work more or less normally while the Blush of Life is active, but otherwise are dead.<br /> <br /> <br /> That would really only work if the vampire was cooperating. Otherwise they could just spend Vitae to repair the damage to their body. Also the daysleep returns the body to its state at the time of death, so it wouldn't last more than about 16 hours.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So you would have to dominate a kindred into wanting this hmmm ok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:42:54-07:00","id":991510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991501#post991501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So you would have to dominate a kindred into wanting this hmmm ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no. The first damage taken from the surgery would wake up her from the mesmerize","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:30:06-07:00","id":991557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991501#post991501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So you would have to dominate a kindred into wanting this hmmm ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not going to be able to dominate someone into wanting to destroy themself without a homebrewed devotion, You could kidnap them and forcibly insert C4 into them, then erase their memories of the procedure. But as Charlaquin pointed out, unless it's used by the next sunset, their body is simply going to expel or dissolve otherwise harmlessly eradicate the foreign substance from their body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T15:53:57-07:00","id":991567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991510#post991510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, no. The first damage taken from the surgery would wake up her from the mesmerize</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You make them want it after the surgery is done. So they will spend a willpower to keep it. Then its a part of them or you could find a dead person put the c4 in then bring them back as a kindred or at least try","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:38:54-07:00","id":991592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991567#post991567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You make them want it after the surgery is done. So they will spend a willpower to keep it. Then its a part of them or you could find a dead person put the c4 in then bring them back as a kindred or at least try</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the kindred would use willpower to keep the change cause dominate ends at the sunrise, the time in which the vampire would go to sleep and use willpower.... I'd rule for no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:48:37-07:00","id":991600,"title":"","content":"There is the devotion Conditioning (Dominate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) that allows the vampire to apply the Subservient condition followed by the Enslaved condition. Someone who has the Enslaved condition counts as always having Mesmerized for the purposes of Dominate, but no amount of damage resolves the condition and it doesn't fade with time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991557#post991557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are not going to be able to dominate someone into wanting to destroy themself without a homebrewed devotion[..]</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2E I find nothing about suicide being beyond the powers Dominate. Even Mesmerize should be able to do it since the condition only resolves after the action has been performed.<br /> My group has house ruled that it requires more advanced supernatural powers (I think Conditioning might be enough) to mind control someone into trying to destroy themselves. Pure Dominate would instantly fail before the action was even attempted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:13:35-07:00","id":991611,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you can heal a wound if there's a foreign object in the way, like a stake or, in this case, a brainsworth of explosives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:33:52-07:00","id":991618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991611#post991611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure you can heal a wound if there's a foreign object in the way, like a stake or, in this case, a brainsworth of explosives.</div> </div> </div> </div>The wooden stake is a mystical effect. Nothing else will force the vampire into torpor the same way. The Cleansing will remove ink from tattoos and piercings. Granted, that's fairly trivial compared to an object replacing an organ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:03:27-07:00","id":991631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991611#post991611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure you can heal a wound if there's a foreign object in the way, like a stake or, in this case, a brainsworth of explosives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, a live body can reject foreign objects, and vampires are much more effective at healing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:05:51-07:00","id":991675,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; You make them want it after the surgery is done. So they will spend a willpower to keep it. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Under the current rules as written, it's not possible to control the thoughts or feelings of a Dominated victim. I'm not even sure it's possible to directly order someone to spend willpower in that manner since is an out-of-character mechanic.<br /> <br /> &quot;When changing memories or creating new ones, the vampire can create the factual content of the memory, but the victim\u2019s thoughts and feelings remain out of her control. She can create an environment that makes him predisposed to certain reactions, but she can\u2019t force him to love a son she\u2019s just invented.&quot; (Blood and Smoke p. 132)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991600#post991600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2E I find nothing about suicide being beyond the powers Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said suicide is beyond the purview of Dominate. It's most certainly possible to get someone to commit suicide using Dominate. If the command is disguised as something innocuous or irreversible and the act does enough aggravated damage in a single turn. It might even be possible with Possession or Conditioning (I wouldn't try it with the latter though because of the inherent ability for its victims to randomly ignore commands.) But 1. It's kind of hard to issue elaborate instructions when you are limited to four word sentences. 2. It's also difficult to do enough aggravated damage to a vampire in a single turn to kill them outright since they only take bashing damage from the vast majority of conventional weapons.<br /> <br /> What I said is that nothing in the entire description of Dominate is going to make a victim <u>want</u> to destroy themself without a devotion. Such manipulation of a person's feelings, memories, and self-preservation instinct is utterly beyond Dominate's ability even at level 5. The book says as much.<br /> <br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; Even Mesmerize should be able to do it since the condition only resolves after the action has been performed. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Nope. Mesmerize is resolved if the victim takes a single point of Bashing or Lethal damage or if they suffer a breaking point fulfilling the vampire's command. It also wears off naturally after a scene. You can't cut open someone's skull or rib cage without doing damage and Mesmerize goes away at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; My group has house ruled that it requires more advanced supernatural powers (I think Conditioning might be enough) to mind control someone into trying to destroy themselves. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> By default, you have to get around the highly restrictive word count, vitae expenditures, time limits, 3 different resist checks at minimum, and damage dealing limitations in a single turn. (Or you just use Majesty 3 and get around the damage dealing limitation) Conditioning gives the victim the opportunity to automatically ignore any Dominate command with willpower expenditure. So it might not be a good idea to use that on a suicide bomber who's last ditch act of freedom is to grab you while detonating himself on your instructions who at that point has nothing to lose gambling on a slim chance of survival in exchange for being utterly free of your control.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:38:07-07:00","id":991691,"title":"","content":"A case of miscommunication on my part. I didn't realize that you meant the wants of the victim. I thought you meant forcing the victim to self destruction in general by using Dominate.<br /> <br /> &quot;Mesmerize is resolved if the victim takes a single point of Bashing or Lethal damage or if they suffer a breaking point fulfilling the vampire's command.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes. The victim has to receive the damage, i.e. the victim has to carry out the command. I just meant it in general; not in the specific context of the brain-bomb surgery. A simple Mesmerize after the surgery would be enough in that particular case.<br /> <br /> &quot;Conditioning gives the victim the opportunity to automatically ignore any Dominate command with willpower expenditure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Only the first condition, Subservient, does this. I specifically wrote Enslaved because it does not allow for the victim to resist commands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T03:31:50-07:00","id":991793,"title":"","content":"The reason Dominate can't mess with how someone feels is because that's what Majesty and Nightmare do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:15:10-07:00","id":991892,"title":"","content":"Could a combination of Celerity 4 + Auspex 2<br /> <br /> Allows Kindred to be quick enough to see and know the path of bullets coming in their direction and parry the bullets with bullets from their own gun or block them with a sword ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:20:37-07:00","id":991895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=991892#post991892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a combination of Celerity 4 + Auspex 2<br /> <br /> Allows Kindred to be quick enough to see and know the path of bullets coming in their direction and parry the bullets with bullets from their own gun or block them with a sword ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quicken Sight (Auspex \u2022, Celerity \u2022) allows the character to apply defense to ranged attacks. Since defense is already applied there's nothing from stopping the character from dodging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T15:56:10-07:00","id":992604,"title":"","content":"Hello kindred!<br /> <br /> There is something about Domination that intrigues me ... It works to get secrets?<br /> I mean, the vampire could Mesmerize (or Dominate) the victim and order him to answer his next question - thus covering all the possibilities offered by Auspex (* or **)? If not, how the victim would react then?<br /> I 'm sad imagining the Domination being so much more powerful than Auspex. I love Mekhet and stuff. XD<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11934-draugr","name":"Draugr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11934_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:03:15-07:00","id":992605,"title":"","content":"Auspex's advantage is that it's subtle. It's not just that you know what you shouldn't know, it's that others never quite know how much you're on to, and maintaining that uncertainty is to your benefit. You just see and intuit. Dominate interrogation happens out in the open (out loud, through writing on paper, w/e) and requires direct eye contact to initiate; as long as you're not the victim, you know exactly when a Ventrue is extracting information, and how much they're extracting. Mekhet can glimpse your secrets while you don't even know they're there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:08:50-07:00","id":992606,"title":"","content":"Dominate also doesn't let you see past obfuscate, or work on most Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:14:27-07:00","id":992608,"title":"","content":"Not really. The victim only remembers what the Dominate user wants him to remember. The Dominate user can always say some random Mekhet dug out the info and told random people. Dominate, however, requires two failed resist checks to ensure accurate information and that accuracy is still dependant on what the victim being interrogated believes is true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:45:45-07:00","id":992625,"title":"","content":"Well, using Dominate to gather secrets has a lot of restirctions to it. For one, Auspex 1 can be used on crowds of people, Auspex 3 is basically post-cognition, Auspex 4 can communicate non-verbally, Auspex 5 is sort-of like long range clairvoyance. All of these are things that are beyond Dominate's ability. In theory, Domiante can force someone to reveal all the same questions as Auspex, and even remove all memories of quesitons asked, but that requires there to be privacy to ask in the first place, meeting the eyes in the second place, and third place is succeeding on your roll against resistances - and that might include your victim falling into frenzy or riding the wave as a defense (I know some Wyrm Dragons that use this trick, ST approval pending). But Uncanny Perception has none of these restrictions - it has an equal chance of working on a powerful elder in frenzy surrounded by allies as it does on an isolated, weak-willed fledging or a mortal from a distance and no one ever being the wiser. <br /> <br /> So, there's really no worry of overlap. There are clear advantages of using all levels of Auspex instead of relying on Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T21:33:42-07:00","id":992758,"title":"","content":"It's far easier to walk into Elysium and start reading people's minds than try to single out individuals, get them alone (circumventing all manner of potential spying techniques like Heightened Senses, Obfuscate, Auspex 5, Animalism, electronic surveillance, etc.), make eye contact, deal with the consequences of someone resisting the power (you know what's hilarious? Resisting Mesmerise but pretending you failed), word your instructions and questions correctly, wipe their memory, and hope they don't notice the conversation lasted longer than they remember.<br /> <br /> Honestly if I were ranking 2nd ed. disciplines in terms of power level (accounting for their uses in combat, social situations, investigation, etc.) I'd rank Dominate quite a fair bit lower than Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:31:55-07:00","id":992806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=992758#post992758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly if I were ranking 2nd ed. disciplines in terms of power level (accounting for their uses in combat, social situations, investigation, etc.) I'd rank Dominate quite a fair bit lower than Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on everything you said except on this last sentence. Dominate can be more viable then Auspex in a lot of situations: it can be useful in combat (in one or two turns depending how the ST interprets the mesmerized condition), social situation (the command can be into a normal sentence, can be with triggers lasting weeks), investigation (in interrogation), can change memories and so on.<br /> Auspex is powerful but just in investigation/uncovery secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:30:13-07:00","id":992872,"title":"","content":"Dominate's numerous extensive restrictions and costs to use in vitae, time to use, and duration for use make it laughably weak when compared to Majesty. Auspex is the penultimate discipline. It should he practically impossible to be pulled into combat since you'd see Obfuscate users or can simply demand the ST to tell you who's going to initiate violence or when someone is going to initiate violence in an area.<br /> Dominate triggers have to be set in advance and can be discovered and undone by Auspex.<br /> Auspex undoes every application of Dominate save level 5, invalidates foundational uses of Nightmare and stealth applications of Protean, unravels Majesty, counters Obfuscate. The only discipline it doesn't really adversely affect is the physicals. Even using Animalism for spying or ambush can be thwarted and expose the user.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:35:36-07:00","id":992873,"title":"","content":"You <i>might </i>see obfuscate users. Clash of Wills and all that. <br /> <br /> Ironically the ones you won't see coming are the ones you need to see the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T04:20:28-07:00","id":992882,"title":"","content":"Dominate weak? Haaaa.... That is a gross misunderstanding. Dominate is plenty powerful. That said, it absolutely does lend itself to certain styles of play over others. All Disciplines do. So, you really can't say that one is more powerful than the others, just that your personal playstyle, or your table's style, favors one over the other. I've seen games where hair trigger Lashing Out makes Nightmare and Majesty less useful on other vamps, for instance. In games with less investigations, Auspex becomes less useful, while more useful in heavy investigation games.<br /> <br /> Every discipline has things it can do no one else can. They all have their niches that they excell at, themes they relflect. None of them are overall weaker than others; its a question of using the right tool for the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T04:44:49-07:00","id":992887,"title":"","content":"I think the usefulness of different disciplines depends mostly on play styles. By which I mean it depends both on how you play your character, but also how your group portray the game.<br /> Preferable all disciplines are portrayed and well rounded in your game, but any discipline can be the be-all-end-all in your game depending on how you/your group/your ST plays/portrays your game.<br /> <br /> For example, in our combat focused game Resilience is the most important discipline of them all (followed by Vigor). It started out as incredibly useful by its own, but after over a year of playing (and our characters ranging from BP 7 to 10) it's a must because it's the prerequisite for Juggernaut's Gait. In a game where combat is rare or practically non-existent Resilience and Vigor would probably be the worst disciplines to invest in.<br /> <br /> Edit: My point is that if the niche a discipline fills doesn't come up in your game the entire discipline can become worthless regardless of how much mechanical oomph it packs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-25-2016, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T05:09:55-07:00","id":992893,"title":"","content":"Dominate 3: &quot;when you are on the point to use Auspex, scream and confess it&quot; <br /> XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T05:57:47-07:00","id":992901,"title":"","content":"That would be 24/7, because it makes you smell blood better, so you're always using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:27:19-07:00","id":992913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=992872#post992872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex undoes every application of Dominate save level 5, invalidates foundational uses of Nightmare and stealth applications of Protean, unravels Majesty, counters Obfuscate. The only discipline it doesn't really adversely affect is the physicals. Even using Animalism for spying or ambush can be thwarted and expose the user.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing that someone (or yourself) has been victim to a discipline can be incredibly important, but it does not undo the effects of that discipline. You still carry out commands, remembers the same implanted memories (except with Auspex 4, see below), feel drawn the same way, feel the same fear, see the same things, etc, even if you know it's due to a discipline.<br /> When it comes to Nightmare 1 and 4 you'd still hallucinate, but knowing the hallucinations aren't real would practically counter them, but the main things with Nightmare 1 is the Intimidate bonus and inability to spend Willpower offensively while Nightmare 4 is the most effective as long as you don't suspect it to be a hallucination in the first place.<br /> <br /> The only two thing Auspex actually does counter is Obfuscate and Dominate 4.<br /> Obfuscate can only be countered for yourself unless you use the devotion Shatter the Shroud (Auspex \u2022\u2022, Vigor \u2022). The other thing is Dominate 4, but that would require that someone realizes the memories has been tampered with, and it requires Auspex 4 to trigger a Clash of Wills. And you can't do it on yourself, so find someone you trust with Auspex 4 to take a look inside your head.<br /> <br /> There's a third power that might look like it would be countered by Auspex, but it really won't. Nightmare 3 grants Delusional which can be resolved before the duration ends by facing proof that the delusion isn't real. Auspex can certainly help, but only as an investigative tool. And since you're literally delusional you don't think something is off so why would you use Auspex in the first place?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:47:20-07:00","id":992923,"title":"","content":"The great thing about Dominate is it has heaps of potential uses if you're creative and prepare well. The sad thing about Dominate is it has heaps of rolls and restrictions, can require a huge amount of vitae and has several easy counters. It's sort of the opposite of Majesty, Majesty is really easy to use and few restrictions and counters but lacks the sort of potential and versatility of Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:52:50-07:00","id":992924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=992872#post992872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate's numerous extensive restrictions and costs to use in vitae, time to use, and duration for use make it laughably weak when compared to Majesty. Auspex is the penultimate discipline. It should he practically impossible to be pulled into combat since you'd see Obfuscate users or can simply demand the ST to tell you who's going to initiate violence or when someone is going to initiate violence in an area.<br /> Dominate triggers have to be set in advance and can be discovered and undone by Auspex.<br /> Auspex undoes every application of Dominate save level 5, invalidates foundational uses of Nightmare and stealth applications of Protean, unravels Majesty, counters Obfuscate. The only discipline it doesn't really adversely affect is the physicals. Even using Animalism for spying or ambush can be thwarted and expose the user.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with MCN that dominate is not weak at all. Every discipline has restrictions and vitae costs. Once you have mesmerized someone ( which is free ) you can keep giving them commands for the rest of the scene. It might not be the best in combat, but my players have done pretty ok with it in combat, they dominate one bad guy to shoot/ attack the other bad guy ect. Even had someone dominate a bad guy in a fight and told him to &quot;go home&quot; he left while the fight raged on. Effectively took out the baddie in 1 hit.<br /> <br /> If you are talking about costs. Iron Edict costs 1 and Confidant/Charm costs 1 so they are cost equivalent. both have to be done on the second turn. while Mesmerize would stop someone from shooting you first turn, Awe would not.<br /> <br /> Auspex you would have to use it to know that someone is Obfuscated as using it multiple times per scene would be costly. I cant see a vampire ( unless he was extremely paranoid) doing that 20 times a night. It also takes your turn and if someone jumped you before you did it, then you are in combat. things change during the scene. If you walk in and immediately ask &quot;Who is going to attack me&quot; or &quot;is there an obfuscated vampire here&quot; you might get a No, but as you talk and discuss things, there is nothing stopping the person from changing their mind, obfuscating and attacking you. ( assuming you are not in a 1on1 conversation )<br /> <br /> You are talking about cost effectiveness. To sit there and know everything would be very expensive. And Not helpful, if anyone gets higher in initiative and dominates, charms or nightmares the Auspex user.<br /> <br /> This applies to even myself ( especially with Auspex ) I find that people who have come to these forums and said that a discipline is weak, is that they do not properly know how to use/apply it.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT : someone answered while I was typing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=992887#post992887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the usefulness of different disciplines depends mostly on play styles. By which I mean it depends both on how you play your character, but also how your group portray the game.<br /> Preferable all disciplines are portrayed and well rounded in your game, but any discipline can be the be-all-end-all in your game depending on how you/your group/your ST plays/portrays your game.<br /> <br /> For example, in our combat focused game Resilience is the most important discipline of them all (followed by Vigor). It started out as incredibly useful by its own, but after over a year of playing (and our characters ranging from BP 7 to 10) it's a must because it's the prerequisite for Juggernaut's Gait. In a game where combat is rare or practically non-existent Resilience and Vigor would probably be the worst disciplines to invest in.<br /> <br /> Edit: My point is that if the niche a discipline fills doesn't come up in your game the entire discipline can become worthless regardless of how much mechanical oomph it packs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had Majesty in a combat heavy game. I have found that if you Idol and stop the fight before it starts... It is pretty darn effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 10-25-2016, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T07:02:33-07:00","id":992931,"title":"","content":"Vampires are pretty decent in a fight, but their real strength lies in not having to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T10:02:08-07:00","id":992996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=992931#post992931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are pretty decent in a fight, but their real strength lies in not having to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that they are a lot more more then decent in fight if they are focused on this, simply the most part of them are socially focused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:32:10-07:00","id":993169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=992931#post992931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are pretty decent in a fight, but their real strength lies in not having to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. The last ditch attempt of a Ventrue elder set on fire to Mesmerize my character, whilst on Gauru, on a grapple? Cute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:12:14-07:00","id":993300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993169#post993169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. The last ditch attempt of a Ventrue elder set on fire to Mesmerize my character, whilst on Gauru, on a grapple? Cute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what you're point is here. The vampire is on fire and in a grapple with a werewolf... Does that mean the wolf is on fire too? However. <br /> Since we are making up crap.. I'm gonna give this vampire 1 dot in protean. He's gonna sink into the ground, which effectively puts out that fire. Celerity for when he comes up and wants to go first, then yeah. He's going to dominate that werewolf to go pick a fight with his pack alpha. <br /> <br /> We were just talking about &quot;decent in a fight&quot;. Decent ... Or better at not having to fight. Stop it before it starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":