<div class=\"message\">No, being on fire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry for the misunderstangin, I'm not so used to the english common saying and I didn't know exactly the meaning of be on fire in this specific case <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:02:36-07:00","id":993403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993169#post993169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. The last ditch attempt of a Ventrue elder set on fire to Mesmerize my character, whilst on Gauru, on a grapple? Cute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your ST was too nice. Anyone actually running a real Ventrue elder would've had that elder use Feral Infection and turn your character into their attack dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 10-26-2016, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:18:11-07:00","id":993405,"title":"","content":"In response to your Feral Infection, I cast &quot;Elodoth Auspice Power&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:23:38-07:00","id":993407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993405#post993405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In response to your Feral Infection, I cast &quot;Elodoth Auspice Power&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the Elodoth didn't frenzy too. Feral Infection is an AOE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T04:14:11-07:00","id":993420,"title":"","content":"Can we please not get into a Vamp v. Wolf argument? This always comes down to whatever the ST favors, personal biases, and player creativity. Its been done to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T04:51:47-07:00","id":993429,"title":"","content":"I mean to be fair, the dude was on fire, so he probably wasn't thinking all that clearly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:29:04-07:00","id":993444,"title":"","content":"About the Crossroads bane. It seens to me a tricky one. How it works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11934-draugr","name":"Draugr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11934_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T06:32:09-07:00","id":993469,"title":"","content":"Pretty much? You knowingly go through an intersection (which are freaking everywhere in a city), you get all your dice pools capped. Any time there's two roads crossing, and you pass over them with full knowledge, you trigger the bane.<br /> <br /> Now, I suppose that you can argue that a vampire can have drivers and spend the entire trip with eyes glued to the phone and earphones on without being able to sense what's going on around you would count as not knowing. But if you drove yourself, or even watched the road? You're FUBAR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T07:59:27-07:00","id":993493,"title":"","content":"By RAW, you're pretty screwed. Yeah. Personally, I find it downright unplayable.<br /> <br /> But it's clearly inspired by old mythology and superstition where crossroads were meant to be where two worlds met, rather than just any crossing streets. Back when criminals and the like were buried at crossroads, the crossroads in question were on the outskirts of town. It's this kind of crossroads that myth and superstition tend to be referring to.<br /> <br /> So to make it playable, I'd personally only count crossroads for the bane if those crossroads are outside of a town/city/what-have-you, rather than every single intersection. It fits the inspiration better and makes the bane playable. Might be erring on the side of too weak at this point, honestly, but I'll take &quot;too weak&quot; over &quot;can't leave the block your Haven is on.&quot;The latter is a bane that makes the entire group, Storyteller included, suffer. Not just the vampire who takes it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:27:36-07:00","id":993508,"title":"","content":"Yeah, vampire banes are about symbolism more than literal facts (moonlight is <i>not</i> sunlight, despite the fact that it is) and intersections in a city just don't feel like they count to me. They are false, pretender-crossroads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:29:55-07:00","id":993509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993420#post993420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we please not get into a Vamp v. Wolf argument? This always comes down to whatever the ST favors, personal biases, and player creativity. Its been done to death.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're right. I apologize about that. I should not have fed into it. I agree with you, but that was sort of my point, when something is already half dead and dying. Certain powers aren't going to help much. But that applies to anyone and everything. Sometimes vampires,werewolves, changelings, whatevers just get themselves into crap that they cant get out of.<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as the Crossroads thing, I agree that RAW would make it completely unplayable. I would probably shift the meaning to apply to important crossroads or Important intersections not every single one. Like the point where Highway X and Highway Y cross. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:34:08-07:00","id":993512,"title":"","content":"You have to pass through a crossroads. It's quite inconvenient, but heading left or right should allow you to traversing the city via a zigzag pattern.<br /> But I would personally never take it because the penalty for Crossroads (and Symbols) is by far the most severe. My late game low Humanity Gangrel would prefer not to have his attack dice pools lowered to a twentieth of what he regularly can output.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:39:22-07:00","id":993516,"title":"","content":"Unplayable is a bit much, it's only for a scene and if you have a high Humanity it might not even matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T08:52:00-07:00","id":993518,"title":"","content":"Only for a scene, and then you cross another one and it's &quot;only for a scene&quot; again, for all scenes, forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:13:46-07:00","id":993528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993518#post993518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only for a scene, and then you cross another one and it's &quot;only for a scene&quot; again, for all scenes, forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that we've moved from a white room to a white moving car driving forever but it's more of a lateral shift than an improvement.<br /> <br /> 'You travel to the Elysium. Once there...' Providing the Elysium is not situated on a crossroads, you should be fine as the travel scene, which may involve crossroads, is over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:20:59-07:00","id":993531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993403#post993403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your ST was too nice. Anyone actually running a real Ventrue elder would've had that elder use Feral Infection and turn your character into their attack dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Burn 1 WP, ignore command, maul kindred to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:36:55-07:00","id":993537,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can do that in Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:38:03-07:00","id":993572,"title":"","content":"Nah, Malus is right, Feral Instincts allows you to spend a Willpower to ignore the command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:40:50-07:00","id":993574,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see it now. Right at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:53:32-07:00","id":993584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993512#post993512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to pass through a crossroads. It's quite inconvenient, but heading left or right should allow you to traversing the city via a zigzag pattern.<br /> But I would personally never take it because the penalty for Crossroads (and Symbols) is by far the most severe. My late game low Humanity Gangrel would prefer not to have his attack dice pools lowered to a twentieth of what he regularly can output.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ehhh.... while some STs might insist that taking a left at an intersection isn't &quot;passing through&quot; a crossroads, I'm going to argue that it is. You enter the intersection of two streets, then you leave it. Nothing says you must leave through the opposite side. Now, if you were on foot and stayed a fair distance away from the intersection before crossing streets, I could see that argument. But if you're going by car, I would argue that is passing through.<br /> <br /> YMMV, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T11:07:51-07:00","id":993594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993572#post993572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, Malus is right, Feral Instincts allows you to spend a Willpower to ignore the command.</div> </div> </div> </div> Plus, supernaturals get a nice Resolve+Composure roll to resist falling under the power anyways on top of any mental defenses they might have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T11:20:32-07:00","id":993600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993584#post993584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ehhh.... while some STs might insist that taking a left at an intersection isn't &quot;passing through&quot; a crossroads, I'm going to argue that it is. You enter the intersection of two streets, then you leave it. Nothing says you must leave through the opposite side. Now, if you were on foot and stayed a fair distance away from the intersection before crossing streets, I could see that argument. But if you're going by car, I would argue that is passing through.<br /> <br /> YMMV, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that entering it is what the bane is.. A zigzag pattern would not override that curse. Imagine if you will. Walking a block, getting super confused, managing to walk another block... getting confused. and another and another ... How would you walk 6 blocks? let alone travel miles to said Elysium? You could pass hundreds of crossroads if you lived within a city.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Back to the werewolf vs vampire thing. I think MCN was right several posts ago, we should drop that discussion in this thread at least. We can all build perfect white room scenarios to destroy the other opponent, but any good player knows there are hundreds of other forces in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T11:21:29-07:00","id":993601,"title":"","content":"The thing about Crossroads is it's completely debilitating during scenes where you're traveling through the city and a complete nonissue during scenes when you're in a single location. In a LARP it would be the least harsh of the sample Banes because the majority of the game tends to take place at Elysium and in the case that you do need to travel, the transit is usually skipped over. Even in tabletop, how often do dice rolls actually happen while the character is traveling? Maybe Drive rolls? You can hire a chauffeur. Maybe some combat if you get mugged on your way somewhere else? Gonna need some bodyguards. Feeding rolls? Yah, that's the tough one. But if you've got a decent size Herd, maybe an Oath of Fealty or a few serfs paying red rent for use of your Feeding grounds, maybe some flunkies you can send out to abduct vessels for you, you should be able to get by. What the Bane really does is exactly what Banes should do - it creates a weakness that those in the know can exploit, and that you have to play a bit differently to mitigate. You're vulnerable while traveling, so you take precautions to minimize your need to travel and to protect yourself while in transit. Mostly this means a lot of Retainers. Maybe it's just me, but in my experience little enough of the game focuses on travel within the city that this Bane seems pretty manageable. Unless you're talking about a nomadic game, but then, those tend to focus more on open road and rural areas where crosdroads are less common and more avoidable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-26-2016, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:34:53-07:00","id":993635,"title":"","content":"I was thinking the best time to take advantage of it would be during a foot chase scene.<br /> <br /> But I'm also gearing up to put some Dark Eras stuff in my game and the farther you go back the less busy the road systems are, though crossroads still exist.<br /> <br /> It would probably be a nice bane for something like a Mabry or other vampire that lives away from people. Alternatively you have those subterranean vampires. The concept seems more fitting for the kind of vampire that would be found in the middle of nowhere or some other isolating spot. Dracula in his castle, rather than Angel in Los Angeles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:58:14-07:00","id":993652,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I find that all the banes are either 1) trivally avoidable, or 2) remove you from play. Like the holy day bane. You are active for six of seven days. That's not that great of a bane for a PC, simply because it makes a day of the week you can't play, rather than hinder you from being actually in play. They're flavorful, but not exactly something that will weaken you that much. <br /> <br /> I find that banes are actually far more relevant on NPCs than PCs, because then you can exploit the strix / elder vampire in question, draw them into a situation where the NPC is weak and the PCs can fight normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:10:03-07:00","id":993658,"title":"","content":"No reason NPCs can't do the same to PCs though. Or PCs to other PCs. And keeping your Bane a secret and/or covering up when someone finds can become a story catalyst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:30:06-07:00","id":993667,"title":"","content":"It's not that bad. As stated before, travel scenes don't usually use much dicerolling but the worst it comes down to is getting a chauffeur and closing your eyes till you get there. On foot, you just take one step to the left or right and cross the street next to the X instead of strolling right through the intersection.<br /> The spirit of the Bane may be different, but if we're going by the actual wording...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:52:28-07:00","id":993680,"title":"","content":"hunnn .. Some interesting answers so far. Thanks for the opinions, folks.<br /> <br /> But it makes me wonder .. How often do you guys usually create NPCs with banes?<br /> <br /> In general, I used to give 1 or more banes to kindred with a century or two... Because really seems like that improve the character., and, I must to say, banes are a very very cool stuff to play XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11934-draugr","name":"Draugr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11934_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:59:46-07:00","id":993780,"title":"","content":"I give NPCs Banes based on what Breaking Points they would be likely to regularly experience. For example, a character who routinely kills their vessels by overfeeding would probably want to take a Bane for impassioned killing. An assassin might take a Bane for premeditated murder. A cloistered hermit might take a Bane for going a year without human contact. Most Acolytes probably take a Bane for learning Cruac. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T19:15:15-07:00","id":993836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993658#post993658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No reason NPCs can't do the same to PCs though. Or PCs to other PCs. And keeping your Bane a secret and/or covering up when someone finds can become a story catalyst.</div> </div> </div> </div> In theory, yes. Realistically, however, having a party changes the dynamic a lot and the difficulty of arranging it, as well as the fact that many PCs have higher humanity than an elder NPC would, and far more than a strix, thus being less affected by banes. Granted, the humanity level will change depending on concept and playstyle, but its been my experience that banes aren't as crippling for PCs. <br /> <br /> As for PC v PC? My games don't have that, so its a non-issue for me. There's some tension, but nothing that would escalate beyond a few words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draugr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=993680#post993680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it makes me wonder .. How often do you guys usually create NPCs with banes?</div> </div> </div> </div> Often. I find that creative weaknesses are tons of fun in play, plus banes tend to reflect iconic actions of vampires in stories, making them very flavorful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T21:56:57-07:00","id":995507,"title":"","content":"at what page is the ghoul discipline limit stated in 2nd edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T22:13:19-07:00","id":995510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995507#post995507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">at what page is the ghoul discipline limit stated in 2nd edition</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghoul Discipline limit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T02:34:42-07:00","id":995559,"title":"","content":"Probably he means the impossibility for ghoul to spill vitae and the fact to not add the discipline value in the dice pool. Anyway now I can't see the page I'm not at home. If none else will answer before I come back, I'll check later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T02:38:50-07:00","id":995560,"title":"","content":"Page 297 has the limitations Ghouls have regarding Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T03:19:32-07:00","id":995568,"title":"","content":"And if you mean dot limits, they don't have any. <br /> <br /> I don't think they can learn devotions though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T03:35:45-07:00","id":995571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995568#post995568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you mean dot limits, they don't have any. <br /> <br /> I don't think they can learn devotions though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you are right, no devotion for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T17:53:14-07:00","id":995884,"title":"","content":"Is that an out-of-book errata thing, or am I missing something here? Because I can't seem to find anything in either the Devotions section or the Ghoul section about that. Closest I can find is that they can't learn Coils or Scales, or use any power involving spilling blood or feeding it to another, both under the Discipline section of &quot;Playing a Ghoul&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T18:10:33-07:00","id":995891,"title":"","content":"I searched through the 2E PDF and found not a single instance of the word devotion in the ghoul section. I'm pretty sure it's not brought up.<br /> <br /> So, what is RAW in this case? Can ghouls learn devotions because the rules doesn't forbid them, or can't they learn devotions because the book doesn't say they can?<br /> It probably doesn't matter. Personally I'd allow ghouls to buy devotions (and kindred merits) as long as they make sense for characters without beasts. I just found it an interesting conundrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T19:01:43-07:00","id":995908,"title":"","content":"From first edition's Ghouls book.<br /> <br /> 'Ghouls aren\u2019t barred from learning Devotions, but they must be taught each one. That is, they cannot simply figure Devotions out on their own even if they have the requisite Discipline combinations already. Furthermore, the experience-point costs listed for Devotions in Vampire are doubled for ghouls. Finally, a ghoul cannot use any Devotion that consists of Dominate or Majesty on a Kindred victim.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T19:39:15-07:00","id":995917,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but this is something second edition may well have changed. <br /> <br /> One thing to consider: Revenants explicitly <i>can't</i> learn devotions. Personally, I'd consider that alone to be enough to bar ghouls from them because Revs are a step up on the vamp scale. But even if you don't agree with that, revenants are commonly ex-ghouls. So if ghouls can learn devotions then you'll have revenants with devotions that they can't learn because they did so when they were <i>less</i> of a vampire than they are now. <br /> <br /> It just doesn't mesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T19:50:44-07:00","id":995922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995917#post995917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but this is something second edition may well have changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said it was from first edition.<br /> <br /> It's up to the group to decide whether they're letting rules slip over to first edition or not. Some people here may go with a, 'if second edition hasn't mentioned it, it hasn't changed,' stance, but it's usually brought up only when it supports their argument.<br /> <br /> And while it may have changed, nothing in the only book out has changed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T19:59:39-07:00","id":995927,"title":"","content":"Hopefully this will all be cleared up in Half-Damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T20:05:58-07:00","id":995930,"title":"","content":"Just as a funny side note: Blood sorcery also isn't listed as something ghouls can't learn. I seem to recall a thread discussing the possibilities of ghouls assisting with rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T21:27:25-07:00","id":995950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995930#post995930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a funny side note: Blood sorcery also isn't listed as something ghouls can't learn. I seem to recall a thread discussing the possibilities of ghouls assisting with rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, by the rules as written ghouls can totally learn Theban and Cruac, because they are Disciplines and they are not listed among the Disciplines they can't learn. They can't <i>use</i> them, because doing so requires them to spill blood. But they can learn them if they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T22:27:43-07:00","id":995964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995950#post995950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, by the rules as written ghouls can totally learn Theban and Cruac, because they are Disciplines and they are not listed among the Disciplines they can't learn. They can't <i>use</i> them, because doing so requires them to spill blood. But they can learn them if they want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The first point of Cruac is spent like any other Discipline; it isn't spilt. So they can use level one rituals.<br /> <br /> Also, re: ghoul devotions, I'm of the opinion that 1e should be ignored entirely when it comes to mechanics. If you say that 1e rules carry over, you're saying that you need 1e core to play 2e. That's silly. If the book doesn't bar Ghouls from learning devotions, then I think that's evidence enough that they can.<br /> <br /> I also disagree with the assertion that Revenants are &quot;a step up,&quot; considering they pay more for Disciplines than Ghouls do and don't keep their Blood Pool overnight while Ghouls do and while neither of them get all the advantages of being a full-fledged Vampire, Revenants get the weaknesses while Ghouls do not. Revenants are the worst off of the three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T22:57:23-07:00","id":995975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995964#post995964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first point of Cruac is spent like any other Discipline; it isn't spilt. So they can use level one rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah. Neat!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995964#post995964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, re: ghoul devotions, I'm of the opinion that 1e should be ignored entirely when it comes to mechanics. If you say that 1e rules carry over, you're saying that you need 1e core to play 2e. That's silly. If the book doesn't bar Ghouls from learning devotions, then I think that's evidence enough that they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's kind of a misrepresentation of the &quot;default to 1e rules for things that are not covered by 2e&quot; position. You don't <i>need </i>to know if Ghouls can learn Devotions or not to play Requiem. It wasn't in the core book of <i>either</i> edition. The thing is, books have limited space and can't possibly cover every possible situation. If you encounter a situation not covered by the book, like a Ghoul trying to learn a Devotion, it is on the Storyteller to make a call. For the purposes of making such a call, I see nothing wrong with referring to a rule from a previous edition when one exists. I mean, I also see nothing wrong with ignoring a rule from a previous edition when one exists. In neither case is the previous-edition book that the rule is found in to be &quot;needed&quot; to play the current edition. It's just a tool the Storyteller can use or not use as they see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T00:46:22-07:00","id":995990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995964#post995964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, re: ghoul devotions, I'm of the opinion that 1e should be ignored entirely when it comes to mechanics. If you say that 1e rules carry over, you're saying that you need 1e core to play 2e. That's silly. If the book doesn't bar Ghouls from learning devotions, then I think that's evidence enough that they can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering ghouls are Mortals+some vampire powers rather than Vampires-some vampire powers, why would lack of a text mean they can learn devotions. If there is no text saying that ghouls can learn devotions, then they can't learn devotions. I mean, there's no text saying ghouls can't learn werewolf gifts...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T00:58:27-07:00","id":995992,"title":"","content":"The book wasn't made with Werewolf in mind, though, so that's... kiiind of a different case. And it does lay out the restrictions on every other Discipline-related power, so not touching on Devotions either way kind of stands out.<br /> I know I'll allow it at least for the short limited-crossover minor-template campaign I'm putting together, if any of my group decides to take the Ghoul option. Mostly just curious to hear if there's an official rule about the matter since the book kind of misses it (sounds like there currently isn't), and hearing other players' interpretations in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 10-31-2016, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T02:59:48-07:00","id":996010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995964#post995964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Revenants ... pay more for Disciplines than Ghouls do</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely certain this is true. There's nothing in the rules about ghouls actually <i>sharing</i> their regnant's clan, so they may actually need to pay full price.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995964#post995964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and don't keep their Blood Pool overnight while Ghouls do </div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but the pool is spent to <i>reanimate their lifeless corpse. </i>It comes down to &quot;has vampire-like traits which require a bit of vitae to maintain&quot; vs &quot;Is <i>actually a vampire</i> with an inefficient reanimation engine&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T04:10:53-07:00","id":996020,"title":"","content":"Only one vitae is spent, just like regular vampires. The rest is expelled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T07:48:06-07:00","id":996067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=995990#post995990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering ghouls are Mortals+some vampire powers rather than Vampires-some vampire powers, why would lack of a text mean they can learn devotions. If there is no text saying that ghouls can learn devotions, then they can't learn devotions. I mean, there's no text saying ghouls can't learn werewolf gifts...</div> </div> </div> </div>I could be wrong ( as werewolves are not really my thing.. ) but doesn't it say in the book somewhere, only werewolves or their kin, can take werewolf gifts? Or you would have to meet the prerequisite of being some type of werewolf? and that templates can't overlap? (you cant have a vampire/werewolf or Ghoul/ werewolf?) So It really does say that ghouls cant learn werewolf gifts, though not in those words.<br /> <br /> Also there generally isn't an all inclusive list of what ghouls can or can not do, you have to interpret it from the text given.<br /> <br /> &quot;Learning Disciplines: Ghouls may learn Disciplines under<br /> the same rules as Kindred. They may not learn Coils or Scales<br /> of the Dragon.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Many vampires develop the abilities listed here for each<br /> Discipline, but some manifest new powers of the Blood. These<br /> new Discipline techniques, called Devotions, can manifest<br /> spontaneously in some Kindred, or can be developed by<br /> careful honing of Discipline abilities. Once a vampire knows<br /> a Devotion, she can teach it to another Kindred in much the<br /> same way as the standard Discipline techniques. Any vampire<br /> with the appropriate prerequisite Discipline dots can develop<br /> any Devotion for which she has the dots \u2014 as long as she has a<br /> teacher, or has plenty of time to practice.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> Though it doesn't out right say that a ghoul can or can't, it does say follow the rules for Kindred Disciplines and the above is how one learns a new &quot;discipline technique.&quot; Which to me says that a ghoul follows that same curve. That is how I interpret it. Though the others make a valid point that in 1E ghouls couldn't learn them, which very well might come out again in the Half-Damned book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996010#post996010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not entirely certain this is true. There's nothing in the rules about ghouls actually <i>sharing</i> their regnant's clan, so they may actually need to pay full price.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>&quot;Clan</b>: Your ghoul has a regnant, usually the vampire who first<br /> gave her Vitae and spent a point of Willpower on her. Think<br /> about who this regnant is (maybe one of the other player\u2019s<br /> characters), <b>and decide on his clan.</b><br /> Disciplines: Select two dots of Disciplines that are<b> in-clan f</b>or<br /> your character\u2019s regnant. At least one physical Discipline dot<br /> is recommended, but not required. (You might want to look at<br /> the ghoul Discipline rules below first.)<br /> <br /> Ghouls can use most Disciplines, <b>including bloodline<br /> Disciplines, </b>but suffer some restrictions.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> <i>Though </i>it does not out right say &quot;You are in your regnant's clan&quot; It heavily implies it by having you figure out what are &quot;in-clan&quot; disciplines and allowing you to take bloodline disciplines, which you can only do if you are in a clan.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 10-31-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:19:30-07:00","id":996081,"title":"","content":"Wow, we kind of read the same passage and took it in two totally different directions. See, I read:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Select two dots of Disciplines that are<b> in-clan for<br /> your character\u2019s regnant.</b><br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>And noted that the disciplines are described as in clan for the ghoul's <b>regnant</b>, <i>not the ghoul themselves.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T09:20:30-07:00","id":996111,"title":"","content":"I've noted before the line about bloodline Disciplines. With the assumption that a ghoul retains all disciplines should they be embraced (otherwise playing ghouls would lead to a whole lot of XP loss for anyone who focused on Disciplines), that would make the ghoul able to gain bloodline Disciplines from bloodlines they might not end up joining, something that previously has been restricted to the En.<br /> For such chronicles I'd restrict bloodline Disciplines and allow the ghoul-turned-vampire to retain previous Disciplines.<br /> <br /> But on the subject; when it comes to Discipline Experience costs I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a>. The ghoul isn't part of a clan, and it would be weird if a ghoul can learn certain Disciplines more easily than most vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T10:45:29-07:00","id":996143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996081#post996081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, we kind of read the same passage and took it in two totally different directions. See, I read:<br /> <br /> And noted that the disciplines are described as in clan for the ghoul's <b>regnant</b>, <i>not the ghoul themselves.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Precisely. Just like a picture, people can see two different things while looking at the same picture. I took it the way I did because it is so very similar to being your sire. When you are creating a vampire you pick your sire's clan so you can have those &quot;in clan&quot; disciplines. If you can learn bloodline disciplines, you have to be part of that bloodline, which means you have to be part of the parent clan. Which is given to you by your sire.<br /> <br /> If they are not in a clan and everything is out of clan, then it would open a can of worms. No ghoul could ever have Nightmare, Majesty, Protean, Auspex, or Dominate, because you have to be of that clan to take them. And I know there are ghouls out there with those abilities. Like it was pointed out, if you are not in a clan and learn a bloodline discipline, what would stop you from changing regnants and learning another one, and another one and another one? Which is why if they are stuck in a clan / bloodline it would prevent that from happening.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Why would they call that section &quot;Clan&quot; and not just say &quot;Clanless&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;Clan</b>: Your ghoul has a regnant, usually the vampire who first<br /> gave her Vitae and spent a point of Willpower on her. Think<br /> about who this regnant is (maybe one of the other player\u2019s<br /> characters), <b>and decide on his clan.</b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996111#post996111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But on the subject; when it comes to Discipline Experience costs I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a>. The ghoul isn't part of a clan, and it would be weird if a ghoul can learn certain Disciplines more easily than most vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean &quot;more easily&quot; than a vampire? Making a ghoul learn disciplines the same way a vampire does &gt; with some in and out of clan costs &lt; is exactly what the book tells us to do. &quot;Ghouls may learn Disciplines under the same rules as Kindred.&quot;<br /> <br /> if everything was out of clan and cost 4. wouldn't it have been more appropriate to say, &quot;Ghouls may learn Disciplines under the same rules as Revenants&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 10-31-2016, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T10:49:42-07:00","id":996146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996143#post996143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No ghoul could ever have Nightmare, Majesty, Protean, Auspex, or Dominate, because you have to be of that clan to take them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's not actually a problem. Vampires (and also Revenants) <i>can </i>learn another clan's unique discipline: They just have to consume a point of the teacher's vitae first. <br /> <br /> Which ghouls do. A lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:41:32-07:00","id":996172,"title":"","content":"Nevermind. Not really worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 10-31-2016, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:04:04-07:00","id":996191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996143#post996143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean &quot;more easily&quot; than a vampire? Making a ghoul learn disciplines the same way a vampire does &gt; with some in and out of clan costs &lt; is exactly what the book tells us to do. &quot;Ghouls may learn Disciplines under the same rules as Kindred.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>More easily as in, a ghoul with a clan would be able to learn that clan's disciplines easier than an actual vampire who happened not to be of that clan. It doesn't sit right with me. Your opinion may differ.<br /> But saying that's what the book tells us is up for debate since there are different opinions about whether or not ghouls belong to clans. Neither stance is explicitly written in the book. If ghouls don't belong to clans all disciplines would default to being out-of-clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T12:46:09-07:00","id":996217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996191#post996191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More easily as in, a ghoul with a clan would be able to learn that clan's disciplines easier than an actual vampire who happened not to be of that clan. It doesn't sit right with me. Your opinion may differ.<br /> But saying that's what the book tells us is up for debate since there are different opinions about whether or not ghouls belong to clans. Neither stance is explicitly written in the book. If ghouls don't belong to clans all disciplines would default to being out-of-clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls learn them the same way a vampire does.( not the same way a revenant does ) Which means: A vampire learns in clan disciplines easier than a vampire who isn't in that clan. There is far more evidence in the book that points to ghouls having a clan than there is ghouls are clanless.<br /> <br /> If ghouls don't belong to clans why does it have you pick 2 disciplines that are in clan for your regnant? ( just like when you are sired )Why cant I just start with Protean and Majesty? if my regnant for some reason had one dot in every discipline possible, why couldn't I just start with anything I wanted?<br /> <br /> If ghouls don't have a clan, how can they learn bloodline disciplines? If I have to follow the rules for learning disciplines as a kindred does, it says that I would need to be of that bloodline, not even diablerie allows it. To become part of a bloodline, you have to be part of the parent clan.<br /> <br /> Again I ask<br /> <br /> Why would they call that section &quot;Clan&quot; and not just say &quot;Clanless&quot;<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;</b><b>Clan</b>: Your ghoul has a regnant, usually the vampire who first<br /> gave her Vitae and spent a point of Willpower on her. Think<br /> about who this regnant is (maybe one of the other player\u2019s<br /> characters), and decide on his clan. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Why would they even bother to mention &quot;Clan&quot; let alone give it it's own section? It implies heavily that your clan is your regnant's, like your sire would be.<br /> It could have just as easily been written<br /> <br /> Though clanless, your ghoul must still choose two disciplines that are in clan for your regnant upon creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I am not trying to fight at all, but I would love to know if I have been playing ghouls wrong for the last couple of years by giving them a clan. If there is evidence to support that they are clanless I would like to know it. Or if even they mentioned it in the previous ghoul book, just to give me a baseline on it. <br /> I would like to be convinced one way or the other ( either by developer clarification) or some strong book text to support that they are more like revenants than kindred. If these questions could be answered logically, then maybe it would make more sense to me that they are clanless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 10-31-2016, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:18:51-07:00","id":996227,"title":"","content":"Without any explicit mention there's bound to be different opinions about what's intended. It all boils down to interpretations and preferences. I just wanted to explain what I meant with easier learning, and point out that your interpretation isn't the only one.<br /> If you think it works and want it to work different from my interpretation, you're better off following your own interpretation. I don't wish to convince you that mine is the correct or better one. I just wanted to share my version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T15:58:12-07:00","id":996309,"title":"","content":"Pg 298 Ghoul and Mortal Merits. All references to clan refer specifically to <b><i>Regnant</i></b>'s clan.<br /> Ghouls can learn Disciplines just fine but they don't get a Clan discount because they are not members of a Clan because they aren't Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 10-31-2016, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T20:28:35-07:00","id":996415,"title":"","content":"Pardon if this is a stupid or bad question to be asked here, but I kind of need to know for reference. When it comes to a vampire's &quot;biology&quot;, is it all magic? Or is there still some semblance of a biological function present? My biggest question is if the brain of the vampire still sends out signals and whatnot for movement and the like? <br /> <br /> (And if anyone is willing to answer as well, I have the same questions for Prometheans and Sin-Eaters. Please and thank you for reading this question.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T03:48:36-07:00","id":996518,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure vampires are 100% magic. Or at least, 90%. They can fake it, of course. There's references to the blush of life being able to fool an MRI scan. <br /> <br /> Prometheans and Sin Eaters are both more grounded in reality. A promethean has things that resemble biology in function if not in form. A Sin-Eater is basically just healed from the point of death and is more or less a normal human for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T03:48:57-07:00","id":996519,"title":"","content":"They require sustenance, they require rest periodically, they use energy, they reproduce, they are composed of cells and organs, they respond and adapt to their environment. They even excrete extraneous waste material. So in the strictest sense, yes they are a life form with biological features. However, they don't biomechanically function identically to humans. Yes, the brain (and heart) still function and serves as a control center but they don't do everything a human brain does for the human body because there is no inherent need for it to do so and there's been no elaboration as to the why and hows any of the aforementioned creatures function so that leaves it up to the individual players to determine. If you want to say a vampire's brain acts as a sort of energy antenna that draws and then filters thermal energy from their immediate vicinity to animate the body, it's not like the developers are qualified (or inclined) to say you don't know what you're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T03:56:44-07:00","id":996520,"title":"","content":"Mmm as far as I know heart and brain are not working and are dead as everything else. <br /> The stake trough heart isn't a proof of its functionality, cause a knife or a sword into it wouldn't have the same effect of the stake. It's a kind of &quot;mystical&quot; nemesis. <br /> <br /> Brain doesn't work too. If I'm not wrong their EEG is flatline.<br /> <br /> Yes they are composed of biological matter but this matter is dead, so I'd say they are 100% magic creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-01-2016, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T04:19:37-07:00","id":996524,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't excrete. They <i>vomit</i> food back up if they eat food, either right away or if using the blush of life they vomit it up later. But they don't excrete &quot;extraneous waste material.&quot; They drink blood and convert it to vitae. You can cut them open and cause them to bleed a bit (although they lose no vitae in the process) but that's not excretion. Bloody tears aren't excretion either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T06:48:46-07:00","id":996558,"title":"","content":"Vomiting up food and drink because it does not contain any nutritional value to the vampire constitutes excretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:04:14-07:00","id":996562,"title":"","content":"<i>Technically, </i>it's an aborted consumption. You excrete things you're done with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:28:42-07:00","id":996573,"title":"","content":"Except they'd extract and process blood or vitae contained therein. It's no different than a human or dog swallowing a penny or Lego and vomiting it up or crapping it out later. It's still excretion, comparative efficiency in processing isn't a pre requisite to classify as a life form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T07:40:24-07:00","id":996581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996573#post996573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except they'd extract and process blood or vitae contained therein.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't think they would. There's a special bloodline that can eat flesh and get Vitae from it, most vampires can't do that and would just vomit it up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:09:06-07:00","id":996638,"title":"","content":"I didn't say they could convert flesh or water to vitae. I said that if they eat or drink something with blood in it they'll take the blood and dispense with the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T09:32:50-07:00","id":996646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996638#post996638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say they could convert flesh or water to vitae. I said that if they eat or drink something with blood in it they'll take the blood and dispense with the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that would work usually. I run my games where vampires will mix stuff like beer and wine with blood in order to get drunk without feeding on a drunk person. Usually mixed with blush of life in order to avoid vomiting immediately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T10:35:09-07:00","id":996679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996646#post996646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, that would work usually. I run my games where vampires will mix stuff like beer and wine with blood in order to get drunk without feeding on a drunk person. Usually mixed with blush of life in order to avoid vomiting immediately.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can blush of life and get drunk or high as RAW. as long as you are &quot;alive&quot; you can suffer the consequences. You can also spend a vitae to burn it out of your system. <br /> <br /> Though if you consumed beer without the blush of life, it should go down and come right back up. Violently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:16:58-07:00","id":996704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996558#post996558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vomiting up food and drink because it does not contain any nutritional value to the vampire constitutes excretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very <i>liberal</i> definition of the word &quot;excretion.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T12:49:53-07:00","id":996767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996415#post996415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon if this is a stupid or bad question to be asked here, but I kind of need to know for reference. When it comes to a vampire's &quot;biology&quot;, is it all magic? Or is there still some semblance of a biological function present? My biggest question is if the brain of the vampire still sends out signals and whatnot for movement and the like? <br /> <br /> (And if anyone is willing to answer as well, I have the same questions for Prometheans and Sin-Eaters. Please and thank you for reading this question.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The brain does not control the vampire's bodily functions by way of neural stimuli, no. Vampires can in fact survive decapitation or destruction of the brain, though it would likely force them into torpor from being full on lethal damage, and would take a lot of Vitae to regenerate.<br /> <br /> Vampires' faculties and functions are entirely controlled by vitae, the life force that sustains and animates them. Whether it is biological or magical is debatable - it certainly doesn't function according to our current understanding of biology. But that doesn't necessarily mean it isn't an entirely natural, non-magical phenomenon. Just one that modern science is yet to model.<br /> <br /> For Prometheans, Pyros serves a similar role as Vitae does to vampires. Not sure about Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T13:54:23-07:00","id":996790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996767#post996767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The brain does not control the vampire's bodily functions by way of neural stimuli, no. Vampires can in fact survive decapitation or destruction of the brain, though it would likely force them into torpor from being full on lethal damage, and would take a lot of Vitae to regenerate.<br /> <br /> Vampires' faculties and functions are entirely controlled by vitae, the life force that sustains and animates them. Whether it is biological or magical is debatable - it certainly doesn't function according to our current understanding of biology. But that doesn't necessarily mean it isn't an entirely natural, non-magical phenomenon. Just one that modern science is yet to model.<br /> <br /> For Prometheans, Pyros serves a similar role as Vitae does to vampires. Not sure about Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alrighties, thank you for the answer! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:49:36-07:00","id":996929,"title":"","content":"Can a Nosferatu purchase the Striking Looks merit in character creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T19:08:42-07:00","id":996938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996929#post996929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Nosferatu purchase the Striking Looks merit in character creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason a Nosferatu wouldn't be able to buy Striking Looks. Striking Looks can be anything from beauty to hideousness. And the Nosferatu is not limited to being hideous. It's just that humans somehow generally find Nosferatus more disturbing than other vampires. Unnatural beauty can do this just as well as a hideous visage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:59:42-07:00","id":996989,"title":"","content":"for a very weak vampire do health levels mean vitae, say even on a german shepherd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:14:58-07:00","id":996992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996989#post996989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for a very weak vampire do health levels mean vitae, say even on a german shepherd</div> </div> </div> </div>It is dependent on the Size of the animal.<br /> Size 0 = 0 Vitae<br /> Size 1 = 1 Vitae<br /> Size 2-3 = 2 Vitae<br /> Size 4-5 = 3 Vitae<br /> Each additional Size over 5 grants one additional Vitae.<br /> Page 95, second column.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:02:35-07:00","id":998527,"title":"","content":"So, while re-reading the Strix Chapter, I found this on page 201:<br /> <br /> &quot;Soulless victims produce no Vitae \u2014 the source of their vital essence has already been removed.&quot;<br /> <br /> This only affects Strix, or even Kindred can't use the blood of a Soulless victim to acquire Vitae?<br /> <br /> Edit: Since it is on the side bar about &quot;Breath Drinking&quot;, I'm guessing it applies only to that. However, I kind of like the concept applying even to blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T11:32:05-07:00","id":998834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=998527#post998527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, while re-reading the Strix Chapter, I found this on page 201:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Soulless victims produce no Vitae \u2014 the source of their vital essence has already been removed.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> This only affects Strix, or even Kindred can't use the blood of a Soulless victim to acquire Vitae?<br /> <br /> Edit: Since it is on the side bar about &amp;quot;Breath Drinking&amp;quot;, I'm guessing it applies only to that. However, I kind of like the concept applying even to blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's specific to breath drinking. If a vampire somehow gained access to the breath drinking move (maybe through a Bloodline or something), they wouldn't be able to gain Vitae by using it on Soulless victims either. If you want to make that a universal thing that applies to normal feeding as well as breath drinking though, that seems pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T12:02:36-07:00","id":998846,"title":"","content":"Wait, nevermind, wrong thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:13:38-08:00","id":1000348,"title":"","content":"Is there any reference to vampires being unable to recover WP during the Daysleep in the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:28:17-08:00","id":1000356,"title":"","content":"No, there's also no reference to them being able to recover WP during the Daysleep in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:47:35-08:00","id":1000370,"title":"","content":"Rose has said that the intent was for them to be unable to, but that nothing breaks if you allow them to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T14:06:54-08:00","id":1000425,"title":"","content":"It was intended to be in the books, but because it got left out, its more of a common forum houserule now than anything. Without an errata, the no willpower thing isn't really an official rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T23:32:24-08:00","id":1000629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1000425#post1000425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was intended to be in the books, but because it got left out, its more of a common forum houserule now than anything. Without an errata, the no willpower thing isn't really an official rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree. The book is meant to be standalone rules package. And nowhere in it, does it mention sleep to give you back WP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T04:33:37-08:00","id":1000699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1000629#post1000629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. The book is meant to be standalone rules package. And nowhere in it, does it mention sleep to give you back WP <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Even if might just be kidding, I feel compelled to point out that's not how the rules work. As a template, vampires modify the base mortal rules that the template overlays. Everyone, from vamps to werewolves to demons and prometheans, starts with everything that a mortal does. And mortals regain willpower with sleep. Without a direct statement to change the base mortal assumptions, you have to go forwards with the base mortal rules. And, yes, the books do say that monsters do use the base mortal rules - its in the beginning of the Traits section, and also direct you to the WoD/CofD/GMC core books for more details (which contradicts the idea of &quot;stand alone&quot;). And the rules in each supernatural book are abridged - we know there are entire sections of core rules not reproduced in each book. Word count is a cruel mistress that way.<br /> <br /> Unless you're saying that mortals and ghouls don't regain willpower from sleep in a Vampire game either. By coincidence, there's also no direct mention of regaining willpower from sleep in the Werewolf, Beast, Demon or Mage* books either, for either the large templates or small ones like Stigmatic. Are you suggesting that no one in those games either regain willpower by sleeping? The only book that seems to mention regaining willpower with sleep is in the CofD core / GMC Rules Update. So, are we saying that base mortals created with the CofD rules are the only ones regaining willpower, or supernaturals as well? Going by your logic, no supernatural or mortal made without the GMC/CofD core can regain willpower with rest. Its one or the other. Amusingly, the ephemeral critters rules in each book do include regaining willpower once a day for free, so that's a thing.<br /> <br /> So, between references to using the mortal core rules in every supernatural book and the lack of willpower-through-sleep rule in every supernatural rulebook, I'm personally leaning towards regaining willpower. I've never heard anything suggesting that non-vamps were intended to not regain willpower from sleep. If anything, I've heard the opposite.<br /> <br /> * The mage book does have a Life spell for regaining willpower with a magical night-of-sleep-in-an-instant, but it does qualify &quot;if applicable.&quot; The soul loss rules do mention regaining willpower through sleep, but again it has a qualifier where mages may not gain willpower, but mortals might. Beast and Demon do have a Nightmare power (the power is called Nightmare in DtD) that robs a character of regaining willpower with a night's rest, but no word if that applies to mortal victims only, or supernaturals as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:24:27-08:00","id":1000712,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a coil or scale or something in that lets you regain willpower from sleep (away from books right now), meaning that vampires don't get willpower from sleep?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:44:55-08:00","id":1000719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1000712#post1000712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a coil or scale or something in that lets you regain willpower from sleep (away from books right now), meaning that vampires don't get willpower from sleep?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, no 2e coil allows for regaining willpower from daysleep (well, coil of ziva kind of does, but that's because the vampire becomes human again). But at the same time I'm pretty sure Rose or one of the writers has weighed in on this in the past and said vampires aren't meant to gain willpower from sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:49:35-08:00","id":1000724,"title":"","content":"There isn't anything in any published material that makes any reference to vampires not getting willpower back from sleep. This is entirely a forum thing based on what Rose said in the past. <br /> <br /> Very likely, the game will go forwards under the assumption that willpower is regained from sleep, should any new material show up that references that. Its kind of odd to force writers to operate under a rule that's not written down anywhere, and likewise confusing for new players who don't come to the forums as often as regulars to get that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:04:43-08:00","id":1000728,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there is an answer on this somewhere already, I just don't have the books at easy access currently. Can Animalism be used to influence werewolves at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T06:21:42-08:00","id":1000736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1000728#post1000728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure there is an answer on this somewhere already, I just don't have the books at easy access currently. Can Animalism be used to influence werewolves at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They're not animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:03:27-08:00","id":1000759,"title":"","content":"Well, the 4 dot power that works on humans and vampires works on them too, but that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:13:34-08:00","id":1000763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1000425#post1000425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was intended to be in the books, but because it got left out, its more of a common forum houserule now than anything. Without an errata, the no willpower thing isn't really an official rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As Charlaquin pointed out that Rose did make a post saying that No Willpower was meant to be. When Rose says something on how rules are suppose to work, most take them as &quot;official Rule&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: It wouldn't break the game to allow it. So whatever works for your group is what you all should do. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-09-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:15:30-08:00","id":1000766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1000736#post1000736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. They're not animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. My friends and I use 1E, so I suppose I mostly meant the 5 dot frenzy power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:34:54-08:00","id":1000776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1000724#post1000724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't anything in any published material that makes any reference to vampires not getting willpower back from sleep. This is entirely a forum thing based on what Rose said in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also nothing in any published material about them not getting a Beat every time they sleep. Does that happen? In a book meant to be playable standalone, a rule not being in the book means it isn't a rule in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1000724#post1000724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very likely, the game will go forwards under the assumption that willpower is regained from sleep, should any new material show up that references that. Its kind of odd to force writers to operate under a rule that's not written down anywhere, and likewise confusing for new players who don't come to the forums as often as regulars to get that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt it. Most of the books that have mistakenly lacked references to regaining Willpower during sleep due to the master copy of the rules chapter being based on vampire have added references to it in the errata stage. It would also be easy to include a passage in something like half-Damned saying something like &quot;ghouls, unlike vampires, do regain a point of Willpower when they sleep.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T09:54:33-08:00","id":1000854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1000766#post1000766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense. My friends and I use 1E, so I suppose I mostly meant the 5 dot frenzy power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Level 4 and 5 in 2nd edition work on them. The first edition version, it's up to the ST if they can use the level 5 power to put a werewolf in or out of Death Rage, or invoke or remove a fear response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T10:25:08-08:00","id":1000870,"title":"","content":"You might be able to justify Animalism 1 allowing a vampire to <i>understand</i> a werewolf in Urhan form, but definitely not command them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:15:10-08:00","id":1001795,"title":"","content":"So, something came up in a play by post game I'm running, and I already know how I plan to rule, but I'm curious to see other STs' opinions on the matter.<br /> <br /> If a human under the effects of Sanguinary Invigoration (page 159) donates blood, does the stored blood retain the properties granted to it by the Scale (namely, treating the Blood Potency of a vampire who drinks it as four dots lower for the purposes of feeding restrictions, four dots higher for the purposes of smelling it, and counting as the Vitae of the vampire who's Vitae was used to perform the Scale for the purposes of Vitae Addiction and Blood Bonds)? As a follow up, since the quantity of stored blood required to add up to one Vitae is dependent on the Blood Potency of the vampire drinking it, would the vampire treat their Blood Potency as four dots lower for this purpose as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T10:08:08-08:00","id":1001829,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd rule that once out of the body, the blood loses all properties granted by the scale for precisely the properties you mention. Otherwise it'd always be sufficient for a Vampire to lick blood off of the floor or walls rather than drink from a living Vessel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T10:42:59-08:00","id":1001840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001829#post1001829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd rule that once out of the body, the blood loses all properties granted by the scale for precisely the properties you mention. Otherwise it'd always be sufficient for a Vampire to lick blood off of the floor or walls rather than drink from a living Vessel.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> sufficient to lick blood off the floor and walls, provided it has been out of the body for less than a night and you can get [Blood Potency x2] Pints. Good luck licking two pints off the walls though.<br /> <br /> I'm not asking about whether cold or stored blood is worth Vitae, RAW is already perfectly clear on that. I'm asking specifically about the effects of Sanguinary Invigoration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-11-2016, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:32:45-08:00","id":1001857,"title":"","content":"Considering the concoction has to be injected in the human within 10 minutes or it's useless, and the effects only last for one week within the human I'm inclined to think that enhanced blood is not meant to be stored. If the blood is stored I would immediately have its bonuses drop incrementally by one after 10 minutes at a rate of 1 per night or so and after a week it's generically donated week-old blood. If they want it to last longer, they're going to have to research a new scale for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T11:47:56-08:00","id":1001863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001857#post1001857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the concoction has to be injected in the human within 10 minutes or it's useless, and the effects only last for one week within the human I'm inclined to think that enhanced blood is not meant to be stored. If the blood is stored I would immediately have its bonuses drop incrementally by one after 10 minutes at a rate of 1 per night or so and after a week it's generically donated week-old blood. If they want it to last longer, they're going to have to research a new scale for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Personally, I ruled that it retains the full effects for one week and then returns to functioning like regular stored blood, but the slow drop in benefits is a cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T12:40:15-08:00","id":1001881,"title":"","content":"Stored Vitae is the same as cold blood by RAW.<br /> <br /> To me, this indicates that it loses the magical effects of being Vitae once it reaches that point. The power clearly relies on the Vampire's Vitae in the target's system (even inflicting Vinculum on anyone who drinks from the mortal), so I would allow it to work for a few minutes after leaving the body before going inert and basically just being normal cold blood.<br /> <br /> But then, I do tend towards a harsher reading of the cold blood rules than some people according to previous threads. I've never been fond of the blood bags as health potions thing that some vampire games seem to allow, and the &quot;cold blood&quot; rules in 2e seem designed partially to make it an impractical strategy.<br /> <br /> So I'm biased in that I don't really want vampires running around with vials of blood potions of any sort, but that's how I'd probably run it in my games based on my interpretation and understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T12:54:29-08:00","id":1001888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001881#post1001881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stored Vitae is the same as cold blood by RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it as stored blood counts as cold blood that has been out of the body for more than a few minutes but less than a full night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001881#post1001881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, this indicates that it loses the magical effects of being Vitae once it reaches that point. The power clearly relies on the Vampire's Vitae in the target's system (even inflicting Vinculum on anyone who drinks from the mortal), so I would allow it to work for a few minutes after leaving the body before going inert and basically just being normal cold blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001881#post1001881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, I do tend towards a harsher reading of the cold blood rules than some people according to previous threads. I've never been fond of the blood bags as health potions thing that some vampire games seem to allow, and the &amp;quot;cold blood&amp;quot; rules in 2e seem designed partially to make it an impractical strategy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's consistent with the intent. The sheer volume of blood required to sustain a vampire on stored blood makes it completely impractical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001881#post1001881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm biased in that I don't really want vampires running around with vials of blood potions of any sort, but that's how I'd probably run it in my games based on my interpretation and understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, it's a reasonable interpretation.<br /> <br /> So, related question: If we take Sanguinary Invigoration out of the equation, would folks allow a BP6 vampire to gain a point of Vitae by drinking 12 pints of cryogenically stored Kindred blood, without having to spend Willpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:21:22-08:00","id":1001906,"title":"","content":"Cryogenically stored vitae IS cold blood. I would count it as vitae for purposes of successfully feeding them but I'd incorporate a blood potency minimum of the cryogenically frozen blood to be nourishing. (like no more than two blood potency lower than the consuming vampire.) Since there's no means of instantly gauging someone's blood potency anymore either, finding someone suitable to take their vitae to store is going to take considerable time and effort to prepare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:36:02-08:00","id":1001914,"title":"","content":"Protean 3 and 4<br /> <br /> After you use Protean 3 to change into a wolf or whatever, can you take on aspects using Protean 2 or 4? Can you skip using 2 before 4 if you're using 3, if your level 2 changes are traits of the beast you already used level 3 to turn into?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10328-bkwrm79","name":"bkwrm79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T13:58:37-08:00","id":1001922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001906#post1001906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cryogenically stored vitae IS cold blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's what I said...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001906#post1001906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would count it as vitae for purposes of successfully feeding them but I'd incorporate a blood potency minimum of the cryogenically frozen blood to be nourishing. (like no more than two blood potency lower than the consuming vampire.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Why? The rules for cold blood already cover vampires of higher Blood Potency needing more to derive nourishment from it, and the rules for feeding restrictions do allow vampires of Vitae 6+ to gain sustained s from non-Kindred blood by spending Willpower equal to the Vitae gained. In my mind there is no question of whether a BP6 vampire can gain a point of Vitae from 12 pints of stored blood. The question is if they need to spend a point of Willpower if the donor of the stored blood was another vampire. Or, like, say they have Unnatural Affinity for werewolves and the donor was a werewolf. Does stored/cold blood &quot;remember&quot; what type of Creature it came from, is what I'm getting at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001906#post1001906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since there's no means of instantly gauging someone's blood potency anymore either, finding someone suitable to take their vitae to store is going to take considerable time and effort to prepare.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why the donor's Blood Potency would matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-11-2016, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T14:10:51-08:00","id":1001933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bkwrm79</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001914#post1001914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protean 3 and 4<br /> <br /> After you use Protean 3 to change into a wolf or whatever, can you take on aspects using Protean 2 or 4?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bkwrm79</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001914#post1001914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you skip using 2 before 4 if you're using 3, if your level 2 changes are traits of the beast you already used level 3 to turn into?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Whether or not you have 3 active doesn't really matter, you have to have 2 active to activate 4. But, you don't have to manifest any of your Protean 2 traits it you don't want to. So you can sprout giant bat wings without needing to also have a monkey tail, Webbed limbs, and eccholocation if you want, but it still costs a total of 2 Vitae (and if you find you need that echolocation later in the scene, you've already paid for it and can manifest it if you want). Being a Wolf doesn't affect that either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T15:37:02-08:00","id":1001955,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt; What? Why? The rules for cold blood already cover vampires of higher Blood Potency needing more to derive nourishment from it, and the rules for feeding restrictions do allow vampires of Vitae 6+ to gain sustained s from non-Kindred blood by spending Willpower equal to the Vitae gained. In my mind there is no question of whether a BP6 vampire can gain a point of Vitae from 12 pints of stored blood. The question is if they need to spend a point of Willpower if the donor of the stored blood was another vampire. Or, like, say they have Unnatural Affinity for werewolves and the donor was a werewolf. Does stored/cold blood &quot;remember&quot; what type of Creature it came from, is what I'm getting at. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Aside from Vitae Reliquary, there's really no mechanics for storing vitae in second edition other than it breaking down into generic blood. Stored blood is rudimentary cryogenics already but it carries a lifespan. Some random vampire who tosses their vitae into a bag, mixes in some anti-coagulants, and sticks it in a freezer is going to have it break down into a mix of human and/or animal blood. If that's the scenario you're talking about then yes they'd have to spend a willpower. But if you're talking about someone going out of their way to cryogenically preserve the eldritch properties of vitae to keep the vinculum and vitae addiction risks via (insert whatever in game methodology you use) if the situation falls upon me to mechanize I would install minimum requirements on the type of vitae that would be sufficient to feed a kindred who needs vitae for sustenance because it's easier to just say the stored vitae has to be X blood potency concentration than making a making a pint to ML to cc's per point of stored vitae chart. But with my group, this is the stuff where my players would have already written up the specifics and consulted with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T16:21:23-08:00","id":1001969,"title":"","content":"Considering they need to drink an absolute shitload of it, I don't think saying ex-vitae cold blood can nourish high-potency kindred without spending willpower is going to have <i>too</i> much impact on the game. I mean, it does potentially give an elder another way of dodging vinculum, but it's really roundabout.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'd totally have werewolf blood still count as werewolf blood when it's stored. By all accounts it keeps it's mystical properties like boiling in contact with silver outside of an uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T16:50:14-08:00","id":1001977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001969#post1001969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering they need to drink an absolute shitload of it, I don't think saying ex-vitae cold blood can nourish high-potency kindred without spending willpower is going to have <i>too</i> much impact on the game. I mean, it does potentially give an elder another way of dodging vinculum, but it's really roundabout.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'd totally have werewolf blood still count as werewolf blood when it's stored. By all accounts it keeps it's mystical properties like boiling in contact with silver outside of an uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you examine wolfblood ( or changeling or whatever ) under a microscope... does it show up as werewolf blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T16:57:23-08:00","id":1001983,"title":"","content":"Not under a microscope, no. Ephemeral stuff kind of flips the bird at conventional biology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:15:07-08:00","id":1001991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001983#post1001983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not under a microscope, no. Ephemeral stuff kind of flips the bird at conventional biology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire &quot;blood&quot;, vitae reverts to just totally human.. I assume so it's not a masquerade breech if suddenly there is alien blood at crime scenes. I assumed the same thing for other &quot;supernaturals&quot; or everyone would know that there is something out there that goes bump in the night. Blood would come up as inhuman or some subspecies of human. Which is why I asked on about werewolf blood. If you put it in a bag and bloodtested it... what would it come up as? If it comes up as non-human werewolf blood, then I would think it keeps it's properties, but that would mean that people know about supernaturals... How could they not? <br /> <br /> I think that cold blood also is the way it is because the life force is gone. it takes more blood to get that life force to make it the vitae which vampires live off. Because vitae is not blood. Blood is just the medium by which the transfer the energy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T17:38:56-08:00","id":1002003,"title":"","content":"I'd say yes to all as long as it's within the one week duration of the scale, though it would be far less nourishing(raw Vitae gained) per unit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 11-11-2016, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T18:59:42-08:00","id":1002041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1001991#post1001991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but that would mean that people know about supernaturals... How could they not?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>do</i> know about them. That's the thing. You get weird blood at a crime scene and it gets hushed up and nobody talks about it, but the rumours spread.<br /> <br /> Werewolf blood registers as human to all known forensic techniques, but it's <i>not</i>, and to other supernaturals that's an important distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T21:22:45-08:00","id":1002104,"title":"","content":"Doesn't vampire blood not show up as just normal human blood, but instead is tonnes of different individuals blood when they test it forensically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T22:26:53-08:00","id":1002122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1002104#post1002104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't vampire blood not show up as just normal human blood, but instead is tonnes of different individuals blood when they test it forensically?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what I remember it shows up as a mix of the blood from whoever they've drunk from recently, but it starts decaying in the vampire's system, so unless freshly gained the blood will appear quite old. If a vampire has only fed from a single person or animal recently though the blood would just appear to be the blood of that person or animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T04:10:44-08:00","id":1002174,"title":"","content":"So once again, this is my interpretation of some fuzzy bits of game lore.<br /> <br /> The thing that nourishes Vampires is, basically, the life force within blood rather than purely the blood itself. It gets filtered out when drunk and made into Vitae. This life force fades very quickly, which is why cold blood is so much less potent than stuff taken directly from a living thing (or another vampire, since it's already been purified). So no matter where the blood came from, the nourishing aspect of it (how much Vitae you get) drops to &quot;cold blood&quot; a few minutes after the body dies or the blood leaves the body. So cold blood from a vampire, to me, would require Willpower for someone BP 6+ to drink.<br /> <br /> If the blood has supernatural properties innate to it, like the aforementioned boiling when exposed to silver, that sticks around indefinitely, but the actual nourishing properties fade after a few minutes. It's just simply not &quot;living&quot; blood anymore, and that life is how Vampires sustain themselves.<br /> <br /> Again, that's just how I'd run it. Not for any balance or mechanical reasons, but it seems most consistent with the fluff in the book to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T04:50:14-08:00","id":1002186,"title":"","content":"Isn't the game quite explicit about that blood is only the vessel for Vitae? There's even a discipline based around stealing Vitae through breath drinking (similar to how the Strix does it), as well as a merit to gain Vitae from eating the liver of a human. There's also a bloodline that stores Vitae in fat tissue and can consume flesh instead of blood to gain Vitae.<br /> And, notably, Vitae is latin for life, not blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T05:19:39-08:00","id":1002189,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it really comes down to &quot;Are you willing to say that blood that has contained vitae has enough residual mojo to be recharged to that state more easily by those who normally find the process strenuous enough to require willpower?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T07:25:02-08:00","id":1002211,"title":"","content":"I don't remember where I read it but I swear I read somewhere that vitae stops having mystical properties after it's been outside of a valid storing thing (vampire, ghoul, strix, blood magic relic, etc) for about a day. It's the rule I use when I run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T07:54:38-08:00","id":1002214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1002186#post1002186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't the game quite explicit about that blood is only the vessel for Vitae? There's even a discipline based around stealing Vitae through breath drinking (similar to how the Strix does it), as well as a merit to gain Vitae from eating the liver of a human. There's also a bloodline that stores Vitae in fat tissue and can consume flesh instead of blood to gain Vitae.<br /> And, notably, Vitae is latin for life, not blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is perfectly explicit that Vitae is life force and it is what vampires actually feed on, blood is just the medium they get it from. Of course, it's also explicit that a vampire's Vitae is so inexorably bound to their blood that Strix can't feed on them via breath drinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T07:59:51-08:00","id":1002219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1002211#post1002211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember where I read it but I swear I read somewhere that vitae stops having mystical properties after it's been outside of a valid storing thing (vampire, ghoul, strix, blood magic relic, etc) for about a day. It's the rule I use when I run.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for cold blood. They say blood that has been out of the body for more than a few minutes, but no more than a day, contains only small amounts of Vitae, which is why it takes such a large volume of cold blood to equal one Vitae. It also says that cryogenically stored blood is &quot;similarly unpalatable&quot;, which reads to me like it is similar to blood that has been out of the body for more than a few minutes but no more than a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:23:36-08:00","id":1003438,"title":"","content":"What is the <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Half-Damned book about ?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:24:38-08:00","id":1003439,"title":"","content":"Ghouls, revenants and dhampir and how to play them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-15-2016, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T19:44:45-08:00","id":1004211,"title":"","content":"outside of blood healing is a ghoul mortal when taking damage (scoured &quot;Blood and smoke&quot; and the second edition core book, still need advice)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T19:52:35-08:00","id":1004213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1004211#post1004211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">outside of blood healing is a ghoul mortal when taking damage (scoured &quot;Blood and smoke&quot; and the second edition core book, still need advice)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but they can use resilience to avoid aggravated damage if they have it in their repertoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T05:40:38-08:00","id":1004349,"title":"","content":"do ghouls still frenzy <br /> they don't get bonus stats since they've got no BP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T05:49:59-08:00","id":1004352,"title":"","content":"Frenzy is the Beast taking control. Ghouls do not have a Beast and can't frenzy. (Though it's a completely valid question since Ghouls can use Disciplines such as Animalism and Auspex without a Beast despite the fluff describing those Disciplines as using the character's Beast.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T06:06:11-08:00","id":1004363,"title":"","content":"Normally, no. But they can be imbued with a paroxysm of rage if affected by powers (like Animalism) that enable a vampire to infect others with their Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T08:39:22-08:00","id":1005715,"title":"","content":"would a 200 Kg Gangrel be size 6 or 7<br /> what maximum size could a human possibly reach","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T08:53:06-08:00","id":1005719,"title":"","content":"Size is tricky. The animal stat blocks lists a 150lb Cougar as the same size as a 400lb African Lion or even larger Tiger.<br /> Here is a reference for large people, though I wouldn't use these necessarily as <i>healthy</i> peop<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_the_heaviest_people\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_o...eaviest_people</a><br /> <br /> Back to Animal stats though, they list Bear(assuming brown because that's what most people think of) at Size 7 and 6-800lbs is not uncommon for coastal bears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 11-20-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T09:31:19-08:00","id":1005734,"title":"","content":"Six, with the giant merit, is the biggest humans can reach by RAW and probably by realism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T09:47:36-08:00","id":1005742,"title":"","content":"Size is a weird scale since it seems to be based on some sort of effective volume rather than actual volume or weight. A spear has Size 4, which is the same as people under ~150 cm. The spear being extremely long compensates for lack of volume and weight. The scale is also exponential, so Size 6 covers a larger span than Size 5. For gameplay purposes, though, I'd say humans can't become larger than Size 6, even though some people with gigantism and some people on Rathamus' list probably reaches Size 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T11:34:05-08:00","id":1005772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1005715#post1005715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would a 200 Kg Gangrel be size 6 or 7<br /> what maximum size could a human possibly reach</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a character with the giant merit in, I think, Chicago - but instead of being a Shaquille, he's morbidly obese.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, you can rename merits as the <b>ChroD corebook</b> featuring the <b>God Machine Chronicle</b>, promotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T12:33:06-08:00","id":1005806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1005715#post1005715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would a 200 Kg Gangrel be size 6 or 7<br /> what maximum size could a human possibly reach</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Guinness, the tallest woman in the world was 8 ft 1 in. tall but she had scoliosis. The tallest man was also, by last official record, 8 ft. 11 in., however, his coffin in was over 10 ft. long to accommodate his height. The heaviest people in the world usually weigh between 1100 and 1300 lb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-20-2016, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T13:24:21-08:00","id":1005832,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Wadlow\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Wadlow</a>, the aforementioned tallest man who ever lived, I could easily see being size 7. <br /> <br /> I mean seriously, look at the dude:<br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5c/Robert_Wadlow.jpg/350px-Robert_Wadlow.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The guy standing next to him here is almost <i>6 feet tall</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T14:38:13-08:00","id":1005861,"title":"","content":"Fortunately we do now have Advanced Merits. There's some special things in vampire that can grant extra Size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T22:33:27-08:00","id":1007043,"title":"","content":"Hey, so I was wondering about what happens to a vampire who has a body part amputated. Basically, as part of a hair brained scheme, my character is planning on cutting of part or the entirety of his hand. I know you can heal aggravated damage, but would that be aggravated damage? Can he grow it back as per healing aggravated damage? In character I'm working under the assumption &quot;no&quot; but mechanically, it'd be nice to know either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T22:37:20-08:00","id":1007045,"title":"","content":"Yes. Aggravated damage includes removal and destruction of limbs. Sawing off your hand would be considered doing Aggravated damage to yourself. It would heal as Aggravated damage does, as well. Though you can spend a point of Willpower to avoid that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T22:40:48-08:00","id":1007049,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the quick response! I probably won't spend the willpower, since the point is he needs a dismembered hand as planted somewhere as part of his scheme, but that's super helpful for future note!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T23:41:22-08:00","id":1007061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1007045#post1007045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Aggravated damage includes removal and destruction of limbs. Sawing off your hand would be considered doing Aggravated damage to yourself. It would heal as Aggravated damage does, as well. Though you can spend a point of Willpower to avoid that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't it count as lethal for a vampire though, as per page 90?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-22T23:55:12-08:00","id":1007069,"title":"","content":"I thought aggravated just because it's not getting stabbed through the hand, I'm talking about straight up REMOVING the hand, which seems like, even as a vampire, might be kinda hard to get over. Lethal seems fairly easy to get over considering the level of damage. That's why I was thinking lower aggravated damage, since it'd be hard to get over, but the rest of his body would be fine. Would it be a high level of lethal damage instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T00:23:52-08:00","id":1007076,"title":"","content":"Page 91: &quot;In dramatic instances, severed limbs regenerate or even simply reattach (if she\u2019s able to heal the entire injury in a turn).&quot;<br /> Since Aggravated damage can't be healed in a turn it stands to reason that Lethal damage is enough to sever limbs. It makes sense since Aggravated damage is only dealt by supernatural sources or extreme damage to the body's structural integrity (i.e. by upgrading damage taken after having taken full Lethal). While the removal of a limb IS a huge thing, it doesn't really affect the body's structural integrity.<br /> In fact, I'd rule that careful amputation of limbs would only deal Lethal to mortals as well. It's not the loss of biomass that's harmful, it's the wounds inflicted that leads to loss of limbs. Otherwise everyone who has lost limbs would have permanently lost Health levels as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T01:17:30-08:00","id":1007094,"title":"","content":"Fascinating! That makes a lot of sense actually. Oh man, this is awesome. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12572-electrographic","name":"Electrographic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T05:03:30-08:00","id":1007171,"title":"","content":"Sure, Lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T07:49:01-08:00","id":1007238,"title":"","content":"While I don't think there's necessarily a problem with having it be lethal, I figure I'd provide a different perspective here.<br /> <br /> I think the cause and effect is backwards. Losing a limb doesn't cause aggravated damage. Aggravated damage causes the loss of limb.<br /> <br /> I'm basing this off Arm Wrack/Leg Wrack:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ending the Tilt: If the Tilt is inflicted as a result of an attack,<br /> mark an X under the leftmost Health box affected by that attack.<br /> The Tilt ends when the damage that caused it has healed. <b>If the<br /> damage that inflicts this Tilt is aggravated, the character loses<br /> the use of his arm (<i>or completely loses his arm</i>) permanently.</b> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Granted, the damage downgrade of Vampires doesn't represent less structural damage so much as being less affected by injuries (I believe the excuse given is that they don't need their internal organs and such), so maybe if it would have done the Aggravated damage before downgrading, then it removes the limb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T10:10:38-08:00","id":1007303,"title":"","content":"Remember that aggravated damage is downgraded to lethal for vampires if it's not from a bane, just like the lethal-bashing downgrade, so it might be that losing a limb normally is represented with agg damage, but for a vampire that's represented as lethal damage, and can be healed appropriately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T11:17:21-08:00","id":1007336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1007238#post1007238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't think there's necessarily a problem with having it be lethal, I figure I'd provide a different perspective here.<br /> <br /> I think the cause and effect is backwards. Losing a limb doesn't cause aggravated damage. Aggravated damage causes the loss of limb.<br /> <br /> I'm basing this off Arm Wrack/Leg Wrack:<br /> <br /> Granted, the damage downgrade of Vampires doesn't represent less structural damage so much as being less affected by injuries (I believe the excuse given is that they don't need their internal organs and such), so maybe if it would have done the Aggravated damage before downgrading, then it removes the limb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is how I look at it as well. That also means even careful amputation would need to be aggravated for humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T11:25:03-08:00","id":1007343,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily. I think in combat the aggravated damage is needed to get through the bone in one swing. Surgical amputations involve saws and crap and would probably be an extended action. As would holding someone down and hacking away with a machete, I guess. <br /> <br /> On the other hand amputations <i>do</i> take a long time to heal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:26:12-08:00","id":1007803,"title":"","content":"I'm currently building an NPC for my game and I had a random question. I have this NPC that is undercover in the carthian movement but is really with the ordo can this npc have meirts from both covenants ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T13:11:31-08:00","id":1007820,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think so.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously they'll get lynched if the Carthians find out, so it's a sort of trade off.<br /> <br /> Also, NPC. Doesn't really matter if they're balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T14:09:53-08:00","id":1007834,"title":"","content":"You're allowed to have Status with multiple Covenants, so long as the total of all of them doesn't pass 5. So for every dot of Carthian status they have, they have one less they can get in Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> The Covenat Merits tend to only have one dot of Status as a prerequisite, so you could probably get from more than one, but you aren't going to be as trusted by either group, and if you share what you learn with your other Covenants they will probably murder you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T14:36:07-08:00","id":1007843,"title":"","content":"That's <i>open</i> multiple membership though. There's nothing stopping you having too much status if nobody <i>knows</i> about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T17:33:16-08:00","id":1007885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1007843#post1007843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's <i>open</i> multiple membership though. There's nothing stopping you having too much status if nobody <i>knows</i> about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the higher up in status you get within one covenant, the harder it also is to hide it from the general public, at which point those in other covenants are going to find out. That's sort of the point of status. The more you have the more you've (theoretically) done to advance the covenant's goals. Sometimes the overlap wouldn't matter, particularly if the covenants are allied but other times it could. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T17:33:48-08:00","id":1007886,"title":"","content":"That's why you take Right of Return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T17:47:33-08:00","id":1007888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1007843#post1007843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's <i>open</i> multiple membership though. There's nothing stopping you having too much status if nobody <i>knows</i> about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, it is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her combined dots in one type of Status (City, Clan, or Covenant)<br /> cannot exceed five, and she may never have as many dots in her<br /> affiliated group as she does to the group to which she belongs. </div> </div> </div>There is no mention of &quot;open&quot; affiliation or exceptions to the rule. So by RAW, you can't have more than five. If you want to house rule that &quot;secret&quot; affiliation doesn't count, however, have at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T17:54:19-08:00","id":1007890,"title":"","content":"You can't seem to have more than four in one group, and that's providing you have five in your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T02:11:22-08:00","id":1007996,"title":"","content":"You can't even have more than two in your secondary group since the dot total is capped at five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T02:15:24-08:00","id":1007998,"title":"","content":"It's a <i>social</i> merit. You can't get more than a given amount of status because the rest of the covenant is concerned about split loyalties. <br /> <br /> If nobody <i>knows</i> about it, what's stopping you? You're a mole. It's essentially <i>fake</i> status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T03:26:34-08:00","id":1008013,"title":"","content":"That is the more logical way to handle it, and definitely a house rule that I don't see why any ST wouldn't allow. We were just discussing how it works RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T03:44:06-08:00","id":1008019,"title":"","content":"How is this for a Protean 2 trait:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Maw:</b> Your mouth enlongates and your teeth grow, giving your face a somewhat canine or similar shape. You don't need a grapple to use your bite attack, and your bite can initiate a grapple.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of also adding +1 damage to the bite and/or don't allow careful feeding. Thoughts?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T04:39:52-08:00","id":1008026,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'd allow it to bypass the need to initiate a grapple as well as grant a double bonus to initiating a grapple.<br /> <br /> I'd either allow it to bypass the need to establish a grapple for feeding purposes. Or grant a +2 to initiating a grapple and choose at the time the trait is acquired that they do an additional +1 damage each round after grapple is established or they assign a -1 penalty on most attempts to break the grapple","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:27:05-08:00","id":1008036,"title":"","content":"They're literally copying how werewolves work in their canine forms. &quot;I grapple with my mouth&quot; basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T05:40:49-08:00","id":1008039,"title":"","content":"It's actually how it works for all vampires in Frenzy already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:13:20-08:00","id":1008048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1008036#post1008036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're literally copying how werewolves work in their canine forms. &amp;quot;I grapple with my mouth&amp;quot; basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of the rule that allows creatures with protruded/elongated jaws to successfully bite someone without having to grapple them first and that vampires have to grapple first before biting. I fail to see the point or necessity in giving them an additional bonus to grappling someone to facilitate the act of biting someone when the power in question already eliminates the need to successfully grapple before biting in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:35:25-08:00","id":1008053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1008048#post1008048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of the rule that allows creatures with protruded/elongated jaws to successfully bite someone without having to grapple them first and that vampires have to grapple first before biting. I fail to see the point or necessity in giving them an additional bonus to grappling someone to facilitate the act of biting someone when the power in question already eliminates the need to successfully grapple before biting in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said before, all vampires already gain the very same benefits whenever they Frenzy. I think it is very much something Protean 2 should be able to do, even if it's a bit redundant since most vampires Frenzy during battle anyway (in my experience).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:40:32-08:00","id":1008054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1008048#post1008048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware of the rule that allows creatures with protruded/elongated jaws to successfully bite someone without having to grapple them first and that vampires have to grapple first before biting. I fail to see the point or necessity in giving them an additional bonus to grappling someone to facilitate the act of biting someone when the power in question already eliminates the need to successfully grapple before biting in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are not understanding it. You can make a bite attack without a grapple.That's one thing. Also, you can use your bite to grapple, bitting someon to inmovilize it, for example, like a dog can. As said, is literally how bite works for wolfs and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T09:19:35-08:00","id":1008130,"title":"","content":"Seems like a pretty legit Protean trait to me. I would definitely say it prevents subtle feeding, and probably make it a 0L weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T11:25:38-08:00","id":1008218,"title":"","content":"Thanks for everyone's input. I will add the Subtle Feeding prohibition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T16:44:36-08:00","id":1008718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1007886#post1007886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why you take Right of Return.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T16:48:15-08:00","id":1008719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1008718#post1008718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Carthian Law Merit. Makes it so your dots in Carthian Status don't count towards the normal five dot limit in Covenant Status, so you can have up to 5 in Carthians and 5 total between any other Covenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T04:03:26-08:00","id":1008874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1008719#post1008719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a Carthian Law Merit. Makes it so your dots in Carthian Status don't count towards the normal five dot limit in Covenant Status, so you can have up to 5 in Carthians and 5 total between any other Covenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Secret of the Covenants stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T04:47:23-08:00","id":1008883,"title":"","content":"Page 116 in VtR 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:20:35-08:00","id":1010298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=996767#post996767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The brain does not control the vampire's bodily functions by way of neural stimuli, no. Vampires can in fact survive decapitation or destruction of the brain, though it would likely force them into torpor from being full on lethal damage, and would take a lot of Vitae to regenerate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Oh ho. This is interesting. Sorry for dredging up something from almost last month, but I need to poke at this.<br /> <br /> In every vampire game I've seen going back to VtM a decapitation was fatal as it separated the brain from the heart. Now, if the brain is not really a big deal, and the head only the convenient spot where the eyes, ears, nose and mouth (fangs) happen to be located, then that kinda changes how you go about fighting vampires. <br /> <br /> So, ok--if vampires are 100% magical (which seems to be the case), why would decapitation inflict full lethal anyway? It's just a head... maybe 11lbs of mass--less than half a leg and a smaller volume. If the brain has no significance whatsoever, and the heart (seat of vitae) is the real deal then how much damage might losing one's head actually do? (Sure, a lot of sensory tilts and some trouble feeding will ensue.)<br /> <br /> Second, do we have any evidence from the VtR literature that decapitation is instant death for vampires? Particularly VtR 2e?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:38:19-08:00","id":1010308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010298#post1010298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. Oh ho. This is interesting. Sorry for dredging up something from almost last month, but I need to poke at this.<br /> <br /> In every vampire game I've seen going back to VtM a decapitation was fatal as it separated the brain from the heart. Now, if the brain is not really a big deal, and the head only the convenient spot where the eyes, ears, nose and mouth (fangs) happen to be located, then that kinda changes how you go about fighting vampires.<br /> <br /> So, ok--if vampires are 100% magical (which seems to be the case), why would decapitation inflict full lethal anyway? It's just a head... maybe 11lbs of mass--less than half a leg and a smaller volume. If the brain has no significance whatsoever, and the heart (seat of vitae) is the real deal then how much damage might losing one's head actually do? (Sure, a lot of sensory tilts and some trouble feeding will ensue.)<br /> <br /> Second, do we have any evidence from the VtR literature that decapitation is instant death for vampires? Particularly VtR 2e?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that Decapitation would fall under the Killing Blow rules; Auto-damage, and it might take a few hacks to actually lop off the head. Which isnt as easy as one might think. <br /> Also, I think that no creature can survive without a head in Chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:31:48-08:00","id":1010327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010298#post1010298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. Oh ho. This is interesting. Sorry for dredging up something from almost last month, but I need to poke at this.<br /> <br /> In every vampire game I've seen going back to VtM a decapitation was fatal as it separated the brain from the heart. Now, if the brain is not really a big deal, and the head only the convenient spot where the eyes, ears, nose and mouth (fangs) happen to be located, then that kinda changes how you go about fighting vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's pretty common in vampire fiction for that to be one of the go-to ways to kill them, so I think it would be perfectly reasonable to rule that decapitation kills vampires. Functionality, I don't think it makes much difference anyway (more on why in a bit). But yeah, there's nothing in the rules as written saying decapitation causes final death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010298#post1010298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, ok--if vampires are 100% magical (which seems to be the case), why would decapitation inflict full lethal anyway? It's just a head... maybe 11lbs of mass--less than half a leg and a smaller volume. If the brain has no significance whatsoever, and the heart (seat of vitae) is the real deal then how much damage might losing one's head actually do? (Sure, a lot of sensory tilts and some trouble feeding will ensue.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got the cause and effect reversed. Decapitation doesn't cause full lethal, full lethal is required to decapitate. Actually, Chronicles of Darkness doesn't actually have a rule for decapitation (and this is why the question of decapitation killing vampires or not is purely academic). For the sake of internal consistency, any rule for how to decapitate a vampire would need to apply to humans as well, since their anatomy is the same and there's no reason it should be easier to destroy or remove a vampire's head than a human's. And auto-kill buttons like that can be problematic from a game design perspective because if they're more efficient than normal combat they'll always be used and if they're less efficient they'll never be used. That said, for the sake of verisimilitude, decapitation should be possible. So, Chronicles of Darkness treats it as a largely narrative effect. If you kill your target (that is to say, if you cause aggravated damage in their last health box), the final blow can be described as decapitation if you like.<br /> <br /> Now, the Arm Wrack and Leg Wrack Tilts are permanent if the damage that caused them was aggravated - either dismembering, destroying, or otherwise making the affected appendage useless. So we can expand this line of thinking to the head as well. If the last health box is filled with aggravated damage, the head can be removed or destroyed. Of course, this happens to line up perfectly with the narrative take on decapitation, since full aggravated damage kills the target.<br /> <br /> Vampires, however, are a slightly different case. They take lethal damage from non-magical sources that would do aggravated to mortal humans (and bashing from non-magical sources that would do lethal). That damage reduction doesn't occur because the body is less significant harmed, however; the same stuff happens to the vampire's body, it's just marked off as less severe because vampires don't need most of their body to survive. That means, theoretically, a vampire should actually gain the &quot;permanent&quot; version of Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack if the damage that causes it is lethal, but would have been aggravated to a human (&quot;permanent&quot; here in quotation marks because the limb can be regrow with Vitae expenditure). By extension, filling a vampire's last health box with lethal damage should be able to destroy or remove a vampire's head, if the damage would have been aggravated to a mortal. That's enough damage to cause Torpor, but not Final Death, which means the head can be regrown with Vitae expenditure, just as an arm or leg can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010298#post1010298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, do we have any evidence from the VtR literature that decapitation is instant death for vampires? Particularly VtR 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as far as I'm aware. It's just the most internally consistent interpretation of the rules for how vampires take damage, from my perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-30-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T15:18:15-08:00","id":1010362,"title":"","content":"I mostly considered decapitaction to be Final Death because general lore says it is. Even the real life rituals that people did to suspected vampires tended to include decapitation along with the stake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T15:56:58-08:00","id":1010379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010362#post1010362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly considered decapitaction to be Final Death because general lore says it is. Even the real life rituals that people did to suspected vampires tended to include decapitation along with the stake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to go that way myself. Not that there hasn't been the odd exception (some of the Hammer Dracula films IIRC).<br /> <br /> I can see it making an interesting Devotion, though.<br /> Something like:<br /> <br /> <b>TWO PARTS, ONE MIND</b><br /> <i>(Protean 4, Resilience 3)</i><br /> The vampire\u2019s body has completely transcended its mortal limitations: Decapitation no longer brings Final Death. The two parts can exist independently forever, if need be. <br /> Furthermore, the connection between head and body is not necessarily severed. <br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: None. Wits + Blood Potency, to control the headless body (lasts until Sunrise)<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Failure</b>: the Vampire is unable to control his body. His head still functions as normal (sight, hearing, speech per GM\u2019s discretion). Obviously it is incapable of movement.<br /> <b>Success</b>: As long as the eyes can see the body they can control it. All actions suffer a die penalty between -1 to -3 (due to spatial differences between the heads viewpoint and the bodies location).<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The vampire has complete control of her body for the rest of the night. No sight of it is needed, as the body, somehow, has a mystical awareness of itself. There are no dice penalties.<br /> <br /> The head can be reattached by placing it on top of the neck and healing all damage that caused the decapitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","user":"FutureBondVillain","date":". 11-30-2016, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T16:13:32-08:00","id":1010385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010362#post1010362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly considered decapitaction to be Final Death because general lore says it is. Even the real life rituals that people did to suspected vampires tended to include decapitation along with the stake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's totally reasonable. Not the way I would run it, but it does make perfect sense within the context of vampire lore.<br /> <br /> For me, it just doesn't make sense for vampires to need their brains to survive <i>and</i> for called shots to the head to benefit from vampires' damage reduction. If one goes, they'd both have to go for it to be internally consistent to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-30-2016, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T17:40:01-08:00","id":1010420,"title":"","content":"The amount of damage required to decapitate a vampire without Resilience would definitely seem to kill a Vampire as effectively as a wooden stake through the heart does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T17:45:52-08:00","id":1010424,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the very interesting, and thorough, perspectives. It sounds like the best balance is in admitting there is no called shot for decapitation (though I seem to remember ones for heart and head) and expressing vampiric toughness through narration.<br /> <br /> For example: Arthurian legend has quite a bit of sudden decapitation in it. We can assume a few things by this then. That decapitees were not vampires. Or the swords were patently magical. Or previous blows caused substantial injury that was just not apparent or effective yet (another trope).<br /> <br /> And continuing the example... that devotion, FutureBondVillian, would be the Green Knight right there.<br /> <br /> I think there could be some good material for body horror in this area, but only once or twice before it got old. I was imagining a headless vampire trying to drink by sticking it's stump into a victim....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:02:35-08:00","id":1010433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010424#post1010424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the very interesting, and thorough, perspectives. It sounds like the best balance is in admitting there is no called shot for decapitation (though I seem to remember ones for heart and head) and expressing vampiric toughness through narration.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are called shot rules, including called shots to the head and heart. It's just that they don't cause decapitation. A called shot to the head has a -3 penalty and reduces the damage threshold for inflicting the Stunned Tilt by 1. A called shot to the heart has a -3 penalty and if the attack does at least 5 damage it pierces the heart. Which doesn't actually do anything beyond the normal amount of damage by RAW, unless the target is a vampire and the weapon is made of wood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010424#post1010424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example: Arthurian legend has quite a bit of sudden decapitation in it. We can assume a few things by this then. That decapitees were not vampires. Or the swords were patently magical. Or previous blows caused substantial injury that was just not apparent or effective yet (another trope).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Arthurian legend has the benefit of not being a tabletop roleplaying game, so it doesn't have to concern itself with balancing a combat system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-30-2016, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:46:48-08:00","id":1010446,"title":"","content":"Is there any reason a Vampire with Auspex 2 couldn't use it on themself, to discern things like mental control and whatnot? Or use Auspex 4 to determine things like their memories being False? (IC justification for doing so notwithstanding)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Really, it's a good question in general; can Vampires target themselves with their Disciplines, by default?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T18:53:45-08:00","id":1010454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010446#post1010446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any reason a Vampire with Auspex 2 couldn't use it on themself, to discern things like mental control and whatnot? Or use Auspex 4 to determine things like their memories being False? (IC justification for doing so notwithstanding)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Really, it's a good question in general; can Vampires target themselves with their Disciplines, by default?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. Although, I am in the camp that says it would be extremely ill-advised to attempt to target yourself with Dominate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T19:11:57-08:00","id":1010458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010454#post1010454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why not. Although, I am in the camp that says it would be extremely ill-advised to attempt to target yourself with Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could have its uses. Primarily in counteracting other mind control power. But likely with typical side effects, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T19:36:07-08:00","id":1010461,"title":"","content":"There are physical limitations, being inside one's own aura makes it difficult to read, and it's pretty difficult to make eye contact with yourself (unless you're a Tzimisce).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T19:47:10-08:00","id":1010463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010461#post1010461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are physical limitations, being inside one's own aura makes it difficult to read, and it's pretty difficult to make eye contact with yourself (unless you're a Tzimisce).</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just use a mirror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010458#post1010458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could have its uses. Primarily in counteracting other mind control power. But likely with typical side effects, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of reviving an old, at times heated argument, the reason I think it would be ill-advised is that in order to use Dominate on someone, you must Mezmerize them. That is to say, you must put them in a state of mind where their autonomy is suppressed and receptive to suggestion from an outside source; a state which clouds the subject's faculties in such a way that they don't clearly remember the events that transpired while they were in that state. I don't imagine a person in such a state would have the presence of mind necessary to actually give commands using Dominate. Which would mean attempting to Dominate yourself would leave you Mezmerized, waiting for someone to come along to tell you what to do, and otherwise pretty much just on auto-pilot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T20:41:04-08:00","id":1010473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010463#post1010463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the risk of reviving an old, at times heated argument, the reason I think it would be ill-advised is that in order to use Dominate on someone, you must Mezmerize them. That is to say, you must put them in a state of mind where their autonomy is suppressed and receptive to suggestion from an outside source; a state which clouds the subject's faculties in such a way that they don't clearly remember the events that transpired while they were in that state. I don't imagine a person in such a state would have the presence of mind necessary to actually give commands using Dominate. Which would mean attempting to Dominate yourself would leave you Mezmerized, waiting for someone to come along to tell you what to do, and otherwise pretty much just on auto-pilot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh I don't see the mesmerized condition as automatically shutting you down, myself, the wording implies you just become a little meek, in my mind. The only time you act hypnotized is when doing something you wouldn't normally do due to the condition, and I imagine if you're commanding yourself you probably want to do what you're telling yourself to do. I do agree it'd make everything kinda hazy afterward, though, which can be a fun issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T20:54:12-08:00","id":1010478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010473#post1010473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh I don't see the mesmerized condition as automatically shutting you down, myself, the wording implies you just become a little meek, in my mind. The only time you act hypnotized is when doing something you wouldn't normally do due to the condition, and I imagine if you're commanding yourself you probably want to do what you're telling yourself to do. I do agree it'd make everything kinda hazy afterward, though, which can be a fun issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may appear to act normally, but you're still in command receiving mode, which in my mind would make it kind of hard to give commands.<br /> <br /> Let me put it this way: I wouldn't allow a Ventrue with the Mezmerized Condition to use Dominate before the Condition was resolved. Doesn't matter if it's on herself or someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-01-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:05:35-08:00","id":1010483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010463#post1010463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could just use a mirror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dominate requires direct eye contact, it won't work through things like reflections and recordings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the risk of reviving an old, at times heated argument, the reason I think it would be ill-advised is that in order to use Dominate on someone, you must Mezmerize them. That is to say, you must put them in a state of mind where their autonomy is suppressed and receptive to suggestion from an outside source; a state which clouds the subject's faculties in such a way that they don't clearly remember the events that transpired while they were in that state.. </div> </div> </div>I will point out that the Mesmerised condition only blanks out memories if it is resolved, not if you allow it to fade naturally at the end of a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","user":"PrinceRaven","date":". 12-01-2016, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:05:35-08:00","id":1010484,"title":"","content":"Double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","user":"PrinceRaven","date":". 12-01-2016, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:34:52-08:00","id":1010500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010483#post1010483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate requires direct eye contact, it won't work through things like reflections and recordings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't work through recordings, but there's no reason it shouldn't work through reflections.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010483#post1010483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will point out that the Mesmerised condition only blanks out memories if it is resolved, not if you allow it to fade naturally at the end of a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you're referring to this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;If you resolve this Condition, gain a +3 die bonus to resist further attempts to Mesmerize you in the same scene; you also can\u2019t quite remember what happened while you were under the vampire\u2019s spell.&quot; </div> </div> </div>The two clauses in the sentence are separated by a semicolon, meaning they are independent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T21:52:41-08:00","id":1010508,"title":"","content":"There's always the option to make some sort of &quot;Autohypnosis&quot; Devotion (or something similar for other Disciplines) as a compromise, if folding the Beast inward seems too weird or unintuitive as a default ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T01:47:28-08:00","id":1010553,"title":"","content":"I would go the Devotion route. Self-suggestion is a thing after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T03:35:18-08:00","id":1010566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010483#post1010483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dominate requires direct eye contact, it won't work through things like reflections and recordings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of does. The very mechanics of seeing aside, mirrored sunglasses don't protect the wearer or hinder the user. And if you want to spend enough blood to install a trigger about following directions left on a recording to go perform an act after watching a certain television show or to do some activity until you hear a radio commercial, that's certainly valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T06:19:55-08:00","id":1010599,"title":"","content":"Mirrors ARE direct eye contact. Theyre just a redirection of the same light, really. Granted, it's less certain from a metaphysical standpoint. Regardless, Id allow it, even on others. And I still think mesmerized shouldnt prevent dominate uses but to each their own.<br /> <br /> Anyway auspex was the more important one to me regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T06:39:20-08:00","id":1010606,"title":"","content":"From a metaphysical standpoint, as far as vampires are concerned the reflection of a thing does not count as the thing. <br /> <br /> Exhibit A: Moonlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T07:10:51-08:00","id":1010619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010606#post1010606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a metaphysical standpoint, as far as vampires are concerned the reflection of a thing does not count as the thing. <br /> <br /> Exhibit A: Moonlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh thats not quite the same. Im pretty sure if you let sunlight in through a window and let it reflect off an actual mirror that reflection would still burn a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T08:12:28-08:00","id":1010649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010500#post1010500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't work through recordings, but there's no reason it shouldn't work through reflections.<br /> <br /> <br /> I assume you're referring to this:<br /> <br /> The two clauses in the sentence are separated by a semicolon, meaning they are independent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a huge thread about being able to dominate yourself. I am with Charlaquin that you are going to forget stuff once you do dominate yourself. So your will is crushed and you are susceptive to commends. In order to issue commands your will needs to be strong enough to impose the command. Your will is stronger than theirs sort of thing.. that is the very essence of dominate. So even if you say that you can dominate yourself, how could you give the command if you cant quite remember what you were doing? Everything is a little foggy... <br /> <br /> <br /> You could have someone else dominate you... though.. Why would you even want to, either way you aren't going to remember what was done or what you did...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T10:16:41-08:00","id":1010691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010433#post1010433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are called shot rules, including called shots to the head and heart. It's just that they don't cause decapitation. A called shot to the head has a -3 penalty and reduces the damage threshold for inflicting the Stunned Tilt by 1. A called shot to the heart has a -3 penalty and if the attack does at least 5 damage it pierces the heart. Which doesn't actually do anything beyond the normal amount of damage by RAW, unless the target is a vampire and the weapon is made of wood.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, but Arthurian legend has the benefit of not being a tabletop roleplaying game, so it doesn't have to concern itself with balancing a combat system.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, which was my first comment: that CofD handles these dicey matters of balance by shoving them onto Storyteller narration. I think that is a good thing. Full stop. So if you want to do Arthurian legend spread over CofD like a thick layer of Nutella, you have to do the 'Telling yourself--mechanics will only loosely guide. Again, only a quick at-hand example. <br /> <br /> The &quot;Storytelling solution&quot; solidly moves the game away from tactical simulation and quite intentionally redirects (as many of its sub-systems do) toward fast action, emotion and story. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T10:26:46-08:00","id":1010695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010606#post1010606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a metaphysical standpoint, as far as vampires are concerned the reflection of a thing does not count as the thing.<br /> <br /> Exhibit A: Moonlight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eheh, not exactly. It's magic, and while we know moonlight is reflected sunlight, from a magical perspective moonlight is its own thing (see: Lune). Also, to roil these waters... how do you know it's reflected sunlight? Because someone told you so. Might the moon actually shine with the light of Lune? Maybe. Depends on the story. People sure thought so until they came up with ways to test and a good, working hypothesis otherwise!<br /> <br /> Mirrorshades do not prevent Dominate from working, which would be an excellent point to mention if you could accidentally mesmerize.<br /> <br /> So yes, make a custom devotion if you want to dig into your own memories and sift through the damage done by your Kindred friends.... Or, hire someone you trust (or whom you can owe a boon to) to do it for you. There was an excellent (inspiring) example of this in the Kiddie Pool play thread on these forums, a while back.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T11:59:39-08:00","id":1010741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010695#post1010695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So yes, make a custom devotion if you want to dig into your own memories and sift through the damage done by your Kindred friends.... Or, hire someone you trust (or whom you can owe a boon to) to do it for you. There was an excellent (inspiring) example of this in the Kiddie Pool play thread on these forums, a while back.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>If you dug into your own memories, How would you remember what you ... remembered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T13:39:34-08:00","id":1010792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010741#post1010741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you dug into your own memories, How would you remember what you ... remembered?</div> </div> </div> </div>The exact same way those Ordo Dracut merits worked to enable them to go back and somehow retroactively &quot;know&quot; something they never saw was obfuscated or that their original memories were somehow tampered with sometime after the experience took place and unerringly detect exactly what was removed.<br /> <br /> I would not say the current discipline repertoire allows it, but I can see just about any discipline devotion in combination with Resilience being thrown together to allow a user to go back and discover they were victimized by a power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T15:10:08-08:00","id":1010839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010792#post1010792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The exact same way those Ordo Dracut merits worked to enable them to go back and somehow retroactively &quot;know&quot; something they never saw was obfuscated or that their original memories were somehow tampered with sometime after the experience took place and unerringly detect exactly what was removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not familiar with which merits you mean? I may have missed them in the book and I dont play Ordo much..I dont see any that allow that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010792#post1010792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not say the current discipline repertoire allows it, but I can see just about any discipline devotion in combination with Resilience being thrown together to allow a user to go back and discover they were victimized by a power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about allowing to make a devotion to cover a base that a different discipline covers. Wouldn't &quot;Knowing if you were messed with&quot; and &quot;digging out deep memories&quot; be Auspex? I mean, would you allow a protean devotion that would allow you to take control of another person's body? ( Dominate 5 ) or a Protean devotion to negate damage ( Resilience) while in... ooze form or something? Why make a devotion to mezmerize yourself so you can dig up memories you might have forgotten or so that you can know if you have been messed with because that's Auspex...<br /> <br /> Auspex 4: <i>By focusing, the vampire can drag up a full memory from the victim, including things that the victim has forgotten or that were suppressed by magic (though doing so takes a Clash of Wills).</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T15:20:01-08:00","id":1010840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010839#post1010839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not familiar with which merits you mean? I may have missed them in the book and I dont play Ordo much..I dont see any that allow that.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're from 1st Edition, in the Ordo Dracul Covenant book. I don't remember the specifics, but from what I remember they were &quot;memory palace&quot; kind of things, where you could periodically check to see if your memories marched the archived ones. Also the third Merit in the sequence made it impossible to read your mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T15:38:09-08:00","id":1010847,"title":"","content":"Amusingly, I've actually been toying with Devotions meant to recreate those (I could also do them as merits, but devotions are more acceptable, custom-wise, in the game they're meant to be used for)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:25:52-08:00","id":1010990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010500#post1010500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't work through recordings, but there's no reason it shouldn't work through reflections.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as has been brought up, with the obvious exception of certain Medusa interpretations, reflections usually do not work for things that require direct eyesight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The two clauses in the sentence are separated by a semicolon, meaning they are independent. </div> </div> </div>Independent but closely related. Personally, I believe said relation is that both pertain to the first clase in the sentence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010566#post1010566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It kind of does. The very mechanics of seeing aside, mirrored sunglasses don't protect the wearer or hinder the user.</div> </div> </div> </div>And? Directly looking through a transparent barrier and looking at someone's reflection in a mirror are not the same thing.<br /> That does bring up an interesting point, if you can dominate yourself through a mirror, could you accidentally dominate yourself while attempting to dominate someone wearing mirrored sunglasses? How about if they're standing next to a mirror or another reflective surface that is reflecting your eyes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you want to spend enough blood to install a trigger about following directions left on a recording to go perform an act after watching a certain television show or to do some activity until you hear a radio commercial, that's certainly valid. </div> </div> </div>It is explicitly stated in the rulebook that you cannot Dominate through a recording.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010619#post1010619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh thats not quite the same. Im pretty sure if you let sunlight in through a window and let it reflect off an actual mirror that reflection would still burn a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that all natural light is just reflected sunlight wouldn't that mean a vampire would burn indoors if the building was not completely lightproof?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T04:36:50-08:00","id":1011012,"title":"","content":"I think my point is a reflection more directly represents something, and sort of reflects it 'unchanged', as opposed to bits of light just bouncing off randomly for the sake of seeing things. Metaphysically, I see a mirror reflecting sunlight at a vampire as making more sense than glancing out an otherwise shade-covered window and being burned because to see anything outside technically means reflected sunlight. Similarly, I see a mirror as being fine for dominating. But that's just me, I realize it's a tricky, open-to-interpretation area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:41:42-08:00","id":1011046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010990#post1010990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Independent but closely related. Personally, I believe said relation is that both pertain to the first clase in the sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b<a href=\"http://theoatmeal.com/comics/semicolon\" target=\"_blank\">http://theoatmeal.com/comics/semicolon</a><br /> <br /> It's like Charlaquin said. Independent. Just put a period there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>If you resolve this Condition, gain a +3 die bonus to resist further<br /> attempts to Mesmerize you in the same scene; you also can\u2019t<br /> quite remember what happened while you were under the<br /> vampire\u2019s spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you resolve this Condition, gain a +3 die bonus to resist further<br /> attempts to Mesmerize you in the same scene.<br /> <br /> <b>You also can\u2019t quite remember what happened while you were under the<br /> vampire\u2019s spell.</b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010990#post1010990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that all natural light is just reflected sunlight wouldn't that mean a vampire would burn indoors if the building was not completely lightproof?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. if it's not light proof the light would spill all over the place and yes, you would refer to the sunlight chart..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T06:47:29-08:00","id":1011052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1010839#post1010839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure about allowing to make a devotion to cover a base that a different discipline covers. Wouldn't &quot;Knowing if you were messed with&quot; and &quot;digging out deep memories&quot; be Auspex? I mean, would you allow a protean devotion that would allow you to take control of another person's body? ( Dominate 5 ) or a Protean devotion to negate damage ( Resilience) while in... ooze form or something? Why make a devotion to mezmerize yourself so you can dig up memories you might have forgotten or so that you can know if you have been messed with because that's Auspex...<br /> <br /> Auspex 4: <i>By focusing, the vampire can drag up a full memory from the victim, including things that the victim has forgotten or that were suppressed by magic (though doing so takes a Clash of Wills).</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! Why not? When someone suggests &quot;make a Devotion&quot; the first thing that springs to my mind at least is &quot;combine two+ Disciplines to achieve your effect&quot;. So want to dominate yourself? That'll be including Auspex 4 please. Want to control someone else's body? Dominate 5 + Protean 5 to physically possess them with full control. Protean to negate damage? Protean 4+Resilience to halve bashing like good ol' Flesh of Marble from VtM (for example). <br /> <br /> Why do all this? Because Discipline powers as written are narrow and intended to be utilized as such. That's why we have Devotions--to break the mold and permit characters to create their own, custom requiem with blood-powers that reflect their personal needs and outlook. So arguing &quot;I can use X discipline to do what I want!&quot; is really not in spirit; the answer should be &quot;burn that saved XP to make a Devotion.&quot; Or, get help from another character to work your edge case.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf <br /> <br /> PS. Side note: From the books the reason elders are still scary is because they've had time to come up with a slew of special Devotions to let them do what they need to do. These stick around after torpor and can be extremely powerful if they require high levels of blood potency to purchase. The Unholy at BP1 is still going to rip your coterie in half, because she's <b><i>planned</i></b> for people like you....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T07:06:00-08:00","id":1011062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011052#post1011052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure! Why not? When someone suggests &quot;make a Devotion&quot; the first thing that springs to my mind at least is &quot;combine two+ Disciplines to achieve your effect&quot;. So want to dominate yourself? That'll be including Auspex 4 please. Want to control someone else's body? Dominate 5 + Protean 5 to physically possess them with full control. Protean to negate damage? Protean 4+Resilience to halve bashing like good ol' Flesh of Marble from VtM (for example).<br /> <br /> Why do all this? Because Discipline powers as written are narrow and intended to be utilized as such. That's why we have Devotions--to break the mold and permit characters to create their own, custom requiem with blood-powers that reflect their personal needs and outlook. So arguing &quot;I can use X discipline to do what I want!&quot; is really not in spirit; the answer should be &quot;burn that saved XP to make a Devotion.&quot; Or, get help from another character to work your edge case.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. Side note: From the books the reason elders are still scary is because they've had time to come up with a slew of special Devotions to let them do what they need to do. These stick around after torpor and can be extremely powerful if they require high levels of blood potency to purchase. The Unholy at BP1 is still going to rip your coterie in half, because she's <b><i>planned</i></b> for people like you....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My point there was.. Controlling someone else's body is Dominate 5. it's already in the game, Why make a devotion for something that already exists??<br /> Resilence already lets you downgrade damage and there is a devotion to negate it completely. Digging up memories is Auspex 4. Avoiding attacks is Celerity 1<br /> When you rewrite things that already exist, to make it easier to get, it feels like cheating to me. ( or if you are making it harder to do, it just feels stupid, like requiring protean 5 and dominate 5 to take over someone's body... )<br /> <br /> I am 110% in on making devotions to create NEW things for your disciplines to do, but not creating one for something that is already written. I do not think that they are narrow. I think that people do not know how to fully utilize them, to think of outside the box ideas, creativity. The celerity devotion thread is a perfect example. They wanted a Celerity Protean devotion to avoid taking damage from 1 attack, where celerity 1 already lets you do that.<br /> <br /> For example: I wrote a devotion that is like Summoning, but Instead you bring yourself to the victim/target instead of them coming to you. That is something that is not in the game, but my character wanted to be able to find people. So it was an Auspex+ Majesty devotion to turn the summoning power around.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: References:<br /> Dominate 5: Controlling a victim\u2019s memories and actions is one thing, but<br /> for some vampires the truest expression of control comes from<br /> suppressing the victim\u2019s will entirely, taking complete control of<br /> his body. The vampire moves her mind into the victim, using<br /> his body instead of her own.<br /> <br /> Auspex 4:By focusing, the vampire can drag up a full memory from the<br /> victim, including things that the victim has forgotten or that<br /> were suppressed by magic<br /> <br /> Celerity 1: Interrupt the action of another character with a brief action of<br /> her own. This could be an attack, making it possible to disable an<br /> opponent in mid-action. It may be movement, avoiding harm by<br /> shifting out of reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-02-2016, 10:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T10:10:20-08:00","id":1011125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011062#post1011062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My point there was.. Controlling someone else's body is Dominate 5. it's already in the game, Why make a devotion for something that already exists??</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> You miss my point, sir. Duplicating the word-for-word effect of an existing power with the same plus another Discipline, plus extra cost (XP or otherwise) is simply silly; doing something different is not. If, say, we wanted a Dominate+Protean Devotion I would expect it NOT to, for example, leave the vampire's body behind--said body would be merged with the subject, removing a key weakness of Dominate 5.<br /> </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011062#post1011062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resilence already lets you downgrade damage and there is a devotion to negate it completely. Digging up memories is Auspex 4. Avoiding attacks is Celerity 1<br /> When you rewrite things that already exist, to make it easier to get, it feels like cheating to me. ( or if you are making it harder to do, it just feels stupid, like requiring protean 5 and dominate 5 to take over someone's body... )</div> </div> </div> </div>All subject to the specifics of their mechanics. So does your new Devotion do something differently? Does it trade off a disadvantage of the base power for a different one (likely more severe, in many cases)? Does it enable you to target something the base power does not--for example, Auspex 4 lets you rifle through memories, but memories of <b><i>someone else</i></b>; if you want to search yourself, you'll need a Devotion to swap the target.<br /> <br /> This is why I note that Disciplines are narrow and should be interpreted narrowly. They're quite powerful within their narrow sphere, and if you let that focus off you can players pulling all kinds of silly stunts. Like mesmerizing themselves in the mirror, which has been beaten to death, staked and burned in the past two pages of this thread. Again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011062#post1011062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am 110% in on making devotions to create NEW things for your disciplines to do, but not creating one for something that is already written. I do not think that they are narrow. I think that people do not know how to fully utilize them, to think of outside the box ideas, creativity. The celerity devotion thread is a perfect example. They wanted a Celerity Protean devotion to avoid taking damage from 1 attack, where celerity 1 already lets you do that.<br /> <br /> For example: I wrote a devotion that is like Summoning, but Instead you bring yourself to the victim/target instead of them coming to you. That is something that is not in the game, but my character wanted to be able to find people. So it was an Auspex+ Majesty devotion to turn the summoning power around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that people often don't ponder the full implications of their discipline. And &quot;narrow&quot; can cover a lot of ground. Celerity is an excellent example of that, insomuch as it gives a variety of useful effects for vitae cost regardless of level. I do recall the other thread, and even posted a contribution, which pursued a purely situational benefit otherwise also obtainable through Instant Transformation and Celerity 1 (for initiative). That's actually spurred a rules question I'll post next in this thread.<br /> <br /> Your example is an excellent Devotion, and practically powerful. Did you realize that the old &quot;summoning&quot; effect from Majesty was axed in 2e? Seems so from my read, so you could reasonably do a Majesty 1 Devotion to let you attract a specific person in the area with Awe, without drawing the attention of the entire room. This is an example of using a Devotion to alter the narrow scope of a Discipline power and achieve a specific effect: bringing *that guy*, without being a rock star.<br /> <br /> Now, this will probably offend your sense of order, but I would happily consider a heavily concept-based offer from a player to use another Discipline and duplicate an existing effect (such as damage reduction)--so long as the cost involved is equal or better and we have an understanding on how it will interact with the other Discipline. Questions at work need to be: Is this driven by concept, or meta-gaming? Is this going to break systems if combined? And the like. (Example: Player doesn't want a high-Resilience Gangrel, but wants to take less damage by turning briefly into stone... ok.)<br /> <br /> Players making their lives more difficult and expensive for the sake of concept is EXACTLY what I want them doing.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T10:22:25-08:00","id":1011129,"title":"","content":"Quick question:<br /> <br /> <b>Surprise</b><br /> Characters who don\u2019t realize they\u2019re about to be on the<br /> receiving end of bloody violence have a chance to notice the<br /> ambush by rolling Wits + Composure, contested by the attacker\u2019s<br /> Dexterity + Stealth. Any character who fails the roll cannot take<br /> an action in the first turn of combat, and can\u2019t apply Defense<br /> for that turn. Determine Initiative in the second turn as normal.<br /> <br /> This obviously will apply during the first turn of hostilities, and certainly so if a given character is oblivious to any threat (buried to the armpits in an engine block repair, for example). But:<br /> <br /> 1. Does surprise apply if a given character is aware of the tense situation, ready to fight, but not aware of a specific, hidden opponent (such as through Obfuscate)? Would they lose defense on failed roll to the sole, hidden opponent? [Logically, yes, I assume.]<br /> <br /> 2. On subsequent rounds are opponents able to re-hide themselves (e.g. through Obfuscate) and gain the benefits of a surprise check again? Or is the character too keyed-up to fall for that trick again?<br /> <br /> 3. What about powers that re-position an opponent, or disorient them? Could those be used to re-apply surprise rolls? (E.g. Protean 5 with Instant Transformation, or a short-range teleport effect, or something that instantly spins/reorients a target)<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T11:18:44-08:00","id":1011148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011125#post1011125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you realize that the old &amp;quot;summoning&amp;quot; effect from Majesty was axed in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Devotion in 2e. Requires Majesty <i>or</i> Dominate 4 and functions pretty much identically to the 1e version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011129#post1011129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Does surprise apply if a given character is aware of the tense situation, ready to fight, but not aware of a specific, hidden opponent (such as through Obfuscate)? Would they lose defense on failed roll to the sole, hidden opponent? [Logically, yes, I assume.]</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume correctly. Suprise attacks after the first turn still ignore defense but don't prevent the target from acting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011129#post1011129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. On subsequent rounds are opponents able to re-hide themselves (e.g. through Obfuscate) and gain the benefits of a surprise check again? Or is the character too keyed-up to fall for that trick again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically yes, but in practice it's very difficult to hide during combat. There are some powers that do make it possible, like Hit and Run from Forsaken. Obfuscate probably won't work, because if you're in combat, there's too much attention on you to initiate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011129#post1011129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. What about powers that re-position an opponent, or disorient them? Could those be used to re-apply surprise rolls? (E.g. Protean 5 with Instant Transformation, or a short-range teleport effect, or something that instantly spins/reorients a target)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's explicitly something Celerity allows you to do, so yeah. I probably wouldn't allow it with Protean 5, at least not against other vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T12:11:12-08:00","id":1011161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011148#post1011148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a Devotion in 2e. Requires Majesty <i>or</i> Dominate 4 and functions pretty much identically to the 1e version.<br /> <br /> &lt;snip&gt;<br /> <br /> It's explicitly something Celerity allows you to do, so yeah. I probably wouldn't allow it with Protean 5, at least not against other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, and good--I'll have to look up that Devotion. <br /> <br /> The Protean 5 sequence as proposed went along the lines of:<br /> <br /> 1. Get attacked, use Celerity 1 to interrupt, Protean 5 to turn to smoke (which spreads out in a volume).<br /> 2. Next round, use Celerity 1 to go first, transform back to solid form, attack.<br /> <br /> Part of this would hinge on two things: will the smoke fill a sufficient volume to enable the vampire to reposition behind her target, and is the action to solidify again reflexive or instant? (It's instant to activate Protean 5.)<br /> <br /> BTW, researching this causes me to note that the Instant Transformation merit of 1e is obsolete, as all Protean forms take 1 Instant Action to adopt--instead of three rounds before. Glad they dropped that undramatic clause.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T12:44:56-08:00","id":1011173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011161#post1011161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Protean 5 sequence as proposed went along the lines of:<br /> <br /> 1. Get attacked, use Celerity 1 to interrupt, Protean 5 to turn to smoke (which spreads out in a volume).<br /> 2. Next round, use Celerity 1 to go first, transform back to solid form, attack.<br /> <br /> Part of this would hinge on two things: will the smoke fill a sufficient volume to enable the vampire to reposition behind her target, and is the action to solidify again reflexive or instant? (It's instant to activate Protean 5.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems reasonable to me. Although, it also seems like a lot of Vitae to spend on a single suprise attack, when you could get the same result with Celerity alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011129#post1011129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, researching this causes me to note that the Instant Transformation merit of 1e is obsolete, as all Protean forms take 1 Instant Action to adopt--instead of three rounds before. Glad they dropped that undramatic clause.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instant Transformation was a Devotion that required Protean and Celerity. The thing is, it's function can be reproduced in 2e with normal application of Vigor and Celerity, as you demonstrated above, thanks to the interrupt ability of Celerity and Protean transformation being an Instant action in 2e. No need for a Devotion if the component Disciplines can already be used to produce exactly the effect you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:14:57-08:00","id":1011181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011173#post1011173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems reasonable to me. Although, it also seems like a lot of Vitae to spend on a single suprise attack, when you could get the same result with Celerity alone.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Um what? Now I'm really confused. Having just re-read Celerity it says nothing about preventing defense--which is the main point of surprise IMO. Sure, you can interrupt and preempt another's attack, but that's a defensive use of Celerity. Nixing the <i>target</i>'s defense is <i>offensive </i>as it effectively raises your attack dice<i>.</i> I don't see a base Celerity ability that does that. (You could make a Devotion, though!) </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011173#post1011173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instant Transformation was a Devotion that required Protean and Celerity. The thing is, it's function can be reproduced in 2e with normal application of Vigor and Celerity, as you demonstrated above, thanks to the interrupt ability of Celerity and Protean transformation being an Instant action in 2e. No need for a Devotion if the component Disciplines can already be used to produce exactly the effect you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. And it's totally obsolete not just because of Celerity, but because transforming only takes a round in 2e anyway! In 1e VtR and all of VtM transformations took 3 rounds, or faster with blood.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:22:45-08:00","id":1011187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011181#post1011181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Um what? Now I'm really confused. Having just re-read Celerity it says nothing about preventing defense--which is the main point of surprise IMO. Sure, you can interrupt and preempt another's attack, but that's a defensive use of Celerity. Nixing the <i>target</i>'s defense is <i>offensive </i>as it effectively raises your attack dice<i>.</i> I don't see a base Celerity ability that does that. (You could make a Devotion, though!) </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Celerity doesn't <i>directly</i> deny the opponent's Defense, but it does allow you to make surprise attacks, the main point of which, as you said, is to deny the opponent their Defense. Page 131.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Multiply her speed by her dots in Celerity plus one. Moving in this way is sudden, jarring, the vampire appears to shift from point to point without crossing the space in-between. She may use this to briefly avoid detection or launch surprise attacks. </div> </div> </div>So instead of spending one Vitae to interrupt the attack, use the interrupt to tactivate Primeval Miasma (costing an additional three Vitae), use your movement to expand your volume, and spend one more Vitae at the start of the next round to pop to the top of the Initiative queue, end Primeval Miasma to appear behind the target and make a surprise attack, you could just spend 1 Vitae to interrupt the attack, 1 Vitae to multiply your Speed, use your movement to move behind the target faster than they're able to perceive, and use the interrupt to make a surprise attack. Same result, three less Vitae, one fewer action, and only requires one Discipline dot instead of six.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-02-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:38:18-08:00","id":1011192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011187#post1011187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity doesn't <i>directly</i> deny the opponent's Defense, but it does allow you to make surprise attacks, the main point of which, as you said, is to deny the opponent their Defense. Page 131.<br /> <br /> So instead of spending one Vitae to interrupt the attack, use the interrupt to tactivate Primeval Miasma (costing an additional three Vitae), use your movement to expand your volume, and spend one more Vitae at the start of the next round to pop to the top of the Initiative queue, end Primeval Miasma to appear behind the target and make a surprise attack, you could just spend 1 Vitae to interrupt the attack, 1 Vitae to multiply your Speed, use your movement to move behind the target faster than they're able to perceive, and use the interrupt to make a surprise attack. Same result, three less Vitae, one fewer action, and only requires one Discipline dot instead of six.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Scribbles notes furiously.*<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:20:47-08:00","id":1011217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011187#post1011187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity doesn't <i>directly</i> deny the opponent's Defense, but it does allow you to make surprise attacks, the main point of which, as you said, is to deny the opponent their Defense. Page 131.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So instead of spending one Vitae to interrupt the attack, use the interrupt to tactivate Primeval Miasma (costing an additional three Vitae), use your movement to expand your volume, and spend one more Vitae at the start of the next round to pop to the top of the Initiative queue, end Primeval Miasma to appear behind the target and make a surprise attack,<b> you could just spend 1 Vitae to interrupt the attack, 1 Vitae to multiply your Speed, use your movement to move behind the target faster than they're able to perceive, and use the interrupt to make a surprise attack.</b> Same result, three less Vitae, one fewer action, and <b>only requires one Discipline dot</b> instead of six.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I was saying... This is already there in game for a lot less than what it was proposed with said Devotion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> lf Also it would offend my sense of order if a (example) Daeva didnt want to bother with getting Auspex and having all that bad stuff to go with it ( potential BB, addiction, getting in trouble blah blah ) so they made a devotion to read people's minds and know who is the most dangerous or weakest or whatever and called it a Majesty devotion. I would flat out consider that cheating. I am Not sure what point we seem to disagree on here, but I am saying if there is something in RAW that already covers what you are trying to do... then dont make a devotion for it, follow the rules in place.<br /> If there isnt something ( like the reverse summoning ) then make a devotion for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-02-2016, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:28:42-08:00","id":1011224,"title":"","content":"I think you two are largely agreeing past each other. If a Discipline does a thing, get the Discipline if you want to do that thing. If you want to do a thing and no Discipline does it, make a Devotion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T18:01:12-08:00","id":1011286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1011224#post1011224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you two are largely agreeing past each other. If a Discipline does a thing, get the Discipline if you want to do that thing. If you want to do a thing and no Discipline does it, make a Devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we are. Really this is where you step in as a storyteller and arbitrate if something makes sense. We can concur: make devotions sensibly. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T03:56:37-08:00","id":1012479,"title":"","content":"A couple Protean questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Should the ability to mix and match parts of your Beast Skin's animals be a Merit or a Devotion? Think dog with a snake for a tail or lion headed bear, that kind of lthing. <br /> <br /> 2) When using Force of Nature are you still limited to 3 Predatory Aspects and an Unnatural one or can you obviate that limit? The wording is a bit confussing to me on that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T04:07:56-08:00","id":1012484,"title":"","content":"For (1), I'd say it depends: Is the mis-matched form a permanent thing, or can you invent new ones on the fly? The former I would say is a merit, the latter a devotion. <br /> <br /> For (2), I'm pretty sure Force of Nature lets you use as many aspects as you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T04:26:42-08:00","id":1012490,"title":"","content":"If it doesn't cost anything extra to activate and just modifies an existing power a Merit is enough (see Swarm Form), but if you need to pay extra Vitae (which seems reasonable for mixing animal forms) it would definitely be a Devotion instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T06:20:23-08:00","id":1012539,"title":"","content":"Thanks. It seems my quimeric idea merits a Devotion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:39:04-08:00","id":1012695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1012484#post1012484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For (1), I'd say it depends: Is the mis-matched form a permanent thing, or can you invent new ones on the fly? The former I would say is a merit, the latter a devotion.<br /> <br /> For (2), I'm pretty sure Force of Nature lets you use as many aspects as you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree here that if you pick the same form. Like your dog with a snake tail and tongue or whatever, then it would be a merit. But if you want to be able to be a flying dog once and water breathing bird the next time.. then I would suggest something more along the lines of a devotion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T13:03:26-08:00","id":1012737,"title":"","content":"Not that water breathing is generally a concern for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T16:09:02-08:00","id":1012851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1012737#post1012737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that water breathing is generally a concern for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>True story, but vampires arent the only ones that can take disciplines either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T11:21:57-08:00","id":1013284,"title":"","content":"Is there a rule of thumb for converting XP costs in 1e to experience costs in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:18:14-08:00","id":1013314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1013284#post1013284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a rule of thumb for converting XP costs in 1e to experience costs in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Find the mean cost per dot (for anything that scales from 1 to 5 dots, this should be the same as the cost of the third dot), and divide that by 5. Round to the nearest whole number. The exception is &quot;power stats&quot; (Blood Potency and such), which were prohibitively expensive in 1e, so their cost was significantly reduced from what would have been 10 Experiences to 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-06-2016, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:54:29-08:00","id":1014029,"title":"","content":"So, has any developer ever commented on Tilts as they apply to vampires, given they're the one splat that didn't get them in their book (something I'm still annoyed about as the side effects of that decision become more obvious with each new book otherwise)? Like, can Vampires be Stunned without a called shot to the head, can they heal Arm Wrack even if it's not strictly from damage, etc?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Amusingly, Hurt Locker answered them. Good timing. Though, doesn't cover Stun, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 12-07-2016, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T16:14:46-08:00","id":1014043,"title":"","content":"1. If a vampire drinks from a ghoul does it develop a Blood Bond for the ghouls regnant? <br /> (I assume the vampire could also tell the blood was different from a normal human)<br /> <br /> 2. Am I right in stating that you no longer need to have Auspex equal to another vampire's Obfuscate to break it? You just need (a reason) to use Clash of Wills, and win the contest? As such you don't need Auspex at all, except that it gives you more dice in the CoW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T16:34:41-08:00","id":1014049,"title":"","content":"1. No, they drink the ghoul's actual blood, not their vitae stores. But even if they find a way to take those stores unless the ghoul is part of a ghoul family with that ability or their regnant found a way to keep their vitae's potency indefinitely, no.<br /> <br /> 2. Correct you don't require Auspex, but Auspex increases your range of detection and you potentially can add it to the clash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T20:44:37-08:00","id":1014130,"title":"","content":"You also need to be able to sense their predatory aura, without Auspex you can't just decide to lash out against an invisible vampire in the room unless they've done something to make themselves visible to you (like attack you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T22:07:03-08:00","id":1014160,"title":"","content":"Raven, is it not impossible to sense their Predatory Aura if they're Obfuscated?<br /> <br /> I was thinking about being alerted to their presence by their &quot;passing signs&quot;, like creaking floor boards, etc. (as per Obfuscate 3 description). Or having some other reason to think there was a vampire there.<br /> <br /> Other than adding to the Clash of Wills roll, does having Auspex even help?<br /> <br /> Would you be able use the &quot;sense danger&quot; aspect of Auspex 1 to realise there was a threat there, thus allowing you to use a Clash of Wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12158-futurebondvillain","name":"FutureBondVillain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T22:11:58-08:00","id":1014165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1014160#post1014160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about being alerted to their presence by their &quot;passing signs&quot;, like creaking floor boards, etc. (as per Obfuscate 3 description). Or having some other reason to think there was a vampire there.<br /> <br /> Other than adding to the Clash of Wills roll, does having Auspex even help?<br /> <br /> Would you be able use the &quot;sense danger&quot; aspect of Auspex 1 to realise there was a threat there, thus allowing you to use a Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>We've discussed that before on the forum, I was for a general 'lashing out' when you're not sure who exactly is there. I don't recall if the book had a solid answer one way or another but at the least it's a reasonable house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T22:21:04-08:00","id":1014168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1014160#post1014160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raven, is it not impossible to sense their Predatory Aura if they're Obfuscated?<br /> <br /> I was thinking about being alerted to their presence by their &quot;passing signs&quot;, like creaking floor boards, etc. (as per Obfuscate 3 description). Or having some other reason to think there was a vampire there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably wouldn't allow Lashing Out against an aura you can't sense, personally. But, it's not an unreasonable thing to allow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1014160#post1014160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than adding to the Clash of Wills roll, does having Auspex even help?<br /> <br /> Would you be able use the &quot;sense danger&quot; aspect of Auspex 1 to realise there was a threat there, thus allowing you to use a Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, explicitly so. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beast\u2019s Hackles \u2022<br /> The Beast focuses on danger and weakness. A vampire who borrows her Beast\u2019s senses can use that focus to know if someone is about to attack her, or to pinpoint the weakest person in the room. The Beast is sensitive to things that other people cannot normally perceive; using this Discipline can pierce Obfuscate (see \u201cClash of Wills,\u201d p.125). </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T12:12:36-08:00","id":1014877,"title":"","content":"Strange question, and I'm not sure how all the rules apply in 2E either. My understanding is ghouls cannot typically reproduce. And a ghoul that without Vampire Vitae for a certain period begins to age again (at a vastly accelerated rate, something like a year a day). This is from my 1E understanding, so I'm sorry if that's changed since that.<br /> <br /> But my question is, can a ghoul have a child while in said aging period where they are devoid of vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T12:30:48-08:00","id":1014883,"title":"","content":"Ghouls can reproduce, there's ghoul families. It's just more difficult due to how close with death they are. Yes they could also reproduce during that period, though I believe any rapid aging would cause a miscarriage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T12:42:55-08:00","id":1014890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1014883#post1014883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls can reproduce, there's ghoul families. It's just more difficult due to how close with death they are. Yes they could also reproduce during that period, though I believe any rapid aging would cause a miscarriage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I wasn't super aware of ghoul families in Requiem. And I mostly meant the ghoul being the father in this case, but I gotcha.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:27:05-08:00","id":1015023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1014883#post1014883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls can reproduce, there's ghoul families. It's just more difficult due to how close with death they are. Yes they could also reproduce during that period, though I believe any rapid aging would cause a miscarriage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that it would likely cause a miscarriage, but It did occur to me that their bodies are literally aging, weeks months years of time are happening to your body. If a miscarriage didn't occur, could the baby grow with them? The weeks, months happening all in a matter of days?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  spelling fail.... 12-09-2016, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:30:53-08:00","id":1015024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1015023#post1015023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you that it would likely cause a miscarriage, but It did occur to me that their bodies are literally aging, weeks months years of time are happening to your body. If a miscarriage didn't occur, could the baby grow with them? The weeks, months happening all in a matter of days?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their body is rapidly aging, but it's not rapidly growing in that time. A clean shaven 20 year old wouldn't turn into a 40 year old who hasn't shaved or groomed in 20 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T17:55:04-08:00","id":1015041,"title":"","content":"Now, see, while it's true that IRL ageing and growing are two different things, this is vampire magic we're talking about here. <br /> <br /> Like, if, hypothetically, a kid was ghouled and managed to go twenty years before they missed a dose, I think they would sprout up to adulthood at an abnormal rate once they did. Or at least try. It's probably kind of messy. Anyway the point is something similar could happen here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T18:03:31-08:00","id":1015046,"title":"","content":"I was referring to vampire magic.<br /> <br /> If a kid was ghouled and went for twenty years, I don't think you would just have a physically normal adult. You would probably have something that didn't pass through adolescence, a worn-looking adult the size of a child.<br /> <br /> But yes, anything can happen here. With the books themes you don't use ghouling as some sort of perfect time stasis, even while it stops diseases, it's filling you with undeath. But if you're having some sort of space adventure and vampires are ferrying humanity to the stars, or you just want it, you can do whatever you want. This shouldn't have to be repeated as often as it is. Have all ghouls become mages, it's your game. Answers here just usually refer to the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-09-2016, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T12:43:41-08:00","id":1015340,"title":"","content":"Is there a bloodline that can do shapeshifting or flesh-crafting? And if so, which book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T13:41:54-08:00","id":1015354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1015340#post1015340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a bloodline that can do shapeshifting or flesh-crafting? And if so, which book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The closest to Tzim-style fleshcrafting I can remember in canon material off the top of my head is the Norvegi from the Mekhet Clan book. They had a Discipline called Bloodworking that mimicked a lot of Viscissitude's combat tricks like flesh spikes, bloodclot armor, and body needles. It wasn't very flexible at all though, and mostly not very useful outside combat. David Hill did a cool Protean Devotion that might be closer to what you're looking for, it's on the homebrew hub.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T14:06:16-08:00","id":1015366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1015354#post1015354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest to Tzim-style fleshcrafting I can remember in canon material off the top of my head is the Norvegi from the Mekhet Clan book. They had a Discipline called Bloodworking that mimicked a lot of Viscissitude's combat tricks like flesh spikes, bloodclot armor, and body needles. It wasn't very flexible at all though, and mostly not very useful outside combat. David Hill did a cool Protean Devotion that might be closer to what you're looking for, it's on the homebrew hub.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks much! Found the devotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T18:53:24-08:00","id":1015469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1014160#post1014160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raven, is it not impossible to sense their Predatory Aura if they're Obfuscated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally yes. You can lash out at someone using Obfuscate 4 though, and if someone is invisible per Obfuscate 3 and attacks you you are able to perceive them and lash out to break Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was thinking about being alerted to their presence by their &quot;passing signs&quot;, like creaking floor boards, etc. (as per Obfuscate 3 description). Or having some other reason to think there was a vampire there. </div> </div> </div>You can track them but per the rules you won't be able to lash out as you can't actually sense where their beast is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other than adding to the Clash of Wills roll, does having Auspex even help?<br /> <br /> Would you be able use the &quot;sense danger&quot; aspect of Auspex 1 to realise there was a threat there, thus allowing you to use a Clash of Wills? </div> </div> </div>Yeah the ability to just instantly Clash with every single use of Obfuscate in the room makes Auspex 1 fantastic. Personally I use the phrase &quot;Is anything here hidden from me?&quot; That way you still get to clash against uses of Obfuscate that aren't dangerous to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T06:06:46-08:00","id":1015652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FutureBondVillain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1014160#post1014160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than adding to the Clash of Wills roll, does having Auspex even help?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without Auspex you won't even have a Clash of Wills roll. You might be thinking about the reflexive Wits + Composure roll for noticing people using Obfuscate, but that's a mundane roll that Auspex does not add to. You only get a Clash of Wills when you use an Auspex power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T07:11:15-08:00","id":1015663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1015652#post1015652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Without Auspex you won't even have a Clash of Wills roll. You might be thinking about the reflexive Wits + Composure roll for noticing people using Obfuscate, but that's a mundane roll that Auspex does not add to. You only get a Clash of Wills when you use an Auspex power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any vampire is capable of lashing out to break Obfuscate if they perceive the vampire in question, though technically it's called a &quot;predatory aura contest&quot; not a Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T08:16:58-08:00","id":1015678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1015340#post1015340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a bloodline that can do shapeshifting or flesh-crafting? And if so, which book?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's this which is written by David Hill, one of the writers for vampire, it's not exactly official though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions/page2\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions/page2\"> Blood and Smoke Bloodline Disciplines conversions - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions/page2\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions/page2 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This thread is for all of us to post our own conversions of the multiple Bloodline Disciplines that were published over the years to update them to the Blood and Smoke rules and paradigm. I'll start by cross-posting this conversion of Cachexy from the old fora: CACHEXY \u25cf Infection The Vampire is a </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T12:49:06-08:00","id":1015789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1015678#post1015678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's this which is written by David Hill, one of the writers for vampire, it's not exactly official though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions/page2\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions/page2\"> Blood and Smoke Bloodline Disciplines conversions - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions/page2\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions/page2 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This thread is for all of us to post our own conversions of the multiple Bloodline Disciplines that were published over the years to update them to the Blood and Smoke rules and paradigm. I'll start by cross-posting this conversion of Cachexy from the old fora: CACHEXY \u25cf Infection The Vampire is a </div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Charlaquin mentioned that. It's not really what I'm looking for, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T14:34:09-08:00","id":1015851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1015789#post1015789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Charlaquin mentioned that. It's not really what I'm looking for, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give an example of what you're looking for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T15:50:22-08:00","id":1015876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1015851#post1015851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you give an example of what you're looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that is more &quot;at will&quot; that doesn't involve taking flesh off other beings and using it to fleshcraft. It's fine, there are other vicissitude writeups in the homebrew thread, so it's not like there's a lack of options. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T20:17:30-08:00","id":1015956,"title":"","content":"It's also been converted in the Translation Guide along with most Masquerade Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T08:48:22-08:00","id":1016123,"title":"","content":"In Secrets of the Covenant, CotC section, there's mention of the God-Eaters. I don't seem to recall that being a thing before. Has it come up before in any books? From where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T02:21:10-08:00","id":1016955,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to gain Ritual Disciplines (Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery) through Diablerie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T02:38:21-08:00","id":1016960,"title":"","content":"Nope, no blood sorcery, coils, scales or bloodline-only disciplines if they exist","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:09:47-08:00","id":1017014,"title":"","content":"Ummm.... while I agree on the Coils* and bloodline powers**, I don't recall that blood sorceries being banned from that list. Especially Cruac. Blood Sorceries are considered proper Disciplines in their own right. Unlike bloodline disciplines, which specifically says that outsiders can't learn these abilities, I don't see anything in the core book that forbids blood magic Disciplines from being learned.<br /> <br /> * Coils, and thus Scales, are technically pseudo-Disciplines instead of true ones. That's why they're not available to be diablerized.<br /> ** Joining a bloodline through diablerie has happened before, and the first discipined gained was the bloodline's. But that's kind of an extreme case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:18:39-08:00","id":1017023,"title":"","content":"I'm asking because as far as I can find in 2E only Bloodline Disciplines are explicitly impossible to gain through diablerie. Coils, Scales and Rituals aren't Disciplines at all. However, both Cr\u00faac and Theban Sorcery are technically disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T19:50:48-08:00","id":1017453,"title":"","content":"Hello Storytellers<br /> <br /> I was wondering ... how the Nosferatu curse interacts with Majesty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11934-draugr","name":"Draugr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11934_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T20:10:08-08:00","id":1017460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draugr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1017453#post1017453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello Storytellers<br /> <br /> I was wondering ... how the Nosferatu curse interacts with Majesty?</div> </div> </div> </div>Treat any Presence or Manipulation failures as dramatic failures. So Confidant and Loyalty are affected as per the bane's text. The other three powers don't have dice pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T15:53:45-08:00","id":1017834,"title":"","content":"Yeah, thats make sense.<br /> But what about Awe?<br /> <br /> the text says<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;For the rest of the scene, he suffers no<br /> penalties to Social rolls from his actions or appearance&quot;<br /> <b>Vampire The Requiem Second Edition pg133</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11934-draugr","name":"Draugr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11934_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T16:58:03-08:00","id":1017856,"title":"","content":"&quot;From his actions or appearance&quot;<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu Clan Bane is neither. It's a Bane. It doesn't have to take physical manifestation, and it only affects mortals, not other Vampires. Not Touchstones, either. So I would personally rule that it still applies while using Awe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T18:40:28-08:00","id":1017899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1017856#post1017856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;From his actions or appearance&quot;<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu Clan Bane is neither. It's a Bane. It doesn't have to take physical manifestation, and it only affects mortals, not other Vampires. Not Touchstones, either. So I would personally rule that it still applies while using Awe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're totally right. Thank you.<br /> in fact, I realized that even the regular social penalty from Humanity loss (for the other clans) it's not related to the Awe effects, now that you mentioned it.<br /> I ruled Awe wrong for all that time! I practically turned every Daeva in my games immune to social penalties for degeneration!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11934-draugr","name":"Draugr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11934_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T20:46:15-08:00","id":1017933,"title":"","content":"So, with a Kindred teacher, a Ghoul can learn just about any Discipline, except for high level Cruac (and some Animalism) which involves spilling Vitae. Would you rule that even non-Ghouls can learn Theban Sorcery? In Blood &amp; Smoke, it only says that you need to expend Willpower to use Theban Sorcery, so do you even need to be a Ghoul at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T22:08:34-08:00","id":1017957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1017933#post1017933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with a Kindred teacher, a Ghoul can learn just about any Discipline, except for high level Cruac (and some Animalism) which involves spilling Vitae. Would you rule that even non-Ghouls can learn Theban Sorcery? In Blood &amp; Smoke, it only says that you need to expend Willpower to use Theban Sorcery, so do you even need to be a Ghoul at all?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You'd need to be a ghoul or vamp or other discipline user to learn theban, because it's a discipline and you can't learn disciplines as a normal human or as another splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T22:23:29-08:00","id":1017965,"title":"","content":"They can learn those Disciplines, they just couldn't use them. And the teacher would need to have them, of course.<br /> <br /> In Blood &amp; Smoke it also says, 'Only priests of Lancea et Sanctum Status \u2022 or more may learn Theban Sorcery or miracles for use with it.'<br /> <br /> Part of me thinks there's a certain vampiric tinge to the Theban rites, that requires one to be a vampire or at least closely associated with one, as through a ghoul. Another part looks at Hunter and the Malleus Maleficarum and their Benedictions and figures someone's sold their weapons to both sides of a conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T22:59:03-08:00","id":1017978,"title":"","content":"That restriction on only the Lance being able to learn Theban is more of a social one than an actual metaphysical requirement I think. The Lance only teach status holding members Theban, but if you learn it while not being Lance you can still use it without issue, you just won't get the free rite known for every dot of the discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T00:18:06-08:00","id":1017990,"title":"","content":"I probably wouldn't write an NPC who was a non-vampire and knew Theban Sorcery. I might allow a player to make such a character, but not without working closely with me to figure out why it's an important part of the character that they know Theban abs how it fits in the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:32:29-08:00","id":1020607,"title":"","content":"Feeding off sleeping people: The Kiss, The Assault, or neither? That is Scarred, Swooning, or neither? One would imagine Swooning, but an &quot;invigorating sensation&quot; seems counter-productive on sleeping individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:37:52-08:00","id":1020609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1020607#post1020607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeding off sleeping people: The Kiss, The Assault, or neither? That is Scarred, Swooning, or neither? One would imagine Swooning, but an &quot;invigorating sensation&quot; seems counter-productive on sleeping individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to be this guy, but: ever had a wet dream?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:40:44-08:00","id":1020611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1020607#post1020607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeding off sleeping people: The Kiss, The Assault, or neither? That is Scarred, Swooning, or neither? One would imagine Swooning, but an &quot;invigorating sensation&quot; seems counter-productive on sleeping individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say The Kiss if you want them to stay asleep. As mentioned above, an invigorating, even arousing sensation doesn't necessarily mean waking up, but anything that could be described as a violent feeding will probably disturb your sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:45:35-08:00","id":1020616,"title":"","content":"The only problem I see with it is that Swooning usually tags the vampire as the target of the Condition's effects.<br /> <br /> Really I'd just have the sleeping character 'know' somehow that the vampire is the one, perhaps their presence and Kiss influencing their dreams. There's certainly fiction backing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T19:27:59-08:00","id":1021111,"title":"","content":"If I spend a point of Vitae on Resilience's active effect, does the damage reduction that this grant last for only that specific attack, or does it subtract that from every attack I receive in that round? Because I notice you can only use the active effect once per turn but I'm not sure how to interpret that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T19:56:21-08:00","id":1021119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021111#post1021111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I spend a point of Vitae on Resilience's active effect, does the damage reduction that this grant last for only that specific attack, or does it subtract that from every attack I receive in that round? Because I notice you can only use the active effect once per turn but I'm not sure how to interpret that.</div> </div> </div> </div>All for the round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T20:12:48-08:00","id":1021121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021111#post1021111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I spend a point of Vitae on Resilience's active effect, does the damage reduction that this grant last for only that specific attack, or does it subtract that from every attack I receive in that round? Because I notice you can only use the active effect once per turn but I'm not sure how to interpret that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Benefits last the full turn. The language is there to clarify that you can't stack Resilience on itself to, say, spend two Vitae and reduce damage by double your Resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T21:03:15-08:00","id":1021132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021111#post1021111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I spend a point of Vitae on Resilience's active effect, does the damage reduction that this grant last for only that specific attack, or does it subtract that from every attack I receive in that round? Because I notice you can only use the active effect once per turn but I'm not sure how to interpret that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good question. There is a line is resilience that states, <i>&quot;but no effect of Resilience may be used more than once per turn.</i>&quot; So I figure that it says the EFFECT of resilience can't be used more than once per turn. that if 10 people hit you, you could only ignore the damage once, because if you did it the other 9 times, you would be using the effect 10 times that turn.<br /> <br /> It also says, <i>Cost: None or 1 Vitae per effect,</i> so again if you wanted to down grade two attacks, it would be 2 effects and you can't do that in a single turn.<br /> <br /> Next it literally says &quot;<i>Duration; 1 action (for active effects)&quot;</i> so that is 1 single hit. Not<u> one turn</u> which would be every bad guys' actions... it says 1 action. = 1 hit. 1 attack 1 time per turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T21:48:37-08:00","id":1021143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021132#post1021132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it literally says &quot;<i>Duration; 1 action (for active effects)&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That is incorrect. It says &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Duration: Permanent (for persistent effects) or one turn (for active effects)</span></span>&quot;. Are you reading the most up to date version?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T21:54:37-08:00","id":1021144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021143#post1021143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is incorrect. It says &quot;<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Duration: Permanent (for persistent effects) or one turn (for active effects)</span></span>&quot;. Are you reading the most up to date version?</div> </div> </div> </div>I sure thought it was, but I copy pasted right out of my book. I have bought the VTR 2E premium +pdf &gt;.&gt; -runs off to check actual book-<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Alright. it does say per turn in the physical book, so my PDF must be off. But it still does say &quot;No effect may be used more than 1 per turn&quot;<br /> <br /> So if 10 baddies hit for for 2 and you have 1 resilience, 0 damage gets through for 1 vitae? or is that using the effect 10 times ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-23-2016, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:18:01-08:00","id":1021148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021144#post1021144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Alright. it does say per turn in the physical book, so my PDF must be off. But it still does say &quot;No effect may be used more than 1 per turn&quot;<br /> <br /> So if 10 baddies hit for for 2 and you have 1 resilience, 0 damage gets through for 1 vitae? or is that using the effect 10 times ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Benefits last the full turn. The language is there to clarify that you can't stack Resilience on itself to, say, spend two Vitae and reduce damage by double your Resilience.<br /> <br /> So if, over the span of one combat turn, ten baddies each hit you with a two-damage attack, and you have Resilience 1 and spend one Vitae to use the damage reduction active effect, you take no damage that turn, because each attack's damage is independently reduced by (Resilience + 1).<br /> <br /> If each baddie hit you with a four-damage attack, however, you would take a big old 20 damage, because you cannot spend a second Vitae to use the damage reduction effect twice in one turn, so the best your Resilience can do is reduce each attack's damage from four to two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:29:20-08:00","id":1021153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021144#post1021144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sure thought it was, but I copy pasted right out of my book. I have bought the VTR 2E premium +pdf &gt;.&gt; -runs off to check actual book-<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Alright. it does say per turn in the physical book, so my PDF must be off. But it still does say &quot;No effect may be used more than 1 per turn&quot;<br /> <br /> So if 10 baddies hit for for 2 and you have 1 resilience, 0 damage gets through for 1 vitae? or is that using the effect 10 times ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it this way: For 1 Vitae, you get your Resilience dots in effective points of general armor for 1 turn. So, if you have Resilience 1, you spend the Vitae for the turn, and you get hit by 10 baddies for 2 damage each, you take a total of 10 damage, just as if you were wearing 1/0 armor that turn. If you had 2 dots of Resilience, you'd take 0 damage just as if you were wearing 2/0 armor. You're still only using the effect once, its effect just lasts for the turn. If it didn't say you could only use it once per turn, you'd be able to spend 2 Vitae to add double your Resilience in effective armor for the turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:39:57-08:00","id":1021158,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Didn't see Loserman's answer. answered my question..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-23-2016, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:41:12-08:00","id":1021159,"title":"","content":"Hrm. My book says 'Mechanically this is similar to armor,' and armor has the following caveat, 'When applying armor to an attack dealing lethal damage, the character always takes at least one point of bashing damage from the shock of the blow.'<br /> <br /> Stances on this? Is Resilience <i>that</i> mechanically similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-23-2016, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:52:43-08:00","id":1021164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021159#post1021159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm. My book says 'Mechanically this is similar to armor,' and armor has the following caveat, 'When applying armor to an attack dealing lethal damage, the character always takes at least one point of bashing damage from the shock of the blow.'<br /> <br /> Stances on this? Is Resilience <i>that</i> mechanically similar?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it's not <i>that</i> similar. That may in fact be part of the reason it reduces damage similarly to Armor rather than actually giving you Armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T03:34:20-08:00","id":1021213,"title":"","content":"Those same rules for armor call put vampires as being exempt from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T06:19:26-08:00","id":1021248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021153#post1021153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of it this way: For 1 Vitae, you get your Resilience dots in effective points of general armor for 1 turn. So, if you have Resilience 1, you spend the Vitae for the turn, and you get hit by 10 baddies for 2 damage each, you take a total of 10 damage, just as if you were wearing 1/0 armor that turn. If you had 2 dots of Resilience, you'd take 0 damage just as if you were wearing 2/0 armor. You're still only using the effect once, its effect just lasts for the turn. If it didn't say you could only use it once per turn, you'd be able to spend 2 Vitae to add double your Resilience in effective armor for the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resilience dots plus one for non-bane damage, though. The first dot of Resilience grants the equivalent of 2/0 armour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T06:43:34-08:00","id":1021249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021248#post1021248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Resilience dots plus one for non-bane damage, though. The first dot of Resilience grants the equivalent of 2/0 armour.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right. I forgot about the extra +1, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T09:05:26-08:00","id":1021292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021213#post1021213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those same rules for armor call put vampires as being exempt from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're still affected by some Lethal damage, like that from the werewolf's bite, the bite of other vampires, and Mage magic. There's probably going to be a lot more, too.<br /> <br /> It's been a while but I'm pretty sure I just reduced the damage to 0. Some people are very literal about these things, nice to see we're at least on the same page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-23-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T09:28:47-08:00","id":1021301,"title":"","content":"Huh. Vampire doesnt have that clause. Hurt Locker page 140 bottom right corner covers it, and Hurt Locker was the last book I read. Vamp core implies vamps go take at least 1B.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T09:35:24-08:00","id":1021303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021301#post1021301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. Vampire doesnt have that clause. Hurt Locker page 140 bottom right corner covers it, and Hurt Locker was the last book I read. Vamp core implies vamps go take at least 1B.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hurt Locker has a few things like this where something will affect monsters differently than it does mortals, despite the core books for the monsters in question not saying so. It also has a lot of optional rules. I would consider these instances to be optional rules as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T22:33:00-08:00","id":1021479,"title":"","content":"Can Majesty defy sexual orientation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T23:34:08-08:00","id":1021484,"title":"","content":"That's a question for you and your table to answer, but I'd say yes. Since Majesty seems to supernaturally manipulate attentions, feelings and emotions, and not specifically 'sexual attraction,' which I suppose would be more controversial to some people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T04:45:23-08:00","id":1021524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021479#post1021479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Majesty defy sexual orientation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's break it down.<br /> <br /> Awe is not inherently sexual, you can be in awe of someone without being sexually attracted to someone.<br /> Confidant is not inherently sexual, you can be charmed by someone etc. etc.<br /> Green Eyes can invoke feelings of lust in someone but it cannot specify a target of that lust. It can al be used to make someone perform sexual acts but they do so out of an obsessive desire to please the Majesty user, not out of any sexual attraction towards them (or whoever you tell them to perform sexual acts with).<br /> Loyalty is not inherently sexual, yada yada.<br /> Idol is not inherently sexual, yada yada.<br /> <br /> That being said, if you use Majesty on someone enough you can probably addle their mind to the point that you can begin altering aspects of their personality, including sexual orientation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T08:45:02-08:00","id":1021581,"title":"","content":"Remember: it's still rape. Roll for Breaking Point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T11:15:48-08:00","id":1021621,"title":"","content":"At Humanity 8, though, most vampires won't be bothered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:16:37-08:00","id":1021642,"title":"","content":"Lashing Out specifically mentions that Vigor doesn't add to Monstrous Beast. Is this accurate?<br /> <br /> It seems strange to me that Nosferatu have a merit that adds to Monstrous Beast (Unsettling Gaze), but none of their Disciplines require Strength, and they get Vigor to give them even less reason to buy up the Attribute rather than the cheaper and more effective Discipline.<br /> <br /> Does it maybe mean that you can't use the Active effects? Because the passive just flat-out adds to strength dots, making it pretty weird that they don't apply to Lashing Out when they apply to everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T12:58:22-08:00","id":1021655,"title":"","content":"Vigor does not apply to lashing out rolls. That is very accurate and not strange at all. Just as Majesty and Nightmare don't apply to the Seductive Beast. It would be incredibly unbalancing if they did, and they would pretty much become requirements to contest other vampires. It's not surprising at all and entirely in line with the role of Lashing Out as a mechanic, if not necessarily the fluff. Nosferatu <i>do</i> get Strength as one of their bonus Attributes however. And the fact that they get Vigor doesn't really disincline them toward building Strength anymore than it does any other clan who wants to use the Monstrous beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T13:10:19-08:00","id":1021659,"title":"","content":"Majesty and Nightmare don't directly apply to Presence dots for Seductive Beast. It's not really an equivalent comparison.<br /> <br /> Other Clans don't get a Merit to encourage them to focus on Monstrous Beast.<br /> <br /> And Vigor does discourage from buying Strength, since it adds to Strength for less cost than buying Strength itself and with more benefit. For everything except, apparently, Lashing Out. In every other way, a dot of Strength gained from Vigor is exactly the same as a dot of Strength bought on its own. So it's absolutely strange that there's a random exception called out in the book that isn't actually listed in the Vigor write-up, where you would expect it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T13:28:33-08:00","id":1021667,"title":"","content":"I smell a late-in-production rule patch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T13:47:15-08:00","id":1021671,"title":"","content":"The reason no disciplines add any bonuses to Lashing Out is almost definitely balancing reasons. One aspect should not be a lot more viable just because there's an extra bonus. And I completely agree with that despite playing a Kerberos with the Atrocious Merit and four dots of Vigor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T14:09:49-08:00","id":1021682,"title":"","content":"It's so that you don't have one aspect of the Beast that caps out five dice higher than the other two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T04:55:07-08:00","id":1021941,"title":"","content":"Maybe the reason Nosferatu have that merit because Vigour doesn't add to Lashing Out, but it makes sense for Nos to excel with the Monstrous Beast because the monstrosity of the vampiric condition is their whole schtick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021621#post1021621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Humanity 8, though, most vampires won't be bothered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suspending consent is a breaking point at 8 but impassioned violence is a breaking point at 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T16:04:00-08:00","id":1022112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1021621#post1021621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Humanity 8, though, most vampires won't be bothered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forcing someone into sexual activity is definitely a lower sin than 8. 8 might just be for the use of the discipline. But, like forcing someone to murder another through the use of your disciplines, this is something more than using Majesty to have someone give you their ticket for the U2 goodbye tour. Your mileage shouldn't vary in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T20:14:49-08:00","id":1022188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022112#post1022112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forcing someone into sexual activity is definitely a lower sin than 8. 8 might just be for the use of the discipline. But, like forcing someone to murder another through the use of your disciplines, this is something more than using Majesty to have someone give you their ticket for the U2 goodbye tour. Your mileage shouldn't vary in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly.<br /> <br /> But the question was just if Majesty defies sexual orientation. If you use it to rape or murder a thousand people or live five hundred years or whatever ideas you want to tack onto it, you'll be using a lot of Breaking Points, but that's not what the question asked.<br /> <br /> Activating Majesty is not forcing someone into sexual activity. Or violence, impassioned or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T03:54:11-08:00","id":1022265,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but activating Majesty to force another sexual identity on someone is practically equivalent to forcing them to have sex with people they normally wouldn't have. Call it forced prostitution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T06:32:37-08:00","id":1022301,"title":"","content":"I guess it's what you do <i>after </i>activating Majesty that counts after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T09:04:24-08:00","id":1022364,"title":"","content":"The proof of the pudding is in the eating. As they say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T11:38:25-08:00","id":1022865,"title":"","content":"Total apologies if this has been asked, but, per RAW, and per common sense: Can you use Unnatural Aspects while in a Swarm Form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T12:01:47-08:00","id":1022880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022865#post1022865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Total apologies if this has been asked, but, per RAW, and per common sense: Can you use Unnatural Aspects while in a Swarm Form?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the general consensus is that yes, you can. The RAW isn't explicit on the issue, but you do use the Swarm as a form of Beast's Skin, and you can use both Predatory Aspect and Unnatural Aspect with the normal use of Beast's Skin, so there doesn't seem to be any reason that wouldn't include Swarm Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T12:09:11-08:00","id":1022884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022880#post1022880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the general consensus is that yes, you can. The RAW isn't explicit on the issue, but you do use the Swarm as a form of Beast's Skin, and you can use both Predatory Aspect and Unnatural Aspect with the normal use of Beast's Skin, so there doesn't seem to be any reason that wouldn't include Swarm Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be my general hatred of the mechanics of Swarm Form, but the logic of a size 0/1 creature doing +2L damage is painful. To me, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T12:18:53-08:00","id":1022891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022884#post1022884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be my general hatred of the mechanics of Swarm Form, but the logic of a size 0/1 creature doing +2L damage is painful. To me, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://static1.squarespace.com/static/51b63587e4b06e9f0987f4e3/t/51c30853e4b097ff213c02bf/1371736148029/piranha-copia.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The whole point of the swarm is that it's not one creature doing it. It's dozens if not hundreds, maybe even thousands. And while a 'natural' swarm of ants may not be interested in killing you, when controlled by an external force they're just a weapon and there's nothing natural about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-27-2016, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T12:25:29-08:00","id":1022893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022884#post1022884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It may be my general hatred of the mechanics of Swarm Form, but the logic of a size 0/1 creature doing +2L damage is painful. To me, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not one size 0/1 creature. Hundreds, maybe thousands of them, all with supernaturally empowered claws.<br /> <br /> Imagine a swarm of hornets. Now imagine every single hornet in that swarm has tiny wolverine claws (the X-men character, not the animal). Is it so unbelievable that this mob of miniature monstrosities could do as much damage as one smack with a lead pipe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-27-2016, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:52:23-08:00","id":1022971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022893#post1022893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not one size 0/1 creature. Hundreds, maybe thousands of them, all with supernaturally empowered claws.<br /> <br /> Imagine a swarm of hornets. Now imagine every single hornet in that swarm has tiny wolverine claws (the X-men character, not the animal). Is it so unbelievable that this mob of miniature monstrosities could do as much damage as one smack with a lead pipe?</div> </div> </div> </div>No it really doesn't make much sense because jabbing someone with a steel needle does the same amount of damage as jabbing them an iron needle. Swarm Form also doesn't actually give the user the ability to inject the neurotoxic, hemotoxic or other paralyzing venom of insects nor transmit the bacterial or viral agents that can cause allergic reactions and illness or death that would actually make being attacked by a swarm of tsetse flies, fire ants, hornets, et al. potentially deadly. Arguably a fair trade off since the swarm forms are immune to being stomped on, disoriented, or killed by a single spray from a can of Raid or quick jet spray from a water hose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:01:14-08:00","id":1022979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022893#post1022893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not one size 0/1 creature. Hundreds, maybe thousands of them, all with supernaturally empowered claws.<br /> <br /> Imagine a swarm of hornets. Now imagine every single hornet in that swarm has tiny wolverine claws (the X-men character, not the animal). Is it so unbelievable that this mob of miniature monstrosities could do as much damage as one smack with a lead pipe?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it makes perfect sense. Terrifying little monsters attacking you for 2 more damage. though I dont see that working at all if you use the form tilt out of the demon book that was pasted in here a while ago. <br /> <br /> <br /> I dont think that that the needle example is quite on par with what Charlaquin tried to point out as they are both needles... Now if you said one was motel hot and the other wasnt, then one is going to do some more damage than the other... Wasps in swarm form aren't any more real as the wolf or tiger you turn into. They are just part of the beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:49:08-08:00","id":1023007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022971#post1022971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it really doesn't make much sense because jabbing someone with a steel needle does the same amount of damage as jabbing them an iron needle.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but jabbing them with a thousand needles is going to be a problem, especially if those needles are supernaturally enhanced to damage those they are jabbed into on more than just a physical level. And, again, we're talking about an amount and severity of damage on par with one thwack from an aluminum baseball bat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022971#post1022971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarm Form also doesn't actually give the user the ability to inject the neurotoxic, hemotoxic or other paralyzing venom of insects nor transmit the bacterial or viral agents that can cause allergic reactions and illness or death that would actually make being attacked by a swarm of tsetse flies, fire ants, hornets, et al. potentially deadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it does? That's why you do damage in swarm Form. Just like using Beast's Skin to turn into a cobra allows you to transmit a hemotoxin, hence the stat block for snakes specifying that its bite can introduce a poison with Toxicity between 3 and 10, and/or inflict the Poisoned Tilt. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022971#post1022971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguably a fair trade off since the swarm forms are immune to being stomped on, disoriented, or killed by a single spray from a can of Raid or quick jet spray from a water hose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swarm Form doesn't grant any special immunity to damage that isn't already part of the rules for swarms or the rules for how vampires take damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022979#post1022979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it makes perfect sense. Terrifying little monsters attacking you for 2 more damage. though I dont see that working at all if you use the form tilt out of the demon book that was pasted in here a while ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true, and probably a big part of the reason for Swarm Form working by attack rolls instead of straight up damage like the Swarm Tilt and the Swarm Extreme Environment. For the record, I do use the Swarm Tilt in place of the Swarm Form rules, and accordingly claws from Unnatural Aspect wouldn't help a Swarm Form vampire do any more damage at my table. But tragedyjones was asking about the rules as written, not about the rules as modified to suit Charlaquin's table, so I answered accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-27-2016, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T04:54:45-08:00","id":1023194,"title":"","content":"Hrm... Swarm Form / Protean 3 gives poison? Interesting...<br /> <br /> What are some good poisonous swarms? Spiders, perhaps, though I like my swarms being flying.<br /> <br /> On the other hand you probably cant attack with a poisonous bite and agg-dealing uberclaws at the same time, so its a tradeoff.<br /> <br /> Right now I plan on going Wolf / Rat / Bird (Owl? Bat?) / Swarm of Locusts or Flies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 12-28-2016, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:19:49-08:00","id":1023198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1023194#post1023194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm... Swarm Form / Protean 3 gives poison? Interesting...<br /> <br /> What are some good poisonous swarms? Spiders, perhaps, though I like my swarms being flying.<br /> <br /> On the other hand you probably cant attack with a poisonous bite and agg-dealing uberclaws at the same time, so its a tradeoff.<br /> <br /> Right now I plan on going Wolf / Rat / Bird (Owl? Bat?) / Swarm of Locusts or Flies.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Swarm For doesn't in 2nd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:43:05-08:00","id":1023207,"title":"","content":"Nothing in Beast's Skin/Swarm Form says that you gain the venomous or toxic qualities of the animal, but nothing says you don't either. It's up to the ST to decide.<br /> <br /> Side note: Owls might make some vampires nervous due to the existence (or rumours) of Strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T09:22:33-08:00","id":1023310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1023007#post1023007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very true, and probably a big part of the reason for Swarm Form working by attack rolls instead of straight up damage like the Swarm Tilt and the Swarm Extreme Environment. For the record, I do use the Swarm Tilt in place of the Swarm Form rules, and accordingly claws from Unnatural Aspect wouldn't help a Swarm Form vampire do any more damage at my table. But tragedyjones was asking about the rules as written, not about the rules as modified to suit Charlaquin's table, so I answered accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. I was agreeing with you. As written I see it working as well. The last bit was just an added thought since both of us use that. ^.^ <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T10:42:09-08:00","id":1023343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1023198#post1023198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Swarm For doesn't in 2nd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then how are you able to do damage as a swarm of bees?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T11:09:56-08:00","id":1023351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1023343#post1023343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then how are you able to do damage as a swarm of bees?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bees individually have stingers and mandibles. And they aren't made of adamantium, vibranium, nth metal, feminum, mithril, harbenite or any other fictitious element created to be synonomous for nigh indestructible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T11:25:39-08:00","id":1023357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1023351#post1023351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bees individually have stingers and mandibles. And they aren't made of adamantium, vibranium, nth metal, feminum, mithril, harbenite or any other fictitious element created to be synonomous for nigh indestructible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022971#post1022971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarm Form also doesn't actually give the user the ability to inject the neurotoxic, hemotoxic or other paralyzing venom of insects nor transmit the bacterial or viral agents that can cause allergic reactions and illness or death that would actually make being attacked by a swarm of tsetse flies, fire ants, hornets, et al. potentially deadly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is clearly contradicted by the fact that you can do damage (which could potentially be deadly) in Swarm Form. Which is it? Does Swarm Form allow you to transmit those agents, or can swarms of insects be deadly without transmitting those agents?<br /> <br /> And re: adamantium, you're the one who said,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1022971#post1022971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it really doesn't make much sense because jabbing someone with a steel needle does the same amount of damage as jabbing them an iron needle.</div> </div> </div> </div>so again your arguments seem to be contradicting each other. At any rate, the point of my original &quot;tiny wolverine claws&quot; comment was to illustrate that the claws in question are unnatural and supernaturally empowered to be more harmful than mundane stingers and mandibles, which if you're arguing can be harmful without poison, is reason enough for Unnatural Aspect to allow it to do more damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-28-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T19:32:49-08:00","id":1024065,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been covered before however: Is Touch of Shadow potent enough to counter Vampire Blood Senses on a quantity of Vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12727-son-of-gaia","name":"Son-of-Gaia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12727_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T04:41:22-08:00","id":1024224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Son-of-Gaia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1024065#post1024065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this has been covered before however: Is Touch of Shadow potent enough to counter Vampire Blood Senses on a quantity of Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally run it like, the vampire senses blood and <i>definitely </i>knows it is <i>right there </i>in front of him, but somehow can't actually <i>see </i>it. Making for a very confused and irritated vampire, who may or may not correctly deduce someone's using Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> No idea on the official ruling, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T06:08:33-08:00","id":1024255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Son-of-Gaia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1024065#post1024065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this has been covered before however: Is Touch of Shadow potent enough to counter Vampire Blood Senses on a quantity of Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's when you roll a Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T06:58:46-08:00","id":1024289,"title":"","content":"I would say that, without auspex, no clash of wills would occurr. But the mundane ways still stay effective as described in the power text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:53:27-08:00","id":1024322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1024289#post1024289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that, without auspex, no clash of wills would occur. But the mundane ways still stay effective as described in the power text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex isn't required to see through Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:00:16-08:00","id":1024328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1024322#post1024322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Auspex isn't required to see through Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought &quot;seeing through&quot; required a Clash of rolls using Auspex, and &quot;guessing where that prick is standing&quot; is the one that doesn't require Auspex? The former is like a blindfolded man taking off his blindfolds, and the latter is like a blind man using his hearing to make up for his lack of sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:19:15-08:00","id":1024346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1024322#post1024322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Auspex isn't required to see through Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct. I would say a supernatural ability in conflict causes a Clash of Wills, Vampire Blood Sense is indeed a supernatural sensory power that may well conflict with any 'Concealing Power' if the Blood Sense is appropriate to sense things the situation.<br /> <br /> The question I have is this: Are other Vampires without the Blush valid things to sense with Blood Sense as they are just cold walking corpses without those vital signs of life that Blood Sense seems to hon in on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-30-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T08:20:16-08:00","id":1024347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1024322#post1024322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Auspex isn't required to see through Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex allows you to ask: is there any hidden object here? and now is when occurrs a clash of wills (obfuscate+ bp vs auspex+ bp. What do you use in a clash of wills if not auspex?).<br /> But, as I said, you can still use all other mundane rolls to see object hidden with obfuscate as specified in the power description.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for example to see someone using obfuscate 3 you can track him by indirect clues but even achieving all the required successes you still don't see him. You just know he is there and NOW you can lash out to shatter all his active obfuscate powers.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, with auspex, you can roll a clash of wills and obtain the same effect of the mundane roll, then you still have to lash out to shatter his obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-30-2016, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T20:55:51-08:00","id":1024618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1024346#post1024346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question I have is this: Are other Vampires without the Blush valid things to sense with Blood Sense as they are just cold walking corpses without those vital signs of life that Blood Sense seems to hon in on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably yes, but vampires can auto-recognize each other anyway, it's kind of a mix of the predatory aura and just the general behaviour of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T05:49:23-08:00","id":1024731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1024346#post1024346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question I have is this: Are other Vampires without the Blush valid things to sense with Blood Sense as they are just cold walking corpses without those vital signs of life that Blood Sense seems to hon in on?</div> </div> </div> </div>In and of itself, Kindred Senses doesn't apply to a specific kindred's vitae, but if, for example, that kindred fed off a human or animal, living touchstone (maybe that's why you're looking for them) you could track them that way. As has been pointed out, vampires automatically sense each other's vampiric predatory aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T05:04:42-08:00","id":1025372,"title":"","content":"This might be a silly question that's already been covered, but are vampires affected by Toxicity from stuff like poisons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T05:11:05-08:00","id":1025373,"title":"","content":"Since vampires don't have a metabolism only literally flesh eating viruses could theoretically harm vampires, and only if they normally cause lethal instead of bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T06:50:19-08:00","id":1025412,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> How the &quot;360-degree field of vision&quot; of Protean 2 extra senses works?<br /> <br /> In an ambush per example, the player with the 360Vision would never get ambushed or it would take dices from the attacker?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6586-skulhamba","name":"Skulhamba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6586_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T06:54:55-08:00","id":1025413,"title":"","content":"They can still be surprised and ambushed. A character having a 360 degree field of vision needs to be accounted for when assessing penalties and bonuses that would normally be granted when attacking from the side or rear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:31:56-08:00","id":1025453,"title":"","content":"This series is awful, but I couldn't resist...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/3/33308/1121602-neji9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:21:45-08:00","id":1025474,"title":"","content":"359 degree vision: not worth the savings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T01:38:55-08:00","id":1025779,"title":"","content":"So, another possibly answered question (sorry if it's been answered, but 55 pages is a lot to go through for one question). Now, I was looking at the Revenant side text and it mentioned that Revenants couldn't learn stuff like blood sorceries and coils of the wyrm; however, it didn't mention them being unable to take Invictus Oaths and Carthian Laws. How would you rule that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T03:26:24-08:00","id":1025816,"title":"","content":"Me personally? If I'm not sure, I would ask myself if a human or ghoul member can do something. If not, what is the reason and does that reason apply to revenants. So in answer to your question, if a revenant can find a notary willing to notarize their oath and a liege willing to accept their service, yes they can participate in an oath. (Given the social stigma of being a revenant or affiliated with a Masquerade breaching hunting screw up waiting to happen, that is going to be unlikely. But I can think of a few instances of an Invictus member agreeing as leverage or a boon to the revenant's creator also.)<br /> If they can join the Carthian Movement, they can use Carthian Law and count as a voting member.<br /> <br /> Personally, I have a revenant character in my setting and he knows a few Theban Sorcery rituals from his time as a ghoul and he can use them. His regnant was an inquisitor and the Sanctified bishop in the domain considers his state of revenancy to be a divine decree that he is intended for damnation and any powers he had innately are a gift from God. His regnant will uplift him once his murderers are brought to justice, one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:23:05-08:00","id":1026063,"title":"","content":"So, I'm having other interpretation problems about the Auspex limits.<br /> I'm writing a little list of questions, can you tell me which between them are legit for auspex 1/2 which are not and, possibly, why?<br /> <br /> 1) What is her Bane/weakness?<br /> 2) does she know John/have any kind of link with John?<br /> 3) Does she know the deepest secret of John? (If yes: What is the secret she know about John?)<br /> 4) what is her deepest secret?<br /> 5) When she talk with John last time?<br /> <br /> Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:12:21-08:00","id":1026100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026063#post1026063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm having other interpretation problems about the Auspex limits.<br /> I'm writing a little list of questions, can you tell me which between them are legit for auspex 1/2 which are not and, possibly, why?<br /> <br /> 1) What is her Bane/weakness?<br /> 2) does she know John/have any kind of link with John?<br /> 3) Does she know the deepest secret of John? (If yes: What is the secret she know about John?)<br /> 4) what is her deepest secret?<br /> 5) When she talk with John last time?<br /> <br /> Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I interpret the book on a very literal level. So this is only my interpretation of it. Others will likely have their own opinions.<br /> <br /> Level one says, <i>&quot;This level of Auspex can only answer immediate questions about danger or weakness&quot; </i><br /> I take immediate as meaning right now. Will &quot;she&quot;( whoever your she is ) hurt me? Hurt John? &gt; right now &lt; Not did they, will they next week or whatever. So I don't see any of those questions being about an immediate strength or weakness. I would not allow them for level 1.<br /> Unless she was trying to pick a fight with you and knew John was hiding in the next room waiting to ambush you, or something.<br /> <br /> Level two says: <i>&quot;This level of Auspex focuses on questions concerning the secrets and weaknesses of a single character.&quot; </i>And <i>&quot;The Beast sniffs out the victim\u2019s dark secrets, things that she doesn\u2019t want anyone else to know.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So your #1 Falls directly into that category. A bane is a major weakness as they often lead to your character getting hurt.<br /> #2 is her knowing John some sort of terrible secret or weakness to her character? if not, then it doesn't fall into this category.<br /> #3 is a little iffy. I suppose it is a secret that she knows, but it's John's secret and he is apparently not there. But I would probably let them both slide.<br /> #4 Absolutely. I would say it's closely related to &quot;psychological vulnerability.&quot; As you generally dont want secrets to get out because emotionally someone can get hurt ( or even physically )<br /> #5 Again, is this some sort of secret or weakness on her part? If not, then it doesn't fall into this category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:26:48-08:00","id":1026110,"title":"","content":"By my standards... I don't allow Auspex omniscience or unlimited fishing expeditions. I also don't allow questions or commands at any level that use out of character terminology. So commands/requests to only hit someone until you do x levels of damage or questions that make direct reference to Humanity scores, Banes, Attribute ratings Health, Dirge, Mask etc. yield nothing. Find a way to phrase it using in world terminology. <br /> <br /> Level 1 or 2 only. Higher levels of Auspex may have different results.<br /> <br /> 1a. Nothing. <br /> 1b. Something current or recent will be revealed. <br /> 2a. Unless there's a specific reason the person doesn't want others to know John, No result.<br /> 2b. See 2a. <br /> 3. Nothing. You should be directing the power at John to find his secrets, not a 3rd party.<br /> 4. The &quot;deepest&quot; secret is beyond the scope of level two, but some current and pressing concern would be revealed.<br /> 5. Usually falls in the realm of Auspex omniscience. Unless the last meeting was meant to be a secret, the question yields nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 01-03-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:40:52-08:00","id":1026117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026110#post1026110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By my standards... I don't allow Auspex omniscience or unlimited fishing expeditions. I also don't allow questions or commands at any level that use out of character terminology. So commands/requests to only hit someone until you do x levels of damage or questions that make direct reference to Humanity scores, Banes, Attribute ratings Health, Dirge, Mask etc. yield nothing. Find a way to phrase it using in world terminology.<br /> <br /> Level 1 or 2 only. Higher levels of Auspex may have different results.<br /> <br /> 1a. Nothing.<br /> 1b. Something current or recent will be revealed.<br /> 2a. Unless there's a specific reason the person doesn't want others to know John, No result.<br /> 2b. See 2a.<br /> 3. Nothing. You should be directing the power at John to find his secrets, not a 3rd party.<br /> 4. The &quot;deepest&quot; secret is beyond the scope of level two, but some current and pressing concern would be revealed.<br /> 5. Usually falls in the realm of Auspex omniscience. Unless the last meeting was meant to be a secret, the question yields nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying that you do not allow Auspex to reveal banes when it is literally a weakness to that character which falls directly into something that Auspex could know. Under so many levels too. It's a weakness, It's a secret. It's a psychological vulnerability.<br /> &quot;Uhg the sound of ringing bells is the <i>bane </i>of my existence&quot;<br /> <br /> Your character wouldn't know they are taking Damage equal to 10- humanity, but they might want to keep it a well hidden secret that when they go into someone's house uninvited it hurts like a bitch...<br /> And also Your dirge and mask can also be secrets and it's listed under dot 2's suggested questions. &quot;<i>What is this person\u2019s Vice/Requiem? The sound of conspiratorial whispers. The smell of drugs wafting off a junkie. &quot; </i>That means, their mask or dirge could be junkie.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T12:58:04-08:00","id":1026125,"title":"","content":"I'm saying if you ask &quot;What is Vampire Max's bane?&quot; You get nothing. If you want to learn that the vampire in your hypothetial example has hearing church bells as a bane, you better phrase the question using in character terms to the effect of &quot;Is there any object or location (choose one) that said vampire finds repulsive?&quot;<br /> <br /> Since the question is asking what their vice is, the attendant hallucination can also mean the individual has a personal feeding preference/obsession for feeding off humans who are high on a drug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 01-03-2017, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T13:07:29-08:00","id":1026129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026125#post1026125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm saying if you ask. &quot;What is Vampire Max's bane?&quot; You get nothing. If you want to learn that the vampire in your hypothetial example has hearing church bells as a bane, you better phrase the question using in character terms to the effect of. &quot;Is there any object or location (choose one) that said vampire finds repulsive?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, valid. I see your point there. the original poster asked what the scope of the power is and what it can and can not find out. We all require to ask the right questions, however. The scope of the power does allow you to find the banes, masks, dirges and perhaps if asked properly, humanity. It would probably be beneficial to not tell him that you can't get those answers. As it confused even me that you did not allow your table to find out those things as it seemed you did not think it was in the scope of the power. <br /> You just require it to be asked as your character would ask. And that's 100% acceptable. <br /> Myself, I ask my players OOC what they are trying to find out so I can give them the proper response. If their vampire asks, &quot;What is Bob's psychological vulnerability?&quot; Or whatever. I want to know what exactly they are looking for so they often just say, Dirge or bane or whatever so They don't feel screwed if I misunderstand and answer with something they weren't really intending. Some of my players are really new to RPing and don't quite grasp it yet so it's better to ask OOC sometimes, then I work with them to getting the question for IC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T19:18:28-08:00","id":1026267,"title":"","content":"Who says the word &quot;Bane&quot; isn't in-world?<br /> <br /> Every single Vampire has banes. Keep in mind that Banes aren't just the three you can pick. Clan Banes qualify. Fire and sunlight are Banes. Bloodline weaknesses are also Banes.<br /> <br /> Bane is an in-world term. Fire and sunlight are &quot;great banes&quot; in specific.<br /> <br /> The real trick is how to word the Auspex question so that you don't get &quot;sunlight&quot; as your answer. That's pretty useless. And I wouldn't allow &quot;what are <i>all</i> of Max's banes&quot; as a question, since you don't get multiple answers for Auspex questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T06:45:54-08:00","id":1026474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026267#post1026267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says the word &quot;Bane&quot; isn't in-world?<br /> <br /> Every single Vampire has banes. Keep in mind that Banes aren't just the three you can pick. Clan Banes qualify. Fire and sunlight are Banes. Bloodline weaknesses are also Banes.<br /> <br /> Bane is an in-world term. Fire and sunlight are &quot;great banes&quot; in specific.<br /> <br /> The real trick is how to word the Auspex question so that you don't get &quot;sunlight&quot; as your answer. That's pretty useless. And I wouldn't allow &quot;what are <i>all</i> of Max's banes&quot; as a question, since you don't get multiple answers for Auspex questions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since fire and sunlight aren't secrets or hidden weaknesses, I don't think it would register on Auspex, Because you would already know they are weak to that. Everyone who has Auspex should know that about vampires. Even if they are Ordo and have mastered that to overcome it, they still need to dump tons of vitae into not getting hurt, so losing all that vitae is a weakness too.<br /> Exceptional success you can get multiple answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T06:55:50-08:00","id":1026479,"title":"","content":"How many times per night would you have a vampire with a Vitae addiction roll to resist the temptation to bite down and drink the good stuff straight from his own vein?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:08:46-08:00","id":1026483,"title":"","content":"Personally, I simply wouldn't. Biting yourself for vitae is kind of... Well, boring. Lacking drama. Taking the fangs out of vitae addiction. Its the need for vitae from others that is the stuff of stories. <br /> <br /> I might allow it as a stop gap measure, or the equivalent of inflicting self harm to bring short term catharsis. But rolling to bite yourself is not going to prompt new stories in general. Its a roll for the sake of rolling, which would slow down the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:14:48-08:00","id":1026488,"title":"","content":"None, unless the vampire also has the Deprived Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:20:14-08:00","id":1026493,"title":"","content":"I ask, because of this passage in the rules:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any time he\u2019s faced with further opportunities to drink Vitae, he must indulge, succeed in a Resolve + Composure roll, or gain the Deprived Condition. </div> </div> </div><br /> @MCN: I don't agree that it is boring. I think it is a logical step in the addiction narrative. It could especially be quite a dramatic mechanism in a 1-on-1 Chronicle. YMMV, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:23:26-08:00","id":1026498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026474#post1026474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since fire and sunlight aren't secrets or hidden weaknesses, I don't think it would register on Auspex, Because you would already know they are weak to that. Everyone who has Auspex should know that about vampires. Even if they are Ordo and have mastered that to overcome it, they still need to dump tons of vitae into not getting hurt, so losing all that vitae is a weakness too.<br /> Exceptional success you can get multiple answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if you know that you are in front of a ghost, for example, are you allowed, trough auspex 2, to ask:<br /> <br /> &quot;How can it be forced to come at me?&quot; If the ghost has the ban that force him to come when someone tell his name 3 times in front of a mirror for example.<br /> <br /> And, knowing that ban, is legit to ask with a second question: &quot;what is its name?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:26:52-08:00","id":1026500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026479#post1026479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many times per night would you have a vampire with a Vitae addiction roll to resist the temptation to bite down and drink the good stuff straight from his own vein?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your standard night? 0 times. A night where they're locked in a cell with no other distraction than their own thoughts? Every &quot;scene&quot; they have blush of life active and maybe 2-4 times otherwise, with an exceptional success stopping all future rolls for that night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:01:11-08:00","id":1026524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026500#post1026500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Your standard night? 0 times. A night where they're locked in a cell with no other distraction than their own thoughts? Every &quot;scene&quot; they have blush of life active and maybe 2-4 times otherwise, with an exceptional success stopping all future rolls for that night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I am not sure an addict would need to roll to drink from themselves, because it doesn't really gain anything. Though if you are locked up in a cell and you are starting to go through withdraw, then I can see you being more tempted to shoot yourself up. <br /> <br /> Same breath. I dont see anything wrong with making your players roll a few times a night if that's the way you want to roll it. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026498#post1026498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, if you know that you are in front of a ghost, for example, are you allowed, trough auspex 2, to ask:<br /> <br /> &quot;How can it be forced to come at me?&quot; If the ghost has the ban that force him to come when someone tell his name 3 times in front of a mirror for example.<br /> <br /> And, knowing that ban, is legit to ask with a second question: &quot;what is its name?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure if I would allow &quot;How can it be forced to come at me&quot; I might dive right into &quot;What's it's name?&quot; that is probably a major secret. I might allow something like, &quot;is it dangerous to me?&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;how can I provoke it?&quot; Usually knowing how to provoke something, would be knowing a vulnerability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:03:05-08:00","id":1026525,"title":"","content":"Alright, cheers. Good advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:17:14-08:00","id":1026532,"title":"","content":"Swarm Form has a requirement of Beast's Skin (Protean 3). Looking for some RAW and common sense feedback.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Swarm Form</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To attack those within her swarm, roll Strength + Brawl, ignoring Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast's Skin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In animal form, she takes on the beast\u2019s Physical Attributes and Skills, and its Size, Speed, and Health.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the Swarm Form merit allow you to substitute your direct Strength + Brawl of your Vampire form? On one hand I imagine it has to since most 0-1 size creatures will have minuscule attack pools. Then again, those successes ignore defense, and potentially inflicting a full Kindred pool's worth of damage or blood drain per turn could add up very quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast's Skin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She may be unable to use some Physical Merits at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you allow a swarm to utilize Claws of the Unholy and/or Riding the Wave merits?<br /> <br /> Finally, has anyone statted up creepy-crawly stats for bug swarms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:24:35-08:00","id":1026537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026532#post1026532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarm Form has a requirement of Beast's Skin (Protean 3). Looking for some RAW and common sense feedback.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does the Swarm Form merit allow you to substitute your direct Strength + Brawl of your Vampire form? On one hand I imagine it has to since most 0-1 size creatures will have minuscule attack pools. Then again, those successes ignore defense, and potentially inflicting a full Kindred pool's worth of damage or blood drain per turn could add up very quickly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Would you allow a swarm to utilize Claws of the Unholy and/or Riding the Wave merits?<br /> <br /> Finally, has anyone statted up creepy-crawly stats for bug swarms?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1012287-swarm-form\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1012287-swarm-form\"> Swarm form - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1012287-swarm-form\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1012287-swarm-form </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> To attack those within her swarm, roll Strength + Brawl, ignoring Defense. Divide the damage however you wish among those inside. Apply a victim&rsquo;s armor to the damage normally. The damage is lethal (bashing to Kindred). Alternately, a success may instead allow the vampire to take one Vitae from a victim. Does this mean that the attacking swarm of bats uses its bat strength or its normal strength? Can you use your protean claws in swarm form? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This thread has some great stuff for you. <br /> <br /> I would allow claws of the unholy... I am not entirely sold on Ride the wave fight style, I can see it either way, but I would probably rule No to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:28:16-08:00","id":1026538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026537#post1026537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread has some great stuff for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent, thank you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T02:48:31-08:00","id":1026942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1025413#post1025413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can still be surprised and ambushed. A character having a 360 degree field of vision needs to be accounted for when assessing penalties and bonuses that would normally be granted when attacking from the side or rear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is the right game mechanics too, but how many dices take from the attacker or give to the player using the 360\u00ba since it is a level 2 discipline power?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6586-skulhamba","name":"Skulhamba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6586_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:19:51-08:00","id":1026951,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Discipline level has any direct influence on the dice bonus/penalty. I'd just completely negate the modifier for attacks coming from behind or the sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:47:27-08:00","id":1026958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skulhamba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1026942#post1026942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is the right game mechanics too, but how many dices take from the attacker or give to the player using the 360\u00ba since it is a level 2 discipline power?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it depends on the circumstances. If 360 Charlie is walking down a bike path in some park at night looking for a midnight jogger to feed and a vigilante set up a tree stand to wait in ambush 500 yards away with an Remington 700 equipped with laser sights etc. The shooter gets the penalties associated with shooting from medium or long range. 360 Charlie doesn't get any bonuses to react to Remington Sniper because by the time he hears the shot being fired, the bullet is already in flight. If 360 Charlie had merely walked past the tree stand I would grant him an unmodified perception check to notice it. Unless Remington Sniper took precautions to hide it.<br /> <br /> If, however, 360 Charlie is walking along and a vigilante armed with a fireaxe and using an expert two handed grip charges out of the bushes from behind when 360 Charlie is about 3 yards away. 360 Charlie doesn't get any penalties on his surprise roll because his 360 vision alerted him the moment the bushes started moving and rustling as Fireaxe Jack made his charge. If 360 Charlie was actually waiting for a potential ambusher and actively searching for one, I would give him a +2 bonus to his surprise check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T03:12:11-08:00","id":1027507,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Claws of the Unholy:</u></b> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These claws ingore all armor </div> </div> </div>Does it means, as per armor piercing quality, that they ignore also durability? So could a Gangrel with those claws destroy a vault Bank without even have Vigor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T03:37:52-08:00","id":1027512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1027507#post1027507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Claws of the Unholy:</u></b><br /> <br /> Does it means, as per armor piercing quality, that they ignore also durability? So could a Gangrel with those claws destroy a vault Bank without even have Vigor?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could rule either way, personally I'd say they ignore durability as well as armour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T03:41:11-08:00","id":1027513,"title":"","content":"That's going to be one of those things you have to adjudicate based on what you want for your own games. <br /> <br /> Personally, I said a Gangrel trapped in a basement that had concrete sheet floors and a ceiling and walls each 2 ft thick was stuck. Their claws could pierce through about one inch into the concrete but they lacked the personal strength to continue cutting and while their claws dealt aggravated damage and ignore durability, their fingers and hands did not. Yes if they wanted to sit there and try chipping away a hole big enough to fit through, they could but it would take far longer time than they had before their activities could be discovered. You also have the issue of things breaking apart once their durability reached zero.<br /> <br /> But if you want characters to be able to slice their way into a bank vault, walk in, take the contents and walk out, that's fine too. Personally I'd make sure they're halfway intelligent about it so they don't have the door pieces falling on them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T04:11:56-08:00","id":1027528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1027513#post1027513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's going to be one of those things you have to adjudicate based on what you want for your own games.<br /> <br /> Personally, I said a Gangrel trapped in a basement that had concrete sheet floors and a ceiling and walls each 2 ft thick was stuck. Their claws could pierce through about one inch into the concrete but they lacked the personal strength to continue cutting and while their claws dealt aggravated damage and ignore durability, their fingers and hands did not. Yes if they wanted to sit there and try chipping away a hole big enough to fit through, they could but it would take far longer time than they had before their activities could be discovered. You also have the issue of things breaking apart once their durability reached zero.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I got your point but, even if the fingher can't ignore durability, the structure just stands to represent the time and the &quot;number&quot; of blows you need to deal to destroy the object. I mean: if the claws can ignore durability, I actually don't need to pass through the enteire vault with a single blow and the full hand (if the attack roll doesn't deal all the structure value in damage, otherwise it should), beacause the gangrel (without vigor) can litterally digs in the steel, accumulating, hit by hit, the proper number of successes to destroy the vault bank (or concrete wall). This is just an hipotetical scenario I'm wondering about, reading the claws of Unholy merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:08:47-08:00","id":1027574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1027528#post1027528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually don't need to pass through the enteire vault with a single blow and the full hand (if the attack roll doesn't deal all the structure value in damage, otherwise it should), beacause the gangrel (without vigor) can litterally digs in the steel, accumulating, hit by hit, the proper number of successes to destroy the vault bank (or concrete wall). This is just an hipotetical scenario I'm wondering about, reading the claws of Unholy merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as I pointed out, the way I adjudicate it, that would be possible, but damaging the wall doesn't make it disappear into nothingness. They'd end up with a couple thousand pounds of broken concrete abruptly falling on top of them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:24:36-08:00","id":1027588,"title":"","content":"Yes I agree with this for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T15:09:52-08:00","id":1027862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1027507#post1027507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Claws of the Unholy:</u></b><br /> <br /> Does it means, as per armor piercing quality, that they ignore also durability? So could a Gangrel with those claws destroy a vault Bank without even have Vigor?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Claws of the Unholy do Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Durability: How hard the object is to damage. Subtract<br /> Durability from any damage dealt to the object.<b> Durability<br /> has no effect against attacks that deal aggravated damage.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T16:01:00-08:00","id":1027891,"title":"","content":"Nice, I didn't remember this thing. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:37:59-08:00","id":1029796,"title":"","content":"Can a vampire in torpor be fed blood and convert it into vitae? <br /> Mostly comes up if one can't wake because of not having vitae at dusk but itd be interesting if one used a staked vampire as a vitae converter (if they found a way to remove it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:49:31-08:00","id":1029804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1029796#post1029796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a vampire in torpor be fed blood and convert it into vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition. I don't believe it's changed for second. It wouldn't waken the vampire, though they might not sleep as long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mostly comes up if one can't wake because of not having vitae at dusk but itd be interesting if one used a staked vampire as a vitae converter (if they found a way to remove it) </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing you're talking about a human doing so. They wouldn't be able to pull out the Vitae without, presumably, destroying the vampire. Like by pressing it.<br /> <br /> Or magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-10-2017, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:54:19-08:00","id":1029810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1029796#post1029796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a vampire in torpor be fed blood and convert it into vitae?<br /> Mostly comes up if one can't wake because of not having vitae at dusk but itd be interesting if one used a staked vampire as a vitae converter (if they found a way to remove it)</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume a scale for the Coil of the Voivode could convert blood into a vitae state for the purposes of waking a vampire up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:55:16-08:00","id":1029811,"title":"","content":"Feeding Vitae to a vampire in Torpor can wake them up. And since the vampire can be fed Vitae it should be possible to feed them regular blood as well.<br /> However, draining Vitae from a vampire is not the easiest thing to do. As far as I know there's two ways to do it: The vampire willingly spills Vitae from an orifice or wound, or another vampire feeds from them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T16:11:31-08:00","id":1029816,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify. Feeding Vitae to a vampire in torpor will wake them up prematurely only if the Vitae is from a vampire at least 2 Blood Potency higher. There is presumably some magic Disciplines and Merits that would allow for premature awakenings, as well.<br /> <br /> 'Regular' Vitae in a vampire could help them spend less time in torpor. If a vampire's in torpor due to damage, they'll use up all their Vitae in an attempt to heal it. If they still have damage after that, they fall into torpor longer than they usually would, specifically they're treated as 1 Humanity lower for how long they spend in torpor. I'd allow 'regular' Vitae to be ingested solely to help the vampire use its reflexive healing, though it doesn't specifically suggest this in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:30:41-08:00","id":1031266,"title":"","content":"So, with merits like Secret Society Junkie, is the Herd there subject to merit limits? I know a few merits explicitly say the herd granted isn't, but SSJ doesn't, so does it cap at 5 as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T16:22:33-08:00","id":1031376,"title":"","content":"I'd say it does count toward the limit because it doesn't expressly exempt itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T17:52:36-08:00","id":1031394,"title":"","content":"Wouldnt they get refunded any actual Herd dots to just bring them to cap? I'd think you have to try pretty hard to go over if your not taking the actual merit (herd in this example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T22:50:41-08:00","id":1031467,"title":"","content":"I have a question: Does the first level of the Coil of Ziva work through the hard cap reduction of Cruac?<br /> For example: We have a vampire with 5 Humanity, level 5 Ziva, and level 1 Cruac. Is his effective humanity 9 or 10 for the purpose of how his banes affect him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12860-your3rdshadow","name":"Your3rdShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T03:39:14-08:00","id":1031520,"title":"","content":"Personally I wouldn't have allowed your character to develop powers of conflicting mechanical nature in the first place, so ultimately it's up to your ST what your Humanity rating will be. They might assert the inherent superiority of the Coils over sorcery and ignore the cap set by Cruac entirely. They might assert the inherent superiority of Cruac by saying the Coils don't raise your Humanity above the cap imposed. Since the book says Cruac simply ceased functioning if a character raised their Humanity, I would go with that option and refund XP spent on the Cruac discipline the moment your character tried to cast a Cruac ritual and it fails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T05:37:45-08:00","id":1031545,"title":"","content":"Cruac limits the actual humanity dots you can have, not what your effective humanity can be. So it would treat your effective humanity as 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:24:21-08:00","id":1031702,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12860-your3rdshadow","name":"Your3rdShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:42:49-08:00","id":1031783,"title":"","content":"Hey!<br /> <br /> Can vampires be audio recorded?<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6586-skulhamba","name":"Skulhamba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6586_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:06:36-08:00","id":1031805,"title":"","content":"I believe so.<br /> <br /> Hollow Mekhet cannot, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T02:51:51-08:00","id":1032059,"title":"","content":"When one sort of vampire has a weakness where they can't do something that usually means the rest can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T04:47:36-08:00","id":1032081,"title":"","content":"Vampires can be captured in photos or audio recordings like anyone else. It's just that they unconsciously look away from the camera in photos and videos by default. Like nofather said Hollow Mekhet are the exception where they can't be indirectly viewed at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T05:29:58-08:00","id":1032097,"title":"","content":"In the Ordo part of Secrets of the Covenants there's an Ordo researcher who records his meeting with presumably a Hollow Mekhet. He expresses some annoyance over only being able to record half the conversation (which is the only half we get to read).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:41:08-08:00","id":1032267,"title":"","content":"There's one in the Mekhet clanbook too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T04:23:08-08:00","id":1032584,"title":"","content":"Protean 3 <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">In animal form, she takes on the beast\u2019s Physical Attributes and Skills, and its Size, Speed, and Health<br /> <br /> Does the kindred retain his Defense?<br /> Does he treat in animal form all lethal attack as bashing ?<br /> <br /> Also is there a penalty in melee or ranged combat against creatures of size 1 or 2 ?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your answers.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T04:59:43-08:00","id":1032591,"title":"","content":"Defense is derived from Physical Attributes and Skills, so I would say they use the Animal's defense.<br /> <br /> Protean 3 says you attack as the animal does; so if they have natural weapons (such as 0L claws), then lethal. Otherwise no. That said, the book also says you can use Disciplines as normal; feel free to use Predatory or Unnatural Aspect to enhance damage in animal form.<br /> <br /> I've never seen anything about attack bonuses or penalties due to Size in CofD. I may have missed something, but there is no bonus for being small to my knowledge. That said, two caveats;<br /> 1. Your ST may decide to give a bonus/penalty anyway, of course. Before attempting to convince them to give you a defense bonus when small, remember that NPCs can then do the same to you.<br /> 2. If you are going for Size 1 (or 0, but you specifically mentioned size 1 or 2), you may be best served by using Swarm Form. It's fairly difficult to damage a vampire in Swarm Form. They only take one damage at most or two for an Exceptional Success unless it's an Area of Effect attack of some kind. Swarm Form attacks are Lethal by default (downgraded to Bashing for Vampires as usual), since you asked about Lethal attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:28:34-08:00","id":1032646,"title":"","content":"I think the question about lethal-to-bashing was about how the vampire takes damage when shifted, rather than how they deal it.<br /> <br /> Just in case: I don't think there's an explicit ruling on that, but taking damage as a living mortal while in animal form would be a rather significant disadvantage, so at my own table I'd rule that they still downgrade non-supernatural, non-bane damage when shifted. Not only does it keep a significant benefit from the vampire's state, it also adds a bit to the creepy factor from an unknowing mortal's perspective, which feels appropriate when we're talking vampires. Imagine shooting that very hungry and angry wolf in the face - <i>point-blank</i> mind you - yet all but <i>ignores</i> the wound as it lunges, and there isn't even any blood, and... oh, there it is...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 01-16-2017, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:26:34-08:00","id":1032709,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure a vampire protean 3'd into an animal works just like a vampire of that species would if they existed. So damage is downgraded, sunlight is burny and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:36:39-08:00","id":1032794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1032584#post1032584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Protean 3 <br /> In animal form, she takes on the beast\u2019s Physical Attributes and Skills, and its Size, Speed, and Health<br /> <br /> Does the kindred retain his Defense</div> </div> </div> </div>Defense is a derived trait, determined by the Lower of Wits or Dexterity (or the higher of the two, in the case of animals) + Athletics. Since the vampire's Wits, Dexterity, and Athletics change in animal form, her Defense will change accordingly. An argument could be made that they should still use the lower of Wits or Decterity, since they're not really an animal, but I would personally rule that they use the higher in animal form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1032584#post1032584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does he treat in animal form all lethal attack as bashing ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you're talking about vampires' ability to downgrade damage from mundane sources of lethal damage to bashing (and aggravated to lethal)? Yes, the vampire retains that ability in animal form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1032584#post1032584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also is there a penalty in melee or ranged combat against creatures of size 1 or 2 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1032584#post1032584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks in advance for your answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-16-2017, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:42:59-08:00","id":1033319,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the answers! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One more question: If using an animal form of Protean the player falls in torpor does he stays in the animal form or come back to his original form?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6586-skulhamba","name":"Skulhamba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6586_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:14:29-08:00","id":1033341,"title":"","content":"I say they remain in animal form until sunrise then they revert to their foundation form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T08:20:52-08:00","id":1033375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1032794#post1032794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defense is a derived trait, determined by the Lower of Wits or Dexterity (or the higher of the two, in the case of animals) + Athletics. Since the vampire's Wits, Dexterity, and Athletics change in animal form, her Defense will change accordingly. An argument could be made that they should still use the lower of Wits or Decterity, since they're not really an animal, but I would personally rule that they use the higher in animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wits is retained. Only physical traits are changed.<br /> Since the vampire retains all mental faculties I'd say using the lower makes most sense. I think the reason animals use the higher is because of how much they are driven by reflexes instead of conscious thought.<br /> I'd say a simple ~two dot Merit could grant the vampire the ability to always use Dex instead of Wits when in an animal form (barring Swarm Form where you don't appear to change attributes) so that you tap into those reflexes. I say always Dex instead of always the higher of the two so that the character can't use their human Wits instead of the animal's Dex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:27:52-08:00","id":1033444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1033375#post1033375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wits is retained. Only physical traits are changed.<br /> Since the vampire retains all mental faculties I'd say using the lower makes most sense. I think the reason animals use the higher is because of how much they are driven by reflexes instead of conscious thought.<br /> I'd say a simple ~two dot Merit could grant the vampire the ability to always use Dex instead of Wits when in an animal form (barring Swarm Form where you don't appear to change attributes) so that you tap into those reflexes. I say always Dex instead of always the higher of the two so that the character can't use their human Wits instead of the animal's Dex.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, you're right. For some reason I thought it was all Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T06:56:29-08:00","id":1033986,"title":"","content":"Werewolves get a similar merit, so there's definitely precedence there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:49:47-08:00","id":1035221,"title":"","content":"How can, mechanicaly, someone with Auspex see through oubliette (Obfuscate 4)?<br /> I mean, even if someone is aware that has been used this power, the only way I know to dissipate obfuscate effects is to lash out and win the roll. But if the lord of the heaven is not in that room is there a way to see through illusion with Auspex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:16:42-08:00","id":1035230,"title":"","content":"It's a Clash of Wills. Technically when you come into contact with something under the effects of the illusion, the illusion temporarily dissipates and you don't need Auspex to notice. (It's in the entry for Oubliette.) There's an example of how someone with Auspex would go against Oubliette would play out as a Clash of Wills on page 126 in the book. The presence or absence of the illusion generator is irrelevant.<br /> If I'm going to allow them to tear down the entire illusion (as opposed to simply not being affected by it), just have the Auspex user lash out and if Oubliette user is another PC, have them roll if they want to spend the willpower. If it's an NPC using Oubliette I'd probably rule it's an automatic success for the Auspex user.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 01-20-2017, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T16:35:32-08:00","id":1035513,"title":"","content":"You don't need to lash out to see through Oubliette with Auspex, succeeding in the Clash of Wills roll will allow the Auspex user to see through it. What lashing out would do is shatter any active illusions the vampire had active so that others could see through it.<br /> <br /> (Also Oubliette is Obfuscate 5)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T01:23:56-08:00","id":1035659,"title":"","content":"I see. I thought lash out was needed to see an obfuscate vampire because this sentece (obfuscate 3 description):<br /> <br /> &quot;If another vampire manages to percive him, through Auspex, attacks or any other means, she can PERCIVE his predatory aura (not see him) and lash out. If she wins the predatory contest Cloack of Night shatters as does any other obfuscate effect&quot;<br /> <br /> So it seems to me that winning the clash of wills just let you percive the presence (the aura) but not see her. And the only way to really see her is to win the predatory contest. So with Auspex you just know that someone is there hidden to your sight. You can feel her and try to shatter his power with your own aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T18:00:59-08:00","id":1035910,"title":"","content":"No, that sentence is saying that in addition to being able to perceive the vampire you may also perceive their predatory aura and can lash out to completely shatter it, allowing anyone to perceive them. There is also a devotion called Shatter the Shroud that allows you to spend 2 vitae to immediately shatter Obfuscate without spending another instant action on a predatory aura contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:30:00-08:00","id":1040851,"title":"","content":"What would be the stats/ attributes of a real giant?<br /> <br /> (Yes, it is for Requiem<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6586-skulhamba","name":"Skulhamba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6586_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:36:07-08:00","id":1040856,"title":"","content":"How big?<br /> <br /> Basically you'd up Size, which would increase Health, and then probably raise probably Strength and Presence while maybe lowering Dexterity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:32:40-08:00","id":1040900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1039537-posthumous-embrace-and-ghouls?p=1040817#post1040817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B5Qw108SV6C6RkVXWkQ1VjFLaFk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">IMAGE</a><br /> </div></div> </div> </div> Does this look accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did I make that flow chart correctly, and if not what where was my mistake?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:37:31-08:00","id":1041789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1040900#post1040900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did I make that flow chart correctly, and if not what where was my mistake?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are quite a few mistakes.<br /> <br /> \u2022 From &quot;Exsanguinated to death?&quot;, the yes arrow should lead to &quot;Does Humanity roll fail?&quot; and the &quot;no&quot; arrow should lead to &quot;simple death.&quot;<br /> \u2022 From &quot;Is currently a ghoul?&quot;, the yes arrow should lead to &quot;does regnant Blood Potency roll fail?&quot;<br /> \u2022 From &quot;does regent Blood Potency roll fail?&quot;, the yes arrow should lead to &quot;exposed to vampiric Vitae after death?&quot; and the no arrow should lead to &quot;becomes revenant&quot;.<br /> \u2022 From &quot;exposed to vampiric Vitae after death?&quot;, the yes arrow should lead to &quot;does sire Blood Potency roll fail?&quot; and the no arrow should lead to &quot;simple death&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that's all the changes you would need to make, but I'd have to look over the revised flowchart to be sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:11:18-08:00","id":1042063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1041789#post1041789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are quite a few mistakes.<br /> <br /> -snip-<br /> <br /> , but I'd have to look over the revised flowchart to be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, thank you. How about <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B5Qw108SV6C6YVJPV0RGdnN4MW8/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:21:55-08:00","id":1042070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1042063#post1042063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, thank you. How about <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B5Qw108SV6C6YVJPV0RGdnN4MW8/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one makes it impossible for someone who had not come into contact with Vitae before death to become a Revenant. It should be possible for anyone who is exsanguinated to become a Revenant. Also you should check for the character being a ghoul before checking for postmortem vitae exposure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:35:26-08:00","id":1042082,"title":"","content":"Without a graphical aid, here's what I would do.<br /> <br /> 1. Is this character a ghoul? If yes, go to 2. If no, go to 3.<br /> 2. The character's regnant rolls Blood Potency. If the roll is successful, go to 8. If it fails, go to 3.<br /> 3. Did this character die by exsanguination? If yes, go to 4. If no, go to 5.<br /> 4. The vampire who exsanguinated the character rolls Humanity +2. If the roll is successful, go to 9. If the roll fails, go to 10.<br /> 5. Has this character consumed vampiric Vitae in their lifetime? If yes, go to 6. If no, go to 9.<br /> 6. Has this character been exposed to vampiric Vitae within one week of death? If yes, go to 7. If no, go to 9.<br /> 7. The vampire who's Vitae this character was exposed to after death rolls Blood Potency. If the roll is successful, go to 11. If the roll fails, go to 9.<br /> 8. The character rises as a Revenant in one week, minus a day for each success rolled.<br /> 9. The character rests in peace.<br /> 10. The character rises as a Revenant at an unpredictable time during the next week.<br /> 11. The character rises as a vampire in one week, minus a day for each success rolled.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T15:48:15-08:00","id":1042088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1042070#post1042070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one makes it impossible for someone who had not come into contact with Vitae before death to become a Revenant. It should be possible for anyone who is exsanguinated to become a Revenant. Also you should check for the character being a ghoul before checking for postmortem vitae exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the first part<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR 2nd Ed pg 94</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a vampire exsanguinates a contaminated mortal, roll the vampire\u2019s Humanity + 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>contaminated was the word that made the flow chart start because of that sentence, without it nothing comes back thirsting for blood from beyond the grave. (Unless I missed something, which if I did, I would love to find out about it) And the second part, being a ghoul does not preclude or enhance the chance of the posthumous embrace, thus is only a factor to consider if a posthumous embrace is no longer an possibility. That was the problem that caused all the crossed lines in my first attempt, the urge to factor in something in chronological order rather than based backward from end consequence. Thank you so much for proof checking it!<br /> <br /> My favorite scenario is a ghoul that was exsanguinated by a vampire and exposed to blood after death. One roll for Posthumous Embrace and two different types of rolls that may cause him to rise as a Revenant (because he's meet the prerequisites for requiring those rolls) One could just follow the whole path that one qualifies for as if the rolls failed, the rolls various pools and then check the time lines to see which one would take place first. I wouldn't except on a lark, but one could.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1042082#post1042082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without a graphical aid, here's what I would do.<br /> <br /> 1. Is this character a ghoul? If yes, go to 2. If no, go to 3.<br /> 2. The character's regnant rolls Blood Potency. If the roll is successful, go to 8. If it fails, go to 3.<br /> 3. Did this character die by exsanguination? If yes, go to 4. If no, go to 5.<br /> 4. The vampire who exsanguinated the character rolls Humanity +2. If the roll is successful, go to 9. If the roll fails, go to 10.<br /> 5. Has this character consumed vampiric Vitae in their lifetime? If yes, go to 6. If no, go to 9.<br /> 6. Has this character been exposed to vampiric Vitae within one week of death? If yes, go to 7. If no, go to 9.<br /> 7. The vampire who's Vitae this character was exposed to after death rolls Blood Potency. If the roll is successful, go to 11. If the roll fails, go to 9.<br /> 8. The character rises as a Revenant in one week, minus a day for each success rolled.<br /> 9. The character rests in peace.<br /> 10. The character rises as a Revenant at an unpredictable time during the next week.<br /> 11. The character rises as a vampire in one week, minus a day for each success rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is awesome! Am I misunderstanding (inflating) the importance of being exposed to vampire vitae in this process?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-01-2017, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:59:37-08:00","id":1042120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1042088#post1042088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About the first part<br /> <br /> contaminated was the word that made the flow chart start because of that sentence, without it nothing comes back thirsting for blood from beyond the grave. (Unless I missed something, which if I did, I would love to find out about it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you're right! I missed the &quot;contaminated&quot; part. In that case, I'm going to have to revise my own list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1042088#post1042088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the second part, being a ghoul does not preclude or enhance the chance of the posthumous embrace, thus is only a factor to consider if a posthumous embrace is no longer an possibility. That was the problem that caused all the crossed lines in my first attempt, the urge to factor in something in chronological order rather than based backward from end consequence. Thank you so much for proof checking it!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1042088#post1042088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is awesome! Am I misunderstanding (inflating) the importance of being exposed to vampire vitae in this process?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I think it's me who missed the fact that Vitae exposure is necessary for a revenant when the victim is exsanguinated. Here's an accordingly revised version of my non-graphical flowchart.<br /> <br /> 1. Is this character a ghoul? If yes, go to 2. If no, go to 3.<br /> 2. The character's regnant rolls Blood Potency. If the roll is successful, go to 8. If it fails, go to 4.<br /> 3. Has this character consumed vampiric Vitae in their lifetime? If yes, go to 4. If no, go to 11.<br /> 4. Did this character die by exsanguination? If yes, go to 5. If no, go to 6.<br /> 5. The vampire who exsanguinated the character rolls Humanity +2. If the roll is successful, go to 6. If the roll fails, go to 9.<br /> 6. Has this character been exposed to vampiric Vitae within one week of death? If yes, go to 7. If no, go to 11.<br /> 7. The vampire who's Vitae this character was exposed to after death rolls Blood Potency. If the roll is successful, go to 10. If the roll fails, go to 11.<br /> 8. The character rises as a Revenant in one week, minus a day for each success rolled.<br /> 9. The character rises as a Revenant at an unpredictable time during the next week.<br /> 10. The character rises as a vampire in one week, minus a day for each success rolled.<br /> 11. The character rests in peace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:03:59-08:00","id":1044543,"title":"","content":"<b>New question:</b> Can a vampire, which is targeted by a mage's spell, use the lash out ability to contest this spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11079-bardobobs","name":"bardobobs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:06:15-08:00","id":1044544,"title":"","content":"No. Lashing Out can only be used to cancel supernatural abilities that explicitly allows it, such as Awe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:06:29-08:00","id":1044545,"title":"","content":"I would rule that as a No. I don't know much about mages and their spells but usually you roll Resolve or Composure +BP to resist things. Even if Vampire world you don't use Lash out to &quot;resist&quot; powers. You can lash out to break awe, dread presence and Obfuscate. but that's like popping a bubble on them, not stopping a bubble coming at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:11:43-08:00","id":1044549,"title":"","content":"Mage spells are resisted according to the Withstand rules which does not use more than a single trait (most often Resolve, Stamina or Composure for vampires). It is also possible to trigger a Clash of Wills by using a conflicting supernatural ability of your own. They're never contested, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T09:47:08-08:00","id":1044570,"title":"","content":"Oh! I am just full of random questions today! Vigor. Just want a confirmation ( or a correction ) When you use protean to shift into a wolf and they have 4 Str, if you have 4 vigor do you have 8 str as a wolf or do you lose the vigor dots when shifted?<br /> <br /> I have always ruled that they stack on just like in your &quot;human&quot; form, but since I am here, I thought I would clarify. <br /> <br /> Thanks all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T10:02:11-08:00","id":1044578,"title":"","content":"You retain the use of all your Disciplines in animal form. There's no reason to think it wouldn't apply to the passive effects of the physical Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T15:12:53-08:00","id":1044742,"title":"","content":"There is a Cruac spell or theme or something that lets you shapeshift but you lose all Disciplines for the duration but Protean retains the use of Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T18:10:58-08:00","id":1044795,"title":"","content":"Auspex 1 and similar tend to be instant actions with no duration, but in the case of something like piercing obfuscate, or seeing other hidden things, do you still notice them after that intial impression?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T19:31:24-08:00","id":1044825,"title":"","content":"I believe Auspex would break Obfuscate for that particular vampire. So yes. If you manage to pierce Obfuscate with your Auspex you can see them. I do not think Auspex 1 is strong enough to break Obfuscate, but it could certainly let you know if there is a threat in the room... even if you can't see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T17:19:26-08:00","id":1045512,"title":"","content":"Auspex 1 is definitely &quot;strong enough&quot; to let you see through Obfuscate (if you win the Clash of wills) and is indeed the only Auspex ability that can let you see an invisible character. Of course the more Auspex (and Blood Potency) you have the better your chances of winning the Clash. You can definitely still perceive the vampire after using Auspex, otherwise how would you be able to shatter the Obfuscate with another instant action to lash out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T22:03:56-08:00","id":1045615,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Majesty effect area:</u></b><br /> <br /> What is the size of the area in which Majesty has effect? For example, a vampire is using Idol on a crowd, 500 yards away from another PC/NPC spying him with a binocular. Should Idol/awe have effect on her too?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T02:41:41-08:00","id":1045658,"title":"","content":"No, Jeff Jeffries is three blocks away, he has no means of interacting with anyone, and disciplines don't work through electronic and audio visual enhancing equipment without a specific devotion or discipline created to do exactly that.<br /> Idol also enhances Awe which says it only applies to talking normally to someone.<br /> On the flip side of that, if they can be affected by it, then that means Jeff Jeffries can lash out against it, which is an auto lose for the Daeva who can't see him. It can turn surveillance into a lash out sniping game and suddenly everyone knows Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:01:05-08:00","id":1045733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1045658#post1045658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Jeff Jeffries is three blocks away, he has no means of interacting with anyone, and disciplines don't work through electronic and audio visual enhancing equipment without a specific devotion or discipline created to do exactly that.<br /> Idol also enhances Awe which says it only applies to talking normally to someone.<br /> On the flip side of that, if they can be affected by it, then that means Jeff Jeffries can lash out against it, which is an auto lose for the Daeva who can't see him. It can turn surveillance into a lash out sniping game and suddenly everyone knows Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree with this. I think since Idol washes over a crowd, that It could get someone watching you through binoculars. They aren't a whole lot different than glasses. You're not watching a video feed through a TV, or any other electronic device, you are actually watching them with your own eyeballs through an enhancing lens. It sort of brings you into the effect of it. ( If Dominate can work through Mirrored glasses... ) I wouldn't allow someone to dominate through a recorded video feed, or have majesty work through video feed, but I absolutely would let a microphone allow you to give commands once they were done...<br /> <br /> Second if you allow a vampire to lash out from that far away to break awe ( which you would have to have a good reason to know they are doing it because it's not a neon sign telling you it's on ) then you must let the vampire contest it. However, that said. I would not allow you to lash out from that far away because Lashing out is like attacking. It's visual posturing. It's an aggressive action, if they cant see you, how can they be afraid of you? How can you make the proper actions to lash out, if you are that far away?<br /> <br /> &quot;To lash out, the vampire must take a simple action appropriate<br /> to the aspect of predator used. A monstrous Beast growls,<br /> threatens, gnashes teeth, or calls to action. A seductive Beast<br /> sidles up to the prey, whispers beautiful lies, or gives a telling<br /> gaze from across the crowd. A competitive Beast draws a line in<br /> the sand, announces terms, or takes the role of mouse in a chase.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1045512#post1045512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex 1 is definitely &quot;strong enough&quot; to let you see through Obfuscate (if you win the Clash of wills) and is indeed the only Auspex ability that can let you see an invisible character. Of course the more Auspex (and Blood Potency) you have the better your chances of winning the Clash. You can definitely still perceive the vampire after using Auspex, otherwise how would you be able to shatter the Obfuscate with another instant action to lash out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was originally thinking that you would have to ask something like, &quot;Where is the Obfuscated vampire&quot; and I didn't see an equivalent question on there, but it does say that you can use Beast's Hackles to find invisible things with a clash of wills. so I do stand corrected! Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-08-2017, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:42:53-08:00","id":1045818,"title":"","content":"............","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-08-2017, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:48:02-08:00","id":1045824,"title":"","content":"Is &quot;When you are going to try to control me with your power jump out from this window&quot; is a Dominate valid command?<br /> Does the vampire that is on the point of use awe jump out from the window before using it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:52:27-08:00","id":1045827,"title":"","content":"Might be better phrased as &quot;The next time you would attempt to influence me by supernatural means, jump out the nearest window instead.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T10:18:29-08:00","id":1045844,"title":"","content":"For Dominate 1, that phrase is way too long. For dominate 2, Why not use &quot; Forget how to use Majesty&quot; or even &quot;Don't use Majesty&quot; ? Unless you are using dominate 3 to set up a command for later, I don't see that working at all. if you wanted them to jump out of a window, why not just tell them to do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T10:28:38-08:00","id":1045848,"title":"","content":"Because you don't want them to be punished unless they do something to warrant a punishment, and you still want them to be able to use those abilities against other targets. &quot;Don't use Dominate or Majesty against me&quot; would stop them from doing so, but it might not be nearly petty enough for the Dominate user's tastes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T10:31:54-08:00","id":1045851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1045844#post1045844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Dominate 1, that phrase is way too long. For dominate 2, Why not use &amp;quot; Forget how to use Majesty&amp;quot; or even &amp;quot;Don't use Majesty&amp;quot; ? Unless you are using dominate 3 to set up a command for later, I don't see that working at all. if you wanted them to jump out of a window, why not just tell them to do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it could be a &quot;security strategy&quot; for a speech between two enemies tryng to make a truce. <br /> If she try to use her powers on me this could save me. Anyway, yes, Dominate 3 was what I thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T10:34:47-08:00","id":1045854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1045848#post1045848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you don't want them to be punished unless they do something to warrant a punishment, and you still want them to be able to use those abilities against other targets. &amp;quot;Don't use Dominate or Majesty against me&amp;quot; would stop them from doing so, but it might not be nearly petty enough for the Dominate user's tastes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but also for another reason, in this way you know she tried to manipulate you. Just commanding her to do not use it you will never know if she tried and if she is &quot;trustworthy&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T10:43:32-08:00","id":1045859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1045851#post1045851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it could be a &quot;security strategy&quot; for a speech between two enemies tryng to make a truce.<br /> If she try to use her powers on me this could save me. Anyway, yes, Dominate 3 was what I thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Juuuust throwing this out there, but If you use Dominate when trying to make a truce with an Enemy... it might not go over to well in the future when / if they figure it out.<br /> <br /> Yes you could set up a contingency with Dominate 3. But I would think it would need to say Once you activate awe against me, jump out of a window. I don't think you could set it up for thinking about it because they might think about doing it before you even have your meeting and set off the contingency. Usually it's based on some sort of action not a thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: You added. <br /> <br /> You could dominate her to ask her if she is trustworthy. &quot;Answer all questions Truthfully&quot; ( dominate 1 ) Do you plan on fucking me over ever in the future? Are you trustworthy? Do you often back stab your friends/colleagues? ect<br /> <br /> Though, again, If you dominate her to see if she is trustworthy, it sort of implies you are not. She might start to wonder about that missing gap in time or wonder why she can't quite remember what you all talked about ... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-08-2017, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T14:01:30-08:00","id":1045984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1045851#post1045851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it could be a &quot;security strategy&quot; for a speech between two enemies tryng to make a truce.<br /> If she try to use her powers on me this could save me. Anyway, yes, Dominate 3 was what I thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like your idea of having your character install a self-defenestration command on someone to take effect if they screw you, it's not a good prevention tactic because your character is still screwed. They can order your character to go with them while they toss themselves through the nearest window. If you think the character is negotiating in good faith you should probably have your character install a more benign command for the other character to provide your character with a 1 minute warning before using their power in his presence or something to that effect. That way it gives your character time to leave or lash out before it would impact your character. If you are reasonably certain they intend to screw your character six ways from Sunday at the first opportunity, by all means have them eat plate glass the next time they try to cross your character. They're enemies, they're supposed to be doing crap like that to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T23:28:12-08:00","id":1046199,"title":"","content":"Well this, if extended to uses of Majesty to everyone, could be a nice and sadic punishment for any future use of this. I know this is not the most effective way to use it, but could be funny in a sadic way and last for: number of succeses in weeks, &quot;removing&quot; majesty for that time.<br /> <br /> She use Majesty and wake up herself falling in the void, she don't know what is happened and, using Majesty to feed wake up again out of a window....untill she don't understand the link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T03:33:15-08:00","id":1046232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1046199#post1046199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well this, if extended to uses of Majesty to everyone, could be a nice and sadic punishment for any future use of this. I know this is not the most effective way to use it, but could be funny in a sadic way and last for: number of succeses in weeks, &quot;removing&quot; majesty for that time.<br /> <br /> She use Majesty and wake up herself falling in the void, she don't know what is happened and, using Majesty to feed wake up again out of a window....untill she don't understand the link.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want sadistic and effective, have your character command her to immediately sever or bite off her tongue for a week whenever she uses Majesty. If she uses the power in public and around unknowing mortals. It would be an ongoing Masquerade breach if she shows up later with her tongue fully healed because everyone will have seen her take out her own tongue. She'll look like a desperate attention whore if she tries to explain it was just a prank and may get her perma banned from places if she keeps doing it.<br /> <br /> If you want to do an elaborate mind screw, you have the character install the command while disguised so if she hires (or involuntarily attracts) some random Mekhet to memory violate her, it doesn't trace back to your character. Bonus points if you possess another vampire who also doesn't like her either and install it in her while cruising around in that vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-09-2017, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T03:37:33-08:00","id":1046234,"title":"","content":"I like it, but the last part doesn't work. You can't use any Disciplines when possessing another character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T04:06:52-08:00","id":1046241,"title":"","content":"Devotion time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T04:34:31-08:00","id":1046243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1046234#post1046234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, but the last part doesn't work. You can't use any Disciplines when possessing another character.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>can</i>. That's why I said you get bonus points if you can do it. You don't need Possession to pull this off.<br /> The easiest way is to simply select someone who has Dominate in their repertoire already and command them to install the desired command on her the next time they see her.<br /> If you have Possession, you possess them and go pay her a visit.<br /> If you have Chain of Command, slightly different. Install on the soon to be possessed person with the command to mesmerize the target. Then you show up and install the command. Then possess them and go pay them a visit. (Use your host to carry your physical body for you.)<br /> There's no restriction on the number of commands that can be installed on a single target any longer.<br /> <br /> Chain of Command allows other possibilities by incorporating others to install multiple commands but the problem is though, the more random elements you need to incorporate for successful use of Dominate, the more likely there is for something to go wrong, so I generally prefer sticking with possession rather than telephone.<br /> <br /> If I had a character doing it to prove a point and had Chain of Command I'd have my character use it her own minions to install sequential commands. Bob installs mesmerize. Kevin installs the command about tongue severing the next time Majesty is used... Stuart installs a second application of mesmerize... Dave installs &quot;a command for the 2nd time Majesty is used...&quot; ad nauseaum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-09-2017, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T04:53:05-08:00","id":1046249,"title":"","content":"Page 133, in the description for Possession: &quot;She cannot use Disciplines or Blood Sorcery when possessing someone else, nor can she access any supernatural powers her victim may possess, but she otherwise controls his body totally.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T05:45:31-08:00","id":1046265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1046249#post1046249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 133, in the description for Possession: &amp;quot;She cannot use Disciplines or Blood Sorcery when possessing someone else, nor can she access any supernatural powers her victim may possess, but she otherwise controls his body totally.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The command is installed BEFORE you possess them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T05:55:00-08:00","id":1046270,"title":"","content":"I apologise for not reading your post properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T13:57:21-08:00","id":1046467,"title":"","content":"<b>How useful is an extra point of Blood Potency for a new character?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T14:10:26-08:00","id":1046474,"title":"","content":"Hard to say.<br /> <br /> It offers you a +1 to Physical rolls when Frenzying. Being able to spend 2 Vitae a turn allows you to use an ability and heal, or spend more to heal. Vampires are sort of glass cannons in that they don't heal very well, but can do a lot of damage. It really enhances senses a lot. But most things you'll only be seeing a +1 bonus to your die pools with. Things like Lashing Out. Which can be nice but it's only one die. Though if someone wants to fight your Lashing Out, they have to spend a point of Willpower if you're of higher Blood Potency. It also gives you some better resistances.<br /> <br /> That said, I found while playing that the Power Traits are basically the most expensive thing you can get, not counting 5-dot Merits, Rituals or Artifacts which can get ridiculously high. And in my game whenever I ended up trying to save for Primal Urge, I usually got swayed by something more useful immediately. That's Werewolf, though, and vampires don't have that much in comparison. So starting off at 2 can give you a little leg up in that regard, and it certainly fits if you want a character who is 'more' vampire than your standard feeble neonate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T14:15:47-08:00","id":1046475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1046467#post1046467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How useful is an extra point of Blood Potency for a new character?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between Blood Potency 1 and Blood Potency isn't <i>huge</i>, but it isn't insignificant. The big thing is it allows you to spend an extra point of Vitae per turn, which significantly expands your options in combat or other turn-based situations. You can store an extra point of Vitae, which is a nice but small bonus. You get an extra +1 to physical dice pools in Frenzy which is a mixed blessing unless you take advantage of it, like with Riding the Wave or Coil of the Wyrm. It gives you +1 Supernatural Tolerance, which is actually great to have. It gives you +1 to Lash Out dice pools, which is cool. And it gets you one step closer to Blood Potency 3, which is one step closer to Blood Potency 4, etc. and at higher levels of Blood Potency it becomes one of the most useful things you can spend experiences on.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, it depends on the character. A combat wombat who rides the wave at the drop of a hat, Lashes Out at everything that moves, and is constantly spending Vitae on physical intensity and healing will get a ton of mileage out of every dot of Blood Potency. A more reserved, mental or Social focused character who pulls all of the strings and has minions to do the dirty work for them will still find an extra dot of Blood Potency useful, but perhaps a bit less so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T17:10:12-08:00","id":1046532,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin describes the mechanical aspects pretty well, but depending on your group's setting there might also be social implications. For example, in your city having Blood Potency 1 might lead to being treated as worthless. Blood Potency 2 might be when a vampire starts showing that they've handled themselves well enough to not be considered a waste of space (and herd). Well, at least to those who are still able to discern a difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T23:46:36-08:00","id":1046656,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the responses! It definitely seems more efficient to use five of the starting 10 Merit points for an extra Blood Potency dot and then buying five Merits with your first five Experiences than to do it the other way around. It also seems more interesting for story reasons; I'd be likely to use my remaining five points to buy some &quot;inherent&quot; Merits like Acute Senses or Fleet of Foot (stuff you'd gain as part of the transformation), then add in more esoteric things like Allies or Haven as they cropped up in the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <b>New question!</b><br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I understand quite how Willpower works. You start off with dots equal to your Resolve + Composure. This is your maximum amount of Willpower. You can then &quot;spend&quot; it on stuff, like attempting to Ride the Wave of a Frenzy. I assume this is marked on your character sheet in the same way Health damage is, using the boxes beneath the dots. You can also &quot;lose&quot; a <i>dot </i>of Willpower, such as when you perform the Embrace on someone. In this case, you'd completely remove the dot and thereby reduce your maximum Willpower pool by one.<br /> <br /> <i>Spent </i>Willpower &quot;damage&quot; can be regained though your Mask/Dirge (are there other ways?). <i>Lost </i>Willpower <b>dots </b>must be replaced by purchasing a new dot for 1 Experience. I assume you don't buy new dots of Willpower directly, instead improving your Resolve and/or Composure stats and getting it that way. Does doing so grant an immediate dot of Willpower, or does it merely increase the potential and I'd need to fill the new, &quot;empty&quot; dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T00:02:15-08:00","id":1046662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1046656#post1046656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the responses! It definitely seems more efficient to use five of the starting 10 Merit points for an extra Blood Potency dot and then buying five Merits with your first five Experiences than to do it the other way around. It also seems more interesting for story reasons; I'd be likely to use my remaining five points to buy some &quot;inherent&quot; Merits like Acute Senses or Fleet of Foot (stuff you'd gain as part of the transformation), then add in more esoteric things like Allies or Haven as they cropped up in the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <b>New question!</b><br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I understand quite how Willpower works. You start off with dots equal to your Resolve + Composure. This is your maximum amount of Willpower. You can then &quot;spend&quot; it on stuff, like attempting to Ride the Wave of a Frenzy. I assume this is marked on your character sheet in the same way Health damage is, using the boxes beneath the dots. You can also &quot;lose&quot; a <i>dot </i>of Willpower, such as when you perform the Embrace on someone. In this case, you'd completely remove the dot and thereby reduce your maximum Willpower pool by one.<br /> <br /> <i>Spent </i>Willpower &quot;damage&quot; can be regained though your Mask/Dirge (are there other ways?). <i>Lost </i>Willpower <b>dots </b>must be replaced by purchasing a new dot for 1 Experience. I assume you don't buy new dots of Willpower directly, instead improving your Resolve and/or Composure stats and getting it that way. Does doing so grant an immediate dot of Willpower, or does it merely increase the potential and I'd need to fill the new, &quot;empty&quot; dot?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Embrace doesn't let you lose a dot of willpower.<br /> By the way, buying a dot of composure or resolve, immediately increase your willpower pool. In the same way buying a dot in Strenght rise your derived trait such as speed, and buying stamina rise your Health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-10-2017, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T00:23:47-08:00","id":1046670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1046662#post1046662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embrace doesn't let you lose a dot of willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry. It's a dot of Humanity. My bad!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:49:21-08:00","id":1046798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1046656#post1046656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the responses! It definitely seems more efficient to use five of the starting 10 Merit points for an extra Blood Potency dot and then buying five Merits with your first five Experiences than to do it the other way around. It also seems more interesting for story reasons; I'd be likely to use my remaining five points to buy some &quot;inherent&quot; Merits like Acute Senses or Fleet of Foot (stuff you'd gain as part of the transformation), then add in more esoteric things like Allies or Haven as they cropped up in the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <b>New question!</b><br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I understand quite how Willpower works. You start off with dots equal to your Resolve + Composure. This is your maximum amount of Willpower. You can then &quot;spend&quot; it on stuff, like attempting to Ride the Wave of a Frenzy. I assume this is marked on your character sheet in the same way Health damage is, using the boxes beneath the dots. You can also &quot;lose&quot; a <i>dot </i>of Willpower, such as when you perform the Embrace on someone. In this case, you'd completely remove the dot and thereby reduce your maximum Willpower pool by one.<br /> <br /> <i>Spent </i>Willpower &quot;damage&quot; can be regained though your Mask/Dirge (are there other ways?). <i>Lost </i>Willpower <b>dots </b>must be replaced by purchasing a new dot for 1 Experience. I assume you don't buy new dots of Willpower directly, instead improving your Resolve and/or Composure stats and getting it that way. Does doing so grant an immediate dot of Willpower, or does it merely increase the potential and I'd need to fill the new, &quot;empty&quot; dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also spend Willpower to gain bonuses on rolls (+3) and resistance stats (+2 if it's not rolled).<br /> <br /> For most living things, you also regain willpower when you sleep. For vampires, the intent is that they do not. There are some merits and supernatural powers for vampires that can regain their Willpower, but off the top of my head it's mostly just Mask/Dirge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T01:54:20-08:00","id":1047128,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Obfuscate 5:</b></u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He can turn an alleyway into a maze that nobody can escape from </div> </div> </div>Ho can you deal with this? I like this idea so much but how is it represented mechanically? I can use all the Obfuscate powers, at any distance and at any time but interacting with the object will show its real nature (for a brief istant) so, touching a wall where before there was a door could reveal that door right? Same thing is going towards an obfuscate stairs.<br /> And how could an alleyway become a maze? Can you &quot;close&quot; the two side of the street?<br /> <br /> A PC that is trying to escape from an Oubliette should roll something or is just a flavor concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T03:34:02-08:00","id":1047146,"title":"","content":"It's technically just flavor description. The average person is very reliant on sight to navigate and it is disorienting to have the scenery visually changing every time you touch it. I wouldn't automatically require someone to roll just to get out, they would have to describe how they're getting out/dealing with the shifting imagery. They'll need to do something that shows some thought as to how they'll overcome the illusion. (Using a stick to tap along the floor/ground or wall ahead of you at a slowed movement rate to find the exit or door knob works.) And of course if they lash out, the illusion goes away for good.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D has the concept of disbelieving illusions for saving throws (which you normally don't get for illusions) but technically the dissolution warp effect would constitute auto success. If you want to go that route, you could give them a perception check with a -5 penalty and add an Occult or Intelligence bonus to the perception check if they know it's an illusion or application of Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-11-2017, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T15:49:34-08:00","id":1047430,"title":"","content":"<b>How much of a vampire's body must remain intact (at the time of Embrace) for it to function?</b><br /> <br /> The Mekhet clan book has a vampire that was mummified before her Embrace; she had all of her internal organs <i>removed</i> and <i>then</i> became a vampire. She points this out, and that she can still think (despite having <i>no brain</i>) and Feed (despite having <i>no stomach</i>). Could someone whose, say, muscles were atrophied be posthumously Embraced and still be able to move around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","user":"Gellydog","date":". 02-11-2017, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T18:26:07-08:00","id":1047471,"title":"","content":"Nitocris, right? I think she was lying about that, or at least someone else suggests she was.<br /> <br /> Posthumous embraces require it to occur 'before significant decomposition sets in.' But you could always justify it happening later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T18:29:00-08:00","id":1047473,"title":"","content":"<b>Are there any Gangrel or Nosferatu bloodlines that combine Protean and Nightmare?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T18:34:59-08:00","id":1047477,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel have the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Carnon\" target=\"_blank\">Carnon</a>, from Circle of the Crone. And the Nosferatu have the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rakshasa_(VTR)\" target=\"_blank\">Rakshasa</a>, from Bloodlines: the Hidden.<br /> <br /> You can see all the bloodlines <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Bloodlines_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. And various other first edition Vampire things <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Vampire:_the_Requiem\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. There's also a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf Wiki.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Added links for Carnon and Rakshasa. 02-11-2017, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T18:52:00-08:00","id":1047480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1047477#post1047477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gangrel have the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Carnon\" target=\"_blank\">Carnon</a>, from Circle of the Crone. And the Nosferatu have the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rakshasa_(VTR)\" target=\"_blank\">Rakshasa</a>, from Bloodlines: the Hidden.<br /> <br /> You can see all the bloodlines <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Bloodlines_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. And various other first edition Vampire things <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Vampire:_the_Requiem\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. There's also a <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf Wiki.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Merci. Gangrel and Nosferatu are my two favorite clans, so I thought it might be fun to combine them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T21:03:10-08:00","id":1047531,"title":"","content":"In that case I'd definitely recommend taking a look at the Moroi from the Ordo book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T00:18:38-08:00","id":1047588,"title":"","content":"Does the Daeva Clan Bane apply to 'living' supernaturals? Or some? Or only pure mortals? I've personally been figuring I'd use the same rules as what counts as a mortal for The Kiss/Assault to apply, since it seems to be in the same ballpark, but I wanted to know what others think, or if a dev has commented on it in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T01:02:13-08:00","id":1047597,"title":"","content":"The first sentence in the bane description makes me believe that it should apply to regular humans and minor splats only (basically everyone with Integrity). However, a crossover heavy chronicle might gain if it's extended to mages, bound, beasts and werewolves.<br /> The Kiss/Assault has examples that covers most major splats already. If I were to expand on the list I'd guess all humans, minor splats and mages (and probably deviants when that book comes out) are subject to Scarred/Swooning while vampires, werewolves, mummies, changelings, bound, demons, beasts and stranger things are immune unless the vampire spends a Willpower point.<br /> <br /> Edit: It seems weird to me that the Daeva clan bane is basically pointless for all Daevas at BP 6+. It would be incredibly rare to drink from the same human more than once after that since it is so extremely expensive for a resource vampires has a harder time replenishing than other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-12-2017, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T08:20:25-08:00","id":1047709,"title":"","content":"Celerity can be used to restore the surprise. How? What contested roll should be used? I'd say no stealth beacause is something based on speed. What about Dex + Brawl/weapon + Celerity vs. Wits + Composure + celerity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-12-2017, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T06:39:32-08:00","id":1048212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1047709#post1047709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity can be used to restore the surprise. How? What contested roll should be used? I'd say no stealth beacause is something based on speed. What about Dex + Brawl/weapon + Celerity vs. Wits + Composure + celerity?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I apologize, but I have no idea what you are asking here.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T06:48:48-08:00","id":1048215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1048212#post1048212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I apologize, but I have no idea what you are asking here.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I try to express myself better. Sorry for my bad english :P<br /> I'd just know what kind of roll do you use to regain the surprise using celerity. It is written you can launch surprise attack using celerity. I suppose it is not intended to be used while you are hidden beacause it is already contempled the surprise roll in that situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T07:00:59-08:00","id":1048219,"title":"","content":"People don't really expect to be attacked by the guy standing halfway down the street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T07:06:39-08:00","id":1048221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1048219#post1048219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People don't really expect to be attacked by the guy standing halfway down the street.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so how does celerity help in the roll? Even without celerity I can punch someone that doesn't expect to be attacked. It'd just add celerity to the surprise roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T07:21:10-08:00","id":1048225,"title":"","content":"There's a <i>bit</i> of a difference between a regular sucker punch and a dude just appearing out of thin air in front of you and swinging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T07:31:30-08:00","id":1048230,"title":"","content":"Ok, still didn't understand how celerity is involved in the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T07:38:52-08:00","id":1048233,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> is well aware of that and is actually wondering how that is represented mechanically.<br /> I'd say Dexterity+Subterfuge vs Wits+Composure makes the most sense. Rushing with Celerity is really not the same thing as ambushing or sneaking up on someone like with regular surprise rolls. Your opponent probably already has eyes on you so you'd need to fool them into thinking you're going to do one thing and then do another. That's Subterfuge for me. It would make sense to add Celerity to the roll, but I think being able to deny your opponent Defence can be too powerful and that specific Celerity power doesn't have a per Scene limit. I'd also say that every subsequent attempt would come at a cumulative -1 penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:23:02-08:00","id":1048378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1048215#post1048215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I try to express myself better. Sorry for my bad english :P<br /> I'd just know what kind of roll do you use to regain the surprise using celerity. It is written you can launch surprise attack using celerity. I suppose it is not intended to be used while you are hidden beacause it is already contempled the surprise roll in that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what I am understanding you want to know either, &quot;How can I make a surprise attack with Celerity?&quot; or &quot;How can I regain a surprise in combat?&quot; <br /> for &quot;How can I make a surprise attack with Celerity?&quot;<br /> Mechanically you just do. roll the first round as a surprise attack which means there is no defense and they don't get a turn that round. As someone said, you dont really expect the guy who is two blocks away to suddenly stab you in the back. You can use the Danger Sense merit or roll a Wit+ Comp to notice the danger coming, but I think celerity would negate that because you literally move faster than the eye can see. Personally I definitely would not give them a roll to notice the sneak attack if they were also Obfuscated. Though if you were just hiding and waiting to ambush, then using celerity to jump them when they got close, then I would allow the Danger Sense to be rolled.<br /> <br /> I assume you are using the text that states the following:<br /> <br /> <i>Multiply her speed by her dots in Celerity plus one. Moving<br /> in this way is sudden, jarring, the vampire appears to shift from<br /> point to point without crossing the space in-between. <u><b>She may<br /> use this to briefly avoid detection or launch surprise attacks.</b></u></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1048221#post1048221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, so how does celerity help in the roll? Even without celerity I can punch someone that doesn't expect to be attacked. It'd just add celerity to the surprise roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really use dice to surprise attack, you roll your Brawl or weaponry without subtracting the defense. With Celerity you don't have to roll the stealth checks or whatever, as you just appear there and boom, swing. <br /> <br /> <i><u><b>&quot;Surprise </b></u>When your character<br /> walks into an ambush or unexpectedly stumbles into<br /> an opponent, you must check to see if he can respond.<br /> Roll Wits + Composure. If you get no successes your character<br /> is taken unawares and cannot act in the first turn of<br /> combat. Initiative is rolled for him in the next turn. One<br /> or more successes allow your character to behave normally<br /> and respond to the encounter.\u200b<br /> <b>A character taken by surprise has no Defense</b> in the<br /> first turn of combat. His Defense trait is not subtracted<br /> from attackers dice pools. His armor (if any) still is,<br /> though.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> To answer the second &quot;How can I regain surprise in combat&quot; You can't. The two characters are already fighting, they are both going to be on guard. Even if you are moving faster than the eye can see, the other character is still waiting for something to happen and prepped to react. Once initiative is rolled, there is no going back to unaware.<br /> <br /> <i>Targets already involved in combat cannot be ambushed.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-13-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T13:21:42-08:00","id":1048404,"title":"","content":"Ok thank you all. I misunderstood the text. I thought it was possible to regain surprise with celerity? Even during fight. <br /> Well, ok <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Anyway, just to say, I don't like the &quot;interview with vampire&quot; celerity effect. I prefer a more realistic view, like let a running people record go at 2x \u00f7 6x <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> But this is just a personal taste of mine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T06:17:28-08:00","id":1049816,"title":"","content":"Yes, me again :P<br /> <br /> Auspex 4: what is the range of the &quot;full memory&quot; thay someone can uncover at activation? The last night? The last month? The whole childood? How do you deal with this power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T07:31:16-08:00","id":1049838,"title":"","content":"As I previously stated, I don't allow gratuitous fishing expeditions with Auspex use. A player should have an idea of what they're looking for or what incident they want to corroborate, as such, they should be using their social skills (which are often nonexistent for Mekhet) to try and get the person to direct their thoughts toward the matter. Most people's memories are not that great (eidetic memory is a merit, not an innate ability), so the further back they go wandering aimlessly, the less likely they're going to pull up something useful. If they get a &quot;full memory&quot; they successfully pull up enough details of the 5 Ws of a specific incident &quot;from the perspective of the individual&quot; provided the individual was involved. If they're going around just trying to trigger memories randomly order to set off a condition, they may not get something they'll necessarily &quot;want&quot; their victim to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T04:12:09-08:00","id":1051931,"title":"","content":"Auspex 5 <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The vampire\u2019s senses part from his body, and can travel the world. Multiply the vampire\u2019s Speed by his (Auspex + Blood Potency). The vampire is not bound by gravity, and can travel through physical obstacles and even into the ground. He cannot interact with the physical world in any way when separate from his body.<br /> <br /> the way it is written you are incorporeal but interacting with the real world.<br /> <br /> How about the Shadow? Do you find it a stretch to allow Auspex 5 user to interact with spirits?</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T04:24:08-08:00","id":1051934,"title":"","content":"The Shadow's another realm entirely, Auspex 5 essentially puts them in Twilight. A devotion could probably project them into the Shadow, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T04:27:54-08:00","id":1051939,"title":"","content":"Could a devotion with Vigor allow to interact with the physical world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T04:29:56-08:00","id":1051941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1051939#post1051939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a devotion with Vigor allow to interact with the physical world?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:04:58-08:00","id":1051966,"title":"","content":"Vampire Aye uses Dominate 5 to possess Vampire Bee. While possessed by Aye, Vampire Bee diablerizes Vampire Sea, who had gone into torpor three months prior with the intent of thinning their blood potency and did a slipshod job of concealing their whereabouts. Who gains the benefits and drawbacks of diablerie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:16:37-08:00","id":1051968,"title":"","content":"Vampire Bee","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:43:33-08:00","id":1052118,"title":"","content":"Could Vampire Bee even draw blood from Sea? Dominate 5 &quot;nor can she access any supernatural powers the victim may posess&quot;.<br /> Since vamps don't give up their Vitae by simple cutting, but other vamps can steal it from each other because they're vampires(supernatural ability), could Aye even use Bee's ability to siphon off the Vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T14:26:33-08:00","id":1052185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1051966#post1051966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire Aye uses Dominate 5 to possess Vampire Bee. While possessed by Aye, Vampire Bee diablerizes Vampire Sea, who had gone into torpor three months prior with the intent of thinning their blood potency and did a slipshod job of concealing their whereabouts. Who gains the benefits and drawbacks of diablerie?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since Vampire Aye is the one doing the Diablerie even if it is in Bee's body... I would say that Aye gets the pros and cons. Diablerie taints your soul; it doesn't live in your belly. Once you went back to your body, you take you/your soul. with you and all your powers. Would Vampire Bee gain all your experience? ( and by experience I mean both in and out of game. you get EXP for experiences in game. ) that body is wholey unaware of what you are doing while riding around in it. <br /> <br /> And absolutely Vampire Aye could get blood from Sea. Vampires take blood from the unwilling all the time it's not really a &quot;power&quot; it's what they do. They sink their fangs in and feed... it would be like asking if a human can eat a cheeseburger when you're in it's body. Of course it can... You couldn't use Bee's protean or animalism or whatever disciplines or coils it had, but I don't see why you couldn't feed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T16:45:55-08:00","id":1052272,"title":"","content":"On page 205 there are rules about what happens if a Strix diablerizes a vampire while possessing another vampire. The Strix gains one dot of Shadow Potency while the possessed vampire gains all the benefits and drawbacks of the diablerie, including the potential Humanity loss.<br /> However, this kind of possession is a lot more than what Dominate is able to perform. With Dominate you simply send your consciousness to possess the victim while the Strix possesses with their Corpus and all. I'd say that a Dominate user would receive no benefits from committing diablerie while possessing someone else, and might not even be able to perform diablerie at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:40:22-08:00","id":1052657,"title":"","content":"I can't remember where and probably I'm just wrong but I think I've reade something about cainite Heresy in requiem. Can you confirm or give me some information about this or isn't there in requiem? <br /> Is Caine bound with vampire mytology anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:46:05-08:00","id":1052662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1052657#post1052657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember where and probably I'm just wrong but I think I've reade something about cainite Heresy in requiem. Can you confirm or give me some information about this or isn't there in requiem? <br /> Is Caine bound with vampire mytology anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cainite Heresy is a Hunter Compact from Night Stalkers. They hunt vampires and it's heavily implied that they are the unwitting pawns of other vampires. There is also mention of a Cainite Heresy in Fall of the Camarilla. It's possible that they are the antecedents of the vampires pulling the strings of the modern Hunter Compact of the same name.<br /> And no, Cain has basically nothing to do with vampire mythology in Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-21-2017, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:57:27-08:00","id":1052672,"title":"","content":"Thanks a lot. <br /> Is there a reason beacause they use the Caine name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:58:29-08:00","id":1052674,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cainites\" target=\"_blank\">Cainite Heresy</a> was a real thing drawn upon for both games, though in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:46:04-08:00","id":1053430,"title":"","content":"Also a little fun for the developers to throw something in with a familiar name but a different execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T23:02:50-08:00","id":1053668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1053430#post1053430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a little fun for the developers to throw something in with a familiar name but a different execution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I know but I'd like to know what's the reason behind this name for a group of hunters in the case I will implement them in my chronicle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T23:14:20-08:00","id":1053671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1053668#post1053668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes I know but I'd like to know what's the reason behind this name for a group of hunters in the case I will implement them in my chronicle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of addressed in Night Stalkers. They have a fanatical obsession with killing vampires, and they always ask their victims &quot;Who is Cain?&quot; first. When the victim inevitably has no idea what they are talking about, they kill the victim. If I recall correctly, they might also use &quot;Who is Cain?&quot; as a code phrase to recognize each other. I don't remember what the appropriate response is. At any rate, they seem to be getting fed misinformation about vampires (as well as some accurate information) from their mysterious sponsors, and the importance of this Cain figure might be part of that misinformation.<br /> <br /> It's been a long time since I read the book and I don't have it any more, so I may be misremembering details. I'd recommend picking up a copy if you want to know more about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T23:17:34-08:00","id":1053673,"title":"","content":"Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:41:37-08:00","id":1059638,"title":"","content":"The situation is this: two vampires are obfuscated 3. One know that the other is in the room but can't see her and choose to still on the doorway. The other one is not aware about the vampire that covers the door and want to get out. <br /> How should the situation be solved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:05:07-08:00","id":1059655,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate 1 wants to leave but does not know about Obfuscate 2 being at the door, then why wouldn't they just walk out the door like any other semi intelligent mobile entity? <br /> <br /> <br /> Depending on who you ask on this forum unless number 2 can see number 1 they should step out of the way for no discernible reason other than to let the obfuscated presence that is 1 go by. <br /> As far as I'm concerned 2 can try and Lash Out and force 1 to become visible (if he wins). But he does that at the risk of making himself visible and unable to use any Obfuscate against 1 for the rest of the scene regardless of the outcome since those you attack become immune to your obfuscate. Alternatively he could do something else to try and draw 1 out like use Dread Presence or randomly throwing things around to provoke a response.<br /> <br /> Personally I would just roll the modified perception checks for both parties. If they both fail, 1 goes out the door while 2 continues to wait. If they both succeed they both see each other. If one wins, the other fails, the winner spots the loser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-07-2017, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:24:19-08:00","id":1059713,"title":"","content":"2 leaves through a window because subconsciously the door doesn't register as a viable exit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:59:16-08:00","id":1059728,"title":"","content":"Yes but the door is the only way to get out in this case.<br /> <br /> By the way, isn't needed to percive the obfuscate 2 (with the contested roll or with auspex) before to lash out against her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-07-2017, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T17:45:44-08:00","id":1059848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1059638#post1059638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The situation is this: two vampires are obfuscated 3. One know that the other is in the room but can't see her and choose to still on the doorway. The other one is not aware about the vampire that covers the door and want to get out.<br /> How should the situation be solved?</div> </div> </div> </div>Joke answer: Microwave some popcorn, lindfold and earplug both players, put them in that situation, watch what happens.<br /> <br /> Serious answer: Unless vampire A tries to evade whoever's blocking the exit vampire B automatically succeeds on his roll to block him, vampire A can now see vampire B.<br /> <br /> And yes you need to perceive someone under Obfuscate to be able to lash out against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T23:28:27-08:00","id":1059963,"title":"","content":"Assuming that a member of a bloodline joined her sire's bloodline does she count members of the same bloodline (who did not become members through the intercession of an avus) as thrice-removed for purposes of blood sympathy since four times removed is for clan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T07:20:17-08:00","id":1060068,"title":"","content":"Probably. Without a family tree to reference, I would say they are likely cousins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T05:31:42-08:00","id":1060481,"title":"","content":"Hi guys, <br /> <br /> Let me solve a doubt with you. Abou Nightmare 1 Dread Presence, can a vampire with this discipline create an illusion of something that actually block someone's vision? like a smal point of darkess in front of him or an ilusion of a bag on someone's head and cause blinded tilt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T06:33:29-08:00","id":1060493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1060481#post1060481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi guys,<br /> <br /> Let me solve a doubt with you. Abou Nightmare 1 Dread Presence, can a vampire with this discipline create an illusion of something that actually block someone's vision? like a smal point of darkess in front of him or an ilusion of a bag on someone's head and cause blinded tilt?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, Unfortunately they can not. You could create an illusion of spots or a bag on someone's head, but they will quickly realize it's not real. at best you might be able to give them a negative for a turn, but the bag illusion doesn't last long enough to make it a lasting tilt. They are just quick flashes meant to unsettle/scare your victim. a Few seconds...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;These illusions can only affect two<br /> senses each, and must be small \u2014 no larger than a small dog,<br /> and no louder than a shout. <u><b>They only last for a turn or two </b></u>at<br /> most, but they\u2019re always unsettling.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T07:33:43-08:00","id":1060513,"title":"","content":"That said, a turn or two might be enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T08:25:21-08:00","id":1060528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1060493#post1060493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, Unfortunately they can not. You could create an illusion of spots or a bag on someone's head, but they will quickly realize it's not real. at best you might be able to give them a negative for a turn, but the bag illusion doesn't last long enough to make it a lasting tilt. They are just quick flashes meant to unsettle/scare your victim. a Few seconds...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;These illusions can only affect two<br /> senses each, and must be small \u2014 no larger than a small dog,<br /> and no louder than a shout. <u><b>They only last for a turn or two </b></u>at<br /> most, but they\u2019re always unsettling.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it was actually what i wanted to know, although it is just for a short time (one or two turns) it will still cause a negative effect. then i can presume that in one/two turns a target would not have his defense against the vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T09:18:28-08:00","id":1060544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Glauber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1060528#post1060528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it was actually what i wanted to know, although it is just for a short time (one or two turns) it will still cause a negative effect. then i can presume that in one/two turns a target would not have his defense against the vampire</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh... That would seem to be possible under a very technical reading of the rules, but it's clearly against the intent of the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T10:21:43-08:00","id":1060565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1060544#post1060544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhhh... That would seem to be possible under a very technical reading of the rules, but it's clearly against the intent of the power.</div> </div> </div> </div> I also wouldn't allow for a total loss of defense. I would just give the attacker a plus to hit the victim or perhaps a negative to hit the Nos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T14:38:10-08:00","id":1060665,"title":"","content":"Is there anyone that Vampires absolutely cannot drain for Vitae, even with special Merits and powers? For example, would a Vampire existing in Twilight be able to drain ghosts and spirits of their Corpus with the Unnatural Affinity Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T14:48:52-08:00","id":1060669,"title":"","content":"Fire Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T15:19:58-08:00","id":1060680,"title":"","content":"Fetches, from Changeling first edition.<br /> <br /> 'although fetches bleed like mortals, their blood isn\u2019t nourishing to vampires, and the undead feel a profound sense of unease after feeding on them. This unease usually leads to terrifying dreams the next day \u2014 the vampire can\u2019t shake the feeling that he has transgressed against something more powerful than he, something that had a prior claim to this \u201cmortal.\u201d'<br /> <br /> There's bound to be more. As Elfive pointed out, even a vampire with Unnatural Affinity may regret trying to drain a Helion. Strix in their 'true' forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T16:28:23-08:00","id":1060693,"title":"","content":"With Unnatural Affinity in 2E it's only the ST that can say for certain that something is off limits to vampires. It's just that it might not be healthy when it comes to Strix or entities based around vampire banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T17:16:01-08:00","id":1061078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1060669#post1060669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire Spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoken like a vampire without Resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T20:03:17-07:00","id":1061705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061078#post1061078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spoken like a vampire without Resilience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, pick up the tea pot off the fire without any protection, you can try drinking it's contents but you'll still burn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T00:13:31-07:00","id":1061743,"title":"","content":"I can see some STs having fun with secondary effects if drinking from a fire spirit or helion, but by the rules what you drink from the spirit should be perfectly fine for the vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T02:35:31-07:00","id":1061769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061743#post1061743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see some STs having fun with secondary effects if drinking from a fire spirit or helion, but by the rules what you drink from the spirit should be perfectly fine for the vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the rules, the spirit needs to be of a biological thing to have blood that's drinkable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T03:47:36-07:00","id":1061775,"title":"","content":"The Unnatural Affinity text is a bit weird, but common sense says that being able to physically interact with the being should be enough or several listed examples would be impossible to drink from. Regardless, I was replying to the possibility of deleterious effects for a vampire drinking from a fire spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T07:27:16-07:00","id":1061815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061705#post1061705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, pick up the tea pot off the fire without any protection, you can try drinking it's contents but you'll still burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why I wouldn't if I was a supernaturally resilient creature that didn't require bodily integrity to survive and was fueled by tea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061769#post1061769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the rules, the spirit needs to be of a biological thing to have blood that's drinkable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you enough Coil of Divinity or Unnatiral Affinity - Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T10:48:47-07:00","id":1061881,"title":"","content":"Resilence:<br /> <br /> A pc with 7 healts boxes takes 14 bashing. Does active Resilence come before or after the upgrading damages from bashing to lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T11:27:06-07:00","id":1061892,"title":"","content":"Before, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T11:50:50-07:00","id":1061895,"title":"","content":"Oh that's a pity :'(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T11:58:13-07:00","id":1061900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061881#post1061881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resilence:<br /> <br /> A pc with 7 healts boxes takes 14 bashing. Does active Resilence come before or after the upgrading damages from bashing to lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Resilience goes into effect when you are hit. So if you were hit for 14B it would resist that as per your resilience dots. If you were hit for 2L it would deal with that and you would take 0. You do not mark your damage, then erase it. So if you had 1 resilience you would still take 12 bashing. If you had 5 resilience ( which you couldn't have with only 7 health, most you could have is 1 with that health pool..) and spent your 1 vitae you would only take 8 bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-13-2017, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T12:14:43-07:00","id":1061909,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061815#post1061815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see why I wouldn't if I was a supernaturally resilient creature that didn't require bodily integrity to survive and was fueled by tea.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you write fire elemental on your paper, it does not mean you can actually gain sustenance from your fire elemental. And I think you missed the metaphor that went along with a tea pot... I do believe that the person did not mean a literal tea pot full of literal tea. <br /> <br /> Even if you were a supernaturally resilient creature that had a bane to fire, it might not be beneficial to feed from a fire creature as you might spend more blood healing than you would be able to get drinking. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061815#post1061815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if you enough Coil of Divinity or Unnatiral Affinity - Spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unnatural Affinity: <br /> <br /> <i>Drawback: This advantage does not inherently mean the<br /> character is (more) able to feed from the chosen subject. For<br /> example, ghosts exist in an ethereal state, and don\u2019t have<br /> physical blood.<br /> <br /> <b>If you take this Merit, work with your Storyteller to determine<br /> how your character might feed from these monsters.</b></i><br /> <br /> Just because you wrote ghost on your paper does not mean you can actually feed from a ghost. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T12:15:10-07:00","id":1061910,"title":"","content":"That depends, was the damage from a single source (like falling) or from multiple sources in a single turn (like being shot, stabbed, punched by multiple attackers in the same turn.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T12:40:36-07:00","id":1061921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061910#post1061910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends, was the damage from a single source (like falling) or from multiple sources in a single turn (like being shot, stabbed, punched by multiple attackers in the same turn.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are talking about resilience and how to resist the damage, you are correct in the fact you would use different math for different things.<br /> <br /> Bane sources it's just resilience dots, non-bane sources ( which is what I used in my math) is dots +1<br /> <br /> If that 14 Bashing came from 10 different sources you'd probably be in trouble as it says, &quot;No effect of resilience may be used more than once per turn,&quot; but again I assumed that it came from one source.<br /> <br /> But it wouldn't matter if you were getting shot, punched or stabbed, or even falling, for vampires it's all bashing (unless some other special thing says it's not )<br /> <br /> <br /> (EDIT) Disclaimer:<br /> I vaguely remember a thread on here saying that the effect lasted 1 whole turn, so even if you got hit 10 times that turn you would subtract your resilience dots from each hit for that turn... but I can't seem to find that thread to verify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-13-2017, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T12:41:53-07:00","id":1061924,"title":"","content":"From a single source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T13:10:08-07:00","id":1061943,"title":"","content":"So from a single source... 14 bashing from a single source rolls to 7 lethal. So if Resilience is active for that turn you would take the character's Resilience score +1 and subtract that amount from the tally of 7 lethal. So the character would have no more than 5 lethal since the minimum amount they negate is 2 levels. (Unless they can reflexively heal additional damage by other means.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T13:15:03-07:00","id":1061945,"title":"","content":"How do vampires hunt in places and times with unlit nights? Do they sniff for blood or do they have low-light vision?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T13:40:14-07:00","id":1061960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061945#post1061945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do vampires hunt in places and times with unlit nights? Do they sniff for blood or do they have low-light vision?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. Mechanically speaking, vampires suffer no penalties from lack of lighting short of complete darkness. In complete darkness, they take only -2 to rolls based on vision. This is described as their vision in dark conditions being superior to humans, as well as their other senses compensating for the reduced visual acuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-13-2017, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T13:52:46-07:00","id":1061968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061943#post1061943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from a single source... 14 bashing from a single source rolls to 7 lethal. So if Resilience is active for that turn you would take the character's Resilience score +1 and subtract that amount from the tally of 7 lethal. So the character would have no more than 5 lethal since the minimum amount they negate is 2 levels. (Unless they can reflexively heal additional damage by other means.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd subtract Resilience from the incoming damage: 14B. If they have Resilience 1 they'd end up with 5L and 2B. Just enough to hit that sweet spot where you gain a beat from taking Lethal damage in the three last health boxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T14:15:54-07:00","id":1061982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061960#post1061960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both. Mechanically speaking, vampires suffer no penalties from lack of lighting short of complete darkness. In complete darkness, they take only -2 to rolls based on vision. This is described as their vision in dark conditions being superior to humans, as well as their other senses compensating for the reduced visual acuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>and on anything but a new moon far from any city, there is some light *fanged grin*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T16:19:48-07:00","id":1062048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061943#post1061943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from a single source... 14 bashing from a single source rolls to 7 lethal. So if Resilience is active for that turn you would take the character's Resilience score +1 and subtract that amount from the tally of 7 lethal. So the character would have no more than 5 lethal since the minimum amount they negate is 2 levels. (Unless they can reflexively heal additional damage by other means.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like tessie and I have both said, You take it upon incoming damage, you do not take it, then erase it. If you have 1 resilience, take 14 Bashing, and it is not a bane source you negate 2 bashing damage meaning you take 12 bashing. If you have 7 Health that is 5 Lethal and 2 bashing. <br /> <br /> 14 - 2 = 12 = XXXXX / / <br /> Then if you wanted to or able to you could reflexively heal from the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T16:33:19-07:00","id":1062054,"title":"","content":"Yes I understood Thank you. <br /> <br /> Another question not related to resilence.:<br /> <br /> Can I with, auspex 2, ask: Where is (or what is) &quot;his&quot; heaven? <br /> <br /> It should be a secret. Is it legit? <br /> <br /> What about<b></b>: did him killed mr. X?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T17:05:32-07:00","id":1062071,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can ask haven location. I would penalize the roll based on the ranks of safe place etc. the other character has invested in the merit. And they only get a yes/no imagery.<br /> <br /> Yes, that's a valid question too. But again you only get yes/no imagery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T17:53:34-07:00","id":1062097,"title":"","content":"Auspex exists to dig out secrets. I wouldn't penalize with Safe Place or Haven dots since those dots do not represent any type of supernatural hiding. The answer might not be very helpful since you'd probably get a vision of the location of the haven, but no idea where that location might be unless you happen to recognize it.<br /> <br /> The second question is definitely possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T18:35:06-07:00","id":1062114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061909#post1061909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you write fire elemental on your paper, it does not mean you can actually gain sustenance from your fire elemental. And I think you missed the metaphor that went along with a tea pot... I do believe that the person did not mean a literal tea pot full of literal tea.<br /> <br /> Even if you were a supernaturally resilient creature that had a bane to fire, it might not be beneficial to feed from a fire creature as you might spend more blood healing than you would be able to get drinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>The teapot is the fire spirit and I am the vampire, I understand the metaphor.<br /> <br /> It might not be beneficial but with enough Resilience it could be. As long as the damage is equal to or less than double your resilience dots and you get at least Resilience dots <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">+ 2 vitae the vampire comes out ahead. Even if you end up having to heal a bit of lethal with your own stored vitae could be worth eating a fire spirit in front of someone to prove how hardcore you are.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unnatural Affinity:<br /> <br /> <i>Drawback: This advantage does not inherently mean the<br /> character is (more) able to feed from the chosen subject. For<br /> example, ghosts exist in an ethereal state, and don\u2019t have<br /> physical blood.<br /> <br /> <b>If you take this Merit, work with your Storyteller to determine<br /> how your character might feed from these monsters.</b></i><br /> <br /> Just because you wrote ghost on your paper does not mean you can actually feed from a ghost. </div> </div> </div>Pop across the gauntlet or head down to the underworld and you can physically feed from spirits, converting their essence/plasm into vitae. If your ST won't allow that just don't buy the merit because they clearly don't want players to have it in their game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9368,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","user":"PrinceRaven","date":". 03-13-2017, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T19:49:54-07:00","id":1062137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062114#post1062114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pop across the gauntlet or head down to the underworld and you can physically feed from spirits, converting their essence/plasm into vitae. If your ST won't allow that just don't buy the merit because they clearly don't want players to have it in their game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like vampires can just... do that. This is stuff well outside their standard area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T02:55:44-07:00","id":1062214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062137#post1062137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that like vampires can just... do that. This is stuff well outside their standard area.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's in the setting then they can get there easily. There are 5+ tools at a vampire's disposal to get someone to teach them how to get there or transport back and forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T04:35:58-07:00","id":1062232,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say easy since that kind of knowledge isn't common to vampires, but there are at least two blood sorcery disciplines that could be able to open Avernian Gates or pass through a Locus. In the case of Avernian Gates you don't even need any supernatural powers as long as you know how to open one properly. I'm not familiar enough with Werewolf yet to know if that's the case with Loci as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-14-2017, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:11:31-07:00","id":1062326,"title":"","content":"Vampires have a nigh unstoppable nemeses from the lower depths. There is an entire clan capable of entering the Twilight at will. Bloodlines capable of trapping ghosts, and spirits, and shadows, and opening two way portals to Twilight or Shadow. And all five covenants empowered to exercise control over others and taking what they want using supernatural powers and entities to do so.<br /> A vampire completely ignorant of the existence of otherworldly realms and other supernatural creatures would be the exception, not the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-13-2017, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T09:43:18-07:00","id":1062339,"title":"","content":"Knowledge required to actually access other realms, which was what you said was easy for vampires. I never said knowledge about other realms or their inhabitants. It might be easy to enter other realms once you have that kind of knowledge or entered the right bloodline, but that's certainly not common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062326#post1062326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an entire clan capable of entering the Twilight at will.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The Mekhet that learn Auspex 5 are probably a minority, so it's far from the entire clan.<br /> 2. No Discipline is clan exclusive.<br /> 3. You don't actually enter Twilight. You just send a projection that exists in one type of Twilight. Most likely the least populated that relates to the mages' Mind Arcanum so they wouldn't see any inhabitants.<br /> 4. Twilight is not a different realm so the point is moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T10:20:21-07:00","id":1062358,"title":"","content":"That mental projection explicitly can't touch anything, including other projections. So it wouldn't be able to interact with ghosts or spirits even if it <i>wasn't</i> on the wrong frequency to even see them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:36:40-07:00","id":1062394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062114#post1062114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pop across the gauntlet or head down to the underworld and you can physically feed from spirits, converting their essence/plasm into vitae. If your ST won't allow that just don't buy the merit because they clearly don't want players to have it in their game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they just want players to use it as a way to get around feeding restrictions, not as a way to feed on impossible prey. When I read Unnatural Affinity, I see &quot;My elder doesn't have to spend Willpower to feed on werewolves,&quot; not &quot;my character is physically capable of feeding on ghosts.&quot; If you have some other ability that makes your character capable of feeding on ghosts, then Unnatural Affinity can allow them to do so without having to spend Willpower when their Blood Potency reaches 6 or higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:59:42-07:00","id":1062413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062358#post1062358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That mental projection explicitly can't touch anything, including other projections. So it wouldn't be able to interact with ghosts or spirits even if it <i>wasn't</i> on the wrong frequency to even see them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Obviously SOME things are capable of seeing and interacting with that form else there would be no mention of what happens if they are prevented from returning to their material form.<br /> The ability to physically interact with something has nothing to do with my point that anyone claiming vampires are utterly ignorant about the existence of other realms and supernatural creatures is a moronic assumption given the fact that those very elements are thrown at vampires in a default setting.<br /> <br /> What kind of mass narcissistic delusion are Mekhet operating under to insist other realms of existence aren't real when the pinnacle of their defining power permits them limited entry onto another realm.<br /> How about Acolytes summoning things from who knows where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-14-2017, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:08:12-07:00","id":1062417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062413#post1062413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of mass narcissistic delusion are Mekhet operating under to insist other realms of existence aren't real when the pinnacle of their defining power permits them limited entry onto another realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so first off, no it doesn't. It lets them float around <i>this</i> realm in an intangible state where they can't see any ephemeral beings.<br /> <br /> And second, there is a <i>vast</i> gulf between knowing spirits exist and &quot;popping across the gauntlet&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, summoning, there's where we get a bit of traction, I'll admit. Although depending on how it works using it to feed might turn out to be unsustainable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:08:46-07:00","id":1062418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062413#post1062413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ability to physically interact with something has nothing to do with my point that anyone claiming vampires are utterly ignorant about the existence of other realms and supernatural creatures is a moronic assumption given the fact that those very elements are thrown at vampires in a default setting.<br /> <br /> What kind of mass narcissistic delusion are Mekhet operating under to insist other realms of existence aren't real when the pinnacle of their defining power permits them limited entry onto another realm.<br /> How about Acolytes summoning things from who knows where?</div> </div> </div> </div>I repeat: That's <i>not</i> what I said. That is something <i>you just think</i> I meant.<br /> <br /> And Twilight <i>still</i> isn't another realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:11:57-07:00","id":1062419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062413#post1062413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of mass narcissistic delusion are Mekhet operating under to insist other realms of existence aren't real when the pinnacle of their defining power permits them limited entry onto another realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it doesn't permit them limited entry into another realm. Twilight is a state, not a place. It allows them to project their consciousness in an invisible and intangible form (known in Chronicles of Darkness as &quot;Twilight&quot;) through the material world.<br /> <br /> And yes, many vampires probably know of the existence of other realms. Most probably know very little about those places, and those who think they know something about them are probably at least partially misinformed. Most vampire abilities that allow access to other realms are Bloodline-specific, Bloodlines are said to be very rare, and we also don't know how accurate the 1e Bloodline abilities are to their hypothetical 2e counterparts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:21:07-07:00","id":1062424,"title":"","content":"May have already been answered before, but I am not sure where - can Ephemeral Entities acquire Blood Bonds (up to Stage 3?), provided they had some means of ingesting Vitae?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:25:24-07:00","id":1062427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062424#post1062424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May have already been answered before, but I am not sure where - can Ephemeral Entities acquire Blood Bonds (up to Stage 3?), provided they had some means of ingesting Vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:25:58-07:00","id":1062430,"title":"","content":"Anything can be acquire the blood bond as per FAQ","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-14-2017, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:28:14-07:00","id":1062432,"title":"","content":"Probably, but there's a lack of rules for how to represent the bond considering that most ephemerals don't have an Integrity equivalent, and the one type I know of that does have Integrity (ghosts) can no longer suffer any breaking points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:40:36-07:00","id":1062435,"title":"","content":"Just sort of roleplay it I guess.<br /> <br /> Their alien mindsets might make it more trouble for the vampire than it's worth though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:43:58-07:00","id":1062438,"title":"","content":"I am positive the blood bond isnt just about integrity. It's about love and desire. The integrity/humanity/whatever is just a mechanical tool to help show and guide that obsession. It wouldn't be rocket science to have that ghost suddenly need to be around the vampire above all other things. <br /> Besides the breaking point to not hurt your regnant, it also gives the controller bonuses on rolls against the thrall and the thrall takes negatives on rolls against the regnant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:11:58-07:00","id":1062576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061921#post1061921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you are talking about resilience and how to resist the damage, you are correct in the fact you would use different math for different things.<br /> <br /> Bane sources it's just resilience dots, non-bane sources ( which is what I used in my math) is dots +1<br /> <br /> If that 14 Bashing came from 10 different sources you'd probably be in trouble as it says, &quot;No effect of resilience may be used more than once per turn,&quot; but again I assumed that it came from one source.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a couple pages back but I just wanted to chime in that it is incorrect. The active effect is to subtract dots +1 from all non-bane <b>sources</b> of damage. So if you had Resilience 1 and took 7 hits for 2 damage each, active resilience reduce the damage to zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T18:16:26-07:00","id":1062579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062576#post1062576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was a couple pages back but I just wanted to chime in that it is incorrect. The active effect is to subtract dots +1 from all non-bane <b>sources</b> of damage. So if you had Resilience 1 and took 7 hits for 2 damage each, active resilience reduce the damage to zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't even snag the whole quote where I said : <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1061921#post1061921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> (EDIT) Disclaimer:<br /> I vaguely remember a thread on here saying that the effect lasted 1 whole turn, so even if you got hit 10 times that turn you would subtract your resilience dots from each hit for that turn... but I can't seem to find that thread to verify.</div> </div> </div> </div>So where exactly did I go wrong?<br /> <br /> The book says you can't use the effect ( which is reducing damage ) more than once per turn but it also says from sources. It's contradictory, which I included both in my original post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-14-2017, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T19:49:29-07:00","id":1062615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062579#post1062579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You didn't even snag the whole quote where I said : <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So where exactly did I go wrong?<br /> <br /> The book says you can't use the effect ( which is reducing damage ) more than once per turn but it also says from sources. It's contradictory, which I included both in my original post.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't use the same effect more than once in the same turn. Reducing all sources of damage during the turn is one effect. In other words, you can't spend a second Vitae to double the amount of damage you reduce from each source that turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T20:01:25-07:00","id":1062622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062137#post1062137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that like vampires can just... do that. This is stuff well outside their standard area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone can open an Avernian Gate if they know the key. The Shadow is harder to reach but verges exist and werewolves can be blood bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T06:49:25-07:00","id":1062758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062615#post1062615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't use the same effect more than once in the same turn. Reducing all sources of damage during the turn is one effect. In other words, you can't spend a second Vitae to double the amount of damage you reduce from each source that turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the verification. The example, of 10 hits and subtracting from each hit was correct. If I could have found the thread that confirmed my suspicions I would have stuck to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T17:32:57-07:00","id":1063041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062579#post1062579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So where exactly did I go wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>You &quot;went wrong&quot; by not reading the whole text of the discipline and stating 2 opposite interpretations then wavering between them. I was simply clarifying how exactly it worked as stated in the book, in hopes of clearing up any confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T20:18:33-07:00","id":1063098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1063041#post1063041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You &quot;went wrong&quot; by not reading the whole text of the discipline and stating 2 opposite interpretations then wavering between them. I was simply clarifying how exactly it worked as stated in the book, in hopes of clearing up any confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Charlaquinn cleared any confusion magnificently Well without the condecending tone several hours prior to your unnecessary post. <br /> <br /> I most definitely read the whole text, but as I said I interpreted it two different ways. I am not sure if you have noticed, but there are tons and tons of examples where rules and text can be interpreted differently leading to various uses of powers and this very thread. Including toneless text. So if you wanted to correct the post and be helpful to everyone reading, perhaps you could take some advice on tact from some of the other posters on here. You could have just said something like, &quot;your second example was correct, not the first&quot; instead of attacking me twice. <br /> <br /> I am not perfect, no one on these forums is, but you don't need to talk down to anyone as it's not helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-15-2017, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T14:13:52-07:00","id":1063499,"title":"","content":"I fail to see how quoting then directly replying to your question is &quot;talking down&quot; or &quot;attacking&quot; but I apologize for hurting your feelings by doing so. As stater earlier, I was attempting to clear up your apparent confusion and prevent others who may read your post from becoming confused themselves. I had not considered that the full text of the Discipline as written could be misconstrued to hold other meanings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T17:14:25-07:00","id":1063667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1062438#post1062438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am positive the blood bond isnt just about integrity. It's about love and desire. The integrity/humanity/whatever is just a mechanical tool to help show and guide that obsession. It wouldn't be rocket science to have that ghost suddenly need to be around the vampire above all other things.<br /> Besides the breaking point to not hurt your regnant, it also gives the controller bonuses on rolls against the thrall and the thrall takes negatives on rolls against the regnant.</div> </div> </div> </div>A spirit doing things like the proverbial cat dropping dead squirrels on your porch for it to get your attention probably isn't anyone's dream pet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T17:26:18-07:00","id":1063671,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the spirit wants to please you! Unfortunately, by human standards, spirits are <i>fucking insane.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T17:46:43-07:00","id":1063679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1063667#post1063667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A spirit doing things like the proverbial cat dropping dead squirrels on your porch for it to get your attention probably isn't anyone's dream pet.</div> </div> </div> </div>AHA! some vampires might like that sort of thing! ~.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:06:25-07:00","id":1063801,"title":"","content":"I recall a while back a discussion about Banes - fixing some existing ones, homebrews, and so on - but my Google-Fu is failing me. Can anyone point me in the right direction?<br /> <br /> For context, one of my players decided to get the Bells Bane, which I think it should be reworked, as it only triggers if the ST (aka, me) feels like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T14:42:56-07:00","id":1064041,"title":"","content":"Rules as written, how does removing a limb work for a vampire? Seems to be some confusion here that aggravated damage is too rare a source to represent all the ways you can lose limbs (ie a slash/lethal weapon cutting it off)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T01:45:24-07:00","id":1064221,"title":"","content":"Removing a limb creates either an Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack tilt and deals the same amount of damage that whatever you're using would normally deal to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T10:19:42-07:00","id":1064358,"title":"","content":"So I can do &gt; Stamina lethal (and/or aggravated) to a limb and it's &quot;permanently disabled/removed&quot; (until they spent vitae for a new arm I guess) If I do bashing it's just the tilt. Okay ^^&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:00:14-07:00","id":1064408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1064358#post1064358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I can do &gt; Stamina lethal (and/or aggravated) to a limb and it's &quot;permanently disabled/removed&quot; (until they spent vitae for a new arm I guess) If I do bashing it's just the tilt. Okay ^^&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. It's a losing proposition to do this without say, a bane involved and considerably harder with a vampire with some degree of Resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:09:25-07:00","id":1064413,"title":"","content":"Resilience doesn't actually stop any damage. It just reduces how much damage you note, if that makes sense. It's completely possible to lose a limb and take no damage due to using Resilience.<br /> <br /> Edit: Basically, check for wracks before Resilience is applied.<br /> And yes, it becomes quite freaky when even a low BP vampire can regenerate entire limbs in a single turn as they heal the reduced damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-18-2017, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T12:46:39-07:00","id":1064429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1064041#post1064041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules as written, how does removing a limb work for a vampire? Seems to be some confusion here that aggravated damage is too rare a source to represent all the ways you can lose limbs (ie a slash/lethal weapon cutting it off)</div> </div> </div> </div>As per RAW, only aggravated damage causes permanent arm/leg wrack. If you want to be able to cause it with a sword or something that normally does lethal, I'd rule that it's possible if the damage is aggravated due to rollover.<br /> <br /> For a vampire, most sources that normally deal aggravated damage only deal lethal to them, so I house rule that it can be made &quot;permanent&quot; with lethal damage, as long as the damage <i>would have been</i> aggravated to a mortal human.<br /> <br /> As for regrowing lost limbs, Vitae will indeed do the trick. Though it may take a lot of Vitae to fully heal arm or leg wrack, so depending on the vampire's Blood Potency it may take a few turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T16:30:22-07:00","id":1066624,"title":"","content":"For Covenants, what are the limitations/restrictions? Reading through the lore is all well and good but what's stopping me, a Dragon with 2 Coils from picking up a Carthian Law? What are the actual rules around this, in terms of solid mechanics?<br /> <br /> edit: Found it: Capped at 5 dots of combined covenant status, covenants outside your own can't be equal or greater than your main one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 03-22-2017, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T16:39:35-07:00","id":1066630,"title":"","content":"The reason you can't buy stuff from Covenants is simply because they won't teach you unless you have Status in them. However, there are a multitude of reasons why someone might bend or break the rules in order to teach an outsider, so if you have a good reason for being able to buy Covenant exclusive stuff, go for it. For example my Ordo Gangrel (with 12 Coil dots, 2 Scales, and Sworn of the Dying Light, nonetheless, so quite the established dragon) has bought a Cr\u00faac dot and Rituals because he belongs to an inter-Covenant spanning secret society where there were people from Circle of the Crone willing to teach him.<br /> In the book Secrets of the Covenants there's also some Merits that may allow you to learn some of the secret stuff despite not being a full member. That's one way to go that has some actual rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T16:41:49-07:00","id":1066632,"title":"","content":"While it may not stop you from picking it up, the various Covenants are rather protective of their stuff. Demonstrating the knowledge may get you hunted down and killed, depending on the circumstances and the political situation of the Domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T17:21:11-07:00","id":1066644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1066624#post1066624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Covenants, what are the limitations/restrictions? Reading through the lore is all well and good but what's stopping me, a Dragon with 2 Coils from picking up a Carthian Law? What are the actual rules around this, in terms of solid mechanics?<br /> <br /> edit: Found it: Capped at 5 dots of combined covenant status, covenants outside your own can't be equal or greater than your main one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only restrictions are that several of the Carthian Law merits actually require you to have more than 1 status in the Carthian Movement to buy. You can even circumvent the 5 total covenant status rule with a Carthian Law merit. You technically shouldn't be a 5 status Carthian, 2 status Ordo, 1 status Crone, 1 status Invictus, 1 status Lancea Sanctum member but you can do that with that merit and have access to everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T21:15:41-07:00","id":1066695,"title":"","content":"There is a common sense limitation that is seldom mentioned. Merits must be justified. A vampire that has spent their entire existence in a single city where, for example, the Circle and the Lance have been at war the entire time will not have status in the Circle and the Lance at the same time. There is no merit or trick to get around it. Sometimes a character just can't justify taking up a merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T02:10:37-07:00","id":1066745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1066695#post1066695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a common sense limitation that is seldom mentioned. Merits must be justified. A vampire that has spent their entire existence in a single city where, for example, the Circle and the Lance have been at war the entire time will not have status in the Circle and the Lance at the same time. There is no merit or trick to get around it. Sometimes a character just can't justify taking up a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless he's a double agent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T03:53:41-07:00","id":1066766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1066695#post1066695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a common sense limitation that is seldom mentioned. Merits must be justified. A vampire that has spent their entire existence in a single city where, for example, the Circle and the Lance have been at war the entire time will not have status in the Circle and the Lance at the same time. There is no merit or trick to get around it. Sometimes a character just can't justify taking up a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to getting a covenant's signature abilities, common sense was poisoned, shot, stabbed, bludgeoned, wrapped up in a rug, and dumped in the river to drown. There are more ways to get proprietary knowledge without actually acquiring status in the relevant covenant that it's not even funny. Buying covenant status is simply the cheapest way to do it, not the quickest. ANYTHING can be justified, and ultimately it comes down to whether or not the ST permits it and there's a stigma attached to STs who say no, especially when its glaringly obvious that getting a covenant's signature abilities is an all you can eat buffet style, not dinner reservations at a 4-star restaurant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:53:22-07:00","id":1066802,"title":"","content":"If you want something use Dominate to get it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:34:01-07:00","id":1067515,"title":"","content":"You cannot fall into Torpor by loosing all your Willpower right? Also there isnt any negative effect mechanically when you are depleted from WP as Kindred","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T06:00:39-07:00","id":1067527,"title":"","content":"What is the purpose of Synthesis Embodiment of Strix? What *is* the mental make up of the...thing that emerges? What are their memories? What...is???????","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:06:45-07:00","id":1067555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Montgomery Crobes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1067515#post1067515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot fall into Torpor by loosing all your Willpower right? Also there isnt any negative effect mechanically when you are depleted from WP as Kindred</div> </div> </div> </div>The negative effect of having no willpower is not being able to spend willpower.<br /> <br /> That's a lot more serious than it sounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:02:35-07:00","id":1067592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1067527#post1067527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the purpose of Synthesis Embodiment of Strix? What *is* the mental make up of the...thing that emerges? What are their memories? What...is???????</div> </div> </div> </div>An option to shake things up in case a character is expecting 'just' possession from the enemy. It also allows for some pretty weird combinations when you get strix-werewolves and stuff.<br /> <br /> It seems to resemble Claiming a bit, so I'd say that a strix retains its own memories and can access those of its host. But the strix is fully in charge, though it may gain new interests in case of its new body, like weird ticks or habits. That's just a storyteller thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:05:50-07:00","id":1068248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1067527#post1067527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the purpose of Synthesis Embodiment of Strix? What *is* the mental make up of the...thing that emerges? What are their memories? What...is???????</div> </div> </div> </div> There's several purposes.<br /> 1) Give credence to the idea that the strix are the true origin of vampires.<br /> 2) They had the ability in Requiem for Rome, and it would be very odd if it didn't carry over.<br /> 3) Strix are alien entities not entire concerned with self preservation as much as having fun and dragging vampires down to their level.<br /> 4) Crazy strange things for story hooks. <br /> <br /> The mental makeup of the thing that emerges is no different than any other sort of fresh embrace, or a particularly low Humanity vampire. You don't suddenly absorb memories or new personality shifts beyond just having a Beast that's closer to the forefront than usual. Which is admittedly a big mental shift, but not one that can't be reproduced through rapid-fire Humanity loss in a short time.<br /> <br /> Synthesis effectively kills the strix. Now, you could do a whole Tainted routine and absorb some memories there, but that's not what happens by default. You get a power up shroom, and loss of Humanity. That's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:09:16-07:00","id":1068249,"title":"","content":"So, probably not a simple question, but... I'm working on disease powers for vampires, kind of in the vein of the Morbus, but not necessarily a bloodline, and certainly not in discipline form. How would you go about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T06:32:49-07:00","id":1068273,"title":"","content":"It depends on what kind of disease I'd want them spreading. Mechanically I'd probably set it up as a merit chain requiring Medicine 3 with a relevant Biology or Chemistry specialty. One version they could place vitae on an object that passes a disease onto the next person to come in contact with it. Contagious and noncontagious versions.<br /> Another power could be they touch someone and a virus or bacteria in their body flares up with deleterious symptoms that are highly contagious.<br /> Disease/illness switch. The vampire pulls an active disease from one person and can transfer it into someone else who has an active disease which transfers to the first party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T11:18:26-07:00","id":1068351,"title":"","content":"Is their a reason for a menber of the circle of the crone who knows blood price , not to seek out &quot;surgical heart removal, if he plays it safe and hides his heart well hes got a second chance coming up","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T12:22:26-07:00","id":1068371,"title":"","content":"Quicken Sight says it lets you benefit from aiming instantly - as in the whole pool? (ie for Marksman Firearms + Composure) If it were 1-1 for aiming it'd be half as efficient as just using Physical Intensity. Auspex already has a crap load of ridiculously good devotions so I figured it might be worth it to get this cleared up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T13:48:43-07:00","id":1068404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1068351#post1068351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is their a reason for a menber of the circle of the crone who knows blood price , not to seek out &quot;surgical heart removal, if he plays it safe and hides his heart well hes got a second chance coming up</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than owing a huge boon to the Ordo member who performed the surgery OR having to cut off the loose end that is the same person and having to trust him/her literally with your life in order to perform the surgery in the first place, not really. Well, they would also have to know of that Scale's existence in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1068371#post1068371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quicken Sight says it lets you benefit from aiming instantly - as in the whole pool? (ie for Marksman Firearms + Composure) If it were 1-1 for aiming it'd be half as efficient as just using Physical Intensity. Auspex already has a crap load of ridiculously good devotions so I figured it might be worth it to get this cleared up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever max bonus you can derive from aiming over x number of turns (I think standard is +2 or 3) can be immediately applied to the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 03-26-2017, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:36:15-07:00","id":1068468,"title":"","content":"Ah, so if I can somehow get my hands on just a single dot of Auspex, I can spend a vitae for +7 to my roll, and with other devotions add celerity to my dex for another +3 (eventually +5) and etc. Damn that's strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T17:04:43-07:00","id":1068479,"title":"","content":"Yup, spend a bunch of XP and Vitae, and you too can get all kinds of powers. There's even a Merit that lets you use your Composure as the base number instead of +3.<br /> You can only get max of +3 with aiming naturally, meaning without other XP expenditures to increase it. This is compared to Physical Intensity which would give an inherent +2 without any additional XP expenditure and at BP 1, you have to choose one or the other. It's just not as amazing as you seem to think unless you do spend a bunch of XP on top of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 03-26-2017, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T17:05:05-07:00","id":1068481,"title":"","content":"Does Quicken Sight do that? I figured it'd just be the plus one, with the real benefit being able to apply full defense against firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T17:21:04-07:00","id":1068486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1068248#post1068248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's several purposes.<br /> 1) Give credence to the idea that the strix are the true origin of vampires.<br /> 2) They had the ability in Requiem for Rome, and it would be very odd if it didn't carry over.<br /> 3) Strix are alien entities not entire concerned with self preservation as much as having fun and dragging vampires down to their level.<br /> 4) Crazy strange things for story hooks.<br /> <br /> The mental makeup of the thing that emerges is no different than any other sort of fresh embrace, or a particularly low Humanity vampire. You don't suddenly absorb memories or new personality shifts beyond just having a Beast that's closer to the forefront than usual. Which is admittedly a big mental shift, but not one that can't be reproduced through rapid-fire Humanity loss in a short time.<br /> <br /> Synthesis effectively kills the strix. Now, you could do a whole Tainted routine and absorb some memories there, but that's not what happens by default. You get a power up shroom, and loss of Humanity. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here is a true reason I ask...<br /> ...does it have to kill the Strix? It only kills them if they roll more successes than their Shadow Potency, and otherwise they are catapulted from the body. But...being catapulted doesn't mention that Synthesis *fails* - my last reading of it left me with impression that a Synthesis roll with a less-than-Potency successes follow up roll would end up with Parent-Strix leaving the body, and the body being embraced with Blood Potency 1. It seems that corpse loses a lot of potential humanity in the process, while a living human doesn't actually end up losing any.<br /> I always wanted to play a Strix-Embraced Ventrue whose only strong point would be amazing Domination Dice pool - conflicted with character's strong moral compass and desire to maintain high Humanity. &quot;I'm terribly weak and don't want to die or fall prey to all these (STRONGLY SUSPICIOUS ABOUT MY SUSPICIOUS ORIGIN) vampires, but my only triumph card is something that spits in face of all my beliefs&quot;. <br /> Sounds like something that Strix would expect having fun corrupting, too, so I can see it setting up something like that. But I'm unsure about the mechanics involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T18:24:44-07:00","id":1068502,"title":"","content":"Quicken Sight lets you take the aim action and the attack action in the same round, it doesn't let you take whatever number of aim actions you feel like taking in a single turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T18:45:03-07:00","id":1068504,"title":"","content":"&quot;[..] benefit from aiming instantly.&quot;<br /> I realize that the language is supposed to be natural and that this is almost guaranteed not the intended interpretation, but I could see some STs running it as activating Quicken Sight and then using your instant action to gain the full aiming bonus in a single turn. In fact, I almost prefer that since you can rack up quite the dice bonus if you have the Marksmanship Merit (and still +3 if you don't), but you can't fire until your next turn and actually loses that bonus if you apply defence before you shoot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T18:48:55-07:00","id":1068505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1068504#post1068504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;[..] benefit from aiming instantly.&quot;<br /> I realize that the language is supposed to be natural and that this is almost guaranteed not the intended interpretation, but I could see some STs running it as activating Quicken Sight and then using your instant action to gain the full aiming bonus in a single turn. In fact, I almost prefer that since you can rack up quite the dice bonus if you have the Marksmanship Merit (and still +3 if you don't), but you can't fire until your next turn and actually loses that bonus if you apply defence before you shoot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer this implementation, tbh. Aiming certainly stacks when it's done turn-to-turn but doing it all at once (instant instead of reflexive) and as a sort of intense observation makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T00:36:59-07:00","id":1068574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1066745#post1066745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless he's a double agent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that isn't justification for the Status <b><i>at the same time</i></b>. Having status at a minimum means the group knows the character and the enemies of the group are aware of the character. Mook from A need not know every mook from B but somebody from A knows all of B's mooks if A and B are opponents. Status from the original organization must be shed before status from the new organization can be justified. Double agent is justification for losing the new status and reverting back to the old status.<br /> <br /> It is easy to sequentially gather each covenants goodies. There are a series of merits that allow affiliates of covenants some access also. These merits were necessary because it isn't easy to justify having status in multiple covenants unless the covenants are on good terms, sometimes very good terms are required. Now some people don't care and think having XP is all the justification needed. That is not the game as it was designed so any issues are on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T03:36:51-07:00","id":1068597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1068574#post1068574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, that isn't justification for the Status <b><i>at the same time</i></b>. Having status at a minimum means the group knows the character and the enemies of the group are aware of the character. Mook from A need not know every mook from B but somebody from A knows all of B's mooks if A and B are opponents. Status from the original organization must be shed before status from the new organization can be justified. Double agent is justification for losing the new status and reverting back to the old status.<br /> <br /> It is easy to sequentially gather each covenants goodies. There are a series of merits that allow affiliates of covenants some access also. These merits were necessary because it isn't easy to justify having status in multiple covenants unless the covenants are on good terms, sometimes very good terms are required. Now some people don't care and think having XP is all the justification needed. That is not the game as it was designed so any issues are on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how spies and double agents work at YOUR table. In the real world that's not how it functions, in the real world we call them ambassadors, assets, contacts, political dissidents, and use numerous other politically correct terminology to call them anything other than traitors, which is what they are. Said double agent belongs to opposing sides simultaneously. They may even operate using aliases or fake identities. There's merits for those too.<br /> <br /> It's stupidly easy to gather a covenant's knowledge. Legitimately, you only need a single dot of status to get it. You don't even need that much if you want Invictus Oaths. Realistically, you only need to establish a partial vinculum and ask. Or you can use Majesty, Dominate, Nightmare, or Auspex to pry the information from the unwilling. Or you join covenant 1 via status, get their steal proprietary knowledge ability to take from 2, while simultaneously joining covenant 3 and taking the pseudo status merit for covenant 4 to facilitate joining once you milked covenant 1 for their stuff.<br /> <br /> The game was always designed for it to be easy. Just not while holding concurrent membership. Now you can do it concurrently it doesn't cost you anything when you burn bridges, and you get xp for doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-27-2017, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T10:31:23-07:00","id":1068739,"title":"","content":"Are there printer friendly VtR 2E sheets? I just put new ink in my printer, seems like if I print more than 4 4-page character sheets my printer is just crying for more, it's pretty brutal. The large swathes of dark red/black end up soaking the page a bit, lol - I don't really want to print that double-sided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T10:43:32-07:00","id":1068744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1068739#post1068739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there printer friendly VtR 2E sheets? I just put new ink in my printer, seems like if I print more than 4 4-page character sheets my printer is just crying for more, it's pretty brutal. The large swathes of dark red/black end up soaking the page a bit, lol - I don't really want to print that double-sided.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/Vampire_TheMasquiem_4-Page_Editable.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">This one</a> from Mr. Gone is based on the layout from Masquerade's character sheets, which are monochrome and don't have the decorative, ink-consuming borders. It was made for First Edition, so you'll have to repurpose some of the fields so you can record things like Banes, Touchstones, Aspirations, and Conditions. But it's pretty serviceable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T10:58:10-07:00","id":1068749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1068744#post1068744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/VtR/Vampire_TheMasquiem_4-Page_Editable.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">This one</a> from Mr. Gone is based on the layout from Masquerade's character sheets, which are monochrome and don't have the decorative, ink-consuming borders. It was made for First Edition, so you'll have to repurpose some of the fields so you can record things like Banes, Touchstones, Aspirations, and Conditions. But it's pretty serviceable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! In the meantime, I may see about making a new sheet. I liked VtR's style with the flourishing red text and the like, if I can find a way to modify the sheet without it looking gaudy I'll let you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:23:22-07:00","id":1068828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1068597#post1068597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's how spies and double agents work at YOUR table. In the real world that's not how it functions, in the real world we call them ambassadors, assets, contacts, political dissidents, and use numerous other politically correct terminology to call them anything other than traitors, which is what they are. Said double agent belongs to opposing sides simultaneously. They may even operate using aliases or fake identities. There's merits for those too.<br /> <br /> It's stupidly easy to gather a covenant's knowledge. Legitimately, you only need a single dot of status to get it. You don't even need that much if you want Invictus Oaths. Realistically, you only need to establish a partial vinculum and ask. Or you can use Majesty, Dominate, Nightmare, or Auspex to pry the information from the unwilling. Or you join covenant 1 via status, get their steal proprietary knowledge ability to take from 2, while simultaneously joining covenant 3 and taking the pseudo status merit for covenant 4 to facilitate joining once you milked covenant 1 for their stuff.<br /> <br /> The game was always designed for it to be easy. Just not while holding concurrent membership. Now you can do it concurrently it doesn't cost you anything when you burn bridges, and you get xp for doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I said how the rules work. You don't have to follow the rules if you don't want to but you can't claim to have Status if you can't use it according to the rules. You didn't provide any real world examples of people that would have Status in opposing organizations at the same time. The real world example of someone having Status in opposing organizations is a soldier in the middle of a war going to the enemy and saying &quot;you guys seem cool so I want to join your side&quot; and the army saying &quot;awesome, want to see all our neat intel?&quot; This is not the Demon forum. Vampires don't have Covers.<br /> <br /> The game was always designed for merits to be difficult to justify. It is possible to justify someone getting any merit, but difficult, if not impossible, to justify everyone getting a merit. An example is touchstones. When a vampire loses a touchstone they can have XP enough to buy a small country but without roleplaying a relationship the rules do not allow for replacing or buying a new touchstone. Rules are optional so you can say it is unnecessary. You can exclude touchstones entirely. You can play however you want, but you don't get to reinterpret the given system of rules and say you're way is right.<br /> <br /> I don't fault you for not understanding the rules. I don't care at all how you want to play the game as that is up to you entirely to carry it out. I fault you when you put down the rules while describing them in a flawed way. When it comes to covenant goodies being spread the flaw that exists within the rules is the handwaving that covenants somehow can magically prevent someone from doing as they please. A covenant can kill someone for violating the rules, but it really seems like an honor system backed up with &quot;magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> I didn't reply to you intentionally the first time because I saw no point. I still see no point, but I feel it would be rude to constantly ignore you. We don't agree. Are you so unreasonable that you can't grasp that won't change? I use reason and logic while you provide none. There can be no reconciliation in that dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:12:09-07:00","id":1068891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1068828#post1068828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I said how the rules work. You don't have to follow the rules if you don't want to but you can't claim to have Status if you can't use it according to the rules. <b>You didn't provide any real world examples of people that would have Status in opposing organizations at the same time. </b>The real world example of someone having Status in opposing organizations is a soldier in the middle of a war going to the enemy and saying &quot;you guys seem cool so I want to join your side&quot; and the army saying &quot;awesome, want to see all our neat intel?&quot; This is not the Demon forum. Vampires don't have Covers.<br /> <br /> <b>The game was always designed for merits to be difficult to justify.</b> It is possible to justify someone getting any merit, but difficult, if not impossible, to justify everyone getting a merit. An example is touchstones. When a vampire loses a touchstone they can have XP enough to buy a small country but without roleplaying a relationship the rules do not allow for replacing or buying a new touchstone. Rules are optional so you can say it is unnecessary. You can exclude touchstones entirely. You can play however you want, but you don't get to reinterpret the given system of rules and say you're way is right.<br /> <br /> I don't fault you for not understanding the rules. I don't care at all how you want to play the game as that is up to you entirely to carry it out. I fault you when you put down the rules while describing them in a flawed way. When it comes to covenant goodies being spread the flaw that exists within the rules is the handwaving that covenants somehow can magically prevent someone from doing as they please. A covenant can kill someone for violating the rules, but it really seems like an honor system backed up with &quot;magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>I didn't reply to you intentionally the first time because I saw no point. I still see no point, but I feel it would be rude to constantly ignore you. We don't agree. Are you so unreasonable that you can't grasp that won't change? I use reason and logic while you provide none. There can be no reconciliation in that dynamic.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine:<br /> <br /> 1) This is the bread and butter of undercover cops. Someone who can literally rape minds likely has an easy time forging a new identity.<br /> <br /> 2) Your table, your rules. Mileage on verisimilitude required by STs may vary, there's not a single sentence in any book saying &quot;merits should be [expletive] difficult to justify&quot;, that's your own assumption. I'm going to ignore the false equivalency argument on touchstones.<br /> <br /> 3) No need to get antagonistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T19:11:59-07:00","id":1069777,"title":"","content":"If you have a means of doing lethal to the target, is it fair to upgrade the damage any fighting style does to lethal (ie kick 'em while they're down from street fighting, or Defensive Jab or Combination from Boxing) ie using claws or maybe spiked boots (or like one character, .. punching them while they're down with a gauntlet which would normally render them prone as well to do the attack.. lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T00:26:26-07:00","id":1069919,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">MESMERIZED</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your character\u2019s will is subordinate to that of a vampire. You\u2019re not obviously hypnotized \u2014 you\u2019re a bit quiet and reserved compared to normal, but nothing out of the ordinary. When the vampire who inflicted this Condition gives you a command, you cannot resist. If it\u2019s something that you wouldn\u2019t normally do, you might look like you\u2019ve been hypnotized or that you\u2019re sleepwalking, but otherwise you look and act normally.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#691D00\"><span style=\"font-family:P22Hopper-Edward\">Mesmerize \u2022</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">All a vampire has to do is meet her victim\u2019s eye to catch him in her thrall. Her control isn\u2019t obvious; she just asks him to do something and her victim acquiesces. He could unlock a door, pass her a gun \u2014 or forget ever meeting her. Some cruel vampires mesmerize passers-by just to take the rap for their crimes.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Dramatic Failure: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The victim sees through the vampire\u2019s attempt to control his mind; emboldened, he gains the Steadfast Condition </span></span><span style=\"color:#691D00\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(p. 306)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Failure: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The vampire\u2019s victim proves stronger-willed than she\u2019d thought.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Success: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The vampire holds her victim\u2019s gaze for just a second, but it\u2019s enough to inflict the Mesmerized Condition </span></span><span style=\"color:#691D00\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(p. 305)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">.</span></span> <br /> <br /> The question is very simple . If the Vampire fails at the mesmerized roll does he/she now that she has failed?<br /> <br /> There is no mention in the rules that the dominator understands that he has succeeded until after he says something and he is obeyed. So there is a chance that he says the order and the victim understands his intention . Without proof offcourse.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We are trying to find ways to be true to the intentions of the game rules but give slim chances to the receivers of the Disciplines. So far in Dominate we have the following<br /> <br /> Dont be alone with someone with dominate outside the Elysium<br /> Have a recording device on you at all times.<br /> Have a ghoul/retainer check you up for any abnormal behavior.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T02:02:50-07:00","id":1069933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The question is very simple . If the Vampire fails at the mesmerized roll does he/she now that she has failed?There is no mention in the rules that the dominator understands that he has succeeded until after he says something and he is obeye </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, you know when you fail with a discipline roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From p125 in the core rules, 2ed.<br /> <br /> Each Discipline calls on the Beast, whether using its talents<br /> overtly or expressing it through the blood inside. While the<br /> mechanical effect of a player failing her Discipline roll is that<br /> nothing happens, that\u2019s not strictly true. Something happens.<br /> The Beast won\u2019t just accept the idea that tapping its power<br /> produces no results. Maybe the lights flicker, or the vampire\u2019s<br /> flesh writhes on her bones for just a second. Maybe her victim<br /> sees a second, screaming face trying to escape the vampire\u2019s head<br /> for just a second. Whatever it is, it\u2019s not enough to properly<br /> freak her victim out \u2014 that\u2019s the domain of the Nosferatu,<br /> through their Nightmare Discipline. It\u2019s just something that<br /> reminds the vampire that she\u2019s not human, she\u2019s tapping<br /> something within herself that she doesn\u2019t fully understand and<br /> cannot truly control. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 03-29-2017, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T02:50:04-07:00","id":1069945,"title":"","content":"Then whenever you do a VS roll to initiate a discipline the beast of the defender understands that something happened? In mesmerize its the purview of Dramatic Failure which is very difficult to happen an in the rules there is nothing that gives -dice modifiers to Discipline rolls except when there is resistance rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:49:49-07:00","id":1069956,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily the defender, but the offender should definitely know and be familiar with the feeling of their own disciplines failing. If its actually something that shows the defender might suspect something is wrong. Perhaps with a success on a reflexive wits+ occult roll to notice that a discipline failed, or just leave it to dramatic failures which might be closer to its intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T04:16:54-07:00","id":1069963,"title":"","content":"Even in the case of a failure, something happens in the world. The Beast does not let an exercise of magical power do -nothing-. Flicker of lights, chills, something happens that can be a clue if you know what you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T09:07:30-07:00","id":1070683,"title":"","content":"So I've been curious about the &quot;Extra Sense&quot; of Protean. 360 degree vision with whatever animal sense you can justify. Unlike every other aspect written, this one doesn't have any discrete mechanics written for it. It's been suggested that you can't be surprised, or that you can see invisible entities if they're touching the ground.<br /> It's weird but also cool, problem is without any irrefutable mechanics written it falls on the storyteller's interpretation (which may vary a lot from ST to ST) what mechanical benefits this provides.<br /> <br /> So what would be reasonable advantages to expect when using this aspect? If we amp it to Protean 4 and essentially &quot;use all the senses&quot; what then?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T09:26:17-07:00","id":1070693,"title":"","content":"My opinion: The most important mechanic in Chronicles of Darkness (and any traditional RPG for that matter) is that every action must be processed through a human brain, which determines if the action is possible, and if it has reasonable enough chances of both success and failure and sufficient consequences for failure as to require a random number generator (read: dice) to determine the outcome, and what system is most appropriate for utilizing the random number generator. Therefore, in my opinion, &quot;you have 360 degree vision&quot; <i>is</i> a mechanical advantage all by itself, just like &quot;you have a prehensile tail&quot; or &quot;you can see in the dark.&quot; It affects the decision making process of the brain that is running the system, and will affect what outcomes that brain will determine are possible or impossible and how best to resolve uncertain outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T11:41:35-07:00","id":1070771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1070693#post1070693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My opinion: The most important mechanic in Chronicles of Darkness (and any traditional RPG for that matter) is that every action must be processed through a human brain, which determines if the action is possible, and if it has reasonable enough chances of both success and failure and sufficient consequences for failure as to require a random number generator (read: dice) to determine the outcome, and what system is most appropriate for utilizing the random number generator. Therefore, in my opinion, &quot;you have 360 degree vision&quot; <i>is</i> a mechanical advantage all by itself, just like &quot;you have a prehensile tail&quot; or &quot;you can see in the dark.&quot; It affects the decision making process of the brain that is running the system, and will affect what outcomes that brain will determine are possible or impossible and how best to resolve uncertain outcomes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well written response, thanks man. I kind of liken it to Toph's senses in A:tLA or blind people learning to use echolocation (or bats too lol) so it's interesting. I suppose upping it to Protean 4 wouldn't do much aside from combining all the different senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T12:20:12-07:00","id":1070789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1070771#post1070771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well written response, thanks man. I kind of liken it to Toph's senses in A:tLA or blind people learning to use echolocation (or bats too lol) so it's interesting. I suppose upping it to Protean 4 wouldn't do much aside from combining all the different senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Toph is a good example of it working, yes, or Daredevil for a hearing-based version. I definitely think it would make surprising the character very difficult, as you would have to find a way to circumvent their senses - if you can levitate, you can sneak up on Toph. If you overload Daredevil's senses with loud, disorienting noises, he might not be able to pinpoint your footsteps. I would also think both would be able to detect invisible people, since they're relying on Senses other than sight to detect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:40:17-07:00","id":1071493,"title":"","content":"Invisible yes but it wouldn't help Vs Obfuscate which clouds the brain directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:45:58-07:00","id":1071500,"title":"","content":"One of the Obfuscate powers specifically leaves clues like that. The mind effect cloaks the vampire, not the area around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T19:02:31-07:00","id":1071543,"title":"","content":"Well if the area around them doesn't count, then the reflected light that you would see from them is actually touching your own eye <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but Obf does specifically say &quot;he vanishes entirely&quot;<br /> To be fair though, I do think that Obf 3 could be worded better. It says &quot;He makes no sound&quot; but does cause creaking floorboards. So does obf just make it so his own joints don't pop but all other sounds happen as normal?<br /> <br /> Thinking further about this, the special sense<i> is</i> coming from a Discipline and being circumvented by another Discipline so perhaps a Clash of Wills is in order when someone is Obf in sensory range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T19:16:00-07:00","id":1071547,"title":"","content":"I'd say no to a Clash of Wills. The senses are created through a Discipline, but their function is completely mundane. It's not like Auspex or Mage Sight from MtA where you gain information from an explicitly supernatural sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T19:18:17-07:00","id":1071548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1071543#post1071543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if the area around them doesn't count, then the reflected light that you would see from them is actually touching your own eye</div> </div> </div> </div>Except as you noted, it doesn't affect the eyes, it affects the mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but Obf does specifically say &quot;he vanishes entirely&quot; </div> </div> </div>Yes, he vanishes entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be fair though, I do think that Obf 3 could be worded better. It says &quot;He makes no sound&quot; but does cause creaking floorboards. So does obf just make it so his own joints don't pop but all other sounds happen as normal? </div> </div> </div>You could probably make a devotion that acts like the old Silence spell, drowning sound in an entire area, but Obfuscate 3, as written, would silence the sounds of your bones popping, the katana scabbard rattling against your legs, your trenchcoat flapping around you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thinking further about this, the special sense<i> is</i> coming from a Discipline and being circumvented by another Discipline so perhaps a Clash of Wills is in order when someone is Obf in sensory range? </div> </div> </div>It's not quite being circumvented, and Protean is clearly in the loss scenario. It doesn't matter if you have 360 vision if Obfuscate is still erasing the vampire from your 360 vision. If you're just paying attention to the fact that there's creaks in the floorboards approaching you as if someone was there, that seems like a fine usage, and probably the entire point of having that 'weakness' in Obfuscate 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T19:32:03-07:00","id":1071556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1071547#post1071547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say no to a Clash of Wills. The senses are created through a Discipline, but their function is completely mundane. It's not like Auspex or Mage Sight from MtA where you gain information from an explicitly supernatural sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a good idea for a Protean 4 Devotion!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1071548#post1071548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter if you have 360 vision...</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you're saying and it is probably the spirit of the power but a scabbard or trenchcoat is really no different from a floorboard, they're all objects being moved around by ones body.<br /> My point for Clash of Wills was not so much 360 but more about Tremorsense. The ground is still vibrating in much the same way as floorboards creak, as creaking is nothing but audible vibration.<br /> <br /> Protean **** - Predatory Awareness.<br /> Your senses become supernaturally honed.<br /> Effect: You do not suffer from adverse lighting, acoustic, or other conditions that may otherwise hamper you from locating an animate being or object that you could otherwise potentially sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 03-31-2017, 10:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T19:42:03-07:00","id":1071560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1071556#post1071556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you're saying and it is probably the spirit of the power but a scabbard or trenchcoat is really no different from a floorboard, they're all objects being moved around by ones body.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a given that the ability, and Obfuscate 1, affect what you're wearing despite them not being 'the vampire that used the Discipline.' But it's also a given that they do not affect things like the floor, or clouds of smoke. You would need Obfuscate 2 for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point for Clash of Wills was not so much 360 but more about Tremorsense. The ground is still vibrating in much the same way as floorboards creak, as creaking is nothing but audible vibration. </div> </div> </div>I'm going to say that I hate that tremorsense was there in the first place, it's not a real thing, it's a Dungeons and Dragons sense and I found it awkward that it's there to begin with. That said, it senses tremors and 'someone stepped over there' isn't exactly breaking Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T20:13:15-07:00","id":1071571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1071560#post1071560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to say that I hate that tremorsense was there in the first place, it's not a real thing, it's a Dungeons and Dragons sense and I found it awkward that it's there to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiders sense their prey by vibrations in their webs, so it's not unheard of, even if the common term gamers often use for it comes from D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T03:29:01-07:00","id":1071670,"title":"","content":"Question: Oath of the True Knight offers me armor rating against Kindred and Ghouls. Does this offer my armor against other supernaturals if they decide to mess with me when I'm performing my duties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T07:40:55-07:00","id":1071710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1071571#post1071571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spiders sense their prey by vibrations in their webs, so it's not unheard of, even if the common term gamers often use for it comes from D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>Earthworms use it as well to escape dangers above ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T09:06:20-07:00","id":1071727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1071670#post1071670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Oath of the True Knight offers me armor rating against Kindred and Ghouls. Does this offer my armor against other supernaturals if they decide to mess with me when I'm performing my duties?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T09:45:08-07:00","id":1072578,"title":"","content":"Quick question. Coil of the Wyrm lets me get more health while in Frenzy. IF I were to fill those, and revert (assuming I could ignore Torpor from combat/while in frenzy) would that damage be upgraded to Aggravated on the normal track of lethal? Would it disappear alongside the health boxes? I know I need to heal to avoid Torpor, but I'd need to heal 5 (BP4, means 4 extra health in frenzy) to avoid Torpor once the Frenzy ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T15:08:29-07:00","id":1072718,"title":"","content":"They wrap around I'm afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:48:35-07:00","id":1073202,"title":"","content":"<b>Can you lick the 'feeding wounds' of a corpse to close them?</b><br /> <br /> Context - character has brief but unfettered access to a morgue and wants to take a blood sample from a murder victim. Has no medicine skill, so wants to drain the blood manually and spit into a sample cup. Gonna let that fly, but I'm thinking the bite wound may not respond to the lick like a living victim would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:45:12-07:00","id":1073244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1073202#post1073202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Can you lick the 'feeding wounds' of a corpse to close them?</b><br /> <br /> Context - character has brief but unfettered access to a morgue and wants to take a blood sample from a murder victim. Has no medicine skill, so wants to drain the blood manually and spit into a sample cup. Gonna let that fly, but I'm thinking the bite wound may not respond to the lick like a living victim would.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Gross.<br /> 2. I'd agree with your assessment about licking wounds closed on a corpse. You can't do it for the same reason a vampire can't bite objects and lick them to restore durability and functionality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T11:14:00-07:00","id":1073263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1073244#post1073244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd agree with your assessment about licking wounds closed on a corpse. You can't do it for the same reason a vampire can't bite objects and lick them to restore durability and functionality.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only hesitation is the flavor text: <b>When finished drinking, the vampire merely licks the wound, and it closes, much as he can force his own blood, or Vitae, to seal his wounds.</b><br /> <br /> And since Kindred flesh isn't living, I could ... <i>maybe </i>... see a stretch. But, yeah, I think I'll be saying (undead flesh != dead flesh) in this case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T08:13:28-07:00","id":1075132,"title":"","content":"With the 5th dot in Coil of the Wyrm, can I Ride the Wave mid-frenzy to direct it a many times as I please (rolls allowing, of course) I'm considering capping it off, it's a wee bit vague as to it's utility beyond the rest of the Coil (aside from avoiding Torpor and extending Frenzy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T22:13:49-07:00","id":1075375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1075132#post1075132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the 5th dot in Coil of the Wyrm, can I Ride the Wave mid-frenzy to direct it a many times as I please (rolls allowing, of course)</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T09:05:02-07:00","id":1075495,"title":"","content":"Tremorsense came up at the table and while it's already been ruled a certain way (using D&amp;D 3.5..) since I use Protean a lot what is a good way of defining tremorsense to a DM unfamiliar with Toph ^^&quot; I don't have any other good examples (or examples of rules that work well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T09:58:36-07:00","id":1075510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1075495#post1075495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremorsense came up at the table and while it's already been ruled a certain way (using D&amp;D 3.5..) since I use Protean a lot what is a good way of defining tremorsense to a DM unfamiliar with Toph ^^&quot; I don't have any other good examples (or examples of rules that work well).</div> </div> </div> </div>Toph is the example of an earth bender in the Avatar the Last Airbender series. She was born blind but developed the ability to earthbend by sensing the vibrations emanating from objects and movement. (Sound actually travels through the ground as well.) <br /> <br /> Some examples of animals using &quot;tremorsense&quot; include voles, snakes, spiders, sharks, badgers, and octopii. They sense vibrations from outside sources. Animals that use sonic vibration to &quot;see&quot; (sending out sonic vibrations to locate objects) are dolphins, assassin bugs (yes they exist), bats, whales, shrews, and oil birds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T10:59:45-07:00","id":1075527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1075495#post1075495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremorsense came up at the table and while it's already been ruled a certain way (using D&amp;D 3.5..) since I use Protean a lot what is a good way of defining tremorsense to a DM unfamiliar with Toph ^^&quot; I don't have any other good examples (or examples of rules that work well).</div> </div> </div> </div>Just compare it to echolocation. The idea is the same, the vibrations are just traveling through the ground instead of the air and you're sensing them through touch instead of hearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-09-2017, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T12:55:42-07:00","id":1075556,"title":"","content":"I know there are tonnes of natural examples, but the DM wants a concrete mechanical description :/ Otherwise it'll be severely limited to just whatever is on the same explicit ground. What's a concise way of ruling this, just use echolocation but it travels through ground/walls/objects? Many things cause vibrations so there are nearly always some in the environment (where as echolocation is using a specific sound and listening for how long it takes to return from various surfaces)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-09-2017, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T14:59:09-07:00","id":1075591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1075556#post1075556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there are tonnes of natural examples, but the DM wants a concrete mechanical description :/ Otherwise it'll be severely limited to just whatever is on the same explicit ground. What's a concise way of ruling this, just use echolocation but it travels through ground/walls/objects? Many things cause vibrations so there are nearly always some in the environment (where as echolocation is using a specific sound and listening for how long it takes to return from various surfaces)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure what more mechanical definition is needed? You perceive your surroundings in 360 degrees via vibration. If something is in indirect contact with you (for example, touching the ground, which is touching you) within the range of your perception (let's say earshot), you can perceive its movements by your sense of touch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:45:06-07:00","id":1075650,"title":"","content":"I suppose that works, while also seeing walls/ceiling/attached bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T11:00:14-07:00","id":1078425,"title":"","content":"Hi<br /> <br /> In a city, the important roles (example the seneschal, sheriff or the master of elysium) are always come from the same Covenant as the Prince? Is it rare or impossible to fill these roles with other covenant or covenants members?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13285-dexter","name":"Dexter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T11:35:45-07:00","id":1078438,"title":"","content":"They don't all have to be from the same covenant, but I'd say it's rare to have members from the &quot;opposite&quot; covenant. ie if Lancea are in control, you won't see any Crones holding office (at least publicly/commonly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T00:42:00-07:00","id":1078797,"title":"","content":"Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . I like the idea of a unkown covenant/unaligned Prince like some of the example characters in Damnation City but I wasn't sure how to handle the important figures in a city like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13285-dexter","name":"Dexter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T03:34:13-07:00","id":1078820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dexter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1078425#post1078425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi<br /> <br /> In a city, the important roles (example the seneschal, sheriff or the master of elysium) are always come from the same Covenant as the Prince? Is it rare or impossible to fill these roles with other covenant or covenants members?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have to, but in the interest of the Prince is to have the most important roles filled with the Kindred who he trusts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T03:40:08-07:00","id":1078822,"title":"","content":"There's also the possibility of the &quot;opposite&quot; Covenant retaining positions after a recent shift of power, or even that they're given one as a gesture of goodwill if the current Prince doesn't want to risk an escalation.<br /> Of course, such governments would most likely be somewhat unstable, but that can be a great source of conflict in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T04:24:00-07:00","id":1078830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dexter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1078425#post1078425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi<br /> <br /> In a city, the important roles (example the seneschal, sheriff or the master of elysium) are always come from the same Covenant as the Prince? Is it rare or impossible to fill these roles with other covenant or covenants members?</div> </div> </div> </div> Fun quirk of 2e. Every covenant (save the Ordo Dracul*) has some significant advantage that makes them highly attractive to other covenants. Carthian Law, for instance, grants some rather attractive qualities a Prince like to see in a subordinant, including resistance to betrayal through magic. The Lancea et Sanctum make very good Sheriffs and Hounds with their hunting and judgement magics (as well as historians), while the Circle are very good at general divinations and being overall mystics. The Invictus make very good subordinants, who stay subordinant because of the benefits they get from their Oaths.<br /> <br /> This was actually a deliberate design feature of the game, so that every covenant would have a strong reason to have the others around. It was supposed to break away from the idea that you wanted an absolute single-covenant monopoly, because it just wasn't effective. You can have other covenants in these positions, and they have reasons to support the current regime, even as they want to change things to suit themselves. Thus - political shinanigans and social maneuvering rather than subterfuge against a single ultimate authority.<br /> <br /> As well, its not like most Requiem Princes actually have the pull to be able to pull off single covenant monopolies anyways. The Masquerade-style tyrants who can do anything isn't really how the game really works. Princes need political capital, compromises, and more. If they have the numbers from members? Sure, they'll go for a monopoly. But this isn't always the case. Princes often keep power because they're adapt at herding cats, perhaps through blackmail, not because they force everyone to listen to them.<br /> <br /> A covenant monopoly is a &quot;traditional&quot; way of running a Vampire game, but that's mostly just the perspective of players and STs that fill it out that way. There's really no support for it. There's nothing stopping you, but there's nothing backing it up either. While there is deliberate support for having a mixed covenant power block in the city. <br /> <br /> So, take that as you will. <br /> <br /> <br /> * The Ordo Dracul doesn't really contribute to the city like the others, they're, as always, the odd duck out. They kind of just kind of... there. Sometimes, they're useful when they do their exploring routine, sometimes not. The anti-blood bond ability can be useful, and wyrms nests can make great Elysiums, but those do overlap with other abilities in the game as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-15-2017, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T18:52:25-07:00","id":1079613,"title":"","content":"So for most of the Disciplines, there are sacrifices up to 5 for Threnodies. What are some Protean Sacrifices for 4 / 5? I was thinking not hunting for a month (rather difficult for most), giving into bond or addiction to a vampire or both for 5. Stage 2 or 3 bond for 4 / 5 perhaps. It's all about being a predator and sacrificing those values for some period as witnessed by sleeping under a trodden area or not hunting for a week making 2 / 3<br /> <br /> Thought of a good one: Spend a day among mortals without feeding. Not only is this particularly dangerous, it's quite a huge F-U to your predator instincts and would totally warrant a lv 5 sacrifice following the theme of Protean's sacrifices.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, another question. What order do reflexive actions resolve? ie: dude with a magic ring reflexively destroys X vitae. I reflexively (parkour athletic action) throw a knife potentially prompting a check and rendering him unconscious from being full of lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-17-2017, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T04:44:10-07:00","id":1079743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1079613#post1079613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, another question. What order do reflexive actions resolve? ie: dude with a magic ring reflexively destroys X vitae. I reflexively (parkour athletic action) throw a knife potentially prompting a check and rendering him unconscious from being full of lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's really no &quot;order of resolution&quot; in CofD. The mechanics don't go into that much detail, mostly because its generally not needed. If something is reflexive, then its generally a faster-than-thought, takes little to no time type situation. In your above scenario, there's no reason why someone would be able to notice the ring being activated, pull a knife, throw it, and knock the person unconcious. And that's assuming that knocking a person unconcious stops whatever action they were taking, and Stamina rolls, and all that. If you're reacting to something reflexive, its generally going to be over before your reaction happens.<br /> <br /> There's no &quot;stack&quot; of actions. Everything, when its declared, is resolved pretty much right away. The only guideline is &quot;what makes the most sense in this story?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T05:58:20-07:00","id":1079757,"title":"","content":"Well he would've thrown the knife regardless in that situation, which is why it was sort of the ideal example. Two people enter a room, they both do something reflexive. In this case it's whoever declares first basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T06:40:49-07:00","id":1079770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1079757#post1079757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well he would've thrown the knife regardless in that situation, which is why it was sort of the ideal example. Two people enter a room, they both do something reflexive. In this case it's whoever declares first basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>If timing is critical and the actions are incompatible (for some reason they can't just occur simultaneously), then I go with an initiative roll - with allowance of celerity pre-emption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T08:44:17-07:00","id":1079812,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. For Berserker Style and Protean Claws, would I use my stamina as the durability of the weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T14:44:20-07:00","id":1080013,"title":"","content":"No. You'd be considered unarmed in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T17:13:41-07:00","id":1080089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1079613#post1079613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for most of the Disciplines, there are sacrifices up to 5 for Threnodies. What are some Protean Sacrifices for 4 / 5?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Those sound like good sacrifices. As for 5th level, they usually require some sort of permanent damage so perhaps cutting off appendages and spending willpower to lock it in forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T18:02:09-07:00","id":1080107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1080089#post1080089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Those sound like good sacrifices. As for 5th level, they usually require some sort of permanent damage so perhaps cutting off appendages and spending willpower to lock it in forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>They usually require aggravated, I don't think that'd be &quot;assume permanent&quot; still nasty though, to be sure. I'm currently working on a Threnody that has to be completed in sunlight after a lv 5 sacrifice (ie flaying yourself for a week) with my group to shed my bloodline (in the vein of the one that can shed someone's clan, but disciplines don't go to 6 anymore.)<br /> <br /> One more: Cruac references &quot;levels of damage&quot; where as in every other place of the book it's do an additional or count it as 2L or upgrade 1 lethal to aggravated.<br /> How would the majority interpret this? ie: Destruction Theme and Temple Guardian. It's not referenced particularly often so my group and I are inclined to just treat it as one additional <i>point</i> of damage although it still strikes me as odd. They even use the upgrade terminology in the Destruction Theme. So why use &quot;ignore the first <i>level</i> of damage&quot; as opposed to &quot;ignore the first <i>point</i> of damage&quot; What's the RAI on this? Also, the Tainted condition references <i>levels</i> of damage. <i>Levels</i> will just be synonymous with <i>points</i> then typically associated with inflicting them to yourself, unless anyone has insight into this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-18-2017, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:11:18-07:00","id":1083557,"title":"","content":"1) For the Blood Cleansing Ritual (Voivode Scale) should attempting the process vs. a higher potency Vinculum auto-fail or get a chance die?<br /> <br /> 2) When a Revenant is uplifted into a Clan proper, what happens to the increased Blood Sympathy to their creator? Do they lose it? Do they receive a new sympathy with the part-Sire/part-Avus who brought them in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:24:29-07:00","id":1083566,"title":"","content":"Chance die is standard when the dice pool reaches zero or less. Since the text doesn't explicitly auto-fail chance dice you'd roll a chance die per attempt. You could also spend Willpower points to increase your dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T05:46:26-07:00","id":1083929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1083557#post1083557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) For the Blood Cleansing Ritual (Voivode Scale) should attempting the process vs. a higher potency Vinculum auto-fail or get a chance die?<br /> <br /> 2) When a Revenant is uplifted into a Clan proper, what happens to the increased Blood Sympathy to their creator? Do they lose it? Do they receive a new sympathy with the part-Sire/part-Avus who brought them in?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Chance dice are a thing, and you CAN get a success with them. I mean 1 in 10 isn't bad. Hell, I've gotten 4 successes on a chance die on a MUSH before. That was something I'm not going to forget. Now willpower is a bit of an... Iffy matter, largely because it represents pushing yourself as a person. Could be physically, mentally, socially, spiritually... Either way, you're trying VERY hard, tot he point that you can't do it all the time if only because it exhausts you mentally. I'm not sure if that would really translate into using a scale, since the process itself seems detached from stats and personal effort. I've seen it used, and I've accepted the MUSH staff's interpretation at the time, that this particular scale can be enhanced with WP. But ultimately, it's a personal call in my book even as I've given my two cents.<br /> <br /> 2) I'd say they lose their old blood sympathy. The uplifter is giving them a little bit of their own soul in the pseudo-embrace (Or such is my own understanding), and it's not just a bastardized reanimation by way of the blood anymore. This is a powerful, notable act and I imagine it warrants the attendant consequences. If you need a reason beyond dramatic flow, the idea of the uplifter imprinting their own nature on the vitae within the revenant is always an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T06:17:55-07:00","id":1083935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1083929#post1083929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, I've gotten 4 successes on a chance die on a MUSH before.</div> </div> </div> </div>While VtR 2E doesn't say anything, both CofD and MtA 2E clarifies that the ten on a chance die shouldn't be rerolled. Just fyi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T08:03:41-07:00","id":1083973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1083929#post1083929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Chance dice are a thing, and you CAN get a success with them. I mean 1 in 10 isn't bad. Hell, I've gotten 4 successes on a chance die on a MUSH before. That was something I'm not going to forget. Now willpower is a bit of an... Iffy matter, largely because it represents pushing yourself as a person. Could be physically, mentally, socially, spiritually... Either way, you're trying VERY hard, tot he point that you can't do it all the time if only because it exhausts you mentally. I'm not sure if that would really translate into using a scale, since the process itself seems detached from stats and personal effort. I've seen it used, and I've accepted the MUSH staff's interpretation at the time, that this particular scale can be enhanced with WP. But ultimately, it's a personal call in my book even as I've given my two cents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd forgotten about Willpower, and I agree it's an iffy case. However, I've allowed WP to be spent on Dream Visions rolls which are similarly vague in what they represent, so I should probably let them fly for Cleansing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1083929#post1083929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) I'd say they lose their old blood sympathy. The uplifter is giving them a little bit of their own soul in the pseudo-embrace (Or such is my own understanding), and it's not just a bastardized reanimation by way of the blood anymore. This is a powerful, notable act and I imagine it warrants the attendant consequences. If you need a reason beyond dramatic flow, the idea of the uplifter imprinting their own nature on the vitae within the revenant is always an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my logical instinct as well. That being said, my narrative instinct is leaning toward keeping the old sympathy while gaining more sympathies with the uplift. I like the idea of that connection with the person who killed you staying around even if you reject your killer's Clan and find a new Sire. Lots of potential for unhealthy obsessions or unbalanced victim-tormentor relationships to drive drama. I guess at this point I'm curious on if there was any fluff or mechanics out there that would make this more than just a per-table decision, but doesn't sound like it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T14:58:28-07:00","id":1084173,"title":"","content":"About the willpower. I have been playing where sometimes it's not useful. Say you have 1 die to something and the ST gives you - 5 for whatever, even if you spent the willpower for +3, you're still -1 and at a chance die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T02:43:21-07:00","id":1084391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1084173#post1084173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the willpower. I have been playing where sometimes it's not useful. Say you have 1 die to something and the ST gives you - 5 for whatever, even if you spent the willpower for +3, you're still -1 and at a chance die.</div> </div> </div> </div>I despise when STs liberally throw around +5/-5 like they're pocket sand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T05:45:48-07:00","id":1084430,"title":"","content":"Ban question- does a Nosferatu's ban apply to non face-to-face interaction? Can a haunt send a letter/email normally or will people be inexplicably creeped out by it? (Not vampire related but it's a similar case and I can't find a promethean ask thread- could a promethean?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:27:47-07:00","id":1084630,"title":"","content":"Not normally. But if you're having them roll expression in order to write correspondence to influence the reader and want it to carry across audiovisual media, you could say that something in their word choice or illustration selection unnerves the reader or they &quot;say&quot; something that comes across as offensive or tasteless even if it wasn't the intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T10:30:30-07:00","id":1085070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1084391#post1084391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I despise when STs liberally throw around +5/-5 like they're pocket sand.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was just an example. But it's easily done in combat... if the bad guy's defense is 7 and you only have 3 dice to brawl, you are at -4 so + 3 still gives you -1... which is pointless to use WP. That's where I see it the most. Or doing something against a Safe Place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T18:26:13-07:00","id":1088032,"title":"","content":"Quick Question -<br /> <br /> So in regard to Protean *** - Beast's Skin - she can take on an animal's forms. Now my question is - would this work in regards to mythical animals or supernatural animals like a Hedge Beast for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T20:41:25-07:00","id":1088087,"title":"","content":"It's up to your ST but nothing prohibits it for level 2. It typically only grants a situational bonus or minor animalesque ability so you probably don't want to let the player take fire breathing and give them immunity to flame at level 2 for taking on the aspect of a fire drake. Level 3 requires you to consume the animal in question but if mythical creatures exist in the Hedge, they aren't mythical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-04-2017, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:26:36-07:00","id":1088216,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't show up on camera because they are always just standing out of frame/behind something/facing away/etc. But how does this work if, say, I am taking a photo of a vampire standing in the middle of an empty room? Or walking down a corridor with constant surveillance? Or in a room with multiple cctv cameras arranged so there's no blind spot? Or me taking a selfie with the vampire?<br /> <br /> To make a better question-can the beast be tricked/manoeuvred into a position where it can't avoid showing up on camera?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:59:41-07:00","id":1088231,"title":"","content":"If I'm not wrong it also says that the camera in superexposition of light/out of focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:07:26-07:00","id":1088236,"title":"","content":"So basically, if the vampire can't hide the camera just stops working? Fair enough then, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:10:24-07:00","id":1088237,"title":"","content":"A few things.<br /> Vampires don't &quot;disappear&quot; from photographs and video. They simply don't show up clearly, unless, of course, they wish to do so.<br /> Blurs in photographs and video are caused by two major things, movement and light and shade differential. Photographers understand this and know tricks to diminish or visually eliminate these factors but not entirely. I know how to position myself and set a camera's mechanical features to cause everything in the photograph to blur except the subject. I can also do the same thing to cause the subject to blur and make everything else clear.<br /> Can you trick or coerce a vampire into letting them get a clear picture or recording of them for reasons other than what you tell them (and possibly later use to incriminate them)? Yes.<br /> Can you force them to show up perfectly clear without their knowledge? Without some kind of supernatural power, I'd have to say no. It's a supernatural ability that the Beast somehow always senses when the vampire is being recorded and does something to disrupt identifying it. You're going to need some kind of supernatural power to counter it. It's akin to asking if you can force a chameleon to not turn green or brown when the environment they live in is leaves and sticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:59:03-07:00","id":1088261,"title":"","content":"I like to think in ChroD, pictures do gradually suck your soul out. In the case of Kindred, their lot is spoken for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T07:27:23-07:00","id":1088744,"title":"","content":"So quick question, seems things got nerfed, but thought I'd ask in case it's a matter of interpretation, this was a long post but streamlined it.<br /> <br /> Resilience says you suffer logical impairments from stuff being <i>removed</i> and gives examples such as eyes, limbs, &quot;and so on&quot;.<br /> The most intuitive interpretation here is that when figuring if you're affected by a tilt or not, use the damage from after resilience has been used, and only suffer the tilt if the damage still meets the requirements. Hell if it works on staking (a literal hole in your chest, presumably into your heart) it should work fro the rest of the tilts too. Unless someone legit <i>removes</i> something you're not just getting hit with random tilts unless they're actually inflicted and not just &quot;this dude kicked your knee in, resilience can't save you. Suffer from all logical impairments from all wounds&quot; seems way too conservative for how the discipline is written.<br /> <br /> edit B&amp;S p141:<br /> If an injury specifically removes a limb, an eye, or so on,<br /> the vampire does suffer logical impairments from the injuries.<br /> <br /> second question: I read somewhere you can &quot;cure&quot; a tilt by healing it as though it were a point of lethal, but can't remember where. If that's a thing it'd be cool if someone could find the source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-06-2017, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T07:35:36-07:00","id":1088749,"title":"","content":"1. Staking always requires 5 damage to put a vampire into Torpor. Not Stamina amount of damage.<br /> 2. The text specifies logical impairments from missing limbs and such. I.e. you check for tilts after the damage reduction is applied, unless you lose your limb entire which always inflicts appropriate tilts regardless of damage taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T07:39:31-07:00","id":1088752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1088749#post1088749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Staking always requires 5 damage to put a vampire into Torpor. Not Stamina amount of damage.<br /> 2. The text specifies logical impairments from missing limbs and such. I.e. you check for tilts after the damage reduction is applied, unless you lose your limb entire which always inflicts appropriate tilts regardless of damage taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought, thanks. Oh, and I knew that about staking I was thinking of wracks at the time lol.<br /> This doesn't change from B&amp;S to VTR: 2E eh? Almost everything is the exact same but already had this problem with the parkour merit, stuff arbitrarily getting buffed/nerfed within the same edition lol. Resilience should be kept like this, imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-06-2017, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T20:11:53-07:00","id":1088972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1088752#post1088752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I thought, thanks. Oh, and I knew that about staking I was thinking of wracks at the time lol.<br /> This doesn't change from B&amp;S to VTR: 2E eh? Almost everything is the exact same</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything is exactly the same in both versions of the book, except the cover, the title, and references to the title.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1088752#post1088752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but already had this problem with the parkour merit, stuff arbitrarily getting buffed/nerfed within the same edition lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh... when did this happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T22:34:11-07:00","id":1089007,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm looking at Blood and Smoke right now and it hasn't been changed.<br /> <br /> lol.<br /> <br /> It's possible you have one of the versions of Blood &amp; Smoke before the final print, when they were still editing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-07-2017, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T22:56:03-07:00","id":1089010,"title":"","content":"The 5th dot was changed so that it required meditation, instead of running for a minute. I think it may have been Chronicles that had it as run for a minute, which is technically current (2E, Chronicles of Darkness)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T01:23:15-07:00","id":1089041,"title":"","content":"Blood &amp; Smoke, Werewolf and Promethean say you have to run for a minute, the latter being the most recently published book. It's an error in the Chronicles book. It will probably be in the errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T06:12:02-07:00","id":1089094,"title":"","content":"As something that is dead, ie &quot;not growing, breathing, or carrying on normal cell processes&quot; how does radiation affect vampires or other things? for example - shooting a bullet with a radium core, or exposing someone to radium. Supposedly it gives people cancer, can cause their body to mutate in weird ways (small limbs, incredibly easy to remove or break bones, pieces of them getting medically removed as radiation destroys their body from the inside.) Radium is just.. so nasty.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure vampires would be fine, as it doesn't mystically degrade anything dead/industrial/whatever afaik, strictly living things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-07-2017, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T10:39:06-07:00","id":1089250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1089094#post1089094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As something that is dead, ie &amp;quot;not growing, breathing, or carrying on normal cell processes&amp;quot; how does radiation affect vampires or other things? for example - shooting a bullet with a radium core, or exposing someone to radium. Supposedly it gives people cancer, can cause their body to mutate in weird ways (small limbs, incredibly easy to remove or break bones, pieces of them getting medically removed as radiation destroys their body from the inside.) Radium is just.. so nasty.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure vampires would be fine, as it doesn't mystically degrade anything dead/industrial/whatever afaik, strictly living things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I don't think vampires would be too bothered by it. Mechanically speaking, sounds like a mundane source of aggravated damage, so lethal to vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:36:42-07:00","id":1089347,"title":"","content":"yea, silver shell with incendiary core it is. Aggravated to vampires and werewolves at least. Thanks ^^&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:48:15-07:00","id":1089353,"title":"","content":"Vampires should be affected by radiation normally, by which I mean downgrade the damage. It would make a good way to track them, but a real nasty thing to do. An irradiated vampire passing along small amounts of irradiated material to people while feeding and exposing people to radiation just by being in close proximity is not something that would not be a breaking point for most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T13:58:54-07:00","id":1089364,"title":"","content":"I think radiation should deal bashing towards humans, similar to electricity. Small doses don't do much while extreme doses are best represented with extreme amounts of bashing (and a Tilt/Condition to represent long term effects). In that case vampires wouldn't take damage from radiation unless the radiation is so extreme that it heats up the human body to the point where it would deal lethal damage. I.e. some actual structural damage and not just killing cells (that are already dead in vampires).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T14:52:37-07:00","id":1089397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1089353#post1089353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires should be affected by radiation normally, by which I mean downgrade the damage. It would make a good way to track them, but a real nasty thing to do. An irradiated vampire passing along small amounts of irradiated material to people while feeding and exposing people to radiation just by being in close proximity is not something that would not be a breaking point for most people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the Cleansing, though. They'll only stay irradiated for one night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T20:04:41-07:00","id":1089541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1089397#post1089397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget the Cleansing, though. They'll only stay irradiated for one night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about this radioactive bullet lodged in the vampire's body constantly irradiating the vampire, saliva, and blood. People can survive having objects lodged in their body like that. It isn't clear at all that the Cleansing would not just heal the wound around the bullet just like a person might naturally heal. Assuming the Cleansing actually cleans the surface of the vampire's skin, clothes might still be irradiated depending on the quantity of material. Radioactive material isn't so easy to get rid of and falls into one of those weird situations little covered like extreme pressure or the vacuum of space. Perhaps the Cleansing magics away all the problems or maybe the vampire is screwed for a while like with diseases sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T20:35:36-07:00","id":1089557,"title":"","content":"The cleansing always expels any foreign objects like bullets unless you pay the willpower to keep it there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:31:50-07:00","id":1089607,"title":"","content":"Radiation deals biological damages (if it dosen't reach an high temperature) so it's meaningless for the vampires that have not biological matter... Not alive at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T06:47:36-07:00","id":1089750,"title":"","content":"How the ghoul condition works on sick mortal? <br /> I mean: if a mortal is dyng because a cancer or another mortal diseases (leukemia, etc), can a vampire, ghouling her, heal the disease or does it just stops the disease until the ghoul condition fades?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 05-08-2017, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:02:46-07:00","id":1089785,"title":"","content":"It just puts the disease in stasis. Depending on the severity.<br /> <br /> 'mundane illnesses such as chicken pox or the more common cold run their course naturally. More serious diseases that might be in progress, such as multiple sclerosis, cancer or Parkinson's disease, freeze in their tracks alongside the aging process, growing no worse.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T17:59:08-07:00","id":1090063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1089094#post1089094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As something that is dead, ie &quot;not growing, breathing, or carrying on normal cell processes&quot; how does radiation affect vampires or other things? for example - shooting a bullet with a radium core, or exposing someone to radium. Supposedly it gives people cancer, can cause their body to mutate in weird ways (small limbs, incredibly easy to remove or break bones, pieces of them getting medically removed as radiation destroys their body from the inside.) Radium is just.. so nasty.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure vampires would be fine, as it doesn't mystically degrade anything dead/industrial/whatever afaik, strictly living things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are immune to poison and diseases. There is a huge huge huge thread somewhere with 10+ pages of discussion about this, but since radiation poisons the body causing living tissue to break down /mutate ect I wouldn't say it hurts a vampire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T03:42:49-07:00","id":1090208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090063#post1090063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are immune to poison and diseases. There is a huge huge huge thread somewhere with 10+ pages of discussion about this, but since radiation poisons the body causing living tissue to break down /mutate ect I wouldn't say it hurts a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're only immune if it isn't exposed to their blood. They can drink or have blood that's &quot;sick&quot; and they get sick. But that being said, they'd even ignore the environmental tilt in this edition? Decent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:04:20-07:00","id":1090212,"title":"","content":"I can totally see radiation breaking Vitae down. And no, Vampires can still suffer environmental tilts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:16:18-07:00","id":1090219,"title":"","content":"Radiation damages DNA and its duplication. Kindred vitae is not blood but a mistical source of energy and, Anyway, blood cells are dead as everything else in the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 05-09-2017, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:21:09-07:00","id":1090224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090219#post1090219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Radiation damages DNA and its duplication. Kindred vitae is not blood and, Anyway, blood cells are dead as everything else in the vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Radiation shifts atoms around, It can affect more than living tissue, its just more dramatic and noticeable there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:59:12-07:00","id":1090238,"title":"","content":"Atoms losing elctrons are not a problem per se, they become radioactive and regain electrons lost from another source. They become a problem with living matter, or if their quantity is so high to generate a great heat. <br /> But play this thing as you prefer.<br /> <br /> Edit: well they don't just lose electron but could also tramsmutate, etc but the story dosen't change to much and this is not a physics lesson <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A proof is that fruits treated with high radiation doses rots much later because the only thing the radiation damages are the living microorganism and the apple become radioactive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 05-09-2017, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:45:46-07:00","id":1090269,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know of any fluff or mechanics that speaks on the issue of whether Kindred in natural Torpor are affected differently by Telepathy or Dominate? (2E)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T07:33:27-07:00","id":1090293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090208#post1090208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're only immune if it isn't exposed to their blood. They can drink or have blood that's &amp;quot;sick&amp;quot; and they get sick.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't. In 1e they become carriers, so they can further spread the illness to others they feed on, but it doesn't actually affect them. 2e hasn't specified either way in any official sources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T07:34:23-07:00","id":1090297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090238#post1090238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Atoms losing elctrons are not a problem per se, they become radioactive and regain electrons lost from another source. They become a problem with living matter, or if their quantity is so high to generate a great heat. <br /> But play this thing as you prefer.<br /> <br /> Edit: well they don't just lose electron but could also tramsmutate, etc but the story dosen't change to much and this is not a physics lesson <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A proof is that fruits treated with high radiation doses rots much later because the only thing the radiation damages are the living microorganism and the apple become radioactive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't the electrons go back to where they belong the next morning during the Cleansing anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T10:53:07-07:00","id":1090368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090269#post1090269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know of any fluff or mechanics that speaks on the issue of whether Kindred in natural Torpor are affected differently by Telepathy or Dominate? (2E)</div> </div> </div> </div>*Telephone occupied tone*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T15:47:27-07:00","id":1090504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090293#post1090293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they don't. In 1e they become carriers, so they can further spread the illness to others they feed on, but it doesn't actually affect them. 2e hasn't specified either way in any official sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>are group has been relentless in using 1e whenever there isn't anything 2e. So it's been ruled if you drink off a drunk you get drunk. If you drink off a heroin addict you get high. If you drink and they're diseased you're a carrier (and this is in 2E/B&amp;S)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T22:34:35-07:00","id":1090597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090297#post1090297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't the electrons go back to where they belong the next morning during the Cleansing anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm well...also normal regeneration could I suppose. <br /> The point is that radiation, without considering extreme heat, doesn't have much impact on inanimated object or a dead body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T08:27:57-07:00","id":1090731,"title":"","content":"Radiation does harm nonliving matter, it just takes more of it. Space equipment, especially electronics, are nearly always shielded if intended to remain in service for any length of time.<br /> I'm in the camp of Bashing damage with immunity to the first couple points.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://hps.org/publicinformation/ate/q11162.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://hps.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Laser-Safety-ad.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hps.org/publicinformation/ate/q11162.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Radiation effects of electronic equipment </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://hps.org/publicinformation/ate/q11162.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://hps.org/publicinformation/ate/q11162.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Radiation effects on electrical equipment depend on the equipment and on the type of ionizing radiation to which it is exposed. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:32:59-07:00","id":1090775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090504#post1090504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> are group has been relentless in using 1e whenever there isn't anything 2e. So it's been ruled if you drink off a drunk you get drunk. If you drink off a heroin addict you get high. If you drink and they're diseased you're a carrier (and this is in 2E/B&amp;S)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I see the alcohol and heroine affecting a vampire in the short term, they can just spend a vitae to cleanse themselves of the effects of it.<br /> <br /> However say, Aids. if you drink someone with aids, how can it survive in a vampire? Most diseases need living hosts to survive in and every night when the vampire sleeps, they reset themselves.<br /> <br /> Pg 215 : Vampires do not tire, do not age, do not falter to disease or poison, hunting the night where none but the greatest of predators tread. Vampires&quot;<br /> Pg 91 &quot;Anything that wouldn\u2019t constitute a Health level of damage heals automatically and returns to its original state.&quot;<br /> FAQ: <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">What happens if a vampire feeds on an intoxicated mortal?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The vampire suffers the effects of the drug. The vampire may remove these effects by spending one Vitae, but could conceivably be too intoxicated to concentrate enough to do so.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Poisons not specifically harmful to Kindred follow the same rules as drugs. A Storyteller may choose to make an exception for poisons which break down cellular structure, but that\u2019s at her own discretion.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 05-10-2017, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:42:27-07:00","id":1090896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090597#post1090597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmm well...also normal regeneration could I suppose.<br /> The point is that radiation, without considering extreme heat, doesn't have much impact on inanimated object or a dead body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...radiation pretty much is extreme heat, otherwise we'd get no power from nuclear power. See also microwaves...<br /> <br /> (Even radio waves can be dangerous as Tesla and his assistant found out after playing around with a propotype RADAR and giving themselves what was essentially a sunburn.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:56:15-07:00","id":1090900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090896#post1090896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...radiation pretty much is extreme heat, otherwise we'd get no power from nuclear power. See also microwaves...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be more precise, extreme radiation leads to extreme heat.<br /> But what people think about when they hear radiation is gamma radiation, which is dangerous to normal humans without having to heat them up significantly. It's probably that kind of radiation that we're talking about.<br /> <br /> In either case I restate my stance that radiation should have no effect on vampires until they face enough radiation that the secondary heat is able to structurally damage their dead cells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T22:30:31-07:00","id":1090986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1090896#post1090896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well...radiation pretty much is extreme heat, otherwise we'd get no power from nuclear power. See also microwaves...<br /> <br /> (Even radio waves can be dangerous as Tesla and his assistant found out after playing around with a propotype RADAR and giving themselves what was essentially a sunburn.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Radio waves are a source of heat because they are in the frequency field of relaxation, when 50% of the dipoles, ions, etc fallow the field and the other part no. Their shocks generate heat. <br /> The waves lenght that produces more heat are in the infrared fields..... A lot more less energretic than gamma rays. The heat with gamma rays is provided not as a wave (that it is) but as a particles hit (that it is as well). But gamma ray, for a certain part, cross the biological matter without interact and without provide heat). <br /> We use nuclear fission to generate heat because it is extremely radioactive and the huge quantity of the shocks between radiation and matter (water) increase the heat. <br /> Again, for me, radiation don't provide damages and a radiation source like a nuclear central, provide damages as per extremal environmental heat.... But it is just sooo rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 05-11-2017, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:18:19-07:00","id":1091140,"title":"","content":"CofD has a very cinematic way of handling damage. It's not very detailed. It's not intended to be. Getting bogged down in realism isn't really the design philosophy of CofD, and you're probably better off playing other games if that's what you want.<br /> <br /> Radiation is an environmental hazard in CofD, so I'd just use those rules as-is. I thought that, somewhere or other, there were tweaks for Vampires using environmental hazards, though I can't find them. So I'd just use Environmental Hazard rules with the guidelines in the book (heavy radiation is level 4, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:25:51-07:00","id":1091162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1091140#post1091140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that, somewhere or other, there were tweaks for Vampires using environmental hazards, though I can't find them.</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, this is covered by vampires' damage reduction. Environmental hazards that do lethal only cause bashing to vampires. What you might be thinking of though is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar109_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"109\" data-vbnamecard=\"109\">Claire Redfield</a>'s houserules on vampires and sources of harm <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/40764-unofficial-rules-option-vampires-and-non-combat-sources-of-harm#post40764\">here</a>, which are pretty good as houserules go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:37:02-07:00","id":1091168,"title":"","content":"I dont have it on me but Hurt Locker goes into how some environmental tilts are diminished for vampires","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:42:03-07:00","id":1091173,"title":"","content":"Hurt Locker, p149.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Radiation poisoning, desert exposure, and toxic fumes are of little concern, save for vampires and the desert sun. These beings suffer the same effects of heavy snowfall, rain, and high winds as mortals do, but their powers give them an edge. The undead suffer no ill effects at all from extreme environments up to level three, and suffer level four environments as mortals do lower-level conditions (i.e., bashing damage equal to the environment\u2019s level once per hour, after a number of hours equal to the character\u2019s Stamina). Even then, their undead bodies resist such conditions to an incredible degree, subtracting their Supernatural Tolerance trait from the damage sustained. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T10:27:33-07:00","id":1092367,"title":"","content":"Is the general interpretation of the first dot of Protean that you bury yourself? The first paragraph says you <i>merge</i> with the ground, and after the cost/action are defined it says<i> sink</i> into the ground and that the only way to harm the vampire is to harm the ground (implying they couldn't just dig a bit and smash said kindred in the head with said shovel).<br /> <br /> After reading the Gangrel book (yea yea outdated) I'm more inclined to believe that they would keep the same &quot;core mechanics&quot; as they have in ever so many other areas. What's the general consensus on whether you <i>merge</i> (ie become the thing you're interring your self in) or <i>bury</i> merely displacing the material on the atomic level (how the hell do you even explain that one anyway?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":".  formatting, capitalization. 05-14-2017, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T11:38:01-07:00","id":1092400,"title":"","content":"You merge with the material you're sinking into. As you said yourself the book says merge and it says you need to damage the ground rather than saying you can be dug up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-14-2017, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:03:38-07:00","id":1092444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1092400#post1092400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You merge with the material you're sinking into. As you said yourself the book says merge and it says you need to damage the ground rather than saying you can be dug up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought.. thanks.<br /> <br /> One other question. The Threnody: A More Perfect Monster, if I were to frenzy, would I be able to add double the BP to my attributes, since it's raising the score by my Blood Potency?<br /> Likewise with Coil of the Wyrm - Defense/Initiative/Speed. That'd be awesome and completely in character for the guy I'm playing, he's already &quot;done it once before&quot; in his backstory although the specific mechanics haven't been discussed much yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:32:41-07:00","id":1092462,"title":"","content":"A More Perfect Monster doubles the score while Frenzying adds to rolls and resistances. That means the Attribute bonuses from Frenzy aren't doubled.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: If you Ride the Wave, have the Ride the Wave style Merit, is a member of the Kerberos bloodline, and has Lashed Out with the Monstrous Aspect earlier the same scene you effectively gets to add your Blood Potency three times when destroying objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-14-2017, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:09:56-07:00","id":1092486,"title":"","content":"I'm a hound of actaeon atm, eventually looking for a way to shed bloodlines. That being said, that sounds pretty gnarly lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:39:01-07:00","id":1092510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1092486#post1092486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a hound of actaeon atm, eventually looking for a way to shed bloodlines. That being said, that sounds pretty gnarly lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Afaik there's no official way to shed bloodlines, but my Kerberos character (who has most definitely used the 3xBP thing as an Ordo with maxed Wyrm) did get his bloodline purged when he got into contact with some awful Circle of the Crone types led by some guy named Kovacs. Kovacs meant to essentially scan my character's mind sometime before or after the ritual to find out as many secrets as possible, but some quick thinking and powerful allies got my character to go through the ritual with his mental integrity intact.<br /> The ritual itself was homebrew, and quite surprising since I had no idea what my ST had in mind. Turns out it's a high level Cr\u00faac ritual requiring several participants, loads of chanting, and a vessel. My character, as the vessel, became possessed by an aspect of the Crone. After Kovacs had relayed all the current events in the world to her he asked for a final favour; to purge the bloodline from her vessel, which she did before returning back to wherever she came from.<br /> <br /> So the ritual didn't actually do anything to the bloodline. What was required was direct contact with a vampiric deity to remove it, which I found interesting.<br /> After this my character managed to have another run-in with the Crone which would come to affect my character's development in very interesting ways. He managed to make a Deal with her wherein he was granted a Cr\u00faac ritual of his own to use in the future to contact her. Of course it required learning some Cr\u00faac to be able to use the ritual, but at this point in the chronicle it wasn't harder than kidnapping some random Circle shmuck from the streets to gain the basics, and then work from there. Now the entire group is actually swept up in the whole thing as we've started researching the metaphysics and origins of vampires, in pure Ordo fashion.<br /> We've played for soon three IRL years and I'm lagging behind with just 299 XP amassed right now, so we're quite far into non-standard territory. I don't think many VtR campaigns looks like ours. But it might be inspiration for you and your ST to handle your case of wanting to change bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-14-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T15:53:29-07:00","id":1097337,"title":"","content":"What's the definite guide to Auspex vs Obfuscate? Is it common place to just say &quot;I Clash with Auspex&quot; and roll? After reading Clash of Wills it would seem to me that you have to use Auspex in such a way that it would interact with the Obfuscated item/person and then cause a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> The example given, someone uses Spirit's Touch in an Oublietted Haven to check it out - clashing with Oubliette.<br /> In the uses I've seen, people will ask questions &quot;To the scene&quot; rather than to people or objects, and likewise instead of declaring a use of Auspex they just state &quot;I clash with X&quot;. (where X is the character they know is there, either out of character or via direction sense or something else I guess)<br /> <br /> Is there a standard way of handling say...<br /> <br /> An obfuscated gangrel, using Unmarked Grave? Can one really just walk into the scene (Adv. Direction Sense leading them there?) and just state &quot;I Clash with X&quot; without knowing where I am properly before hand? It is my understanding they would need to use Spirit's Touch on the building, which presumably I'd be interred - thus causing the Clash but also taking their action and giving me time to react (even if it is just to leave, should I lose the Clash and have to re-instate Obfuscate what then? Beast's Hackles? Just boom I Clash with my next turn targeting the scene with Hackles..)<br /> <br /> TLDR:<br /> <br /> Clash of Wills, can people really just walk into a scene and go &quot;I Clash with X character.&quot; Roll it and act based on that? Shouldn't it have to be specifically interacting with said character somehow? Auspex vs Obfuscated Unmarked Grave Gangrel (or fleeing vampire) what are the options?<br /> <br /> Does being hunted alone draw attention to you to break Obfuscate? ie, someone is looking for me, using Obf. 1 isn't enough since just knowing I'm around is enough to &quot;draw attention&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 05-26-2017, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T16:13:28-07:00","id":1097345,"title":"","content":"Clash of Wills is how you resolve an action. It's not an action in itself. Only when you've used Auspex in a way that opposes another character's Obfuscate does Clash of Wills apply. The ST will then tell you that you need to roll Auspex + Blood Potency (or just ask for your Auspex + Blood Potency if they're rolling for everyone like my beast of an ST).<br /> You can never just say that you want a Clash of Wills. You need to actually do something that triggers a Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T17:40:17-07:00","id":1097369,"title":"","content":"It's easy enough to provoke a clash, Auspex 1 with &quot;Is there anything here hidden from me?&quot; will clash with all uses of Obfuscate in the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T18:38:15-07:00","id":1097384,"title":"","content":"Is there a Mechanic for making your own custom Covenant? [COLOR=rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)]<span style=\"font-family:serif\">Covenant</span>[/COLOR]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T21:15:46-07:00","id":1097411,"title":"","content":"No. Just grab a bunch of other people and give them reason to band together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T07:56:15-07:00","id":1097516,"title":"","content":"Where can I find information about the lost clans? I know the core book mentions some of them. Julii are described in Requiem for Rome and Fall of the Camarilla. The Mekhet clanbook mentions both Grettir (as a rumoured origin for Norvegi) and Hollow Mekhet (though they are more like a clan variant).<br /> Are there any other books I'm not thinking of/unaware of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-27T11:02:33-07:00","id":1097565,"title":"","content":"Probably not. Nothing substantial, for sure. The Akhud are, obviously, in the VII book.<br /> <br /> I'd expect something to show up in Thousand Years of Night. Possibly future books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T12:50:07-07:00","id":1097847,"title":"","content":"Probaly some of them could show up in Thousand Years of Night. At least the document we've been showed said so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T12:17:35-07:00","id":1098182,"title":"","content":"Bit of a newbie question: in the health section, it says your health equals Size+Stamina+Resilience. However, in the Resilience section, it says that your Resilience gets added to your Stamina.<br /> <br /> So, if I had a character with 2 Stamina, they would have 7 health. However, if I gave them Resilience 1, would that mean they would then have 8 health (because Resilience increases Stamina), or 9 health (because it increases Stamina, and also gets added to health)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T12:39:04-07:00","id":1098190,"title":"","content":"You only apply Resilience to Health once. In your example you'd have 8 Health.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T12:59:41-07:00","id":1098200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1098190#post1098190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You only apply Resilience to Health once. In your example you'd have 8 Health.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I was wondering why my player's character had so much health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10751-belac93","name":"Belac93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10751_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T17:01:52-07:00","id":1100265,"title":"","content":"Quick question - reflexive actions during surprise rounds doable? I know you lose your action if knocked down/stunned/surprised. Reflexive actions can be done at _any time_ even while stunned or otherwise losing your instant action - and take zero thought/time. Someone surprises you with a stake, Resilience would be a plausible reflexive response during the surprise round?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T19:57:06-07:00","id":1100307,"title":"","content":"Personally I would say yes since the reflexive action can take place in the same turn as the suprise check and you can technically drop or grab something as a reflexive action during surprise. I can see an ST claiming otherwise because the rules say you can't take ANY action in the first turn of combat after surprise, IF you are surprised. I suppose it depends on whether or not you count the surprise check as the first turn of combat or say combat doesn't start until after surprise and initiative is determined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T20:15:35-07:00","id":1100312,"title":"","content":"Say my character is a Psychoanalyst, would &quot;Psychoanalysis&quot; be a speciality for Science or Medicine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T20:35:50-07:00","id":1100318,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate would be ridiculous if you couldn't reflexively heal or use Resilience against surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100312#post1100312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say my character is a Psychoanalyst, would &quot;Psychoanalysis&quot; be a speciality for Science or Medicine?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Medicine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T22:53:03-07:00","id":1100346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100312#post1100312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say my character is a Psychoanalyst, would &amp;quot;Psychoanalysis&amp;quot; be a speciality for Science or Medicine?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow a player to take it for either, though Empathy is frankly a better fit than either in my opinion. It's an ideal candidate for Interdisciplinary Specialty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T23:54:18-07:00","id":1100355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100346#post1100346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd allow a player to take it for either, though Empathy is frankly a better fit than either in my opinion. It's an ideal candidate for Interdisciplinary Specialty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Interdisciplinary Specialty a game mechanic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T00:09:02-07:00","id":1100360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100355#post1100355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Interdisciplinary Specialty a game mechanic?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Merit. CofD page 45 or GMC page 163. One dot, with the prerequisite of having a Specialty in a Skill at 3 dots or higher. Allows you to apply the Specialty to any Skill you have at least one dot in (as long as it makes sense in the narrative).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T04:19:41-07:00","id":1100400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100307#post1100307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would say yes since the reflexive action can take place in the same turn as the suprise check and you can technically drop or grab something as a reflexive action during surprise. I can see an ST claiming otherwise because the rules say you can't take ANY action in the first turn of combat after surprise, IF you are surprised. I suppose it depends on whether or not you count the surprise check as the first turn of combat or say combat doesn't start until after surprise and initiative is determined.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just says can't take &quot;an&quot; action not &quot;any&quot; action, which I figured was like stunned and a few other conditions/states where you can't act (meaning you can't take an instant action) but reflexive stuff is usually free game. Granted, that would mean Celerity interrupting a surprise attack and Resilience soaking the damage is possible, alongside any number of other reflexive things (which with 2E includes using Rapidity with Sunnikuse or other ridiculous levels of bs lol)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T04:57:23-07:00","id":1100404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100265#post1100265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question - reflexive actions during surprise rounds doable? I know you lose your action if knocked down/stunned/surprised. Reflexive actions can be done at _any time_ even while stunned or otherwise losing your instant action - and take zero thought/time. Someone surprises you with a stake, Resilience would be a plausible reflexive response during the surprise round?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stake thru the heart is a bane and IIRC Resilience doesn't works on those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T05:07:46-07:00","id":1100405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100404#post1100404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stake thru the heart is a bane and IIRC Resilience doesn't works on those.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only bane that Resilience specifically doesn't work on is sunlight. Besides, the damage dealt when being staked is not itself a bane. The stake hitting the heart would be the bane, if it's considered a bane at all. IIRC only sunlight, fire and acquired banes are actually refered to as banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-05-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T06:30:28-07:00","id":1100424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100400#post1100400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It just says can't take &quot;an&quot; action not &quot;any&quot; action, which I figured was like stunned and a few other conditions/states where you can't act (meaning you can't take an instant action) but reflexive stuff is usually free game. Granted, that would mean Celerity interrupting a surprise attack and Resilience soaking the damage is possible, alongside any number of other reflexive things (which with 2E includes using Rapidity with Sunnikuse or other ridiculous levels of bs lol)</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpret it to mean what it says. You can't take an action <u>during the first round of combat...</u> That means no reflexive actions in the first round of combat either.<br /> Surprise checks are designated as taking place before combat starts. That means you get to throw in all your legal use powers and modifiers in that turn and activate reflexive actions. You don't get to interrupt reflexive actions and you can't interrupt something you don't know is coming so if you're surprised you don't get to use Celerity to interrupt the free attack in that turn.<br /> You can use reflexive actions to heal damage etc. taken in the surprise round but they aren't considered to go into effect until the start of the next turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T08:03:08-07:00","id":1100448,"title":"","content":"Celerity explicitly calls out it can't be used to interrupt against any action you're unaware, which would include surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> Resilience does work against banes, being staked is not a bane. Any damage ignored by Resilience does not impair the vampire in any way unless a body part was actually removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T12:00:32-07:00","id":1100520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100360#post1100360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a Merit. CofD page 45 or GMC page 163. One dot, with the prerequisite of having a Specialty in a Skill at 3 dots or higher. Allows you to apply the Specialty to any Skill you have at least one dot in (as long as it makes sense in the narrative).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T12:00:32-07:00","id":1100521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100360#post1100360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a Merit. CofD page 45 or GMC page 163. One dot, with the prerequisite of having a Specialty in a Skill at 3 dots or higher. Allows you to apply the Specialty to any Skill you have at least one dot in (as long as it makes sense in the narrative).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T13:48:07-07:00","id":1100564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100448#post1100448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity explicitly calls out it can't be used to interrupt against any action you're unaware, which would include surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> Resilience does work against banes, being staked is not a bane. Any damage ignored by Resilience does not impair the vampire in any way unless a body part was actually removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if something reflexive specifically states it can't be used against unaware actions, in this instance Resilience and other stuff is doable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T04:57:00-07:00","id":1100778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100448#post1100448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celerity explicitly calls out it can't be used to interrupt against any action you're unaware, which would include surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> Resilience does work against banes, being staked is not a bane. Any damage ignored by Resilience does not impair the vampire in any way unless a body part was actually removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's structured as one. Every vampire has that weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T06:26:13-07:00","id":1100803,"title":"","content":"Actually the way resilience works is that it reduces damage without actually preventing the wounds, so what should happen is that it would prevent the damage of the stake going in, but you'd still be torpid due to wood-in-the-heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:54:42-07:00","id":1100831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1100803#post1100803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the way resilience works is that it reduces damage without actually preventing the wounds, so what should happen is that it would prevent the damage of the stake going in, but you'd still be torpid due to wood-in-the-heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>It logically should, but by RAW at least, it doesn't work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T14:17:22-07:00","id":1100961,"title":"","content":"It was a point of contention for a while though, prior to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T23:49:26-07:00","id":1103737,"title":"","content":"IN the corebook in the section for the Ordo Dracul and developing scales on page 155 where it says &quot;Presenting a new Scale to his Mystery Kogaions is grounds for an immediate increase in Order status.&quot; Is this meant to be a free dot of status, or simply a way to justify spending EXP to increase status immediately without further effort?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T03:17:12-07:00","id":1103757,"title":"","content":"I would say a justification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T03:40:42-07:00","id":1103761,"title":"","content":"They should have researched and developed the scale during in game role playing sessions The xp gained doing that should garner enough xp for the player to purchase it. They have a power nobody else does. However if they role play out a formal presentation to the covenant, that is justification to purchase a status increase with xp. The down side is, now the scale is known and available to the rest of the order. Which means more demands may be placed on the character to produce further scales or mysteries, demands to teach it (proof it's a legitimate scale and not a bloodline quirk or botched attempt of another power), or possibly recruit his research associates into the organization. I would not say it's a free or effortless status gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T20:15:11-07:00","id":1104124,"title":"","content":"How would you say toxins and poisons would affect Kindred? Would it only do bashing to them, or would it do nothing because of the lack of functioning systems in their body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T21:52:56-07:00","id":1104153,"title":"","content":"Unless there was magic involved or a poison that specifically destroys blood I'd have it do nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T22:31:21-07:00","id":1104165,"title":"","content":"Right, I know the hemotoxin from Secrets of the Covenants effects Kindred. I just wasn't sure how they dealt with other toxins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T23:14:52-07:00","id":1104171,"title":"","content":"I don't know that there are any rules on it, but I'd say anything that affects respiratory systems probably shouldn't have any effect. I'd maybe argue against anything that affects the nervous system, necrotic venom could have an effect, but regional. If it is a coagulant, it might make it harder to spend vitae? Maybe twice the cost.<br /> <br /> But really, I don't know.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T23:43:48-07:00","id":1104178,"title":"","content":"I remember that somewhere is written that the blood doesn't flow in veins anymore. The blood doesn't flow ay all because the heart is still. The quantity of blood is even not linked to vitae. Losing blood from an injury doesn't let the vampire losing vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T23:57:53-07:00","id":1104185,"title":"","content":"The rules have been made clear, we've discussed them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/115030-snake-venom\">here</a> and they pop up in the FAQ. But Ever Professional was asking about what you would do, which is not necessarily what the rules say. It's a rare circumstance, I imagine. I don't think a regular snake has ever popped up in my games, but serpent imagery and vampires do mix well and there's always serpentine vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-16-2017, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T09:33:59-07:00","id":1104331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1104124#post1104124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you say toxins and poisons would affect Kindred? Would it only do bashing to them, or would it do nothing because of the lack of functioning systems in their body?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR FAQ</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">What happens if a vampire feeds on an intoxicated mortal?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The vampire suffers the effects of the drug. The vampire may remove these effects by spending one Vitae, but could conceivably be too intoxicated to concentrate enough to do so.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Poisons not specifically harmful to Kindred follow the same rules as drugs. A Storyteller may choose to make an exception for poisons which break down cellular structure, but that\u2019s at her own discretion.</span></span></b><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>In the FAQ stickied to the top of the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T22:40:57-07:00","id":1106425,"title":"","content":"Can Kindred use the mortal systems of abjuring, summoning, exorcism, warding, and binding found in the blue book when dealing with ephemeral entities, or do they have to find mortal practitioners?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T03:55:07-07:00","id":1106470,"title":"","content":"Only abjuring could be restricted to mortals since all the others only work through their rituals rather than innate metaphysical qualities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T04:04:02-07:00","id":1106473,"title":"","content":"That's up to the ST. For me it depends on the setting. I do allow high Humanity kindred or Ventrue with a specific homebrewed devotion to do exorcisms. If there are more than three practitioners of Cruac, Theban Sorcery, Vodoun, Ahranite Sorcery, Gilded Cage, Scales etc. scattered across more than two covenants then no. They can consult one of them or find a legitimate mortal practitioner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-22-2017, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T04:37:40-07:00","id":1106486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1106425#post1106425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Kindred use the mortal systems of abjuring, summoning, exorcism, warding, and binding found in the blue book when dealing with ephemeral entities, or do they have to find mortal practitioners?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally allow it; I tend to default to the ephemeral systems allowing integrity to be replaced with whatever equivalent. This does cause some oddities like Werewolves being better at abjuring when away from their ideal harmony, but given high is more 'human' for them, that still makes sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T05:49:31-07:00","id":1106502,"title":"","content":"So...ATYoN question time. Unbridled Force lets me punch someone up to 100 meters away with my fightan magic. Do they get dodge/defence/whatever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T06:41:16-07:00","id":1106520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orzhov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1106502#post1106502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...ATYoN question time. Unbridled Force lets me punch someone up to 100 meters away with my fightan magic. Do they get dodge/defence/whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>The force itself is invisible which negates all defense, but since the character needs to perform some sort of manoeuvre with their hand it could be possible to apply defense or dodge as if it was a ranged attack (i.e. Celerity or full defense if having certain powers), if the defender sees the gesture and knows what it could mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T22:36:23-07:00","id":1107519,"title":"","content":"So, how many Kindred are typically within a city? Is there a chart in the core book, or is it a case by case basis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T00:22:08-07:00","id":1107560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1107519#post1107519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how many Kindred are typically within a city? Is there a chart in the core book, or is it a case by case basis?</div> </div> </div> </div>However many your story needs.<br /> <br /> There was an example in first edition, literally bordered by, 'The truth is, Kindred numbers vary from city to city,' and 'As long as the population doesn't grow so high that people take notice of the predators among them, numbers don't matter.' And people still take that number and insist it is the right number, even when in the same breath they complain about the number not making sense in some cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T03:56:52-07:00","id":1107964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1107519#post1107519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how many Kindred are typically within a city? Is there a chart in the core book, or is it a case by case basis?</div> </div> </div> </div> In previous editions 1 vampire per 12 000 or 10 000 people. I guess it's up to you. It depends on the city itself, timeline and other factors. When designing a city you must remember about the masquerade. I preffer rather low vampire population, because its seems more realistic to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T11:33:49-07:00","id":1108085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1107964#post1107964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In previous editions 1 vampire per 12 000 or 10 000 people. I guess it's up to you. It depends on the city itself, timeline and other factors. When designing a city you must remember about the masquerade. I preffer rather low vampire population, because its seems more realistic to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>There has only been one previous edition of Vampire the Requiem, and the number it gave was 1 vampire per 50,000 humans. That number was given as a rough estimate of a global mean, which is practically useless for assessing the ratio in a typical city. Which is fine, since there really shouldn't be a typical city ratio. They really shouldn't have even given the 1 in 50,000 figure because it has lead to more confusion than anything and ultimately everyone is just going to ignore it in favor of whatever ratio suits their story anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T13:03:24-07:00","id":1108476,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know when the Half Damned book is going to come out? I swear I read something that said April- June and June is almost over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T13:11:38-07:00","id":1108479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1108476#post1108476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone know when the Half Damned book is going to come out? I swear I read something that said April- June and June is almost over.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably saw it on the Current Projects page, which used to give rough windows with a disclaimer that those windows are statements of intent and that intent is subject to change as circumstances demand. You really can't trust any projected dates further out than &quot;this Wednesday&quot; when it comes to Onyx Path releases. Accordingly, the Current Projects page doesn't even give those release windows anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-27-2017, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T10:20:24-07:00","id":1110908,"title":"","content":"Are there any restrictions on the illusions created with Dread Presence beyond the short duration and size? Can they be used not for intimidation, but just as normal illusions? Could you whisper to a teammate at distance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/928-niv3k","name":"NIV3K","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T12:23:56-07:00","id":1110945,"title":"","content":"They're supposed to engender fear or revulsion. They only affect up to two senses at a time. They can't cause harm. <br /> I'm of the personal opinion that no, you can't use it to conceal communication and/or exploit typical sensory ranges but yes, you could use it to generate a whisper to scare someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T12:51:30-07:00","id":1110952,"title":"","content":"You can only get Clan disciplines, correct? Bloodline disciplines only come with that bloodline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T13:03:57-07:00","id":1110957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1110952#post1110952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can only get Clan disciplines, correct? Bloodline disciplines only come with that bloodline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each clan has their own specific discipline (Auspex, Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare, and Protean) that requires you to be part of that clan or drink the blood of someone in that clan. However, there are the five common disciplines (Animalism, Celerity, Obfuscate, Resilience, and Vigor) that any vampire can learn, it's just easier when it's an in-clan discipline.<br /> <br /> You are correct in that only the members of a bloodline may learn their unique discipline (or devotions, or merits).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T13:27:08-07:00","id":1111395,"title":"","content":"Simple question: Colossus devotion, does it ignore Resilience and Resilience based armour (Rhino's Hide, Flesh of Iron) because I'd be inclined to say no. Things that bypass Resilience typically mention Resilience or supernatural armour by name/type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T14:05:21-07:00","id":1111406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1111395#post1111395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple question: Colossus devotion, does it ignore Resilience and Resilience based armour (Rhino's Hide, Flesh of Iron) because I'd be inclined to say no. Things that bypass Resilience typically mention Resilience or supernatural armour by name/type.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recognize either of these. Are they 1E Devotions?<br /> <br /> In 2E nothing that bypasses armour can bypass Resilience (without explicitly mentioning Resilience) because Resilience isn't armour. It removes damage similar to armour but it doesn't have an armor rating that can be affected by armor penetration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T15:51:15-07:00","id":1111434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1111406#post1111406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't recognize either of these. Are they 1E Devotions?<br /> <br /> In 2E nothing that bypasses armour can bypass Resilience (without explicitly mentioning Resilience) because Resilience isn't armour. It removes damage similar to armour but it doesn't have an armor rating that can be affected by armor penetration.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/5sY0ny1z\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/5sY0ny1z\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/5sY0ny1z\" target=\"_blank\"> https://pastebin.com/5sY0ny1z </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> David Hill created a bunch of Devotions that were supposed to be an Easter egg for Secrets of the Covenants, but there was an editorial oversight of some stripe and the clue to find them wasn't included. They can all be found here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/u/ericateachesnyc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/u/ericateachesnyc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/u/ericateachesnyc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://pastebin.com/u/ericateachesnyc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/u/knightchelsea\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/u/knightchelsea\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/u/knightchelsea\" target=\"_blank\"> https://pastebin.com/u/knightchelsea </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T05:45:23-07:00","id":1111625,"title":"","content":"How does Aegis of Defiance work, exactly? Most mind effecting powers are subtle when it comes to commanding other people, so does the vampire have to know about the power they are defying (and if so, how), or can they just use it whenever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T06:42:09-07:00","id":1111636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1111395#post1111395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple question: Colossus devotion, does it ignore Resilience and Resilience based armour (Rhino's Hide, Flesh of Iron) because I'd be inclined to say no. Things that bypass Resilience typically mention Resilience or supernatural armour by name/type.</div> </div> </div> </div> Resilience is not actually armor. Its -like- armor, but it is actually something different. Colossus does not ignore it.<br /> <br /> Rhino's Hide and Flesh of iron are 1e devotions, so how they interact with Colossus is going to depend on how one translates them over. Though, my knee jerk reaction is to just call for a Clash of Wills in this case. That's generally the best thing to do when you have two competing abilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1111625#post1111625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does Aegis of Defiance work, exactly? Most mind effecting powers are subtle when it comes to commanding other people, so does the vampire have to know about the power they are defying (and if so, how), or can they just use it whenever?</div> </div> </div> </div> Basically, there are two abilities here, depending on if you know you're under an effect, or not.<br /> <br /> If you know, you can reflexively use this to effectively remove the mind control effect altogether. While disciplines are subtle, some uses are very much unsubtle. Telling someone to shoot themselves in the head is pretty obviously mind control.<br /> <br /> If you don't know, you can defy specific order or inclinations, but only those orders or inclinations - successive orders / influences apply as normal. You as a player decide when to use the devotion, and not necessarily the character. Reflexive activation doesn't always require conscious thought - the Beast's instincts can do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T03:43:18-07:00","id":1114100,"title":"","content":"Commanding animals to attack somone using animalism: when those animals will stops to attack? After how many damage taken? What will lead the animals to desist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T13:30:55-07:00","id":1114727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114100#post1114100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Commanding animals to attack somone using animalism: when those animals will stops to attack? After how many damage taken? What will lead the animals to desist?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more - how long until they get there? Any chronicle I've used Animals in it's &quot;They won't be here for 5 minutes&quot; or something so it's kinda meh and useless despite the &quot;you always have allies in a fight&quot; flavour.<br /> As for how long? That depends on how you word the command. &quot;Attack them!&quot; great they get their attack out, stop unless your ST isn't being harsh. &quot;Kill Them!&quot; is a bit different they'll go until they're dead. &quot;Devour them!&quot; would be the best, as they'll attempt to kill the target and/or eat any evidence before leaving to do their normal animal things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:27:18-07:00","id":1114754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114727#post1114727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more - how long until they get there? Any chronicle I've used Animals in it's &amp;quot;They won't be here for 5 minutes&amp;quot; or something so it's kinda meh and useless despite the &amp;quot;you always have allies in a fight&amp;quot; flavour.<br /> As for how long? That depends on how you word the command. &amp;quot;Attack them!&amp;quot; great they get their attack out, stop unless your ST isn't being harsh. &amp;quot;Kill Them!&amp;quot; is a bit different they'll go until they're dead. &amp;quot;Devour them!&amp;quot; would be the best, as they'll attempt to kill the target and/or eat any evidence before leaving to do their normal animal things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Five minutes? Typically depending on the area I'll have the animals come in at the most five turns later. Otherwise, I typically have them come in two or three turns later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:43:03-07:00","id":1114761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114754#post1114754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Five minutes? Typically depending on the area I'll have the animals come in at the most five turns later. Otherwise, I typically have them come in two or three turns later.</div> </div> </div> </div>It delegates the discipline to &quot;Find this for me&quot; instead of &quot;Fight this for me&quot; although anything worth finding is Obfuscated typically.. lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:53:24-07:00","id":1114766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114761#post1114761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It delegates the discipline to &amp;quot;Find this for me&amp;quot; instead of &amp;quot;Fight this for me&amp;quot; although anything worth finding is Obfuscated typically.. lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate is such a fun discipline; but yeah, five minutes is surprising there are animals everywhere you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:58:37-07:00","id":1114768,"title":"","content":"Some powers go the way of the Spirit arcana, if the Storyteller doesn't want you to use them they can just block it like that. It's rather unfair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T15:59:51-07:00","id":1114796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114768#post1114768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some powers go the way of the Spirit arcana, if the Storyteller doesn't want you to use them they can just block it like that. It's rather unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, that's the least of your problems depending on the ST/DM, System, and &quot;intended plot&quot;, but that's getting off topic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T19:03:25-07:00","id":1114855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114768#post1114768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some powers go the way of the Spirit arcana, if the Storyteller doesn't want you to use them they can just block it like that. It's rather unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you mean? I haven't had any troubles with the spirit arcana in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T20:07:57-07:00","id":1114877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114855#post1114855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean? I haven't had any troubles with the spirit arcana in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lucky you?<br /> <br /> A fairly common complaint among other players of spirit mages and those who wanted to play werewolf games and on and on was that if a storyteller felt overworked, they would simply shut it out. 'There's no spirits around,' is basically the same as there not being animals around. There's spirits everywhere. But not every storyteller wants to design every scene with a mirror-world beyond what they've plotted for it, or have to think up animals that might be there just in case someone uses Animalism or, having already written their adventure or whatever, to change it by adding spirits or animals that could derail their scenes. I imagine it also came up with the Death arcana, where the ability to summon ghosts worked similarly, but I think people were more put off by the necromancer angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T20:46:14-07:00","id":1114891,"title":"","content":"Ghouls who know Protean 1 (e.g. Gangrel ghouls): what happens if they use Unmarked Grave? They asphyxiate? Or do they enter suspended animation? Or do they eventually pass out and get expelled?<br /> <br /> How have you ruled this?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T21:38:34-07:00","id":1114911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114877#post1114877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lucky you?<br /> <br /> A fairly common complaint among other players of spirit mages and those who wanted to play werewolf games and on and on was that if a storyteller felt overworked, they would simply shut it out. 'There's no spirits around,' is basically the same as there not being animals around. There's spirits everywhere. But not every storyteller wants to design every scene with a mirror-world beyond what they've plotted for it, or have to think up animals that might be there just in case someone uses Animalism or, having already written their adventure or whatever, to change it by adding spirits or animals that could derail their scenes. I imagine it also came up with the Death arcana, where the ability to summon ghosts worked similarly, but I think people were more put off by the necromancer angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I guess that makes sense. I'm general I've always tried to design my scenes with the characters in mind. If a player is a necromancer, there will be a ghost or two. If the player is a shaman, there will be a spirit or two. I dislike the idea of players putting experience into something and them never being able to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T22:55:27-07:00","id":1114937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114727#post1114727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more - how long until they get there? Any chronicle I've used Animals in it's &quot;They won't be here for 5 minutes&quot; or something so it's kinda meh and useless despite the &quot;you always have allies in a fight&quot; flavour.<br /> As for how long? That depends on how you word the command. &quot;Attack them!&quot; great they get their attack out, stop unless your ST isn't being harsh. &quot;Kill Them!&quot; is a bit different they'll go until they're dead. &quot;Devour them!&quot; would be the best, as they'll attempt to kill the target and/or eat any evidence before leaving to do their normal animal things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Five minutes?? Well everywhere I can see birds or dogs or rats (sometimes) in the city I'v been. In the forest even more. For me it's matter of turns but, anyway, the question was different.<br /> <br /> The dogs at a border check, a patrol with dogs etc. In that situation the dogs are there...they are coming to you with their masters and you says: &quot;kill your masters&quot;. Now, the policemen probably open the fire at some point. How many damages should the dogs receive before to stop? Will they fight until death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-12-2017, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T23:45:45-07:00","id":1114959,"title":"","content":"Scenario: A Vampire-With-a-Strix-Inside is in a fight with some Werewolves and Vampires. It's been around the block enough to know that Werewolf teeth are a real pain against its host body. He would like to disable said teeth.<br /> <br /> There are rules for targeting limbs (for a wrack) and the head itself (for stunning). If one would target the muzzle of a wolf with a sword to cause a &quot;muzzle wrack&quot;, would you make it a -2 that needs damage more-than-stamina to disable, a -3 with the same, or -4 to cause an instant wrack just like with targeting a hand to break fingers? So the goal would be to break the teeth/muzzle.<br /> <br /> Also, a Vampire needs to be Torpid to be open for Strix possession. Would it be possible for a materialized Strix to do enough damage in combat to a future host to make them go down (and not heal enough in 1 turn to get up again), then possess the body on the next turn?<br /> <br /> Do normal Torpor length rules apply with a Strix possession, or can it use the host body immediately after possessing, even if it was Torpid because of too much lethal damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T04:02:57-07:00","id":1115015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114937#post1114937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Five minutes?? Well everywhere I can see birds or dogs or rats (sometimes) in the city I'v been. In the forest even more. For me it's matter of turns but, anyway, the question was different.<br /> <br /> The dogs at a border check, a patrol with dogs etc. In that situation the dogs are there...they are coming to you with their masters and you says: &quot;kill your masters&quot;. Now, the policemen probably open the fire at some point. How many damages should the dogs receive before to stop? Will they fight until death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that commands are free to issue and it's bringing the weight of a discipline to bear, not merely animal ken - I think they'd fight until death or until/if told otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T04:50:49-07:00","id":1115027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114100#post1114100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Commanding animals to attack somone using animalism: when those animals will stops to attack? After how many damage taken? What will lead the animals to desist?</div> </div> </div> </div> The animal stat compendium have rules an entry that says &quot;use this ofr a swarm.&quot; So, use that for a swarm. Alternatively, other games make animal (or zombie!) swarms as an Environmental Tilt. <br /> <br /> When will animals stop attacking? Probably when their target is dead or has been chased off. IE - no longer a threat. What will lead animals to desist? Its a mind control power, so only more magic will stop it. Or the order becomes impossible to fulfill (like using Obfuscate / Celerity to vanish and the animals unable to figure out what happen or how to find you).<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114891#post1114891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls who know Protean 1 (e.g. Gangrel ghouls): what happens if they use Unmarked Grave? They asphyxiate? Or do they enter suspended animation? Or do they eventually pass out and get expelled?<br /> <br /> How have you ruled this?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div> I think there was a word from Rose, back when she was vampire developer, that said that ghouls were fine. Don't quote me on it. Back in 1e, they would suffociate. In 2e? We'll probably see rules for that kind of thing in the upcoming Half-Damned book. <br /> <br /> Personally? They get all the same benefits as a vampire, because its lame as hell to have to purchase a power you can't use. You spent xp on it, you get full benefits from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T04:50:49-07:00","id":1115028,"title":"","content":"double double (post), toil and trouble<br /> fire burn, caudron bubble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T04:56:54-07:00","id":1115029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114959#post1114959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scenario: A Vampire-With-a-Strix-Inside is in a fight with some Werewolves and Vampires. It's been around the block enough to know that Werewolf teeth are a real pain against its host body. He would like to disable said teeth.<br /> <br /> There are rules for targeting limbs (for a wrack) and the head itself (for stunning). If one would target the muzzle of a wolf with a sword to cause a &amp;quot;muzzle wrack&amp;quot;, would you make it a -2 that needs damage more-than-stamina to disable, a -3 with the same, or -4 to cause an instant wrack just like with targeting a hand to break fingers? So the goal would be to break the teeth/muzzle.<br /> <br /> Also, a Vampire needs to be Torpid to be open for Strix possession. Would it be possible for a materialized Strix to do enough damage in combat to a future host to make them go down (and not heal enough in 1 turn to get up again), then possess the body on the next turn?<br /> <br /> Do normal Torpor length rules apply with a Strix possession, or can it use the host body immediately after possessing, even if it was Torpid because of too much lethal damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>The penalty roughly corresponds to size of the targeted area. I'd say -4 just like hands. Maybe -3 in the non-human forms. The damage required is dependent on how sturdy the targeted area is. If you're looking to break the jaw I'd say Stamina damage. Jaw bones are massive and you can easily break a hand against it so they're obviously a lot sturdier than hands.<br /> <br /> Just remember that a werewolf heals 1-6 bashing per turn based on Primal Urge, can spend one Essence to heal as many lethal damage, and heals all bashing and lethal damage automatically while in Gauru.<br /> Also, Rahu can ignore Tilts for two turns, and there's a Gift that allows werewolves to spend an Essence to heal Tilts reflexively. This Gift costs no Essence and is used automatically in Basu-Im. Don't expect Tilts hang around or even do much on werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:09:03-07:00","id":1115034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1114959#post1114959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scenario: A Vampire-With-a-Strix-Inside is in a fight with some Werewolves and Vampires. It's been around the block enough to know that Werewolf teeth are a real pain against its host body. He would like to disable said teeth.<br /> <br /> There are rules for targeting limbs (for a wrack) and the head itself (for stunning). If one would target the muzzle of a wolf with a sword to cause a &quot;muzzle wrack&quot;, would you make it a -2 that needs damage more-than-stamina to disable, a -3 with the same, or -4 to cause an instant wrack just like with targeting a hand to break fingers? So the goal would be to break the teeth/muzzle.</div> </div> </div> </div> Targetting a jaw is likely going to be -4, the same as a hand. Targetting teeth specifically will be a -5, same as eye. Of course, werewolves and vampires heal very fast, so its very likely going to end up as healed the next turn. Tilts are very ineffective against vamps and wolves unless done with agg damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, a Vampire needs to be Torpid to be open for Strix possession. Would it be possible for a materialized Strix to do enough damage in combat to a future host to make them go down (and not heal enough in 1 turn to get up again), then possess the body on the next turn? </div> </div> </div> Sure. It would go something like this - <br /> Turn 1 - put vampire into torpor.<br /> Turn 2 - Activate Possess Kindred. Spend willpower, make the roll, spend the turn possessing the body<br /> Turn 3 - Free to act. Given the wording that it takes &quot;a turn&quot; to possess the body, I'm assuming that means that the possession doesn't fully take for a full round, and thus no reflexive actions (such as Celerity) are possible until the full initiative count goes through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do normal Torpor length rules apply with a Strix possession, or can it use the host body immediately after possessing, even if it was Torpid because of too much lethal damage? </div> </div> </div> Torpor rules do not apply to strix possessions. Damage, stake through the heart, you name it. Strix possessed beings don't torpor, they keep going until the body is destroyed through agg damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T05:17:21-07:00","id":1115039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115029#post1115029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just remember that a werewolf heals 1-6 bashing per turn based on Primal Urge, can spend one Essence to heal as many lethal damage, and heals all bashing and lethal damage automatically while in Gauru.<br /> Also, Rahu can ignore Tilts for two turns, and there's a Gift that allows werewolves to spend an Essence to heal Tilts reflexively. This Gift costs no Essence and is used automatically in Basu-Im. Don't expect Tilts hang around or even do much on werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Luckily&quot; the two PC's that plan on attacking a powerful Elder Vampire are newly changed, so only Primal Urge 1 and also don't have that Gift currently. Will have to see next session if they come up with a better plan that &quot;charge in head on&quot; or if they manage to make it through all the mortal security without &quot;using up&quot; their Gauru. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A -3 with stamina amount of damage seems pretty reasonable if/when they go Big Wolfy (-4 for normal wolf size) and reveal what they are. Now all I need to do is manage to roll 1-2 successes, which I've so far been struggling to do even with 15-20 dice pools. Meanwhile the PC's manage to roll exceptionals with 6 dice. Not that I want to kill them, but so far nothing I've thrown at them has even posed a challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 07-12-2017, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T06:56:35-07:00","id":1115072,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2102_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2102\" data-vbnamecard=\"2102\">MCN</a>! I appreciate the confirmation--when it comes to ghouls the gameline(s) have generally been willing to give them the short end of the stick, as if in-game abuse wasn't enough. It's lame, and boring, and yeah: if you spend XP on something it should function as advertised. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115039#post1115039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... two PC's that plan on attacking a powerful Elder Vampire ... Will have to see next session if they come up with a better plan that &quot;charge in head on&quot; or if they manage to make it through all the mortal security without &quot;using up&quot; their Gauru. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ... Not that I want to kill them, but so far nothing I've thrown at them has even posed a challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves do two things well: keep going, and kill things. You'll need to get clever as a Storyteller to deal with this, as they are being very straightforward with their advantages. Opposing them force-on-force will lead to a great deal of frustration at the table--for all of you. You will literally have to come up with a bigger and badder monster-of-the-week to make a dent; eventually you've beaten Galactus a few times and then what?<br /> <br /> Back to the problem at hand: vampire elders are powerful and cagey. Vampire elders with strix in them are perhaps less cagey, but have perspective and powers that should be even more destabilizing to meat-bound furballs. Use them. <br /> <br /> &quot;Keep going?&quot; - Distract them with things that are more important to them (family, territory, etc--they have ties, surely! Or serious (&quot;the spirits in your apartment building are eating each other--all of them; the magath resulting from that are especially crazy and seem to take peculiar interest in you and yours!&quot;). Even co-opt them into doing something the Strix wants or is interested in (&quot;I applaud your persistence and primal majesty. *golf clap* Surely you represent the best hope for... humanity. Let me propose a more meaningful and... challenging prey&quot;). They're also ephemeral creatures and could have substantial influence and contact with the Hisil: mundane or ghoul security becomes much weirder when purposefully left &quot;Open&quot; on a locus....<br /> <br /> &quot;Kill things?&quot; - Not if the things are out of reach. Play for time: redirect them physically (&quot;the elevator goes into freefall, when you come too in its smashed remains the concrete walls of the sub-basement define an intricate maze...&quot;), pause them at dramatic moments (&quot;as you step onto the polished orange floor a massive arc of lightning snaps from the chandelier; your form flows, healing around the burned tissue but the arc holds you twitching in place. As you watch, your target completes his ritual and the loyal servant twists and changes: in moments you recognize and echo on his form--that magath!&quot;). If all else fails, and the strix really likes his elder puppet for its utility, he could dominate a thrall into staking another vampire and himself, then jump into the other vamp and put the elder's body on ice for a while--maybe 20 years or so.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T08:23:26-07:00","id":1115098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115072#post1115072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're also ephemeral creatures and could have substantial influence and contact with the Hisil: mundane or ghoul security becomes much weirder when purposefully left &amp;quot;Open&amp;quot; on a locus....<br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13318\" data-vbnamecard=\"13318\">Cainite</a> If memory serves the vampire book explicitly states that the Strix aren't ephemeral entities; however, the strix do have some notable interaction with other worlds; there is the shadowy strix world that all strix come from, then there is the shadowy realm that can be accessed via Cruac (which could be that realm), and if memory serves strix also have interesting effects on infrastructure. The tengu mentioned in werewolf 2e also have some interaction with werewolves, so I imagine that'd be something to draw on. I'd also think about granting the strix some of the elder devotions in 1000 years of night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:00:25-07:00","id":1115174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115039#post1115039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I want to kill them, but so far nothing I've thrown at them has even posed a challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A quick suggestion: Throw something at them that they're unprepared for and can't kill. Preferably something slow that they can flee from, like an ephemeral with high Resistance and defensive Numina. Then if they want to do something about their enemy they have to research bane and/or ban and defeat it that way.<br /> <br /> And no, Strix aren't ephemerals. They are not made out of ephemera. They use similar but ultimately distinct and separate rules. And it's unreasonably annoying for me that not even the books seems to know that. There's a sidebar mentioning &quot;demonic owls made of smoke with a strange connection to vampires&quot; in the section for ephemeral entities in the core books for Chronicles of Darkness, Demon, Promethean, and Werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:36:53-07:00","id":1115194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115174#post1115174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, Strix aren't ephemerals. They are not made out of ephemera. They use similar but ultimately distinct and separate rules. And it's unreasonably annoying for me that not even the books seems to know that. There's a sidebar mentioning &amp;quot;demonic owls made of smoke with a strange connection to vampires&amp;quot; in the section for ephemeral entities in the core books for Chronicles of Darkness, Demon, Promethean, and Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves, the books are supposed to be somewhat written from that splat's perspective, so said splat's misconceptions about strix is why they get put under ephemeral entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T12:38:06-07:00","id":1115195,"title":"","content":"So, could a vampire have a ghost that formed when they died? And if so, could a Hollow Mekhet have two ephemeral entities gunning for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T13:00:37-07:00","id":1115211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115195#post1115195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, could a vampire have a ghost that formed when they died? And if so, could a Hollow Mekhet have two ephemeral entities gunning for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what a Hollow Mekhet's Ka is. So, yes to the first question, no to the second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:08:23-07:00","id":1115243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115211#post1115211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what a Hollow Mekhet's Ka is. So, yes to the first question, no to the second.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the other clans? Can they have their ghost follow them around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:27:15-07:00","id":1115254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115243#post1115243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about the other clans? Can they have their ghost follow them around?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. Their ghosts would just follow the normal ghost rules instead of the modified ones for Ka.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T18:58:55-07:00","id":1115331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115243#post1115243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the other clans? Can they have their ghost follow them around?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's going to be a whole 'nother can of worms. You are going to need to talk to your ST first about it, because that is going to touch on the entire nature of what ghosts are, what vampires are, and likely a bit more. There's nothing to support it in either case, so its something you're going to need to figure out whole cloth. <br /> <br /> No one is going to stop you, but anyone who does this is going to need some work involved to work it out and all. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T19:07:28-07:00","id":1115335,"title":"","content":"As far as I know only humans have been confirmed to leave ghosts.<br /> However, due to the post humous Embrace it should be possible for a human to leave a ghost behind only to raised as a vampire once the ghost has been created. And it ties into the whole Hollow Mekhet thing as they originally became Hollow due to post-humous Embraces.<br /> Of course, the whole thing hinges on that ghosts are created before it's too late to perform the post-humous Embrace (I can't recall seeing anywhere if ghosts are instantly generated), and that the ghost is disconnected from the body and won't be affected by the Embrace. Or that Fate makes sure that nobody who would be post-humously Embraced is going to leave a ghost at all (potentially unless Hollow).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:47:06-07:00","id":1115385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115331#post1115331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's going to be a whole 'nother can of worms. You are going to need to talk to your ST first about it, because that is going to touch on the entire nature of what ghosts are, what vampires are, and likely a bit more. There's nothing to support it in either case, so its something you're going to need to figure out whole cloth. <br /> <br /> No one is going to stop you, but anyone who does this is going to need some work involved to work it out and all. </div> </div> </div> </div>Generally I'm the one dming vampire games, and while I know I can just design it on my own, I was just wondering if the other clans besides Mekhet did that. Mostly because it might come up in the event that my players begin looking for their own ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:49:11-07:00","id":1115387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115335#post1115335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know only humans have been confirmed to leave ghosts.<br /> However, due to the post humous Embrace it should be possible for a human to leave a ghost behind only to raised as a vampire once the ghost has been created. And it ties into the whole Hollow Mekhet thing as they originally became Hollow due to post-humous Embraces.<br /> Of course, the whole thing hinges on that ghosts are created before it's too late to perform the post-humous Embrace (I can't recall seeing anywhere if ghosts are instantly generated), and that the ghost is disconnected from the body and won't be affected by the Embrace. Or that Fate makes sure that nobody who would be post-humously Embraced is going to leave a ghost at all (potentially unless Hollow).</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I wasn't sure about that because ghosts are a very confusing subject by looking at the rules (at least it is for me). So I figured I'd seek some advice on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:58:15-07:00","id":1115391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115385#post1115385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally I'm the one dming vampire games, and while I know I can just design it on my own, I was just wondering if the other clans besides Mekhet did that. Mostly because it might come up in the event that my players begin looking for their own ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be very rare for other clans to do that, and perhaps more typical ghosts wouldn't spend all their time messing with their vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:15:06-07:00","id":1115394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115391#post1115391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it would be very rare for other clans to do that, and perhaps more typical ghosts wouldn't spend all their time messing with their vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I remembered something about ghosts and Nosferatu from the Nosferatu clan book, but I wasn't sure if that carried over into second edition as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:17:49-07:00","id":1115396,"title":"","content":"In the strix part of the book in 2e, it says Cruac users can use the Gathering Cry to essentially summon strix to their location. What level of ritual should that be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:34:22-07:00","id":1115397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115396#post1115396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the strix part of the book in 2e, it says Cruac users can use the Gathering Cry to essentially summon strix to their location. What level of ritual should that be?</div> </div> </div> </div>The lower the better. Summoning Strix is a bad idea unless you know what you're doing (and if you know what you're doing you wouldn't summon Strix) so I'd say one or two dots just to make it easier for people to make that mistake. Besides, it's not like it forces Strix to arrive. You basically announce that you want them to come to you and hope for the best so one dot seems reasonable from a mechanical standpoint as well.<br /> <br /> On the topic of ghosts: I just remembered that one of the devs for Geist 2E wrote that the Rank of a newly created ghost is dependent on the Integrity rating of the &quot;creator&quot; and that people with Integrity 10 never leaves ghosts at all. It doesn't say anything about whether or not a ghost can be created when someone is Embraced, but it strongly implies that vampires facing a final death won't leave ghosts behind. Just a sidenote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T22:58:20-07:00","id":1115404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115397#post1115397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The lower the better. Summoning Strix is a bad idea unless you know what you're doing (and if you know what you're doing you wouldn't summon Strix) so I'd say one or two dots just to make it easier for people to make that mistake. Besides, it's not like it forces Strix to arrive. You basically announce that you want them to come to you and hope for the best so one dot seems reasonable from a mechanical standpoint as well.<br /> <br /> On the topic of ghosts: I just remembered that one of the devs for Geist 2E wrote that the Rank of a newly created ghost is dependent on the Integrity rating of the &amp;quot;creator&amp;quot; and that people with Integrity 10 never leaves ghosts at all. It doesn't say anything about whether or not a ghost can be created when someone is Embraced, but it strongly implies that vampires facing a final death won't leave ghosts behind. Just a sidenote.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the lower the better for the ritual makes sense.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly not sure about vampires and ghosts to be honest; I only have what 2e currently has and some of the 1e books, and I have found very little to nothing on vampires and ephemeral entities. Are there 1e books that talk about that at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T00:52:28-07:00","id":1115422,"title":"","content":"Not that I know of. Book of the Dead describes how vampires interact with the Underworld, but that's basically it unless I've overlooked something. I can't help but notice that VtR is the only 2E core book without rules for ephemeral entities so I get the impression vampires interact more rarely with ephemerals than the other 2E splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T04:48:33-07:00","id":1115472,"title":"","content":"Does the auspex 2 questions must be provided all at once or the player can wait for every answer prior to going on with the fallowing questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T05:31:25-07:00","id":1115487,"title":"","content":"Up to the table to decide. I prefer the latter since it's less annoying for the player, and the ST doesn't have to remember a bunch of questions while trying to answer them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T06:46:01-07:00","id":1115505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115385#post1115385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally I'm the one dming vampire games, and while I know I can just design it on my own, I was just wondering if the other clans besides Mekhet did that. Mostly because it might come up in the event that my players begin looking for their own ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah. In that case, nope. Hollow Mehket are the only ones who do that, and even then, there's a specific ritual that needs to be followed before it happens, and the so-called ghost is actually just a splinter that takes half the vampire's soul, including their echo and reflection; its not a true ghost, but a literal reflection given ephemeral form. The vampire loses parts of themselves to give this thing form; its not a fully realized independant entity. If the other clans wanted to do something similar, they would need similar costs.<br /> <br /> Lots of people oversimplify this issue, and make assumptions about what ghosts are and are not. Often, on these forums, people incorrectly claim that a ghost is just an ephemeral imprint of a person upon their death. While that is a possible answer, the truth is that there is no definitive answer in the first place. The Hollow are special in that they don't actually make a ghost, but more in that split themselves into more than one body. Vampires leaving ghosts upon their Embrace might very well be something STs may consider impossible, depending on how they view ghosts. <br /> <br /> Until Sin-Eaters comes out, where more information on ghosts might show up, all we can do is leave it up to individual STs. \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115394#post1115394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I remembered something about ghosts and Nosferatu from the Nosferatu clan book, but I wasn't sure if that carried over into second edition as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nosferatu can talk to ghosts, but that's regular ghosts, unassociated with vampires as a whole.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115404#post1115404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the lower the better for the ritual makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div> Check out the Void Cruac style. That's kind of like summoning a strix. Rather than being a specific ritual, could very well just be a side effect of using Cruac as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm honestly not sure about vampires and ghosts to be honest; I only have what 2e currently has and some of the 1e books, and I have found very little to nothing on vampires and ephemeral entities. Are there 1e books that talk about that at all? </div> </div> </div> In general? Vampires don't deal with ephemeral entities. The strix are the closest thing, and even then, they're not true ephemeals. The focus of vampires is on the living and other vampire types, and often ignore any special worlds or critters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T11:35:12-07:00","id":1115612,"title":"","content":"A Daeva uses Majesty 2: Confidant on a person, and gets an exceptional success, so the Charmed condition lasts for several nights. That same night the Daeva is possessed by a Strix. Does the Charmed condition end, or is it &quot;transferred&quot;?<br /> <br /> Also, would the answer be the same if the Daeva went into &quot;temporary&quot; Torpor, full lethal damage for a few hours?<br /> <br /> Would the charmed person seeing either of these events happen have any effect on your answer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T15:44:39-07:00","id":1115704,"title":"","content":"I'd say it wears off in all circumstances because the persona who enacted the effect in question is no longer conscious in order to maintain the effects. Whether or not the victim sees their violator get possessed or beaten into torpor has no bearing on it. Granted they should react appropriately to the condition on them but no, a strix deciding to possess someone is not suddenly immune to retaliation from a strix hunter their new meat puppet charmed a few nights ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T18:55:19-07:00","id":1115752,"title":"","content":"On the flip side, nothing about the power indicates it's a sustained effort on the part of the vampire. Instead, it seems to be all in the victim's head after the initial use of the power.<br /> <br /> I'd say it sticks around. If the victim is unaware of any possession, the Strix may benefit from it as the victim believes they're the same person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T20:58:45-07:00","id":1116229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1115752#post1115752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the flip side, nothing about the power indicates it's a sustained effort on the part of the vampire. Instead, it seems to be all in the victim's head after the initial use of the power.<br /> <br /> I'd say it sticks around. If the victim is unaware of any possession, the Strix may benefit from it as the victim believes they're the same person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, it's not sustained. It was something done one time that lasts days. Like a burn, it happened, and it lingers, taking days to fully go away. <br /> <br /> I would say that neither torpor nor getting possessed break it. If the strix can convince the charmed person they are the vampire, then that's all it takes.<br /> <br /> However if the strix dramaticly failed on convincing the charmed person that they are the vampire, then I would let Them think something is fishy at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T23:37:58-07:00","id":1117107,"title":"","content":"Am I understanding it correctly that it's pretty much impossible to notice something hidden by Obfuscate unless you have Auspex?<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 2: Touch of Shadow:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;...if he masks a desk, people subconsciously register that it\u2019s there and won\u2019t bump in to it, but they can\u2019t recognize what\u2019s right in front of them unless the vampire forces them to interact with it.&quot; </div> </div> </div>But then it says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;In order to notice the occluded object, observers must succeed at a reflexive Wits + Composure penalized by the vampire\u2019s Obfuscate dots.&quot; </div> </div> </div>So, does that mean that when forced to come into contact with a hidden object you can roll to notice it, or can you try to notice it even without bumping into it?<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 3: Cloak of Night:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;...he vanishes entirely. He leaves no scent and makes no sound, though his passing leaves incidental signs, like drifting smoke or creaking floorboards.... Used with Cloak of Night, Touch of Shadow can now affect other people. The normal rules for piercing Touch of Shadow apply..... Only the struck victim can perceive the vampire.... The vampire can be tracked by indirect clues, as mentioned above.... rolling Wits + Resolve - Obfuscate.&quot; </div> </div> </div>So wait a minute. It basically says that you are impossible to detect by others, only the person you attack. But then it says you can be tracked really easily by a Perception roll? What if you are in a concrete floored room with no smoke, does that mean tracking would be impossible? Would there need to be some obvious sign to even make the attempt?<br /> <br /> A scenario if you will:<br /> Someone is intruding a Vampire Haven. Vampire has strapped the entrances full of Obfuscated Claymore mines with tripwires. It would be impossible for anyone to detect the traps without Auspex until it all goes boom?<br /> <br /> Also, expecting an imminent attack, the Vamp has Obfuscated several of his Ghouls armed with machine guns. Anyone walking in would never be able to see them until they all open fire and make mincemeat out of them? Surprise round with several sets of M4 Autofire would kill most things with no chance to react.<br /> <br /> Also, a Werewolf can do a Lashing Out (or the equivalent) with Hunter's Aspect, right? To shatter the Obfuscate of and attacking Vamp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 07-17-2017, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T03:47:14-07:00","id":1117135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, does that mean that when forced to come into contact with a hidden object you can roll to notice it, or can you try to notice it even without bumping into it? </div> </div> </div>Yes, you roll when you bump into it. When forced to interact. This is at least my interpretation of RAI. Onyx path might be really good at making a good setting, rules however are a bit clumsy at times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So wait a minute. It basically says that you are impossible to detect by others, only the person you attack. But then it says you can be tracked really easily by a Perception roll? What if you are in a concrete floored room with no smoke, does that mean tracking would be impossible? Would there need to be some obvious sign to even make the attempt? </div> </div> </div>Like every other thing, there must be a reason to roll. If you have no reason to be able to make a roll, you don't get to roll. There must be some way to &quot;track&quot; the obfuscated &quot;invisible&quot; vampire, cracking floorboards, a hole in a moving crowd, swirling fog or smoke, rings on the water or walking through a metal detector could be reasons to roll. Standing still in a empty white room is not a reason however.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Someone is intruding a Vampire Haven. Vampire has strapped the entrances full of Obfuscated Claymore mines with tripwires. It would be impossible for anyone to detect the traps without Auspex until it all goes boom? </div> </div> </div>Unless they are making a change in the environment then no, you don't get to roll. If its a lot of dust on the floor and there is a noticeable lack of dust under the invisible mines, you get a roll. However, unless you actually succeeded on that roll, you wouldn't notice the lack of dust really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, expecting an imminent attack, the Vamp has Obfuscated several of his Ghouls armed with machine guns. Anyone walking in would never be able to see them until they all open fire and make mincemeat out of them? Surprise round with several sets of M4 Autofire would kill most things with no chance to react. </div> </div> </div>Yes this is true as well. Only if they again make some noise, like chitchatting with each other, moving around or doing stuff that might leave things to track would you get a roll to notice them, however you better succeed fully in the first turn because otherwise you're fucked. Like for instance if said victim walked into a room with 4 invisible ghouls with machine-guns ready to shoot, the victim would probably die from 4 surprise attacks from machine-guns. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, a Werewolf can do a Lashing Out (or the equivalent) with Hunter's Aspect, right? To shatter the Obfuscate of and attacking Vamp. </div> </div> </div>Yes they could use their aura in an aura vs aura contest and if they win the obfuscate shatters. However, you still need to find the bloodsucker to &quot;aim&quot; at him.<br /> I'n not that well read on werewolf so i dont know what gift that would equal to auspex in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T16:02:22-07:00","id":1117979,"title":"","content":"On the subject of Obfuscate would the Extra Sense Predatory Aspect be able to Clash of Wills it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T16:10:15-07:00","id":1117982,"title":"","content":"No, it gets fooled like hearing, smelling or seeing. Obfuscate gets you be erasing you subconsciously, not being invisible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T16:22:33-07:00","id":1117991,"title":"","content":"But it doesn't hide indirect evidence like creaking floor boards and Extra Sense lists tremor sense as a posable ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T16:27:26-07:00","id":1117993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1117991#post1117991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it doesn't hide indirect evidence like creaking floor boards and Extra Sense lists tremor sense as a posable ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> if you have that, then it gives a reason to track the obfuscated vampire by indirect clues. Which would be an extended wits+ resolve + kindred senses - obfuscate and needs successes equal to the obfuscated vampires wits + stealth + obfuscate. If sucessful, you could lash out and reveal the vampire. However this is not a Clash of Will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T18:38:05-07:00","id":1118020,"title":"","content":"So, can Auspex reveal the location of ephemeral entities on its own, or what a devotion be needed for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T02:08:58-07:00","id":1118112,"title":"","content":"Im not completely sure about the auspex and ephemeral beings thing. It can pick up vampires in astral projection, which are mentally projected in Twilight. However I don't think vampires could pick up other things in Twilight, it doesn't really fit the vampire setting, they aren't know for hanging around with ghosts and spirits. If they could perceive them easily i guess they would be a bigger deal. <br /> But then again, you could make an argument about it working if asking the right question.<br /> <br /> In my take, you would need a Devotion to see ephemeral beings. Maybe just an Auspex Devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T03:14:04-07:00","id":1118120,"title":"","content":"With Auspex 1 you can ask: is there any enthity concealed from my sight? <br /> It is legit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T03:49:14-07:00","id":1118125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1118112#post1118112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im not completely sure about the auspex and ephemeral beings thing. It can pick up vampires in astral projection, which are mentally projected in Twilight. However I don't think vampires could pick up other things in Twilight, it doesn't really fit the vampire setting, they aren't know for hanging around with ghosts and spirits. If they could perceive them easily i guess they would be a bigger deal. <br /> But then again, you could make an argument about it working if asking the right question.<br /> <br /> In my take, you would need a Devotion to see ephemeral beings. Maybe just an Auspex Devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't usually deal with ephemerals, but that is not to say that vampiric powers won't have an effect on them. With the right question Auspex should definitely reveal that there are beings in Twilight around. You can always houserule it if you don't like it, but that would definitely be an artificial limitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T06:01:59-07:00","id":1118141,"title":"","content":"I personally allow Auspex 1 to give you a glimpse of them with the right question, but say you'd need a devotion (or a conversion of a 1e discipline like blood tenebrous) to keep the perception active for a full scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T07:53:09-07:00","id":1118167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1118125#post1118125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires don't usually deal with ephemerals, but that is not to say that vampiric powers won't have an effect on them. With the right question Auspex should definitely reveal that there are beings in Twilight around. You can always houserule it if you don't like it, but that would definitely be an artificial limitation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I think we're on the same page, i had a brainfart. Got a bit mixed up in words and meaning.<br /> But, I do agree that you could perceive ephemeral beings if asked the right question, like &quot;is there any being hidden from sight in here&quot; or the like. What I don't think Auspex 1 can do however is to give you some form of &quot;sight&quot; that makes you able to &quot;see&quot; them, just perceive a form of invisible presence.<br /> Like i guess the auspex user would get a feeling and perceive something with his sixth sense, not get a visual description of the beings form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T10:57:46-07:00","id":1118216,"title":"","content":"I would say that you wouldn't perceive them in any case.<br /> <br /> You could ask &quot;are there any ephemeral creatures here?&quot; and you would get a vision that's a glorified &quot;yes.&quot; Remember that Auspex is question-and-answer (with the answers generally being visions). It wouldn't actually reveal creatures that the vampire is physically incapable of seeing: creatures in Twilight or across the Gauntlet, for example.<br /> <br /> If someone is hiding under a bed and Auspex tells you someone is hiding here, it doesn't let you see through the bed to physically see them hiding there. It just lets you know they're hiding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T13:06:48-07:00","id":1118254,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly asking because I'm running a game for an Ordo Dracul coterie, and we have two Mekhet. I was thinking about making it an auspex devotion to let then see ephemeral entities, like the Khaibit bloodline has, but I didn't want an xp tax on something they could already do with auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T16:34:28-07:00","id":1118305,"title":"","content":"Auspex 5 doesn't even allow seeing or interacting with ephemeral entities even though a character essential becomes an ephemeral entity in a way. Auspex shouldn't allow for anything more than detecting the presence of ephemeral entities by itself, and even that would be questionable, but I would allow it. The Ordo Dracul should have plenty of knowledge about summoning, exorcism, abjuration, warding and binding. Allowing those abilities along with Auspex detecting whether or not an ephemeral entity is nearby should do the job. I don't think seeing an ephemeral entity would be useful without an ability to do anything to the entity which is why the Khaibit can see them. Force a manifestation so you can deal with the entity and then you can see them fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 07-19-2017, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T23:00:31-07:00","id":1118844,"title":"","content":"i been doing some research while reading first edition corebook.<br /> Is it me, or the vampires of VtR (in comparation to VtM), are COMPLETELY AND UTTERLY EVIL? so far i dont see any semblance of &quot;Humanity&quot; on them (i see them less of a Tragic Figures and more of well..Real Fucking Monsters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T23:33:40-07:00","id":1118851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1118844#post1118844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i been doing some research while reading first edition corebook.<br /> Is it me, or the vampires of VtR (in comparation to VtM), are COMPLETELY AND UTTERLY EVIL? so far i dont see any semblance of &quot;Humanity&quot; on them (i see them less of a Tragic Figures and more of well..Real Fucking Monsters)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not bright on 1E stuff in general myself, but any point where you particularly thought so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:06:41-07:00","id":1118911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1118844#post1118844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i been doing some research while reading first edition corebook.<br /> Is it me, or the vampires of VtR (in comparation to VtM), are COMPLETELY AND UTTERLY EVIL? so far i dont see any semblance of &quot;Humanity&quot; on them (i see them less of a Tragic Figures and more of well..Real Fucking Monsters)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:32:50-07:00","id":1118917,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not seeing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:34:33-07:00","id":1118920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1118844#post1118844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i been doing some research while reading first edition corebook.<br /> Is it me, or the vampires of VtR (in comparation to VtM), are COMPLETELY AND UTTERLY EVIL? so far i dont see any semblance of &amp;quot;Humanity&amp;quot; on them (i see them less of a Tragic Figures and more of well..Real Fucking Monsters)</div> </div> </div> </div>Read Loki's portrayal in Three Shades of Night","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T05:46:35-07:00","id":1118927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1118844#post1118844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i been doing some research while reading first edition corebook.<br /> Is it me, or the vampires of VtR (in comparation to VtM), are COMPLETELY AND UTTERLY EVIL? so far i dont see any semblance of &quot;Humanity&quot; on them (i see them less of a Tragic Figures and more of well..Real Fucking Monsters)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, no I don't follow you here. How are V:tR vampires evil? Especiallycompared to V:tM where everything was evil for the lulz ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T09:24:23-07:00","id":1118991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1118844#post1118844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i been doing some research while reading first edition corebook.<br /> Is it me, or the vampires of VtR (in comparation to VtM), are COMPLETELY AND UTTERLY EVIL? so far i dont see any semblance of &quot;Humanity&quot; on them (i see them less of a Tragic Figures and more of well..Real Fucking Monsters)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have read over the first and second edition stuff and I don't see them like that at all. I am not entirely sure what you are reading that made you get to that conclusion.<br /> <br /> Vampires certainly CAN be real fucking monsters. But you dont HAVE to be one. You can play their personalities however you'd like. No where in the book does it say they have to be slobbering monsters foaming at the maw. They can be anything from Anne Rice's Louis or Lestat to Dracula Untold to John Carpenter's Vampires to What we do in the Shadows....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T10:19:46-07:00","id":1119020,"title":"","content":"I mean, in 1e they're beholden to the same karma meter as mortals. I hate to think what he'd make of 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T09:50:29-07:00","id":1119272,"title":"","content":"Quick Question about Obfuscate 4. <br /> Can i use Obfuscate 4 to take the looks of a person that i know it exists but i havent seen his face?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T13:20:59-07:00","id":1119331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Montgomery Crobes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1119272#post1119272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick Question about Obfuscate 4.<br /> Can i use Obfuscate 4 to take the looks of a person that i know it exists but i havent seen his face?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. You can even take the appearance of someone that neither you nor the observer has seen. If you take the appearance of a roommate's estranged parent then the roommate imagines what the parent looks like and that is the appearance they see. It could be 6 different appearances to 6 different people and each's memories would reconcile the conflict as a fuzzy memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T21:39:34-07:00","id":1121184,"title":"","content":"Are Methuselahs in the 1000 years of night book supposed to be the vampire equivalent of archmages and beast incarnates, or is it just a term being used for really old vampires. I was really confused because it said something about then being as powerful when they woke up as they went to sleep, but otherwise there was nothing describing what a Methuselah actually is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T23:25:43-07:00","id":1121206,"title":"","content":"No, they are normal vampire with no particular mechanics or ability and even no so powerful. So that it let me a little disappointed.<br /> Also the devotions are not so epic. In the core book there are devotions far more powerful (see Juggernaut Gait, force of Nature...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-27-2017, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:13:41-07:00","id":1121527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1121206#post1121206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they are normal vampire with no particular mechanics or ability and even no so powerful. So that it let me a little disappointed.<br /> Also the devotions are not so epic. In the core book there are devotions far more powerful (see Juggernaut Gait, force of Nature...)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a little dissapointing then. I did like some of the devotions; they were pretty neat when I first looked at them. That Annals of Death one was pretty neat, and the telekinesis devotion was also pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:28:58-07:00","id":1121542,"title":"","content":"Methusalha is basically just a title for social influence. Which, being vampire is a social game, makes sense. There's no real mechanics behind it, though. This is more like achieving &quot;Hell&quot; in Demon - just a point in time when you get to hang up the spy racket instead of a time when you become something more/less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T16:22:08-07:00","id":1121607,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling there IS more behind it than what the elder book told us. It hinted at Methuselahs having unique abilities and such, just didn't show any of it off. As it is, I plan to just use the template for them that I threw together, if/when I introduce one in my current chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T17:01:56-07:00","id":1121622,"title":"","content":"I thought the idea was that they didn't lose blood potency in torpor or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T20:20:58-07:00","id":1121681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1121607#post1121607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling there IS more behind it than what the elder book told us. It hinted at Methuselahs having unique abilities and such, just didn't show any of it off. As it is, I plan to just use the template for them that I threw together, if/when I introduce one in my current chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the book referred to elder Devotions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T22:54:05-07:00","id":1121727,"title":"","content":"I agree. Also in the 1ed there was devotions linked to BP like dark decree if I'm not wrong. I expected something more honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T04:34:26-07:00","id":1121784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1121681#post1121681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the book referred to elder Devotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The long years and their thickening blood have allowed these<br /> ancients to master many abilities, studying Disciplines and<br /> sorcery that most elder Kindred can only begin to learn before<br /> they succumb to sleep, or fall at the hands of their enemies.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's what I mean. If it just means they learn a few elder devotions that'd be rather disappointing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T05:53:28-07:00","id":1121795,"title":"","content":"Ghoul Families, <sup>are like magnets</sup> How do they work? Can a member of a ghoul family learn Disciplines without having tasted Vitae? What if the 'parent clan' is Mekhet, and they use only the 'free' applications of said Disciplines (first dot of Obfuscate, first dot of Auspex with limit of one use per scene, the 'passive' benefit of Celerity)? Would they be required to spend more Experiences to learn them without the benefits of The Blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","name":"Redline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T08:40:46-07:00","id":1121876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1121784#post1121784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;The long years and their thickening blood have allowed these<br /> ancients to master many abilities, studying Disciplines and<br /> sorcery that most elder Kindred can only begin to learn before<br /> they succumb to sleep, or fall at the hands of their enemies.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's what I mean. If it just means they learn a few elder devotions that'd be rather disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, reads just like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Learning Elder Devotions in Play</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In game terms, the concept of elders learning Devotions more slowly than in their younger nights is represented by higher Experience costs for Devotions with higher Discipline dot requirements. To some extent, this is only as true as a given game table makes it, depending on the frequency with which the players earn Beats and how they decide to spend their Experiences. But, the idea is still the same: elder Devotions should feel unique and unsettling, and learning one should be a notable moment for a character.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 07-28-2017, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:00:16-07:00","id":1121888,"title":"","content":"I personally wouldn't allow a ghoul family member to develop a discipline unless they have come into contact with vitae.<br /> Yes, I would require them to spend experience to develop a discipline. <br /> Any ghoul can use the passive powers of the disciplines that don't require vitae expenditure. The thing that makes ghoul families special is that their aging slows considerably and they can use the disciplines they know even when there is no vitae in their bodies and they haven't had vitae in a while. Regular ghouls can't use their powers if they haven't gotten their monthly hit, even if they have a point or two of vitae in them currently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T14:37:59-07:00","id":1122056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1121888#post1121888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally wouldn't allow a ghoul family member to develop a discipline unless they have come into contact with vitae.<br /> Yes, I would require them to spend experience to develop a discipline.<br /> Any ghoul can use the passive powers of the disciplines that don't require vitae expenditure. The thing that makes ghoul families special is that their aging slows considerably and <b>they can use the disciplines they know even when there is no vitae in their bodies and they haven't had vitae in a while</b>. Regular ghouls can't use their powers if they haven't gotten their monthly hit, even if they have a point or two of vitae in them currently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Ghoul families get the passive benefits even when &quot;dry&quot;? Please cite (1e) passage--this is interesting... and I've just re-read Ghouls without finding the reference.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T14:44:40-07:00","id":1122062,"title":"","content":"I don't know if that's accurate but the first dot of most Disciplines doesn't require you to spend any Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T15:58:41-07:00","id":1122108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1122056#post1122056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what? Ghoul families get the passive benefits even when &quot;dry&quot;? Please cite (1e) passage--this is interesting... and I've just re-read Ghouls without finding the reference.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a benefit of ghoul families in 2nd edition, not first edition.<br /> <br /> A group of Night Doctors studying ghoul behavior in Shanghai say that Vitae behaves strangely in the bodies of ghoul family members, giving them abilities unlike those of normal ghouls. They can retain the Disciplines and other qualities of their regnant\u2019s blood even after the last of it is spent. (Blood and Smoke p. 296)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T16:26:26-07:00","id":1122123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1122108#post1122108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a benefit of ghoul families in 2nd edition, not first edition.<br /> <br /> A group of Night Doctors studying ghoul behavior in Shanghai say that Vitae behaves strangely in the bodies of ghoul family members, giving them abilities unlike those of normal ghouls. They can retain the Disciplines and other qualities of their regnant\u2019s blood even after the last of it is spent. (Blood and Smoke p. 296)</div> </div> </div> </div>Really now? Oh, that gives me so many ideas. I am super excited for the ghoul book now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T20:46:00-07:00","id":1122194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1122123#post1122123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really now? Oh, that gives me so many ideas. I am super excited for the ghoul book now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise! And I need to revise my homebrew placeholder....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T14:07:33-07:00","id":1122803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1122108#post1122108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a benefit of ghoul families in 2nd edition, not first edition.<br /> <br /> A group of Night Doctors studying ghoul behavior in Shanghai say that Vitae behaves strangely in the bodies of ghoul family members, giving them abilities unlike those of normal ghouls. They can retain the Disciplines and other qualities of their regnant\u2019s blood even after the last of it is spent. (Blood and Smoke p. 296)</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It's the sentence directly after that one which intrigues me.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">It\u2019s even possible that some members of such family lines can pass down these </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">gifts to their offspring, without any Kindred involvement at all.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Also, I should have clarified. When I asked whether ghoul family members should pay more Experiences for Disciplines <b>if they have no regnant</b>, I meant <i>more than a vampire would pay.</i></span></span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","user":"Redline","date":". 07-30-2017, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/550-redline","name":"Redline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T14:34:22-07:00","id":1122808,"title":"","content":"No, they have to pay the same base experience cost that their regnant would pay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T00:16:26-07:00","id":1122936,"title":"","content":"im still reading up on VtR (recently ordered second ed through drivethroughrpg), as i read it im working on my setting game. i got a question about old vampires, im currently working on a vampire from the north american civil war (who happends to be a sheriff). but as i read the book i wonder more about the rules on elder vampires, how potent would this character's blood be. and if being older he must decide to go to torpor every once on a while or can he lie down in peace for a bit? to explain to me please how being an old vampire works","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T00:30:23-07:00","id":1122937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1122936#post1122936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">im still reading up on VtR (recently ordered second ed through drivethroughrpg), as i read it im working on my setting game. i got a question about old vampires, im currently working on a vampire from the north american civil war (who happends to be a sheriff). but as i read the book i wonder more about the rules on elder vampires, how potent would this character's blood be. and if being older he must decide to go to torpor every once on a while or can he lie down in peace for a bit? to explain to me please how being an old vampire works</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood potency is at least 1 + 1 more per each 50 years active. So your vampire could have as much as blood potency 4 (say embraced in 1865, +1 BP in 1915, +2 in 1965, and +3 in 2015). Blood potency can be increased further with experience (5 experiences per bp) and diablerie.<br /> <br /> Torpor is not <i>required</i> when your blood potency reaches 6. However, it may be desirable if you have no way to feed. There are several ways to feed outlined in the core rules (the ability to feed on other supernaturals, an Invictus merit that allows a vampire to accept tithes of blood from Kindred in their territory, and an Ordo Dracul scale that enables vampires to feed on specific mortals as if the vampire's blood potency were lower)<br /> <br /> Beyond that I'm not sure what you're asking when you ask &quot;how being an old vampire works.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's a thread discussing how BP 6+ elders might deal with feeding requirements: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/698414-logistics-of-blood-potency-6\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...lood-potency-6</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 07-31-2017, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T03:59:55-07:00","id":1122959,"title":"","content":"Also there's like, an entire book on elder vampires now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T05:15:38-07:00","id":1122977,"title":"","content":"Yeah, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/214130/Thousand-Years-of-Night\" target=\"_blank\">Thousand Years of Night</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:29:44-07:00","id":1123661,"title":"","content":"Is there a book with information on the clans other then the clan books, I didn't find the fiction very informative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:44:58-07:00","id":1123669,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of information scattered across many books, obviously starting with the core. The bloodline books expand upon the clans within the context of their bloodlines.<br /> <br /> What kind of information are you looking for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:52:53-07:00","id":1123671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1123669#post1123669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of information scattered across many books, obviously starting with the core. The bloodline books expand upon the clans within the context of their bloodlines.<br /> <br /> What kind of information are you looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>General information like whether they're beasts are different, how they structure themselves in society, and what makes them different to other vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:07:55-07:00","id":1123677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1123671#post1123671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General information like whether they're beasts are different, how they structure themselves in society, and what makes them different to other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay the clan books are really best for that.<br /> <br /> Alternatives are <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/88846/The-Danse-Macabre\" target=\"_blank\">the Danse Macabre</a>, which has a good amount of information on each clan and what they're like at different tiers of play, its probably one of the best. <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1441/Coteries?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Coteries</a> and <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1590/Nomads?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Nomads</a> has information on what they're like socially, individually and with others.<br /> <br /> Obviously the core books have the information everything else grows from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:42:45-07:00","id":1123698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1123677#post1123677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay the clan books are really best for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's worrying, those books didn't seem to have any info in them....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatives are <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/88846/The-Danse-Macabre\" target=\"_blank\">the Danse Macabre</a>, which has a good amount of information on each clan and what they're like at different tiers of play, its probably one of the best. <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1441/Coteries?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Coteries</a> and <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1590/Nomads?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Nomads</a> has information on what they're like socially, individually and with others. </div> </div> </div>I'll give those books a look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T18:51:42-07:00","id":1123735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1123698#post1123698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's worrying, those books didn't seem to have any info in them....</div> </div> </div> </div>They have tons of info in them, it's just conveyed in epistolary style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T00:42:12-07:00","id":1124649,"title":"","content":"If a strix possesses the corpse of a kindred (or a kindred), does he has access to the kindred's disciplines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T01:28:25-07:00","id":1124657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1124649#post1124649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a strix possesses the corpse of a kindred (or a kindred), does he has access to the kindred's disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe it is stated in the book that if the Strix possesses a kindred then they have access to their disciplines. However, I don't think that they get to use the Kindred's disciplines if they are possessing that Kindred's dead-er body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T02:52:52-07:00","id":1124673,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's detailed in the embodiments section. They can use their hosts disciplines (with a penalty to the roll if they've only been possessing them for a short time) but not their coils, oaths or blood sorcery. Strix can <i>use</i> Cruac, bur they have to bring their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T11:50:04-07:00","id":1132730,"title":"","content":"Nightmare 4: It states that it affect every sense, so also the tact<br /> <br /> The hallucination of a wall will stop someone trying to pass trough?<br /> When someone fall trough such wall does it resolve the hallucination or she still would see the wall?<br /> If I create the hallucination of a wall can I hide behind? If not How could I justify this to a player trying to do it?<br /> <br /> The hallucination to be on fire will procure pain? How long does it will last?<br /> <br /> So what are the conditions to resolve the hallucination?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-22-2017, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T11:13:14-07:00","id":1133090,"title":"","content":"YMMV, but here is my take on it Marcus:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1132730#post1132730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hallucination of a wall will stop someone trying to pass trough?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe so:<br /> 1) The hallucination is not actually there. Even if the character can &quot;feel&quot; it by trying to touch it, the hand would still move through it;<br /> 2) The book states &quot;... though no matter how awful the hallucinations can\u2019t cause actual harm or inflict significant pain.&quot; (p. 136). If a character tries to bash through the door, the character will not suffer harm or significant pain.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER<br /> <br /> The hallucination is <b>nightmarish</b>. This is important to remember. You don't just end up in a room with no doors in a nightmare: you are buried alive, for example. One could punch through the &quot;wall&quot;, but dirt and earth would start coming from the hole. Or water. Or blood. Or maybe the door is not there because it turned into a huge maw with glass teeth. Sure, you can try going through it, lol. So there are other ways to prevent the target of the hallucination from passing through a door affected with Waking Nighmare.<br /> <br /> With that in mind:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1132730#post1132730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When someone fall trough such wall does it resolve the hallucination or she still would see the wall?</div> </div> </div> </div> and <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1132730#post1132730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what are the conditions to resolve the hallucination?</div> </div> </div> </div>The hallucination lasts for a scene. There is no resolution stated. I don't think it would follow the logic common in other games where one &quot;disbelieves&quot; an illusion, since there is nothing like that in the book. Since it just lasts for a scene with no stated resolution, I say one cannot escape the nightmare aside from physically escaping it (i.e. skedaddling the hell out of there). So punch/fall all you want - you can't really fight the nightmare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1132730#post1132730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I create the hallucination of a wall can I hide behind? If not How could I justify this to a player trying to do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but keep in mind that the perceptions could vary from victim to victim, so the wall in question, being nightmarish and all, might not be straight, or even euclidean. One could have trouble with that. Also, it is inescapably nightmarish - this defeats the attempts at stealth in a fair number of circumstances. For example, if you are trying to set up a hiding stop to eavesdrop on some secret negotiations, the parties coming to negotiate are not going to appreciate having <i>a wall with goat eyes stare at them</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1132730#post1132730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hallucination to be on fire will procure pain? How long does it will last?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but not significant pain (see above). The pain shouldn't last longer than the effects of Waking Nightmare. One could even argue that physically leaving the nightmarish fire ends the pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14844-chubby-russian","name":"Chubby Russian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T13:11:10-07:00","id":1133132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chubby Russian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1133090#post1133090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">YMMV, but here is my take on it Marcus:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't believe so:<br /> 1) The hallucination is not actually there. Even if the character can &amp;quot;feel&amp;quot; it by trying to touch it, the hand would still move through it;<br /> 2) The book states &amp;quot;... though no matter how awful the hallucinations can\u2019t cause actual harm or inflict significant pain.&amp;quot; (p. 136). If a character tries to bash through the door, the character will not suffer harm or significant pain.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER<br /> <br /> The hallucination is <b>nightmarish</b>. This is important to remember. You don't just end up in a room with no doors in a nightmare: you are buried alive, for example. One could punch through the &amp;quot;wall&amp;quot;, but dirt and earth would start coming from the hole. Or water. Or blood. Or maybe the door is not there because it turned into a huge maw with glass teeth. Sure, you can try going through it, lol. So there are other ways to prevent the target of the hallucination from passing through a door affected with Waking Nighmare.<br /> <br /> With that in mind:<br /> <br /> and <br /> <br /> The hallucination lasts for a scene. There is no resolution stated. I don't think it would follow the logic common in other games where one &amp;quot;disbelieves&amp;quot; an illusion, since there is nothing like that in the book. Since it just lasts for a scene with no stated resolution, I say one cannot escape the nightmare aside from physically escaping it (i.e. skedaddling the hell out of there). So punch/fall all you want - you can't really fight the nightmare.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, but keep in mind that the perceptions could vary from victim to victim, so the wall in question, being nightmarish and all, might not be straight, or even euclidean. One could have trouble with that. Also, it is inescapably nightmarish - this defeats the attempts at stealth in a fair number of circumstances. For example, if you are trying to set up a hiding stop to eavesdrop on some secret negotiations, the parties coming to negotiate are not going to appreciate having <i>a wall with goat eyes stare at them</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, but not significant pain (see above). The pain shouldn't last longer than the effects of Waking Nightmare. One could even argue that physically leaving the nightmarish fire ends the pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many thanks. The only thing that still let me doubtful is the ability to conceal yourself behind an hallucination (nightmarish wall/door wathever) but I can handle it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T10:09:09-07:00","id":1136955,"title":"","content":"Once you have committed Diablerie is it permanent visible on your aura?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T11:22:02-07:00","id":1136973,"title":"","content":"That's up to the storyteller. Diablerie detection is most likely not going to be based on aura reading but a Mekhet successfully consulting a psychic entity using an unresistible power that provides correct answers via telepathic projection with no explicit statute of limitation or restrictions as to what kind of question can be asked. Has this person ever committed diablerie? If the person did the act at one point, the answer is going to be &quot;yes&quot;. But if you want to get technical (as in actual aura reading) the psychic residue of the person the diablerist destroyed only remains until the Tainted Condition is resolved. (As determined by time passage based on the victim's blood potency or how much aggravated damage the diablerist sustains.) Whether or not the ST wants to say the Mekhet's Beast detects the information based only on the current state of the person in question is up to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-03-2017, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T13:17:03-07:00","id":1137006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1136973#post1136973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you want to get technical (as in actual aura reading) the psychic residue of the person the diablerist destroyed only remains until the Tainted Condition is resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. This is mixing 1e and 2e. The diablerie streaks in the aura in 1e and the Tainted Condition in 2e both disappear over time, so the two are similar but they are not the same thing. Second edition doesn't state whether or not diablerie is at all visible in the vampire's aura, but that's because aura reading isn't much of a thing in vampire anymore. Auspex works differently, and the rules states that asking if someone is a diablerist is a valid question. As long as the vampire can be considered a diablerist it'll be possible for Auspex users to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:38:30-07:00","id":1137076,"title":"","content":"I didn't say anything about diablerie streaks. In fact I deliberately did not use that terminology even though the second edition book does describe diablerie as stains on one's aura. So you're the one confusing editions. And yes really it does work exactly as I described it. Aura reading is STILL a thing in 2nd edition. Not only do kindred see each other's auras, they even get the ability to fling portions of their own auras onto others. And there's also a psychic power in 2nd edition where the user gets to distinguish different colors to pick up on moods and certain supernatural effects just like in first edition. And since Dragons can get mortal only psychic powers, they can read auras in the same manner as 1st edition too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:50:22-07:00","id":1137081,"title":"","content":"here is the tainted condition that the book describes, The highlighted portion is what you are all talking about. By my reading of the Condition it would fade when the condition ends. This is why, The Traces of the victims soul is what causes the tainted condition and that condition is not permanent. The traces would fade with the condition and the condition fades after 1 month per Blood Potency of the Victim. However I do agree that it is a ST call as to how they would like it to happen in their chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your character committed diablerie, and <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>now retains traces<br /> of her victim\u2019s soul</b></span>. Once per chapter, the victim can come back<br /> to haunt your character and try to force her destruction. This<br /> brief burst penalizes any one dice pool by the victim\u2019s Blood<br /> Potency dots, or adds to a dice pool opposing your character.<br /> This takes the form of subtle manifestations, or whispers that<br /> urge and distract. Your character may have multiple instances<br /> of this Condition, reflecting different victims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:50:32-07:00","id":1137082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1137076#post1137076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say anything about diablerie streaks. In fact I deliberately did not use that terminology even though the second edition book does describe diablerie as stains on one's aura. So you're the one confusing editions. And yes really it does work exactly as I described it. Aura reading is STILL a thing in 2nd edition. Not only do kindred see each other's auras, they even get the ability to fling portions of their own auras onto others. And there's also a psychic power in 2nd edition where the user gets to distinguish different colors to pick up on moods and certain supernatural effects just like in first edition. And since Dragons can get mortal only psychic powers, they can read auras in the same manner as 1st edition too.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Auras, I'm not entirely sure that Kindred see each other's auras in 2e. I don't really remember that being anywhere under Predatory Aura. I thought they feel what it's like more than see what it looks like.<br /> <br /> Also, the only aura reading I can think of is the Auspex question: &quot;Is this creature a supernatural entity.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, I think Coil of Zirnitra is supposed to be a rare coil. I don't think I'll be letting that much of a game changer being something any Ordo Dracul can just start out with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T15:59:45-07:00","id":1137088,"title":"","content":"I did misread tsusasi a bit, but I want to point out that I said aura reading isn't <i>much</i> of a thing since the updated Auspex did away with aura reading and the Aura Reading Merit is generally off limits. I also want to point out that the Predatory Aura and the psychic aura that aura reading refers to are two unrelated concepts. The Predatory Aura does not show different colours, patterns or intensities depending on mood, spiritual health or state of being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T11:45:04-07:00","id":1138951,"title":"","content":"Can you create your own Coils ?<br /> <br /> I've got an idea for a coil that has a kindred bind machines into them. So for example replacing your arm with a prosthetic one. Then using their blood to take command of it making it work better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T11:55:43-07:00","id":1138955,"title":"","content":"Well, you've gotta be able to. They didn't just come out of thin air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T13:01:23-07:00","id":1138972,"title":"","content":"The book even says that creating a new Coil can be a good chronicle hook. We kinda do that during downtime, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T03:46:17-07:00","id":1139399,"title":"","content":"Are there any limitations against a player purchasing Humanity dots? If they have the XP to spend can they buy back as many Humanity dots as they like? Can they buy multiple dots at a time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T04:10:08-07:00","id":1139406,"title":"","content":"Well, similar to buying other traits you should have an ingame reason for buying Humanity. Even if it's not technically forbidden it makes it quite difficult to buy more than one dot of Humanity at a time outside of character creation and time skips.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 09-11-2017, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T05:23:36-07:00","id":1139413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1139399#post1139399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any limitations against a player purchasing Humanity dots? If they have the XP to spend can they buy back as many Humanity dots as they like? Can they buy multiple dots at a time?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's up to your ST. I'd allow it for circumstances like several months or years passing during downtime or something unusual like the Humanity loss taking place while the character is possessed or under the long term control of someone using Majesty or vinculum or Dominate and suddenly they aren't controlled anymore. Or if they get their personality rewritten extensively and the Humanity gain facilitates the new personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T19:53:26-07:00","id":1140068,"title":"","content":"This seems like a silly and potentially non-simple question but it came up and I'm curious on peoples views. I'm imagining the answers are going to be storyteller specific.<br /> <br /> Does petrified wood count as wood for purposes of staking?<br /> <br /> On one hand, it's not wood but in name. Any 'wood' is replaced by minerals, making it effectively a rock. On the other hand, that symbolism might be all that's necessary to count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T05:41:34-07:00","id":1140136,"title":"","content":"For me no. There's no &quot;mystical anti vampire symbolism&quot; in snapping a piece of copper laced quartz into a shiv. As a matter of fact, petrification or decomposition of wood would be sufficient for a previously staked vampire to come out of torpor. But I also consider using crossbows and bows of fiberglass or aluminum with lead or steel tips as staking to be garbage because arrows and bolts &quot;used to be made of wood&quot; doesn't count either. For me much of the &quot;symbolism&quot; comes in the preparation of the stake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-23-2018, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T06:11:51-07:00","id":1140144,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> IMO, that'd only work if that's a specific Bane of the vamp in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T07:34:17-07:00","id":1140158,"title":"","content":"I see staking as an unusually specific universal bane. Wood + Heart = Torpor. Accept no substitutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T16:23:38-07:00","id":1140347,"title":"","content":"Which is more important to the symbolism of staking? The material qualities of the stake (wood), or the act of staking being meant to pin something down and prevent it from arising again?<br /> <br /> Either way goes, but I'm biased towards the latter considering what in-game logic and fluff they use to justify fire and sunlight being universal banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Clarity 09-14-2017, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T16:43:02-07:00","id":1140353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140347#post1140347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is more important to the symbolism of staking? The material qualities of the stake (wood), or the act of staking being meant to pin something down and prevent it from arising again?<br /> <br /> Either way goes, but I'm biased towards the latter considering what in-game logic and fluff they use to justify fire and sunlight being universal banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banes in vampire are curses. Plain and simple. That's all the symbolism there's to them, and curses are damned specific (pun intended).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T16:54:18-07:00","id":1140357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140353#post1140353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Banes in vampire are curses. Plain and simple. That's all the symbolism there's to them, and curses are damned specific (pun intended).</div> </div> </div> </div>But curses still run on symbolism, don't they? When the princess fell into death-lile slumber because she was pricked by a needle, it wasn't because the needle was tipped with esoteric poison designed to fell royalty. It was because the letting of blood symbolized death, and sleep is death's brother. When the prince awoke another sleeping princess with a kiss, it wasn't because he was born under destined stars and genetically inherited curse-dispelling. It was because true love's kiss symbolizes life, which thus dispels death-like sleep. <br /> <br /> I'd put Anathemas from Beast, imposed by a specific Hero's mind in a Wrong Genre Savvy moment, feels lile a better place to have specifically worded curses. Similarly, individual vampires' Humanity-callousing banes are exactly that; specific to the individual, and thus being specific in nature. Universal curses, I feel, would be based more on archetypes. <br /> <br /> <br /> Then again, I can easily refute myself by saying that the symbolism of using what was alive but is now dead (wood) to defeat what is ought to be dead but moving as if it were alive (vampires) is also perfectly valid. In the end it's all preferences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T17:23:22-07:00","id":1140361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140357#post1140357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But curses still run on symbolism, don't they? When the princess fell into death-lile slumber because she was pricked by a needle, it wasn't because the needle was tipped with esoteric poison designed to fell royalty. It was because the letting of blood symbolized death, and sleep is death's brother. When the prince awoke another sleeping princess with a kiss, it wasn't because he was born under destined stars and genetically inherited curse-dispelling. It was because true love's kiss symbolizes life, which thus dispels death-like sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the point is that menstrual blood, which also symbolizes life probably wouldn't have broken the curse. Again, specific. Because rarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140357#post1140357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd put Anathemas from Beast, imposed by a specific Hero's mind in a Wrong Genre Savvy moment, feels lile a better place to have specifically worded curses. Similarly, individual vampires' Humanity-callousing banes are exactly that; specific to the individual, and thus being specific in nature. Universal curses, I feel, would be based more on archetypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast bears nothing to do with the topic at hand. All of the vampiric banes are specific in nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140357#post1140357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, I can easily refute myself by saying that the symbolism of using what was alive but is now dead (wood) to defeat what is ought to be dead but moving as if it were alive (vampires) is also perfectly valid. In the end it's all preferences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Debatable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T17:24:58-07:00","id":1140362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140353#post1140353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banes in vampire are curses. Plain and simple. That's all the symbolism there's to them, and curses are damned specific (pun intended).</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the 'great curses' are explained in terms of symbolism. P101-102.<br /> <br /> 'Sunlight represents truth and honesty. It stands for visibility, where Kindred exist in deceptive darkness. While it isn't always immediately deadly, it burns Kindred flesh.'<br /> <br /> 'Fire represents humankind's dominance over the natural world, and ability to manipulate its environment as a tool. This symbolically human tool destroys Kindred flesh like nothing else.'<br /> <br /> There's further reasons, from the Lancea et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone, getting into more specifics, the former believing the pain of sunlight is punishment from God, the latter that fire burns as a lesson.<br /> <br /> Like I said when originally asking, I think storytellers could go either way depending on where they leaned. But the book clearly embraces the symbolism of the great banes. Two of them, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-14-2017, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T17:36:58-07:00","id":1140363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140361#post1140361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but the point is that menstrual blood, which also symbolizes life probably wouldn't have broken the curse. Again, specific. Because rarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... going by this schema that curses need specificity, menstrual blood has the extra symbolism of feminine power, and a kiss has the extra symbolism of love versus hate, and wood has the stuff I mentioned. <br /> <br /> So a wooden stake doubles up on anti-undead symbolism, meaning that regardless of how curses and the Curse work in Vampire, it ought to be a bane of vampires. Fun analysis. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beast bears nothing to do with the topic at hand. All of the vampiric banes are specific in nature. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, on second thought bringing in Beast was out-of-context. <br /> <br /> But are all vampire banes specific? Even fire and sunlight? I may be misrememberig things, then. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Debatable. </div> </div> </div>On my self-rebuttal regarding why does it have to be wood in particular, or my statement regarding that it's up to each table to decide which part of the game's lore they want to stick to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T17:55:55-07:00","id":1140367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140362#post1140362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both the 'great curses' are explained in terms of symbolism. P101-102.<br /> <br /> 'Sunlight represents truth and honesty. It stands for visibility, where Kindred exist in deceptive darkness. While it isn't always immediately deadly, it burns Kindred flesh.'<br /> <br /> 'Fire represents humankind's dominance over the natural world, and ability to manipulate its environment as a tool. This symbolically human tool destroys Kindred flesh like nothing else.'<br /> <br /> There's further reasons, from the Lancea et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone, getting into more specifics, the former believing the pain of sunlight is punishment from God, the latter that fire burns as a lesson.<br /> <br /> Like I said when originally asking, I think storytellers could go either way depending on where they leaned. But the book clearly embraces the symbolism of the great banes. Two of them, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't changes the fact that they're specific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140363#post1140363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On my self-rebuttal regarding why does it have to be wood in particular, or my statement regarding that it's up to each table to decide which part of the game's lore they want to stick to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something dead dealing with something dead seems at odds with the themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T18:15:06-07:00","id":1140380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140362#post1140362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both the 'great curses' are explained in terms of symbolism. P101-102.<br /> <br /> 'Sunlight represents truth and honesty. It stands for visibility, where Kindred exist in deceptive darkness. While it isn't always immediately deadly, it burns Kindred flesh.'<br /> <br /> 'Fire represents humankind's dominance over the natural world, and ability to manipulate its environment as a tool. This symbolically human tool destroys Kindred flesh like nothing else.'<br /> <br /> There's further reasons, from the Lancea et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone, getting into more specifics, the former believing the pain of sunlight is punishment from God, the latter that fire burns as a lesson.<br /> <br /> Like I said when originally asking, I think storytellers could go either way depending on where they leaned. But the book clearly embraces the symbolism of the great banes. Two of them, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does speak in terms of symbolism, but telling the truth doesn't burn a vampire like sunlight. A gun represents mastery over the natural world just as well, but vampires aren't weak to bullets. You need sunlight and fire, no substitutes. The book is pretty clear, RAW: &quot;when a <b>wooden stake</b> penetrates the Kindred heart.&quot;<br /> <br /> The other banes don't have near as much leeway as people keep trying to give wooden stakes. I don't know why they think stakes are special.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T18:29:43-07:00","id":1140382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140367#post1140367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something dead dealing with something dead seems at odds with the themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something rightfully dead forcing something that should be dead but is not to stay dead like itself. Reinforcing the natural order, I'd name it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140380#post1140380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does speak in terms of symbolism, but telling the truth doesn't burn a vampire like sunlight. A gun represents mastery over the natural world just as well, but vampires aren't weak to bullets. You need sunlight and fire, no substitutes. The book is pretty clear, RAW: &quot;when a <b>wooden stake</b> penetrates the Kindred heart.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, so it says. At least we now know there's a default answer people can widely accept. That's a good sign.<br /> <br /> Fire is special in that it's <i>the</i> mastery of the natural world, so we can give it more weight than a weapon that harnesses fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The other banes don't have near as much leeway as people keep trying to give wooden stakes. I don't know why they think stakes are special. </div> </div> </div>Plenty of room for alternate interpretation of other banes, especially sunlight. We were talking about stakes in the first place, so it gets special treatment by definition in the discussion.<br /> <br /> That said, a part of me keeps trying to treat stakes 'special' because having a particular material be required for the composition stake isn't so intuitive to me. Compared to the symbolism behind the act of staking, which is immediately noticeable. Which is why I keep coming up with answers for &quot;Why does it have to be wood?&quot; myself, because my viewpoint doesn't come with an automated answer to the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T19:01:41-07:00","id":1140388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140382#post1140382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, a part of me keeps trying to treat stakes 'special' because having a particular material be required for the composition stake isn't so intuitive to me. Compared to the symbolism behind the act of staking, which is immediately noticeable. Which is why I keep coming up with answers for &quot;Why does it have to be wood?&quot; myself, because my viewpoint doesn't come with an automated answer to the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be glad is not a <b>specific </b>type of wood, then. There's plenty of those around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T19:17:40-07:00","id":1140391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140388#post1140388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Be glad is not a <b>specific </b>type of wood, then. There's plenty of those around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I swear I saw hawthorn wood somewhere (but can't recall where it was from) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T19:46:16-07:00","id":1140401,"title":"","content":"Apparently iron stakes are an occasional weakness too, as opposed to wooden. And obviously other sources have the result different, where the staking instantly kills the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T06:17:01-07:00","id":1140501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1140158#post1140158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see staking as an unusually specific universal bane. Wood + Heart = Torpor. Accept no substitutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure why there is so much debate about what can or can not stake a vampire. As someone pointed out, the book explicitly and undeniably says &quot;WOOD.&quot; Sure you can shove a quartz shiv into someone and sure it does damage and hell it might even be enough to torpor them, but it's not wood and won't function the same. like Elfive says. Wood+heart= Torpor. \u200bA stake does not end a vampire's life, it simply puts them to 'sleep' until the wood is taken out. <br /> <br /> Now if you want to get into the symbolism of wood, think about the Tree of Life. Perhaps the stake is just a representation of that, the wood is just a piece of life and it is simply putting the dead back where it belongs. It is one of the holiest of symbols. Wood is life, a Vampire is Death, the two together is a balance of nature, putting the vampire in a state of sleep. perfectly balanced.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T18:47:23-07:00","id":1140946,"title":"","content":"Well the idea behind the stake is that IRL it was used to pin a suspected vampire (corpse) to it's own coffin/grave and prevent it from rising to drink the blood of the townspeople.<br /> A quick search didn't turn up any instances of wooden stakes being used, possibly because they would have decomposed along with the body, but I did see some examples of iron stakes being used. Perhaps wood was used when/where iron was too expensive for use in this manner.<br /> <br /> IRL Bulgarian grave site where iron stakes were used <a href=\"http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-2786765/The-vampire-graves-Archaeologists-uncover-medieval-corpses-buried-iron-stake-stop-joining-undead.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/arti...ng-undead.html</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T02:58:15-07:00","id":1141010,"title":"","content":"I'm working on converting the Moirai (Mekhet Clanbook) to 2nd edition for a chronicle I'm starting. I'm looking at the Manteia Devotion and I cannot figure out who's supposed to get the bonuses and penalties. Is it supposed to be the character that used the Devotion, the target of the Devotion, or everyone? Why does the Devotion even have a target?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T03:33:03-07:00","id":1141013,"title":"","content":"The divination comes in the form of [person] does [thing]. the [person] is the target. Any roll, by anyone, that would, if it succeeded, bring about [thing] gets a bonus. any roll that would avert [thing] gets a penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T17:24:07-07:00","id":1141263,"title":"","content":"Not being able to outside of torpor is more like a Ban than a Bane to me because it seems to be more of a prohibition than a destructive force that annihilates them. Of course I realize that vampires muddle the terms of Ban and Bane because they don't use the word Ban as other gamelines do, lumping it all together. I like the distinction and think its a useful tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T18:45:29-07:00","id":1143107,"title":"","content":"How long does it take a vampire to heal? I can't seem to find anything in the book regarding what kind of action is required to spend Vitae to heal, if there even is an action. I thought I saw something once that you can spend a Vitae immediately after the damage is dealt, or that you can spend a Vitae on your turn to heal and still perform other actions, or that it takes your entire turn to heal. Which is correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T19:46:59-07:00","id":1143120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1143107#post1143107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does it take a vampire to heal? I can't seem to find anything in the book regarding what kind of action is required to spend Vitae to heal, if there even is an action. I thought I saw something once that you can spend a Vitae immediately after the damage is dealt, or that you can spend a Vitae on your turn to heal and still perform other actions, or that it takes your entire turn to heal. Which is correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spending Vitae to heal bashing and lethal damage is a reflexive action; healing aggravated take 5 points of vitae and rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-22T21:02:36-07:00","id":1143136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1143107#post1143107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does it take a vampire to heal? I can't seem to find anything in the book regarding what kind of action is required to spend Vitae to heal, if there even is an action. I thought I saw something once that you can spend a Vitae immediately after the damage is dealt, or that you can spend a Vitae on your turn to heal and still perform other actions, or that it takes your entire turn to heal. Which is correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Malus said.<br /> <br /> Most of the specifics are on page 91, under 'Healing.' That it is reflexive is on the previous page, under 'Tricks of the Damned.' Blush of Life, Kindred Senses, Physical Intensity and Healing are reflexive actions. You can use as many per turn as your Blood Potency allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-23-2017, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-23T01:52:25-07:00","id":1143174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1143107#post1143107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does it take a vampire to heal? I can't seem to find anything in the book regarding what kind of action is required to spend Vitae to heal, if there even is an action. I thought I saw something once that you can spend a Vitae immediately after the damage is dealt, or that you can spend a Vitae on your turn to heal and still perform other actions, or that it takes your entire turn to heal. Which is correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>As before of me has been said. That's means that, if in a turn someone deal to you enough damages to sent you on torpor, you can heal this damages if you have blood and continue to fight or escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T13:51:11-07:00","id":1143889,"title":"","content":"Can vampires perceive revenants as being different or is it something that they would need to taste the blood to detect??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T19:17:30-07:00","id":1143942,"title":"","content":"Without Auspex they would just seem like young, starving Kindred who are rapidly falling to their Beast.<br /> A strange clue could also come up if striking up a conversation with one or stumbling across one who just woke from his Daysleep with his hair matted in dark, flaky, day-old blood or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T23:00:57-07:00","id":1143981,"title":"","content":"Can Touch of Shadow be used on multiple target's at once, paying the cost and making the rolls for each separately? Or does using it again instantly turn off the previous use, making Cloak the Gathering the only way to affect multiple targets at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T16:24:10-07:00","id":1144556,"title":"","content":"Hello to all ! Some questions<br /> <br /> Are Rites of the Dragon and the Testament of Longinus Legal in Second Edition? There are references for both of them in the Covenant descriptions (p42) but is the actuall printed book from the First Edition Legal?<br /> <br /> I have 5 successes in a Dominate roll and my opponent 3 to the resist roll. To determine if i rolled exceptional success i count my successes or i subtract the successes of the defender?<br /> <br /> in the first case, i have 5 so exceptional <br /> <br /> in the second 2 so no exceptional.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T16:27:16-07:00","id":1144558,"title":"","content":"There is no &quot;legal&quot;. Some materials in the books might be outdated, but whatever isn't can be used if your group wants to use it.<br /> <br /> As for your other question: Your five successes are an Exceptional despite the opponents three successes. Some house rule it to be the other way, though. My group does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T06:25:11-07:00","id":1144732,"title":"","content":"It's never come up, but I personally would have the opponent's roll cancel the exceptional <i>only</i> if they also rolled 5 successes. This is mostly to stop fights between high-power individuals looking like a sudden death match in smash bros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T16:45:52-07:00","id":1145008,"title":"","content":"Besides Claws of the Unholy and bloodlines, are there any 2e material for vampires dealing aggravated damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T17:05:26-07:00","id":1145016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1145008#post1145008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides Claws of the Unholy and bloodlines, are there any 2e material for vampires dealing aggravated damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feeding the Chrone - Cruac rite level 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T18:18:20-07:00","id":1146873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1143981#post1143981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Touch of Shadow be used on multiple target's at once, paying the cost and making the rolls for each separately? Or does using it again instantly turn off the previous use, making Cloak the Gathering the only way to affect multiple targets at once?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it doesn't say that you can only maintain one at a time. I would say that you would need to spend 1 round using it on each subject as well, as the power does say it targets only one person/object at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T18:31:32-07:00","id":1146874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1145008#post1145008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides Claws of the Unholy and bloodlines, are there any 2e material for vampires dealing aggravated damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>A couple Carthian powers can cause it, like to violators of Establish Precedent and Empower Judiciary. A few Cruac rituals, Gorgon's Gaze, Mantle of the Crone, and Feeding the Crone (Marcus got this but wanted to list it anyways). And a Theban sorcery, Blandishment of Sin (you need to upgrade it but it's not exactly difficult).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T05:46:35-07:00","id":1150309,"title":"","content":"Can Vampires even drink water without the Blush of Life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:22:07-07:00","id":1150314,"title":"","content":"You <i>might </i>get away with water because it's a major constituent of blood. Maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T06:41:43-07:00","id":1150321,"title":"","content":"Vampirism is a supernatural curse, not a biological condition. Water should be treated as any other non-blood liquid. The reason blood isn't expelled is because it's stored and used up. The vampiric body has no reason to store water and no way to get rid of it outside of purging it or using Blush of Life, like other beverages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T01:08:50-07:00","id":1150569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1150309#post1150309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Vampires even drink water without the Blush of Life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but they can't hold it down long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T04:20:28-07:00","id":1150599,"title":"","content":"Hi folks =F<br /> \u200b<br /> Should heated metal be treated as fire damage? Could this be considered a provocation to frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11934-draugr","name":"Draugr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11934_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T05:17:55-07:00","id":1150607,"title":"","content":"I think the answer might actually be no to the first but yes to the second. It can't <i>actually</i> hurt them, but the beast isn't taking any chances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T05:21:33-07:00","id":1150609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draugr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1150599#post1150599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi folks =F<br /> \u200b<br /> Should heated metal be treated as fire damage? Could this be considered a provocation to frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>If my memory assist me I think the first question has been already rised and, as often happens with these kind of matters, there were different interpretations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> My personal interpretation is no: fire is a mystical bane not linked to the heat itself, althogh intense heat can set on fire flameable things like clothes (not skin since skin doesn't get fire, just carbonizes itself).<br /> <br /> About the second question, it's a painful and harmful source so definetly yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-18-2017, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:24:58-07:00","id":1150838,"title":"","content":"Well fire is treated as fire damage, heated metal is treated as heated metal damage unless the heat actually sets something on fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T17:37:05-07:00","id":1152340,"title":"","content":"Are 2 dots in Expression (without dots in Crafts) and a specialty sufficient for purchasing the Taste merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T01:45:46-07:00","id":1152437,"title":"","content":"I would allow it if I was running but other storytellers may rule otherwise. No harm in asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T14:53:47-07:00","id":1152618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1152437#post1152437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would allow it if I was running but other storytellers may rule otherwise. No harm in asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it would make sense for a character with Expression (Writing) to have a respected &quot;Taste&quot; concerning literature. Though the specific character I asked the question for has Expression (Criticism). It's an unfairly general specialty but it makes sense for the character (a professional critic should have a highly-regarded taste concerning art in general)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T15:41:26-07:00","id":1152622,"title":"","content":"Well the Merit talks about being able to discern minor details in fashion, food, or architecture so your proposal doesn't seem unreasonable.<br /> If you or the ST is a complete purist, you could always homebrew a custom Merit that uses Expression and applies only to literature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T17:16:05-07:00","id":1152643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1152618#post1152618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it would make sense for a character with Expression (Writing) to have a respected &amp;quot;Taste&amp;quot; concerning literature. Though the specific character I asked the question for has Expression (Criticism). It's an unfairly general specialty but it makes sense for the character (a professional critic should have a highly-regarded taste concerning art in general)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine, you can apply all the benefits of the Taste merit to any review or critical work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T11:58:26-07:00","id":1152859,"title":"","content":"can you diablerise a vampire suffering form soul loss? (soulless or thrall conditions)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T13:29:42-07:00","id":1152905,"title":"","content":"Vampires aren't susceptible to soul loss in the first place (not explicitly stated, but all soul loss mechanics in VtR core only mentions Integrity, not Humanity) so it would be a matter of how you implement soul loss as a house rule in the first place.<br /> If it works like it does on humans I see no reason you wouldn't be able to diablerize them. Disciplines, Skills and Blood Potency are present and accounted for. However, if soul loss is implemented the same way it affects mages (slowly losing your magical abilities) you might not be able to gain a Discipline dot, any Blood Experiences or, if it's not possible to diablerize at all at that stage, not even a Skill dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T13:51:36-07:00","id":1152921,"title":"","content":"Or maybe they are seceptible to it, but havkbf it makes them human. And maybe someone found a way to induce soul loss in the form of a drug... just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T14:07:21-07:00","id":1152933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1152859#post1152859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you diablerise a vampire suffering form soul loss? (soulless or thrall conditions)</div> </div> </div> </div>If their soul or whatever constitutes it, is missing, I'd say no. (How do you take nothing and gain something from it?) If soulless is just some slapdash description to mean reduced or suppressed potency or ability then I'd say yes, they can be diablerized. (And I'd proceed to do something like have the unconsumed part return to restore the victim to unlife slightly diminished with full knowledge of what was done to them and immunity to their diablerist's powers.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T22:04:40-07:00","id":1153062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1152859#post1152859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can you diablerise a vampire suffering form soul loss? (soulless or thrall conditions)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can take the soul out but the beast is still present to consume?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T04:35:14-07:00","id":1153112,"title":"","content":"True but the beast holds the dead body together and a soul in a dead body moves on so no more vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T07:38:15-07:00","id":1153166,"title":"","content":"It is implied that vampires are subject to soul loss in the sample plots hooks for the Photographer Strix with the vain Daeva rival plot.<br /> <br /> This brings up a good point that the mechanic in Requiem mention Integrity. This leads to two divergent interpretations, possibly more.<br /> <br /> 1. Eye bite on vampires equals diablerie plain and simple.<br /> 2. Vampires can exist without souls, and thus it is the Beast which supernaturally animates and powers vampires and what is devoured by diablerie isn't the soul but the Beast in the shape of the soul in question. The soul is the structure that allows the vampire to maintain the Man.<br /> <br /> I like the second interpretation better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T07:56:36-07:00","id":1153171,"title":"","content":"are you suggesting that soul loss on a vampire might result in instant draugr","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T09:22:13-07:00","id":1153195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1153166#post1153166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is implied that vampires are subject to soul loss in the sample plots hooks for the Photographer Strix with the vain Daeva rival plot.<br /> <br /> This brings up a good point that the mechanic in Requiem mention Integrity. This leads to two divergent interpretations, possibly more.<br /> <br /> 1. Eye bite on vampires equals diablerie plain and simple.<br /> 2. Vampires can exist without souls, and thus it is the Beast which supernaturally animates and powers vampires and what is devoured by diablerie isn't the soul but the Beast in the shape of the soul in question. The soul is the structure that allows the vampire to maintain the Man.<br /> <br /> I like the second interpretation better.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal interpretation was always #1. I remember David Hill once mentioning something along the lines of vampire souls being more tied into their physicality, which supposedly is what allows regular Diablerie in the first place and Thousand Years of Night supports this somewhat by saying that diablerising a mortal is possible but noticeably harder. This to me hints that a vampiric body without a soul cannot exist at all. When a Kindred loses their soul (or what passes for it) he instantly turns to ash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T18:01:38-07:00","id":1153346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ahather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1153171#post1153171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are you suggesting that soul loss on a vampire might result in instant draugr</div> </div> </div> </div>Inevitable and much quicker draugr if the Humanity loss follows the same algorithm Integrity loss does for humans. Like a building slowly collapsing due loss of internal supports.<br /> <br /> I have seen interesting metaphysic analogies in CofD that outline the soul as such, but I can see the other interpretation too even though the presumed metaphysics are very different and that is potentially significant if you're Storytelling a game with NPCs or PCs that investigate and devise experiments to test the metaphysics. (I am looking at you Ordo using the scientific method)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T18:23:08-07:00","id":1153353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1153195#post1153195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My personal interpretation was always #1. I remember David Hill once mentioning something along the lines of vampire souls being more tied into their physicality, which supposedly is what allows regular Diablerie in the first place and Thousand Years of Night supports this somewhat by saying that diablerising a mortal is possible but noticeably harder. This to me hints that a vampiric body without a soul cannot exist at all. When a Kindred loses their soul (or what passes for it) he instantly turns to ash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally a valid interpretation, and by definition means a vampire can't suffer the Soulless Condition because that'd be instant death instead.<br /> <br /> _IF_ a vampire could suffer the Soulless Condition that would mean the soul isn't the animating force, leaving the Beast the likely candidate for that job, and the Beast being the true seat of vampiric power also makes a lot of sense too, especially given Discipline descriptions focusing on being empowered by the Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T07:03:51-07:00","id":1153915,"title":"","content":"I'm running a game for a PC ghoul and there's a good chance that before long she'll be Embraced. Right now she's got a stage 3 Blood Bond with a vampire, but a different vampire may lay claim to her and attempt to Embrace her instead.<br /> <br /> So what happens to her Blood Bond in either event? Does the Stage 3 persist if her current regnant Embraces her? What about the other Kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T07:17:12-07:00","id":1153918,"title":"","content":"Since blood bonds don't affect vampires any different than humans/ghouls, there's no reason for it to disappear. However, if one vampire would like to embrace another vampire they might have a plan to deal with blood bonds. Ordo Dracul has a Scale for getting rid of blood bonds, and I don't see any reason for there not being a Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery ritual for the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T07:30:52-07:00","id":1153919,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's a reason vamps tend not to embrace other people's ghouls. That bond is going <i>nowhere. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T08:01:05-07:00","id":1153927,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the Blood Bond end with the thralls death though? Does it persist even in death? I always believed it ended with death, but then again, Blood Bound ghoul-childes and ghoul ghosts seems like fun things to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T09:27:45-07:00","id":1153934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1153919#post1153919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there's a reason vamps tend not to embrace other people's ghouls. That bond is going <i>nowhere. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the vinculum wears off after a year. The question is, do you want to be responsible for the actions of a vitae addict who'll be acting in the interests of someone you just screwed in the meantime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T11:42:05-07:00","id":1153949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1153927#post1153927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't the Blood Bond end with the thralls death though? Does it persist even in death? I always believed it ended with death, but then again, Blood Bound ghoul-childes and ghoul ghosts seems like fun things to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It ends with the regnant's death. And by death we mean death death not just half-assed undeath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T17:03:23-07:00","id":1154017,"title":"","content":"I have been re-reading the 2E Core and a couple of question have arise.<br /> <br /> On page 92 under &quot;Lashing out&quot; it says after describing the contested roll between aggressor and recipient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core Pg 92;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the aggressor scores more successes, the victim gains the Condition associated with the aggressor\u2019s Beast. As well, the aggressor gains a +2 die bonus on any rolls to pursue her aspect\u2019s interests for the remainder of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Followed by:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core Pg 92;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the opposition scores more successes, he turns the confrontation on the aggressor. The opposition imposes the Condition associated with his Beast, and gains a +2 die bonus on any rolls to pursue his Beast\u2019s compulsions for the remainder of the scene.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My question is, is there a difference between &quot;Aspect\u00b4s interests&quot; and &quot;Beast\u00b4s compulsion&quot;?<br /> <hr /><br /> On the same page on the &quot;Flight&quot; response it says after saying that the recipient can flee and it cost nothing, it goes and says<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core Pg 92;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The aggressor may pursue. The victim gains the Condition associated with the initiating vampire\u2019s aspect of the Beast.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that the recipient gains the condition when he flees or just when the aggressor decides to pursue?<br /> <hr /><br /> On page 96 on the exceptional success on a feeding roll, it says<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core Pg 96;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptional Success: Things go phenomenally well. During the scene, the Storyteller must give at least three important, identifying features or personality traits about the vessel. Once, at an appropriate time in a later scene, you may request the vessel\u2019s involvement. If you do so, take a Beat. This involvement may be abstract: for example, if they\u2019re dead, or if they gave a detailed description to the police.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am confuse as how that works, the text seems to imply that thing go particularly well but the examples given seems of things that are bad for the PC, like the police having a description of the PC.<br /> <hr /><br /> On page 105 on &quot;Ridding the Wave&quot; it says<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core Pg 105;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To ride the wave, spend a Willpower point, and make the normal Resolve + Composure resistance roll. The Willpower point does not add to this roll. Success holds off the frenzy for a turn as if she\u2019d spent Willpower to fight the frenzy. She can continue to do this until she fails, runs out of Willpower, or until she accumulates five successes. Treat any failure on this roll as a dramatic failure.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean the PC needs to reach the 5 success on a single roll or can accumulate the successes in various rolls?<br /> <hr /><br /> On page 203, under &quot;frenzy and the predatory aura&quot; in regard to the Strix it says<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core Pg 203;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and a vampire\u2019s first instinct when she senses a presence she can\u2019t see is probably \u201cObfuscate,\u201d not \u201cStrix.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean a Vampire can always feel a vampire when he is using obfuscation? Doesn't that kind of invalidate the power?<br /> <br /> Thanks for any answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T17:31:55-07:00","id":1154022,"title":"","content":"I have a question regarding the discipline of Dominate and memory alterations for mesmerize, iron edict, and lying mind.<br /> <br /> I think mesmerize is pretty clear that it can be used to alter the subject's memory of the current scene. <br /> I also think that lying mind is pretty clear that it can be used to alter the subject's memories in a pretty comprehensive way.<br /> <br /> The question I have is regarding Iron edict. My understanding the discipline is that it extends the duration of control potentially until dawn while also increasing the complexity of commands which can be given. In the power's description it says: &quot;...the vampire can take some time to play with his (the victim's) thoughts and memories.&quot; This leads me to wonder if a vampire could alter the subject's memories of the current night, including previous scenes. <br /> <br /> However, memory alterations are not mentioned again within the power. So, is this just a slip of the tongue on the writer's part, or can iron edict be used to change memories better than mesmerize, but not as good as lying mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T18:11:28-07:00","id":1154030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154017#post1154017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am confuse as how that works, the text seems to imply that thing go particularly well but the examples given seems of things that are bad for the PC, like the police having a description of the PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;When things go as intended, the vessels give context for the vampire's existence.&quot; The examples given are for abstract involvement of a former vessel in a scene \u2014 you could also just have the vessel be in the same place as your character in a later scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On page 105 on &quot;Ridding the Wave&quot; it says<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Does that mean the PC needs to reach the 5 success on a single roll or can accumulate the successes in various rolls? </div> </div> </div>The explicit comparison to resisting frenzy would seem to indicate that once you stop rolling you drop into frenzy, since normal resistance is &quot;spend Willpower for X turns, then roll Resolve + Composure + X to see if you succumb to frenzy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On page 203, under &quot;frenzy and the predatory aura&quot; in regard to the Strix it says<br /> [\u2026]<br /> Does that mean a Vampire can always feel a vampire when he is using obfuscation? Doesn't that kind of invalidate the power? </div> </div> </div>Not really:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cloak of Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The vampire can also spend a point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd to vanish completely.</b> Rather than being overlooked or \u201cjust an average person,\u201d the vampire disappears from the perception of everyone around him.<br /> <br /> <b>If the vampire attacks someone or cries out, Cloak of Night continues to obscure him,</b> adding Obfuscate to the surprise roll. Only the struck victim can perceive the vampire.<br /> <br /> <b>If another vampire manages to perceive him, through Auspex, attack, or any other means, she can sense his predatory aura</b> and lash out. If she wins the predatory aura contest, Cloak of Night shatters, as does any other use of Obfuscate the vampire made.</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire who is invisible but talking to another vampire registers to Kindred senses as being a talking vampire that the listener cannot see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T18:29:47-07:00","id":1154033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154030#post1154030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The explicit comparison to resisting frenzy would seem to indicate that once you stop rolling you drop into frenzy, since normal resistance is &quot;spend Willpower for X turns, then roll Resolve + Composure + X to see if you succumb to frenzy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but my question is more along the lines of Riding the wave would function like<br /> <br /> A) Turn 1: PC spend WP, rolls and get 2 successes. Holds off frenzy for a turn.<br /> Turn 2: PC spend WP, rolls and get 3 successes. Hold off frenzy for a turn.<br /> Turn 3: PC spend WP, rolls and get 5 successes, thus an exceptional success and rides the wave.<br /> <br /> or<br /> B) Turn 1: PC spend WP, rolls and get 2 successes. Holds off frenzy for a turn.<br /> Turn 2: PC spend WP, rolls and get 3 successes. Has accumulate 5 successes in 2 turns and thus rides the wave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154030#post1154030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really:A vampire who is invisible but talking to another vampire registers to Kindred senses as being a talking vampire that the listener cannot see.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad there, i should have clarified. I mean more on things like the typical Nosferatu spies as information network. If a vampire (say a Daeva) enters a room and a nosferatu is hiding spying in the same room via obfuscate then the Daeva knows there is another vampire in the room?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-29-2017, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T19:15:17-07:00","id":1154038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154033#post1154033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay but my question is more along the lines of Riding the wave would function like<br /> <br /> A) Turn 1: PC spend WP, rolls and get 2 successes. Holds off frenzy for a turn.<br /> Turn 2: PC spend WP, rolls and get 3 successes. Hold off frenzy for a turn.<br /> Turn 3: PC spend WP, rolls and get 5 successes, thus an exceptional success and rides the wave.<br /> <br /> or<br /> B) Turn 1: PC spend WP, rolls and get 2 successes. Holds off frenzy for a turn.<br /> Turn 2: PC spend WP, rolls and get 3 successes. Has accumulate 5 successes in 2 turns and thus rides the wave.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Accumulates&quot; means the latter is how Riding the Wave functions, yes. Regular frenzy resistance comes down to one roll in which you either enter frenzy (until you satisfy the inciting drive or hit a breaking point) or don't (and either gain/exacerbate the Tempted Condition or recover the Willpower you spent), whereas riding the wave has you roll every turn to allow you to pick the drive you pursue at the risk of locking yourself into a breaking point down the line if you fail any of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My bad there, i should have clarified. I mean more on things like the typical Nosferatu spies as information network. If a vampire (say a Daeva) enters a room and a nosferatu is hiding spying in the same room via obfuscate then the Daeva knows there is another vampire in the room? </div> </div> </div>\u2026No? The section you were asking about specifically concerned the fact that Strix register a Predatory Aura regardless of their current shape or body, but Face in the Crowd's core powers are based on turning the Predatory Aura off/inside-out; it's part of a flavor statement that Kindred will not by default assume that registering the presence of a strange vampire they can't see means they're talking to an atavistic shadow-owl, so any contradiction it implies with the mechanics can be dismissed as unintentional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T19:17:50-07:00","id":1154039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154038#post1154038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Accumulates&quot; means the latter is how Riding the Wave functions, yes. Regular frenzy resistance comes down to one roll in which you either enter frenzy (until you satisfy the inciting drive or hit a breaking point) or don't (and either gain/exacerbate the Tempted Condition or recover the Willpower you spent), whereas riding the wave has you roll every turn to allow you to pick the drive you pursue at the risk of locking yourself into a breaking point down the line if you fail any of them.<br /> <br /> \u2026No? The section you were asking about specifically concerned the fact that Strix register a Predatory Aura regardless of their current shape or body, but Face in the Crowd's core powers are based on turning the Predatory Aura off/inside-out; it's part of a flavor statement that Kindred will not by default assume that registering the presence of a strange vampire they can't see means they're talking to an atavistic shadow-owl, so any contradiction it implies with the mechanics can be dismissed as unintentional.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, thanks for the clarifications <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T15:22:09-07:00","id":1154234,"title":"","content":"<b><u><i>Celerity:</i></u></b><br /> <br /> Is it possible to use the second active ability of <i>Celerity</i> to move out of reach of an attach and then attack during the same interruption?<br /> To be even clearer : is the following example correct? (and if it isn't ...Why? And most importantly,How?)<br /> <br /> <i>Quasimodo the Nosferatu is attacking Belle the Daeva with an axe.<br /> So, during his turn, Quasimodo moves in reach with Belle and then declares to attack her with Weaponry.<br /> Belle, before the dice are rolled, responds that wants to use celerity. She expends one Vitae and uses her instant action to attack Quasimodo with her knive. Because of the fact that she has made an instant action, she can immediately make a movement, and so she does, exiting Quasimodo's range of attack.<br /> From the moment that Quasimodo has already moved and his declared action is no longer possible, the round ends.</i><br /> <br /> Furthermore don't you think that if used in this way <i>Celerity</i> becomes way too powerful? Maybe to the point that no other Physical discipline is better?<br /> And if you don't, why do you disagree ?<br /> ( If it's possible i am expecially intrested in the point of wiew of the Book Designers )<br /> <br /> Thank you from Rome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13629-strikeforce1","name":"strikeforce1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T15:29:36-07:00","id":1154236,"title":"","content":"Celerity does not let you interrupt someone with your full turn; it only lets you interrupt with a &quot;brief action.&quot; You can move or you can attack; you cannot do both during the interrupt.<br /> <br /> In specific:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strikeforce1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154234#post1154234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Because of the fact that she has made an instant action, she can immediately make a movement, and so she does, exiting Quasimodo's range of attack.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>is the mistake here. You don't get to move <i>because</i> you made an Instant Action. The two are unrelated entirely. You get one &quot;brief action&quot; during Celerity's interrupt, not two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T17:25:46-07:00","id":1154260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strikeforce1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154234#post1154234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u><i>Celerity:</i></u></b><br /> <br /> Is it possible to use the second active ability of <i>Celerity</i> to move out of reach of an attach and then attack during the same interruption?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could move behind them or just leave yourself a few steps out of reach so you can close the gap on your turn (assuming I haven't overlooked something in the rules), all in all I don't think Celerity is overpowered because if you try and use it like that your only going to get away with it in a one on one fight and will burn through your Vitae fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T18:03:18-07:00","id":1154266,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers !<br /> Which anyway lead me to this :<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>Celerity (2) :</i></u></b><br /> <br /> It is written that using the second Active ability of Celerity,the character can make a brief action before an action that an other subject has declared takes place.<br /> &quot; <i>This could be an attack, making it possible to disable an opponent in mid-action. It may be movement, avoiding harm by shifting out of reach. Or it could be any other instant action, like activating a Discipline or dodging&quot;</i><br /> <br /> In what is written seems that moving is considered an istant action, like activating a discipline. Still, from the rules, usually movement is not an istant action; on the contrary &quot;<i>A character can move his Speed in a single turn and still take an Instant Action&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> Therefore :<br /> <br /> 1) the moving istant action mentioned in Celerity must be a double movement Action? <br /> <br /> 2)It is possible to do something less expensive in term of time than an Istant Action during the reaction made with <i>Celerity ? </i><br /> To make an example, can I make the Reflexive Action granted me by <i>Sleight of Hand </i>during the interruption and still make my Istant Action during my turn?<br /> <br /> 3)Even further, can I move during the interruption and still take an Istant Action during my turn, or the movement action made during the interruption has to be an Istant Action ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13629-strikeforce1","name":"strikeforce1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T18:27:31-07:00","id":1154269,"title":"","content":"What happens, mechanically, if you're made to forget your Touchstone through Dominate or similar channels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T05:14:29-07:00","id":1154346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strikeforce1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154266#post1154266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) the moving istant action mentioned in Celerity must be a double movement Action?<br /> <br /> 2)It is possible to do something less expensive in term of time than an Istant Action during the reaction made with <i>Celerity ? </i><br /> To make an example, can I make the Reflexive Action granted me by <i>Sleight of Hand </i>during the interruption and still make my Istant Action during my turn?<br /> <br /> 3)Even further, can I move during the interruption and still take an Istant Action during my turn, or the movement action made during the interruption has to be an Istant Action ?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is, that the move action that is done as an interruption, is only your normal speed at most. Unless you use a second blood to make it 2xSpeed. So 2 blood potency is needed.<br /> <br /> Reflexive actions can be done at any time even without Celerity. They cost no time and can be done even on an enemy's turn. Healing with blood is a reflexive and so is stuff like the Resilience discipline. So you can lessen damage even after attack dice have been rolled.<br /> <br /> As far as I'm aware, a Celerity action does not impede your normal turn, so it's the only thing that allows you to have more that 1 attack in a round. But you can't use it to do a third attack, as in interrupt with a Celerity attack twice then do your normal turn.<br /> <br /> Or does the Celerity attack remove that ability to do your normal turn? That seems kinda weak if that is true. The wording is kind of unclear, it says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;However, the vampire is still limited to one instant action&quot; </div> </div> </div>That would mean that if you are first in initiative, you can basically never use an interrupt unless you shift your initiative down.<br /> <br /> Also, you can only use Celerity interrupt as many times in a scene (so in a fight) as you have dots in Celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 10-31-2017, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T06:48:59-07:00","id":1154359,"title":"","content":"They very explicitly avoided giving people the ability to have extra attacks per turn in 2e. It really screws up the action economy and makes whatever power or merit that grants it a must-have.<br /> <br /> Celerity does not allow you to attack twice in a turn. You only get one instant action per turn; if you use it for your interrupt, you don't get it on your proper turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T07:03:20-07:00","id":1154365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154346#post1154346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording is kind of unclear, it says That would mean that if you are first in initiative, you can basically never use an interrupt unless you shift your initiative down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you hold your action or something, yes. But you're not always guaranteed to be first in initiative, so saying you can 'basically never use interrupt' is only true providing you always get first in initiative.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T07:45:49-07:00","id":1154373,"title":"","content":"[snipped and reposted in own thread]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":".  simple question not so simple 10-31-2017, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:49:09-07:00","id":1154503,"title":"","content":"This is a &quot;simple questions&quot; threat, Khanwulf. Given your question is, as you say, subjective as well as inviting some further discussion, you may want to give that post its own thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:55:12-07:00","id":1154505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154503#post1154503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a &quot;simple questions&quot; threat, Khanwulf. Given your question is, as you say, subjective as well as inviting some further discussion, you may want to give that post its own thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sigh. You're probably right. It started out simple...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:48:06-07:00","id":1155151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1154269#post1154269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens, mechanically, if you're made to forget your Touchstone through Dominate or similar channels?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW: You gain the Amnesia (Persistent) Condition. You also have a strong case via Sanctity of Merits for a refund if the Touchstone was not your free chargen one. Whether you maintain the mechanical advantages of the Touchstone is a per-table decision.<br /> <br /> YMMV: If your table has a process to determine when a Touchstone no longer grants its bonuses due to neglect (for example if your ST says that failing to interact with a Touchstone for six months means you can't claim mechanical bonuses) then in theory that would apply. However, I'd argue the mechanical bonuses would still apply in the meantime. You might not know why that bartender you swear you never met before was able to talk you out of frenzy, or why unloading your troubles on them bolsters your confidence (willpower gain), or why their advice helps you come to terms with the evils you inflict (degeneration bonus) - but they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T00:39:00-07:00","id":1155322,"title":"","content":"What happens if a vampire (lets say over bp 5) drinks from a cup with several kindred blood spilled inside, for several times. Through who she would get the blood bond? Is it a kind of clash of wills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:48:10-07:00","id":1155411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1155322#post1155322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a vampire (lets say over bp 5) drinks from a cup with several kindred blood spilled inside, for several times. Through who she would get the blood bond? Is it a kind of clash of wills?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Blood bond is not a clash of wills. There is a roll stated in the book to resist it and it's a willpower to roll that resist. I think this question is absolutely impossible for us to answer. If he drank a cup full of kindred vitae, not blood, but kindred vitae and it was still fresh, then I think I would make a list of vampires then roll the dice to see who got the third stage blood bond. <br /> <br /> I am sure it is completely buried now, but I do believe somewhere it was stated that you could only get 1 stage bond per 24 hours. so it would take 3 days to get that third bond. The first two days this poor vampire would likely be blood bonded to ALL the contributers as he can only spend 1 willpower per turn to resist.. which means he could only resist one of them<br /> <br /> Though some people say it is 1 drink per scene.. and of course all that goes out the window if they have the Coil of the Voivode, because then they could get 3rd stage bonded in one drink....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T09:41:44-07:00","id":1155426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1155411#post1155411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first two days this poor vampire would likely be blood bonded to ALL the contributers as he can only spend 1 willpower per turn to resist.. which means he could only resist one of them</div> </div> </div> </div>It's per action; not per turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T09:52:31-07:00","id":1155430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1155322#post1155322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a vampire (lets say over bp 5) drinks from a cup with several kindred blood spilled inside, for several times. Through who she would get the blood bond? Is it a kind of clash of wills?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no mechanics. Assuming they aren't already immune because of a preexisting oath, vinculum, or ritual protection, I'd say they get +1 step bound to each vampire who contributed at least one vitae to the drink.<br /> If I'm not interested in screwing around with arbitrarily throwing around multiple bonds between NPCs at once (and I'm usually not) I'd say the combination of different types of vitae nullified the vinculum creation effect.<br /> If it's a scheme concocted by the PCs to try and fuck over an NPC, I'd rule a +1 step vinculum establishes only toward the PC who contributed the most toward the drink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T10:55:19-07:00","id":1155447,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that the 24h time between the drinks was from 1ed. I remember that now is possible to close a vinculum at 3rd stage in one night.<br /> <br /> Furtermore I understand the point, every contributor rolls, but if many jave success, ar the third drink, who prevail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:02:08-07:00","id":1155448,"title":"","content":"I think it's still there, simply because otherwise you end up having to figure out what constitutes separate drinks.<br /> <br /> Like, why would the bond deepen if you take 3 vitae with a breath between each, but not if you drank them all at once? There needs to be some time for it to &quot;settle in&quot; simply to allow elders to feed properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:28:04-07:00","id":1155460,"title":"","content":"Rose says it's now based on when makes sense in the story so if someone comes to trust you more you can bond them more but I do it the old way when STing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:13:59-07:00","id":1155474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1155426#post1155426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's per action; not per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only get one action per turn, but I do concede that these are different in the case of someone doing something to you, like 10 vampires trying to dominate you on their turns. I guess if you had 10 willpower you could burn it all<br /> <br /> In this case your action is to drink the vitae in the cup...<br /> <br /> I also think that the per scene or per night rule is necessary because if everyone could just drop three shots with one vitae in each making a third stage blood bond in a matter of sections then the scale of the voivode is utterly useless, you know, The one that allows you to drop 3 vitae into shots and make a third stage bond in a matter of seconds...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:24:42-07:00","id":1155479,"title":"","content":"It's 3 to get to second or 5 to get to third but you're right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:30:43-07:00","id":1155482,"title":"","content":"Ten different vampires are all going to establish eye contact on the exact same character at the exact same second and mesmerize him ten different times in the span of three seconds? I don't think so. <br /> <br /> And so what if a single coil of Voivode is rendered useless by a vampire being able to blood bond a person across scenes in a single night? There's a Cruac ritual that renders it useless. There's plenty of disciplines rendered useless with the application of a coil. Not to mention there's a scale, Carthian Law and Invictus oath that renders blood bonds as useless or ineffective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T20:23:55-07:00","id":1155633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1155482#post1155482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ten different vampires are all going to establish eye contact on the exact same character at the exact same second and mesmerize him ten different times in the span of three seconds? I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swwwwiiiing and a miss. I never once said that was probable or realistic. It was a silly example of how you could expend a silly amount of willpower... it was not meant to be a \u201cthis happens all the time\u201d example. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1155482#post1155482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And so what if a single coil of Voivode is rendered useless by a vampire being able to blood bond a person across scenes in a single night? There's a Cruac ritual that renders it useless. There's plenty of disciplines rendered useless with the application of a coil. Not to mention there's a scale, Carthian Law and Invictus oath that renders blood bonds as useless or ineffective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood bonding is something every vampire is \u201cborn\u201d with the ability to do, why would you need to take a scale to learn how to do it. <br /> <br /> Sure some scales render disciplines or merits less functional, but not all vampires have the \u201caccess\u201d to get those things. Please note the difference. <br /> <br /> However. I mentioned a single scene, you compared with across scenes.. so again. I think you completely missed what I was saying. <br /> <br /> Also I am not aware of this cruac ritual that you have referenced that allows you to 3rd stage blood bond as the coil does. Making the coil useless to take.. however as per rules, you probably can\u2019t be in both covenants at the same time.. <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4714\" data-vbnamecard=\"4714\">Live Bait</a> ah yes!! In my haste I think I got 3 happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T10:09:36-07:00","id":1155765,"title":"","content":"I think the Cruac ritral referred to is the one that makes the caster imbue to Blood Bonds and addiction. I don't agree that it makes Voivode useless as it only protects the caster and you can still use it on others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T17:33:26-07:00","id":1155897,"title":"","content":"Another question arised after a PC of mine took swarm form merit. <br /> Now is *almost* unstoppable. <br /> <br /> If he get bound: swarm form;<br /> He take just 1 or max 2 damages per attack (by every source but area effect)<br /> He ignore the defense while attacks, adding this with lethal from protean 4.... or even aggravated... <br /> <br /> What could be a smart/original/creative way to counter this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T18:12:18-07:00","id":1155907,"title":"","content":"Fire, mind control, another swarm, Masquerade breaches, Cruac and Theban rituals.<br /> <br /> Can you be more specific about what you mean by counter it? Are you trying to kill him, or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T03:30:12-08:00","id":1155993,"title":"","content":"Take 1 can of hair spray and a small flame, apply early adventure game logic to create a overly complext scheme to trap swarm in small jar.<br /> Now I want a Requiem point and click adventure game, I have overthought what you need the swarm in a jar for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T04:20:28-08:00","id":1156002,"title":"","content":"Strips of duct tape, with the sticky side up will stop crawling bugs and mice. Glue traps and glue boards will stop them as well as mice and rats cold and they won't be chewing their way free. Drop a 5x5 (or larger) plyboard over top of them as an area of effect and tap dance on it to an accompaniment of the popping noises and squeals of their death cries. Or just douse the area with alcohol and light a match.<br /> <br /> A hair dryer on high, a garden hose, an electric air pump, or pressure washer doing focused blasts (not waving it around wildly) will easily disperse even flying vermin outside their survival radius where they'll instantly shrivel and die. Bonus points if you blast them straight into a sewer, bonfire, stream, or nest of a different vermin type (like termites, hornets, fire ants) or glue trap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T06:53:37-08:00","id":1156327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1155897#post1155897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question arised after a PC of mine took swarm form merit.<br /> Now is *almost* unstoppable.<br /> <br /> If he get bound: swarm form;<br /> He take just 1 or max 2 damages per attack (by every source but area effect)<br /> He ignore the defense while attacks, adding this with lethal from protean 4.... or even aggravated...<br /> <br /> What could be a smart/original/creative way to counter this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Swarm form is more or less like Protean 5: it makes you <b><i>extremely hard</i></b> to kill. You may not be very effective within it, but you're going to die hard for sure.<br /> <br /> How to deal with it? Obfuscate all exits. Bring fire (flamethrowers especially). Use a net (for size 1 forms, not insects). Use mental powers that can stun/remove actions (I have not specific examples to cite, but a custom Devotion for Auspex would work). Dominate the swarm into a contained area (it only has to make eye contact with you, which is pretty easy when it has 1,000 eyes).<br /> <br /> Now... it's annoying as ST to encounter a player swinging a power that takes all the drama out of situations for him (or her). But let me gently suggest that you approach the situation in a few ways:<br /> <br /> 1. Talk to the player and define with him or her the core direction being played toward: if &quot;unkillable bastard&quot; is their thing, then they need to know that their opponents will find other ways to attack their Requiem out of necessity.<br /> <br /> 2. Put yourself in the NPCs' shoes. They may not (yet) know about the PC's capabilities, but once they do, they'll be having this same conversation and ultimately it'll be easier to attack things the PC cares about, instead of him himself. You don't have to kill someone to defeat them: keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> 3. Assuming NPCs want to challenge the PC directly, they can come up with plans, and also develop powers themselves (or hire such muscle) to complicate things. Trap the PC, kill off most of his swarm, and let one escape to reform into a starving vamp. Run with the &quot;you survived death again--now consequences&quot; plot for a session or two. Let the NPCs think they got him. Let the other PCs think he's toast. This is traditional stuff.<br /> <br /> Have fun. Your player put a lot of effort into something potent and iconic. Let him enjoy himself, too.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:42:22-08:00","id":1156343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156327#post1156327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Swarm form is more or less like Protean 5: it makes you <b><i>extremely hard</i></b> to kill. You may not be very effective within it, but you're going to die hard for sure.<br /> <br /> How to deal with it? Obfuscate all exits. Bring fire (flamethrowers especially). Use a net (for size 1 forms, not insects). Use mental powers that can stun/remove actions (I have not specific examples to cite, but a custom Devotion for Auspex would work). Dominate the swarm into a contained area (it only has to make eye contact with you, which is pretty easy when it has 1,000 eyes).<br /> <br /> Now... it's annoying as ST to encounter a player swinging a power that takes all the drama out of situations for him (or her). But let me gently suggest that you approach the situation in a few ways:<br /> <br /> 1. Talk to the player and define with him or her the core direction being played toward: if &quot;unkillable bastard&quot; is their thing, then they need to know that their opponents will find other ways to attack their Requiem out of necessity.<br /> <br /> 2. Put yourself in the NPCs' shoes. They may not (yet) know about the PC's capabilities, but once they do, they'll be having this same conversation and ultimately it'll be easier to attack things the PC cares about, instead of him himself. You don't have to kill someone to defeat them: keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> 3. Assuming NPCs want to challenge the PC directly, they can come up with plans, and also develop powers themselves (or hire such muscle) to complicate things. Trap the PC, kill off most of his swarm, and let one escape to reform into a starving vamp. Run with the &quot;you survived death again--now consequences&quot; plot for a session or two. Let the NPCs think they got him. Let the other PCs think he's toast. This is traditional stuff.<br /> <br /> Have fun. Your player put a lot of effort into something potent and iconic. Let him enjoy himself, too.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Step 1) NPC uses down and dirty combat against the swarm. Step 2) Molotovs and celerity means most of the swarm is reduced to ashes. 3) you re-consolidate yourself into a mess of kindred form. Step 4) Stake the fucker, ransom him to his coterie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T09:46:40-08:00","id":1156376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156343#post1156343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Step 1) NPC uses down and dirty combat against the swarm. Step 2) Molotovs and celerity means most of the swarm is reduced to ashes. 3) you re-consolidate yourself into a mess of kindred form. Step 4) Stake the fucker, ransom him to his coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. &quot;Storyteller characters might deal some damage, but they\u2019re never able to initiate a Down and Dirty Combat.&quot; p. 176. If this is an NPC on NPC fight, then whatever; the one who wins who the ST wants for story purposes. Why roll? If your ST tries this on you, then he's being a dick on purpose. My list as you quoted was expressly intended to encourage STs *not* to be dicks.<br /> <br /> 2. You can skip #1 and go directly to #2 if you want. Celerity and any fire will do the trick, assuming you can affect enough coverage. Personally? Flamethrowers are easy enough to make and classified as &quot;airguns&quot;....<br /> <br /> 3. Step #3 and #4 follow if some bit of the PC is unable to escape. Works on NPCs with swarm form even better.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T11:27:25-08:00","id":1156417,"title":"","content":"Whats it like to pull back from the brink? (of becoming Draugr) I got the impression at humanity 1, even if he does decide to improve his humanity to 2, he's not going to break down weeping, that will have to wait till he gets back up to 3 or 4, instead hes at first motivated mostly by fear for his own psyche.<br /> <br /> Think im right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T11:57:53-08:00","id":1156422,"title":"","content":"Netflix's Van Helsing got quite a few examples of the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T13:24:21-08:00","id":1156457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156327#post1156327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Swarm form is more or less like Protean 5: it makes you <b><i>extremely hard</i></b> to kill. You may not be very effective within it, but you're going to die hard for sure.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I missed something. Why you wouldn't be very effective in swarm form? You keep your stats, rolling Strength+brawl+vigor without subtracting defense. Furthermore you could use protean 4 as well to deal lethal (or even aggravated), <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T14:27:28-08:00","id":1156476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156457#post1156457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I missed something. Why you wouldn't be very effective in swarm form? You keep your stats, rolling Strength+brawl+vigor without subtracting defense. Furthermore you could use protean 4 as well to deal lethal (or even aggravated),</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There have been other discussions on whether the stats change to those of the creature (per Beast's Skin, p.140) or you use the vampire's stats. Also, (weak, IMO) arguments from absence about applying Vigor or not, or allowing physical intensity.<br /> <br /> I probably understated things by not being very careful with my words. I'm personally inclined to use creature stats and add Vigor and physical intensity, which means a high-strength vampire drops several dice in damage to offset ignoring Defense.<br /> <br /> I'd also let someone deal lethal and/or aggravated (when a frenzying swarm per Claws of the Unholy)--because Beast's Form indicates Disciplines are used normally. And, I'm not scared of dealing with the PC on other levels.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T14:42:06-08:00","id":1156484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156476#post1156476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There have been other discussions on whether the stats change to those of the creature (per Beast's Skin, p.140) or you use the vampire's stats. Also, (weak, IMO) arguments from absence about applying Vigor or not, or allowing physical intensity.<br /> <br /> I probably understated things by not being very careful with my words. I'm personally inclined to use creature stats and add Vigor and physical intensity, which means a high-strength vampire drops several dice in damage to offset ignoring Defense.<br /> <br /> I'd also let someone deal lethal and/or aggravated (when a frenzying swarm per Claws of the Unholy)--because Beast's Form indicates Disciplines are used normally. And, I'm not scared of dealing with the PC on other levels.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that normal beast skin will use animal stats, but for swarm the book specifically states:roll strength+brawl ignoring defense. A size 0 insect has strength 0 so I'm pretty sure the book means the vampire Strength + brawl","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T15:30:34-08:00","id":1156501,"title":"","content":"You missed the massive Speed reduction that accompanies Swarm Form.<br /> You missed the fact that when you stack merits (Swarm Form and Claws of the Unholy are both merits) you get the worst aspect/drawbacks of each merit. That means lethal damage that vampires autodowngrade to bashing damage. You're also forgetting that Claws of the Unholy is ONLY useable while in frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T16:07:03-08:00","id":1156508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156501#post1156501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You missed the massive Speed reduction that accompanies Swarm Form.<br /> You missed the fact that when you stack merits (Swarm Form and Claws of the Unholy are both merits) you get the worst aspect/drawbacks of each merit. That means lethal damage that vampires autodowngrade to bashing damage. You're also forgetting that Claws of the Unholy is ONLY useable while in frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>About &quot;massive&quot; speed reduction: flock of birds (size 1) or swarm of flying bees are not less fast than a normal man/vampire (without considering celerity that both of them can have). Crows have speed 14 according to the animals stats.<br /> <br /> About merits stack, I'm really lost here. A PC can have dozen of merits at once and use them togheter, each one with its own Drawback, and in the specific swarm form doesn't have any drawback. <br /> The basic damage in swarm form is lethal (bashing to kindred as every other normal lethal soruce, as per protean 2 claws), non the less if you use protean 4 that specifically allow you to deal lethal even to vampire, the damage stay lethtal, and again, if you have claws of the unholy merit and you are in frenzy, it is aggravated since this merit enanches protean 4 claws.<br /> <br /> And, about claws of the unhoy: NO, I'm not forgettig that it's useable ONLY in frenzy (or ridig the wave<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-06-2017, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T19:19:43-08:00","id":1156539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156484#post1156484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that normal beast skin will use animal stats, but for swarm the book specifically states:roll strength+brawl ignoring defense. A size 0 insect has strength 0 so I'm pretty sure the book means the vampire Strength + brawl</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, which is where your swarm is going to lose damage if your form is insects. You'll be dependent on Vigor and brawl, effectively. But! You're also not reduced by defense, which is significant.<br /> <br /> Crows are size 2. As are cats. Yes, I find this as much of a bummer as you. Make a homebrew merit to up the swarm creature size limit....<br /> <br /> I would love a citation that merits take the lower/most restrictive option when multiple merits conflict. This seems directly contradictory to the nature of merits and their sanctity.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T21:26:05-08:00","id":1156567,"title":"","content":"EDITED AND CAN BE DELETED","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":".  Change my mind. 11-07-2017, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T23:13:48-08:00","id":1156588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156539#post1156539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, which is where your swarm is going to lose damage if your form is insects. You'll be dependent on Vigor and brawl, effectively. But! You're also not reduced by defense, which is significant.<br /> <br /> Crows are size 2. As are cats. Yes, I find this as much of a bummer as you. Make a homebrew merit to up the swarm creature size limit....<br /> <br /> I would love a citation that merits take the lower/most restrictive option when multiple merits conflict. This seems directly contradictory to the nature of merits and their sanctity.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes sorry, crows are size 2. Bats, anyway, are size 1 and have speed 15.<br /> <br /> The reason why I think the book means the full vampire strength+ brawl is that you are not just a bug, a bat or a rat, you are a swarm. <br /> So I guess that more strong the PC is more the swarm is big and able to deal damages.<br /> <br /> In fact if you are going to consider strength 0 and you don't have vigor, you will not deal any damage, which is weird to me. Even compared to the swarm condition in other manual the swarm deal up to 4 damages per turn (automatically).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-07-2017, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T05:47:02-08:00","id":1156646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156588#post1156588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes sorry, crows are size 2. Bats, anyway, are size 1 and have speed 15.<br /> <br /> The reason why I think the book means the full vampire strength+ brawl is that you are not just a bug, a bat or a rat, you are a swarm.<br /> So I guess that more strong the PC is more the swarm is big and able to deal damages.<br /> <br /> In fact if you are going to consider strength 0 and you don't have vigor, you will not deal any damage, which is weird to me. Even compared to the swarm condition in other manual the swarm deal up to 4 damages per turn (automatically).</div> </div> </div> </div>For the sake of the &quot;simple answers&quot; thread here let me note that Swarm Form is contentious, and multiple posters in other threads have suggested fixes, tweaks and the use of versions that appear in other splats. There's a lot in VtR's version to make you go &quot;huh?&quot; I'll leave it to the reader to search for the other threads.<br /> <br /> I'm not the one to contend that swarms are slow: nothing in VtR's version reduces their speed, plus you can use Celerity.<br /> <br /> I will contend that as written swarms *can* drop quite a bit of damage, which means you're pushing your brawl+Vigor as damage dice. In return, you're auto-reducing incoming damage to 1, and nothing says you cannot feed while a swarm, though the Storyteller would have to rule on whether blood could come from multiple targets as you spread damage around. While a Swarm Form vampire is not going to one-round OMGWTFBBQ an opponent, they are going to seriously mess them up on the long run, if they cannot immediately affect an escape. This is thematically appropriate I think.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. Again, Storytellers can &quot;fix&quot; Swarm Form to their taste, up to an including expanding the merit upwards to add the vamp's strength, or raise the Size of the swarm critters, or etc. Charge a bit of XP for a few more dots and don't worry about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T07:01:51-08:00","id":1156664,"title":"","content":"Note that a swarm doesn't have stats of a single member of the swarm, it has an aggregate. And so using the animal stats is the way to go. See below for the stats of a Swarm of Vermin per the Chronicles of Darkness Core book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD2Ep121</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>TRAINED GUARD DOG</b><br /> <br /> \u201c*bark! bark!* Grrrrr...\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>Description</i>: It\u2019s a Doberman Pinscher, a Rottweiler, or a German Shepherd. Its teeth are bared and its ears are pointed at you. You\u2019re in its territory and it plans to rip you to pieces with all its friends. It can track you wherever you run, and it\u2019s faster than you.<ul><li><b>Attributes</b>: Intelligence 1, Wits 4, Resolve 3, Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3, Presence 3, Manipulation 0, Composure 1</li> <li><b>General Dice Pools</b>: Born Survivor 7, Marathon Runner 7, Aggressive Growl 5</li> <li><b>Combat Dice Pools</b>: Bite 6, Tackle 6</li> <li><b>Initiative</b> <b>Modifier</b>: +5</li> <li><b>Defense</b>: 7</li> <li><b>Health</b>: 7</li> <li><b>Willpower</b>: 0</li> <li><b>Size</b>: 4</li> <li><b>Speed</b>: 12</li> </ul>Doubles as: K-9 hound, wild animal, <b>swarm of vermin</b>, genetic experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>One should of course modify this template for different kinds of swarms (bats/birds/etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T08:39:28-08:00","id":1156697,"title":"","content":"Can I use Stir the Beast to frenzy with the intent of harming or embarrass someone using Idol?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T09:09:28-08:00","id":1156707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156697#post1156697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use Stir the Beast to frenzy with the intent of harming or embarrass someone using Idol?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess just if you win the roll to act agaist her, then yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T11:51:27-08:00","id":1156749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156697#post1156697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I use Stir the Beast to frenzy with the intent of harming or embarrass someone using Idol?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Just not be in the vicinity when they turn on Idol or as you turn on frenzy. Or turn on frenzy before they activate Idol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-07-2017, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T12:28:01-08:00","id":1156762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156707#post1156707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess just if you win the roll to act agaist her, then yes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Like Marcus said you'd have to win the roll to act against. So you'd have to want to act against.. then win the roll to frenzy.. then win each subsequent round after to keep attacking. Even if you frenzy with the intent to harm someone, doesnt mean that you can keep doing it. It says that disciplines can be redirected while you are in a frenzy. So if you were in a kill frenzy and failed to attack the target you wanted, you would probably just go after an easier target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T13:24:35-08:00","id":1156778,"title":"","content":"it has to say some where in VTR 2 book but I cann\u2019t find it. how do kindred heal agg damage. Do they spend vitae or is it done over time. Please help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20755-seph038","name":"Seph038","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T13:42:02-08:00","id":1156783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seph038</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156778#post1156778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it has to say some where in VTR 2 book but I cann\u2019t find it. how do kindred heal agg damage. Do they spend vitae or is it done over time. Please help.</div> </div> </div> </div>5 vitae per 1 aggravated damage and a full day rest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T13:55:40-08:00","id":1156784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156783#post1156783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 5 vitae per 1 aggravated damage and a full day rest</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks you. I just couldn\u2019t find it in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20755-seph038","name":"Seph038","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T14:24:20-08:00","id":1156794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seph038</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156784#post1156784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks you. I just couldn\u2019t find it in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's exactly in the paragraph where it explain the healing: P. 91: Healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T16:27:46-08:00","id":1156833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156762#post1156762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Like Marcus said you'd have to win the roll to act against. So you'd have to want to act against.. then win the roll to frenzy.. then win each subsequent round after to keep attacking. Even if you frenzy with the intent to harm someone, doesnt mean that you can keep doing it. It says that disciplines can be redirected while you are in a frenzy. So if you were in a kill frenzy and failed to attack the target you wanted, you would probably just go after an easier target.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no roll for Stir the Beast, you just pay willpower and pick the objective of the frenzy so someone could pick &quot;teach Alice she can't use Idol to control me&quot; and let the beast do it's thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T17:18:52-08:00","id":1156841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156833#post1156833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no roll for Stir the Beast, you just pay willpower and pick the objective of the frenzy so someone could pick &quot;teach Alice she can't use Idol to control me&quot; and let the beast do it's thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And Alice could use Idol to show Bob that he cant use frenzy to attack her.. I am aware there is no roll to stir the beast, but there IS a roll to make sure you can attack the person with Idol. and it is an EVERY TURN roll. If you failed.. you would simply attack someone else, because as per the book, you can redirect frenzy with Disciplines. <br /> <br /> From the Book:<br /> <br /> For example, if Veronica falls to her Beast due to hunger and leaps at<br /> Elspeth, Elspeth might Dominate her to attack Dominic instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T18:12:05-08:00","id":1156850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156841#post1156841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the Book:<br /> <br /> For example, if Veronica falls to her Beast due to hunger and leaps at<br /> Elspeth, Elspeth might Dominate her to attack Dominic instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Diverting a frenzying vampire's attentions toward &quot;another, similar target&quot; doesn't strike me as very doable for &quot;demonstrate that this vampire cannot use their supernatural charisma to influence me.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T18:41:36-08:00","id":1156857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156841#post1156841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the Book:<br /> <br /> For example, if Veronica falls to her Beast due to hunger and leaps at<br /> Elspeth, Elspeth might Dominate her to attack Dominic instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>From 2 sentences before that one.<br /> &quot;If a character tries to coerce her behaviour contrary to the beast's desires, either via Social actions or through Disciplines, the effort fails.&quot;<br /> I already knew that being in frenzy could ignore idol I just wanted to check if I could go strait to frenzy or if I still needed to make the roll to activate Stir the Beast.<br /> Thanks for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T20:29:59-08:00","id":1156885,"title":"","content":"As you pointed out *contrary to the desires* it fails. So if you go into a kill frenzy and try to make it a fear frenzy.. it fails. But as the book explicitly states.. you can change a hungry frenzy for a hunger frenzy. Those words are directly from the book. So I don\u2019t know why you think it\u2019s not possible. <br /> <br /> A frenzy doesn\u2019t ignore idol.. why wouldn\u2019t it just switch the target like the example in the book. If a level 1 Dominate can switch the target a level 5 power better be able to as well. <br /> <br /> Also you can\u2019t use frenzy to give commands like \u201cmake sure this vampire can\u2019t use disciplines on Me.\u201d Pretty sure you get three options, kill, feed, run.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as Marcus and I both said already. You'd Have to make the roll to even want to attack the Idol user. It\u2019s very clearly stated, \u201cyou can\u2019t so much as crack a joke\u201d if you don\u2019t make the roll. Why would frenzy be less harmful than a joke? Then I would think you need to roll every subsequent turn as per the Idol rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-07-2017, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T21:17:22-08:00","id":1156892,"title":"","content":"If the Frenzy goal is &quot;kill Bob&quot; then Bob's Idol will fail, because Disciplines can't go against the Frenzy goal.<br /> <br /> If the Frenzy goal is &quot;kill someone&quot; then Bob's Idol will succeed, because Disciplines can redirect the target so long as it doesn't go against the Frenzy goal.<br /> <br /> This is one of the benefits to being able to set the goal, rather than fall victim to a Frenzy where the Beast (ST) picks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T21:38:57-08:00","id":1156895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156885#post1156885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure you get three options, kill, feed, run.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A target or goal, no more than a few words.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Defy the Idol</i><i>-user</i> is reasonably succinct, as are most other specified goals targeting the vampire attempting to thwart you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But as Marcus and I both said already. You'd Have to make the roll to even want to attack the Idol user. It\u2019s very clearly stated, \u201cyou can\u2019t so much as crack a joke\u201d if you don\u2019t make the roll. </div> </div> </div>It's also very directly implied that Idol works as a modification to Awe, <i>which you are explicitly able to resist by lashing out, which even a vampire in frenzy can do</i>. Better still, frenzy boosts one form of predatory aura (somewhat ambiguously in the case of the default bonus and explicitly in the case of the next tier of the Coil that is under discussion here). Countering the &quot;softest&quot; vampiric archetype with the most brutal one is within spec.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T22:27:23-08:00","id":1156901,"title":"","content":"Awe can be broken by Lashing Out, yeah, but Lashing Out at someone who has Idol active would definitely be one of those things that requires you to succeed at the Resolve + BP - Majesty to be able to do, if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-08-2017, 02:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T00:02:36-08:00","id":1156915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156857#post1156857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From 2 sentences before that one.<br /> &quot;If a character tries to coerce her behaviour contrary to the beast's desires, either via Social actions or through Disciplines, the effort fails.&quot;<br /> I already knew that being in frenzy could ignore idol I just wanted to check if I could go strait to frenzy or if I still needed to make the roll to activate Stir the Beast.<br /> Thanks for the answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll better explain my point:<br /> With stir the beast you can go in Frenzy without a provocation; you can even punch at someone with no provocation. For sure you can argue or say something against someone.<br /> I'm pretty sure that be aware to be under Majesty effect could be considererd as a big provocation to go into Frenzy even without stir the beast.<br /> <br /> IDOL do not allow you to do anything, even speak, against its user, no because a threathen but because you feel completely subjugated by.the vampire.<br /> For this reason I would say that you really wouldn't want to go frenzy against the vampire. So if you know you are under majesty and want to force ylurself to go frenzy against your &quot;subjugated&quot; will, you must win the majesty roll: resolve+bp - majesty. Then, if you win, you could use that very turn to stir the beast.<br /> <br /> Majesty in general, even the 1st power, if take effect and wins the contested aura rolls, wouldn't allow the affected character to go in frenzy.<br /> <br /> If not this is what would happen:<br /> <br /> 1) I use majesty 1. <br /> <br /> 2) Ok roll your aura vs the npc one<br /> <br /> 1) I win<br /> <br /> 2) ok npc go int frenzy since you are forcing her free will.<br /> <br /> 1) d'ho<br /> <br /> Making Majesty useless (vs other supernaturals at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-08-2017, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T02:20:53-08:00","id":1156933,"title":"","content":"As I understand it it goes.<br /> Character 1 activates Idol.<br /> Character 2 rolls Resolve + Blood Potency and if successful can spend a point of Willpower to activate Stir the Beast.<br /> Assuming the objective set requires harm to come to C1 C2s beast will ignore the effects of idol while pursuing its objective.<br /> <br /> Now I've noticed that Lay Open the Mind doesn't list a range or state that it requires line of sight, it seems unwise to allow someone to read the mind of the Prince from the safty of their own haven and I'm sure that this behaviour would have been brought up if it was intended so what is everyone's take on this? I'm inclined to go with you need to be able to perceive the target such as hearing their voice or seeing them (not by phone or CCTV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T03:35:33-08:00","id":1156947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156933#post1156933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it it goes.<br /> Character 1 activates Idol.<br /> Character 2 rolls Resolve + Blood Potency and if successful can spend a point of Willpower to activate Stir the Beast.<br /> Assuming the objective set requires harm to come to C1 C2s beast will ignore the effects of idol while pursuing its objective.<br /> <br /> Now I've noticed that Lay Open the Mind doesn't list a range or state that it requires line of sight, it seems unwise to allow someone to read the mind of the Prince from the safty of their own haven and I'm sure that this behaviour would have been brought up if it was intended so what is everyone's take on this? I'm inclined to go with you need to be able to perceive the target such as hearing their voice or seeing them (not by phone or CCTV.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my view it should go: <br /> <br /> C1 activate awe<br /> C2 and C1 contest with their own aura<br /> If C1 wins he reflexively activate Idol<br /> C2 try to act against him, going into frenzy and rolls: resolve+bp minus Majesty. <br /> If C2 wins the rolls he spend a wp to stir the beast. <br /> C2 can now attack him but C1 probably would use majesty 2/3 to divert his frenzy on someone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-08-2017, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T03:38:20-08:00","id":1156950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156901#post1156901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awe can be broken by Lashing Out, yeah, but Lashing Out at someone who has Idol active would definitely be one of those things that requires you to succeed at the Resolve + BP - Majesty to be able to do, if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my reading awe can be resisted just at the activation time (or as soon as you enter in a room with an awe user) and not later. Am I wrong?<br /> <br /> This will exclude by rule further lashing out attempts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T08:52:51-08:00","id":1157024,"title":"","content":"It's been pointed out many many times on these forums (by Rose herself) that you do NOT get a memo saying you are under the effects of awe. ( or even Charm, and Idol ) That it is not something you KNOW is happening. Unless you know that Said Vampire can do awe and often uses it, then you wouldn't have any reason to suspect that you are under some sort of supernatural pull. Once Idol has been kicked off, it's far too late to just simply break awe and be done with it.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, you have to resist awe at the time it's turned on. (Same with Dread Presence.) So say you lash out because you think they are doing something funky and they aren't , then you're the one that's in trouble.<br /> <br /> Also, Since Idol is Reflexive and Awe is instant, you can do them both on your turn. Awe, then immediately Idol. I would not let any character just simply roll to lash out just because a vampire did Awe. That goes back to you aren't suppose to know it's happening to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156933#post1156933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it it goes.<br /> Character 1 activates Idol.<br /> Character 2 rolls Resolve + Blood Potency and if successful can spend a point of Willpower to activate Stir the Beast.<br /> Assuming the objective set requires harm to come to C1 C2s beast will ignore the effects of idol while pursuing its objective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Character 2 rolls Resolve + BP - 5 and if successful he can spend WP ( assuming he isnt enthralled )<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156895#post1156895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;A target or goal, no more than a few words.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Defy the Idol</i><i>-user</i> is reasonably succinct, as are most other specified goals targeting the vampire attempting to thwart you.</div> </div> </div> </div>personally I dont think &quot;Defy&quot; is a good enough goal for Frenzy, because it's too vague. What does defy actually mean in the context of the situation? Spit in the vampire's face? Not get into the car with them? Kill them? Eat them? Knock them out? Not drink the purple koolaid? Show the other people in the room they aren't cool? That's why I think the goal has to be short and specific. There are many threads in here that while in frenzy you can't do wildly thoughtful or execute mastermind plots. Because it is so very primal and down to the baser instincts. Fight, Flight, Feed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156947#post1156947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">C2 can now attack him but C1 probably would use majesty 2/3 to divert his frenzy on someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the goal is to Kill Idol User, Why wouldn't idol just redirect that to someone else if you are saying that Charm would be able to redirect it? Also I do not understand why people don't think Idol would redirect &quot;Kill Idol User&quot; to someone else if the book gives the example that &quot;Eating Elspeth&quot; can be redirected to &quot;Eat Dominic&quot; Obviously the goal/ target of the initial frenzy was to attack and eat Elspeth and the book states that Elspeth, redirected it to eat Dominic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-08-2017, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:10:33-08:00","id":1157044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157024#post1157024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been pointed out many many times on these forums (by Rose herself) that you do NOT get a memo saying you are under the effects of awe. ( or even Charm, and Idol ) That it is not something you KNOW is happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conscious knowledge is generally not something that the Beast troubles itself too much with and <i>growling</i> (much less any of the other kinds of actions taken to simply invoke an aspect of the Beast) is kind of far beneath the threshold of harm or embarrassment. Lashing out already costs Willpower and doesn't have great odds of success against superior opposition compared to a flatly penalized resistance roll, either.<br /> <br /> It's a safe bet that the insulation lashing out provides against certain Disciplines is built on having the bonus for winning the conflict in the case of a contested challenge, and given that Awe is the first example of that insulation in the book I'd think it's within the realm of intended use that lashing out in defense can either be done instinctively or without breaking the terms of Majesty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> personally I dont think &quot;Defy&quot; is a good enough goal for Frenzy, because it's too vague. [\u2026] That's why I think the goal has to be short and specific. </div> </div> </div>Most other specified goals to that end are similarly succinct. &quot;Drive King out of the room,&quot; &quot;Visibly harm King,&quot; and similar can be described in short sentences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are many threads in here that while in frenzy you can't do wildly thoughtful or execute mastermind plots. Because it is so very primal and down to the baser instincts. Fight, Flight, Feed. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon&quot; is not incompatible with &quot;attack/humiliate/escape [the vampire who is attempting to be untouchable and in control of the room].&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I do not understand why people don't think Idol would redirect &quot;Kill Idol User&quot; to someone else if the book gives the example that &quot;Eating Elspeth&quot; can be redirected to &quot;Eat Dominic&quot; Obviously the goal/ target of the initial frenzy was to attack and eat Elspeth and the book states that Elspeth, redirected it to eat Dominic. </div> </div> </div>Because the Elspeth example is for a regular hunger-based frenzy and Stir the Beast is neither a regular frenzy nor likely to be invoked for the sake of hunger alone. If only one person in the room fits the bill for &quot;punish the person who insulted the Beast's host,&quot; then blunt redirection isn't an option.<br /> <br /> Having functional control of some number of other people in the room enables some level of maneuvering to <i>produce an alternative target</i> to redirect to, but even assuming the Beast won't recognize directives tied to specific individuals the range of possible redirection is not created equal for every stimulus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:36:55-08:00","id":1157051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157024#post1157024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the goal is to Kill Idol User, Why wouldn't idol just redirect that to someone else if you are saying that Charm would be able to redirect it? Also I do not understand why people don't think Idol would redirect &quot;Kill Idol User&quot; to someone else if the book gives the example that &quot;Eating Elspeth&quot; can be redirected to &quot;Eat Dominic&quot; Obviously the goal/ target of the initial frenzy was to attack and eat Elspeth and the book states that Elspeth, redirected it to eat Dominic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Idol itself does not allow any kind of command while charmed and enthralled do. Idol, in my view, is an overwhelming enhancment of your presence that let you appear as a God. <br /> <br /> I.e. You would think 100 times before to attack or argue with the CEO of your company even if you think he ia wrog and he is humiliating you, but if you get too angry.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:54:06-08:00","id":1157056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157051#post1157051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because Idol itself does not allow any kind of command while charmed and enthralled do. Idol, in my view, is an overwhelming enhancment of your presence that let you appear as a God.<br /> <br /> I.e. You would think 100 times before to attack or argue with the CEO of your company even if you think he ia wrog and he is humiliating you, but if you get too angry.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people keep their composure with their boss even if they are too angry and go vent about it later. Idol very much puts up a bubble around the user which makes you have to roll to actually attack them. that means you actually have to try to fight their power to attack them. It is an unspoken &quot;Don't attack me&quot; command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T11:26:34-08:00","id":1157070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157024#post1157024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the goal is to Kill Idol User, Why wouldn't idol just redirect that to someone else if you are saying that Charm would be able to redirect it? Also I do not understand why people don't think Idol would redirect &amp;quot;Kill Idol User&amp;quot; to someone else if the book gives the example that &amp;quot;Eating Elspeth&amp;quot; can be redirected to &amp;quot;Eat Dominic&amp;quot; Obviously the goal/ target of the initial frenzy was to attack and eat Elspeth and the book states that Elspeth, redirected it to eat Dominic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules in the book explicitly say that no social skill or discipline can get the beast to act against its desire.<br /> &quot;If a character tries to coerce her behaviour contrary to the beast's desires, either via Social actions or through Disciplines, the effort fails.&quot;<br /> The example given about redirecting a frenzying vampire with dominate was a frenzy with the aim &quot;feed&quot; so &quot;eat him not me&quot; didn't prevent the desired outcome, a frenzy with the desire &quot;put this idol happy whore in her place&quot; could be redirected from beating her into torpor to having her beg you to stop but not beating someone else into torpor unless that would prove to the intended victim that you could hurt people that they were trying to protect and as the beast is direct it probably wouldn't occur to the beast that that was a valid way to achieve its goal. If it was obvious after you did it that you had made your point the frenzy could then end and you would be back under idol to someone terrified of you and very upset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T19:47:42-08:00","id":1157179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157070#post1157070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The rules in the book explicitly say that no social skill or discipline can get the beast to act against its desire.<br /> &quot;If a character tries to coerce her behaviour contrary to the beast's desires, either via Social actions or through Disciplines, the effort fails.&quot;<br /> The example given about redirecting a frenzying vampire with dominate was a frenzy with the aim &quot;feed&quot; so &quot;eat him not me&quot; didn't prevent the desired outcome, a frenzy with the desire &quot;put this idol happy whore in her place&quot; could be redirected from beating her into torpor to having her beg you to stop but not beating someone else into torpor unless that would prove to the intended victim that you could hurt people that they were trying to protect and as the beast is direct it probably wouldn't occur to the beast that that was a valid way to achieve its goal. If it was obvious after you did it that you had made your point the frenzy could then end and you would be back under idol to someone terrified of you and very upset.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can argue this in total circles. Your opinion on what is possible in a redirect differs from mine. <b>It says Disciplines fail if it's in direct conflict, however you can redirect them</b>. You have to take both sentences. I think Idol can redirect, that it is not directly in conflict. Your beast wants to hurt someone. hurt someone else and that might be sufficient to hurt the idol user too. actually win win as it might hurt them both! Especially if that someone is a loved one. There is more than one way to hurt someone. Again I think a direct conflict would be telling the beast to stop fighting, to run away, To feed instead of kill. But kill for kill... is right in line with it.<br /> <br /> Also. I think everyone else in the room would protect the Idol User. They would try to stop the user from getting hurt because they wouldn't want that. That's what the power does.. It makes it so you don't want to hurt them. Then again. you might not think that's what Idol does and that's fine too. <br /> <br /> You have mentioned that Stir the beast is not a normal frenzy however. it says right in stir the beast, that you have no more control than you normally would once you are in a frenzy. So, ultimately you will do what works for your games, and I will do what works for mine. That is perfectly acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T20:19:39-08:00","id":1157182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157179#post1157179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also. I think everyone else in the room would protect the Idol User. They would try to stop the user from getting hurt because they wouldn't want that. That's what the power does.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a function of the Enthralled Condition, which Idol interacts with but does not directly cause just by activating Awe and Idol in a room full of unprimed people.<br /> <br /> The base effect of Idol without respect to the Conditions applied by subsidiary powers is &quot;it is incredibly difficult for characters to act against the vampire due to how untouchably superior she seems.&quot;<br /> <br /> Using Idol allows you to accelerate multiple people from neutral to an abbreviated version of Enthralled for cheap, but on its own Idol does not do anything other than make the vampire feel fascinating, forgivable, and important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T03:03:44-08:00","id":1157232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1156850#post1156850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diverting a frenzying vampire's attentions toward &quot;another, similar target&quot; doesn't strike me as very doable for &quot;demonstrate that this vampire cannot use their supernatural charisma to influence me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind the actual difficulties of striking eye contact with a frenzied individual bent of ripping you apart with their bare claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T04:21:00-08:00","id":1157243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157232#post1157232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nevermind the actual difficulties of striking eye contact with a frenzied individual bent of ripping you apart with their bare claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rose said that the eyes contact is more a flavor statement and that it's part of the standard dominate roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-09-2017, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T04:24:28-08:00","id":1157245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157243#post1157243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rose said that the eyes contact is more a flavor statement and that it's part of the standard dominate roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it should be penalized by say, Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T04:48:31-08:00","id":1157249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157245#post1157245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then it should be penalized by say, Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How about it's penalized by a contested roll of a resistance attribute and powerstat? Like it is already. <br /> What have defense with it to do? You mean you don't look you opponent in the face in a fight and that should be portrayed by defense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T05:06:01-08:00","id":1157252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157245#post1157245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then it should be penalized by say, Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't understand why it should.<br /> <br /> Wits in the roll stands for the purpose to meet the gaze at the right moment. You are not shooting laser beams from your eyes (that should be with no defense penality as well xD)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T08:52:46-08:00","id":1157288,"title":"","content":"<b>Grapple:</b><br /> <br /> Hi guys, trying grapple in my Vampire Chronicle, i've found some problems about the use of grapple maneuvers.<br /> <br /> <b>1)</b> Is trying to get in grapple an opponent considered an attack? Can I , to make an example , do it with the second attack granted by Street Fighting 5?<br /> <br /> <b>2)</b> Some merits ( such as Police Tactics 1) give a bonus if you choose to use one specific maneuver. The problem is : you choose the maneuver <i>after </i>rolling the dices. To use the bonus must i declare wich maneuver i use <i>before</i> i roll or must i add some dices after the main roll is done?<br /> <br /> <b>3)</b> Is There a difference between who<i> resists </i>an Overpower Maneuver and who <i>makes</i> the same? If not wich is the sense of Grappling 1?<br /> <br /> <b>4) If during the highest initiative of the two I break the grapple and I have the lowest initiative, do i get to act in my initiative level?<br /> <br /> 5) Most importantly, in order to use a power that does not require to move to be used( as Majesty or Nightmare) do I need to win a grapple maneuver to succeed?<br /> Must I give up resisting the grapple (usually getting a lot of damage) to use the power? </b><br /> <br /> Thank you for you answers ! Bye","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13629-strikeforce1","name":"strikeforce1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T09:16:01-08:00","id":1157296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strikeforce1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157288#post1157288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Grapple:</b><br /> <br /> Hi guys, trying grapple in my Vampire Chronicle, i've found some problems about the use of grapple maneuvers.<br /> <br /> <b>1)</b> Is trying to get in grapple an opponent considered an attack? Can I , to make an example , do it with the second attack granted by Street Fighting 5?<br /> <br /> <b>2)</b> Some merits ( such as Police Tactics 1) give a bonus if you choose to use one specific maneuver. The problem is : you choose the maneuver <i>after </i>rolling the dices. To use the bonus must i declare wich maneuver i use <i>before</i> i roll or must i add some dices after the main roll is done?<br /> <br /> <b>3)</b> Is There a difference between who<i> resists </i>an Overpower Maneuver and who <i>makes</i> the same? If not wich is the sense of Grappling 1?<br /> <br /> <b>4) If during the highest initiative of the two I break the grapple and I have the lowest initiative, do i get to act in my initiative level?<br /> <br /> 5) Most importantly, in order to use a power that does not require to move to be used( as Majesty or Nightmare) do I need to win a grapple maneuver to succeed?<br /> Must I give up resisting the grapple (usually getting a lot of damage) to use the power? </b><br /> <br /> Thank you for you answers ! Bye</div> </div> </div> </div>1) yes, grapple is an attack, in fact you subtract defense to your grapple roll.<br /> <br /> 2) you choose it first to roll. As soon as your initiative comes<br /> <br /> 3) don't know.<br /> <br /> 4) no. Your action in that turn IS to break the grapple. In the next turn you will act again at your own initiative.<br /> <br /> 5) no you don't need to win the grapple to use mental discipline but yes you should give up resisting it. With the logical exception of Dominate. If someone is taking you from.behind you can't meet his gaze. But it's not ruled, just up to the storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T11:30:05-08:00","id":1157319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157296#post1157296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 4) no. Your action in that turn IS to break the grapple. In the next turn you will act again at your own initiative.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Page 89 in CoD rulebook<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Break Free from the grapple. The character throws off his opponent; they\u2019re both no longer grappling. Succeeding at this move is a reflexive action, so the character can take another action immediately afterwards. </div> </div> </div>So I believe the one that manages to break the grapple can do their action (but no movement?), the loser loses their turn, for that round. Seems like the winner has their action at that initiative point for that round, but goes back to their normal initiative on later rounds.<br /> <br /> Also with an exceptional success I think you can do the damage maneuver, then use break free, then attack with a normal attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 11-09-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T12:37:17-08:00","id":1157337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157319#post1157319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 89 in CoD rulebook<br /> <br /> So I believe the one that manages to break the grapple can do their action (but no movement?), the loser loses their turn, for that round. Seems like the winner has their action at that initiative point for that round, but goes back to their normal initiative on later rounds.<br /> <br /> Also with an exceptional success I think you can do the damage maneuver, then use break free, then attack with a normal attack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oh I missed this. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:38:21-08:00","id":1157576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157319#post1157319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also with an exceptional success I think you can do the damage maneuver, then use break free, then attack with a normal attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can still only take one instant action per turn. The damage maneuver is an instant action, so you could not then take an attack action if breaking out on the exceptional success (unless you have fighting style which lets you make a Reflexive attack of some sort.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T09:58:51-08:00","id":1157580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157182#post1157182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a function of the Enthralled Condition, which Idol interacts with but does not directly cause just by activating Awe and Idol in a room full of unprimed people.<br /> <br /> The base effect of Idol without respect to the Conditions applied by subsidiary powers is &quot;it is incredibly difficult for characters to act against the vampire due to how untouchably superior she seems.&quot;<br /> <br /> Using Idol allows you to accelerate multiple people from neutral to an abbreviated version of Enthralled for cheap, but on its own Idol does not do anything other than make the vampire feel fascinating, forgivable, and important.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that you would not try to save someone who is awesome fascinating or important? Someone who feel is just utterly divine? I know that If I saw someone about to be attacked. Even if I didn't know them or were under some crazy mind control power... I would try to help them. Especially if the Idol user said, &quot;Help me&quot; it would be incredibly difficult to act against that person's desire for help.. As you said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157245#post1157245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then it should be penalized by say, Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a huge thread about eye contact during the middle of a fight. It's possible, there is no negative. It is what it is. To recap, every good fighter watches the other's eyes instead of hands or feet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-10-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T10:05:35-08:00","id":1157582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To recap, every good fighter watches the other's eyes instead of hands or feet.</div> </div> </div> </div>A) That's some bullshit. B) it's physically impossible when you're doing something like grappling or chewing their throats off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T10:35:06-08:00","id":1157589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157580#post1157580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're saying that you would not try to save someone who is awesome fascinating or important? Someone who feel is just utterly divine? I know that If I saw someone about to be attacked. Even if I didn't know them or were under some crazy mind control power... I would try to help them. Especially if the Idol user said, &quot;Help me&quot; it would be incredibly difficult to act against that person's desire for help.. As you said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again: The things you are talking about are represented by the way Idol interacts with the intermediate levels of Majesty. Its baseline utility is giving you space to work the room and establish the chain of Conditions that correspond to that utter fanatical loyalty. An extra five dice on a roll to tell people to help you does not translate to &quot;the Idol asked me for help and I would willingly court death for their favor&quot; on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T12:21:56-08:00","id":1157609,"title":"","content":"Dominate does not require a vampire to look at someone's eyes. It requires someone to look at the vampire's eyes. There is a penalty to avoid looking at someone's eyes while attacking or defending. Obviously, fighting while distracted will give a penalty. There is no penalty to make eye contact while defending. Looking at someone attacking you is going to be standard. It still doesn't matter for Dominate since eye contact is defined as someone looking at the vampire's eyes. There would be some grapple moves that could prevent a Dominate roll altogether if they are already in place before a Dominate attempt can begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T13:01:25-08:00","id":1157620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157580#post1157580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you're saying that you would not try to save someone who is awesome fascinating or important? Someone who feel is just utterly divine? I know that If I saw someone about to be attacked. Even if I didn't know them or were under some crazy mind control power... I would try to help them. Especially if the Idol user said, &amp;quot;Help me&amp;quot; it would be incredibly difficult to act against that person's desire for help.. As you said.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best argument against this is the lack of a condition, 2nd edition gives conditions for everything so if one is not provided I would assume that there is no intent for such an interpretation of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T17:28:28-08:00","id":1157661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157582#post1157582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A) That's some bullshit. B) it's physically impossible when you're doing something like grappling or chewing their throats off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Watch an MMA fight or a boxing fight. they do not stare at hands and feet. So I am not sure why you think that's bullshit? Take some Tae Kwon Do classes or something. They literally teach you to watch your opponent's eyes... Second. Yes. If you are already grappled or pinned or whatever, you're right you can't make eye contact, The Ruling in the other thread was that you did not get a penalty to Dominate while in combat. Not because you're distracted or anything... otherwise every fight with multiple people would give you a negative for being distracted with the other attackers...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4714\" data-vbnamecard=\"4714\">Live Bait</a> There are plenty of things that don't have conditions. Frenzy, Blush of Life. Any of the 5th dot powers. Just because it's not listed doesn't mean you dont use common sense and close reading to interpret the intentions of the power. Like the whole ghoul thing and Devotions. It wasn't listed that they could but with some logic and common sense you could figure out it was intended. Then a developer dove in and confirmed it. If an almighty divine power was in the room asking for help because some psycho frenzied monster was trying to kill it... You help it. Or you roll Resolve+BP - 5 to go against the wishes of the vampire. Because NOT helping it is CAUSING HARM. and as we know Idol says we can't cause them harm without Resolve+BP - 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-10-2017, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T19:56:49-08:00","id":1157683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157661#post1157661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an almighty divine power was in the room asking for help because some psycho frenzied monster was trying to kill it... You help it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you rightly assume the untouchable god-monster can take care of itself with regards to berserker offenses better than mere mortal you can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or you roll Resolve+BP - 5 to go against the wishes of the vampire. Because NOT helping it is CAUSING HARM. and as we know Idol says we can't cause them harm without Resolve+BP - 5. </div> </div> </div>The principle of harm does not work on an unstated equivalence for the First Law of Robotics. Not throwing yourself in front of a speeding Gangrel is not the same thing as acting against the Idol because the Enthralled Condition is what represents that &quot;or through inaction allow the Idol to come to harm&quot; caveat that you're assuming is innate to the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T02:13:58-08:00","id":1157719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1157582#post1157582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A) That's some bullshit. B) it's physically impossible when you're doing something like grappling or chewing their throats off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can say it for experience: Someone teach you to look at the eyes of your opponent, someone else teach to look at his shoulder to have a peripheral vision of the whole body. But It's impossible to never look at the opponent eyes, even for just an instant, and even if you are directly trying to not watch at them. You should stay still with a silly and rigid expression. If you are fighting and are distracted, eyes watch around in a blink without you could even notice it. Eyes move constantly and without always a `conscious willing.<br /> In a grappling (from behind) or bite at her throat I could agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-11-2017, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T10:36:38-08:00","id":1158210,"title":"","content":"When a vampire frenzies, does it look any different? I know protean makes a vamp transform, but does a vampire without any points in protean change due to the beast surfacing during frenzy or rage? <br /> <br /> -Also, much love to everyone here! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T10:48:01-08:00","id":1158215,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it does to an extent. People who are pissed off look different than they do when they're happy. Do these changes convey any sort of bonus above and beyond what they get for being in frenzy like shooting death beams from their glowing eyes or super senses, or better swimming ability from webbed hands. Not unless your ST allows it. I allow minor changes for cosmetic purposes to encourage players to be more descriptive and award bonus XP if its consistant but not mechanical bonuses for combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T11:24:02-08:00","id":1158228,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Brassfit referred to just cosmetic changes like buffy. <br /> I usually describe frenzy vamp as full black eyes, theet extremely long and face lineament more marked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T20:21:26-08:00","id":1158326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brassfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1158210#post1158210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a vampire frenzies, does it look any different? I know protean makes a vamp transform, but does a vampire without any points in protean change due to the beast surfacing during frenzy or rage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Published banes can affect the vampire's appearance based on hunger; it certainly wouldn't be beyond reason for a variant based on different stimuli and Attributes to exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T05:34:53-08:00","id":1158428,"title":"","content":"Fangs out, eyes are (depending on frenzy provocation) filled with hate, predatory hunger or wide eyed fear, face may be twisted into a snarl or completely void of emotion. The key to identifying a frenzy is really the behaviour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T15:10:00-08:00","id":1158655,"title":"","content":"Your beast should be able to feel when another is unleashed, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T16:30:49-08:00","id":1158699,"title":"","content":"Where can I find the &quot;Impaled&quot; tilt (Thrown Weapon Style, Hurt Locker)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T20:04:49-08:00","id":1158754,"title":"","content":"does a vampire incur any penealties if trying to lash out at their sire via disciplines or any other attack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T20:43:31-08:00","id":1158758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1158754#post1158754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does a vampire incur any penealties if trying to lash out at their sire via disciplines or any other attack?</div> </div> </div> </div>They actually get a bonus.<br /> <br /> P99, under Discipline Sympathies. 'As well as feeling the sensations of their relatives, vampires are more capable of using their Disciplines on those with whom they share blood ties. If a vampire uses a Discipline on a relative, add the blood sympathy bonus to the roll. Rolls made to enact Cr\u00faac sorcery use double this modifier.'<br /> <br /> That said, often but not always a sire will be of higher Blood Potency than their childe. Higher Blood Potency often means greater supernatural tolerance against a variety of Disciplines, and responding to a vampire with higher Blood Potency Lashing Out requires a Willpower, as mentioned on p92.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T02:51:43-08:00","id":1158836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1158699#post1158699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I find the &quot;Impaled&quot; tilt (Thrown Weapon Style, Hurt Locker)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe there is a typo in that part, the tilt is actually called &quot;Pinned&quot;. It's on page 143.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T04:12:13-08:00","id":1158866,"title":"","content":"Thanks, one of my players wanted to know if he could stake someone with it because that seemed too good to be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T09:31:34-08:00","id":1158991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emmens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1158754#post1158754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does a vampire incur any penealties if trying to lash out at their sire via disciplines or any other attack?</div> </div> </div> </div> depends. Did the site remember to put a bit of Vinc on the new vampire?<br /> <br /> joking aside, there are no mechanical penalties, but there are easy ways around all vampire disciplines. Lashing out, avoiding eye contact, tracking clues, clash of wills. Things a sire has a better chance of winning. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T12:43:21-08:00","id":1159975,"title":"","content":"Is Dominate 4 able to/intended to permit removal of skill dots? Their suppression (i.e. Amnesia Condition)?<br /> <br /> If yes, would you limit such to a specific category or categories of skills (mental, physical, social)?<br /> <br /> I assume that it could not be used to <i>implant</i> skills, as that's against the theme of vampire powers.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T12:54:19-08:00","id":1159979,"title":"","content":"I could see it working for mental skills but for the most part it would be a case of not knowing where you heard something, you may be more willing to believe someone who tells you you're wrong but you could still blurt out pi or the correct leagal term on demand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T16:19:15-08:00","id":1160037,"title":"","content":"For the swarm form merit it states that a success allows you to take 1 vitae. Is this per success or is it limited to one vitae no matter how many successes you get?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1785-giles","name":"Giles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T16:30:25-08:00","id":1160043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1159979#post1159979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see it working for mental skills but for the most part it would be a case of not knowing where you heard something, you may be more willing to believe someone who tells you you're wrong but you could still blurt out pi or the correct leagal term on demand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. So this is how you get a Jason Bourne-character. Had fine skills and &quot;forgot&quot; how he learned them, but still there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T03:43:07-08:00","id":1160164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Giles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1160037#post1160037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the swarm form merit it states that a success allows you to take 1 vitae. Is this per success or is it limited to one vitae no matter how many successes you get?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go with one, very few things allow you to drink more than one Vitae per turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T03:59:04-08:00","id":1160165,"title":"","content":"Subtle feeding is limited to 1 Vitae/turn while violent feeding grants successes Vitae/turn to a maximum of the vampire's Blood Potency. I think Swarm Form should follow the regular rules for violent feeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T05:07:28-08:00","id":1160170,"title":"","content":"But as it uses a fight roll I would assume it's already a violent feeding so it's probably 1 per success ( but not with the usual added lethal?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1785-giles","name":"Giles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T05:09:58-08:00","id":1160171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1160164#post1160164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would go with one, very few things allow you to drink more than one Vitae per turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Tessie said, violent feeding allow you to ingest BP vitae per turn but reading again the swarm form it seems also to me that you can get only a Vitae if you win the strength+Brawl roll (even without damage maybe).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T05:53:04-08:00","id":1160182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1160171#post1160171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Tessie said, violent feeding allow you to ingest BP vitae per turn but reading again the swarm form it seems also to me that you can get only a Vitae if you win the strength+Brawl roll (even without damage maybe).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's how I read it, but that seems really inefficient which makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1785-giles","name":"Giles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T07:06:28-08:00","id":1160198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1160165#post1160165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Subtle feeding is limited to 1 Vitae/turn while violent feeding grants successes Vitae/turn to a maximum of the vampire's Blood Potency. I think Swarm Form should follow the regular rules for violent feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought this was the case but p94 of Blood &amp; Smoke says it gives only one, can you give me a source on the pre success rule? I'd like to be able to help people if they make the same mistake I did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T07:28:56-08:00","id":1160207,"title":"","content":"Read the whole section on pages 94-95. It says that the bite move takes one Vitae, but the bite move is only the lead in to the feed move that takes successes amounts of Vitae.<br /> <br /> &quot;She steals one Vitae per success. Against mortals, this causes one point of lethal damage per Vitae taken. The number of Vitae taken may not exceed the vampire\u2019s Blood Potency dots.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T08:01:47-08:00","id":1160214,"title":"","content":"Many thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T12:01:09-08:00","id":1160272,"title":"","content":"Ok would the swarm form be able to do the feeding as normal or do the swarm attack or are they just limited to to swarm attack or 1 vitae and no damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1785-giles","name":"Giles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:23:37-08:00","id":1160330,"title":"","content":"I would say &quot;Alternatively, a success may instead allow the vampire to take one Vitae from the victim.&quot; Means you can mix damage and taking Vitae how you wish. Remember that drawing Vitae from anyone who doesn't have the ability to store it (not a kindred, ghoul or Strix) does one lethal damage per Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T19:36:43-08:00","id":1160392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1160330#post1160330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say &quot;Alternatively, a success may instead allow the vampire to take one Vitae from the victim.&quot; Means you can mix damage and taking Vitae how you wish. Remember that drawing Vitae from anyone who doesn't have the ability to store it (not a kindred, ghoul or Strix) does one lethal damage per Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's how I would rule it as well.(but keeping in mind that no more vitae stolen / turn than blood potency).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T15:36:10-08:00","id":1160669,"title":"","content":"I would say no to regular feeding (on conscious targets) because it causes panic and anyone inside gets the Distracted Condition.<br /> As for Vitae in combat, it originally thought it meant that if you hit, you get to take one Vitae. After re-reading however, it appears that &quot;Alternately, a success may instead allow the vampire to take one Vitae from a victim.&quot; seems more likely to mean that each success pulls one Vitae.<br /> This interpretation also works with the previous sentence which talks about dividing successes between those inside the swarm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T05:19:31-08:00","id":1160819,"title":"","content":"If someone lasses out agenst my character and does not have I higher Blood Potecy than me can I use Willpower to increase my dice pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T05:33:25-08:00","id":1160823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1160819#post1160819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone lasses out agenst my character and does not have I higher Blood Potecy than me can I use Willpower to increase my dice pool?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yes<br /> <br /> <br /> (characters)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T20:31:28-08:00","id":1161406,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Stun</b></u><br /> <br /> Hi guys , I was wondering if : a)The stun tilt is appplicable to Vampires in the same manner it is to nomal humans.<br /> b) The stun tilt must be employed when one gets more damages than his stamina or just after a direct attack to the head as written in the Tilt.<br /> <br /> Thanks and bye <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13629-strikeforce1","name":"strikeforce1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T02:36:30-08:00","id":1161454,"title":"","content":"We've had this come up, yes you can stun vampires. The head/anywhere question was not to my understanding agreed I'm afraid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T20:13:54-08:00","id":1162071,"title":"","content":"Is Conditioning (the Dominate Devotion) really supposed to used Wits and not Int, it seems really strange to me. Anyone know the rationale for it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T23:47:35-08:00","id":1162107,"title":"","content":"Always about Dominate:<br /> Mesmerism allows to impress 4 words commands. Does a command like: &quot;execute all my commands&quot; (as per the example of iron edict) allows to give all commands without any lengths restriction for a scene? Can you explain me better the mechanic behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-24-2017, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T04:50:34-08:00","id":1162146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodyquill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1162071#post1162071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Conditioning (the Dominate Devotion) really supposed to used Wits and not Int, it seems really strange to me. Anyone know the rationale for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rationale is that they just did a cut and paste of the rank 4 power from first edition, back when it's use had to be subtle about applying it and it took weeks or months to get results. Now you don't have to worry about subtlety since victims of Dominate never remember being dominated unless the user wants them to remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-24T05:02:17-08:00","id":1162149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1162107#post1162107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Always about Dominate:<br /> Mesmerism allows to impress 4 words commands. Does a command like: &amp;quot;execute all my commands&amp;quot; (as per the example of iron edict) allows to give all commands without any lengths restriction for a scene? Can you explain me better the mechanic behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about level 1 only Mesmerism. If you only use that, they'll follow the next simple 4-7 word instructions at which point Mesmerize wears off. If a scene passes, Mesmerize also wears off. <br /> But... I can also see an ST declaring &quot;Follow all my commands&quot; as being too complex and open ended for just rank 1 because it's stated that at level 1 the commands are supposed to be fairly quickly issued and carried out and the obvious intention is that level 1 alone is not to work all night. Iron Edict extends that time frame of Mesmerize for one night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T01:51:51-08:00","id":1162389,"title":"","content":"Mesmerised does not wear off after a command, it lasts for a scene or until the Mesmerised condition is resolved. During that time the vampire who used Mesmerism may give them as many simple and direct 4 word commands as they like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T02:53:35-08:00","id":1162407,"title":"","content":"Yes but a 4 word command could be: &quot;Execute my commands&quot;<br /> <br /> After that could I command him: &quot;go to him and punch him. <br /> Then: &quot;go to her and listen to what she's saying without let you be noticed.&quot;<br /> And whatevere for the duration of a scene?<br /> <br /> I know them are not 4 words command, but the firs actually is a valid command, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T03:38:01-08:00","id":1162416,"title":"","content":"&quot;Do my bidding&quot; is given as an example of a command too open ended for Mesmerise so I would assume &quot;Execute my commands&quot; is also too open ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-25T03:50:36-08:00","id":1162419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1162407#post1162407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but a 4 word command could be: &quot;Execute my commands&quot;<br /> <br /> After that could I command him: &quot;go to him and punch him.<br /> Then: &quot;go to her and listen to what she's saying without let you be noticed.&quot;<br /> And whatevere for the duration of a scene?<br /> <br /> I know them are not 4 words command, but the firs actually is a valid command, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No it's not, as Live Bait pointed out. It's open for to much interpretation. And each command is a 3-4 word sentence that much be quite precise.<br /> &quot;listen to me&quot; - would be a valid command to make him more or less stand still and listen.<br /> next turn you could say &quot;punch that guy&quot; (which might break the Condition for him, it might be a breaking point)<br /> &quot;listen to that conversation&quot; ,&quot;report what they said&quot; are both valid if given in the right circumstance, although depending on ST, it might be a scene break between.<br /> <br /> So actually the Mesmerized Condition in it self is a &quot;execute my commands&quot;, with the caveat they cant be to long, complicated or to open.<br /> Longer, more complex commands takes Iron Edict.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T15:08:52-08:00","id":1163107,"title":"","content":"So, with Vitae Addiction and the Bond, the book uses the word &quot;drink&quot; a lot, and implies the taste is part of the addictive qualities, but doesn't really imply that for the bond. So, does say, injecting someone with Vitae cause either the Addiction or Bond, or both, or would it more likely just be an unhealthy thing to do that has no real mystical effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T16:37:15-08:00","id":1163120,"title":"","content":"Just wondering if Merder Expert made the jump to 2E. It was my favorite to pair with obsficate. Also if it made the jump what book is it in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20755-seph038","name":"Seph038","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar20755_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T17:08:41-08:00","id":1163130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1163107#post1163107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, with Vitae Addiction and the Bond, the book uses the word &quot;drink&quot; a lot, and implies the taste is part of the addictive qualities, but doesn't really imply that for the bond. So, does say, injecting someone with Vitae cause either the Addiction or Bond, or both, or would it more likely just be an unhealthy thing to do that has no real mystical effect?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a thread about this. It is meant to imply imbibed, consumed. Even if you shoot it up, you still get addicted and bonded. There are examples in the book of a nosferatu spitting vitae into the eye of it's victim and a gangrel cutting himself and the victim, then pressing the wounds together. Any time vitae enters your body you are subject to bond and addiction. ( you can ghoul this way too )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-27-2017, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T10:12:13-08:00","id":1163966,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Archery:</b></u><br /> <br /> A couple of questions about bows:<br /> <br /> 1) are they considered ranged attacks? And so do they negate defence?<br /> 2) from the moment that they can be used with Athletics, can i apply Vigor's active power to add damage?<br /> 3) If the two previous questions are answered yes, then isn't it a little too much easy to impale a Kindred with an arrow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13629-strikeforce1","name":"strikeforce1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:49:28-08:00","id":1164000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strikeforce1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1163966#post1163966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Archery:</b></u><br /> <br /> A couple of questions about bows:<br /> <br /> 1) are they considered ranged attacks? And so do they negate defence?<br /> 2) from the moment that they can be used with Athletics, can i apply Vigor's active power to add damage?<br /> 3) If the two previous questions are answered yes, then isn't it a little too much easy to impale a Kindred with an arrow?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I used the Hurt Locker for this information<br /> Yes bows are Dex + Athletics ranged attacks. <br /> there is a -2 penalty per person that's in your way.<br /> <br /> it has to be a wooden stake, it has to be as per RAW. not metal, not an arrow, not plastic, not a pencil. Wooden stake. But you already have -3 for a heart shot, then you have to do 5 damage. then if there is anything in the way you have more negatives. Then you have to hope they dont have resilience which would negate some of that damage. Buuut you can't shoot a wooden stake from a normal bow without some huge negatives. A crossbow you probably could create one to shoot a stake though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:13:33-08:00","id":1164006,"title":"","content":"Yeah this is similar to a previous question about hot metal causing fire damage. The Bane is not just &quot;wood&quot; but &quot;a wooden stake.&quot;<br /> Stakes are fat and sturdy enough to be hammered into things and arrows need to be flexible to work properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:14:45-08:00","id":1164009,"title":"","content":"Arrows are made of carbon or graphite and plexiglass. Crossbow bolts are made of carbon, graphite, and aluminum. They're also capped with steel tips if you're doing more than shooting through burlap bags, no wood. If you're jury rigging crossbows and compound recurve bows to fire chunks of sharpened wood to &quot;stake&quot; a vampire, you're right back to square one of using improvised weapons. So no, it's really not ridiculously easy to impale a vampire with a stake using bows and crossbows. But if a player wants to spend the XP to hyperspecialize like that, I don't care. It's easy to counter if they get stupid and arrogant about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:28:50-08:00","id":1164016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strikeforce1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1161406#post1161406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Stun</b></u><br /> <br /> Hi guys , I was wondering if : a)The stun tilt is appplicable to Vampires in the same manner it is to nomal humans.<br /> b) The stun tilt must be employed when one gets more damages than his stamina or just after a direct attack to the head as written in the Tilt.<br /> <br /> Thanks and bye <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With careful reading between splatbooks, my recommendation is to ONLY stun vampires for head attacks that inflict Size damage. GMC and Werewolf have stun for damage anywhere =&gt; Size, and for head at Size-1. I view the difference as intentional and a side-effect of the undead physiology.<br /> <br /> YMMV.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T13:53:51-08:00","id":1165132,"title":"","content":"<b>\u200bHow organized to people typically play the clans?</b><br /> <br /> Clan Status is something you can buy dots in, but most of the fluff I've read seems to focus much more on the Covenants as sources of organization for Kindred society. Is that an accurate reading?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T14:31:35-08:00","id":1165140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1165132#post1165132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u200bHow organized to people typically play the clans?</b><br /> <br /> Clan Status is something you can buy dots in, but most of the fluff I've read seems to focus much more on the Covenants as sources of organization for Kindred society. Is that an accurate reading?</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, the only consistent thing tying a clan together is commonality of themes and mechanics plus the fact that solitary Kindred still come from somewhere.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, a childe represents an investment of Humanity and a greater point of influence for their sire than most other vampires without the Vinculum, your sire is the vampire with the most notional care for your well-being and interest in seeing you integrated with the All Night Society, Dynasty Membership is a covenant-agnostic Merit, and even vampires with no direct relation to you can find their way to you through sympathy if they're nearby and share your clan.<br /> <br /> Clan Status is generally the vector by which you get characters who play to and reshape their own clan's archetypes being better at influencing their fellows through mundane channels, and it serves as one of the ways for an out-of-town vampire to shake things up in a city without pulling on more discrete connections or mystical force, which is useful considering how much investment Disciplines and Blood Potency take and how much politicking City and Covenant Status are gated behind by comparison.<br /> <br /> There's relatively little inherent and deliberate organization to the clans, but vampires are people and their lineages tell you things about them and the world they inhabit that their less inborn mystical/social ties can't as readily establish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T15:40:40-08:00","id":1165159,"title":"","content":"They're not particularly organized, I think, except 'older is better' but like Satchel suggests lineage can connect people. There's a few domains that have heavy clan influence in the clanbooks, and it's a ready thing to fall back on when there's no ideology like the covenants, or said ideologies are weakened or lopsided. It's easy to imagine a domain of Invictus of a certain clan who exclude members of other clans, or a domain where the Circle is spiritually dominant to the extreme and the only Lancea et Sanctum presence are descended from one member allowed to survive, or part of some bloodline that for whatever reason avoided death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T18:08:31-08:00","id":1166212,"title":"","content":"I don't get round to playing much and thus this hasn't come up but forewarned is forearmed so...<br /> <br /> You can downgrade a failure to a dramatic failure for a beat. What are the guidelines for making a dramatic failure more costly? So far, all I could find was that one extended actions, additional attempts were made at -2. Is that apt for instant actions too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T18:36:45-08:00","id":1166217,"title":"","content":"I reach out from the shadows and grab the passerby &lt;roll failure&gt; You stumble out looking like a drunken fool and she hurries off.<br /> I reach out from the shadows and grab the passerby &lt;roll botch/dramatic failure&gt; She belts out a bloodcurdling scream and drags you off balance, planting you facefirst onto the dingy sidewalk. At the same time, the two police cruisers killing time around the corner fire up and peel out towards the commotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T18:40:49-08:00","id":1166218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1166217#post1166217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I reach out from the shadows and grab the passerby &lt;roll failure&gt; You stumble out looking like a drunken fool and she hurries off.<br /> I reach out from the shadows and grab the passerby &lt;roll botch/dramatic failure&gt; She belts out a bloodcurdling scream and drags you off balance, planting you facefirst onto the dingy sidewalk. At the same time, the two police cruisers killing time around the corner fire up and peel out towards the commotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>So pure RP fuel, hence Dramatic. Okay, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T03:42:54-08:00","id":1166262,"title":"","content":"Lifting object:<br /> <br /> An old character of mine (Gangrel and Physically oriented with bp 7), asked me how much could he lift at max. <br /> Until now since, very oddly acording to me, CoD doesn't provide any table about the feats of strength, I used the WoD sheet. But now that he can easily exced the 15 dot of strength in that table, and the weight increases seems to be not costant, I would like to know if anyone of you has a houserule for that or simply how do you deal with this. In example using blood he can reach strength 22. Then, rolling strenght (22) + stamina he could reach 32. How much could he lift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T14:05:47-08:00","id":1166335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1166262#post1166262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lifting object:<br /> <br /> An old character of mine (Gangrel and Physically oriented with bp 7), asked me how much could he lift at max.<br /> Until now since, very oddly acording to me, CoD doesn't provide any table about the feats of strength, I used the WoD sheet. But now that he can easily exced the 15 dot of strength in that table, and the weight increases seems to be not costant, I would like to know if anyone of you has a houserule for that or simply how do you deal with this. In example using blood he can reach strength 22. Then, rolling strenght (22) + stamina he could reach 32. How much could he lift?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's highly consistent from 11-15 strength. <br /> I would just continue the pattern and add 1000 lbs more with each point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T18:25:17-08:00","id":1166371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1166218#post1166218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So pure RP fuel, hence Dramatic. Okay, thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well it can be pure RP but you as the ST can also use it to introduce problems. As above maybe the next time the character goes to see his contact at the local PD, he has a dice penalty to get the favor he's looking for because the contact is still trying to cover for the botched feeding incident. Or maybe the girls boyfriend finds a clue at the scene and starts looking for your player, leading to his discovery of Vampires and eventual transformation into a Hunter who pops up at another inopportune time.<br /> <br /> Basically it means the action not only fails but something extra bad happens on top of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T19:43:49-08:00","id":1166583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1166371#post1166371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically it means the action not only fails but something extra bad happens on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there guidelines for how bad?<br /> <br /> As a player, how much of a risk is downgrading failures to dramatic failures for beats? Will a rapidly progressing vamp (taking dramatics for every failure) only live a few weeks or will they live a long, abet highly inconvenient, unlife?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T20:00:45-08:00","id":1166587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1166583#post1166583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there guidelines for how bad?<br /> <br /> As a player, how much of a risk is downgrading failures to dramatic failures for beats? Will a rapidly progressing vamp (taking dramatics for every failure) only live a few weeks or will they live a long, abet highly inconvenient, unlife?</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on what your ST finds appropriate. There's no compiled guideline as to what's appropriate (aside from extended actions giving a -2 penalty to the next roll), but take a look at the written out effects of dramatic failures in the book for getting inspiration. There's a list of common actions in the book (starting on page 171), as well as dramatic failure consequences for every single power activation that has a roll. <br /> And as a tip, if you can't come up with a fitting consequence, the ST should say no to choosing a dramatic failure. Forcing it can disrupt the flow of the session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T11:41:39-08:00","id":1166754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1166587#post1166587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as a tip, if you can't come up with a fitting consequence, the ST should say no to choosing a dramatic failure. Forcing it can disrupt the flow of the session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good tip. Reinforces that it comes back to ST fiat, not because you are not allow agency, but because, these rules are to help experience the world and if they go against that, then they are overruled. So if I use the printed failures as a baseline, and then play it by ear, I should be fine. I am thinking that each downgrade per story makes the next more likely to be worse. Is that bad metagaming or a good idea for pacing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T12:47:28-08:00","id":1166774,"title":"","content":"A better tip then ignoring dramatic failures if you don't improvise one on the spot. Ask the other players if they have a idea for what would be an interesting turn of events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T04:48:06-08:00","id":1168348,"title":"","content":"The book says that if a Willpower is spent to prevent the Cleansing from healing a wound, the wound becomes permanent. Does this mean such wounds can never be healed, even later through a conscious use of Vitae? If something like a scar, tattoo, or piercing is kept through the use of Willpower do they also become permanent, or does the vampire have to spend a Willpower every day to prevent the change from reverting back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 12-17-2017, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T05:10:18-08:00","id":1168350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1168348#post1168348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says that if a Willpower is spent to prevent the Cleansing from healing a wound, the wound becomes permanent. Does this mean such wounds can never be healed, even later through a conscious use of Vitae? If something like a scar, tattoo, or piercing is kept through the use of Willpower do they also become permanent, or does the vampire have to spend a Willpower every day to prevent the change from reverting back?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it become permanent until the vampire want to heal it. But I'm not very sure about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:08:04-08:00","id":1168585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1168348#post1168348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book says that if a Willpower is spent to prevent the Cleansing from healing a wound, the wound becomes permanent. Does this mean such wounds can never be healed, even later through a conscious use of Vitae? If something like a scar, tattoo, or piercing is kept through the use of Willpower do they also become permanent, or does the vampire have to spend a Willpower every day to prevent the change from reverting back?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's unclear whether the wound (damage boxes) become permanent until the vamp purposefully heals them, or if the appearance/effect of the injury becomes permanent. Likely a mix of the two, frankly. <br /> <br /> Permanent would imply &quot;remains so until another Willpower is used to change it&quot;, at the very least.<br /> <br /> I can provide an example if you like: in my own campaign a certain NPC managed, as a mortal, to greatly inconvenience and irritate an NPC vamp, who eventually poisoned him and embraced him postumously for the sole purpose of breaking him physically and mentally. Said NPC was chained up, physically abused and damaged, and then through Dominate and Majesty made to &quot;appreciate&quot; his new state so he would &quot;want&quot; to stay that way overnight. End result was something closer to a crippled Nos than his Ventrue sire--but then again the intent was never to let the plaything go, after all.<br /> <br /> Fast-forward past [events] and NPC is out, and PCs may be able to help him by, essentially, re-breaking or cutting off damaged parts and NPC &quot;remembering&quot; what he looked like originally as he passes through daysleep. Breaking-point rolls for everyone!<br /> <br /> Kinda like breaking a badly-healed bone, to enable it to set properly, is how I'm looking at it.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T12:25:32-08:00","id":1168594,"title":"","content":"Since you automatically spend Vitae to heal yourself while sleeping, but you also need to spend Vitae to wake up at night, the Willpower is spent to keep the auto-heal from activating. The wound isn't permanent (unless you refuse to ever heal it) but you won't accidentally knock yourself into torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T01:43:50-08:00","id":1168744,"title":"","content":"Let's consider a spirit (or wathever) with influence fire 4/5. What distance can he create flames and set things on fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T03:31:58-08:00","id":1168750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1168744#post1168744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's consider a spirit (or wathever) with influence fire 4/5. What distance can he create flames and set things on fire?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really a vampire question, since vampires generally don't deal with ephemeral beings, let alone rank 4~5 ones. You might get a more complete answer from the werewolf or mage forums.<br /> <br /> Anyways, this kind of thing usually is determined by sensory range. Normally, ephemerals are limited by the Manifest Conditions. If something has the appropriate Manifest Condition, it's within range of the spirits Influences. If it doesn't have the appropriate Manifest Condition, then nope. Mind you, Rank 4+ beings with create can make their own resonant conditions, but getting somewhere to actually create said Conditions is tricky. Few such beings want to suffer essence bleed, then expend massive amounts of essence to do this. A rank 4+ fire spirit could use Reaching from the hisil, which is a lot easier than an angel or ghost could accomplish.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the case of a Influence 4, do note that this is a &quot;new example&quot; of the influence, the equivalent of a sapling or young foal. Influence 4 fire is likely going to be at the lowest size and temperature unless other influences are used after the fact. Influence 5 fire is as big and hot as you want.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T05:07:15-08:00","id":1168771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1168744#post1168744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's consider a spirit (or wathever) with influence fire 4/5. What distance can he create flames and set things on fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sensory. Potentially across the Gauntlet depending on what's going on with the Gauntlet, or how much time the spirit or others have used preparing it. Mass Create (Influence 5) can fill an entire area with fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T03:38:31-08:00","id":1169305,"title":"","content":"Charmed condition lasts bp hours. A ghoul with Majesty 2, having bp 0, could anyway use it for 1 hour effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T03:45:23-08:00","id":1169306,"title":"","content":"It's not unprecedented that ghouls can learn Disciplines they can't actually use, but only an asshole ST wouldn't grant them that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T07:44:02-08:00","id":1169350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1169306#post1169306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not unprecedented that ghouls can learn Disciplines they can't actually use, but only an asshole ST wouldn't grant them that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, the way I see it, players investing in powers they know from the start they can't use and expect the ST to grant them an exception to the rules without prior consultation are the assholes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T08:56:08-08:00","id":1169371,"title":"","content":"Ok, so mechanically majesty 2 couldn't be used by ghoul. Is it right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-21-2017, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T09:15:17-08:00","id":1169375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1169371#post1169371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so mechanically majesty 2 couldn't be used by ghoul. Is it right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is probably RAW yes. But one could assume BP 0 would count as BP 1 for these instances. <br /> <br /> Kinda agree with Tessie here, it's kinda a dick move to have to spend exp on things you cant move. I've expressed my view on disciplines and ghouls before.<br /> In my Head Canon, ghouls can use disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T09:29:22-08:00","id":1169377,"title":"","content":"At my own table at least, I'd be inclined to let it last for whichever is the shorter duration between one hour and the current scene, at absolute minimum. BP 0 is usually treated more-or-less as &quot;BP 1 but with some exceptions&quot; though, so if a flat hour feels appropriate at your table then it's really not going to break anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 12-21-2017, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T09:54:57-08:00","id":1169391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1169350#post1169350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, the way I see it, players investing in powers they know from the start they can't use and expect the ST to grant them an exception to the rules without prior consultation are the assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assume makes an ass of you and me. Of course there has to be a discussion when the rules don't add up, but in this case it's the rules not adding up; not that we know for a fact Majesty 2 isn't supposed to work for ghouls. Only Disciplines requiring spilling blood are explicitly unavailable for ghouls, so the player can definitely be excused by finding out that the rules just straight up doesn't work after having bought the dot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another way to deal with it is saying that Charmed applies as long as Awe applies to the target. It'd be weird of Charmed can lapse (not resolve) while the victim is still under the effect of Awe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T10:13:46-08:00","id":1169395,"title":"","content":"Ok so let's say that a good agreement could be:<br /> - lasting for just one scene<br /> - lasting until awe effect is active.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't go for the last one cause if I make a request that'd lead the charmed minion to go away from the vampire, the effect will fade.<br /> Lasting a scene seems reasonable to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T12:05:22-08:00","id":1169437,"title":"","content":"So, I was reading the Chary discipline and I'm trying to figure out how to use part of the Eating Flies aspect. It said that insects can't be used for the discipline, but I wasn't aware there were any size zero creatures that weren't insects. Was there something I missed in one of the threads about size zero creatures?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T12:28:24-08:00","id":1169443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1169437#post1169437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was reading the Chary discipline and I'm trying to figure out how to use part of the Eating Flies aspect. It said that insects can't be used for the discipline, but I wasn't aware there were any size zero creatures that weren't insects. Was there something I missed in one of the threads about size zero creatures?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Etruscan shrew<img src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etruscan_shrew#/media/File:Suncus_etruscus.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>is definitely a size 0 mammal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/ff/Suncus_etruscus.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T13:17:19-08:00","id":1169454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1169443#post1169443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Etruscan shrew is definitely a size 0 mammal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T17:40:28-08:00","id":1169534,"title":"","content":"I was thinking maybe tiny fish, baby mice etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T20:47:52-08:00","id":1170078,"title":"","content":"If you Embraced a ghoul, do they keep the two discipline dots from being ghouls (For a total of 5), or do they just get one extra discipline dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23575-mrmonsterguy18","name":"MrMonsterGuy18","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T00:20:49-08:00","id":1170110,"title":"","content":"I would say they keep the 2 dots for a total of 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T04:44:34-08:00","id":1170140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMonsterGuy18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1170078#post1170078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you Embraced a ghoul, do they keep the two discipline dots from being ghouls (For a total of 5), or do they just get one extra discipline dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they spend xp to gain additional disciplines while they were a ghoul? If they did, I\u2019d say they don\u2019t get anything and simply refund them the xp they spent beyond a third discipline dot. <br /> Alternatively, you can reset them to zero disciplines, reissue them three free dots to spend (refund them the Xp they spent if they purchased more disciplines as a ghoul) and allow them to purchase whatever disciplines are now available to their character as a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T04:45:25-08:00","id":1170141,"title":"","content":"They would get 1 more. I'm pretty sure this is RAW as well.<br /> But alas, if you would gain 5, every kindred would first ghoul their future childer just to make them a tid bit stronger as you gain 1 discipline dot the moment you're ghouled.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T15:53:43-08:00","id":1170302,"title":"","content":"Why would a ghoul &quot;Forget&quot; how to do things it knew how to do when it was alive? Why would the vitae in his system suddenly not work anymore? It's the same thing.. And as Poseur said, if you got 2from ghoul, then 3 from vampire, to have 5. every vampire would do that first.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am sure upon embrace they would keep what they spent exp on and the same thing is gifted to them. <br /> For example. If they had 2 dots in Majesty when they were alive, and they are now a Daeva, give them their two dots of Majesty and have them pick their third. <br /> Example. If they had 3 dots Majesty, 2 Nightmare, 2 Celerity, and 1 vigor, because they had been a ghoul forever.... When they are vamped, give them the 1 additional discipline dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T22:20:14-08:00","id":1170374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMonsterGuy18</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1170078#post1170078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you Embraced a ghoul, do they keep the two discipline dots from being ghouls (For a total of 5), or do they just get one extra discipline dot?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on if getting the vampire template gives 3 disciplines right away or those 3 disciplines are assumed to have been learned since becoming a vampire. I know for sure that the 6 Arcana dots a mage gets at character gen is assumed to have been after that mage has learned from the order etc, gained his free dot in high speech etc. Dave has said that a newly awakened mage only has 3 dots in arcana. <br /> <br /> If the 3 free disciplines are a result of instantly becoming a vampire then the ghoul should get those 3 and have 5 points, if its assumed that each new vampire PC has had some training then one would need to know how many discipline dots a brand new vampire gets...it might even be zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T12:23:50-08:00","id":1172346,"title":"","content":"Is there ever a reason to buy a dot of strength instead of buying a dot of vigour (other than vigour already being maxed out)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T12:27:40-08:00","id":1172348,"title":"","content":"If you just want a dot of Strength, Vigor is the cheaper way to go. If you want very high Strength, you'll have to get both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T12:40:24-08:00","id":1172354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1172346#post1172346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there ever a reason to buy a dot of strength instead of buying a dot of vigour (other than vigour already being maxed out)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lashing Out doesn't include Vigor in the Monstrous Beast. Individual STs might also not allow Vigor where you're supposed to look strong without actually demonstrating it, such as Strength + Intimidation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":"not with 01-01-2018, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T13:16:11-08:00","id":1172363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1172346#post1172346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there ever a reason to buy a dot of strength instead of buying a dot of vigour (other than vigour already being maxed out)?</div> </div> </div> </div>From a in-char veiw, maybe it's better for keeping ones humanity higher. <br /> Only thing ooc i can think of is Lashing Out rolls, they don't benefit from Vigor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T19:06:13-08:00","id":1172478,"title":"","content":"Enfeebling Aura can remove Vigour but not Strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T21:24:58-08:00","id":1172524,"title":"","content":"Another question, if you embrace and elder's ghoul (who get 4 discipline dots according to A Thousand Years of Night) what would happen with their disciplines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23575-mrmonsterguy18","name":"MrMonsterGuy18","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T22:44:37-08:00","id":1172548,"title":"","content":"Embracing a ghoul is a unique enough situation you could probably have them start with extra disciplines.<br /> <br /> Standard character creation builds off of a standard human having been embraced and active as a vampire for a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T03:23:29-08:00","id":1172589,"title":"","content":"As stated before, you don't loose any discipline dots if you're embraced. But considering that Ghouls start out with 1 dot they'd get 2 more if they are embraced. Ghoul PCs start out with 2 dots and gain another dot if embraced. An Elder ghoul might be ruled as a PC ghoul or an NPC ghoul, gaining either 1 or 2 dots, or ruled as already having basic knowledge.<br /> If Ghouls got 4 dots all together when being embraced, all vampires would start their embraces by spending 1 vitae and willpower to ghoul them before, and if you didn't you would loose out on the arms race. Considering how rare it would be for an Elder ghoul to actually be embraced however, either way would work I guess. <br /> <br /> So when you're a vampire you get 3 dots worth of disciplines, if some o them where gifted for free before you get the difference in dots.<br /> However say for this, if a PC ghoul has bought another 3 dots worth of disciplines, I'd say he still gets one dot for free when embraced, you don't want to rob your players of exp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T04:23:42-08:00","id":1172602,"title":"","content":"There are no official rules, but, as Poseur said, giving out the missing free dots is common with different groups.<br /> <br /> I find that you are going to have to be a bit flexible too, because its entirely possible to have a former Deava's ghoul, then drank some Mehket blood, and now is embraced as a Venture, so the discipline affinities are a bit messed up. Play it by ear and go with what makes the most sense for your story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T13:51:23-08:00","id":1173075,"title":"","content":"Hello all,<br /> I've got two questions regarding strix rules - in specific , in the case where a strix posses a living human:<br /> 1) Predatory aura - Does a vampire can detect a strix-possessed human by its aura?<br /> 2) Sunlight - does a strix take damage from sunlight when possessing living? <br /> I've got confused a bit..<br /> Any help would be welcome!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23643-yairb88","name":"yairb88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T15:04:24-08:00","id":1173093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yairb88</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1173075#post1173075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello all,<br /> I've got two questions regarding strix rules - in specific , in the case where a strix posses a living human:<br /> 1) Predatory aura - Does a vampire can detect a strix-possessed human by its aura?<br /> 2) Sunlight - does a strix take damage from sunlight when possessing living?<br /> I've got confused a bit..<br /> Any help would be welcome!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1)Not sure but probably. Would probably work like dominate possession.<br /> 2) Strix usually don't take damage from sunlight unless engulfed and trapped by it, and possessing a host renders it immune to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T21:38:52-08:00","id":1173159,"title":"","content":"The book states a strix possessing a corpse is almost indistinguishable from a vampire, including predatory aura. So a strix possessing a living person would also have a predatory aura and seem like a vampire using blush of life.<br /> <br /> Strix are protected from the banes of sunlight and fire while embodied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T22:54:25-08:00","id":1173417,"title":"","content":"Could the scale fealty's reward be used on the same ghoul more than once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T18:37:46-08:00","id":1173658,"title":"","content":"Fealty's Reward can't be performed on a ghoul in the first place.<br /> The first sentence says the target must be a mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 01-05-2018, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T21:00:45-08:00","id":1173682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1173658#post1173658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fealty's Reward can't be performed on a ghoul in the first place.<br /> The first sentence says the target must be a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are still mortal, so i assume ghouls are also still mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T21:45:59-08:00","id":1173691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1173417#post1173417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the scale fealty's reward be used on the same ghoul more than once?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Based off what I read, Fealty's reward is pretty much active until the person is no longer a ghoul, so it would only need to be done the one time unless the person stopped being a ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T07:31:29-08:00","id":1173749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1173682#post1173682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are still mortal, so i assume ghouls are also still mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can grow old and die of old age, therefore they are mortal.<br /> <br /> Ghouls do not grow old and die of old age. They are not mortal.<br /> <br /> The scale turns people into a ghoul. If they are ever not a ghoul, they die. You can't turn a ghoul into a double ghoul, so it seems unlikely that it can be used more than once on the same target regardless of the 'mortal' issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T07:46:16-08:00","id":1173750,"title":"","content":"Nitpick - mages aren't mortal. They're still <i>human</i>, but they're no longer a mortal. Mortal, in CofD terms, is an ordinary human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-06-2018, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T08:14:42-08:00","id":1173761,"title":"","content":"I've never really seen &quot;mortal&quot; being defined at all, except for in VtR where they include both ghouls and mages since they are considered more human than not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T08:17:01-08:00","id":1173762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1173750#post1173750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick - mages aren't mortal. They're still <i>human</i>, but they're no longer a mortal. Mortal, in CofD terms, is an ordinary human.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is somewhat unclear on that point, to be fair:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> mortal: An ordinary human. Although Kindred are, to<br /> varying degrees, aware of other monsters in the World of<br /> Darkness, they frequently use \u201cmortal\u201d to describe everyone<br /> who\u2019s not one of them. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In reference to the effects of a bite, the word \u201cmortal\u201d applies<br /> to humans, ghouls, warlocks, and other things that are mostly<br /> human. Vampires, werewolves, mummies, fairies, and other<br /> things far removed from humanity are not normally subject to<br /> the Assault and the Kiss. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T11:47:28-08:00","id":1173805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1173749#post1173749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can grow old and die of old age, therefore they are mortal.<br /> <br /> Ghouls do not grow old and die of old age. They are not mortal.<br /> <br /> The scale turns people into a ghoul. If they are ever not a ghoul, they die. You can't turn a ghoul into a double ghoul, so it seems unlikely that it can be used more than once on the same target regardless of the 'mortal' issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to die of old age is not a very good metric for being mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-06T11:50:22-08:00","id":1173806,"title":"","content":"Being subject to death is one of the definitions of the word. Thus 'im-mortal.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:42:52-08:00","id":1174340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1173749#post1173749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can grow old and die of old age, therefore they are mortal.<br /> <br /> Ghouls do not grow old and die of old age. They are not mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>A ghoul's aging is only paused. They most definitely would grow old and die without vitae in their system. As a matter of fact, they would do so very very rapidly if they were old and some reason unable to keep that pause button going. A ghoul's age catches up to them in a matter of weeks without vitae.<br /> <br /> For example, if some reason Heroin stopped the effects of aging while I had it in my system, I wouldn't be classified as Immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:02:31-08:00","id":1174375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1173806#post1173806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being subject to death is one of the definitions of the word. Thus 'im-mortal.'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ghouls are still subject to death. They just dont die from old age while being a ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:16:18-08:00","id":1174383,"title":"","content":"Death meaning your life has an expiration date. Anything can die by violent means.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ghouls would qualify as mortal because their &quot;inmortality&quot; is temporary and can be reversed (they not only start to age again when they miss the Vitae upkeep,but age catches back to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 01-08-2018, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T17:17:53-08:00","id":1174402,"title":"","content":"When they run out of vitae and start to age again, they are no longer a Ghoul because Ghouls do not age.<br /> When they take that sip of Vitae and receive the infusement of WP, they are no longer mortal and no longer age because they are now a Ghoul and Ghouls do not age.<br /> Just because Ghouls can't manufacture the immortality juice themselves, doesn't make them any less immortal.<br /> <br /> Substitute the word flight for immortality. A human cannot fly without outside equipment. Just because he needs the plane and it may land at some point doesn't mean he's not in flight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 01-08-2018, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T04:58:03-08:00","id":1174522,"title":"","content":"Ghouls are NEVER immortal. They can ALWAYS die by sustaining massive amounts of physical damage or by being deprived of basic nutrients such as oxygen, water, and food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T05:15:09-08:00","id":1174525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1174402#post1174402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When they run out of vitae and start to age again, they are no longer a Ghoul because Ghouls do not age.<br /> When they take that sip of Vitae and receive the infusement of WP, they are no longer mortal and no longer age because they are now a Ghoul and Ghouls do not age.<br /> Just because Ghouls can't manufacture the immortality juice themselves, doesn't make them any less immortal.<br /> <br /> Substitute the word flight for immortality. A human cannot fly without outside equipment. Just because he needs the plane and it may land at some point doesn't mean he's not in flight.</div> </div> </div> </div>People are getting confused by human and mortal. You can be a mortal human or an immortal human (see the Purified). Even vampires are technically not immortal, sure they cant die from old age but they can still meet death via the sun/fire. Mummies are immortal but no longer human. Demons are mortal non humans. Mages are human and mortal. Prommies are mortal nonhumans, Werewolfs are half-human mortals. Changelings are mortal humans. Deviants are prob mortal humans.<br /> <br /> Theres actually very few immortals <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T07:38:53-08:00","id":1174549,"title":"","content":"Note: The Unchained may extend their lifetime indefinitely by use of their covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T15:18:25-08:00","id":1174669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1174522#post1174522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls are NEVER immortal. They can ALWAYS die by sustaining massive amounts of physical damage or by being deprived of basic nutrients such as oxygen, water, and food.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be misunderstanding the idea of immortality. The Greek gods were considered immortals and yet they could be and were killed by each other, Titans, etc.<br /> As stated above immortality is generally understood to be synonymous with unaging, as very few creatures have been considered to be truly unkillable.<br /> <br /> If this is not the case, then what could the devotion possibly mean by mortal? Vampires can be killed, Mages can be killed, Demons can be killed, Warewolves can be killed. What could they possibly be excluding by specifying that the target must be mortal? The God Machine alone can't benefit from this Devotion but every other thing in existence can?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T16:37:43-08:00","id":1174685,"title":"","content":"If you define immoral as can not be killed either by old age or damage in any way, then the only things truly immortal (possible besides the Arisen) would be some Horrors with the Immortal Dread Power...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In most cases, cannot die by old age or doesn't age at all is the definition of immortal. Ergo here lies the Kindred, Ghouls, Demons, Exarchs, The God-Machine etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T09:52:30-08:00","id":1174894,"title":"","content":"I agree with the two above on the issue of immortality. For the more comprehensive 'cannot be destroyed ever, at all, by time or force' maybe indestructible or eternal?<br /> <br /> Or we could change immortal to eternal or unchanging, given that immortal has 'mort' in it and vampires are definitely dead. After all, dead comes after life. But then, life is rooted in the notion of animation and the Kindred carry on moving... So now the Kindred are still living. So the earlier concern over 'mort' comes back upon itself. Hmm....<br /> <br /> Okay, so mortal means 'it can die' and to die presumes having a life. However, life could be seen as simple animation. However, most living things cease being animated while we have evidence of certain beings carrying on without ceasing, assuming nothing stops them. Given that, we can divide life into the finite and the infinite. Finite life runs out. Infinite does not.<br /> <br /> As such, all transitory life beings are definitively mortal; they will die. (Unless they become immortal... oh dear, these tangents...) Whereas permanent life beings could persist forever; they may not die. As such, they are not <i>inherently</i> susceptible to death. (Unless they lose it?... wait...) HOWEVER as a transitory life can be made into a permanent life but this is not necessary (only some people become vampires, for example) we can discount the incidental, because otherwise, all life is immortal and this is absurd. If we can discount the incidental, then dead-by-external-cause has no bearing on designation; as such, being mortal means you have a finite life. Ghouls are thus mortal, as their infiniteness is not inherent. They same with Mages. Not vampires. Even when they starve, they live...well...they aren't very animate anymore but...WHERE DOES THIS END!?<br /> <br /> In sum: Mortality, as both word and concept, is rooted in an historical paradigm that explains things via teloes. We don't do that anymore, so thinking about it is weird. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  This is now an Ordo application. :) 01-10-2018, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T10:11:49-08:00","id":1174904,"title":"","content":"I see no need to define that particular subset of immortals. In fact, this whole discussion is pretty much meaningless because they're all valid definitions. Many words don't have a singular, all-encompassing definition. That's the nature of language.<br /> And the word immortal is not defined as a rules term in the Storytelling System, so anytime the word does show up in one of the books you'll have to take the context of the word into account. That means any definitions you come up with in this discussion will ultimately just be confusing since the books won't retroactively adhere to what you think the word should mean.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the case of Fealty's Reward I think &quot;mortal&quot; is just a synonym for anyone who's capable of being ghouled in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T10:20:10-08:00","id":1174910,"title":"","content":"Well now, that is worse and most useful version of mortal proposed thus far. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T11:17:52-08:00","id":1174925,"title":"","content":"Generally, as far I am concerned and for the purposes of CofD, a mortal is anyone without a template (though merit templates muddy that up a bit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T11:34:08-08:00","id":1174930,"title":"","content":"I think for the purposes of requiem, immmortals are the kindred, strix, some sets of non-Kindred vampires, and a few outliers, like that Dvora antagonist in 1000 years of night.<br /> <br /> For Fealty's Reward, if it doesn't transition the amount of time that a ghoul needs to drink vitae from per month to per year, I imagine the process can be done upon them again at the end of said year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T19:37:32-08:00","id":1175341,"title":"","content":"Is the Coil of Zirnitra part of its own Mystery (a Mystery of Zirnitra), a different Mystery (like the Coil of Quintessence is part of Voivode) or no Mystery at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T21:40:36-08:00","id":1175367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1175341#post1175341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Coil of Zirnitra part of its own Mystery (a Mystery of Zirnitra), a different Mystery (like the Coil of Quintessence is part of Voivode) or no Mystery at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to be part of its own Mystery, though a near extinct one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T08:02:47-08:00","id":1175972,"title":"","content":"What happens if a vampire deals with their provocation while spending Willpower to postpone frenzy? <br /> <br /> Say a hunger frenzy triggers, but the vampire retains control long enough to top up (or just push themselves out of the low-vitae 'danger zone')?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T08:17:58-08:00","id":1175975,"title":"","content":"If the source of the provocation disappears, then they wouldn't go into frenzy. But in the scenario you described it's still kind of vague. If it's a case where they were hungry and grabbed some human and started feeding and spent a willpower to avoid tearing their throat out in the process I would simply not apply the negative modifier for hunger. The Beast could still want to eat until satisfied. If it's a case of waking up hungry, knowing your ghoul will be back in an hour and deciding to grab a few vitae reliquaries instead, there is no target to direct the frenzy and no longer any trigger. Frenzy averted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T21:08:52-08:00","id":1176169,"title":"","content":"Question: does Blood &amp; Smoke cover how long it takes vitae to break down? Because there's a blurb about vitae in the communion wine, iirc, whereas I was under the impression in 1e that vitae in nwod breaks down far quicker than vitae in owod. All I could find is a statement on the distinction between vitae and blood volume (ie. that they're not directly correlated).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T00:19:42-08:00","id":1176202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kindred Vitae is a dangerous food. First off, Vitae is addicting<br /> (see Vitae Addiction, p. 99). As well, it causes the blood bond<br /> (see Blood Bonds, p. 90). However, it\u2019s efficient. Every Vitae<br /> taken is a Vitae earned, and this causes no additional damage<br /> to the victim. Stored Kindred Vitae is <b>effectively cold blood</b>. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cold blood</b> from a corpse or kept outside the body for<br /> more than a few minutes (but no more than a night) is far<br /> less satisfying. To gain a single point of Vitae, a vampire must<br /> consume as many pints of this blood as her Blood Potency times<br /> two. Technologically stored blood, for example in refrigerated<br /> plasma bags, is similarly unpalatable to potent Kindred. </div> </div> </div>Page 95 (Emphasis added)<br /> <br /> These are what the book has to say on the matter. I don't know if more recent supplements have added more detail. Seems Vitae (whether in blood or in its more purified, vampiric form) starts to lose potency after a few minutes and is worthless after a night. Of course, an ST might not consider this enough evidence and present their own ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T01:05:25-08:00","id":1176210,"title":"","content":"Is massive amount of heat or an open flame( to both so that it would cause combustion) necessary for aggravated damage or boiling oil would cause lethal( or even bashing) damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T04:03:30-08:00","id":1176238,"title":"","content":"The Banes seem to work more on symbolism, so only actual flames do Aggravated, same as only actual daylight and not certain types of lamps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T05:51:51-08:00","id":1176255,"title":"","content":"Boiling oil would only inflict bashing damage to vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T06:00:43-08:00","id":1176257,"title":"","content":"I have a question which may already have been answered somewhere within the massiveness of this thread.<br /> <br /> Do vampires detect other vampires (though the Predatory Aura) that are currently possessing a human or animal? This question goes both for the body that lies in torpor and especially the possessed that now walks around with a vampire mind in them.<br /> <br /> Another question is in regards to Raising the familiar (Animalism 2). It is said that the vampire can speak to the animal at any distance, but can the animal contact the vampire themselves? The rules say there is some sort of sympathetic link; does that mean the animal can send emotions or the like through it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","user":"Lorsa","date":". 01-15-2018, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","name":"Lorsa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T07:15:24-08:00","id":1176271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorsa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176257#post1176257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question is in regards to Raising the familiar (Animalism 2). It is said that the vampire can speak to the animal at any distance, but can the animal contact the vampire themselves? The rules say there is some sort of sympathetic link; does that mean the animal can send emotions or the like through it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The word the section uses is &quot;communicating&quot; in the context of being able to use Feral Whispers on the animal from any distance; this and the also-mentioned issuing of commands are both discussed in Feral Whispers' success text, and the former is immediately framed in terms of being able to ask and receive answers to questions.<br /> <br /> I would suspect, given the imagery involved and the placement of the power within the Discipline, that the familiar doesn't have enough autonomy to initiate contact on its own outside Feral Whispers already establishing a scene-long capacity for communication; the Ventrue and the Gangrel both approach the workarounds for that limitation from different directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T08:15:38-08:00","id":1176290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176255#post1176255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boiling oil would only inflict bashing damage to vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it does require combustion for heat to cause aggravated injury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T09:56:57-08:00","id":1176309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176290#post1176290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it does require combustion for heat to cause aggravated injury.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, their Banes are Fire and Sunlight, not heat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T11:14:13-08:00","id":1176327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>alexanderbk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176290#post1176290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it does require combustion for heat to cause aggravated injury.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire his hot but not all hot things are fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T15:28:01-08:00","id":1176391,"title":"","content":"I have a ghoul whose regnant died in one of my games. What would be required for another vampire to take over as Regnant? What effect would the change have on the Ghoul if the new Regnant was part of a different clan, had different disciplines, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T17:36:23-08:00","id":1176423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176391#post1176391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a ghoul whose regnant died in one of my games. What would be required for another vampire to take over as Regnant? What effect would the change have on the Ghoul if the new Regnant was part of a different clan, had different disciplines, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>What I have done in the past, is that the blood bond breaks upon death. But then if some other vampire wants to take over everything stays the same, they just continue to use the vitae to maintain their ghoul status as normal. New disciplines would just mean that ghoul can learn those in the future with exp. <br /> <br /> However, if the ghoul is going to let the ghoul status wear off and years down the road someone else ghouls them, then I think it would start over. New everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T17:40:19-08:00","id":1176424,"title":"","content":"If its 2nd edition, give the ghoul his monthly vitae hit. If I were a vampire though, I'd probably just kill the ghoul unless he can teach me a discipline I don't have or has something kickass I could use or like them on a personal level. I think ghouls are a needy vitae hemorrage that isn't worth the investment or risk most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T18:04:49-08:00","id":1176427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176424#post1176424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were a vampire though, I'd probably just kill the ghoul unless he can teach me a discipline I don't have or has something kickass I could use or like them on a personal level.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems least rational, most wasteful thing you could possibly do. Like killing your rich uncle's butler after he dies just because, &quot;hey, *I* can't afford a butler.&quot; A good ghoul is a valuable resource. Why not offer to set them up with another vampire, and earn yourself a couple of favors? Or just say &quot;good luck!&quot; and cut them loose?<br /> <br /> Edit: That's ignoring, of course, that most people (even most Kindred) probably don't jump to MURDER as the first solution for everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T18:35:10-08:00","id":1176434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176427#post1176427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems least rational, most wasteful thing you could possibly do. Like killing your rich uncle's butler after he dies just because, &quot;hey, *I* can't afford a butler.&quot; A good ghoul is a valuable resource. Why not offer to set them up with another vampire, and earn yourself a couple of favors? Or just say &quot;good luck!&quot; and cut them loose?<br /> <br /> Edit: That's ignoring, of course, that most people (even most Kindred) probably don't jump to MURDER as the first solution for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Jumping to murder is not something that most vampires do. That is the thought of a humanity 1 vampire and most don't sit there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176424#post1176424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If its 2nd edition, give the ghoul his monthly vitae hit. If I were a vampire though, I'd probably just kill the ghoul unless he can teach me a discipline I don't have or has something kickass I could use or like them on a personal level. I think ghouls are a needy vitae hemorrage that isn't worth the investment or risk most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, that said. The original poster asked what happened in the scope of the rules. You telling them what you would do if you were a vampire doesnt help answer the question in anyway whatsoever. We have no idea what the background of the game is. What if this ghoul works for the prince or something and their death would immediately take your head. You dont know. So you might not even murder the ghoul in the game either because honestly we would need to know a whole lot more before we make choices like that. <br /> <br /> So I think this thread should stick to things about the rules and how we interpret them and then let the posters of the questions deal with what they would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T22:56:34-08:00","id":1176469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176427#post1176427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems least rational, most wasteful thing you could possibly do. Like killing your rich uncle's butler after he dies just because, &quot;hey, *I* can't afford a butler.&quot; A good ghoul is a valuable resource. Why not offer to set them up with another vampire, and earn yourself a couple of favors? Or just say &quot;good luck!&quot; and cut them loose?<br /> <br /> Edit: That's ignoring, of course, that most people (even most Kindred) probably don't jump to MURDER as the first solution for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like inheriting a $3 million mansion and selling it as quickly as possible because I can't afford the 1.3 million dollars a year property taxes plus the $1500 a month maintenance fees when my salary is $27,000 a year. It's called living within your means. And unless you're rolling in blood dolls or massive feeding grounds keeping a ghoul maintained to be useful is significantly more than 1 vitae a month.<br /> <br /> Good and valuable are subjective terms. The hairdressing and fashion skills of the Invictus Nosferatu librettist's pet hairdresser is unlikely to impress the Ordo Dracul Ventrue cartographer who spends most of their waking hours trying to ascertain if bus and train routes run parallel to ley lines in the city.<br /> <br /> As for selling the ghoul to another vampire. I think I'll pass on slave trafficking. (Did that with one character. Ended up being a political fiasco as the ghoul was a Manchurian candidate.)<br /> <br /> And no. I don't think I'm going to let a rogue ghoul skip off. Masquerade breach and all. (Did that one too. Ended up getting my character staked.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 01-16-2018, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T21:51:46-08:00","id":1176692,"title":"","content":"Do you count the years a vampire has spent in torpor in that vampire's age? If my character was Embraced 700 years ago, but she's spent the last 200 years in torpor, would you say she's 700 years old or 500?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","name":"Sean Snyder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T23:35:41-08:00","id":1176705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176469#post1176469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More like inheriting a $3 million mansion and selling it as quickly as possible because I can't afford the 1.3 million dollars a year property taxes plus the $1500 a month maintenance fees when my salary is $27,000 a year. It's called living within your means.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, by your analogy the best action is the<i> burn the mansion down</i>? I still don't think that's a good idea.<br /> <br /> I just disagree with your approach entirely. Ghouls aren't slaves for the most part, they're servants. And if they were so hard to keep fed, then they'd be a lot rarer than the fluff indicates. I think you're way overblowing the difficulty and cost of maintaining a ghoul, as well as completely discounting the fact that, <i>hey, they're people. </i>All but the most jaded vampire is going to balk at murdering someone in cold blood just because they're inconvenient (the core book lists &quot;premeditated killing&quot; as a breaking point at Humanity <b>2</b>), and if their Humanity <i>is</i> that low, they're probably old and powerful enough to meet your high standards for ghoul ownership.<br /> <br /> Both of the examples you give of not killing a ghoul turning out badly are hardly indicative of some universal law. (sounds more like you've got a Storyteller who likes to punish you...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T00:50:56-08:00","id":1176718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sean Snyder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176692#post1176692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you count the years a vampire has spent in torpor in that vampire's age? If my character was Embraced 700 years ago, but she's spent the last 200 years in torpor, would you say she's 700 years old or 500?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO 700 years old, but many Kindred might try to use this argument to emphasize that the vampire had shorter requiem. A good try to diminish the impact it has on others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T03:59:29-08:00","id":1176741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sean Snyder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176692#post1176692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you count the years a vampire has spent in torpor in that vampire's age? If my character was Embraced 700 years ago, but she's spent the last 200 years in torpor, would you say she's 700 years old or 500?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you count the time you have spent asleep in your age or not? Why wouldnt a vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T04:14:20-08:00","id":1176744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176741#post1176741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you count the time you have spent asleep in your age or not? Why wouldnt a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>That.... is an excellent point.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Although, to be fair, while there are some similarities between me and a vampire (I, too, am quite pale and often day sleep and walk the streets at night), I do not often sleep for years in a corpse-like slumber. The closest I've come to that is sleeping for 26 hours after being extremely ill and not sleeping for three days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23703,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","user":"Sean Snyder","date":". 01-17-2018, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","name":"Sean Snyder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T07:23:32-08:00","id":1176944,"title":"","content":"Dhampir, are they Immortals? Do they grow old and die? Can they stave off age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T08:10:15-08:00","id":1176953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176944#post1176944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dhampir, are they Immortals? Do they grow old and die? Can they stave off age?</div> </div> </div> </div>Half-Damned gives some conflicting impressions but...<br /> 1) No<br /> 2) Yes<br /> 3) Maybe? (They can use blood sorcery)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T17:00:16-08:00","id":1177087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176944#post1176944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dhampir, are they Immortals? Do they grow old and die? Can they stave off age?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember <i>exactly</i>, but I believe that a dhampyr ages normally as a child, but then around the ages 18-24 (or maybe it was 26) they stop aging normally, and instead for every 20 years, they age one single year. But they never show signs of their age, just like vampires, and if they make it to 3000 years of age (around age 78) and they die of natural causes, they'd look like they did when they were 18.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","name":"Sean Snyder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T03:53:22-08:00","id":1177228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sean Snyder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1177087#post1177087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember <i>exactly</i>, but I believe that a dhampyr ages normally as a child, but then around the ages 18-24 (or maybe it was 26) they stop aging normally, and instead for every 20 years, they age one single year. But they never show signs of their age, just like vampires, and if they make it to 3000 years of age (around age 78) and they die of natural causes, they'd look like they did when they were 18.</div> </div> </div> </div>This must be 1E information, because absolutely none of this accompanies their (very different) 2E presentation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T03:59:58-08:00","id":1177230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1177228#post1177228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This must be 1E information, because absolutely none of this accompanies their (very different) 2E presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very possible. I don't remember where I read it. Perhaps I should not cite information without knowing its source. It's entirely possible this is, in fact, from Vampire: The Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","name":"Sean Snyder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T17:17:53-08:00","id":1177456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sean Snyder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1176744#post1176744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Although...I do not often sleep for years in a corpse-like slumber. The closest I've come to that is sleeping for 26 hours after being extremely ill and not sleeping for three days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Torpor is like a vampire coma and coma patients do slumber like that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T19:48:29-08:00","id":1177495,"title":"","content":"So i am reading the Core 2nd and I found on the devotion section this paragraph<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Core pg;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a vampire knows a Devotion, she can teach it to another Kindred in much the same way as the standard Discipline techniques. Any vampire with the appropriate prerequisite Discipline dots can develop any Devotion for which she has the dots</div> </div> </div> </div>This made me wonder, whats the advantage from learning a Devotion you want from someone rather that make it yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T20:14:17-08:00","id":1177500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1177495#post1177495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This made me wonder, whats the advantage from learning a Devotion you want from someone rather that make it yourself?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have the fictional positioning to do so in relatively short order rather than gin up an arbitrary pretext for your character spontaneously Just So Happening to develop an identical twist of the Blood in a neck of the mechanics that's used for strange vampiric powers that aren't covenant secrets, bloodline gifts, or regular Discipline effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T02:40:07-08:00","id":1177543,"title":"","content":"Does the treatment and roles of ghouls differ much between VTM and VTR besides being more expensive and disciplines being easier to come by in VTR?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T06:41:48-08:00","id":1177575,"title":"","content":"Ghouls might be seen as property but are valuable and protected property at worst. They are considered better than humans but less than Kindred and part of the All Night Society at best. Only fringe cases treat them as disposable and abused slaves as is Masquerade.<br /> <br /> EDIT: in short, although being a Ghoul in either game is hardly all good (though it has its perks) it is orders of magnitude better in Requiem than Masquerade","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 01-20-2018, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T15:58:02-08:00","id":1177701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1177456#post1177456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Torpor is like a vampire coma and coma patients do slumber like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah this made me think of a coma patient waking up after x years and wanting to claim they are x years younger than they really are !!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T18:07:55-08:00","id":1177740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1177456#post1177456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Torpor is like a vampire coma and coma patients do slumber like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... never thought of it that way. This is also an excellent point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","name":"Sean Snyder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T04:22:01-08:00","id":1178401,"title":"","content":"I had a question earlier which I believe was missed. It was phrased like this:<br /> <br /> Do vampires detect other vampires (though the Predatory Aura) that are currently possessing a human or animal? This question goes both for the body that lies in torpor and especially the possessed that now walks around with a vampire mind in them.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have a good answer?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","name":"Lorsa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T05:09:36-08:00","id":1178409,"title":"","content":"I think the &quot;corpse&quot; would be easily identified as Kindred. I would say there is no automatic way to find out an animal or person is possed by a vampire without using Auspex or similar means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T05:12:14-08:00","id":1178410,"title":"","content":"I would think that the vampire would continue to have a predatory aura and the animal or person they are possessing would not. This is primarily because a) there's nothing in Possession or Subsume the Lesser Beast that suggests the predatory aura functions differently and b) you cannot use disciplines while possessing a person or animal, and just like disciplines the predatory aura is a manifestation of the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T17:53:32-08:00","id":1179682,"title":"","content":"If one were to be in torpor long enough to lose their last dot of blood Potency is there any written effect? A) they cannot lose their last dot or b) they become a revenant and must be uplifted are two different approaches I could see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T18:11:50-08:00","id":1179684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1179682#post1179682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one were to be in torpor long enough to lose their last dot of blood Potency is there any written effect? A) they cannot lose their last dot or b) they become a revenant and must be uplifted are two different approaches I could see.</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire in torpor long enough will go down to one dot of blood potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T18:49:57-08:00","id":1179689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1179684#post1179684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A vampire in torpor long enough will go down to one dot of blood potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any mention that it only will or can reduce them to 1 Blood Potency? I'm just thinking of thor century long torpor and thinking on how to get that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T18:54:55-08:00","id":1179693,"title":"","content":"It used to be you couldn't drop below 1 BP but now there are more different things with a permanent/indefinite 0 Blood Potency rating and powers that can purposely and permanently/indefinitely knock you down to 0 BP I'd say it's ST discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T21:36:40-08:00","id":1179732,"title":"","content":"As fascinating as the implication of deliberately dropping to BP0 to gain the advantages we have the mechanics for is, I feel like the fact of what torpor is makes it clear the answer is &quot;no&quot; \u2014 relative Humanity means nothing for the torpor of a vampire whose Blood Potency is that low, and pretty much all of the other things that reduce a vampire's BP explicitly or near-implicitly put a floor of 1 on that reduction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T00:34:51-08:00","id":1179772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1179689#post1179689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any mention that it only will or can reduce them to 1 Blood Potency? I'm just thinking of thor century long torpor and thinking on how to get that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You lose 1 point of Blood Potency every 25 years. It's mentioned twice in the core book, almost the same sentence. P89, 'For every twenty-five years a vampire spends in torpor, she loses a dot of Blood Potency.'<br /> <br /> The lowest you can get is one. This is asked and answered in the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zXoidmr88S_my76fkV-ITr27wHSdtVdeFMfcpXMkhY4/edit#heading=h.1qt04h6hl8no\" target=\"_blank\">FAQ</a>.<br /> <br /> 'How low can a normal vampire\u2019s Blood Potency go in torpor?<br /> A vampire\u2019s Blood Potency can go as low as 1.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T18:47:08-08:00","id":1180005,"title":"","content":"If my Prince issues a command to capture a powerful rogue vampire who could easily destroy him, because the Prince wants to question him, how could the Prince ensure the vampire does not cause chaos and answers the questions? The rogue vampire could be staked until questioning is ready, but after that? I was thinking of having this vampire blood bonded to the Prince, but aren't older vampires immune to blood bonds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","name":"Sean Snyder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T19:23:35-08:00","id":1180018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sean Snyder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1180005#post1180005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my Prince issues a command to capture a powerful rogue vampire who could easily destroy him, because the Prince wants to question him, how could the Prince ensure the vampire does not cause chaos and answers the questions? The rogue vampire could be staked until questioning is ready, but after that? I was thinking of having this vampire blood bonded to the Prince, but aren't older vampires immune to blood bonds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Older vampires are immune to vitae addiction, but they are still vulnerable to the blood bond. Your Prince could blood bond the rogue kindred, and proceed to keep using dominate on the rogue kindred until they are the Prince's pet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T19:29:42-08:00","id":1180021,"title":"","content":"Older vampires aren't immune to blood bonds. It's possible they can resist the formation of each step if they spend willpower, same as any other vampire but if their BP is higher than the prospective regnant's they have a better resist chance. Blood bonds only last for a year so it's not exactly intelligent to assume a blood bond is an infallible shield.<br /> Feeding him 3+ separate times to blood bond him before unstaking him would be the most likely yield a full vinculum.<br /> If this vampire is significantly more powerful than the prince (and I'm not referring to power as solely a blood potency factor) other vampires may well not go against that vampire, possibly assisting him in undermining the prince's plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T09:26:36-08:00","id":1180185,"title":"","content":"Blood Bonding him would be a very good step. While they do only last a year, it might be worth mentioning they last a year from the last drink. Make it a habit to feed the vampire once a month or something and it will never end. If you treat the bonded vampire well, it could build a very powerful second in command as you should be able to trust something bonded explicitly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T13:39:57-08:00","id":1180232,"title":"","content":"I have 6 players, do I need to come up with a Sire for each of them? I was thinking of just making two and splitting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23777-erdrix","name":"Erdrix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T13:44:27-08:00","id":1180237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erdrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1180232#post1180232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have 6 players, do I need to come up with a Sire for each of them? I was thinking of just making two and splitting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let the players come up with their own sires. Letting players create part of the setting makes them more invested (and often makes a setting feel more rich since not everything is created by a single person) and it saves you some time and energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T13:58:25-08:00","id":1180239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1180237#post1180237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let the players come up with their own sires. Letting players create part of the setting makes them more invested (and often makes a setting feel more rich since not everything is created by a single person) and it saves you some time and energy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Problem with that is half of them would come up with Bob from accounting and the other half would be Louis from Interview. Though, they are world building in our prelude even though every place they come up with is a variation of a bar. <br /> <br /> Basically, I want to know if it's necessary or can I get away with two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23777-erdrix","name":"Erdrix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T14:01:39-08:00","id":1180240,"title":"","content":"You can always handwave some of them as just ''the sire exist'' no need for a name or anything if the sire never make a show in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T14:14:52-08:00","id":1180245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erdrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1180239#post1180239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Problem with that is half of them would come up with Bob from accounting and the other half would be Louis from Interview. Though, they are world building in our prelude even though every place they come up with is a variation of a bar.<br /> <br /> Basically, I want to know if it's necessary or can I get away with two.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Make it so that none of them know their sire, Problem solved. For whatever hand waving reason, they were created and left. only make the sire if it's important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T14:31:41-08:00","id":1180251,"title":"","content":"So, it's really not as import as I was thinking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23777-erdrix","name":"Erdrix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T14:38:10-08:00","id":1180252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erdrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1180251#post1180251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it's really not as import as I was thinking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely depends on what role you'd have them planned in the game. Some sires can be extremely important to have thought out while others might be completely non-existent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T14:38:57-08:00","id":1180253,"title":"","content":"As most other things, is as importatn as the story demands. You can handwave it now and later if the story goes that way (for example if none know their Sires and one or more wnat to find out who they were), you can come up with something interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:09:35-08:00","id":1180258,"title":"","content":"Thank you everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23777-erdrix","name":"Erdrix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:45:44-08:00","id":1180327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erdrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1180251#post1180251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it's really not as import as I was thinking?</div> </div> </div> </div>It really, really depends on the game and on the player. I've had players who didn't care at all about their sire, and I've had players who were heavily invested in their sire. I'd ask your players to see what they think would be the most fun for them, and go from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T01:53:37-08:00","id":1180367,"title":"","content":"are these adaptations OP(well mortals are lost against a Protean 2, Resilience 2 vampire anyway if they are not a swat crew):<br /> -Hunter pelt: +2 armor against mundane weapons<br /> -Feline sinew: +1 Dex or Wits (or both, result is meant to be +1 defense)<br /> -Poison glands: +1 lethal if coated on claws, will cause Blindness if spat in the eyes<br /> (This keyboard lacks a question mark key)<br /> Advice, criticism, opinions, your own custom adaptations(the latter one only if generosity compels you) are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12198-alexanderbk","name":"alexanderbk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T05:33:48-08:00","id":1181092,"title":"","content":"Before &quot;A thousand years of night&quot; has been released, some people suggested making Devotions with high Bloog Potency requirements as an effective substitute for higher dots in disciplines. Are there indeed some Devotions with high BP prerequisite in ATYoN? <br /> <br /> If not, does it mean that high BP requirements have been entirely abandoned as a model for elder powers? Or is it still a valid option in homebrew material (i.e., does it fit reasonably well with the rest of the system)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","user":"Lanic","date":". 01-31-2018, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T09:57:19-08:00","id":1181155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181092#post1181092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before &quot;A thousand years of night&quot; has been released, some people suggested making Devotions with high Bloog Potency requirements as an effective substitute for higher dots in disciplines. Are there indeed some Devotions with high BP prerequisite in ATYoN?<br /> <br /> If not, does it mean that high BP requirements have been entirely abandoned as a model for elder powers? Or is it still a valid option in homebrew material (i.e., does it fit reasonably well with the rest of the system)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually I was surprised to have not found any devotion with high BP requirement as per Dark Decree in 1st ed. I would say that for me is still valid as homebrew but to answer to your question, no, there aren't high BP devotions in ATYoN unfortunately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T15:36:16-08:00","id":1181509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181092#post1181092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before &quot;A thousand years of night&quot; has been released, some people suggested making Devotions with high Bloog Potency requirements as an effective substitute for higher dots in disciplines. Are there indeed some Devotions with high BP prerequisite in ATYoN?<br /> <br /> If not, does it mean that high BP requirements have been entirely abandoned as a model for elder powers? Or is it still a valid option in homebrew material (i.e., does it fit reasonably well with the rest of the system)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It fits fine as a design point for homebrew. Also note that while the Thousand Years Devotions don't specifically require Blood Potency or age, many of them are prohibitively <i>expensive</i> for thinner-blooded Kindred to use, similarly to Juggernaut's Gait in the corebook. When a Devotion costs five Vitae per turn of use, vampires below Blood Potency 5 need to focus the blood over time just to use it for one turn, and even the Blood Potency 5 vampire, with a full Vitae pool, will completely drain herself after three turns. Thicker blooded vampires gain more use out of expensive Devotions because they have the reserves to store up for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:02:37-08:00","id":1181716,"title":"","content":"What happens if you try to drink from someone you think is mortal but is actually a supernatural you don't have Unnatural Affinity for? Obviously you don't get any Vitae but do they still take damage? RAW looks like no but I'm not positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:28:52-08:00","id":1181722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181716#post1181716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if you try to drink from someone you think is mortal but is actually a supernatural you don't have Unnatural Affinity for? Obviously you don't get any Vitae but do they still take damage? RAW looks like no but I'm not positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they naturally take damage from blood loss? In that case they simply take the damage. Also, if they still have blood the vampire should get nourishment from the blood as if they drank human blood. Unnatural Affinity upgrades that blood to count as Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T11:30:08-08:00","id":1181723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181716#post1181716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if you try to drink from someone you think is mortal but is actually a supernatural you don't have Unnatural Affinity for? Obviously you don't get any Vitae but do they still take damage? RAW looks like no but I'm not positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things:<br /> <br /> 1: You dont have to have Unnatural affinity to feed on something that is not mortal. BP 1 Neonate Joe can drink werewolf or changeling blood same as human blood. ( though I assume it would be harder to catch a werewolf and pin them down to eat them. ) Unnatural Affinity is for BP 6 Elder Bob who can't feed on humans and doesnt want to worry about Blood Bonds, so he takes that to feed on werewolves (or whatever) because it's worth it to him...<br /> <br /> <br /> 2: I suppose it would depend on what exactly they were. Changelings would still take the lethal for the blood loss because OUCH getting drained hurts. Vampires wouldn't because vampires don't get bothered with blood loss as a living thing does. <br /> <br /> ( this one is a house rule for me) Werewolves don't take Lethal damage unless you're taking more than 1 per round. Because werewolves give 2.5 x how much you would be doing. and it just gets complicated if you are only taking say less than a half of a lethal every turn in damage... However, say you can take 10 Vitae in a turn because your BP is 10, so that would be like 3 Lethal in blood loss... <br /> <br /> I hope that made sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:04:16-08:00","id":1181766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181716#post1181716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if you try to drink from someone you think is mortal but is actually a supernatural you don't have Unnatural Affinity for? Obviously you don't get any Vitae but do they still take damage? RAW looks like no but I'm not positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify further, what Unnatural Affinity does is it lets vampires who aren't nourished by mortal blood nourish themselves by feeding from that supernatural being as if they were feeding from vampire blood. It's for thick-blooded vampires who would rather hunt down changelings than risk the Vinculum or burn Willpower.<br /> <br /> Drinking somebody's blood damages them. I don't agree with Vitalis's house rule. Werewolf blood doesn't, to my knowledge, yield more vitae than mortal blood, a Blood Potency 10 vampire is still just draining one Vitae of blood per turn, and werewolves have to spend Essence to regenerate lethal damage on a per-turn basis. Just feed from werewolves like you would any other non-vampire supernatural, and be prepared for them to get very angry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 02-02-2018, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T13:08:07-08:00","id":1181770,"title":"","content":"&quot;The number of Vitae taken may not exceed the vampire\u2019s Blood Potency dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Page 94. Requires the Feed move so won't apply to the Kiss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-02-2018, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T14:20:38-08:00","id":1181797,"title":"","content":"Well, I stand corrected.<br /> <br /> Although that's still a maximum, not an automatic value, so you'd have to roll ten successes to extract that much Vitae in one turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:16:54-08:00","id":1181814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181770#post1181770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The number of Vitae taken may not exceed the vampire\u2019s Blood Potency dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Page 94. Requires the Feed move so won't apply to the Kiss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had assumed in combat (feed move), when I gave the example. yes<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181766#post1181766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To clarify further, what Unnatural Affinity does is it lets vampires who aren't nourished by mortal blood nourish themselves by feeding from that supernatural being as if they were feeding from vampire blood. It's for thick-blooded vampires who would rather hunt down changelings than risk the Vinculum or burn Willpower.<br /> <br /> Drinking somebody's blood damages them. I don't agree with Vitalis's house rule. Werewolf blood doesn't, to my knowledge, yield more vitae than mortal blood, a Blood Potency 10 vampire is still just draining one Vitae of blood per turn, and werewolves have to spend Essence to regenerate lethal damage on a per-turn basis. Just feed from werewolves like you would any other non-vampire supernatural, and be prepared for them to get very angry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are at least 2 threads in here somewhere that list what different splat blood does. my google fu sucks but I am sure others can verify<br /> <br /> Were-creature 2.5 and it gave a -1 per vitae taken to aggressive frenzy checks<br /> Promethean .5 and tasted like crap<br /> Changeling normal, but it made you higher than a kite.<br /> Mage normal - but you would see magical things<br /> Demon in cover Normal<br /> Demon in demon form, unknown /varies<br /> Ghoul Normal<br /> Geist was also .5 if I am not mistaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-02-2018, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:20:40-08:00","id":1181818,"title":"","content":"That was first edition, and I believe it was Rose Bailey who said that they scrapped the whole concept for second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:29:01-08:00","id":1181822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181818#post1181818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was first edition, and I believe it was Rose Bailey who said that they scrapped the whole concept for second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're right it was 1E, but I am pretty sure in one of the debates she came on and said it was perfectly fine to keep it... Though I cant find it at all, but I did find this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/578185-what-might-be-the-effects-of-drinking-blood-from-other-major-splats\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...r-major-splats</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924390-effects-of-vampires-drinking-from-supernatural-beings\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924390-effects-of-vampires-drinking-from-supernatural-beings\"> Effects of Vampires drinking from supernatural beings - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924390-effects-of-vampires-drinking-from-supernatural-beings\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/924390-effects-of-vampires-drinking-from-supernatural-beings </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Reading VTR 1e i found certain outcomes but am curious about others \u200bMages- causes hallucinations and derangements, Vitae intake same as normal humans </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:29:45-08:00","id":1181823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181814#post1181814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are at least 2 threads in here somewhere that list what different splat blood does. my google fu sucks but I am sure others can verify</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1050476-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-changeling-edition?p=1153184#post1153184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings can absorb Glamour from any sophont with emotions. Vampires count. Ghosts count. <b>No special effects for taking energy from specific other monsters... we've been trying to cut down on those in second edition, because it means making up a wide variety of special effects and if every one is just a different flavor of magic potion, the fun gets lost.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">characterlimit</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:33:17-08:00","id":1181825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1181823#post1181823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">characterlimit</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That's new. I don't really keep up with the changeling thread as much as the vampire ones. But even in that thread people refer to enjoying the strange rules. So each to their own!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T19:23:57-08:00","id":1181888,"title":"","content":"Just found an old thread where Rose confirmed how Unnatural Affinity is supposed to work, so forget about that part of my question I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T07:59:53-08:00","id":1182264,"title":"","content":"When creating a Ghoul, is the Willpower loss permanent or is it like just spending a point of Willpower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","name":"Raktus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T08:17:58-08:00","id":1182268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1182264#post1182264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When creating a Ghoul, is the Willpower loss permanent or is it like just spending a point of Willpower?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's just spending a point of willpower <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T06:51:27-08:00","id":1182579,"title":"","content":"DISCLAIMER: This isn't even remotely related to Vampire, or anything in the Chronicles of Darkness. Just a simple question to which simple answers are welcome. Also, knowing myself pretty well, there will likely be a lot of stuff said that isn't important for the question, I'll just ramble. Sort of like I'm doing right now...<br /> <br /> So last year for my birthday, my girlfriend made me a carrot cake, because those are my favorite. She made it with pineapples, not knowing that I'm allergic, and I ate it and broke out in hives, it was a lot of fun. She felt super bad. I laughed. Side note: Three days later I made us mango and peach smoothies, forgetting I'm also allergic to mangoes. I promptly broke out in hives again. Anyway, she's also made me cheesecakes because those are also my favorite. I'm allowed to have two favorites! Now, being a trained culinary arts professional like she is, she thought it might be fun to make a carrot cake flavored cheesecake, so she went online to find some recipes but couldn't find anything other than people making carrot cakes and putting a cheesecake on top of it, which is not what she wanted. So she made this cheesecake last night, I haven't been able to eat it yet because it wasn't the appointed time (I believe the stars have to be aligned in just the right way), and it looks pretty cool. It's got the spices and whatnot inside that go into carrot cakes, with shredded carrots decorating the sides and a large marzipan carrot on top, to which she took a toothpick dipped in cocoa powder to make the carrot look more real. Which brings me to my question: Does a carrot cake flavored cheesecake sound good?<br /> <br /> Also, to make this more appropriate for the Vampire theme, what would be the proper roll for resisting the urge to eat it before she wakes up? I was thinking that I would spend a point of Willpower and roll Resolve + Composure.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot to mention that she came up with the recipe herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23703,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","user":"Sean Snyder","date":". 02-05-2018, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","name":"Sean Snyder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T08:03:38-08:00","id":1182601,"title":"","content":"Roll as if for frenzy. Remember that you can opt to Ride the Wave and go binge eating, I don't know, hamburgers instead? <br /> <br /> Carrot cake flavoured cheese cake sounds absolutely delicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T00:48:06-08:00","id":1182830,"title":"","content":"Update: Carrot cake flavored cheesecake is very delicious. I highly recommend it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","name":"Sean Snyder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T03:28:10-08:00","id":1182857,"title":"","content":"Whyyyyyyy???? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I miss Rose already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T10:01:00-08:00","id":1182968,"title":"","content":"What happened with Rose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T10:09:47-08:00","id":1182973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1182968#post1182968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happened with Rose?</div> </div> </div> </div>She left Onyx Path as a full time employee. I believe she will be doing some freelance work with them still, and she'll still be involved in Cavaliers of Mars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T10:26:39-08:00","id":1182975,"title":"","content":"She's made several one-book RPGs on her Patreon as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-10T18:27:26-08:00","id":1184582,"title":"","content":"Ah, my bad, was thinking of call lightning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T03:16:54-08:00","id":1185529,"title":"","content":"Is it just me or is Touch of the Morrigan pretty mediocre, if not outright bad, in second edition? At least compared to first edition where it dealt damage equal to number of successes (at least 3 since that was the target number). In second edition it deals Potency amount of damage, which equals extra successes+1 instead of total amount of successes, but regular attacks can get huge dice pools through Frenzy, Vigor and Physical Intensity in second edition.<br /> It seems especially worthless for the Childer of the Morrigan who have Protean as an in clan Discipline and can get 2L AP2 claws at Protean 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T05:02:39-08:00","id":1185547,"title":"","content":"No, it's not just you, although the damage you do is actually the number of successes you rolled when you hit activation was your damage not the success target number, typically 3 would be on the low end of the damage spectrum because if you could cast the spell you were usually tossing 9 dice minimum each turn so you probably hit the target number in the first turn anyway. I don't think the 2nd ed. sorcery rules are worth the effects especially considering casting times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T05:52:51-08:00","id":1185551,"title":"","content":"I wrote successes rolled and said 3 was the minimum.<br /> <br /> And I agree that the casting times are way too long for most rituals. I actually read through rituals (and found out how underwhelming Touch of the Morrigan is) after I got the idea of making a pact with the Crone to get an instant/reflexive ritual.<br /> I'm leaning heavily towards Feeding the Crone, but Mantle of Amorous Fire is also pretty sweet. Like using Awe, only you can't resist. Costs a WP, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T08:42:33-08:00","id":1190996,"title":"","content":"I had a question about Bows and Arrows... and since I'm playing a game of Vampire this seemed like the most logical place to ask...<br /> In Hurt Locker it mentions in Combat Archery not having to take an action to load the arrow on to the string.<br /> What would the normal action economy on firing a bow, reloading and firing again be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","name":"Raktus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T08:54:01-08:00","id":1191001,"title":"","content":"I'd allow pulling out an arrow, nocking it, quickly selecting your target, and firing, to count as a single action. <br /> <br /> What you describe is two turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T09:05:42-08:00","id":1191004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1191001#post1191001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd allow pulling out an arrow, nocking it, quickly selecting your target, and firing, to count as a single action.<br /> <br /> What you describe is two turns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your ruling directly fights with the Combar Archery merit which explicitly allows to do it all as a single action. <br /> <br /> So, it should normally be shoot an arrow, next action is reload an arrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T09:12:49-08:00","id":1191006,"title":"","content":"So it takes longer to notch an arrow than to reload a gun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","name":"Raktus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T09:32:30-08:00","id":1191012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1191006#post1191006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it takes longer to notch an arrow than to reload a gun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reloading a gun is also an instant action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T09:33:20-08:00","id":1191013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1191006#post1191006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it takes longer to notch an arrow than to reload a gun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without a merit both take an action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T10:00:49-08:00","id":1191025,"title":"","content":"Does a Revenant need the Fertile Vitae Merit to use animalism 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T11:54:57-08:00","id":1191066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1191006#post1191006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it takes longer to notch an arrow than to reload a gun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. It takes longer to draw an arrow from a quiver, notch the arrow, pull the drawstring, select your target and fire than it does to pull an already preloaded magazine or cartridge from your pouch, dropping the empty one on the ground, replacing it, chambering the first bullet and firing, yes. But if you're talking about reloading a revolver or magazine cartridge or clip using a speedloader, then guess what? Pulling that arrow out, nocking it, pulling the drawstring, selecting your target and firing will be faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T16:57:40-08:00","id":1191481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1191025#post1191025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Revenant need the Fertile Vitae Merit to use animalism 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. On one hand, Anim** is described as being like the Embrace but on the other, Revenants can't full Embrace even with Fertile Vitae.<br /> I would allow it with Fertile Vitae because the player has spent XP on it, but not without that and I wouldn't allow the Devotion that lets them go weeks on one Vitae unless/until the Revenant is uplifted..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T07:14:10-08:00","id":1193097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1191481#post1191481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. On one hand, Anim** is described as being like the Embrace but on the other, Revenants can't full Embrace even with Fertile Vitae.<br /> I would allow it with Fertile Vitae because the player has spent XP on it, but not without that and I wouldn't allow the Devotion that lets them go weeks on one Vitae unless/until the Revenant is uplifted..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> good thing Revenents cant use Devotions at all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T18:15:09-08:00","id":1193379,"title":"","content":"Ha good catch, that slipped my mind completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T03:18:32-08:00","id":1193476,"title":"","content":"I was wondering how it works with former ghouls that get &quot;re-ghouled&quot;.<br /> <br /> That is, if a ghoul has a time where they do not receive any vitae, I understand that they will, at some point, be unable to sustain their &quot;ghoul nature&quot;. In this case, they will undergo accelerated aging as well as loosing the ability to use their powers.<br /> <br /> What if another vampire, at a later time, gives vitae to this former ghoul? Will the vampire in question be forced to spend a willpower point to turn the person into a ghoul again, or is the vitae enough?<br /> <br /> Also, will the ghoul re-gain all their &quot;lost&quot; disciplines? That is, will the discipline dots in the character sheet go away when they can no longer sustain themselves due to lack of vitae, or do they still remain but become &quot;inactive&quot;?<br /> <br /> Lastly, how would this be different for a member of a ghoul family?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","name":"Lorsa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T03:42:08-08:00","id":1193482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorsa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1193476#post1193476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, how would this be different for a member of a ghoul family?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any of the other questions have official answers (so do what works best in your game) but this one I can try. Ghouls from biological ghoul families are ghouls even when they run out of Vitae. When they run out of Vitae they're basically in a suppressed state rather than losing ghouldom entirely. Hence they would lose access to Disciplines but not actually lose them entirely, even if regular ghouls does that, and Vitae should be enough to &quot;reactivate&quot; them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T04:48:43-08:00","id":1193488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1193482#post1193482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think any of the other questions have official answers (so do what works best in your game) but this one I can try. Ghouls from biological ghoul families are ghouls even when they run out of Vitae. When they run out of Vitae they're basically in a suppressed state rather than losing ghouldom entirely. Hence they would lose access to Disciplines but not actually lose them entirely, even if regular ghouls does that, and Vitae should be enough to &quot;reactivate&quot; them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the answer!<br /> <br /> Since there is no official answer, perhaps I can extend the question to &quot;what would YOU do&quot;? Getting some ideas for how other people would rule would help me decide what works best for my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","name":"Lorsa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:30:15-08:00","id":1193518,"title":"","content":"Depends on if the players play ghouls or are heavily invested in ghoul NPCs. In that case I'd recommend Disciplines to be suppressed rather than lost.<br /> If ghouls are less important, them losing Disciplines becomes less of a problem, and more of an incentive to keep tabs on your ghouls. Especially along with the WP cost.<br /> <br /> A third option is to have former ghouls forget Disciplines over time. For every year spent without Vitae they lose one dot of their highest Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T11:27:21-08:00","id":1193639,"title":"","content":"I think it was in the 1e Ghouls book, but at a previous point they lost Discipline dots at a rate of 6 months of lack-of-Vitae per dot. <br /> <br /> Personally I think this sucks, and that all Ghouls should retain their &quot;knowledge&quot;, even if they have an acclimation period on acquiring Vitae again. It's good descriptive fodder and material for role-playing, even if the ghoul in question is an NPC.<br /> <br /> Fortunate, 2e agrees. P. 298 &quot;A ghoul in withdrawal cannot use any Disciplines (even those that do not cost Vitae or which have persistent effects), but retains knowledge of them if his withdrawal ends.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, following on the above by inference: once a ghoul, always a ghoul--you do not need further Willpower to consume and make use of Vitae again, ever.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T01:24:32-08:00","id":1194182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1193639#post1193639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was in the 1e Ghouls book, but at a previous point they lost Discipline dots at a rate of 6 months of lack-of-Vitae per dot.<br /> <br /> Personally I think this sucks, and that all Ghouls should retain their &quot;knowledge&quot;, even if they have an acclimation period on acquiring Vitae again. It's good descriptive fodder and material for role-playing, even if the ghoul in question is an NPC.<br /> <br /> Fortunate, 2e agrees. P. 298 &quot;A ghoul in withdrawal cannot use any Disciplines (even those that do not cost Vitae or which have persistent effects), but retains knowledge of them if his withdrawal ends.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, following on the above by inference: once a ghoul, always a ghoul--you do not need further Willpower to consume and make use of Vitae again, ever.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the added information. In that case I guess the difference is that a member of a ghoul family may actually use &quot;no cost&quot; Disciplines even if they are in withdrawal?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5082-lorsa","name":"Lorsa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T12:41:13-07:00","id":1194329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorsa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1194182#post1194182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the added information. In that case I guess the difference is that a member of a ghoul family may actually use &amp;quot;no cost&amp;quot; Disciplines even if they are in withdrawal?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a valid family merit, and it was hinted (in VtR book IIRC) that was exactly what a family in Japan had. They do not get that benefit automatically, however... Unless you want to do that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T04:38:57-07:00","id":1195219,"title":"","content":"What would be a fitting effect of getting an Exceptional Success when Lashing Out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T04:59:47-07:00","id":1195224,"title":"","content":"Nothing. Not every exceptional success is entitled to anything beyond the results.<br /> The one who got the exceptional success (and only that person) gets the relevant bonus doubled against their victim for the duration.<br /> The victim has two of the three different lash out loss conditions inflicted. The first one from the attacker's chosen aura. The second one, determined by the victim's highest innate Power Attribute. (I wouldn't stack the same effect personally since they could get resolved for a single event but whatever... )<br /> Some other scene long minor effect adjudicated by the ST based on the context of the encounter.<br /> If the Lash Out was to dispel Majesty, Nightmare etc. the one using the discipline finds themself under the effects of the power in regards to the one lashing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-14-2018, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T05:12:52-07:00","id":1195230,"title":"","content":"Im with tsusasi on this that it don't need anything but tsusasi gives some good examples, so let's give some other ones. <br /> The vampire get Sated because the beast is contempt with being so obviously superior.<br /> Regaining a point of willpower.<br /> Gain the 8-again quality to peruse the aspects interest as well as the +2. <br /> Get Inspired towards the aspects interest. <br /> The victim is so cowed by the aspect it looses 10-again against her for as long she has the corresponding condition or just a flat -2 perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:25:52-07:00","id":1195890,"title":"","content":"I'm rereading Birthing the God (the Cr\u00faac rite in Thousand Years of Night).<br /> Is &quot;For every five Vitae spent creating the god, it has a level of Size.&quot; supposed to count the Vitae spent on Attributes/Disciplines, or is it a separate cost?<br /> <br /> Edit: Same thing with Blood Potency. Is it supposed to be granted separately, or is Attributes/Disciplines, Blood Potency and Size tied together based on how much Vitae you dump into the ritual?<br /> <br /> Second edit: Does &quot;common Disciplines&quot; exclude the Clan unique Disciplines? I'd really like to see such a creature with Protean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-15-2018, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T11:08:15-07:00","id":1196132,"title":"","content":"Reading the devotion: shatter the shroud I suddenly became aware to haven't understood how auspex + predatory aura works vs obfuscated kindred.<br /> I always thought that with Auspex 1 (winning the clash) you were able to perceive the kindred presence (without actually seeing her), and, lashing out, you were able to shatter any obfuscate power active on her or activated by her, making her visible for anyone.<br /> <br /> If it is not working in such way, could you please clarify this point to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T11:42:34-07:00","id":1196149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196132#post1196132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the devotion: shatter the shroud I suddenly became aware to haven't understood how auspex + predatory aura works vs obfuscated kindred.<br /> I always thought that with Auspex 1 (winning the clash) you were able to perceive the kindred presence (without actually seeing her), and, lashing out, you were able to shatter any obfuscate power active on her or activated by her, making her visible for anyone.<br /> <br /> If it is not working in such way, could you please clarify this point to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>The advantage of Shatter the Shroud is that it works on any supernatural hiding ability and doesn't require an extra roll or a point of Willpower \u2014 it allows you to simply spend two Vitae and break the veil if if you win the initial Clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:16:31-07:00","id":1196158,"title":"","content":"Lashing Out to end Obfuscate only works on the third dot. Not the first or fourth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T21:55:15-07:00","id":1196365,"title":"","content":"So...how exactly do the passive/active effects of Resilience work? Say a vampire with Resilience 2 takes 5 aggravated damage from fire, and they activate the active effect.<br /> <br /> They already downgrade two of that damage into lethal because of the passive effect.<br /> Does the active effect ignore two <i>more</i> of the remaining 3 aggravated damage, resulting in 1A, 2L from the attack?<br /> <br /> Or does it 'upgrade' the passive effect, causing the two points of damage that would have been downgraded to be ignored instead, resulting in 3A from the attack?<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards the latter, but not sure how correct that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T22:43:36-07:00","id":1196374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1195890#post1195890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm rereading Birthing the God (the Cr\u00faac rite in Thousand Years of Night).<br /> Is &quot;For every five Vitae spent creating the god, it has a level of Size.&quot; supposed to count the Vitae spent on Attributes/Disciplines, or is it a separate cost?<br /> <br /> Edit: Same thing with Blood Potency. Is it supposed to be granted separately, or is Attributes/Disciplines, Blood Potency and Size tied together based on how much Vitae you dump into the ritual?<br /> <br /> Second edit: Does &quot;common Disciplines&quot; exclude the Clan unique Disciplines? I'd really like to see such a creature with Protean.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Birthing is in Secrets of the covenant?<br /> <br /> So the way its worded i would say that you contribute blood for its attributes + powers, and then for every 3 or 5 blood contributed it gets the size and blood potency. Ie its not an extra cost. (otherwise it should have said &quot;Thw god has a base size of X and for every 3 extra blood contributed it gains an additional point.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for common disciplines i think this does mean no clan disciplines. I think the way its worded means one of the contributing vampires needs to have the discipline except for Resiliance, vigor and celerity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T23:21:24-07:00","id":1196378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196365#post1196365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm leaning towards the latter, but not sure how correct that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bearing in mind the forever-quandary of leaning too hard on semantics, it <i>does</i> specify that the passive effect applies whenever damage is <i>dealt</i>, and generally damage from a single source is modified up or down <i>before</i> dealing it to a subject.<br /> <br /> Resilience dots overlapping their active and passive effects rather than stacking them effectively makes the active effect &quot;spend one Vitae to heal [Resilience] points of aggravated damage as it is received,&quot; which is nothing to sneeze at, but the stacking read has the benefit of also making it so that a defensive power that specifically works on things that normally cut through your natural undead defenses enables a vampire who has it to bounce back with less downtime, which is in keeping with the literal name of the Discipline. (But again, semantics might not be the strongest basis for decision-making. Granted, this <i>is</i> also the Discipline that makes you harder to stake and lets you recover from superficial whole-body harm with a single point of Vitae \u2014 if anything had a strong claim for cutting five days of recovery down to one, it would be Resilience.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T23:35:26-07:00","id":1196384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196365#post1196365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...how exactly do the passive/active effects of Resilience work? Say a vampire with Resilience 2 takes 5 aggravated damage from fire, and they activate the active effect.<br /> <br /> They already downgrade two of that damage into lethal because of the passive effect.<br /> Does the active effect ignore two <i>more</i> of the remaining 3 aggravated damage, resulting in 1A, 2L from the attack?<br /> <br /> Or does it 'upgrade' the passive effect, causing the two points of damage that would have been downgraded to be ignored instead, resulting in 3A from the attack?<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards the latter, but not sure how correct that is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did think the former but when considering it, 2 resilience negating 4 agg seems really powerful (esp resilience 3 meaning only 2L taken). So id say its probably the latter, and the active effect overrides the persistent. (Does vigor celerity have anything in their write ups that would support this?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-17-2018, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T01:02:42-07:00","id":1196409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196374#post1196374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for common disciplines i think this does mean no clan disciplines. I think the way its worded means one of the contributing vampires needs to have the discipline except for Resiliance, vigor and celerity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The five common disciplines are: Vigor, Celerity, Resilience, Obfuscate, and Animalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T05:48:34-07:00","id":1196454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196365#post1196365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...how exactly do the passive/active effects of Resilience work? Say a vampire with Resilience 2 takes 5 aggravated damage from fire, and they activate the active effect.<br /> <br /> They already downgrade two of that damage into lethal because of the passive effect.<br /> Does the active effect ignore two <i>more</i> of the remaining 3 aggravated damage, resulting in 1A, 2L from the attack?<br /> <br /> Or does it 'upgrade' the passive effect, causing the two points of damage that would have been downgraded to be ignored instead, resulting in 3A from the attack?<br /> <br /> I'm leaning towards the latter, but not sure how correct that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Resilence active effects are reflexive so.you can use whenever in the turn. That implies that the passive effect occur before:<br /> You downgrade [resilence] aggravated damage (since it's not an action. It simply happens) than you can activate reflexively one or more effect at once. I.e. you can spend 1 bp to ignore [resilence] aggravated damage (the remaining one) and another bo to ignore the remaining [resilence+1] not aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> I.e.: you have resilence 2 and take 4 damages from fire or claws of unholy. <br /> You suffer just 2 aggravated and 2 lethals. Than you spend 2 bp; one to ignore the 2 remaining aggravated and one to ignore up to 3 (but you have just 2) lethal damages. You don't take any damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-17-2018, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T06:39:09-07:00","id":1196462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196454#post1196454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I.e.: you have resilence 2 and take 4 damages from fire or claws of unholy.<br /> You suffer just 2 aggravated and 2 lethals. Than you spend 2 bp; one to ignore the 2 remaining aggravated and one to ignore up to 3 (but you have just 2) lethal damages. You don't take any damage</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're just making it confusing by mixing two damage sources without separating them. I'm not sure if you mean that both types of damage are equal (which isn't true since Claws of the Unholy isn't a bane) or if you mean two damage from each source since that's what the math more closely resembles.<br /> Also, BP generally refers to Blood Potency, which can also be confusing for people not used to Masquerade.<br /> <br /> If your example is four damage from fire (4A), the character first downgrades two points to lethal (2A+2L), and can spend a Vitae to ignore two points of damage (2L).<br /> If your example is four points of damage from Claws of the Unholy (4), the character first automatically downgrades two points to lethal (2A+2L) and can spend a Vitae to ignore three points of damage (1L).<br /> Doing the math for myself I think you're confused about the two active effects of Resilience. One removes [dots+1] non-bane damage and the other removes [dots] bane damage. Agg damage is not automatically bane damage, and bane damage that has been downgraded is still damage from a bane. If it did Resilience would be able to remove twice as much aggravated damage than lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:01:21-07:00","id":1196465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196374#post1196374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Birthing is in Secrets of the covenant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Total brain fart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the way its worded i would say that you contribute blood for its attributes + powers, and then for every 3 or 5 blood contributed it gets the size and blood potency. Ie its not an extra cost. (otherwise it should have said &quot;Thw god has a base size of X and for every 3 extra blood contributed it gains an additional point.&quot; </div> </div> </div>It just seems a bit weird to me since Size doesn't scale very smoothly. If you want to create just a basic servant you'll be able to gain something with Size 5. On the other hand, if you want something that is an unstoppable juggernaut (as the name of the Rite implies) you could easily reach double digits in Size, which is prohibitively massive. Not from the damage taken for performing the right (Resilience grants both Health and damage reduction) but in that it'll be close to impossible to hide or bring it to inhabited areas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for common disciplines i think this does mean no clan disciplines. I think the way its worded means one of the contributing vampires needs to have the discipline except for Resiliance, vigor and celerity. </div> </div> </div>That &quot;Alternatively&quot; is throwing me off. It sounds like you can give it all common Disciplines and Cr\u00faac, or you can choose only the physical Disciplines and only then are they for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:01:38-07:00","id":1196466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196462#post1196462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you're just making it confusing by mixing two damage sources without separating them. I'm not sure if you mean that both types of damage are equal (which isn't true since Claws of the Unholy isn't a bane) or if you mean two damage from each source since that's what the math more closely resembles.<br /> Also, BP generally refers to Blood Potency, which can also be confusing for people not used to Masquerade.<br /> <br /> If your example is four damage from fire (4A), the character first downgrades two points to lethal (2A+2L), and can spend a Vitae to ignore two points of damage (2L).<br /> If your example is four points of damage from Claws of the Unholy (4), the character first automatically downgrades two points to lethal (2A+2L) and can spend a Vitae to ignore three points of damage (1L).<br /> Doing the math for myself I think you're confused about the two active effects of Resilience. One removes [dots+1] non-bane damage and the other removes [dots] bane damage. Agg damage is not automatically bane damage, and bane damage that has been downgraded is still damage from a bane. If it did Resilience would be able to remove twice as much aggravated damage than lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got your point but let me try this way: both resilence and normal healing are reflexive so, in the fire case, I could use 1 vitae to normally heal 2Lethal and 1 vitae for resilence to ignore 2 Agg. Is it right?<br /> <br /> About claws of unholy, the merit states that it ignores any armor except resilence, since resilence passive effect doesn't work as an armor while the active effect does, it still should be possible to heal the 2 lethal then use the active resilence to ignore 2 agg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-17-2018, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:22:12-07:00","id":1196471,"title":"","content":"You can use the active Resilience to ignore 2A and 1L since two dots of Resilience can ignore three points of damage. Then you can use one Vitae to heal the remaining 1 lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:38:17-07:00","id":1196478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196471#post1196471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use the active Resilience to ignore 2A and 1L since two dots of Resilience can ignore three points of damage. Then you can use one Vitae to heal the remaining 1 lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I always considered this active effect not valid for aggravated... actually I always confused aggravated with bane damages. I just went to read it better. Thanks, seems even better than how I always used it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-17-2018, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T11:05:30-07:00","id":1196537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196471#post1196471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use the active Resilience to ignore 2A and 1L since two dots of Resilience can ignore three points of damage. Then you can use one Vitae to heal the remaining 1 lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not realize that the first active effect of Resilience also effects aggravated damage. Huh. Well, time to buy Resilience for my Mekhet now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T18:19:43-07:00","id":1196670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196537#post1196537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did not realize that the first active effect of Resilience also effects aggravated damage. Huh. Well, time to buy Resilience for my Mekhet now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth remembering that sunlight damage explicitly doesn't get the benefits of Resilience and fire damage isn't made any more effective than usual by the Tenebrous Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T19:16:44-07:00","id":1196683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1196670#post1196670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth remembering that sunlight damage explicitly doesn't get the benefits of Resilience and fire damage isn't made any more effective than usual by the Tenebrous Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I remember. I'm just in an eras game right now as a Mekhet, so I figure splashing some resilience will be useful when Obfuscate inevitably fails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T04:05:08-07:00","id":1199342,"title":"","content":"If you are mass embraced from a heap of massacre victims, or otherwise brought into unlife by a careless sire or rushed for time all filthy and such, is there a way to change what the Cleansing &quot;resets&quot; you to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T05:57:21-07:00","id":1199351,"title":"","content":"I think they talked about this in first edition, but if a vampire embraced a dead Promethian, would the new vampire remember being a Promethian or would it be born anew? I ask because Promethians are related to corpses and humanity, if only vaguely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T06:19:44-07:00","id":1199355,"title":"","content":"I definitely think that a vampire invested enough to ask around will eventually find some ritual to &quot;reset&quot; the Cleansing. I don't know of one in published material, and I imagine different covenants have discovered different rituals in different regions; it's good story bait to work out with your Storyteller.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what the question is, re: Promethean Embrace. Is it whether the Embrace would rise as a Kindred or as a recreated Promethean? Or whether the vampire would rise with the Promethean's memories or with none at all? Points to consider:<ul><li>It might simply be that the Embrace fails: the body lacked even the aftertraces of life necessary for undeath. This may be more likely for Prometheans hewn from nonliving material, such as the Unfleshed.</li> <li>If the Promethean was created primarily from a single living body, one might consider the strange possibility that the Embrace raises <i>the original living human</i> to living death as a vampire, as if the Promethean's existence had been lost time or deleted footage.</li> <li>The Embrace definitely wouldn't raise a body as once again Created simply by using the remains of one. A Matchless exception case aspected to the Blood is possible, but probably requires more extreme circumstances, which might not even involve an attempted Embrace.</li> <li>If a vampire rises with the vestiges of the Promethean's false life, its knowledge is probably especially spotty and limited, like rising from the generative act all over again. The intelligence of a Promethean is partly learned and partly inborn from the Azothic Memory, and once the Azoth gutters with the Promethean's final death, the Blood will not stoke it.</li> <li>The body might rise with no human or quasihuman intelligence at all. Fear this possibility. In the best case scenario, it's a waste of blood. More likely, you've given the Beast a body without the Man to hold it back, a natural-born draugr. Or if it is intelligent, you might have inadvertantly permitted the darkness within the Blood to incubate a Bird of Dis into the world.</li> </ul>I'm personally inclined to maintain the finality of a Promethean's last death: some manner of conceptual persistence beyond material death is one of the treasures of the soul they seek through the Great Work. So if I ran a game in which this happened, I would probably opt first for the rising of a draugr, second for something strixlike, and third for the undead life of the person whose body was used to construct the Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T06:19:56-07:00","id":1199356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199351#post1199351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they talked about this in first edition, but if a vampire embraced a dead Promethian, would the new vampire remember being a Promethian or would it be born anew? I ask because Promethians are related to corpses and humanity, if only vaguely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not one of the writers or anything, but i'm pretty sure if you're going off the book alone, a Promethean can't be embraced to begin with. I may be wrong, but unless there is some extra material you're referring to they can't.<br /> <br /> Having said that, assuming they can be, vampires have touchstones of their past lives, which mean they'd have to remember them at least a bit, especially if recently turned. A promo to vamp will probably remember and may forget later on. Of course this opens up the can of worms of them never having had humanity to remember to fend off the beast, since they were still trying to attain an understanding of humanity as a promo. But again, I'm not a writer for either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13063,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","user":"Lord Jub-Jub","date":". 03-25-2018, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T15:07:22-07:00","id":1199496,"title":"","content":"Question:<br /> <br /> So, unless I'm mistaken, ghouls who get fed on by vampires, get 1 lethal damage for any 1 vitae taken by the vampire, regardless of how much vitae the ghoul had at his disposal, correct? But, if the ghoul has vitae at his disposal, does he lose them when the vampire drinks from him?<br /> <br /> Or to rephrase the question: When a vampire drinks from a ghoul, does he inflict lethal damage, does he take the ghoul's expendable vitae, or both at the same time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T15:21:19-07:00","id":1199500,"title":"","content":"The ghoul could donate the vitae when he's fed from, but it's up to them, the vitae in their system follow their own volition. The vamp could try draining the helpless fuck for it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T15:31:47-07:00","id":1199506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199500#post1199500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ghoul could donate the vitae when he's fed from, but it's up to them, the vitae in their system follow their own volition. The vamp could try draining the helpless fuck for it though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So if I understand you correctly, a ghoul who is being fed on by a vampire can choose whether she donates her vitae points or her health? So if a vampire NPC subjects the player ghoul to 'the kiss', the player can then choose whether he distances himself from his vitae, or keeps his vitae and takes lethal damage instead?<br /> <br /> Any quote, page number or reference from a book or other official source to back this up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T16:01:47-07:00","id":1199518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199506#post1199506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So if I understand you correctly, a ghoul who is being fed on by a vampire can choose whether she donates her vitae points or her health? So if a vampire NPC subjects the player ghoul to 'the kiss', the player can then choose whether he distances himself from his vitae, or keeps his vitae and takes lethal damage instead?<br /> <br /> Any quote, page number or reference from a book or other official source to back this up?</div> </div> </div> </div>SO i thought that once the ghoul imbibed the vitae it was digested as normal in his system and converted to a energy source and isnt actual blood sitting around somewhere to be stolen. So they will get treated like all other humans and take lethal damage per blood drained, as far as i remember and i may be remembering from any version of vampire, you cant access/drink just the vitae in a ghoul.<br /> <br /> I'll try find some source for this though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-25-2018, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T16:11:18-07:00","id":1199522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199506#post1199506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So if I understand you correctly, a ghoul who is being fed on by a vampire can choose whether she donates her vitae points or her health? So if a vampire NPC subjects the player ghoul to 'the kiss', the player can then choose whether he distances himself from his vitae, or keeps his vitae and takes lethal damage instead?<br /> <br /> Any quote, page number or reference from a book or other official source to back this up?</div> </div> </div> </div>The workings of Vitae are exposed on <b>The Blood</b>, and no, he'd still take Lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T16:50:13-07:00","id":1199531,"title":"","content":"Okay so the ghoul still takes lethal damage from being fed on. But does he also lose his &quot;stored vitae&quot; (e.g. does he also lose vitae points) when a vampire drinks from him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T17:16:19-07:00","id":1199543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199531#post1199531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so the ghoul still takes lethal damage from being fed on. But does he also lose his &quot;stored vitae&quot; (e.g. does he also lose vitae points) when a vampire drinks from him?</div> </div> </div> </div>nope. Vitae in a ghoul isnt flowing through his veins or sitting in his stomach, the vitae gets absorbed like any other blood would and passed out his system, all thats left behind is &quot;mystical&quot; energy he can use to fuel whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T17:21:56-07:00","id":1199544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199543#post1199543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nope. Vitae in a ghoul isnt flowing through his veins or sitting in his stomach, the vitae gets absorbed like any other blood would and passed out his system, all thats left behind is &quot;mystical&quot; energy he can use to fuel whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, this is a pretty clear answer.<br /> <br /> Another question then: Is it true that ghouls lose their stored vitae points naturally if they don't actively use them? With which frequency? One point per week? Month?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T17:57:41-07:00","id":1199549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199544#post1199544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks, this is a pretty clear answer.<br /> <br /> Another question then: Is it true that ghouls lose their stored vitae points naturally if they don't actively use them? With which frequency? One point per week? Month?</div> </div> </div> </div>Im no requiem 2e expert mind you so dont take what i say as 100% gospel, i just remember reading it, which must have been from &quot;the blood&quot; book which is 1e ofc. Reading 2e it says they spend 1 vitae per month to continue being a ghoul and if they fail they gain the deprived condition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T10:11:00-07:00","id":1199749,"title":"","content":"Expert or not, your answers are welcome and do seem to be accurate so far.<br /> <br /> So, a few more questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Are ghouls by default addicted to vampire vitae (the book states they experience a fraction of their regnant's hunger for blood) or do they only become addicted when failing their Composure + Resolve roll when drinking vitae?<br /> <br /> 2. I know vampires are by default addicted to blood, but does this mean vampires always carry the 'Addicted' condition, or does the condition only come into play when drinking from another vampire?<br /> <br /> 3. When committing diablerie, you gain the 'Tainted' condition and the description of Auspex says you can use Auspex to see if a vampire carries the marks of a diablerist. Does this refer to the 'Tainted' condition? Does this mean Auspex only picks up these diablerist marks when you have the 'Tainted' condition, or does a diablerist always show up as a diablerist for someone using Auspex even after losing the 'Tainted' condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T10:35:06-07:00","id":1199758,"title":"","content":"1. I think it's safe to assume that a ghoul will eventually fail the resolve + composure roll at some point, but I don't imagine they'd be addicted by default.<br /> <br /> 2. Vampires aren't addicted to blood by default, anymore than you or I are addicted to food, or water, or air.<br /> <br /> 3. I've always assumed it was referring to the Tainted condition and run it as such. When the condition fades you're free from that particular indicator. I've heard of people who run it otherwise, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:03:56-07:00","id":1199766,"title":"","content":"1. Unless the ghoul is a PC or the NPC recently turned into one, I have them as vitae addicts. It\u2019s Russian Roulette though, eventually they\u2019re going to succumb to vitae addiction.<br /> <br /> 2. No they aren\u2019t addicted to blood by default. Nor are they addicted to vitae by default. Whenever they taste vitae (save the Embrace or delineated exceptions) the mechanics for vitae addiction and vinculum come into play. <br /> <br /> 3. I run it as detectable via Auspex only if the individual in question currently has the Tainted Condition in effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:11:15-07:00","id":1199767,"title":"","content":"3. In first edition the taint of diablerie disappears with time since Auspex used to look at the subject's aura. It's easy to connect the Tainted Condition with how it worked in first edition, but it's not actually how it works in second edition. Now you can directly ask if a person is a diablerist, and whether or not they are a diablerist doesn't change with time. They either have committed it or they haven't.<br /> Tainted is not supposed to be an indicator for diablerie. It has a different purpose, as stated in its description.<br /> <br /> Edit: But I do understand people who gets confused if they are used to first edition. My group also handles it like in first edition since that's what most of us were used to when we started our current chronicle, and there's no reason to change it during play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-26-2018, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:29:01-07:00","id":1199771,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, odd, I always thought vampires are addicted to blood, at least lore-wise. Or as Jack in Vampire The Masquerade - Bloodlines puts it: <i><b>&quot;Blood is your new rack o' lamb, it's your new champagne - blood is your new fucking heroin kid!&quot;</b></i> (yes, I know The Masquerade is a different universe, not the same as The Requiem).<br /> <br /> I might be mistaken but I was pretty certain I saw blood for vampires being referred to in a similar fashion in one of the Vampire The Requiem books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:54:18-07:00","id":1199777,"title":"","content":"Although blood is a primary ingredient of vitae, blood and vitae are not the same. Vampires need blood for sustenance, not vitae (until their blood potency is much higher). Blood does not carry any mystical properties in and of itself, vitae does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:57:49-07:00","id":1199781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199777#post1199777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although blood is a primary ingredient of vitae, blood and vitae are not the same. Vampires need blood for sustenance, not vitae (until their blood potency is much higher). Blood does not carry any mystical properties in and of itself, vitae does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, and I was under the assumption that vampires are addicted to blood, but not necessarily to vitae (unless they start drinking from other vampires of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T12:06:44-07:00","id":1199785,"title":"","content":"Blood /= Vitae<br /> <br /> Blood is the medium for Vitae to flow, it's diluted in mortals but highly concentrated in vampires.<br /> Usually the difference is, blood is in mortals, blood in vampires are vitae. The vampiric curse purifies what little vitae is in a relative large amount of blood into pure Vitae.<br /> The weaken form is essence, life, food and sex and stimulants all in one, but needed for survival. Addictive, yes but the thing you'd be a junkie after, the Beast takes care of the needs for you if you refuse.<br /> Vitae, in it's purest form is all that above spiced up to eleven, it ain't above survival anymore, it's euphoric beyond excessive eating, it's like cocaine compared to morning coffee with the benefit of also being food. That rush is more then intoxicating it's purely addictive from the first go.<br /> <br /> <br /> But sure blood is addictive to vampires in the same way food is addictive towards humans. Some people do have a problem with food, most don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 03-26-2018, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T12:17:51-07:00","id":1199791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199781#post1199781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, and I was under the assumption that vampires are addicted to blood, but not necessarily to vitae (unless they start drinking from other vampires of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That\u2019s like saying you\u2019re addicted to water. It\u2019s pursuit is a necessity for their existence, not to experience the next contact high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T12:20:44-07:00","id":1199792,"title":"","content":"'Vitae' literally means 'life' or &quot;life force'.<br /> <br /> So it goes without saying that blood =/= vitae. Because blood itself isn't life, but in World of Darkness, blood does carry the life force of a creature. Plants have very little to no life force in them. They are eaten by herbivores, who have a bit more life force in them. They are eaten by carnivores, who have more life force. And at the top of the mortal food chain is humans, with the most life force in them out of all mortal creatures. But then you get into supernatural territory and realize there are creatures with even more life force in them. Werewolves and vampires come to mind. Because don't be fooled, vampires themselves might not be alive, but they do carry a highly concentrated dosage of life force in their veins to sustain their undead state and to pull off neat supernatural tricks.<br /> <br /> That's how I'd describe vitae to a newbie.<br /> <br /> Of course there is a lot of magic mumbo-jumbo going on with vitae and vampirism if you really take a careful look at it, and some of it can't logically be explained other than &quot;that's just how it is&quot;, but if I was a scientist in the Ordo Dracul who tried to come up with a natural explanation for vitae and all that jazz, I'd probably explain it something like how I explained it above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T12:39:37-07:00","id":1199800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199791#post1199791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. That\u2019s like saying you\u2019re addicted to water. It\u2019s pursuit is a necessity for their existence, not to experience the next contact high.</div> </div> </div> </div>That being said, you don't need to be running on empty for &quot;seeing an open wound&quot; to be a potential frenzy trigger, and a vampire operating normally does not pick up an extra edge to their hunger any sooner than a BP1 specimen spending Vitae at the same rate \u2014 the extra capacity gives you a higher potential safety margin, but every vampire has &quot;hungry&quot; and &quot;starving&quot; at the same concrete levels in the absence of complicating factors like banes and injury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T12:41:00-07:00","id":1199802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199791#post1199791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. That\u2019s like saying you\u2019re addicted to water. It\u2019s pursuit is a necessity for their existence, not to experience the next contact high.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You say that, and the book itself also draws a parallel between our need for water and the vampire's need for blood, but it also says this:<br /> <br /> <i>If you have a thirsty man, a glass of water, and something<br /> between them, you have compelling drama. The need\u2019s the thing.<br /> The vampire is fascinating, not because of her alien nature,<br /> but because all of her motivations are familiar. We know those<br /> needs. We know what it is to thirst. That darkness comes from<br /> a place we all understand. We did this.<br /> <b>The Beast magnifies need.</b> The vampire is a glorious vortex<br /> of needs. <b>She is never quenched</b>, and so she is always a story.<br /> There is you. There is the glass of water. In between, is<br /> amphetamine bedlam.<br /> <b>Be thirsty.</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Blood</b><br /> Everything comes back to this. Pick any door. It doesn\u2019t<br /> matter. In this funhouse nightmare, every hallway comes back<br /> to the feeding room.<br /> Like anyone else, vampires need food. They thirst for the blood<br /> of the living. <b>A vampire\u2019s hunger is more urgent than a mortal\u2019s.</b><br /> If he exhausts himself and fails to feed, he\u2019ll slip into torpor, the<br /> long sleep of the dead.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Emphasis done by me to make the point. The point that in the back of your mind, you are always thirsty, the beast is always thirsty. You have a little bit more on your hands than just a means to survival. When I drink a glass of water, I rarely enjoy it, unless I was really thirsty, then I enjoy it a lot. But a vampire seems to be always thirsty. The moment you are no longer topped off, you are thirsty and crave for blood. Sure, you can ignore that craving, and for a while it will be easy to do so, but after a while, when you have less than 5 vitae left in your system, you're already staring to experience hunger, and if you don't feed, the beast will force you to feed.<br /> <br /> When you always crave for something, that's when you get into the territory of an addict. Sure, you could argue that you always hunt for blood because you need to, not necessarily because you want to. That's fair enough. But ask any junky, any alcoholic or any smoker who tried to quit but couldn't, and they will tell you the exact same thing; that they take their choice of drugs not because they want to, but because they need to.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not saying you or the others are wrong. I'm not saying that I'm convinced I'm right (because if I was, I wouldn't ask about this subject). But I do think blood is a bit more to a vampire than water is to us humans. If I'm wrong then I gladly see someone point out how or why I'm wrong and I'll happily stand corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T14:41:19-07:00","id":1199840,"title":"","content":"Honestly my take (and how i run my games) is i treat blood as BOTH sustenance AND an addiction. I especially treat the reaction to being low on blood as closer to a junkie needing his fix than someone feeling hungry. <br /> But this is my decision and i understand running it differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:01:42-07:00","id":1200807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1199749#post1199749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expert or not, your answers are welcome and do seem to be accurate so far.<br /> <br /> So, a few more questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Are ghouls by default addicted to vampire vitae (the book states they experience a fraction of their regnant's hunger for blood) or do they only become addicted when failing their Composure + Resolve roll when drinking vitae?<br /> <br /> 2. I know vampires are by default addicted to blood, but does this mean vampires always carry the 'Addicted' condition, or does the condition only come into play when drinking from another vampire?<br /> <br /> 3. When committing diablerie, you gain the 'Tainted' condition and the description of Auspex says you can use Auspex to see if a vampire carries the marks of a diablerist. Does this refer to the 'Tainted' condition? Does this mean Auspex only picks up these diablerist marks when you have the 'Tainted' condition, or does a diablerist always show up as a diablerist for someone using Auspex even after losing the 'Tainted' condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I would assume a ghoul taken at character creation had fallen to adiction but they need to fail the roll before they are in play unless the ST skips that because you spent the merit dots so it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> 2. Vampires do not start with the Addicted condition unless the do as part of your character concept.<br /> <br /> 3. I know of no official ruling but I go by tainted because Strix give Auspex users a reading of being a Diablerist and there's more drama to be had from a vampire claiming to have been under Strix control or done something else that gives the Tainted condition than knowing that Auspex is infallible also as everything else Uncanny Perception gives you is quite short term so allowing it to pick up one long term thing is a poor fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T09:56:39-07:00","id":1200845,"title":"","content":"Blood and Vitae.<br /> <br /> Vampires are addicted to blood by default. There are a raft of mechanics to support this, with the key being hunger frenzy. You could, if you wanted to draw a line, claim its not the vampire as a <i>person </i>who is addicted to blood, but their beast is, as that's what drives them to frenzy when deprived. <br /> <br /> Sure, the vampiric body converts blood into vitae and thus uses vitae to sustain their hunger. But in their base state vampires need, want and crave with murderous intensity the acquisition of blood. Ignoring that need takes great will. Ignoring the frenzy of the beast to <i>get that blood</i> takes a Willpower every three seconds until you have enough banked to pass the check and take your Tempted Condition. That's... severe; you are literally restraining the intense desire to murder to get your fix.<br /> <br /> Now Vitae is a great substitute for blood, and every vamp knows this to some extent. After all, they had to take in vitae to be embraced. But it's not until there is further exposure that they start rolling for explicit addition to Vitae, suffer bond effects and the like. <br /> <br /> Have you ever eaten so much salt that half an hour later it felt you could drink an ocean and not get the water you crave? That's a fraction of the experience for a vampire who is less than full capacity--and to even stop feeding on reaching capacity is a reasonable check (or at least as been in previous versions). The difference, as you've said, is in concentration: a relatively small amount of Vitae can constitute a point, while you need relatively more blood to convey the same effect.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T03:16:33-07:00","id":1201571,"title":"","content":"Auspex question.<br /> <br /> Can it be used through a telescope or binoculars? Specifically Auspex 2 and 4. It's just a set of lenses, no different to glasses in principle. The book only says 'individual targeted in the scene' so if you set up a scene in which you're spying on someone from far away, as long as you can make out which individual it is then it should work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3775-al-rascala","name":"Al Rascala","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T06:49:06-07:00","id":1201601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al Rascala</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1201571#post1201571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex question.<br /> <br /> Can it be used through a telescope or binoculars? Specifically Auspex 2 and 4. It's just a set of lenses, no different to glasses in principle. The book only says 'individual targeted in the scene' so if you set up a scene in which you're spying on someone from far away, as long as you can make out which individual it is then it should work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I see no reason why this wouldn't work. Based on your story I would even allow Auspex being used on a vampire you see on live television. You could potentially get very interesting scenarios that way.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, it's up to the individual storyteller to decide how powerful he allows Auspex to be. I would allow Auspex being used on someone you see through binoculars or even on live television, but another storyteller might think that goes too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T07:16:16-07:00","id":1201606,"title":"","content":"I personally would say no because Auspex is based on sensorial clues that the beast can acquire; I would require to be in the same environment at least, to be able to smell, see and hear the clues on the target.<br /> But nothing in the book is stated about this so I guess every interpretation is valid. But again, Auspex is already enough powerful without needing to drastically increase the area effect in my opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T15:28:38-07:00","id":1201718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1201606#post1201606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would say no because Auspex is based on sensorial clues that the beast can acquire; I would require to be in the same environment at least, to be able to smell, see and hear the clues on the target.<br /> But nothing in the book is stated about this so I guess every interpretation is valid. But again, Auspex is already enough powerful without needing to drastically increase the area effect in my opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well obviously when using Auspex through binoculars or through television I would give a big penalty on the roll, that goes without saying. If it doesn't, well, I'll say it here; the more &quot;outlandish&quot; the way of using Auspex, the higher the penalty on the roll. For example, I'd give the player a -3 when he's using Auspex through binoculars and a -5 when he's trying to use Auspex on someone he sees on television.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T17:14:38-07:00","id":1201748,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Ventrue Life;n1201601]<br /> Based on your story I would even allow Auspex being used on a vampire you see on live television. You could potentially get very interesting scenarios that way.<br /> /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> But... um... vampires don't show up in recordings: video, photo, live or otherwise. Per canon anyway. Your vampire may vary.<br /> <br /> (I'd probably permit Auspex through a lens device. Imagine if it's a box that sees around corners and you're only a few dozen feet from the target? Sure.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T17:32:52-07:00","id":1201758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1201748#post1201748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... um... vampires don't show up in recordings: video, photo, live or otherwise. Per canon anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite how the Lost Visage works in 2e. Check page 60 of the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T18:28:11-07:00","id":1201782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1201758#post1201758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not quite how the Lost Visage works in 2e. Check page 60 of the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh ok then. You just never get the face.... Carry on then. I suppose with ST approval you could examine a photo or recording and let the Beast inform you that it thinks that smudge is a vamp.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T19:17:52-07:00","id":1201802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1201782#post1201782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh ok then. You just never get the face.... Carry on then. I suppose with ST approval you could examine a photo or recording and let the Beast inform you that it thinks that smudge is a vamp.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not a smudge though, at least not necessarily. The Beast just instinctively looks away from any camera it doesn't want to show it's face to.<br /> <br /> Now, what the book doesn't say--but what I personally ruled because it makes sense--is that a vampire can choose to appear on a picture or on footage normally, but only with the vampire's consent.<br /> <br /> This is because I imagine 'The Lost Visage' being a built-in security measure that gives the vampire an easier time upholding the masquerade. It's the beast inside you making sure you don't accidentally break the masquerade because you didn't see there is a security camera pointed at you. But this built-in security measure could quickly become a burden if you have absolute no control over it. This could be intentional and an interesting way of running the game, but I personally find it more interesting to give the vampire some control over his 'lost visage'. I want the vampire to be able to choose to appear normally on a photo or video, accepting the negative consequences this might have in the future. So that's how I run it.<br /> <br /> Another way you could run it of course is to give the beast full control over the lost visage. It's up to it to decide if it wants to be seen on tape or not. Perhaps that could be interesting as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T22:41:03-07:00","id":1201859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1201802#post1201802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's not a smudge though, at least not necessarily. The Beast just instinctively looks away from any camera it doesn't want to show it's face to.<br /> <br /> Now, what the book doesn't say--but what I personally ruled because it makes sense--is that a vampire can choose to appear on a picture or on footage normally, but only with the vampire's consent.<br /> <br /> This is because I imagine 'The Lost Visage' being a built-in security measure that gives the vampire an easier time upholding the masquerade. It's the beast inside you making sure you don't accidentally break the masquerade because you didn't see there is a security camera pointed at you. But this built-in security measure could quickly become a burden if you have absolute no control over it. This could be intentional and an interesting way of running the game, but I personally find it more interesting to give the vampire some control over his 'lost visage'. I want the vampire to be able to choose to appear normally on a photo or video, accepting the negative consequences this might have in the future. So that's how I run it.<br /> <br /> Another way you could run it of course is to give the beast full control over the lost visage. It's up to it to decide if it wants to be seen on tape or not. Perhaps that could be interesting as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a nifty Merit, or a Devotion using Auspex and/or Majesty!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T07:06:58-07:00","id":1201907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al Rascala</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1201571#post1201571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex question.<br /> <br /> Can it be used through a telescope or binoculars? Specifically Auspex 2 and 4. It's just a set of lenses, no different to glasses in principle. The book only says 'individual targeted in the scene' so if you set up a scene in which you're spying on someone from far away, as long as you can make out which individual it is then it should work?</div> </div> </div> </div>No they're not. They consist of lenses, prisms, springs, and electronic circuitry to provide image stabilization and enhancement. The lenses, prisms, and mirrors in binoculars are also chemically treated to make them scratch, moisture, and impact resistant. Today's telescopes can also plug into a laptop or connect wirelessly to smart phones and integrate with programs designed to focus on specified planets, stars, and constellations for a fraction of the cost of money you spent on your last cell phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T12:45:36-07:00","id":1201991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1201802#post1201802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a smudge though, at least not necessarily. The Beast just instinctively looks away from any camera it doesn't want to show it's face to.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, not necessarily - but it <i>can</i> be. Flash-smeared images or over-/under-exposed film are both also examples the book provides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T18:48:34-07:00","id":1202094,"title":"","content":"In Vampire The Requiem 2nd Edition; I remember reading somewhere that your Humanity score caps your dice pool for frenzy checks. Is this correct? If yes, where in the source material is this mentioned? And is this cap applied before or after all the other modifiers to the roll are applied?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T19:08:25-07:00","id":1202100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1202094#post1202094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Vampire The Requiem 2nd Edition; I remember reading somewhere that your Humanity score caps your dice pool for frenzy checks. Is this correct? If yes, where in the source material is this mentioned? And is this cap applied before or after all the other modifiers to the roll are applied?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would be clan Gangrels Bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T20:25:17-07:00","id":1202114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1202100#post1202100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be clan Gangrels Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also part of the effect of the Jaded Condition, which you get from dramatic failure on a detachment roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:15:43-07:00","id":1202557,"title":"","content":"How do vampires fares against ghosts and spirits (either manifested, claimed or still in an ephemeral state)?<br /> I don't just mean in term of combat. <br /> Vampires are well known as talented social manipulator and i am also wondering how that theme interacts with the various ephemerals.<br /> <br /> I know that the khaibit bloodline in 2e has some abilities against ephemerals, but i am more wondering about ''standard'' vampires. <br /> <br /> thank you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:23:04-07:00","id":1202560,"title":"","content":"Nothing prohibits Dominate or Majesty to work on ephemerals. Due to high attributes it could be more difficult for high Rank ephemerals. The standard rules block in most core books claim ephemerals get to add Rank when contesting supernatural powers, but fortunately for the vampires it was proved false in Werewolf 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:36:26-07:00","id":1202568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1202557#post1202557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do vampires fares against ghosts and spirits (either manifested, claimed or still in an ephemeral state)?<br /> I don't just mean in term of combat. <br /> Vampires are well known as talented social manipulator and i am also wondering how that theme interacts with the various ephemerals.<br /> <br /> I know that the khaibit bloodline in 2e has some abilities against ephemerals, but i am more wondering about ''standard'' vampires. <br /> <br /> thank you</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware Kindred are able to use summoning and exorcism. However, I believe they are unable to to use Abjurism due to their lack of an integrity stat. I believe there was a Daeva bloodline in 1e that dealt with the wider world of darkness, and there was the Dead Wolves. I know of two Cruac rituals that interact with ghosts in 2e.<br /> <br /> Wyrm's nest merits are intetesting and can be connected to a Haunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:46:31-07:00","id":1202579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1202568#post1202568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I'm aware Kindred are able to use summoning and exorcism. However, I believe they are unable to to use Abjurism due to their lack of an integrity stat. I believe there was a Daeva bloodline in 1e that dealt with the wider world of darkness, and there was the Dead Wolves. I know of two Cruac rituals that interact with ghosts in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadnt realized that Abjurism necessitate the integrity stat.Then again, i could easily substitute it for humanity.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking of having the vampire nature interferes with the summoning/exorcisms and to counter that the vampire had to spend vitae points equal to the rank of the ephemeral. I kind of want to make it possible to vampires to use summoning/exorcism but also make it maybe easier for the character to use a mortal occultists to do the rituals instead.<br /> Would you think it is an unnecessary change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T08:41:03-07:00","id":1202605,"title":"","content":"I believe various books say that integrity-equivalents can generally stand in for systems except where noted. I tend to assume that means Humanity, Harmony, etc all work for Abjurism. It makes sense enough, even odd ones like Satiety and Harmony always mean &quot;more human&quot; at higher levels, so they'd be better at human-based means of dealing with such entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:14:27-07:00","id":1202617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1202579#post1202579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hadnt realized that Abjurism necessitate the integrity stat.Then again, i could easily substitute it for humanity.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking of having the vampire nature interferes with the summoning/exorcisms and to counter that the vampire had to spend vitae points equal to the rank of the ephemeral. I kind of want to make it possible to vampires to use summoning/exorcism but also make it maybe easier for the character to use a mortal occultists to do the rituals instead.<br /> Would you think it is an unnecessary change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Abjurism has various integrity modifiers, along with virtue and vice modifiers, so my group generally just says vampires can't do Abjurism due to their debatable lack of a soul, or at least a human soul.<br /> <br /> Mortal occultists have a leg up on kindred because of their access to merits like Medium and Invoke Spirit, Abjurism, a whole list of Rites unavailable to the Kindred from Dark Eras 2, and based on the theme of vampire just a more general predilection for investigating the supernatural. Also considering the fact that ghouls who have some sort of terminal illness pre-ghouling gain the ability to see and interact with ghosts, a vampire's best chance to deal with anything ephemeral is just to get someone else to deal with it.<br /> <br /> I often joke with my groups about how vampires seem know the least among anyone in the cofd universe about the supernarural, despite their immortality, because vampires tend to dig a hole and hide in it due to the fact that they don't like the idea of dying again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:44:34-07:00","id":1202713,"title":"","content":"Question:<br /> <br /> Can someone elaborate on Mask and Dirge archetypes for me? The book gives me the impression that a Dirge is your dirty little secret, but does it have to be a secret? For example, I can imagine a vampire with the Child archetype as her dirge being pretty terrible at hiding her Dirge. Would it be okay if a vampire's Dirge is pretty obvious to everyone in the room, or would that defeat the whole purpose of Dirges?<br /> <br /> What about Masks? Does a Mask have to be a petty lie or can your Mask also be something you aspire to be? For example, what if a vampire aspires to be a good scholar, could Scholar be that vampire's mask? Or does that once again defeat the purpose of Masks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:02:51-07:00","id":1202726,"title":"","content":"Mask is who you pretend to be. Dirge is who you really are. Mask is the shield you use against the intrigue and subterfuge of vampire society, or the disguise you wear to mingle with mortals. Dirge is the core root of who you are that reminds you that there's more to you than meets the eye; it's your true sense of identity.<br /> <br /> I imagine neonates play to their Dirge more than their Mask, because they haven't yet really lived enough to feel like they need that shield that the Mask presents. That's fine. I imagine older vampires would play more to their Mask and not let their Dirge out as often, because it represents vulnerability. That's fine, too. I think when the book says &quot;secret self&quot; here it's more keeping in mind the typical vampire that doesn't let others get to know the &quot;real&quot; person behind the mask. It doesn't literally have to be a secret, but knowing someone's Dirge does give potential leverage and makes it easier to manipulate them, so vampires often learn to hide it quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T12:59:58-07:00","id":1203959,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer!<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's another question:<br /> <br /> Does the 'Good Time Management' merit (p. 44 in the Chronicles of Darkness book) also apply to hunting for a feeding scene for vampires? How exactly does it apply?<br /> <br /> If this merit allows you to find a victim to feed on in half the time you'd normally spend on searching for a victim, I'd argue that this merit is a little overpowered and something any player should take. After all, feeding is something you have to do almost every night and if you can cut down your hunting time by half that means you have a lot more spare time each night to plot, scheme and do jobs. That's a pretty big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T13:04:15-07:00","id":1203961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1203959#post1203959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the 'Good Time Management' merit (p. 44 in the Chronicles of Darkness book) also apply to hunting for a feeding scene for vampires? How exactly does it apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it? Feeding scenes with dice are managed as a single instant action, not an extended action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T15:29:11-07:00","id":1204010,"title":"","content":"I am playing a vampire with Theban Sorcery which requires maintaining your humanity and my humanity is 5 - my touchstone is this REALLY OLD GUY who could die at any point, should I pre-emptively get a new touchstone or does the sanctity of merits kick in before I suffer being languid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T15:50:24-07:00","id":1204019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1204010#post1204010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am playing a vampire with Theban Sorcery which requires maintaining your humanity and my humanity is 5 - my touchstone is this REALLY OLD GUY who could die at any point, should I pre-emptively get a new touchstone or does the sanctity of merits kick in before I suffer being languid?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sanctity of Merits is for the extras you get from the Merit. I'd angle for a spare if I were you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T17:09:35-07:00","id":1204039,"title":"","content":"You specifically can't get the same merit you lost with Sanctity of Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T18:26:51-07:00","id":1204056,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's anything that explicitly forbids that. All you need is in-game explanation, as usual. Loosing a touchstone, but buying the same merit bound to your best friend that's been a part of your character for a long time but still not represented by any mechanical dots would be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:36:15-07:00","id":1204199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1204010#post1204010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am playing a vampire with Theban Sorcery which requires maintaining your humanity and my humanity is 5 - my touchstone is this REALLY OLD GUY who could die at any point, should I pre-emptively get a new touchstone or does the sanctity of merits kick in before I suffer being languid?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sancity kicks in as soon as you lose the guy, problem is that most ST\u2019s will require a narrative explanation for you spendimg the XP recovered. So, you might at the very least want to start seeding your role play with potential angles to get at another Touchstone, to purchase either before or after you lose your current one to old age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:58:56-07:00","id":1204208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1204010#post1204010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am playing a vampire with Theban Sorcery which requires maintaining your humanity and my humanity is 5 - my touchstone is this REALLY OLD GUY who could die at any point, should I pre-emptively get a new touchstone or does the sanctity of merits kick in before I suffer being languid?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure why sanctity of merits would kick in. The touchstone Merit isn't buying touchstones, it's about being able to have a touchstone connected to that level of humanity. So, I don't think sanctity of merits would kick in because losing the touchstone doesn't stop you from being able to have a touchstone at said level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T10:37:57-07:00","id":1204215,"title":"","content":"The text does state that though. P. 88:<br /> <br /> \u201cTaking a new Touchstone requires the Touchstone merit ...\u201d<br /> <br /> Which makes sense. You don\u2019t need the merit to be able to connect to potential Touchstones. You need Humanity for that, hence Touchstones detaching when you lose Humanity.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t read p. 88 and the merit itself in any other way than actually buying a connection to a specific person or object. If that Touchstone is subsequently lost or killed (which is different from detached) Sactity applies as it would with any other merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:20:10-07:00","id":1204343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1204199#post1204199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sancity kicks in as soon as you lose the guy</div> </div> </div> </div>Sanctity kicks in at the end of the chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T08:55:00-07:00","id":1204878,"title":"","content":"Well getting a +3 to detachment rolls for having more than one touchstone would be handy, plus merits are relatively cheap XP-wise. Yes, I will focus on getting another touchstone next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T14:53:43-07:00","id":1205763,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain to me exactly how this merit works? Explain it to me like I'm 6 years old; with a hypothetical example please. :^)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Patient (\u2022)<br /> Effect: Your character knows how to pace herself and take<br /> the time to do the job right the first time. When taking an<br /> extended action, you may make two additional rolls, above<br /> what your Attribute + Skill allows. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:06:18-07:00","id":1205771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1205763#post1205763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain to me exactly how this merit works? Explain it to me like I'm 6 years old; with a hypothetical example please. :^)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can help.<br /> <br /> Extended actions are where you make a number of rolls equal to the attribute and skill you are using. Say a character is researching local occult rumors, they make an extended action.<br /> <br /> Let's give our hypothetical character 2 occult and 2 intelligence; 2+2 gives them a total of four, and so they can roll their 4 dice 4 times to get to the required success number.<br /> <br /> However, a characer with the Patient merit adds two rolls to this, in the event that they didn't get the number needed in the the first four rolls. So our character can roll their 4 dice 6 times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T15:16:42-07:00","id":1205777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1205763#post1205763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone explain to me exactly how this merit works? Explain it to me like I'm 6 years old; with a hypothetical example please. :^)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actions in the ChroD system are broadly broken up into two narrative timescales based on how the rolling works.<br /> <br /> Most rolls are instant actions \u2014 it comes down to a single roll with modifiers to the number and qualities of the dice, but generally a single success is enough to accomplish the task you set out to do. An exceptional success gives you something extra, usually in the form of allowing you to apply a Condition to yourself or (where appropriate) another character, most often the Inspired Condition (which you can resolve on a roll that fictionally benefits from the action that gave you the Condition in order to recover a point of spent Willpower and treat the roll as an exceptional success if it rolls three successes or more instead of five successes or more).<br /> <br /> Rolls representing things that take a long time and can be abandoned and resumed more or less at your leisure are extended actions \u2014 the Storyteller sets a number of successes the character needs to accumulate on rolls of a specific dice pool over time (usually more than five), and the character makes rolls representing a set amount of invested time per attempt. A failed roll at any point in this process means the character suffers a setback and must either abandon their accumulated progress or take a Condition of the Storyteller's choosing to continue to roll.<br /> <br /> Notably, the character automatically fails if they cannot accumulate the necessary number of successes within a number of rolls equal to the sum of the action's Attribute + Skill + Specialty dice \u2014 so if a character with Intelligence 3, Academics 2, and a Specialty in History wants to take an extended action to research an obscure political figure from the Roman Senate, they outright will not succeed if they fail to accumulate the necessary successes in six rolls or less. If that same character has the Patient Merit, they can make up to eight rolls before their efforts fall to naught.<br /> <br /> Also notably, exceptional success on any roll in the set during an extended action tends to give you a couple of options \u2014 you can reduce the amount of time it takes the rest of the rolls you make, you can reduce the number of successes you need to accumulate to succeed at the task by your dots in the relevant Skill, or you can apply whatever the specific exceptional success result is for this action when you reach the required total.<br /> <br /> All of this is covered in the core rules \u2014 Vampire 2e's got the relevant information on page 170-171.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T16:14:20-07:00","id":1205806,"title":"","content":"Normally extended rolls have a hard cap on the number of rolls determined by your Attribute + Relevant Skill to successfully complete a task with each roll representing a given time frame. That merit allows you to add two additional rolls to most extended roll tasks.<br /> <br /> Hypothetical example from my own gaming experience. <br /> My character was tasked by her grandsire to research and successfully demonstrate the casting of a Gilded Cage ritual within three months time. My character, who has a propensity for either extreme procrastination or obsessive compulsive perfectionism, kept putting off the task until she got a veiled warning (threat) from her grandsire about what might happen if she didn\u2019t complete the assignment on time after a month had passed and she hadn\u2019t so much as read her notes. First was the research part. Intelligence + Academics. Each roll represented six hours of research with ten successes needed to successfully research the details of the ritual (what it does), the ways and means needed to invoke it, and the incantation. My character breezed through that part and was done in two evenings. With her pool, she could have rolled eight times. With the Patient merit, she could have rolled two more times for a total of ten times. The next part was practicing the casting in front of her grandsire before being allowed to cast it for real. Since she\u2019s not actually casting, her dice pool this time is Presence + Expression, each roll representing three minutes of simulated casting. She needs five successes to satisfy her grandsire that her understanding of the ritual is sufficient to attempt a real casting. She can roll six times. However, at this part she has a -3 to each roll due to her occultation merit and the fact that the verbal portion of the incantation is in a language she didn\u2019t speak (at the time). Since this isn\u2019t an example of an extended roll where someone dies from blood loss, explodes, or the materials turn back into farm animals and crops, etc. etc. etc. when times runs out, this is where the Patient merit can be put to use, thus she could get eight rolls instead of six. <br /> Whether or not this merit is allowed to be applied to spellcasting rolls or be allowed to inflate the success total to get an exceptional success is up to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-11-2018, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T17:02:44-07:00","id":1205828,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12436_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12436\" data-vbnamecard=\"12436\">Ever Professional</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> you guys are the bomb. Amazing answers everyone! Very clear!<br /> <br /> <br /> I have another question:<br /> <br /> When a ghoul or revenant gets embraced, does he/she keep the disciplines she already had as a ghoul/revenant?<br /> Or does she lose those disciplines and allocate 3 dots to disciplines similar to when a normal human gets embraced?<br /> If she gets to keep her disciplines; does she still allocate 3 new dots to disciplines on top of that?<br /> <br /> So for example; a ghoul or revenant with vigor and obfuscate gets embraced by a daeva, what exactly happens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T18:07:42-07:00","id":1205849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1205828#post1205828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12436_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12436\" data-vbnamecard=\"12436\">Ever Professional</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> you guys are the bomb. Amazing answers everyone! Very clear!<br /> <br /> <br /> I have another question:<br /> <br /> When a ghoul or revenant gets embraced, does he/she keep the disciplines she already had as a ghoul/revenant?<br /> Or does she lose those disciplines and allocate 3 dots to disciplines similar to when a normal human gets embraced?<br /> If she gets to keep her disciplines; does she still allocate 3 new dots to disciplines on top of that?<br /> <br /> So for example; a ghoul or revenant with vigor and obfuscate gets embraced by a daeva, what exactly happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall, when you embrace a ghoul they gain 1 extra free discipline dot, keeping their existing ones, so if the only had their 2 free dots, they have the normal starting 3, but if they'd accumulated, say, 10 dots of disciplines as a ghoul, they'd then have 11 total.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T23:20:38-07:00","id":1205947,"title":"","content":"At my table <br /> For ghouls, unless there\u2019s an important element in the story necessitating why a newly embraced vampire needs more than their 3 in clan disciplines to start, I would strip them away at embrace, allow them to select their 3 from whatever counts as in clan, plus one additional discipline they knew (even if it is out of clan now) the rest of the Xp they spent on disciplines is refunded and which can be spent on those disciplines to be applied to skills specific to those disciplines, blood potency, or vampire unique merits. They also lose vitae addiction (or reset the resist penalty) and blood bonds at embrace.<br /> Revenants keep whatever they acquired. If they paid out of clan cost for disciplines that are in clan when they\u2019re uplifted, they get the difference in experience back. They don\u2019t clear or reset vitae addiction or vinculums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-12-2018, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T04:54:38-07:00","id":1205988,"title":"","content":"By RAW I think they keep them, only getting any dots if they have less than 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T07:01:34-07:00","id":1206011,"title":"","content":"I would say they keep all the disciplines they have. I really don't see why to delete what they've acquired and learnt after the embrace, that is a boost normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T07:53:26-07:00","id":1206022,"title":"","content":"An exception, of course, might be unique bloodline disciplines if not embraced into that bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T23:14:16-07:00","id":1206296,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers everyone!<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's another question:<br /> <br /> Do conditions only go away if you do something that would resolve them or can they go away on their own if enough time passes? I assume persistent conditions have to be resolved and won't go away automatically, but what about conditions that aren't persistent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T23:20:34-07:00","id":1206300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206296#post1206296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers everyone!<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's another question:<br /> <br /> Do conditions only go away if you do something that would resolve them or can they go away on their own if enough time passes? I assume persistent conditions have to be resolved and won't go away automatically, but what about conditions that aren't persistent?</div> </div> </div> </div>The player and Storyteller can agree that a Condition is irrelevant to the play and can just waive it away... but I can\u2019t remember if this is something published or just common sense/ homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T23:21:45-07:00","id":1206301,"title":"","content":"Yes, Conditions can go away on their own. Some (often those inflicted by various powers or abilities, like the Predatory Aura Conditions) specify that they go away unresolved after a certain time span. Others, like Guilty or Shaken, don't have a specified duration, but you're advised to just agree with the ST to cross them off your sheet if circumstances just change enough that the context they were inflicted in no longer is relevant. It's preferable to resolve Conditions so they don't become dead weight, but if they do become dead weight, go ahead and toss it overboard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T23:48:35-07:00","id":1206304,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> <br /> \u200bAh yes, I read that part. I was just wondering if there was anything more concrete than just &quot;yeah remove conditions that are no longer relevant to the story tbh&quot;. I guess there isn't. That's fine. Thanks for the answer boys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T00:15:35-07:00","id":1206313,"title":"","content":"Here's another question:<br /> <br /> For the Daeva clan bane, it says &quot;roll humanity&quot; after the 2nd and consecutive drink from the same mortal. Does that mean you roll your Humanity score as a dice pool (so humanity 6 = a dice pool of 6 dice) or does it mean you roll similarly as when you encounter a breaking point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T00:28:25-07:00","id":1206318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206313#post1206313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's another question:<br /> <br /> For the Daeva clan bane, it says &amp;quot;roll humanity&amp;quot; after the 2nd and consecutive drink from the same mortal. Does that mean you roll your Humanity score as a dice pool (so humanity 6 = a dice pool of 6 dice) or does it mean you roll similarly as when you encounter a breaking point?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it is case of rolling your humanity as a dice pool because the Daeva clan curse doesn't say what level of humanity to use for such a breaking point roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T01:57:40-07:00","id":1206345,"title":"","content":"You roll your Humanity as number of dice, so if you have six dots of Humanity, you roll six dice. All of the clan banes cause you more problems the lower your Humanity falls.<br /> <br /> You can recognize a call for a detachment roll anyway, because there is no fixed dice pool for detachment: your base dice before modifiers are specified by the severity of the breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T04:22:07-07:00","id":1206368,"title":"","content":"If a condition isn't persistent, they leave the character at the end of the scene, per RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T04:53:20-07:00","id":1206376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206368#post1206368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a condition isn't persistent, they leave the character at the end of the scene, per RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just bullshit. If that was the case then the book wouldn't say that Conditions should be removed sparingly if they're not relevant anymore.<br /> <br /> Edit: Page 193 in the subsection Lingering Conditions:<br /> &quot;We recommend doing this sparingly, but bottom line: If a <br /> Condition doesn\u2019t feel relevant to the story anymore, just let it go.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:53:21-07:00","id":1206446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206368#post1206368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a condition isn't persistent, they leave the character at the end of the scene, per RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you thinking of Tilts? Cause those go away at the end of the Scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:11:48-07:00","id":1206454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206446#post1206446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Are you thinking of Tilts? Cause those go away at the end of the Scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every tilt. Blind tilt or arm wrack etc are not going away until you recover the injury.... and for a mortal it could take weeks or months while just few turns for a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T08:23:52-07:00","id":1206459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206454#post1206454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not every tilt. Blind tilt or arm wrack etc are not going away until you recover the injury.... and for a mortal it could take weeks or months while just few turns for a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You should convert it into a Condition then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tilts do not give characters Beats when they end, but the<br /> effects of a Tilt can very easily cause a Condition. For instance,<br /> a character in a fight gets a handful of road salt flung in his eyes<br /> and receives the Blinded Tilt. When combat ends, this shifts<br /> to the Blind Condition. Resolving this Condition will give the<br /> character a Beat. If the character enters combat again before the<br /> Condition is resolved, the Blinded Tilt applies again. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T21:58:16-07:00","id":1206791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206376#post1206376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's just bullshit...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You could have expressed disagreement without being so hostile. Please don't do this again.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T03:17:05-07:00","id":1206839,"title":"","content":"Can humans or ghouls participate in Invictus oaths? I\u2019m looking particularly at the oath of matrimony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1438-delinquent-panda","name":"Delinquent Panda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T07:22:21-07:00","id":1206874,"title":"","content":"Limbs lost/regrowth:<br /> <br /> What's the mechanich to completely lose an arm/leg during a fight? I mean not just the arm wrack but losing the entire limb after an hit dealt to a specific target. More damages than stamina?<br /> <br /> How exactly the regrowth of lost limbs works? Is it healing all the damages suffered losing the arm, enough to consider the limb as regrown (even during a fight) or is it necessary to spend a full day sleeping?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-14-2018, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:03:26-07:00","id":1206881,"title":"","content":"Ill defined. Losing a limb seems to require taking enough aggravated damage in your limb to suffer a wrack. Healing it seems to require just healing the damage. Now enter someone with Resilience who loses an arm without taking damage and spends a Vitae to heal superficial damage and suddenly regrows the arm from scratch.<br /> Personally I'd treat limb loss without damage as a Condition that is resolved by spending time and Vitae as if you were healing a point of Aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:10:19-07:00","id":1206882,"title":"","content":"Per hurt locker:<br /> &quot;Creatures with superhuman healing abilities, like werewolves or vampires, are not so easily laid low. They may heal the Arm/Leg Wrack Tilts in place of healing lethal damage, over time or in an instant (fueled by Essence or Vitae) if they choose. Arm Wrack counts as one point of damage for healing purposes, while Leg Wrack counts as two. If the Tilt is caused by aggravated damage, the character may heal the damaged limb, or regrow a new one entirely, when she heals the associated damage.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:21:41-07:00","id":1206886,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much. <br /> Other question: a target has justbeen taken in a grapple. Other fighters, in the same turn, try to grapple him before the grapple control has been defined. Can the target use his defense or not? <br /> In the case the opponent has the grapple control, do the other fighters roll without defense was applied?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:25:27-07:00","id":1206888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206881#post1206881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now enter someone with Resilience who loses an arm without taking damage and spends a Vitae to heal superficial damage and suddenly regrows the arm from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Whenever he next slumbers&quot; strikes me as the antithesis of &quot;suddenly.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:05:42-07:00","id":1206905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206888#post1206888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Whenever he next slumbers&quot; strikes me as the antithesis of &quot;suddenly.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is an argument to be made for specifically healing tilts per vitae as opposed to spending only one and healing all associated damage upon slumber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:20:04-07:00","id":1206935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Delinquent Panda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1206839#post1206839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can humans or ghouls participate in Invictus oaths? I\u2019m looking particularly at the oath of matrimony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. <br /> The yes. There is no physiological reason they can\u2019t, as is the case with the vampire disciplines and magic.<br /> The no. Invictus oaths usually require a notary to notarize them but the core book says most notaries refuse to notarize them if they involve humans and ghouls as participants for X reasons. Nothing is spelled out but it\u2019s between the lines. Notaries are defined as being chosen for their adherence to Invictus ideals which entails preservation of the status quo and the Masquerade. They\u2019d be leaving their fingerprints all over a Masquerade violation that involving humans in such an Invictus oath entails. To say nothing of the disruption to the status quo they would be creating by giving a human \u201cequal recognition\u201d as kindred as an active participant in formal contracts. (Ie. Sookie\u2019s status in vampire society due to her \u201cmarriage\u201d to Eric.)<br /> The real trick should be finding a notary willing to validate such an arrangement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-14-2018, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T15:08:51-07:00","id":1207029,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, thanks for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1438-delinquent-panda","name":"Delinquent Panda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T03:41:59-07:00","id":1207210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1207012-pledge-to-the-worthless-one-worthless?p=1207182#post1207182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that\u2019s still a problem, you could always bring back Glorious Reclamation. It was a Merit that appeared in the open dev blog previewing the Circle of the Crone Merits and Rituals for Secrets of the Covenants, and unfortunately didn\u2019t make it into the final version (and even more unfortunately got scrubbed from the preview document for some reason). I don\u2019t remember how much it cost, for some reason I think it was two dots, but at any rate, it was a Circle of the Crone Merit that allowed you to learn a single Theban Sorcery Ritual as a Cruac Ritual. That would allow Brood ritemasters to learn the Pledge to the Worthless One without having to maintain Humanity. I actually distinctly remember wanting to use the Merit for exactly this purpose, which is why I was disappointed when Rose said she was cutting it. I wish she hadn\u2019t removed it from the document so I could review the specifics of how it worked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does anyone else remember anything about Glorious Reclamation? It sounds very interesting but I missed it in the preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T07:55:51-07:00","id":1207271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1207210#post1207210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else remember anything about Glorious Reclamation? It sounds very interesting but I missed it in the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few references to it in the Secrets of the Covenants threads, but no quotes actually provide the text of the merit.<br /> It was a 2 dot merit that granted access to a single Theban ritual. No idea what the requirements were.<br /> <br /> The comments <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/acolyte-merits-and-rituals-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> confirm the dot level of the merit, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T08:22:10-07:00","id":1207281,"title":"","content":"Thanks. And activating the stolen ritual seems to have cost a point of Willpower in addition to the usual Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T08:31:38-07:00","id":1207283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1207210#post1207210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does anyone else remember anything about Glorious Reclamation? It sounds very interesting but I missed it in the preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing I remember was that David Hill confirmed that the intent was for you to only be able to take it once, though that was not clear from the text itself. Apparently I was correct that it was two dots. We can probably safely assume that you needed to have enough Cruac to actually perform the rite you learned, and I think you still had to pay the 2xp to learn the Ritual, but I\u2019m not positive about that. I don\u2019t remember any other drawbacks, apart from the fact that the Lancea et Sanctum would obviously be pretty unhappy if they learned you could do one of their miracles.<br /> <br /> Normally I don\u2019t approve of invoking devs like this, but I think this is a bit of a special case, since the Merit was actually removed from the open dev document. If <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> is still around and remembers that Merit, and light you could shed on it would be much appreciated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1207281#post1207281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. And activating the stolen ritual seems to have cost a point of Willpower in addition to the usual Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense, since Cruac costs Vitae and Theban costs Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T03:58:25-07:00","id":1209570,"title":"","content":"Question: Since there's a penalty for using big ranged weapons in melee, what stops a person from walking away at the start of their round and then firing without the penalty?<br /> <br /> My guess is that the penalty applies when you had to use your defense during that round. Even when you walk away, you still get the penalty if before walking away you had to use your defense. Is that a correct assumption?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T04:30:22-07:00","id":1209573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1209570#post1209570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Since there's a penalty for using big ranged weapons in melee, what stops a person from walking away at the start of their round and then firing without the penalty?<br /> <br /> My guess is that the penalty applies when you had to use your defense during that round. Even when you walk away, you still get the penalty if before walking away you had to use your defense. Is that a correct assumption?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the correct assumption is common sense. You don't walk back 9 meters, fire a machine gun then the other guy walks up to you and tries to stab just to have it repeat turn after turn.<br /> If a PC was in melee and tried to get rid of the penalty for that by walking back a few meters within their Speed, i'd still apply the penalty. Combat is messy and trying to get a small feel of that even within the formal structure of turns is usually a good thing imho. It makes sense that if you had to use your Defense then the penalty applies. However I do think that CofD doesn't give us a clear definition of what the rules views as in melee range. I would say though, if you are within the enemies Speed so they can reach you on their turn without them spending an action to do so, you're in close combat for most instances,otherwise: common sense\u2122 applies.<br /> <br /> This reminds me of the old Spear argument in D&amp;D fights with free movement, and Reach weapons combined with the traits that gives unlimited Attacks of Opportunity and just walking back and have enemies come to you, or still attack them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T18:45:07-07:00","id":1209848,"title":"","content":"What if your speed is nearly twice that of the speed of the person you are backing away from. In which case their movement wouldn't take them back into melee combat even if they were somehow moving out of turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23776,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","user":"Raktus","date":". 04-21-2018, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","name":"Raktus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T19:23:07-07:00","id":1209862,"title":"","content":"Got two questions, can twilight judge merit allow Dragon to learn any other coil other than their main one up to 5th tier. Second question I was looking at the coil of ziva and the 4th tier embrace the banes didn't make sense to me, did it mean I could add banes up to my wp amount and use them as breakingpoints?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24155-flazeo25","name":"flazeo25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T21:30:31-07:00","id":1209894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>flazeo25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1209862#post1209862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got two questions, can twilight judge merit allow Dragon to learn any other coil other than their main one up to 5th tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a three-dot Merit with a four-dot Covenant Status prerequisite (when every Coil outside your Mystery can be learned up to the level of your Covenant Status rating already), I don't see why not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second question I was looking at the coil of ziva and the 4th tier embrace the banes didn't make sense to me, did it mean I could add banes up to my wp amount and use them as breakingpoints? </div> </div> </div>Normally, a vampire's player can trade the acquisition of a bane for the removal of a Humanity breaking point from consideration from then on, and this can be done up to three times; Ziva 4 changes this number to the character's Willpower rating, which is usually a larger number than 3, enabling the character to acquire more banes and thus trade out more breaking points.<br /> <br /> Ziva does <i>weird things</i> in the course of hacking your Humanity, considering that each bane you take makes Detachment rolls harder and the preceding Coils' effects are essentially &quot;reduce the effects of all your banes,&quot; &quot;add bonus dice to Detachment by spending Vitae,&quot; and &quot;replace a Condition you get from Detachment rolls with the one that lets you ride the wave easier.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:40:49-07:00","id":1210548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1209570#post1209570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Since there's a penalty for using big ranged weapons in melee, what stops a person from walking away at the start of their round and then firing without the penalty?<br /> <br /> My guess is that the penalty applies when you had to use your defense during that round. Even when you walk away, you still get the penalty if before walking away you had to use your defense. Is that a correct assumption?</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't a penalty per se but a bonus to the defending player defense. I tend to rule on favor of the defending player. For that, my take is that if at the start of the turn, the ranged attackers were at melee range of the defending player, he gets the bonus defense. Otherwise multiple attackers could be surrounding one player in melee and only the attacked one would get the penalty. The ranged players could still walk away, but the melee player would just have to act after all of them acted to close the distance at the end of the turn so that he could get the defense bonus again the next turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1209848#post1209848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if your speed is nearly twice that of the speed of the person you are backing away from. In which case their movement wouldn't take them back into melee combat even if they were somehow moving out of turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, the next turn the defending player wouldn't have the bonus with my take. But you have to remember that if the speed is only twice of that of the defending player, he may still attempt a charge attack, which doubles his speed and sacrifice his full defense for the turn, to melee-attack the ranged character. Another option would be sacrifice your action to move at twice your speed to get close to him, thought that wouldn't have much point. Yeah... with that much speed, it's almost impossible that the defense bonus enters in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12173-basilistik","name":"Basilistik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T15:14:12-07:00","id":1210623,"title":"","content":"Shooting into Close Combat: -2 per combatant avoided in a single shot (not applicable to autofire); -4 if grappling. <br /> <br /> There can be a negative if there are other people involved in the brawl. And I agree with Poser. You dont walk away to get your attack without the negative. Use common sense. Combat is suppose to be more fluid than turn based, it's just that we have to do turns. We are suppose to use our imagination to make this fluid and make sense. so if the Lady who is shooting wants to move, the guy with the knife either goes with or darts away for cover. Knife guy wouldn't let Gun Lady walk away and fire while he just stood there looking pretty. <br /> <br /> And Raktus, if the person is turning and running, and the second person is chasing. this makes chase rules apply... or if he is that fast... Wouldn't the one slower try to just dip into a safe space and thus not letting the shooter shoot?<br /> <br /> <br /> Fight smarter, not harder","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:37:25-07:00","id":1211188,"title":"","content":"Looking over unholy claws merit does it specific what unnatural aspects type has to be since there''s a few that give it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24155-flazeo25","name":"flazeo25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T16:36:07-07:00","id":1211211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>flazeo25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211188#post1211188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking over unholy claws merit does it specific what unnatural aspects type has to be since there''s a few that give it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both Claws from Predatory Aspect and Horrid Talons from Unnatural Aspect will turn into Claws of the Unholy if in Frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T19:21:18-07:00","id":1211266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211211#post1211211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both Claws from Predatory Aspect and Horrid Talons from Unnatural Aspect will turn into Claws of the Unholy if in Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the Merit specifies that it only works &quot;When wielding claws born of Unnatural Aspect...&quot;<br /> Unnatural Aspect produces Horrid Talons, though an argument could be made that both Hooked Hands and Barbed Hands could be considered &quot;Claws borne of Unnatural Aspect&quot; as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-24-2018, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T03:12:20-07:00","id":1211343,"title":"","content":"Dangit. Wrote directly from memory. Anyway, all damage dealing claws from Protean 4 should trigger Claws of the Unholy, if I remember the old discussion about the dev's intent for the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T04:42:13-07:00","id":1211738,"title":"","content":"Does a Draugr still have enough intelligence to use the more subtle vampire powers? I.e. feed in Mist Form or Dominate a victim into freezing up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:27:28-07:00","id":1211790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211738#post1211738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Draugr still have enough intelligence to use the more subtle vampire powers? I.e. feed in Mist Form or Dominate a victim into freezing up?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While there isn't a lot of information on them in the book, I would say that they are perfectly capable of doing anything a wild beast would be able to do. So feeding in mist form, turning into animals and attack so they dont get caught. or whatever is a major yes. Dominate is iffy, because there are several threads that a frenzied vampire can't use it, so I dont know why a draugr reduced to it's baser and primal needs would be able to use something that requires so much speech. <br /> <br /> They become lost to her Beast and a threat, and a predator, which to me says they are almost always in a perpetual state of frenzy. Maybe not on a murderous rampage, but brought down to the base, Feed, Fuck ( though not all vampires have that primal drive) , Survive. ~~~ whatever it takes to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:44:54-07:00","id":1211795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211738#post1211738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a Draugr still have enough intelligence to use the more subtle vampire powers? I.e. feed in Mist Form or Dominate a victim into freezing up?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cSome draugr are careful predators, acting with stealth and bestial cunning, or retaining ritualistic behaviors from their former lives. For example, a fallen Mekhet might set up clever ambushes and sleep in an old library, nesting among moldering books he can no longer read.\u201d<br /> <br /> So I\u2019d say yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:56:07-07:00","id":1211891,"title":"","content":"Back to the ability to use dominate/majesty while in Frenzy: these disciplines are the Beast's will and charm extension. Why when the Beast takes the control shouldn't be able to use its own power? <br /> Is just changing the way she use them, I would say even more freely and istinticvely than the vampire would do. <br /> &quot;A whisp in the dark: *come to me...*, an hand stretch through you under the moon ray. And you leave your friends to get down into the dark cellar&quot;<br /> Even with my poor english it sounds pretty much horrorific and Bestial to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:22:04-07:00","id":1211904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211891#post1211891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the ability to use dominate/majesty while in Frenzy: these disciplines are the Beast's will and charm extension. Why when the Beast takes the control shouldn't be able to use its own power?<br /> Is just changing the way she use them, I would say even more freely and istinticvely than the vampire would do.<br /> &quot;A whisp in the dark: *come to me...*, an hand stretch through you under the moon ray. And you leave your friends to get down into the dark cellar&quot;<br /> Even with my poor english it sounds pretty much horrorific and Bestial to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This horse has been beaten to death on this site. Why is it that a draugr can't read anymore? It used to be able to, but now it can't. Why? Because it has devolved into some primal beast who just doesn't function like that. Why can't a tiger pick up a hammer? Why can't a shark set traps? They just don't think like that. Why bite the thing closest to you when the thing over there is bigger and tastier? <br /> <br /> <br /> While frenzied, the vampire does everything in her power<br /> to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires. <b>She does so with immediate,<br /> forceful, and destructive abandon</b>. If there\u2019s someone in the<br /> way, she throws him or decks him. If she\u2019s hungry, she bites the<br /> closest thing to her mouth. That said, the Beast isn\u2019t stupid.<br /> It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified,<br /> or starving animal predator is, and it will lash out with the<br /> predatory aura if that will help sate it.<br /> <br /> <br /> While it does say they will do everything in their power, it also says &quot;<b>immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon&quot; </b> Dominate and Majesty are not immediate, forceful or used with destructive abandon. Setting up an ambush and laying in wait, then using dominate to get your prey to come over alone doesn't sound like something your beast would do when you are in a frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:37:29-07:00","id":1211912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211904#post1211904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This horse has been beaten to death on this site. Why is it that a draugr can't read anymore? It used to be able to, but now it can't. Why? Because it has devolved into some primal beast who just doesn't function like that. Why can't a tiger pick up a hammer? Why can't a shark set traps? They just don't think like that. Why bite the thing closest to you when the thing over there is bigger and tastier?<br /> <br /> <br /> While frenzied, the vampire does everything in her power<br /> to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires. <b>She does so with immediate,<br /> forceful, and destructive abandon</b>. If there\u2019s someone in the<br /> way, she throws him or decks him. If she\u2019s hungry, she bites the<br /> closest thing to her mouth. That said, the Beast isn\u2019t stupid.<br /> It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified,<br /> or starving animal predator is, and it will lash out with the<br /> predatory aura if that will help sate it.<br /> <br /> <br /> While it does say they will do everything in their power, it also says &quot;<b>immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon&quot; </b> Dominate and Majesty are not immediate, forceful or used with destructive abandon. Setting up an ambush and laying in wait, then using dominate to get your prey to come over alone doesn't sound like something your beast would do when you are in a frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1) A frenzying vampire =/= a draugr.<br /> <br /> 2) Perhaps you could do some more research on predatory animals. There are plenty of creepy predators who lay traps. While I agree that a frenzying vampire would likely not do such a thing (a frenzying vampire wants something and he wants it <b>now</b>) a draugr certainly could and would.<br /> <br /> 3) Just because Marcus gave a weak example doesn't mean a frenzying vampire can't use Dominate or Majesty at all. I can very easily picture a frenzying Ventrue using dominate on his fleeing target and shouting &quot;SIT DOWN!&quot; before he eats his victim or beats him to a pulp (or whatever the Beasts's desire is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T11:55:56-07:00","id":1211917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211912#post1211912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> 1) A frenzying vampire =/= a draugr.<br /> <br /> 2) Perhaps you could do some more research on predatory animals. There are plenty of creepy predators who lay traps. While I agree that a frenzying vampire would likely not do such a thing (a frenzying vampire wants something and he wants it <b>now</b>) a draugr certainly could and would.<br /> <br /> 3) Just because Marcus gave a weak example doesn't mean a frenzying vampire can't use Dominate or Majesty at all. I can very easily picture a frenzying Ventrue using dominate on his fleeing target and shouting &quot;SIT DOWN!&quot; before he eats his victim or beats him to a pulp (or whatever the Beasts's desire is).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1.) I never said they were Equal, only that they were both similar, both reduced down to nothing but the beast. <br /> 2.) I agree with that, especially in the case with spiders, some do set some pretty wicked traps, but not while they are in a frantic frenzy. As you know a Frenzy is the total lose of control, Dominate is decidedly a very controlled, thought out action. <br /> 3.) to be fair, I said dominate was &quot;iffy&quot; in the case of a draugr. There are several other threads about dominate in a frenzy. Majesty is the most subtle discipline out there. How would popping Idol or awe help a vampire, Kill, Run, or Feed? I can't see how any use of majesty would help a vampire accomplish a frenzied goal with immediate destructive abandon. In your case of a Ventru using dominate on a fleeing target, they would know that eating or beating the victim would just break it anyway, so perhaps chasing them down and just beating them to death would be better. or if it was a hunger frenzy, eat something closer and not running. A lion does not simply ask it's prey to sit so it can saunter up and eat it. ( nor does any human ) <br /> <br /> They are capable of thinking like an enraged, terrified or starving animal -- ANIMAL... They don't make the most logical choices, because they don't have human thought processes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:06:01-07:00","id":1211922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211904#post1211904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This horse has been beaten to death on this site. Why is it that a draugr can't read anymore? It used to be able to, but now it can't. Why? Because it has devolved into some primal beast who just doesn't function like that. Why can't a tiger pick up a hammer? Why can't a shark set traps? They just don't think like that. Why bite the thing closest to you when the thing over there is bigger and tastier?<br /> <br /> <br /> While frenzied, the vampire does everything in her power<br /> to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires. <b>She does so with immediate,<br /> forceful, and destructive abandon</b>. If there\u2019s someone in the<br /> way, she throws him or decks him. If she\u2019s hungry, she bites the<br /> closest thing to her mouth. That said, the Beast isn\u2019t stupid.<br /> It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified,<br /> or starving animal predator is, and it will lash out with the<br /> predatory aura if that will help sate it.<br /> <br /> <br /> While it does say they will do everything in their power, it also says &quot;<b>immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon&quot; </b> Dominate and Majesty are not immediate, forceful or used with destructive abandon. Setting up an ambush and laying in wait, then using dominate to get your prey to come over alone doesn't sound like something your beast would do when you are in a frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Reading is not something belonging from the Beast but from the human side of the vampire. So it's perfectly understandable why a dragur shouldn't be able to read.<br /> <br /> If we want to literally analyze the text:<br /> <br /> &quot;the vampire does everything in her power to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires&quot;<br /> Disciplines (Dominate and Majesty included exactly in the same way as Vigor/Celerity are) are exactly the definition of vampire's powers and, moreover, the Beast's powers.<br /> <br /> &quot; the Beast isn\u2019t stupid.&quot;<br /> That's said, biting, punching, killing someone in a place full of military is stupid if there is another way to deal with.<br /> <br /> &quot;It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified,or starving animal predator is&quot;<br /> Have you ever seen a documentary about wolves? Often starved at death but still not throwing themselves against the first herd of Buffalo. They still plan, follow and wait for the right moment. And animals have not disciplines to compare with...<br /> <br /> &quot;it will lash out with the predatory aura if that will help sate it.&quot;<br /> Among the predatory auras there are also the Seductive and Competitive auras, that are exactly the previous step through Majesty and Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-26-2018, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:15:48-07:00","id":1211927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211891#post1211891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the ability to use dominate/majesty while in Frenzy: these disciplines are the Beast's will and charm extension. Why when the Beast takes the control shouldn't be able to use its own power? <br /> Is just changing the way she use them, I would say even more freely and istinticvely than the vampire would do. <br /> &amp;quot;A whisp in the dark: *come to me...*, an hand stretch through you under the moon ray. And you leave your friends to get down into the dark cellar&amp;quot;<br /> Even with my poor english it sounds pretty much horrorific and Bestial to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was reading through the elder's book, and it mentioned how while most draugr were rage filled monsters, there were also draugr that retained some of their old instincts.<br /> <br /> For example, the draugr in the book, Jack Lacroix, uses traps, snares, and his old skinning knife when hunting kindred because he was a trapper for most of his life and requiem; Jack also has three Dominate, so maybe draugr can use dominate. I'm not too sure, seeing as it does rely on the vampire's ability to communicate with others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T12:29:17-07:00","id":1211933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211922#post1211922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Reading is not something belonging from the Beast but from the human side of the vampire. So it's perfectly understandable why a dragur shouldn't be able to read.<br /> <br /> If we want to literally analyze the text:<br /> <br /> &quot;the vampire does everything in her power to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires&quot;<br /> Disciplines (Dominate and Majesty included exactly in the same way as Vigor/Celerity are) are exactly the definition of vampire's powers and, moreover, the Beast's powers.<br /> <br /> &quot; the Beast isn\u2019t stupid.&quot;<br /> That's said, biting, punching, killing someone in a place full of military is stupid if there is another way to deal with.<br /> <br /> &quot;It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified,or starving animal predator is&quot;<br /> Have you ever seen a documentary about wolves? Often starved at death but still not throwing themselves against the first herd of Buffalo. They still plan, follow and wait for the right moment. And animals have not disciplines to compare with...<br /> <br /> &quot;it will lash out with the predatory aura if that will help sate it.&quot;<br /> Among the predatory auras there are also the Seductive and Competitive auras, that are exactly the previous step through Majesty and Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are failing to read the whole text. You can't analyze something if you don't take in the the sentence that follows directly after your claim. &gt; They do everything in their power. She does so.. ( So meaning the sentence prior) .... WITH DESTRUCTIVE IMMEDIATE FORCEFUL ABANDON. &lt;-- literally in the book.<br /> <br /> I dont know what the military has to do with it. But you're right it's not stupid. It's not going to chase prey into a burning building, It's not going to stay in a burning building to get the target. But yeah... unfortunately if you are in a military compound and your vampire snaps and goes into a frenzy.. She just might end up doing it in front of the military. it's the very loss of control and you can't control when that happens ( unless of course you have riding the wave ) She isn't just going to let Vampire A stab her to death while she eats B... That's what they mean by not stupid.<br /> <br /> Starving wolves also wouldn't pass up a lone human with a shot gun in favor of the buffalo herd, They also wouldn't pass up eating another wolf if it was injured or the rabbit that walked across it's path. It would eat all those things first before it took the time to plot out an attack on a herd.<br /> <br /> Lashing out could give your opponent a huge negative to combative things, so I see that as a beast crippling it's target on the hunt. Lashing out has consistently been stated as an immediate and forceful and very obvious action. And can be self-destructive if you were to fail. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-26-2018, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T13:33:31-07:00","id":1211957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211933#post1211933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are failing to read the whole text. You can't analyze something if you don't take in the the sentence that follows directly after your claim. &gt; They do everything in their power. She does so.. ( So meaning the sentence prior) .... WITH DESTRUCTIVE IMMEDIATE FORCEFUL ABANDON. &lt;-- literally in the book.<br /> <br /> I dont know what the military has to do with it. But you're right it's not stupid. It's not going to chase prey into a burning building, It's not going to stay in a burning building to get the target. But yeah... unfortunately if you are in a military compound and your vampire snaps and goes into a frenzy.. She just might end up doing it in front of the military. it's the very loss of control and you can't control when that happens ( unless of course you have riding the wave ) She isn't just going to let Vampire A stab her to death while she eats B... That's what they mean by not stupid.<br /> <br /> Starving wolves also wouldn't pass up a lone human with a shot gun in favor of the buffalo herd, They also wouldn't pass up eating another wolf if it was injured or the rabbit that walked across it's path. It would eat all those things first before it took the time to plot out an attack on a herd.<br /> <br /> Lashing out could give your opponent a huge negative to combative things, so I see that as a beast crippling it's target on the hunt. Lashing out has consistently been stated as an immediate and forceful and very obvious action. And can be self-destructive if you were to fail.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No I'm not failing anything, I'm just providing my interpretation of the whole text as you are giving yours and in the same way you are citing pieces of text ( i.e.: WITH DESTRUCTIVE IMMEDIATE FORCEFUL ABANDON).<br /> <br /> WITH DESTRUCTIVE IMMEDIATE FORCEFUL ABANDON literally means that if there is the chance to achieve its goal, the beast will do as more direct, immediate and violent way as possible. BUT going on reading, the TEXT, it clearly say: IT'S NOT STUPID!!! So back again to the military example: if the Frenzy vampire is in front of an army - read as heavy armed people - ( a riot or whatever better example comes to your mind) she WILL not do something so stupid to jump to the throat of the closest soldier, because it's just so stupid that it will mean death for her. While she could Majesty/Dominate a soldier (IN THE MOST IMMEDIATE AND FORCEFUL WAY - Shut the fucking up and follow me in that dark warehouse-), leading him in a private place and then VIOLENTLY jumping to his throat, tears away shreds of skin, to satisfy her hunger.<br /> So, as you see, I'm reading the whole text in its context...giving my interpretation. You can play frenzy as you wish, but forbidding the Beast to use its very powers (Since discipline comes from the beast) is like forbidding a starved wolf to prey with its pack, just because it's starved and it want to eat right now, going alone and directly through a prey in a herd and through its death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-26-2018, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:07:38-07:00","id":1211972,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a> 's perceptive on the Beast and frenzy is mostly derived from how they are portrayed in VTM and VTR 1e, correct? I definitely see where you're coming from, but I do think VTR 2e changed the Beast and frenzy a bit.<br /> <br /> The Beast in VTR 2e definitely isn't stupid and it definitely isn't as dumb as an animal. I get the feeling you're too hung up on that one sentence you keep quoting over and over again. I get the feeling you take that one sentence way too literally. Understandably so, because the Beast in VTR 1e most definitely was an aggressive, destructive primal bestial force. But the Beast is more than that in 2e.<br /> <br /> Might I remind you of the Predatory Aura? Read that chapter again, it literally proposes 3 types of Beasts (or 3 states the Beast might be in). There is the bestial Beast to be sure, but also a competitive Beast and even a seductive Beast.<br /> <br /> I also suggest reading the 'Moving Up' chapter starting at page 56. It suggests that Beast is more or less our primal instincts and not a literal animal. Let me propose something radical. This might sound off-topic, but hear me out:<br /> <br /> If you're familiar with Sigmund Freud, you might know he proposed the human psyche can be split into 3 categories: the Id, the Ego and the Super-Ego, or the unconscious, conscious and preconscious parts of the psyche.<br /> The Id is the humans basic drive to fulfill his primary needs. The Id seeks shelter and protects us from incoming danger, but it also seeks pleasure and immediate gratification.<br /> The Super-Ego is the moral compass of the human, the standard the human sets for himself, the desire to be something greater, to follow long-term goals.<br /> The Ego is the combination of the Id and the Super-Ego and forms our core. The Ego is the mediator between the Id and the Super-Ego, is tries to keep both the Id and the Super-Ego satisfied and tries to keep both in balance. The Ego is often the driver, but it has to steer two horses with fundamentally opposing interests.<br /> <br /> One could easily argue that the Beast is the Id, Humanity is the Super-Ego and the vampire himself is the Ego. Indeed, reading through page 56 and 57 of VTR 2e seems to draw that comparison as well.<br /> <br /> It might be tempting to say the Id (and by extension the Beast) is the animal part of the human/vampire brain, and indeed it seems logical to say so, but the Id never operates alone and it certainly doesn't forget about everything the Ego has taught the Id. Indeed, the Id will use everything the Ego knows about the world to get what it wants. An animal seeking pleasure doesn't know that heating up crack on a spoon and smoking it gives him the best high he ever experienced, but a human might. The Id of the human knows that crack might give him what it wants, because the Ego of the human knows. The Id and Ego work in tandem.<br /> <br /> One could argue the Beast and the vampire are no different in that regard. There is nothing in the book suggesting the Beast cannot utilize the knowledge the vampire has gathered through his life/unlife to get what it wants.<br /> <br /> Of course the argument made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> holds up as well: it's the Beast that gives the vampire his Disciplines in the first place. The Disciplines are the powers of the Beast, not of the Man. So wouldn't it be weird then if all of the sudden a frenzied vampire or draugr can't use Dominate or Majesty anymore? That notion seems to go directly against the established lore of VTR 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-26-2018, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:25:07-07:00","id":1211984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211972#post1211972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course the argument made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> holds up as well: it's the Beast that gives the vampire his Disciplines in the first place. The Disciplines are the powers of the Beast, not of the Man. So wouldn't it be weird then if all of the sudden a frenzied vampire or draugr can't use Dominate or Majesty anymore? That notion seems to go directly against the established lore of VTR 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dominate and Majesty both work off of a slow buildup of effects that is, in point of fact, out of keeping with the &quot;immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon&quot; of frenzy.<br /> <br /> Marcus went out of his way to argue that there's a difference between a draugr and a frenzied vampire, but that cuts the other way, too: a vampire at a Monstrous or Animalistic level of Humanity is not wholly in thrall to her Beast's desires, and it's a mistake to assume the latter is necessarily anything like the former in controlled circumstances.<br /> <br /> The Beast is the <i>source of</i> Disciplines in the same sense that the human brain is the <i>source of</i> literature \u2014 that doesn't mean you can wake a frustrated starving novelist in the middle of the night and expect a polished manuscript two hours later. Lashing out is the Beast's primary method of psychic warfare for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:29:36-07:00","id":1211987,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24044_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24044\" data-vbnamecard=\"24044\">Ventrue Life</a> here.<br /> As I already said in the first post of mine, there are 3 kind of predatory aura, and the text specifically says Frenzy vampire can lash out and not: can lash out with Bestial aura. Lashing out is violent and immediate? Yes, sure. But each one in different way. Lashing out requires actions aligned with the chosen kind:<br /> <br /> - Bestial: not needing to specify this. It's obvious.<br /> - Seductive: A seductive Beast sidles up to the prey, whispers beautiful lies, or gives a telling<br /> gaze from across the crowd. (That's definitely not violent as you Vitalis seems to intend it. It requires brain to do it, even just a languid sight...so if this is possible, why not Majesty?<br /> - Competitive Beast draws a line in the sand, announces terms, or takes the role of mouse in a chase. The same as per Seductive.<br /> <br /> Again, if lashing out, with seductive in example, is allowed, why shouldn't be allowed Majesty...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-26-2018, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:32:48-07:00","id":1211989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211984#post1211984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast is the <i>source of</i> Disciplines in the same sense that the human brain is the <i>source of</i> literature \u2014 that doesn't mean you can wake a frustrated starving novelist in the middle of the night and expect a polished manuscript two hours later. Lashing out is the Beast's primary method of psychic warfare for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That comparison doesn't hold up if you go by what I said earlier. I compared the Beast to the Id. The Id most certainly is <b>not</b> the source of literature, the Ego and Super-Ego are. Yet the Beast <b>is</b> the source of a vampire's Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:42:55-07:00","id":1211995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211984#post1211984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast is the <i>source of</i> Disciplines in the same sense that the human brain is the <i>source of</i> literature \u2014 that doesn't mean you can wake a frustrated starving novelist in the middle of the night and expect a polished manuscript two hours later. Lashing out is the Beast's primary method of psychic warfare for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's different here, quite the opposite indeed: You cannot ask a polished manuscript by a sleepy novelist because the novelist is not in her best shape (her brain is sleepy). On the contrary, the Beast is sleeping while the MAN is in control. When she lose the control you have the very Beast, as its top, like you have the very Novelist when she is as more awake as possible.<br /> Yes a man can lose his brain (madness, aging,..) and the faculty to create literature, but it's actually the opposite that happens when the Beast take the control of the man.<br /> By the way, mine and yours are just interpretations. The point is that no one of us can give an exact and sure answer because simply there isn't according to the text as it is written and I doubt any developers is going to give us the answer to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:52:52-07:00","id":1212000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211989#post1211989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That comparison doesn't hold up if you go by what I said earlier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost certainly, because it's the weakest and least relevant part of my post. Address the fact that it is specifically frenzy's interaction with the ability of the Beast to use practices that are antithetical to a gradual buildup that is under discussion or get away from this equivocating about the source of a developed power being interchangeable with the careful use of a developed power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1211995#post1211995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the contrary, the Beast is sleeping while the MAN is in control. When she lose the control you have the very Beast, as its top, like you have the very Novelist when she is as more awake as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast is sleeping when <i>the vampire</i> is sleeping. That's what the <i>hunger</i> is. The Beast is not running at its peak performance when it is rankled and starving and pushing for immediate gratification just because that is when it is least <i>resistible </i>any more than the novelist is running on all cylinders fresh out of bed in the middle of REM in dire need of a midnight snack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:00:56-07:00","id":1212003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212000#post1212000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast is sleeping when <i>the vampire</i> is sleeping. That's what the <i>hunger</i> is. The Beast is not running at its peak performance when it is rankled and starving and pushing for immediate gratification just because that is when it is least <i>resistible </i>any more than the novelist is running on all cylinders fresh out of bed in the middle of REM in dire need of a midnight snack.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the opposite that happens to an human when, under the effect of adrenaline because of whatever reason, he can give its best not feeling (obviously under certain &quot;human limits&quot;) pain, hunger, weakness, sickness etc.<br /> And again it is opposite to what the mechanic of the Frenzy would suggest: adding blood potency to any physical action (even if starved), just like adrenaline &quot;does&quot;.<br /> <br /> Here, we are arguing on the fact that the Beast is acting in a way where it is not allowed or able to use her full powers because its blindness and violent way to act, not because it is starved and weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:16:54-07:00","id":1212012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212003#post1212003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the opposite that happens to an human when, under the effect of adrenaline because of whatever reason, he can give its best not feeling (obviously under certain &quot;human limits&quot;) pain, hunger, weakness, sickness etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may notice that <i>all of these are more immediate effects than &quot;take a moment, make eye contact, and render someone suggestible so that you can tell them to do a thing or alter their memories&quot; or &quot;take a moment, make the whole room starstruck, call someone over to you, and work on their ego to make them your fanatically loyal follower.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here, we are arguing on the fact that the Beast is acting in a way where it is not allowed or able to use her full powers because its blindness and violent way to act, not because it is starved and weak. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Weakness&quot; in the way that you are talking about has nothing to do with the fact that <i>acting blindly and violently is frequently suboptimal compared to the more measured and time-consuming effects of &quot;spend three seconds to make a person suggestible or starstruck.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Seductive and Competitive auras being things the Beast could conceivably use <i>if they would help it get what it wants</i> does not translate to Majesty and Dominate being things the Beast is likely to use to fulfill the immediate need to feed or establish dominance, nor do the physical cues that signify those uses of the predatory aura have to all be usable by a Beast in frenzy <i>because that list is for the lashing out mechanic in general</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T15:25:30-07:00","id":1212018,"title":"","content":"Ok maybe I wasn't clear. I convey with you saying that, if it's not a sure death condamn, the frenzy will jump to the throat and stop. I'm just saying that, in an hypotetical scenario, where the vampire is sourronded by whatever potentially lethal for him, let's say an army, and she get frenzy for hunger, she will not jump on the throat of the first policeman/soldier, she could instead use disciplines to lead someone apart. Then feeding as much violently as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:42:47-07:00","id":1212081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212018#post1212018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok maybe I wasn't clear. I convey with you saying that, if it's not a sure death condamn, the frenzy will jump to the throat and stop. I'm just saying that, in an hypotetical scenario, where the vampire is sourronded by whatever potentially lethal for him, let's say an army, and she get frenzy for hunger, she will not jump on the throat of the first policeman/soldier, she could instead use disciplines to lead someone apart. Then feeding as much violently as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book Literally unequivocally undeniably tells you what the beast does in a hunger frenzy. If she\u2019s hungry, she bites the closest thing to her mouth. That said she isn't stupid... She will use the thing she is biting as a human shield, or try to back out of the room while eating it or perhaps even obfuscate to keep on nom noming without issues. She wont just stand there and take the shots. She will use her defense and wits to keep eating until the beast is satisfied.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24044_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24044\" data-vbnamecard=\"24044\">Ventrue Life</a> I am quoting information from the 2nd Edition books and I have never played VTM. We are blurring the lines of frenzy and Draugr which shouldn't happen. The same thing does not apply to both.<br /> <br /> I totally agree with this &quot; The Id is the humans basic drive to fulfill his primary needs. The Id seeks shelter and protects us from incoming danger, but it also seeks pleasure and immediate gratification. &quot; Dominating someone, hauling them to a safe location, and feeding is not &quot;Immediate gratification. &quot;<br /> <br /> Book: <i>While a<b> vampire\u2019s rational consciousness is no longer in<br /> control</b> during frenzy, that\u2019s no reason to yank control away<br /> from the player </i><br /> <br /> plotting, planning, dominating, moving ... are all rational thought processes. ( especially bad choices because dominate is going to fail as soon as you actually hurt them )<br /> <br /> <i>She can grab and bite as a single instant action,<br /> as she ravenously mauls her victim</i><br /> <br /> <i>It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an<b> enraged, terrified,<br /> or starving animal predator is</b>, and it will lash out with the<br /> predatory aura if that will help sate it.</i><br /> <br /> Again, Using logical human thought processes speak of control.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Normally, this is a chance for a player to explore what their<br /> <b>character\u2019s basest, most practical desires</b> lead to without the<br /> restraint of Humanity. The player r<b>oleplays out unbridled<br /> anger or insatiable thirst.</b> The choices the player makes<br /> serve to highlight why it\u2019s so important for the character to<br /> maintain control</i><br /> <br /> Fight, Flight, Feed<br /> <br /> <br /> There is even a merit that you can get ( Beast Whisperer ) that allows you to talk and sooth the beast where otherwise no one could. You might go into a hunger frenzy and know that eating your only way home before dawn would be a terrible terrible thing... but the point is.. You dont care and you do it anyway. You can't say, &quot;Oh I will go find something else because eating Joey would be really really really stupid.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's like an addict. They know sticking the needle in their arm is bad and they know every time could be their last... but they can't control themselves enough to stop. (even with teenagers and their phones. That ding goes off and they know that they can get kicked out of class or their phones taken away or they could fail that test.. but they have to look anyway because they can't not.) Sometimes you set aside the logical and safer choices for that immediate gratification ....<br /> <br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> Guy in a bar. Normal average man drinking his beer. Guy 2 keeps poking at him. Saying whatever. Eventually in front of 20 other witnesses the man snaps, grabs his beer mug and smashes it into the man's face and keeps hitting him even though everyone is screaming stop. Maybe even the bartender has a shotgun pointed at him. But he doesn't stop. because he snapped. ( Frenzied. )<br /> <br /> The smarter safer choice would have been to go outside... or you know.. not fight at all. But he lost control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-26-2018, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T19:09:52-07:00","id":1212105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212081#post1212081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The book Literally unequivocally undeniably tells you what the beast does in a hunger frenzy. If she\u2019s hungry, she bites the closest thing to her mouth. That said she isn't stupid... She will use the thing she is biting as a human shield, or try to back out of the room while eating it or perhaps even obfuscate to keep on nom noming without issues. She wont just stand there and take the shots. She will use her defense and wits to keep eating until the beast is satisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what is Majesty/Dominate but another defense mechanism?<br /> <br /> How is using Dominate and Majesty any different from using Obfuscate? Why does, according to your logic, the Beast use the latter but not the former? What is the concrete difference here? Where is the line and why do you draw it there?<br /> <br /> These are legit questions. Because I see absolutely zero reason why a hungry Beast would use Obfuscate to get what it wants, but not use Dominate or Majesty to get what it wants.<br /> <br /> Or to quote the book: &quot;While frenzied, the vampire does <b>everything</b> in her power to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires.&quot;<br /> <br /> If using a Discipline makes it easier or faster for the frenzied vampire to get what the Beast wants, it will do so. I see no reason why not. I can think of a couple of dozen ways how Dominate and Majesty can be very useful to the Beast and how it can be used in extremely direct, violent ways to give the Beast what it wants. Just use your creativity, I'm sure you can come up with at least a few ways yourself as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212081#post1212081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominating someone, hauling them to a safe location, and feeding is not &quot;Immediate gratification. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And I never said it was. But dominating someone, commanding him to come over and sit down, and eating him right then and there, most definitely counts as immediate gratification. Especially if the vampire in question is weak in the physical department but extremely strong in the mental department. In that case it might perhaps be the surest and most direct way possible. Anything else would be less direct and more likely to fail for such a vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212081#post1212081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Example:<br /> <br /> Guy in a bar. Normal average man drinking his beer. Guy 2 keeps poking at him. Saying whatever. Eventually in front of 20 other witnesses the man snaps, grabs his beer mug and smashes it into the man's face and keeps hitting him even though everyone is screaming stop. Maybe even the bartender has a shotgun pointed at him. But he doesn't stop. because he snapped. ( Frenzied. )<br /> <br /> The smarter safer choice would have been to go outside... or you know.. not fight at all. But he lost control.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if that man could control his opponent with a single gaze to make smashing his face in easier, I'm sure he would do that. In fact that's exactly what Killgrave from Jessica Jones does when he gets angry. I don't know if you ever watched Jessica Jones on Netflix, but if you did, I'd argue that Killgrave is a pretty good representation of what a Ventrue might be like. When does Killgrave use his mind control powers the most? When he wants <i>immediate gratification</i> and can't be arsed to do it the &quot;normal way&quot;, or when he's simply is too angry and too enraged to get things done the &quot;normal way&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T19:14:37-07:00","id":1212106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212018#post1212018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok maybe I wasn't clear. I convey with you saying that, if it's not a sure death condamn, the frenzy will jump to the throat and stop. I'm just saying that, in an hypotetical scenario, where the vampire is sourronded by whatever potentially lethal for him, let's say an army, and she get frenzy for hunger, she will not jump on the throat of the first policeman/soldier, she could instead use disciplines to lead someone apart. Then feeding as much violently as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>^<br /> THIS!<br /> <br /> The Beast is monstrous, but not stupid, and above all, not suicidal! The book makes that <i>very</i> clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:38:16-07:00","id":1212127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212105#post1212105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what is Majesty/Dominate but another defense mechanism?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are, once again, <i>very poor</i> defense mechanisms for any problem that demands the immediate attention of the Beast, which tend to be matters of petty vengeance, gnawing hunger, or raw terror.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is using Dominate and Majesty any different from using Obfuscate? Why does, according to your logic, the Beast use the latter but not the former? What is the concrete difference here? Where is the line and why do you draw it there? </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate does not take several seconds of sustained effort to leverage the basic effect of &quot;people pay you no special attention that you don't directly call to yourself&quot; or its slightly more advanced and expensive effects of &quot;people can't see you/think you're someone they expect to see.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These are legit questions. Because I see absolutely zero reason why a hungry Beast would use Obfuscate to get what it wants, but not use Dominate or Majesty to get what it wants. </div> </div> </div>Face in the Crowd costs nothing to use, takes as much time to use as it takes to lurk away from an overwhelmingly disadvantageous situation, and makes you functionally invisible to bystanders. There is a reasonably high likelihood of encountering a situation where a character will enter an atavistic fear-state and want to disappear from onlookers' attention without needing to justify sustained eye contact and nuanced verbosity, which cannot be said for Awe or Mesmerize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If using a Discipline makes it easier or faster for the frenzied vampire to get what the Beast wants, it will do so. I see no reason why not. I can think of a couple of dozen ways how Dominate and Majesty can be very useful to the Beast and how it can be used in extremely direct, violent ways to give the Beast what it wants. Just use your creativity, I'm sure you can come up with at least a few ways yourself as well. </div> </div> </div>Dominate's entire chain of effects is keyed off of taking a turn and getting someone to look you in the eye so you can make them open to verbal commands and Majesty likewise relies on conversational behavior for literally all of its effects to work except &quot;your appearance and behavior don't apply penalties to your Social rolls.&quot; Nothing about this makes it especially easy to resolve &quot;I need blood&quot; or &quot;this guy needs a lesson in pain&quot; relative to simply seeing an opportunity for satisfaction and taking it by force. &quot;Doing everything in your power to accomplish a thing&quot; is a statement of <i>ruthlessness</i>, not <i>breadth of likely instruments</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I never said it was. But dominating someone, commanding him to come over and sit down, and eating him right then and there, most definitely counts as immediate gratification. </div> </div> </div>Trying to incite a staring contest and using your words to make somebody approach you when you are in a state that elevates your physical performance and lets you feed as soon as the mechanics allow is only &quot;immediate gratification&quot; in the sense that ordering a pizza instead of making a sandwich is immediate gratification. Are you in the habit of having frenzied characters text local pizza places for delivery when they find themselves hungry and alone after dark?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially if the vampire in question is weak in the physical department but extremely strong in the mental department. In that case it might perhaps be the surest and most direct way possible. Anything else would be less direct and more likely to fail for such a vampire. </div> </div> </div><i>You literally get better at every Physical roll when you are in frenzy.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T21:39:31-07:00","id":1212144,"title":"","content":"I agree 110 % with Satchel. <br /> <br /> I have supported everything with contextual evidence and cited book passages. <br /> <br /> Last thing I am going to say is that Killgrave is a manipulative thoughtful bastard. Yes I can see him being a venture. I do agree with that. However. nothing he has done is in a \u201cfrenzy\u201d. At least nothing I can recall. Everything he did was a thoughtful action, not done out of lost control. He is the epitome of control. <br /> <br /> If you would like to quote movies for prime examples. Please see The Hulk. He literally rages and goes into a frenzy where he can\u2019t do much of anything he could before. He can\u2019t even talk except 2 words. I could probably YouTube up 1000 other prime examples of frenzied vampires or movie characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T23:08:11-07:00","id":1212161,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a>, I don\u2019t think your citations of the text are helping here. Two people can get completely different meanings out of the exact same words. To you, the \u201cimmediate, forceful abandon\u201d line you keep quoting might be unequivocal proof that dominate and majesty are not valid options, but to me there\u2019s nothing about immediacy, force, or abandon that precludes those disciplines (though admittedly dominate isn\u2019t especially immediate in most situations), so quoting it again in bold doesn\u2019t really do anything to convince me otherwise.<br /> <br /> While I\u2019ve long since lost patience for this argument, I will state my opinion on the matter and move on. If an action directly and immediately advances the goal of the frenzy, I think it should be possible. Granted, in the majority of situations, most uses of dominate and majesty are not going to do that. The turn it takes to establish the Mesmerized condition is a turn that could be spent doing something more directly applicable to the goal. Activating Awe doesn\u2019t generally help you kill, feed, or escape any faster. Idol in a fear frenzy though? Absolutely I\u2019d allow that, and I think anyone who would allow obfuscate in that situation should too. I think \u201cdoes this action directly advance my goal?\u201d is a pretty good metric for Frenzy, especially because it\u2019s situational. Instead of blanket banning certain disciplines, it says you can theoretically do anything <i>if and only if</i> it gets immediate results, which the contentious disciplines <i>usually</i> don\u2019t but <i>conceivably</i> could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T00:14:44-07:00","id":1212167,"title":"","content":"Agree with Charlaquin.<br /> <br /> I'm trapped in a cage I cannot break with frenzy bonuses, instead to hit the steal bars with my head, I would rather dominate the jailer to let me free. It's not just immediate, it's the only thing I can do to achieve my goal. Then I can give such a command snarling and dribbling...but still.<br /> Anything you said hasn't let me change my idea for even a second.<br /> So go for your interpretation but be aware that it's not the only and absolute truth, it's just your interpretation. A truth would have been if the text would have said: While frenzy you can just use physical disciplines. But that's not the case.<br /> <br /> Moreover, I feel very limiting to see a frenzy vampire just like an animal. It doesn't give any further deepness to the game treating it as a Bersrkr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-27-2018, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T01:31:01-07:00","id":1212177,"title":"","content":"I remember the old days when the trained assassin would have to drop all their weapons in frenzy and make only brawl attacks, regardless of the situation. Got pretty ridiculous, and the trajectory of moving away from 'the idiot beast' has been a blessing at my table more times than I can count. <br /> <br /> I think a lot of the white-room issues here are solved by things like modifiers before a roll, or even the necessity of a roll in the first place. Like the military base situation. If a character understands there's a danger that an entire military base can mobilize against them, I'm not going to ask for a frenzy check because they were insulted by a superior or sprained their ankle going down the stairs. <br /> <br /> I don't always see eye to eye with Charlaquin on game stuff, but she really nails my feelings on this issue as well. I would never blanket disallow any discipline, but would expect the player to justify any uses with a good faith effort to show how it advances the beast's agenda. <br /> <br /> A frenzied vampire against a single target - the target's defense is high enough that the frenzier is reduced to a chance die on attack. At what point do you let the frenzier start looking at alternate paths to the agenda - such as disciplines (&quot;lay down&quot;) or using the environment to get an advantage? <br /> <br /> What's more, Vitalis is forgetting (unless I missed mention) a major aspect. Even if his interpretation is correct, that Dominate would always be against the beast's agenda - that doesn't mean it can't be used. It just means Vitalis can charge his player a WP for that turn. So what we're really talking about here, is the decision point of when to charge a player that WP for an action.<br /> <br /> The answer to that is more nuanced, and much more per-table oriented. For me, I look at things like Frenzy not forcing a player to always spend WP/Vitae for action bonuses. That frenzied kindred only diablerize with player choice. That always, always - mechanics are subservient to narrative to conclude that there's room to wiggle, and that wiggling is supported by the text. And such wiggling usually allows me to find horror aspects to frenzy more in kind to my playstyle. <br /> <br /> Mindless beasts are boring to me. You show me a clever beast that is being smart in advancing its goal while ignoring Humanity, morality, social conventions, status - I'm going to support you every time. I'm going to find consequences for those actions regardless. Unless there are no stakes at all and consequences aren't justified - in which case, a frenzy roll isn't really justified either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:01:20-07:00","id":1212201,"title":"","content":"I can live with the answers <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4047_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4047\" data-vbnamecard=\"4047\">Holy</a> provided. You both make good points. I will most definitely consider them.<br /> <br /> Like Holy, I also got really sick and tired of the 'Beast as dumb bestial animal' shit from Vampire The Masquerade (and to some extend Vampire The Requiem), so maybe I'm a little biased here. But I think looking at &quot;what is the most direct path for the Beast to get what it wants?&quot; keeping all the tools of the vampire in mind, is a good way of handling frenzies. After giving it a second thought, I agree that Majesty most likely won't be useful in most frenzy cases. Dominate I'm more leaning towards being pretty useful in at least a few cases.<br /> <br /> So my final verdict:<br /> <br /> Majesty during frenzy? Most likely not gonna be used.<br /> Dominate during frenzy? Highly situational but it's more likely to get used than Majesty.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is of course just my opinion on the matter, based on my interpretation of the material, the arguments being made here and above all what I personally find fun and reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:27:21-07:00","id":1212219,"title":"","content":"Im in the camp of disciplines are usable during Frenzy, it's the Beasts powers after all. <br /> <br /> If it could use any discipline that's not reflexive it should be able to use them all, although it might not be in the interest of the Beast to use every part of a discipline in most circumstance. There's no difference between gnarling towards someone to &quot;stop&quot; with dominate then it is to sneak up behind some using obfuscate. Using dominate to make elaborate mind altering commands over the cause of several turns to make some plot, that probably a bit to much and not within the confines of most frenzies but it shouldn't be off the table. Say for instance the beast wants to humiliate and shame someone and that's the goal of the frenzy, then the second or third dot of dominate is quite useful and probably the most direct way of making that happen.<br /> Majesty is also probably very common and useful for the Beast to turn on if it can, eating on someone and acting like a bloodsucking monster while no one really bats an extra eye. Or getting the target to come to you instead of walking up to it. Getting some allies if attacked is pretty useful and no more a weird thing then to seek shelter or using a human shield for protection.<br /> Why would the Beast run around in the forest looking for a animal to hunt when it could summon a shitload of them with Animalism.<br /> <br /> Disciplines is not a tool for a vampire, especially not the Beast, but a part of her as much as a hand or a foot. It ain't a pair of lock-picks to open a fragile wooden door, but a steady kick to it, it is not a go around solution but a natural part of her being, her body. Dominating someone to come with her is not the same as buying the victim a few drinks and having causal small-talk so she could get her somewhere more private. It's the equivalent to physically picking the victim up.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:07:24-07:00","id":1212258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212161#post1212161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If an action directly and immediately advances the goal of the frenzy, I think it should be possible. Granted, in the majority of situations, most uses of dominate and majesty are not going to do that. The turn it takes to establish the Mesmerized condition is a turn that could be spent doing something more directly applicable to the goal. Activating Awe doesn\u2019t generally help you kill, feed, or escape any faster.</div> </div> </div> </div> &lt;-- that is what I have been trying to say. And you have to activate Awe to activate Idol( though you can do that in the same turn, but it's still 1 turn where you could have been running and you didn't ) I was citing the book and bolding the lines that lead me to believe what I believed, rather than just giving examples of situations that don't really come from anywhere. <br /> <br /> Marcus's example of being trapped in a cage while frenzied.. I am not even sure why you would go into a frenzy while you are trapped in a cage, but I could totally see the vampire spazzing out, then calming down. THEN dominating the person to let them out once the vampire has had a moment to think clearly. <br /> <br /> Alright experienced players. Have you ever once in actual game play used Dominate or Majesty in a frenzy? Dominate like you said by definition is not immediate. It takes a turn to catch the eye, a turn to make the command then a turn for you to act. That is 3 turns you could have been just smashing the thing's face in. Same with Idol. It takes a turn to Awe and Idol and a turn for you to do something after that vs a turn you could have probably used Celerity and bolted out the door. Awe and Idol is one turn So there is actually a huge difference between snarling out &quot;stop&quot; and turning invisible to run from your opponent. ( you vanish in 1 turn and are hard to follow ~ Snarling out stop takes 2, thus not immediate. ) <br /> <br /> After 4 years of game play online and in person. I have never once thought either of those things would help my frenzied vampire fight, feed or flee. Nor has anyone in games I have been in ever used them in a situation. I am not saying it's impossible, but it shouldn't be a &quot;well I am a venture so I dominiate all the time even in a frenzy&quot; .... I am asking people like Charlaquin and Holy Who I know have been around here a good long time ( longer than me ) if you have personally used either of those things? ( why not toss in the Seductive lashing out too. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:43:10-07:00","id":1212273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you ever once in actual game play used Dominate or Majesty in a frenzy </div> </div> </div>Yes, or well yes my players has a few times. Dominated other chars to help them kill someone, dominated people to stop fighting so they could be eaten on. Majesty to get them inside someones house or making a npcs come to him when he was locked up and hungry. <br /> Dominate has been successfully used to win combat when the PC has had a combat pool of 2 dice in frenzy, before defense being subtracted. <br /> Turns are dramatic time, usually lasting about three seconds, but are subject to the rule of dramatic rationalism or whatever makes sense now. Even though, dominate 1 takes at most 2 turns.One to establish and next to command, and a handful of seconds is pretty immediate to me. The &quot;establish eye contact&quot; part is part of the activation roll, Rose has made that clear as well.<br /> And to be fair, Frenzy is more then &quot;smashing faces&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:10:30-07:00","id":1212317,"title":"","content":"Well fuck. I had a thorough response here, but the forum ate it. I\u2019ll have to re-write it later I guess...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-27-2018, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:15:12-07:00","id":1212344,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24044_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24044\" data-vbnamecard=\"24044\">Ventrue Life</a> - Do you own the Requiem 1E Chronicler's Guide? It discusses replacing the Beast with something called the Other. 2E may have been influenced slightly by that by making the Beast not just an unintelligent monster. Basically the Other is intelligent, methodical, and is almost like having another NPC in the PC's head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:16:33-07:00","id":1212346,"title":"","content":"If there was already the opportunity to establish build up. Yes on both. I\u2019ve played or STed both Dominate and Majesty using characters go and prepare the room in advance, either knowing a fight was coming or in anticipation of things turning ugly. Starting from ground zero, yes on Dominate, no for Majesty except for two scenarios of using Idol to flee. The Summoning devotion would work if the requirements were already met. Dominate 1 has the chance to become single turn use when they get an exceptional success which is something a starting character can do somewhat reliably and only becomes more reliable as they pick up skill specializations or get celerity for home brew devotions. Majesty at ground zero doesn\u2019t get that option but with the right home brew devotions it could. Using Dominate 1 with a succinct phrase such as \u201cGo play in traffic, assholes.\u201d While drawing a gun or baton is useful for dispatching with potential defenders while proceeding towards the target you\u2019re going to beat and doubles as intimidation. \u201cWait a minute.\u201d curtails fleeing attempts to advance on someone to feed. \u201cGet them outta my way.\u201d Enlists help to clear an escape route more effectively than starting a shoving match with multiple people at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-27-2018, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:24:01-07:00","id":1212347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212258#post1212258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marcus's example of being trapped in a cage while frenzied.. I am not even sure why you would go into a frenzy while you are trapped in a cage, but I could totally see the vampire spazzing out, then calming down. THEN dominating the person to let them out once the vampire has had a moment to think clearly.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Upon entering frenzy, determine what the Beast wants. Does it want to escape? Does it want to punish the person who insulted his host? Does it want blood? Typically, Frenzy ends when that thing occurs </div> </div> </div>So, according to the example of mine it seems that if the frenzy has been provoked by the desire to escape, it will never ends until the vampire achieve its goal (escaping).<br /> That's said, even if it's going to end after a scene, that's doesn't imply that, using dominate, is not representing the most direct and immediate way to get free for the Beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212258#post1212258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Alright experienced players. Have you ever once in actual game play used Dominate or Majesty in a frenzy? Dominate like you said by definition is not immediate. It takes a turn to catch the eye, a turn to make the command then a turn for you to act. That is 3 turns you could have been just smashing the thing's face in. Same with Idol. It takes a turn to Awe and Idol and a turn for you to do something after that vs a turn you could have probably used Celerity and bolted out the door. Awe and Idol is one turn So there is actually a huge difference between snarling out &quot;stop&quot; and turning invisible to run from your opponent. ( you vanish in 1 turn and are hard to follow ~ Snarling out stop takes 2, thus not immediate. )</div> </div> </div> </div>My players used when in Frenzy against enemies they cannot overwhelm with just physical attribute and in a lot of other occasions. Always under the principle: Is this the most direct and violent way to achieve your goal without risking final death??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212258#post1212258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> After 4 years of game play online and in person. I have never once thought either of those things would help my frenzied vampire fight, feed or flee. Nor has anyone in games I have been in ever used them in a situation. I am not saying it's impossible, but it shouldn't be a &quot;well I am a venture so I dominiate all the time even in a frenzy&quot; .... I am asking people like Charlaquin and Holy Who I know have been around here a good long time ( longer than me ) if you have personally used either of those things? ( why not toss in the Seductive lashing out too. )</div> </div> </div> </div>So you always fell into Frenzy in relatively safe situation.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-27-2018, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:00:54-07:00","id":1212362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212258#post1212258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &lt;-- that is what I have been trying to say. And you have to activate Awe to activate Idol( though you can do that in the same turn, but it's still 1 turn where you could have been running and you didn't ) I was citing the book and bolding the lines that lead me to believe what I believed, rather than just giving examples of situations that don't really come from anywhere. <br /> <br /> Marcus's example of being trapped in a cage while frenzied.. I am not even sure why you would go into a frenzy while you are trapped in a cage, but I could totally see the vampire spazzing out, then calming down. THEN dominating the person to let them out once the vampire has had a moment to think clearly. <br /> <br /> Alright experienced players. Have you ever once in actual game play used Dominate or Majesty in a frenzy? Dominate like you said by definition is not immediate. It takes a turn to catch the eye, a turn to make the command then a turn for you to act. That is 3 turns you could have been just smashing the thing's face in. Same with Idol. It takes a turn to Awe and Idol and a turn for you to do something after that vs a turn you could have probably used Celerity and bolted out the door. Awe and Idol is one turn So there is actually a huge difference between snarling out &amp;quot;stop&amp;quot; and turning invisible to run from your opponent. ( you vanish in 1 turn and are hard to follow ~ Snarling out stop takes 2, thus not immediate. ) <br /> <br /> After 4 years of game play online and in person. I have never once thought either of those things would help my frenzied vampire fight, feed or flee. Nor has anyone in games I have been in ever used them in a situation. I am not saying it's impossible, but it shouldn't be a &amp;quot;well I am a venture so I dominiate all the time even in a frenzy&amp;quot; .... I am asking people like Charlaquin and Holy Who I know have been around here a good long time ( longer than me ) if you have personally used either of those things? ( why not toss in the Seductive lashing out too. )</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played VTR for over 10 years (I started with VTR 1e in 2007) and I have most certainly seen it come up.<br /> <br /> I've only been storytelling myself for 2 years and in those 2 years I've yet to see a player propose using Dominate/Majesty in a frenzy, but during my years as a player I often came back to playing Ventrue, they are my favorite clan, and I've been allowed to use Dominate during frenzy at least a couple of times. Not often, but not never either.<br /> <br /> The most memorable time was when I was riding in a taxi and I succumbed to a hunger frenzy. This was during VTR 1e so frenzy rules were a bit different. I wanted to eat the taxi driver but we were on the middle of a highway driving at 120km/h. So I asked the GM if my frenzying Ventrue could and would dominate the driver by establishing eye contact through the mirror and demand him to pull over. The GM allowed it. Before I knew it the taxi was pulled over on the emergency strip of the road and my Ventrue was nomming on the poor driver. It all went by in a matter of seconds. Ofcourse it didn't go without any trouble. The taxi driver tried to resist the bite and when all was said and done I realized the car horn was honking because of our struggles and I now had a group of spectators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:05:21-07:00","id":1212364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212347#post1212347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My players used when in Frenzy against enemies they cannot overwhelm with just physical attribute and in a lot of other occasions. Always under the principle: Is this the most direct and violent way to achieve your goal without risking final death??</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are durable, is the thing, and Majesty and Dominate are the specific purview of the two clans that are most invested in unlife with people around that frenzy complicates at best and annihilates at worst. The Ventrue curse is set up such that the two biggest coping mechanisms in their toolbox are proxies and desensitization, the latter of which only helps with the impact of breaking points and which actively lengthens the duration of failure to ride the wave in practical terms; the Daeva are less directly attached to the get-a-subordinate-to-do-it methodology but also have the most suitable common Disciplines to the acts of violence and/or escape.<br /> <br /> The Storytelling chapter emphasizes that frenzy is a <i>loss of control</i> for vampires, and specifically <i>contrasts</i> that with the greater control Disciplines afford them \u2014 it seems <i>entirely in keeping with the fiction </i>that a character under the thrall of their Beast's immediate desires will be less able to benefit from the specific psychic abilities that let them control people in any sort of refined manner; in Beast: the Primordial's terms, a frenzied vampire leans on Atavisms instead of Nightmares, because animal caution does not afford greater facility with precision tools than blunt instruments and words are a precision tool. The &quot;psychic&quot; Disciplines are going to see more basic use by the Beast than the vampire proper if they see any use at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:10:37-07:00","id":1212367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212273#post1212273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, or well yes my players has a few times. Dominated other chars to help them kill someone, dominated people to stop fighting so they could be eaten on. Majesty to get them inside someones house or making a npcs come to him when he was locked up and hungry.<br /> Dominate has been successfully used to win combat when the PC has had a combat pool of 2 dice in frenzy, before defense being subtracted.<br /> Turns are dramatic time, usually lasting about three seconds, but are subject to the rule of dramatic rationalism or whatever makes sense now. Even though, dominate 1 takes at most 2 turns.One to establish and next to command, and a handful of seconds is pretty immediate to me. The &quot;establish eye contact&quot; part is part of the activation roll, Rose has made that clear as well.<br /> And to be fair, Frenzy is more then &quot;smashing faces&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear you had a vampire in a murder frenzy stop and take 2-3 turns to ask Dominate another character to help kill the target? Dominating someone to tell them to stop fighting wouldn't work because as soon as you started eating them, the dominate would break and they would resume fighting. So how does that help?<br /> <br /> And in A frenzy or a hunger frenzy they went to a house and used majesty talked to the person to get them to let them in the house then eat them?<br /> <br /> Frenzy is by definition the loss of control. You're no longer thinking properly, clearly, you disregard things you shouldn't disregard. You do things that aren't the best choices. How do people justify these extremely premeditated and thought out plots as an action of an &quot;out of control monster?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I can see all of these as perfectly fine actions for someone who has control over their mental faculties. When you're hungry, yeah totally dominate the man across the room to make him come to you. But when your friend is standing right next to you and there is food two houses over. When you snap... you don't go two houses over, majesty the man who answers the door and ask him politely to let you in so you can eat him. You.... eat your friend.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212346#post1212346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there was already the opportunity to establish build up. Yes on both. I\u2019ve played or STed both Dominate and Majesty using characters go and prepare the room in advance, either knowing a fight was coming or in anticipation of things turning ugly. Starting from ground zero, yes on Dominate, no for Majesty except for two scenarios of using Idol to flee. The Summoning devotion would work if the requirements were already met. Dominate 1 has the chance to become single turn use when they get an exceptional success which is something a starting character can do somewhat reliably and only becomes more reliable as they pick up skill specializations or get celerity for home brew devotions. Majesty at ground zero doesn\u2019t get that option but with the right home brew devotions it could. Using Dominate 1 with a succinct phrase such as \u201cGo play in traffic, assholes.\u201d While drawing a gun or baton is useful for dispatching with potential defenders while proceeding towards the target you\u2019re going to beat and doubles as intimidation. \u201cWait a minute.\u201d curtails fleeing attempts to advance on someone to feed. \u201cGet them outta my way.\u201d Enlists help to clear an escape route more effectively than starting a shoving match with multiple people at once.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All these were done in a Frenzy? You have had a frenzied vampire tell it's target to go play in traffic? and someone in a hunger frenzy tell someone to wait a minute so they could saunter up and eat them?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212347#post1212347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So, according to the example of mine it seems that if the frenzy has been provoked by the desire to escape, it will never ends until the vampire achieve its goal (escaping).<br /> That's said, even if it's going to end after a scene, that's doesn't imply that, using dominate, is not representing the most direct and immediate way to get free for the Beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> My players used when in Frenzy against enemies they cannot overwhelm with just physical attribute and in a lot of other occasions. Always under the principle: Is this the most direct and violent way to achieve your goal without risking final death??</div> </div> </div> </div>Frenzy is suppose to be used as a dramatic tool. If you are simply locked in a cage with no immediate threat or immediate danger.. Why would you frenzy at all? That's what I don't understand. Even if you did frenzy and freak out, when the beast realized that it was stuck without further aid ( or the end of the scene ) he would calm down to let the vampire take control again and form a plan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212347#post1212347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you always fell into Frenzy in relatively safe situation.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually the last time my vampire frenzied. he was with one other party member and they had walked into a meeting with a drug cartel which had several heavily armed guards. The two of them were outnumbered probably 5 to 1. My vampire had no weapons whatsoever and all the guards had guns... Walking out would have been the smarter choice. Summoning allies would have been the smarter choice. Dominating them to stop shooting would have been good. Not fighting 10 people with automatic weapons would have been the better option. But he snapped and started ripping them apart.. He got shot oh so many times. But as frenzy says it's violent and messy and out of control. so that's what he did. Violent, messy, and without thought to what would have been the smarter or more logical choice.<br /> <br /> I have had my story teller make my vampire go into a hunger frenzy when the only other person in the room was his lover. He ended up killing him.<br /> <br /> I have frenzied in a police station. Frenzied in burning building and let the other party members almost die for it, when I could have saved them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212362#post1212362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've played VTR for over 10 years (I started with VTR 1e in 2007) and I have most certainly seen it come up.<br /> <br /> I've only been storytelling myself for 2 years and in those 2 years I've yet to see a player propose using Dominate/Majesty in a frenzy, but during my years as a player I often came back to playing Ventrue, they are my favorite clan, and I've been allowed to use Dominate during frenzy at least a couple of times. Not often, but not never either.<br /> <br /> The most memorable time was when I was riding in a taxi and I succumbed to a hunger frenzy. This was during VTR 1e so frenzy rules were a bit different. I wanted to eat the taxi driver but we were on the middle of a highway driving at 120km/h. So I asked the GM if my frenzying Ventrue could and would dominate the driver by establishing eye contact through the mirror and demand him to pull over. The GM allowed it. Before I knew it the taxi was pulled over on the emergency strip of the road and my Ventrue was nomming on the poor driver. It all went by in a matter of seconds. Ofcourse it didn't go without any trouble. The taxi driver tried to resist the bite and when all was said and done I realized the car horn was honking because of our struggles and I now had a group of spectators.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that, but why not just dive into the driver's seat and eat him? It's more immediate and violent and less premeditated. A vampire would almost assuredly survive the crash. If there was even a crash. The driver would likely slam on the breaks and try to get out of the car giving you free reign to eat him while he tries not to crash the car and is distracted with mortal thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One last edit and thought: I think we are confused on what out of control actually looks like. Crimes of passion and rage are frenzies, premeditated murder and plotted out courses of action or not frenzies. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-27-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:35:11-07:00","id":1212370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212364#post1212364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are durable, is the thing, and Majesty and Dominate are the specific purview of the two clans that are most invested in unlife with people around that frenzy complicates at best and annihilates at worst. The Ventrue curse is set up such that the two biggest coping mechanisms in their toolbox are proxies and desensitization, the latter of which only helps with the impact of breaking points and which actively lengthens the duration of failure to ride the wave in practical terms; the Daeva are less directly attached to the get-a-subordinate-to-do-it methodology but also have the most suitable common Disciplines to the acts of violence and/or escape.<br /> <br /> The Storytelling chapter emphasizes that frenzy is a <i>loss of control</i> for vampires, and specifically <i>contrasts</i> that with the greater control Disciplines afford them \u2014 it seems <i>entirely in keeping with the fiction </i>that a character under the thrall of their Beast's immediate desires will be less able to benefit from the specific psychic abilities that let them control people in any sort of refined manner; in Beast: the Primordial's terms, a frenzied vampire leans on Atavisms instead of Nightmares, because animal caution does not afford greater facility with precision tools than blunt instruments and words are a precision tool. The &quot;psychic&quot; Disciplines are going to see more basic use by the Beast than the vampire proper if they see any use at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I read this is that it's actually a loss of control for the Vampire because is the BEAST that takes control. The difference is even not so subtle.<br /> Obviously we are focusing on Dominate and Majesty but the same can be applied to every other discipline: Nightmare, Animalism etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:49:46-07:00","id":1212372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212370#post1212370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I read this is that it's actually a loss of control for the Vampire because is the BEAST that takes control.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vampire losing control <i>means</i> the Beast has lost control \u2014 the compartmentalization Kindred do about the fact that their nature drives them to be bloodhungry, sunshy, territorial and vengeful under strain does not actually mean that there is a separate entity that takes over their bodies when they're threatened just because there's a poetic name attached to it. &quot;The Beast&quot; is more than just how a vampire acts during frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:52:50-07:00","id":1212375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212258#post1212258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> that is what I have been trying to say. And you have to activate Awe to activate Idol( though you can do that in the same turn, but it's still 1 turn where you could have been running and you didn't )</div> </div> </div> </div>You can activate Awe and Idol and move in the same turn. By any logic that says you can\u2019t activate Idol in a fear Frenzy because you could be running instead, you shouldn\u2019t be able to activate Face in the Crowd and Cloak of Night either, or attacking someone who\u2019s in your way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212258#post1212258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was citing the book and bolding the lines that lead me to believe what I believed, rather than just giving examples of situations that don't really come from anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but so were Marcus and Ventrue Life. Repeatedly quoting \u201cimmediate, forceful abandon\u201d wasn\u2019t helping your case any more than repeatedly quoting \u201cthe Beast isn\u2019t stupid\u201d was helping theirs. We\u2019ve all read the book and interpreted the words through the filters of our own experiences and biases. Quoting the same text that I interpret differently than you isn\u2019t a very effective way of communicating the reason for your interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212258#post1212258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Marcus's example of being trapped in a cage while frenzied.. I am not even sure why you would go into a frenzy while you are trapped in a cage, but I could totally see the vampire spazzing out, then calming down. THEN dominating the person to let them out once the vampire has had a moment to think clearly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being trapped in a cage seems like a perfectly reasonable Frenzy trigger to me. You\u2019re stuck inside. You want to get out. Maybe to kill the person who trapped you.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s worth noting that I don\u2019t consider fight, feed, and flee to be the only valid goals for a Frenzy. And I generally treat Frenzy triggers the same way I do Breaking Points, in that if a player tells me, \u201cthis is a Frenzy trigger/Breaking Point for my character,\u201d I don\u2019t tell them no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212258#post1212258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Alright experienced players. Have you ever once in actual game play used Dominate or Majesty in a frenzy? Dominate like you said by definition is not immediate. It takes a turn to catch the eye, a turn to make the command then a turn for you to act. That is 3 turns you could have been just smashing the thing's face in. Same with Idol. It takes a turn to Awe and Idol and a turn for you to do something after that vs a turn you could have probably used Celerity and bolted out the door. Awe and Idol is one turn So there is actually a huge difference between snarling out &amp;quot;stop&amp;quot; and turning invisible to run from your opponent. ( you vanish in 1 turn and are hard to follow ~ Snarling out stop takes 2, thus not immediate. ) <br /> <br /> After 4 years of game play online and in person. I have never once thought either of those things would help my frenzied vampire fight, feed or flee. Nor has anyone in games I have been in ever used them in a situation. I am not saying it's impossible, but it shouldn't be a &amp;quot;well I am a venture so I dominiate all the time even in a frenzy&amp;quot; .... I am asking people like Charlaquin and Holy Who I know have been around here a good long time ( longer than me ) if you have personally used either of those things? ( why not toss in the Seductive lashing out too. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I have seen players use both Dominate and Majesty during Frenzy in actual play. I will say that I have only seen Dominate used in Frenzy in LARP, where establishing eye contact is a matter of actually establishing eye contact, instead of an abstract measure of time spent - in actual LARP play, Eye contact happens immediately or it doesn\u2019t happen at all - you have to take advantage of the player\u2019s reflexive habit of looking people in the eye, because if they have time for their rational thought processes to kick in, they\u2019ll look away. This in fact messed me up a bit when I switched to tabletop, as I didn\u2019t realize giving a command in the same turn you establish Mezmerized wasn\u2019t possible without an exceptional success until an earlier conversation with you on these forums about the same subject. After that conversation, I have not seen a player use Dominate in Frenzy in tabletop.<br /> <br /> As for Idol, I have seen that used in Frenzy, both in LARP and in tabletop. It takes exactly as much \u201ctime\u201d as activating Obfuscate, which I have seen used for the same purposes in Frenzy by characters who have it. Generally, to avoid being attacked while in a fear Frenzy. I have not seen any of the other Majesty Powers used during Frenzy.<br /> <br /> As for Lashing out, I usually only see the Monstrous Beast used during Frenzy, though I have occasionally seen the Competitive as well. Seductive I have not seen, though I can easily imagine a scenario where it would be appropriate. I just don\u2019t like to roleplay rape, so that scenario doesn\u2019t come up in my games.<br /> <br /> Again, it\u2019s important to note that I allow lots of goals beyond kill, feed, and escape in Frenzy, and I allow players to declare Frenzy triggers for their own characters when they feel it\u2019s appropriate, so the differences in our interpretations of what is or isn\u2019t possible in Frenzy is bound up in a more complex set of interrelated differences in our interpretations of Frenzy as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:00:52-07:00","id":1212378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212367#post1212367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see that, but why not just dive into the driver's seat and eat him? It's more immediate and violent and less premeditated. A vampire would almost assuredly survive the crash. If there was even a crash. The driver would likely slam on the breaks and try to get out of the car giving you free reign to eat him while he tries not to crash the car and is distracted with mortal thought. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's fucking stupid. The beast is not fucking stupid.<br /> <br /> Trying to eat a driver on a ONE-HUNDRED-AND-TWENTY kilometers per hour highway is a sure way to instantly kill your driver, kill a lot more other people, get heavily injured yourself, cause a commotion and in the end you still don't have had your lunch yet! <br /> <br /> No offense but what you're suggesting is absolutely silly. If you wanna roleplay your Beast like that, that's fine, but the Beast in my games is smarter than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:21:01-07:00","id":1212381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212378#post1212378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because that's fucking stupid. The beast is not fucking stupid.<br /> <br /> Trying to eat a driver on a ONE-HUNDRED-AND-TWENTY kilometers per hour highway is a sure way to instantly kill your driver, kill a lot more other people, get heavily injured yourself, cause a commotion and in the end you still don't have had your lunch yet!<br /> <br /> No offense but what you're suggesting is absolutely silly. If you wanna roleplay your Beast like that, that's fine, but the Beast in my games is smarter than that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just because you say &quot;no offense&quot; doesn't mean you're not being a jerk about it. I have actually seen that exact scenario in a few movies. Someone in the backseat or passenger seat attacks the driver, even in high speeds. Perhaps you should tell people who create literature and movies that they are fucking stupid. I am sure they will agree with you. <br /> <br /> Unless you're some elder vampire with 5 vigor, you're probably not going to kill the driver in one turn. That gives the driver time to slow down and pull off the road. and a vampire would take all bashing even if there was an accident, so you'd probably not even get that hurt. <br /> <br /> Jumping out of moving vehicles is also fucking stupid, but people do it in a panic more than you'd think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:31:16-07:00","id":1212387,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Yeah, lets keep this civil, everyone. Calling a scene from someone else\u2019s game \u201cfucking stupid\u201d is pretty disrespectful, and respect is rule 1, 2, and 3 here.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:39:59-07:00","id":1212390,"title":"","content":"I've allowed a grappled frenzier with no real chance of breaking their immobilization to issue &quot;Let me go&quot; through Dominate rather than keep rolling brawl pools.<br /> I've allowed a frenzier in a bar to activate Awe so the bouncers wouldn't intervene while they beat the crap out of their target.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:41:17-07:00","id":1212391,"title":"","content":"The only thing I want to point out is that Dominate per RAW only takes 1-2 rounds. There are no rules about spending a turn catching your victims gaze. The only requirement iirc is that the victim is able to see the Kindreds eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:48:14-07:00","id":1212392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212391#post1212391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I want to point out is that Dominate per RAW only takes 1-2 rounds. There are no rules about spending a turn catching your victims gaze. The only requirement iirc is that the victim is able to see the Kindreds eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitalis's description was &quot;catch their gaze, issue a command, and act,&quot; i.e. it takes at least three steps for you to do something if you're working Dominate into the process as opposed to the one-step process of &quot;act.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212378#post1212378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because that's fucking stupid. The beast is not fucking stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lexicon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast: The inchoate urges that drive vampires <b>away from the Man.</b><br /> frenzy: <b>A berserk state</b> in which the Beast takes total control over a vampire. Rage, fear and hunger can induce frenzies; when precision is needed, the term is qualified by cause (rage frenzy, fear frenzy or hunger frenzy). Unqualified, the term generally indicates rage frenzy.<br /> Man, the: The vampire\u2019s <b>human impulses and self-control.</b> Used to compliment or contrast the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uncontrolled frenzy is something vampires try to avoid for very good reasons, generally speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:53:53-07:00","id":1212395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212392#post1212392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitalis's description was &quot;catch their gaze, issue a command, and act,&quot; i.e. it takes at least three steps for you to do something if you're working Dominate into the process as opposed to the one-step process of &quot;act.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, however Vitalis specifically used the term &quot;turn&quot; so I wished to ensure accuracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:59:58-07:00","id":1212397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212395#post1212395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough, however Vitalis specifically used the term &quot;turn&quot; so I wished to ensure accuracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026That's still accurate. It takes one turn to use Mesmerize, one turn to issue a command, and at least one turn to do something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T13:04:46-07:00","id":1212399,"title":"","content":"Would the person issued a command not act in the same turn he was commanded? I don't see why they would wait at all to carry out a vampires commands.<br /> <br /> Regardless that was not the assertion made by Vitalis. The assertion was-<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I misread Vitalis's argument. It is about a turn after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","user":"Heroofthemists","date":". 04-27-2018, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T13:10:32-07:00","id":1212400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212399#post1212399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the person issued a command not act in the same turn he was commanded? I don't see why they would wait at all to carry out a vampires commands.<br /> <br /> Regardless that was not the assertion made by Vitalis. The assertion was-<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I misread Vitalis's argument. It is about a turn after.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty sure catching the victim\u2019s gaze is part of the same turn you activate Mezmerize. That\u2019s the reason you can\u2019t issue the command in the same turn without an exceptional success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T13:13:07-07:00","id":1212403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212400#post1212400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure catching the victim\u2019s gaze is part of the same turn you activate Mezmerize. That\u2019s the reason you can\u2019t issue the command in the same turn without an exceptional success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, except in the case of an exceptional success. But I do not see how, barring special circumstances, a third turn is implied for a dominate victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T13:15:25-07:00","id":1212404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212399#post1212399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the person issued a command not act in the same turn he was commanded?</div> </div> </div> </div>The victim isn't going to literally fall on your fists or move their blood into your gullet for you if you tell them to hold still.<br /> <br /> &quot;It takes a turn to catch the eye, a turn to make the command then a turn for <u>you</u> to act. That is 3 turns you could have been just smashing the thing's face in.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:31:09-07:00","id":1212426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212367#post1212367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be clear you had a vampire in a murder frenzy stop and take 2-3 turns to ask Dominate another character to help kill the target? Dominating someone to tell them to stop fighting wouldn't work because as soon as you started eating them, the dominate would break and they would resume fighting. So how does that help?<br /> <br /> And in A frenzy or a hunger frenzy they went to a house and used majesty talked to the person to get them to let them in the house then eat them?<br /> <br /> Frenzy is by definition the loss of control. You're no longer thinking properly, clearly, you disregard things you shouldn't disregard. You do things that aren't the best choices. How do people justify these extremely premeditated and thought out plots as an action of an &quot;out of control monster?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I can see all of these as perfectly fine actions for someone who has control over their mental faculties. When you're hungry, yeah totally dominate the man across the room to make him come to you. But when your friend is standing right next to you and there is food two houses over. When you snap... you don't go two houses over, majesty the man who answers the door and ask him politely to let you in so you can eat him. You.... eat your friend.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You asked for examples of play and I provided. You are however begging the question, presuming to know reasoning behind the actions as if a white room scenario.<br /> I won't go into detail, just a quick summary. <br /> The dominate thing, was aimed at a friend to help murder another person, how is that not about loosing control? I presume the Beast is smart enough to know by instinct it can't hit for shit but he's buffed off physical-capped friend sure can beat someone. <br /> Well of course it works, even if the Condition as stated resolves by damage (which we kindly ignore at our table, but that's another story) if you got fangs in you, you are by default Swooned so not much to do if just a random mortal npc or at least in an established grapple already, and by taking lethal damage you're beaten down (usually).<br /> <br /> Yeah the Invitation Bane is a thing and we up play the severity of it as well.<br /> <br /> Yeah we're are not in disagreement about this loss of control. Neither is any elaborate plots taking place in frenzy, just instinctual response to the scene, played out from the perspective of a instinctual, primal monster that ain't stupid. You are begging the question in that you presume to know the scenes and circumstance actions and outcomes take place in without any actual knowledge about it, which is dishonest in the attempt of a civil discussion or the very least presumptuous about the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> About the friend eating, I agree in that case as well, but I was nut saying any situation like that. I would say that if there was people around though (but for whatever reason your friend was the eating victim) the Beast could still make use of say Obfuscate to be left alone while eating.<br /> <br /> So in short, don't make presumptions about situations that probably was acted out way different from what you choose to imagine them to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:57:43-07:00","id":1212443,"title":"","content":"","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-27-2018, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:17:48-07:00","id":1212461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212381#post1212381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just because you say &quot;no offense&quot; doesn't mean you're not being a jerk about it. I have actually seen that exact scenario in a few movies. Someone in the backseat or passenger seat attacks the driver, even in high speeds. Perhaps you should tell people who create literature and movies that they are fucking stupid. I am sure they will agree with you.<br /> <br /> Unless you're some elder vampire with 5 vigor, you're probably not going to kill the driver in one turn. That gives the driver time to slow down and pull off the road. and a vampire would take all bashing even if there was an accident, so you'd probably not even get that hurt.<br /> <br /> Jumping out of moving vehicles is also fucking stupid, but people do it in a panic more than you'd think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was indeed not my intention to offend you, else I wouldn't have said &quot;no offense&quot;. If you did take offense then I'm sorry to hear that, I apologize. I merely wished to express how dumb I personally think your proposed scenario is.<br /> <br /> That being said, I've seen Interview With The Vampire, which has your proposed scenario, and I thought it was stupid there too.<br /> <br /> The way I see your proposed scenario play out is NOT like this:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1LyG0S_arq8\" data-code=\"1LyG0S_arq8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1LyG0S_arq8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Indeed, in reality it would more likely go like this:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OVS6k8c79jQ\" data-code=\"OVS6k8c79jQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/OVS6k8c79jQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, not ideal. Not ideal at all. A vampire doing what you proposed will likely work himself into more trouble than he was already in, and him getting a meal out of it is all but guaranteed. Much easier to just Dominate the driver, tell him to pull over, and eat him then. <br /> <br /> It's fine if you wanna play up the callousness and destructiveness of the Beast. You can play the Beast however you want. Me? I personally tend to play the Beast like a sly, witty, cunning predator with the smarts of a human but the instincts of an animal. The Beats is monstrous, the Beast is dangerous, the Beast does not give a damn about humanity, the Beast couldn't care less about etiquette, morality, standards, none of that, but it does care about survival, about getting what it wants but being smart about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think ultimately the most important question that has not really been addressed but should be: when a vampire enters frenzy, does only the Man lose control, or does the Beast lose control too? When a vampire is in frenzy, is the Beast also frenzying? Is the Beast in a blind rage during frenzy, or is it merely the Man who goes into a blind rage, giving the Beast control for a while?<br /> <br /> There's a difference and I think the difference means a lot. Does the book say anything about this? Because I have not seen this question being addressed by the book.<br /> <br /> It sounds like when you roleplay frenzy, you roleplay the Beast being in a frenzied rage, while I always assumed the Man is in a frenzied rage, which gives the Beast a window to seize control from the Man and play around for a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:37:22-07:00","id":1212470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212461#post1212461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think ultimately the most important question that has not really been addressed but should be: when a vampire enters frenzy, does only the Man lose control, or does the Beast lose control too? When a vampire is in frenzy, is the Beast also frenzying? Is the Beast in a blind rage during frenzy, or is it merely the Man who goes into a blind rage, giving the Beast control for a while?</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the fact that &quot;the Man&quot; <i>is the vampire's self-control</i>, &quot;the Beast is as good at coming up with a plan as a crazed shit-house rat&quot; is a direct quotation, as is &quot;The Man might just be a tool to make a cleverer Beast.&quot; &quot;The Beast&quot; <i>is</i> the blind rage, the hunger, the fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:48:27-07:00","id":1212471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212461#post1212461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's fine if you wanna play up the callousness and destructiveness of the Beast. You can play the Beast however you want. Me? I personally tend to play the Beast like a sly, witty, cunning predator with the smarts of a human but the instincts of an animal. The Beats is monstrous, the Beast is dangerous, the Beast does not give a damn about humanity, the Beast couldn't care less about etiquette, morality, standards, none of that, but it does care about survival, about getting what it wants but being smart about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think ultimately the most important question that has not really been addressed but should be: when a vampire enters frenzy, does only the Man lose control, or does the Beast lose control too? When a vampire is in frenzy, is the Beast also frenzying? Is the Beast in a blind rage during frenzy, or is it merely the Man who goes into a blind rage, giving the Beast control for a while?<br /> <br /> There's a difference and I think the difference means a lot. Does the book say anything about this? Because I have not seen this question being addressed by the book.<br /> <br /> It sounds like when you roleplay frenzy, you roleplay the Beast being in a frenzied rage, while I always assumed the Man is in a frenzied rage, which gives the Beast a window to seize control from the Man and play around for a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>The beast isn't a thinking person living inside of the vampire. There are not two people living in there. That's why in 100 different places in the book it is referred to devolving into something animalistic. What you are saying sounds very much like you think there are two sentient people in there. And yes.. I posed this question already. Just not in your same words. Several of you are using very thought out and premeditated examples for vampires while they are in a frenzy.<br /> <br /> Like... Charlaquin said requoting this stuff over and over isn't helping, but it's there. It is the total loss of control. It says it reduces you down to the most basic of instincts. Fight, Flight, or feed. You snap. You lose control to something that doesn't have an IQ of 100.. but the IQ of a Tiger, Shark or Lion. It says you act in any manor that a TERRIFIED, STARVING, or ENRAGED predator is. It says that Rational Thought is gone. It says you do no not so smart things.<br /> <br /> It even says when you try to fight it, you hit things, snarl, and hiss all very bestial things. It says &quot;immediate and extreme response, usually meaning a blood-soaked frenzy.&quot; Not something like Oh pardon me, Sit down while I get all my friends to help me kill you.<br /> <br /> As Satchel quoted: The lexicon's definition of frenzy is this : frenzy: A berserk state in which the Beast takes total control over a vampire. Rage, fear and hunger can induce frenzies; when precision is needed, the term is qualified by cause (rage frenzy, fear frenzy or hunger frenzy). Unqualified, the term generally indicates rage frenzy. When someone is blinded by rage or hunger they do things they know are stupid, but they just don't care anymore.<br /> <br /> Also quoted prior; The Beast: The inchoate urges that drive vampires away from the Man. This is not a sentient thing that shares your body. This is like your baser instinct that tries to push you away from human stuff. ( inchoate : <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">just begun and so not fully formed or developed; rudimentary. ) It very clearly does not have HUMAN intelligence. that would be like saying my anger has thought processes or that Bob's hunger actually speaks to him. It's just an urge that pushes you to take action. when you frenzy you snap and just take action ... </span></span><br /> <br /> A vampire that has fallen entirely to the beast the Draugr, cant even read anymore! It doesn't go home to the bed it knew, it doesn't shower or make sure the paychecks keep coming, it acts like an animal and finds a den, leaves when it needs hunt and acts violently when things come into it's territory.<br /> <br /> I saw your videos. Vampires aren't human so if they caused a wreck like that second one and got tossed out.. They would get up and walk the fuck away. They already didn't care about the human in it... And I don't see why the Beast would care about anyone in the cars around it either as long as it's hunger was satisfied in the end. Actually forming a wreck like that might get you more bodies to feed on... <br /> <br /> <br /> And yes I do play the beast as being in a frenzied rage or a hunger frenzy because I don't think the beast is a person.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212470#post1212470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the fact that &quot;the Man&quot; <i>is the vampire's self-control</i>, &quot;the Beast is as good at coming up with a plan as a crazed shit-house rat&quot; is a direct quotation, as is &quot;The Man might just be a tool to make a cleverer Beast.&quot; &quot;The Beast&quot; <i>is</i> the blind rage, the hunger, the fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>We keep saying this... and this argument is devolving. I see it sort of stems from a disagreement of what &quot;Out of control&quot; actually means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-27-2018, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:54:36-07:00","id":1212475,"title":"","content":"Hey guys... can\u2019t we just use the Other as an alternate to the Beast if we want a rational frenzy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T16:03:26-07:00","id":1212478,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a><br /> <br /> See, now we're getting somewhere. Because I was under the impression that the Beast very much is indeed a second entity inside the vampire's head, in the same way a person with Dissociative Identity Disorder has multiple entities in his head. I guess it's because of what's written on page 278 under 'Frenzy' and 'Twist: The Beast Guides', where it implies that A) every Beast is different and handles situations differently, based on the personality of the vampire, and B) it suggests allowing other players to play your Beast as a sentient, tempting force. That's how I've been playing it ever since I got VTR 2e, mostly because I got sick and tired of the Beast being a dumb animal no smarter than the Hulk.<br /> <br /> So I suppose you could say we're both right and it entirely depends on how you want to portray the Beast! I certainly agree that most of the text you quoted implies that the Beats is a dumb animal, but even the book itself literally suggests to play the Beast as a sentient cunning force.<br /> <br /> I suppose in the end it's up to each gaming table to decide how their Beasts are played out. Both takes on the Beast seem to be supported by the book, but I concur that after re-reading the 2e book, your take on the Beast is probably the default intended way to play the Beast, while my take on the Beats is suggested as a twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-27-2018, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T16:07:49-07:00","id":1212479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212470#post1212470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting aside the fact that &amp;quot;the Man&amp;quot; <i>is the vampire's self-control</i>, &amp;quot;the Beast is as good at coming up with a plan as a crazed shit-house rat&amp;quot; is a direct quotation, as is &amp;quot;The Man might just be a tool to make a cleverer Beast.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;The Beast&amp;quot; <i>is</i> the blind rage, the hunger, the fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's just your interpretation. <br /> <br /> In general, there are plenty of example where a not stupid and self suicide Beast would like to dominate. Such as there are plenty of example where dominate would be the only way to achieve the goal.<br /> <br /> The trapped vampire is a perfectly lecit reason for frenzy, at least because, first or after, she will get starved... and frenzy, by raw, does not end until you achieve the goal, that obviously you cannot achieve if you are not able to break the cage. <br /> <br /> I can also see a vampire with no physical disciplines and bp 1 (that is not a big boost in frenzy) have to fight against well armed hunter/s or, having as the only way to win, Dominate.<br /> <br /> There would be a lot more situations justifing the needing of mental disciplines even in frenzy... but we are interpreting Frenzy in 2 opposite ways so, go as you wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T16:20:06-07:00","id":1212482,"title":"","content":"So, after all this, these are my stances:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Is the Beast a separate entity that is part of the vampiric curse, or is it part of the vampire himself? Is it merely the 'id' to the vampire's 'ego', or is there actually a bestial monster coiled up inside the vampire, waiting to get out?</b><br /> By default, probably the former, but the latter is suggested as an alternative at page 278 of VTR 2e.<br /> <br /> <b>When a vampire enters frenzy, does the Man lose control, does the Beast lose control, or both?</b><br /> By default, probably both. The Man loses control over his Beast, who takes over because it is either in an animalistic rage, or starving, or scared shitless, and acts accordingly. However, you're free to play the Beast as a sentient, cunning, intelligent force if your table is okay with portraying the Beast that way.<br /> <br /> <b>Does the Beast act intelligently during a frenzy? </b><br /> Most likely not, unless you choose to go by the 'Twist: Beast Guides' interpretation of the Beast on page 278 of VTR 2e.<br /> <br /> <b>Is the Beast capable of using Dominate and would it do so? </b><br /> I'd still say yes, the Beast is capable of using Dominate, but unless Dominate is the most direct way for the Beast to get what it wants, it likely wouldn't go that route. It would be a rare occurrence indeed. It might happen during a hunger frenzy, but a rage frenzy? Probably not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T16:21:22-07:00","id":1212483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212478#post1212478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span><br /> <br /> See, now we're getting somewhere. Because I was under the impression that the Beast very much is indeed a second entity inside the vampire's head, in the same way a person with Dissociative Identity Disorder has multiple entities in his head. I guess it's because of what's written on page 278 under 'Frenzy' and 'Twist: The Beast Guides', where it implies that A) every Beast is different and handles situations differently, based on the personality of the vampire, and B) it suggests allowing other players to play your Beast as a sentient, tempting force. That's how I've been playing it ever since I got VTR 2e, mostly because I got sick and tired of the Beast being a dumb animal no smarter than the Hulk.<br /> <br /> So I suppose you could say we're both right and it entirely depends on how you want to portray the Beast! I certainly agree that most of the text you quoted implies that the Beats is a dumb animal, but even the book itself literally suggests to play the Beast as a sentient cunning force.<br /> <br /> I suppose in the end it's up to each gaming table to decide how their Beasts are played out. Both takes on the Beast seem to be supported by the book, but I concur that after re-reading the 2e book, your take on the Beast is probably the default intended way to play the Beast, while my take on the Beats is suggested as a twist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I propose using the Other as an alternate to or along with the Beast. I don\u2019t remember the rules clearly (and thus may be completely wrong here), but IIRC the Other is a much better fit as an Alter-Ego style loss of control than the Berserk style loss of self-control that the Beast typically represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T16:22:22-07:00","id":1212484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212479#post1212479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, that's just your interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literal direct and unambiguous quotations, dude.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The trapped vampire is a perfectly lecit reason for frenzy, at least because, first or after, she will get starved... and frenzy, by raw, does not end until you achieve the goal, that obviously you cannot achieve if you are not able to break the cage. </div> </div> </div>Then you're stuck until daylight, until you beat the bars out of shape, or until you force your way out by mutilating yourself to fit through the gaps. This is within spec for a situation where frenzy is bad news, setting aside that imprisonment is usually going to trigger frenzy <i>long before </i>you're stuck in a cage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can also see a vampire with no physical disciplines and bp 1 (that is not a big boost in frenzy) have to fight against well armed hunter/s or, having as the only way to win, Dominate. </div> </div> </div>You're describing the archetypal cloistered Ventrue in an absolute worst-case scenario, wherein Physical Intensity and innate undead resilience are going to be all they've got to rely on if they've lost their wits. You're not owed an easy way out that far into the failure-state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T18:19:33-07:00","id":1212505,"title":"","content":"The way I read it, Frenzy is<i> supposed</i> to be a bad thing that creates more problems than it solves.<br /> If a panicked, I mean Frenzied creature acted rationally all the time then what would really differentiate this state of mind from the standard? A few dice bonuses and the inability to switch actions?<br /> That doesn't seem like much of a penalty. Does a panicking calf care that there is traffic coming when the coyote is nipping at it's heels or does it flee in the most direct way possible? Does the dehydrated man at sea just die of thirst or does he irrationally drink the sea water when the thirst overwhelms him?<br /> <br /> Frenzy is not meant to be rational, it is pure panic and reckless abandon. Whatever the Man was doing before this point has not worked, so the base impulses of the Beast take over and force the most direct, violent, physical course of action. This is why physical actions get such large bonuses.<br /> From Dictionary.com Frenzy - 1.extreme mental agitation; wild excitement or <i>derangement.</i><br /> Note that derangement can be a lot of things, but it doesn't necessarily mean stupid just like the book says about Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-27-2018, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T18:36:34-07:00","id":1212508,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the impression I\u2019m picking up is that players don\u2019t want options limited while in frenzy. Which is where we transform berserkers into rational berserkers. (Which I do not say as a means of derision, because I saw something in a visual novel or something few years ago that pretty much boils down to that concept, and I liked it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T00:48:01-07:00","id":1212555,"title":"","content":"How would a member of the Circle of the Crone who isn't particularly interested in learning Cruac be treated? Is extensive knowledge of blood sorcery required for anyone who wants to rise in the covenant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23991-bacchicone","name":"BacchicOne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T01:32:43-07:00","id":1212563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BacchicOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212555#post1212555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a member of the Circle of the Crone who isn't particularly interested in learning Cruac be treated? Is extensive knowledge of blood sorcery required for anyone who wants to rise in the covenant?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there's a place for those who don't know it, or much of it. The covenant book really gets into it, but as long as they are earnest about their membership in the covenant they can rise to the top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T01:50:23-07:00","id":1212566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212505#post1212505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I read it, Frenzy is<i> supposed</i> to be a bad thing that creates more problems than it solves.<br /> If a panicked, I mean Frenzied creature acted rationally all the time then what would really differentiate this state of mind from the standard? A few dice bonuses and the inability to switch actions?<br /> That doesn't seem like much of a penalty. Does a panicking calf care that there is traffic coming when the coyote is nipping at it's heels or does it flee in the most direct way possible? Does the dehydrated man at sea just die of thirst or does he irrationally drink the sea water when the thirst overwhelms him?<br /> <br /> Frenzy is not meant to be rational, it is pure panic and reckless abandon. Whatever the Man was doing before this point has not worked, so the base impulses of the Beast take over and force the most direct, violent, physical course of action. This is why physical actions get such large bonuses.<br /> From Dictionary.com Frenzy - 1.extreme mental agitation; wild excitement or <i>derangement.</i><br /> Note that derangement can be a lot of things, but it doesn't necessarily mean stupid just like the book says about Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Frenzy gives more problem than it solves indeed, but not even can we consider it as self-destructive (exactly in the same way as a lonely, starved wolf, wouldn't jump in the middle of an herd of buffalo:<br /> <br /> - Frenzy with a your coterie member means you are gonna feed from him; kill him to death if the frenzy is about angry.<br /> - Starved/angry in presence of your touchstone/lover/family means kills them<br /> - Frenzy in a mall/street means kills everyone, fucking the masquerade<br /> - Frenzy to escape from a danger means using celerity under the sight of everyone, smashing any obstacle and, again, breaking the masquerade<br /> - even if not breaking the masquerade, feeding to death from a mortal, could be a breaking point for most vampire that maybe would like to keep their humanity<br /> - etc. etc.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that, these, are already enough example of how a normal Frenzy is enough savage and problematic.<br /> But still, if the mall/street is full of armed policemen, openly attacking them would be a suicide, so here is where disciplines come to help, isolating one of them in the most direct way possible, feeding/killing him as soon as he would be in a relative safe area, even if full of people. I'm not talking about a patient, rational Beast. Just not a suicidal one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-28-2018, 05:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T03:48:45-07:00","id":1212586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BacchicOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212555#post1212555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a member of the Circle of the Crone who isn't particularly interested in learning Cruac be treated? Is extensive knowledge of blood sorcery required for anyone who wants to rise in the covenant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Due to how extremely decentralised the Circle is it could vary from group to group within the same domain. Some might see proficiency in Cr\u00faac as proof of spiritual exaltment and have that be a requirement for high standing, while other groups might have a single Cr\u00faac practitioner (with an apprentice or two) that carries out a specialised role, and all the others simply don't learn it. I think the Covenant book even mentioned domains where nobody had learned any Cr\u00faac at all.<br /> As for the average domain, I'd say that Cr\u00faac could help get you higher ranking positions, but it's not required and there's no gatekeeping for non-sorcerous members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:07:11-07:00","id":1212739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212566#post1212566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Frenzy gives more problem than it solves indeed, but not even can we consider it as self-destructive (exactly in the same way as a lonely, starved wolf, wouldn't jump in the middle of an herd of buffalo:<br /> <br /> - Frenzy with a your coterie member means you are gonna feed from him; kill him to death if the frenzy is about angry.<br /> - Starved/angry in presence of your touchstone/lover/family means kills them<br /> - Frenzy in a mall/street means kills everyone, fucking the masquerade<br /> - Frenzy to escape from a danger means using celerity under the sight of everyone, smashing any obstacle and, again, breaking the masquerade<br /> - even if not breaking the masquerade, feeding to death from a mortal, could be a breaking point for most vampire that maybe would like to keep their humanity<br /> - etc. etc.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that, these, are already enough example of how a normal Frenzy is enough savage and problematic.<br /> But still, if the mall/street is full of armed policemen, openly attacking them would be a suicide, so here is where disciplines come to help, isolating one of them in the most direct way possible, feeding/killing him as soon as he would be in a relative safe area, even if full of people. I'm not talking about a patient, rational Beast. Just not a suicidal one.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lone starving wolf would indeed go after that herd of buffalo. The herd would run and panic and the wolf would eat whatever it could catch. <br /> <br /> <br /> The armed guards are not going to be all in the same spot at the same time. Maybe one or two in a location at a time. the mall of America is loaded with them, but I never see more than 2 at a time. Lots of people sure. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s not suicide. Attack the one. Drain him dry. Use him like a human shield for the other one. Maybe kill him too when you\u2019re done. You\u2019d have that moment of, \u201coh gods what have I done?!\u201d \u2014 then you run. <br /> But I see this scenario having a major problem. if you\u2019re that close to going into a hunger frenzy why would you go into a mall? Kill frenzy, sure, you have no idea when someone is going to make you snap. But you are not a human you could probably take getting shot 4-5 times and walk away. <br /> <br /> The witnesses would be unreliable at best. But it would cause more problems ... which is why frenzy is something you should be afraid of happening in public places.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh! I had a thought. People who are drowning often panic and accidentally drown the people who are trying to save them because they are in this wild incoherent state. They aren\u2019t stupid but rational thought is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-28-2018, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T17:47:18-07:00","id":1212854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212566#post1212566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Frenzy gives more problem than it solves indeed, but not even can we consider it as self-destructive (exactly in the same way as a lonely, starved wolf, wouldn't jump in the middle of an herd of buffalo:<br /> <br /> - Frenzy with a your coterie member means you are gonna feed from him; kill him to death if the frenzy is about angry.<br /> - Starved/angry in presence of your touchstone/lover/family means kills them<br /> - Frenzy in a mall/street means kills everyone, fucking the masquerade<br /> - Frenzy to escape from a danger means using celerity under the sight of everyone, smashing any obstacle and, again, breaking the masquerade<br /> - even if not breaking the masquerade, feeding to death from a mortal, could be a breaking point for most vampire that maybe would like to keep their humanity<br /> - etc. etc.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that, these, are already enough example of how a normal Frenzy is enough savage and problematic.<br /> But still, if the mall/street is full of armed policemen, openly attacking them would be a suicide, so here is where disciplines come to help, isolating one of them in the most direct way possible, feeding/killing him as soon as he would be in a relative safe area, even if full of people. I'm not talking about a patient, rational Beast. Just not a suicidal one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of this but I do wanna point out that a Beast does never drive a vampire to commit diablerie. I think even drinking from another vampire is not something the beast would do unless you already are addicted to Vitae.<br /> <br /> Diablerie is the one thing both the Man and the Beast hate equally. The Beast probably hates it even more, actually. Comitting diablerie is the surest way to turn your own Beast against you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:00:22-07:00","id":1212861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212854#post1212854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diablerie is the one thing both the Man and the Beast hate equally. The Beast probably hates it even more, actually. Comitting diablerie is the surest way to turn your own Beast against you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an awful lot to get out of &quot;a character in uncontrolled frenzy will not extend the normal immediacy of response to hunger, rage, or fear to the very involved process of <i>drinking a vampire twice-past empty and venting Willpower the character may not even have left</i>.&quot; Diablerie is basically the complete opposite of an impulsive act in circumstances where the victim is someone in a position to put you in frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T18:35:56-07:00","id":1212878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212861#post1212861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an awful lot to get out of &quot;a character in uncontrolled frenzy will not extend the normal immediacy of response to hunger, rage, or fear to the very involved process of <i>drinking a vampire twice-past empty and venting Willpower the character may not even have left</i>.&quot; Diablerie is basically the complete opposite of an impulsive act in circumstances where the victim is someone in a position to put you in frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what you're trying to say here. What I just said is literally mentioned in the book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;You are forbidden from devouring the heartsblood of your Kindred. If you violate this commandment, the Beast calls to your own Blood.&quot;</b><br /> (p. 60, VTR 2e)<br /> Granted, this one can be interpreted as <i>&quot;don't commit diablerie, because it will make the Beast crave for Vitae&quot;</i>. It can also be interpreted as your own Beast turning against you when you commit diablerie. So okay, maybe this quote isn't enough to prove what I said, but:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Normally, a frenzied Beast will not force its host to commit diablerie. However, a vampire riding the wave may choose diablerie as the desire.&quot;</b><br /> (p. 105, VTR 2e)<br /> This one is pretty clear cut and dry though. Clearly diablerie is something even a frenzied Beast wouldn't do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b><br /> <br /> And to add to that: clearly diablerie can be chosen as a goal for a frenzied vampire who's riding the wave, so it's not as &quot;complete opposite of an impulsive act&quot; as you might think. When you look at the game mechanics it seems perhaps something that takes a lot of time, thought and effort, but that's from a mechanical point of view. From a lore point of view, you're basically just sucking on that vampire's wrist until there is nothing left but a hollow corpse. That doesn't sound very complicated to me at all. Sounds pretty straight forward to me, something a frenzied vampire could easily do, or at least attempt (but won't, unless he's riding the wave).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-28-2018, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:29:39-07:00","id":1212906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212878#post1212878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And to add to that: clearly diablerie can be chosen as a goal for a frenzied vampire who's riding the wave, so it's not as &quot;complete opposite of an impulsive act&quot; as you might think. When you look at the game mechanics it seems perhaps something that takes a lot of time, thought and effort, but that's from a mechanical point of view. From a lore point of view, you're basically just sucking on that vampire's wrist until there is nothing left but a hollow corpse. That doesn't sound very complicated to me at all. Sounds pretty straight forward to me, something a frenzied vampire could easily do, or at least attempt (but won't, unless he's riding the wave).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am floored by the fact that you think Diablerie is something so simple. Just drain it dry and boom you have committed Diablerie. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You have to willfully pull the soul from the body at the time it tries to leave. You have to spend a will power and roll a strength + resolve every turn to choose to do this. So not only do you have to drain the vampire dry, you have to fill the lethal box, then go above and beyond that to fill even their aggravated, then above and beyond that you have to fight to swallow down their soul. The fact that you have to spend willpower, means you really really want to get it done. And that it requires resolve is another thing to test your character's desire to get it done. It is not something so &quot;simple as sucking on a wrist&quot; <br /> <br /> <i> To commit diablerie, a vampire must drink from her victim<br /> beyond the point of Final Death. Once a Kindred victim is<br /> completely without Vitae, each point that would otherwise<br /> be taken becomes instead one point of lethal damage. Once<br /> the victim\u2019s Health boxes are full of aggravated damage, the<br /> victim\u2019s very soul struggles against his assailant as he reaches<br /> Final Death<br /> <br /> <br /> Most Kindred will kill a human at some point during<br /> her Requiem, but Amaranth is far more than extinguishing a life:<br /> It\u2019s the willful destruction of a soul\u200b</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:33:27-07:00","id":1212908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212906#post1212906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am floored by the fact that you think Diablerie is something so simple. Just drain it dry and boom you have committed Diablerie. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You have to willfully pull the soul from the body at the time it tries to leave. You have to spend a will power and roll a strength + resolve every turn to choose to do this. So not only do you have to drain the vampire dry, you have to fill the lethal box, then go above and beyond that to fill even their aggravated, then above and beyond that you have to fight to swallow down their soul. The fact that you have to spend willpower, means you really really want to get it done. And that it requires resolve is another thing to test your character's desire to get it done. It is not something so &quot;simple as sucking on a wrist&quot; <br /> <br /> <i> To commit diablerie, a vampire must drink from her victim<br /> beyond the point of Final Death. Once a Kindred victim is<br /> completely without Vitae, each point that would otherwise<br /> be taken becomes instead one point of lethal damage. Once<br /> the victim\u2019s Health boxes are full of aggravated damage, the<br /> victim\u2019s very soul struggles against his assailant as he reaches<br /> Final Death<br /> <br /> <br /> Most Kindred will kill a human at some point during<br /> her Requiem, but Amaranth is far more than extinguishing a life:<br /> It\u2019s the willful destruction of a soul\u200b</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I read all of that before I made my post, I am 100% aware of the rules for diablerie because my Nosferatu character attempted it last week, and I still stand by what I said.<br /> <br /> Diablerie is something a frenzied vampire can do when riding the wave, so it can't be THAT complicated, which is entirely my point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:42:05-07:00","id":1212913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212878#post1212878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>&quot;Normally, a frenzied Beast will not force its host to commit diablerie. However, a vampire riding the wave may choose diablerie as the desire.&quot;</b><br /> (p. 105, VTR 2e)<br /> This one is pretty clear cut and dry though. Clearly diablerie is something even a frenzied Beast wouldn't do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your framing this as some sort of <i>moral backbone</i> to the Beast is where I take issue: <i>a frenzied Beast is a Beast responding to specific stimuli, the vast majority of which will be dealt with long before your character is in a position to inadvertently eat a soul.</i><br /> <br /> Hunger doesn't drive the Beast to go deeper than Vitae, the necessity of torpor means fear will very seldom push a vampire to take a threat into themself, and likewise the narrative beats the Beast runs on make it hard to take much satisfaction in punishing a slight when the adversary can't acknowledge they've been beaten.<br /> <br /> This isn't <i>the Beast has standards</i>, this is <i>the Beast has desires that are met before diablerie falls on its radar and if those needs are met then the Beast doesn't naturally take the wheel</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to add to that: clearly diablerie can be chosen as a goal for a frenzied vampire who's riding the wave, so it's not as &quot;complete opposite of an impulsive act&quot; as you might think. </div> </div> </div>I don't know how else to explain to you the difference between &quot;the idmonster that undeath has blended into your soul gets touchy about certain matters of safety and survival&quot; and &quot;it is possible for you to goad the idmonster that undeath has blended into your soul toward the specific goal of utterly consuming the essence of another vampire.&quot;<br /> <br /> Resisting frenzy is draining, and riding the wave only marginally less so for most Kindred; unless you're dealing with a <i>very</i> weak or weakened vampire, the act of diablerie can easily take half your Willpower if you mix it with a riled-up Beast. The mechanical reason to ride the wave for diablerie is the same reason you ride the wave for any other Strength-based act: it adds your Blood Potency to the roll and that kind of bonus can be fairly substantial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:56:31-07:00","id":1212920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212913#post1212913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't <i>the Beast has standards</i>, this is <i>the Beast has desires that are met before diablerie falls on its radar and if those needs are met then the Beast doesn't naturally take the wheel</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is why a normal frenzy &quot;The beast wont force it's host to commit diablerie&quot; because the conditions are met. If you hunger frenzied you have all the vitae you can have. There isn't any more and diablerie wont help you get it. And if you are in a kill frenzy, your target is dead, deader than dead, super dead. Diablerie wont make them more dead. it wont help your beast complete it's goal. When you ride the wave you have slightly more control over what you do, which is why you can pick diablerie as one of the options. <br /> <br /> You can't accidentally diablerize..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:45:00-07:00","id":1212933,"title":"","content":"While I agree with you that you can't &quot;accidentally&quot; diablerize a vampire, I do disagree with this statement.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; And if you are in a kill frenzy, your target is dead, deader than dead, super dead. Diablerie wont make them more dead. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, vampires can have a piece of wood shoved through their heart, their remains, with that wood still shoved in their heart, placed in a concrete box and buried or tossed in the ocean and be found &quot;not dead&quot; hundreds or thousands of years later. So if that vampire is hated to the point where their utter death/destruction becomes an objective to accomplish in frenzy, there is the argument that the vampire isn't deader than disco until their body crumples to ash in their enemy's hands. And despite all that, diablerie is <b>still</b> not a guarantee since vampires can create soul phylacteries, horcruxes, and use soul/body/mind transferal tactics to cheat the Grim Reaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T22:34:26-07:00","id":1212944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212933#post1212933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with you that you can't &amp;quot;accidentally&amp;quot; diablerize a vampire, I do disagree with this statement.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; And if you are in a kill frenzy, your target is dead, deader than dead, super dead. Diablerie wont make them more dead. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, vampires can have a piece of wood shoved through their heart, their remains, with that wood still shoved in their heart, placed in a concrete box and buried or tossed in the ocean and be found &amp;quot;not dead&amp;quot; hundreds or thousands of years later. So if that vampire is hated to the point where their utter death/destruction becomes an objective to accomplish in frenzy, there is the argument that the vampire isn't deader than disco until their body crumples to ash in their enemy's hands. And despite all that, diablerie is <b>still</b> not a guarantee since vampires can create soul phylacteries, horcruxes, and use soul/body/mind transferal tactics to cheat the Grim Reaper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me if I am wrong but are you saying that you do not die when you are full Aggravated? \u2014diablerie is after that point. <br /> <br /> A stake might not even fill lethal boxes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T05:57:34-07:00","id":1213026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1212944#post1212944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forgive me if I am wrong but are you saying that you do not die when you are full Aggravated? \u2014diablerie is after that point. <br /> <br /> A stake might not even fill lethal boxes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine that. Full aggravated damage not permanently killing someone. It\u2019s not like it\u2019s never happened before... oh wait, yes it does. Remember the time that vampire exsanguinated that woman? Oh yeah, that\u2019s right. She was dealt full aggravated damage but she got up less than a half hour later and started moving around again. And remember that guy who was sodomized and beaten to death during that Acolyte Hunt. They left his corpse for the dogs to eat. You can still see where the dogs tore out his throat.<br /> <br /> So yes, I\u2019m saying that full aggravated damage doesn\u2019t always completely kill something. It happens EVERY time a vampire is created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-29-2018, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:24:35-07:00","id":1213034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1213026#post1213026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine that. Full aggravated damage not permanently killing someone. It\u2019s not like it\u2019s never happened before... oh wait, yes it does. Remember the time that vampire exsanguinated that woman? Oh yeah, that\u2019s right. She was dealt full aggravated damage but she got up less than a half hour later and started moving around again. And remember that guy who was sodomized and beaten to death during that Acolyte Hunt. They left his corpse for the dogs to eat. You can still see where the dogs tore out his throat.<br /> <br /> So yes, I\u2019m saying that full aggravated damage doesn\u2019t always completely kill something. It happens EVERY time a vampire is created.</div> </div> </div> </div>First I am not talking about a mortal at full aggravated... I was talking about a vampire at full aggravated.<br /> <br /> Second, no a mortal does not have to go full aggravated to turn into a vampire. You drain them of all their blood. That\u2019s what it says. There is no damage requirement at all. There are only two things stated to make a vampire, drain them dry and give them vitae.<br /> <br /> <i>The sire drains a mortal completely of his lifeblood, then feeds him a bit of her own Vitae to rouse him back to the land of the living.<br /> It\u2019s just two things:<br /> Bite the mortal.<br /> Feed his corpse. <b> Pg 93</b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> Third, it does say a vampire at full aggravated hits final death. Not sure why there is question about that ....<br /> <br /> <i>&quot; When her last box is marked with aggravated damage, she suffers Final Death&quot; <b>Pg 90</b><br /> &quot;Final Death: A Kindred\u2019s real, true, ultimate death; when her Requiem ceases and she never again rises as a vampire.&quot;</i><b>Pg74</b> ( or how I put it. Dead, deader then dead, super dead. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":".  EDIT to put book references in 04-29-2018, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T06:36:00-07:00","id":1213038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1213026#post1213026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yes, I\u2019m saying that full aggravated damage doesn\u2019t always completely kill something. It happens EVERY time a vampire is created.</div> </div> </div> </div>And <i>after</i> that happens, taking full agg sets your body rotting. Kindred don't have the option of a second Embrace to save their skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:42:14-07:00","id":1213070,"title":"","content":"Guys lets be honest at this point we are just arguing semantics and interpretations. We all agree on the actual written rules (that a Beast won't force a vampire to diablerie, unless that vampire chooses that goal while Riding the Wave), we just have different interpretations of how those rules play out on the screen. That's fine, but it's not really a discussion I'm interested in having.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-29-2018, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T02:53:37-07:00","id":1213368,"title":"","content":"Question:<br /> <br /> Does anyone know if there is any merit somewhere in any book that would allow for a vampire to have multiple masks and/or multiple dirges, like the Virtuous and Vice-ridden merits for mortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T03:34:00-07:00","id":1213369,"title":"","content":"No, but if you're not averse to house rules you could just adapt Virtuous/Vice-Ridden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T07:34:09-07:00","id":1213424,"title":"","content":"Or, if you're feeling more adventurous, you could straight up use Vice-Ridden, granting the vampire a Vice in addition to their Mask and Dirge (complete with the Breaking Point modifier if acting in accordance with the Vice).<br /> Perhaps the Kindred took their Vice with them into undeath, or (which I would find more interesting) it's the Kindred's beast that exercises a rare influence upon her. If the latter, maybe it is drawn towards acting out the Vice in Frenzy (as long as doing so wouldn't be counterproductive to the stated goal of the Frenzy) and/or it has the curious side effect of the Kindred's eyes gleaming faintly yellow during fitting moments (such as fulfilling the Vice, entering Frenzy, achieving the goal of a Frenzy, committing diablerie, et cetera).<br /> I know that you specifically asked about multiple Masks and Dirges but I really got into the idea of a vampire having a Vice, with all the implications that brings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-30-2018, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:50:39-07:00","id":1213467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1213368#post1213368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question:<br /> Does anyone know if there is any merit somewhere in any book that would allow for a vampire to have multiple masks and/or multiple dirges, like the Virtuous and Vice-ridden merits for mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one, but it\u2019s very specific - you need Invictus Status or City Status 3+ and hold a position of power in the domain Invictus or the city, and it allows you to treat that position as an additional Mask. It\u2019s called Oath of Office, it\u2019s from Secrets of the Covenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:44:20-07:00","id":1213577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1213467#post1213467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one, but it\u2019s very specific - you need Invictus Status or City Status 3+ and hold a position of power in the domain Invictus or the city, and it allows you to treat that position as an additional Mask. It\u2019s called Oath of Office, it\u2019s from Secrets of the Covenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes I knew about that one but forgot about it. Thanks for reminding me. It's not exactly what I was looking for but still, appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T17:04:47-07:00","id":1213595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1213577#post1213577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yes I knew about that one but forgot about it. Thanks for reminding me. It's not exactly what I was looking for but still, appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I figured it was a little narrower than what you were looking for, but just mentioned it for thoroughness\u2019 sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T12:04:32-07:00","id":1215869,"title":"","content":"Question about Psychic Vampires from the Hurt Locker book (page 101 - 103):<br /> <br /> It says:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;By and large, Psychic Vampirism works on most things in the Chronicles of Darkness. However, a psychic vampire cannot steal the life energy of an actual vampire. She can steal Willpower if her Psychic Vampirism Merit is strong enough. Psychic vampires cannot steal the life of ghosts or spirits, unless they have the Soul Eater Merit. Using psychic vampirism on supernatural creatures is slightly tougher; subtract their Supernatural Potency trait (Blood Potency, Gnosis, Primal Urge, etc.) from the roll to activate the power.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The first dot of this Merit says:<br /> <br /> <i>Amateur (\u2022):<br /> With this basic level, your character can cause bashing damage. She causes one bashing damage per success on her roll. Every two points of bashing damage gives her one Ephemera (this can be accumulated over multiple turns). She can use one Ephemera to heal a point of bashing damage, or two Ephemera to heal one lethal damage.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The other dots basically just built on to that, but my question is this:<br /> <br /> Can a Psychic Vampire still use his/her powers to damage Kindred? Or is that tied to the stealing life energy, meaning that damaging the Kindred doesn't work either?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 05-06-2018, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T13:24:11-07:00","id":1215882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1215869#post1215869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Psychic Vampires from the Hurt Locker book (page 101 - 103):<br /> <br /> It says:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;By and large, Psychic Vampirism works on most things in the Chronicles of Darkness. However, a psychic vampire cannot steal the life energy of an actual vampire. She can steal Willpower if her Psychic Vampirism Merit is strong enough. Psychic vampires cannot steal the life of ghosts or spirits, unless they have the Soul Eater Merit. Using psychic vampirism on supernatural creatures is slightly tougher; subtract their Supernatural Potency trait (Blood Potency, Gnosis, Primal Urge, etc.) from the roll to activate the power.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The first dot of this Merit says:<br /> <br /> <i>Amateur (\u2022):<br /> With this basic level, your character can cause bashing damage. She causes one bashing damage per success on her roll. Every two points of bashing damage gives her one Ephemera (this can be accumulated over multiple turns). She can use one Ephemera to heal a point of bashing damage, or two Ephemera to heal one lethal damage.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The other dots basically just built on to that, but my question is this:<br /> <br /> Can a Psychic Vampire still use his/her powers to damage Kindred? Or is that tied to the stealing life energy, meaning that damaging the Kindred doesn't work either?</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't work<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:18:03-07:00","id":1215893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1215882#post1215882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't work</div> </div> </div> </div>Care to elaborate? Because the people at my table seem to think it should work, while I personally lean more on the side that it shouldn't work, but it's unclear to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:29:27-07:00","id":1215898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1215893#post1215893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Care to elaborate? Because the people at my table seem to think it should work, while I personally lean more on the side that it shouldn't work, but it's unclear to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It works by stealing life energy, and as that sidebar says, they can't do that to Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T17:31:29-07:00","id":1217205,"title":"","content":"Question:<br /> <br /> Is there a Dominate power or perhaps something else that would allow a vampire to switch bodies with someone? For example, would it be possible with some kind of Devotion relating to Dominate or something to possess a person and then have that person who's possessed temporarily take your body, effectively swapping bodies for a while?<br /> <br /> Does something like that already exist in one of the books and if not, do you think this would fall into the realm of Devotions if I want to homebrew it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T17:42:21-07:00","id":1217206,"title":"","content":"I believe Asnam is the name of a Daeva bloodline that does something similar. I don't remember where I saw them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T20:00:24-07:00","id":1217250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1217205#post1217205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question:<br /> <br /> Is there a Dominate power or perhaps something else that would allow a vampire to switch bodies with someone? For example, would it be possible with some kind of Devotion relating to Dominate or something to possess a person and then have that person who's possessed temporarily take your body, effectively swapping bodies for a while?<br /> <br /> Does something like that already exist in one of the books and if not, do you think this would fall into the realm of Devotions if I want to homebrew it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean like the Freaky Friday plot where characters switch bodies, no there's not currently anything. Rathamus mentions the Asnam bloodline, their signature discipline is a Majesty offshoot where they can, at different levels, use their followers as havens, willpower and vitae cookie jars with the apex power of turning a newborn baby into a phylactery that the Asnam will subsume if they meet Final Death, killing the other person instead. They're in the Circle of the Crone covenant book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T13:56:22-07:00","id":1217768,"title":"","content":"A thing i do in my games is have my players select an aspiration that comes from their beast. Essentially something that the beast wants and it always ends up as a breaking point. i call it a dark aspiration.<br /> <br /> So the thing is one of my players cant think of something. The other problem is that i cant think of anything either. So i am asking here if anyone has an idea. <br /> Usually the personality of the beast is influences by what banes the character has (clan banes and others) and what disciplines (and at what level) the character has. For example a character with a lot of Dominate will end up with a beast that is domineering.<br /> <br /> In this case the player is a Gangrel with 1 dot of animalism and Resilience and 2 dot of protean. <br /> As for the character he was orphaned with his little sister and made a group of street kids for protection. As a vampire he has expanded the street kid network to control several groups that he use for information (contact) and minor help (allies for delivering messages of doing small distractions). <br /> <br /> I get the feeling that the beast would want something in regard to the street kids/orphans group and as a gangrel it would be animalistic, feral and physical. <br /> But i cant seem to find something interesting. <br /> I also dont want to go too far and have something like ''wants to form the street kids into a cannibal cults that hunt with him''. Since he has 7 humanity something that would ... slide subtly towards that kind of thing would be better.<br /> <br /> If anyone can think of something it would be much appreciated. <br /> thank you<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T14:02:11-07:00","id":1217770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1217768#post1217768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing i do in my games is have my players select an aspiration that comes from their beast. Essentially something that the beast wants and it always ends up as a breaking point. i call it a dark aspiration.<br /> <br /> So the thing is one of my players cant think of something. The other problem is that i cant think of anything either. So i am asking here if anyone has an idea.<br /> Usually the personality of the beast is influences by what banes the character has (clan banes and others) and what disciplines (and at what level) the character has. For example a character with a lot of Dominate will end up with a beast that is domineering.<br /> <br /> In this case the player is a Gangrel with 1 dot of animalism and Resilience and 2 dot of protean.<br /> As for the character he was orphaned with his little sister and made a group of street kids for protection. As a vampire he has expanded the street kid network to control several groups that he use for information (contact) and minor help (allies for delivering messages of doing small distractions).<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that the beast would want something in regard to the street kids/orphans group and as a gangrel it would be animalistic, feral and physical.<br /> But i cant seem to find something interesting.<br /> I also dont want to go too far and have something like ''wants to form the street kids into a cannibal cults that hunt with him''. Since he has 7 humanity something that would ... slide subtly towards that kind of thing would be better.<br /> <br /> If anyone can think of something it would be much appreciated.<br /> thank you</div> </div> </div> </div>Procreation is a pretty primal motive, maybe the beast wants a childe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T16:52:47-07:00","id":1217824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1217768#post1217768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anyone can think of something it would be much appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a cool idea.<br /> <br /> Pitch 1: The beast wants to terrorize the children while in the guise of a bestial human, to better teach them the fear of predators and strangers they will need to survive in the world. Resilience grants the beast capabilities to soak any damage from those who fight back, Animalism allows control over which animal is being used for inspiration, Protean is used to manifest aspects of that chosen animal. <br /> <br /> Pitch 2: It actively wants to protect the 'territories' of the Children, ruthlessly preying upon any competitors or threats to the group who get too close.<br /> <br /> Pitch 3: If you want to go fully antagonistic, it is threatened by children growing up, and seeks to prey upon, destroy, or dominate a child on the threshold of adulthood. (Or for a less one-sided struggle, pit a favored animal against the chosen victim.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:51:30-07:00","id":1218409,"title":"","content":"Question about Dhampir...<br /> Can they buy Covenant merits if they have status?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus","name":"Raktus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T07:45:27-07:00","id":1218533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1217770#post1217770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Procreation is a pretty primal motive, maybe the beast wants a childe?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1217824#post1217824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pitch 1: The beast wants to terrorize the children while in the guise of a bestial human, to better teach them the fear of predators and strangers they will need to survive in the world. Resilience grants the beast capabilities to soak any damage from those who fight back, Animalism allows control over which animal is being used for inspiration, Protean is used to manifest aspects of that chosen animal.<br /> <br /> Pitch 2: It actively wants to protect the 'territories' of the Children, ruthlessly preying upon any competitors or threats to the group who get too close.<br /> <br /> Pitch 3: If you want to go fully antagonistic, it is threatened by children growing up, and seeks to prey upon, destroy, or dominate a child on the threshold of adulthood. (Or for a less one-sided struggle, pit a favored animal against the chosen victim.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Really like those ideas thx.<br /> I'll run them by my player see if one them strikes the right chord.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:07:54-07:00","id":1218544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1217768#post1217768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thing i do in my games is have my players select an aspiration that comes from their beast. Essentially something that the beast wants and it always ends up as a breaking point. i call it a dark aspiration.<br /> <br /> So the thing is one of my players cant think of something. The other problem is that i cant think of anything either. So i am asking here if anyone has an idea.<br /> Usually the personality of the beast is influences by what banes the character has (clan banes and others) and what disciplines (and at what level) the character has. For example a character with a lot of Dominate will end up with a beast that is domineering.<br /> <br /> In this case the player is a Gangrel with 1 dot of animalism and Resilience and 2 dot of protean.<br /> As for the character he was orphaned with his little sister and made a group of street kids for protection. As a vampire he has expanded the street kid network to control several groups that he use for information (contact) and minor help (allies for delivering messages of doing small distractions).<br /> <br /> I get the feeling that the beast would want something in regard to the street kids/orphans group and as a gangrel it would be animalistic, feral and physical.<br /> But i cant seem to find something interesting.<br /> I also dont want to go too far and have something like ''wants to form the street kids into a cannibal cults that hunt with him''. Since he has 7 humanity something that would ... slide subtly towards that kind of thing would be better.<br /> <br /> If anyone can think of something it would be much appreciated.<br /> thank you</div> </div> </div> </div>I would link the 'dark aspiration' to the character's Dirge. Or make all your players choose Virtues and Vices (like most mortal characters would do), not to replace Mask and Dirge, but in addition to Mask and Dirge. Then use their chosen Vice to come up with an idea for what the Beast wants.<br /> <br /> I really like your idea though. 'Dark aspirations', very nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T11:09:06-07:00","id":1218618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raktus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1218409#post1218409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Dhampir...<br /> Can they buy Covenant merits if they have status?</div> </div> </div> </div>From reading p.113 and 123 of VtR 2nd I don't see why not. The hurdle is that dot of Covenant status. Once achieved, many more doors open. That said, the Covenants are likely to be wary of a Dhampir acting among them in anything but the most deferential and circumspect manner. <br /> <br /> Similarly, a Ghoul might acquire Covenant status, but will still be a Ghoul and second-class in virtually every respect.<br /> <br /> The status Merit reflects establishing your personal value to the group in a way that is sufficiently widespread and unchallenged such that you are considered a reliable and trusted asset/member. How you <i>get</i> to that point is the crux of the story.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T15:52:58-07:00","id":1218710,"title":"","content":"Hopefully I'm not derailing by asking a simple question. <br /> <br /> I seem to recall in some edition of Masquerade or maybe even nWOD Requiem, vitae would heal mortals, but that does not seem to be the case in Requiem 2E. <br /> <br /> Do kindred have no means to heal those mortals/animals they drink from beyond the mundane elements of time and medical care?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24230-maddasher","name":"MadDasher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T17:16:35-07:00","id":1218738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadDasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1218710#post1218710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully I'm not derailing by asking a simple question. <br /> <br /> I seem to recall in some edition of Masquerade or maybe even nWOD Requiem, vitae would heal mortals, but that does not seem to be the case in Requiem 2E. <br /> <br /> Do kindred have no means to heal those mortals/animals they drink from beyond the mundane elements of time and medical care?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I am aware, the only healing properties that vitae is capable of normally is when ghouls or vampires spend vitae to heal. Otherwise, there is that one scale that lets a Kindred heal aggravated as if it were lethal (I think it affects mortals as well).<br /> <br /> But otherwise, I honestly can't think of one outside or that. I don't think it's a usual theme in vampire that you heal what you hurt (based off experience and reading).<br /> <br /> I could see room for some obscure bloodline capable of healing people though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T17:24:25-07:00","id":1218740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MadDasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1218710#post1218710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully I'm not derailing by asking a simple question.<br /> <br /> I seem to recall in some edition of Masquerade or maybe even nWOD Requiem, vitae would heal mortals, but that does not seem to be the case in Requiem 2E.<br /> <br /> Do kindred have no means to heal those mortals/animals they drink from beyond the mundane elements of time and medical care?</div> </div> </div> </div>No edition allowed vitae to heal without the mortal first imbibing it and becoming ghouled. They could then use that blood to heal themselves. In Masq and maybe requiem too (not sure) vampires could also lick wounds caused from bites to heal them. There has never been a situation (bar some odd thaum ritual or devotion i havnt read) where you could drip vitae on a mortal and heal them as far as im aware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T18:46:14-07:00","id":1218759,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23776\" data-vbnamecard=\"23776\">Raktus</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> <br /> <br /> Dhampir can gain Covenant Status merits (although that is a rare thing indeed according to most of the fluff in the book Half-Damned, for example the Ordo Dracul fluff found on page 17) so I would assume dhampir can also gain merits that have Covenant Status as a prerequisite. <br /> <br /> Dhampir can <b>not</b> however learn Coils or Scales of the Dragon (also found on page 17 of Half-Damned). Same goes for Theban Sorcery and Cruac. Only true vampires can learn those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T19:07:49-07:00","id":1218766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1218759#post1218759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23776-raktus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23776\" data-vbnamecard=\"23776\">Raktus</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a><br /> <br /> Dhampir can gain Covenant Status merits (although that is a rare thing indeed according to most of the fluff in the book Half-Damned, for example the Ordo Dracul fluff found on page 17) so I would assume dhampir can also gain merits that have Covenant Status as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> Dhampir can <b>not</b> however learn Coils or Scales of the Dragon (also found on page 17 of Half-Damned). Same goes for Theban Sorcery and Cruac. Only true vampires can learn those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can learn Cruac with a special merit (Mother's Army Recruit at 3), though it's expensive for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T19:16:54-07:00","id":1218768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1218766#post1218766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can learn Cruac with a special merit (Mother's Army Recruit at 3), though it's expensive for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah cool, I haven't seen that Merit (or I have and glossed over it). Which book can I find it in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T22:43:09-07:00","id":1218811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1218768#post1218768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah cool, I haven't seen that Merit (or I have and glossed over it). Which book can I find it in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Half-Damned","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T02:25:48-07:00","id":1220212,"title":"","content":"We are running a game in 1100 a.D. Costantinopoli setting. A player of mine, ex soldier of the Roman empire, wants now to have a personal group of soldiers (5 guards), always with him, possibly Ghouls and above the average.<br /> I'm here asking to you for some advice on how to rule/play this.<br /> <br /> 1) Is there a merit to represent this or should be it just played ghouling some soldiers?<br /> <br /> 2) What could the consequences be to go around the city with armed and armored soldiers, not anymore belonging to the city army?<br /> <br /> Since he has taken the merit realted to the shield uses (don't remember the name at the moment), that gives huge advantages fighting in a group with other shield equipped mates, I would like to avoid the awkard situation in which the only way he can be in any physical difficulty would be against other vampires with particular and strong disciplines (like animalism 4 or majesty 5), not paying a right price (either in term of roleplay or PX). So what is supposed to be the right price for this? <br /> <br /> Any advice on how to deal with this and any possible and smart drawback would be very appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T05:36:11-07:00","id":1220232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1220212#post1220212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Is there a merit to represent this or should be it just played ghouling some soldiers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Retainer works best for competent minions, but if he wants five of them it'll be costly. If you think it's too costly you could alleviate it with a home brew Merit tagged to an existing Retainer that represents having multiple retainers, but they must all share the same field.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1220212#post1220212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) What could the consequences be to go around the city with armed and armored soldiers, not anymore belonging to the city army?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately I don't know how acceptable it was for nobles to have private armies at the time. Armed guards of some sort were most likely acceptable, but uniformed soldiers could either be just showing off that you have armed guards (with whatever social implications that might have) or be interpreted as rebellious intentions (somewhat helped by the fact that there's only five of them) in case it's not socially acceptable. You'd have to ask a historian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T06:28:56-07:00","id":1220242,"title":"","content":"People weren't allowed to walk around the city or village proper armored and carrying shields, swords and spears etc. Cultural norms frowned upon Roman citizens walking around carrying weapons and &quot;farming utensils&quot; like a barbarian and it was also against the law. (In Rome itself it was sacrilege.) Nor could you walk around with a private armed and armored retinue. However, the further away you got from major urban centers, enforcement became less rigid, it tended to revert to regional customs and the practicalities of existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-19-2018, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T07:13:10-07:00","id":1220248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1220242#post1220242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People weren't allowed to walk around the city or village proper armored and carrying shields, swords and spears etc. Cultural norms frowned upon Roman citizens walking around carrying weapons and &quot;farming utensils&quot; like a barbarian and it was also against the law. (In Rome itself it was sacrilege.) Nor could you walk around with a private armed and armored retinue. However, the further away you got from major urban centers, enforcement became less rigid, it tended to revert to regional customs and the practicalities of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a kind of what I was supposing. Thanks<br /> <br /> Other question not related to this topic:<br /> <br /> Is &quot;what is his deepest secret&quot; a lecit Auspex 2/3 question? Or should it be more specific?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering about this since it seems a way too powerful but, a sample question is exactly as much generic as this: what is one of this person's psycological vulenrability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T08:49:12-07:00","id":1220258,"title":"","content":"For level 2, no. For level 3, it would need to be more specific. Deepest secret could be the one he\u2019s consciously kept about himself the longest. Or about someone else. It could be something that\u2019s been hidden via Dominate to avoid even Auspex prying and can\u2019t actually be retrieved without a devotion. Asking a person\u2019s psychological vulnerability is actually very specific.<br /> <br /> Remember, I don\u2019t allow gratuitous fishing expeditions for anything and every detail using Auspex. It has to be specific or something the victim fears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-19-2018, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T08:54:26-07:00","id":1220260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1220258#post1220258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For level 2, no. For level 3, it would need to be more specific. Deepest secret could be the one he\u2019s consciously kept about himself the longest. Or about someone else. It could be something that\u2019s been hidden via Dominate to avoid even Auspex prying and can\u2019t actually be retrieved without a devotion. Asking a person\u2019s psychological vulnerability is actually very specific.<br /> <br /> Remember, I don\u2019t allow gratuitous fishing expeditions for anything and every detail using Auspex. It has to be specific or something the victim fears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not for auspex 2? <br /> Anyway, what could a lecit question be in this case? If you would like to uncover a secret with which to leverage him in example.<br /> <br /> EDIT: is asking for the place where the target lie during the day a valid qiuestion? Should the answer just give a generic place (like showing the furniture in the heaven) or making the Auspex user perfectly aware on how to reach the heaven?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 05-19-2018, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T10:56:58-07:00","id":1220281,"title":"","content":"I think it's a legitimate auspex Question. It has several examples that just get you some random weaknesses to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T11:00:42-07:00","id":1220283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1220212#post1220212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) What could the consequences be to go around the city with armed and armored soldiers, not anymore belonging to the city army?</div> </div> </div> </div>Romans required their soldiers to actually purchase their armor and arms, and they could still be used indefinitely (because let's be honest: they weren't full auto assault rifles). As for drawbacks, lack of anonymity comes to mind. People will remember the guy walking around with five armored bodyguards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T14:37:19-07:00","id":1220628,"title":"","content":"<i><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Enticing (\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Cannot have the Atrocious or Cutthroat Merits<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your character\u2019s seductive Beast oozes with ease and<br /> confidence. Her smoky looks tantalize the imagination. Every<br /> movement of her hands makes promises. Any rolls to invoke<br /> the seductive Beast gain the 8-again quality.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Your character does not get the 10-again quality on<br /> any rolls to invoke or resist the monstrous or competitive Beasts.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Can someone explain to me how this merit works? Or if you really wanna help me, explain to me what exactly I get to roll in these 4 example situations while having the Enticing merit:<br /> <br /> 1. I'm te agressor, I use the Seductive Beast, and the opponent responds with the Monstrous Beast.<br /> 2. I'm the defender, I get challenged by someone with the Monstrous Beast, and I respond with the Seductive Beast.<br /> 3. I am the agressor, I use the Seductive Beast, and the opponent responds with the Seductive Beast.<br /> 4. I'm the defender, I get challenged by someone with the Seductive Beast, and I respond with the Seductive Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 05-20-2018, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T14:53:49-07:00","id":1220629,"title":"","content":"It would not surprise me if the wording in the drawback (&quot;invoke or resist&quot;) is an artefact from earlier in the writing process where you had to respond with the same beast. I recommend completely ignoring it and just have all rolls your character makes with the seductive Beast (regardless of what aspect your opponent uses) gain 8-again, and all rolls your character makes with either of the other two aspects lose 10-again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T15:46:10-07:00","id":1220638,"title":"","content":"If you buy Enticing, you lose 10 again to use Monstrous or Competitive and you cant buy the other merits that give 8 again to the other two aura formats.<br /> <br /> If it's Predator Aura vs Predator Aura, there's no resist check per se. It's pres vs str or int. <br /> If for some reason your character can't use Seductive Beast, (such as someone successfully lashing out to break Awe) and you can't do your Dance of the Seven Veils because you can't see them or it could cause other complications, effectively reducing you to turning it Competitive (trying to find them). You lose 10 again. It could also be a matter of your ST saying certain response methods might not be appropriate. (Ie. Someone lashes out using Monstrous aura by yanking you out of your seat and bouncing your head on the table. Grabbing your crotch suggestively (Seductive) or calling them a mouth breathing gorilla (Competitive) may not be appropriate responses. So they get relegated as attempts to be Monstrous. No 8 again. <br /> One ST I game with says if someone lashes out to break your discipline effect, you have to lash back in the same manner they used to try and break your effect. So you may not get to use your merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T16:24:49-07:00","id":1220648,"title":"","content":"does a revenents blood count as kindred for feeding Requirements? If so, it would really hurt the fluff for 2 bloodlines from 1st edition that revolved around not inducing the viniculam and being seen as tasty snacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T04:04:44-07:00","id":1220779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1220648#post1220648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does a revenents blood count as kindred for feeding Requirements? If so, it would really hurt the fluff for 2 bloodlines from 1st edition that revolved around not inducing the viniculam and being seen as tasty snacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes revenant vitae counts as kindred vitae for those needing kindred vitae for sustenance.<br /> <br /> Yes those bloodlines could still exist in your setting and be viewed as edible commodities. And in the case of Les Gens Libres, a potential threat to the status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T06:34:38-07:00","id":1220814,"title":"","content":"Revenants and their feeding requirements/habits are viewed as such an unsustainable problem in most domains that farming them for your feeding issues (over, say, the accepted practice of Torpor) would be looked on as a major problem. (This makes for a great plotline into which PCs may be entangled, btw.)<br /> <br /> As a result, you won't have (many) vamps out there attempting to replicate revenants. Bloodlines of tasty snacks, OTOH, <b><i>are</i></b> desirable to replicate. Ditto if you find mortals of unusual and vital flavor. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T06:41:50-07:00","id":1220815,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, if you have a captured revenant you could probably come up with a creative solution to let it feed on mortals you've brought, and you feed from the revenant in turn. There are some problems that needs to be overcome, but I don't think they're impossible for a BP6+ vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T07:14:45-07:00","id":1220824,"title":"","content":"Purchase a KFC or Popeye's franchise, a farm with lots of chickens, and get three revenants. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-21-2018, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T07:54:21-07:00","id":1220834,"title":"","content":"That could work.who cares that human blood tastes better. it will still sustain them.<br /> <br /> THe Kallisti...from the invictus book would be more dangerous as theiir disciplines could subvert a blood bond.<br /> <br /> I would like to see one blood bound to an elder kept as a slave called a 'concubine' dispargingly. fuming and plotting her escape.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T08:41:28-07:00","id":1220850,"title":"","content":"Who said anything about them not feeding off humans? The chickens are there to prevent the revenant from killing a human every night. And you may as well make some money off the mess as well. And it makes you look like a &quot;humanitarian&quot; to protect the humans and the revenant's Humanity score. Even if you're only doing it because you don't want to be troubled with creating a mass grave.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T13:04:27-07:00","id":1220911,"title":"","content":"oh is their any drawback in trying to take one of Les Gens Libres as a slave via the viniculam or the conditioning devotion or Majesty? I see the problem with the Kallisti, but not with Les Gens Libres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T17:59:40-07:00","id":1221012,"title":"","content":"Uh yeah. Several. You need to know a specific ritual and some vitae from one of the progenitors of the line to find them, (they\u2019re supposed to be undetectable without the ritual) they get devotions to temporarily break vinculums and make themselves highly resistant to mind control.<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re using some of the 2nd edition conversions I\u2019ve seen for them, they\u2019re also immune to being blood bound as their bloodline gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-21-2018, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T05:34:35-07:00","id":1221132,"title":"","content":"oh on Dhampirs tried making a thread on this... it say's a dhampir child can rule the school if he wants, was looking over their powers how would he go about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T06:37:43-07:00","id":1221142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221132#post1221132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh on Dhampirs tried making a thread on this... it say's a dhampir child can rule the school if he wants, was looking over their powers how would he go about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you be much more specific with your question? Dhampir get fate-related powers and if they're hanging with schoolmates of similar young age and have a clue what they are they'll be an (un)holy terror to cross. <br /> <br /> I suspect you're using slang, however....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T06:59:01-07:00","id":1221145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221142#post1221142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you be much more specific with your question? Dhampir get fate-related powers and if they're hanging with schoolmates of similar young age and have a clue what they are they'll be an (un)holy terror to cross.<br /> <br /> I suspect you're using slang, however....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>would like ideas how to effectively uae their powers.<br /> <br /> as none of the powers wowed me that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-22-2018, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T16:11:23-07:00","id":1221565,"title":"","content":"Question - Safest way for a vampire to approach and speak with a Hunter without giving self away? Disciplines not to use? Bring a ghoul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T17:01:08-07:00","id":1221577,"title":"","content":"Poessesion would probaly be the very best way to do so in safety, thus even if the hunters kill him your body will be safe, like you care about a random mortal off the street!<br /> <br /> Another way is Surgical heart removal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T18:34:31-07:00","id":1221587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221565#post1221565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question - Safest way for a vampire to approach and speak with a Hunter without giving self away? Disciplines not to use? Bring a ghoul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will depend heavily on your Humanity, the focus of the hunter in question, the reason for the meeting, the meaning of &quot;giving yourself away,&quot; and the timeframe you have to work with. Assuming you're specifically aiming to keep a lid on the fangs and assuming neither immediate nor inessential levels of urgency\u2026<br /> <br /> Are you a calloused elder with an ashen complexion and a dim grasp of social mores, and drawing from Lordly stock besides? Use a go-between who knows how to broach the topic at hand and delegate from there.<br /> <br /> Are you a fresh young neonate Shadow who's still keeping up with the times and paid religious attention to vampiric best practices? Going in person with the Blush and a beginner's grasp of Obfuscate should do you right as long as you keep the ball rolling in the right direction.<br /> <br /> Are you a Serpent who's been around the block and kept up appearances around town for sixty years? Make sure your tracks are covered, throw together a pseudonym, and arrange the meeting through a soon-to-be-mutual acquaintance in a moderately comfortable environment.<br /> <br /> We may need more information to go off of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221577#post1221577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poessesion would probaly be the very best way to do so in safety, thus even if the hunters kill him your body will be safe, like you care about a random mortal off the street!</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though the capstone power of a clan-specific Discipline in the expectation that discovery will result in murder is both not useful general advice for this scenario and presupposing the failure of its explicit purpose \u2014 &quot;Hunters might murder you for being a vampire&quot; is a thing that is presumably already accounted for in the question of &quot;How do I approach a hunter as a vampire without giving myself away?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T19:22:02-07:00","id":1221596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221587#post1221587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though the capstone power of a clan-specific Discipline in the expectation that discovery will result in murder is both not useful general advice for this scenario and presupposing the failure of its explicit purpose \u2014 &quot;Hunters might murder you for being a vampire&quot; is a thing that is presumably already accounted for in the question of &quot;How do I approach a hunter as a vampire without giving myself away?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>your right sorry. was Trying to show the safest way to go about it.<br /> <br /> but your ideas are all good to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T03:33:13-07:00","id":1221644,"title":"","content":"Okay I'm planning to read the Covenant books to have a better grasp of the philosophies of the Covenants because while Secrets were fun it left things too open ended. Just asking but because there have been changes between covenants from 1e to 2e is there any paticualar fluff in the books I should ignore as it no longer matters for the 2e interpretation of the Covenants? Actually it's probably too much to ask the question to all of them, sorry about that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 05-24-2018, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T04:10:14-07:00","id":1221646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221644#post1221644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I'm planning to read the Covenant books to have a better grasp of the philosophies of the Covenants because while Secrets were fun it ledt things to open ended. Just asking but because there have been changes between covenants from 1e to 2e is there any paticualar fluff in the books I should ignore as it no longer matters for the 2e interpretation of the Covenants? Actually it's probably to much to ask the question to all of them, sorry about that</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I, myself and my table sees the 1ed Covenant books as a complement to 2ed. There is not much information of the 2ed Covenants out there. Secrets is a good book, sure but it lacks information about them. The books are inspirational when it comes to information and how to present the workings, ideas etc of the Covenants, but some things are surely way different. The Invictus for instance are really archaic and aristocratic in first ed and quite anachronistic and reactionary to a fault. I see this as the old European guard, still there at a few places but more modern in most places, more 2ed if you will. I love all the covenant books except the CoC book ( but then I don't like the CoC at all and find they don't fit much at all in the setting) and use them to fill the gaps, and usually they present some good points and foundation you can build on together from what you get from 2ed. Like the Dragons are really not the same without their secret codes, handshakes and elaborate titles, or an explanation of what a Chrysalis is, and L&amp;S is just sin-eating Judas-christians without their religion and theology to base their views. The Chartian book is perhaps not that great and it misses much of the workings of the covenant imho but it ain't plainly apologistic and lacking cohesion like the CoC-book. Although the 2ed CoC is way better then 1ed, I think 2ed CoC and 1ed book are the one that changed the most and has the least amount of useful material to export from 1ed to 2ed. And that's with bias aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T06:23:09-07:00","id":1221682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221644#post1221644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I'm planning to read the Covenant books to have a better grasp of the philosophies of the Covenants because while Secrets were fun it left things too open ended. Just asking but because there have been changes between covenants from 1e to 2e is there any paticualar fluff in the books I should ignore as it no longer matters for the 2e interpretation of the Covenants? Actually it's probably too much to ask the question to all of them, sorry about that</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there's been significant thematic changes to most of the covenants.<br /> The Invictus went from wanting to be the top of the heap by maintaining a feudalism style of government that bordered on anachronistic to being content as &quot;advisors&quot; to another covenant in power. They don't have any unique covenant advantages, just a demi-magical covenant position that can confer quasi mystical benefits on others if that person notarizes a contract.<br /> The Ordo Dracul don't care about personal transcendence any longer. Whereas before it was mostly lip service, they were largely apolitical in favor of their pursuits and maintained some credibility by adhering to a scientific methodology with religious zealotry. Now they're blatant power whores dedicated to overthrowing God and replacing him by any means. They don't care about scientific principles, only shortcuts to success. This is exemplified in the mechanics for Scales, from their cheap XP cost and lack of actual prerequisites, to the barbarism required to enact them.<br /> The Carthian Movement went from largely wanting to ram some version or other of socialism they control on kindred society by violence and backed by an area effect dispel non-Carthian vampire magic, to getting some mystical powers fueled by statism worship designed to help them violently seize and retain control.<br /> The Lancea et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone, although sorcery mechanics got a major overhaul, thematically they changed the least.<br /> The Circle of the Crone is still a Christianophobic and misandrystic neopagan religious cult that taps into the social justice warrior scene for their membership. They still maintain the largest repertoire of rituals available and are second to none when it comes to what can be accomplished with their ritual magics.<br /> The Lancea et Sanctum is still a monotheistic Abrahamic religious cult that uses the imagery, hierarchy, and ritualism of the Roman Catholic Church to lure in those who prefer orthodoxy. Like the Invictus, they are content to &quot;advise&quot; and their sorcery provides teeth to those dedicated to the enforcement of kindred laws and the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-29-2019, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:30:56-07:00","id":1221699,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Invictus lost there drive to be at the top or lost there preference for feudal organization. It has more to do with there reasoning. They want power not for the powers sake but for keeping the masquerade, which by being on top allows them to keep more control. They still enjoy there power but they now have a goal with it, to keep the status-quo, which doesn't mean keeping themselves archaic but to make the silence remains and humans unaware. Thus that makes them keeping the standard vampire city structure lay out less to do with it being feudal but to keep a hierarchy which is reinforced by their oaths, so they have a system of control","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:53:28-07:00","id":1221708,"title":"","content":"curious, on or ordo dracul? is it reasonable for a local version to be more interested in science then &quot;overthrowing god&quot; or is their any question raised if I as ST cause the local ordo to tolerate Coil of Ziva?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T09:27:43-07:00","id":1221731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221708#post1221708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">curious, on or ordo dracul? is it reasonable for a local version to be more interested in science then &quot;overthrowing god&quot; or is their any question raised if I as ST cause the local ordo to tolerate Coil of Ziva?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do it but you wouldn't be sticking to the theme presented for them in 2nd edition since overthrowing god is their mission statement.<br /> I personally see no reason for the Coil of Ziva NOT to be accepted by the Ordo Dracul. It's one of those things they would only disavow publicly if it's known because admitting that cannibalism is an acceptable route to power is not only going to repel prospective followers they intend to exploit in other means besides eating them, but it provides incentive for everyone else to make the Ordo Dracul kill on sight.<br /> Why would the specifics of the Mystery of Ziva be known in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T09:46:08-07:00","id":1221738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221708#post1221708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">curious, on or ordo dracul? is it reasonable for a local version to be more interested in science then &amp;quot;overthrowing god&amp;quot; or is their any question raised if I as ST cause the local ordo to tolerate Coil of Ziva?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think tausai overstated the shift in emphasis in the ordo dracul. They were never exclusively a scientific organization in 1e, and there is nothing stopping them from employing the scientific method in 2e. Likewise, while \u201cspitting in the eye of god\u201d is and always has been central to the order\u2019s philosophy, it has been and still is up to the individual dragon to interpret that for themselves. At their core, the ordo dracul is about ascending beyond the vampiric condition, turning their curse into a blessing, by any means necessary. Some theistic dragons take the defiance of god literally, others see it as symbolic. Some dragons apply scientific rigor to their pursuit of asenscion, others engage in mysticism and ritual. What matters to the order is results, not how you achieve them or why you seek them.<br /> <br /> More generally speaking, it\u2019s important to remember that the Covenants are not monoliths. While there are some broad trends across domains, for the most part there is no one way any Covenant behaves. Each domain is unique, and while the culture of the ordo dracul in one city may be one of literal interpretation of the word of Dracula, another city\u2019s chapter may see all that as irrelevant in modern times and only be interested in pursuing the coils as a scientific endeavor. Still another may have an entirely different perspective; there are no universal truths about the Covenants, which is part of why Secrets of the Covenants may come across as vague. The 1e Covenant books give great examples of how each Covenant might behave in a particular domain, and those examples are generally not incompatible with 2e at all. They\u2019re just not the whole story. Take them as the examples they are, and then modify or re-write them as you see fit for your own domain and your own story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:12:30-07:00","id":1221790,"title":"","content":"oh on Kalllisti or Les Gens Libres? Could either of their disciplines do anything about the conditioning devotion which does <b>not </b>work through creating or inflaming emotions, so theirs <b>nothing </b>for Perfidy to invert?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T12:59:03-07:00","id":1221807,"title":"","content":"Les Gens Libres have a devotion that allows them to resist Conditioning. As you noted, Conditioning in 2nd edition doesn't install specific feelings or emotions. Whether or not you actually allow users to install memories of feeling a certain way (and could thus be subject to warping with Perfidy) is largely an ST call. There's an NPC in one setting who has a homebrewed merit chain and devotion that allows him to insert certain emotions into altered memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T13:23:14-07:00","id":1221820,"title":"","content":"Hmmn Think a Kallisti enslaved in such a way would lose humanity something Feirce? when they saw their was no escape from conditioning?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> or would they possibly if it isnt too unpleasant ask for a bloodbond, to at least take the unpleasant edge off of their existence. as it<br /> <br /> What else can I do with a Kallisti slave? use them as a social tool? since Perfidy can be used against politicians corporations cults etc.<br /> <br /> Though I should probaly specify in my will that if I meet final death they should be Destroed IMMEDIATELY for my Childer's protection.<br /> <br /> Or is a bombcolor or some kind of contingency sorcery, or dominate better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-24-2018, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T18:56:48-07:00","id":1221910,"title":"","content":"Couple of questions about 'Healing' and 'The Cleansing', based on this piece of text:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Healing</b><br /> Kindred blood seeks to return a vampire to the state of her<br /> Embrace. Her hair and fingernails regrow as she sleeps. More<br /> importantly, Vitae can force her injured body to reconstruct,<br /> mending bones and knitting torn flesh in seconds. In dramatic<br /> instances, severed limbs regenerate or even simply reattach (if<br /> she\u2019s able to heal the entire injury in a turn).<br /> A single point of Vitae heals two points of bashing damage, or<br /> one point of lethal damage. A single aggravated wound requires<br /> five Vitae and a full day\u2019s sleep. Aggravated damage is the only<br /> type of wound that leaves a scar on Kindred. The scar appears<br /> natural, unlike the original damage.</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>The Cleansing</b><br /> While Kindred sleep, they return to the time of their<br /> Embrace. Anything that wouldn\u2019t constitute a Health level of<br /> damage heals automatically and returns to its original state.<br /> For this reason, many sires recommend their childer groom<br /> for the Embrace, as part of the ritual of entering the Danse.<br /> If an injury would require Vitae to heal (represented by<br /> Health levels), the vampire will unconsciously heal it during<br /> daysleep. Sometimes, this means the vampire will not have the<br /> Vitae necessary to wake. As she falls to slumber, she may spend<br /> Willpower points to \u201cpreserve\u201d wounds through her rest, to keep<br /> herself from healing them and spending excessive Vitae. This cost<br /> is one Willpower per wound, and makes the wound permanent.<br /> Sometimes, Kindred force other marks to remain. For<br /> example, vampires often keep scars, tattoos, and piercings for<br /> spiritual reasons or just to fit in with the flock. Many Kindred<br /> remove long hair, in favor of wigs or cleaner, more modern<br /> styles. The vampire spends Willpower to fight the healing<br /> process while she sleeps. After a day\u2019s rest, any damage heals<br /> as normal, but her body remains changed.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> When you &quot;preserve&quot; wounds, does that actually make the damage in your health boxes permanent as well? Say my vampire has 2 aggravated damaged, I wanna use Willpower to prevent my vampire from healing 1 dot of aggravated damage to make sure he doesn't lose all his Vitae over the day, does that mean he now permanently has 1 aggravated damage? Or is the &quot;permanent&quot; nature of 'The Cleansing' only a visual/aesthetic thing? If the actual aggravated wound becomes permanent, is there any way he can get rid of it?<br /> <br /> If the answer to &quot;is the aggravated damage permanent if I spend 1 Willpower&quot; is &quot;no&quot;, I have another question: Do I spend 1 Willpower once to keep the aggravated wound on my vampire until I'm ready to heal it, or do I have to spend 1 Willpower each day during daysleep?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T19:39:21-07:00","id":1221917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"