nd spending excessive Vitae. This cost<br /> is one Willpower per wound, and makes the wound permanent.<br /> Sometimes, Kindred force other marks to remain. For<br /> example, vampires often keep scars, tattoos, and piercings for<br /> spiritual reasons or just to fit in with the flock. Many Kindred<br /> remove long hair, in favor of wigs or cleaner, more modern<br /> styles. The vampire spends Willpower to fight the healing<br /> process while she sleeps. After a day\u2019s rest, any damage heals<br /> as normal, but her body remains changed.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> When you &quot;preserve&quot; wounds, does that actually make the damage in your health boxes permanent as well? Say my vampire has 2 aggravated damaged, I wanna use Willpower to prevent my vampire from healing 1 dot of aggravated damage to make sure he doesn't lose all his Vitae over the day, does that mean he now permanently has 1 aggravated damage? Or is the &quot;permanent&quot; nature of 'The Cleansing' only a visual/aesthetic thing? If the actual aggravated wound becomes permanent, is there any way he can get rid of it?<br /> <br /> If the answer to &quot;is the aggravated damage permanent if I spend 1 Willpower&quot; is &quot;no&quot;, I have another question: Do I spend 1 Willpower once to keep the aggravated wound on my vampire until I'm ready to heal it, or do I have to spend 1 Willpower each day during daysleep?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Question ive had for a bit, is it impossible to be rid of the scars from aggravated damage?<br /> <br /> if in your neonatehood you were a poacher or a disobedient childe and got branded, you may want a way to cleanse the scar's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T20:49:22-07:00","id":1221930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221910#post1221910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you &quot;preserve&quot; wounds, does that actually make the damage in your health boxes permanent as well? Say my vampire has 2 aggravated damaged, I wanna use Willpower to prevent my vampire from healing 1 dot of aggravated damage to make sure he doesn't lose all his Vitae over the day, does that mean he now permanently has 1 aggravated damage? Or is the &quot;permanent&quot; nature of 'The Cleansing' only a visual/aesthetic thing? If the actual aggravated wound becomes permanent, is there any way he can get rid of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's aesthetic. Aggravated damage is extremely bad for vampires, but not &quot;permanent loss of Health boxes&quot; bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the answer to &quot;is the aggravated damage permanent if I spend 1 Willpower&quot; is &quot;no&quot;, I have another question: Do I spend 1 Willpower once to keep the aggravated wound on my vampire until I'm ready to heal it, or do I have to spend 1 Willpower each day during daysleep? </div> </div> </div>Once. The resource-jenga spending Willpower per wound courts in more dire situations is enough of a setback without making it a recurrent price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T05:44:21-07:00","id":1221995,"title":"","content":"Just wondering, but in any of the books state where the blood inside the vampire actually go to? This was something I was wondering ever since I read in the core that Vitae and blood was different as Vitae is like an occult reaction blood has when circulating through a vampire, and that spending Vitae just leaves blood inert but vampires still keep it. I ask because Vampires don't really digest stuff, there corpses so where does the blood actually go? Is it absorbed somewhere or does it just disappear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T06:45:01-07:00","id":1222013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221995#post1221995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just wondering, but in any of the books state where the blood inside the vampire actually go to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per 2e Core:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vitae is not blood; at least, not directly. Kindred create Vitae as a byproduct of processing the blood they absorb. There\u2019s no digestion; <b>the blood seeps through the gullet and washes through decaying tissues</b>. Vitae is the perverse fuel that exists within the Kindred\u2019s blood. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T07:39:30-07:00","id":1222028,"title":"","content":"So basically blood just assimilates directly into a vampires body then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T08:29:02-07:00","id":1222045,"title":"","content":"on Belonging to more than one covenant?<br /> <br /> Is their a reason other then wanting the excitement of playing through that kind of plot arc, to try playing a spy of one covenant on another? when in 2nd edition, their willing to tolerate dual covenant membership?<br /> <br /> Way I take it, the invictus views anyone who belongs to another covenant but also works with them, as a &quot;Spokes person&quot; for that covenant.<br /> <br /> Sanctum will probaly view an invictus or carhian as looking for 'meaning'<br /> <br /> not sure what the circle will think viewing him as an ally on the periphery but not willing to give it their all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-25-2018, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T09:08:34-07:00","id":1222052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1221917#post1221917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question ive had for a bit, is it impossible to be rid of the scars from aggravated damage?<br /> <br /> if in your neonatehood you were a poacher or a disobedient childe and got branded, you may want a way to cleanse the scar's.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take is that if you cut out the damaged flesh, and expend the Willpower while healing, you can heal the body back to an original, undamaged state. <br /> <br /> Similarly, if you mangle yourself (or have it done for you), and expend the Willpower to keep the wound, then the effects of the mangling remain even as the damage is eventually &quot;healed&quot; and removed from wound boxes.<br /> <br /> I have an NPC who was hate-embraced and then tortured into a wreck, then dominated to love his &quot;new&quot; body and expend that Willpower to keep it. Repeatedly. Fixing this involves cutting off damaged bits and letting the NPC daysleep while remembering how he once was. (i.e. more Willpower)<br /> <br /> Am not sure if the embrace would permit healing old wounds, such as amputations, however. I think not... which is where some Ordo Scales come in, IIRC.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T14:10:18-07:00","id":1222110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222052#post1222052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Am not sure if the embrace would permit healing old wounds, such as amputations, however. I think not... which is where some Ordo Scales come in, IIRC.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And the Bron Bloodlines signature power...<br /> <br /> oh just thought?<br /> <br /> Would the emotions of obsession generated by the blood bond be too problematic in a ghoul you employee as a Nanny Governess, or tutor for your Dhampir?<br /> <br /> or would it be easy to make them take that 'charge' as a display of trust, and honor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-25-2018, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T17:35:00-07:00","id":1222132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222110#post1222110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And the Bron Bloodlines signature power...<br /> <br /> oh just thought?<br /> <br /> Would the emotions of obsession generated by the blood bond be too problematic in a ghoul you employee as a Nanny Governess, or tutor for your Dhampir?<br /> <br /> or would it be easy to make them take that 'charge' as a display of trust, and honor?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The blood bond doesn't make people not functional or problematic. Else how could a vampire have a ghoul for centuries? If the blood bonded individual is treated with care and concern, they probably wont develop psychotic creepy tendencies. Though it is your game and you can have it as creepy or not creepy as you wanted it to be. <br /> <br /> And likely if you have Blood bonded level 3 and told them to take care of your child they would be honored and would do everything they can not to upset you or hurt you ( directly or indirectly ~ Physically or emotionally )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T18:22:48-07:00","id":1222139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222132#post1222132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The blood bond doesn't make people not functional or problematic. Else how could a vampire have a ghoul for centuries? If the blood bonded individual is treated with care and concern, they probably wont develop psychotic creepy tendencies. Though it is your game and you can have it as creepy or not creepy as you wanted it to be.<br /> <br /> And likely if you have Blood bonded level 3 and told them to take care of your child they would be honored and would do everything they can not to upset you or hurt you ( directly or indirectly ~ Physically or emotionally )</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think ive been exposed to too much nonsense on the forums (sighs)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T23:07:42-07:00","id":1222174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222139#post1222139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think ive been exposed to too much nonsense on the forums (sighs)</div> </div> </div> </div>Here\u2019s what the book actually says about 3rd stage blood bonds:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Has someone\u2019s name alone make you bite your lower lip in anticipation? Has it ever aroused you to imagine her reaction to something you\u2019ve done? Have you ever sabotaged something that could have been special, for fear of its intrusion between you and her? Has your brain gone wild, imagining the worst possible scenario when she meets someone new? Have you ever thought to intervene in order to protect what you have? Have you ever tried to agitate her, because her irritation is better than her neglect? This is the feeling of a full blood bond. It\u2019s nothing short of infatuation. It\u2019s a tantalizing, forceful affection that always eats at the back of your mind. </div> </div> </div>So, it creates an obsession, and obsessions have the potential to become dangerous, but they are not always necessarily so. It\u2019s that \u201cI\u2019d do anything for you\u201d kind of feeling, and there certainly might be a risk when putting someone who feels that way about you in charge of a child you had with someone else. Then again, they might do a great job at it, recognizing that if harm came to the Dhampir it would upset you, and that\u2019s something they don\u2019t want. As with everything in life, it\u2019s complicated. It depends on the individual how they behave under the influence of such a powerful preoccupation with earning their regnant\u2019s affection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T04:53:03-07:00","id":1222209,"title":"","content":"Since mortals has absolutely no way to resist the blood bond it means the vast majority of ghouls will be stage three blood bonded after their regnant grants them their third drink. Since ghouls are supposed to be &quot;loyal and effective aides&quot; from an out of setting perspective and seen as a &quot;necessary burden&quot; from most vampires in setting, it's clear that blood bonds still allows the thrall to function efficiently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T05:00:48-07:00","id":1222210,"title":"","content":"any reason to ghoul as opposed to just bonding a Mortal for such a task? just thought<br /> <br /> Dominate or Majesty would allow them to ensure they were obeyed, when needed, though dominate would breed resentment.<br /> <br /> Majesty would also make it easier if you need to explain away something to an outsider in a hurry.<br /> <br /> Auspex lets you ensure they cant lie to you.<br /> <br /> and let's you know if people the two of you are meeting are dangerous<br /> <br /> still dont think a gangrel or nosferatu would benefit from ghouling their childs caretaker. as proteans totallly useless<br /> <br /> and Nightmare's too destructive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-26-2018, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T05:33:47-07:00","id":1222214,"title":"","content":"Majesty is more likely to breed resentment than Dominate. Victims of Dominate don't remember being dominated or what they do in that time frame. Majesty victims emphatically do remember being exploited or ripped off and CAN refuse requests.<br /> <br /> Blood bonds and disciplines are specifically used to ignore specific dynamics of relationship interactions and each one has its own drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T06:23:17-07:00","id":1222229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222214#post1222214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Majesty is more likely to breed resentment than Dominate. Victims of Dominate don't remember being dominated or what they do in that time frame. Majesty victims emphatically do remember being exploited or ripped off and CAN refuse requests.<br /> <br /> Blood bonds and disciplines are specifically used to ignore specific dynamics of relationship interactions and each one has its own drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dont think their will be much resentment if one's nanny/Governess uses majesty to make a Dhampir child stay safe, and stay on Mommy's good side, VERY importanty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T05:58:38-07:00","id":1222387,"title":"","content":"How does long term domination effect some one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T06:25:30-07:00","id":1222393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222229#post1222229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dont think their will be much resentment if one's nanny/Governess uses majesty to make a Dhampir child stay safe, and stay on Mommy's good side, VERY importanty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it you haven't watched Archer and seen how he treated Woodhouse.<br /> Or if a vampire's mortal child prefers the servant to their parent because Majesty or Dominate usage creates perverse attraction or subservience in the victim to the user. Are you sure the vampire parent would be fine with that?<br /> <