 is basically a person who is so obsessed with another that they would kill anyone that would get in the way of their perceived love or even kill the one they love if they fall short to what they think. Vampires would mostly be less extreme normally but with how Touchstones work and how important it is to them they will certainly be more obsessive then normal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T07:10:34-07:00","id":1222647,"title":"","content":"That would be a interesting character to play","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T07:40:18-07:00","id":1222652,"title":"","content":"I mean the Daeva's are all Yanderes also, if they fall to there clan bane","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T11:39:05-07:00","id":1222686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222576#post1222576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> only problem I have is this allows ghouls to have more vitae then a revenent<br /> <br /> curious<br /> <br /> can a Revenent who's a former ghoul... Rwetain clan specific disciplines, he allready learned<br /> <br /> if so he might get a bit for teaching them<br /> <br /> worse I think Ghouls can learn devotions but revenents cant?<br /> <br /> to be fair that's because revenents have no clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>You shouldn\u2019t compare a ghoul to a revenant. These things are about the same as a wolf and a dog and a coyote. <br /> <br /> Resilience gives you stamina dots. Ghouls can hold as much as their stamina dots. So if you have 5 resilience and 5 stamina for whatever reason, yes.... yes you\u2019re ghoul can have 10 vitae. <br /> <br /> Yes, your revanent would retain their knowledge from being a ghoul. So they would keep what they have access to. <br /> <br /> And you are correct, ghouls can learn devotions. Revenants can\u2019t, but I would say that this is a specific case. To me it wouldn\u2019t make sense for someone to forget how to do something they knew before, but it would prevent them from learning more, as the book says.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T12:48:20-07:00","id":1222693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222686#post1222686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You shouldn\u2019t compare a ghoul to a revenant. These things are about the same as a wolf and a dog and a coyote.<br /> <br /> Resilience gives you stamina dots. Ghouls can hold as much as their stamina dots. So if you have 5 resilience and 5 stamina for whatever reason, yes.... yes you\u2019re ghoul can have 10 vitae.<br /> <br /> Yes, your revanent would retain their knowledge from being a ghoul. So they would keep what they have access to.<br /> <br /> And you are correct, ghouls can learn devotions. Revenants can\u2019t, but I would say that this is a specific case. To me it wouldn\u2019t make sense for someone to forget how to do something they knew before, but it would prevent them from learning more, as the book says.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You COULD argue the blood just couldnt sustain the power anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, sad thing is, devotions a ghould would have learned were likely NOT meant to prepare him for existence as a revenent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T14:30:02-07:00","id":1222709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222693#post1222693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> You COULD argue the blood just couldnt sustain the power anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, sad thing is, devotions a ghould would have learned were likely NOT meant to prepare him for existence as a revenent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is nothing anyone can do to prepare for being a revenant. They are mistakes...<br /> <br /> <br /> If you had a ghoul that ended up as a revenant and made them change their devotions out because revenants can't learn them, then suddenly they get uplifted to a vampire, who can learn them, what do you do when they want them back? It wouldn't make much sense to make them forget it.<br /> <br /> Preventing them from learning more seems much more coherent story wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 05-28-2018, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T14:41:58-07:00","id":1222713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222709#post1222709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There is nothing anyone can do to prepare for being a revenant. They are mistakes...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> know that<br /> <br /> was being sarcastic<br /> <br /> (though their is that revenant dynasty that was created when the last Dhampir of a extinct clan performed some ritual.... was wondering can a Dhampir be embraced?)<br /> <br /> oh another thing I've wondered?<br /> <br /> how do new sects, bloo