lling a stranger is bad ,, but abusing someone trust in you seems like it would by more of a breaking point , vampire does have a sexual predator subtext ,,,.you know long term abuse vs just stabbing someone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T19:27:26-07:00","id":1222785,"title":"","content":"Half damned says Dhampir's and ghoul's sometimes manifest Chary<br /> <br /> and some long extinct clan had a discipline identical to it... in spite of manyy of the power's of Chary ONLY mattering because of a revenents unique condition<br /> <br /> or Am I just being an idiot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T19:35:33-07:00","id":1222789,"title":"","content":"My &quot;houserule&quot; (it's not really a houserule, the book actually suggests doing this) with touchstones and Breaking Points is that when you commit a certain Breaking Point with your Touchstone as the victim, that Breaking Point will count as 1 of 2 Humanity lower.<br /> <br /> So, to use Dominate as an example: 'Depriving another of consent with a Discipline' is a Breaking Point at Humanity 8 normally, so if you do this to your Touchstone, it will be a Breaking Point at Humanity 7 or perhaps even 6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T05:50:42-07:00","id":1222868,"title":"","content":"oh was thinking the 'Scarred' Condition should end without resolving after a period of time as I've never caused injury to another worse then a scrape or bruise, mostly when I was an innocent aged kid, and I am no saint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-29-2018, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:09:10-07:00","id":1223391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222868#post1222868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh was thinking the 'Scarred' Condition should end without resolving after a period of time as I've never caused injury to another worse then a scrape or bruise, mostly when I was an innocent aged kid, and I am no saint.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The Scarred Condition is more like \u201cmentally scarred\u201d or traumatized than an actual scar. It comes specifically from being fed on violently by a vampire, and it\u2019s effects are entirely nonphysical.<br /> <br /> 2. All Conditions expire without resolving when they are no longer dramatically relevant. Scarred is no exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T14:19:48-07:00","id":1223397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1223391#post1223391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The Scarred Condition is more like \u201cmentally scarred\u201d or traumatized than an actual scar. It comes specifically from being fed on violently by a vampire, and it\u2019s effects are entirely nonphysical.<br /> <br /> 2. All Conditions expire without resolving when they are no longer dramatically relevant. Scarred is no exception.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I knew the first as I was posting was asking that having to cause lethal damage is a lot.<br /> <br /> NPC's who arent usualy violent may rarely encounter such a sitch<br /> <br /> <br /> Didnt know the 2nd though sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T17:49:37-07:00","id":1223448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1223397#post1223397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew the first as I was posting was asking that having to cause lethal damage is a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It involves hitting someone with a weapon twice to get rid of a two-dice penalty to resist fear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> NPC's who arent usualy violent may rarely encounter such a sitch </div> </div> </div>And that makes things that much more troubling for them when they run across a vampire who isn't bothering with pleasantries before they treat them to dinner. This is not a Condition that arises from non-escalatory circumstances \u2014 the Bestial Condition is even worse for your hypothetical wouldn't-hurt-a-fly NPC, and vampires don't even need to deal damage to put that on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T19:05:12-07:00","id":1223471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1223448#post1223448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It involves hitting someone with a weapon twice to get rid of a two-dice penalty to resist fear.<br /> <br /> And that makes things that much more troubling for them when they run across a vampire who isn't bothering with pleasantries before they treat them to dinner. This is not a Condition that arises from non-escalatory circumstances \u2014 the Bestial Condition is even worse for your hypothetical wouldn't-hurt-a-fly NPC, and vampires don't even need to deal damage to put that on them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've hurt flies... killed them (but dont rip their wings off)<br /> <br /> but for some reason cant bring myself to hurt Mammal's or birds.<br /> <br /> some dogs a neighbour had forgot to take care of came over to my parents house. they were half starved.<br /> <br /> but they kepts leaping on me trying to lick mebeing very friendly... I wound up twisting my ankle, rather then step on one of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> My parents wound up taking them to the pound... only to find out a few days latter they belonged to neighbours who were upset... cause they didnt hafve a breeding license...<br /> <br /> and now were going to have to schedule vaccinations and fixing for the puppies..<br /> <br /> <br /> point is I chose to twist a ankle rather then stepping on a dog.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T20:28:46-07:00","id":1223500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1223471#post1223471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">point is I chose to twist a ankle rather then stepping on a dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't really have a whole lot of bearing on the rather more specific situation of &quot;victims of violent feedings become disturbed, angry, paranoid, and prone to lashing out.&quot; The mechanical teeth of that aspect are &quot;you're easier to spook or intimidate until you hit someone hard enough that they're going to need some time to recuperate, at which point you come to your senses and probably have some fences to mend.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;NPCs who aren't usually violent&quot; <i>become sufficiently violent for the Resolution criterion to be an outside possibility</i> as the narrative effect the Condition represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T22:17:32-07:00","id":1223510,"title":"","content":"oh ok... <br /> <br /> <br /> and it can also be resolved by being deemed irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T23:01:43-07:00","id":1223522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1223510#post1223510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it can also be resolved by being deemed irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which the book recommends doing <i>sparingly</i>, and <i>for the sake of the ongoing narrative</i> in particular. If you just don't feel comfortable having a character become incentivized to commit violence as a consequence of a destabilizing encounter with the supernatural, there is exactly <i>one vector</i> for that specific Condition under normal circumstances, which most socially-minded vampires will avoid unless that is their specific goal.<br /> <br /> The Condition isn't irrelevant just because you don't foresee it being resolved anytime soon by that character and choose to completely ignore its narrative effects \u2014 a Scarred character will continue to be easily intimidated until they land a solid swing, because a vampire grabbed them and bit into them and stole their blood and they were not given any pleasant illusions about that fact.<br /> <br /> Like, what's your actual plan here? What kind of timetable are you expecting traumatic exposure to vampirism to clear on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T08:15:34-07:00","id":1224168,"title":"","content":"My creative juices aren't flowing, so I'm gonna ask you guys for help here.<br /> <br /> Can someone help me come up with more 'all willpower' scenarios for the Courtesan mask/dirge archetype?<br /> <br /> The book says this:<br /> <br /> <b>Courtesan</b><br /> A courtesan exists to see others enjoy themselves. He revels<br /> not for himself, but to let others bask in his revelry. He\u2019s a<br /> master of the art of enjoyment.<br /> <b>Single Willpower:</b> Put yourself out for another\u2019s pleasure.<br /> <b>All Willpower:</b> Be the last one dancing when the party\u2019s<br /> on fire.<br /> <br /> Usually the example given in the book gives me a pretty good framework to work from, but not with this archetype. Be the last one dancing when the party's on fire? What does that even mean? I doubt it's meant in the literal sense here. So what then, would be a good alternative example for the 'all willpower' clause for Courtesan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T09:57:27-07:00","id":1224187,"title":"","content":"I think what they mean is the Courtesan is trying to lift the mood and make people feel happy even in a very serious situation where it normally isn't appropriate. The example they are giving you is them trying to have fun with everyone while they are kinda being on fire, thus have other stuff that's really more important to do. Something like that anyhow. Very Devil may care, reckless at it's greatest, not necessarily because they enjoy risks, they just want the party to keep going","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 06-02-2018, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T03:01:34-07:00","id":1224302,"title":"","content":"When exactly can a Strix make use of the Kindred Disciplines Dread Power? Only while possessing a Kindred? While in Shadow Form? While possessing something other than a Kindred? I mean, does a Strix with Vigor gain the extra Strength while possessing a corpse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 06-03-2018, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T04:51:01-07:00","id":1224314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224168#post1224168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My creative juices aren't flowing, so I'm gonna ask you guys for help here.<br /> <br /> Can someone help me come up with more 'all willpower' scenarios for the Courtesan mask/dirge archetype?<br /> <br /> The book says this:<br /> <br /> <b>Courtesan</b><br /> A courtesan exists to see others enjoy themselves. He revels<br /> not for himself, but to let others bask in his revelry. He\u2019s a<br /> master of the art of enjoyment.<br /> <b>Single Willpower:</b> Put yourself out for another\u2019s pleasure.<br /> <b>All Willpower:</b> Be the last one dancing when the party\u2019s<br /> on fire.<br /> <br /> Usually the example given in the book gives me a pretty good framework to work from, but not with this archetype. Be the last one dancing when the party's on fire? What does that even mean? I doubt it's meant in the literal sense here. So what then, would be a good alternative example for the 'all willpower' clause for Courtesan?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looking at the Single Willpower clause, it sounds like the vampire has to ensure that everyone is satisfied, and must not stop until everyone's appetites are fulfilled to the very end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T05:39:57-07:00","id":1224327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224302#post1224302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When exactly can a Strix make use of the Kindred Disciplines Dread Power? Only while possessing a Kindred? While in Shadow Form? While possessing something other than a Kindred? I mean, does a Strix with Vigor gain the extra Strength while possessing a corpse?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Strix can use Kindred Disciplines when embodied in vampiric hosts, and some Strix become practiced enough at the strangely physical uses of Vitae that they <i>retain the ability even after leaving the host behind.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> A Strix can use their host's Disciplines but only while inside the host, but Disciplines gained through Kindred Disciplines are always available (though not always useful, in case of Cr\u00faac for example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T06:59:51-07:00","id":1224348,"title":"","content":"I think even with the dread power, they need to be in a host, though not neccessarily a kindred host.<br /> <br /> e.g. a corpse host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T19:48:38-07:00","id":1224526,"title":"","content":"<i><b>Honey Trap (\u2022)</b><br /> Effect: Your character\u2019s blood not only bonds, but it<br /> invigorates. When a vampire tastes your character\u2019s Vitae, she<br /> regains a point of Willpower. If this results in a new bond, or<br /> steps up an existing bond, she also takes a Beat.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Am I assuming correctly that the Willpower gain and Beat gain refer to the player with the Honey Trap merit? Does this also apply when a vampire forcefully drains vitae from the Honey Trap player?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T21:12:05-07:00","id":1224549,"title":"","content":"No, it refers to the imbiber. It's to encourage the imbiber to drink more. Either to ensure a vinculum is initially established or to seek out the opportunity to imbibe again and strengthen or complete the bond.<br /> <br /> And yes it would apply even if fed from involuntarily. That's a risk you better be prepared to take if you're going to use perversion to enslave other vampires.<br /> <br /> And another thing, if a vampire with higher blood potency imbibes, you've just given them a free willpower to resist the establishment of a vinculum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-14-2018, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T21:20:21-07:00","id":1224550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224549#post1224549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it refers to the imbiber. It's to encourage the imbiber to drink more. Either to ensure a vinculum is initially established or to seek out the opportunity to imbibe again and strengthen or complete the bond.<br /> <br /> And yes it would apply even if fed from involuntarily That's a risk you better be prepared to take if you're going to use perversion to enslave other vampires.<br /> <br /> And another thing, if a vampire with higher blood potency imbibes, you've just given them a free willpower to resist the establishment of a vinculum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> O really? So in other words, this Merit is borderline useless. Why would any player ever take this Merit other than to purposefully give their character a handicap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T21:28:23-07:00","id":1224551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224550#post1224550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">O really? So in other words, this Merit is borderline useless. Why would any player ever take this Merit other than to purposefully give their character a handicap?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Ven, look at what a blood bond does. Even a first-stage bond gives the average neonate cause to think twice about causing you harm and lets you talk them into things quicker. It's there to further incentivize you to use the bond and to provide PCs incentives to accept bonds from other vampires even though the Vinculum isn't represented with Conditions.<br /> <br /> Also, <i>it's a one-dot Merit</i>. What were you expecting out of that kind of investment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T21:39:00-07:00","id":1224553,"title":"","content":"Honey Trap is downright ridiculous, I've had an entire coterie basically doing my bidding with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T21:42:27-07:00","id":1224555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224551#post1224551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026Ven, look at what a blood bond does. Even a first-stage bond gives the average neonate cause to think twice about causing you harm and lets you talk them into things quicker. It's there to further incentivize you to use the bond and to provide PCs incentives to accept bonds from other vampires even though the Vinculum isn't represented with Conditions.<br /> <br /> Also, <i>it's a one-dot Merit</i>. What were you expecting out of that kind of investment?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't agree that this Merit is useful or even worth 1 dot. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> already pointed out, the merit gives the drinker a Willpower, which they can then immediately use to resist the bond. If this is a BP6+ elder, chances are they are going to be just fine if they're careful and don't take more than 3 Vitae at a time. Vampires with less than 6 Blood Potency have no reason to drink from you and most likely won't because Vitae addiction is a thing you want to avoid like the plague, most players know that and most NPCs who aren't freshly embraced fledgelings know that as well.<br /> <br /> All in all, this Merit seems useless to players, unless as a player you get yourself a Kindred Retainer with the True Friend Merit and then also give the Honey Trap Merit to that Retainer (if your storyteller allows it, personally I would never allow that), then all of the sudden this is a god-tier Merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> I mean, lets compare this to Kiss of the Succubus, the unique Daeva merit which also costs only 1 experience. It basically does the same thing if you look at it from an abstract perspective, with 2 massive key differences: it doesn't cost you anything other than 1 Willpower if you use it on Kindred and you actually <b>gain</b> Vitae, heck, after a while you'll actually get yourself a nice harem of people who are practically begging you to <b>give</b> you their Vitae, basically resulting in a free Herd (though some storytellers could demand you buy the Herd Merit if you want to gain that sort of benefit from it, and rightfully so). It can also be used on Kindred, which, when you're BP6 and actually have to feed on Kindred, is super duper useful. Now compare that Kiss of the Succubus awesomeness to Honey Trap... yeah...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-04-2018, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T21:46:10-07:00","id":1224560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224553#post1224553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honey Trap is downright ridiculous, I've had an entire coterie basically doing my bidding with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How? Don't your players have free will? Or do you deprive them of their agency by using persuasion rolls against them in the same way they would roll when they try to persuade an NPC?<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely curious. Can you give me an example of how you got the (other?) players dance to your tunes with Honey Trap?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T22:06:05-07:00","id":1224564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224550#post1224550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> O really? So in other words, this Merit is borderline useless. Why would any player ever take this Merit other than to purposefully give their character a handicap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it\u2019s not useless. No, it\u2019s not going to let a weaker character auto win over an elder BP character. But someone playing an Ordo Dracul character that chose the Mystery of the Voivode and purchased this merit would quickly get an obscene level of control over someone. Someone who wants to play a character who wants to use perversion as an influence building tool in their repertoire isn\u2019t required to become an Ordo Dracul tool in order to make their character concept viable. Elders who require kindred blood to sustain them are more likely to find willing participants if they offer to be mutually bonded or have willpower to offer as part of the deal. Alternatively, a younger vampire with this merit could more effectively prostitute themselves or secure a high level mentorship from high blood potency elder if they have something more to offer than just vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-04-2018, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T22:06:22-07:00","id":1224565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224555#post1224555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't agree that this Merit is useful or even worth 1 dot. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> already pointed out, the merit gives the drinker a Willpower, which they can then immediately use to resist the bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>And doing so then means they've lost any actual benefit for doing so when Willpower recovery is starkly limited for vampires and the roll is <i>one stat</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this is a BP6+ elder, chances are they are going to be just fine if they're careful and don't take more than 3 Vitae at a time. </div> </div> </div>Are you unfamiliar with the meaning of the words &quot;cumulative -1 die penalty&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires with less than 6 Blood Potency have no reason to drink from you and most likely won't because Vitae addiction is a thing you want to avoid like the plague, most players know that and most NPCs who aren't freshly embraced fledgelings know that as well. </div> </div> </div>Vitae addiction is not called out as especially dangerous for vampires and for players it is a <i>Beat engine</i>. Vampires with an existing third-stage bond can safely drink from you without risking a new bond and you can leverage the resource of free Willpower accordingly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All in all, this Merit seems useless to players, unless as a player you get yourself a Kindred Retainer with the True Friend Merit and then also give the Honey Trap Merit to that Retainer (if your storyteller allows it, personally I would never allow that), then all of the sudden this is a god-tier Merit. </div> </div> </div>It's a Merit that makes you that much closer to indispensable in a society of resource-hungry immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T00:39:04-07:00","id":1224594,"title":"","content":"So, as far as I was aware ghouls can't have supernatural merits and what not. However, I was looking through their section of the 2e book and I couldn't find where I read that. Can anyone give me a page number?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T05:15:53-07:00","id":1224631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224594#post1224594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as far as I was aware ghouls can't have supernatural merits and what not. However, I was looking through their section of the 2e book and I couldn't find where I read that. Can anyone give me a page number?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure where it is in Requiem, or if it's actually there at this moment. However on p.56 in CofD it says &quot;These Merits require the character remain human (nonsupernatural.)<br /> If the character becomes a vampire, ghoul, mage, or any other supernatural character type, these Merits disappear.&quot; about Supernatural Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T07:21:53-07:00","id":1224678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224560#post1224560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How? Don't your players have free will? Or do you deprive them of their agency by using persuasion rolls against them in the same way they would roll when they try to persuade an NPC?<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely curious. Can you give me an example of how you got the (other?) players dance to your tunes with Honey Trap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires can't easily regain Willpower. Suck from the vein and you will. You'll also get BEATS, your ability to resist the bond will be reduced more and more. Usually point the beat clause up and be a marginally descent master and they'll beg you for their fix without rolling any dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T08:20:43-07:00","id":1224703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224631#post1224631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not sure where it is in Requiem, or if it's actually there at this moment. However on p.56 in CofD it says &amp;quot;These Merits require the character remain human (nonsupernatural.)<br /> If the character becomes a vampire, ghoul, mage, or any other supernatural character type, these Merits disappear.&amp;quot; about Supernatural Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so that's where I read it. Thanks, so do ghouls lose all supernatural merits (like the various wolf-blooded merits), or is it just stuff like psychokinesis and other blue book supernatural merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T08:29:56-07:00","id":1224705,"title":"","content":"Wolf-Blooded Tells are explicitly not lost even if the Wolf-Blooded becomes a non-werewolf template. Any other Supernatural Merits are immediately lost or suppressed (in case the ghoul stops being a ghoul they could regain access, but if not then the ST should allow Sanctity of Merits or maybe even refund it as XP to allow the ghoul to buy Disciplines).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T09:35:22-07:00","id":1224726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224565#post1224565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you unfamiliar with the meaning of the words &quot;cumulative -1 die penalty&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, which is why I said an elder with BP6 should only take 3 vitae at a time. That way he always gets to roll 3 dice to resists the Blood Bond (6-3=3). That's more often than not going to result in a success. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224565#post1224565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vitae addiction is not called out as especially dangerous for vampires and for players it is a <i>Beat engine</i>. Vampires with an existing third-stage bond can safely drink from you without risking a new bond and you can leverage the resource of free Willpower accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I simply cannot agree with this. How is being addicted to the blood of other predators not dangerous? You think the other vampires are just going to be fine with you running around trying to steal Vitae from them in the same way a heroin addict tries to get his fix?<br /> <br /> Have you ever been addicted to something in real life Satchel? Have you ever seen an addict in real life? I have. It's not pretty. And Vitae addiction is worse because the stuff you are addicted to comes from other very dangerous predators.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224565#post1224565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a Merit that makes you that much closer to indispensable in a society of resource-hungry immortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That will 100% depend on your game, your storyteller and players. I for one would stay the fuck away from vampires with the Honey Trap Merit in the same way I stay the fuck away from cocaine dealers in real life. A Willpower and a Beat isn't worth that amount of trouble, it isn't worth risking Vitae addiction and/or getting in a bond with someone you might not even trust.<br /> Now if this Honey Trap vampire is also my True Friend and I'm a BP6 elder, <i>then</i> it becomes interesting. <i>Then</i> I'd be drinking from that Honey Trap vampire all the time.<br /> From a player perspective though? I would never take this Merit unless I trusted the Storyteller would do something interesting with it. For example in a situation where my Sire becomes a BP6 vampire and asks my character for a drink. That's when I might consider getting Honey Trap, but even then I can see it being a double edged sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T09:53:26-07:00","id":1224731,"title":"","content":"1.) The cumulative penalty mentioned is per drink. Same Elder drink three Vitae three times from the same person will roll 3 dice, 2 dice and 1 die. The fourth drink would be a chance die.<br /> <br /> 2.) The effects of Addicted (Persistent) aren't that bad, nor as persistent as you'd think. And addictions does not have to be as bad as those you've experienced. People whose lives are turned upside down because of drugs are people who had other problems (often mental health problems, or leading to mental health problems) before they started with drugs. These are not represented by the Addicted Condition. Rather, think about functional alcoholics instead. People who definitely have a problem, but a problem that's manageable for the time being, and might even stop drinking on their own without support groups and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T10:08:01-07:00","id":1224739,"title":"","content":"Given the choice, I'd stay away from all vampires, period. Every single one of the fuckers is walking around with a highly addictive substance on their person and carrying weapons that can reduce you to a drooling sycophant or unthinking drone. Or just flat out mangle you. But you don't always have full control over who you might incidentally encounter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel the same way about touchstones. They're completely useless except to give the ST and other players additional weapons to put my character in torpor without ever having to confront my character directly. I have zero desire in taking turns playing &quot;Let's Rescue Penelope Pitstop from Dick Dastardly&quot;. If that's your bag, fine but I'm not interested in that when I want to play Vampire. <br /> <br /> The fact is, not all merits are going to be equally useful to all character types at all times. Nor do you always buy a merit to maximize their primary skills. You can do it to offset weaker points in your character's stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-04-2018, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T10:15:34-07:00","id":1224741,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> <br /> \u200b1) You're right, I forgot about the &quot;further attempts to resist the bond suffer a -1 die penalty&quot; part.<br /> <br /> 2) If you look at what it takes to get rid of the Addicted (Persistent) condition, I still don't really agree. You either need to regain or lose Humanity/Integrity to shake the addiction, or you succeed at a Breaking Point exceptionally well. To me that translates to: you're gonna be stuck with this until you get a brutal wake up call (losing Humanity/Integrity or gaining an exceptional success on a Breaking Point) or until you manage to overcome a past trauma (regaining Humanity/Integrity). Never mind that the whole idea that alcoholism is somehow not that bad is ludicrous to me. I understand the misconception though. Alcohol has been normalized in our society, it's legal and nobody bats an eye when you get yourself drunk on a Friday night. So we often forget that alcohol is in fact also a hard drug, just like cocaine, heroin and crack. Being addicted to alcohol is not in any way less terrible than being addicted to those other substances. &quot;Functional alcoholics&quot; do not exist. They can pretend to be functional, sure. They can act the part and fool everyone around them. But to call such an alcoholic functional is a stretch. Their addiction is destructive and sooner or later will lead to negative consequences if they don't shake their addiction. The only reason why alcoholics don't end up in a cold wet ditch is because alcohol is legal and easy to get. But I digress. I could simply point out that even the book itself says that Vitae addiction is comparable to being addicted to a hard drug.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> <br /> If your storyteller constantly turns your Touchstones into damsels in distress, your storyteller is in my opinion a terrible storyteller. The purpose of Touchstones is to have an interesting personal connection to the mortal world that keeps your character grounded. Additionally, they give you a +2 or +3 bonus on Breaking Point rolls, so they have a clear mechanical advantage as well. That being said, I do see where you're coming from and I do agree with the point you're trying to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-04-2018, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T11:23:12-07:00","id":1224768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224560#post1224560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> How? Don't your players have free will? Or do you deprive them of their agency by using persuasion rolls against them in the same way they would roll when they try to persuade an NPC?<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely curious. Can you give me an example of how you got the (other?) players dance to your tunes with Honey Trap?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Persuasion rolls in CofD explicitly do not rob PCs of their agency. VtR explicitly says the rules in that book are not for PCs, and to look at CofD core for rules to persuade PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the subject\u2019s player chooses, he may offer a beneficial<br /> alternative, and the initiator\u2019s player can impose a Condition<br /> (see p. 75) on his character. This offer exists between play-<br /> ers, it does not need to occur within the fiction of the game<br /> (though it can). The alternative must be beneficial, and not<br /> a twist of intent. The Storyteller adjudicates.<br /> The initiator\u2019s player chooses a Condition to impose on<br /> the subject. It must make sense within the context of the<br /> scenario. </div> </div> </div>Subject in this paragraph being the person who got persuaded. They can either give in, or offer an alternative and take a Condition.<br /> <br /> Moreover, if you really don't think any players will ever take the risk (not promise) of a Blood Bond in exchange for a Willpower and a Beat, I don't know what to tell you. That is exactly the sort of thing many players would do.<br /> <br /> You also seem to be arguing that being able to make a roll once = able to make a roll every single time. That's the sort of reasoning people use in White Room debates. Someone with Honey Trap will be more appealing to snack on for an Elder than someone without it, and even six dice can turn up a failure.<br /> <br /> It's definitely niche, but for someone who wants to blood bond a large stable of others, it makes it a little easier for the tiny cost of a single XP. It's also useful if you want to play support for your group, because giving members of your coterie a Willpower for one Vitae is incredibly useful.<br /> <br /> Comparing to the Daeva one seems a bit misplaced, too. It explicitly only works on mortals. It's for Daeva to build their harem (their Curse encourages either massive promiscuity in their biting, or a dedicated harem, and this is clearly made for the latter). It's for addicting mortals to you. Honey Trap is for encouraging other Vampires to get themselves blood bound to you. Or maybe tempting away a new ghoul (pre-stage three).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T12:18:51-07:00","id":1224776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224705#post1224705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf-Blooded Tells are explicitly not lost even if the Wolf-Blooded becomes a non-werewolf template. Any other Supernatural Merits are immediately lost or suppressed (in case the ghoul stops being a ghoul they could regain access, but if not then the ST should allow Sanctity of Merits or maybe even refund it as XP to allow the ghoul to buy Disciplines).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about the wolf-blooded tells, but the other wolf-blooded merit's that gave them stuff. Thanks for the info, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T12:32:57-07:00","id":1224783,"title":"","content":"theirs a number of Cruac rituals and Sanctified Miracles that have a range of 1 mile no more no less.<br /> <br /> Ideas on ways to boost the range<br /> <br /> would a merit be enough?<br /> <br /> Especialy if tied to an altar? <br /> <br /> or think its a bad idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T12:47:09-07:00","id":1224785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224783#post1224783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">theirs a number of Cruac rituals and Sanctified Miracles that have a range of 1 mile no more no less.<br /> <br /> Ideas on ways to boost the range<br /> <br /> would a merit be enough?<br /> <br /> Especialy if tied to an altar?<br /> <br /> or think its a bad idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Merit tied to Altar could work for Cr\u00faac (having to do it at an altar being both a way to make altars more relevant and a built in drawback). Just don't allow too much boosting. Perhaps 2 to 5 dots, multiply the range with the dot rating of the Merit for all rituals that has a range other than self, touch, or the vague &quot;the target must be present&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T12:59:53-07:00","id":1224790,"title":"","content":"&quot;Functional alcoholics&quot; do not exist.<br /> <br /> There is currently no cure for addiction. Getting psychiatric help to readjust your thought processes in conjunction with being weaned off a drug using watered down versions of the same drug in question is not a cure. If they resume consumption of their drug they will fall back to old habits and their dependence returns full force. Functional addicts usually refers to people who are at the point where they abstain from their drug use and have taken steps or have ended theirs other self destructive habits and curb their dependence. So &quot;functional addicts&quot; exist but the emphasis is on the fact that they aren't consuming. Not that they are not addicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-04-2018, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T14:03:31-07:00","id":1224803,"title":"","content":"Actually, I was just referring to people with addictions that are still capable of managing their lives (rather than sober addicts that you're describing). Their addiction is certainly making it harder to do and it will have consequences (especially on relationships) but an alcoholic that manages to keep both their occupation (even if not as productive) and their family (though with declining relations) for several years can only be referred to as a functional addict (and are classified as such by professionals). They also have a much bigger shot at kicking the habit (or resolving the Condition in game terms) without outside intervention while they still have a stable life.<br /> The only myth about functional addicts (or rather something they tend to tell themselves) is that they can manage their addiction so it doesn't eventually become worse. Only complete sobriety can fix that, and only for as long as they keep sober.<br /> <br /> As for resolving Addicted, that should be fairly trivial (if somewhat time consuming) for player characters.<br /> High Humanity PCs have an easy time triggering Breaking Points and will sooner or later fall (or buy up their Humanity if they fell below their usual level before getting the Condition) while low Humanity PCs will encounter less Breaking Points but much worse in terms of dice pools and therefore fall easier once they have to roll. They also have a bigger incentive raising Humanity due to the possibility of draugrhood.<br /> Human PCs on the other hand gets Breaking Points from interacting with the supernatural, and in a game about supernatural horror (in this case vampires) it means they should encounter at least one Breaking Point per session on average. Some of these will be easy (meaning easier time getting an Exceptional) while others will get the full -5 penalty (and therefore easily fall unless they have monstrous Res.+Comp. and exceptionally high Integrity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T16:43:45-07:00","id":1224835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224785#post1224785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a Merit tied to Altar could work for Cr\u00faac (having to do it at an altar being both a way to make altars more relevant and a built in drawback). Just don't allow too much boosting. Perhaps 2 to 5 dots, multiply the range with the dot rating of the Merit for all rituals that has a range other than self, touch, or the vague &quot;the target must be present&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or maybe use a hormunculi<br /> <br /> I dont think a garden works as a good focus unless you have reason to believe an enemy will move close to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T18:22:28-07:00","id":1224862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224726#post1224726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I simply cannot agree with this. How is being addicted to the blood of other predators not dangerous? You think the other vampires are just going to be fine with you running around trying to steal Vitae from them in the same way a heroin addict tries to get his fix?</div> </div> </div> </div>You think vampires are incapable of working out tense but functional arrangements for distilled life without resorting to theft immediately? In a setting where there's already magical workarounds to turn other vampires into bendy straws for you? In the face of mechanics that amount to &quot;topping off your safety margin of the stuff that keeps you alive is now a much more attractive option to you, so hopefully you've got ironclad self-control or don't mind rolling with a minor penalty on your resistances until you get your fix&quot;?<br /> <br /> These are monsters that risk going on murder sprees from a bad week unless they routinely keep in touch with the living and you think <i>having to roll to avoid a mild Condition if they don't indulge their addiction when given the opportunity</i> is going to be a universally meaningful impediment to the average character?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That will 100% depend on your game, your storyteller and players. </div> </div> </div>The Merit is cheap to buy and not suited to every playstyle but fits a sufficiently major niche that its inclusion contributes to the general mechanics. It does not have to be universally desirable in order to be considered <i>not useless</i>, particularly not when the playstyle you seem to expect it to mesh with sounds extremely risk-averse in a mechanical framework where risky behavior is specifically rewarded for the sake of generating interesting decisions.<br /> <br /> A character with Honey Trap who makes use of it regularly has an identifiable complication in their Requiem. If you're not interested in that complication, you are under no obligation to spend those five Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T19:36:40-07:00","id":1224874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224862#post1224862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are monsters that risk going on murder sprees from a bad week unless they routinely keep in touch with the living and you think <i>having to roll to avoid a mild Condition if they don't indulge their addiction when given the opportunity</i> is going to be a universally meaningful impediment to the average character?</div> </div> </div> </div>From a mechanical point of view? No. From a roleplay point of view? Heck yes. I asked it before and I will ask again: Have you ever been addicted to something? Have you ever had to deal with addicts? If yes, then you know that addiction is much more than &quot;having to roll to avoid a mild Condition if they don't indulge their addiction when given the opportunity&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224862#post1224862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Merit is cheap to buy and not suited to every playstyle but fits a sufficiently major niche that its inclusion contributes to the general mechanics. It does not have to be universally desirable in order to be considered <i>not useless</i>, particularly not when the playstyle you seem to expect it to mesh with sounds extremely risk-averse in a mechanical framework where risky behavior is specifically rewarded for the sake of generating interesting decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I would agree with it if the risk that Honey Trap brings would give you a clear and tangible benefit. The only reason why VTR 2e is a game where risky behavior is encouraged is because that risky behavior is rewarded either with Willpower, or with Beats, or with Conditions that then turn into Beats which is how you grow your character. Honey Trap doesn't do this. It does the quite the opposite. It gives the characters drinking from your Honey Trap character all the mechanical benefits and what do you get in return? You lose Vitae, and you have a small chance that the person who fed from you is going to come back for more, which is a very double-edged sword and can either be a good thing or a really bad thing. There is no clear or tangible benefit to getting the Honey Trap Merit as a player, none at all.<br /> <br /> CofD is all about risk versus reward. You take risks because you are rewarded for it. You take risks because you believe the reward you might get is worth it. Most Merits and other mechanics in CofD find a fine balance between the risk and reward. Honey Trap, in my opinion, does not strike that balance. I see very clear risks, and very uncertain rewards.<br /> <br /> This Merit seems much more like a Merit a storyteller could give to one of his/her NPCs, to then see how the players deal with it. But even then, if I was that player, I'd think twice before drinking from that Honey Trap NPC again (or any Kindred for that matter, as long as I'm not playing a BP6+ Kindred that is). But perhaps that's because I actually <i>roleplay</i> and take the Vitae addiction very seriously (because addictions <i>are</i> a <i>very</i> serious matter), instead of meta-gaming and just seeing the Vitae addiction as just a minor mechanical inconvenience that also gives me Beats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224862#post1224862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character with Honey Trap who makes use of it regularly has an identifiable complication in their Requiem. If you're not interested in that complication, you are under no obligation to spend those five Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only as complicated as the other players and storyteller make it. In the hands of a good player and good storyteller, I can see this merit resulting in interesting drama, fair enough. But at a table with just an average player and average storyteller, I don't think this Merit is worth taking, but that's just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-04-2018, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T19:45:52-07:00","id":1224879,"title":"","content":"Moving on, I have another question. One of my players in the Vampire game I'm storytelling approached me with this Merit:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Killer Instinct (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Prerequisite:<br /> Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022, Medicine \u2022, Wits \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Effect:<br /> Your character\u2019s experience with the darkness inherent in this world has left her cold and calculating, so she can see the fragile threads that hold life together. Activating this Merit requires an instant action to assess a creature, human,animal, monster, or otherwise. When making an attack against that target, you may divide the dots in this Merit among any of the three following effects:<br /> \u2022 Ignore 1/1 armor on the target.<br /> \u2022 Convert 1 bashing damage caused in that attack to lethal.<br /> \u2022 Ignore one point of the target\u2019s Defense.<br /> The turn spent assessing a target can be combined with a turn used for aiming.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's from Beast: The Primordial on page 117. I do not own a copy of that book so I have a couple of questions before I allow my player to get this Merit.<br /> <br /> 1) Is this a general Merit? Can Vampires get this Merit?<br /> 2) Does the upgrading from Bashing to Lethal also work on vampires?<br /> 3) Should I allow my player to take this Merit on his vampire character and is there anything I should keep in mind as a storyteller with regards to balance and storytelling pertaining this Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-04-2018, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T20:50:31-07:00","id":1224882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224874#post1224874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a mechanical point of view? No. From a roleplay point of view? Heck yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is a distinction you have drawn that is not borne out by the mechanics to the degree you insist it must as a general facet of addiction. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1199464-is-vitae-addiction-a-joke?p=1199687#post1199687\">You made a thread about it before</a>. The purpose of the Addicted Condition is not to model an overpowering drive so much as a persistent distraction and detriment. It's not hunger frenzy, it's just <i>always there</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I asked it before and I will ask again: Have you ever been addicted to something? Have you ever had to deal with addicts? If yes, then you know that addiction is much more than &quot;having to roll to avoid a mild Condition if they don't indulge their addiction when given the opportunity&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Spare me the invasive personal questions and the no-true-Scotsman argumentation, please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I would agree with it if the risk that Honey Trap brings would give you a clear and tangible benefit. The only reason why VTR 2e is a game where risky behavior is encouraged is because that risky behavior is rewarded either with Willpower, or with Beats, or with Conditions that then turn into Beats which is how you grow your character. Honey Trap doesn't do this. It does the quite the opposite. It gives the characters drinking from your Honey Trap character all the mechanical benefits and what do you get in return? You lose Vitae, and you have a small chance that the person who fed from you is going to come back for more, which is a very double-edged sword and can either be a good thing or a really bad thing. There is no clear or tangible benefit to getting the Honey Trap Merit as a player, none at all. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Your character can effectively offer an alternative to acting out for Willpower to encourage other Kindred to keep in contact with them, and in so doing bring the mechanics of Vitae addiction and blood bonds closer to the forefront of the game.&quot; That's about as much of a tilt as I'd expect from a one-dot Merit that changes a basic thing about how your character interacts with their template.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> CofD is all about risk versus reward. You take risks because you are rewarded for it. You take risks because you believe the reward you might get is worth it. Most Merits and other mechanics in CofD find a fine balance between the risk and reward. Honey Trap, in my opinion, does not strike that balance. I see very clear risks, and very uncertain rewards. </div> </div> </div>Is this the part where I point out that the Ghoul section has a one-dot Merit whose literal sole effect is &quot;vampires get double the Vitae from feeding on you&quot; and nothing else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Merit seems much more like a Merit a storyteller could give to one of his/her NPCs, to then see how the players deal with it. But even then, if I was that player, I'd think twice before drinking from that Honey Trap NPC again (or any Kindred for that matter, as long as I'm not playing a BP6+ Kindred that is). But perhaps that's because I actually <i>roleplay</i> and take the Vitae addiction very seriously (because addictions <i>are</i> a <i>very</i> serious matter), instead of meta-gaming and just seeing the Vitae addiction as just a minor mechanical inconvenience that also gives me Beats. </div> </div> </div>Again, spare me this absurd argument that I'm somehow not a real roleplayer because I know what a -1 penalty means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T20:59:38-07:00","id":1224883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224879#post1224879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moving on, I have another question. One of my players in the Vampire game I'm storytelling approached me with this Merit:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Killer Instinct (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Prerequisite:<br /> Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022, Medicine \u2022, Wits \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Effect:<br /> Your character\u2019s experience with the darkness inherent in this world has left her cold and calculating, so she can see the fragile threads that hold life together. Activating this Merit requires an instant action to assess a creature, human,animal, monster, or otherwise. When making an attack against that target, you may divide the dots in this Merit among any of the three following effects:<br /> \u2022 Ignore 1/1 armor on the target.<br /> \u2022 Convert 1 bashing damage caused in that attack to lethal.<br /> \u2022 Ignore one point of the target\u2019s Defense.<br /> The turn spent assessing a target can be combined with a turn used for aiming.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's from Beast: The Primordial on page 117. I do not own a copy of that book so I have a couple of questions before I allow my player to get this Merit.<br /> <br /> 1) Is this a general Merit? Can Vampires get this Merit?<br /> 2) Does the upgrading from Bashing to Lethal also work on vampires?<br /> 3) Should I allow my player to take this Merit on his vampire character and is there anything I should keep in mind as a storyteller with regards to balance and storytelling pertaining this Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>1.) Yes.<br /> 2.) No. (Technically yes, but vampires automatically downgrades it like any other lethal damage.)<br /> 3.) It's honestly not that great, imo. The upgrade to lethal doesn't work on vampires and things that bypass armour does not bypass Resilience, leaving ignoring up to three points of Defense being the only reliable use for vampires. Personally I don't think that's enough to be worth the XP cost. I'd allow it, but have a hard time seeing anyone in my group take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T21:50:33-07:00","id":1224888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224882#post1224882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The purpose of the Addicted Condition is not to model an overpowering drive so much as a persistent distraction and detriment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got anything from the source material to back up that assessment, or is this just your interpretation? If you want to play the (vitae) addiction as a minor inconvenience that requires no further roleplaying, then be my guest. It's your game, you can play how you want. But the lore does not back you up on that. The lore suggests the Vitae addiction is much worse than that, which is indeed exactly what my thread was about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224882#post1224882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spare me the invasive personal questions and the no-true-Scotsman argumentation, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spare me the smug attitude. I'm just pointing out to you that real addiction does not work the way you think it works. Nothing invasive about that. Again, you can roleplay however you want, but on my table we look beyond the mechanics, we take roleplay seriously, and addiction is a very serious subject that we want to do justice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224882#post1224882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this the part where I point out that the Ghoul section has a one-dot Merit whose literal sole effect is &quot;vampires get double the Vitae from feeding on you&quot; and nothing else?</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that even comparable? That merit is super useful, for obvious reasons. double Vitae for your regnant means half lethal damage for you. It means a BP5 regnant in a hunger frenzy could feed from your ghoul character, get 15 Vitae, and your character might actually survive it while every other ghoul would be super dead. That's way more useful than anything Honey Trap has to offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-05-2018, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T21:56:06-07:00","id":1224889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224883#post1224883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1.) Yes.<br /> 2.) No. (Technically yes, but vampires automatically downgrades it like any other lethal damage.)<br /> 3.) It's honestly not that great, imo. The upgrade to lethal doesn't work on vampires and things that bypass armour does not bypass Resilience, leaving ignoring up to three points of Defense being the only reliable use for vampires. Personally I don't think that's enough to be worth the XP cost. I'd allow it, but have a hard time seeing anyone in my group take it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer. Can you explain to me why exactly the &quot;upgrade bashing to lethal&quot; doesn't work on vampires? The Merit literally states that bashing damage <i>inflicted</i> gets upgraded to lethal. So one could argue that you shoot a vampire, <i>inflict</i> 6 bashing damage (because mundane weapons only do bashing to vampires), <i>then</i> upgrade it to 1 lethal + 5 bashing. No doubt that argument is false, but I'd like to know why that argument doesn't work in case the player brings it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T22:58:56-07:00","id":1224903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224888#post1224888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got anything from the source material to back up that assessment, or is this just your interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The effects of the Addicted Condition are that you take a Beat when you choose to get a fix rather than fulfill and obligation and that you may receive the Deprived Condition \u2014 i.e. become irritable, anxious, and unable to focus \u2014 if you are unable to feed your addiction. It does not compel you to act violently, burn bridges, or otherwise jump to the far end of &quot;the addiction is not just slowly taking over your life, it has already taken it over&quot; on its own. It makes those outcomes easier to get to, but as a ludonarrative element it is very clearly not the sole thing to use for a wholesale loss of control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to play the (vitae) addiction as a minor inconvenience that requires no further roleplaying, then be my guest. </div> </div> </div>Stop doing this terrible thing you're doing where you treat my awareness of the mechanics for Vitae addiction not mandating the furthest extremes of addict behavior as blowing off the narrative effects of a Persistent Condition modified to act as a widget for vampires to mess with people for leverage. The game allows broader manifestations of addiction than you prefer and that doesn't justify this passive-aggressive if-you-don't-wanna-be-a-roleplayer-then-fine line you're pushing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the lore does not back you up on that. </div> </div> </div>The lore says that normal blood contaminated with drugs doesn't fulfill the need for Kindred Vitae and that characters can tempt the addict with Vitae to contest their ability to resist gaining the Condition that incentivizes them to indulge, which is a more consistent vector than mundane addictions get but not otherwise worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The lore suggests the Vitae addiction is much worse than that, which is indeed exactly what my thread was about. </div> </div> </div>The lore suggests that characters with Vitae addiction are more susceptible to the leverage of a substance that they need in order to be active. Ninety percent of the mechanics for making Vitae addiction compel any particular action are part of the regular vampire template already.<br /> <br /> Vitae Addiction is there as a tool for vampires to use and a complication for them to encounter in the process of using blood to bind people to their will; at worst, it provides a narrative impetus for frenzy rolls and penalties thereon, but the worst elements of the supernatural addiction that vampires truck with are just &quot;being a vampire.&quot; The inability of younger Kindred to safely handle processed Vitae is a problem of particular vulnerability more than general addiction symptoms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spare me the smug attitude. I'm just pointing out to you that real addiction does not work the way you think it works. </div> </div> </div>Which requires the presumption that I think &quot;real addiction&quot; works the way the Addicted Condition works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing invasive about that. </div> </div> </div>You asked me if I had ever had or dealt with people who had what you yourself describe as a very serious problem. The only way in which this is not an aggressive act of prying into my personal life is the clear presumption on your part that I haven't and therefore must not know better than you about the workings of a roleplaying game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, you can roleplay however you want, but on my table we look beyond the mechanics, we take roleplay seriously, and addiction is a very serious subject that we want to do justice. </div> </div> </div>You were saying something about a smug attitude before?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is that even comparable? That merit is super useful, for obvious reasons. double Vitae for your regnant means half lethal damage for you. It means a BP5 regnant in a hunger frenzy could feed from your ghoul character, get 15 Vitae, and your character might actually survive it while every other ghoul would be super dead. That's way more useful than anything Honey Trap has to offer. </div> </div> </div>The Merit in question can be held by non-ghouls and being a ghoul is of debatable value outside the context of having supernatural powers in exchange for courting addiction and enslavement on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your mortal character might not die from a vampire attack&quot; is about on par with &quot;your vampire character has something extra to incentivize being a dealer for other vampires in this game where 'make it easier to tempt people' is a thing every character has access to from character generation.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-05-2018, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T23:23:20-07:00","id":1224905,"title":"","content":"First of all the Producer merit is Human only. And it doesn\u2019t mean the human takes half damage, it means if a vampire decides to exsanguinate the human while in hunger frenzy, they\u2019re still just as dead, but the vampire gets twice as much vitae for the same effort. <br /> But even if it did, there is absolutely no advantage for a human to be chained up in a vampire\u2019s basement to serve as a blood battery.<br /> <br /> As for the upgrade to lethal bit. A while back the developers said that unless a fighting style or merit expressly called out as being applicable to vampires, the damage upgrade aspect doesn\u2019t apply to them. The merit itself basically condenses the practice of studying a fighting style to analyze it for weaknesses in order to make more effective strikes to vital areas, like joints and nerve clusters or armor flaws into a single turn action. Since vampires can\u2019t be rendered unconscious by the oxygen flow to their brain being cut off and don\u2019t register pain the same way, it\u2019s kind of pointless. From a game balance POV, it nullifies one of the innate advantages of being a walking corpse and being able to shrug off unarmed and weapons based attacks for awhile. But by all means go ahead and let every unarmed combatant beat your vampires unconscious with their bare hands if that\u2019s the kind of thing you want going on in your games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-05-2018, 02:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T23:46:36-07:00","id":1224908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224903#post1224903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The effects of the Addicted Condition are that you take a Beat when you choose to get a fix rather than fulfill and obligation and that you may receive the Deprived Condition \u2014 i.e. become irritable, anxious, and unable to focus \u2014 if you are unable to feed your addiction. It does not compel you to act violently, burn bridges, or otherwise jump to the far end of &quot;the addiction is not just slowly taking over your life, it has already taken it over&quot; on its own. It makes those outcomes easier to get to, but as a ludonarrative element it is very clearly not the sole thing to use for a wholesale loss of control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irrelevant. I already pointed out that I'm of the opinion that from a mechanical point of view the Addicted (Persistent) condition does not mesh well with how real addiction works, which leads to a ludonarrative dissonance. Your argument does nothing to refute that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224903#post1224903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which requires the presumption that I think &quot;real addiction&quot; works the way the Addicted Condition works.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't. I know you don't, and neither do I. Which is entirely irrelevant to this argument. The whole point is that you handwave the serious repercussions of addiction based on how mild the mechanics of the Addicted condition are. Which to mean means you either don't understand how addiction works in real-life or you just don't care and decide to downplay the effects of being addicted in your game because the mechanics allow you to. Which again, is entirely fine if everyone at your table is cool with that, but that's not how we do things at my table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224903#post1224903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Merit in question can be held by non-ghouls and being a ghoul is of debatable value outside the context of having supernatural powers in exchange for courting addiction and enslavement on a regular basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Double vitae for the Kindred = half Lethal damage for you&quot; is really not debatable. That's how the Merit works regardless of whether you are a ghoul or not. If you cannot see the value of that, then well, it cannot be helped, it's your loss I guess. I won't try to convince you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224903#post1224903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Your mortal character might not die from a vampire attack&quot; is about on par with &quot;your vampire character has something extra to incentivize being a dealer for other vampires in this game where 'make it easier to tempt people' is a thing every character has access to from character generation.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't and if you serously believe those two statements are equivalent then I dunno what to say. I think at this point this argument has ran it's course. No point in dragging this on further. We already went way of the original topic and this is a thread for questions and answers, not pointless internet arguments.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T00:01:59-07:00","id":1224910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224905#post1224905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all the Producer merit is Human only. And it doesn\u2019t mean the human takes half damage, it means if a vampire decides to exsanguinate the human while in hunger frenzy, they\u2019re still just as dead, but the vampire gets twice as much vitae for the same effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to say but you're way off base my dude. Simple math: If the vampire needs 10 Vitae to get filled up and decides to drink from you, he'll do 10 lethal damage to you, but if you have the Producer merit, you'll only do 5 lethal damage to you. The Producer merit will be the difference of 5 lethal damage. A normal human has 7 health on average so that normal human will be long dead even before this vampire who needs 10 Vitae had his fill. A human with the Producer merit though? That human will only get 5 lethal damage and survive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224905#post1224905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the upgrade to lethal bit. A while back the developers said that unless a fighting style or merit expressly called out as being applicable to vampires, the damage upgrade aspect doesn\u2019t apply to them. The merit itself basically condenses the practice of studying a fighting style to analyze it for weaknesses in order to make more effective strikes to vital areas, like joints and nerve clusters or armor flaws into a single turn action. Since vampires can\u2019t be rendered unconscious by the oxygen flow to their brain being cut off and don\u2019t register pain the same way, it\u2019s kind of pointless. From a game balance POV, it nullifies one of the innate advantages of being a walking corpse and being able to shrug off unarmed and weapons based attacks for awhile. But by all means go ahead and let every unarmed combatant beat your vampires unconscious with their bare hands if that\u2019s the kind of thing you want going on in your games.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't want that to happen in my games, so I am relieved that the Killer Instinct merit doesn't work that way. Thanks for the information, this is extremely useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-05-2018, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T02:20:48-07:00","id":1224920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224888#post1224888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just pointing out to you that real addiction does not work the way you think it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still wrong. You've seen one way addictions can affect a life and for some reason have decided your anecdotal experiences is how all addictions work. You even think functional addicts is a myth when that's a classification used by actual rehab programs. <i>That</i> is a disservice to addicts by removing all nuances from addictions and forcing them to fit into a single mold.<br /> <br /> Also, your whole &quot;take roleplay seriously&quot; shtick is extremely elitistic. It implies how your group roleplays is better than other ways and is smug as all fucking hell. There are so many better ways to say that your group puts more focus on what's &quot;realistic&quot; rather than the mechanics (that, frankly, are designed to make the game fun rather than realistic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T03:10:37-07:00","id":1224923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224920#post1224920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're still wrong. You've seen one way addictions can affect a life and for some reason have decided your anecdotal experiences is how all addictions work. You even think functional addicts is a myth when that's a classification used by actual rehab programs. <i>That</i> is a disservice to addicts by removing all nuances from addictions and forcing them to fit into a single mold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I've seen just one way addiction can affect a life and that's what I base my entire point of view on... If only that was indeed the case...<br /> <br /> The example for highly functional addicts you gave was alcoholism, and I wanted to point out that you often see highly functional alcoholics but not because alcoholism isn't fucking with their (mental) health, but because alcohol is legal, cheap and easy to get, so it's an addiction that is easy to indulge and thus doesn't have such an immediate or catastrophic impact as for example heroin or crack, which is illegal, expensive and difficult to get.<br /> <br /> Thing is, with hard drugs, it will screw with your mental and physical health (and you're right that most addicts already have mental issues to begin with). So even a highly functional addict will suffer from his addiction to some degree and to write that off as a minor nuisance doesn't sit well with me.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that highly functional addicts usually are highly functional because they have otherwise relatively stable and mundane lives. Functional addicts will quickly become dysfunctional when stressful and/or dramatic situations get introduced into their lives. Guess what vampires and ghouls have to deal with almost all the time...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224920#post1224920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, your whole &quot;take roleplay seriously&quot; shtick is extremely elitistic. It implies how your group roleplays is better than other ways and is smug as all fucking hell. There are so many better ways to say that your group puts more focus on what's &quot;realistic&quot; rather than the mechanics (that, frankly, are designed to make the game fun rather than realistic).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If that's what you take away from what I said, then go ahead. That's not at all what I was implying though.<br /> <br /> I literally said multiple times that you and everyone else are within their right to play however you want. You wanna play the Vitae addiction as just a minor inconvenience? Go ahead. I won't think any less of you. But it's not how I want to play VTR. I want to put emphasis on the dark, tragic and gruesome nature of the heavy topics that are covered by this game. I want to add some realism to my games, even though this is a game about supernatural creatures. I do think downplaying the effects being an addict can have on your character's already hectic life is doing a disservice to the actual subject, but if everyone at your table is okay with it, then bloody go for it, more power to you guys, you do you. No really, I mean it, this isn't even meant in a sarcastic way.<br /> <br /> I do think meta-gaming is bad though (especially when the meta-gaming results in less actual roleplaying), but that's an entire different can of worms that really shouldn't be opened right here and right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't want to continue this discussion, but I did want to reply to you to defend myself after being called &quot;elitistic&quot; (I think you mean elitist?) and smug.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-05-2018, 07:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T04:07:42-07:00","id":1224924,"title":"","content":"You said you didn't want to continue this discussion, but I have to reply to this part because I hope it can prevent future unintentional insults.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224923#post1224923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's what you take away from what I said, then go ahead. That's not at all what I was implying though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that's not what you <i>mean</i> to imply, but it's what you <i>do</i> imply every time you word yourself that way, regardless of your intentions.<br /> <br /> &quot;But perhaps that's because I actually <i>roleplay&quot;</i><br /> <br /> &quot;but on my table [..] we take roleplay seriously&quot;<br /> <br /> What these two clauses are saying is that our way or roleplaying is not &quot;actual roleplay&quot; or &quot;serious roleplay&quot;. That's extremely condescending because it straight out says our way of playing the game is not roleplaying; that we're doing it wrong. It seriously undermines your later explanations of our &quot;right to play however [we] want&quot; when you've already insulted those styles of roleplaying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T04:17:05-07:00","id":1224925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224924#post1224924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said you didn't want to continue this discussion, but I have to reply to this part because I hope it can prevent future unintentional insults.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I believe that's not what you <i>mean</i> to imply, but it's what you <i>do</i> imply every time you word yourself that way, regardless of your intentions.<br /> <br /> &quot;But perhaps that's because I actually <i>roleplay&quot;</i><br /> <br /> &quot;but on my table [..] we take roleplay seriously&quot;<br /> <br /> What these two clauses are saying is that our way or roleplaying is not &quot;actual roleplay&quot; or &quot;serious roleplay&quot;. That's extremely condescending because it straight out says our way of playing the game is not roleplaying; that we're doing it wrong. It seriously undermines your later explanations of our &quot;right to play however [we] want&quot; when you've already insulted those styles of roleplaying.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I replied that way is not because I think I'm better than you, but because I think &quot;but the mechanics for being an addict isn't that bad&quot; is a really poor counter argument when I try to explain why I take Vitae addiction so seriously and why I think most vampires (and players who aren't meta-gaming) would rather avoid getting addicted. It does sound to me like some people here aren't taking roleplaying seriously. And if that's the case: that's honestly fine! Really! Again, no sarcasm intended.<br /> <br /> Some people have a 'beer, pretzels and casually rolling dice on a Friday night' approach to roleplaying. Some people don't want to take roleplaying seriously. And that's 100% fine. It's not how we do things at my table, but I won't think any less of you if that's how you decide to approach roleplaying at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-05-2018, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T05:17:29-07:00","id":1224934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224925#post1224925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason I replied that way is not because I think I'm better than you, but because I think &quot;but the mechanics for being an addict isn't that bad&quot; is a really poor counter argument when I try to explain why I take Vitae addiction so seriously and why I think most vampires (and players who aren't meta-gaming) would rather avoid getting addicted. It does sound to me like some people here aren't taking roleplaying seriously. And if that's the case: that's honestly fine! Really! Again, no sarcasm intended.<br /> <br /> Some people have a 'beer, pretzels and casually rolling dice on a Friday night' approach to roleplaying. Some people don't want to take roleplaying seriously. And that's 100% fine. It's not how we do things at my table, but I won't think any less of you if that's how you decide to approach roleplaying at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing you're implying though is that your way is the &quot;roleplaying seriously&quot; way and other styles or other views on roleplaying ain't serious. I myself consider the addicted rules to be drama based and used for story building, not to mimic the real nuance of addiction. The addiction rules are imho kind of 'meh', it let's you off the hook way to easy and does not reflect the deeper or darker ways of some addictions. But here the thing though, not all addictions are equal, not every person addicted nor every substance you can be addicted to. The Condition is not meant to portray the real world nuance of extreme and sad addiction, nor the social stigma and every other part of that sad thing. As a nicotine addict, i think the addiction rules seems to fit that state way better then say alcoholism or heroin addiction. I'm not comparing or saying what substance or Vitae for that matter is worse and what each of them should be like in a mechanical way, all I am saying is that the Rules are way to lenient if you compare many forms of addiction the rules apply towards, therefore I think, mostly because CofD is drama-focused, that the rules are there to inspire drama and story and make functional addicts, not to portray the worst and saddest kinds of addictions. If you actually wanted the darker parts of addiction to be portrayed through a mechanical lens, i recommend building on the addicted condition, make a tiered system of Conditions about addiction or something.<br /> <br /> That being said, our group usually responds OOC with things like &quot;oh, that doesn't seem so bad&quot; or &quot;well, this doesn't really effect me much&quot; towards many conditions, addicted being one of them. The general thing being that Conditions should bring drama and story to the table, like the rest of the rules, not take away agency of the PCs. Although we portray in character and by descriptions things usually way worse then they are in a strict mechanical way. As another example, Leg wracked I'm looking at you. Although a Tilt, but same logic applies, the description says that one of your legs/feet are dislocated, strained or broken, and halves your speed and takes a -2 on physical rolls that require movement. Speaking out from own experience about strained feet, there is noooo way in hell i only got halved speed by that, or that i could run 2 km in double the normal time, with a athletics roll with a -2 penalty even by spending willpower unless perhaps, and that's really perhaps, my life depended on it. This is because this rule set is not meant for simulating reality, it's for drama, story and fun and allowing the player to keep it's power of agency over her PC and keep the PCs agency in-character. Same logic applies to being shot by a gun. Or Wound penalties etc etc.<br /> <br /> tl:dr: the rules are not meant to simualte reality, the are for story, fun and drama, but you could tweak or layer on more penalties or get new Conditions to better simulate a part of the world closer to reality if that's what you want.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, about meta-gaming and avoiding getting addicted. That's an ass-hat statement if I ever saw one. That's implying that people that get addicted want to be addicted. Most people like drugs because of how it makes them feel, and by a lot of psychological bias etc in action, people don't consider the risks involved as much as one perhaps should, but we humans are seldom rational and logical, we act out of emotion, feelings, affect and guide our world around bias and heuristics. Ergo &quot;it will never happen to me&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 06-05-2018, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T09:58:20-07:00","id":1224991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224934#post1224934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The thing you're implying though is that your way is the &quot;roleplaying seriously&quot; way and other styles or other views on roleplaying ain't serious. I myself consider the addicted rules to be drama based and used for story building, not to mimic the real nuance of addiction. The addiction rules are imho kind of 'meh', it let's you off the hook way to easy and does not reflect the deeper or darker ways of some addictions. But here the thing though, not all addictions are equal, not every person addicted nor every substance you can be addicted to. The Condition is not meant to portray the real world nuance of extreme and sad addiction, nor the social stigma and every other part of that sad thing. As a nicotine addict, i think the addiction rules seems to fit that state way better then say alcoholism or heroin addiction. I'm not comparing or saying what substance or Vitae for that matter is worse and what each of them should be like in a mechanical way, all I am saying is that the Rules are way to lenient if you compare many forms of addiction the rules apply towards, therefore I think, mostly because CofD is drama-focused, that the rules are there to inspire drama and story and make functional addicts, not to portray the worst and saddest kinds of addictions. If you actually wanted the darker parts of addiction to be portrayed through a mechanical lens, i recommend building on the addicted condition, make a tiered system of Conditions about addiction or something.<br /> <br /> That being said, our group usually responds OOC with things like &quot;oh, that doesn't seem so bad&quot; or &quot;well, this doesn't really effect me much&quot; towards many conditions, addicted being one of them. The general thing being that Conditions should bring drama and story to the table, like the rest of the rules, not take away agency of the PCs. Although we portray in character and by descriptions things usually way worse then they are in a strict mechanical way. As another example, Leg wracked I'm looking at you. Although a Tilt, but same logic applies, the description says that one of your legs/feet are dislocated, strained or broken, and halves your speed and takes a -2 on physical rolls that require movement. Speaking out from own experience about strained feet, there is noooo way in hell i only got halved speed by that, or that i could run 2 km in double the normal time, with a athletics roll with a -2 penalty even by spending willpower unless perhaps, and that's really perhaps, my life depended on it. This is because this rule set is not meant for simulating reality, it's for drama, story and fun and allowing the player to keep it's power of agency over her PC and keep the PCs agency in-character. Same logic applies to being shot by a gun. Or Wound penalties etc etc.<br /> <br /> tl:dr: the rules are not meant to simualte reality, the are for story, fun and drama, but you could tweak or layer on more penalties or get new Conditions to better simulate a part of the world closer to reality if that's what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked your comment because I 100% agree and you're basically making my argument for me. All I was ever saying is that &quot;oh, the mechanics of the Addicted condition aren't that bad, therefor being addicted isn't that bad&quot; is a horribly bad argument (not an argument <i>you</i> ever made, I know, but that's what this whole discussion about addiction started).<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out that the books (VTR and Half-Damned) do say that Vitae is like a hard drug. Hence I compared being addicted to Vitae is like a hard drug. The book even says that many Vitae addicts often start using other hard drug substances as a substitute when they can't get their Vitae fix. Hence I pointed out that being addicted to a hard drug is not pretty and way more than just a minor nuisance. &quot;But the mechanics for Addicted aren't that bad, so Vitae addiction isn't that bad either&quot; is a horribly bad counter argument to that. There is a clear ludonarrative dissonance here, where the lore says X but the mechanics do not portray X accurately, as you also pointed out. And again, I'm fine with that. I'm just pointing out that using the mechanics of the Addicted condition as an argument when the other person (me) is arguing lore and the reality of (Vitae) addiction, is disingenuous at best. At that point you really shouldn't feel insulted when I point out that you (Satchel) aren't roleplaying seriously or don't seem to be taking the lore of the game very seriously.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I feel like I'm starting to repeat myself, so I'll just say that I agree with you, and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224934#post1224934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: also, about meta-gaming and avoiding getting addicted. That's an ass-hat statement if I ever saw one. That's implying that people that get addicted want to be addicted. Most people like drugs because of how it makes them feel, and by a lot of psychological bias etc in action, people don't consider the risks involved as much as one perhaps should, but we humans are seldom rational and logical, we act out of emotion, feelings, affect and guide our world around bias and heuristics. Ergo &quot;it will never happen to me&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're misrepresenting my argument. I'm not implying that people who get addicted want to get addicted at all. Quite the opposite in fact. I said any person who is aware of the dangers of being addicted to a hard drug would <i>try</i> to avoid Vitae addiction like the plague. Emphasis on trying. In other words, if I'm a BP5 or lower vampire, I'd try to avoid drinking Kindred Vitae like the plague, given that I know damn well how addictive that stuff is. I sure as fuck would not even consider drinking from a Honey Trap. Saying &quot;but that Willpower + Beat my dude, and the Addicted condition really isn't that bad either, it gives you more Beats my dude&quot; is meta-gaming and a piss-poor counter argument.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want to play an addict because out-of-character you think the chaos and drama would be interesting, and you can find a good in-character justification for why your BP5&gt; vampire would drink from a Honey Trap (perhaps your character is in a bad place and the Honey Trap tricks your character into drinking from her, after which your character realizes her blood makes him temporarily forget all his problems), then by all means, go for it, that's something I'd fully support at my own table if one of my players approached it from that angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-05-2018, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T13:21:10-07:00","id":1225065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224991#post1224991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Stuff..]<br /> <br /> But I feel like I'm starting to repeat myself, so I'll just say that I agree with you, and leave it at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I do feel that we share most of our view on this matter as well. As you pointed out, there is a faulty line of thought to argue that mechanics = reality and that you are advised to role-play toward said mechanics instead of grounding it in reality. I do agree with you, that it is quite weird to say &quot;rules says it ain't bad, therefor it can't be that bad&quot; for my character&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're misrepresenting my argument. I'm not implying that people who get addicted want to get addicted at all. Quite the opposite in fact. I said any person who is aware of the dangers of being addicted to a hard drug would <i>try</i> to avoid Vitae addiction like the plague. Emphasis on trying. In other words, if I'm a BP5 or lower vampire, I'd try to avoid drinking Kindred Vitae like the plague, given that I know damn well how addictive that stuff is. I sure as fuck would not even consider drinking from a Honey Trap. Saying &quot;but that Willpower + Beat my dude, and the Addicted condition really isn't that bad either, it gives you more Beats my dude&quot; is meta-gaming and a piss-poor counter argument.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want to play an addict because out-of-character you think the chaos and drama would be interesting, and you can find a good in-character justification for why your BP5&gt; vampire would drink from a Honey Trap (perhaps your character is in a bad place and the Honey Trap tricks your character into drinking from her, after which your character realizes her blood makes him temporarily forget all his problems), then by all means, go for it, that's something I'd fully support at my own table if one of my players approached it from that angle. </div> </div> </div>First of, I want to apology about calling your argument &quot;ass-hat&quot;, and by doing that implying that you are one, for that I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> I see from where you're arguing but I can only partly agree. Yes, it's rational to try to avoid such things, but most don't act rational. And given the rumors of how awesome a drug (vitae) is, many would more then likely try it out, even with the knowledge about it's slavemaking/addictive (supernatural)powers. Like, I'm pretty sure all addicts knew about the potential dangers with their drug of choice before taking it the first time (probably not realizing the whole scope of it, but still) because other reasons, feeling empty, sad, depressed or just wanting to try it for whatever reason.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T17:44:21-07:00","id":1225121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1225065#post1225065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do agree with you, that it is quite weird to say &quot;rules says it ain't bad, therefor it can't be that bad&quot; for my character&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing: outside of Ventrue Life's strawman, <i>nobody said this. </i>&quot;The mechanics of the Addicted Condition do not at their baseline compel the full extent of possible drastic behaviors an addict might engage in, and therefore the degree to which a vampire is able to manage Vitae addiction is less narrow than the extremes mentioned in the writeup to illustrate the potential outcomes beyond those inherent in being a vampire who needs Vitae to live&quot; is not &quot;The mechanics of the Addicted Condition aren't that bad, therefore being addicted isn't that bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honey Trap is a Merit that exists as a game mechanic whose narrative effects are not necessarily under the control of the character who has it. If someone makes a claim that the Merit \u2014 which does not inherently exist as a deliberate quality in the narrative \u2014 is &quot;useless,&quot; <i>counterarguments to that position proceed from the perspective of the mechanics that a character's player would use it with. </i>Dismissing the possibility that players might willingly pursue Conditions for the resources they provide as &quot;metagaming&quot; is, yes, absurd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T18:08:59-07:00","id":1225124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1225121#post1225121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing: outside of Ventrue Life's strawman, <i>nobody said this. </i>&quot;The mechanics of the Addicted Condition do not at their baseline compel the full extent of possible drastic behaviors an addict might engage in, and therefore the degree to which a vampire is able to manage Vitae addiction is less narrow than the extremes mentioned in the writeup to illustrate the potential outcomes beyond those inherent in being a vampire who needs Vitae to live&quot; is not &quot;The mechanics of the Addicted Condition aren't that bad, therefore being addicted isn't that bad.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I just agreed to the premise, I'm not arguing against anyone based on that premise. My agreement toward the difference between mechanical and reasonable differences are at a point I made earlier. In that I said that the mechanical side has a focus toward one thing, and the fluff another, if you want more nuance or guide a specific characters addiction, another home-brewed Condition might be more suitable for that. I don't think we are in disagreement here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honey Trap is a Merit that exists as a game mechanic whose narrative effects are not necessarily under the control of the character who has it. If someone makes a claim that the Merit \u2014 which does not inherently exist as a deliberate quality in the narrative \u2014 is &quot;useless,&quot; <i>counterarguments to that position proceed from the perspective of the mechanics that a character's player would use it with. </i>Dismissing the possibility that players might willingly pursue Conditions for the resources they provide as &quot;metagaming&quot; is, yes, absurd. </div> </div> </div>Not sure if this is directed towards me, as I've yet to say anything about the Honey Trap merit but I'll say what I think of the merit. I personally, think that this merit is really, really good. It gives &quot;free&quot; willpower (willpower being quite hard to come by at our table) toward other people, even if the PC that has this merit don't have use for it, it's heavily implied that this is a better(stronger) drug then normal Vitae. It has interesting and real implications between characters and can be used for both building interesting concepts as well as with plots etc. I have no problem with this merit, i frankly quite like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T18:56:32-07:00","id":1225132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1225065#post1225065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of, I want to apology about calling your argument &quot;ass-hat&quot;, and by doing that implying that you are one, for that I'm sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to apologize. Your comments never offended me. I'm glad that we came to an understanding, and I can even see your point of view on the Honey Trap merit. I'm still of the opinion that in most games the Honey Trap merit won't be worth taking, but I can see it being an interesting merit when you have a group of solid roleplayers and above all, a good storyteller. It's a very niche merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T19:01:31-07:00","id":1225134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1225121#post1225121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/I]Dismissing the possibility that players might willingly pursue Conditions for the resources they provide as &quot;metagaming&quot; is, yes, absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you serious? It's one thing to deliberately go chasing after Conditions and admit that in doing so you're meta-gaming. But deliberately chasing after Conditions and then denying that this behavior is meta-gaming, THAT'S absurd. Do you even know what meta-gaming means?<br /> <br /> And I quote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>In role-playing games, a player is metagaming when they use knowledge that is not available to their character in order to change the way they play their character (usually to give them an advantage within the game), such as knowledge of the mathematical nature of character statistics, or the statistics of a creature that the player is familiar with but the character has never encountered. The player may be aware of the set location of specific equipment, which may have them move through the world contrary to the character's motivations. It can also include plot information, such as renaming a character with a false name to their real name before it is revealed.</i><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metagaming\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metagaming\" target=\"_blank\"> Metagame - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metagaming\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metagaming </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-05-2018, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T19:10:37-07:00","id":1225137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224920#post1224920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're still wrong. You've seen one way addictions can affect a life and for some reason have decided your anecdotal experiences is how all addictions work. You even think functional addicts is a myth when that's a classification used by actual rehab programs. <i>That</i> is a disservice to addicts by removing all nuances from addictions and forcing them to fit into a single mold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note on this:<br /> <br /> I'm a functioning alcoholic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T20:25:49-07:00","id":1225158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1225124#post1225124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this is directed towards me, as I've yet to say anything about the Honey Trap merit but I'll say what I think of the merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm addressing the starting point of the discussion because I feel it is important for its context to be kept in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1225134#post1225134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you serious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But deliberately chasing after Conditions and then denying that this behavior is meta-gaming, THAT'S absurd. </div> </div> </div>It is indeed. You'll notice that <i>that hasn't happened here</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't need to <i>deny</i> that out-of-character reasons for pursuing negative in-character outcomes are metagaming by definition to observe that you've taken a <i>very dismissive attitude to a behavior that is built into the way Conditions work</i> in a discussion that you instigated by making a claim about the value of an out-of-character resource and then proceeded to spend the rest of the discussion leaning on points of in-character undesirability to defend that claim.<br /> <br /> I'm not denying it's metagaming, I'm saying that <i>that's acceptable and accounted for and it looks bad when you still vocally treat it as inferior to your own roleplaying preferences.</i>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T20:49:11-07:00","id":1225160,"title":"","content":"Every game is totally different and the needs there would be entirely situational. For example the unnatural affinity would be utterly useless in a game that had only humans and vampires and nothing else. <br /> <br /> I played in a game where another player and I blood bonded to each other so no one could do it to us. He took honey trap merit and it ended up being totally useful to my addicted vampire who ended up always having full willpower. But again. That was situational. I can see how a game like that wouldn\u2019t be for everyone, but for us, it was great. <br /> <br /> Secondly, all this stuff about addictions and addicts ... Uhg. There are different levels of addiction. It\u2019s like a spectrum and you can be anywhere on it. One person might be willing to sell their body for another fix and someone else on that same drug might be able to just wait until they can scrounge up enough cash. Don\u2019t treat them all the same. Don\u2019t base it on one person. The mechanics for addiction are just fine... it makes you more tempted, and that\u2019s what t should be. You\u2019re more easily talked into doing things for your fix.. leverage. <br /> <br /> And every player meta games everything they decide to put a dot on a sheet. Is this good for my character? Is it going to help me in the next fight? Is it a stepping stone to my goal? <br /> Your characters don\u2019t really pick their dots, you do... then justify it in narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 06-05-2018, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T00:57:49-07:00","id":1225189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1224910#post1224910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A normal human has 7 health on average so that normal human will be long dead even before this vampire who needs 10 Vitae had his fill. A human with the Producer merit though? That human will only get 5 lethal damage and survive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to point out here, 10 lethal damage does not automatically kill a 7 health human. It means they fill up on lethal and then upgrade 3 of them to aggravated. And every minute afterwards they suffer one more lethal (upgrading to aggravated) until they get medical attention. They need to fill on aggravated to be completely dead, so in a sense 7 health is actually 14 lethal damage worth.<br /> <br /> So they can still be saved from death if someone manages to stabilize them with perhaps a wits+medicine roll and takes them to a hospital or takes care of them in another way. The victim will likely fall unconscious and stay that way until they heal 1 lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 06-06-2018, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T01:54:51-07:00","id":1225193,"title":"","content":"An individual only provides as much Vitae as their unmodified Health dots. So a human with 7 Health can only provide 7 Vitae before they can't provide anymore. At this point they are at full lethal and will need medical treatment, but there is no rolling over. By RAW, it's the taking of Vitae that deals damage, not the bite itself (unless feeding violently), so you can't even over-feed.<br /> <br /> A vampire can't kill by feeding non-violently by RAW, though of course I imagine most STs would allow it narratively.<br /> <br /> Of course, just taking more than Stamina puts peoples' lives at serious risk via the Drained condition, and my players were loathe to take more than that typically. Odd how often people talk about draining people dry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T05:00:36-07:00","id":1225218,"title":"","content":"They still need to be stabilised or they'll continue to take damage. Combined with rolls to even keep consciousness a fully fed on mortal has a hard time staying alive without assistance (such as people capable of calling 112/911).<br /> Also note that they still contain more blood (total exsanguination is automatically fatal (despite what a certain Scale in SotC thinks) and should be represented by full aggravated damage) meaning the vampire can overfeed and deal more than their victim's Health in damage causing rollover; they simply won't get Vitae from it. If the mortal is already wounded (even if it's just bashing from a relatively light disease) then you're also at risk of overfeeding even if you keep within their Vitae limits. For example, a mortal with 7 Health and 2 bashing gets fed on and the vampire takes all 7 Vitae they can get, the preexisting bashing will roll over to cause two aggravated damage.<br /> My recommendation is to never take more than the victim's apparent Size in Vitae, if you care about not leaving corpses around. If you need to feed more then once, spread it out over several hunting rolls (which often leads to taking even less Vitae per victim). For example, if my theoretical BP 5 character has only 3 Vitae and needs 12 to fill up, I'd have her feed on three mortals, taking 4+4+4 Vitae despite two Size 5 people being able to provide at least 12 Vitae (except if they've already been fed on, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T06:27:56-07:00","id":1225240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1225218#post1225218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also note that they still contain more blood (total exsanguination is automatically fatal (despite what a certain Scale in SotC thinks)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reasonably certain Bleed the Sin does not require human subjects to literally have no blood in their body, given the mention of dialysis machines and other technology.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, it's worth remembering that even with the majority of their Health left unmarked by a feeding, human vessels still suffer the Drained Condition if they lose more Vitae than their Stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:29:32-07:00","id":1225255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1225240#post1225240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reasonably certain Bleed the Sin does not require human subjects to literally have no blood in their body, given the mention of dialysis machines and other technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know that a dialysis machine only filters blood and that the body's blood volume is only marginally lowered until the procedure is finished, but then there's this line: &quot;The subject must remain effectively bloodless for at least ten minutes in order for this Scale to take effect.&quot; It makes no sense. Also, I think the line &quot;the Dragon bleeds a subject of all their blood or Vitae.&quot; means the blood must actually be lost instead of just filtered. I don't think an unmodified dialysis machine is capable of removing &quot;the weight of their sin&quot; from the subject's blood before reintroducing it to their body. It would make a whole lot more sense if mortal subjects required blood transfusions instead of just dialysis.<br /> <br /> Edit: Not to mention how nonsensical the benefit of Bleed the Sin is. For some reason the effect of the subject is affected by the vampire's number of dots in Coil of Ziva despite the procedure not mentioning any meaningful interaction between the Dragon and the subject. It makes it absolutely useless for anyone who doesn't have the Coil (something I dislike since I prefer Scales not to have any hard prerequisites, but that's just my opinion). Not that having more than two dots in the Coil makes any difference either since at two dots all purchasable Integrity equivalents have already become free. Basing it on dot ratings like that makes a lot more sense (and would be a lot less broken for a second dot's Scale) with the first edition's XP system where it only becomes a discount rather than free trait dots. Using the word sin in both title and text also reminds me more of first edition where Integrity were Morality, Humanity was much more based on morality than trying to keep human, and Breaking Points were referred to as Sins. But in second edition the only limits on how often you could use the Scale to gain free dots of Integrity or Humanity would be self imposed (such as requiring to act human in order to gain Humanity).<br /> <br /> That coupled with the second dot being the best dot in the entire Coil, the fourth dot being difficult to use if you also take advantage of the second dot, the fifth dot acting like a Scale, and one of the Scales working like a Coil dot (while also putting the victim to torpor after drinking them to full aggravated damage), makes the whole Mystery of Ziva a complete mess. It's such a shame because it's a really cool Mystery filled with awesome ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-06-2018, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T12:46:06-07:00","id":1226277,"title":"","content":"Hello everybody! A just recently bought VtR second edition and I am getting familiar with the rules. Can you help me with this question?<br /> <br /> Celerity allows interruption of actions for Vitae. The action can be played as many times as the character's celerity dots. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the vampire is still limited to one instant action. She cannot use Celerity to make two attacks, or an attack followed by another instant action. Likewise she cannot move further in a single turn than her Speed would allow. </div> </div> </div>Let's say the character has Celerity 4. Does this mean that everytime the character activates Celerity to interrupt (up to 4 times), she can attack or move as much as her Speed allows, or does it mean that she can move/attack only once per turn and all the other interrupt actions have to be something else? (Concealing, going prone, speaking, but not attacking). (I am confused whether the text in quote simply forbids taking several actions per interrupt, or multiple attack actions per turn.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T12:54:04-07:00","id":1226279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>irigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1226277#post1226277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everybody! A just recently bought VtR second edition and I am getting familiar with the rules. Can you help me with this question?<br /> <br /> Celerity allows interruption of actions for Vitae. The action can be played as many times as the character's celerity dots. <br /> <br /> Let's say the character has Celerity 4. Does this mean that everytime the character activates Celerity to interrupt (up to 4 times), she can attack or move as much as her Speed allows, or does it mean that she can move/attack only once per turn and all the other interrupt actions have to be something else? (Concealing, going prone, speaking, but not attacking). (I am confused whether the text in quote simply forbids taking several actions per interrupt, or multiple attack actions per turn.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The vampire can't make more instant actions than they have; vampires only have one instant action.<br /> <br /> So say they want to interrupt their opponents attack to move out of the way; they can do so much as their speed allows. If they wanted to attack instead it would be their first and only attack of the turn order, of if they had already attacked they couldn't do so again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T13:00:39-07:00","id":1226281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1226279#post1226279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So say they want to interrupt their opponents attack to move out of the way; they can do so much as their speed allows. If they wanted to attack instead it would be their first and only attack of the turn order, of if they had already attacked they couldn't do so again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the explanation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24286-irigi","name":"irigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24286_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T17:13:33-07:00","id":1226335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222470#post1222470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there like a permanent Condition that's like Mindbreak through tons of Dominate or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Enslaved, created through the Conditioning Devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 06-10-2018, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T17:15:15-07:00","id":1226336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1222733#post1222733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Ventrue ever DOMINATE there touchstone/former touchstones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Touchstones should represent cinflict in the form of parts of your life you have not ceded to the Beast. Imo, Dominating or bonding a touchstone should be a *big deal,* and have narrative weight, but vampires certainly do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T17:22:44-07:00","id":1226338,"title":"","content":"In order to use any Dominate Power other than Mesmerize through Chain of Command do you, practically speaking, need to use Chain of Command twice? Once to Mesmirize, once to use the other power?<br /> <br /> Are the Conditions created by Chain of Command keyed to you or the person who used them? I.e. once Mesmirize is used the victim has the mesmerized condition. Can you give more commands? Can the person you Chained through? Both?<br /> <br /> Can you use Dominate Devotions through Chain of Command? I.e. Conditioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T20:36:00-07:00","id":1226363,"title":"","content":"The one with the devotion needs to actually know the Dominate power in question. They mesmerize their agent and in the course of that, give instructions to use a Dominate power on someone else. When that agent encounters the victim, he uses the vampire\u2019s dice pool to use the Dominate power as per instructions. <br /> There\u2019s a few general interpretations. 1. Mesmerize is considered to be installable as a \u201cfreebie\u201d in the instructions left with the agent as well as whatever other Dominate power as a single use of Chain of Command. 2. You have to implant two power uses in the agent but Mesmerize doesn\u2019t count toward the single application of a Dominate programmed into someone to be installed. 3a. Literal interpretation. You can\u2019t implant two Dominate powers in a single agent at one time. Which means you use the agent to install Mesmerize in the target, then you approach the target and apply the other power. 3b. You install Mesmerize on the target and use your agent to install the Dominate command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T20:54:19-07:00","id":1226365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1226363#post1226363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a few general interpretations. 1. Mesmerize is considered to be installable as a \u201cfreebie\u201d in the instructions left with the agent as well as whatever other Dominate power as a single use of Chain of Command. 2. You have to implant two power uses in the agent but Mesmerize doesn\u2019t count toward the single application of a Dominate programmed into someone to be installed. 3a. Literal interpretation. You can\u2019t implant two Dominate powers in a single agent at one time. Which means you use the agent to install Mesmerize in the target, then you approach the target and apply the other power. 3b. You install Mesmerize on the target and use your agent to install the Dominate command.</div> </div> </div> </div>4. The ability to have an agent Mesmerize and instruct a given target is the main use of the Devotion without preparing the target beforehand, because Mesmerize otherwise only makes a target susceptible to <i>your</i> instructions.<br /> <br /> This is a power that builds on the level of Dominate that lets you set triggers for all the other Dominate powers that can play out without your direct involvement; intricate domino chains of mortal conduits for your Beast's commands are still best suited to locales you've set up beforehand, at least as far as a two-Experience Devotion is concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T12:06:57-07:00","id":1226870,"title":"","content":"oh curious? How effective do you think Apple of eden would be at creating hunter's<br /> <br /> if the citys government is oppressive and you want to see it overthrown?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T14:14:57-07:00","id":1226926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1226870#post1226870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> oh curious? How effective do you think Apple of eden would be at creating hunter's<br /> <br /> if the citys government is oppressive and you want to see it overthrown?</div> </div> </div> </div>0 to 100% effective. It depends entirely on the mindset of the person eating the apple. You'd need a lot of apples to get enough people to overthrow a city government, unless it was some feudal era city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T14:20:09-07:00","id":1226929,"title":"","content":"oh sorry by city's government meant the court of local kindred.<br /> <br /> <br /> Think Im right that its a fair way to set things in motion. (Only thing is you need to make sure they dont see you)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T14:32:19-07:00","id":1226938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1226929#post1226929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh sorry by city's government meant the court of local kindred.<br /> <br /> Think Im right that its a fair way to set things in motion. (Only thing is you need to make sure they dont see you)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's about as likely as ghouls being used to take over the domain. Which, again, goes from 0 to 100% likely depending on the apple-eaters and who's directing them. One person finding out someone is a vampire does not automatically mean they're going to kill that vampire, or that the vampire has any bearing on the power structure of the domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T14:40:07-07:00","id":1226939,"title":"","content":"didnt say it was perfect but potentialy effective.<br /> <br /> then again, the apples could be a boon to those who allready follow the code if a Kindred decided to give them to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T11:13:23-07:00","id":1227177,"title":"","content":"I remember reading way back in 1st Edition (either in Vampire the Requiem or Hunter The Vigil, I don't exactly recall) that snake venom was particularly nasty to vampires because it caused lethal damage and snake venom was notorious for burning away Vitae.<br /> <br /> Is this still the case in 2e? How do vampires react to snake venom? Does snake venom do lethal or just bashing damage to vampires in 2e? Does it burn away their Vitae or not?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>And as a follow up question: When a Gangrel decides to shapeshift into a viper with Protean, does the Gangrel in viper form also inflict venom with his bites like real snakes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-13-2018, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T11:51:18-07:00","id":1227189,"title":"","content":"It's in Requiem's core.<br /> <br /> It would probably just do bashing, now, but still dissolve Vitae one per dot of damage. It was only some venoms that attack the blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as a follow up question: When a Gangrel decides to shapeshift into a viper with Protean, does the Gangrel in viper form also inflict venom with his bites like real snakes? </div> </div> </div>It says you can gain Merits based on Storyteller discretion, I figure it's up to the Storyteller but can't really see a reason not to. It's not as if you're gaining a unique ability far beyond the ken of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-13-2018, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T13:58:11-07:00","id":1227221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">What happens if a vampire feeds on an intoxicated mortal?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The vampire suffers the effects of the drug. The vampire may remove these effects by spending one Vitae, but could conceivably be too intoxicated to concentrate enough to do so.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Poisons not specifically harmful to Kindred follow the same rules as drugs. A Storyteller may choose to make an exception for poisons which break down cellular structure, but that\u2019s at her own discretion.</span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div>Per the FAQ, this is how poisons work on Kindred now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T15:53:18-07:00","id":1227256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227221#post1227221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Per the FAQ, this is how poisons work on Kindred now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough, but when a vampire suffers the effect of a venom, does he get lethal damage like mortals or bashing because vampires typically downgrade lethal to bashing unless otherwise specified? Sounds like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> thinks it should be bashing and my gut feeling says the same, but I want to double check to make sure.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that the &quot;snake venom dissolves Vitae&quot; clause from 1e is not carried over to 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T16:06:27-07:00","id":1227261,"title":"","content":"oh curious anything Im missing for why a high humanity Revenant wouldnt take a bout of torpor every now and then to help cut down on hunting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T16:08:23-07:00","id":1227263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227261#post1227261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious anything Im missing for why a high humanity Revenant wouldnt take a bout of torpor every now and then to help cut down on hunting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because each time you go in torpor you encounter a Breaking Point until you drop below Humanity 6.<br /> <br /> Besides, what difference does it make to a revenant? Why would a revenant care whether he sleeps 1 day, 1 month or 1 year between each night? If anything, going in Torpor will make unlife even worse, because Torpor is not a pleasant experience. It's not like you're just sleeping like a human. A vampire or revenant in Torpor has all kinds of fucked up nightmares that won't stop until he wakes up again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-13-2018, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T17:26:28-07:00","id":1227278,"title":"","content":"Hemotoxin is the IRL venom that destroys blood and it's most common in vipers I believe. I would probably make it destroy Vitae point for point on a vamp instead of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T19:58:41-07:00","id":1227326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227256#post1227256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough, but when a vampire suffers the effect of a venom, does he get lethal damage like mortals or bashing because vampires typically downgrade lethal to bashing unless otherwise specified? Sounds like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> thinks it should be bashing and my gut feeling says the same, but I want to double check to make sure.<br /> <br /> Does this mean that the &quot;snake venom dissolves Vitae&quot; clause from 1e is not carried over to 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe they would downgrade the damage to bashing because if a mortal would take lethal damage they would take bashing damage is the general rule of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T20:26:33-07:00","id":1227333,"title":"","content":"in half damned it Said the Mikhalli had the discipline of Bereschligost mechanically identical to Chary.<br /> <br /> Also says that Dhampir's ghoul's and other kindred ajacent beings some times demonstrate Chary<br /> <br /> <br /> but NO ONE but a revenant has any use for first dot of Chary even if they could learn it and several others too.<br /> <br /> is this an &quot;Oops!&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-13T20:40:25-07:00","id":1227335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227333#post1227333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but NO ONE but a revenant has any use for first dot of Chary even if they could learn it and several others too.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to their clan curse they have some odd sleeping schedules that might make it worth having. Especially considering the more competitive atmosphere and that those they embrace may be blood-hungry revenants that might try to take advantage during daysleep or longer torpor, such as across a harsh winter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T07:42:10-07:00","id":1227434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227263#post1227263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because each time you go in torpor you encounter a Breaking Point until you drop below Humanity 6.<br /> <br /> Besides, what difference does it make to a revenant? Why would a revenant care whether he sleeps 1 day, 1 month or 1 year between each night? If anything, going in Torpor will make unlife even worse, because Torpor is not a pleasant experience. It's not like you're just sleeping like a human. A vampire or revenant in Torpor has all kinds of fucked up nightmares that won't stop until he wakes up again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> fair enough<br /> <br /> Is the torpor nightmares thing the reason to not just stake prisoner's why the invictus use the oath of the model prisoner?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T08:49:23-07:00","id":1227445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227434#post1227434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the torpor nightmares thing the reason to not just stake prisoner's why the invictus use the oath of the model prisoner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes someone who's punished is useful to keep around and active. For instance someone who may have betrayed the Invictus, but is willing to turn on their conspirators. If they're staked, they're a non-entity, but if they're up and about they can tell you who they were working with.<br /> <br /> Plus it allows the Invictus to appear to be gracious and merciful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T08:54:10-07:00","id":1227447,"title":"","content":"a carthian or acolyte?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],