/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T10:00:11-07:00","id":1227460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227459#post1227459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can Strix possess someone who's been staked?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Blood &amp; Smoke, p205, 'Notably, as the joined entity uses the Strix\u2019s banes and the victim is already in torpor, staking does not have any effect beyond the physical damage inflicted'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:00:01-07:00","id":1227468,"title":"","content":"oh? Coil of the wyrm? Any reason for someone wanting to make a berserker focused on the coil to pick a clan other then Gangrel<br /> <br /> The claws from protean are a HUGE boon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:13:26-07:00","id":1227471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227468#post1227468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh? Coil of the wyrm? Any reason for someone wanting to make a berserker focused on the coil to pick a clan other then Gangrel<br /> <br /> The claws from protean are a HUGE boon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everyone wants to be Gangrel, and since it's not generally a hack and slash game increasing killing power isn't always the highest priority.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:15:15-07:00","id":1227473,"title":"","content":"for someone with Coil of the wyrm? iif thats part of your concept a reason to go for any other clan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T11:27:36-07:00","id":1227478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227473#post1227473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for someone with Coil of the wyrm? iif thats part of your concept a reason to go for any other clan?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a circular logic. Yes, if you want to play a Gangrel with Coil of the Wyrm, you should pick Gangrel. But not everyone wants to be Gangrel, and the coil is available to every clan, so you can be other clans. Doing Aggravated damage is not the end-all be all of the game, and there are other methods to do it to vampires, having the coils control of the Beast implies a vampire could be less psychologically vulnerable to fire, for instance, and you could use it as a weapon. Or you could just do Lethal, or Bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T12:23:33-07:00","id":1227493,"title":"","content":"is their a reason to use the coil for anything but a combat monster?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T12:29:24-07:00","id":1227495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227493#post1227493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is their a reason to use the coil for anything but a combat monster?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be worth it solely for the increased ability to control the Beast, rather than being controlled by it.<br /> <br /> You ask a lot of questions, some which might already have answers in the text. If you want to talk to people or get answers at a faster, more chatlike pace, there's a Chronicles of Darkness Discord server that has a Vampire the Requiem channel (and channels for every other game). I think you can reach it <a href=\"https://discord.me/cofd\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T13:10:22-07:00","id":1227503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227493#post1227493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is their a reason to use the coil for anything but a combat monster?</div> </div> </div> </div>The second dot enhances your predatory aura and your Kindred senses when you're in frenzy after the first dot lets you declare a frenzy for any simple goal. The predatory aura is one of the simplest ways for a vampire to regain Willpower and Kindred senses directly help you track people down. If you're making a character with a strong attachment to a Haven or Feeding Grounds it directly benefits that kind of territorial character concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does the Auspex multiplier for Kindred senses apply to all its ranges or just the scent-based range?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T14:06:26-07:00","id":1227516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227503#post1227503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The predatory aura is one of the simplest ways for a vampire to regain Willpower</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't see how. If there's something I've missed it'd be very helpful for my Kerberos character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T14:10:04-07:00","id":1227517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227516#post1227516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't see how. If there's something I've missed it'd be very helpful for my Kerberos character.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1218397-advice-on-gauging-the-strengths-and-weaknesses-between-splats?p=1218507#post1218507\">Lowered exceptional threshold</a> from all three Conditions it can impose means easy Inspired for playing into those weaknesses, especially with the +2 bonus the vampire gets within the scene to pursue those drives. Combine this with the fact that it costs nothing to use the aura against mortals, and\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T14:19:50-07:00","id":1227522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227503#post1227503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Auspex multiplier for Kindred senses apply to all its ranges or just the scent-based range?</div> </div> </div> </div>It really looks like it's just the scenting blood range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T14:42:31-07:00","id":1227526,"title":"","content":"does a vessel who's cooperation is procured through dominate gain the Swooning or scarred condition, since the feeding isnt violent, but is probaly very scary regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T15:00:02-07:00","id":1227532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227526#post1227526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does a vessel who's cooperation is procured through dominate gain the Swooning or scarred condition, since the feeding isnt violent, but is probaly very scary regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say it depends entirely on the situation. But if the feeding is non-violent it will likely result in the person getting the Swooning condition. But since he's already Mesmerized/Dominated as well, the Swooning won't really add much. Depending on how your storyteller rules things, the Swooning will either disappear at the end of the scene or stay on the victim for a while. In that case the Swooning condition might be beneficial later down the line, but it's not really going to be of much help to you during the scene the victim is Mesmerized/Dominated, since those conditions are already better than Swooning.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Which leads me to a question related to this.<br /> <br /> Usually the Mesmerized/Dominated condition breaks when the victim suffers lethal or bashing damage greater than her Stamina attribute. Does this include damage taken from feeding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-14-2018, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T15:09:00-07:00","id":1227534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227532#post1227532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually the Mesmerized/Dominated condition breaks when the victim suffers lethal or bashing damage greater than her Stamina attribute. Does this include damage taken from feeding?</div> </div> </div> </div>In all likelihood, given that it would be very strange for there not to be an exception built into those Conditions if there were supposed to be one and they're by no means the only mechanics based on that threshold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T18:34:26-07:00","id":1227572,"title":"","content":"Feeding more than someone's Stamina attribute gives the Drained condition, which can easily be life-threatening for a mortal. I think it certainly fits for breaking those other Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T19:05:32-07:00","id":1227574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227572#post1227572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feeding more than someone's Stamina attribute gives the Drained condition, which can easily be life-threatening for a mortal. I think it certainly fits for breaking those other Conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a really good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T11:41:38-07:00","id":1227707,"title":"","content":"Questions about touchstones:<br /> <br /> 1. What does getting detached from a touchstone mean? Does your character stop caring about that touchstone altogether, or does she still care but simply not gain the benefits from the touchstone anymore?<br /> <br /> Say for example my character has his human ex-girlfriend as a touchstone attached to humanity 6, and my character drops to humanity 5, what happens from a narrative point of view? Does he stop caring about his ex-girlfriend altogether? Or does he still care about her but to a lesser degree? Or does his relationship with his ex-girlfriend become more toxic? What happens?<br /> <br /> 2. What happens if a touchstone starts acting in a way that isn't in line with what you need from that touchstone?<br /> <br /> To use the ex-girlfriend as an example again: Say my character has his ex-girlfriend as his touchstone because she was always the rock in the ocean to him. She had a solid head on her shoulders and knew that was right not just for herself but for my character as well. She kept him straight. After the embrace, she kept reminding him why he should care about his humanity, and humanity as a whole. But now this ex-girlfriend has changed. She became a reckless junky who sells her body to the highest bidder just so she can get enough money for her next hit. These days she isn't above pick-pocketing and thieving to get what she needs. She's no longer the ex-girlfriend my character fell in love with, she is no longer the person he wanted or needed. He can't stand what she has become. Her current behavior just makes him hate her, it makes him hate himself and it makes him just not care anymore. What consequences does this have from a mechanical point of view? Does my character lose his touchstone? Does she stop being a touchstone for him? What happens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T12:35:17-07:00","id":1227721,"title":"","content":"1. It could be narrated any number of ways short of death or destruction of the touchstone to explain why they don't interact. The ex moved out of state and acquired a new significant other. The vampire got a status increase/decrease and is spending time to prove their worth. The great grandmother's wedding ring is stored in a safety deposit box and the bank employee who was letting in the vampire at night doesn't work there anymore and the vampire hasn't gotten around to retrieving it or ensnaring another bank employee to let them inside at night.<br /> <br /> 2. That's really not possible for inanimate touchstones (unless the vampire's grip on reality is tenuous) but it could be cause for detachment in cases of people touchstones.<br /> <br /> Per your example, that sounds like your ST screwing around with your touchstone to stir up drama appropriate to touchstones. Mechanically as long as the vampire's Humanity rating stays at the correct level, and the character interacts with her (maybe to enable her behavior, maybe to try and straighten her out) it counts as attached. Ceasing to interact with her counts as detached.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-15-2018, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T12:39:41-07:00","id":1227724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227721#post1227721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. It could be narrated any number of ways short of death or destruction of the touchstone to explain why they don't interact.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Detached</i> Touchstones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T12:50:15-07:00","id":1227728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227724#post1227724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Detached</i> Touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is what the previous poster's inquiry pertained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T13:13:24-07:00","id":1227735,"title":"","content":"Ah. My mistake. I misread. Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T18:21:14-07:00","id":1227794,"title":"","content":"More touchstone questions:<br /> <br /> 1. When a touchstone gets detached because of humanity loss, does the vampire still care about that touchstone? Would a vampire of humanity 4 still interact with the detached touchstones next to his humanity 6 and 5 dots,.or only his newest touchstone attached to his humanity 4 dot?<br /> <br /> 2. What happens when a detaches touchstone dies? Should the vampire care? Would the vampire care under normal circumstances?<br /> <br /> 3. When my humanity 6 touchstone dies, do I have to replace it before I can buy new touchstones for my lower humanity dots? Why would a Kindred replace a detached touchstone (e.g. getting a new touchstone next to humanity 6 while his current humanity is 4) from a narrative perspective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-15-2018, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T18:36:51-07:00","id":1227798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227794#post1227794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. When a touchstone gets detached because of humanity loss, does the vampire still care about that touchstone? Would a vampire of humanity 4 still interact with the detached touchstones next to his humanity 6 and 5 dots,.or only his newest touchstone attached to his humanity 4 dot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Touchstones having the relation they do with detachment, I think it's a safe bet that a Touchstone ceasing to be attached just means the relationship is no longer strong enough to do more than justify the vampire's continued activity \u2014 they still care about them (they're still an Anchor), but they've stopped being able to draw upon that connection to reinforce their ability to keep up the practice of relating to humans as more than food.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. When my humanity 6 touchstone dies, do I have to replace it before I can buy new touchstones for my lower humanity dots? Why would a Kindred replace a detached touchstone (e.g. getting a new touchstone next to humanity 6 while his current humanity is 4) from a narrative perspective? </div> </div> </div>The Touchstone Merit represents additional things that your character treats as Anchors and can use to vent troublesome frenzy-related Conditions \u2014 it doesn't matter that having dinner your high school sweetheart twice a month stopped helping you keep from backsliding into monstrosity years ago, she's still a confidante and a source of comfort when you actually spend that time with her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T19:15:54-07:00","id":1227801,"title":"","content":"1. Yes. But from a mechanical standpoint they don't get any benefit for doing so. Narratively they may see each other just as frequently but the vampire doesn't quite view the relationship the same way. Or maybe they just distance themselves a bit more to avoid hurting the touchstone. Or maybe after some time and xp expenditure, the detached touchstone attaches at a lower Humanity level. <br /> <br /> 2. Depends on the ST. It may invoke a Humanity check the same as an attached touchstone death or destruction. Would they care? Maybe? It depends on their relationship at the time. I tend to take a hands off approach in telling players how their character should feel and react unless it's a complete 180 or stupidly inappropriate.<br /> <br /> 3. That's up to your ST how that plays out mechanically. (I recommend you have your character prepare for a stint in torpor unless you have a backup touchstone lined up to replace it.) I personally find the notion of vampires having more than two active touchstones unless they're family members to stretch credibility because of the time investiture required to maintain them plus hunting plus whatever vampire centric clan/city/covenant melodrama they're pursuing at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T20:35:12-07:00","id":1227808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227801#post1227801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Yes. But from a mechanical standpoint they don't get any benefit for doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, they <i>do</i>, it's just that the mechanical benefits are entirely separate from bolstering your Detachment rolls \u2014 you still get Willpower for fighting to keep up the relationship with them, they can still talk you down from frenzy, making meaningful connections with them still helps you resolve Conditions that mess with your ability to resist frenzy, and they still count as your Touchstones in all the ways your clan banes care about. They just aren't giving you a bonus die or two on a specific type of roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T20:43:34-07:00","id":1227809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227808#post1227808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, they <i>do</i>, it's just that the mechanical benefits are entirely separate from bolstering your Detachment rolls \u2014 you still get Willpower for fighting to keep up the relationship with them, they can still talk you down from frenzy, making meaningful connections with them still helps you resolve Conditions that mess with your ability to resist frenzy, and they still count as your Touchstones in all the ways your clan banes care about. They just aren't giving you a bonus die or two on a specific type of roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know this. That's super useful information. Nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T20:51:50-07:00","id":1227810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227801#post1227801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Yes. But from a mechanical standpoint they don't get any benefit for doing so. Narratively they may see each other just as frequently but the vampire doesn't quite view the relationship the same way. Or maybe they just distance themselves a bit more to avoid hurting the touchstone. Or maybe after some time and xp expenditure, the detached touchstone attaches at a lower Humanity level. <br /> <br /> 2. Depends on the ST. It may invoke a Humanity check the same as an attached touchstone death or destruction. Would they care? Maybe? It depends on their relationship at the time. I tend to take a hands off approach in telling players how their character should feel and react unless it's a complete 180 or stupidly inappropriate.<br /> <br /> 3. That's up to your ST how that plays out mechanically. (I recommend you have your character prepare for a stint in torpor unless you have a backup touchstone lined up to replace it.) I personally find the notion of vampires having more than two active touchstones unless they're family members to stretch credibility because of the time investiture required to maintain them plus hunting plus whatever vampire centric clan/city/covenant melodrama they're pursuing at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm not the player, I'm the ST. I was asking this for one of my players. But yeah I will have to talk about this with my player, but your feedback is welcome.<br /> <br /> What makes you say maintaining touchstones takes a lot of time and work? How much time should I expect my players to put into their touchstones? How much game time should it take up?<br /> <br /> Personally I'd be okay with my players visiting their touchstones on occasion, or perhaps more frequently when they're going through a personal crisis. I do plan on fucking with my player's touchstones, but only in tandem with the main narrative. For example when the players defeated their antagonist, the antagonist might retaliate by going after their touchstones. <br /> <br /> Sometimes during downtime or inbetween arcs I might set up a scene with the touchstone in the spotlights, highlighting the mundane problems the touchstone is going through (mundane compared to the player's problems).<br /> <br /> Do I have the right idea here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T21:39:19-07:00","id":1227812,"title":"","content":"Maintaining ANY meaningful relationship takes time and work. Showing up to binge watch television isn\u2019t meaningful. Add to the fact that most people are not up at all hours of the night, while vampires are only out at night. That means the vampire will never be there to pick them up after they blew a tire on the way to work, or meet for lunch, attend the kids\u2019 soccer games etc. help maintain the lawn ... it can quickly become a one-sided relationship and when that happens the touchstone is going to find other things to do.<br /> That\u2019s up to you how much game time and how you want to devote to it but if my player are investing in the merit, that means game time is going to include it. I personally don\u2019t use players\u2019 touchstones as vengeance/victim levers unless they specifically ask or they target others\u2019 touchstones. There\u2019s allies, mentors, proteges, sires, ghouls contacts etc. for rivals to target in retaliation. I use touchstone interactions for when players \u2018go solo\u2019 or split up or along with hunting scenes. Sometimes a session will be nothing but the players interacting with their respective touchstones, or training or studying with a mentor or attending a clan or covenant meeting the others can\u2019t attend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T23:36:27-07:00","id":1227821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227812#post1227812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maintaining ANY meaningful relationship takes time and work. Showing up to binge watch television isn\u2019t meaningful. Add to the fact that most people are not up at all hours of the night, while vampires are only out at night. That means the vampire will never be there to pick them up after they blew a tire on the way to work, or meet for lunch, attend the kids\u2019 soccer games etc. help maintain the lawn ... it can quickly become a one-sided relationship and when that happens the touchstone is going to find other things to do.<br /> That\u2019s up to you how much game time and how you want to devote to it but if my player are investing in the merit, that means game time is going to include it. I personally don\u2019t use players\u2019 touchstones as vengeance/victim levers unless they specifically ask or they target others\u2019 touchstones. There\u2019s allies, mentors, proteges, sires, ghouls contacts etc. for rivals to target in retaliation. I use touchstone interactions for when players \u2018go solo\u2019 or split up or along with hunting scenes. Sometimes a session will be nothing but the players interacting with their respective touchstones, or training or studying with a mentor or attending a clan or covenant meeting the others can\u2019t attend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't say I 100% agree there. My oldest and bestest friend is someone I see twice a month to once a week at most. Usually we just do whatever we feel like when we do see each other. Known the dude for 20+ years and our friendship is still going strong.<br /> <br /> It helps that in my game the players started as humans and their touchstones are relationships they already established during the human part of the game, so the relationship is already there, they just have to maintain it. How much of that happens &quot;on screen&quot; is something I kinda wanna leave up to them.<br /> <br /> Do you think using touchstones to get to players is too mean? I think it makes sense, of course if the antagonist in question has been able to learn about the players' touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T11:27:03-07:00","id":1227878,"title":"","content":"does Blood scourge need revisions? to make it work in a combat scene like say it clings to you till you choose to release it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T12:25:03-07:00","id":1227883,"title":"","content":"No, you create it when you need it. It isn't created at the ritual's completion. Though it should be specified whether or not it's a reflexive or an instant action to create the whip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T13:02:57-07:00","id":1227887,"title":"","content":"Personally I would have it as reflexive. I always thought of it as something as a surprise weapon so I'd say it be that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T13:16:42-07:00","id":1227889,"title":"","content":"ACK!!!! AM SO SORRY Had meant to ask about Blood Blight!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T09:32:47-07:00","id":1228054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1227821#post1227821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think using touchstones to get to players is too mean? I think it makes sense, of course if the antagonist in question has been able to learn about the players' touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not an issue of being \u201ctoo mean\u201d. As I said, if they start targetting others\u2019 touchstones (or if they throw them in the line of fire) then they can\u2019t consider theirs sacrosanct either. It\u2019s a matter of their purpose in the game isn\u2019t supposed to be \u201ctarget for rivals\u201d. They\u2019re supposed to be tools for vampires to retain their Humanity. Targetting touchstones is already borderline metagamey since Humanity is an abstract concept. Killing someone\u2019s wife or child in retaliation for an offense makes sense. Killing their high school rival or smashing their grandfather\u2019s watch or defacing the tombstone with their name on it to send them in torpor does not. Honestly things like \u201cpermanently scarring her face, crushing limbs\u201d (to result in a -2 reduction to Presence or Strength or Dexterity dots) makes more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-17-2018, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T10:34:39-07:00","id":1228065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228054#post1228054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not an issue of being \u201ctoo mean\u201d. As I said, if they start targetting others\u2019 touchstones (or if they throw them in the line of fire) then they can\u2019t consider theirs sacrosanct either. It\u2019s a matter of their purpose in the game isn\u2019t supposed to be \u201ctarget for rivals\u201d. They\u2019re supposed to be tools for vampires to retain their Humanity. Targetting touchstones is already borderline metagamey since Humanity is an abstract concept. Killing someone\u2019s wife or child in retaliation for an offense makes sense. Killing their high school rival or smashing their grandfather\u2019s watch or defacing the tombstone with their name on it to send them in torpor does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring Auspex. Auspex can potentially tell you the significance of those persons and objects. But yeah, if a player doesn't wants the Touchstone messed with terminally, True Friend is a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T16:48:07-07:00","id":1228144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228054#post1228054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a matter of their purpose in the game isn\u2019t supposed to be \u201ctarget for rivals\u201d. They\u2019re supposed to be tools for vampires to retain their Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire's Touchstone mechanics specifically include &quot;think about how the character might lose this relationship and what they might do when it is threatened.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Targetting touchstones is already borderline metagamey since Humanity is an abstract concept. Killing someone\u2019s wife or child in retaliation for an offense makes sense. Killing their high school rival or smashing their grandfather\u2019s watch or defacing the tombstone with their name on it to send them in torpor does not. </div> </div> </div>Humanity being an abstract concept doesn't make the maintenance of a character's relationship to their Touchstone exist in purely abstract terms. You're one of a handful of immortals in the city and your waking hours are limited \u2014 you think nobody's going to notice that you visit the graveyard every couple of weeks or hang out every Monday night with the guy who beat you to the QB spot or never let that tacky old showpiece out of your sight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T17:51:33-07:00","id":1228427,"title":"","content":"Questions re: Ordo Dracul Merits in Secrets of the Covenants, and Ordo Lore in 2e. Ideally for a Dev/Freelancer since these are somewhat &quot;canon&quot; questions.<br /> <br /> * Rites of the Impaled has Sworn as a Prerequisite, but the Impaled in 1e were not a subset of the Sworn. Can you confirm that this has officially changed in the 2e Ordo? The Impaled were a seperate 'sub-faction' that ostensibly included non-Sworn in 1e.<br /> <br /> * Twilight Judge does <b>not</b> have Sworn as a Prerequisite, but in 1e all Twilight Judges were members of the Sworn of the Dying Light. Can you confirm this has officially changed in the 2e Ordo?<br /> <br /> * Do you still consider the contents &quot;Rites of the Dragon&quot; - the published, available work by Greg Stolze - to be (mostly) the canonical Rites of the Dragon for 2e, with the possible exceptions of places in which game mechanics (Coil of Hunger vs Mystery of the Voivode) have presented different traditional Mysteries?<br /> <br /> * Has the concept of the different &quot;Rites&quot; - Damacene, Philadelphian, Wallachian, etc - been kept from 1e to 2e within the Ordo? Is the Genius/Voivode of SotC involved in the Philadelphian Rite's establishment, if so? <br /> <br /> * In 1e Ordo Dracul, the Kogaion was responsible for the maintenance of the Wyrm's Nest in a city. Is this still a large part of their &quot;job description&quot;, or is it being used as a more generic &quot;local covenant leader&quot; title in 2e?<br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","user":"wampa","date":". 06-19-2018, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T11:41:22-07:00","id":1228634,"title":"","content":"My corrected Question is how's the cruac Ritual blood blight work, does it HANG , does it need to be performed right in front of someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T12:17:45-07:00","id":1228642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228634#post1228634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My corrected Question is how's the cruac Ritual blood blight work, does it HANG , does it need to be performed right in front of someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 152, 'The subject of a blood ritual does not need to be present for the ritual to take effect,'<br /> <br /> When you get the successes, it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T13:10:21-07:00","id":1228658,"title":"","content":"Is &quot;Protect little Johnny?&quot; A valid goal for riding the wave?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T13:18:11-07:00","id":1228662,"title":"","content":"Depends on the frenzy provocation. If Johnny is insulting the vampire in question then no. If Johnny is being harassed/seduced by Random Asshole, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T13:54:25-07:00","id":1228674,"title":"","content":"would that exempt him from being attacked?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T14:12:04-07:00","id":1228677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228674#post1228674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would that exempt him from being attacked?</div> </div> </div> </div>P104, 'While frenzied, the vampire does everything in her power to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires. She does so with immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon. If there\u2019s someone in the way, she throws him or decks him.'<br /> <br /> If Johnny gets in the way Johnny might get attacked. If Johnny's a touchstone, they might be able to talk the vampire down, but they wouldn't want to stand in the vampire's path while doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T15:06:55-07:00","id":1228688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228658#post1228658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is &quot;Protect little Johnny?&quot; A valid goal for riding the wave?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Short answer is &quot;sort of&quot;. You've still got to go with the core idea of frenzy, but you can execute it in a way that protects Johnny.<br /> <br /> Remember that there are three kinds of frenzy: hunger, anger, and fear.<br /> <br /> Now, you're in hunger frenzy, and Johnny's a tasty looking sort, but you're not all alone in the wilderness with him - you can ride the wave to redirect that hunger frenzy to someone else! If he's the only thing for miles and miles around though, you're probably pretty screwed - you need to avoid frenzy there, not ride the wave.<br /> <br /> If you're in anger frenzy, the inherent idea of the frenzy should still be offensive - &quot;hurt those guys who were making fun of me.&quot; If you're Riding the Wave, you can keep tearing the **** out of whichever one of them is trying to punch your friend Johnny in the face at any given moment. If you're just frenzying, maybe you just pick the guy closest to you and poor Johnny is on his own against those two chaps with the baseball bats. If Johnny has just said something terrible mean to you that *caused* the anger frenzy, you can Ride the Wave to redirect that anger frenzy to the local architecture rather than ripping Johnny's face off. But the &quot;goal&quot; of riding the wave is &quot;sate the beast with property damage rather than personnel damage.&quot; You're redirecting that anger by Riding the Wave.<br /> <br /> If you're in fear frenzy, Riding the Wave might let you pick up Johnny as you run away, but you've still gotta GTFO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2853,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","user":"wampa","date":". 06-19-2018, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T15:48:55-07:00","id":1228696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wampa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228688#post1228688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short answer is &quot;sort of&quot;. You've still got to go with the core idea of frenzy, but you can execute it in a way that protects Johnny.<br /> <br /> Remember that there are three kinds of frenzy: hunger, anger, and fear.<br /> <br /> Now, you're in hunger frenzy, and Johnny's a tasty looking sort, but you're not all alone in the wilderness with him - you can ride the wave to redirect that hunger frenzy to someone else! If he's the only thing for miles and miles around though, you're probably pretty screwed - you need to avoid frenzy there, not ride the wave.<br /> <br /> If you're in anger frenzy, the inherent idea of the frenzy should still be offensive - &quot;hurt those guys who were making fun of me.&quot; If you're Riding the Wave, you can keep tearing the **** out of whichever one of them is trying to punch your friend Johnny in the face at any given moment. If you're just frenzying, maybe you just pick the guy closest to you and poor Johnny is on his own against those two chaps with the baseball bats. If Johnny has just said something terrible mean to you that *caused* the anger frenzy, you can Ride the Wave to redirect that anger frenzy to the local architecture rather than ripping Johnny's face off. But the &quot;goal&quot; of riding the wave is &quot;sate the beast with property damage rather than personnel damage.&quot; You're redirecting that anger by Riding the Wave.<br /> <br /> If you're in fear frenzy, Riding the Wave might let you pick up Johnny as you run away, but you've still gotta GTFO.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a few things in your post that are no longer true. The different kinds of Frenzy are no longer distinguished from each other (though still common categories). Secondly, if you Ride the Wave you get to choose the goal. It doesn't have to be related to the Frenzy trigger at all. If you Frenzy because of starvation but manages to Ride the Wave, you can instead choose to absolutely demolish that chair instead. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228674#post1228674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would that exempt him from being attacked?</div> </div> </div> </div>If protecting Johnny is the goal, the Frenzied vampire won't attack him because doing so would be counter to the goal. If Johnny happens to be between the vampire and the threat, then the vampire might still grab and throw Johnny away, but only because it's preferable to Johnny being stabbed or whatever by the attacker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T18:02:10-07:00","id":1228716,"title":"","content":"Just wondering but has there ever been anything concrete on exactly when vampirism first came about. I pretty much know the rough dates for the main clans but I'm more wondering on exactly when the Curse as a thing started making people into vamps which I would take it would be around the time when the Strix first showed up. Now I doubt there is any info on that given Kindreds whole thing is it's vague history but I'm asking just to make sure because I'm trying to graph out whether the Strix and Kindred were around after or before the Uratha were born/humans first discovered magic. I figure the oldest splat are Beasts but the description of the ancient Strix in the core does paint the image that they were around since the beginning of humanity. I'm just wondering if that beginning is pre-Sundered World or after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T18:18:40-07:00","id":1228721,"title":"","content":"It's whenever the ST says vampires first came into being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T18:22:18-07:00","id":1228724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228721#post1228721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's whenever the ST says vampires first came into being.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought it be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T02:50:29-07:00","id":1228814,"title":"","content":"I've heard about a story in the Mekhet clan book (but personally never read) that's about a Mekhet reaching longer and longer back into vampire (or at least his Clan's) until he gets a vision of a blob of darkness in a cave. Doesn't really say anything about the time period, though, and at this rate it's a third hand account.<br /> The oldest mentions of actual vampire history in the books comes from Ancient Mysteries/Bloodlines. If you have those books, look at the Egyptian and Babilonian sections and you might find the earliest confirmed date over 1000 BC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T04:01:04-07:00","id":1228824,"title":"","content":"Many different Versions.<br /> <br /> I Prefer the tale of the Amanotsukai from Circle of the Crone<br /> <br /> others may like &quot;Were here to tempt mortals&quot; <br /> <br /> others may think &quot;The strix came from some otherwhere, and created kindred, eventually some started to come into existence with some degree of humanity left&quot; <br /> <br /> Others may think &quot;someone made a pact with Satan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T10:10:03-07:00","id":1228885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228814#post1228814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard about a story in the Mekhet clan book (but personally never read) that's about a Mekhet reaching longer and longer back into vampire (or at least his Clan's) until he gets a vision of a blob of darkness in a cave. Doesn't really say anything about the time period, though, and at this rate it's a third hand account.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relevants:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether Mekhet or not, the vampire playing this piece may re-live the experiences of any <u>destroyed</u> Mekhet vampire existing before Chantal DeFay; if others are listening, they may find themselves sharing the hallucination. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wait in a cave; I am cold and alien and before words, and the voices outside show the Tall Ones, who with unfamiliar sounds deliberate over stopping for the night. I hiss and begin to croon. They need only walk into the shadow, my tentacles and blades will grasp them and embrace them and make them my food... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T10:28:42-07:00","id":1228894,"title":"","content":"We've had writers confirm that the Mekhet have a pre-human origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T12:00:19-07:00","id":1228928,"title":"","content":"So, I was reading the half damned book again, and I came across the sidebar about Ghouls and the Strix. It mentioned how Strix are less likely to possess ghouls because they still have a soul (I assume its because of the possess living embodiment being higher than the possess Kindred one), but it also mentions the protective layers of Viniculum. What exactly does that mean though? Sorry if this has been asked before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T12:59:31-07:00","id":1228939,"title":"","content":"oh the Cruac Ritual &quot;Donning the Beasts flesh&quot; from secrets of the covenants how longs the transformation last, is it a one time only thing, it says nothing about crumbling to dust...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-20T22:05:31-07:00","id":1229079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228928#post1228928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was reading the half damned book again, and I came across the sidebar about Ghouls and the Strix. It mentioned how Strix are less likely to possess ghouls because they still have a soul (I assume its because of the possess living embodiment being higher than the possess Kindred one)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah though fuck if I know where that's from, every book seems to go back and forth on whether something has a soul and what that means. The core is pretty clear on them having souls, the 'vampires have no souls' thing seems to be part of Masquerade. Mechanically it's just more difficult to Possess or Synthesize with Living compared to vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but it also mentions the protective layers of Viniculum. What exactly does that mean though? Sorry if this has been asked before. </div> </div> </div>I think it's just a flowery description of what a ghoul is. They are arguably defined by their Vinculum and its part of what keeps them ghouls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1228939#post1228939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh the Cruac Ritual &quot;Donning the Beasts flesh&quot; from secrets of the covenants how longs the transformation last, is it a one time only thing, it says nothing about crumbling to dust...</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks more indefinite. I'd probably have it wear off during Daysleep, though, as you do turn to normal. It looks like it's based on Beast's Skin in the core, which is also indefinite, but presumably the hide doesn't just poof when you're done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T00:17:37-07:00","id":1229101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229079#post1229079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's just a flowery description of what a ghoul is. They are arguably defined by their Vinculum and its part of what keeps them ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I get it. A strix couldn't expend vitae to keep the body's ghoulish nature going, so they would have serve a kindred to remain within the ghoul because some kindred is gonna figure out something's up when this one ghoul's regents keep dying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T07:47:25-07:00","id":1229150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229079#post1229079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It looks more indefinite. I'd probably have it wear off during Daysleep, though, as you do turn to normal. It looks like it's based on Beast's Skin in the core, which is also indefinite, but presumably the hide doesn't just poof when you're done.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Think it would need to be reenchanted? a fair question I think.<br /> <br /> oh?<br /> <br /> What disciplines work in frenzy, know that Protean Vigor Fortitude and Celerity do, does Nightmare work? or obfuscate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 06-21-2018, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T22:51:45-07:00","id":1229308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229150#post1229150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think it would need to be reenchanted? a fair question I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to like magic objects, and I'd allow it to be kept around. Theoretically you could have a blood sorcerer with a closet full of them they could put on when they wanted. But it doesn't say anything about it as far as I can tell so another ST could justify having it last until sunup or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What disciplines work in frenzy, know that Protean Vigor Fortitude and Celerity do, does Nightmare work? or obfuscate? </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's a list or that disciplines become unavailable when you frenzy. Frenzy is about immediate gratification, however, so more long-running things wouldn't (normally) make sense, like Conditioning, which takes a period of weeks. But I could see an angry vampire flipping on Majesty and turning a mob of humans into a weapon with which they flail away at, or a vampire using Dominate on someone given the right circumstances (something like Preacher, or a scene in Supernatural where some demons hand hunters a bottle of drain cleaner and tell them to drink it). There's a lot of ways a frenzy can go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-22-2018, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T07:14:11-07:00","id":1229361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229308#post1229308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to like magic objects, and I'd allow it to be kept around. Theoretically you could have a blood sorcerer with a closet full of them they could put on when they wanted. But it doesn't say anything about it as far as I can tell so another ST could justify having it last until sunup or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What about Giving them to kindred allies or subordinates as boons?<br /> <br /> Makes a heck of a 'bone' to toss a revenant something to let them fly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229308#post1229308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's a list or that disciplines become unavailable when you frenzy. Frenzy is about immediate gratification, however, so more long-running things wouldn't (normally) make sense, like Conditioning, which takes a period of weeks. But I could see an angry vampire flipping on Majesty and turning a mob of humans into a weapon with which they flail away at, or a vampire using Dominate on someone given the right circumstances (something like Preacher, or a scene in Supernatural where some demons hand hunters a bottle of drain cleaner and tell them to drink it). There's a lot of ways a frenzy can go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nightmare 5 would work in frenzy not seeing how lesser degrees of nightmare would if its in implanting a subtle phobia... Similarly Protean 1 doesnt work but could obfuscate let you slowly and deliberately 'stalk' someone? as opposed to a mad rush?<br /> <br /> Oh can weapons be used in frenzy? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 06-22-2018, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T07:40:28-07:00","id":1229366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229361#post1229361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmare 5 would work in frenzy not seeing how lesser degrees of nightmare would if its in implanting a subtle phobia... Similarly Protean 1 doesnt work but could obfuscate let you slowly and deliberately 'stalk' someone? as opposed to a mad rush?<br /> <br /> Oh can weapons be used in frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing subtle about Nightmare. If the goal of the Frenzy is to intimidate someone (especially if Riding the Wave) then all levels of Nightmare works.<br /> Protean 1 is a great way to hide. It also brings some protection. Perfect for escaping a more powerful opponent if they can't see you hide.<br /> It should be possible to use weapons in Frenzy. The Beast uses the vampire's own Skills, so why not use a tool in combination with Weaponry if that leads to a better dice pool than Brawl?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T07:45:14-07:00","id":1229367,"title":"","content":"oh if I have &quot;Smite The Heretics!!!&quot; or &quot;Defend the temple!!!&quot; As my goal riding the wave, does that shield my comrades?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 06-22-2018, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T07:55:14-07:00","id":1229369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229361#post1229361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Giving them to kindred allies or subordinates as boons?<br /> <br /> Makes a heck of a 'bone' to toss a revenant something to let them fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Secrets of the Covenants, p184, 'Donning the Beast\u2019s Flesh allows the Acolyte to skin a beast, and craft a mystical hood, cloak, mask, or other article of clothing from its flesh. When <i><b>any vampire</b></i> dons the accessory, he can take the rough shape of the animal with the expenditure of a point of Vitae and three turns of transformation.'<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine. It's pretty clear that any vampire can wear it. You could give it as a gift to the Prince, for instance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh can weapons be used in frenzy? </div> </div> </div>Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">oh if I have &quot;Smite The Heretics!!!&quot; As my goal riding the wave, does that shield my comrades?</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> If you're riding the wave you can choose whatever targets you want. So it shields them if you want.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T11:04:55-07:00","id":1229620,"title":"","content":"Mass Embrace 2 questions.<br /> <br /> 1 Can it be used on behalf of another kindred letting them embrace a whole slew of new kindred (Its the ONLY WAY a kindred Can create a brood in 2nd edition Was just reading the Coteries book)<br /> <br /> 2 Can a Revenant be uplifted as part of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T11:39:30-07:00","id":1229622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229620#post1229620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Can it be used on behalf of another kindred letting them embrace a whole slew of new kindred (Its the ONLY WAY a kindred Can create a brood in 2nd edition Was just reading the Coteries book)<br /> <br /> 2 Can a Revenant be uplifted as part of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason to think so. The Mass Embrace specifically calls out the Dragon who performs the Scale as the one who Embraces. And there's no reason to think it would uplift revenants.<br /> <br /> Though just making a new Scale that does that seems like it would be easy, from a mechanical standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T11:53:45-07:00","id":1229628,"title":"","content":"The book says only the Dragon can perform Mass Embrace, but Scales are just learned procedures and not internalised abilities. I think anyone (that meet other specific prerequisites, like the ability to Embrace in this case) should be able to perform Scales as long as someone who knows the Scale helps them.<br /> <br /> Uplifting Revenants is not the same as Embracing a human, so no alternative techniques to Embracing people should work on uplifting humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T12:22:51-07:00","id":1229635,"title":"","content":"Think Im wrong on it being ONLY wayh to make a brood in 2nd edition, without becoming a Draugr?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T13:57:32-07:00","id":1229645,"title":"","content":"Can you take a bane for the breaking point of creating a Scale? If so, is it tied to an specific level of humanity or whenever/wherever it applies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24344-zaser321","name":"zaser321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T14:11:43-07:00","id":1229647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229635#post1229635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think Im wrong on it being ONLY wayh to make a brood in 2nd edition, without becoming a Draugr?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know. There might be something in Dark Eras, but you seem to have access to the books. The game does encourage homebrewing, so you can add it in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zaser321</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229645#post1229645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you take a bane for the breaking point of creating a Scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>There doesn't seem to be a special qualifier for it. 'When losing Humanity, a character can take a bane and a Beat. If he does so, he becomes unable to lose Humanity from that particular breaking point again.' So yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If so, is it tied to an specific level of humanity or whenever/wherever it applies? </div> </div> </div>It would be tied to making a Scale. The banes tend to have effects based on Humanity, though, like, 'If she does not sleep with at least a handful of dirt from her region of death, all her dice pools are capped by her Humanity for the next night.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T15:20:17-07:00","id":1229663,"title":"","content":"OH? Question? How many people can be affected by Mass Embrace?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T16:23:45-07:00","id":1229669,"title":"","content":"Doing some planning for a Victorian-ish era campaign in the distant near future, and I got to wondering: What are gender roles like for Vampires during those days? On one hand, you'd get a lot of Embraces of people with a very defined view of gender roles for men and women, on the other hand most of those gender roles are rooted in things that fall away after the Embrace (fertility, being physically weaker, etc...) and it's going to be a bit hard for a male Invictus neonate to maintain that a female Alder should step aside and let the men like him handle the politics and running of the Covenant, isn't it? I'm sort of coming down on the side of &quot;gender roles are for the living&quot;, which could provide a fun sort of culture clash for the recently embraced (and of course you'd always get some stubborn holdouts who won't let go of the biases of life).<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T17:15:15-07:00","id":1229677,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1292_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1292\" data-vbnamecard=\"1292\">Unahim</a> If you can make a whole paragraph, and a story out of it, I don't think it's a simple question. Sounds good though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T17:17:43-07:00","id":1229680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229663#post1229663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OH? Question? How many people can be affected by Mass Embrace?</div> </div> </div> </div>There doesn't seem to be a limit, though reason suggests that given how long it takes and vampires not being known for daytime activeness there could be a cap at some point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229669#post1229669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doing some planning for a Victorian-ish era campaign in the distant near future, and I got to wondering: What are gender roles like for Vampires during those days? On one hand, you'd get a lot of Embraces of people with a very defined view of gender roles for men and women, on the other hand most of those gender roles are rooted in things that fall away after the Embrace (fertility, being physically weaker, etc...) and it's going to be a bit hard for a male Invictus neonate to maintain that a female Alder should step aside and let the men like him handle the politics and running of the Covenant, isn't it? I'm sort of coming down on the side of &quot;gender roles are for the living&quot;, which could provide a fun sort of culture clash for the recently embraced (and of course you'd always get some stubborn holdouts who won't let go of the biases of life).<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Undeath would be considered one of the great equalizers, especially since most embraces in that period would be done by vampires from older periods. But it's easy to imagine the more traditional groups like the Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum as attempting to force more traditional roles in things. It could be a good plot point or aspect of a setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T17:20:11-07:00","id":1229681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229677#post1229677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1292_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1292\" data-vbnamecard=\"1292\">Unahim</a> If you can make a whole paragraph, and a story out of it, I don't think it's a simple question. Sounds good though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I embellished it, but the core question is &quot;Do Vampire gender roles throughout history conform to those of humans?&quot; which seems simple enough ^^ Hard to judge exactly, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229680#post1229680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Undeath would be considered one of the great equalizers, especially since most embraces in that period would be done by vampires from older periods. But it's easy to imagine the more traditional groups like the Invictus and Lancea et Sanctum as attempting to force more traditional roles in things. It could be a good plot point or aspect of a setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, reading the Invictus book, there's such an emphasis on grooming the childe for rulership in his or her own right, as well as Embracing to get a potential asset, that Embracing women would become much rarer under strict gender norms, I think. After all, a woman would be unable to do any of the work that would make a childe most of use to you. They couldn't hold pretty much any political office within the Invictus aside from maybe Confessor then, either. They'd just be a drain, since all the tasks mortal society gave women in those days, Ghouls just do better, with less baggage.<br /> <br /> And the LS covenant book explicitly points out that some of the Dark Apostles were females, and that the Covenant therefore has always been surprisingly progressive in this respect. Here I find it easier than the Invictus scenario to imagine a domain where the leading Sanctified is a chauvinist and just blatantly ignores that part, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 06-23-2018, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T17:57:30-07:00","id":1229687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229681#post1229681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, reading the Invictus book, there's such an emphasis on grooming the childe for rulership in his or her own right, as well as Embracing to get a potential asset, that Embracing women would become much rarer under strict gender norms, I think. After all, a woman would be unable to do any of the work that would make a childe most of use to you. They couldn't hold pretty much any political office within the Invictus aside from maybe Confessor then, either. They'd just be a drain, since all the tasks mortal society gave women in those days, Ghouls just do better, with less baggage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is even if they're not in the forefront, a female vampire could still be useful. Vampires aren't exactly known for strict work ethic and being at the forefront of populist actions. They're behind the scenes manipulators. A drop of Vitae, a use of Dominate or Auspex or various other abilities and a woman vampire could have many men being complete slaves to them, even if they're not able to hold a 'real world' political office.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the LS covenant book explicitly points out that some of the Dark Apostles were females, and that the Covenant therefore has always been surprisingly progressive in this respect. Here I find it easier than the Invictus scenario to imagine a domain where the leading Sanctified is a chauvinist and just blatantly ignores that part, though. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I mean, presumably in your setting vampires didn't just spawn in the Victorian era on their own. At some point someone would see that there are older, more powerful, intelligent, and experienced vampires who are of a group humanity doesn't think well of. But if you're having sexism transfer over from humanity-to-vampirism, the act of joining a covenant wouldn't magick it away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T18:32:58-07:00","id":1229695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229647#post1229647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There doesn't seem to be a special qualifier for it. 'When losing Humanity, a character can take a bane and a Beat. If he does so, he becomes unable to lose Humanity from that particular breaking point again.' So yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>The breaking point for developing a Scale is an abstraction of what will in practice be a lot of different things \u2014 assuming that similar logic to diablerie not being removable holds for the much broader reminder-of-your-inhumanity of committing various degrees of monstrous behavior to twist your vampirism into one of a dozen different knots, I don't think a bane would meaningfully cover all five possible degrees of breaking points a Humanity 5+ character could suffer from Scale development.<br /> <br /> If you want to really lean into Cloistered Vampire R&amp;D, it might be worth allowing, but I don't foresee much good arising from letting a Dragon treat development of new Scales based on every level of the Coils as equivalent in metaphysical weight to &quot;learning a dot of Cr\u00faac&quot; would be for an Acolyte. As with that scenario, the more likely outcome is &quot;characters either desensitize themselves out of the threat range or put in the work to build their self-control back up&quot; \u2014 this is a process that takes weeks at best to complete and it's grounds for an immediate bump in Status; it doesn't really gain much from taking a bane.<br /> <br /> Being able to come up with new effects near-wholesale at the cost of breaking point rolls and committed resources is pretty much the Ordo's counterpart to &quot;Cr\u00faac stunts your Humanity and costs blood&quot; and &quot;Theban Sorcery calls for a certain degree of self-control and consumes ritual components to use&quot; and the main other variable-rank breaking points are diablerie and diceless feeding scenes, one of which explicitly can't be cored out with a bane per the FAQ and the other of which can arise from something as innocuous as playing to your Mask a lot; the sheer diversity of things &quot;developing a new Scale&quot; can entail in practice should probably not be treated as all the same thing from the purposes of the out-of-character decision to take a bane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T18:46:34-07:00","id":1229698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229695#post1229695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The breaking point for developing a Scale is an abstraction of what will in practice be a lot of different things \u2014 assuming that similar logic to diablerie not being removable holds for the much broader reminder-of-your-inhumanity of committing various degrees of monstrous behavior to twist your vampirism into one of a dozen different knots, I don't think a bane would meaningfully cover all five possible degrees of breaking points a Humanity 5+ character could suffer from Scale development.<br /> <br /> If you want to really lean into Cloistered Vampire R&amp;D, it might be worth allowing, but I don't foresee much good arising from letting a Dragon treat development of new Scales based on every level of the Coils as equivalent in metaphysical weight to &quot;learning a dot of Cr\u00faac&quot; would be for an Acolyte. As with that scenario, the more likely outcome is &quot;characters either desensitize themselves out of the threat range or put in the work to build their self-control back up&quot; \u2014 this is a process that takes weeks at best to complete and it's grounds for an immediate bump in Status; it doesn't really gain much from taking a bane.<br /> <br /> Being able to come up with new effects near-wholesale at the cost of breaking point rolls and committed resources is pretty much the Ordo's counterpart to &quot;Cr\u00faac stunts your Humanity and costs blood&quot; and &quot;Theban Sorcery calls for a certain degree of self-control and consumes ritual components to use&quot; and the main other variable-rank breaking points are diablerie and diceless feeding scenes, one of which explicitly can't be cored out with a bane per the FAQ and the other of which can arise from something as innocuous as playing to your Mask a lot; the sheer diversity of things &quot;developing a new Scale&quot; can entail in practice should probably not be treated as all the same thing from the purposes of the out-of-character decision to take a bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have to agree, it would be like a vamp with &quot;The Vast Dynasty&quot; wanting to take a bane for the embrace thus allowing him to embrace anyone he wanted for free... I shiver at the thought.<br /> <br /> <br /> In both cases though, its best not to have ANY banes at all then, as each bane takes a die from your degeneration rolls.<br /> <br /> A question? Can coil of Ziva add bonuses to creating a new scale?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 06-23-2018, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T20:27:06-07:00","id":1229720,"title":"","content":"Question:<br /> <br /> How does Lashing Out work against Awe (Majesty 1)? Do you simply roll your Lashing Out dice pool and if you get a success you are unaffected by Awe? Can the Daeva using Awe try to counter your Lashing Out with her own Predatory Aura? How does that work exactly?<br /> <br /> Since we're talking about Lashing Out. How does one use Lashing Out against someone using Obfuscate and when would you be allowed to use that? How would that exactly work and play out?<br /> <br /> <br /> You'd help me the most if you could give me an example scenario for both. Already much appreciated to whoever can help me get a better grip on these 2 situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T20:33:26-07:00","id":1229721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229698#post1229698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have to agree, it would be like a vamp with &quot;The Vast Dynasty&quot; wanting to take a bane for the embrace thus allowing him to embrace anyone he wanted for free... I shiver at the thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Performing the Embrace costs a Humanity dot, it's not lost from a Breaking Point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T20:37:40-07:00","id":1229725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229721#post1229721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Performing the Embrace costs a Humanity dot, it's not lost from a Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not if you have 5 dots of Coil of the Voivode <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-23T21:12:42-07:00","id":1229733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229720#post1229720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question:<br /> <br /> How does Lashing Out work against Awe (Majesty 1)? Do you simply roll your Lashing Out dice pool and if you get a success you are unaffected by Awe? Can the Daeva using Awe try to counter your Lashing Out with her own Predatory Aura? How does that work exactly?<br /> <br /> Since we're talking about Lashing Out. How does one use Lashing Out against someone using Obfuscate and when would you be allowed to use that? How would that exactly work and play out?<br /> <br /> <br /> You'd help me the most if you could give me an example scenario for both. Already much appreciated to whoever can help me get a better grip on these 2 situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>In both cases, go to the standard resolution options for lashing out \u2014 they either give ground and take flight or offer a counter-challenge to fight you off, and if you win then the relevant catch in the Discipline kicks in.<br /> <br /> The young Daeva turns on the charm, and the elder Haunt stands her ground and bares her fangs. The Serpent either answers the challenge (anteing some precious Willpower in the process) or excuses himself from her presence; if he makes the clash and loses it, he loses the social grease of his Discipline against her.<br /> <br /> The old Lord puts it all together from the transformed furniture and the missing doorways (and, most importantly, the knife imbedded in the wall) and declares some terms to the Shadow invading his Haven. The Mekhet responds in kind or backs down; if they can't measure up to the Ventrue's Beast, their attempt to keep their target off balance falls apart completely as their perceptual filters shatter.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu attempts to win a border dispute with their Savage neighbor in the expected way and engages the foundational power of their terrifying Discipline. The Gangrel gives ground or makes a move of her own; if the Haunt doesn't dignify the proposed spiritual arm-wrestling contest with a response, they've lost the advantage of being too scary to seriously attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T09:59:04-07:00","id":1230038,"title":"","content":"Can Pool of Forbidden Truths be used on behalf of another? or does it not show things that dont concern the performer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T12:51:47-07:00","id":1230088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1229720#post1229720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question:<br /> <br /> How does Lashing Out work against Awe (Majesty 1)? Do you simply roll your Lashing Out dice pool and if you get a success you are unaffected by Awe? Can the Daeva using Awe try to counter your Lashing Out with her own Predatory Aura? How does that work exactly?<br /> <br /> Since we're talking about Lashing Out. How does one use Lashing Out against someone using Obfuscate and when would you be allowed to use that? How would that exactly work and play out?<br /> <br /> <br /> You'd help me the most if you could give me an example scenario for both. Already much appreciated to whoever can help me get a better grip on these 2 situations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just keep in mind that one does not generally know that they have been hit by awe. It's not a power that one goes, &quot;Oh he is using awe again.&quot; But Lashing out is generally one of those visible things. People know you have done something or acted out in some way. So if you think they are using awe and they werent, you just attacked them for no reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-26T18:07:42-07:00","id":1230425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230088#post1230088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just keep in mind that one does not generally know that they have been hit by awe. It's not a power that one goes, &quot;Oh he is using awe again.&quot; But Lashing out is generally one of those visible things. People know you have done something or acted out in some way. So if you think they are using awe and they werent, you just attacked them for no reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure a vampire who knows about Majesty would know when a Daeva is using it, it would be pretty obvious I'd assume. Else the book wouldn't say you can lash out against it (or the book would tell us how a vampire can find out if a Daeva is using Awe, just like how we can find out an Obfuscated vampire with a Wits+Composure-Obfuscate).<br /> <br /> A Nosferatu who's getting sick and tired of his Daeva rival constantly using Awe would probably think: <b>&quot;Ohhhh look at her, she looks REALLY stunning tonight, absolutely gorgeous, hmmm... wait hold up, the bitch is using Awe again isn't she? Yeah, nah, not gonna happen lady.&quot; </b>and then use Lashing Out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 06-26-2018, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T00:11:06-07:00","id":1230475,"title":"","content":"Again, from the FAQ:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Does a vampire affected by Majesty 1, Awe, know that they\u2019re being affected by a supernatural power?</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Not automatically. They just feel what Awe wants them to feel. However, they retain their faculties enough that if a Daeva seems too amazing to be true, they might be able to turn around and defy it with the predatory aura.</span></span><br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T04:08:18-07:00","id":1230490,"title":"","content":"Does an ordinary Human affected by a viniculam figure out they were bewitched somehow when it wears off if they have no prior supernatural experience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T04:53:43-07:00","id":1230495,"title":"","content":"Which doesn't contradict what Ventrue Life says. The problem with Awe being a zero skill, zero cost, no resist instant action sledgehammer power for attention whore characters to spam \u201clook at me\u201d also means there\u2019s no reason a player should arbitrarily NOT come to the conclusion their character is being manipulated by the Awe user and take steps to bring it to a screeching halt. After all, being a zero skill, zero cost, no resist power also means the Daeva can\u2019t prove they weren\u2019t using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T05:36:29-07:00","id":1230506,"title":"","content":"Lashing out, has side effects unfortunately .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T06:32:35-07:00","id":1230521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230495#post1230495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Awe being a zero skill, zero cost, no resist instant action sledgehammer power for attention whore characters to spam \u201clook at me\u201d also means there\u2019s no reason a player should arbitrarily NOT come to the conclusion their character is being manipulated by the Awe user and take steps to bring it to a screeching halt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that lashing out costs precious Willpower that the Daeva may not need to spend in response is a not-insignificant reason reason to think twice before making that escalation; unless they're trying to bring you in close or you're trying to keep an eye on the rest of the room, the primary threat is &quot;the Social character has turned on their bonus dice for direct Social actions,&quot; and there are plenty of contexts where being the center of attention isn't abrupt or unusual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T08:39:15-07:00","id":1230552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230490#post1230490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does an ordinary Human affected by a viniculam figure out they were bewitched somehow when it wears off if they have no prior supernatural experience?</div> </div> </div> </div>They might just think said person was particularly interesting, even if they can't think of anything about them that was particularly interesting, and no one they tell the story to seems particularly interested. 'You had to be there.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T10:47:21-07:00","id":1230588,"title":"","content":"curious Awe will only be so much benefit if your humanitys that low.<br /> <br /> at higher Majesty you get powers that totally replace conventional socialization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T14:13:17-07:00","id":1230638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230495#post1230495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which doesn't contradict what Ventrue Life says. The problem with Awe being a zero skill, zero cost, no resist instant action sledgehammer power for attention whore characters to spam \u201clook at me\u201d also means there\u2019s no reason a player should arbitrarily NOT come to the conclusion their character is being manipulated by the Awe user and take steps to bring it to a screeching halt. After all, being a zero skill, zero cost, no resist power also means the Daeva can\u2019t prove they weren\u2019t using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a &quot;no resist&quot; power, but that's because it doesn't do that much by itself when you think about it. It doesn't make you agree to any plans the vampire suggests, or do favours for them. It makes you treat them nicely, but you don't have to *do* anything.<br /> <br /> Everything that makes people do stuff is still a social roll or a subsequent use of Majesty.<br /> <br /> In Requiem for Rome, it's even said that a lot of vampires don't even think of those powers as Disciplines, and believe Daeva are just that attractive and alluring because they are, while for the Daeva themselves the use of Majesty is almost reflexive and not something they consciously do necessary. I don't dislike that way of thinking.<br /> <br /> Making other Vampires always notice when you turn on Majesty can easily make it useless, so I prefer to come down on punishing it only when it's being used too egregiously. But Lashing Out is still a big step to take, you're taking quite a big risk in order to break a power which, again, isn't really *doing* all that much on its own. Why do you care if Daeva girl is being popular across the room? She can knock herself out, and social rolls aren't magical mind control, so even with Awe she won't be able to make anyone do anything that just isn't in their nature (unless she uses the advanced dots, in which case she's suicidal in the face of other vamps), so who cares again, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 06-27-2018, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T16:09:42-07:00","id":1230674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230638#post1230638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It might be a &quot;no resist&quot; power, but that's because it doesn't do that much by itself when you think about it. It doesn't make you agree to any plans the vampire suggests, or do favours for them. It makes you treat them nicely, but you don't have to *do* anything.<br /> <br /> Everything that makes people do stuff is still a social roll or a subsequent use of Majesty.<br /> <br /> In Requiem for Rome, it's even said that a lot of vampires don't even think of those powers as Disciplines, and believe Daeva are just that attractive and alluring because they are, while for the Daeva themselves the use of Majesty is almost reflexive and not something they consciously do necessary. I don't dislike that way of thinking.<br /> <br /> Making other Vampires always notice when you turn on Majesty can easily make it useless, so I prefer to come down on punishing it only when it's being used too egregiously. But Lashing Out is still a big step to take, you're taking quite a big risk in order to break a power which, again, isn't really *doing* all that much on its own. Why do you care if Daeva girl is being popular across the room? She can knock herself out, and social rolls aren't magical mind control, so even with Awe she won't be able to make anyone do anything that just isn't in their nature (unless she uses the advanced dots, in which case she's suicidal in the face of other vamps), so who cares again, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to make Majesty past 1 noticeable for Kindred - after all, they need to know it's happening to Lash Out to respond - but I compensate by making Lashing Out similarly noticeable by other vampires. If Popular Daeva Girl is just trying to look good for her mortal 'associates' and Random Surly Gangrel lashes out because &quot;omg no majesty&quot;, her Harpy friends who happen to be present will say all sorts of nasty things about RSG's terrible manners to much scarier people.<br /> <br /> This keeps it so that Awe isn't 'useless because you can just lash out', but keeps it firmly as an aid and tool in the social arsenal rather than a sledgehammer when employed against other kindred - higher level uses of Majesty are more direct in application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2853-wampa","name":"wampa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-27T16:32:28-07:00","id":1230679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wampa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230674#post1230674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This keeps it so that Awe isn't 'useless because you can just lash out', but keeps it firmly as an aid and tool in the social arsenal rather than a sledgehammer when employed against other kindred - higher level uses of Majesty are more direct in application.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel I should reiterate: Lashing Out costs Willpower to initiate, is not particularly subtle, and does not cause Awe to stop working on anybody other than yourself. It escalates the situation in a way that is not appropriate for every social context, and the contexts for which it <i>is</i> appropriate are hardly going to raise eyebrows more than they already would have. If the Daeva is unaware of your presence then the main thing you have working against you is a reduced ability to notice anything else, and if they've turned on Awe to try and impress you in a confrontation then baring your fangs or drawing a line in the sand is practically expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T12:12:48-07:00","id":1230882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wampa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230674#post1230674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This keeps it so that Awe isn't 'useless because you can just lash out', but keeps it firmly as an aid and tool in the social arsenal rather than a sledgehammer when employed against other kindred - higher level uses of Majesty are more direct in application.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, how is it sledgehammering? Like I said before, within Vampire society, it doesn't make any of your plans just go through like that without a hitch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T12:47:14-07:00","id":1230897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230882#post1230882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, how is it sledgehammering? Like I said before, within Vampire society, it doesn't make any of your plans just go through like that without a hitch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Majesty is referred to as a sledgehammer because Dominate is more like a scalpel, comparitively. Majesty revolves around making people like you and controlling their emotions while Dominate is about specific commands. I suppose that would make Nightmare the chainsaw of the three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T13:34:05-07:00","id":1230912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230897#post1230897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Majesty is referred to as a sledgehammer because Dominate is more like a scalpel, comparitively. Majesty revolves around making people like you and controlling their emotions while Dominate is about specific commands. I suppose that would make Nightmare the chainsaw of the three.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, Majesty as a whole, but the word is being applied just to Awe in this context, as in this sentence: &quot;The problem with Awe being a zero skill, zero cost, no resist instant action sledgehammer power&quot;. And I just don't think that makes any sense, any Majesty power that could be considered a &quot;sledgehammer&quot; is not zero skill, zero cost or no resist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T18:56:11-07:00","id":1230976,"title":"","content":"I always considered Dominate the sledgehammer for forcing people to do things whether they want to do it or not, subsuming their will pretty much entirely, while Majesty makes them want to do things by contrast. Which is also why I'd need a relatively good reason for someone to say their character knows they're under the effect of the Discipline. Dominate is telling someone to do something with a gun to their head, while Majesty is convincing them it was their idea all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T20:26:51-07:00","id":1231000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230976#post1230976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always considered Dominate the sledgehammer for forcing people to do things whether they want to do it or not, subsuming their will pretty much entirely, while Majesty makes them want to do things by contrast. Which is also why I'd need a relatively good reason for someone to say their character knows they're under the effect of the Discipline. Dominate is telling someone to do something with a gun to their head, while Majesty is convincing them it was their idea all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tricky part there is that the most definitely Majesty allows you to make someone do things is that it makes it easier to get them to listen to you and it lets you steer their emotional state \u2014 it's more useful for engendering loyalty than precision on its own, which is why the archetypal Daeva manipulator is a creature of actual social engineering rather than just a funnel for Majesty and the Vinculum.<br /> <br /> Dominate, by contrast, has a more discrete impact on its victims and does not build from a root power that by-design attracts attention; its capacity for use as a blunt instrument doesn't change the fact that a master of Dominate can get people to do what she wants without even knowing she exists, which is the trade you make between a Discipline whose primary target is a person and a Discipline whose primary target is a crowd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T21:23:57-07:00","id":1231008,"title":"","content":"Scalpels and sledgehammers are perhaps not good analogies because while one is precise, neither are 'area of effect.' More like a sniper rifle versus a bomb, or laser versus lightbulb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T21:36:01-07:00","id":1231010,"title":"","content":"I was wondering, how do you guys handle NPC's using Majesty against PC's? Since they don't force the subject to obey and using social rolls against players is not really a thing. So a power giving bonuses to social rolls doesn't really affect PC's that much. Also suddenly telling players that a character seems really convincing and you want to believe them screams &quot;supernatural power being used&quot;.<br /> <br /> Do you just tell them or give them conditions and trust that they can RP the fact that they might have no idea they are being influenced in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T22:39:58-07:00","id":1231024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231010#post1231010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, how do you guys handle NPC's using Majesty against PC's? Since they don't force the subject to obey and using social rolls against players is not really a thing. So a power giving bonuses to social rolls doesn't really affect PC's that much. Also suddenly telling players that a character seems really convincing and you want to believe them screams &quot;supernatural power being used&quot;.<br /> <br /> Do you just tell them or give them conditions and trust that they can RP the fact that they might have no idea they are being influenced in some way?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To answer your question, I generally avoid using social powers on PCs at all, due to personal taste rather than any real belief that this is how things should be run. That said, your presumption that using social rolls against players is not a thing is incorrect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Suggestions<br /> for using Social maneuvering on other player-controlled characters<br /> can be found in the The World of Darkness Rulebook or The<br /> God-Machine Chronicle. </div> </div> </div>Can be found under &quot;Social Maneuvering&quot; on page 173.<br /> <br /> In CofD core, on page 82 under &quot;Resolution,&quot; it gives rules for having players be the target. The player can either accept what the social roll was for, or they can offer a &quot;beneficial alternative&quot; and take a Condition. This is what I would probably do, if it ever came up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T02:25:13-07:00","id":1231054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231024#post1231024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can be found under &quot;Social Maneuvering&quot; on page 173.<br /> <br /> In CofD core, on page 82 under &quot;Resolution,&quot; it gives rules for having players be the target. The player can either accept what the social roll was for, or they can offer a &quot;beneficial alternative&quot; and take a Condition. This is what I would probably do, if it ever came up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I actually remembered that but to me that seemed it was more meant for PC vs PC social maneuver. So far I've always left NPC interactions up to RP. Supernatural powers seem to me like they would be the only worth while thing to roll against PC's for, how the words are received by them regardless of how bad my RP is and how much I stumble in my words.<br /> <br /> Only once I've had it come up that a vampire used Majesty 4 against a PC and succeeded. The request that came with it was in line with what the PC would have done anyway, but the Vamp just wanted to make sure that she was safe against betrayal since she was allowing herself to be staked by the PC as part of an ambush against the Vamps nemesis.<br /> <br /> In that instance I gave the player the condition card and told him that his character was very adamant in protecting her, not knowing that he was under a power since he was already leaning in that direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 06-29-2018, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T04:06:15-07:00","id":1231067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231010#post1231010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, how do you guys handle NPC's using Majesty against PC's? Since they don't force the subject to obey and using social rolls against players is not really a thing. So a power giving bonuses to social rolls doesn't really affect PC's that much. Also suddenly telling players that a character seems really convincing and you want to believe them screams &quot;supernatural power being used&quot;.<br /> <br /> Do you just tell them or give them conditions and trust that they can RP the fact that they might have no idea they are being influenced in some way?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well. for Awe, I tend to roleplay them very socially, talking about the consequences around them, their jokes are funny, they say the comforting words, the right words, they seem to be the kind a guy that people want to be with, etc etc. This is both a way to get a feel of that starstruckness the power gives but also says something to the players and their PCs. Can it at times give away that the npcs are using awe in a meta way, sure but I fail to see that as a negative thing on their own. But then again, I have players that add to play, not play against me as a ST etc, they tend to avoid negative forms of meta gaming. But my players are scarred shitless about simple dots in disciplines after being subjects to them as PC mortals, actually seeing from the other perspective what they tend to do with their powers against npcs all the time.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, this is not far from how i present people with maxed out or likewise insane social stats and merits, so the players are never sure. Daeva tend to have both, making it harder to be in the know. <br /> <br /> Also, why is not social rolls npcs vs pc a thing. If the PCs can use the rules against the NPCs, the opposite should apply. Even though I consider myself quite socially adept and with a good vocabulary, I'm far from being a Blood God social savant. If needed, i might present a stat or make a roll, using social maneuvering against the PC from the god-machine rules. E.g. the players may opt to not follow trough and introduce a condition and such instead. But, here's the thing, I would never allow a NPCs to roll for anything that I wouldn't let a PC roll for. Sometimes there's just not enough dice in a world to succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T09:58:09-07:00","id":1231134,"title":"","content":"I think that giving certain conditions to the PC affected by awe or particular charismatic NPC, could be the right way to handle it because, the beat/s earned by following the condition (inspired or whatever else is fitting in that situation) is, for the player, exactly as tempting as awe should be for the character affected. You could also consider to ask to your player to spend a willpower in order to ignore what that &quot;awesome&quot; guy is saying. The rest is role playing and player should be able to act in the proper way if the master says: you really think that person is awesome for what he say and how he moves.<br /> <br /> Then, considering higher Majesty level (3rd dot on), no way. I will follow the rules exactly as stated in the book and exactly how they would apply to the NPC. Ignoring these powers could make a high social prince/Harpy/whatever, stupidly useless and under powered.<br /> By my side, I'm always try to limiting every discipline uses just to very dramatic or critical situation and I think to have found a good balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T10:35:08-07:00","id":1231147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231134#post1231134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that giving certain conditions to the PC affected by awe or particular charismatic NPC, could be the right way to handle it because, the beat/s earned by following the condition (inspired or whatever else is fitting in that situation) is, for the player, exactly as tempting as awe should be for the character affected. You could also consider to ask to your player to spend a willpower in order to ignore what that &quot;awesome&quot; guy is saying. The rest is role playing and player should be able to act in the proper way if the master says: you really think that person is awesome for what he say and how he moves.<br /> <br /> Then, considering higher Majesty level (3rd dot on), no way. I will follow the rules exactly as stated in the book and exactly how they would apply to the NPC. Ignoring these powers could make a high social prince/Harpy/whatever, stupidly useless and under powered.<br /> By my side, I'm always try to limiting every discipline uses just to very dramatic or critical situation and I think to have found a good balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this. When an NPC succeeds at a social roll against a PC, I give them a Condition. They can then decide to follow it or not.<br /> <br /> For instance, an NPC trying to talk a PC into following a course of action he had not intended on could put a Condition called &quot;Conflicted&quot; on the PC. The PC was sure what the right path forward was, but because of the NPC raising some very good points in an eloquent manner, there's a little feeling of doubt at his core. The condition would probably penalize Resolve, and would resolve when the PC decides to go along with the NPCs plan. It would fade naturally without granting a beat once the dilemma is no longer relevant (so if you stick to your original plan, it vanishes once you complete that plan).<br /> <br /> Conditions like this offer various little penalties/incentives to the players for buying into the idea that, yes, NPC X or Y really is that good of a social manipulator, in a way that is generally fun for everyone involved. Also lets you play with Conditions like that more outside of the Disciplines, which can be a bit of a declaration of war to employ against PCs, while a good old social roll rarely is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T13:34:38-07:00","id":1231210,"title":"","content":"I, OF COURSE, can't find the thread where Rose spoke about what Majesty is like. But seriously, if you use it and it's like flicking a switch and everyone knows you're using it. Then it would be a masquerade breach, because every human and vampire would know and feel and notice that you are doing something Supernatural.<br /> <br /> If Johnny Depp or Scarlet Johannson walked into a room and started mingling everyone would notice it's because they have like a permanent Awe on. ( or whoever star you might like... ) It's not supernatural, but I would think that awe might be something like that. Someone who just looks stunning or is telling the funniest jokes or whatever to make you think they are pretty wicked awesome at the moment.<br /> <br /> Later you go home and think about it and realize that they might not have been that awesome, but in the moment it was the best! ~~ or even if you kick it up and say they charmed you and convinced you to lend them something you never would have normally. You don't realize you have been supernaturally mind fucked. You just think that YOU were the one being kind of stupid in the moment. We all make choices in the moment and go back and some of them were just not that great. It wasn't because you were rolled... or maybe it was, We shouldn't know! Majesty isn't like that or every use of it would be against Vampire code.<br /> <br /> Are there exceptions? yes. of course. Say Bob the Daeva runs around testing his majesty on everyone and talking about it, so when Bob walks into a room, you slap down his Awe when you think he is being too cool. But that lady over at the bar giving you googly eyes and making your pants get too tight and making it too hard to think about anyone else or notice anyone else. Then suddenly you have the urge to go talk to her... Majesty or Hormones? -shrugs- You shouldn't know.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rose said that it is subtle, super subtle. That it's not something everyone knows otherwise it wouldn't be effective. If everyone KNOWS you are using this power to be super cool, then they wouldn't think you are super cool, and they would more than likely think you are lying about whatever is coming out of your mouth, thus sort of negating the whole power.<br /> <br /> <br /> When someone sidles up to you and starts flirting with you, making it difficult to notice the room around you, you don't automatically start snarling and growling and baring your fangs to make them less cool, because wouldn't you look like a damn fool if they were just flirting??<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/67072-how-subtle-are-dominate-and-majesty-now\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...nd-majesty-now</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/217291-can-you-use-awe-selectively\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...we-selectively</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/703900-2ed-majesty\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...00-2ed-majesty</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/814460-questions-about-majesty/page3\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-majesty/page3</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1230976#post1230976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always considered Dominate the sledgehammer for forcing people to do things whether they want to do it or not, subsuming their will pretty much entirely, while Majesty makes them want to do things by contrast. Which is also why I'd need a relatively good reason for someone to say their character knows they're under the effect of the Discipline. Dominate is telling someone to do something with a gun to their head, while Majesty is convincing them it was their idea all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! This..<br /> <br /> With Majesty .. you have convinced them it was their idea to come along or to offer up their car or clean out their bank for you... A vampire shouldn't know that in the moment they are under a spell, because then a human would know too. Making it so you know you are being conned while being conned takes away from what Majesty is...<br /> <br /> Sure maybe after the vampire has left, awe or charm or whatever has warn off and you get a chance to think.... then you might realize that you were really dumb or you were duped, but there shouldn't be a neon light saying -flashes sign below-<br /> OH! HEY! THEY ARE USING MAJESTY ON ME. I BETTER LASH OUT AND STOP THEM.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I just keep adding. Sorry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> If you play it that everyone knows you are using Majesty and thus don't think you're awesome. Do you then play it where everyone knows you are using Nightmare? Because if someone kicked on Dread Presence... I would lash out and slap that shit down every time! ( or for those that only let the higher levels of it be automatically known, Would you still be as scared if you knew it wasn't real because you knew you were just under a supernatural spell? )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 06-29-2018, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T19:30:05-07:00","id":1231284,"title":"","content":"This is what Rose said about Majesty and whether vampires can figure out they've been Awed. It's in the FAQ, about that very question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not automatically. They just feel what Awe wants them to feel. However, they retain their faculties enough that if a Daeva seems too amazing to be true, they might be able to turn around and defy it with the predatory aura. </div> </div> </div>Saying it breaks the Masquerade is a bit an of an overexaggeration. A vampire who knows Majesty exists may or may not decide to go with it (on its own, the lower Dot abilities are not harmful, and Lashing out can cause a scene, or fail and just leave you Awed and suddenly on the Majestic vampire's bad side). This doesn't mean that an ordinary mortal, suddenly seeing someone interesting, is going to think to themselves that they must be under a magic spell and it's clearly from a vampire. The person just seems overly charismatic or attention-getting, similar to how Striking Looks can work.<br /> <br /> There was an example of Majesty (or whatever the VtM version of it was) in one of the Setite novels that was well done, the perspective character was talking to another vampire, that they liked, and noticed that they enjoyed their company overmuch, considering the situation. They were being too amiable. They didn't Lash Out, but asked the other vampire to tone it down so they could think clearly.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that mortals can't really Lash Out and don't have a Clash of Wills to activate against this stuff, so it doesn't matter if it is out of the ordinary, that's just part of being in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> The question of whether mind control can be used on PCs is about as old as 'charm person,' and I don't believe anyone has come up with a single answer that encompasses all solutions. Some people will just walk right up to the Dominator of Mind-Command and punch them in the face even if you describe how their character doesn't want to. Others will get the gist of things just by a description. Sometimes you need to back descriptions with mechanical oomph. It depends on the group. I think it's unreasonable to completely take it off the table, especially with gamelines that are effectively about mind control in one form or another. Some people might not want their characters to be usurped in any way, but when dealing with blood bonds and long-term changes you can talk to the player beforehand and see what they think about it and perhaps reach a compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T21:38:39-07:00","id":1231297,"title":"","content":"Rose posted something else too, in a thread. Unahim referenced it too. It\u2019s out there. It\u2019s an example how your friend can always talk you into stupid stuff, but you don\u2019t blame your friend and you don\u2019t think your friend is doing anything supernatural, <br /> You just think you make bad decisions when you\u2019re around them. <br /> <br /> And people were talking about \u201cknowing\u201d awe has been turned on, like \u201cknowing\u201d the light has been turned on. If you ~know~ When a supernatural ability is activated, then why wouldn\u2019t everyone get the feeling or see the light switch or whatever it is that makes someone 100% without a doubt know something supernatural is being used? And if it\u2019s that obvious and blunt, why couldn\u2019t a human notice it? And thus, it would be a masquerade breech when you use it around humans. <br /> <br /> I disagree with the people who say majesty is blunt and everyone knows when you\u2019re doing it. I much rather go with the it\u2019s subtle and someone would have to have a damn good reason to think you\u2019re using it. if you guess and lash out, and you\u2019re wrong, then you might have opened a can of worms. lashing out should be a risk. You shouldn\u2019t know for sure Joe has kicked on majesty just because you noticed them. You can assume, you can guess, you can use logic. But it shouldn\u2019t be a neon sign that gets turned on above their heads for all to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-29T22:06:21-07:00","id":1231302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231297#post1231297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And people were talking about \u201cknowing\u201d awe has been turned on, like \u201cknowing\u201d the light has been turned on. If you ~know~ When a supernatural ability is activated, then why wouldn\u2019t everyone get the feeling or see the light switch or whatever it is that makes someone 100% without a doubt know something supernatural is being used? And if it\u2019s that obvious and blunt, why couldn\u2019t a human notice it? And thus, it would be a masquerade breech when you use it around humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Rose and the book say, you know there's someone who's got an awe-inspiring spotlight on them, it's part of the spotlight. A vampires faculties can include the ability to suspect that 'That's something Serpents do,' because while they may not have the core book most vampires have vague ideas about what the other most common vampires can do. <i>It doesn't mean they're right,</i> <i>however</i>. In the example I mentioned before the perspective character was already enamored with the Majestic-user. Which is another reason why you don't have vampires lashing out in all directions. Standing out doesn't necessarily mean Majesty is being used. Having Striking Looks and getting a success on Socialize + Presence roll could probably cause a similar in the spotlight moment. Meanwhile a human doesn't even necessarily recognize the person is a vampire, let alone that vampires may have that sort of ability. A human can recognize that something's weird about it, especially when it gets to certain extremes, but that doesn't mean 'Vampire Alert.' A masquerade breach would be a vampire announcing they're a vampire, not just someone being ridiculously charming.<br /> <br /> Awe is a big spectacular ability, affecting everyone in sight, but not everything is awe. If someone said you automatically know when awe is on whenever it's on all the time they were mistaken. But it's not outside the realms of reason a vampire who knows about it can piece things together. Auspex and some other abilities could likely also help.<br /> <br /> But it's especially something you can 'know' compared to Dominate, which explicitly calls out the fact that, 'you also can't quite remember what happened while you were under the vampire's spell.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-30-2018, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T00:50:58-07:00","id":1231313,"title":"","content":"And exactly because Majesty is something you can 'know', it has to be a bit subtle. When you cheat someone out of something important using one of the higher dots of Majesty, they remember what happened and may retaliate when the feelings wear off. When you do that with Dominate, they may not even remember ever meeting you at all. That is a huge boon of Dominate. And while people keep saying Majesty is AoE, that's not true for most of its dots: Confidant, Green Eyes, Loyalty... all single target. So for the most part, Majesty competes directly with Dominate in application.<br /> <br /> Making Majesty both more knowable, more counterable (once you're Dominated, good luck) <i>and </i>more obvious than Dominate is clearly painting one as just plain inferior to the other. Dominate is the obvious one: people can tell the one affected is not acting naturally most of the time. But the victim will rarely if ever remember anything about what happened. It is less <i>knowable</i>. Majesty is more subtle, its very effects make you want to not believe something supernatural is going on. But the higher dots past <i>Awe</i> are very <i>knowable</i> after the fact.<br /> <br /> It's hard to think anything bad about a vampire using Awe <b>and that should include thinking they're using Awe in the first place.</b> Like Rose said, Awe makes you feel what it wants you to feel, and it doesn't want you to feel that what is happening isn't entirely normal. So yes, Rose says that you can sometimes figure it out. Her sentence has the structure &quot;If... might...&quot; That's two degrees of doubt in a single sentence. If you turn around and use that to say half of all uses of Awe in a social setting with Vampires is detected and foiled, I really think you're reinterpreting a statement that says &quot;It's possible, maybe, sometimes&quot; to be &quot;Vampires be Lashing out against them Daeva errydayyyyy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I found the quote in question (at least I think this is it):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/498296-life-after-majesty?p=502067#post502067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Uhm, so, about last night?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Yeah?</i><br /> <br /> &quot;I don't usually... do that. Take somebody home.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>It's pretty new to me, too.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;We didn't... sleep together, did we?&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Only literally.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, good.&quot; *pause* &quot;That was awkward to ask.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>It was awkward to answer. Look... you want to get dinner Thursday?</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, okay. I mean. Sounds good.&quot; <div align=\"right\">--actual play</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> It really depends on the context. If you get affected by Majesty, you'll probably rationalize it:<br /> <br /> &quot;I was lonely.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He was funny.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;She was really on fire last night.&quot;<br /> <br /> Depending on what you did under the effects, you may think you were being dumb and be too embarrassed or annoyed to want to associate with the vampire. Or, you may remember it as a good time, and even though you don't feel the same crush or trust or whatever that you did last night, you remember it and are more likely to be friendly to the vampire.<br /> <br /> If you've frequently experienced Majesty, you're likely to have some weird feelings:<br /> <br /> &quot;Some nights I need to let go.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dunno why, but around her I completely lose it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He's a guilty pleasure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Without Majesty, you probably vary on how you respond, depending on what else is going on. You might seek the vampire out, because you know you like their company. You may avoid them, because you know you do stupid shit when they ask.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that since the bigger powers build on Awe, other people you're with are likely to back up your impressions of the vampire:<br /> <br /> &quot;You've got a thing. I can kinda understand it, but it's a thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, he was hot in those jeans.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Her bullshit always sounds profound until you actually think about it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice how nothing in here is described as being some form of supernatural attraction. Awe and Majesty feel just like high levels of mundane charisma and social skills, and maybe some personal magnetism. The best way to think about whether or not someone would Lash Out against Awe, is to determine if they'd Lash Out in this situation if the vampire just had higher attributes and skills. If the answer is yes, go for it. If the answer is no, there needs to be some very clear reason why you're doing it against something that looks and feels exactly that way.<br /> <br /> Similarly, fallout against Majesty after the fact is mostly identical to fallout from being completely mundanely talked into stupid shit.<br /> <br /> This one is also good:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/167874-lashing-out-and-awe?p=169331#post169331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lashing out to throw off Awe works the same as lashing out without provocation. It just has the additional effect of throwing off Majesty. You pick an aspect of the Beast, you roll, and the vampire you're lashing out at chooses fight or flight. Willpower is spent and Conditions are imposed as normal.<br /> <br /> This almost always represents an escalation of an encounter, and it can get pretty messy, since lashing out against someone trying to Awe you doesn't change their effect on anyone else nearby. At the very least, you run the risk of looking like an asshole.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that nobody besides the participants perceive the effects of lashing out... they only see the physical actions the vampires take to lash out and resist. So when the Gangrel resists the Daeva's Awe, people see her growl menacingly or sidle up with a distracting and sharp-toothed smile, and they see the Daeva's response. They don't perceive the supernatural contest that underlies that interaction.<br /> <br /> The predatory aura is called an &quot;aura&quot; because it's an ambient effect that allows vampires to recognize each other. Lashing out is focusing the aura on one person and cracking it like a whip.<br /> <br /> Other vampire capabilities are actually manifestations of the aura. For example, Awe itself is &quot;tinting&quot; your aura to show you in a good light, while Face in the Crowd is turning your predatory aura inwards so that neither peer nor prey notices you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems pretty clear, exactly what I said before this quote: Lashing Out against Awe is exactly like Lashing Out without there being Awe, but just happens to end Awe. Because usually the provocation will be something else happening, not just &quot;Oh, there's Awe going on.&quot; And yes, it can easily get messy.<br /> <br /> Author's intent seems perfectly clear with this much quoting backing it up, how you choose to play it is of course entirely up to you, but I'd be pretty bummed if I were at a table where playing what should be the most socially apt, incredibly alluring Clan turns into playing the clan constantly getting beaten down with Lashing Out attempts from everyone and their grandmother, with all of its members thought of as cheating hacks that only use a &quot;crutch&quot;, and who are secretly ridiculed because what's left of their powers (single target manipulation in private, presumably, if any group of vampires they meet is constantly having at least a few Lash Out whenever they try) is completely overshadowed by the Dominate of our true lords and saviours, the Ventrue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 06-30-2018, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T03:41:22-07:00","id":1231327,"title":"","content":"Honestly, by this point we're playing with words here. Majesty is overt because you can know something's up. Majesty is subtle because you can't figure out whether that &quot;something&quot; is Majesty or not. The two sentences don't seem exclusive to me, and instead together they give me the image of &quot;always be on guard when around a Serpent,&quot; which seems like the default mode for any vampire interacting with any other vampire, Daeva or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> A question of my own, tangentially related to all those arguments; Do the &quot;psychic&quot; Disciplines work over the internet? (Majesty, Dominate, Nightmare, Auspex) I'm not with the pdfs right now so I can't check, and it's been awhile since I read any of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T03:51:21-07:00","id":1231329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231327#post1231327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question of my own, tangentially related to all those arguments; Do the &quot;psychic&quot; Disciplines work over the internet? (Majesty, Dominate, Nightmare, Auspex) I'm not with the pdfs right now so I can't check, and it's been awhile since I read any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can your vampire project their predatory aura by screen and fiber-optics? I doubt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T04:02:31-07:00","id":1231331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231329#post1231329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can your vampire project their predatory aura by screen and fiber-optics? I doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I very much doubt it as well. However, fine place for a devotion that would allow for real time face to face using of the &quot;psychic&quot; disciplines. I also remember a spirits touch on video tapes and such from the Mekhet book if i recall that one correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T04:04:40-07:00","id":1231332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231329#post1231329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can your vampire project their predatory aura by screen and fiber-optics? I doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knee jerk reaction is of course &quot;Hell no,&quot; but the CoD does contain &quot;...Wait what?!&quot; sort of things often enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T06:08:35-07:00","id":1231345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231327#post1231327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question of my own, tangentially related to all those arguments; Do the &amp;quot;psychic&amp;quot; Disciplines work over the internet? (Majesty, Dominate, Nightmare, Auspex) I'm not with the pdfs right now so I can't check, and it's been awhile since I read any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually the answer is no. The big Capt. Obvious fact is that the vampire either has to see their victim, the victim has to see the user, or be in the location or have the object on hand. And you aren\u2019t actually seeing each other over electronic devices, you\u2019re seeing a projected image. Live feeds aren\u2019t \u201creal time\u201d there is a few second delay. There\u2019s also often range limitations but there are noted exceptions to powers that can be used over large distances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T06:56:16-07:00","id":1231347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231345#post1231345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Usually the answer is no. The big Capt. Obvious fact is that the vampire either has to see their victim, the victim has to see the user, or be in the location or have the object on hand. And you aren\u2019t actually seeing each other over electronic devices, you\u2019re seeing a projected image. Live feeds aren\u2019t \u201creal time\u201d there is a few second delay. There\u2019s also often range limitations but there are noted exceptions to powers that can be used over large distances.</div> </div> </div> </div>As expected. So I suppose if anyone or anything pulls it off, it\u2019d set off alarm bells for just about everybody. Makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T07:11:29-07:00","id":1231349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231345#post1231345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-