re's an Auspex only devotion or alternative to Spirit's Touch in 1st edition that allows the user to visually identify vampires on video recordings, even if they were blurred.<br /> There's a Theban Sorcery ritual where you can implant visions and instructions in an object that gets passed on to the next person to touch the object.<br /> There's a Dominate devotion that let's the user impart the ability to use a Dominate power onto someone else as part of the command. But nothing official about projecting powers across electrical signals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-07-2018, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T12:14:35-07:00","id":1231411,"title":"","content":"Think a Majest or Dominate/Auspex/Nightmare devotion that lets you combo its power's with astral projection would be reasonable? <br /> <br /> let you pop in as a terrifying or seductive and beautiful ghost?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T13:56:36-07:00","id":1231443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231411#post1231411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think a Majest or Dominate/Auspex/Nightmare devotion that lets you combo its power's with astral projection would be reasonable? <br /> <br /> let you pop in as a terrifying or seductive and beautiful ghost?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say, why not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also have thought to a devotion Auspex 5 + Vigor to be able to manipulate phisical world.<br /> With Devotions you can obtain almost any effect you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T06:27:03-07:00","id":1231568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231387#post1231387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a Devotion at some point that allowed Dominate with a recorded tape? Might be imagining it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No but I and a group of people entertained the thought of having a Devotion for that in this thread a few dozen pages back.<br /> <br /> There is indeed a Devotion in the Daeva clan book which allows a Daeva to record her Awe (Majesty) and have the recording affect the people who watch it, effectively allowing her to use Awe over television and the internet. So I don't see why a Ventrue couldn't develop a similar devotion for Mesmerize (Dominate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T07:13:21-07:00","id":1231575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231568#post1231568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is indeed a Devotion in the Daeva clan book which allows a Daeva to record her Awe (Majesty) and have the recording affect the people who watch it, effectively allowing her to use Awe over television and the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it worked, as evidenced by the fact that the Devotion in question was called <i>Picture Perfect</i> and had a Storyteller-discretion capacity to be used through paintings, drawings, or sculpture; it required the character to have Awed the photographer/artist in the first place (in an edition where Awe was a rolled power that only provided bonus social dice and worked less well in crowds) and couldn't be used if you were taking the photo yourself or using an automated process. It wasn't &quot;the Daeva gains social benefits across media&quot; so much as an extension of the same thematic space that gives us Enchantment and The Wish \u2014 the Daeva occupy a prime niche in the space of vampire-as-tempter-or-muse, and that extends to the interpersonal phenomena of celebrity and image in a way that Dominate doesn't logically follow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I don't see why a Ventrue couldn't develop a similar devotion for Mesmerize (Dominate). </div> </div> </div>As it stands this is represented by Entombed Command, which is most limited by its single-target focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T07:22:00-07:00","id":1231576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231575#post1231575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how it worked, as evidenced by the fact that the Devotion in question was called <i>Picture Perfect</i> and had a Storyteller-discretion capacity to be used through paintings, drawings, or sculpture; it required the character to have Awed the photographer/artist in the first place (in an edition where Awe was a rolled power that only provided bonus social dice and worked less well in crowds) and couldn't be used if you were taking the photo yourself or using an automated process. It wasn't &quot;the Daeva gains social benefits across media&quot; so much as an extension of the same thematic space that gives us Enchantment and The Wish \u2014 the Daeva occupy a prime niche in the space of vampire-as-tempter-or-muse, and that extends to the interpersonal phenomena of celebrity and image in a way that Dominate doesn't logically follow.<br /> <br /> As it stands this is represented by Entombed Command, which is most limited by its single-target focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not wrong, there were an official devotion or dominate 6 power in 1ed that allowed the Ventrue to mesmerize a crowd. So I guess that it's not so weird to design a devotion, maybe with majesty 1 or Vigor don't know right now, that allow you to bypass the single target limitation.<br /> <br /> I've already proposed a homebrewed devotion: Dominate 3 Vigor x (not sure now about requisites), that allows the Ventrue to write the command in a book/paper/wall and, the first that would have read it, would have been affected (losing the usual contested roll) by the command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-01-2018, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T09:06:37-07:00","id":1231596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231568#post1231568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No but I and a group of people entertained the thought of having a Devotion for that in this thread a few dozen pages back.<br /> <br /> There is indeed a Devotion in the Daeva clan book which allows a Daeva to record her Awe (Majesty) and have the recording affect the people who watch it, effectively allowing her to use Awe over television and the internet. So I don't see why a Ventrue couldn't develop a similar devotion for Mesmerize (Dominate).</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha, yep, it was certainly the Daeva clan book one that I remembered, I haven't read that far back in this thread. And it does set a precedent that Dominate should be able to follow somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T11:56:17-07:00","id":1231621,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what logic follows that just because Awe can do something, Dominate can do it, too. Or vice-versa. Sure, they both fall within the &quot;social engineering&quot; sphere, but only in the sense that Animalism and Protean both fall into the &quot;animals&quot; sphere. The effects, limitations, means, methods, are all vastly different. They are entirely different Disciplines. As stated earlier, Awe sets one up as a muse and celebrity, that's kind of its niche, and so that Devotion makes sense for it. Dominate has none of that, so you can't really call it precedent-setting for Dominate.<br /> <br /> Not to say if you can think of a way to do it with Dominate, you can't go for it (though I think the whole 'eye contact' thing being one of the core aspects of the Discipline that is also based in Vampire mythos makes it a bad idea to try to get rid of it from a narrative perspective). Using Majesty to justify things for Dominate, however, is flawed logic. Like saying Animalism can have a way to do agg damage with claws because Protean gets Claws of the Unholy and they're both animal-related Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T12:29:13-07:00","id":1231624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231621#post1231621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what logic follows that just because Awe can do something, Dominate can do it, too. Or vice-versa. Sure, they both fall within the &quot;social engineering&quot; sphere, but only in the sense that Animalism and Protean both fall into the &quot;animals&quot; sphere. The effects, limitations, means, methods, are all vastly different. They are entirely different Disciplines. As stated earlier, Awe sets one up as a muse and celebrity, that's kind of its niche, and so that Devotion makes sense for it. Dominate has none of that, so you can't really call it precedent-setting for Dominate.<br /> <br /> Not to say if you can think of a way to do it with Dominate, you can't go for it (though I think the whole 'eye contact' thing being one of the core aspects of the Discipline that is also based in Vampire mythos makes it a bad idea to try to get rid of it from a narrative perspective). Using Majesty to justify things for Dominate, however, is flawed logic. Like saying Animalism can have a way to do agg damage with claws because Protean gets Claws of the Unholy and they're both animal-related Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree about one point here: the classification for whome both Protean and Animalism are animal-related disciplines such as Dominate and Majesty are Social related disciplines.<br /> <br /> First of all Majesty and Dominate are CONTROL related disciplines. And for that I would assimilate Abnimalism much more to them than to Protean.<br /> Protean is not animal related discipines: is a shapenshifting related discipline. 1st dot is fusion with soil, 5th is becoming mist. Both of these powers aren't really animal related.<br /> <br /> That said, about the eyes contact part you stated, well, each person in a crowd can see the vampire's eyes at once (and maybe Awe can play a determinant role here). Dominate specifies that is not the vampire that need to look in the eyes of anyone she want to mesmerize but it's the victim who need to see her eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-02-2018, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T00:27:34-07:00","id":1231734,"title":"","content":"Question: To fortify themself against awe using Predatory Aura is it still a contested roll, isn't it? I mean, to wash out the Awe effect do you still need to win the predatory aura contested roll and not just to achieve a success on it. Am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-02-2018, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T05:03:38-07:00","id":1231764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231734#post1231734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: To fortify themself against awe using Predatory Aura is still a contested roll, isn't it? I mean to wash out the Awe effect you still need to win the predatory aura contested roll not just to achieve a success on it. Am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that is dependent on the mechanics used and time constraints. (I really don't like bogging down game play with predatory aura contests as the solution to no resist checks and dislike the developers' selective cognitive dissonance of the mechanics regarding mind and emotion control.) When I allowed a single instant act of concentration of Awe to affect people retroactively who showed up later, dispelled only by winning a predatory aura contest, it immediately deteriorated to Daeva players cockblocking other players' hunting attempts, date raping their ghouls and touchstones, and ripping them off by having their ghoul show up and pick everyone's pockets, so the Nosferatu preemptively flings Dread Presence or the Mekhet using Obfuscate on the Daeva to make everyone ignore them as their declared action everytime they arrive on the scene or as a first response to the Daeva showing up. Meanwhile the Ventrue or Gangrel's only option was to become drooling sycophants who can get robbed blind or leave the scene. So I changed the mechanics. Awe doesn't work retroactively on people who show up later. (The player has to take another instant action to keep tossing it around to get newcomers.) A single success on a predatory aura roll dispels it, unless it's activated with the express purpose of influencing that character, then it's winning a predatory aura contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-02-2018, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T05:27:02-07:00","id":1231770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231764#post1231764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that is dependent on the mechanics used and time constraints. (I really don't like bogging down game play with predatory aura contests as the solution to no resist checks and dislike the developers' selective cognitive dissonance of the mechanics regarding mind and emotion control.) When I allowed a single instant act of concentration of Awe to affect people retroactively who showed up later, dispelled only by winning a predatory aura contest, it immediately deteriorated to Daeva players cockblocking other players' hunting attempts, date raping their ghouls and touchstones, and ripping them off by having their ghoul show up and pick everyone's pockets, so the Nosferatu preemptively flings Dread Presence or the Mekhet using Obfuscate on the Daeva to make everyone ignore them as their declared action everytime they arrive on the scene or as a first response to the Daeva showing up. Meanwhile the Ventrue or Gangrel's only option was to become drooling sycophants who can get robbed blind or leave the scene. So I changed the mechanics. Awe doesn't work retroactively on people who show up later. (The player has to take another instant action to keep tossing it around to get newcomers.) A single success on a predatory aura roll dispels it, unless it's activated with the express purpose of influencing that character, then it's winning a predatory aura contest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your mechanic sounds good to me.<br /> The only concern I have is that, usually, predatory Aura is an instant action directed to a specific target (the Awe user in this case), so this implies the awe user would like to contest this aura lashing out by himself as well, to not be affected by the X condition at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T05:47:05-07:00","id":1231777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231734#post1231734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: To fortify themself against awe using Predatory Aura is it still a contested roll, isn't it? I mean, to wash out the Awe effect do you still need to win the predatory aura contested roll and not just to achieve a success on it. Am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tsusasi's player problems notwithstanding, lashing out to break a Discipline's effect on you works the same way as a normal predatory aura contest, per previous discussion of this topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T05:53:10-07:00","id":1231779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231764#post1231764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that is dependent on the mechanics used and time constraints. (I really don't like bogging down game play with predatory aura contests as the solution to no resist checks and dislike the developers' selective cognitive dissonance of the mechanics regarding mind and emotion control.) When I allowed a single instant act of concentration of Awe to affect people retroactively who showed up later, dispelled only by winning a predatory aura contest, it immediately deteriorated to Daeva players cockblocking other players' hunting attempts, date raping their ghouls and touchstones, and ripping them off by having their ghoul show up and pick everyone's pockets, so the Nosferatu preemptively flings Dread Presence or the Mekhet using Obfuscate on the Daeva to make everyone ignore them as their declared action everytime they arrive on the scene or as a first response to the Daeva showing up. Meanwhile the Ventrue or Gangrel's only option was to become drooling sycophants who can get robbed blind or leave the scene. So I changed the mechanics. Awe doesn't work retroactively on people who show up later. (The player has to take another instant action to keep tossing it around to get newcomers.) A single success on a predatory aura roll dispels it, unless it's activated with the express purpose of influencing that character, then it's winning a predatory aura contest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. I wouldn't want to play with your players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231734#post1231734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: To fortify themself against awe using Predatory Aura is it still a contested roll, isn't it? I mean, to wash out the Awe effect do you still need to win the predatory aura contested roll and not just to achieve a success on it. Am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not explained, but I believe the intention is that the Majesty user still can choose between &quot;fighting&quot; and &quot;fleeing&quot;. I.e. choosing whether to respond with their own Lash (which may cost a WP point depending on relative Blood Potency).<br /> My table instead pits the Lashing Out dice pool against the Clash of Wills dice pool for Awe, and contesting it is reflexive and free. So Power Attribute + Blood Potency vs Majesty + Blood Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T08:20:35-07:00","id":1231815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231770#post1231770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Your mechanic sounds good to me.<br /> The only concern I have is that, usually, predatory Aura is an instant action directed to a specific target (the Awe user in this case), so this implies the awe user would like to contest this aura lashing out by himself as well, to not be affected by the X condition at least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The rules aren\u2019t very specific as to how to handle continuous running wide area/multitarget effects where the one activating the power in question also currently isn\u2019t present to target. And no, I\u2019m not going to arbitrarily disallow players from turning off deleterious effects that cripple their overall effectiveness if someone wants to make the effort. In the case of Awe, if you walk into the vicinity after it\u2019s been turned on, you aren\u2019t subject to the effect so you have no need to Lash Out and accidentally disrupt that person\u2019s activities. Granted you can still opt to Lash Out but that makes you the aggressor. And on the other side of that, If you\u2019re going to throw around powers that handicap other players after the fact, you\u2019re stating an intention that you plan to take advantage of them and should be prepared to deal with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-02-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T08:58:02-07:00","id":1231825,"title":"","content":"I don't really understand why you don't let Awe affect people who arrive after Awe is already activated. It's described as an aura you exude during the duration and not a Condition like Mesmerized that's applied during activation that holds for a scene regardless if the user stays in the locale.<br /> There's no reason to think they'd retroactively be placed under Awe (which leads me to believe you're not using the word incorrectly). Is it that you've assumed it's only possible to Lash Out against the user of Awe when Awe is activated? Since Lashing Out isn't reflexive then it would be impossible to ever Lash Out during the activation. Combined with the fact that Awe is subtle enough that you might not even realise it's activated (at least until the user starts talking to you) it's pretty clear that you're supposed to be able to Lash Out to disrupt Awe at any time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T10:13:04-07:00","id":1231863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231825#post1231825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really understand why you don't let Awe affect people who arrive after Awe is already activated. It's described as an aura you exude during the duration and not a Condition like Mesmerized that's applied during activation that holds for a scene regardless if the user stays in the locale. <br /> <br /> There's no reason to think they'd retroactively be placed under Awe (which leads me to believe you're not using the word incorrectly). Is it that you've assumed it's only possible to Lash Out against the user of Awe when Awe is activated? Since Lashing Out isn't reflexive then it would be impossible to ever Lash Out during the activation. Combined with the fact that Awe is subtle enough that you might not even realise it's activated (at least until the user starts talking to you) it's pretty clear that you're supposed to be able to Lash Out to disrupt Awe at any time.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a mechanics standpoint, when you activate Awe (it's an instant action) the user says or does something to draw attention to themself. If someone's not present to witness that action then they can't be &quot;awed&quot; by it. Technically Awe only modifies your appearance, not impressions you've already left on others due to prior actions. The user can &quot;look&quot; like they may have murdered someone and have it ignored but not get away with actually murdering someone in front of audience. (Go read page 7 of the Daeva clanbook. That is an in-character example, not only of how humans act when awed, but how humans (and by extension vampires) would notice Awe being used. And in that example they are not automatically affected by it because they take steps to avoid being ensnared.<br /> <br /> It's not an issue of me assuming it's only possible to Lash out against an Awe user only after it's activated first. (It certainly is possible.) It's an issue of player agency and not wanting to bog down the game with unnecessary mechanics for players who wish to retain their agency. Most of the time my players are actually pretty good about not deliberately and actively screwing each other over but there's always someone who likes to push and see how much he can get away with and who will tolerate being screwed with, or the inexperienced player who may be trying to see what they can get away with or just wasn't thinking at the time. And from an in character perspective when I ST, my NPC vampires do not play dumb and ignore it when Daeva run amok hijacking prospective vessels from the other clans &quot;because it's an innate ability for them&quot;. It's also an innate ability for vampires to instill fear, make people disappear, run out into oncoming traffic and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-02-2018, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T13:59:29-07:00","id":1231926,"title":"","content":"It's been like 3 pages of Awe back and forth. Maybe it should be it's own thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T14:15:03-07:00","id":1231933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231621#post1231621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what logic follows that just because Awe can do something, Dominate can do it, too. Or vice-versa. Sure, they both fall within the &quot;social engineering&quot; sphere, but only in the sense that Animalism and Protean both fall into the &quot;animals&quot; sphere. The effects, limitations, means, methods, are all vastly different. They are entirely different Disciplines. As stated earlier, Awe sets one up as a muse and celebrity, that's kind of its niche, and so that Devotion makes sense for it. Dominate has none of that, so you can't really call it precedent-setting for Dominate.<br /> <br /> Not to say if you can think of a way to do it with Dominate, you can't go for it (though I think the whole 'eye contact' thing being one of the core aspects of the Discipline that is also based in Vampire mythos makes it a bad idea to try to get rid of it from a narrative perspective). Using Majesty to justify things for Dominate, however, is flawed logic. Like saying Animalism can have a way to do agg damage with claws because Protean gets Claws of the Unholy and they're both animal-related Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You miss the point as to why people think a Devotion for Awe sets a precedent for Dominate. It's not about similarities between Majesty and Dominate in regards to what they do. The important part is that it shows Disciplines can be carried on through objects. That's it. That's why it sets a precedent that Dominate should be able to follow &quot;somehow&quot;. That last word was important. It means it might not end up being entirely the same, or even the same medium, but it means there is probably a conceivable way to imagine a devotion whom's effects are carried on through an object.<br /> <br /> A Dominate devotion that Mesmerizes the next person to look into a certain mirror would be <i>rad</i>, you must admit. And speaks to the &quot;eye contact&quot; thing in an indirect way.<br /> <br /> That said, concerning Dominate through video:<br /> Subliminal messages in film that hypnotize you into doing things are some of the most common urban legends concerning video that exist. A Dominate devotion that adds subliminal messages to video is absolutely thematic. The effect is still entering through the eyes, as well. It should probably have large drawbacks and limitations in order to not make it too powerful, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 07-02-2018, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T14:22:49-07:00","id":1231935,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> Are you saying this is all your house rules? Because it isn't supported by the book. By the book, the vampire creates an aura of power, and all the mechanical buffs that follow apply to the vampire and nobody else. It doesn't matter if someone was there at the start or not.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure how it affects player agency, since all Awe does (again, mechanically) is remove dice penalties and add a dice bonus to the user.<br /> <br /> Auspex give the user secrets, no matter how hard the target tries to hide them, from dot one.<br /> Obfuscate gives near-perfect invisibility from dot one.<br /> Dominate gives mind control from dot one.<br /> Protean gives near-invulnerability and an effectively free Haven from dot one<br /> <br /> And so on, and so on.<br /> <br /> I don't know why people get so up-in-arms about how supposedly overpowered Awe is and feel a need to nerf it into the ground with things like &quot;I always know when I'm affected, so I lash out!&quot; and &quot;It only works when I say so, because the book makes it too potent.&quot; All the signature disciplines are potent at dot one.It's a deliberate design decision.<br /> <br /> I also feel house rules don't belong in this thread at all, since they end up in lengthy, multi-page discussions, and most of the time nobody was asking for house rules to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T14:34:24-07:00","id":1231942,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Like I said a page or two ago as well, Awe, by itself, is really not making a Daeva's plans succeed on its own any time soon. It's really not that dangerous unless you believe a social roll can mind control someone into doing something they would never, ever do (like some people believe of natural 20's in D&amp;D social rolls as well...) which is simply not the case. This sounds like the entirety of tsuasi's problem. Like Rose has said before, Awe can't make something exist that isn't there. It can't make people agree to things they'd never do, it can only make them agree to things they probably wouldn't do, but there has to be a <i>chance</i> to begin with.<br /> <br /> &quot;it immediately deteriorated to Daeva players cockblocking other players' hunting attempts, date raping their ghouls and touchstones, and ripping them off by having their ghoul show up and pick everyone's pockets&quot; -&gt; How can you not do all of this better with Dominate? Seeing as the targets won't even <i>remember</i> in that case? How is this Daeva always aware of all hunting attempts and where they're happening? Are all of the other players' ghouls and touchstones sexually into her? (By Rose's express words, Awe doesn't automatically make people want you sexually or agree to sleep with you, I can find the quote if you want...) Why are people not retaliating after their pockets are clearly emptied each and every time the Daeva is near? So many questions, and none of them related to Awe.<br /> <br /> Also, you don't have to do anything specific to activate Awe. It just lends a supernatural grace to everything you do and say from that point onwards. So whether people arrive before or after doesn't matter, it's active all the time and enhancing you all the time. They see you when you have Awe on, boom, &quot;ooh, so graceful&quot;. Doesn't matter when you activate it.<br /> <br /> Awe is activate on the vampire, not on the onlookers. In RPG terminology it would be described as a &quot;buff&quot; to yourself, not a &quot;debuff&quot; on others.<br /> <br /> But yeah, anyway, the entire problem is allowing Awe to be mind control when it only buffs social rolls and takes away negatives (alright, it does slightly more than that, but not when it comes to <i>convincing people to do things</i>). If you wouldn't allow someone with very high social skills to do something with a roll, you shouldn't allow a vampire with approximately the same dicepool with Awe from doing it either. Is the gist of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 07-02-2018, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T14:40:49-07:00","id":1231944,"title":"","content":"Actually I think that, compared to other disciplines, Majesty is the most underpowered until the 3rd dot. Then it starts to become aligned, or even more powerful, than other counterpart.<br /> Even Nightmare 1, despite it is the most similar and almost a reversed copy of Awe, is quite more powerful than it thanks to 2 turns hallucinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T17:19:46-07:00","id":1231998,"title":"","content":"Question: The talk about Majesty and lashing out and mortals has me thinking about ghoul v. ghoul. Ghouls aren't quite mortal (they give up any supernatural merits they may have possessed). Neither are they Kindred. They can't lash out. Does that mean a ghoul subjected to Majesty by another ghoul is pretty much screwed? Is there a ghoul-specific method for ghouls to deal with this that gives them a bit more protection against other ghouls only? The ghoul book doesn't go into this as far as I recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24354-corbie","name":"Corbie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24354_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T17:55:40-07:00","id":1232002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231944#post1231944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think that, compared to other disciplines, Majesty is the most underpowered until the 3rd dot. Then it starts to become aligned, or even more powerful, than other counterpart.<br /> Even Nightmare 1, despite it is the most similar and almost a reversed copy of Awe, is quite more powerful than it thanks to 2 turns hallucinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The interesting thing about Majesty is that it's the only clan-specific Discipline of the bunch that's completely and unconditionally free until the third dot; given that its effects to that point are &quot;add your Majesty dots to Social rolls, ignore most Social penalties, and apply your Majesty dots as a penalty to attempts to notice stuff around you or see through you&quot; (and the less salient &quot;lay the groundwork for the higher-level powers&quot;), that's a very solid incentive for Daeva who aren't aiming to funnel their efforts into their clan's two physical Disciplines to become practiced at talking their way past problems.<br /> <br /> The Daeva Discipline wheelhouse is sort of a plain-yet-practical package that puts them in a space where they often have more Vitae to spare for less specialized applications of the Blood by virtue of their social focus \u2014 ghouls, the Vinculum, the Blush of Life, and so on all come into play a lot more readily with characters whose mechanics are geared to help them cycle Vitae through the mortal population, and Majesty is the medium through which the Daeva manage that all the more easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corbie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1231998#post1231998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: The talk about Majesty and lashing out and mortals has me thinking about ghoul v. ghoul. Ghouls aren't quite mortal (they give up any supernatural merits they may have possessed). Neither are they Kindred. They can't lash out. Does that mean a ghoul subjected to Majesty by another ghoul is pretty much screwed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means a ghoul subjected to Awe by another ghoul cannot negate the Social bonuses that ghoul receives. This does nothing to worsen the contested roll every other facet of the Discipline calls for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-02-2018, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T02:44:39-07:00","id":1233021,"title":"","content":"In our Session our ST insists when reading the Mystery of the Voivode (Call to Serve / 3rd Rank) (p158), that in order to use it and actually Blood Bond someone he must want to be Blood Bonded to you. I am trying to explain to him that the phrase 'The must want to follow, and they must want to follow immediately' is a fluff and not a mechanic...you cannot demand from someone else to agree to become blood bonded to you in order to use 'Call to Serve' as he thinks....Wtf i am so confused that i want your opinion about who is right?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T02:55:37-07:00","id":1233022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Montgomery Crobes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1233021#post1233021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our Session our ST insists when reading the Mystery of the Voivode (Call to Serve / 3rd Rank) (p158), that in order to use it and actually Blood Bond someone he must want to be Blood Bonded to you. I am trying to explain to him that the phrase 'The must want to follow, and they must want to follow immediately' is a fluff and not a mechanic...you cannot demand from someone else to agree to become blood bonded to you in order to use 'Call to Serve' as he thinks....Wtf i am so confused that i want your opinion about who is right?!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yea, it's fluff. It's just clarifying what the Dragon from the previous sentence wants, it's not stating a requirement for the use of the Coil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T03:00:48-07:00","id":1233023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Montgomery Crobes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1233021#post1233021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our Session our ST insists when reading the Mystery of the Voivode (Call to Serve / 3rd Rank) (p158), that in order to use it and actually Blood Bond someone he must want to be Blood Bonded to you. I am trying to explain to him that the phrase 'The must want to follow, and they must want to follow immediately' is a fluff and not a mechanic...you cannot demand from someone else to agree to become blood bonded to you in order to use 'Call to Serve' as he thinks....Wtf i am so confused that i want your opinion about who is right?!</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;They must want to follow&quot; means that they must be blood bonded because those who are blood bonded are compelled into wanting to follow your character. It's a description of the blood bond; not a prerequisite for applying the Coil. The second part stresses the importance of inflicting the blood bond quickly rather than over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T12:18:06-07:00","id":1233065,"title":"","content":"oh curious? Is a Ordo Dracul Twilight Judge more likely in your opinion, to grant a special dispensation on the Coil of Ziva.<br /> <br /> When theirs a experiment he Agree's would have Merit that would Benefit from it.<br /> <br /> or more practical uses to gain an agent who is better able to endure the ravages of his Humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T14:55:10-07:00","id":1233090,"title":"","content":"That's up to the individual judge. Yes, they can allow you access to it without repercussion, but why would they? what is it for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T15:02:32-07:00","id":1233092,"title":"","content":"I'd say it depends on the level of influence/positive regard the Ordo Dracul has within the domain at large. If they're the most powerful (Dragon prince, Axesworn hounds and sheriff, Mysteries Harpy etc.) it would be practiced openly and a Twilight Judge's permission wouldn't be needed.<br /> If they're somewhat influential and seek to be well-regarded, they'd likely be careful about granting permission only to those who they reasonably expect to be responsible with their other experiments and not go a murder binge.<br /> Alternatively, if they're planning to assist the Carthians in a massacre to seize power, learning it may be practically mandatory.<br /> If they don't care about other covenants' opinions they'll probably have lower standards as to who would be given permission but likely would not advertise it.<br /> If their influence is minor and they don't wish to draw the ire of the most powerful covenants, then those being allowed to learn it would probably be kept minimal, at least at an official level.<br /> As to how other covenants may learn about it, well that depends on how much multi-covenant memberships are permitted and how much of the special power whoring to non-status members goes on in the setting. If either are common, then I find it unlikely that Dragons would be able to keep their mysteries and scales a secret so official Ordo policy about that coil is going to be determined from there.<br /> <br /> I really don't think they prioritize the Humanity level of their wetworks operatives. The Humanity level of an Axesworn Knight that goes around assassinating others firsthand is not more sacrosanct than that Humanity level of the Dying Light Journeyman who is flays humans and kindred alive and times how long it takes for them to expire, nor is their service deemed more or less valuable than the Mysteries Oracle who shuns contact with other sentient beings for a month as they lock themself away in a sensory deprivation chamber and starve themself into torpor for about a year to induce an accurate precognitive trance for a few hours once they awaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T16:32:01-07:00","id":1233111,"title":"","content":"How do gangrel, species wide I mean, stay among the ranks of vampire society? They are animalistic and are known for the red rage, so I don't understand how they can get themselves into politics and such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T17:42:27-07:00","id":1233122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1233111#post1233111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do gangrel, species wide I mean, stay among the ranks of vampire society? They are animalistic and are known for the red rage, so I don't understand how they can get themselves into politics and such</div> </div> </div> </div>Politics isn't always people in suits being gentle with each other. Sometimes it's gang fights and Survivor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T17:43:31-07:00","id":1233123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1233111#post1233111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do gangrel, species wide I mean, stay among the ranks of vampire society? They are animalistic and are known for the red rage, so I don't understand how they can get themselves into politics and such</div> </div> </div> </div>They're only animalistic in the sense that their powerset affinities encourage them to spend time around animals. They're still vampires made from people and their 2e mechanics are angled toward steering whatever frenzy they find themselves dealing with. They're no more handicapped by participation in the All Night Society than the Nosferatu are \u2014 territorial squabbles are an evergreen point of contention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T21:55:09-07:00","id":1233141,"title":"","content":"Ahh I think I understand now. While yes, they are quite beastly, they do make up for it by being dangerous adversaries in case of open conflict happening, and probably have better relations with the &quot;lower&quot; people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T02:32:05-07:00","id":1233158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1233141#post1233141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh I think I understand now. While yes, they are quite beastly, they do make up for it by being dangerous adversaries in case of open conflict happening, and probably have better relations with the &quot;lower&quot; people</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, one of my favorite archetypes of the political Gangrel is the aggressive CEO businessman, using force of will and aggressive takeovers and bullying as her modus operandi. And to be fair, both business and politics can be really dirty and animalistic. More then a few politicians, executives and managers rule as if they where the team alpha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T13:38:06-07:00","id":1233256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1233111#post1233111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do gangrel, species wide I mean, stay among the ranks of vampire society? They are animalistic and are known for the red rage, so I don't understand how they can get themselves into politics and such</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was wondering for a bit is the Die Cap of their humanity on all rolls to resist frenzy, before or after modifiers?<br /> <br /> MUCH better if its after modifiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T20:17:57-07:00","id":1233330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1233256#post1233256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Was wondering for a bit is the Die Cap of their humanity on all rolls to resist frenzy, before or after modifiers?<br /> <br /> MUCH better if its after modifiers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's probably after modifiers, it wouldn't be much of a clan bane if it didn't really affect most members of the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T21:50:05-07:00","id":1233345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1233330#post1233330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably after modifiers, it wouldn't be much of a clan bane if it didn't really affect most members of the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also &quot;all dice pools to resist frenzy are limited thus&quot; is more straightforwardly read as a universal cap instead of trying to read a bonus-applicable maximum starting point into a fairly direct statement.<br /> <br /> First Edition's Humanity cap explicitly applied before penalties, but given the nature of the mechanics Second Edition puts that limit on and its more central place in the game's ludonarrative toolbox, I don't feel it makes much of a difference for the cap to be a simple &quot;no more than this many dice, period&quot; effect \u2014 you'll still only be rolling ten dice in the absolute best of circumstances and more likely less than six, and for the Feral Curse in particular the workaround is &quot;get more dice on the roll and a say in the outcome, but if you fail you're not stopping until you roll for Humanity loss.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T15:16:17-07:00","id":1233525,"title":"","content":"Can a Vampire exorcize or do abjurations?<br /> <br /> Does she substitute the integrity rating needed with her humanity rating?<br /> <br /> If so how does virtue/vice bonuses/penalties work on her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24344-zaser321","name":"zaser321","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T15:42:35-07:00","id":1233531,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s up for the ST to decide. I usually permit it. Either by allowing the rituals and merits to be purchased and allowing Humanity to be substituted for Integrity or as a Dominate/Resilience devotion that can be used to perform exorcisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T08:27:47-07:00","id":1234647,"title":"","content":"So, weird question. Spirit's Touch, most people tend to assume you need to touch the object/place to use it, especially since in 1e you did. But despite the name, the power says you just turn your senses on an object/place the same way you do a person, and never mentions having to touch anything. Am I understanding correctly that in 2e you needn't actually touch what you're using Spirit's Touch on?<br /> <br /> <br /> (And as for Exorcisms, I allow it, substituting Humanity as appropriate, and with Mask/Dirge replacing Virtue/Vice (better to call on your human side to use human 'rituals', after all))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 07-13-2018, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T09:53:15-07:00","id":1234684,"title":"","content":"Abjuration explicitly calls out using the power of the soul. Pretty much every supernatural has its soul transmuted or maimed in some way. I don't allow it, because anything whose soul has been changed enough to no longer have Integrity no longer has the metaphysical power to abjure any longer.<br /> <br /> Summoning and exorcism just make use of manipulating Conditions in a way that, while ritualized, don't really do anything magical, and so those are fine. I mean, lighting a fight to make resonance for a Fire Spirit isn't rocket science (per the in-book example). But you need Integrity to Abjure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T11:38:33-07:00","id":1234722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1234684#post1234684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abjuration explicitly calls out using the power of the soul. Pretty much every supernatural has its soul transmuted or maimed in some way. I don't allow it, because anything whose soul has been changed enough to no longer have Integrity no longer has the metaphysical power to abjure any longer.<br /> <br /> Summoning and exorcism just make use of manipulating Conditions in a way that, while ritualized, don't really do anything magical, and so those are fine. I mean, lighting a fight to make resonance for a Fire Spirit isn't rocket science (per the in-book example). But you need Integrity to Abjure.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just sounds to me like a reason to fluff it differently for other character types. But to each their own, I can see either side as being valid. One note I always make is that no matter how an integrity-equivalent works, I always have a high level be what's important either way; a Werewolf is better off at Harmony 5, but one at Harmony 9 has a better connection to rituals focused around 'human will'. Even Beasts with a higher Satiety are more able to sever ephemeral ties when their own ephemeral side isn't getting in the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T17:30:43-07:00","id":1234829,"title":"","content":"When it comes down to it, I don't think house rules belong in this thread unless someone is explicitly asking for them (and in that case, it's not really so simple a question anymore).<br /> <br /> As such, I don't think it's appropriate to answer with &quot;the answer is that anyone can use abjuration, human or not&quot; because this is not supported by the RAW. Unless a book or writer answers (or has answered) differently, abjuration and binding and warding require Integrity, though it is ultimately up to the GM and how they want to handle it.<br /> <br /> Though I suppose you could also interpret it that someone without Integrity doesn't get the modifiers based on Integrity, I find that to be further of a stretch.<br /> <br /> The two posts prior to mine stated &quot;I do it this way,&quot; so I tried to provide an answer using the book rather than how I personally run it (which I find to be entirely irrelevant to the &quot;Simple Answer&quot; thread).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T17:55:22-07:00","id":1234835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1234829#post1234829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes down to it, I don't think house rules belong in this thread unless someone is explicitly asking for them (and in that case, it's not really so simple a question anymore).<br /> <br /> As such, I don't think it's appropriate to answer with &quot;the answer is that anyone can use abjuration, human or not&quot; because this is not supported by the RAW. Unless a book or writer answers (or has answered) differently, abjuration and binding and warding require Integrity, though it is ultimately up to the GM and how they want to handle it.<br /> <br /> Though I suppose you could also interpret it that someone without Integrity doesn't get the modifiers based on Integrity, I find that to be further of a stretch.<br /> <br /> The two posts prior to mine stated &quot;I do it this way,&quot; so I tried to provide an answer using the book rather than how I personally run it (which I find to be entirely irrelevant to the &quot;Simple Answer&quot; thread).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something you can argue as RAW, too. Per Humanity:<br /> <br /> &quot;This system replaces the Integrity system in in the World of<br /> Darkness Rulebook or The God-Machine Chronicle. Mortal<br /> characters who are Embraced replace Integrity with Humanity,<br /> and start with seven dots (regardless of their Integrity scores).<br /> <b>These ratings are compatible</b>. For example, if a Discipline affects<br /> a vampire character based on her Humanity rating, Integrity will<br /> work similarly on her mortal counterpart.&quot;<br /> <br /> One can argue that Humanity is compatible for the sake of Abjuration, per that text.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T03:05:18-07:00","id":1234896,"title":"","content":"Abjuration is the only one that's informed by Integrity. Exorcism, Binding and Warding are based on knowledge about the entity and how to manipulate its nature, rather than any innate spiritual strength. Technically a robot should be able to perform those, if properly programmed.<br /> Also, I think house rules are good answers if the book is ambiguous and has no definitive answer, but only if properly marked as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-for