=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T11:37:02-08:00","id":1267362,"title":"","content":"The second dot of Courtoisie's Fighting Style - am I correct in reading the effect as &quot;pick one of these&quot;, or do people allow multiple swaps?<br /> <br /> I know the equivalent Spina Disc gave you a menu and one swap per success, but that'd be pretty substantial for a single Merit benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T07:44:28-08:00","id":1267570,"title":"","content":"was reading half damned a bit and wondered... the Protectionists from near the end of the book, <br /> <br /> <br /> How you think they'd feel about 'Ornamental Ghouls'<br /> <br /> or leave them alone as long as their master is pleased with them as long as they can smile and curtsey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T01:58:57-08:00","id":1267790,"title":"","content":"Ayyy, thanks for the Auspex answers! <br /> <br /> As another question: does it ever concretely explain what the Cacophony is and how it functions, or provide mechanics beyond the Cacophony Savvy merit? It seems to be at least partially mystical, if not completely so. But it talks about a code, but also in a way that's at least partially just sort of like intuitively, on some level, understood by Vampires (even if not mastered without some amount of effort)?<br /> <br /> Any sort of enlightenment regarding this would be great, even if it's just &quot;yeah it's intentionally vague&quot;. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T07:35:33-08:00","id":1267838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1267790#post1267790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As another question: does it ever concretely explain what the Cacophony is and how it functions,</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1ys5jnf4ypMYyoyYQB0qF7VTiHLDANUcOtoxfRg7QvNw/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> lexicon</a>, it's underground vampire culture. It works the same way regular clandestine communication works except vampires are involved. You learn what channels to keep up with in your locale and keep a hand in to stay on the relevant mailing lists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems to be at least partially mystical, if not completely so. </div> </div> </div>It's mystical in the same sense that the effects of a vampire living in a place is partially mystical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T18:03:49-08:00","id":1269044,"title":"","content":"Does the armor gained from Oath of the True Knight stack with any mundane armor such as reinforced clothing?<br /> <br /> Also, would it be reasonable to assume that the armor gained from that Merit is basically &quot;status armor&quot;, as in; people are less willing or able to hit you because of who you are? Does that mean frenzying Kindred or Kindred outsiders who have no clue who you are don't suffer the armor penalty when they attack you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T18:10:26-08:00","id":1269047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1269044#post1269044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the armor gained from Oath of the True Knight stack with any mundane armor such as reinforced clothing?<br /> <br /> Also, would it be reasonable to assume that the armor gained from that Merit is basically &quot;status armor&quot;, as in; people are less willing or able to hit you because of who you are? Does that mean frenzying Kindred or Kindred outsiders who have no clue who you are don't suffer the armor penalty when they attack you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditionally armor of the metaphysical variety don't stack with mundane armor that way unless noted by the text.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;status armor&quot;, nope. While the text leaves it open how it could manifest(I'd argue a more Resilience style incarnation as the norm), it is none the less essentially a magical incarnation of the authority vested in the vampire. Folks who don't know will find their bullets and knives sliding off as much the regular offender.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T20:28:16-08:00","id":1269084,"title":"","content":"Can oath of the model prisoner be used by a Hunter who is captured to promise humane treatment in exchange for dutiful behavior from them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T20:43:39-08:00","id":1269089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1269084#post1269084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can oath of the model prisoner be used by a Hunter who is captured to promise humane treatment in exchange for dutiful behavior from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>In exchange for them not tormenting him, he could not attempt to leave, or sow chaos for them (which includes attacking them).<br /> <br /> He could ask to learn it from them, to be a part of it. Or if he already knows it (or found out from another) he can make the oath without their assent being necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T21:54:33-08:00","id":1269119,"title":"","content":"I think if he was a hostage they have reason to keep alive and treat humanely they may see advantage in convincing a Notary to Witness the Oath","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T02:33:26-08:00","id":1269157,"title":"","content":"Notaries usually refuse to notarize oaths that involve humans or ghouls. If they break that practice by binding the life of the prince to a Masquerade breaching serial murderer of kindred, that notary better make damn sure the prince doesn't survive. (I always found that oath to be more useful to effortlessly murder the prince. And since Invictus oaths aren't proprietary, it's a cheap tool for suicidal hunters. Take the oath, set yourself on fire and kindred society will eat itself. Or better yet, force it on some other kindred the hunters plan to kill anyway.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-20-2018, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T02:39:48-08:00","id":1269159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1267838#post1267838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1ys5jnf4ypMYyoyYQB0qF7VTiHLDANUcOtoxfRg7QvNw/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> lexicon</a>, it's underground vampire culture. It works the same way regular clandestine communication works except vampires are involved. You learn what channels to keep up with in your locale and keep a hand in to stay on the relevant mailing lists.<br /> <br /> It's mystical in the same sense that the effects of a vampire living in a place is partially mystical.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, yeah, that all makes sense. Between the &quot;Mortals walk the streets, and there is a humming in the back of their lizard brains [...] The Mortal wants to hum along to the Cacophony.&quot; and the. . .sometimes outrageousness of Cacophony Savvy (the second dot letting you, without any rolls or ways to resist, discover any new Kindred's favored places to feed and names they go by, without any sort of qualifiers or conditions), I felt it best to ask around and see if there was something I was missing. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T06:10:22-08:00","id":1269200,"title":"","content":"I think a Notary could be convinced to make an exception if they have the teenage daughter of a hunter and want to keep her alive and unharmed but not see her cause trouble, as a bargaining chip with her Father.<br /> <br /> or think theyd suggest Conditioning or blood bonds instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T06:40:26-08:00","id":1269207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1269157#post1269157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the oath, set yourself on fire and kindred society will eat itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very explicitly not how it works. Taking an oath to not make trouble for your captors while in their custody and then self-immolating is trying to make trouble for your captors and nobody involved is making an attempt to brutalize, torture, or execute you unauthorized \u2014 you just will die that little bit faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T07:51:58-08:00","id":1269227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1269207#post1269207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's very explicitly not how it works. Taking an oath to not make trouble for your captors while in their custody and then self-immolating is trying to make trouble for your captors and nobody involved is making an attempt to brutalize, torture, or execute you unauthorized \u2014 you just will die that little bit faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually oaths are explicitly designed so one party can fuck over the other party by reneging prematurely on the deal.<br /> And Oath of the Model Prisoner is a special snowflake case to boot. It doesn't require a notary. It doesn't require the captors to be willing parties. And if either party reneges on it, a completely uninvolved third party suffers the consequences.<br /> <br /> Tell me again why a sociopathic group of serial killers (hunters) dedicated to destroying another group of sociopathic killers (vampires) wouldn't use a magic spell to kill the leader of the vampires at the cost of self immolating themself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T08:12:56-08:00","id":1269237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1269227#post1269227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Oath of the Model Prisoner is a special snowflake case to boot. It doesn't require a notary. It doesn't require the captors to be willing parties. And if either party reneges on it, a completely uninvolved third party suffers the consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's astounding that you managed to get even one of these three things more than passably right.<br /> <br /> There's <i>a rumor that</i> the Oath of <i>Abstinence</i> can be sworn without a Notary as part of its status as a weird Oath with no second party \u2014 the Oath of the Model Prisoner explicitly mentions bringing the subject before a Notary in its description and specifies its lack of need for captorial assent as a thing you can leverage <i>if you are yourself a Notary or have been taught the Oath</i>. &quot;I can set consequences for my unauthorized mistreatment while imprisoned by you&quot; being a thing that characters can use as insurance doesn't translate to &quot;I can self-harm to hurt my captors&quot; in any sensible reading of the Oath. Besides which, you don't think the vast majority of Invictus vampires are going to think twice about <i>teaching a vampire hunter this agreement?</i> By your own description, they're a group of sociopathic killers \u2014 they're under no obligation to play softball as members of the covenant <i>built around keeping the Masquerade</i>.<br /> <br /> The highest relevant authority suffers a point of lethal damage and knows the reason why <i>in circumstances where an offender is losing Willpower and taking aggravated damage</i>. Those circumstances are &quot;While imprisoned, you try to escape or bring chaos to your captors&quot; and &quot;While you are imprisoned, your captors attempt to brutalize, torture, or execute you without a sentence from the highest echelons of local vampire society.&quot; Again: Killing yourself is, at best,<i> not them doing those things they're not supposed to do</i>, and at worst is <i>you doing those things you're not supposed to do</i>. Yeah, sure, let's suppose the Prince takes a point of lethal damage in the event that it counts as the latter. <i>He can take more lethal damage than you can take aggravated damage and having you locked down or formally executed with impunity might not even ping it a second time.</i><br /> <br /> It's a bad read all around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T09:32:44-08:00","id":1269265,"title":"","content":"Many hunters are just trying to be neighbourhood watch. I could see them eagerly playing the part of dutiful hostage if they thought it would keep them alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T23:08:35-08:00","id":1270289,"title":"","content":"Would an eating disorder carry over into a vampire's feeding habits after her Embrace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T03:32:22-08:00","id":1270300,"title":"","content":"Uh...sure I guess? I don't think there's anything in the book about persistent Conditions dropping off due to the Embrace.<br /> <br /> Some of them would have their effects lessened I suppose. Or exacerbated. That would be an interesting type of horror -- the chronic over-eater being unable to ever keep anything down, or perhaps it translating into an inability to keep from exsanguinating their victims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T19:48:05-08:00","id":1270498,"title":"","content":"Curious On Feeding Is it safe to say that a &quot;Willing&quot; victim is not defined by moral consent.<br /> <br /> e.g. someone compelled by Majesty would gain swooning not scarred.<br /> <br /> Is it safe to say being ordered to submit to a feeding by dominate is a very scary experience.<br /> <br /> Don't see how it could be otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T20:19:44-08:00","id":1270505,"title":"","content":"Anyone under the influence of a vinculum or application of a discipline is not considered \u201cwilling\u201d. <br /> <br /> Swooning vs Scarred is applied based on how the vampire goes about feeding, not whether or not the individual is \u201cwilling\u201d. Does the vampire attempt to feed off the person under false pretenses and without resorting to physical assault? If yes, that\u2019s usually Swooning. Does the vampire simply maneuver to sink their teeth into the victim and feed? If that\u2019s the methodology, then that\u2019s Scarred.<br /> <br /> The person ordered to submit to being fed upon via Dominate isn\u2019t going to remember being fed upon. They\u2019re mesmerized and ordered to submit. Mesmerize breaks with the attendant Lethal damage from the feeding but they\u2019re usually under the effects of Swooning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T20:27:48-08:00","id":1270508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <