<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1273359#post1273359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the core book when it talks about the Daeva weakness it mentions that the obsession the Daeva has towards a mortal has a lot of the traits of a 2nd stage blood bond.<br /> <br /> Does this include the humanity 3 breaking point for causing direct or indirect harm to the obsession?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dependent Condition explicitly replicates all the effects of a second-stage blood bond, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T20:26:17-08:00","id":1273380,"title":"","content":"A curious thing I came up with.<br /> <br /> if a Kindred knows Coil of Ziva and raises his effective Humanity to 10 it says it will Deactivated any clan banes but the Ventrue clan bane.<br /> <br /> For Nosferatu does this cause shapeshifting?<br /> <br /> My guess?<br /> <br /> <br /> It does but little by little as part of pursuing the Coil. or raising humanity.<br /> <br /> Rather then all at once.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T21:37:14-08:00","id":1273389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1273379#post1273379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dependent Condition explicitly replicates all the effects of a second-stage blood bond, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>OOF. In that case I guess I'm going to have to categorize the Daeva up with the Nosferatu in terms of impactful Banes.<br /> <br /> Gangrel come next, Mehket and Ventrue bring up the rear. Thanks for the answer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24063-admiral-cheesecake","name":"Admiral Cheesecake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T22:32:55-08:00","id":1273395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1273380#post1273380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A curious thing I came up with.<br /> <br /> if a Kindred knows Coil of Ziva and raises his effective Humanity to 10 it says it will Deactivated any clan banes but the Ventrue clan bane.<br /> <br /> For Nosferatu does this cause shapeshifting?<br /> <br /> My guess?<br /> <br /> <br /> It does but little by little as part of pursuing the Coil. or raising humanity.<br /> <br /> Rather then all at once.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to answer the nosferatu question. I believe that, say the vampire was absolutely hideous (and believing that humanity 10 would rid the curse), he would lose subtle traits, like a slithering, snake like tongue, while one with a perverting gaze would lose that. I think this because the nosferatu clanbook says that these little things are what cause the curse, as the big ugly stuff is merely shock factor (which is true in real life)<br /> <br /> As for my own question, is the wyrm scale, heart removable surgery very niche or something? I agree it would be great with dealing with stake crazy mortals, but not being able to gain vitae through feeding is pretty bad (which I don't quite understand why it can't just be a reduced rate, since the text states that veins are moved into a mockery of a heart)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T23:01:45-08:00","id":1273396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1273395#post1273395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for my own question, is the wyrm scale, heart removable surgery very niche or something? I agree it would be great with dealing with stake crazy mortals, but not being able to gain vitae through feeding is pretty bad (which I don't quite understand why it can't just be a reduced rate, since the text states that veins are moved into a mockery of a heart)</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole &quot;you can regenerate from complete bodily destruction&quot; thing has its appeal to the extremely paranoid or the absurdly dedicated, particularly given the options available for receiving Vitae through other channels.<br /> <br /> It's a specific application of the vampiric nature through the use of occult processes to do something kind of weird for vampires, and it's a specific application based on knowledge of a fifth-dot Coil effect \u2014 &quot;niche&quot; is practically in the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T07:07:11-08:00","id":1273433,"title":"","content":"I can see the value in that then. to be honest I've never really factored in regenerating from the heart (obviously meaning you can be reckless in a desperate situation, or fake death). Have you ever used the scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T07:23:36-08:00","id":1273438,"title":"","content":"I see many uses for the Scale if your from the Circle. And want to <i>test </i>a mortal hero<br /> <br /> Scale allows the possiblety of him triumphing over you with you reviving to continue tempering him.<br /> <br /> or a valuble agent on a suicide mission.<br /> <br /> <br /> Curious where to put the box containing the heart? Best to keep it at hand, or in another city?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T07:32:40-08:00","id":1273439,"title":"","content":"honestly I think more of the sanctum when I think of testing mortals (I've only recently read about the crones belief in mortal heroes)<br /> <br /> honestly the Scale would be a big fuck you to the Malleus maleficarum, especially the longineus lot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T08:11:16-08:00","id":1273440,"title":"","content":"a &quot;Fuck You&quot; Because they went to all the work of killing him but he <i>doesn't </i>stay dead?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 12-08-2018, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T18:49:50-08:00","id":1273529,"title":"","content":"So here's something about Riding the Wave that isn't clear to me.<br /> <br /> Can you whip yourself into a frenzy to then attempt to ride it, or do you need Coil of the Wyrm for that?<br /> <br /> Would you say that even without Coil of the Wyrm you can attempt Riding the Wave when the situation makes sense for it, even if the Storyteller didn't already ask for you to resist frenzy? Say something pisses you off, not enough for an actual frenzy check, but enough that it severely pisses you off, can use your anger to fuel your Beast and attempt a Riding the Wave? Would you say that's legit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T18:53:35-08:00","id":1273533,"title":"","content":"Riding the Wave is an alternative to resisting Frenzy when you face a Frenzy trigger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T19:04:48-08:00","id":1273535,"title":"","content":"something on ordo Dracul I was just wondering? do you need a mentor for your mystery with a better grasp on it then yours., or is it ok for someone to achieve things through experimentation<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing is Coil of the Ascendant doesn't become more resistant to sunlight till 5 Dots is reached.<br /> <br /> I could see them cautiously placing a single limb into the sunlight while making sure the rest of their body is totally shielded. with the limb in question being incinerated within seconds.<br /> <br /> as part of their experiments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T02:04:02-08:00","id":1273564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1273529#post1273529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's something about Riding the Wave that isn't clear to me.<br /> <br /> Can you whip yourself into a frenzy to then attempt to ride it, or do you need Coil of the Wyrm for that?<br /> <br /> Would you say that even without Coil of the Wyrm you can attempt Riding the Wave when the situation makes sense for it, even if the Storyteller didn't already ask for you to resist frenzy? Say something pisses you off, not enough for an actual frenzy check, but enough that it severely pisses you off, can use your anger to fuel your Beast and attempt a Riding the Wave? Would you say that's legit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Another hot topic in the past <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I and other were in favour of the idea that almost everything is a Frenzy threat for a vampirebut not everything requires a roll to resist to it if you want to. <br /> Let's make an example: your prey is escaping? That's for sure something that make you frustrated or hungry, not enough to threat your ability to maintain the control but enough to be able to free your beast if you wish.<br /> Same if you are fighting but still not hurted.<br /> <br /> Beast is always lurking from the very deep of the vampire shadows waiting for anything to be able to free itself. The Frenzy rolls are just something occurring when the stimulus is actually threatening the vampire capability to mantain the control.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other side I wouldn't allow to free the beast (and ride it) if you are in a quite place, not angry and not hungry at all. <br /> With the coil you can free (and ride) the beast even in your haven when you are calm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T13:33:32-08:00","id":1273622,"title":"","content":"curious? on a feeding action how to account for help from a ghoul who lures someone out to be a vampires snack?<br /> <br /> Teamwork actions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T21:42:56-08:00","id":1273662,"title":"","content":"team work action would probably be best, but at the same time it could just be individual actions (example being your ghoul intimidates a party girl, with you as the savior","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T07:52:46-08:00","id":1273717,"title":"","content":"oh giving a bonus to your feeding rolly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T00:36:39-08:00","id":1274152,"title":"","content":"In the core book, the paragraph on the banes of the strix, when they explain the counting bane i don t understand if the strix must count one specific kind of item or ALL items in disarray<br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T02:52:34-08:00","id":1274160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1274152#post1274152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the core book, the paragraph on the banes of the strix, when they explain the counting bane i don t understand if the strix must count one specific kind of item or ALL items in disarray<br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>All small items in disarray. Like a hand full of rice being thrown on the ground, pearls being thrown on the ground, coins, etc. I wouldn't go as far as counting things that are naturally in disarray. For example, a strix in the forest with this bane isn't going to count all the leafs and dead tree branches constantly, that would be ridiculous, but anything else is fair game in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T04:59:38-08:00","id":1274688,"title":"","content":"Has this been done anywhere? If so where are the rules for it?<br /> Vampires are corpses and their only internal organs in the torso are the heart and stomach. So they dont have to worry about all the specifics keeping a person alive. <br /> <br /> My point being that someone must have figured they could do some extreme body modification on themselves for benefits that a human would not survive.<br /> I'm talking beyond just hidden flesh caches. Maybe some implanted metal plates around the heart to avoid staking or some steel wires in the neck to protect from decapitation. <br /> Or anything else the player comes up with. <br /> I figure the more extreme stuff would take a high medicine roll from someone performing the surgery and some of them would have drawbacks.<br /> <br /> So yeah. I think someone must have tried. Just dont know where and the amount of books across both gamelines scares the crap out of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13691-margul","name":"Margul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T05:11:02-08:00","id":1274693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Margul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1274688#post1274688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has this been done anywhere? If so where are the rules for it?<br /> Vampires are corpses and their only internal organs in the torso are the heart and stomach. So they dont have to worry about all the specifics keeping a person alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know Vampires do not have ANY living internal organ (not even brain, heart etc). I'm pretty sure to have read they do not have brain and heart signals at all. Buy they still have any internal organs frozen in the status they were at the moment of their death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T05:39:13-08:00","id":1274697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Margul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1274688#post1274688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has this been done anywhere? If so where are the rules for it?<br /> Vampires are corpses and their only internal organs in the torso are the heart and stomach. So they dont have to worry about all the specifics keeping a person alive.<br /> <br /> My point being that someone must have figured they could do some extreme body modification on themselves for benefits that a human would not survive.<br /> I'm talking beyond just hidden flesh caches. Maybe some implanted metal plates around the heart to avoid staking or some steel wires in the neck to protect from decapitation.<br /> Or anything else the player comes up with.<br /> I figure the more extreme stuff would take a high medicine roll from someone performing the surgery and some of them would have drawbacks.<br /> <br /> So yeah. I think someone must have tried. Just dont know where and the amount of books across both gamelines scares the crap out of me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes. In the first edition covenant and bloodline books there are several factions across the various covenant books and individual bloodlines that engage in extensive body modification or stunt showmanship to highlight the fact that they're capable of doing things beyond human limitations with willpower and vitae expenditure.<br /> <br /> As far as second edition is concerned, the mechanics for Scales and Night Doctor Surgery does infer that there are limits to organ removals, blood transfusions, exsanguinations etc.<br /> <br /> As for inserting armor underneath their skin or becoming high end prison wallets, that's ST discretion. Do keep in mind however, that when a vampire uses the Blush of Life, a vampire is effectively alive and needs to eat, drink, excrete waste, can grow hair etc. and shows up as alive under medical examination. And also, by default, a vampire's body reverts itself to their physical state at their time of death every day so you may want to take those factors into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T08:55:53-08:00","id":1274728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1274693#post1274693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know Vampires do not have ANY living internal organ (not even brain, heart etc). I'm pretty sure to have read they do not have brain and heart signals at all. Buy they still have any internal organs frozen in the status they were at the moment of their death.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah this is correct. Unless a vampire uses Blush of Life, his body is dead, just a cold, walking corpse, puppeteered by the mystical blood of the vampire. While a vampire needs his eyes to see, his mouth and tongue to speak, and his fangs and gullet to drink blood, he doesn't actually need any of those organs to stay alive.<br /> <br /> You cut a vampire's leg off, and the only thing you'll achieve is slowing her down a little.<br /> You shoot a bullet through the vampire's skull, and at best he'd be annoyed because he's gonna have to drink some more blood now to heal his wounds. <br /> You disembowel a vampire and spill her guts out, and she will be slowed down, certainly, she might even think twice about continuing the fight, but death will not be a concern for her.<br /> <br /> The only organ the vampire needs is his heart. Staking that and he will be in torpor. Destroying it and he will die, for real this time.<br /> <br /> I've heard stories that even beheading a vampire isn't enough to kill him in VTR, but there are no clear rules on this. But, if you adhere to the idea that a vampire doesn't need any of his organs other than his heart, then it makes sense that beheading him wouldn't kill him. It would blind him, disorient him, render him mute and make feeding impossible for him, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T11:10:13-08:00","id":1274740,"title":"","content":"vampires die from beheading, UNLESS you use the heart removal surgery scale","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T11:16:33-08:00","id":1274743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1274740#post1274740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">vampires die from beheading, UNLESS you use the heart removal surgery scale</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the decapitation blow fills their health track with aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T11:17:55-08:00","id":1274744,"title":"","content":"ahh really? my bad Ventrue life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T15:58:39-08:00","id":1274797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1274728#post1274728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah this is correct. Unless a vampire uses Blush of Life, his body is dead, just a cold, walking corpse, puppeteered by the mystical blood of the vampire. While a vampire needs his eyes to see, his mouth and tongue to speak, and his fangs and gullet to drink blood, he doesn't actually need any of those organs to stay alive.<br /> <br /> You cut a vampire's leg off, and the only thing you'll achieve is slowing her down a little.<br /> You shoot a bullet through the vampire's skull, and at best he'd be annoyed because he's gonna have to drink some more blood now to heal his wounds.<br /> You disembowel a vampire and spill her guts out, and she will be slowed down, certainly, she might even think twice about continuing the fight, but death will not be a concern for her.<br /> <br /> The only organ the vampire needs is his heart. Staking that and he will be in torpor. Destroying it and he will die, for real this time.<br /> <br /> I've heard stories that even beheading a vampire isn't enough to kill him in VTR, but there are no clear rules on this. But, if you adhere to the idea that a vampire doesn't need any of his organs other than his heart, then it makes sense that beheading him wouldn't kill him. It would blind him, disorient him, render him mute and make feeding impossible for him, however.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> destroying heart does not have any definitive effect. Staking the vampire heart it's just a mystical bane (it works JUST WITH WOOD and not with metal i.e.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T16:12:58-08:00","id":1274798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1274797#post1274797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> destroying heart does not have any definitive effect. Staking the vampire heart it's just a mystical bane (it works JUST WITH WOOD and not with metal i.e.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. With the Surgical Heart Removal Scale for Coil of the Wyrm, it mentions that if the surgeon accidentally destroys the heart during the process (which happens if you roll a dramatic failure), the vampire suffers Final Death. It also mentions that if the successfully removed heart is destroyed, the vampire also suffers Final Death. On top of that, the vampire needs his heart to process Vitae (the Scale states that without his heart in his body, the vampire can't gain Vitae).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T19:41:50-08:00","id":1274823,"title":"","content":"Those are all related to the mystical effects of the scale. There is no evidence that these are universally applicable, rather than only applicable to the scale.<br /> <br /> If you shoot a vampire in the heart, there is no special effect. Unless the projectile is made of wood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T20:55:24-08:00","id":1274827,"title":"","content":"well, it's probably the total destruction of the heart, such as burning the damn thing to a crisp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T23:09:35-08:00","id":1274840,"title":"","content":"I agree with Maina here. As far as the vampire doesn't suffer full aggravated it shouldn't normally die. What you mentioned is a particular effect of that scale.<br /> While in 1 ed. It was clearily stated cutting off head would have resulted in final death, in 2 ed it is not. Furthermore a shotgun in the heart would definitely destroy heart (as head) but the kindred will not incurr in final death (if not suffering enough damages).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-17-2018, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T05:07:48-08:00","id":1274864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1274823#post1274823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are all related to the mystical effects of the scale. There is no evidence that these are universally applicable, rather than only applicable to the scale.<br /> <br /> If you shoot a vampire in the heart, there is no special effect. Unless the projectile is made of wood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's one way to interpret it, but not the only way. After all, it's a popular trope in many media, destroying a vampire's heart is one of the only reliable ways to destroy a vampire in a lot of settings and stories. Read that I said <i>destroying</i>, not just damaging it.<br /> <br /> In V5 there's a flaw you can get that makes your character suffer Final Death when staked through the heart, instead of just entering torpor. I know, it's not the same, it's not even the same game line, but something to think about.<br /> <br /> Also, just hitting a vampire's heart with a wooden projectile isn't enough to torpor him, it has to be a wooden stake specifically. None of that &quot;bullets with a wooden tip&quot; nonsense. Crossbows work because they can fire wooden stakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T05:19:13-08:00","id":1274867,"title":"","content":"I have no evidence of this, but heart and brain are mystically important in my opinion because in the first resides the beast (and the power to process blood and animate the corpse), while in the second the Man (the mind), so if you destroy one of this part (with aggravated damage) you eliminate the component in it. This means that the vampire would survive (in torpor whit no beast, in wassail with no man).<br /> In case of beheading we would have a frenzyng body and a torpid head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T19:35:59-08:00","id":1275005,"title":"","content":"is the vampiric condition of creative stagnation still considered mystical? I've noticed it is, while downplayed, still an element of their condition, but it now sounds more pseudo mystical, much like the vigil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T11:09:40-08:00","id":1275123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1275005#post1275005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is the vampiric condition of creative stagnation still considered mystical? I've noticed it is, while downplayed, still an element of their condition, but it now sounds more pseudo mystical, much like the vigil</div> </div> </div> </div>Not mystical as far as I know, just a byproduct of longevity. It's a fact that as humans grow older, they become more conservative and less capable of learning new things. That's more true for vampires who live for centuries. After a while, you just become pretty much incapable of adapting to new developments. That's where 'the sleep of the ages' (e.g. torpor) comes in. Going in torpor rebuilds and refreshes the mind of the vampire, reverting it back to a younger state, making the vampire more willing and capable of adapting and learning new things.<br /> <br /> That's just my interpretation though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T11:29:05-08:00","id":1275128,"title":"","content":"sounds reasonable, and much simpler to actually roleplay. thanks for answering!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T12:24:34-08:00","id":1275140,"title":"","content":"Whats a Ventru probably going to do with a Revenant who he thinks is a worthy Kindred, but not a worthy Ventru? <br /> <br /> Send him packing? <br /> <br /> Take him to Elysium a few times Hoping he comes to someones notice?<br /> <br /> or try introducing him to a prospective sire?<br /> <br /> If hes worked for you faithfully and you feel the need to reward him but he doesn't have the poise of a Ventru?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T12:36:25-08:00","id":1275144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1275140#post1275140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats a Ventru probably going to do with a Revenant who he thinks is a worthy Kindred, but not a worthy Ventru?<br /> <br /> Send him packing?<br /> <br /> Take him to Elysium a few times Hoping he comes to someones notice?<br /> <br /> or try introducing him to a prospective sire?<br /> <br /> If hes worked for you faithfully and you feel the need to reward him but he doesn't have the poise of a Ventru?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As a Ventrue, all of these questions can be answered very easily. Just put yourself in the Ventrue's shoes and ask yourself: How is this going to benefit <i><b>me</b></i>? What course of action would benefit <i><b>me</b></i> the most? How can <b><i>I</i></b> improve <i><b>my</b></i> position using this?<br /> <br /> If you're a proper Ventrue, you probably have at least 10 Kindred on call, all owing you a favor. Asking one of them to embrace this Revenant could be that favor. But again, ask yourself this: how would this benefit the Ventrue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T13:18:20-08:00","id":1275151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1275140#post1275140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats a Ventru probably going to do with a Revenant who he thinks is a worthy Kindred, but not a worthy Ventru? <br /> <br /> Send him packing? <br /> <br /> Take him to Elysium a few times Hoping he comes to someones notice?<br /> <br /> or try introducing him to a prospective sire?<br /> <br /> If hes worked for you faithfully and you feel the need to reward him but he doesn't have the poise of a Ventru?</div> </div> </div> </div>Find someone who is looking for a prospective childe and present the revenant as a candidate. Now two kindred owe him a favor.<br /> <br /> In one setting I run, the Khaibit have a high mortality turnover rate so they are always looking for prospective candidates and embracing privileges. Perhaps there's a clan, bloodline or faction in your setting with similar needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 12-18-2018, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T15:14:19-08:00","id":1275177,"title":"","content":"Question:<br /> <br /> How does contesting a blood ritual work? Does the successes from the contested roll subtract from the ritualist's rolled successes? Or does it work like how contesting normal Disciplines works, meaning that it only actually makes the ritualist fail if you roll more dice on your contested roll than the ritualist on his roll? What if you win the contested roll against the ritualist? Can he continue the ritual with the Stumbled Condition, or does the ritual immediately fail entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T16:21:48-08:00","id":1275199,"title":"","content":"One thing I dislike about 2nd edition Khaibit, is they don't work as Vampiric Butlers anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or would Revenants be better for that job anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T17:31:25-08:00","id":1275212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1275199#post1275199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I dislike about 2nd edition Khaibit, is they don't work as Vampiric Butlers anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or would Revenants be better for that job anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that setting the Khaibit hunt VII (demons), fairies, and werewolves, mages, and other vampires who are sloppy about bringing spirits and elementals here. Or they travel with a member of the Bron as their bodyguards. The Bron, in their search for the Holy Grail, have made enemies with the Seelie Court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T19:14:41-08:00","id":1275220,"title":"","content":"I don't see Revenants as something vampires would keep around. They're walking Masquerade-breaches waiting to happen. Ghouls are a better option for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T20:51:14-08:00","id":1275231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1275177#post1275177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question:<br /> <br /> How does contesting a blood ritual work? Does the successes from the contested roll subtract from the ritualist's rolled successes? Or does it work like how contesting normal Disciplines works, meaning that it only actually makes the ritualist fail if you roll more dice on your contested roll than the ritualist on his roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>The normal rules for contested actions don't involve subtracting successes, so I'd assume the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if you win the contested roll against the ritualist? Can he continue the ritual with the Stumbled Condition, or does the ritual immediately fail entirely? </div> </div> </div>I'd go with the former, given the weight of a three-dice penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T04:54:09-08:00","id":1275265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1275220#post1275220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see Revenants as something vampires would keep around. They're walking Masquerade-breaches waiting to happen. Ghouls are a better option for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>says in half damned some vampirs keep them as servants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T06:03:45-08:00","id":1275279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1275265#post1275265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> says in half damned some vampirs keep them as servants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some does not mean Most.<br /> <br /> Maina is correct, unless a vampire is capable of effortlessly cleaning up after their serial murderer servant on nightly basis without catching the attention of the local police and raising the ire of other vampires, they aren't keeping revenants indefinitely as servants because MOST vampires don't have those kind of political connections, herds, or feeding grounds. They are a lot more expensive to maintain than a ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T09:55:47-08:00","id":1275317,"title":"","content":"Possibly the very reason Some kindred think their classier?<br /> <br /> One thing would a kindred that kept a revenant as a Servant Suffer the social penaltys for Any blood farms or you think a Rich enough Ventrue would have ways around that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T12:59:40-08:00","id":1277063,"title":"","content":"So, here's a short little excerpt from the Humbled Condition, which is the source of my question:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Your character has felt the touch of the divine and trembled.<br /> She feels unworthy and wretched. For as long as the Condition<br /> lasts, she suffers a \u20132 die penalty to Resolve rolls and may not<br /> regain Willpower from her <u>Requiem</u>.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Condition refers to your requiem, which is described at the start of the book as:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;What are you going to do to make it through tonight? What<br /> about tomorrow night? And after the deeds are done and your<br /> belly\u2019s full, how are you going to live with yourself? What are<br /> you going to do with your damnation that makes it worth all<br /> the sins along the way?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> But what does this mean in game terms? I often see mechanics refer to &quot;your requiem&quot;, but it's never clearly defined what that means from a mechanical point of view. Is your requiem simply your Dirge? Is it your Dirge and Touchstones? Or your Mask, Dirge and Touchstones?<br /> <br /> I also saw some mechanics refer to &quot;your masquerade&quot;, so I suppose the same question applies there as well.<br /> <br /> My initial gut feeling tell me that &quot;your masquerade&quot; = your Mask, and &quot;your requiem&quot; = your Dirge, perhaps your Touchstones as well. <br /> <br /> Anyone has a clear answer for me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T13:28:53-08:00","id":1277067,"title":"","content":"It's your Dirge. In development the Mask and Dirge Anchors were initially called Masquerade and Requiem, and this reference wasn't caught when devs decided to rename them so you didn't have two things with the same name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T16:15:58-08:00","id":1277111,"title":"","content":"Hows the Circle to safeguard a Maiden it wants kept safe from any situation that might compel her to kill? Script her unlife thoroughly? Assign a Mekhet or Nosferatu as her minder?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T17:14:25-08:00","id":1277121,"title":"","content":"Part of being a maiden is that it isn't a permanent status. But keeping them away from vampire social gatherings or situations that would instigate frenzy can go a long way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T13:17:48-08:00","id":1277244,"title":"","content":"and chaperogning her whenever she feeds.<br /> <br /> oh can a ghoul perform the Cruac ritual pool of forbidden truths<br /> <br /> <br /> I can see a ghoul (or Revenant) being taught Cruac just to perform that one ritual if its possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 12-28-2018, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T14:41:25-08:00","id":1277262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1277244#post1277244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh can a ghoul perform the Cruac ritual pool of forbidden truths</div> </div> </div> </div>Any reason why they wouldn't be able to? They can any other one dot Cr\u00faac rituals and assist with higher dot rituals if a vampire is leading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T17:02:01-08:00","id":1277282,"title":"","content":"How does it work when a vampire wears mundane armor but then also uses Resilience's active affect to negate damage?<br /> <br /> I know by default armors do not stack, but the FAQ states that Resilience <i>acts like</i> armor, but <i>is not</i> armor, which makes me think that Resilience is the exception to the &quot;armors do not stack&quot; rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T17:06:26-08:00","id":1277283,"title":"","content":"As you said it's not armor and should stack. I also think mundane and supernatural armor do stack. It's multiple layers of mundane armor that doesn't stack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T18:38:22-08:00","id":1277290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1277262#post1277262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any reason why they wouldn't be able to? They can any other one dot Cr\u00faac rituals and assist with higher dot rituals if a vampire is leading it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Because the ritual involves spilling blood.<br /> <br /> But having someone else to gain the &quot;Primeval truths&quot; condition is worth a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T05:51:47-08:00","id":1277339,"title":"","content":"I hadn't read it in a while and forgot about that part. It does say blood, not Vitae, and as a first dot ritual it shouldn't require spilling Vitae without at least mentioning the increased cost (1 for activation, 1 for spilling). On the other hand it's in SotC so it might just not be very thought through like much of the other mechanical stuff.<br /> Regardless I'd go with the literal interpretation (blood and not necessarily Vitae, though I'm not sure if vampires can avoid spilling/using Vitae since they naturally don't bleed without spilling Vitae or using Blush of Health) since it fits with how Cr\u00faac is supposed to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T14:06:01-08:00","id":1277706,"title":"","content":"curious if your a member of the circle and want to help a mortal go on a power trip, ideas on how to do so other then ghouling them and give them LOTS and LOTS of vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T14:26:10-08:00","id":1278157,"title":"","content":"Does Obfuscate (Face in the Crowd) works on animals? How so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T15:24:36-08:00","id":1278175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1278157#post1278157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Obfuscate (Face in the Crowd) works on animals? How so?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My guess is that it doesn't. But that's just a gut feeling. Just like how Dominate doesn't work on animals either, nor does Majesty, nor does Nightmare to the best of my knowledge. For animals, you have the Animalism Discipline. If you don't have Animalism, then your control over animals is limited (though using your Predatory Aura against them should work). It kinda plays into the whole trope of animals being more keen on the predator you really are, they aren't as easily fooled by your masquerade, and react accordingly (unless, again, you have Animalism). That is not to say that animals instinctively dislike you (unless you have that one bane, Hated by Beasts), they just aren't fooled by your attempts at masquerading as one of the Kine. Again, that's just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 01-03-2019, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T16:15:08-08:00","id":1278187,"title":"","content":"It should work on animals. Unlike Dominate it isn't based around your ability to communicate orders to the animal. Animals will overlook you if they expect a human to be there, but almost all wild animals treats all humans with suspicion and that's still going to apply and break Face in the Crowd. Obfuscate 4 would work much better, but that's to expect from a higher dot power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T04:54:57-08:00","id":1278545,"title":"","content":"oh idea? A Dhampir Malison based around a rejuvenating Blood Bath?<br /> <br /> Since I think some would look for other means of longevity since they cant be embraced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T17:02:42-08:00","id":1279077,"title":"","content":"Question: Would in your opinion a Skill Specialization in 'Christianity' belong under the Academics Skill or the Occult Skill? Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T17:53:20-08:00","id":1279086,"title":"","content":"Probably neither. I might put Christian History or Lore in Academics, or Christian Miracles or Angelology in the Occult, but it's a wide net.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T18:17:33-08:00","id":1279090,"title":"","content":"A skill specialty can go with more than one skill, so it depends on what you intend to do with it. Rifles could reasonably be a firearms or a crafts specialty for example, depending on whether you're building and maintaining them or shooting things with them. <br /> <br /> Which is basically a way of saying I agree with nofather.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T02:51:49-08:00","id":1279147,"title":"","content":"I'd go one step further and say that most Specialties can work on most Skills. I wouldn't even divide it into Christian History/Christian Miracles because that divide comes naturally from what the different Skills applies to, and it makes Interdisciplinary Specialty hella more useful if you don't limit your Specialty in such a way. Just set Christianity on whichever Skill you want.<br /> <br /> Edit: Some Skills where Christianity might apply (either as a direct Specialty or through Interdisciplinary Specialty):<br /> Academics: History of Christianity, ease of studying related scripture, theology, recognising Christian rituals<br /> Computer: Ease of searching for bible passages (if you'd have to roll for it)<br /> Occult: Recognising biblical miracles, recognising Christian artefacts, angelology, interpreting omens relating to the book of Revelations, recognising Christian rituals<br /> Empathy: Comforting someone who has a crisis of faith, see through lies about someone's denomination, receiving a confession<br /> Expression: Holding a sermon<br /> Persuasion: Theological argumentation<br /> Subterfuge: Lie about your or see through lies about someone's denomination or faith<br /> <br /> Some are definitely a bit more useful than others and some would benefit more from a related Specialty. I can definitely see priests take Sermons and Theology as Specialties in Expression and Academics on top of a more general Christianity Specialty (remember that Specialties do stack). It really depends on what you want to get out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-07-2019, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T03:54:32-08:00","id":1279156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279077#post1279077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Would in your opinion a Skill Specialization in 'Christianity' belong under the Academics Skill or the Occult Skill? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>In and of itself, Christianity is too broad. I would have the character narrow it down and decide from there. For instance, an ordained Baptist minister might know a lot about Paul's journey to Rome and many New Testament interpretations about the End of Times but not know anything about how the Catholic Church influenced Spanish and Portuguese interactions with the indigenous populations during the 1500s or the major doctrinal differences between Pentecostals and Seventh Day Adventists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T08:16:26-08:00","id":1279214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279077#post1279077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Would in your opinion a Skill Specialization in 'Christianity' belong under the Academics Skill or the Occult Skill? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty loose with specialties, and as Tessie mentioned, any specialty can <i>probably</i> be shoehorned into just about any skill.<br /> <br /> On the idea of broadness vs. narrowness, I think it's important to remember that a Skill Specialty is 1 XP, and a Skill Dot is 2 XP. Looking at it from that mechanical angle, a natural cut-off point is to say a player should, on average, be able to leverage a Skill Specialty on 50% of their rolls with that skill. I've found that easier to go with than trying to get into the weeds of deciding the actual various subsections of Socialist Economic theory or what have you.<br /> <br /> Also, it's going to be very table-dependent on where those lines are drawn anyway. A player with a specialty of <i>Academics: Christianity</i> will theoretically get more use out of it in the Chronicle set in Vatican City rather than the one set in Tokyo.<br /> <br /> As such, my experience is players more often define a specialty too narrowly so I will either suggest a more broad version, or will be very lenient in allowing the specialty to be applied to rolls. For those few instances where something ends up being too broad and the player is pretty much using it every time they roll - either we will work together to narrow it, or I'll encourage the player to spend 1 XP and 'cash out' the specialty for a full skill dot - but often I won't find that out until after a few sessions of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T10:18:44-08:00","id":1279242,"title":"","content":"oh idea? Mass Embrace needs a cap of some kind.<br /> <br /> my suggestion?<br /> <br /> Blood Potency Squared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T11:51:27-08:00","id":1279270,"title":"","content":"It already have plenty of soft caps in how many humans you can store in the same place without drawing attention, how many humans you can Embrace without drawing attention, and how many you can afford to turn into draugr. Not to mention the danger of having 90% of the subjects Frenzying at the same time.<br /> The practical concerns alone make it limited as all subjects need to fit in a space that can contain the Vitae while also allowing it to spread to each subject. As is it's plenty limited and always comes with Humanity loss. Compare to The Vast Dynasty that allows you to Embrace a literally infinite number of people without even rolling for detachment if you're below Humanity 4.<br /> <br /> Also, that wasn't a question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T12:12:48-08:00","id":1279277,"title":"","content":"Think my idea is fair? <br /> <br /> If they enter Frenzy... the Sire may HAVE to stay and incapacitate the lot of them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T13:07:53-08:00","id":1279289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279277#post1279277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think my idea is fair?<br /> <br /> If they enter Frenzy... the Sire may HAVE to stay and incapacitate the lot of them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or have them tear each other to shreds, which can be additional breaking points since you were the cause for it. Or they break free and cause numerous Masquerade violations. Especially considering that some of them will be draugr so they won't stop causing trouble just because they exit Frenzy after a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T15:40:21-08:00","id":1279321,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer guys. I decided to give my priest character the Academics (Christianity) Speciality and give him the Interdisciplinary Specialty (Christianity) Merit as advised by some of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T12:28:06-08:00","id":1279534,"title":"","content":"Is there any clarification on what exactly can Grafting Unholy Flesh steal?<br /> Uratha's regeneration and shapeshifting abilities? Mage's spells? Changeling Contracts (or whatever they are called now)? What about the magnitude (whole Discipline, or just a dot)?<br /> Is it free? Does the body part decay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24954-blodm\u00e5ne","name":"blodm\u00e5ne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24954_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T14:05:13-08:00","id":1279560,"title":"","content":"It's up to the ST but personally I allow them to steal any innate power or ability or single spell, contract, ritual, single discipline level, gift etc. that the victim knows. Other STs may allow access to an entire discipline line, arcanum etc. The one using the Scale has to know the character has the power in question (not just assume) and they must take a body part symbolic of the power being stolen. <br /> <br /> No it's not free. The scale user has to follow the directions to use the scale and pay the recurring costs to keep the stolen organ viable and pay 1 vitae and 1 willpower for every point needed by the respective creature to use the power. The body part doesn't decay while it's on the vampire (if he's spending vitae to keep the organ viable) and the victim can't regenerate it or use the stolen power while it's still being used but once it's removed or destroyed the scale user can't use the power and the donor or victim can resume using that power and regenerate or heal the damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T14:20:20-08:00","id":1279561,"title":"","content":"What I meant by free is in Experiences terms.<br /> The &quot;directions&quot; do not infer any &quot;costs&quot;. The attachment and all that are merely, well, quite aptly described, directions.<br /> <br /> On another thread I was aghast when some one answered me that Werewolves doing lethal to Kindred, since I thought that was too powerful, it being cost-free and all, but this is ridiculous! hahah<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and the victim can't regenerate it <b>or use the stolen power</b> while it's still being used </div> </div> </div>Oh my! This is what I call playing favorites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24954,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24954-blodm\u00e5ne","user":"blodm\u00e5ne","date":". 01-08-2019, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24954-blodm\u00e5ne","name":"blodm\u00e5ne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24954_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T15:27:58-08:00","id":1279577,"title":"","content":"Yeah I tend towards it being a -single- power; one spell, one ritual, one level of a discipline, etc.<br /> And yes, it's bad for the victim, but you need to subdue that werewolf (or whatever) to begin with....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T17:41:30-08:00","id":1279604,"title":"","content":"oh wondered for a bit does a member of the ordo Dracul NEED a mentor with the Coils hes learning or can gain it from experimentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T23:45:54-08:00","id":1279652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279604#post1279604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh wondered for a bit does a member of the ordo Dracul NEED a mentor with the Coils hes learning or can gain it from experimentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The inherent hierarchy of the Ordo, i.e. the Mentor/Student relationship, breaks down if you make teachers irrelevant. However, I believe one of the 1E supplements (I want to say the Ordo Covenant book itself) has expanded Chrysalis (Coil learning) rules, and having a mentor vs. working on your own breakthrough is accounted for in those modifiers. It balances the avoidance of teachers with a risk of failing to learn the coil in question. It may have even signified a loss of XP with dramatic failures. So no, you don't NEED a mentor in every case. But I would advise you think carefully about the ramifications of making it just as easy with a mentor as without.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T00:06:46-08:00","id":1279654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279652#post1279652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inherent hierarchy of the Ordo, i.e. the Mentor/Student relationship, breaks down if you make teachers irrelevant. However, I believe one of the 1E supplements (I want to say the Ordo Covenant book itself) has expanded Chrysalis (Coil learning) rules, and having a mentor vs. working on your own breakthrough is accounted for in those modifiers. It balances the avoidance of teachers with a risk of failing to learn the coil in question. It may have even signified a loss of XP with dramatic failures. So no, you don't NEED a mentor in every case. But I would advise you think carefully about the ramifications of making it just as easy with a mentor as without.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, to speak to a more practical point, esoteric research and inquiry into the vampiric condition is a lot easier to conduct with resources that other vampires who've been at this for longer than you will usually have a vested interest in, and the Dragons' general disdain for external politicking means &quot;get a mentor, get a student&quot; is usually the most ingrained and expedient workaround to a thousand and one nights of independent study.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T01:05:44-08:00","id":1279657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279242#post1279242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh idea? Mass Embrace needs a cap of some kind.<br /> <br /> my suggestion?<br /> <br /> Blood Potency Squared.</div> </div> </div> </div>I use humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T02:49:18-08:00","id":1279663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blodm\u00e5ne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279561#post1279561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant by free is in Experiences terms.<br /> The &amp;quot;directions&amp;quot; do not infer any &amp;quot;costs&amp;quot;. The attachment and all that are merely, well, quite aptly described, directions.<br /> <br /> On another thread I was aghast when some one answered me that Werewolves doing lethal to Kindred, since I thought that was too powerful, it being cost-free and all, but this is ridiculous! hahah<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh my! This is what I call playing favorites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Scales cost experience to learn but the numerous price breaks Dragons get to learn Mysteries and Scales make any claim that experience as a deterrent due to the cost is laughable.<br /> <br /> And while I happen to share the opinion that the Ordo Dracul are and continue to be major beneficiaries of developer favoritism, stealing, blocking or imitating other groups\u2019 signature abilities isn\u2019t restricted to a single faction within Vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279577#post1279577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I tend towards it being a -single- power; one spell, one ritual, one level of a discipline, etc.<br /> And yes, it's bad for the victim, but you need to subdue that werewolf (or whatever) to begin with....</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing says they can\u2019t do so voluntarily, be tricked into agreeing, or get another power in exchange.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279604#post1279604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh wondered for a bit does a member of the ordo Dracul NEED a mentor with the Coils hes learning or can gain it from experimentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the fact that presenting a new Mystery or Scale is automatic status increase for Dragons, and that knowing x number of powers no longer translates to covenant rank anymore no they do not <u>need</u> a mentor to learn Mysteries or Scales. But if a player has not established having a working relationship with a teacher or purchase a qualified mentor with experience, I do not allow them to just purchase a mystery or scale once the player can front the xp cost. They actually have to roleplay research and experimentation in game to justify learning the power. And no, I do not let players make a single research roll and trip over a magical book that just materializes and tells them how to do everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T03:43:02-08:00","id":1279669,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's definitely possible to develop Coils (or, as the book points out, alternate coil dots in already established Coils) on your own but it should be rare.<br /> The first Coil dot that anyone develops should always require some sort of foundation, imo, but it could potentially be notes about the Mystery and the internalisation of Coils rather than full mentorship. Any coil dots after that (even in other Mysteries) is &quot;merely&quot; applying the principles in new ways so theoretically possible without any external support at all. But that would be rare and not something that I would allow without good reason. Especially not for, say, a Carthian who learned a single Coil dot through espionage and then try to develop additional dots on their own without having the Ordo mindset or putting in effort and resources into mystical research and studies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1279663#post1279663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing says they can\u2019t do so voluntarily, be tricked into agreeing, or get another power in exchange.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a reminder that only vampires and ghouls can receive the benefits of the Scale so it wouldn't work for other supers (unless deemed that other supers can be ghouled).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-09T12:52:57-08:00","id":1279763,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's not like the Scales that target &quot;mortals&quot; where there's an argument for &quot;anything 'living' is mortal to Vamp powers&quot; it explicitly says Vampires and ghouls are who can benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T08:05:39-08:00","id":1281098,"title":"","content":"When you fail a roll, you can opt for a dramatic failure and receive a Beat. But what about <i>automatic</i> dramatic failures? Do <i>automatic</i> dramatic failures give Beats, or only when it's specifically stated it gives Beats (for example the Coil of Zirnitra's 'Opening the Third Eye')?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-16T08:18:26-08:00","id":1281102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1281098#post1281098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you fail a roll, you can opt for a dramatic failure and receive a Beat. But what about <i>automatic</i> dramatic failures? Do <i>automatic</i> dramatic failures give Beats, or only when it's specifically stated it gives Beats (for example the Coil of Zirnitra's 'Opening the Third Eye')?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The second one. Normal Dramatic Failures do not grant a Beat unless they say so. The Beat is for Choosing to make things more dramatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T11:11:19-08:00","id":1281326,"title":"","content":"Dram-fails also often give conditions that give beats, but that's indirect, and part of the condition mechanics, not the dram-fail mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T20:00:07-08:00","id":1282063,"title":"","content":"What are the limits on animalism 2? Is there a maximum size for an animal to be raised? Do I need a functioning corpse or a skeleton would do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T22:28:06-08:00","id":1282084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1282063#post1282063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a maximum size for an animal to be raised?</div> </div> </div> </div>Insofar as you can only raise a corpse you have at your disposal, yes, but otherwise not really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do I need a functioning corpse or a skeleton would do? </div> </div> </div>You need to be able to have drained its blood and fed it Vitae, and the comparison to the Embrace and talk of &quot;dead veins&quot; suggests that a complete skeleton is firmly off the table for Animalism 2 on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T00:39:17-08:00","id":1282095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1282063#post1282063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the limits on animalism 2? Is there a maximum size for an animal to be raised? Do I need a functioning corpse or a skeleton would do?</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to be an animal corpse and a skeleton is not a corpse. That\u2019s up to your ST if some bones or a taxidermist product in a zoo constitutes a corpse. There is no express size limitation or time frame of death before reanimating but the flavor text implies the initial ritual to turn the animal into a familiar had to have been consumed for its blood and fed vitae in a type of Embrace. (Which makes using skeletons problematic.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T23:40:17-08:00","id":1282393,"title":"","content":"The Invictus merit Noblesse oblige ( from secrets of covenants), could exist a version which use covenant status and position instead of city status?<br /> Do you think another covenant vampire could purchase either version for his covenant?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T11:00:09-08:00","id":1282460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1282393#post1282393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Invictus merit Noblesse oblige ( from secrets of covenants), could exist a version which use covenant status and position instead of city status?<br /> Do you think another covenant vampire could purchase either version for his covenant?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, nothing in the published material translates to the ability to swap their covenant position with 3+ status for a touchstone. It's up to the ST whether or not they want to allow it. I'd allow it personally if it's a position that has officially recognized duties to kindred outside the covenant. (Like Notary or Reeve.) but not for something covenant exclusive like Archivist or Grand Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I personally wouldn't allow other covenants to have their own version of Noblesse Oblige. That's up to your ST if they want the merit or your edited version available to non Invictus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T09:55:12-08:00","id":1283527,"title":"","content":"Real simple question that I wanted to double check:<br /> <br /> When failing a detachment roll, do you lose a single dot of Humanity, or do you jump to the level of the breaking point?<br /> <br /> So for example, if I'm at Humanity 7 and commit a Humanity 3 Breaking Point, and I fail my detachment roll, do I now have Humanity 6 or 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T10:06:47-08:00","id":1283530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1283527#post1283527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real simple question that I wanted to double check:<br /> <br /> When failing a detachment roll, do you lose a single dot of Humanity, or do you jump to the level of the breaking point?<br /> <br /> So for example, if I'm at Humanity 7 and commit a Humanity 3 Breaking Point, and I fail my detachment roll, do I now have Humanity 6 or 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former. The breaking point's relation to the roll is whether it happens at all and how many dice you roll before modifiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T11:00:16-08:00","id":1283541,"title":"","content":"Your character will have a Humanity rating of 6 in that example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T09:18:26-08:00","id":1283734,"title":"","content":"Resilience and Vigor add directly to Stamina and Strength, respectively. Spending Vitae on physical intensity adds dice to a roll using these stats. <br /> <br /> Is it intended that, for example, the illustrative effects of high attributes (6+) in <i>Thousand Years of Nights</i> be applied to individuals who total 6+ thanks to Resilience or Vigor? Or should we keep them to natural 6+ derived from high-BP stat purchases?<br /> <br /> Similarly is it intended that these effect apply when pushing the dice contributions from, say, Strength to 6+ through physical intensity?<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T13:49:58-08:00","id":1283789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1283734#post1283734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resilience and Vigor add directly to Stamina and Strength, respectively. Spending Vitae on physical intensity adds dice to a roll using these stats.<br /> <br /> Is it intended that, for example, the illustrative effects of high attributes (6+) in <i>Thousand Years of Nights</i> be applied to individuals who total 6+ thanks to Resilience or Vigor? Or should we keep them to natural 6+ derived from high-BP stat purchases?<br /> <br /> Similarly is it intended that these effect apply when pushing the dice contributions from, say, Strength to 6+ through physical intensity?<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say it applies to anything that raises your Attributes stats passively. Someone with a high amount of Strength through Vigor is no different from someone with a high amount of Strength through Blood Potency 6+, in my opinion that is.<br /> <br /> I don't think it applies to things like Physical Intensity. Sure, Physical Intensity allows a vampire to push his body beyond the natural limits, but it's a brief and intense burst of power that clearly requires effort on the vampire's part. The <i>&quot;When he can barely walk through a crowd without accidentally hurting someone,&quot;</i> -part doesn't apply to Physical Intensity, is what I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T06:15:47-08:00","id":1283902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1283789#post1283789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it applies to anything that raises your Attributes stats passively. Someone with a high amount of Strength through Vigor is no different from someone with a high amount of Strength through Blood Potency 6+, in my opinion that is.<br /> <br /> I don't think it applies to things like Physical Intensity. Sure, Physical Intensity allows a vampire to push his body beyond the natural limits, but it's a brief and intense burst of power that clearly requires effort on the vampire's part. The <i>&quot;When he can barely walk through a crowd without accidentally hurting someone,&quot;</i> -part doesn't apply to Physical Intensity, is what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, on both points, my strong leaning. The thing that gives me pause is how it took until the Thousand Years book to address, descriptively, the effects of supernaturally extreme attributes on the character and environment. If a six Stamina was so implacable a difference why not mention it before? Word count?<br /> <br /> It's extremely easy to reach six Strength/Stamina as a vamp, thanks to the physical Disciplines.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T06:30:55-08:00","id":1283907,"title":"","content":"Word count and the fact that it became more relevant in 1kYoN that is geared towards characters that can have more than just two Attributes above five. I don't think any other game has similar descriptions despite the various ways it's possible to reach 6+ Attributes before Supernatural Potency 6+. A starting character in Mage could potentially reach 11+ dots in an Attribute without even having to check for Paradox (but definitely cause Quiescence should they ever interact with Sleepers while the spell is active).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T13:06:55-08:00","id":1283990,"title":"","content":"Ghouls can store an amount of Vitae equal to their Stamina.<br /> Does that mean ghouls who learn Resilience (which passively increases your Stamina) can also store more Vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-31T13:15:21-08:00","id":1283994,"title":"","content":"From the developer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/57764-ghouls-with-resilience?p=57767#post57767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Stamina enhancements from supernatural effects don't count towards total Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T04:20:44-08:00","id":1284103,"title":"","content":"Resilience: If an injury specifically removes a limb, an eye, or so on, the vampire DOES suffer logical impairments from the injuries. Does this apply to the damage before or after reduction?<br /> Say the Lick gets chopped in the neck for 5 damage but it gets Resilienced down to zero. Is it just not enough to remove the head or is the head chopped off but he takes no damage?<br /> What about an eye? Does he have a bloody, mangled eye that still functions because it's still in his head or is it too far gone to function yet no damage is taken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 02-01-2019, 07:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T05:49:31-08:00","id":1284113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284103#post1284103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resilience: If an injury specifically removes a limb, an eye, or so on, the vampire DOES suffer logical impairments from the injuries. Does this apply to the damage before or after reduction?<br /> Say the Lick gets chopped in the neck for 5 damage but it gets Resilienced down to zero. Is it just not enough to remove the head or is the head chopped off but he takes no damage?<br /> What about an eye? Does he have a bloody, mangled eye that still functions because it's still in his head or is it too far gone to function yet no damage is is taken</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book contradicts itself and the developers contradicted each other so it's whatever your ST decides.<br /> <br /> Since Resilience is a worthless misnomer if it doesn't actually stop the impairments that arise from blocked damage, I personally say an attack does purely cosmetic damage that instantly closes up but does not affect functionality if Resilience reduces the damage to zero. If damage gets through after reduction but does not meet the threshold sufficient to sever limbs then they retain use of the limb or body part (And yes, I've been on the giving and receiving end of that.). Whether or not the vampire suffers a penalty depends on how close to actually meeting that threshold even after damage reduction takes place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T06:06:55-08:00","id":1284114,"title":"","content":"How great a disadvantage is kindred with a penthouse or hotel room at, when it comes to haven? if its entered during the Day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T06:32:39-08:00","id":1284119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284114#post1284114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How great a disadvantage is kindred with a penthouse or hotel room at, when it comes to haven? if its entered during the Day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Watch the first episode of season 5 of American Horror Story Hotel for the answer to your question. (Hint: It's not a disadvantage at all.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T07:16:09-08:00","id":1284128,"title":"","content":"When feeding a human vitae, do they automatically heal damage/injuries? I feel like I remember reading something that said that....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T08:35:14-08:00","id":1284142,"title":"","content":"Only if they're turned into a ghoul first. Otherwise, you're just potentially installing a vinculum stage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-01T08:54:24-08:00","id":1284144,"title":"","content":"Even if they're a ghoul it's not automatic. Ghouls have to spend the Vitae to heal, just like vampires do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T07:12:51-08:00","id":1284489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284103#post1284103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resilience: If an injury specifically removes a limb, an eye, or so on, the vampire DOES suffer logical impairments from the injuries. Does this apply to the damage before or after reduction?<br /> Say the Lick gets chopped in the neck for 5 damage but it gets Resilienced down to zero. Is it just not enough to remove the head or is the head chopped off but he takes no damage?<br /> What about an eye? Does he have a bloody, mangled eye that still functions because it's still in his head or is it too far gone to function yet no damage is taken?</div> </div> </div> </div>The damage is purely cosmetic unless there is a Tilt applied, in which case you can say that something is really torn up or broken, with a mechanical effect. Otherwise Resilience keeps it from being that bad, even if it looks superficially gruesome in the moment. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d say lost limbs and eyes, decapitation, etc. are well beyond superficial cosmetic damage and needs to be reserved for stuff that Resilience doesn\u2019t negate. <br /> <br /> To be frank, the only reason for the statement that Resilience doesn\u2019t negate the appearance of damage is to allow for a scene in which the house blows up but a charred corpse walks out of the flames and is now pissed off and even more dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T10:11:10-08:00","id":1284532,"title":"","content":"A technical reading does point towards loss of limbs being theoretically possible despite ignoring all damage. Resilience doesn't do anything to prevent a blade slicing through muscles and bone; it only prevents the resulting damage in Health boxes.<br /> Luckily you only need to heal the damage for limbs to reattach or regrow.<br /> <br /> But it should be noted that loss of limb is something that mortals would deal with when they take <i>aggravated</i> damage. This means it can't happen with regular weapons unless the damage wraps around from full lethal to aggravated damage. For vampires this means full bashing to lethal damage, but at least it means that in normal cases it's impossible for vampires to lose limbs without also taking damage in excess of what Resilience can ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T12:53:11-08:00","id":1284556,"title":"","content":"By raw, while in the first edition was specified that a vampire could be killed removing his head or burning him up, here a vampire can only die when all his health boxes are filled with aggravated. <br /> So, even if I can see there are rooms for different interpretations, I would go this way: as Resilence does not prevent injuries, just damages, so I would say that in order to remove a limb (like head) I consider the damage (pre soak) as what is needed to remove or not the limb, and eventually, with resilence, the damage will not be applied.<br /> That's also very inspirational: a dead corp, without the lower part of he body, slouching with a smile painted on his face. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T13:23:42-08:00","id":1284561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1283994#post1283994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the developer.<br /> <br /> <i>Originally posted by <b>Rose Bailey</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/57764-ghouls-with-resilience?p=57767#post57767\">View Post</a></i><br /> <i>No. Stamina enhancements from supernatural effects don't count towards total Vitae.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> So from what I gathered, Resilience adds to your Health levels. But how about Vigor and Speed? The book doesn't say that Vigor should be used to calculate Speed, so I guess Speed isn't affected by Vigor?<br /> <br /> How about Merits that have a certain amount of Stamina as a prerequisite (for example the Relentless Merit, which requires 3 dots of Stamina)? Does Resilience count when checking to see if you meet the prerequisites for the Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 02-03-2019, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T13:39:40-08:00","id":1284563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284561#post1284561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So from what I gathered, Resilience adds to your Health levels. But how about Vigor and Speed? The book doesn't say that Vigor should be used to calculate Speed, so I guess Speed isn't affected by Vigor?<br /> <br /> How about Merits that have a certain amount of Stamina as a prerequisite (for example the Relentless Merit, which requires 3 dots of Stamina)? Does Resilience count when checking to see if you meet the prerequisites for the Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attribute dots gained through Disciplines counts as actual dots unless stated otherwise. Vigor increases Strength which increases Speed. Both Vigor and Resilience counts towards Strength and Stamina prerequisites on Merits.<br /> An example of when they don't apply is when Lashing Out with the Monstrous Aspect, which specifically states that Vigor does not apply to the Strength+Blood Potency dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T13:43:20-08:00","id":1284564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284561#post1284561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> So from what I gathered, Resilience adds to your Health levels. But how about Vigor and Speed? The book doesn't say that Vigor should be used to calculate Speed, so I guess Speed isn't affected by Vigor?<br /> <br /> How about Merits that have a certain amount of Stamina as a prerequisite (for example the Relentless Merit, which requires 3 dots of Stamina)? Does Resilience count when checking to see if you meet the prerequisites for the Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure to have read that Vigor adds to Speed. After all it's specified that physical intensity does not increase derivate traits.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that as Resilence increases Stamina it also affect merits involving it. Otherwise why stating that Resilence increases Stamina and not just Health boxes if you can't never use Resilence dots when Stamina is called to purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-03-2019, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T14:37:54-08:00","id":1284577,"title":"","content":"Sweet thanks guys.<br /> <br /> Here's one more question:<br /> <br /> If a vampire diablerizes another vampire... who happens to be the host of a strix... what happens?<br /> <br /> Does the strix's vampire host get reduced to a corpse host? Does the strix get sucked into the diablerist as well, giving the diablerist a cozy new shadowy friend inside his body? Or does the strix just die just like the vampire host it used? Or does the strix simply get ejected out of the vampire body during the diablerie process?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 02-03-2019, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T16:04:57-08:00","id":1284596,"title":"","content":"Good question! Fall of the Camarilla might have a definite answer, so I'll reread that when I have a chance. But I think the Strix would end up inside the Diablerist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T17:11:37-08:00","id":1284610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284577#post1284577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a vampire diablerizes another vampire... who happens to be the host of a strix... what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply put, that doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> Your target needs to be torpid to be subjected to diablerie and the Strix a) aren't subject to torpor, b) can't possess a vampire who isn't already torpid themselves and c) aren't ejected from a body unless it's taken enough damage to destroy the host, which happens to be the threshold for diablerie to begin in the first place.<br /> <br /> In the event that it somehow <i>does</i> happen, the endless variety of weird shit the Owls get up to may change the answer, but in general the process suggests that your last guess is the closest probable outcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T07:23:38-08:00","id":1284704,"title":"","content":"sounds like fodder for some weird ass Dracul Experiment!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T07:49:01-08:00","id":1284708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284610#post1284610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, that doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> Your target needs to be torpid to be subjected to diablerie and the Strix a) aren't subject to torpor, b) can't possess a vampire who isn't already torpid themselves and c) aren't ejected from a body unless it's taken enough damage to destroy the host, which happens to be the threshold for diablerie to begin in the first place.<br /> <br /> In the event that it somehow <i>does</i> happen, the endless variety of weird shit the Owls get up to may change the answer, but in general the process suggests that your last guess is the closest probable outcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but what if the Strix enters the torpid body while the diablerie process is already ongoing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T08:17:51-08:00","id":1284715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284708#post1284708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but what if the Strix enters the torpid body while the diablerie process is already ongoing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The process of possessing a vampire requires the Strix to be very close to the body, costs Willpower, and is contested by a three-part dicepool that probably won't be terribly small if the diablerist isn't after their soul just for kicks.<br /> <br /> &quot;What if a weird witch-owl decides to be borderline suicidal within an extremely narrow window of time and space?&quot; is inherently the sort of question you build a plot around, because a look at how the Strix generally operate will tell you that's not the kind of thing that just <i>happens</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T08:31:27-08:00","id":1284721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284715#post1284715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The process of possessing a vampire requires the Strix to be very close to the body, costs Willpower, and is contested by a three-part dicepool that probably won't be terribly small if the diablerist isn't after their soul just for kicks.<br /> <br /> &quot;What if a weird witch-owl decides to be borderline suicidal within an extremely narrow window of time and space?&quot; is inherently the sort of question you build a plot around, because a look at how the Strix generally operate will tell you that's not the kind of thing that just <i>happens</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I understand that this doesn't normally happen, I understand that this is a weird and exceptional situation, and I expected I might have to homebrew if I want to make this happen, but before I do, I was just wondering if there are rules or ideas about this already, before I go and make shit up that is inconsistent with the established lore and rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T09:23:35-08:00","id":1284735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284721#post1284721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, I understand that this doesn't normally happen, I understand that this is a weird and exceptional situation, and I expected I might have to homebrew if I want to make this happen, but before I do, I was just wondering if there are rules or ideas about this already, before I go and make shit up that is inconsistent with the established lore and rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what if whatever you make up does contradict previously published rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T09:59:33-08:00","id":1284746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1284735#post1284735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what if whatever you make up does contradict previously published rules?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess I'm a bit of a purist like that. I can't help it. If I break the rules (and sometimes I do), I want to do so consciously, not accidentally. I always feel terrible when I accidentally break the rules.<br /> <br /> When a ST breaks the rules, it should be a conscious and well-considered choice, not something that happens by accident because the ST didn't bother doing his research. I'm not saying that this is the universal truth, but that's the standard I hold myself to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T09:05:59-08:00","id":1285261,"title":"","content":"Following up on the Resilience topic, is it then feasible for a vampire to survive decapitation? Has the trope of &quot;sever head from heart&quot; been, um, staked?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T09:18:18-08:00","id":1285262,"title":"","content":"Technically possible, I think, but it would require exceptional circumstances to naturally happen in a game. Decapitation is instantly lethal for mortals so it should require getting full aggravated damage to lop someone's head off. That's dealing twice the amount of Health boxes in damage when using a sword or other weapon. Dealing that amount of damage is difficult even before accounting for additional Health boxes from Resilience, and multiple swings at the neck might not hit the same spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T09:33:19-08:00","id":1285263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285261#post1285261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following up on the Resilience topic, is it then feasible for a vampire to survive decapitation? Has the trope of &quot;sever head from heart&quot; been, um, staked?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's possible. Resilence does not deny injuries just let them be armful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T10:49:09-08:00","id":1285294,"title":"","content":"So... is there a threshold damage for decapitation at work? Or is it better to just arbitrate &quot;ok, killing blow full damage (~14) would normally kill her--so the head comes off!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Player: &quot;yay! Ding dong! The witch is dead!&quot;<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;The head rolls away, eyes wide in shock. Then they snap into focus and glare at you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Player: ...&quot;um.&quot;<br /> <br /> Witch: &quot;You're going to regret this my dearie!&quot; *burrows into the ground with its teeth*<br /> <br /> Player: &quot;Oh sh-&quot; <i>&lt;transmission interrupted&gt;</i><br /> <br /> I'm asking all this because being able to reasonably use the talking head trope to counter 'decapitation kills everything' would be <i>fantastic</i> for messing with players....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:16:46-08:00","id":1285306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285294#post1285294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... is there a threshold damage for decapitation at work? Or is it better to just arbitrate &amp;quot;ok, killing blow full damage (~14) would normally kill her--so the head comes off!&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Player: &amp;quot;yay! Ding dong! The witch is dead!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> GM: &amp;quot;The head rolls away, eyes wide in shock. Then they snap into focus and glare at you.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Player: ...&amp;quot;um.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Witch: &amp;quot;You're going to regret this my dearie!&amp;quot; *burrows into the ground with its teeth*<br /> <br /> Player: &amp;quot;Oh sh-&amp;quot; <i>&lt;transmission interrupted&gt;</i><br /> <br /> I'm asking all this because being able to reasonably use the talking head trope to counter 'decapitation kills everything' would be <i>fantastic</i> for messing with players....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>By raw decapitation during fight is not contemplated between the aimed hits. <br /> But I guess you could threat it as cutting off a leg after a head aimed attack (-3). The problem would arise when someone with a bit of vigor and BP 3 would pump all the vitae amount in just one single attack. I see tons of heads rolling around \ud83e\udd23","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T11:23:33-08:00","id":1285312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285294#post1285294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... is there a threshold damage for decapitation at work? Or is it better to just arbitrate &quot;ok, killing blow full damage (~14) would normally kill her--so the head comes off!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Player: &quot;yay! Ding dong! The witch is dead!&quot;<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;The head rolls away, eyes wide in shock. Then they snap into focus and glare at you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Player: ...&quot;um.&quot;<br /> <br /> Witch: &quot;You're going to regret this my dearie!&quot; *burrows into the ground with its teeth*<br /> <br /> Player: &quot;Oh sh-&quot; <i>&lt;transmission interrupted&gt;</i><br /> <br /> I'm asking all this because being able to reasonably use the talking head trope to counter 'decapitation kills everything' would be <i>fantastic</i> for messing with players....<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why this shouldn't be possible. There are no hard rules for when an enemy is decapitated, and there are no rules stating that decapitation kills a vampire.<br /> <br /> Since Resilience doesn't actually heal wounds (visually, it does of course reduce/remove wounds in your Health track), it just ignores the damage being done, it's perfectly possible that if a vampire receives a blow that would have been lethal but Resilience is what's keeping him alive, he could still be alive even with his head severed. He'd likely be in torpor though. Or not. If it's a strix-possessed vampire or it's an Ordo Dracul member with Coil of the Wyrm currently in a frenzy.<br /> <br /> Honestly, with this sort of stuff, I'd actually be alright with going for the cinematic and dramatic approach and just kinda handwave the actual rules or mechanics for it. If it's dramatically appropriate for the vampire to be beheaded, have her be beheaded. If it's dramatically appropriate for her to still be conscious at that point and have the head and body move separately from each other, make it so. As long as it's a one-time thing or an anomaly, I think it will be cool and the players wouldn't feel cheated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T12:25:15-08:00","id":1285334,"title":"","content":"The threshold I used was full aggravated damage for mortals (meaning full lethal for vampires in most cases) since any less would set a precedent for killing characters before they've taken enough damage. That could potentially make aiming much more powerful than it already is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T12:34:34-08:00","id":1285338,"title":"","content":"I'm boring, and tend to say that since decapitation is what happens when you hit full agg, anything less than full agg doesn't decapitate you. If you say &quot;full agg for an average human (=14 lethal) decapitates&quot; you end up with the question of &quot;well, this guy has Stamina 4 and/or the Giant merit or something, so he can survive 14 lethal if he gets to a hospital\u2026how did he survive the guillotine??&quot;<br /> <br /> In other words, decapitation potentially happens at full agg, but never earlier. If an effect like Resilience gives you extra health boxes, or vampires downgrade lethal to bashing, or anything like that, so you don't reach full agg, then you don't get beheaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T13:21:00-08:00","id":1285354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285338#post1285338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm boring, and tend to say that since decapitation is what happens when you hit full agg, anything less than full agg doesn't decapitate you. If you say &quot;full agg for an average human (=14 lethal) decapitates&quot; you end up with the question of &quot;well, this guy has Stamina 4 and/or the Giant merit or something, so he can survive 14 lethal if he gets to a hospital\u2026how did he survive the guillotine??&quot;<br /> <br /> In other words, decapitation potentially happens at full agg, but never earlier. If an effect like Resilience gives you extra health boxes, <b>or vampires downgrade lethal to bashing</b>, or anything like that, so you don't reach full agg, then you don't get beheaded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything else I included in &quot;full lethal&quot; but the automatic downgrading of damage works the same way as the damage reduction from Resilience; by the vampire just ignoring the damage. It doesn't actually make the vampire more physically/structurally hardy, and thus not more resistant against decapitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T17:55:53-08:00","id":1285442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285312#post1285312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are no rules stating that decapitation kills a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This right here. Thanks!<br /> <br /> I'm dealing with well-troped former WoD players and the decapitation thing was explicit in that setting. I'll use this to point out that they know less than they think they do... which is horrifying, of course.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T08:36:04-08:00","id":1285575,"title":"","content":"So I'm running a long-term game (will span 600 years or so, starting at 1705) and I'm kind of having a little bit of a problem with Protean 5. As it stands, I've let people know that I'm restricting 5s in non-physical disciplines until further notice, but at some point the Gangrel at the party will end up getting it. How to challenge the group of them in a fight is already a thing I have to think about, and the ability to turn into blood-drinking mist is, at first blush, the pinnacle of that. Yeah, there's fire, but there sure aren't flamethrowers anytime soon (other than wizards). Any particular advice on this front -- either Protean 5 specifically, or fights that challenge them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:06:48-08:00","id":1285579,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason the powerful Theban Sorcerors and Cruac Acolytes cannot summon an efreet, fire salamander, animated flame sword or other type of fire elemental in your setting? What about air elementals to disperse the mist?<br /> <br /> And yes flamethrowers actually were a thing. The modern flamethrower is based off the Byzantium siphon design made in the late 600 AD. But on a smaller scale, there's no reason to say opponents couldn't coat their weapons with pitch and oil then set ablaze taking swipes at the bloody mist, or fire flame arrows from a distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:33:24-08:00","id":1285588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285575#post1285575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How to challenge the group of them in a fight is already a thing I have to think about, and the ability to turn into blood-drinking mist is, at first blush, the pinnacle of that. Yeah, there's fire, but there sure aren't flamethrowers anytime soon (other than wizards). Any particular advice on this front -- either Protean 5 specifically, or fights that challenge them?</div> </div> </div> </div>A few notes:<br /> <br /> * Fire has always been a huge, huge thing in civilization. Buildings were mostly out of wood (even the &quot;stone&quot; castles were supported by heavy wood buttressing), and the main source of light and heat was burning stuff. Oil lamps from this period on are vital, and oil can get sprayed, thrown or otherwise ignited to hilarious effects. Fire is also really, really hard to contain during the period--the modern measures that have greatly reduced fire risk are not present.<br /> <br /> * Gangrel survive. It's what they do. Protean 5 and to a lesser extent Resilience 5 underline this. Animalism serves as a tripwire, giving the Gangrel time to prepare so he can... survive. Don't take that away from the player. Instead, show that just because you're physically intact doesn't mean you aren't hurt. Everyone around you that you care about is less durable, even vulnerable, and while your body lives your mind and soul may not. Or not without injury. What steps will you take as you age to safeguard what is really important to you, now that you can in short order, live through danger?<br /> <br /> (BTW, the movie The Last Witchhunter (2015) hooks onto aspects of this.)<br /> <br /> * Surprise. Use it sparingly, and when necessary for the story apply it viciously and without remorse in overwhelming force. Go for staking, which paralyzes and prevents misting. Prep the encounter scene in advance and ensure the antagonists have had enough time to prepare and work out the PC's movements.<br /> <br /> But really, the role of the Gangrel should be &quot;the one that comes back to get the rest out of trouble.&quot; The party should know their unstoppable bud has their back. Or not--in which case they should be honestly afraid. Ultimately the greatest vulnerability of a Gangrel is betrayal; and that's a fact that drives a wedge between them and others, reinforcing their loner-hood.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 02-12-2019, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T09:57:58-08:00","id":1285599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285579#post1285579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason the powerful Theban Sorcerors and Cruac Acolytes cannot summon an efreet, fire salamander, animated flame sword or other type of fire elemental in your setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood sorcery explicitly can't create or summon banes and every vampire suffers from the bane of fire to some degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:14:49-08:00","id":1285626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285599#post1285599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood sorcery explicitly can't create or summon banes and every vampire suffers from the bane of fire to some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the books you're using, for that bit. But there are some rituals that can make it easier for spirits to come into the world, for example, like a super-powerful mortal summoning (effectively making Resonant and a big pool of Essence). You could bring in a fire spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:20:18-08:00","id":1285628,"title":"","content":"how would you portray a living beheaded kindred? just have the vampire calmly put his head back on lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:01:05-08:00","id":1285653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285628#post1285628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how would you portray a living beheaded kindred? just have the vampire calmly put his head back on lol</div> </div> </div> </div>When my character dismembered one, the blood just kind of pooled around the largest pieces, coalesced into a black blob and oozed back into a &quot;human&quot; shape resembling Armus from the Star Trek The Next Generation episode and smelled like charred rotting animals. <br /> <br /> Another setting where my character was watching the execution of a Belial's Brood character. He was decapitated but his body started moving to get the head. The sheriff started hacking hands and feet. The hands (Like Thing from the Addams Family) and feet still moved to try and retrieve the head. That was a train wreck of frenzies and maimings as far as public executions went.<br /> <br /> I've run them like the Headless Horseman. They don't &quot;need&quot; their head but they usually withdraw if they lost their head midbrawl. It will eventually grow back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:13:32-08:00","id":1285659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285628#post1285628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how would you portray a living beheaded kindred? just have the vampire calmly put his head back on lol</div> </div> </div> </div>No.... As a kindred with a severed leg can't run until the leg grows back, a beheaded kindred can't move, think, see, until the head has grown back. A kind of torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:46:41-08:00","id":1285673,"title":"","content":"well I would say you could do surprises as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> said. There is even a Cruac spell that allows it to happen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T17:05:14-08:00","id":1285735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285659#post1285659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.... As a kindred with a severed leg can't run until the leg grows back, a beheaded kindred can't move, think, see, until the head has grown back. A kind of torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Kindred with a severed leg couldn't run because the leg is mechanically important for running. A Kindred without a head is likely able to walk around (though not see that much) since the brain is already dead and has nothing to do with either movement or the ability to think. I would consider the heart a much more likely seat of consciousness considering that's the only organ that is metaphysically important in any way for a Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T04:20:04-08:00","id":1285849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285735#post1285735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Kindred with a severed leg couldn't run because the leg is mechanically important for running. A Kindred without a head is likely able to walk around (though not see that much) since the brain is already dead and has nothing to do with either movement or the ability to think. I would consider the heart a much more likely seat of consciousness considering that's the only organ that is metaphysically important in any way for a Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you can go for whatever you prefer as there are no rules about it. So if you want to allow to an headless vampire to go around without being able to hear, think and see go for it. I personally prefer a semi torpid state in this case. It prevent the character to walks smasing himself against tables and walls. Obviously this' valid just if you consider a dead brain as the center of thoughts ... But as long as you are considering dead eyes the center of sight this should be the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-08-2019, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T18:10:15-08:00","id":1286593,"title":"","content":"When you Dominate someone and the command is &quot;forget this scene happened&quot;, and someone else uses Dominate on the same person with the command &quot;tell me what happened during that scene&quot;, what happens?<br /> <br /> Does the person answer &quot;I don't know&quot;?<br /> <br /> Or does this become a Clash of Wills between both Dominate users?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T18:30:06-08:00","id":1286597,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would say the victim answers with &quot;I don't remember&quot; (not &quot;I don't know.&quot;) That scenario would potentially result in the character learning they were mind controlled. But discovering that you (the character) were mind controlled does equal you (the character) have their memories restored. Under base rules, they'd need someone with Auspex 4 to win a Clash of Wills on that particular memory in that block of time.<br /> The Clash of Wills (Dominate v. Dominate) would be for when one command is in progress of being carried out and another command is being installed that would stall or end the first command prematurely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-10-2019, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T07:51:42-08:00","id":1288259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1285588#post1285588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A few notes:<br /> <br /> * Fire has always been a huge, huge thing in civilization. Buildings were mostly out of wood (even the &quot;stone&quot; castles were supported by heavy wood buttressing), and the main source of light and heat was burning stuff. Oil lamps from this period on are vital, and oil can get sprayed, thrown or otherwise ignited to hilarious effects. Fire is also really, really hard to contain during the period--the modern measures that have greatly reduced fire risk are not present.<br /> <br /> * Gangrel survive. It's what they do. Protean 5 and to a lesser extent Resilience 5 underline this. Animalism serves as a tripwire, giving the Gangrel time to prepare so he can... survive. Don't take that away from the player. Instead, show that just because you're physically intact doesn't mean you aren't hurt. Everyone around you that you care about is less durable, even vulnerable, and while your body lives your mind and soul may not. Or not without injury. What steps will you take as you age to safeguard what is really important to you, now that you can in short order, live through danger?<br /> <br /> (BTW, the movie The Last Witchhunter (2015) hooks onto aspects of this.)<br /> <br /> * Surprise. Use it sparingly, and when necessary for the story apply it viciously and without remorse in overwhelming force. Go for staking, which paralyzes and prevents misting. Prep the encounter scene in advance and ensure the antagonists have had enough time to prepare and work out the PC's movements.<br /> <br /> But really, the role of the Gangrel should be &quot;the one that comes back to get the rest out of trouble.&quot; The party should know their unstoppable bud has their back. Or not--in which case they should be honestly afraid. Ultimately the greatest vulnerability of a Gangrel is betrayal; and that's a fact that drives a wedge between them and others, reinforcing their loner-hood.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hey buddy! Thanks for the detailed answer! My problem with Protean 5 isn't really the &quot;incredibly difficult to harm&quot; part, since as you said, that's kind of a a theme with Gangel. It's the ability to kill people while being nigh-unkillable -- except by people with some appreciable form of fire, which outside of actually weaponizing it, is just torches and such. It's not an impossible position, obviously, it just turns every fight into &quot;do his opponents have enough fire on them to stop him from entering their lungs and eating them&quot;. This is a very swingy ability -- up until now, a fight with a small group of 4-6 British Soldiers wasn't a guarantee win. Now almost every fight would be an assured victory unless I force the issue, either by having his opponents have weaponized fire such as oil canisters or have them go &quot;boy this mist sure is horrifying we better grab torches and wave them at it really aggressively while it chokes our friend to death.<br /> <br /> It feels pretty likely that I'm going to nerf it on some level, even if it's just to remove the &quot;entering lungs&quot; aspect of the ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:31:38-08:00","id":1288337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1288259#post1288259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey buddy! Thanks for the detailed answer! My problem with Protean 5 isn't really the &quot;incredibly difficult to harm&quot; part, since as you said, that's kind of a a theme with Gangel. <b>It's the ability to kill people while being nigh-unkillable</b> -- except by people with some appreciable form of fire, which outside of actually weaponizing it, is just torches and such. It's not an impossible position, obviously, it just turns every fight into &quot;do his opponents have enough fire on them to stop him from entering their lungs and eating them&quot;. This is a very swingy ability -- up until now, a fight with a small group of 4-6 British Soldiers wasn't a guarantee win. Now almost every fight would be an assured victory unless I force the issue, either by having his opponents have weaponized fire such as oil canisters or have them go &quot;boy this mist sure is horrifying we better grab torches and wave them at it really aggressively while it chokes our friend to death.<br /> <br /> It feels pretty likely that I'm going to nerf it on some level, even if it's just to remove the &quot;entering lungs&quot; aspect of the ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple things that are nuances, but important to the presentation:<br /> <br /> 1. The form isn't mist--it's smoke. Breathing in smoke is going to produce a noticeable reaction.<br /> <br /> 2. It's up to you how you make the smoke react to sources of flame, but as for me? I'd have any open flame cause harm and the smoke naturally recoil from it. That... gets noticed pretty quick when you are, as you say, trying to figure out why your bud just started choking to death next to you. (A very Lovecraftian horror, to be sure.)<br /> <br /> 3. Humans don't wander around in the dark without a light, unless they're already stirred up to do so or just damn lost. They'll bring a torch, candle or lamp. The first two if swung close to Andy Asphyxiation there in order to see enough to help, will interrupt the ash-cloud form of the player and cause him harm or to withdraw. The lamp is safest to him, but lamps get knocked over and such in good, horrifying chaos, setting fire to barns and curtains and coaches and erstwhile allies and the like. Hilarity, as I said.<br /> <br /> 4. Note that you can suck blood from open wounds, too. It doesn't have to be lungs, which is the most obvious form of attack.<br /> <br /> 5. Keep in mind movement rates for the cloud in relation to victims. If they stand still while not holding flame then the cloud can envelope them and get going. If they're moving the cloud may not be able to catch up. I've not checked the book on this, but it is something to track.<br /> <br /> 6. The first time your player runs into a ghoul and he sucks someone else's Vitae out he's going to get a LOT more circumspect about who he's drawing the precious life out of. It's like running around and casually biting everyone. Blood bonds and sympathy all around.<br /> <br /> 7. Oh, and revenants. That too.<br /> <br /> This is an important topic for me and if you want to post a thread there may be some crowdsourced ideas on how to deal with the power.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 02-15-2019, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T15:21:46-08:00","id":1288412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1288259#post1288259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Hey buddy! Thanks for the detailed answer! My problem with Protean 5 isn't really the &quot;incredibly difficult to harm&quot; part, since as you said, that's kind of a a theme with Gangel. It's the ability to kill people while being nigh-unkillable -- except by people with some appreciable form of fire, which outside of actually weaponizing it, is just torches and such. It's not an impossible position, obviously, it just turns every fight into &quot;do his opponents have enough fire on them to stop him from entering their lungs and eating them&quot;. This is a very swingy ability -- up until now, a fight with a small group of 4-6 British Soldiers wasn't a guarantee win. Now almost every fight would be an assured victory unless I force the issue, either by having his opponents have weaponized fire such as oil canisters or have them go &quot;boy this mist sure is horrifying we better grab torches and wave them at it really aggressively while it chokes our friend to death.<br /> <br /> It feels pretty likely that I'm going to nerf it on some level, even if it's just to remove the &quot;entering lungs&quot; aspect of the ability.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess you are losing the point here: a requiem 2ed. fifth power is, almost in any case, equivalent to a 6th/7th dot of a Masquerade discipline. It's normal and designed to be absolutely awful.Vampire in requiem are the terrible creatures of the horror stories; powerful demons. So why do not thinking to let your 4-6 soldiers patrol to act as in a horror/Lovecraftian book?<br /> <br /> For example they could be horrified seeing a mate of them being suffocated by a sentient cloud of smoke. One of them, panicking, could shoot at the mist screaming and falling down on his back, the other could run away as the bullets pass through the cloud harmless. Now the Gangrel has to deal with an huge problem: a big Masquerade breach. Should him chase the remaining 4 soldiers? Maybe they took different paths or, maybe, they are still together but running as hell and him, as an ash-cloud, can move just up to half his speed. Maybe he need to shapeshifting back as human, or maybe as an animals to be faster (2 vitae). Let's say he reaches them again, jumping to the throat of another soldier, the others will shoot at him, probably with an all-out attack (maybe he's gonna use other vitae to use Resilence or healing himself up). Want him to become mist again? Good, other 3 vitae (5 in total now). Yes he can drink them back up but, again, the patrol could again run away, he will become human/wolf/whatever again, reaching them another time but this time, maybe, the environment has changed. Maybe one of the survivor has enough cold blood to think about what he experienced and open the gas from a stove. Long story short, changing to mist again, the soldier open a lighter throwing it in the room: Boom.<br /> Maybe now he suffer 4 aggravated. He has Resilence? Fine! Other vitae spent. Maybe at the end he'll kill anyone or possibly someone could be escaped letting the Masquerade deeply breached. But surely hasn't been an easy meal.<br /> <br /> As mist you are fucking slow. Let them run away. Breach in the Masquerade means other badasses vampires out on him. Would becoming mist save him than? I wouldn't bet on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-16-2019, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:50:39-08:00","id":1288498,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> has it on all points. All the powers are frankly terrifying in a white room, but that's not where you play and if you look at it from the perspective of the victims things quickly turn into a mess for incautious vamps.<br /> <br /> And very, very good point on the power scaling of dots between VtM and VtR. I had forgotten that one. (This is also one reason why 6+ Blood Potency does not result in Disciplines at 6+ dots.)<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T01:31:58-08:00","id":1288545,"title":"","content":"I agree. Compared to Masquerade, in Requiem Devotions system has acquired much more importance. With Devotions you can transcend the power level of a 5th dot Requiem Discipline (that's already a 7th power level from Masquerade). I'm thinking to devotions such as: Bones of the Mountain, Juggernaut Gait, Force of Nature, Dark decree and so on).<br /> <br /> I think that Requiem, yes can have huge fights and epic battles and can be played as an action RPG if you like to go that way, but you should use proper antagonists. But when played in a city environment, without involving other supernaturals, the play style should be adapted in a way I tried to describe in my previous post, because the power gap between Kindred and Humans is to high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-16-2019, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T14:04:12-08:00","id":1288992,"title":"","content":"I have 2 questions:<br /> <br /> 1) If your vampire falls into a frenzy, and the frenzy's goal is to beat the opposing vampire, yet the opposing vampire turns out to be a lot stronger and quickly manages to fill up a good chunk of your Health with lethal damage, does the frenzying vampire realize she's losing and turn tail? Is a frenzying Beast smart enough to cut its losses and make a run for it? Or will the Beast continue to fight till the bitter end because that was the original frenzy goal?<br /> <br /> 2) If you accidentally kill a vampire (for example you fill a vampire's Health with aggravated damage with your Claws of the Unholy), can you diablerize him if you immediately go for it? Or does the killing have to happen as part of the diablerie ritual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T15:34:22-08:00","id":1289020,"title":"","content":"1. I would say the frenzy goal changes from beating that vampire to fleeing that vampire. I'd install a long term competitive condition on the fleeing vampire to where they feel compelled to one up that vampire in another arena. I don't run the Beast as a moron that will knowingly kill itself.<br /> <br /> 2. I would say a body who's health track is filled with aggravated damage is not an eligible target for diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-17-2019, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T16:43:44-08:00","id":1289032,"title":"","content":"My rule of thumb is, a frenzy's goal can change if you hit another frenzy trigger. Taking enough lethal damage could be a trigger for a &quot;run away&quot; frenzy, so that would be a valid goal change. (Similarly, if you're frenzying to destroy someone, the taste of their blood might change the goal to &quot;feed to satiety&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-17T16:44:31-08:00","id":1289033,"title":"","content":"Also, yeah, by book Diablerie has to be performed on a torpid vampire. A vampire agged in their last health box is dead, not torpid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:04:39-08:00","id":1289908,"title":"","content":"What happens if you use Dominate 3, Entombed Command, and give the command <i>&quot;when Billy the Ventrue makes eye contact with you, do not--under any circumstances--follow his commands&quot;</i>?<br /> <br /> Would that effectively make the person immune to Dominate from the mentioned Ventrue Billy? Or would that result in a Clash of Wills when Billy tries to Dominate him? Or would that Entombed Command not work for some reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 02-20-2019, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:25:10-08:00","id":1289914,"title":"","content":"Text book Clash of Wills. Both commands are mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> An extremely dangerous command, though, if Billy the Ventrue figures it out and gives reverse orders without using Dominate. &quot;Do not kill your Sire.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:26:42-08:00","id":1289915,"title":"","content":"I have some Mandragora questions... A little background, I am an Ordo Dracul Mekhet that wants to learn Majesty. My touchstone and I purchased a strawberry plant (small Mandragora) and I invested WP and vitae in it.<br /> <br /> 1) Is it worth putting a point of retainer into the Mandragora? Is it capable of listening to me and acting as a servant? I know it can move around when no one is watching, but what is it capable of doing? Does it just sit there and take up resources?<br /> 2) Does a small Mandragora automatically get <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Majesty 1, Resilience 1, and Vigor 1? Is there anyway I can learn disciplines from it - specifically Majesty? It is a strawberry plant so will eating the berries do anything?<br /> 3) I am Ordo so I definitely want to do some experiments on it. Any ideas of what I can do?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:28:25-08:00","id":1289916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1289908#post1289908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if you use Dominate 3, Entombed Command, and give the command <i>&quot;when Billy the Ventrue makes eye contact with you, do not--under any circumstances--follow his commands&quot;</i>?<br /> <br /> Would that effectively make the person immune to Dominate from the mentioned Ventrue Billy? Or would that result in a Clash of Wills when Billy tries to Dominate him? Or would that Entombed Command not work for some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>That just goes straight to a Clash of Wills, assuming negatively-defined commands even work at all \u2014 Dominate is first and foremost a power for making people do and believe what you tell them, and the ability to supersede other magical commands is not a special aspect of it that turns into a complete alteration of how its main Conditions operate once you have the third dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:20:43-08:00","id":1289934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1289908#post1289908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if you use Dominate 3, Entombed Command, and give the command <i>&amp;quot;when Billy the Ventrue makes eye contact with you, do not--under any circumstances--follow his commands&amp;quot;</i>?<br /> <br /> Would that effectively make the person immune to Dominate from the mentioned Ventrue Billy? Or would that result in a Clash of Wills when Billy tries to Dominate him? Or would that Entombed Command not work for some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll definitely go for a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:48:34-08:00","id":1289947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1289908#post1289908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if you use Dominate 3, Entombed Command, and give the command <i>&amp;quot;when Billy the Ventrue makes eye contact with you, do not--under any circumstances--follow his commands&amp;quot;</i>?<br /> <br /> Would that effectively make the person immune to Dominate from the mentioned Ventrue Billy? Or would that result in a Clash of Wills when Billy tries to Dominate him? Or would that Entombed Command not work for some reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. As Tessie said. It's a Clash of Wills. No Dominate immunity since the eye contact could be established for the purpose of memory alteration, not issuing directives to perform. <br /> <br /> If you want to game the system for purposes of overriding instructions, you install an Entombed Command along the lines of &quot;If Billy gives you a command, inform me and get my approval first before fulfilling it.&quot; Of course that won't stop memory alteration but you can throw a monkey wrench in potential frame jobs or set ups using Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:57:31-08:00","id":1289953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1289915#post1289915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some Mandragora questions... A little background, I am an Ordo Dracul Mekhet that wants to learn Majesty. My touchstone and I purchased a strawberry plant (small Mandragora) and I invested WP and vitae in it.<br /> <br /> 1) Is it worth putting a point of retainer into the Mandragora? Is it capable of listening to me and acting as a servant? I know it can move around when no one is watching, but what is it capable of doing? Does it just sit there and take up resources?<br /> 2) Does a small Mandragora automatically get <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;\">Majesty 1, Resilience 1, and Vigor 1? Is there anyway I can learn disciplines from it - specifically Majesty? It is a strawberry plant so will eating the berries do anything?<br /> 3) I am Ordo so I definitely want to do some experiments on it. Any ideas of what I can do?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That's up to you and your ST if a Mandragora can function as a retainer. Unless you have other powers to use on a mandragora, it can't uproot itself and walk around if that's what you mean by moving. It moves within the reach of its branches and roots. <br /> <br /> Typically mandragora would be used to function as a stationary barrier for security or to produce lacrima. A poisonous (to humans) substance that can be a potential substitute for vitae or consumable drink for vampires. Or possibly a component for vampiric alchemical mixtures or potions.<br /> <br /> No you can't teach or learn disciplines by default from a mandragora. That's ST fiat on whether or not it's possible. That said, there was an Invictus NPC in one setting I played in who used lacrima to bottle and sell discipline powers as one time per drink use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-20-2019, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:40:11-08:00","id":1290033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1289916#post1289916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That just goes straight to a Clash of Wills, assuming negatively-defined commands even work at all \u2014 Dominate is first and foremost a power for making people do and believe what you tell them, and the ability to supersede other magical commands is not a special aspect of it that turns into a complete alteration of how its main Conditions operate once you have the third dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe negatively-defined commands work. Do not leave this room. Don't get up. Don't speak. That reverse bounceback, that's just silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9015-zee-patrick","name":"zee PaTrick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:12:19-08:00","id":1290168,"title":"","content":"Greetings Requiem fans. I just wanted to take a moment an applaud the participants of this forum thread. Great and passionate content for VtR2. I just started reading this thread 1 week prior and over 180 pages have passed. I have been running VtR2 for the past 3 years without much use of internet resources and it was great to read some of the same discussions and solutions come up and evolve.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T22:28:59-08:00","id":1290243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zee PaTrick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290033#post1290033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe negatively-defined commands work. Do not leave this room. Don't get up. Don't speak. That reverse bounceback, that's just silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those aren't negatively-defined commands, though, those are just commands that you <i>can</i> phrase as things they shouldn't do \u2014 all of those examples are just saying &quot;stay [in this room/seated/silent]&quot; backwards and occasionally with more words, which isn't exactly a habit you want to get into with Dominate if you haven't gone the extra mile in prepping the subject to save on Vitae costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T22:37:37-08:00","id":1290244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290243#post1290243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those aren't negatively-defined commands, though, those are just commands that you <i>can</i> phrase as things they shouldn't do \u2014 all of those examples are just saying &amp;quot;stay [in this room/seated/silent]&amp;quot; backwards and occasionally with more words, which isn't exactly a habit you want to get into with Dominate if you haven't gone the extra mile in prepping the subject to save on Vitae costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same can be said about any negative, including my example.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ignore what Billy says.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T23:13:07-08:00","id":1290254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290244#post1290244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same can be said about any negative, including my example.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ignore what Billy says.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the active verb form of that command? What do they do in a scenario where you are giving this order without the framework of Entombed Command? What do they do in a scenario where Billy never says anything to them?<br /> <br /> Like, seriously, I realize this is a somewhat tricky semantic point here, but <i>what Dominate does</i> does not allow you to mess with perception. It lets you make people do things, and it lets you make people remember things differently than how they did. Making them <i>ignore things</i> is what Obfuscate is for.<br /> <br /> I can train a dog to sit, stay, and hush. I can train it to do those things on particular cues. I cannot train it to Ignore Billy without having that behavior mean a specific thing that requires it to still acknowledge Billy as the first step of that process.<br /> <br /> The only thing &quot;ignore Billy's commands&quot; does as a command is put a gate in front of Billy's commands that Billy can brute-force his way through, and you get that from literally any other conditional command as a bonus to what you're already having them do. &quot;If Billy approaches you, avoid Billy's gaze&quot; accomplishes the same goal without getting into weird orders-that-aren't-orders for a power built around dictating events and activities to people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T00:08:01-08:00","id":1290262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290254#post1290254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the active verb form of that command? What do they do in a scenario where you are giving this order without the framework of Entombed Command? What do they do in a scenario where Billy never says anything to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290254#post1290254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, seriously, I realize this is a somewhat tricky semantic point here, but <i>what Dominate does</i> does not allow you to mess with perception. It lets you make people do things, and it lets you make people remember things differently than how they did. Making them <i>ignore things</i> is what Obfuscate is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're willfully misinterpreting what I said. You're interpreting &quot;ignore&quot; to mean &quot;overlook&quot;, which is clearly not what I meant. I mean &quot;ignore&quot; as in &quot;reject&quot;. Ignore his commands. Reject his commands. That has nothing to do with Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290254#post1290254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can train a dog to sit, stay, and hush. I can train it to do those things on particular cues. I cannot train it to Ignore Billy without having that behavior mean a specific thing that requires it to still acknowledge Billy as the first step of that process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever had a dog? You can most certainly train dogs to ignore things.<br /> <br /> Acknowledging Billy's presence is not the issue. It's fine for the Dominated victim to acknowledge Billy's presence. I just want him to ignore anything Billy says. Hence &quot;Ignore what Billy says&quot;, not just &quot;Ignore Billy&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290254#post1290254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing &quot;ignore Billy's commands&quot; does as a command is put a gate in front of Billy's commands that Billy can brute-force his way through, and you get that from literally any other conditional command as a bonus to what you're already having them do. &quot;If Billy approaches you, avoid Billy's gaze&quot; accomplishes the same goal without getting into weird orders-that-aren't-orders for a power built around dictating events and activities to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's not an &quot;order-that-isn't-an-order&quot;, it's just an order. &quot;Ignore what Billy says&quot; is just as valid an order as &quot;avoid Billy's gaze&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>\u200bEdit:</b> I do have to give kudos to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> though, &quot;when Billy gives you orders, come to me and ask for my permission first before doing anything Billy says&quot; is an even better safeguard against Dominate than a simple &quot;when Billy looks you in the eyes, ignore his commands&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 02-21-2019, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T00:36:56-08:00","id":1290264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290262#post1290262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever had a dog? You can most certainly train dogs to ignore things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had at least one dog for over half my life. Talking of willful misinterpretation, though, are you aware of what &quot;acknowledge&quot; means, and why it might have some bearing on the order of operations that makes the application of Dominate that this is an analogy for little more than &quot;I'm putting a Clash of Wills in front of this person's use of Dominate but not otherwise using Dominate in a narratively significant way&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it's not an &quot;order-that-isn't-an-order&quot;, it's just an order. &quot;Ignore what Billy says&quot; is just as valid an order as &quot;avoid Billy's gaze&quot;. </div> </div> </div>It's an &quot;order&quot; that exists purely to apply the Clash of Wills rules in a way that doesn't engage with the fiction in a meaningful fashion.<br /> <br /> Dominate doesn't have special rules for conflicting supernatural compulsions and the existing rules for those are just &quot;whoever is stronger and/or luckier takes precedence&quot; \u2014 there's no reason to conclude that vampires looking to block a rival's attempt at subverting their assets would command them to do nothing instead of do something else given that one of these things does not engage with the problem as anything more than staving off one use of a power that costs nothing to initiate.<br /> <br /> &quot;If Billy tries to catch your eye, excuse yourself&quot; and &quot;If Billy tries to tell you to do something, stab him&quot; are both actual conditional orders to do something that addresses the fact that Billy is entirely capable of just trying again if his attempt to Mesmerize your patsy fails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T00:41:35-08:00","id":1290265,"title":"","content":"I guess that leads me to a new question:<br /> <br /> What would you guys recommend if I want to guard my minions against a Ventrue's Dominate? How can I make sure a Ventrue isn't just going to walk up to my minion and use my own minion against me with Dominate? Countering his Dominate with my own Entombed Command could potentially work, as we discussed above. But what other options would I have? What if I don't have access to Dominate myself? How would a Mekhet protect his minions against Dominate meddling? How would a Nosferatu? A Gangrel?<br /> <br /> Or is Dominate literally so overpowered that there is no way I can protect my minions against it, other than telling all my minions to avoid eye contact? Which in no way is a solid protection, the Ventrue can just brute-force the eye contact with a grapple and hold move, or if the Ventrue also has 1 dot in Majesty he can just use Awe.<br /> <br /> And even if somehow a high-Resolve human with the Indomitable Merit manages to resist a Ventrue's attempt at Mesmerize, what's stopping the Ventrue from simply trying again? As long as the failure is not a dramatic failure, the human does not necessarily realize the Ventrue tried to mesmerize him. So the Ventrue can then just try again, and again, and again, and again, until the ghoul finally realizes something weird is going on. There's no Vitae cost to Mesmerize, so other than Storyteller intervention, there's nothing stopping a Ventrue from just trying over and over again until he succeeds.<br /> <br /> Of course, this only counts against humans. I'd argue a vampire is much more likely to pick up what's going on after 1 failed Mesmerize attempt, and respond accordingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, to make this question an even broader question: How would an ST set up a murder mystery or some other kind of L.A. Noire style detective mystery when the Ventrue player can just Mesmerize every single suspect or human who might know something, and always guaranteed get all the information each individual has, including confessionals if the human is dominated to confess his crimes? The only hurdle I can personally think of is having another Ventrue pull the strings behind the scenes with Dominate (to counter the player's Dominate) or other kind of supernatural meddling with the memory of the humans. Surely there are other ways to prevent Dominate from being the end-all be-all tool in a detective mystery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 02-21-2019, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T01:24:06-08:00","id":1290270,"title":"","content":"The most straightforward limitation is sheer logistics: the vampire can only give one command at a time, can only prime a single target at a time, can only be in one place at a time, isn't invisible by default, and needs to spend a nontrivial amount of time making their statements.<br /> <br /> Without The Lying Mind, Mesmerize only lets you edit memories of things that happened pretty recently. (<i>With</i> The Lying Mind, you have to engage in fairly obvious blood-based behavior and are spending a minute of description for the crudest of alterations.) Without Obfuscate, the vampire has to give some thought to the problem of witnesses. (<i>With</i> Obfuscate, keeping any involved party that isn't yourself costs precious Vitae.) If your mark is being watched (as they might well be in a detective story), they're going to look and/or sound odd if giving up the information or making the confession is out of sorts for them. (If they <i>aren't</i> being watched, it's possible that's deliberate; they could be a plant or they could be missing vital information or the thing they witnessed wasn't the important part.)<br /> <br /> There's a reason this kind of complex machination generally involves establishing a power base or doing a lot of scattered piecemeal assembly here and there, and that's because these issues exist even with mundane conspiracy-intrigue scenarios. Time is at a premium when you're allergic to daylight, &quot;information is power&quot; is a truism for more than just the Mekhet, and greater degrees of stealth and information control take up resources you could save for other things.<br /> <br /> That being said, yes, this is less of a concern for vampires dealing with purely human systems when allowed to act with relative freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T02:15:01-08:00","id":1290276,"title":"","content":"Dominante gives orders. Do not follow other orders IS an order indeed. <br /> <br /> When you have a general and a caporal and the General gives to you, as a soldier, the order to not follow what the caporal says to you, you are not doing what the caporal orders.<br /> It's not that the soldier do not hear or it's not aware about the caporal's orders. It's just he MUST to follow another direct order that impose to him to not perform other commands. So Obfuscate doesn't enter in this at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-21-2019, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T03:20:02-08:00","id":1290285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290265#post1290265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that leads me to a new question:<br /> <br /> What would you guys recommend if I want to guard my minions against a Ventrue's Dominate? How can I make sure a Ventrue isn't just going to walk up to my minion and use my own minion against me with Dominate? Countering his Dominate with my own Entombed Command could potentially work, as we discussed above. But what other options would I have? What if I don't have access to Dominate myself? How would a Mekhet protect his minions against Dominate meddling? How would a Nosferatu? A Gangrel?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a vampire you could always develop a Devotion that protects against mental influences (for example Auspex+Resilience, unlike Mesmerize should cost Vitae to activate and Clash during a scene or reflexively to individual attempts). Or an Obfuscate Devotion to fake being under a mental effect that has been successfully resisted/contested.<br /> Otherwise it's only to protect the eyes (or stab them out).<br /> <br /> The eye contact thing does take an instant action so a failed Mesmerize attempt should be noticable for anyone who's perceptive and/or trained to notice such things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T04:56:02-08:00","id":1290297,"title":"","content":"Vampire<br /> * Auspex to detect it<br /> * Blood Sorcery to detect or prevent it<br /> * Dominate as mentioned above<br /> * Isn't there a -1 for retrying at the ST's discretion?<br /> <br /> Other Splats<br /> * Mage Mind Arcana for protecting or detecting. <br /> * Mortal merit that acts a Supernatural Tolerance. <br /> <br /> My books are in another state for the moment so I am going from memory. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:04:14-08:00","id":1290311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290265#post1290265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that leads me to a new question:<br /> <br /> What would you guys recommend if I want to guard my minions against a Ventrue's Dominate? How can I make sure a Ventrue isn't just going to walk up to my minion and use my own minion against me with Dominate? Countering his Dominate with my own Entombed Command could potentially work, as we discussed above. But what other options would I have? What if I don't have access to Dominate myself? How would a Mekhet protect his minions against Dominate meddling? How would a Nosferatu? A Gangrel?<br /> <br /> Or is Dominate literally so overpowered that there is no way I can protect my minions against it, other than telling all my minions to avoid eye contact? Which in no way is a solid protection, the Ventrue can just brute-force the eye contact with a grapple and hold move, or if the Ventrue also has 1 dot in Majesty he can just use Awe.<br /> <br /> And even if somehow a high-Resolve human with the Indomitable Merit manages to resist a Ventrue's attempt at Mesmerize, what's stopping the Ventrue from simply trying again? As long as the failure is not a dramatic failure, the human does not necessarily realize the Ventrue tried to mesmerize him. So the Ventrue can then just try again, and again, and again, and again, until the ghoul finally realizes something weird is going on. There's no Vitae cost to Mesmerize, so other than Storyteller intervention, there's nothing stopping a Ventrue from just trying over and over again until he succeeds.<br /> <br /> Of course, this only counts against humans. I'd argue a vampire is much more likely to pick up what's going on after 1 failed Mesmerize attempt, and respond accordingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or, to make this question an even broader question: How would an ST set up a murder mystery or some other kind of L.A. Noire style detective mystery when the Ventrue player can just Mesmerize every single suspect or human who might know something, and always guaranteed get all the information each individual has, including confessionals if the human is dominated to confess his crimes? The only hurdle I can personally think of is having another Ventrue pull the strings behind the scenes with Dominate (to counter the player's Dominate) or other kind of supernatural meddling with the memory of the humans. Surely there are other ways to prevent Dominate from being the end-all be-all tool in a detective mystery?</div> </div> </div> </div>You assume your minions can be subverted and plan accordingly. Therefore you don't entrust them with information that you want to keep confidential. If you need them to remember something at a critical juncture, you erase their memories and set them to be restored via trigger phrase or action. If you want to get byzantine, you install pawns with contradictory and false information.<br /> <br /> A cumulative -1 penalty to successive attempts after failing prevents trying over and over.<br /> <br /> Mechanically I would just port over Conditioning from 1st edition. It assigns a penalty to Dominate use on anyone who isn't the conditioner.<br /> <br /> You can engineer a Resilience devotion to make your minions resistant to all Dominate effects. <br /> <br /> One game I played in my character's sire had a devotion called widdershins, that turned the next successful activation of a mind or emotion activating power against the user to the would be victim. The user became Majestied, Dominated, Nightmared, Animalism frenzied etc. at the bidding of the victim. (It only took one instance of a younger Ventrue fucking with his ghoul and having it reversed on her at a semi formal elysium gathering to inform everyone that his minions were not to be screwed with.)<br /> <br /> As for your murder mystery. Create extraneous characters that don't know anything and have zero involvement in the story and add some red herrings. Better yet, have a few people confess to it in order to protect someone else. (Bonus points if one of those confessions is based on false memories implanted by a Ventrue or scrambled by a Mekhet with a fetish for triggering traumatic memories in someone.) After wasting several hours and gallons of vitae chasing through dead end clues, maybe your Ventrue player will realize that perhaps his time will be better spent looking for more evidence before mind raping everyone. But honestly, you should be more worried about the Mekhet simply using Auspex to find out everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:05:26-08:00","id":1290313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290285#post1290285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For a vampire you could always develop a Devotion that protects against mental influences (for example Auspex+Resilience, unlike Mesmerize should cost Vitae to activate and Clash during a scene or reflexively to individual attempts). Or an Obfuscate Devotion to fake being under a mental effect that has been successfully resisted/contested.<br /> Otherwise it's only to protect the eyes (or stab them out).<br /> <br /> The eye contact thing does take an instant action so a failed Mesmerize attempt should be noticable for anyone who's perceptive and/or trained to notice such things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That reminds me of another question.<br /> <br /> So far I've always been running Disciplines as the vampire being aware when his Discipline failed, based on the fact that according to the book, there's always <i>something</i> happening when a Discipline is used, even when the Discipline fails, and that the Beast isn't happy with Disciplines failing. For example, a failed Mesmerize use might send a noticeable chill down the would-be victim's spine, as she visibly recoils and turns her gaze away from the vampire. As such, I've always allowed the players to roleplay their vampire as being immediately aware of the fact that the Mesmerize failed, and allow the player to try it again.<br /> <br /> Is that how it's supposed to be played out though? And would I severe cripple the Dominate Discipline if I changed it to vampires being unaware of their Discipline failure until the victim does something that goes against the Mesmerize command?<br /> <br /> For example, the Ventrue fails Mesmerize, but doesn't realize it failed yet, he commands the human to &quot;stand still&quot;, which the human does, but when the Ventrue approaches the human, the human backs away from the Ventrue, saying <i>&quot;hey, stay the fuck away from me!&quot;</i>, which then immediately makes it clear the Mesmerize failed.<br /> <br /> But in another example, the Ventrue's Mesmerize fails, but doesn't realize it failed yet. He commands the human to &quot;speak the truth&quot;, followed with a question. The human answers the question, but he's lying. Perhaps rolling a Manipulation + Subterfuge against the Ventrue's Wits + Empathy to see if the Ventrue notices the human is just lying. The Ventrue fails this roll too, and thus he does not realize the Mesmerize failed and the human is just straight up lying, and leaves the scene believing he got the truth out of the human with his Dominate Discipline.<br /> <br /> Would that be a fair way of handling Mesmerize?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 02-21-2019, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:12:31-08:00","id":1290314,"title":"","content":"Unless there was special circumstances (dramatic failure, fate magic, etc) I let the vampire know. Say the victim has indomitable, &quot;you Beast reaches out to lay low the mind of this guard and meets an unusual amount of resistance, with a final effort you crush his will.&quot; <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:35:01-08:00","id":1290326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290265#post1290265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you guys recommend if I want to guard my minions against a Ventrue's Dominate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blind/deafen them.<br /> Use animal minions.<br /> Ghoul them and teach them Obs.<br /> Keep your minions away from them.<br /> <br /> Other than that, not much. Once the Ventrue is in a room with your folks and free of time constraints, they are eventually gonna break through. As mentioned above, 1E Conditioning gave some resistance buffs, but that got stripped with 2E. I think there may have been some Carthian Book devotions that did a similar thing, but I'd need to go research that for sure. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290265#post1290265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, to make this question an even broader question: How would an ST set up a murder mystery ... Surely there are other ways to prevent Dominate from being the end-all be-all tool in a detective mystery?</div> </div> </div> </div>This speaks to me, as one of my players went heavy on Dominate and I've needed to get creative to keep mysteries and mortal roadblocks a challenge. At the end of the day, though, yeah - you need to accept that Dominate is a game changer. But so is Auspex, and at least Dominate can be resisted each step of the way. Most Auspex abilities can't be resisted at all. You will not be able to run basic mysteries when a clever players brings Dominate into it. However, on a meta level, it isn't much different than the Celerity character who isn't going to be challenged by basic combat anymore either.<br /> <br /> First step is talking with the player/ST to figure out limits. This kind of thing will escalate pretty quickly if it isn't handled in the social contract, and nipping the '<i>Well, I'll just buy this <b>other </b>ability to short-circuit through your plots!</i>' is better handled there than with mechanics.<br /> <br /> As for in-story efforts:<br /> <br /> Go abstract with the investigation. Dominate just becomes another avenue for collecting Clues rather getting perfect insight into crimes/motivations.<br /> <br /> You can have witnesses be inaccessible. My player had an antagonism with a more powerful Kindred, decided to mess with his stuff, walked right up to his security guard, Dominated them to gain access to the site, did a bunch of political/physical damage to the location. The next time he showed up to do something similar, he was met with video screens and intercoms rather than real human security at the gates. Can't Dominate a TV. You can have folks in jail or abroad so the mystery has to be followed up by phone / email.<br /> <br /> Remember the Masquerade. If the character is brute forcing things instead of taking a lot of time to be creative / subtle, that can bite them. Lost visage will mostly protect them personally from cameras, but not audio recordings or the like.<br /> <br /> Remember Humanity. You are absolutely within your rights to impose a penalty on breaking point checks for removing free will. There are diminishing returns on this since a bane or a point or two drop will put them outside the danger zone. But also keep in mind putting the player on the hook for any crimes / damage to the person is also fair game. I had my player make some checks after they caused a shootout between some cops and criminals, even though he didn't technically pull any triggers. <br /> <br /> Mortals can also be protected. If you are messing with people's assets, for example if you need to Dominate the DA, that person might be a minion or at least under the purview / domain of an established Kindred. It won't stop the Dominate in the moment, but the other Kindred could have a case before the Prince, Harpies, etc and political consequences could easily come down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:18:04-08:00","id":1290355,"title":"","content":"In a game I ran a Ventrue was abusive to his ghoul, disowned him, framed him, resummoned him (devotion) and so on. During some odd failures, successes and humanity loss this ghoul managed to plot. <br /> <br /> He faked his own death through others, which the Ventrue accepted without a glance, thus he did not try to summon him anymore. Next he continues stalking his master with obsession and plotting, accidentally becoming a vessel for an otherworldly summoning ritual. End of the story this insignificant ghoul that was dominated, abused and broken became a great multi-session plot piece for the game. <br /> <br /> Never underestimate the power of the mundane.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:31:13-08:00","id":1290422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290326#post1290326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blind/deafen them.<br /> Use animal minions.<br /> Ghoul them and teach them Obs.<br /> Keep your minions away from them.<br /> <br /> Other than that, not much. Once the Ventrue is in a room with your folks and free of time constraints, they are eventually gonna break through. As mentioned above, 1E Conditioning gave some resistance buffs, but that got stripped with 2E. I think there may have been some Carthian Book devotions that did a similar thing, but I'd need to go research that for sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This speaks to me, as one of my players went heavy on Dominate and I've needed to get creative to keep mysteries and mortal roadblocks a challenge. At the end of the day, though, yeah - you need to accept that Dominate is a game changer. But so is Auspex, and at least Dominate can be resisted each step of the way. Most Auspex abilities can't be resisted at all. You will not be able to run basic mysteries when a clever players brings Dominate into it. However, on a meta level, it isn't much different than the Celerity character who isn't going to be challenged by basic combat anymore either.<br /> <br /> First step is talking with the player/ST to figure out limits. This kind of thing will escalate pretty quickly if it isn't handled in the social contract, and nipping the '<i>Well, I'll just buy this <b>other </b>ability to short-circuit through your plots!</i>' is better handled there than with mechanics.<br /> <br /> As for in-story efforts:<br /> <br /> Go abstract with the investigation. Dominate just becomes another avenue for collecting Clues rather getting perfect insight into crimes/motivations.<br /> <br /> You can have witnesses be inaccessible. My player had an antagonism with a more powerful Kindred, decided to mess with his stuff, walked right up to his security guard, Dominated them to gain access to the site, did a bunch of political/physical damage to the location. The next time he showed up to do something similar, he was met with video screens and intercoms rather than real human security at the gates. Can't Dominate a TV. You can have folks in jail or abroad so the mystery has to be followed up by phone / email.<br /> <br /> Remember the Masquerade. If the character is brute forcing things instead of taking a lot of time to be creative / subtle, that can bite them. Lost visage will mostly protect them personally from cameras, but not audio recordings or the like.<br /> <br /> Remember Humanity. You are absolutely within your rights to impose a penalty on breaking point checks for removing free will. There are diminishing returns on this since a bane or a point or two drop will put them outside the danger zone. But also keep in mind putting the player on the hook for any crimes / damage to the person is also fair game. I had my player make some checks after they caused a shootout between some cops and criminals, even though he didn't technically pull any triggers.<br /> <br /> Mortals can also be protected. If you are messing with people's assets, for example if you need to Dominate the DA, that person might be a minion or at least under the purview / domain of an established Kindred. It won't stop the Dominate in the moment, but the other Kindred could have a case before the Prince, Harpies, etc and political consequences could easily come down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some great tips! Sadly I can't use all of them because the game I'm running takes place in 1888-1918 London, so no video cameras, limited photo cameras, no TVs, audio recordings exist but are primitive, phones exist but limited, certainly not everyone has one, most communication happens verbally, through messengers and through letters.<br /> <br /> As for your Breaking Points suggestion. That wouldn't feel right to me. 'Depriving another of consent with a Discipline' is normally a Humanity 8 Breaking Point. This Ventrue is Humanity 6. I did make him roll a Humanity 6 Breaking Point when he Dominated his own Touchstone (who's part of this mystery), but having him roll a Breaking Point every time he dominates a human to get him to speak the truth wouldn't be right. Of course if he uses Dominate to have the human commit a murder, that's another story. That I would count as a 'premeditated killing' Breaking Point, and probably give a -1 penalty on the Detachment roll because he made someone else do it for him with Dominate.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of throwing vital witnesses in jail though. That does actually make sense for the current mystery I'm running. That will certainly make this much more of an ordeal than just simply walking up to the guy and doing the usual Dominate stuff.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 02-21-2019, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T17:24:50-08:00","id":1290606,"title":"","content":"So here's another question about something I'm not quite sure I'm doing right:<br /> <br /> On Obfuscate 3, Cloak of the Night:<br /> <br /> 1. When Lashing Out against someone who's Obfuscated with Cloak of the Night (after locating them), you can shatter the shroud. When doing so successfully, does that mean <i>everyone</i> can see the Obfuscated vampire?<br /> 2. What's stopping the vampire from simply reactivating Obfuscate after being revealed, other than the Vitae cost?<br /> 3. If the answer to question 2 is &quot;nothing&quot;, how does one counter Obfuscate on a more permanent basis? <br /> 4. What happens if an Obfuscated vampire (still talking about Cloak of the Night) engages one of my friends in a grapple and doesn't spend a Vitae to also make my friend invisible? Do I see my friend wrestling with the air?<br /> 5. What's stopping someone form attacking the last known location of the Obfuscated vampire? Would you impose a die penalty for that? What if he actually hits her, does that reveal her to him?<br /> 6. If a vampire drops out of sight with Cloak of the Night, but I still know her general location, can I Lash Out against her, despite not seeing her?<br /> <br /> On Obfuscate 1, Face in the Crowd:<br /> <br /> 7. Is it possible to use Face in the Crowd but still have your coterie know who/where you are?<br /> 8. Can you launch surprise attacks with Face in the Crowd, or is that restricted to Cloak of the Night, given that people still see &quot;some guy&quot; when using Face in the Crowd, while Cloak of the Night actually makes you invisible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T18:25:24-08:00","id":1290616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290606#post1290606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's another question about something I'm not quite sure I'm doing right:<br /> <br /> On Obfuscate 3, Cloak of the Night:<br /> <br /> 1. When Lashing Out against someone who's Obfuscated with Cloak of the Night (after locating them), you can shatter the shroud. When doing so successfully, does that mean <i>everyone</i> can see the Obfuscated vampire?<br /> 2. What's stopping the vampire from simply reactivating Obfuscate after being revealed, other than the Vitae cost?<br /> 3. If the answer to question 2 is &quot;nothing&quot;, how does one counter Obfuscate on a more permanent basis? <br /> 4. What happens if an Obfuscated vampire (still talking about Cloak of the Night) engages one of my friends in a grapple and doesn't spend a Vitae to also make my friend invisible? Do I see my friend wrestling with the air?<br /> 5. What's stopping someone form attacking the last known location of the Obfuscated vampire? Would you impose a die penalty for that? What if he actually hits her, does that reveal her to him?<br /> 6. If a vampire drops out of sight with Cloak of the Night, but I still know her general location, can I Lash Out against her, despite not seeing her?<br /> <br /> On Obfuscate 1, Face in the Crowd:<br /> <br /> 7. Is it possible to use Face in the Crowd but still have your coterie know who/where you are?<br /> 8. Can you launch surprise attacks with Face in the Crowd, or is that restricted to Cloak of the Night, given that people still see &quot;some guy&quot; when using Face in the Crowd, while Cloak of the Night actually makes you invisible?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes<br /> 2. Nothing<br /> 3. Blood magic, special items or areas, mages, werewolves or similiar senses <br /> 4. Yes and I would reduce would bypass the perception roll for locating them an imposs a -2 or -3 to attack (partially Blind)<br /> 5. Nothing, but sounds like a perception just to have a chance (Blind -5) to attack. Failed perception auto miss. <br /> 6. I do not remember if they both end as being built on each other or not. If Face is still active then no. If not yes. <br /> 7. If memory serves me when touching someone they become aware of your general presence. <br /> 8. I give Obfuscate dots as a penalty to the target while using Face in the Crowd to launch a surprise attack. Perception (- Obfuscate) vs Stealth.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind I am going from memory and using events from my game. I had a Mekhet player who was not happy with me after he was using cloak of night and grappling a foe, when I gave his allies a chance to attack him. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 02-21-2019, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T18:49:40-08:00","id":1290624,"title":"","content":"1. All Obfuscate effects are broken.<br /> 2. Nothing but the one who shattered Obfuscate is immune to it for the rest of the scene.<br /> 3. A high innate perception skill. <br /> 4. Yes. <br /> 5. Nothing. I penalize the roll at -2<br /> 5a. No. You may hit them but that doesn't mean you see them bleed. <br /> 5b. I reduce the Obfuscate penalty for detection if they successfully hit the obfuscated character.<br /> 6. Yes but I penalize the Predatory Aura activation by the target's Obfuscate score.<br /> 7. Elaborate. Will they see the obfuscated character Yes. Will they still know they're a vampire? Yes. Will they all come up with the same description of the character at the time by memory? No.<br /> 8. Yes. But Obfuscate breaks immediately. The perception check for Danger Sense abilities or surprise is penalized at -1.<br /> The one using Obfuscate 1 is, after all, in plain sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:21:37-08:00","id":1290683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290606#post1290606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's another question about something I'm not quite sure I'm doing right:<br /> <br /> On Obfuscate 3, Cloak of the Night:<br /> <br /> 1. When Lashing Out against someone who's Obfuscated with Cloak of the Night (after locating them), you can shatter the shroud. When doing so successfully, does that mean <i>everyone</i> can see the Obfuscated vampire?<br /> 2. What's stopping the vampire from simply reactivating Obfuscate after being revealed, other than the Vitae cost?<br /> 3. If the answer to question 2 is &quot;nothing&quot;, how does one counter Obfuscate on a more permanent basis? <br /> 4. What happens if an Obfuscated vampire (still talking about Cloak of the Night) engages one of my friends in a grapple and doesn't spend a Vitae to also make my friend invisible? Do I see my friend wrestling with the air?<br /> 5. What's stopping someone form attacking the last known location of the Obfuscated vampire? Would you impose a die penalty for that? What if he actually hits her, does that reveal her to him?<br /> 6. If a vampire drops out of sight with Cloak of the Night, but I still know her general location, can I Lash Out against her, despite not seeing her?<br /> <br /> On Obfuscate 1, Face in the Crowd:<br /> <br /> 7. Is it possible to use Face in the Crowd but still have your coterie know who/where you are?<br /> 8. Can you launch surprise attacks with Face in the Crowd, or is that restricted to Cloak of the Night, given that people still see &quot;some guy&quot; when using Face in the Crowd, while Cloak of the Night actually makes you invisible?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes, alle effects are broken<br /> 2. Nothing, but for the scene who lashed out will see him<br /> 3. For the scene who shattered is immune, I also like to use environment other than Supernatural means. Like activating anti-fire system, spread something on the, floor, using a fire extinguisher to create a cloud. Everything would dramatically increase the chance to track him down.<br /> 4. Yes, an external observer would see him struggling against a mystical force<br /> 5. Nothing. Indeed you can always attack someone you can't see with a -5 (plus -defense) malus. That's until the obfuscated is in that very place. As soon as he will slips away I wouldn't allow any other roll if not with an all out firearms attack at area.<br /> 6. No. Predatory aura don't just need to know somewhere is there. It need you to FEEL the other presence to lash out against. And you can perceive it either with Auspex (or other mysticals) or tracking him down, seeing the very laat clue that let yourself feel sure he is RIGHT THERE.<br /> 7. I let face in the crowd working just if you are not already seeing him. You can't just disappear in front of someone. You need at first letting him lose you at least for a turn. In exemple, the trafficlight become green for pawns, a little crowd pass between you. For just a second someone overpose himself in front of the Nosferatu and the second after he is not there anymore. You look around, in the crowd, but you just see anonymous faces...<br /> 8. You definitely can. If your enemy is not directly looking at you he will not follow you going behind him. So I would allow a surprise attack with a bonus up to Obfuscate level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-22-2019, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:17:27-08:00","id":1290731,"title":"","content":"5. Nothing. If there are no other forms of perception at work (a moment on this point), then you have a perception check and/or attack penalty as if Blind.<br /> <br /> Personally if the Obfuscated vampire is known to be/have been at that spot I'd keep the penalties down to Blind. If the Obfuscee is actively relocating themselves then that's an Active Defense and will make them virtually impossible to hit. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind that there are ways to detect the presence of an Obfuscated vamp that do not rely on sight: you may note their changing footprints in the dust (or muck) on the ground. You may find their passage in swirling fog or smoke. You may detect squeaks and such as they cross the floor. Etc. <br /> <br /> Obfuscate only seems impenetrable--like Dominate or Auspex or any of the Disciplines--if you interpret it broadly. Keep things narrow and literal so you, as GM, have mental wiggle room to plan around the powers. That said, they are, indeed, powerful: the intent has been to make it easy for vampires to be inhuman and abusive, at a cost to their Humanity of course.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:46:35-08:00","id":1290880,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers guys.<br /> <br /> Well, I guess here we go again. There's another thing I'm wondering after reading through the VtR 2e book again:<br /> <br /> <br /> When a Strix enters a host, the Strix does not suffer from his own banes, nor does his host suffer his banes, which is why Strix inside a Kindred host can go outside during the day into the sun without any troubles.<br /> <br /> But does a host &quot;shell&quot; protect the Strix against all his banes, or only the 'common banes', or also against the 'uncommon banes'? Does a Strix with the Loner bane inside a vampire host still retreat when another Strix (also inside a host) comes nearby? Does a strix inside a human host still stop to count rice if he has the Counting bane?<br /> <br /> With the Abjuration bane it's quite explicit that the bane is still in effect even when the Strix is inside a host. But what about the other 'uncommon banes'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 02-22-2019, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:44:43-08:00","id":1290895,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24044_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24044\" data-vbnamecard=\"24044\">Ventrue Life</a> consider for the moment how you would go about telling if that shadowy owl-form was counting rice or not? I mean, realistically? Is it picking them up with its ?beak? and sorting them?<br /> <br /> It seems like a straightforward interpretation would hold that the shell inherits uncommon banes and only protects against against those inherent to the condition of being a Strix. Similarly if you want, you could inflict the shell's uncommon banes on the Strix inside: such as fleeing bells or unable to enter without invitation. It would annoy the Strix, of course, and that's good drama material to an otherwise overwhelming uber-foe.<br /> <br /> My 2 vitae for what it's worth.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T17:34:04-08:00","id":1290939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290880#post1290880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Strix enters a host, the Strix does not suffer from his own banes</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what &quot;The victim's banes are replaced entirely with those of the Strix&quot; means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T17:50:45-08:00","id":1290943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290939#post1290939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not what &quot;The victim's banes are replaced entirely with those of the Strix&quot; means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you serious? Literally in the same sentence:<br /> <br /> &quot;The victim's banes are replaced entirely with those of the Strix\u2014<b>and hiding within a corpse means the Strix isn\u2019t in contact with those banes.</b>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T18:02:30-08:00","id":1290946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290895#post1290895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> consider for the moment how you would go about telling if that shadowy owl-form was counting rice or not? I mean, realistically? Is it picking them up with its ?beak? and sorting them?</div> </div> </div> </div>By making a mental note of each counted rice grain? I'm pretty sure the fact that counting a pile of rice is difficult is entirely the point of that bane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290895#post1290895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like a straightforward interpretation would hold that the shell inherits uncommon banes and only protects against against those inherent to the condition of being a Strix. Similarly if you want, you could inflict the shell's uncommon banes on the Strix inside: such as fleeing bells or unable to enter without invitation. It would annoy the Strix, of course, and that's good drama material to an otherwise overwhelming uber-foe.<br /> <br /> My 2 vitae for what it's worth.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. I guess in hindsight I could have known before asking, given that the next section talks about humans mistakenly believing that vampires can't cross running water and have to count objects in disarray, and suggesting that this false belief might be based on human interactions with strix inside a vampire host.<br /> <br /> I already figured this would be the case. Oh well, at least now I know for sure.<br /> <br /> PS: I like your idea of the strix having to deal with the vampire's uncommon banes as well, but I'm not sure that makes sense. The whole reason a strix inside a vampire host doesn't burn in the sun is because the vampire's banes are <b><i>replaced</i></b> with the strix's banes when possessed by a strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T18:09:58-08:00","id":1290949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290943#post1290943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you serious? Literally in the same sentence:<br /> <br /> &quot;The victim's banes are replaced entirely with those of the Strix\u2014<b>and hiding within a corpse means the Strix isn\u2019t in contact with those banes.</b>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The instance I'm quoting from, meanwhile, is from <i>the mechanics of the first Embodiment that deals with vampires.</i> A point of reference which also specifies that <i>possessing a body means the host is the one who takes any damage a bane would do</i>.<br /> <br /> It would be <i>nonsensical</i> to specify that the host uses the Strix's banes if that meant a Strix in a meatsuit wasn't still subject to its usual behavioral compulsions and didn't have its few sources of material harm still be supernaturally enforced.<br /> <br /> The whole trouble with Embodied Strix is that the host forms an extra layer of Health in front of the Owl's Corpus, and the only forms of possession that don't clone the Strix's banes onto the host for the duration are fragile and/or time-limited without a pretty high-level Dread Power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-22-2019, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T18:19:20-08:00","id":1290952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290949#post1290949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The instance I'm quoting from, meanwhile, is from <i>the mechanics of the first Embodiment that deals with vampires.</i> A point of reference which also specifies that <i>possessing a body means the host is the one who takes any damage a bane would do</i>.<br /> <br /> It would be <i>nonsensical</i> to specify that the host uses the Strix's banes if that meant a Strix in a meatsuit wasn't still subject to its usual behavioral compulsions and didn't have its few sources of material harm still be supernaturally enforced.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not nonsensical at all, as it explains why a strix-possessed vampire can walk in the sun unharmed.<br /> <br /> The vampire who's possessed by a strix does not suffer his own banes, because his own banes are replaced by the strix's. Meanwhile, the strix inside the body doesn't suffer from his banes, because he's protected by the meat shell around him, as stated in the sentence I quoted. Which is why the strix isn't harmed by sunlight, and fire only lethally damages the strix's host body, even when that body is a vampire's. Hence my confusion, and question whether that means the strix is protected from <i>all</i> his banes or only his fire and sunlight banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T20:53:19-08:00","id":1290990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1290952#post1290952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hence my confusion, and question whether that means the strix is protected from <i>all</i> his banes or only his fire and sunlight banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>For which see &quot;vampiric hosts use the Strix's banes for the duration of the possession, nonvampiric hosts of Strix without Preservation decay over time or are more fragile and need the upkeep required of a living body, and the Strix being insulated from damage does not mean it doesn't still have the banes it has.&quot;<br /> <br /> Possess Corpse specifies that banes break through the body's &quot;everything deals bashing damage&quot; durability, and Possess Revenant and Possess Kindred are subject to the standard copy-over; you might make a case for Possess Living being an exception if not for the fact that, as you point out, there's a core Strix bane that specifically applies across host bodies even if that Embodiment didn't have a natural point at which it immediately switches to Possess Corpse.<br /> <br /> The context you brought up &quot;the Strix does not suffer from those banes&quot; in is pretty clearly about the Strix not <i>suffering damage from </i>those banes, given that the section you quoted from goes on is discussing Kindred hosts and frames the process that is usually carried out with fire as a generalized process of surrounding the host with the Strix's banes \u2014 it doesn't <i>not suffer those banes</i> just because it's insulated from direct contact with them any more than I stop being allergic to poison ivy just because I put on an NBC suit.<br /> <br /> Your question is pretty much inherently answered by the Banes section: &quot;Host bodies protect against <b>the damage and repulsion of the two great banes</b>&quot; and &quot;<b>It is repulsed from the bane as though it were sunlight, and if the material is used as a weapon against the Strix \u2014 even in Shadow Form \u2014 it deals lethal damage</b>&quot; does not in any way imply that wearing another body stops the Strix from exhibiting its more behavioral quirks even if there weren't fiction in the books where a character specifically leverages the counting compulsion of an embodied Strix against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T05:43:01-08:00","id":1292126,"title":"","content":"I'm having some difficulties with the effects of a homebrew devotion. I wish to create a Devotion that allows me to conserve my vitae potent after it leaves my body.<br /> It should be Resilience for the &quot;remain potent&quot; factor, or should it be Vigor, or should be both? And there is any way to understand this on the rules or it's just GM fiat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T05:54:29-08:00","id":1292128,"title":"","content":"GM fiat. I would make it a Scale or a Blood Sorcery Ritual, but if you want a Devotion I'd go with Resilience primary and maybe some Vigor as a secondary Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T05:57:09-08:00","id":1292129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292126#post1292126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having some difficulties with the effects of a homebrew devotion. I wish to create a Devotion that allows me to conserve my vitae potent after it leaves my body.<br /> It should be Resilience for the &quot;remain potent&quot; factor, or should it be Vigor, or should be both? And there is any way to understand this on the rules or it's just GM fiat?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go for just Resilence. Vigor gives power but vitae already has it. It just need to last longer.<br /> <br /> My very schematic view is:<br /> <br /> - Vigor gives concreteness, allow to apply something on others, ...<br /> - Resilence gives durability and allows something to last longer.<br /> - Celerity gives quickness (making something reflexive i.e.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-27-2019, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T06:11:52-08:00","id":1292132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292126#post1292126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having some difficulties with the effects of a homebrew devotion. I wish to create a Devotion that allows me to conserve my vitae potent after it leaves my body.<br /> It should be Resilience for the &quot;remain potent&quot; factor, or should it be Vigor, or should be both? And there is any way to understand this on the rules or it's just GM fiat?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd actually somehow tie the Devotion in to Blood Potency. Have it be a Devotion that requires both Vigor and Resilience, and have the duration of your Vitae's potency depend on the vampire's Blood Potency, for example, 1 hour per dot in Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> If anything, this sounds like something that belongs in Blood Sorcery territory. Have it be a Theban miracle, Cruac ritual or a Scale for Coil of the Ascendant.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Preserve the Vitae</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite Coil:</b> The Warm Face<br /> <b>Procedure:</b> The subject, who needs to be a vampire who knows how to use the Warm Face (Coil of the Ascendant \u2022\u2022), has to use blush of life before the start of the procedure. The vampire then hooks himself up to a device that can draw blood and store it. The vampire uses physical intensity to pump his blood through into a container, hard and fast. The amount of Vitae that can be used for physical intensity is limited by the vampire's Vitae/turn limit, as determined by his Blood Potency. The Vitae spent using physical intensity gets stored in the container used for this procedure. The vampire can then bleed additional Vitae into the container if he so desires. When the procedure is finished, the Vitae inside of the container will be preserved for a prolonged period of time.<br /> <b>Outcome:</b> The Vitae inside the container will remain potent for a number of hours equal to the Vitae spent through physical intensity. During this time, the contents of the container can be used for Cruac rituals or other blood sorcery that requires Vitae, or it can be fed to humans or vampires, with the normal consequences of doing so. Even when the blood inside the container is spilled or mixed with another liquid, the Vitae will remain potent.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are no hard rules on this, so anything goes. That's just how I would do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 02-26-2019, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T06:16:19-08:00","id":1292133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292126#post1292126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having some difficulties with the effects of a homebrew devotion. I wish to create a Devotion that allows me to conserve my vitae potent after it leaves my body.<br /> It should be Resilience for the &amp;quot;remain potent&amp;quot; factor, or should it be Vigor, or should be both? And there is any way to understand this on the rules or it's just GM fiat?</div> </div> </div> </div>For what purpose? So your character can consume it months or years later? So your character can take all night getting around to trapping someone in a vinculum or to make something like Lord of the Land or Oubliette last longer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T06:33:22-08:00","id":1292135,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for the quick answers, I have more than enough material to work on now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292133#post1292133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what purpose? So your character can consume it months or years later? So your character can take all night getting around to trapping someone in a vinculum or to make something like Lord of the Land or Oubliette last longer?</div> </div> </div> </div>To put it on barrels and do a fermentation process to make wine out of my Vitae and use it as a delicacy.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T07:20:58-08:00","id":1292153,"title":"","content":"Assuming it keeps the property of triggering an addiction but does not establish a vinculum, I'd make it a merit that uses willpower expenditure and has prerequisites of Crafts 3 with a specialization in wine distillation or beer brewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T07:52:24-08:00","id":1292161,"title":"","content":"I would make a Scale out of the whole process. Preserving Vitae through &quot;mundane&quot; transmutation into a beverage. Int+Crafts to perform the process. For each interval of time (months seem most fitting) after the process is finished the wine (or other beverage) loses one dot of Blood Potency (for purposes of Vitae Addiction and/or Vinculum resistance rolls, depending on which traits you wish to preserve) until at BP0 where it no longer provides Vitae.<br /> The interval can be dependent on how long the process takes. Longer fermentation increases the time before the Vitae degrades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-26-2019, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T03:49:34-08:00","id":1292433,"title":"","content":"It's sooo difficult to create a threat to even just one or two kindred with dominate 2 or Majesty. <br /> I.e. a driver of one of their was dominated 3 to crash against a police patrol as soon as they would have met one. <br /> It resulted in both of them spamming dominate and Majesty, not even on in a smart way, letting every agent (6) powerless, just spamming it every turn. <br /> Any suggestion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:13:21-08:00","id":1292489,"title":"","content":"Remember that Dominate 2 requires sustained eye contact, and at least three turns plus one Vitae per use\u2014plenty of time for the other agents to react. Awe doesn't stop people from being hostile toward you, it just removes penalties from social rolls, so it won't help you Social Maneuver against someone whose impression is already Hostile. Confidant similarly has to be used on each person one by one, leaving time for the others to react, and it resolves if the target makes a significant sacrifice for the vampire\u2014at which point the target, according to the book, feels tricked or ripped off. And because of Awe, they most definitely remember the vampire's face, and can radio in an APB.<br /> <br /> Dominate and Majesty are powerful, but they're not magic bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T08:22:40-08:00","id":1292493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292433#post1292433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's sooo difficult to create a threat to even just one or two kindred with dominate 2 or Majesty.<br /> I.e. a driver of one of their was dominated 3 to crash against a police patrol as soon as they would have met one.<br /> It resulted in both of them spamming dominate and Majesty, not even on in a smart way, letting every agent (6) powerless, just spamming it every turn.<br /> Any suggestion?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Dominate: Have them encounter more than one person at a time. It generally takes two instant actions to Dominate someone into not attacking you (one to inflict Mesmerized, one to issue the command) which is great when it's a one-on-one fight but extremely costly if you face multiple opponents. In a two-on-one fight it means you've taken 3-4 attacks before you've decommissioned the first of them.<br /> Also remember that Mesmerized resolves on any damage taken <i>and</i> if you take a breaking point as a part of the command. A breaking point for a mortal could be to stand idly by while their friend gets punched by a monster. In fact, experiencing anything overtly supernatural (being dominated is implicitly excepted) like the Gangrel coterie mate using Protean or anyone using inhuman amounts of strength is a breaking point for almost all mortals. Once Mesmerized is resolved they gain +3 to contest further Mesmerize attempts that scene meaning it's extremely difficult to spam it on the same person.<br /> <br /> For Majesty: Start the fight before any Majesty Conditions have been applied. Awe by itself is not great when the threat of violence is already present. It definitely helps the vampire to talk themselves out of a tight spot, but only if that options was already present. Just activating Awe doesn't create new opportunities. Charmed does present new options, but when already in a conflict they're limited, and in a violent conflict almost nonexistent (provided you've already applied Charmed as applying it requires a social interaction that I would disallow in a violent conflict). In your example a Charmed police officer might be persuaded to look the other way (and thus resolve Charmed one that's done) but that's something that still requires social manoeuvering. If there's six officers on the scene it'll be much more difficult as you need to persuade the whole group. It also takes a bunch of time to set it up as you need one instant action for Awe and then one instant action per officer to be Charmed. With Green Eyes you can basically skip the social manoeuvering, but that instead costs one Vitae per target (provided whatever you want them to do isn't a breaking point or they risk taking damage).<br /> <br /> Basically, ramp up how fast the conflict escalates to a fight. Dominate takes a bunch of time to apply and is sometimes only temporary (if they take a breaking point) while Majesty can basically not end a fight at all once it's broken out. Also, increase the number of opponents. It takes time per opponent before Dominate and Majesty (except Awe) has any effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:09:23-08:00","id":1292541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292489#post1292489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that Dominate 2 requires sustained eye contact, and at least three turns plus one Vitae per use\u2014plenty of time for the other agents to react. Awe doesn't stop people from being hostile toward you, it just removes penalties from social rolls, so it won't help you Social Maneuver against someone whose impression is already Hostile. Confidant similarly has to be used on each person one by one, leaving time for the others to react, and it resolves if the target makes a significant sacrifice for the vampire\u2014at which point the target, according to the book, feels tricked or ripped off. And because of Awe, they most definitely remember the vampire's face, and can radio in an APB.<br /> <br /> Dominate and Majesty are powerful, but they're not magic bullets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why you say 3 turns? It just need 1/2 turns. With the first turn you inflict mesmerized condition, and the mesmerized become quite and calm, in the second you can command for the whole scene without even looking at him. Furthermore it does not require sustained eye contact. It esplicitly says you need to cross the eyes of your target for just a moment in order to inflict the condition. Then you can control him with 4 words commands for the whole scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292493#post1292493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Dominate: Have them encounter more than one person at a time. It generally takes two instant actions to Dominate someone into not attacking you (one to inflict Mesmerized, one to issue the command) which is great when it's a one-on-one fight but extremely costly if you face multiple opponents. In a two-on-one fight it means you've taken 3-4 attacks before you've decommissioned the first of them.<br /> Also remember that Mesmerized resolves on any damage taken <i>and</i> if you take a breaking point as a part of the command. A breaking point for a mortal could be to stand idly by while their friend gets punched by a monster. In fact, experiencing anything overtly supernatural (being dominated is implicitly excepted) like the Gangrel coterie mate using Protean or anyone using inhuman amounts of strength is a breaking point for almost all mortals. Once Mesmerized is resolved they gain +3 to contest further Mesmerize attempts that scene meaning it's extremely difficult to spam it on the same person.<br /> <br /> For Majesty: Start the fight before any Majesty Conditions have been applied. Awe by itself is not great when the threat of violence is already present. It definitely helps the vampire to talk themselves out of a tight spot, but only if that options was already present. Just activating Awe doesn't create new opportunities. Charmed does present new options, but when already in a conflict they're limited, and in a violent conflict almost nonexistent (provided you've already applied Charmed as applying it requires a social interaction that I would disallow in a violent conflict). In your example a Charmed police officer might be persuaded to look the other way (and thus resolve Charmed one that's done) but that's something that still requires social manoeuvering. If there's six officers on the scene it'll be much more difficult as you need to persuade the whole group. It also takes a bunch of time to set it up as you need one instant action for Awe and then one instant action per officer to be Charmed. With Green Eyes you can basically skip the social manoeuvering, but that instead costs one Vitae per target (provided whatever you want them to do isn't a breaking point or they risk taking damage).<br /> <br /> Basically, ramp up how fast the conflict escalates to a fight. Dominate takes a bunch of time to apply and is sometimes only temporary (if they take a breaking point) while Majesty can basically not end a fight at all once it's broken out. Also, increase the number of opponents. It takes time per opponent before Dominate and Majesty (except Awe) has any effect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks Tessie, they are good advices but the point was a bit different since the agents wouldn't open fire so easily.<br /> Imagine the scene: The car crash against their, they would be surely on guard but there could have been several reason for the crash: Sickness, losing the control, drugged driver and so on.<br /> <br /> My main intention would just to give them some triouble to deal with, using a nice effect of dominate. But what's happened was instead, agents on guard and PCs mesmerizing, charming them one by one. Since they are mortal (I don't want to put anytime supernaturals or ghouls or mortals aware about supernaturals. I want supernaturals to be something rare and horrorific so I can't abuse about such creatures) they saw every mate of theri to behave in a very weird and horrorifc way: gants changing attitude in seconds. But still it's not enough to let them yell: Mooonster, opening the fire.<br /> I was dreaming about corruption maybe, or a funny chases, but nothing has happened, just a boring Dominate/Majesty spam <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:40:41-08:00","id":1292553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292541#post1292541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why you say 3 turns? It just need 1/2 turns. With the first turn you inflict mesmerized condition, and the mesmerized become quite and calm, in the second you can command for the whole scene without even looking at him. Furthermore it does not require sustained eye contact. It esplicitly says you need to cross the eyes of your target for just a moment in order to inflict the condition. Then you can control him with 4 words commands for the whole scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Dominate 2 specifically you need an instant action to inflict Mesmerized, an instant action to control them, then one to two turns per sentence to give commands. Dom 1 is faster but also less flexible.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, this thread is glitching out heavily for me, I think because we've crossed some threshold of &quot;too many responses&quot;. Would people object to making a new one and linking it back to this one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T12:00:28-08:00","id":1292559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292541#post1292541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why you say 3 turns? It just need 1/2 turns.</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes three turns to actually use Iron Edict (which is what Draconis specifically talked about). One turn to apply Mesmerized, a second turn to activate Iron Edict, and at least a third turn to issue the command. The Exceptional Success bonus for Mesmerize only applies on the same turn which is before you've activated Iron Edict. If you do get an Exceptional on Mesmerize you could still issue a basic command without spending an extra turn.<br /> Also, Iron Edict must be reactivated for additional commands unless you bake everything into a single command that takes many turns to issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292541#post1292541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Tessie, they are good advices but the point was a bit different since the agents wouldn't open fire so easily.<br /> Imagine the scene: The car crash against their, they would be surely on guard but there could have been several reason for the crash: Sickness, losing the control, drugged driver and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got it. My advice was for future encounters. Dominate and Majesty has limits so if you don't want them to be an auto-solve button you'll have to have these limits in mind when designing encounters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292541#post1292541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since they are mortal [..] they saw every mate of theri to behave in a very weird and horrorifc way: gants changing attitude in seconds. But still it's not enough to let them yell: Mooonster, opening the fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, seems like it would cause at least one of them to face a breaking point and thus snap out of it with increased resistance to further Dominate commands. The officer doesn't have to open fire, but it's certainly a complication that is now difficult to fix with Dominate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292541#post1292541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was dreaming about corruption maybe, or a funny chases, but nothing has happened, just a boring Dominate/Majesty spam <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You could've had the driver cause additional complications. From their perspective they've just blacked out a little between the moment they saw the cop car and they crashed into said car. They should be confused and can act in ways that appear irrational or influenced by the police, if they don't outright panic and try to drive away. Whatever the driver does the PCs wouldn't have time to influence them with Disciplines, and if the driver drives away with the PCs, they become accomplishes in the police's eyes, causing complications for both Dominate (as it's difficult to get eye contact with someone who's about to cuff you) and Majesty (that just isn't particularly effective in this situation).<br /> <br /> And remember to also include social manoeuvering when the PCs use Majesty. Charmed would only make it easier to persuade the officers. A high social character can often do the same things that a character with Majesty 1+2 can do. Would you have been as disappointed if it was a high social character who defused the situation through mundane means?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T12:30:32-08:00","id":1292570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1292559#post1292559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It takes three turns to actually use Iron Edict (which is what Draconis specifically talked about). One turn to apply Mesmerized, a second turn to activate Iron Edict, and at least a third turn to issue the command. The Exceptional Success bonus for Mesmerize only applies on the same turn which is before you've activated Iron Edict. If you do get an Exceptional on Mesmerize you could still issue a basic command without spending an extra turn.<br /> Also, Iron Edict must be reactivated for additional commands unless you bake everything into a single command that takes many turns to issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I got it. My advice was for future encounters. Dominate and Majesty has limits so if you don't want them to be an auto-solve button you'll have to have these limits in mind when designing encounters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I dunno, seems like it would cause at least one of them to face a breaking point and thus snap out of it with increased resistance to further Dominate commands. The officer doesn't have to open fire, but it's certainly a complication that is now difficult to fix with Dominate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You could've had the driver cause additional complications. From their perspective they've just blacked out a little between the moment they saw the cop car and they crashed into said car. They should be confused and can act in ways that appear irrational or influenced by the police, if they don't outright panic and try to drive away. Whatever the driver does the PCs wouldn't have time to influence them with Disciplines, and if the driver drives away with the PCs, they become accomplishes in the police's eyes, causing complications for both Dominate (as it's difficult to get eye contact with someone who's about to cuff you) and Majesty (that just isn't particularly effective in this situation).<br /> <br /> And remember to also include social manoeuvering when the PCs use Majesty. Charmed would only make it easier to persuade the officers. A high social character can often do the same things that a character with Majesty 1+2 can do. Would you have been as disappointed if it was a high social character who defused the situation through mundane means?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes I got it now. I've always considered activating Iron edict and talk the command the same action. It was a oversight of mine. Well I guess Dominate 1 would be fine enough in this situation anyway. Furthermore there's an example in the power text that suggest you are able to give commands for the whole night: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cObey my direct instructions when I give them to you,\u201d which effectively gives them control over the minion until the sun comes up </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> I will keep your advices in mind for next encounters anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T18:26:34-08:00","id":1292669,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone. I'm currently looking through some of the books for a bit of information I remember reading but can't quite place.<br /> <br /> It was talking about various clans and how their princes tend to be. Mentioning the most and least common title holders ect. If anyone could help me find that I'd appreciate it. I'm currently looking through Damnation City but I'm not sure if it is in there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24063-admiral-cheesecake","name":"Admiral Cheesecake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T03:45:24-08:00","id":1292724,"title":"","content":"Damnation City has several examples of how the domain of a certain clan/covenant combination prince may look, the respective clanbooks have a few examples of their type holding different city posts. The covenant books all also feature examples of different clan and covenant and/or city posts. The clan and covenant books are first edition though and many of the covenant posts don\u2019t exist or are radically different in 2nd edition, specifically in Invictus and the Ordo Dracul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T09:17:02-08:00","id":1293058,"title":"","content":"Can you take a bane for the breaking points of Diablerie or Embracing since they are automatic humanity losses? I know for sure you probably can't with diablerie, but I've heard mixed things about the embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T09:27:51-08:00","id":1293061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1293058#post1293058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you take a bane for the breaking points of Diablerie or Embracing since they are automatic humanity losses? I know for sure you probably can't with diablerie, but I've heard mixed things about the embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. The Embrace isn't a breaking point, it's a straight 1 dot lose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T10:24:46-08:00","id":1293080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1293061#post1293061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think so. The Embrace isn't a breaking point, it's a straight 1 dot lose.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe a scale with a requiste from the Mystery of the Voivode to be researched? If you can Mass Embrace with only a single humanity loss - there maybe is a way to embrace a single time with no humanity loss? I don't know - maybe for the cost of two banes. LOL","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T10:25:59-08:00","id":1293081,"title":"","content":"One of the tiers of Voivode (The Vast Dynasty) turns the Embrace into a breaking point, which you can take a bane for.<br /> <br /> Diablerie is technically a breaking point now, but the devs have said that was a mistake, it's supposed to be an un-bane-able loss like the Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T10:32:12-08:00","id":1293083,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> - Credit to <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Vasilios.Baggeas\" target=\"_blank\">Vasilios Baggeas</a></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Bloods Groomed Scion </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Prerequisite: The Vast Family </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Procedure: First the Dragon must ensure that the subject is suffering from either the Enslaved, Enthralled or similar such persistent Condition although the Dragon need not be the one to inflict said Condition. The subject of this procedure must then be subjected to a third level blood bond to the Dragon with the third taste of Vitae being laced with a socially prepared alchemical mixture. After all of the above criteria have been meet the Dragon may drain the subject of their Blood. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Outcome: the Dragon spends a point of Willpower and the subject will arise as a newly Embraced Vampire.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T11:56:52-08:00","id":1293107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1293081#post1293081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the tiers of Voivode (The Vast Dynasty) turns the Embrace into a breaking point, which you can take a bane for.<br /> <br /> Diablerie is technically a breaking point now, but the devs have said that was a mistake, it's supposed to be an un-bane-able loss like the Embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not automatic loss. It's &quot;only&quot; a breaking point that you can't take a Bane for. As it says in the core book, it's <i>always</i> a breaking point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T12:53:56-08:00","id":1293119,"title":"","content":"Okay I see if you get 5 dots in Mystery of the Voivode and get Vast Dynasty embracing then is no longer automatic AND then you can take a bane for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:31:41-08:00","id":1293794,"title":"","content":"Good evening! Please remind me, can you poison a vampire?<br /> I remember that they can be carriers of diseases. Also the poison gas will not work on them, since they do not breathe. But what about contact poisons? I remember that they have no metabolism in the conventional sense of the word. But what becomes of vitae, into which poison falls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:35:20-08:00","id":1293797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1293794#post1293794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good evening! Please remind me, can you poison a vampire?<br /> I remember that they can be carriers of diseases. Also the poison gas will not work on them, since they do not breathe. But what about contact poisons? I remember that they have no metabolism in the conventional sense of the word. But what becomes of vitae, into which poison falls?</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves you can't poison a Vampire. The only way drugs can affect him is letting the vamp drink from a drugged man","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T09:40:31-08:00","id":1293801,"title":"","content":"Poisons can't damage a vampire unless it physically destroys blood or the vampire's body, like corrosives or certain snake venoms that coagulate blood.<br /> Poisons that have entered the vampire's body would probably remain until the Cleansing (with a slight possibility of being naturally cleansed before that if the vampire uses Blush of Health to restore body functions). If the poison has entered the vampire's Vitae (probably from drinking from a poisoned vessel) feeding it to mortals can possibly affect them, but only if the vampire managed to ingest enough of the substance. The original vessel would already have diluted the poison once in most cases, making it unlikely that anyone would get poisoned further down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T12:47:00-08:00","id":1293858,"title":"","content":"Note that this all applies only to <i>mundane</i> poisons: I wouldn't be surprised if a Dragon somewhere has made a Vitae-based alchemical mixture that &quot;poisons&quot; vampires.<br /> <br /> But if you're drinking wine with cyanide in it, yeah, that won't affect you. The body functions that poisons disrupt just don't really matter to you any more. It's the same reason you can shrug off injuries that would kill humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T13:39:00-08:00","id":1293878,"title":"","content":"If memory serves hurt locker has some expanded rules on posioning vampires, but outside of that I remember some poison mentioned in secrets of the covenants that functions as a hemotoxin under one of the sanctum's rituals that lets them summon a snake. So outside of hurt locker rules, if the poison isn't a hemotoxin or corrosive like Tessie said, I'd rule it as mundane poisons not really affecting vampires. There are a few supernatural poisons out there, so might want to keep an eye out in the books for those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T02:00:50-08:00","id":1293987,"title":"","content":"Poison rules are in the Rules FAQ, stickied to this forum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Poisons not specifically harmful to Kindred follow the same rules as drugs. A Storyteller may choose to make an exception for poisons which break down cellular structure, but that\u2019s at her own discretion.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T15:58:48-08:00","id":1294522,"title":"","content":"The book states that witnessing something terryfing is a breaking point for a mortal. Does it imply that a mortal who has been dominated, witnessing a vampire biting someone else, would resolve the condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T16:28:42-08:00","id":1294531,"title":"","content":"It absolutely could. Witnessing the supernatural in general can be a breaking point for a mortal, and seeing a vampire biting into someone's neck and drinking their blood counts as supernatural. (Which is why it's best to feed where nobody can see you too closely\u2026)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T13:53:58-08:00","id":1294872,"title":"","content":"When/how do newly-turned vampires get their first Touchstone? Do they start out lacking one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T14:02:19-08:00","id":1294877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1294872#post1294872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When/how do newly-turned vampires get their first Touchstone? Do they start out lacking one?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They start with one touchstone as part of character creation. Usually something from their past or a strong link to their humanity.<br /> <br /> I ran a Dark Ages style game and one of the vampires had a table as his touch stone in the Inn/Tavern he owned. So every time a brawl broke out he was concerned for it. When he would spend time with it he would entertain guests at his personal table in the center of the room, or sit and brood or sulk from the days events.<br /> <br /> It was a lot of fun. Inanimate object are harder for the ST but with a little thought you can make them interesting and present.<br /> <br /> I have seen wife, mom, mom with cancer (spending time considering ghouling to stop the spread), friend, enemy, girlfriend, lover, movie theater, street urchins (general), touchstone and the variety is almost a thread worth creating on its own.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T17:37:04-08:00","id":1294932,"title":"","content":"With the Body of Will Devotion, the dice pool is Stamina + Survival + Resilience.<br /> <br /> In most circumstances, Resilience adds to your Stamina score.<br /> Does this mean you effectively add your Resilience to the dice pool twice?<br /> <br /> If my character has Stamina 3 (unmodified), Survival 2 and Resilience 3, does that mean my dice bool becomes 6 + 2 + 3 = 11?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T17:56:40-08:00","id":1294934,"title":"","content":"Is it worth getting the 1e clan books and covenant books to use for 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T18:59:16-08:00","id":1294949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1294934#post1294934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it worth getting the 1e clan books and covenant books to use for 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, yes. Flavor-wise I enjoyed them a lot more than <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i> and found them more useful. (Though be warned, some are better quality than others.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T14:56:58-08:00","id":1295395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1294932#post1294932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Body of Will Devotion, the dice pool is Stamina + Survival + Resilience.<br /> <br /> In most circumstances, Resilience adds to your Stamina score.<br /> Does this mean you effectively add your Resilience to the dice pool twice?<br /> <br /> If my character has Stamina 3 (unmodified), Survival 2 and Resilience 3, does that mean my dice bool becomes 6 + 2 + 3 = 11?</div> </div> </div> </div>No other Discipline or Devotion adds the Discipline dots twice so I would highly doubt if it were the intention for this one. More likely is that the author overlooked how Resilience interacts with Stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T19:10:53-08:00","id":1295438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1295395#post1295395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No other Discipline or Devotion adds the Discipline dots twice so I would highly doubt if it were the intention for this one. More likely is that the author overlooked how Resilience interacts with Stamina.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, but what if the roll was... for the sake of making my point... say... Stamina + Survival + Vigor. And lets say my character still has Resilience 3 and Stamina 3 (unmodified, modified with Resilience it becomes 6). Survival is still 2, and Vigor is also 3. Would my dice pool be 6 + 2 + 3 = 11?<br /> Or 3 + 2 + 3 = 8?<br /> <br /> If in this case it's 6 + 2 + 3 = 11 (which is what I'd assume, there is no reason to believe Resilience doesn't add to Stamina in this case) then shouldn't the Stamina + Survival + Resilience roll not also be 6 + 2 + 3 = 11?<br /> <br /> I guess I just answered my own question... but I still want to hear other people's opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T01:33:22-08:00","id":1295526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1295438#post1295438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True, but what if the roll was... for the sake of making my point... say... Stamina + Survival + Vigor. And lets say my character still has Resilience 3 and Stamina 3 (unmodified, modified with Resilience it becomes 6). Survival is still 2, and Vigor is also 3. Would my dice pool be 6 + 2 + 3 = 11?<br /> Or 3 + 2 + 3 = 8?<br /> <br /> If in this case it's 6 + 2 + 3 = 11 (which is what I'd assume, there is no reason to believe Resilience doesn't add to Stamina in this case) then shouldn't the Stamina + Survival + Resilience roll not also be 6 + 2 + 3 = 11?<br /> <br /> I guess I just answered my own question... but I still want to hear other people's opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case I'd go for stamina 6, yes. Discipline states: it adds Resilence to Stamina. With no limitation specified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T19:39:49-07:00","id":1295720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1294932#post1294932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Body of Will Devotion, the dice pool is Stamina + Survival + Resilience.<br /> <br /> In most circumstances, Resilience adds to your Stamina score.<br /> Does this mean you effectively add your Resilience to the dice pool twice?<br /> <br /> If my character has Stamina 3 (unmodified), Survival 2 and Resilience 3, does that mean my dice bool becomes 6 + 2 + 3 = 11?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my house rules is that no stat, skill, power, etc, adds in twice unless it calls out with 100% clarity. As you explore mechanics in most RPGs they usually do not want mods added twice and you can compare the fails/success percentages. Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T07:33:28-07:00","id":1296125,"title":"","content":"Question about central nervous system damage: In the case of a broken neck or brain injury -- do you impose the normal nervous system effects?<br /> <br /> So with a broken neck, is the character paralyzed? If they're shot in the head, to you take away coginitive function? <br /> <br /> My impulse is to say yes, unless they've got Resilience going, impose wound penalties. But then there's a problem for posthumus embraces (if you died by bullet to the head, daysleep should give you the wound each day).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T08:43:14-07:00","id":1296143,"title":"","content":"Are you asking in regards to vampires? No, I don't usually assign penalties to vampires from damage to their central nervous system. If they're shot in the eye, they may not see out of that eye until the damage is healed but no, vampires don't immediately fall comatose from a bullet to the brain. If their neck is broken, they may feel themself go numb if their Humanity is high enough or have skewed visual and auditory perceptions momentarily but it's not sufficient for them to suffer any penalties or be able to ignore wound penalties since we're obviously talking about extensive damage. (Such scenarios are potential breaking points.) An advantage of being undead is that they don't need those organs and biological systems to function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T08:45:01-07:00","id":1296145,"title":"","content":"For vampires, I say no. Vampires don't use their nervous system to control muscles. The structural damage (i.e. bones and muscles) are far more important since they are used mechanically.<br /> (Also, a broken neck does not automatically mean a severed spinal cord.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-12T10:34:29-07:00","id":1296175,"title":"","content":"No, a bullet into the brain shouldn't let them go comatose. Their brains are already dead and with no electrical signals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T01:33:02-07:00","id":1297904,"title":"","content":"Greetings and Salutations.<br /> <br /> All the rituals in Theban and cruac have a set duration and/or a component that gets &quot;consumed&quot; except <br /> <br /> Donning the Beast\u2019s Flesh (\u2022\u2022\u2022, Transmutation \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Target Successes: 7<br /> Donning the Beast\u2019s Flesh allows the Acolyte to skin a beast,<br /> and craft a mystical hood, cloak, mask, or another article of<br /> clothing from its flesh. When any vampire dons the accessory,<br /> he can take the rough shape of the animal with the expenditure<br /> of a point of Vitae and three turns of transformation. The<br /> animal is a vague approximation, but imperfect in unnatural<br /> ways to a trained observer.<br /> Unlike the transformations granted by Protean, the vampire loses<br /> access to all his Disciplines save for Auspex in the beast\u2019s shape<br /> <br /> The way it is written it implies that once the item is made from the animal the recipient can use it unlimited times as long as he spends a point of vitae and three turns.. Do people think that it was intended from the developers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T03:36:07-07:00","id":1297914,"title":"","content":"Normally the items crafted/augmented via Theban Sorcery or Cruac are only useable by the caster unless the ritual designates otherwise. By my reading of it. I would say this is one of those cases that others can use it as well and the skin is destroyed after one use.<br /> <br /> I can see an argument either way about allowing the skin to be used multiple times so I'd say it's up to the ST, but I personally wouldn't allow it. The lack of a Durability rating or even the requirement of the use of a relevant skill to skin a hide or fashion clothing implies a one time use and being able to hang up an infinite number of skins in your closet to pull out later makes it functionally superior to Protean, which is extremely limited and takes longer to implement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T09:47:10-07:00","id":1297986,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the blood sorcery item still be bound by the duration factor. Oh I just realized, the factors come from 1st edition Blood &amp; Sorcery, with the second edition sidebar or note. So no permanent rituals. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T12:03:24-07:00","id":1298018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1297986#post1297986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the blood sorcery item still be bound by the duration factor. Oh I just realized, the factors come from 1st edition Blood &amp; Sorcery, with the second edition sidebar or note. So no permanent rituals.<br /> <br /> Best regards</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To which sidebar you are refering to ?<br /> The way everything is worded the effect immediatelly takes place. In all other rituals there is explicit mention for either component braking down or duration<br /> <br /> Maybe its an omission i find hard to believe that the Devs wanted a permanent item giving a rank 3 power .<br /> <br /> Thanks for all answers though much appreciated. Keep them coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T14:07:59-07:00","id":1298036,"title":"","content":"In either the Blood Sorcery book or VTR2 IT (2nd edition) mentions using the Blood Sorcery book but with a small exception and forgive me my books are not with me. But my point is in the Blood Sorcery book they point out several things blood sorcery can't do like deal with other planes, produce banes (fire), and I think make something permanent.<br /> <br /> So for example when you make a vitae reliqury or blood scourge they both must have a duration, based on the Duration factor you selected. <br /> <br /> Found it... <br /> <br /> Vampire the Requiem 2e pg151<br /> <br /> Inventing new Rituals<br /> The supplement Blood Sorcery: Sacraments<br /> and Blasphemies provides a detailed system for<br /> improvising new rites and miracles, in which<br /> characters gain dots in ritual Themes as they<br /> progress in the Ritual Disciplines. If you\u2019re using that system, refer to that book for when new Theme dots are gained and how to calculate the target number of successes and dice pool for improvised rituals, except for the time taken per roll. The ritual extended action here replaces the one in that book.<br /> <br /> Page 27 Blood Sorcery - Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies<br /> <br /> The Limitations of Blood Sorcery<br /> <br /> Blood has its limits. There are some goals that the Ritual Disciplines can\u2019t achieve no matter how dedicated the sorcerer is. Both Ritual Disciplines harness the nature of vampires, and they are limited by that nature.<br /> <br /> No ritual may summon or destroy banes: Fire and sunlight remain inviolate despite rumors of Sanctified miracles causing the covenant\u2019s enemies to combust. And no ritual may completely ward off banes.<br /> <br /> Blood sorcery has no analogue to the \u201ccounter-magic\u201d found in the ritual magics of some supernatural creatures. Once a ritual has been successfully cast, it can\u2019t be \u201cdispelled\u201d by the powers available to the Kindred.<br /> <br /> Blood sorcery can produce flashes of oracular insight, but not the granting of new magical senses\u2014that\u2019s the province of the Auspex Discipline.<br /> <br /> The effects of blood sorcery can\u2019t be made permanent. Rituals may have their Duration factor extended for months, but eventually, the power will wear off.<br /> <br /> Blood sorcery can\u2019t access other realms of existence\u2014it deals with the world as vampires know it, not any of the strange spiritual realms spoken of in the lore of other supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 03-19-2019, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T15:12:15-07:00","id":1298053,"title":"","content":"Note that the sidebar says &quot;If you're using that system.&quot; By default, in 2e, you're not. Yeah, they based the -core- rituals off those rules, but the Secrets of the Covenants ones are kinda their own thing (the Theme addon to the rituals was shoe horned and does not match up to the books). As written, that ritual makes a permanent item that any Vampire can use, yes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T16:13:54-07:00","id":1298065,"title":"","content":"For the most part I agree with you. Especially when you look at the release schedule. Shows where the direction was going. <br /> <br /> 2012 Blood Sorceries 1e<br /> (almost like a Mage Light ritual system) <br /> 2014 Vampire the Requiem 2e<br /> 2016 secret of the covenets 2e<br /> <br /> I do find it interesting that secrets if memory serves me used the themes listed with each ritual. Maybe for backwards compatibility.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T07:17:56-07:00","id":1298136,"title":"","content":"Edit: responded to wrong post....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 03-20-2019, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T07:28:28-07:00","id":1298321,"title":"","content":"How do you properly pronounce <i>Weihan Cynn</i>? I'm not sure what language it's from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T08:01:43-07:00","id":1298329,"title":"","content":"Why In Sin. Slight emphasis on the second syllable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T09:44:01-07:00","id":1298350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1298329#post1298329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why In Sin. Slight emphasis on the second syllable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correction.<br /> <br /> It's a hard &quot;K&quot; sound and shows up in Anglo-Saxon in various places. One meaning is &quot;kind&quot;. Think of it as the English word &quot;kin&quot; (as in kinfolk) or &quot;race&quot; as in people. This is not the only possibility however, as the position and extra 'n' looks like it is the adjective 'cyn' (akin, suitable, fit, proper). There are obvious similarities between the two uses, but they are not exactly analogous to our English usage.<br /> <br /> You can use the soft 's' sound if you're Korean and latinizing your name Shin, however. I don't think given the context that's what the source for CofD is, though.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T11:55:48-07:00","id":1299009,"title":"","content":"I believe they do but just checking. Revenants can select banes to help bolster against humanity loss, correct? Just like Kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25183-reslin","name":"Reslin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25183_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T12:22:20-07:00","id":1299014,"title":"","content":"Yes. They can take up to three different banes to stymie Humanity loss under the same requirements as a full kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T13:28:30-07:00","id":1299025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1299014#post1299014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. They can take up to three different banes to stymie Humanity loss under the same requirements as a full kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25183-reslin","name":"Reslin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25183_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T16:01:07-07:00","id":1300695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1298350#post1298350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correction.<br /> <br /> It's a hard &quot;K&quot; sound and shows up in Anglo-Saxon in various places. One meaning is &quot;kind&quot;. Think of it as the English word &quot;kin&quot; (as in kinfolk) or &quot;race&quot; as in people. This is not the only possibility however, as the position and extra 'n' looks like it is the adjective 'cyn' (akin, suitable, fit, proper). There are obvious similarities between the two uses, but they are not exactly analogous to our English usage.<br /> <br /> You can use the soft 's' sound if you're Korean and latinizing your name Shin, however. I don't think given the context that's what the source for CofD is, though.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha, I believe you're correct! I found <i>cynn</i> in an Old English lexicon meaning &quot;tribe, people, grouping&quot; (pronounced /kyn:/ in IPA, or like &quot;kin&quot; with the German <i>\u00fc</i> vowel and a long <i>n</i>). Still no sign of the first word, alas\u2026I'll keep searching through my Germanic dictionaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T16:39:34-07:00","id":1300701,"title":"","content":"Ooh, might have found it: <i>\u01bf\u01e3\u0121an</i> is the genitive singular of <i>\u01bf\u01e3\u0121e</i>, &quot;scales, balance&quot;. So <i>\u01bf\u01e3\u0121an cynn</i> is &quot;the tribe/faction of the scales/balance&quot;, pronounced approximately &quot;WAY-ahn KEEN&quot;. (IPA, /'w\u00e6j.an 'kyn:/)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T16:34:17-07:00","id":1300976,"title":"","content":"AUSPEX 1: Does it allows to see obfuscated vampire (succeding the clash of wills) passively, or it has to be an active question, so that it would just be possible on activation as per: &quot;Is there a vampire using Auspex 5 here&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T17:07:52-07:00","id":1300981,"title":"","content":"Auspex only ever reveals Obfuscate via Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> When the goal of Auspex (give the vampire accurate information) conflicts with the goal of Obfuscate (remain hidden), there is a Clash of Wills to determine which goal is achieved. Same as any conflict between Disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T17:34:02-07:00","id":1300984,"title":"","content":"That said, I'd say &quot;is there an Obfuscated vampire here?&quot; is a valid Auspex 1 question, since it would reveal any other predators hiding from you (something in the Beast's interests). At that point, if there <i>is</i> an Obfuscated vampire there, you Clash to see if Auspex reveals them or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T13:53:38-07:00","id":1301142,"title":"","content":"Does 1st edition supplements, generally, keep up with 2nd edition, or are they to be discarded if changing edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T14:43:59-07:00","id":1301152,"title":"","content":"Honestly, hit and miss. Rule of thumb, the later the book was published, the more useful it is in 2nd edition. Mechanically you'd still have to translate things over though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T15:15:49-07:00","id":1301161,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there are some mechanics that need updating: in general, if a mechanic doesn't feel balanced, ask here and someone's probably converted it.<br /> <br /> For the flavor, on the other hand, and all the ST tools like Damnation City, those are totally usable. The clanbooks, covenant books, settings, and so on are wonderfully useful in either edition. You'll even see the 2e books citing earlier material, like <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i> trying to be backward-compatible with <i>Sacraments and Blasphemies</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T12:26:28-07:00","id":1301369,"title":"","content":"There's still some flavour parts that are no longer applicable. Anything relating to Predatory Aura is changed, as is dealing with Torpor. Just keep in mind how everything works in the new books as you read, and if something makes you go &quot;wait that doesn't make sense&quot;, assume that the newer books take precedence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T15:00:51-07:00","id":1302350,"title":"","content":"I will be the ST for a game soon. Just a few refresher questions.<br /> <br /> 1) Is the Social Combat Mechanic and the Debate Mechanic from DM and RfR respectively still usable in 2nd edition? My intent is to use Social Maneuvers for one-way social endeavors, social combat for spirited exchanges where both participants have goals, and debate for spreading ideas and wooing crowds. (effectively, SM for one-way one-on-one, SC for two-way one-on-one, and DB for two-way one-to-many. Extended actions/modified SM/merits would be used for one-way one-to-many.)<br /> <br /> 2) Is there any agreement as to what 'cities' belong to who? I can't place why but I think I remember Rome as being a Vampire puppet city and the British Empire being a Mage experiment. Interested as I might do a 'from prehistory to modern night and beyond' game.<br /> <br /> 3) Did we ever fix the Venture bane? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T17:57:47-07:00","id":1302387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302350#post1302350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Did we ever fix the Venture bane? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>'s'not broken. :P<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, the Aloof Curse does its job by exerting pressure on characters who've manifested it to either be extremely careful about the ways they interact with the living (and how lucky, then, that developing the Ventrue's signature Discipline makes it very easy to avoid troublesome encounters!) or desensitize themselves down to a level of Humanity that they can function at.<br /> <br /> The ability to offset the downside by buying extra dots in the Touchstone Merit doesn't change the fact that the social penalties for lower Humanity still apply to Touchstones and Lords still have to scrabble for meaningful connection that much sooner \u2014 the clan banes are there as ways to tilt the narrative around a character of that clan, not just to serve as flatly punitive measures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T17:58:15-07:00","id":1302388,"title":"","content":"1. Yes. But they don't impose &quot;Conditions&quot; by default if you're doing that with the Social maneuvers<br /> <br /> 2. No. Personally, I don't care what's in another supernatural group's accessory books. If I want to run a chronicle where Changeling courts have always controlled Rome, I'll do it and have no qualms about telling anyone who think they can dictate that I have to incorporate a kindred population and hierarchy that they can take a flying leap.<br /> <br /> 3. No. The fact that the Mekhet clan still don't get a real weakness remains a running gag. (I fixed your spelling error for you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T18:33:04-07:00","id":1302401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302387#post1302387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'s'not broken. :P<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, the Aloof Curse does its job by exerting pressure on characters who've manifested it to either be extremely careful about the ways they interact with the living (and how lucky, then, that developing the Ventrue's signature Discipline makes it very easy to avoid troublesome encounters!) or desensitize themselves down to a level of Humanity that they can function at.<br /> <br /> The ability to offset the downside by buying extra dots in the Touchstone Merit doesn't change the fact that the social penalties for lower Humanity still apply to Touchstones and Lords still have to scrabble for meaningful connection that much sooner \u2014 the clan banes are there as ways to tilt the narrative around a character of that clan, not just to serve as flatly punitive measures.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be the first I've seen to defend it. :P<br /> <br /> I am looking over my notes from a prior life (it feels like ages since I've played) and it would seem I was working on an alternative to the bane that would make the Venture less 'haughty lord' and more 'dedicated advisor.' I remember the clan book saying the Venture started as house gods, immortal advisers that would guide the family. I felt their bane should be two-fold. First, they treat their touchstones as if the touchstone was their regent in a level 3 blood bond. Second, any encounter (mandatory downtown meeting per month if not roleplayed) would roll humanity and on a failure, the venture would emerge tasked with a goal, as per the condition Tasked.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, or should I start a trend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T18:33:54-07:00","id":1302402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302388#post1302388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. No. The fact that the Mekhet clan still don't get a real weakness remains a running gag. (I fixed your spelling error for you.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Dyslexic, what can you do. :P<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T21:50:25-07:00","id":1302461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302401#post1302401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts, or should I start a trend?</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about the Ventrue's relationship with their clan bane is that it's primarily an accelerator pedal toward all the weird shit that elders get up to; to compare it to its relevant neighbors:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Losing dice on interactions with Touchstones as part of the larger process of losing dice on interactions with humans incentivizes the Ventrue to anchor their wakeful nights through non-living Touchstones \u2014 they're Aloof, not Lonely, and so lack the exemption that the Nosferatu receive enabling them to treat their living Touchstones as things of particular solace. A Lord can more readily justify keeping the threat of torpor away by simple virtue of having less personable Touchstones that don't require them to put in social appearances while they conduct their affairs.<br /> \u2022 By a similar line of thinking, the Ventrue's relation to the uncommon banes is not as intrinsic as it is for the Mekhet, and their strangeness is hidden through distance instead of directed secrecy \u2014 the developed curses of an elder Lord are less intense than those of an ancient Shadow, but where the Tenebrous Curse is there to give the Mekhet weaknesses to hide, the Aloof Curse is there to give the Ventrue peculiarities to separate them from their more human peers (and speed their descent besides). The Mekhet are weird because they're more keyed into the mystical flaws in the vampiric condition, but the Ventrue are weird because they find it <i>really easy</i> to stop caring about having a human perspective and retreat to an unlifestyle where they don't take many visitors.<br /> <br /> The common comparison of the Ventrue to spiders is salient here.<br /> <br /> (On a separate note from the matter of relative states, this also means that Ventrue characters have the prospect of avoiding Conditions brought on by detachment as a ready lever \u2014 even successfully retaining your Humanity still results in a couple days' worth of Bestial, Competitive, or Wanton complicating things, which makes ways to avoid the roll an attractive option one way or the other.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T22:39:45-07:00","id":1302472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302350#post1302350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will be the ST for a game soon. Just a few refresher questions.<br /> <br /> 1) Is the Social Combat Mechanic and the Debate Mechanic from DM and RfR respectively still usable in 2nd edition? My intent is to use Social Maneuvers for one-way social endeavors, social combat for spirited exchanges where both participants have goals, and debate for spreading ideas and wooing crowds. (effectively, SM for one-way one-on-one, SC for two-way one-on-one, and DB for two-way one-to-many. Extended actions/modified SM/merits would be used for one-way one-to-many.)<br /> <br /> 2) Is there any agreement as to what 'cities' belong to who? I can't place why but I think I remember Rome as being a Vampire puppet city and the British Empire being a Mage experiment. Interested as I might do a 'from prehistory to modern night and beyond' game.<br /> <br /> 3) Did we ever fix the Venture bane? :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Social combat has been revamped as of GMC/2e, so you might have a better time using the system built for this edition rather than trying to shoehorn in an old system. It's a core mechanic now. In the core book(s). Up to you, though.<br /> <br /> 2. The core book has a few sample cities for use, if you like, but VtR 2e is fairly deliberately without any sort of canon. It's all suggestion or example for the ST to build off of.<br /> <br /> 3. As stated by others, it isn't broken. If you absolutely must, though, there have been dozens of threads full of dozens more suggestions each on how to &quot;fix&quot; what isn't broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T01:49:05-07:00","id":1302503,"title":"","content":"If you're playing vampire there's a new debate/social combat system in Guide to the Night for 2e, which is actually very closely modeled around the combat system, so it's pretty fast to get into once you get a few core concepts around it. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T04:42:31-07:00","id":1302517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302503#post1302503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're playing vampire there's a new debate/social combat system in Guide to the Night for 2e, which is actually very closely modeled around the combat system, so it's pretty fast to get into once you get a few core concepts around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between the Dev diary and the preview, I may just pick Guide up. Thanks for the recommendation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302472#post1302472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1. Social combat has been revamped as of GMC/2e, so you might have a better time using the system built for this edition rather than trying to shoehorn in an old system. It's a core mechanic now. In the core book(s). Up to you, though.<br /> <br /> 2. The core book has a few sample cities for use, if you like, but VtR 2e is fairly deliberately without any sort of canon. It's all suggestion or example for the ST to build off of.<br /> <br /> 3. As stated by others, it isn't broken. If you absolutely must, though, there have been dozens of threads full of dozens more suggestions each on how to &quot;fix&quot; what isn't broken.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. As above, I am now aware. I wasn't before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, if Linga Bellum can't give you the edge, what is the point? /s<br /> <br /> 2. What I think I half remember is the Guardians really taking a shine to the British Empire; that it aligned with them. Same with the Ven and the Holy Roman Empire, or Vamps in general and Rome. So, I suppose I am trying to find arch-typical cities over canonical places where vampires live. A kind of 'Have you seen Rome? Of course it is a vampire paradise.'<br /> <br /> 3. And I've added to the pile. Weird, when I left it was in vogue to thrash the bane. Really feel ready to play an Elder right now. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302461#post1302461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(..snip...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I did the trend idea, so I'mma move your comment over there and reply. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":"several short posts. 04-04-2019, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T14:01:32-07:00","id":1302640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302517#post1302517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. What I think I half remember is the Guardians really taking a shine to the British Empire; that it aligned with them. Same with the Ven and the Holy Roman Empire, or Vamps in general and Rome. So, I suppose I am trying to find arch-typical cities over canonical places where vampires live. A kind of 'Have you seen Rome? Of course it is a vampire paradise.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the core book has several cities if you want to look over them. The specific cities in core are: Athens, Greece; Beijing, China; Berlin, Germany; Montreal, Canada; Raleigh-Durham-Chapel Hill,<br /> North Carolina; San Francisco, California; Swansea, Wales; Tokyo, Japan<br /> <br /> Each one goes into the history of the domain, the status of each Clan present, locations of note, and the local politics.<br /> <br /> I think the goal, though, is more to show how wildly varied Kindred cities can be, rather than give any idea of what &quot;typical&quot; is. Though some are closer to &quot;typical&quot; than others.<br /> <br /> If there's one commonality, I'd say they're excellent guides on how Kindred society is influenced by Kine history and culture in a region, rather than entirely separate from it. The society in Beijing looks absolutely nothing like the society in San Francisco, and nor should it. Each place has a different culture and history to draw from.<br /> <br /> 2e does away with most of the &quot;every [clan/society/domain/covenant] is the same&quot; baggage that plagued previous versions of Vampire in various degrees. Which, unfortunately, does lead to a lot more work for the STs, but it keeps things interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T17:34:10-07:00","id":1302689,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2003_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2003\" data-vbnamecard=\"2003\">Tabanese</a> dunno if this was already brought up, but Lingua Bellum has actually been converted to 2e in the Guide to the Night book. So if you want to use Lingua Bellum, buy that book.<br /> <br /> Personally I prefer the more simplistic social maneuvering mechanics found in the core Chronicles of Darkness and Vampire the Requiem 2e books, but Lingua Bellum can be cool for a grand and important debate, I suppose.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Whoops, I see <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar294_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"294\" data-vbnamecard=\"294\">Griautis</a> already brought it up. I guess I should have read the whole thread before responding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-04-2019, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T02:47:14-07:00","id":1302769,"title":"","content":"I would definitely recommend Social Manoeuvering from CofD or any of the other core books that include it.<br /> Lingua Bellum is very niche. It's not about persuading anyone or making a point; it's all about establishing social dominance over someone else in front of a crowd. It does not work for trying to persuade people, making a rousing speech, debating ideas, etc. Unless the audience is completely disinterested in whether your idea is actually a good one or not, and completely base their opinions on how well you can verbally eviscerate someone else.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's less social combat and more social duelling, if that makes sense. It's a spectacle that can change your social standing, but not practical for other reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-05-2019, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T04:25:32-07:00","id":1302778,"title":"","content":"I got the impression if was the update on the Requiem debate rules already and only plan to use it in such a context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T08:09:38-07:00","id":1302827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302778#post1302778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the impression if was the update on the Requiem debate rules already and only plan to use it in such a context.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with the old debate rules, but Lingua Bellum was promoted as a brand new system and as it's written it's not appropriate for debates, so I really don't think it's just an update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T08:51:19-07:00","id":1302841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302827#post1302827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not familiar with the old debate rules, but Lingua Bellum was promoted as a brand new system and as it's written it's not appropriate for debates, so I really don't think it's just an update.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's great for debates.<br /> Why do you think it's not appropriate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T09:10:53-07:00","id":1302843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302841#post1302841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's great for debates.<br /> Why do you think it's not appropriate?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I'd like to hear your answer to this too <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> <br /> <br /> Lingua Bellum is not brand new to 2e. It already existed in Requiem for Rome (though it wasn't called Lingua Bellum in that book, if you have Requiem for Rome, check page 179). Guide to the Night took that system found in Requiem for Rome and greatly expanded upon it.<br /> <br /> Both in Requiem for Rome as well as Guide to the Night, Lingua Bellum is presented as specifically for grand debates. In fact the entire purpose of the system existing is to use it in grand debates.<br /> <br /> Social Maneuvering is used if you try to persuade a person in a one-on-one situation, Lingua Bellum is used if you try to persuade an entire audience in a grand debate on Elysium ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T11:06:06-07:00","id":1302868,"title":"","content":"Because nothing about Lingua Bellum is about conveying ideas to the audience. It's all about beating your opponent in a verbal conflict. Many debates can very well end up in Lingua Bellum, but that's when the debate has deteriorated away from actual reasoning to directly attacking your opponent.<br /> <br /> So let me readjust my point: It's a system for popularity contests in the guise of a debate, not for actual debates. It's verbal violence in the place of physical violence. Explicitly so, even.<br /> Not to say it's a bad system, though. Very telling about Kindred society, but at the same time very niche in application.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T11:29:37-07:00","id":1302878,"title":"","content":"Although insult slinging and ridicule is the only debate tactic American politicians are capable of performing or understanding, I have to agree with Tessie on this. Lingua Bellum is more about choosing the proper public social forum to hurl insults and getting a clique to laugh at your sick burns and snappy comebacks than it is about effectively debating a topic.<br /> <br /> And now I'm going to go check the weather to see if Hell froze over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-05-2019, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T17:30:13-07:00","id":1302972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302868#post1302868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's all about beating your opponent in a verbal conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the debate rules were found in a book about Vampires in Rome. That debate was more about looking good and making the other guy look foolish was implied.<br /> <br /> I think the disagreement is that you have higher expectations of debate. Who should win in a contest, the smart one (presumed to have the best argument) or the charismatic one (presumed to be able to woo the crowd)? If you say the former, I understand why both systems seem to neglect debate because it is the latter who is more likely to win according to the rules.<sub> (iirc. Maybe not. Will edit when I check if I am wrong)</sub> But for me, that is just expected. Among vampires, where status is palpable, might is right. It is all the Beast understands and so it doesn't really matter what you say, so long as you look good doing it. (That said, the Rome version mandated that the audience to a debate adopted the winning position. So if it was about allocating troops to the front, your character would believe it wise if the side advocating it won. It might be something you could handle with a condition now.)<br /> <br /> As it happens, the Rome version had both Logic and Retheroic debate style merits to reflect this dual-aspect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T19:00:22-07:00","id":1302981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302972#post1302972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the debate rules were found in a book about Vampires in Rome. That debate was more about looking good and making the other guy look foolish was implied.<br /> <br /> I think the disagreement is that you have higher expectations of debate. Who should win in a contest, the smart one (presumed to have the best argument) or the charismatic one (presumed to be able to woo the crowd)? If you say the former, I understand why both systems seem to neglect debate because it is the latter who is more likely to win according to the rules.<sub> (iirc. Maybe not. Will edit when I check if I am wrong)</sub> But for me, that is just expected. Among vampires, where status is palpable, might is right. It is all the Beast understands and so it doesn't really matter what you say, so long as you look good doing it. (That said, the Rome version mandated that the audience to a debate adopted the winning position. So if it was about allocating troops to the front, your character would believe it wise if the side advocating it won. It might be something you could handle with a condition now.)<br /> <br /> As it happens, the Rome version had both Logic and Retheroic debate style merits to reflect this dual-aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ^<br /> This. A debate is verbal combat, and verbal combats in front of an audience are debates. Furthermore, the book uses the word 'debate' more than 20 times in the Lingua Bellum section. If Lingua Bellum isn't about debates, then I sure wonder why the book brings it up so often.<br /> <br /> And honestly, debates rarely, if ever, are about using actual sound arguments and logic to persuade the audience to your side, and almost always devolve to wrapping up your arguments in good-sounding rhetoric, verbally cornering your opponent and leading him into making mistakes, playing the audience and making your opponent look like a fool. The only place where you might see proper debates without these underhanded tactics is a debate among scientists, and even there I've seen the tactics that Lingua Bellum presents us with being used.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>I do agree that Lingua Bellum is extremely niche, and personally I think it's also a bit too mechanically complex for something I'd rather settle with actual roleplaying and a few dice rolls here and there to see how successful the player is in rallying the crowd and/or convincing his opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-05-2019, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T22:00:42-07:00","id":1303005,"title":"","content":"In case of a tied contested roll, the defender wins, correct? If a character tells a lie and the other character detects for lies, which one is the attacker and which the defender? You could say the person telling the lie 'attacked' the other by lying, but <br /> you can equally argue that the detector was the 'attacker' because they attempted to pierce the meaning. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24354-corbie","name":"Corbie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24354_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T22:35:45-07:00","id":1303012,"title":"","content":"If the detector isn't being addressed and is overhearing a potential lie being told to someone else, you have an argument that the detector is actively looking to undermine the liar. But in most cases, the detector isn't actively trying to alter someone else's perception or mindset, the liar is, therefore the liar is the &quot;attacker&quot;. He has to roll a contested roll to lie successfully. If he wins the lie is believed, if the detector wins, then he knows it's a lie.<br /> <br /> Yes, ties go to the defender. (Or you can reroll.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T01:53:14-07:00","id":1303034,"title":"","content":"This is not really related to this specific topic: attacker <br /> /defender but I'd like a feedback from you on how I'm currently handling different rolls.<br /> <br /> Using the Lie example, if the &quot;defender&quot; is already suspicious and he is actively trying to understand if that specific character is lying, I'l go for a cintested roll (i.e. manip+subterfuge vs Wits+subt/empathy/whatever). On the other hand if it's a normal conversation where a character is lying and the audience has no particular reasons to think he could be laying, what I roll is just a normal roll penalized by the audience wits as it was defense (manip+subt - wits).<br /> This also apply for, let's say, stealth rolls. If someone is actively looking for intruder is contested, otherwise the stealth roll is just penalized by the wits.<br /> Is that the right interpretation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T03:45:48-07:00","id":1303039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1302972#post1302972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the disagreement is that you have higher expectations of debate. Who should win in a contest, the smart one (presumed to have the best argument) or the charismatic one (presumed to be able to woo the crowd)? If you say the former, I understand why both systems seem to neglect debate because it is the latter who is more likely to win according to the rules.<sub> (iirc. Maybe not. Will edit when I check if I am wrong)</sub> But for me, that is just expected. Among vampires, where status is palpable, might is right. It is all the Beast understands and so it doesn't really matter what you say, so long as you look good doing it. (That said, the Rome version mandated that the audience to a debate adopted the winning position. So if it was about allocating troops to the front, your character would believe it wise if the side advocating it won. It might be something you could handle with a condition now.)<br /> <br /> As it happens, the Rome version had both Logic and Retheroic debate style merits to reflect this dual-aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that I don't think more charismatic or rhetorically minded people shouldn't have an advantage, it's that none of the manoeuvres are about presenting or defending an actual idea or position. That is not an option unless one of the Style Merits happen to contain it. The system is in its entirety about making yourself look good while smearing the opponent. Not even the most stereotypical American presidential election debates are that bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T04:20:26-07:00","id":1303045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1303034#post1303034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not really related to this specific topic: attacker <br /> /defender but I'd like a feedback from you on how I'm currently handling different rolls.<br /> <br /> Using the Lie example, if the &amp;quot;defender&amp;quot; is already suspicious and he is actively trying to understand if that specific character is lying, I'l go for a cintested roll (i.e. manip+subterfuge vs Wits+subt/empathy/whatever). On the other hand if it's a normal conversation where a character is lying and the audience has no particular reasons to think he could be laying, what I roll is just a normal roll penalized by the audience wits as it was defense (manip+subt - wits).<br /> This also apply for, let's say, stealth rolls. If someone is actively looking for intruder is contested, otherwise the stealth roll is just penalized by the wits.<br /> Is that the right interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that works for you, sure. Personally in a case like a politician bullshitting or deliberately misrepresenting facts in front of a hostile or friendly audience I just have the relevant individuals simply roll whether or not they believe it when it comes up with the appropriate modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T07:09:02-07:00","id":1303069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1303039#post1303039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not that I don't think more charismatic or rhetorically minded people shouldn't have an advantage, it's that none of the manoeuvres are about presenting or defending an actual idea or position. That is not an option unless one of the Style Merits happen to contain it. The system is in its entirety about making yourself look good while smearing the opponent. Not even the most stereotypical American presidential election debates are that bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding just Debate from the Rome book (as I don't have access to Guide yet), available to everyone is the aggressive logic form of arguing. You make rolls using Int+(apt Skill). So you do argue facts in the abstract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T07:14:13-07:00","id":1303070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1303069#post1303069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding just Debate from the Rome book (as I don't have access to Guide yet), available to everyone is the aggressive logic form of arguing. You make rolls using Int+(apt Skill). So you do argue facts in the abstract.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile all core rolls in Lingua Bellum uses Presence or Manipulation. Some of the Covenant specific Merits can give you access to manoeuvres that uses other Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T07:29:26-07:00","id":1303072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1303034#post1303034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not really related to this specific topic: attacker<br /> /defender but I'd like a feedback from you on how I'm currently handling different rolls.<br /> <br /> Using the Lie example, if the &quot;defender&quot; is already suspicious and he is actively trying to understand if that specific character is lying, I'l go for a cintested roll (i.e. manip+subterfuge vs Wits+subt/empathy/whatever). On the other hand if it's a normal conversation where a character is lying and the audience has no particular reasons to think he could be laying, what I roll is just a normal roll penalized by the audience wits as it was defense (manip+subt - wits).<br /> This also apply for, let's say, stealth rolls. If someone is actively looking for intruder is contested, otherwise the stealth roll is just penalized by the wits.<br /> Is that the right interpretation?</div> </div> </div> </div>That does sound reasonable when lying to a child or totally unsuspecting normies and certainly streamlines by eliminating extra rolls but when used on anyone else partaking in the danse macabre, I would just use bonus dice to represent the preparedness of the one(s) being lied to.<br /> Lying to a naive and trusting neonate or ghoul may give the liar some bonus dice while lying to a jaded competitor would give bonus dice to the one being lied to.<br /> If you're involved with the all night society in any way, then you quickly develop a skeptical eye for the motivations of all others, while if you're skilled in Empathy or Subterfuge then you are unlikely to just turn off such survival mechanisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-06-2019, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T11:22:50-07:00","id":1303135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1303070#post1303070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meanwhile all core rolls in Lingua Bellum uses Presence or Manipulation. Some of the Covenant specific Merits can give you access to manoeuvres that uses other Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touch\u00e9. Not a slam dunk though. You could argue that debates are prepared with Int or Wit, but the execution must use a social attribute given that debates occur in the social sphere. Skills make up how well you know your stuff. Still, what about those bright sparks that can think on their feet. (Fast Talk is a merit, though).<br /> <br /> But yeah, it all seem like a confusing mess. I'm actually inclined to go with my gut and just do as I said I would: use Rome-debate for contested one-to-many, social combat for contested one-to-one, social manuver for uncontested one-to-one, and one-to-many.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T09:26:42-07:00","id":1303544,"title":"","content":"Just like a combat attack does not imply the entire description and what happens in universe, so I'd say is the same with these maneuvers. Just because &quot;Fuck Off&quot; (dodge&quot; is named that, doesn't mean you have to literally tell the other person to fuck off. <br /> <br /> Similarly, as mentioned, I'd say that intelligent debate and preparedness nicely falls under &quot;making plans&quot; rules and general preparation for the debate, thus a highly intelligent character can easily prepare his stuff beforehand, thus gaining a good bonus. (Just like a social liar can try and prepare slander)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T02:45:38-07:00","id":1303906,"title":"","content":"Animalism 4: feral Infection<br /> <br /> If the human/supernatural successes the Resolve+Composure - Vampire successes, this means that is totally uneffected by this power or just that he won't follow the Vampire command? Cause the book is not very clear as it states: A failed roll put the target under the vampire command.<br /> <br /> I'm just not sure if in any case, also who is succeding at the roll, will be still killing eachone else.<br /> <br /> Also, how can someone resolve this condition? Does he need just to wait the end of the scene? That means everyone dead around him? Sounds very...definitive for both who is sourroinding him and hhe himself as at some point &quot;Navy Seals&quot; will arrive to nuke him dow XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T03:41:35-07:00","id":1303908,"title":"","content":"If they make the roll, they do not succumb to the predatory aura effect flooding the area and descend into a frenzied state. That is what places them under the vampire\u2019s command. If they fail the roll they fall into frenzy and attack whomever the vampire tells them to attack. It\u2019s not as if the vampire can give them complex assassination instructions.<br /> <br /> If your character succeeds in the roll, (possible but not likely) he is not in the frenzied state and he can ignore the vampire\u2019s command and yes, your character can still get ripped apart by whatever else is in the area.<br /> If he is a supernatural creature and failed the roll, he can spend a willpower to resist the vampire\u2019s command but he is still in a frenzy state.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s resolved at the end of the scene when the frenzy state wears off or the object in the vicinity is destroyed. If he resisted initially he can leave the area.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s an effective power to damage or destroy another vampire\u2019s haven as well. Blame it on the vermin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T17:26:36-07:00","id":1304050,"title":"","content":"Question about Awe in combat:<br /> <br /> How do you guys run Awe (Majesty 1) in combat? This is assuming violence has already escalated and combat is already ongoing. What happens when someone uses Awe after that? Not just narrative, but mechanically?<br /> <br /> Does it work like how taunting works for most tanks in MMORPGs, e.g. making the person using Awe the most attractive target to attack?<br /> Or does it do it opposite, making people think twice before they attack the Awe-using vampire (and if so, wouldn't that make Awe overlap an awful lot with Dread Presence)?<br /> Or does the Awe using vampire distract everyone from the combat, bringing the combat to a halt?<br /> Or would it, like so many things in CofD, depend entirely on context? If it does, can you give me some examples of &quot;when the Awe-user does this, this happens&quot; and &quot;if the enemy does this, that happens&quot;?<br /> <br /> What about the allies of the Awe-using vampire? Or Dread Presence for that matter? Are allies equally affected, or would it be fair to rule that those who are familiar with the Awe-using vampire and on the same side as him/her are less affected by it, given that they know what is going on and know that using Awe/Dread Presence is part of their ally's tactic?<br /> <br /> <br /> I have my own ideas on how Awe in combat should be handled, but I'm not sure if I'm doing it right:<br /> <br /> Since Awe is an 'I spend nothing, and I roll nothing, turning it on is free and everyone is automatically affected by it'-power, I want to say the effects are rather weak, and by itself (without further use of Social rolls, or other Majesty powers) doesn't do a whole lot when combat has already started. It will, at best, make it easier for the Awe-user to influence his attacker, for example, taunting the attacker (or a group of attackers) with a Presence + Persuasion roll, plus dots in Majesty as a dice bonus (&quot;Hey, moron, you think you're tough? Why don't you try me?!&quot;), or convince them not to attack you with Presence + Intimidation + Majesty (&quot;If you attack me, I will break your neck, punk!&quot;), or to distract someone with Presence + Expression + Majesty, so your teammate might get a surprise attack in (&quot;Hey idiot, over here!&quot;) forcing the enemy to roll a Wits + Composure - your Majesty to notice your friend.<br /> <br /> Passively, when the Awe-using vampire isn't doing any of the above, it might make aggressors decide to prioritize the vampire, believing him/her to be the toughest and most important combatant on the field, or, if they are less experienced or less brave, they might do the opposite, shying away from the vampire, for the same reasons as mentioned earlier, or because they simply don't want to hurt the vampire. However, if the Awe-user isn't doing anything to actively persuade the opponents one way or the other, I'm of the opinion it should be up to the ST to decide how the aggressors react to Awe (assuming that the aggressors are NPCs, or STCs (storyteller characters) if you will).<br /> <br /> I don't think Awe should do a whole lot more than that mechanically, but maybe you disagree. What do you people think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-10-2019, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T18:34:24-07:00","id":1304062,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t allow it to work universally in combat. A person is going to pay more attention to the person who is literally pointing a gun in their face or who physically shoved a dagger into their kidneys, not the Pretty Princess Daeva prancing around screaming for everyone\u2019s attention. (The taunt skill in video games is retarded. When someone is disemboweling you, you\u2019re not going to turn your attention away from them to the person calling your mother a whore.) Nor does turning it on AFTER the fight starts count as getting victims Awed to turn on other powers. They have more important issues requiring their immediate attention.<br /> <br /> Now if that Daeva was the one pointing the gun or shiving someone and decides to follow through with a taunt or suggestion and back it up with Awe, it may work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T19:09:06-07:00","id":1304068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304062#post1304062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t allow it to work universally in combat. A person is going to pay more attention to the person who is literally pointing a gun in their face or who physically shoved a dagger into their kidneys, not the Pretty Princess Daeva prancing around screaming for everyone\u2019s attention. (The taunt skill in video games is retarded. When someone is disemboweling you, you\u2019re not going to turn your attention away from them to the person calling your mother a whore.) Nor does turning it on AFTER the fight starts count as getting victims Awed to turn on other powers. They have more important issues requiring their immediate attention.<br /> <br /> Now if that Daeva was the one pointing the gun or shiving someone and decides to follow through with a taunt or suggestion and back it up with Awe, it may work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> What if the Daeva activates Awe before violence escalates, say at the first turn of combat or during a surprise round?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T20:05:40-07:00","id":1304087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304068#post1304068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> What if the Daeva activates Awe before violence escalates, say at the first turn of combat or during a surprise round?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It depends on the circumstances. If two other parties are about to come to blows with each other, they're most likely going to largely disregard the Daeva except as a potential ally or enemy. If the Daeva is going to try and distract one person so the other can hit first, I'd have the potential victim make a penalized (by the Majesty rating of the Daeva) reflexive Wits + Subterfuge or Danger Sense check.<br /> <br /> Why would a Daeva that got ambushed but made the surprise check use Awe and not Celerity?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T23:30:23-07:00","id":1304114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304050#post1304050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about Awe in combat:<br /> <br /> How do you guys run Awe (Majesty 1) in combat? This is assuming violence has already escalated and combat is already ongoing. What happens when someone uses Awe after that? Not just narrative, but mechanically?<br /> <br /> Does it work like how taunting works for most tanks in MMORPGs, e.g. making the person using Awe the most attractive target to attack?<br /> Or does it do it opposite, making people think twice before they attack the Awe-using vampire (and if so, wouldn't that make Awe overlap an awful lot with Dread Presence)?<br /> Or does the Awe using vampire distract everyone from the combat, bringing the combat to a halt?<br /> Or would it, like so many things in CofD, depend entirely on context? If it does, can you give me some examples of &quot;when the Awe-user does this, this happens&quot; and &quot;if the enemy does this, that happens&quot;?<br /> <br /> What about the allies of the Awe-using vampire? Or Dread Presence for that matter? Are allies equally affected, or would it be fair to rule that those who are familiar with the Awe-using vampire and on the same side as him/her are less affected by it, given that they know what is going on and know that using Awe/Dread Presence is part of their ally's tactic?<br /> <br /> <br /> I have my own ideas on how Awe in combat should be handled, but I'm not sure if I'm doing it right:<br /> <br /> Since Awe is an 'I spend nothing, and I roll nothing, turning it on is free and everyone is automatically affected by it'-power, I want to say the effects are rather weak, and by itself (without further use of Social rolls, or other Majesty powers) doesn't do a whole lot when combat has already started. It will, at best, make it easier for the Awe-user to influence his attacker, for example, taunting the attacker (or a group of attackers) with a Presence + Persuasion roll, plus dots in Majesty as a dice bonus (&quot;Hey, moron, you think you're tough? Why don't you try me?!&quot;), or convince them not to attack you with Presence + Intimidation + Majesty (&quot;If you attack me, I will break your neck, punk!&quot;), or to distract someone with Presence + Expression + Majesty, so your teammate might get a surprise attack in (&quot;Hey idiot, over here!&quot;) forcing the enemy to roll a Wits + Composure - your Majesty to notice your friend.<br /> <br /> Passively, when the Awe-using vampire isn't doing any of the above, it might make aggressors decide to prioritize the vampire, believing him/her to be the toughest and most important combatant on the field, or, if they are less experienced or less brave, they might do the opposite, shying away from the vampire, for the same reasons as mentioned earlier, or because they simply don't want to hurt the vampire. However, if the Awe-user isn't doing anything to actively persuade the opponents one way or the other, I'm of the opinion it should be up to the ST to decide how the aggressors react to Awe (assuming that the aggressors are NPCs, or STCs (storyteller characters) if you will).<br /> <br /> I don't think Awe should do a whole lot more than that mechanically, but maybe you disagree. What do you people think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Awe does nothing more than making you the most important and amazing person in the area. You are suddenly considered as a VIP. So, what happens when you are fighting with someone that made you very angry and that suddenly you recognize him: hey wait but he's Sylvester Stallone (or whatever relevant person you personally like). <br /> If I try to imagine myself in this situation I would surely hesitate to continue fighting. If we think tu a real fight, it's not just a sequejlnce of turn where in every turn there must be an action. A fight is also pauses, study, ec. So it has totally sense for me to at least hesitate: &quot;oh Gid, wait, am I really fighting against Stallone?&quot;<br /> How is this translated mechanically?<br /> Awe add Majesty to your oresence rolls. Then make a Presence+composure roll - opponent's Composure or resolve, to see how deep your &quot;presence&quot; impacts your very opponent. Awe also remove penalities to social rolls making the previous roll feasible: having punched your opponents would have certanly been a penality. <br /> <br /> Using awe is an action so that's mean you are not going to attack him for that very turn at least.<br /> <br /> Oke we were fight but hey... he is Stallone...<br /> <br /> Than if you start again to attack him, depending on the situation or successes rolled, he could try to avoid you keepeing distances, like: hey hey, ok I don't want problem with you ok? Or just saying: &quot;fuc* you man&quot;. Fighting you back.<br /> <br /> You could also activate successive powers than that extremize everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T04:35:04-07:00","id":1304148,"title":"","content":"Awe does exactly what it describes to do.<br /> Meaning, if you turn on Awe, unless social penalties or your presence is relevant, it pretty much does nothing. Others may hesitate to attack you, or may consider their target priority different but that will depend on context and specific people doing it. The only thing you can count on when you use Awe in combat, is the social bonuses you're gonna get if you decide to do social actions. Trying to stop the fighting and talk it out could definitely be one such action and would benefit from Awe immensely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T05:01:37-07:00","id":1304154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304148#post1304148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awe does exactly what it describes to do.<br /> Meaning, if you turn on Awe, unless social penalties or your presence is relevant, it pretty much does nothing. Others may hesitate to attack you, or may consider their target priority different but that will depend on context and specific people doing it. The only thing you can count on when you use Awe in combat, is the social bonuses you're gonna get if you decide to do social actions. Trying to stop the fighting and talk it out could definitely be one such action and would benefit from Awe immensely.</div> </div> </div> </div>As well as making it easier for people to perform sneak attacks due to the penalty to noticing things other than the Awe user. Potentially very effective if the Awe user has a Fighting Style that can distract opponents or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T12:30:28-07:00","id":1304289,"title":"","content":"So after being charmed once by a Daeva Elder (I believe Majesty 5), after it wears off - what is the best way to deal with it? Besides just avoiding the Elder cuz not really an option. I think I realize Majesty was at work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T13:07:27-07:00","id":1304298,"title":"","content":"As in, you got hit by <i>Idol</i>?<br /> <br /> I'd say even afterward you remember how <i>good</i> it felt to be around them, how you got butterflies in your stomach every time they looked at you. You might hate them as a person, or think that as an Invictus they represent everything you and the other Carthians despise most. But you can't shake that memory of what being near them felt like. And next time you see them, you know that might happen again.<br /> <br /> <i>Majesty</i> is insidious like that. It can't give precise commands like <i>Dominate</i>, but that doesn't mean it's any less powerful\u2014its effects stick around long after <i>Mesmerized</i> has worn off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T13:41:17-07:00","id":1304309,"title":"","content":"Did they screw over your character or try to screw over your character? If no, then let sleeping dogs lie.<br /> <br /> If they screwed your character over, or tried to, just shun their company with a flimsy excuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T14:11:16-07:00","id":1304314,"title":"","content":"Actually my character is Ordo Dracul and the Daeva Elder is Lancea et Sanctum. LOL No, it wasn't Idol - I think just the Charmed condition (2nd level, but their dice pool let them have Majesty 5 I think). I did give up some secrets (and got beats for) about things I shouldn't have. But I think the character is conscious of that. Should I just try to communicate by webcam after that? LOL","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T14:30:26-07:00","id":1304319,"title":"","content":"Yes, your character should have immediately realized he got scammed after divulging the first secret. If he's fishing for secrets that can get your character torpored, blood bound, or killed, it probably would be in his best interest to not meet this elder in person any longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T15:54:35-07:00","id":1304329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304319#post1304319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, your character should have immediately realized he got scammed after divulging the first secret. If he's fishing for secrets that can get your character torpored, blood bound, or killed, it probably would be in his best interest to not meet this elder in person any longer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's debatable. Divulging a secret gives a Beat, it does not resolve the condition, and unless the condition is resolved (e.g. it didn't just fade away, but one of the resolution conditions has been met) the charmed character doesn't feel scammed or ripped off.<br /> <br /> I'd say, if the charmed character got himself or his friends in <i>serious</i> trouble by giving away secrets he shouldn't have or doing favors he shouldn't have done, <i>then</i> I'd count the Charmed condition as resolved, which immediately makes the character aware that he got ripped off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-11-2019, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T16:03:09-07:00","id":1304331,"title":"","content":"What is the relationship between vitae pools and feeding scenes?<br /> <br /> I ask because I reread them to refresh myself on the RAW and am confident I misread them the first time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T16:31:54-07:00","id":1304337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304331#post1304331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the relationship between vitae pools and feeding scenes?<br /> <br /> I ask because I reread them to refresh myself on the RAW and am confident I misread them the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Success or failure determines whether you can feed in your intended manner and determine the consequences. Feeding scenes are more about defining how the Kindred interact with the kine than about putting the camera on them maintaining their safety margin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T16:42:12-07:00","id":1304339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304331#post1304331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the relationship between vitae pools and feeding scenes?<br /> <br /> I ask because I reread them to refresh myself on the RAW and am confident I misread them the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't understand your question. Are you asking how much Vitae an average human contains?<br /> <br /> A human has an amount of Vitae equal to his Health boxes. If you take the last Vitae from a human, he either immediately dies or is in critical condition and will die without serious medical intervention (depending on the Storyteller).<br /> <br /> Are you asking how the current amount of Vitae the player has affects his feeding scene? Once more, this is up to the Storyteller. Being hungry (4 or less Vitae) or starving (2 or less Vitae) is a frenzy trigger, and the moment that sweet red nectar enters your vampire's mouth, the Beast might try to take over, trying to completely drain the human to the last drop of Vitae. This could result in a Resolve + Composure roll with a -2 (hungry) or -4 (starving) penalty if the player character wants to fight the urge to drain the human.<br /> <br /> Are you asking how much Vitae you can take per feeding scene? Again, depends on the ST. Some Storytellers allow you to choose how much Vitae you take from the human, and afterwards describe the medical condition the human is in after the feeding (completely fine, a bit woozy, knocked out, dying, dead, etc.). Other Storytellers want to do feeding scenes very intimately, going through the scene on a turn by turn basis, and describing what's happening each passing turn, until you decide to stop sucking blood.<br /> <br /> I'm personally a fan of having my players roll a die to see how much Vitae they gain from the feeding, and I let my players decide which die they wanna roll ( a d4, d6, d8 or a d10, choosing a higher die will potentially yield more Vitae, but it also increases the chance you drain the human dry, killing him in the process), but this is by no means RAW.<br /> I combine this with randomized health for the humans to make feeding more risky and more unpredictable. Not all humans always have full health. Some are sick, some have been in a fight, and some have already been fed on. For humans likely to end up fighting, getting sick or getting fed on, I roll a die to see how much bashing/lethal wounds they already have at the start of the feeding scene, usually a d4 or d6. I always give my players an small indicator of their prey's health, and they are allowed to roll Wits + Medicine checks to further diagnose their prey before going for the bite.<br /> I don't always do this though. Sometimes I do feeding scenes &quot;down and dirty&quot;, allowing my players to make a hunting roll and the amount of successes on their roll is the amount of Vitae they gained, without really going deep into the scene. Sometimes I just don't want to waste time on feeding scenes.<br /> Again, this is by no means RAW, I'm just sharing this to give you some ideas on how you can handle feeding scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-11-2019, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T16:51:36-07:00","id":1304341,"title":"","content":"So I am reading it correctly the second time. I don't how I managed it the first time, but I read it as 'roll the attribute+skill combo that best describes your approach and take that amount of blood points. If the amount causes injury or death, deal with it.'<br /> <br /> I have no idea how I managed to read RAW in that way but it is how I thought it should be done for ages.<br /> <br /> The more you know.<br /> <br /> OH WAIT!<br /> <br /> Did the rules for feeding change between 1E and 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T17:02:22-07:00","id":1304343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304341#post1304341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I am reading it correctly the second time. I don't how I managed it the first time, but I read it as 'roll the attribute+skill combo that best describes your approach and take that amount of blood points. If the amount causes injury or death, deal with it.'<br /> <br /> I have no idea how I managed to read RAW in that way but it is how I thought it should be done for ages.<br /> <br /> The more you know.<br /> <br /> OH WAIT!<br /> <br /> Did the rules for feeding change between 1E and 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how it <i>can</i> be done (as I said in my previous post, I sometimes do it that way if my players want to feed quickly, &quot;down and dirty&quot;-style, in between major events), but by no means how it <i>should</i> be done.<br /> <br /> What Satchel said is right. RAW the hunting roll is merely to establish whether a feeding encounter happens and if it happens on the vampire's terms or not. After the roll, the feeding scene is played out, and either the player chooses how much Vitae he wishes to take from the human, or the Storyteller chooses how much Vitae the player gains, or the scene might be handled in a turn-by-turn basis, gaining an amount of Vitae equal to your Vitae/turn limit for each turn your're feeding, as the Storyteller describes the progression of the scene on a turn-by-turn basis. Or, you can do it my way, and have the players roll dice to determine how much Vitae they gain.<br /> <br /> And no, I don't think the feeding mechanics have changed in any significant way, but my memories on the 1e rules are a little fuzzy and I don't have the book with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-11-2019, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T17:12:16-07:00","id":1304344,"title":"","content":"Cheers. I think I was just a little shocked over my misreading. I'm normally very good about this sort of thing. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T17:33:43-07:00","id":1304726,"title":"","content":"Uplifting a Rev is the same as embracing a mortal, right? Stick a bit of Vitae down the gullet, say a prayer to Longinus and, boom, more competition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T19:21:30-07:00","id":1304745,"title":"","content":"Yes, though in both cases it takes a huge effort of will. Feeding Vitae to a Revenant won't automatically uplift them if you're not trying to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T19:56:03-07:00","id":1304750,"title":"","content":"The kindred has to spend a point of Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T20:04:54-07:00","id":1304754,"title":"","content":"Which has struck me and my entire group as very odd. Why is it so bad to uplift a Revenant to a much more stable existence with less frenzied feeding sprees? It's not like the Humanity dot actually powers the Embrace since they're already mostly Kindred, and accidental posthumous Embraces as well as the Vast Dynasty proves that Humanity loss is purely a response to the action rather than a metaphysical requirement for the Embrace.<br /> I can still see it as a breaking point since it's an inhuman thing to do, but certainly not that monstrous compared to some other breaking points. Yet automatic Humanity loss pegs it as much worse than mass murder and diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T20:55:59-07:00","id":1304762,"title":"","content":"Revenants may be created inadvertantly, but uplifting one is a conscious decision on the part of the one who does it. They are choosing to knowingly empower another violent blood drinking serial killing monster that preys on sentient beings.<br /> Posthumous Embraces also cost a Humanity dot and the Vast Dynasty doesn't eliminate the Humanity loss, it just raises the floor for bringing other kindred into existence from definite to potential degeneration risk. And really, citing the practices of a cult that routinely pursues inhuman atrocities in order to indulge in even more depraved activities doesn't exactly make your point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T21:47:17-07:00","id":1304765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304754#post1304754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which has struck me and my entire group as very odd. Why is it so bad to uplift a Revenant to a much more stable existence with less frenzied feeding sprees? It's not like the Humanity dot actually powers the Embrace since they're already mostly Kindred, and accidental posthumous Embraces as well as the Vast Dynasty proves that Humanity loss is purely a response to the action rather than a metaphysical requirement for the Embrace.<br /> I can still see it as a breaking point since it's an inhuman thing to do, but certainly not that monstrous compared to some other breaking points. Yet automatic Humanity loss pegs it as much worse than mass murder and diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a case to be made that it's not &quot;stabilizing a revenant is bad&quot; so much as &quot;stabilizing a revenant takes a spiritual investment of the self-control and Beast-mitigating ability your character has, which is a resource that requires cultivation and maintenance.&quot; You're giving a more definite and established place in the night to another vampire even if your adoption doesn't proceed to the patronage sires traditionally offer their childer \u2014 you're <i>making them Kindred</i>, and that takes it out of you.<br /> <br /> Remember, Humanity isn't &quot;these things are bad,&quot; it's &quot;these things damage your perspective on mortality and its ability to keep your banes in check.&quot; Aligning your Blood with a vampire that previously began every night distressingly close to frenzy feels like the sort of balancing act that necessarily involves a step down the ladder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T03:21:42-07:00","id":1304775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304762#post1304762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Posthumous Embraces also cost a Humanity dot and the Vast Dynasty doesn't eliminate the Humanity loss, it just raises the floor for bringing other kindred into existence from definite to potential degeneration risk.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Accidental</i> posthumous Embraces are merely a breaking point, and only if you find out you accidentally Embraced someone. That alone proves that Humanity loss is your own reaction to the process, not something inherent in the Embrace.<br /> <br /> I can dig Embraces being automatic Humanity loss due to you creating a vampire out of a mortal. It's pretty dang monstrous. But I fail to see how uplifting a revenant, even if it's a decidedly inhuman thing to do, is worse than, say, ghouling a mortal (a direct parallell since you uplift them closer to being a vampire), siring a dhampir, or consuming another person's very soul. Except for the Embrace, absolutely none of the other objectively non-human things that vampires can do leads to an automatic Humanity loss.<br /> The reasons you two've given makes me think it should be a Humanity 1-2 breaking point, possibly modified by the character's reason to uplift the revenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T06:25:41-07:00","id":1304795,"title":"","content":"No, it costs a dot of Humanity. And you must have skipped the sentence where it says the group should exercise common sense and not twist the rules to go around &quot;accidentally&quot; embracing kindred. Which means, if you, as an ST decide to have some vampire show up at the doorstep of the PCs and say &quot;Hi, I'm your childe&quot; to lead into some drama, or have them abducted and imprisoned by a powerful human who won't free them unless they turn someone/themself into a vampire, you don't proceed to screw the player by stripping away a dot of Humanity. Or if PCs run around feeding vitae to humans they left at Death's door in order to avoid a degeneration check for manslaughter or murder because they rise a week later, they don't dodge the Humanity loss.<br /> <br /> No, it proves your character doesn't just lose Humanity for things they don't know they did. The same way one doesn't degenerate if they did something that would otherwise warrant a check while under the effects of Dominate. <br /> <br /> To be honest, I'm not exactly a fan of it either. (Since it's a form of procreation and humans are normally driven to procreate but that's another matter and it can be done consentually) Nor do I see it as necessarily worse than creating a ghoul or dhampir (honestly, I consider them worse since the former is a form of slavery and emotional abuse and the latter entails inflicting a cursed state on your child to exploit them) but the ghoul status is potentially removable/reversible and creating a dhampir, in most cases, requires the participation of another individual. But go ahead and make it a breaking point check if you like, I allow it to be a check modified by individual circumstances so it doesn't hurt my feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T06:56:29-07:00","id":1304800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304795#post1304795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it costs a dot of Humanity. And you must have skipped the sentence where it says the group should exercise common sense and not twist the rules to go around &quot;accidentally&quot; embracing kindred. Which means, if you, as an ST decide to have some vampire show up at the doorstep of the PCs and say &quot;Hi, I'm your childe&quot; to lead into some drama, or have them abducted and imprisoned by a powerful human who won't free them unless they turn someone/themself into a vampire, you don't proceed to screw the player by stripping away a dot of Humanity. Or if PCs run around feeding vitae to humans they left at Death's door in order to avoid a degeneration check for manslaughter or murder because they rise a week later, they don't dodge the Humanity loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;A sire must choose to commit the Embrace, and that choice comes at the price of a Humanity dot. <b>Posthumous Embraces break that rule.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This costs the donor a Humanity dot <b>only if he makes a deliberate choice to attempt an Embrace</b>. (The troupe should exercise some common sense and avoid \u201caccidental\u201d Embraces achieved through <b>ridiculous contortions of events</b>.)&quot;<br /> <br /> The last part refers to engineering &quot;accidental&quot; Embraces to avoid the cost while still willingly Embracing someone. Otherwise it's black on white that posthumous Embraces doesn't cost a Humanity dot. In my first post I even specified the accidental part even though posthumous Embraces are considered accidental by default by the book (as per my first quote). I even emphasised the accidental part in my second post to make it clearer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1304795#post1304795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it proves your character doesn't just lose Humanity for things they don't know they did. The same way one doesn't degenerate if they did something that would otherwise warrant a check while under the effects of Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say no but your &quot;counterpoint&quot; is the very foundation to my argument. If you don't lose Humanity unless you know you're committing the Embrace, it means that the Humanity loss is your response to committing the Embrace, and not a metaphysical requirement (as opposed to mechanical requirement for gameplay purposes; also the phrasing used in my first post).<br /> <br /> It feels like you either misread my posts or had a knee jerk reaction and defaulted to disagreeing with me. Considering you had to check if hell froze over last time you did agree with me I'd put my money on the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T18:49:10-07:00","id":1305181,"title":"","content":"I'm sure I'm just missing something stupid, but: how does being in a grapple affect you Defense? If character A is being grappled by character B, do they get their defense against character C's attacks? Moreover, if character D tries to shoot character A, they receive a -4 penalty due to the grapple -- but if they're also within close-combat range, does character A also get a Defense equal to the gun's size+1 (from the Firearms in Close Combat section)? Thanks for everyone's help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T20:10:41-07:00","id":1305192,"title":"","content":"* Defense is only hampered by the hold maneuvers (neither grappler has defense during a hold) <br /> <br /> When you are immobilized there are two types<br /> Immobilized with Bindings <br /> Immobilized with Grapple<br /> (No MV. No Def, No Actions)<br /> <br /> * Yes character D suffers - 4<br /> <br /> * Character A gets all the benefits and rules of Defense unless denied his defense (Invisibility, Immobilized, Fast Effects,)<br /> <br /> * Yes Character A gets a Defense of Gun Size +1<br /> <br /> My CoD Action Lists are here<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1296225-cod-action-sheet\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1296225-cod-action-sheet\"> CoD Action Sheet - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1296225-cod-action-sheet\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1296225-cod-action-sheet </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Please see below a Chronicles of Darkness Action Sheet that I typed up from my handwritten notes. I plan on posted the next version which I used with an alter version of CoD using successes instead of dice pool reductions. Here are Google Drive files (https://drive.google.com/open?id=1OrDGeIyME-LMURBiHD5bY3MFFno27m9d) as well. Best Regards Chronicles of Darkness Actions Instant (Standard or Action) Move (Speed in yards or meters) Reflexive Free (Like speaking) Attack Actions Melee (Str + Weaponry &ndash; Defense) Ranged (Dex + Archery/Firearms | No Defense) Thrown (Dex + Athletics &ndash; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T22:33:51-07:00","id":1305207,"title":"","content":"I know ghouls don't get knocked out from bashing damage in 2e but do they also downgrade normal lethal to bashing? If it does could someone tell me where in the books it says that? I've been looking for a while and can't seem to find any reference to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24063-admiral-cheesecake","name":"Admiral Cheesecake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T23:06:01-07:00","id":1305210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Admiral Cheesecake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305207#post1305207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know ghouls don't get knocked out from bashing damage in 2e but do they also downgrade normal lethal to bashing? If it does could someone tell me where in the books it says that? I've been looking for a while and can't seem to find any reference to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they don't as they are still alive. Just dead corpse downgrade lethal to bashing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T03:14:51-07:00","id":1305224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305192#post1305192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">helpful stuff here</div> </div> </div> </div>awesome, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T06:03:23-07:00","id":1305249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305192#post1305192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Defense is only hampered by the hold maneuvers (neither grappler has defense during a hold)<br /> <br /> When you are immobilized there are two types<br /> Immobilized with Bindings<br /> Immobilized with Grapple<br /> (No MV. No Def, No Actions)<br /> <br /> * Yes character D suffers - 4<br /> <br /> * Character A gets all the benefits and rules of Defense unless denied his defense (Invisibility, Immobilized, Fast Effects,)<br /> <br /> * Yes Character A gets a Defense of Gun Size +1<br /> <br /> My CoD Action Lists are here<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1296225-cod-action-sheet\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...d-action-sheet</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have a question related to this:<br /> <br /> How does CofD prevent &quot;kiting&quot; with a firearm, e.g. walking away from your melee opponent before shooting, to avoid that pesky melee/defense penalty?<br /> <br /> In other systems, you have a so-called &quot;attack of opportunity&quot; to make &quot;kiting&quot; as a ranged combatant less ideal, but CofD doesn't have that, so how do I deal with players who try to &quot;cheese&quot; the system by using their Move action to create some distance from their melee opponent and then using their Instant action to shoot without penalties?<br /> <br /> Would still applying that melee penalty on their firearms attack if they <i>start</i> their turn in melee be a good solution? Or does the combat system in CofD already have a different solution?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T07:53:11-07:00","id":1305267,"title":"","content":"Use the range penalties. Firing at medium range is -2 and firing from beyond the gun's long range reduces the attack to a chance dice. <br /> <br /> Firing from close range to avoid penalties in most cases means someone can still move close enough to hit back. <br /> <br /> Implement penalties for firing while moving proportional to how quickly they move. (Despite Hollywood bullshit, it's actually extremely difficult.)<br /> <br /> Have the melee character pull out a gun and shoot back. <br /> <br /> Have the melee character use their brain and move the opposite direction or take cover. Then you can use concealment penalties too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T07:58:46-07:00","id":1305270,"title":"","content":"There's no built in solution, no.<br /> If comes up naturally in the game I'd probably just keep the penalty only if the melee opponent intends to follow the character on their initiative. Especially if they haven't used their movement this turn. Keep in mind that walking sway from an opponent might not be possible without losing LoS depending on the environment.<br /> If someone tries to intentionally cheese it I'd just tell them to cut it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T09:05:34-07:00","id":1305276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305267#post1305267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use the range penalties. Firing at medium range is -2 and firing from beyond the gun's long range reduces the attack to a chance dice. <br /> <br /> Firing from close range to avoid penalties in most cases means someone can still move close enough to hit back. <br /> <br /> Implement penalties for firing while moving proportional to how quickly they move. (Despite Hollywood bullshit, it's actually extremely difficult.)<br /> <br /> Have the melee character pull out a gun and shoot back. <br /> <br /> Have the melee character use their brain and move the opposite direction or take cover. Then you can use concealment penalties too.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how to determine such penalities due to someone that is mooving? Could be valuable to have the target roll dex+atlethics with successes to be used as shooter penalities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T09:45:40-07:00","id":1305283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305249#post1305249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have a question related to this:<br /> <br /> How does CofD prevent &quot;kiting&quot; with a firearm, e.g. walking away from your melee opponent before shooting, to avoid that pesky melee/defense penalty?<br /> <br /> In other systems, you have a so-called &quot;attack of opportunity&quot; to make &quot;kiting&quot; as a ranged combatant less ideal, but CofD doesn't have that, so how do I deal with players who try to &quot;cheese&quot; the system by using their Move action to create some distance from their melee opponent and then using their Instant action to shoot without penalties?<br /> <br /> Would still applying that melee penalty on their firearms attack if they <i>start</i> their turn in melee be a good solution? Or does the combat system in CofD already have a different solution?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted and Storypath do a contested disengage with Athletics I believe, which I really like. I believe they do the same thing with standing from prone while enemies are in close range. Any use of Celebrity speed I would bypass the contest unless the enemy was supernatural and then I would allow Celebrity to be added to the contest dice. <br /> <br /> I have played D&amp;D and White Wolf/Storyteller all my like and the 3.5 Attack of Opportunity almost ruined me, 4.0 was OK, 5.0 is good for me. In 3.5 if you stand on one leg holding your weapon at a 45 degree angle your opponent gets a AoO and don't get me started on Grappling. Sorry couple of hot buttons. <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 04-16-2019, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T09:59:55-07:00","id":1305289,"title":"","content":"I do that if the target is moving to avoid getting shot but I was actually referencing penalties for the shooter moving and shooting at a stationary or mostly stationary target which has nothing to do with the target\u2019s reflexes or lack thereof and due entirely to the fact that most people are trained to fire guns optimally while being stationary. -1 per yard if they are slowly walking directly towards or away, -3 per yard if jogging or running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T16:34:34-07:00","id":1305353,"title":"","content":"If the target is stationary then there is no kiting involved. If the target is chasing the shooter then the target is not stationary.<br /> Remember that the turn system is intended to make real-time combat manageable at the table. If this is becoming a problem at your table then I would suggest that until the chasee gives up following the shooter, then they would still be considered in melee combat for the purposes of defender getting to use his defense.<br /> Of course these aren't whiteroom fights so the shooter would likely run out of space after a short time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T17:22:59-07:00","id":1305356,"title":"","content":"Creating a bloodline. Just so I understand it I need (in addition to the theme elements aka fluff):<br /> + Four disciplines; don't have to align with parent clan.<br /> + A gift.<br /> + A bane, that goes with the clan bane. i.e bloodline members have two banes, clan and bloodline.<br /> Is this correct?<br /> <br /> Additionally, would you consider a gift that allows one to use physical intensity on mental attributes acceptable?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T17:35:12-07:00","id":1305358,"title":"","content":"In general, yes but I've made bloodlines that didn't get 4 &quot;in clan&quot; disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T18:23:59-07:00","id":1305365,"title":"","content":"Oh, additionally, should signature disciplines be included? Would a Ventrue bloodline gaining Auspex be balance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T18:35:46-07:00","id":1305369,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to counter Obfuscate? I thought Animalism could due to the wording of Obfuscate not including animals when it clearly makes the distinction between people, objects &amp; animals but my ST does not agree with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T18:42:51-07:00","id":1305370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305369#post1305369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to counter Obfuscate? I thought Animalism could due to the wording of Obfuscate not including animals when it clearly makes the distinction between people, objects &amp; animals but my ST does not agree with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean besides Auspex?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T19:09:27-07:00","id":1305376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305369#post1305369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to counter Obfuscate? I thought Animalism could due to the wording of Obfuscate not including animals when it clearly makes the distinction between people, objects &amp; animals but my ST does not agree with me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In first edition animals could be used to counter Obfuscate as animals were expressly stated to be immune to its applications. (As were children and the insane because they are used to seeing things that nobody else does.) But since animals also normally avoided vampires by default, ghouling them or using Animalism were the only ways to reliably control them.<br /> <br /> As per the current iteration, by the book itself, a high perception skill can currently detect Obfuscated characters or objects (There are several merits that can do this.) but not cancel it. Obfuscate penalizes perception rolls, it doesn't cancel them. Also, if you are targeted by Obfuscate, you are immune to that Obfuscate user's other applications of Obfuscate. Depending on how you phrase Auspex questions at certain levels, it can also undermine Obfuscate. Successfully Lashing Out on the Obfuscate user breaks all applications of Obfuscate they have running.<br /> <br /> Whether or not animals see through Obfuscate currently is up to the ST, if he says no, then it doesn't.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T20:23:05-07:00","id":1305389,"title":"","content":"In 2ed Obfuscate is generically stated as removing vampire from perception. I'd say Animals are included. <br /> Anyone can try to detect an obfuscated vampire by INDIRECT clues. That's meaning, if you succed the prolonged roll, you will be aware of the very current vampire's position but you still do not see him. I would allow such roll just if the character is aware that an obfuscated is in the area or if he has reasons to guess it. If you manage to perceive the vampire presence either by indirect clues or Auspex, you can then lash out to try to shatter his obfuscate power being then able to see him.<br /> <br /> Note that if someone using obfuscate 3 is attacking someone else in a crowd, Obfuscate will continue to work on anyone but the person being attacked. So others witnesses would just see someone fighting/being pulled away with/by void.<br /> <br /> Auspex 1 is definitely enough to ask if someone using obfuscate is here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T04:06:21-07:00","id":1305428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305389#post1305389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2ed Obfuscate is generically stated as removing vampire from perception. I'd say Animals are included.<br /> Anyone can try to detect an obfuscated vampire by INDIRECT clues. That's meaning, if you succed the prolonged roll, you will be aware of the very current vampire's position but you still do not see him. I would allow such roll just if the character is aware that an obfuscated is in the area or if he has reasons to guess it. If you manage to perceive the vampire presence either by indirect clues or Auspex, you can then lash out to try to shatter his obfuscate power being then able to see him.<br /> <br /> Note that if someone using obfuscate 3 is attacking someone else in a crowd, Obfuscate will continue to work on anyone but the person being attacked. So others witnesses would just see someone fighting/being pulled away with/by void.<br /> <br /> Auspex 1 is definitely enough to ask if someone using obfuscate is here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To add to this for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25190_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25190\" data-vbnamecard=\"25190\">Hogsy</a> :<br /> <br /> With Obfuscate 2 you can extend your Obfuscate effects to other items and people, so if you plan on attacking someone in a crowd while Obfuscated with Obfuscate 3, it's probably smart to spend a Vitae to obfuscate them with Touch of Shadow, which allows the others to roll a Wits + Composure minus your Obfuscate dots, but if they fail that roll, they do not notice what is happening, and you can torment your victim without anyone around him realizing what is going on.<br /> <br /> If you want to go even further, you could even spend two Vitae instead of just one to have your victim vanish completely (just like yourself), rather than just being overlooked, but I'm not 100% certain if that's allowed if you follow the rules as written (do you perhaps know, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> ?).<br /> <br /> As for animals and Obfuscate: I'd say animals see through Obfuscate 1, Face in the Crowd, but not Obfuscate 3, Cloak of Night. Why I say this? Because Obfuscate 1 merely makes you look like nobody important, it doesn't completely hide you from sight, it just makes you look uninteresting, and the effects of Face in the Crowd will cease to mask your presence the moment you do anything to draw attention to yourself or you're unexpected. Of course, what draws a human's attention is not the same thing as what draws a dog's attention. While a human wouldn't be bothered by the mailman entering his front garden to deliver the mail, his dog might be.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for how to counter Obfuscate:<br /> <br /> If you have Auspex, use that to find the obfuscated vampire. <br /> <br /> If you have Resilience, you might try to outlast your obfuscated enemy. If he attacks you, he will no longer be obfuscated. This is when you can use your Lashing Out ability to shatter his Obfuscate. If you are successful, he can no longer affect you with Obfuscate for that scene. If Lashing Out fails or isn't an option, he can go invisible again by spending another Vitae, but you can keep tanking his hits with Resilience, meaning he'll eventually give up or run out of Vitae, while you try to track him down.<br /> <br /> If you're with a group, I highly recommend you work together as a team with assist rolls to track the obfuscated vampire down. You will lose a couple of turns this way, but once you figure out the location of the vampire, you can all try to Lash Out against him. Only one person needs to win that contest to shatter the Obfuscate effect and then everyone can see the vampire. Keep in mind that if multiple people Lash Out against the obfuscated vampire, you will start to get penalties on your Lashing Out rolls, but it's still worth trying, if nothing else, because it will cost the obfuscated vampire a lot of Willpower to keep counter-lashing (unless he has higher Blood Potency).<br /> <br /> If you have Celerity and you're being attacked by someone obfuscated, it might be worth it to interrupt his attack with a grapple, but you can only do this if you are aware that you're being attacked. If you fail to notice the surprise attack, you aren't allowed to use Celerity to interrupt. Once you have the vampire in a grapple, he can't go invisible and run as long as you keep control over the grapple.<br /> <br /> If you have Majesty, you can try to use Awe and some Social rolls to persuade the obfuscated vampire to either stand down, run away, or face you like a man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-17-2019, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T05:14:01-07:00","id":1305441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305428#post1305428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for how to counter Obfuscate:<br /> <br /> If you're alone and you have no access to Auspex or Resilience, I'd say you best run. If you have Auspex, use that to find the obfuscated vampire. If you have Resilience, you might try to outlast your obfuscated enemy. If he attacks you, he will no longer be obfuscated. This is when you can use your Lashing Out ability to shatter his Obfuscate. If you are successful, he can no longer affect you with Obfuscate for that scene. If Lashing Out fails or isn't an option, he can go invisible again by spending another Vitae, but you can keep tanking his hits with Resilience, meaning he'll eventually give up or run out of Vitae, while you try to track him down.<br /> <br /> If you're with a group, I highly recommend you work together as a team with assist rolls to track the obfuscated vampire down. You will lose a couple of turns this way, but once you figure out the location of the vampire, you can all try to Lash Out against him. Only one person needs to win that contest to shatter the Obfuscate effect and then everyone can see the vampire. Keep in mind that if multiple people Lash Out against the obfuscated vampire, you will start to get penalties on your Lashing Out rolls, but it's still worth trying, if nothing else, because it will cost the obfuscated vampire a lot of Willpower to keep counter-lashing (unless he has higher Blood Potency).<br /> <br /> If you have Celerity and you're being attacked by someone obfuscated, it might be worth it to interrupt his attack with a grapple, but you can only do this if you are aware that you're being attacked. If you fail to notice the surprise attack, you aren't allowed to use Celerity to interrupt. Once you have the vampire in a grapple, he can't go invisible and run as long as you keep control over the grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is that I can't use my Resilience if the Obfuscated vampire (cloak of night + face in the crowd) surprises me with a stake. I didn't know about Lashing Out (still new to the game) and suddenly the Cutthroat merit seems like a good choice. The other idea I had to counter an obfuscated character was to learn Obfuscate 1 myself in order to be able to hide my Beast, use Protean to turn into a Dog and hide with a pack of dogs that I'm manipulating through Animalism. It's a costly (vitae-wise) tactic but seems very doable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T05:39:55-07:00","id":1305447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305441#post1305441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My problem is that I can't use my Resilience if the Obfuscated vampire (cloak of night + face in the crowd) surprises me with a stake. I didn't know about Lashing Out (still new to the game) and suddenly the Cutthroat merit seems like a good choice. The other idea I had to counter an obfuscated character was to learn Obfuscate 1 myself in order to be able to hide my Beast, use Protean to turn into a Dog and hide with a pack of dogs that I'm manipulating through Animalism. It's a costly (vitae-wise) tactic but seems very doable.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can use Resilience in a preventive way. You can, on your own turn, activate the active effect of Resilience, and when you're being attacked on the enemy's turn, you can subtract your Resilience + 1 from the total damage done to you.<br /> <br /> That being said, personally I always allow my players to use Resilience immediately after the damage has been dealt, even if that damage is dealt through a surprise attack. I'm not sure if that's RAW, but that's how I do it.<br /> <br /> So how it goes when dealing with a surprise attack::<br /> <br /> Beginning of the surprise attack action -&gt; player gets to roll a Wits + Composure - Obfuscate to notice the surprise attack -&gt; enemy rolls attack with or without calculating for the player's defense (depending on the result of his Wits + Composure roll) -&gt; attack's damage is declared to the player -&gt; player chooses to remove/downgrade damage with the active effect of Resilience -&gt; player updates his Health track with the remaining damage -&gt; end of action.<br /> <br /> When dealing with a stake, the player character falls into torpor if he's still left with 5 damage from the attack <i>after</i> using Resilience.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would like the opinion of other people on this though. How does everyone else handle Resilience? Do you allow players to use it after the damage from the attack has been declared or only before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T05:40:02-07:00","id":1305448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305428#post1305428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To add to this for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25190_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25190\" data-vbnamecard=\"25190\">Hogsy</a> :<br /> <br /> With Obfuscate 2 you can extend your Obfuscate effects to other items and people, so if you plan on attacking someone in a crowd while Obfuscated with Obfuscate 3, it's probably smart to spend a Vitae to obfuscate them with Touch of Shadow, which allows the others to roll a Wits + Composure minus your Obfuscate dots, but if they fail that roll, they do not notice what is happening, and you can torment your victim without anyone around him realizing what is going on.<br /> <br /> If you want to go even further, you could even spend two Vitae instead of just one to have your victim vanish completely (just like yourself), rather than just being overlooked, but I'm not 100% certain if that's allowed if you follow the rules as written (do you perhaps know, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7079_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7079\" data-vbnamecard=\"7079\">Marcus</a> ?).<br /> <br /> As for animals and Obfuscate: I'd say animals see through Obfuscate 1, Face in the Crowd, but not Obfuscate 3, Cloak of Night. Why I say this? Because Obfuscate 1 merely makes you look like nobody important, it doesn't completely hide you from sight, it just makes you look uninteresting, and the effects of Face in the Crowd will cease to mask your presence the moment you do anything to draw attention to yourself or you're unexpected. Of course, what draws a human's attention is not the same thing as what draws a dog's attention. While a human wouldn't be bothered by the mailman entering his front garden to deliver the mail, his dog might be.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for how to counter Obfuscate:<br /> <br /> If you have Auspex, use that to find the obfuscated vampire.<br /> <br /> If you have Resilience, you might try to outlast your obfuscated enemy. If he attacks you, he will no longer be obfuscated. This is when you can use your Lashing Out ability to shatter his Obfuscate. If you are successful, he can no longer affect you with Obfuscate for that scene. If Lashing Out fails or isn't an option, he can go invisible again by spending another Vitae, but you can keep tanking his hits with Resilience, meaning he'll eventually give up or run out of Vitae, while you try to track him down.<br /> <br /> If you're with a group, I highly recommend you work together as a team with assist rolls to track the obfuscated vampire down. You will lose a couple of turns this way, but once you figure out the location of the vampire, you can all try to Lash Out against him. Only one person needs to win that contest to shatter the Obfuscate effect and then everyone can see the vampire. Keep in mind that if multiple people Lash Out against the obfuscated vampire, you will start to get penalties on your Lashing Out rolls, but it's still worth trying, if nothing else, because it will cost the obfuscated vampire a lot of Willpower to keep counter-lashing (unless he has higher Blood Potency).<br /> <br /> If you have Celerity and you're being attacked by someone obfuscated, it might be worth it to interrupt his attack with a grapple, but you can only do this if you are aware that you're being attacked. If you fail to notice the surprise attack, you aren't allowed to use Celerity to interrupt. Once you have the vampire in a grapple, he can't go invisible and run as long as you keep control over the grapple.<br /> <br /> If you have Majesty, you can try to use Awe and some Social rolls to persuade the obfuscated vampire to either stand down, run away, or face you like a man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate 3 applied in combo with 2 does not allow the touched to become invisible. It just allow to use te first power on other people. The second itself just allow to make unnoticed Object and animals but no people.<br /> Furthermore I don't see any distinction between animals and People from any of Obfuscate powers. So I would rules the same for both of them.<br /> <br /> Furthermore you can't interrupt a surprise attack with celerity. Sorry XD In order to interrupt you need to be aware of the attack, and an obfuscated vampire is most probably performing a surprise attack.<br /> <br /> With Majesty you can just make him a friend and go to have a bloody beer togheter. You don't need to convince him to face yourself. <br /> <br /> I would suggest to be creative dealing with Obfiscate. Use a fire extinguisher to get hig bonuses on tracking him through indirect clues. Activate the fire protection system for the main purpose. Throw flour, sands, whatever on the floor. Each of these methods should provide you from +3 to +5 in tracking him out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T05:48:33-07:00","id":1305449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305448#post1305448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore you can't interrupt a surprise attack with celerity. Sorry XD In order to interrupt you need to be aware of the attack, and an obfuscated vampire is most probably performing a surprise attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that. But a surprise attack allows for a Wits + Composure - Obfuscate perception check. If you succeed on the perception check, you get to add your defense against the surprise attack like normal. In that case, I would also allow for a Celerity interrupt. But if you fail that perception check, then yeah, Celerity isn't going to help you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305448#post1305448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Majesty you can just make him a friend and go to have a bloody beer togheter. You don't need to convince him to face yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Awe works, though if you have Idol, the obfuscated vampire must succeed on a Resolve + Blood Potency - Majesty before he's allowed to attack you, so that's pretty useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-17-2019, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T06:45:20-07:00","id":1305457,"title":"","content":"How does losing humanity 'feel' when you embrace? I have a game in the making where both players picked Ventrue and, as such, I am considering a single sire for both. How would doing the deed twice differ from once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T07:03:25-07:00","id":1305458,"title":"","content":"1. Resilience is a big middle finger to staking attempts. At Resilience 4, you can laugh at staking attempts unless they're capable of churning out 10+ damage in a single turn with an improvised weapon. Go back and reread the entry for Resilience.<br /> 2. He has to touch you to use Face in the Crowd on you. You get a resist for that.<br /> 3. If he uses Face of the Crowd on your character, you character is not affected by his Cloak of Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T08:40:38-07:00","id":1305486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305449#post1305449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm aware of that. But a surprise attack allows for a Wits + Composure - Obfuscate perception check. If you succeed on the perception check, you get to add your defense against the surprise attack like normal. In that case, I would also allow for a Celerity interrupt. But if you fail that perception check, then yeah, Celerity isn't going to help you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's not how Awe works, though if you have Idol, the obfuscated vampire must succeed on a Resolve + Blood Potency - Majesty before he's allowed to attack you, so that's pretty useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Agree about obfuscate. I was talking about Surprise attacks indeed. If the victim spots the attack it's not a surprise attack by default anymore <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. We were talking about generic Majesty not just awe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> If we have to stay with awe I'd tend to agree with you: the best you can obtain is a presence roll where the attacker, if he lose the contested, let's say as example: presence+composure/expression vs resolve+ composure, could considere his victim too good or important to deserve to be attacked at all. Otherwise no chance at all with awe as it just boost presence rolls (the very superficial impression) not manipulation ones (read as: you have no bonus in convincing him talking) if not a better first impression to be used in a Social manouvre that still is not useful, as it requires long time, in a combat context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T08:49:59-07:00","id":1305488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305486#post1305486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Agree about obfuscate. I was talking about Surprise attacks indeed. If the victim spots the attack it's not a surprise attack by default anymore <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 2. We were talking about generic Majesty not just awe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> If we have to stay with awe I'd tend to agree with you: the best you can obtain is a presence roll where the attacker, if he lose the contested, let's say as example: presence+composure/expression vs resolve+ composure, could considere his victim too good or important to deserve to be attacked at all. Otherwise no chance at all with awe as it just boost presence rolls (the very superficial impression) not manipulation ones (read as: you have no bonus in convincing him talking) if not a better first impression to be used in a Social manouvre that still is not useful, as it requires long time, in a combat context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to use anything else but Awe, you need to be aware of the person affected by your Awe and need to be able to &quot;connect&quot; with him, else I wouldn't allow the Majesty user to use Confidant. For Confidant to make sense, the Majesty user has to be able to &quot;charm&quot; his victim with kind words, a soft voice, a passionate look, or a gentle touch. That might be difficult if you're dealing with someone who's obfuscated and you have no idea where he is and how he's reacting.<br /> <br /> But if you can come up with a clever way to work around your lack of direct contact with that pesky Obfuscate user, then hell yeah, use Confidant and turn him into your bro, that's also a good way to deal with Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T09:08:11-07:00","id":1305493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305488#post1305488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, to use anything else but Awe, you need to be aware of the person affected by your Awe and need to be able to &amp;quot;connect&amp;quot; with him, else I wouldn't allow the Majesty user to use Confidant. For Confidant to make sense, the Majesty user has to be able to &amp;quot;charm&amp;quot; his victim with kind words, a soft voice, a passionate look, or a gentle touch. That might be difficult if you're dealing with someone who's obfuscated and you have no idea where he is and how he's reacting.<br /> <br /> But if you can come up with a clever way to work around your lack of direct contact with that pesky Obfuscate user, then hell yeah, use Confidant and turn him into your bro, that's also a good way to deal with Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are difinitely right. I was considering Awe as an area effect but actually Confidant it's not. So yes. Just awe could be applicable in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T13:17:41-07:00","id":1305540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305365#post1305365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, additionally, should signature disciplines be included? Would a Ventrue bloodline gaining Auspex be balance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes many bloodlines use the special Discipline of different clans. (Auspex, Dominate, Protean, Nightmare, Majesty)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T03:43:55-07:00","id":1305680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305458#post1305458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Resilience is a big middle finger to staking attempts. At Resilience 4, you can laugh at staking attempts unless they're capable of churning out 10+ damage in a single turn with an improvised weapon. Go back and reread the entry for Resilience.<br /> 2. He has to touch you to use Face in the Crowd on you. You get a resist for that.<br /> 3. If he uses Face of the Crowd on your character, you character is not affected by his Cloak of Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the passive power of Resilience reduces the Aggra damage you suffer by an amount equal to your Dots, but I don't get a reflexive action when I am surprised, do I? I won't be able to use the active power that works against fire and other banes (reduce damage by amount equal to Res dots) and specifically targetted body parts. Cloak of Night is merely an upgrade of Face in the Crowd. They spend 1 blood and now they are invisible to the perception of others (except those they choose), so you need a Mehket to reliably find an obfuscated vampire 'cause even if it attacks a group, only the victim of the attack can lash out and chances are they won't be surviving the surprise round (stake vs 0 defense, yeah hi).<br /> <br /> My question is whether general armor blocks steak damage. It does not mention anywhere that it doesn't but I've been told that it completely ignores it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T05:04:55-07:00","id":1305694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305680#post1305680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the passive power of Resilience reduces the Aggra damage you suffer by an amount equal to your Dots, but I don't get a reflexive action when I am surprised, do I? I won't be able to use the active power that works against fire and other banes (reduce damage by amount equal to Res dots) and specifically targetted body parts. Cloak of Night is merely an upgrade of Face in the Crowd. They spend 1 blood and now they are invisible to the perception of others (except those they choose), so you need a Mehket to reliably find an obfuscated vampire 'cause even if it attacks a group, only the victim of the attack can lash out and chances are they won't be surviving the surprise round (stake vs 0 defense, yeah hi).<br /> <br /> My question is whether general armor blocks steak damage. It does not mention anywhere that it doesn't but I've been told that it completely ignores it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You get to use reflexive actions in response to something happening and since many resistance rolls are reflexive, they would not work otherwise.<br /> General armor on the chest absolutely blocks stake damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T05:09:04-07:00","id":1305697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305680#post1305680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the passive power of Resilience reduces the Aggra damage you suffer by an amount equal to your Dots, but I don't get a reflexive action when I am surprised, do I? I won't be able to use the active power that works against fire and other banes (reduce damage by amount equal to Res dots) and specifically targetted body parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither of those effects are relevant. It's the active effect that decreases non-Bane damage by Resilience dots+1. <s>You're right about it not being possible to activate in <i>successful</i> surprise attacks, but not all attempts are successful.<br /> (Activating Resilience in anticipation of a surprise attack would be a very rare situation since it requires both knowing the attack is coming to the point where you're okay potentially wasting a Vitae while still not having seen through Obfuscate.)</s> See below.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305680#post1305680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and chances are they won't be surviving the surprise round (stake vs 0 defense, yeah hi).</div> </div> </div> </div>You still need to roll at least five successes while also taking a -3 penalty for targeting the heart. Without Vigor that would require having a base Strength+Weaponry dice pool of <i>18</i> before you can reliably stake someone more often than not. Vigor does dramatically reduce the necessary dice pool depending on how many dots you have, though, at the cost of one Vitae that turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305680#post1305680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is whether general armor blocks steak damage. It does not mention anywhere that it doesn't but I've been told that it completely ignores it.</div> </div> </div> </div>General armor is effective against <i>all</i> weapons unless stated otherwise. Whoever told you differently must've house ruled staking or just made up something on the spot. Nothing in the rules comes even close to suggesting that stakes would work different from any other weapon in that regard.<br /> It might've been a situation where the vampire was already incapacitated and it was a killing blow that ignores armor, but that's its own thing and not dependent on whether you use a stake or not.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305694#post1305694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You get to use reflexive actions in response to something happening and since many resistance rolls are reflexive, they would not work otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually true. Surprise attacks nullifies your instant action for that turn and Defense specifically. Any other reflexive actions are okay as long as they don't specifically say you can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-18-2019, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T07:02:51-07:00","id":1305721,"title":"","content":"If you use <s>Facebook</s> <b>Face</b> in the Crowd to pickpocket someone, would you use rules for violence (victim can see you as normal) or would they have to make a Wits + Composure - Obfuscate roll?<br /> <br /> Edit: Or do they just straight up not notice? My impulse is to have the thief roll Dex + Larceny or Wits + Stealth and on a failure the victim makes a perception roll penalized by dots in Obfuscate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":".  autocorrect is the worst. 04-18-2019, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T07:14:46-07:00","id":1305722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305721#post1305721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use Facebook in the Crowd to pickpocket someone, would you use rules for violence (victim can see you as normal) or would they have to make a Wits + Composure - Obfuscate roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pickpocketing someone without them noticing is an opposed roll. If the vampires succeeds with that roll the victim doesn't get to roll at all since they wouldn't notice them anyway and no roll to pierce Face in the Crowd. Otherwise they'd technically have to roll Wits+Composure-Obfuscate after the first roll to actually see the pickpocket when noticing that they're being pickpocketed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T17:28:06-07:00","id":1305857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305680#post1305680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the passive power of Resilience reduces the Aggra damage you suffer by an amount equal to your Dots, but I don't get a reflexive action when I am surprised, do I? I won't be able to use the active power that works against fire and other banes (reduce damage by amount equal to Res dots) and specifically targetted body parts. Cloak of Night is merely an upgrade of Face in the Crowd. They spend 1 blood and now they are invisible to the perception of others (except those they choose), so you need a Mehket to reliably find an obfuscated vampire 'cause even if it attacks a group, only the victim of the attack can lash out and chances are they won't be surviving the surprise round (stake vs 0 defense, yeah hi).<br /> <br /> My question is whether general armor blocks steak damage. It does not mention anywhere that it doesn't but I've been told that it completely ignores it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes armor works against stakes.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T17:37:23-07:00","id":1305859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305722#post1305722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Somehow I quoted the wrong post or person not sure. I am going to bed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the same question regarding reflexive actions and surprise. I currently allow reflexive action during surprise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any character who fails the roll cannot take an action in the first turn of combat, and can\u2019t apply defense for that turn. Determine Initiative in the second turn as normal. </div> </div> </div>The bolded line is what I am currently leaning, but I did have some doubt concerning it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A reflexive action is the sort of thing you don\u2019t even need to think about doing. Most rolls to resist supernatural powers are reflexive. <b> You can take a reflexive action at any time</b> , and it doesn\u2019t take your turn in combat. </div> </div> </div>Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 04-18-2019, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T00:58:02-07:00","id":1305926,"title":"","content":"Active Resilence effect can be activated whenever in the turn, also to address a surprise attack as it is reflexive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T17:38:50-07:00","id":1306117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1305721#post1305721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use <b>Facebook</b> <s>Face</s> in the Crowd to pickpocket someone, would you use rules for violence (victim can see you as normal) or would they have to make a Wits + Composure - Obfuscate roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely a contested action. The vampire would roll Wits + Computers + Obfuscate vs Wits + Composure. Nevertheless, really neat devotion. The Carthians come up with some weird powers.... :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T18:56:14-07:00","id":1306711,"title":"","content":"I really can't figure how Lashing Out works. I can't understand when it would be used or required.<br /> <br /> Could make me some examples of social situations where two vampires Lash out? Even using different aspects of the Beast?<br /> <br /> Should I use Lashing Out when a characters is intimidating another character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T20:09:20-07:00","id":1306727,"title":"","content":"A recent one I ran:<br /> <br /> <i>Harpy, in the middle of Elysium</i>: Miss Williams showed an appalling lack of subtlety in this matter, and if anyone believes she deserves to remain in our city, I invite them to speak up now. <i>[lashes out with Competitive at her target]</i><br /> <i>Miss Williams</i>: You think you can hide behind your pretty words and not face consequences for them? If you want to fight, step outside and let's go. <i>[lashes back with Bestial]</i><br /> <br /> Here, the Harpy's trying to make Miss Williams get overconfident and set herself up to fail, proving the Harpy's point and giving more evidence for why she should be exiled. Williams on the other hand is trying to push the Harpy into a different arena, where Strength will be more useful\u2014or break the rules of Elysium by attacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T20:27:52-07:00","id":1306733,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s used in scenarios where a vampire may want to assert a level of supernatural dominance without resorting to flinging disciplines. Or when they suspect another vampire is using disciplines on them with the intention of assaulting or manipulating them supernaturally.<br /> <br /> One scenario, Stephanie (5 Int. BP 2. Cutthroat merit) was meeting with two other kindred (Gina and Doug) who wanted to finalize a commission they ordered from her for an architectural project. They were meeting at the lobby of a convention center/elysium established for formal business meetings. A Crone elder (Elsbeth) arrived in the middle of their meeting and demanded to speak with Stephanie about commissioning her for a project. When Doug (Str 3 BP 2) spoke up to object to the interruption, Elsbeth immediately Lashed Out with her Monstrous Beast (Str 3. BP 6). She snapped that his dick didn\u2019t entitle him to anything and if he didn\u2019t shut the fuck up, she\u2019d rip it off and feed it to him. (4 successes). Doug opted not to respond (Flight option) so he got up from his seat and let her take it and told Gina he\u2019d wait in the interests of preserving elysium decorum. This immediately pissed off Gina who got up to leave and mildly irritated Stephanie. Not only was this witch bullying her friend but she was also driving away her paying clients. Elsbeth decided that she was going to continue throwing her weight around and Lashed Out against Stephanie using her Seductive Beast (Pres. 4 BP 6) and said she would reimburse her with preferential treatment at her business (she ran a brothel notorious/well known for their orgies) and a boon. (5 successes) Stephanie Lashed Out in response with her Competitive Beast and replied she\u2019d prefer cash paying customers under the circumstances (this elder had reneged on two boons) and she works commissions on a first come first serve basis but if she could win a coin toss she\u2019d listen to her proposal first otherwise she\u2019d have to wait until her prior meeting was finished. (Stephanie got 6 successes due to the Cutthroat merit) Elsbeth lost the toss, threw the quarter at Stephanie (3 Bashing) and stormed out, the incident having been witnessed by several other kindred at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T01:26:41-07:00","id":1306779,"title":"","content":"People before me already have geiven very good examples.<br /> I'd just like to add my two sentences here.<br /> Lashing out it's an act of open violence (not subtle at all). It's evident for anyone when used. So not use it easily in an Elysium or in situation you don't want them to degenerate.<br /> Furthermore, under a more mechanical point of view, you would also like to lash out to prepare to use other powers and discipline as it reduce the successes required to obtain an exceptional success. <br /> You may also want to lash out to achieve a certain grip on that mortal/neonate without using discipline actually. Making him more incline to indulge in his passions when you are tempting him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:14:33-07:00","id":1306933,"title":"","content":"Hello. I've got another question. If someone has a skill that already has 9 again what happens if they then get a merit that also gives them 9 again for that roll?<br /> <br /> Say someone has a weapon with 9-again but then also gets the dot of Professional training that gives them 9-again in an asset skill and that weapon skill is chosen?<br /> <br /> Is it a wasted opportunity? Do they stack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24063-admiral-cheesecake","name":"Admiral Cheesecake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:48:01-07:00","id":1306949,"title":"","content":"If it's two merits giving the 9 again, I'd say they wasted their experience points. If it's a matter of a piece of equipment giving 9 again and the merit giving 9 again, I'd say they have 8 again when they use that skill and that particular piece of equipment simultaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T12:52:09-07:00","id":1306952,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is officially in the book, but I've always ruled that if you get two sources of 9-again it becomes 8-again. If you get a third source, it becomes Rote, then 9-again Rote, then 8-again Rote (which is the maximum possible and is also frankly ridiculous, you don't need anything more than that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:10:27-07:00","id":1307027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Admiral Cheesecake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1306933#post1306933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I've got another question. If someone has a skill that already has 9 again what happens if they then get a merit that also gives them 9 again for that roll?<br /> <br /> Say someone has a weapon with 9-again but then also gets the dot of Professional training that gives them 9-again in an asset skill and that weapon skill is chosen?<br /> <br /> Is it a wasted opportunity? Do they stack?</div> </div> </div> </div>As per the rules: Two 9-Agains doesn't stack unless either sources says that they do (which is rare but I've seen it in Werewolf).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1306952#post1306952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this is officially in the book, but I've always ruled that if you get two sources of 9-again it becomes 8-again. If you get a third source, it becomes Rote, then 9-again Rote, then 8-again Rote (which is the maximum possible and is also frankly ridiculous, you don't need anything more than that).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all house rules (especially how you handle Rote Action as that's separate dice trick unrelated to X-Again). It's not bad house rules unless you play Mage where you'd short out the extra hurdle generally required for Rote Action through spell casting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Note that different dice tricks often means different things.<br /> X-Again is the most common and can represent how you easier get more successes as long as you get successes, meaning it's not easier to hit with heavy weapons that has 9-Again, but when you do hit they tend to score more successes and thus more damage. (It's not perfect due to Dodge rolls, though.)<br /> Rote Action represents doing by rote. Either because everything is drilled into you that you can basically do it blindfolded (like Professional Training) or because you have a manual or map that literally tells you exactly what to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> What does lack any official ruling is what happens when you get 9-Again or 8-Again from one source but remove 10-Again from another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T16:41:03-07:00","id":1307045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1307027#post1307027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What does lack any official ruling is what happens when you get 9-Again or 8-Again from one source but remove 10-Again from another.</div> </div> </div> </div>You reroll a 9 or 8 but don't reroll a 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T17:30:19-07:00","id":1307068,"title":"","content":"Or 9-again and no-10-again cancel out, so you have 10-again and nothing else. Mathematically they're identical, so whichever is easier to remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T11:08:54-07:00","id":1307535,"title":"","content":"Vampires don't regain Willpower from daysleep, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T11:32:26-07:00","id":1307543,"title":"","content":"Rose has gone on record as saying that the intention is that they do not get Willpower from sleep. I believe she also said that it doesn't break anything if you allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T11:55:39-07:00","id":1307549,"title":"","content":"Not by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T19:11:46-07:00","id":1308568,"title":"","content":"Stuff on Dhampirs, made me wonder... how would a Dhampir Child seek influence over their school? ideas how to do so as most of their powers take a lot of thought to use properly.<br /> <br /> Another thing is how to Justify a retainer at a young age<br /> <br /> one idea is curse of aphrodites favor cast on their behalf by their parwents ort at their behest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-29-2019, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T04:59:06-07:00","id":1309409,"title":"","content":"If you have the Acute Senses merit, does it let you add your Blood Potency twice to sensory rolls that already include Blood Potency? For example, all vampires can add their Blood Potency to rolls to detect someone hidden with Obfuscate 3. Does a vampire with Acute Senses get to add their Blood Potency a second time? I think the answer is yes, as it seems appropriate that someone with Acute Senses should be better than average, but I'm not 100% sure if that's correct.<br /> <br /> I'm also assuming that Acute Senses doesn't apply to uses of Auspex, as Auspex doesn't use the 'normal' senses that are boosted by Acute Senses. Is that how other people interpret the merit/discipline interaction?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5233-kathd","name":"KathD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T05:48:49-07:00","id":1309418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KathD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1309409#post1309409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have the Acute Senses merit, does it let you add your Blood Potency twice to sensory rolls that already include Blood Potency? For example, all vampires can add their Blood Potency to rolls to detect someone hidden with Obfuscate 3. Does a vampire with Acute Senses get to add their Blood Potency a second time? I think the answer is yes, as it seems appropriate that someone with Acute Senses should be better than average, but I'm not 100% sure if that's correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems that Acute Senses stacks with Kindred senses (which is what Obfuscate 3 references).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KathD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1309409#post1309409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also assuming that Acute Senses doesn't apply to uses of Auspex, as Auspex doesn't use the 'normal' senses that are boosted by Acute Senses. Is that how other people interpret the merit/discipline interaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex doesn't use your senses at all, except for relaying the information in the answers you get. I would also say no to anything affecting Discipline activation rolls unless it explicitly states it affects Discipline activation rolls or the actual traits used in the dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T06:57:14-07:00","id":1309428,"title":"","content":"Yes you would add Blood Potency again on relevant perception checks. <br /> <br /> Auspex doesn't augment the five senses anymore so you wouldn't use it on perception checks in that respect. You use it to get specific information about a specific victim or specific object or specific place that your five senses wouldn't be able to detect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T07:31:01-07:00","id":1309437,"title":"","content":"If I use Dominate To change someones memories, to keep them from knowing Im using Conditioning on them, does progress of conditioning Survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T07:47:36-07:00","id":1309445,"title":"","content":"Yes. Their memories of what was going on at the time they were being Conditioned is going to correspond to whatever their memories were altered to be. Changing the memories doesn't change the Conditioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-02-2019, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T08:14:54-07:00","id":1309453,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> I'm pretty certain Auspex does boost your traditional five senses.<br /> <br /> When using Auspex in a scene, you multiply the range of your senses by your amount of dots in Auspex. When tasting blood with Auspex active, you gain a +2 dice bonus.<br /> <br /> I'm referring to 'Kindred Senses' and 'A Taste of Blood' on page 90 and 91 of Vampire the Requiem Second Edition.<br /> <br /> The book doesn't explain what &quot;Auspex active&quot; means, but I assume using 'Beast's Hackles' or 'The Spirit's Touch' in that scene counts as activating Auspex for the purposes of determining whether the Kindred's five senses are enhanced or not.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T08:54:36-07:00","id":1309458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1309453#post1309453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using Auspex in a scene, you multiply the range of your senses by your amount of dots in Auspex.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Auspex modifier for Kindred Senses is a permanent boost, not only when you've used Auspex in the scene. Regardless, regular use of Auspex is definitely not based on your senses since it can reveal information that should be completely imperceptible to you. Hence no Acute Senses to Auspex activation rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1309453#post1309453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book doesn't explain what &quot;Auspex active&quot; means, but I assume using 'Beast's Hackles' or 'The Spirit's Touch' in that scene counts as activating Auspex for the purposes of determining whether the Kindred's five senses are enhanced or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the &quot;active Auspex&quot; modifier is a relic from earlier drafts that snuck through editing. Editing is one of OPP's weak points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T10:37:29-07:00","id":1309472,"title":"","content":"You don't roll range for your Mekhet. You are either in range or not in range. In a sense that's an enhancement but it's not anything the player rolls to determine which is what the poster was asking about. And your Mekhet still gets +0 to perception checks unless he's lapping up blood, a flat +2 bonus for tasting blood and only for the purpose of identifying the owner. <br /> <br /> Active means the player spends the vitae or willpower, or uses the reflexive or instant action to activate the power, rolls the dice to determine the results. Since Auspex states every use after the first one in a scene requires vitae to continue using, it's obvious that Auspex doesn't &quot;stay on&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T04:55:04-07:00","id":1309621,"title":"","content":"I was wondering if the +2 L (2 AP) from Horrid Talons overrides the weapon modifiers of a few protean 3 animal forms or if it stacks. On every ability I've seen thus far it states that the weapon becomes a &quot;+X L&quot; weapon, but in this case it states that it gives the weapon a +2 L ( 2 AP) weapon modifier. Does this mean that it would stack with the weapon modifiers granted by animal forms? For example, a Tiger (using 1e animal stats) has +2 L (2 AP) on its claws. Would it stay the same or go up to +4 L (4 AP)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T06:43:52-07:00","id":1309632,"title":"","content":"The plus means it's plus any rolled successes. No weapon damages stack unless explicitly stated that it does.<br /> A vampire in an animal form using Horrid Talons will always get claws that deal +2L, AP2 that doesn't downgrade to bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-04T21:45:56-07:00","id":1309974,"title":"","content":"Question: Does a player have to choose if they want to use the Inspired condition on an action before or after they roll?<br /> For example, when a player rolls and gains 3 successes, can he then choose to resolve the Inspired condition to make it an exceptional success and gain 1 Willpower? Or does the player have to choose to resolve Inspired before the roll is made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T05:17:34-07:00","id":1310021,"title":"","content":"That depends on the ST. If they want all situational modifiers and benefits announced before the roll, you state you are going to have your character use before you roll. If the ST is okay with you rolling and saying \u201cOh I want to resolve the Inspired Condition because it pertains to why my character was Inspired\u201d then you can do that. But no, you don\u2019t get to dictate the ST has to let you modify a roll AFTER you realize you didn\u2019t get the results you wanted from the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T09:22:48-07:00","id":1310044,"title":"","content":"Whats it like being blood bound to someone you hate?<br /> <br /> Whats it like to be a member of the Sanctum Bound to a Acolyte<br /> <br /> KNOWING that what hes done to you is blasphemy but being powerless to do anything but love him<br /> <br /> <br /> Whats it like to be a Extreme Degenerate bound to a more princibled Kindred?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T09:39:30-07:00","id":1310049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1310044#post1310044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats it like being blood bound to someone you hate?<br /> <br /> Whats it like to be a member of the Sanctum Bound to a Acolyte<br /> <br /> KNOWING that what hes done to you is blasphemy but being powerless to do anything but love him<br /> <br /> <br /> Whats it like to be a Extreme Degenerate bound to a more princibled Kindred?</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine falling madly, desperately in love with someone. You know their faith is wrong, you hate them on a deep level, you wish you could get free of them. But the love is overwhelming and you're powerless against it and can't stop thinking how good it makes you feel just being in their presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T15:35:58-07:00","id":1310121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1310044#post1310044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats it like being blood bound to someone you hate?<br /> <br /> Whats it like to be a member of the Sanctum Bound to a Acolyte</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 2nd Corinthians 6:14-15. <br /> <br /> They may pointedly go out of their way to avoid the Acolyte. <br /> <br /> If I were playing the Sanctified, I\u2019d use it as an excuse to proselytize to them at every turn, look for opportunities to entrap them in a mutual vinculum. Ruin their reputation with the other pagans. Instead of slaughtering the regnant for their blasphemy, sabotage their pagan practices at every chance. Attempt to entrap them in a vinculum and view all of it as God putting the character in that position to save the innocent victims and turn the pagan on the right path. (Either convert them or make them regret thinking it was a good idea to try and pervert a devout Sanctified.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T18:22:19-07:00","id":1310161,"title":"","content":"any Valid Reasons to let such a Sanctified Continue to practice his own Religion, and only use him against Belials brood or other Cults of the Circle Who are hostile to you.<br /> <br /> Or Ordo Dracul who want your Holy sites or Artifacts for 'Experiments'<br /> <br /> or Carthians who are Fanatic Seculars.<br /> <br /> <br /> It gives them less circumstances that could justify spending Willpower to go against the blood bond.?<br /> <br /> aught else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T04:18:06-07:00","id":1310260,"title":"","content":"Do you NOT realize that putting someone under a vinculum does not give that person the power to rewrite their victim's personality or grant them immunity to a brutal reprisal by their victim for physical, emotional, and mental abuse. <br /> <br /> I see no valid reason to say the Sanctified will abandon their moral code or religion because of a vinculum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T04:51:21-07:00","id":1310267,"title":"","content":"Given that a full vinculum allows you to attempt a social manoeuvring roll every turn you really could convert them quite easily if you tried just going by game mechanics. That being said it\u2019s also reasonable to say that a individual who is converted from one belief system to its rival would gain some sort of condition to reflect their inner conflict and that players should be given a say in how their character responds to such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T06:10:33-07:00","id":1310273,"title":"","content":"Vinculums don't make unreasonable, morally repugnant, or self destructive requests suddenly possible using Social Maneuvering rules. You also don't get to roll for a week if you created a Hostile impression so it behooves regnants to not conduct themselves like fucksocks and/or go around shitting on the belief systems of their thralls if they actually want them to do something for them.<br /> <br /> And I don't think it's reasonable to say a character is just going to get up one night and embrace a belief system they found abhorrent the night before, no matter how much magic blood gets poured down their throat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T07:35:22-07:00","id":1310282,"title":"","content":"Not without going to actual mind control \u00e0 la Dominate, but that's not what a Vinculum is. A Vinculum manipulates feelings towards the regnant (admittedly quite strongly at the third stage) but it doesn't dictate feelings towards others, nor does it dictate behaviour.<br /> <br /> A regnant does have a much easier time brainwashing their thrall through social manoeuvreing (due to upgrading their impression, and even permanently setting it to perfect at the third stage, making it technically impossible to get a hostile impression) but that requires a lot of effort and successful rolls over a larger period of time. Making completely ludicrous requests instead of gradual persuasion should still just outright fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T15:20:36-07:00","id":1310823,"title":"","content":"Hey all, I'm kind of new to the CoD world and had a couple of questions.<br /> <br /> When feeding, if you do a feeding scene without dice, you have to risk losing a point of humanity (with a greater chance of detachment if you intervene more to direct the narrative of the scene), but if you feed by doing a dice roll, you run no such risk, maybe just complications that come from a Dramatic Failure, correct? Why would one method result in a (potential) humanity loss and the other not, when they are essentially doing the same task?<br /> <br /> And to make sure I understand correctly, is diablerie (not that I expect this to happen a lot) a 4 step process:<br /> <br /> 1. The victim must first be drained of all Vitae<br /> 2. The aggressor continues to drink, but instead of losing Vitae, the victim's Health boxes are filled with lethal damage.<br /> 3. As above, but now all Health boxes are filled with aggravated damage.<br /> 4. The aggressor then spends Willpower and rolls Strength + Resolve each turn until Successes &gt;= victim's Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> So for an undamaged victim with 10 Vitae and 8 Health, for example, it would take at least 27 turns, or about 1.5 minutes, to complete the act? Is the victim able to fight back at all during this time?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24208-marquismark","name":"MarquisMark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T16:02:58-07:00","id":1310830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarquisMark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1310823#post1310823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When feeding, if you do a feeding scene without dice, you have to risk losing a point of humanity (with a greater chance of detachment if you intervene more to direct the narrative of the scene), but if you feed by doing a dice roll, you run no such risk, maybe just complications that come from a Dramatic Failure, correct? Why would one method result in a (potential) humanity loss and the other not, when they are essentially doing the same task?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the diceless method is there to put the spotlight on the character's Anchors and Humanity rating and generate Conditions, while the with-dice method is there to facilitate more wide-angle complications. Lower-Humanity characters can assert fiat more frequently and get away with more stuff that would constitute a detachment check in the framework of the diceless system, as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So for an undamaged victim with 10 Vitae and 8 Health, for example, it would take at least 27 turns, or about 1.5 minutes, to complete the act? Is the victim able to fight back at all during this time? </div> </div> </div>If this seems daunting, it's because you're treating a prerequisite as a part of the process; diablerie practically only works on a vampire in torpor, a process which either requires the Kindred to have a full track of lethal damage or means that the character unconsciously spent as much Vitae as they could to heal their wounds; most vampires will spend Vitae to keep from being damaged into torpor in the first place (setting aside that a violent bite deals lethal damage as well), so an undamaged victim with (for most vampires, at least) a majority of their Vitae is already an aberrant circumstance.<br /> <br /> Unless you're really focused on getting Vitae out of the process as well, the practical means of committing diablerie comes with a prelude of good old-fashioned beat-them-into-a-coma, at which point you just have to spend a few turns filling in the rest of the starter aggravated damage and then undertake the draining process of overcoming the soul itself.<br /> <br /> To answer your second question, in other words, only during your first two steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T20:38:19-07:00","id":1310905,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your reply, Satchel.<br /> <br /> One question to your answer about the no-dice feeding scenes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lower-Humanity characters can assert fiat more frequently and get away with more stuff that would constitute a detachment check in the framework of the diceless system, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the diceless method (to make sure I understand this correcly), the detachment dice pool is always 6 minus the accumulated fiat ticks. So a PC of Humanity 5, who does not inject fiat into a feeding scene, will not have to roll detachment, but if that same PC interjects 3 times, then they would have to roll detachment? In essence, it's easier for a PC to keep his Humanity by just rolling with what the ST and other PCs put into a feeding scene, instead of trying to change the narrative?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24208-marquismark","name":"MarquisMark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T21:14:26-07:00","id":1310916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarquisMark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1310905#post1310905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the diceless method (to make sure I understand this correcly), the detachment dice pool is always 6 minus the accumulated fiat ticks. So a PC of Humanity 5, who does not inject fiat into a feeding scene, will not have to roll detachment, but if that same PC interjects 3 times, then they would have to roll detachment? In essence, it's easier for a PC to keep his Humanity by just rolling with what the ST and other PCs put into a feeding scene, instead of trying to change the narrative?</div> </div> </div> </div>The dicepool is whatever the dicepool is for a detachment check at Humanity [6 - fiat ticks] (generally running the gamut between zero and seven dice after modifiers, depending), but yes, diceless feeding allows lower-Humanity characters more leeway in exerting forceful influence over the narrative of the scene without picking up extra mechanical complications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T01:35:34-07:00","id":1310943,"title":"","content":"Got it now. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24208-marquismark","name":"MarquisMark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T11:26:10-07:00","id":1311413,"title":"","content":"About Praestantia: &quot;Within every Akhud\u2019s veins runs the taint of diablerie, even if he himself has never committed it, strong enough for an Auspex practitioner to sense it.&quot; Does it even affect other Clans who learn this Discipline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T11:56:37-07:00","id":1311417,"title":"","content":"I would assume not. It seems like it's meant as an alternate or additional clan weakness for the Akhud\u2014it doesn't correspond to anything in 1e, but that's one of the many, many clan flaws the devs have used for the Assamites/Banu Haqim in Masquerade, and the 1e Akhud were pretty clearly Assamite-based.<br /> <br /> My guess is, either it was meant to be added to the clan bane section as well, or it was an earlier version of the clan bane that was removed from the bane section (but that mention of it wasn't caught in editing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T07:36:42-07:00","id":1312565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RaphaTheAscended</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1311413#post1311413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Praestantia: &quot;Within every Akhud\u2019s veins runs the taint of diablerie, even if he himself has never committed it, strong enough for an Auspex practitioner to sense it.&quot; Does it even affect other Clans who learn this Discipline?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there are two options for this. One, as suggested by Draconis, is to just use it as an alternate/elder bane for Akhud (though I'm not sure which is standard and which is elder). <br /> <br /> The second is that the diablerie taint is what gives you Praestantia; in-world, the Discipline is an altered version of the Tainted Condition. If this is the route you take, I would say that anyone who takes the Discipline out-of Clan gets the taint of diablerie. You need to drink someone's blood to manifest one of their clan's disciplines, and that trace of diablerie is what makes the Discipline run. If you take this route, your Akhud elders effectively get two banes. <br /> <br /> An interesting thematic point is that in-world everyone might assume the Akhud clan bane is looking like a diablerist, when in fact the bane is an inability to harm clanmates. A side effect masqurading as a bane kind of mirrors the Akhud masqurading as other clans. Maybe the Akhud even think that looking like a diablerist <i>is </i>their bane; given how rare the clan is, one might go lifetimes without running into a clanmate and never even discover their real bane. The lack of self-knowledge is kind of interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I kind of like the latter option, because it might imply that some clan &quot;banes&quot; are almost contagious. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">Unrelated fun fact: the Akhud origin story shows up in Charlie Huston's <i>Half the Blood of Brooklyn</i> where the antagonists are a bunch of Hassidic vampires (vampire Hasidim?).</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T10:38:54-07:00","id":1312598,"title":"","content":"I honestly consider the &quot;tainted by diablerie&quot; thing to be a mistake and would just completely ignore it. First of all there is no specific and perceptible &quot;taint of Diablerie&quot; in second edition. Whether or not you register as a diablerist or not to Auspex users is completely unrelated to the Tainted Condition. The specific phrasing in 1kYoN leads me to believe that the writer was mixing editions, a not particularly uncommon reoccurrence in VtR 2e supplements.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know that the Strix also registers as diablerists, but that's a mystery tied to their weird nature. It's a singular and important departure from the 100% success rate of Auspex (Dramatic Failure and CoWs notwithstanding) and serves as an implication about the nature of Strix.<br /> The Akhud, in contrast, are a Clan that shares all non-Clan exclusive abilities with all other Kindred. There's no mystery about what sets the Akhud apart from the other Clans. If there was, it really shouldn't be condensed to a weird comment about their Clan Discipline (that any other Kindred can also potentially learn) nor should it be &quot;this power makes another power automatically have one result regardless of what result it should've had and despite it being completely unrelated to the normal effects of this power&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T13:38:34-07:00","id":1312637,"title":"","content":"How do the Soulless and Enervated conditions effect Kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T15:01:13-07:00","id":1312652,"title":"","content":"Can they get those Conditions in the first place? While vampires are widely believed to have souls due to the (in character) text on diablerie, there are more things that points to vampires not having souls (such as the Embrace happening after the soul has left, and diablerie having effects not generally relevant to the soul as described in the CofD setting). Even if they do have souls, how to remove a soul can differ depending on which splat it's attempted on, meaning whatever way they would've lost their soul might've not worked anyway.<br /> <br /> If they do suffer from soul loss, I'd imagine it'd be a rapid descent into draugrhood. Unlike humans it's probably not possible to revert it once they hit Humanity 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T17:16:45-07:00","id":1312679,"title":"","content":"I believe that one of the Strix can (the photographer) can inflict the Soulless condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T17:47:55-07:00","id":1312684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1312679#post1312679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that one of the Strix can (the photographer) can inflict the Soulless condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>One would think so, but no. The normal <i>Soul Bite</i> Strix power inflicts the Soulless condition, but doesn't work on vampires; the Photographer's variant does work on vampires, but instead of Soulless the victim's &quot;body falls into a coma or torpor&quot; from which they &quot;cannot be revived unless the negatives [holding their soul] are destroyed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T01:44:42-07:00","id":1312733,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m away from my books at the moment so I was working from memory, thanks for correcting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T08:31:43-07:00","id":1312761,"title":"","content":"No problem; given the weird phrasing, I'm guessing it's a hacky workaround to avoid dealing with Soulless vampires!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T11:45:46-07:00","id":1312803,"title":"","content":"If I beg &quot;a place to crash&quot; from a human I've charmed, will they toss me out of their house as soon as the charmed condition expires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T12:07:49-07:00","id":1312805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1312803#post1312803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I beg &quot;a place to crash&quot; from a human I've charmed, will they toss me out of their house as soon as the charmed condition expires?</div> </div> </div> </div>When the <i>Charmed</i> condition expires, they won't necessarily think anything strange or supernatural happened. So how they react depends how you treated them.<br /> <br /> Most people, if they woke up and realized they'd let a stranger crash on their couch, would probably think &quot;that's odd, I suppose I was feeling generous while I was drunk, I won't do that again&quot; (and not do any more favors for that stranger in the future). But I don't think they'd grab the person's sleeping body and throw them out on the sidewalk.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if they woke up and realized &quot;I promised this person they could sleep here for the next five years&quot;, they'd probably tell the vampire &quot;hey, I was drunk when I said that, I can't actually let you do that&quot; (and not actually let the vampire sleep there for the next five years).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T05:06:41-07:00","id":1314502,"title":"","content":"Can you use the mesmerized condition to interrogate people?<br /> <br /> Example: Person HS is being evasive. Vampire V dominates them, and gives them the mesmerized condition. V then says 'Tell me who shot first.' Does HS confess they shot first? (They did but person GL is trying to cover it up.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T05:14:51-07:00","id":1314505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1314502#post1314502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use the mesmerized condition to interrogate people?<br /> <br /> Example: Person HS is being evasive. Vampire V dominates them, and gives them the mesmerized condition. V then says 'Tell me who shot first.' Does HS confess they shot first? (They did but person GL is trying to cover it up.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, except for the length of the command requiring Dominate 2. Why would you be unsure about that?<br /> A better commond would probably be &quot;recount these events&quot;, or, if you're less interested in it necessarily being the truth, &quot;confess to this&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-26-2019, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T05:38:21-07:00","id":1314510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1314505#post1314505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you be unsure about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seemed more of an Auspex thing.<br /> <br /> When instructed to 'tell the truth', I had the mesmerized say '4 and 4 sums to 8.' Which... technically the truth. Feel bad now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":".  adding to reply 05-26-2019, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T06:11:32-07:00","id":1314516,"title":"","content":"Mesmerize on its own might not work with that command since it's too vague (edited my post to reflect that since I forgot about that limitation) but Dominate victims aren't mindless automatons. They're still themselves and should carry out commands as they would naturally interpret them (as long as the commands are valid for the used Dominate power). That said I think a simple Merit could allow someone to default to the simplest possible resolution of the command rather than carrying it out naturally. Perhaps: Literal-Minded (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Making someone speak the truth or recount memories via Dominate does have some overlap with Auspex, but overlap is not a bad thing. It can also be very different since Dominate will get the oral version filtered through the victim's interpretation of their own memories and quite a lot of omissions of seemingly unimportant details that Auspex 4 would show directly to the interrogator. Unlike Auspex, using Dominate in such a way would also not trigger a Clash of Wills against supernaturally altered memories since you're forcing the victim to access the memory rather than accessing it directly.<br /> For finding out the truth Auspex is still by far superior, with the small drawback that you can't provide any proof (like a confession) for what you claim to have seen, should others doubt you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T06:30:33-07:00","id":1314519,"title":"","content":"True. I think the merit is a nice idea, but I would rephrase it as special training a Ventrue might offer their childe. Thanks for the help. I agree with what you said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-26T08:10:40-07:00","id":1314545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1314502#post1314502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use the mesmerized condition to interrogate people?<br /> <br /> Example: Person HS is being evasive. Vampire V dominates them, and gives them the mesmerized condition. V then says 'Tell me who shot first.' Does HS confess they shot first? (They did but person GL is trying to cover it up.)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Answer to me sincereley&quot; since the command with Doninate 1 last one scene, for the rest of the scene you can ask whatever and he is forced to answer to you saying the truth (or whatever he thinks it's the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T09:29:11-07:00","id":1314717,"title":"","content":"Am I overlooking a clan-specific merit for Ventrue, like Kiss of the Succubus for Daeva or Pack Alpha for Gangrel? I can't seem to find one in the core VTR 2e book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25307-james_nostack","name":"James_Nostack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T09:38:44-07:00","id":1314718,"title":"","content":"Weirdly enough, there is none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T09:43:25-07:00","id":1314721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Nostack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1314717#post1314717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I overlooking a clan-specific merit for Ventrue, like Kiss of the Succubus for Daeva or Pack Alpha for Gangrel? I can't seem to find one in the core VTR 2e book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Distinguished Palate was apparently originally intended to be restricted to Ventrue, and adding a replacement was overlooked when they decided to unlock DP for other clans.<br /> <br /> Olivia Hill, one of the credited (as David Hill) writers on the Requiem corebook, wrote a proposed replacement Ventrue Merit <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/106196-ventrue-specific-merit?p=107577#post107577\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T13:55:45-07:00","id":1314789,"title":"","content":"Do Kindred lose their sex drive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T14:16:16-07:00","id":1314793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1314789#post1314789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Kindred lose their sex drive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. They lose the hormonal drive, but they can still experience arousal (indeed under the Blush of Life they can evince all the effects of sexual arousal) and have sex. It is still &quot;a nice things to do&quot; (and obviously a good hunting strategy) but there is nothing in their nature actively and directly motivating them towards sex. The ecstasy of feeding replaces all that.<br /> <br /> Now, the above is a very general answer. It is strongly implied that Clan and perhaps even Humanity can impact this. Daeva might experience something close to a human sex drive, while Mekhet are at times described as in a state &quot;monks would envy&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T14:17:30-07:00","id":1314794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1314789#post1314789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Kindred lose their sex drive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely not completely. Sex is a common theme with vampires and the book specifically mentions Daeva indulging in order to feel alive again.<br /> <br /> I would assume it gets a bit less intense, just because all the deeply-rooted biological instincts pushing humans toward sex have now been co-opted and twisted by the Beast. But if you combine it with feeding, on the other hand, which the Beast desires\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T14:28:30-07:00","id":1314796,"title":"","content":"Another one: When Tasting Blood, what qualifies as 'active Auspex' use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T14:59:17-07:00","id":1314809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1314796#post1314796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one: When Tasting Blood, what qualifies as 'active Auspex' use?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably a relic from an earlier draft of second edition, or possibly even a writer who mixed first and second edition which is a reoccurring thing in the 2e supplements.<br /> <br /> My advice is just to ignore it as a typo. Neither Auspex ability with a duration is relevant to Taste of Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T15:27:09-07:00","id":1314817,"title":"","content":"Okay. Will do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-27T17:14:27-07:00","id":1314836,"title":"","content":"If you want to try to make that rule fit, perhaps you can activate Auspex 1 or 2 while tasting the blood; if you succeed on the roll, instead of asking a question, you can turn the Beast's senses toward the blood and have it boost your pool.<br /> <br /> But yeah, most likely it's a relic of when Auspex 1 enhanced your senses directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T11:59:32-07:00","id":1315528,"title":"","content":"When does frenzy end? I'm going mad here looking, and maybe it is tired eyes but I can't find the terminating condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T12:02:19-07:00","id":1315531,"title":"","content":"When the Beast gets what it wants, or the end of the scene, whichever comes first.<br /> <br /> If you dram-failed your resistance roll, it doesn't end until a breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T12:03:34-07:00","id":1315532,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much, and A+ customer support response time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T18:16:28-07:00","id":1315608,"title":"","content":"How would kindred see Revenents with the Fertile Vitae merit?<br /> <br /> I imagine the Ordo Dracul would want to do experiments on them.<br /> <br /> other Kindred may at most worry about a potential flood of Revenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T20:19:08-07:00","id":1315622,"title":"","content":"Probably depends on the vampire and the Domain. Embracing still burns away your Humanity, so it's no more of a risk than for normal vampires making a flood of childer (which is similarly catastrophic for the Masquerade).<br /> <br /> The merit notably doesn't specify if you can make accidental revenants, though\u2014and if you can, that's a much bigger problem, seeing how often revenants frenzy while feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T08:35:24-07:00","id":1315699,"title":"","content":"Since when was fear governed by logic?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T16:01:01-07:00","id":1315764,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify something: when a Touchstone is no longer attached (but otherwise is alive &amp; well), that doesn't count as &quot;losing&quot; a Touchstone for the Languid Condition, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25307-james_nostack","name":"James_Nostack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-31T17:31:53-07:00","id":1315775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Nostack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1315764#post1315764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify something: when a Touchstone is no longer attached (but otherwise is alive &amp; well), that doesn't count as &quot;losing&quot; a Touchstone for the Languid Condition, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. The Languid Condition and the -2 penalty to detachment rolls are both a consequence of your last Touchstone outright ceasing to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T09:01:16-07:00","id":1316647,"title":"","content":"Can I transfer control of someone with the enslaved Condition? Or would that probably require a new devotion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T14:33:10-07:00","id":1316705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1316647#post1316647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I transfer control of someone with the enslaved Condition? Or would that probably require a new devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Definitely a new devotion. Possibly mixing in Obfuscate 1, to make the target not be you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T15:17:24-07:00","id":1316713,"title":"","content":"You could tell them to work for someone else but they're enslaved to YOU by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T04:52:52-07:00","id":1317542,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit on how often a character can attempt to use things like Majesty 2 (Confidant) on a target? Most things have a Vitae cost, or a limit on how often they can be used, or something, but as far as I can see, a character can simply spam Confidant until it works. Am I missing some general rules about not being able to retry abilities that the target successfully resisted?<br /> <br /> Also, can any character with enough Carthian Status put a Carthain Law into effect? Or does it have to be agreed upon by all local members of the Covenant, or does a character have to get permission from the Carthian leaders before enacting laws, or are there any other limiting factors? Carthian laws seem a bit powerful for just any Carthian member to start putting loads of them into action all by themselves (even with the XP costs, which seem VERY cheap for what some of the Laws do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","user":"Shadowdragon","date":". 06-10-2019, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T05:05:40-07:00","id":1317544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1317542#post1317542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a limit on how often a character can attempt to use things like Majesty 2 (Confidant) on a target? Most things have a Vitae cost, or a limit on how often they can be used, or something, but as far as I can see, a character can simply spam Confidant until it works. Am I missing some general rules about not being able to retry abilities that the target successfully resisted?<br /> <br /> Also, can any character with enough Carthian Status put a Carthain Law into effect? Or does it have to be agreed upon by all local members of the Covenant, or does a character have to get permission from the Carthian leaders before enacting laws, or are there any other limiting factors? Carthian laws seem a bit powerful for just any Carthian member to start putting loads of them into action all by themselves (even with the XP costs, which seem VERY cheap for what some of the Laws do).</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory deserve, everytime you attempts again to use a discipline that has failed previously, in the same scene, the roll should have a cumulative -3 malus. <br /> I would go for: when you fail 2 times uou can't try again. No hard rules on this though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T07:01:07-07:00","id":1317555,"title":"","content":"There is a cumulative penalty on subsequent uses of a power after the attempt fails. Furthermore, unless the target is successfully &quot;Awed&quot; first, he can spam it until the cows come home and it still won't take effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> Whether or not the Carthians in a setting require a quorum, majority vote, or permission from a higher ranking member to enact is dependent on the setting but technically any Carthian meeting the prerequisites can enact a Carthian Law effect. However, the effectiveness is often directly proportional to the cumulative Carthian covenant status of the perpetrators and/or tied to city status. Mandate from the Masses for instance in a domain with four Carthians. They name one Carthian their leader with 3 covenant status The others have 1 status each. They opt to strip away the Blood Potency of an elysium master who barred them entry because the last time two of them were present they instigated a brawl that resulted in a repair bill exceeding $7000. Consensus is easy to gain and the elysium master loses 1 BP.<br /> Add 5 more kindred, each with 1status and their leader gaining a 4th point of Carthian status. <br /> Same scenario. Only this time, three of the Carthians don't agree because they aren't barred entry. Add to the issue One of them is employed there and gets a lot of other useful tidbits of city information from said elysium master that benefits the Movement in other ways, one of them is the childe of the elysium master, and the leader actually believes they should be barred entry for their behavior. So they accumulated in total 6 status. Again the same result, with elysium master losing only 1 BP even with twice as many Carthians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-10T07:55:10-07:00","id":1317566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1317542#post1317542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a limit on how often a character can attempt to use things like Majesty 2 (Confidant) on a target? Most things have a Vitae cost, or a limit on how often they can be used, or something, but as far as I can see, a character can simply spam Confidant until it works. Am I missing some general rules about not being able to retry abilities that the target successfully resisted?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Successive Attempts: When you fail a roll, you may be able to try again. If time is not an issue and your character is under no pressure to perform, you may make successive attempts with your full dice pool. In the far more likely situation that time is short and the situation is tense, each subsequent attempt has a cumulative \u20131 die penalty \u2014 so the third time a character tries to break down the door that\u2019s keeping her inside a burning building, her roll has a \u20132 die penalty. Successive attempts do not apply to extended actions.&quot;<br /> <br /> On page 173 about rolls in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T14:31:20-07:00","id":1318121,"title":"","content":"Can vampires with the requisite BP and Humanity to do a short Daywalk maintain the Blush of Life while doing so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T14:39:26-07:00","id":1318124,"title":"","content":"Yes, though it would still hurt, the damage just wouldn't be mechanically represented as Lethal (or whatever) until they were exposed for certain amounts of time.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's in the book but I think like blood bonds the time is represented for mechanical simplicity. So it's not like BP 1, Humanity 9 vampire can run outside for 9 minutes in the sun, take a rest indoors in darkness, then run another 9 minutes, take a rest in darkness, then run another 9 minutes and not take damage unless they stay out over 10 minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T08:45:52-07:00","id":1318867,"title":"","content":"Is Conditioning detectable by body language way someone acts differently etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T11:13:23-07:00","id":1318905,"title":"","content":"That depends. In the previous iteration, potentially yes. Victims lost the ability to think independently but it could be written off as confusion or indecision, not necessarily that they were Conditioned. <br /> In this edition, it depends on whether or not you allow someone who is Mesmerized to be detectable based on body language. The effects from Conditioning make the victim count as already Mesmerized for purposes of Dominate use and later on eliminate the need for eye contact to use Dominate and Resolve penalties to normally relevant applications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T09:08:55-07:00","id":1319064,"title":"","content":"So, question pertaining to Vigor... when it says my character can make a Strength + Athletics roll to jump a number of yards/meters equal to success * Vigor+1. Did it mean -leap-? Or am I jumping straight up into the air only with this ability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11491-thehallow1","name":"thehallow1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-17T11:42:13-07:00","id":1319094,"title":"","content":"Normally with the jump rules when you roll to jump it's 1 ft vertically per success, standing broad jump is 2 ft horizontally per success, and running jumps (which require 10 ft minimum to do w/o penalty) horizontally is Size +4 per success. They're less clear as to the vertical ascension in cases like that.<br /> <br /> Yes, that's going to get into some unlikely shit like kindred jumping over a 3 story building with a running start but if the ST let's them invest in the merits, devotions, and so on, have at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T02:41:00-07:00","id":1319238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thehallow1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1319064#post1319064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, question pertaining to Vigor... when it says my character can make a Strength + Athletics roll to jump a number of yards/meters equal to success * Vigor+1. Did it mean -leap-? Or am I jumping straight up into the air only with this ability?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Jumps in CoD are really not well defined. I'm actually using the following rules:<ul><li><i><u>Vertical Jump</u></i>: [(Strength + Vigor + Athletic) successes/3]*(Vigor + 1) meters</li> <li><i><u>Horizontal jump</u></i>: [(Strength + Vigor + Athletic) successes]*(Vigor + 1) meters</li> <li><i><u>Running Horizontal jump</u></i>: [(Strength + Vigor + Athletic) successes] + Size] *(Vigor + 1) in meter</li> </ul>It actually is pretty realistic without considering Vigor. If there is no rush and the PC can take its time to prepare the jump I'm just considering the half of the pool as successes. In fact let's take an average athlete as example:<br /> <br /> Strgth 3 Athl 3. Pool is 6. Let's take the half: 3. The PC in this example can jump:<br /> <br /> - Vertical: 1 meter (from floor to feet - extended legs. It has to be considered the elevation, then you want to add the PC's tallness.)<br /> - Horizontal: 3 meters from still. (that is exactly how much I'm jumping from still position)<br /> - Running jump: 8 meter. <br /> <br /> Let's take the best atlhlete in the word:<br /> <br /> Strgh 4 Ath 5. Pool of 9<br /> <br /> Same example as before: <br /> <br /> - Vertical: 4/3= 1.3 meters (that is still reliable)<br /> - horizontal: 4 meters<br /> - Running: 9 meters (about the world record)<br /> <br /> Then Vigor is basically multiplying this distance as intended in the core book (other than rising the pool)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 06-23-2019, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T17:49:52-07:00","id":1319387,"title":"","content":"Cool, thank you both!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11491-thehallow1","name":"thehallow1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T12:47:17-07:00","id":1320334,"title":"","content":"Is this over arbitrary?<br /> <br /> in one PBP game I ran once A Fledgling asked her sire if he broke ties with his mortal life too When he instructed her to do so.<br /> <br /> HE told her &quot;No I didn't not right away I tried to maintain my position in my Family...<br /> <br /> I wound up murdering my son my little boy in a frenzy&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-23T12:57:40-07:00","id":1320336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1320334#post1320334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this over arbitrary?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how it would be arbitrary, but it seems fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T14:43:36-07:00","id":1320579,"title":"","content":"Mini debate with a friend. <br /> <br /> Would Claws of the unholy ignore Mage Armor?<br /> <br /> One side of the argument is that the text specifically reads that it ignores anything not generated by Resilience.<br /> <br /> The other argument(mine) is that the book was written before Mage was.<br /> <br /> Their counter point is that so was Werewolf, and the merit Living Weapon still specifically calls out magic armor as working against it.<br /> <br /> So what do you fine people think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T15:22:27-07:00","id":1320592,"title":"","content":"I would say it does for a few reasons. Claws of the Unholy does Aggravated damage and Aggravated damage typically ignores or destroys armor by default. I don\u2019t care about the \u201cwell it\u2019s magical armor\u201d argument because the weapon in question is \u201cmagical claws specifically enhanced to rip through or ignore magical armor.\u201d A very specific aspect of Resilience has to be activated in order to block damage from Claws of the Unholy, the same may or may not be the case for Mage Armor.<br /> And I\u2019d allow the armor piercing aspect of Living Weapon to rip through Mage Armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T16:51:08-07:00","id":1320609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1320579#post1320579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what do you fine people think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they just flatly contradict each other.<br /> <br /> Personally, seeing as mages generally have pretty easy access to non-armour Mage Armour, I'd probably let CotU work. Maybe have it work in a more obviously unnatural manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-24T20:51:59-07:00","id":1320653,"title":"","content":"The point because Resilence does work is that it's not an armor. Resilence does not prevent injuries it prevents damages even though injuries are there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-27T14:27:55-07:00","id":1321254,"title":"","content":"There appears to be an intended relationship between Resilience and CotU specifically, perhaps because they are opposite aspects of the Gangrel's nature.<br /> The book calls out Resilience specifically and not just magical or unnatural armor. To allow mage armor to block it would be no different from allow Blood Sorcery to the same.<br /> The only work-around I could see happening is if the Mage uses Death school to craft a spell to specifically mimic Resilience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1320653#post1320653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point because Resilence does work is that it's not an armor. Resilence does not prevent injuries it prevents damages even though injuries are there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the Death specialty spell could animate the Mage's body in a similar way to how Vampires are animated without relying on their internal organs for survival, then the custom spell allows the carnage to happen to the body but suspends the health level damage until the spell ends,, giving the Mage time to heal the suspended damage later on that night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T09:50:34-07:00","id":1322048,"title":"","content":"In-world, do your characters clearly distinguish between vitae addiction, vinculum, and ghouling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T10:20:58-07:00","id":1322056,"title":"","content":"Yes and all of them are considered vitae influenced. Ghouls, depending on the setting are referred to as blood servants or familiars, to distinguish humans retainers from those who aren't blood bound. Among themselves, ghouls tend to refer to other ghouls as empowered. <br /> Bound or Favored (depending on the context by which the vinculum was established) refers only to vampires under vinculum to another vampire.<br /> Addicts refers to those addicted to vitae, regardless of type.<br /> Contaminated or Marked (depending on the view the vampire has about vinculums) refers to a human who is at least partially under vinculum to a vampire but not turned into a ghoul nor succumbed to vitae addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T10:26:25-07:00","id":1323464,"title":"","content":"Question on the Bloodline banes. For character creation are the banes in-effect immediately or only after dropping to 6 humanity like the clan banes. I could not find a reference in the 2nd ed main book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24724-porkchop2073","name":"Porkchop2073","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24724_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T13:11:06-07:00","id":1323497,"title":"","content":"When they join the bloodline (as opposed to simply being sired by someone in the bloodline vs being avused in), the bloodline bane takes effect. The Clan bane impact is directly tied to the Humanity rating, so far the bloodline banes are not, they're merely a warped side effect of their gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T16:58:16-07:00","id":1323548,"title":"","content":"In other words, joining a Bloodline doesn't happen automatically: it costs a <i>dot</i> of willpower. When you spend that dot, you gain the advantages, and also the bane. No earlier, no later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T17:28:27-07:00","id":1323552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1323548#post1323548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, joining a Bloodline doesn't happen automatically: it costs a <i>dot</i> of willpower. When you spend that dot, you gain the advantages, and also the bane. No earlier, no later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see a source to that statement. The Bloodlines section in the core book mentions nothing about Willpower dots as a cost. It only says you need to have a certain BP depending on relation with the Avus, and needing to drink the Avus' Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T16:33:46-07:00","id":1324298,"title":"","content":"Question: When a dhampir buys a Twist, does that Twist apply to every Theme the dhampir has dots in, or do you have to choose one Theme for the Twist upon purchasing the Twist?<br /> <br /> For example, does the Twist 'Blood's Call' (the dhampir can sense his kinship with another dhampir from the Theme\u2019s clan on sight) apply to every clan the dhampir has Twists dots from, or only one specific clan from a specific chosen Twist chosen upon purchasing the Twist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T20:56:42-07:00","id":1326181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1323548#post1323548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, joining a Bloodline doesn't happen automatically: it costs a <i>dot</i> of willpower. When you spend that dot, you gain the advantages, and also the bane. No earlier, no later.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to spend a Willpower dot to join bloodlines anymore. You just have to take blood from an Avus and be the appropriate Blood Potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T08:47:17-07:00","id":1326716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1324298#post1324298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: When a dhampir buys a Twist, does that Twist apply to every Theme the dhampir has dots in, or do you have to choose one Theme for the Twist upon purchasing the Twist?<br /> <br /> For example, does the Twist 'Blood's Call' (the dhampir can sense his kinship with another dhampir from the Theme\u2019s clan on sight) apply to every clan the dhampir has Twists dots from, or only one specific clan from a specific chosen Twist chosen upon purchasing the Twist?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From p. 34 of Half-Damned - &quot;She can then use these Twists within any Theme in which she invests at least one dot.&quot; So yes, you buy a Twist, it applies to all Themes you have spent xp on. So in your example, it would be every clan the dhampir has Themes from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T01:26:47-07:00","id":1327370,"title":"","content":"Revenants and blood sympathy: does an uplifted revenant have two sires or one for purposes of blood sympathy, and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T03:20:13-07:00","id":1327377,"title":"","content":"I would say blood sympathy to the one who uplifts them erases the blood sympathy to the one whose blood initially created them, so one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T07:36:51-07:00","id":1327897,"title":"","content":"Does Embalming Interfere with Rising as a Revenant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T08:31:39-07:00","id":1327905,"title":"","content":"Barring certain religious practices, last will instructions, or family requests, embalming a corpse is a standardized burial practice performed at funeral homes and has been for a long time. (There's actually an old family anecdote about one of my great great uncles &quot;coming back to life&quot; in the funeral home as the mortician was preparing to embalm him.) So if revenants claw their way out of caskets in your setting then I would say no it doesn't interfere with rising as a revenant. If you want to say elaborate embalming procedures are done can prevent an individual from rising as an undead, then go ahead. Sloppy embalming processes or refusing to allow it to take place could be an &quot;explanation&quot; as to how botched burial practices may result in revenants rising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-28-2019, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T12:38:09-07:00","id":1327944,"title":"","content":"suggesting That an unblessed burial might cause rising as a Revenant? <br /> <br /> Asked all this because I was just watching the Maze that said they take all your innards out before your buried.<br /> <br /> made me think.<br /> <br /> It says in requiem all you need is your heart and your head.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T13:17:24-07:00","id":1327950,"title":"","content":"They don't typically remove organs in the current embalming process. They inject formaldehyde into your body using a pump to expel blood and water that was not already drained as well as slow the decay process. Organ removal may occur if you get into something more elaborate or if it involves cremation or transferring the body over a long distance or period of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T13:26:23-07:00","id":1327951,"title":"","content":"Will another kindred sense your predatory aspect if you are in an animal form (such as Protean 3)? I.e will a vampire know if the bat that is following them overhead is a kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24946-mr_stick","name":"Mr_Stick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T14:00:07-07:00","id":1327958,"title":"","content":"Unless they are using Obfuscate 1 or other ability to conceal their predatory aura, I say yes. Protean does not convey any ability to conceal the kindred's auras, in fact it draws upon the Beast to enact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T16:31:09-07:00","id":1327980,"title":"","content":"just getting out of a Hospital would probably be a challenge for a Revenant","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T07:34:58-07:00","id":1328086,"title":"","content":"For Protean 3, do you need to have recently fed on the type of animal you'll turn into? Or is it just that at some time in the past you fed on the animal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T07:57:53-07:00","id":1328090,"title":"","content":"The entry says they have to kill the animal by feeding from it then sleep for one full day and night in Unmarked Grave. So no, I don't think it means they can opt to take the form of anything they fed from at any point of their existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T10:31:24-07:00","id":1328120,"title":"","content":"For some reason I remembered the entry being short on details, but now I just looked at it. You cna hold a number of animal forms equal to the number of Protean dots you have.<br /> <br /> I'm interpreting it as those forms in your &quot;stable&quot; lasting as long as you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-29T11:30:33-07:00","id":1328137,"title":"","content":"Yes. When they get Protean 3 they eat the animal forms they want and sleep 3 days and 3 nights in Unmarked Grave and can turn into them at any time. When they get rank 4 and 5 they eat the animal and sleep in the Unmarked Grave. If they want to change the animal, they designate which one they want to drop for the new one, eat the new one and do the Unmarked Grave sleep. That new animal replaces the old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-29-2019, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:13:58-07:00","id":1328293,"title":"","content":"Then a Raven or Crow will likely be more common then a bat. a dog more then a wolf in a lot of cases especialy for urban Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:55:03-07:00","id":1328303,"title":"","content":"It really depends on where you live. The last character I had with Protean, she had a fox, a raven, and a raccoon. Later she got an alligator. <br /> I live in a suburban area and I have seen the first three as well as bats, owls, hawks, vultures, and muskrats trekking across my front yard at some point or other. And a friend of mine who lives in a more urbanized area has taken pictures of badgers in his and his neighbors' yard. And my nephew said he occasionally saw alligators in his neighborhood when he lived in Florida. A wolf may well be fair game depending on the setting locale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 07-30-2019, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T16:41:50-07:00","id":1328400,"title":"","content":"Live in Oklahoma and seen Racoons in the city<br /> <br /> In the country side seen Rattle snakes And heard though Rarely seen coyotes.<br /> <br /> and armidillas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T03:32:10-07:00","id":1328480,"title":"","content":"Can Auspex 3 be used to find out secret passages in a room? Would the question: is there any secret passage be allowed providing a clear answer to the Mekhet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T04:06:18-07:00","id":1328486,"title":"","content":"I would allow that question. It would provide a yes/no answer and if Obfuscate, Nightmare, or other power is being used to conceal it, provoke a Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T04:19:59-07:00","id":1328491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1328486#post1328486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would allow that question. It would provide a yes/no answer and if Obfuscate, Nightmare, or other power is being used to conceal it, provoke a Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. What about if with a following question would have been asked: where the passage is? <br /> Or more generic: is there any way with Auspex 3 to find out a secret passage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T04:50:02-07:00","id":1328497,"title":"","content":"Yes. I'd allow the follow up question. What I don't allow is questions with multiple answers to provide every correct answer, multiple questions within a single question, loaded statements not based on actual facts or clues known, or questions that have no bearing or relevance to the object or locale. <br /> For example Walking into a house &quot;Where are all the secret passage ways in this house?&quot; (Multiple answers) That question may potentially reveal the coat closet to the left. Not the lever you need to flip behind the desk beside the closet to make the sliding door inside open. Nor would it reveal the descending staircase in the fireplace of the library.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T19:43:09-07:00","id":1328855,"title":"","content":"how well do you think flashbangs work on vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T20:12:17-07:00","id":1328858,"title":"","content":"They may temporarily blind or deafen a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T21:51:20-07:00","id":1328876,"title":"","content":"Might provoke a frenzy roll, since it's a sudden unexpected burst of fiery light. Though if they hold off the Beast for one turn the stimulus is gone, so, not the best way of making them panic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T01:26:27-07:00","id":1328904,"title":"","content":"Does Nightmare 5 work also on vampires? I'd say no but this power would be definitely to weak compared to other 5th dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T02:39:27-07:00","id":1328909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1328904#post1328904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Nightmare 5 work also on vampires? I'd say no but this power would be definitely to weak compared to other 5th dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>It surely works, the question is lethal or bashing damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T02:57:30-07:00","id":1328911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1328909#post1328909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It surely works, the question is lethal or bashing damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree it SHOULD work, but seems a bit of a stretch to me. In the description it talks about heart attacks and similar, hard to believe it can affect a dead body somehow.<br /> But even though it caused bashing damage, still serms the weakest 5th powers ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-02-2019, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T03:51:33-07:00","id":1328917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1328911#post1328911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree it SHOULD work, but seems a bit of a stretch to me. In the description it talks about heart attacks and similar, hard to believe it can affect a dead body somehow.<br /> But even though it caused bashing damage, still serms the weakest 5th powers ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should consider that it leaves ANYWAY the victim with broken condition.<br /> AND if you activate Dread presence you lower the victim composure, making him more vulnerable to successive use of nightmare and other powers.<br /> You don t need to touch or make eye contact, so you can kill someone remaining obfuscate (also nosferatu clan discipline), and it will appear as a natural death.<br /> To me it s a great assassination tool, but probably lacks in other use","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T04:17:07-07:00","id":1328920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1328917#post1328917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should consider that it leaves ANYWAY the victim with broken condition.<br /> AND if you activate Dread presence you lower the victim composure, making him more vulnerable to successive use of nightmare and other powers.<br /> You don t need to touch or make eye contact, so you can kill someone remaining obfuscate (also nosferatu clan discipline), and it will appear as a natural death.<br /> To me it s a great assassination tool, but probably lacks in other use</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure you can use it while obfuscated as it is still an interaction with the target that would leave you be spotted out by him. But I'm not sure about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-02-2019, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T05:42:07-07:00","id":1328931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1328920#post1328920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure you can use it while obfuscated as it is still an interaction with the target that would leave you be sootted by him. Bit I'm not sure about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The doubt is legit, but even without the obfuscate combo i assume that the power range is &quot;everyone the vampire can directly perceive&quot;, meaning that you could kill a bystander from a rooftop, or use the power while in a crowd without being discovered","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-02T17:42:58-07:00","id":1329037,"title":"","content":"Also why would it do bashing to vamps? Nightmare 5 attacks the mind, and vamps don't have any special protection for their psyche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-03T01:31:58-07:00","id":1329078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1329037#post1329037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also why would it do bashing to vamps? Nightmare 5 attacks the mind, and vamps don't have any special protection for their psyche.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mind attacks lead to the deep fear that, as described in the text, incurr in hearth attacks, white hair, ecc. Which are the real source of damage. <br /> Now the deep fear is not mitigates for a Vampire but the consequences could, as no hearth is beating, no blood pressure increasing that can lead to ictus and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-04T04:34:57-07:00","id":1329255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1328911#post1328911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even though it caused bashing damage, still serms the weakest 5th powers ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that it's an attack resisted by Composure instead of Defense (which is based on two traits), and bypass all types of physical Armor. Despite being called the social splat vampires are extremely physically potent, and any defensive characters will absolutely stack Defense and evasive Fighting Styles. This bypasses all of that. You're rolling three traits (one of which at five dots) penalised by a single trait that vampires can't easily increase, so the damage output can be quite high. Unfortunately the lack of options to increase your dice pool and damage modifier is a significant downside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-06T15:19:55-07:00","id":1329657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1329078#post1329078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mind attacks lead to the deep fear that, as described in the text, incurr in hearth attacks, white hair, ecc. Which are the real source of damage.<br /> Now the deep fear is not mitigates for a Vampire but the consequences could, as no hearth is beating, no blood pressure increasing that can lead to ictus and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it doesn't actually imply that as the <i>cause</i> of the damage, it just says &quot;Her victim can't sleep, his hair turns white from terror, and in some cases his heart stops dead.&quot;<br /> If heart attack were the actual cause of the damage then it would <i>nothing</i> at all to vampires, not even bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-06T17:08:27-07:00","id":1329666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1329657#post1329657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it doesn't actually imply that as the <i>cause</i> of the damage, it just says &amp;quot;Her victim can't sleep, his hair turns white from terror, and in some cases his heart stops dead.&amp;quot;<br /> If heart attack were the actual cause of the damage then it would <i>nothing</i> at all to vampires, not even bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my initial concern actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-07T05:30:45-07:00","id":1329722,"title":"","content":"Question about the Cr\u00faac Style, i was reading secret of the covenant again and the piece of fiction Effortles damage has a character activating the effect of her cruac style that require spending a willpower point without casting a ritual, does that means that although you can activate the effect that requires spending willpower during a ritual, you can also activate that effect outisde of combat ? RAW is a bit unclear (at least to me) on that;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T06:31:56-07:00","id":1331764,"title":"","content":"Does riding the wave Qualify as Frenzy for resetting penalties from tempted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T10:15:36-07:00","id":1331792,"title":"","content":"If the penalty applied to the Riding the Wave attempt I'd say yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T11:54:32-07:00","id":1331822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1331764#post1331764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does riding the wave Qualify as Frenzy for resetting penalties from tempted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Riding the Wave of Frenzy is a form of Frenzy so it resolves Tempted. Tempted only penalises resisting Frenzy, which is different from Riding the Wave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T15:02:57-07:00","id":1331871,"title":"","content":"oh on Touchstones?<br /> <br /> do these count as meaningful interaction for purposes of removing tempted?<br /> <br /> is polishing a watch telling time with it.<br /> <br /> Using a sword/Revolver/Assault rifle in battle<br /> <br /> Defending a holy place.<br /> <br /> Conducting Ceremonys in a holy place.<br /> <br /> Burning incense in a touch stone burner.<br /> <br /> Meditating with a touchstone Buddha statue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T15:11:18-07:00","id":1331874,"title":"","content":"I think you'd be hard pressed to find an ST that accepts those as Touchstones in the first place. Touchstones aren't exclusively humans, but they really should remind you of your human life. The house you grew up in is a great example because it really does ground the character in their human life. Objects such as a watch or a sword probably does not unless they're intrinsically linked to their human life.<br /> If you do have those as Touchstones, I'd say that most of those interactions would work. The clock would probably require something like a deep cleaning or being ritualistically wound up. The sword needs to be used ritualistically in battle in order to not just be a tool in the vampire's hands; alternatively you could instead have a maintenance session with the sword, making sure it does not fall into disrepair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T15:26:51-07:00","id":1331876,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm concerned, yes on all of them, but there is also an argument to be made that using the item touchstones as designed does potentially put them at risk of being damaged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T15:34:35-07:00","id":1331878,"title":"","content":"so its best not to use your Daisho except in ceremonial cases? <br /> <br /> and a touchstone doesn't have to be tied to your mortal life just remind you of it somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T19:06:46-07:00","id":1331900,"title":"","content":"When a vampire experiences Final Death, what happens to all the individuals Blood-bonded to them? Does the Bond disappear immediately or fade at the normal rate it fades at when deprived of new blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T19:24:17-07:00","id":1331903,"title":"","content":"As I said, using it does put it at risk of being damaged. Whether or not using it or merely setting it aside and keeping it in a safe or display case gives them the psychological support of a touchstone is a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> As a player, I don't waste XP on touchstones and as an ST, I don't incorporate them unless the player wants. By RAW, a touchstone just needs to reinforce to the kindred character that they used to be human. Some ghoul or their great grandchild could be a touchstone - so they don't have to have been something or someone the kindred had or knew when they were alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-20T20:11:37-07:00","id":1331911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1331900#post1331900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a vampire experiences Final Death, what happens to all the individuals Blood-bonded to them? Does the Bond disappear immediately or fade at the normal rate it fades at when deprived of new blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fluff in the past has implied it shatters immediately and violently. The thralls all know what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T06:56:06-07:00","id":1331951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1331911#post1331911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fluff in the past has implied it shatters immediately and violently. The thralls all know what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. What does this mean about their emotions towards their dead master though? And are there any mechanical rules on it, like the blood bond conditions disappearing immediately without resolving?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T08:02:58-07:00","id":1331961,"title":"","content":"There's no mechanics for it in 2nd edition forcing a reaction or behavior. It's up to the players and ST to decide if the thrall is going to remain loyal to the memory of their dead master, make a symbolic grave and dance on it, or move on with their life with one less toxic influence to worry about any longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-21T09:11:13-07:00","id":1331970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1331951#post1331951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. What does this mean about their emotions towards their dead master though? And are there any mechanical rules on it, like the blood bond conditions disappearing immediately without resolving?</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood bonds aren't represented through Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T12:52:57-07:00","id":1332701,"title":"","content":"Ok, so. 2e, Coil of the Ascendant.<br /> So, a vampire with the first dot, &quot;Surmounting the Daysleep&quot;, does not not need to roll to resist the daily slumber nor does it gain the Lethargic condition as long as Blush of Life is active. Ok good so far. But then at the second dot, &quot;The Warm Face&quot;, Blush of Life now lasts 24 hours. So does this mean that the Vampire can remain awake 24/7 as long as it is willing to spend 1 extra vitae each day?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T12:59:02-07:00","id":1332704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1332701#post1332701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so. 2e, Coil of the Ascendant.<br /> So, a vampire with the first dot, &quot;Surmounting the Daysleep&quot;, does not not need to roll to resist the daily slumber nor does it gain the Lethargic condition as long as Blush of Life is active. Ok good so far. But then at the second dot, &quot;The Warm Face&quot;, Blush of Life now lasts 24 hours. So does this mean that the Vampire can remain awake 24/7 as long as it is willing to spend 1 extra vitae each day?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the idea, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:02:57-07:00","id":1332706,"title":"","content":"Indeed it does. At the cost of an extra Vitae.<br /> <br /> Note that this doesn't do anything to avoid the usual difficulties of being awake during the day (reduced dice pools, burning in the sun, etc). It just means you won't fall asleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:03:14-07:00","id":1332707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1332704#post1332704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the idea, yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thanks! Cuz one of my players has those 2, and I didn't want to say no to him before I had a definite answer. Thankfully it does indeed work like we already used it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:05:43-07:00","id":1332708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1332706#post1332706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed it does. At the cost of an extra Vitae.<br /> <br /> Note that this doesn't do anything to avoid the usual difficulties of being awake during the day (reduced dice pools, burning in the sun, etc). It just means you won't fall asleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't the reduced dice pools the result of the Lethargic Condition? (which they ignore) or are there other penalties as well? Aside from the sun I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T13:40:42-07:00","id":1332717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1332708#post1332708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't the reduced dice pools the result of the Lethargic Condition? (which they ignore) or are there other penalties as well? Aside from the sun I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right here. They ignore lethargic condition and no other penalities are there. So no penalities at all but the sun damages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-26T14:04:23-07:00","id":1332728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1332717#post1332717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are right here. They ignore lethargic condition and no other penalities are there. So no penalities at all but the sun damages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then, that settles it. The Ordo Dracul has completely defeated time.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the replies everyone, you've been extremely helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T08:40:05-07:00","id":1333672,"title":"","content":"How would covenants probably View one of their number being Blood bound to a member of another covenant?<br /> <br /> I think the Sanctum will probably see it as Heretical, on the surface, especialy if its by the Circle<br /> <br /> But if all that hes used for is acting as a Pet Theban sorcerer, or a weapon against other cults in the Circle, will only do so much.<br /> <br /> The Circle would probably have a dissonant Serenity about such an issue that would drive outsiiders Crazy<br /> <br /> The Carthians would be the most Incensed as blood slavery is so antithetical to their princibles.<br /> <br /> The Invictus would disapprove.<br /> <br /> But so long as the Regnant in the Relationship Doesn't treat him worse then a Ghoul, would probably let it slide.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ordo Dracul would go &quot;Must do research on what can be accomplished&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-02T19:49:51-07:00","id":1333782,"title":"","content":"It would largely depend on how the domain at large views vinculums. Why would Invictus or the Circle of the Crone object at all? Invictus oaths function on the premise of someone being subservient to someone else and Cruac is more effective when wielded against someone under vinculum. And personally I've never played in a setting where the Carthian Movement ever actually opposed vinculums. They considered it a valid punishment for stuff like killing someone's ghoul without authorization, sending someone into a long torpor without authorization or would circle jerk each other to keep from getting blood bound when forced to attend mandatory Acolyte blood orgies or Sanctified masses. The only setting I played in it where any covenant opposed it as a matter of policy was the Lancea et Sanctum because that iteration viewed as a form of idolatry. And now since every covenant has a way to break vinculums or render oneself immune, and they only last for a year, I don't see that it carries the same stigma that it had in the previous edition.<br /> <br /> As for a Sanctified being used to provide Theban Sorcery to further the Circle of the Crone's interests to the detriment of the Lancea et Sanctum or their members, I'd play that off as the Theban Sorcery spells not working due to divine intervention (They ostensibly swear oaths to that effect in order to learn Theban Sorcery anyway.) or inquisitors being sent to torpor or kill the sorcerer or regnant in question.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-04T14:52:57-07:00","id":1334024,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn on Lancaea Sanctum Dhampirs?<br /> <br /> It Says they Regard their Dhampirs as gods curse upon the Kindred.<br /> <br /> How do you think they'd react at someone enslaving such a being they spent years training and subverting them to selfish ends<br /> <br /> &quot;HOW DARE YOU!!!!&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> or use the example as a lesson of what could happen from a single Failure for the next Generation of Young Dhampirs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T10:42:11-07:00","id":1335151,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this has been asked, but the thread is too big for me to get through: Do vampires get tired from overexertion the way that mortals do? I assume that a character's still use their Stamina + Athletics to determine how quickly they cover a shorter distance, but they no longer need to breath nor create lactic acid, which means they no longer actually get tired... would a vampire be faster than a mortal in the long run, can they run at a full sprint over long distances? and if so... what does that mean for long distance running. <br /> <br /> The average human can run a marathon in 3 hours or so, the top tier runners can do so in 2. would even an average vampire be able to keep up with the Olympians over the course of the whole race without needing to rest? would they be faster?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T11:15:46-07:00","id":1335158,"title":"","content":"I saw a piece of fiction depicting Norris working out. He complained of the same lactic acid issues despite not producing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T11:26:58-07:00","id":1335164,"title":"","content":"Vampires still suffer wound penalties, so I would assume they also get tired/fatigued, even if it's just for psychosomatic reasons (so I'd say a vampire in frenzy does <i>not</i> suffer fatigue penalties either).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T11:37:39-07:00","id":1335169,"title":"","content":"I see suffering wound penalities much more related to tendons, bones and muscles broken.<br /> I would rather say vampire do not get tired. No reason they should. Also in the chase table in the core there is also a +2 to give to the opponent of a tireless being (which if not a vampire I can't see who then, exception for cars)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T01:14:56-07:00","id":1335281,"title":"","content":"I believe it was stated by a dev that vampires to suffer from fatigue, but they recover from it faster than humans do. Very rapidly, after they stop to take a break. I can't find the source right now, though, so it's possible I'm misremembering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T03:05:02-07:00","id":1335288,"title":"","content":"Well, could be I don't know... but seems a stretch to me to not give siluch advantage to vampire race while they are possessing far much stronger powers. <br /> Also I can remember a novel in Dark era where a vampire was travelling running across the countriside to reach the a city far away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T05:23:07-07:00","id":1335299,"title":"","content":"When we're talking about really short distances, then each character can move up to their speed and take an instant action, or forgo of their action to run a distance of double their speed.<br /> So, no dice roll is really required. Whoever has the highest speed wins. Usually, Stamina + Athletics rolls refer to a chase or a race, not a short burst of movement.<br /> <br /> This is how I would handle a chase.<br /> <br /> Make the roll an extended roll, and decide on a number between 1 and 9 based on how far the two characters start. We'll call this number &quot;distance&quot;<br /> <br /> Then each &quot;turn&quot; both characters roll Stamina + Athletics.<br /> <br /> On a dramatic failure, a character gains the exhausted condition. (If the character is a vampire or generally someone who would not be easily exhausted, you can just have them automatically fail their next roll instead)<br /> On a failure, nothing happens.<br /> On a success, the character being chased adds 1 to distance, and the pursuer subtracts 1 from distance.<br /> On an exceptional success, the character adds 2 to distance or subtracts 2 from distance instead of 1<br /> <br /> If distance reaches 0, then the pursuer wins and catches up to the prey.<br /> If distance reaches 10, then the prey has escaped.<br /> <br /> Like any other extended roll, the total number of rolls each character has is equal to their unmodified dice pool. If a character runs out of rolls, then they need to take a moment to rest and the other character can continue rolling.<br /> <br /> If one of the participants would not be easily exhausted (for instance if that character is a vampire), then give that character 2 extra rolls.<br /> <br /> If both characters run out of rolls, then have the pursuer roll Stamina + Athletics - distance. On a success, the pursuer wins. On a failure, the prey escapes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 09-12-2019, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T16:13:13-07:00","id":1335806,"title":"","content":"If a Strix is in a living human, vampires are still going to catch the Predatory Aura, right? Are they just going to think &quot;This is a vampire using Blush of Life,&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T00:13:54-07:00","id":1335842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1335806#post1335806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Strix is in a living human, vampires are still going to catch the Predatory Aura, right? Are they just going to think &amp;quot;This is a vampire using Blush of Life,&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, core book says &quot;Kindred can\u2019t discern whether someone is a vampire or a Strix possessing a corpse; &quot;<br /> So i think the answer is yes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-01T16:02:33-07:00","id":1338884,"title":"","content":"I remember there was a topic about possible way for a bp6+ to feed from other kindred without suffering the vinculum. Could someone point it out to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T05:49:19-07:00","id":1338979,"title":"","content":"Feed from revenants.<br /> Feed from kindred bloodlines whose vitae does not induce vinculum.<br /> Establish a 3 stage vinculum to someone else.<br /> Cruac ritual that nullifies vinculum formation the next time one imbibes vitae.<br /> Use the Theban ritual Vitae Reliquary to store a LOT of your own vitae to imbibe.<br /> There are a few Invictus oaths that obliquely and expressly indicate vinculums don't form when imbibing vitae from participant kindred.<br /> <br /> Originally it was that they would not become vitae addicts once they needed vitae for sustenance, not that a vinculum couldn't form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T07:46:31-07:00","id":1340948,"title":"","content":"From a Fan-splat what would Happen if a Princess is possessed be a Strix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T09:19:11-07:00","id":1340962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1340948#post1340948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a Fan-splat what would Happen if a Princess is possessed be a Strix?</div> </div> </div> </div>Misa amane? \ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T12:49:26-07:00","id":1340990,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn would like a Fan bloodline or two showing Darkness (Or MAYBE Light) Focused bloodlines..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T14:05:44-07:00","id":1343007,"title":"","content":"So I am not a fan of the two dot Animalism Discipline (Raise the Familiar) and was wondering, mechanically, if there were any other options. For example, maybe using the 1e version rather than the 2e on (and if so any thoughts on the adaptation(, or even if there were fan made versions instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T14:19:40-07:00","id":1343011,"title":"","content":"I Think it would work I suppose though I have to ask what you don't like about Raise the Familiar?<br /> <br /> An animal corpse you can send out as a spy, or use as an attack dog","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T14:39:21-07:00","id":1343017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1343011#post1343011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Think it would work I suppose though I have to ask what you don't like about Raise the Familiar?<br /> <br /> An animal corpse you can send out as a spy, or use as an attack dog</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing I don't like about it - the animal corpse. Yes, I get it, vampires are undead, but its a different state then the rotting corpse. I think Animalism should be about living animals not killing one and controlling its dead remains. <br /> <br /> So, I wanted to see if there were any alternate versions of a second dot power so I can have that be used rather than Raise the Familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:49:30-07:00","id":1343071,"title":"","content":"curious?<br /> <br /> For those who use the Circle of the Crone Titles from first edition of<br /> <br /> Fool<br /> Hero<br /> Father<br /> Hermit<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> Maiden<br /> Scarlet Woman<br /> Mother<br /> Crone<br /> <br /> Think that accidently creating a revenant would be enough to make the leap to Mother or Father? <br /> <br /> or is the unplanned nature going to hinder things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T21:00:43-07:00","id":1343091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1343017#post1343017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing I don't like about it - the animal corpse. Yes, I get it, vampires are undead, but its a different state then the rotting corpse. I think Animalism should be about living animals not killing one and controlling its dead remains.<br /> <br /> So, I wanted to see if there were any alternate versions of a second dot power so I can have that be used rather than Raise the Familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've run into that issue too (players feeling necromancy was out-of-theme with Animalism); I mixed together a bit of 1e and Masquerade to modify the progression, making Subsume the Lesser Spirit a main-path power and allowing a bit of control over other vampires' Beasts (provoking frenzy or granting a roll to break out out of it) at higher levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T05:23:48-07:00","id":1343132,"title":"","content":"Raise the Familiar is something that only makes sense in 2e. In earlier games the Beast was your worst friend at best and the cult that kidnapped you at worst, in 2e it\u2019s Tiger Mum with a check book who wants to make you what they believe is the best possible you and will give you whatever you need to become it.<br /> If you\u2019re going to change it you may want to add a power that ghouls can use, as is they can only use the first dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T15:03:28-07:00","id":1343664,"title":"","content":"I'm actually liking Rise the Familiar. Vampire are undead and having undead minions (animals) it's quite on theme as kings of living and unliving animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T14:00:25-07:00","id":1343859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1343664#post1343664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually liking Rise the Familiar. Vampire are undead and having undead minions (animals) it's quite on theme as kings of living and unliving animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm cool with necromantic powers (like the 1e version of that one, <i>Undying Familiar</i>), it just seems weird as a main-path power. Sort of like how Protean 1 doesn't quite mesh with the rest of Protean, to me. I would make it a Devotion instead, and maybe replace it with something hinting at the &quot;lord of the land&quot; concept that will be fully realized in the capstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T14:59:04-07:00","id":1343867,"title":"","content":"I think the dev blog mentioned that Animalism uses the theme of vampirism-as-infection, going with that whole /the curse wants to get out/ thing. So in that sense, I think it's pretty on brand. Especially given the idea where the second dot is a deepening of the first dot's effects.<br /> <br /> If the discipline were the only way to create animal ghouls, I don't think it would feel like a deviation. So it seems like the weirdness with /Raise the Familiar/ is that it's the only discipline that affects dead things. <br /> <br /> So what if instead of getting rid of Raise the Familiar, we changed the rest of Animalism to include semi-necromantic effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T18:15:01-07:00","id":1343901,"title":"","content":"There is a devotion called Undying Familiar, which lets you have a living familiar. Maybe you can kind of switch the two (with some minor changes)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T18:51:20-07:00","id":1343904,"title":"","content":"(Rose also mentioned an idea for Dominate-necromancy, given how Dominate can control living people's actions. I think if that had been implemented I'd be more okay with Animalism-necromancy as a main-path power.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-26T20:06:23-07:00","id":1343915,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to think of weird, eldrich powers for some elders, and I think maybe just adding a few extra effects to Animalism might make the necromantic stuff feel more at home.<br /> <br /> So maybe anything which has tasted your blood and is currently under the effects of <i>Feral Infection</i>, upon death, has a chance of raising as a short lived, hungry zombie-animal. Or <i>Summon The Hunt</i> can incorporate some of the old Animalism threnodies, like <i>Kill the Messenger</i> which makes an animal carry a message and die shortly after. Maybe <i>Lord of the Land</i> includes effects for controlling plants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T01:45:49-07:00","id":1343943,"title":"","content":"Just giving you the ability to remotely contact any animal ghoul would be a pretty powerful ability for a second level of a discipline. Maybe too powerful since it requires a devotion to get it to last weeks as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T17:39:39-07:00","id":1344537,"title":"","content":"Raise The Familiar makes lots of sense because as an animal guy, it gives you a way to bring back that treasured pet or preserve your pack, flock, or endangered animal beyond death. I could see a Neonate spontaneously developing it when he loses his favorite dog/cat/etc who is his only contact from his living days and with whom he has developed flawless communication. Then it tragically dies and in a desperate attempt to save his best friend, feeds it some of his Vitae and says a prayer to a god in which he no longer believes. Instead of returning as floofy the kitten though, it has a disturbingly familiar cold, menacing hunger and is much nippier than before.<br /> Also it's basically The Embrace performed on an animal, and it builds upon or enhances every other Animalism power in some way. Feral Whispers is required for any real control. Summon the Hunt and Feral Infection benefit by containing your blood alone (unlike a ghoul which has mostly it's own blood) to spread around, as well as enhancing Lord of the Land.<br /> Actually going with the Blood as infection thing, your could even use the Familiar to feed your ghouls or other Familiars since it carries only your blood.<br /> <br /> If necromancy is still your big hangup, then you could just re-skin it as a sort of enhanced ghouling process and keep the mechanics as is. it does seem to be a well thought out power that fits <i>very</i> well mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 10-29-2019, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T01:25:17-07:00","id":1344605,"title":"","content":"Is Mass Embrace still a thing in Requiem 2ed? <br /> How is it working and how can be addressed since the humanity loss happening for each embrace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T01:32:04-07:00","id":1344607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1344605#post1344605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Mass Embrace still a thing in Requiem 2ed?<br /> How is it working and how can be addressed since the humanity loss happening for each embrace?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a thing Kindred do generally, but the Ordo Dracul have a Scale for Coil of the Voivode called &quot;Mass Embrace&quot; (p. 159). It costs a single Humanity dot and a truckload of blood. It also risks creating Humanity 0 monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T04:59:18-07:00","id":1344897,"title":"","content":"Probably someone already asked it but i can t find the thread so...<br /> What is the logic behind mostly acquired bane doing only bashing damage?<br /> Fire and sunlight are also banes and they do at least lethal, what is the difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:20:49-07:00","id":1344945,"title":"","content":"Fire and sunlight, by default, do Aggravated damage, not Lethal and they are a thematic counterpoint to the curse of vampirism.<br /> And personal banes are lesser banes. They are acquired based on the idiosyncracies of the individual or a clan subsect, they are not tied to the inherent nature of kindred. <br /> Mechanically they are supposed to provide minor flaws for roleplaying flavor. If they actually had any serious drawbacks that couldn't be easily mitigated or required excessive resource expenditure to eliminate (Lethal damage and Willpower point hemorraging isn't something to be casually ignored due to the mechanics by which they are replenished.) nobody would opt to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T08:58:07-07:00","id":1344955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1344945#post1344945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire and sunlight, by default, do Aggravated damage, not Lethal and they are a thematic counterpoint to the curse of vampirism.<br /> And personal banes are lesser banes. They are acquired based on the idiosyncracies of the individual or a clan subsect, they are not tied to the inherent nature of kindred. <br /> Mechanically they are supposed to provide minor flaws for roleplaying flavor. If they actually had any serious drawbacks that couldn't be easily mitigated or required excessive resource expenditure to eliminate (Lethal damage and Willpower point hemorraging isn't something to be casually ignored due to the mechanics by which they are replenished.) nobody would opt to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 102 table states that sunlight does lethal from humanity 10 to 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:08:12-07:00","id":1345036,"title":"","content":"The average vampire doesn't have a Humanity rating that high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:21:53-07:00","id":1345039,"title":"","content":"Isn't the average rating of most vampires outside of Elders 5-6? I mean, 7-8 is considered new vampire territory, and 3-4 is considered Elder, so 5-8 would include most ancillae and neonates, and we have a few that might reach 9-10 through sincere effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T13:37:37-07:00","id":1345043,"title":"","content":"4 seems to be the average for ancilla. From the core, p106, 'Most ancilla fall into this range of Humanity.' 7 is pretty clearly new yet established enough to be a PC vampire territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T14:57:46-07:00","id":1345067,"title":"","content":"The average PC is definitely at 5+, considering that you start at 7 and most games never reaches three failed detachment checks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T16:45:22-07:00","id":1345105,"title":"","content":"I also would say average vampire is 5-6","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T17:31:45-07:00","id":1345119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1344897#post1344897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably someone already asked it but i can t find the thread so...<br /> What is the logic behind mostly acquired bane doing only bashing damage?<br /> Fire and sunlight are also banes and they do at least lethal, what is the difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire already does lethal damage to everybody who isn't magically immune or resistant to it and sunlight is core to the Kindred condition to the point where the only way Resilience \u2014 a Discipline that specifically still works to mitigate the damage from other banes, including fire \u2014 helps you with damage from sunlight is by giving you more Health to burn through.<br /> <br /> Bashing damage is a bigger deal for vampires than it is for mortals \u2014 every type of damage requires Vitae to heal, and deferring unconscious spending costs Willpower, which they also don't get for free like mortals do. Repulsion inflicts its damage as dice instead of directly because it has a second effect that's more central to the name of the bane, and Bells likewise triggers frenzy on top of its rolled damage, but Invitation and Plague of Purity just outright inflict 10 - Humanity bashing damage, which is usually going to set you back by at least 3 Vitae to get back to normal if you're at the point where you're taking banes.<br /> <br /> As a vampire, your Health track is your Vitae deficit, which in turn imposes a higher risk of being no better off at the start of the night than a revenant. If you have seven Health and Humanity 3 and entering a dwelling uninvited causes you to take a full track of bashing damage that you can't heal until you leave the building, you're going to think twice about breaking and entering even if in theory you could build up Resilience or drain the residents dry to top off once you're out the window.<br /> <br /> There's also the same logic that means the Strix take lethal damage from their banes: You're a vampire, and once you're dead, you're dead. Lethal damage isn't granular enough for a bane to be a deterrent instead of a killing blow for things that fall unconscious and remain vulnerable at full lethal, but it's plenty for nigh-incorporeal bodyjackers who lose Vitae every time they take aggravated damage and need to spend Willpower to heal at the same rate Kindred spend Vitae (for which they have a three-to-one conversion rate). The stakes are raised dramatically higher when you let the kind of Humanity-based scaling published banes work with apply lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T20:34:08-07:00","id":1345155,"title":"","content":"Can a Vampire Reverse an Acquired Bane?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T03:29:49-07:00","id":1345186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1345119#post1345119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire already does lethal damage to everybody who isn't magically immune or resistant to it and sunlight is core to the Kindred condition to the point where the only way Resilience \u2014 a Discipline that specifically still works to mitigate the damage from other banes, including fire \u2014 helps you with damage from sunlight is by giving you more Health to burn through.<br /> <br /> Bashing damage is a bigger deal for vampires than it is for mortals \u2014 every type of damage requires Vitae to heal, and deferring unconscious spending costs Willpower, which they also don't get for free like mortals do. Repulsion inflicts its damage as dice instead of directly because it has a second effect that's more central to the name of the bane, and Bells likewise triggers frenzy on top of its rolled damage, but Invitation and Plague of Purity just outright inflict 10 - Humanity bashing damage, which is usually going to set you back by at least 3 Vitae to get back to normal if you're at the point where you're taking banes.<br /> <br /> As a vampire, your Health track is your Vitae deficit, which in turn imposes a higher risk of being no better off at the start of the night than a revenant. If you have seven Health and Humanity 3 and entering a dwelling uninvited causes you to take a full track of bashing damage that you can't heal until you leave the building, you're going to think twice about breaking and entering even if in theory you could build up Resilience or drain the residents dry to top off once you're out the window.<br /> <br /> There's also the same logic that means the Strix take lethal damage from their banes: You're a vampire, and once you're dead, you're dead. Lethal damage isn't granular enough for a bane to be a deterrent instead of a killing blow for things that fall unconscious and remain vulnerable at full lethal, but it's plenty for nigh-incorporeal bodyjackers who lose Vitae every time they take aggravated damage and need to spend Willpower to heal at the same rate Kindred spend Vitae (for which they have a three-to-one conversion rate). The stakes are raised dramatically higher when you let the kind of Humanity-based scaling published banes work with apply lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>By this post and others it seems to me that the general opinion is that acquired bane are seen as a nuisance, the kind of things that in films make a vampire hiss and step back.<br /> What kind of impact would have to turn this source of damage to aggravated?<br /> Would it be a lesson too harsh on the consequence of detachment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T03:32:05-07:00","id":1345187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1345155#post1345155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Vampire Reverse an Acquired Bane?</div> </div> </div> </div>As i can remember, No official rules or in game legends exist about this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T04:24:53-07:00","id":1345194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1345186#post1345186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of impact would have to turn this source of damage to aggravated?<br /> Would it be a lesson too harsh on the consequence of detachment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Much the same way that outright <i>death</i> is too harsh a lesson. Encounter an acquired aggravated two or three times in a short period of time and chances are the character just dies unless they have high Resilience.<br /> <br /> No, I think bashing works fine as it is. If you want it more punishing, you could go for lethal. It costs twice as much to heal but I don't see that as too punishing. (And unlike aggravated damage you could heal everything in one night instead of spending huge Vitae reserves over potentially a week to restore yourself.) The only problem I see would instead be that it can make it way too easy to fall into Torpor from damage. With few health boxes and low Humanity it's potentially possible for a Kindred with the no invitation bane to trip on the threshold and stay down until someone carries them out so they can heal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T06:50:50-07:00","id":1345218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1345194#post1345194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Much the same way that outright <i>death</i> is too harsh a lesson. Encounter an acquired aggravated two or three times in a short period of time and chances are the character just dies unless they have high Resilience.<br /> <br /> No, I think bashing works fine as it is. If you want it more punishing, you could go for lethal. It costs twice as much to heal but I don't see that as too punishing. (And unlike aggravated damage you could heal everything in one night instead of spending huge Vitae reserves over potentially a week to restore yourself.) The only problem I see would instead be that it can make it way too easy to fall into Torpor from damage. With few health boxes and low Humanity it's potentially possible for a Kindred with the no invitation bane to trip on the threshold and stay down until someone carries them out so they can heal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your point of view.<br /> Probably bashing are fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T08:42:31-08:00","id":1350444,"title":"","content":"Quickly need your help as I'm having a game in 1 hour:<br /> <br /> Elysium, why kindred should be willing to go there (or any other aggregation event) with the risk Mekhet (or any other proficient Auspex user) could be scanning their minds. How can an Elysiunnbe protected from this? The undetetectability of Auspex is one of the main and most gap and fail in 2ed system on my opinion. Although I love Ausoex design. Inwould just have put the possibility to be detected, failing the roll in example. By this way a Mekhet would have thought much more before to use it on any high status vampire....<br /> How do you deal with it?<br /> <br /> Asking because 1 of my player has Auspex 4 and today tman Elysium session is planned...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T09:28:48-08:00","id":1350452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1350444#post1350444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quickly need your help as I'm having a game in 1 hour:<br /> <br /> Elysium, why kindred should be willing to go there (or any other aggregation event) with the risk Mekhet (or any other proficient Auspex user) could be scanning their minds. How can an Elysiunnbe protected from this? The undetetectability of Auspex is one of the main and most gap and fail in 2ed system on my opinion. Although I love Ausoex design. Inwould just have put the possibility to be detected, failing the roll in example. By this way a Mekhet would have thought much more before to use it on any high status vampire....<br /> How do you deal with it?<br /> <br /> Asking because 1 of my player has Auspex 4 and today tman Elysium session is planned...</div> </div> </div> </div>For your specific player: If they bought Auspex 4, presumably reading minds is the thing they wanted to use the power for, so...let them read minds and have fun with the power they bought? If complications need to be thrown up, well, I don't see why Auspex 1 couldn't detect mind-reading as a form of threat (since it can definitely detect Auspex 5).<br /> <br /> The curse of any well-functioning Discipline is that what players can do, Storyteller characters can do as well (and vice-versa).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23896-mirthless","name":"Mirthless","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T09:34:22-08:00","id":1350453,"title":"","content":"If you fail in using a Discipline, stuff still happens. This is already a rule. If Disciplines are banned from Elysium, then this is enough indication that someone was trying to use one. Furthermore, only the first use of Auspex in a scene is free. After that costs Vitae. A Mekhet shouldn't be using it willy-nilly without a goal in mind. If a Mekhet does have a goal in mind, whether or not you're in Elysium really doesn't matter. They can do it to you anywhere, and you wouldn't even know it. They get Obfuscate, too, after all.<br /> <br /> Even if they do use it and learn a secret, so what? They're only useful insofar you can leverage them. If you find out the Prince is a Diablerist, who cares? You can't prove it. Nobody is going to believe you or act on it. People aren't going to trust the word of an Auspex user just because they know Auspex. Vampires lie. That's rule #1 for the Danse Macabre. If you're important enough that people would take your word on it, you don't need to use Auspex at all. You can say anything you want.<br /> <br /> The &quot;problems&quot; with Auspex are massively overplayed and, oddly enough, the people who like to complain about these &quot;problems&quot; always ignore the drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T10:45:59-08:00","id":1350463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1350453#post1350453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you fail in using a Discipline, stuff still happens. This is already a rule. If Disciplines are banned from Elysium, then this is enough indication that someone was trying to use one. Furthermore, only the first use of Auspex in a scene is free. After that costs Vitae. A Mekhet shouldn't be using it willy-nilly without a goal in mind. If a Mekhet does have a goal in mind, whether or not you're in Elysium really doesn't matter. They can do it to you anywhere, and you wouldn't even know it. They get Obfuscate, too, after all.<br /> <br /> Even if they do use it and learn a secret, so what? They're only useful insofar you can leverage them. If you find out the Prince is a Diablerist, who cares? You can't prove it. Nobody is going to believe you or act on it. People aren't going to trust the word of an Auspex user just because they know Auspex. Vampires lie. That's rule #1 for the Danse Macabre. If you're important enough that people would take your word on it, you don't need to use Auspex at all. You can say anything you want.<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;problems&amp;quot; with Auspex are massively overplayed and, oddly enough, the people who like to complain about these &amp;quot;problems&amp;quot; always ignore the drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if the PC comes to know what are the exact intentions of a NPC about them it's something Plot Breaker imho. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, book specifically states Ausoex is undetectable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T11:46:52-08:00","id":1350474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1350463#post1350463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, book specifically states Ausoex is undetectable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book also has Auspex 1 detect the use of Auspex 5, so take that with a bit of salt. Additionally, Lay Open the Mind requires concentration. Anyone who creeps around at an Elysium without engaging in conversations (because they wouldn't be able to concentrate on two things at the same time) is going to attract suspicion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T12:23:19-08:00","id":1350486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1350463#post1350463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, book specifically states Ausoex is undetectable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book does say &quot;Other vampires have no way to know when someone is using Auspex to discover their secrets&quot;\u2026and then specifically says Auspex 1 can detect Auspex-use. So I'd take that &quot;other&quot; as meaning &quot;non-Auspex-users&quot;. It plays into the theme that the greatest threat to the Shadows is other Shadows, which I've always liked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T12:25:21-08:00","id":1350488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1350444#post1350444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quickly need your help as I'm having a game in 1 hour:<br /> <br /> Elysium, why kindred should be willing to go there (or any other aggregation event) with the risk Mekhet (or any other proficient Auspex user) could be scanning their minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is: They wouldn\u2019t. Unless they are reasonably sure violations, if detected, would be swiftly and harshly punished. And even then they may not show.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How can an Elysiunnbe protected from this? </div> </div> </div>How subtle do you want to be?<br /> The Elysium master (or one of their appointees) could use Auspex just before closing to ask \u201cWhich ones here violated the prohibition about discipline use during the gathering?\u201d That will unfailingly reveal any discipline use unless they have a power of some sort to conceal said activity then it\u2019s a clash of wills.<br /> Use Dominate, Nightmare, or Majesty on attendees telling/threatening them not to use any disciplines once it starts for the duration of the gathering. Relevant clash of wills, predatory aura contests, resist checks.<br /> Use Dominate to command everyone who attends Elysium to remove their clothes if they use a discipline during the meeting. Relevant resist checks but anyone who did not agree to fail the resist check doesn\u2019t get to be allowed inside.<br /> Elysium could be conducted in a magical nexus point that blocks discipline use or divination powers.<br /> Elysium can be held in an area demarcated with Lord of the Land by the Animalism user. Attendance is by invitation only and the prohibition on discipline use stated on arrival.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The undetetectability of Auspex is one of the main and most gap and fail in 2ed system on my opinion. </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not undetectable so much as there are no direct indications to the victim at the time that it\u2019s being used. If the user runs their mouth to people about private details of a conversation or action others know they weren\u2019t present for, well then their Auspex use is detectable by the fact that when they opened their mouth, they admitted to using it and flagged themselves as untrustworthy to everyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although I love Ausoex design. Inwould just have put the possibility to be detected, failing the roll in example. By this way a Mekhet would have thought much more before to use it on any high status vampire....<br /> How do you deal with it? </div> </div> </div>Simple, I don\u2019t allow cost free fishing expeditions and I don\u2019t run NPC vampires with any influence indulge in witchhunts based on hearsay and half truths, which is all an Auspex user has.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-24-2019, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T02:27:08-08:00","id":1350610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1350488#post1350488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The answer is: They wouldn\u2019t. Unless they are reasonably sure violations, if detected, would be swiftly and harshly punished. And even then they may not show.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How subtle do you want to be?<br /> The Elysium master (or one of their appointees) could use Auspex just before closing to ask \u201cWhich ones here violated the prohibition about discipline use during the gathering?\u201d That will unfailingly reveal any discipline use unless they have a power of some sort of power to conceal said activity then it\u2019s a clash of wills.<br /> Use Dominate, Nightmare, or Majesty on attendees telling/threatening them not to use any disciplines once it starts for the duration of the gathering. Relevant clash of wills, predatory aura contests, resist checks.<br /> Use Dominate to command everyone who attends Elysium to remove their clothes if they use a discipline during the meeting. Relevant resist checks but anyone who did not agree to fail the resist check doesn\u2019t get to be allowed inside.<br /> Elysium could be conducted in a magical nexus point that blocks discipline use or divination powers.<br /> Elysium can be held in an area demarcated with Lord of the Land by the Animalism user. Attendance is by invitation only and the prohibition on discipline use stated on arrival.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s not undetectable so much as there are no direct indications to the victim at the time that it\u2019s being used. If the user runs their mouth to people about private details of a conversation or action others know they weren\u2019t present for, well then their Auspex use is detectable by the fact that when they opened their mouth, they admitted to using it and flagged themselves as untrustworthy to everyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Simple, I don\u2019t allow cost free fishing expeditions and I don\u2019t run NPC vampires with any influence indulge in witchhunts based on hearsay and half truths, which is all an Auspex user has.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like your suggestion about asking who uave violated Elysium rules after the Elysium end. <br /> <br /> Anyway, saying Ausoex it's undetectable I was referring during its use and without other Auspex usage tondetrct it (which should be forbidden as well during an Elysium).<br /> That's said, my main concern is not about a withchunt with the secreta discovered through Auspex. It was much more related to the fact that the player can discover any secret plan other PNC had in mind, ruining the surprise.<br /> <br /> As a real example, there is thia NPC Ventrue of a noble dinasty which is dealing with PCs aleays through a Poasessed mortal (which is cool and paranoid enough imho). But in an Elysium game, that he has to attend in person probably, the PCs could easily discover all its intentions related to them in an eye blink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T06:28:17-08:00","id":1350634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1350610#post1350610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a real example, there is thia NPC Ventrue of a noble dinasty which is dealing with PCs aleays through a Poasessed mortal (which is cool and paranoid enough imho). But in an Elysium game, that he has to attend in person probably, the PCs could easily discover all its intentions related to them in an eye blink.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a couple of ways to deal with that. And either of these would be a good reason the Ventrue in question appears only through possessed proxies. If active discipline use is banned during elysium, using a possessed minion is the perfect alibi since powers can't be used through possessed targets by default. (Although it's arguable that a possessed minion can also be considered active use so your mileage may vary.)<br /> <br /> Since the Ventrue is not physically present, he's not an eligible target for Auspex so it's usage only picks up information relevant to the possessed person. Bonus points if the Ventrue implanted an extensive network of worthless garbage details in his puppet to be Majestied or Auspexed out prior to possession.<br /> <br /> The current conglomeration of minds (the possessing character as well as the possessed person) creates a psi screen that blocks telepathic contact and Auspex reading. You either block it outright (Auspex only works on one target at a time.) or give conjoined details that are impossible to differentiate which mind they're reading without spending a few hours. (Note: If detection of possessed minions is necessary to plot furtherance, this option may be a dead giveaway. If you're going to insert mixed details to sift through, it's going to take some prior preparation on your part as the ST.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T12:19:34-08:00","id":1350877,"title":"","content":"So, here another question:<br /> <br /> About Obfuscate 3, book is stating: <br /> &quot;Tracking is an extended action, with the observer rolling <br /> Wits + Resolve - Obfuscate. A vampire observer can apply the <br /> Blood Potency bonus from Kindred senses. Each roll takes <br /> one turn, and the observer must roll more successes than the <br /> vampire\u2019s Wits + Stealth + Obfuscate.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does it means that Obfuscate user just rolls once and the observer can keep rolling until he reachs the required successes? Which pratically means at some point he will find out the obfuscate user for sure. Also, if the obfuscate user is keeping moving does it change anything? <br /> <br /> Once the observer reached out the successes required, he spot the vampire position but can he lash out to break obfuscate effect like with Auspex or can he just attempt a chance attack with -5 as penality?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T12:46:10-08:00","id":1350886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1350877#post1350877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here another question:<br /> <br /> About Obfuscate 3, book is stating:<br /> &quot;Tracking is an extended action, with the observer rolling<br /> Wits + Resolve - Obfuscate. A vampire observer can apply the<br /> Blood Potency bonus from Kindred senses. Each roll takes<br /> one turn, and the observer must roll more successes than the<br /> vampire\u2019s Wits + Stealth + Obfuscate.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does it means that Obfuscate user just rolls once and the observer can keep rolling until he reachs the required successes? Which pratically means at some point he will find out the obfuscate user for sure. Also, if the obfuscate user is keeping moving does it change anything?<br /> <br /> Once the observer reached out the successes required, he spot the vampire position but can he lash out to break obfuscate effect like with Auspex or can he just attempt a chance attack with -5 as penality?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that the required successes are the sum of the vampire's Wits, Stealth, and Obfuscate dots, because otherwise the Wits + Resolve roll would be both resisted and contested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T12:51:39-08:00","id":1350890,"title":"","content":"It's an Extended action so the tracker only gets a number of rolls equal to their Wits + Resolve total (unless they have the Patient merit then its +2 to that total). So no the tracker doesn't get an infinite number of rolls. <br /> <br /> That depends on how you want to run tracking. If the Obfuscate user keeps moving, the tracker keeps rolling since the Obfuscate user keeps moving the goal post and resetting the tracking attempt environment changes. <br /> I normally run tracking with the one being tracked stating when they stop moving then inform the tracker of relevant modifiers and having them roll. The one being tracked doesn't get to move last second to avoid being found. The tracker doesn't get to find a fresh new trail to follow and keep rolling.<br /> <br /> The tracker can technically do either or. They can attempt a penalized physical attack if they want but if they were smart they'd have brought a can of paint or bucket of confetti to throw in the area without penalty instead. If he has Auspex he can ask a relevant question and provoke a Clash of Wills. Or he can Lash out with the Obfuscate penalty (and bonuses, if any) and try to shatter all the Obfuscate effects they have running currently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T18:48:06-08:00","id":1351566,"title":"","content":"How would Majesty work on someone who had something like Dissociative Identity Disorder? Would the Charmed/Enthralled Conditions carry over from one personality to the next, or would switching personalities shake off the Condition? If the later, what if a person switched then switched back, would the original personality still be under the effects of the conditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T18:56:58-08:00","id":1351568,"title":"","content":"I'm... inclined to say that it'd stick to the one it was applied to, rather than carrying over. They're more-or-less different people with different outlooks and in many cases even partitioned memory, and ought to be treated as such.<br /> <br /> That, and mind-/mood-altering effects target... well, the mind, not so much the brain or the other fleshy bits around it, and ChroD treats those as very separate things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 11-28-2019, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T23:00:28-08:00","id":1352747,"title":"","content":"I am looking for a reference is a book that i read i while back about how the loved ones of a vampire some times come back years latter or people that look like them, and how their blood can be used to make solace? I taught it was in thousand years of night but i can't seem to find it maybe someone can help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25553-nightsyko","name":"Nightsyko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T23:45:21-08:00","id":1352760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightsyko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1352747#post1352747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am looking for a reference is a book that i read i while back about how the loved ones of a vampire some times come back years latter or people that look like them, and how their blood can be used to make solace? I taught it was in thousand years of night but i can't seem to find it maybe someone can help?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be the Inamorata, on page 109-11 of TYoN.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T00:08:10-08:00","id":1352764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nightsyko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1352747#post1352747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am looking for a reference is a book that i read i while back about how the loved ones of a vampire some times come back years latter or people that look like them, and how their blood can be used to make solace? I taught it was in thousand years of night but i can't seem to find it maybe someone can help?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in A thousand years, pag 109, the inamorata chapter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T07:48:53-08:00","id":1354355,"title":"","content":"Is the pdf map from damnation city still available somewhere online?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T10:07:53-08:00","id":1355021,"title":"","content":"Hobbyist Clique &amp; Object Fetishism, can they be used with Blood Sorcery? (VTR 2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T12:45:27-08:00","id":1355042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1