g>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1355105#post1355105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">should use of Majesty granted by &quot;The wish&quot; Be subconscious<br /> <br /> As I dislike the idea of them suffering integrity loss to the point of insanity because of the Devotion.<br /> <br /> I know some people would say im anti accountability.<br /> <br /> But I feel that going on a power trip is part of the appeal.<br /> <br /> Being reduced to a slavering lunatic after Humiliating the dumb jock that Stole your Manga<br /> <br /> is just bad in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of this is how breaking points work at any level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T06:46:02-08:00","id":1355827,"title":"","content":"Nightmare 5. Does it effect Kindred?<br /> <br /> If it does is the damage downgraded to bashing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T07:52:25-08:00","id":1355846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1355827#post1355827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmare 5. Does it effect Kindred?<br /> <br /> If it does is the damage downgraded to bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an old debate on it. Reading the text and the effect described it should not. But someone (rightly) pointed out it is a level 5 discipline which would be definitely too weak if not.<br /> There's no official answer to this question though. So go for whatever you feel right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T08:30:58-08:00","id":1355855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1355827#post1355827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmare 5. Does it effect Kindred?<br /> <br /> If it does is the damage downgraded to bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not.<br /> About the way vampires are hurt:<br /> &quot;Kindred take only bashing damage from many sources that<br /> would normally cause lethal damage to humans. This includes<br /> most non-supernatural weapons. &quot;<br /> &quot;Those few terrible things that cause aggravated wounds&quot;<br /> to mortals cause only lethal harm to vampires. This mostly<br /> includes terrible harm from chemicals, certain supernatural<br /> punishment, and the skills of utmost masters in certain fighting<br /> styles meant to maximize debilitating bodily harm. &quot;<br /> &quot;Few rare perversions of nature - Disciplines, Devotions,<br /> and sorceries - cause aggravated wounds to Kindred. &quot;<br /> <br /> It does not fall into any definition if damage category decreases. He is not a non-supernatural weapon, he really is a form of supernatural punishment but does no natural aggravated damage, and he is a kind of nature perversion (Discipline) but nothing is specified if he should cause aggravated damage in text. Then either he simply does the normal damage described, or would do aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T22:09:10-08:00","id":1356433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1355827#post1355827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmare 5. Does it effect Kindred?<br /> <br /> If it does is the damage downgraded to bashing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would lean towards yes, it does downgrade from lethal to bashing on kindred due to it not calling itself out as an exception, like protean 4 does. On the other hand, this is the fifth dot of a discipline, so treating it as an exception to the downgrade is fair enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T22:54:34-08:00","id":1356439,"title":"","content":"I always thought it weird that it affects vampires at all. It's described as working due to the fear response, stopped heart, inability to sleep; these are all things that do not affect vampires. Fear does, certainly, but not the physiological affects of it.<br /> <br /> It certainly makes sense to downgrade it, and it lines up with RAW.<br /> <br /> People keep noting it's a level five Discipline, but this is the only power (not just the only Discpline, but the only power within any non-Bloodline Discipline) that does direct damage. That's noteworthy on its own. Even Protean requires you to actually perform an attack and hit after activating it. On top of that, it inflicts the Broken Condition and lowers the target's Composure for days. It's pretty potent even without Lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-22T13:51:09-08:00","id":1356530,"title":"","content":"So, the way that most of nightmare works makes me think of a fever/delerium. Like, I think of Nightmare 1 as making the victim's brains glitch similar to a really bad fever or sleep deprivation. They're blinking and sick and unsteady and unsure of what's real and what's being done to them. <br /> <br /> With Ntmr 4, whatever I did to you with 1 now stays in you. Even if I die, you are now sick and you carry the hallucination with you. I'm not sustaining the hallucinations, you are.<br /> <br /> So I kind of want to have Nightmare 5 extend that illness theme. It's not just the fear reaction that is harming you, whatever I did to make you hallucinate is inherently harmful. I dunno what. Maybe something with the blood? I feel like that might be a fun scene to describe: the dude is freaking out at nothing, and suddenly his blood starts tearing itself out of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T12:03:22-08:00","id":1357227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1355827#post1355827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nightmare 5. Does it effect Kindred?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Affect<br /> <br /> And yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it does is the damage downgraded to bashing? </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would, as it's neither mundane nor purely physical.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b><br /> <br /> Does the Daeva's Wanton Curse apply to blood taken from Mages? Mages occupy a weird &quot;mortal, but not really&quot; space in CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T15:33:53-08:00","id":1357258,"title":"","content":"I would say yes, anything they can get Vitae from can be the target of their dependency, whether that's animal, human, Mage, Uratha, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T20:45:49-08:00","id":1357297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1357227#post1357227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Affect<br /> <br /> And yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think it would, as it's neither mundane nor purely physical.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Question:</b><br /> <br /> Does the Daeva's Wanton Curse apply to blood taken from Mages? Mages occupy a weird &quot;mortal, but not really&quot; space in CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like to have fun with blood from creatures other than human. I would make the mage blood taste very vibrant and full of energy or make it depended upon which type of magic they have as a major, You could add some of that flavor into the blood to give each a unique taste and then maybe they could gain an addiction to mage blood. Or the reverse a paranoia about feeding on strange...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T12:22:51-08:00","id":1357586,"title":"","content":"When creating a character, do the RAW dictate that your primary, secondary, and tertiary skills have to correspond to your primary, secondary, and tertiary attributes? If your physical attributes get the primary dots, can the mental skills get primary amount of dots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24208-marquismark","name":"MarquisMark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T12:34:10-08:00","id":1357590,"title":"","content":"That is correct. Your skill allotment does not need to correspond with your attribute allotments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T23:28:57-08:00","id":1357699,"title":"","content":"Thank you sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24208-marquismark","name":"MarquisMark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T01:18:11-08:00","id":1357721,"title":"","content":"i'm a bit lost between Social Maneuvering, Lingua Bellum, debate in Requiem for Rome, and Social Combat.<br /> <br /> i'm running a 2e RfR game. should i replace the debate rules for Linuga Bellum, or will they work fine in 2e?<br /> <br /> i've only heard of Social Combat. what is it, where can i find it, and how is it different from Social Maneuvering (with the doors and such?)<br /> <br /> thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T01:41:34-08:00","id":1357727,"title":"","content":"Social Maneuvering are the rules for attempting to convince someone to do something, through soft manipulation or hard leverage. It's flexible enough that it can be used for basically anything you'd want to convince the other party of.<br /> <br /> Lingua Bellum are the rules for a verbal pissing contest. While rooted in the in-game history of debates in the Camarilla, it's not rules for actually debating anything. It's about socially dominating the opponent rather than discussing a specific topic or trying to convince the audience of your point.<br /> <br /> I haven't read the actual debate rules from RfR so I couldn't tell you how they differ from Lingua Bellum. I'm also not sure about social combat, but from the name it seems to fit the same niche as Lingua Bellum (lit. Tongue/Language of War).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T01:44:39-08:00","id":1357728,"title":"","content":"cool, thanks! i found Social Combat, it was an optional system in Danse Macabre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZinR2EXjdSmNAlIoj0eVUtNW61dvSgz-45XyKTOQt4g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">VtR 2v5 Homebrew: VtR 2e base with my favorite V5 mechanics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/241-nicodemus","name":"nicodemus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T04:52:39-08:00","id":1357741,"title":"","content":"One of the humanity 6 breaking points is to survive a car crash. Does this mean any kind of crash, or only ones that would inflict significant damage (damage a human likely wouldn\u2019t be able to survive)? For example: would driving your car through a wall but suffering no actual damage to your body trigger a breaking point roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T07:57:52-08:00","id":1357773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1357741#post1357741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the humanity 6 breaking points is to survive a car crash. Does this mean any kind of crash, or only ones that would inflict significant damage (damage a human likely wouldn\u2019t be able to survive)? For example: would driving your car through a wall but suffering no actual damage to your body trigger a breaking point roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking points in Vampire are about inhuman things, primarily. I'd only make the player roll if it were something that would kill a human\u2014you get into a head-on collision on the highway, soak the damage with Resilience, and walk away unscathed, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T11:07:11-08:00","id":1357835,"title":"","content":"My Gangrel PC went to an ER, slashed her wrists and activated blush of life so she could get a blood transfusion. I treated it as a Breaking Point because the decision to self-harm was made <i>because </i>she knew that there was no real damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T03:13:47-08:00","id":1358165,"title":"","content":"Beast lasts until it achieve its goal. Nothing can change such goal, just deviate the inmediate objective. <br /> Question is: can the Beast change it's goal, spontaniously, in extreme situation. E.g.: Vampire fall in Angry Frenzy. Want to kill that guy. Circunstances then changes and fire come into play. Building is on fire. Can the frenzy change into fear frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T06:02:36-08:00","id":1358181,"title":"","content":"Yes. Personally I don\u2019t require it to be an existential threat to alter it so much as the realization that the same or better outcome could be the result of altering immediate goals with minimal effort or wait time. In your anger frenzy scenario, the vampire could witness his kill target is directing its efforts to breaking someone else out of a deathtrap. The vampire could proceed to attack or decide to accelerate the other\u2019s approach towards the deathtrap. (I usually require a penalized intelligence roll depending on the type of modification of the goals.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T14:00:23-08:00","id":1358244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1358165#post1358165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast lasts until it achieve its goal. Nothing can change such goal, just deviate the inmediate objective. <br /> Question is: can the Beast change it's goal, spontaniously, in extreme situation. E.g.: Vampire fall in Angry Frenzy. Want to kill that guy. Circunstances then changes and fire come into play. Building is on fire. Can the frenzy change into fear frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, it's a clear no.<br /> Should they be able to? Definitely. One way to handle it is to reroll if you'd encounter a new Frenzy trigger. Either roll as if you were resisting (with appropriate penalties), or use the penalties that should've applied as its own dice pool (i.e. -3 means rolling 3 dice) with success shifting the goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T12:45:28-08:00","id":1358466,"title":"","content":"Changing Frenzy-target should deffinitely be possible (I use Face of the Beast, you fear frenzy and run into the building that I have lit on fire, you nope right out of there).<br /> <br /> But changing Frenzy-type, if possible, should be difficult. I feel like part of the &quot;problem&quot; presented by Frenzy, is that your behavior is locked in to an extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T13:15:44-08:00","id":1358472,"title":"","content":"2e largely did away with different types of Frenzy. It's easy to divide most Frenzy triggers into three categories, but they're not handled separately and any naming conventions for them are probably in-game terms at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T16:29:49-08:00","id":1358496,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the type of frenzy is implicitly relevant.<br /> <br /> You can use Disciplines to shift the target from yourself to another during an anger or hunger frenzy, but I dont think you can use Dominate to move them from hunger frenzy to fear frenzy (though maybe Nightmare?) <br /> <br /> When riding the wave, which let's you decide target/type, I don't think you can choose a fear trigger as the target of a hunger frenzy. You don't want to chomp flames, no matter how pretty they look.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 01-02-2020, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T16:58:05-08:00","id":1358499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1358496#post1358496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When riding the wave, which let's you decide target/type, I don't think you can choose a fear trigger as the target of a hunger frenzy. You don't want to chomp flames, no matter how pretty they look.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course you can't change to a Frenzy goal that isn't valid. Even if the Frenzy trigger was spillt blood and lack of Vitae, you can't Ride the Wave and choose to feed from a rock either. You can, however, choose to Ride the Wave and change the goal from feeding to fleeing the confrontation that caused the blood to be spillt, or to beating up the guy who hurt someone in your presence.<br /> <br /> Edit: The reason you can divide most Frenzy triggers into the three old types is because they correspond to base desires that the Beast would most often want to comply with. But when you encounter a Frenzy trigger you don't determine which type of Frenzy it is; you just determine what the Beast's goal would be from that particular context. Depending on the context it can be as vague as &quot;must feed&quot; to something as specific as &quot;show my dominance over this particular individual&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-02-2020, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T00:12:46-08:00","id":1358563,"title":"","content":"I think at this point we just have a verbal disagreement. I am straight up calling the different categories of frenzy goals &quot;frenzy-types&quot;. The only thing that I think hinges on this disagreement is whether we think that you could change targets, without riding the wave or other intervention, if the new target had the same category of trigger.<br /> <br /> So if the trigger is that you threaten my touchstone and as I beat you, your henchman attacks my touchstone. I think that I can naturally change targets there. If, while I'm now killing your henchman, you set the building on fire, I think it ought to be more difficult to run away than it was to turn on the henchman. <br /> <br /> Say that I cut my finger while you're low on blood, and as you approach me, a stabbing victim steps through the door. I think that if the stabbing victim is more convenient for you, you'd go after the stabbing victim. But if, while you go after the stabbing victim, someone else shoots you, I think you might need to roll to resist the current frenzy rather than go straight to fight/flight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 01-03-2020, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-03T17:18:25-08:00","id":1358736,"title":"","content":"Do you mean Frenzy types as in Frenzy/R\u00f6tschreck/Wassail from first edition, or Frenzy types as in a base desire from a non-exhaustive list where specific target would be a qualifier? Because the former doesn't exist, while the latter is more accurate if somewhat reductive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T15:11:13-08:00","id":1358942,"title":"","content":"Do vampires suffer tilts like Stunned or Arm Wrack? <br /> And if they do, how much damage should they heal to remove the tilt?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T16:42:43-08:00","id":1358955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1358942#post1358942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do vampires suffer tilts like Stunned or Arm Wrack?<br /> And if they do, how much damage should they heal to remove the tilt?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no on Stunned but yes on Arm Wrack: if their arm is removed, they can't really use it for anything until they grow it back. Resolving works just the same as RAW: when the damage is healed, the tilt goes away. (They can just heal the damage a whole lot faster than a living human could.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T15:05:20-08:00","id":1360769,"title":"","content":"How does the Nosferatu's Lonely Curse work from a in-character perspective?<br /> The curse has to do with the Nosferatu's unnatural avatar, which often means disgusting and/or disturbing looks.<br /> <br /> However, based on the rules, the Lonely Curse does not take effect until the Kindred descends to Humanity 6 for the first time.<br /> <br /> My question is, what does that mean for a Nosferatu with clearly unnatural looks?<br /> <br /> Do her deformities not exist <i>until</i> she falls to Humanity 6? I don't like this option because it removes all the cool drama of being ostricezed on day 1 of being turned. Plus it contradicts a lot of established lore.<br /> <br /> Do her deformaties exist, but are somehow <b>not</b> a problem <i>until</i> Humanity 6? I also do not like this option as it makes clearly disgusting looks not affect the character at all until they hit Humanity 6, then magically everybody is now repulsed.<br /> <br /> How do you deal with this at your table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2611-guiskj","name":"guiskj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2611_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T17:33:24-08:00","id":1360793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guiskj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1360769#post1360769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, based on the rules, the Lonely Curse does not take effect until the Kindred descends to Humanity 6 for the first time.<br /> <br /> My question is, what does that mean for a Nosferatu with clearly unnatural looks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, that they haven't descended to Humanity 6 yet.<br /> <br /> The long slide downward into the alienating state of undeath is a big part of 2e's take on vampirism. The Curse applies irrespective of how subtly or unsubtly it warps your presence, but until it does you model characters looking weird and horrifying the same way you would without a specific strain of vampirism being involved. Take Striking Looks and wait for the other shoe to drop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T20:07:51-08:00","id":1360805,"title":"","content":"Well, as a vampire's Humanity drops, they tend to look more bestial and corpse like. In the case of the Nosferatu with a physical deformity it simply doesn't manifest until their Humanity drops to 6 the first time. Is it &quot;magical&quot;? Yes. Only humans are repulsed to the point that it causes a social penalty but everything else maybe just thinks you're gross looking but not to the point of it creating a social penalty. it's just as &quot;magical&quot; as the Mekhet who suddenly can't cross running water or is repelled by garlic when they never had any problem before. Or how the Daeva suddenly becomes addicted to their herd after a year without incident. The Ventrue just overnight decides everyone is just a tool to be used or that people aren't worth his time. <br /> Maybe in the case of the Nosferatu they acquired it as a direct consequence of their actions that caused their Humanity to drop. The Nosferatu's Humanity drops as a result of killing someone in their first frenzy and their face is scarred up because the victim fought back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T23:23:31-08:00","id":1361018,"title":"","content":"Under the effects of a frenzy whose resistance roll got a dramatic failure, does the frenzy persist through the daysleep? (<i>Can</i> a character in such a frenzy enter the daysleep?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T02:02:43-08:00","id":1361037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1361018#post1361018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the effects of a frenzy whose resistance roll got a dramatic failure, does the frenzy persist through the daysleep? (<i>Can</i> a character in such a frenzy enter the daysleep?)</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Frenzy hasn't ended, I'd start checking for attempting to stay up after dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T02:30:12-08:00","id":1361038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1361018#post1361018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the effects of a frenzy whose resistance roll got a dramatic failure, does the frenzy persist through the daysleep? (<i>Can</i> a character in such a frenzy enter the daysleep?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The daysleep is a primordial needing for the very Beast. Frenzy is when Beast has the very control over you. I would not even allow to spend willpower to stay awake unless the situation is life threatening (survival is a Beastial instinct after all). I'd rather see the Beast follow its pray, feeling the sun arising, going to hide for rest. That's how the Beast act: it follow its very, primordial, instincts.<br /> <br /> That's only my interpretation though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T14:10:41-08:00","id":1361159,"title":"","content":"Technically speaking not even other Frenzy triggers seem to be able to change the Beast's mind when in Frenzy. It's quite single-minded once it gets into control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T09:25:48-08:00","id":1361286,"title":"","content":"When two people are trying to subdue an enemy, how should the grappling roll works? Two separate rolls? Summing the first two dice pools? And who should do the move in the next turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T09:43:03-08:00","id":1361289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1361286#post1361286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When two people are trying to subdue an enemy, how should the grappling roll works? Two separate rolls? Summing the first two dice pools? And who should do the move in the next turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thecnically speaking, whether you mean the roll to grab the opponent, you roll for each character in order of initiative with the cumulative defense malus for the defender.<br /> If you mean to obtain the control after alredy being in grapple, I can see 2 ways:<br /> <br /> 1. Sum the successes allowing the one who obtained more successes to decide the action<br /> 2. use the teamwork rule: the most proficient character is the primary actor who add to his pool the successes rolled by the secondary actor. In the case the 2nd actor is obtaining (with his first roll) more successes than the ones obtained by the Primary, I'd allow the secondary to chose the move.<br /> <br /> I personally go for the 2nd though because the presence of your mate is somehow also obstructing yourself, that's why I think apply teamwork is more correct than summing successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-16-2020, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T23:18:09-08:00","id":1361392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1361289#post1361289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thecnically speaking, whether you mean the roll to grab the opponent, you roll for each character in order of initiative with the cumulative defense malus for the defender.<br /> If you mean to obtain the control after alredy being in grapple, I can see 2 ways:<br /> <br /> 1. Sum the successes allowing the one who obtained more successes to decide the action<br /> 2. use the teamwork rule: the most proficient character is the primary actor who add to his pool the successes rolled by the secondary actor. In the case the 2nd actor is obtaining (with his first roll) more successes than the ones obtained by the Primary, I'd allow the secondary to chose the move.<br /> <br /> I personally go for the 2nd though because the presence of your mate is somehow also obstructing yourself, that's why I think apply teamwork is more correct than summing successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Teamwork rule is how I usually handle multiple grapplers against a single target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T23:22:00-08:00","id":1361394,"title":"","content":"Now if 2 opposing grapplers were playing wishbone with the target that would be an entirely different scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T06:35:16-08:00","id":1361452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1361394#post1361394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now if 2 opposing grapplers were playing wishbone with the target that would be an entirely different scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL. I'd just make that a plain opposed strength check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T13:09:16-08:00","id":1361548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1361452#post1361452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> LOL. I'd just make that a plain opposed strength check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the wishbone get a roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T14:19:26-08:00","id":1361570,"title":"","content":"If you have multiple characters in a grapple and none of them are working together the way I would roll it is that whoever rolls highest picks a move and a target for that move and everybody else just wasn't able to accomplish anything in the scuffle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T14:49:09-08:00","id":1361576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1361548#post1361548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the wishbone get a roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can get a stamina roll. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T11:35:24-08:00","id":1367270,"title":"","content":"What is the order of operations when applying environmental modifiers?<br /> <br /> So like, say a character has Resolve + Composure = 4, and just got jumped/shot up in public (-1 wounded, -1 surprised). They delay frenzy to avoid a masquerade breach and play dead (+1 public, +1 delay) until nobody is looking. At the opportune moment, they sprint home because dawn is breaking (sunlight -1). They heal a little on the way and are now hungry (-2). Getting home, they discover their haven is on fire (important property -1). The character doesn't delay frenzy again, and rolls.<br /> <br /> Negative Modifiers: -6<br /> Positive Modifiers: +2<br /> <br /> <br /> So during the roll, just adding everything together straightforwardly, you get 0 (chance die). But, you could apply the positive modifier after reaching chance die, and roll 2. How would you rule it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T12:04:58-08:00","id":1367276,"title":"","content":"I don't remember a specific rule on this, but I always apply dice caps after I finish applying modifiers. So rather than hitting 'chance die' and stopping, I will go into negatives. If I am still negative after applying all modifiers, then I set it to a chance die. Also I add modifiers as they come. It seems kind of weird to lump all the negatives into one modifier, then apply it, then lump all the positives, then apply them, as you appear to be doing. It's extra bookkeeping for no real benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T12:23:18-08:00","id":1367281,"title":"","content":"Yep, a chance die is the <i>result</i> of having a negative pool, it's not the pool itself. If you have a base pool of 3 and a -6 modifier, your pool is -3, which means you would roll a chance die. If you spend willpower, your pool is now 0, so you still roll a chance die. You can't say &quot;a chance die plus three dice is a pool of 3&quot; because a chance die could mean anything from 0 to -99.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T12:26:33-08:00","id":1367283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1367270#post1367270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the order of operations when applying environmental modifiers?</div> </div> </div> </div>The order for applying modifiers doesn't really matter because chance die is what you <i>roll</i> when your dice pool is zero or less. If your base dice pool is 4 and you have penalties totalling -6, you end up with a dice pool of -2. If you then apply a +2 bonus, you end up with a dice pool of 0. Then you roll a chance die.<br /> Basically, chance die is never your dice pool. It's what you roll for non-positive dice pools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-12-2020, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T13:05:15-08:00","id":1367287,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> <br /> You're definitely right about the weirdness of lumping it all together. I was trying to construct as convoluted a scenario as possible, and wasn't thinking about how some things might be irrelevant by the time the roll occurs. I guess part of what I'm trying to figure out is how different frenzy modifiers interact. So like, there's the initial frenzy causes (which I imagine as representing how intense the feeling is), and then the conditions of the current situation, -- which one is the dominant frenzy cause? is it now two two separate Frenzies with a Tempted condition in between?<br /> <br /> Generally I kind of play it by ear on whether I go into negatives or cap at chance die and then apply positives based on the mood of the room/story.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> <br /> Great, that basically answers the question. I guess I just was unsure whether the dice pool could take a negative number, or if the value just became zero and couldn't go lower [where a zero dice pool rolls a chance die].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T15:00:44-08:00","id":1367312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1367270#post1367270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the order of operations when applying environmental modifiers?<br /> <br /> So like, say a character has Resolve + Composure = 4, and just got jumped/shot up in public (-1 wounded, -1 surprised). They delay frenzy to avoid a masquerade breach and play dead (+1 public, +1 delay) until nobody is looking. At the opportune moment, they sprint home because dawn is breaking (sunlight -1). They heal a little on the way and are now hungry (-2). Getting home, they discover their haven is on fire (important property -1). The character doesn't delay frenzy again, and rolls.<br /> <br /> Negative Modifiers: -6<br /> Positive Modifiers: +2<br /> <br /> <br /> So during the roll, just adding everything together straightforwardly, you get 0 (chance die). But, you could apply the positive modifier after reaching chance die, and roll 2. How would you rule it?</div> </div> </div> </div>p69 of the core book and p169 of requiem 2e has this little gem <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apply the modifiers<br /> to your dice pool before you roll. Add all the bonuses first,<br /> then apply penalties </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-12-2020, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T09:39:36-08:00","id":1367552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1367312#post1367312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> p69 of the core book and p169 of requiem 2e has this little gem</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man. You know, it's been years since I did a real readthrough of the whole corebook, and these errors have been adding up. I think I'm going to need to devote some time for it. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T21:53:51-08:00","id":1370504,"title":"","content":"Is size supposed to impact speed?<br /> <br /> On p.81 of VtR 2e it says under Step Seven: Determine Advantages<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Others</span><br /> A vampire\u2019s Defense score is equal to the least of her Wits or Dexterity Attributes, with her Athletics Skill added. Size is 5. Health is equal to your character\u2019s Size + Stamina + Resilience. <b>Speed is Size + Strength + Dexterity.</b> </div> </div> </div>But some of the other gamelines seem to contradict this. The CofD Core Book simply says speed is Strength + Dexterity +5, and the Giant merit doesn't mention increasing speed. Likewise, Werewolf says Speed is given by Strength + Dexterity + Species Factor, which is 5 for Humans, and doesn't appear to count Size when calculating Speeds for the alternate forms.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Do the different gamelines have different rules in this regard? I like giving characters the Giant merit and I'm wondering if it should count towards their speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T22:17:50-08:00","id":1370505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1370504#post1370504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is size supposed to impact speed?<br /> <br /> But some of the other gamelines seem to contradict this. The CofD Core Book simply says speed is Strength + Dexterity +5, and the Giant merit doesn't mention increasing speed. Likewise, Werewolf says Speed is given by Strength + Dexterity + Species Factor, which is 5 for Humans, and doesn't appear to count Size when calculating Speeds for the alternate forms.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Do the different gamelines have different rules in this regard? I like giving characters the Giant merit and I'm wondering if it should count towards their speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the answer is <b>no</b>, Size does not impact Speed. It's just a coincidence that humans have a Size equal to their Species Factor by default (and a mistake in the core).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T23:03:02-08:00","id":1370509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1370504#post1370504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is size supposed to impact speed?<br /> <br /> On p.81 of VtR 2e it says under Step Seven: Determine Advantages<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But some of the other gamelines seem to contradict this. The CofD Core Book simply says speed is Strength + Dexterity +5, and the Giant merit doesn't mention increasing speed. Likewise, Werewolf says Speed is given by Strength + Dexterity + Species Factor, which is 5 for Humans, and doesn't appear to count Size when calculating Speeds for the alternate forms.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Do the different gamelines have different rules in this regard? I like giving characters the Giant merit and I'm wondering if it should count towards their speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's in <b>Vampire </b>is a mistake. It was errata'd in the other books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T01:52:54-08:00","id":1370721,"title":"","content":"What Humanity sin is being a Accomplice to Dialbriee?<br /> <br /> If II give a Torpid victim to a Revenant Who has earned my good will?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T03:01:36-08:00","id":1370727,"title":"","content":"I usually rate being an accomplice to a crime the same level as if one committed the crime with negative or positive modifiers depending on the level of involvement. If it\u2019s something that wouldn\u2019t normally rate on a scale they would check (because their Humanity is too low) I\u2019d have them roll at their current level. In the specific example you cited, I\u2019d have them roll for depraved cruelty (level 1), that\u2019s not just driving the getaway car or destroying evidence after the fact, it\u2019s facilitating the act that otherwise couldn\u2019t have taken place (a form of entrapment) as well as helping put the revenant on the path of diablerie addiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 02-27-2020, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T04:29:50-08:00","id":1370732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1370727#post1370727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it\u2019s something that wouldn\u2019t normally rate on a scale they would check (because their Humanity is too low) I\u2019d have them roll at their current level.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's not normally a check, why have them roll at all?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The impression I get is that instead of adding modifiers (aside from the listed modifiers) the severity of the breaking point should be adjusted by changing which level it's a breaking point on. As such my group has as a thumb rule that any breaking point carried out by someone else but still because of you (i.e. there's a level of distance between you and the event) increases the level of the breaking point by one for you. Since diablerie is always a breaking point, we'd put it at Humanity 1.<br /> <br /> Note that having someone carry out a breaking point should be a breaking point in its own right. Probably at around Humanity 5 if it's knowingly, and Humanity 6 if you do it accidentally or realise it after the fact. But don't roll multiple detachment checks for the same event. Just roll for the worst one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-27T11:54:57-08:00","id":1370810,"title":"","content":"I thought diablerie is always a breaking point in part because it's fracturing your mind/soul. Similar to the Chimera Virus replacing your brain. <br /> <br /> If you're orchestrating someone else diablerizing a victim, I feel like it's probably just on the same level as premeditated murder or torture. Maybe +1 for the distance, maybe -1 because diablerie is so heinous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T11:36:11-08:00","id":1372175,"title":"","content":"Ideas how to handle a Hunting Roll where the Sire Is helping his child With his first hunt or two? <br /> <br /> Teamwork Action Rules? <br /> <br /> Or better for Sire to Seduce the Vessel and offer them to the Childe once possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T13:58:23-08:00","id":1372328,"title":"","content":"Question: does Obfuscate work on animals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T15:24:21-08:00","id":1372342,"title":"","content":"In the previous edition it did not work on animals but the book also expressly said it did not work on animals, the mentally insane or children. The current edition doesn\u2019t say one way or another, so it\u2019s up to the ST to decide. Personally I say it does not because if you expressly require multiple levels of Animalism in order to communicate with and manipulate the emotional state of animals because their minds are too different and animals are incapable of developing disciplines when ghouled, then there is no reason Obfuscate should be an exception other than favoritism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T16:34:07-08:00","id":1372349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372342#post1372342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the previous edition it did not work on animals but the book also expressly said it did not work on animals, the mentally insane or children. The current edition doesn\u2019t say one way or another, so it\u2019s up to the ST to decide. Personally I say it does not because if you expressly require multiple levels of Animalism in order to communicate with and manipulate the emotional state of animals because their minds are too different and animals are incapable of developing disciplines when ghouled, then there is no reason Obfuscate should be an exception other than favoritism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is also a middle ground there. In my opinion, Obfuscate 1, 2, and 4 don't work on animals, but Obfuscate 3 does. Obfuscate 5 is a gray area. I feel this way because Obfuscate 3 actually makes you go invisible as opposed to simply being overlooked. Last time I checked, animals don't have the ability to see invisible creatures, though some might instinctively sense their general presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T16:37:01-08:00","id":1372350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372175#post1372175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas how to handle a Hunting Roll where the Sire Is helping his child With his first hunt or two?<br /> <br /> Teamwork Action Rules?<br /> <br /> Or better for Sire to Seduce the Vessel and offer them to the Childe once possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go with teamwork. Have the sire roll first and however many successes he gets, the neonate gets as a bonus on her roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T19:23:07-08:00","id":1372365,"title":"","content":"That's funny, the last time I checked, there are many species of animals that can detect things humans can't. Often because their method of seeing, hearing, touching, smelling and tasting are superior and/or they emphatically don't work the same way as they do for humans. <br /> <br /> I'm of the opinion if you want to use disciplines which are expressly designed to affect the thoughts and behavior of humans for the obvious purpose of facilitating vampiric predation to extend to animals then make a devotion that incorporates an appropriate rank of Animalism or propose a suitable merit chain with relevant prerequisites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T21:22:21-08:00","id":1372376,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> I'm glad you find my musings hilarious.<br /> <br /> I would like to point out though that nowhere in the 2e writings is it ever expressed that Obfuscate is expressly designed to affect humans only. Animalism, on the other hand, is also not expressly designed to affect animals only, as Animalism 4 explicitly affects humans and vampires as well. So if Animalism has powers that can affect people, I see no reason why the other Disciplines can't (to some degree) affect animals.<br /> <br /> But you do you. If you want to rule that Obfuscate doesn't affect animals unless you pick up specific homebrew Devotions, that's perfectly fine. But if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25591_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25591\" data-vbnamecard=\"25591\">Emerus</a> or anyone else wants to rule that Obfuscate also (in part) affects animals, that's 100% absolutely fine as well and won't break the game (in my experience).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T22:20:28-08:00","id":1372384,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses guys! I think I'll rule that Obfuscate 3 is the only dot that works on animals by default, and create a simple Animalism 1 + Obfuscate 1 Devotion that allows the rest of Obfuscate to affect animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T01:02:48-08:00","id":1372395,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate works on all entities: Human, ghost, spirits, werewolves, mage and Animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T01:16:54-08:00","id":1372397,"title":"","content":"The thing is, some of its dots only refer to people as the targets. Not victims, not creatures. This is why I started having doubts in the first place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T02:21:13-08:00","id":1372403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372397#post1372397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, some of its dots only refer to people as the targets. Not victims, not creatures. This is why I started having doubts in the first place</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you provide some example? Some dots affect specifically Animals and object (2nd dot e.g.) in the sense they can be affected by the power, actively. But everyone around them has the same issues in noticing whoever is under obfuscate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T02:44:23-08:00","id":1372409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372403#post1372403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you provide some example? Some dots affect specifically Animals and object (2nd dot e.g.) in the sense they can be affected by the power, actively. But everyone around them has the same issues in noticing whoever is under obfuscate</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For instance, the first dot Face in the Crowd says &quot;For the rest of the scene, people\u2019s eyes just slide off the vampire. People can tell that someone\u2019s there...&quot;<br /> Notice how it speaks about people being affected by this power, not creatures.<br /> <br /> The second dot Touch of Shadow, can hide an animal, sure, but whether something can be hidden FROM an animal is still unclear.<br /> <br /> The third dot, Cloak of Night, says &quot;The vampire can also spend a point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd to vanish completely. Rather than being overlooked or \u201cjust an average person,\u201d the vampire disappears from the perception of everyone around him.&quot;<br /> Here is says everyone around him, so it could be an indication that this affects creatures other than people. (and by people, i assume we're talking about humans, vampires, werewolves, mages and any other creature with a human-like mind)<br /> <br /> The fourth dot The Familiar Stranger also says &quot;People perceive the vampire as though he were who they\u2019d expect to see based on his chosen disguise&quot;<br /> Once again, it says people.<br /> <br /> The fifth dot Oubliette says &quot;The vampire creates a realm of his own, hiding a place from mundane senses and scrambling the perceptions of everyone within.&quot;<br /> Ok, so like Cloak of Night, Oubliette seems to affect everyone, not just people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, in conclusion, it is this strange wording that drove me to ask the original question. There are hints that some Obfuscate dots affect only people, while some others can affect animals and other creatures. But I cannot be sure, so i wanted to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25591,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","user":"Emerus","date":". 03-03-2020, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T18:40:32-08:00","id":1372598,"title":"","content":"Well Obf 1 and 4 seem to be more about the way people react to &quot;generic person&quot; vs the way an animal would. To a dog, a stranger is a stranger and all are met with whatever emotion the dog normally directs towards strangers, while humans are more discerning about things like &quot;is this stranger supposed/allowed to be here?&quot; etc.<br /> Basically it should work on say, a raven, but it doesn't really matter much because a raven will react to a human stranger in the same way if it has a badge and a gun or if it's wearing gang colors. Does a raven EXPECT to see it's owner or a stranger? How would you rationalize that? That seems to be the reason for such wording IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 03-03-2020, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T01:14:50-08:00","id":1372643,"title":"","content":"I totally agree with Rathamus. This is also my explanation.<br /> Ob. 1 let yourself to be not considered while you're in public places. Other people will be still seeing just they will not care about you. You are a generic face doing uninteresting things (Yes, also lockpicking a door). For an animal...does it really matter? If you are inside a private property such power wouldn't have effect neither on the guard dog nor on the owner of the property.<br /> <br /> I see a point on the 4th power as you could state to the master: I'd take the apparance of the owner of the dog. Would this affect the dog? While I admit it's not clearily specified, I'd rule yes as seems other powers (like 2 or 3 or 5) are working on animals as well so I can't see a reason why they won't in just this specific case as it is not clearily specified they only affect people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T05:49:33-08:00","id":1372683,"title":"","content":"Animals aren't people they're things and if discipline powers should work universally on things then there's no reason to disallow a Ventrue from using Dominate to command a car to start and drive into a window since the power is all about them using their force of will. Or a Gangrel to use Protean to put wings on a motorcycle so they have a flying vehicle since the power is all about transmogrification or a Daeva to seduce a bank vault into opening because it loves her since Majesty is all about inducing admiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T07:59:13-08:00","id":1372711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372683#post1372683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animals aren't people they're things and if discipline powers should work universally on things then there's no reason to disallow a Ventrue from using Dominate to command a car to start and drive into a window since the power is all about them using their force of will. Or a Gangrel to use Protean to put wings on a motorcycle so they have a flying vehicle since the power is all about transmogrification or a Daeva to seduce a bank vault into opening because it loves her since Majesty is all about inducing admiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't make sense: dominate mesmerize people able to understand the command given by words which an animals is not able to understand. In fact Dominate works on any &quot;race&quot; able to understand the language (werewolves, mages, fairy, up to spirit and ghost). There are no evidences that Dominate or Majesty won't work on other races. To Command animals there is a specific discipline called animalism though. For striges, which are the farthest from human, there is a specifc power which make them outside the range of mental disciplines...that means, somehow, which there is no reason to not make them universal.<br /> <br /> The car example does not even deserve a word. Protean does not either (also because it acts on yourself not on other).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T08:29:17-08:00","id":1372715,"title":"","content":"So, one thing to add to this debate is the reason Obfuscate 2 doesn't work on humans. It isn't about size (you can use Touch of Shadow on a door). It's about how relevant humans are to one another. Background-person is way more important to a person than a background-thing, so it takes more &quot;juice&quot;. <br /> <br /> So my guess is that (if we're going to be discerning) Obfuscate 1 should result in just the default behavior. Put it another way - you strip away behavior that hinges on your particular identity. Dogs respond with whatever their &quot;default human&quot; behavior is, so if they've been trained to bark at everyone except their master, they're going to bark at you. <br /> <br /> (If we're still being discerning) Obfuscate 2 should only hide things that aren't incredibly relevant to a given subject. So maybe applying Obfuscate 2 to a mouse won't hide it from a hungry snake. If you try to obfuscate a bag of corn, it might not work on a crow. I bet, if you try to use it on one of those piglets dressed in tiger stripes, the tiger that adopted the piglets would see through Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 3 says that it removes all trace of the user. So we're talking all direct visual images, reflections, sounds, smells, etc. So I'd say that it works across the board. <br /> <br /> Obfuscate 4 says that it works on all senses. You're basically replacing a particular identity with another. And it can work with Obfuscate 2 to trick people about objects. So I'd say it would work on the tiger-piglet example above.<br /> <br /> To be honest though, the idea behind Obfuscate has been stated to as &quot;terrifying invisible murder power, why will nobody help me?&quot; So I feel like I'd only let animals see through the discipline when it's thematic and creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T08:38:47-08:00","id":1372718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372715#post1372715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, one thing to add to this debate is the reason Obfuscate 2 doesn't work on humans. It isn't about size (you can use Touch of Shadow on a door). It's about how relevant humans are to one another. Background-person is way more important to a person than a background-thing, so it takes more &quot;juice&quot;.<br /> <br /> So my guess is that (if we're going to be discerning) Obfuscate 1 should result in just the default behavior. Put it another way - you strip away behavior that hinges on your particular identity. Dogs respond with whatever their &quot;default human&quot; behavior is, so if they've been trained to bark at everyone except their master, they're going to bark at you.<br /> <br /> (If we're still being discerning) Obfuscate 2 should only hide things that aren't incredibly relevant to a given subject. So maybe applying Obfuscate 2 to a mouse won't hide it from a hungry snake. If you try to obfuscate a bag of corn, it might not work on a crow. I bet, if you try to use it on one of those piglets dressed in tiger stripes, the tiger that adopted the piglets would see through Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 3 says that it removes all trace of the user. So we're talking all direct visual images, reflections, sounds, smells, etc. So I'd say that it works across the board.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 4 says that it works on all senses. You're basically replacing a particular identity with another. And it can work with Obfuscate 2 to trick people about objects. So I'd say it would work on the tiger-piglet example above.<br /> <br /> To be honest though, the idea behind Obfuscate has been stated to as &quot;terrifying invisible murder power, why will nobody help me?&quot; So I feel like I'd only let animals see through the discipline when it's thematic and creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do not agree on Obfuscate 2. Why shouldn't it work on something that someone else is looking for (like a door, manufact, or whatever)? It seems very thematic to me which you are looking for the only way out to the building infested by monsters (hence very important for you) and you can't quite notice that emergency door which is right in front of you. Furthermore it's written that whoever is looking for that object must win the contested roll to notice it (why should I roll for something I'm not interested to...). And again, Obfuscate 4 and 5 are extending the power of the 2nd dot which by default should be applicable on any of the allowed target for the 4th and 5th.That poor snake should look for another mouse to eat in my opinion. <br /> I mean, your interpretation is based on no evidences, which make this an house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-04-2020, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T10:26:45-08:00","id":1372737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372718#post1372718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I do not agree on Obfuscate 2. ...<br /> I mean, your interpretation is based on no evidences, which make this an house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, to be clear, if we're playing in my game, Obfuscate 2 applies to animals the same way it does to people (edit: it applies to onlooking animals the same way it applies to onlooking people). Hungry snakes stay hungry at my table. Unless it would be cooler/creepier for animals to see through it. But even then, it wouldn't affect the <i>play</i>, just the mood.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I don't think my spit-balling is that far-fetched. Why is hiding a person more difficult than hiding an object or animal? What is it about a human onlooker's mind, or a human body, that it takes more to hide a human? We know it can't be about size. And I can't think of any other feature of the human body it would be about (unless you think it's got to do with our souls or something). So it's probably got to do with onlookers' minds.<br /> <br /> So it's specific to how onlookers think about people. We know from the description of Obfuscate 1 that if you get into a fight, bystanders need to roll Wits+Composure - Obfuscate dots to notice. So by default, Obfuscate 1 makes you a background-person and keeps anyone from getting more interested. Then, by doing something that stand out a lot, Obfuscate has to work against onlookers' minds to keep you hidden. But being very out of place isn't enough to break Obfuscate 2. The onlooker has to actually be actively be fighting the discipline. Why the asymmetry? Again, it looks like it's a difference between how people think about other people and how they think about objects.<br /> <br /> I do agree that the door in a building building would stay hidden. But that is because the door has been reduced to a background-object. The discipline fights against the searcher reclassifying the door as anything other than a background-object.<br /> <br /> I think the point where you and I seem to be diverging is trying to expand this interpretation to other psychologies. I trying to think of what an animal thinks about in the same way that we think about other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 03-04-2020, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T00:10:19-08:00","id":1372915,"title":"","content":"My take on this is:<br /> -obfuscate cloud the mind, not senses<br /> -animals and humans both have minds<br /> So the question is, what are the differences between the two kind of minds?<br /> Both have the same attributes and the willpower trait<br /> Apparently the only mechanical difference is the lack of integrity, due to the lack of a soul.<br /> So does the lack of a soul made a target immune to obfuscate?<br /> The strix example seems to state that mental disciplines works even on a soulless mind.<br /> Then probably dominate doesn t work on animals, for language issues, but i don t see a reason to immunize animals from obfuscate, auspex or even majesty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T03:24:47-08:00","id":1372925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372915#post1372915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then probably dominate doesn t work on animals, for language issues, but i don t see a reason to immunize animals from obfuscate, auspex or even majesty</div> </div> </div> </div>If so, then you should be able to use Dominate once you've applied Feral Whispers. The usability is limited since you already get the effects of the first two dots and will be limited by the animal's mind when using the third and fourth dots. Possession could be really rad, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T03:29:41-08:00","id":1372926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372175#post1372175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas how to handle a Hunting Roll where the Sire Is helping his child With his first hunt or two? <br /> <br /> Teamwork Action Rules? <br /> <br /> Or better for Sire to Seduce the Vessel and offer them to the Childe once possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would do a team work roll, however I would keep the sires rill secret and in reserve as he lets the new vampire try, coming to the aid with the additional successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T03:41:54-08:00","id":1372928,"title":"","content":"Now here's a question about Obfuscate I've always been wondering but never asked (as it doesn't come up that often at my table):<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 1 imposes a penalty to the onlooker's rolls to notice you, while Obfuscate 3 adds your Obfuscate rating to surprise attacks. Am I correctly assuming that if a vampire using Obfuscate 3 attacks someone, that someone has to roll Wits + Composure - Obfuscate contested by your Dexterity + Stealth + Obfuscate to notice you in time to even react or apply his defense, and if the victim fails the contested roll, he doesn't get to react or apply his defense before the attack lands?<br /> <br /> What if another person you obfuscated by using Touch of Shadow through Obfuscate 3 decides to launch an ambush on someone? Does that person also add your Obfuscate dots to his surprise attack roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","user":"Tomorrow's Nobody","date":". 03-05-2020, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T03:55:38-08:00","id":1372931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372928#post1372928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now here's a question about Obfuscate I've always been wondering but never asked (as it doesn't come up that often at my table):<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 1 imposes a penalty to the onlooker's rolls to notice you, while Obfuscate 3 adds your Obfuscate rating to surprise attacks. Am I correctly assuming that if a vampire using Obfuscate 3 attacks someone, that someone has to roll Wits + Composure - Obfuscate contested by your Dexterity + Stealth + Obfuscate to notice you? I know the victim of your attack automatically notices you after your attack lands, I'm talking about onlookers now.<br /> <br /> What if another person you obfuscated by using Touch of Shadow through Obfuscate 3 decides to launch an ambush on someone? Does that person also add your Obfuscate dots to his surprise attack roll?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Here is a copy from Obfuscate 3 <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The vampire can be tracked by indirect clues, as mentioned above. Tracking is an extended action, with the observer rolling Wits + Resolve - Obfuscate. A vampire observer can apply the Blood Potency bonus from Kindred senses. Each roll takes one turn, and the observer must roll more successes than the vampire\u2019s Wits + Stealth + Obfuscate. Teamwork may be applied. </div> </div> </div>I was never a fan of this mechanic as let's say the Vampire has a total of 9 [target], and the observer is 4d dice [7 less 3 obfuscate], it will take 9 rounds to locate the vamp! I had a player try to enforce this rule while attacking a single target surrounded by 8 body guards, he grappled the first and fed while surrounded by the others. He argues that they had to make the roles, I either gave them compounded bonuses each round or gave them perception - obfuscate vs stealth + obfuscate<br /> <br /> Anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T04:47:55-08:00","id":1372937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372931#post1372931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here is a copy from Obfuscate 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was never a fan of this mechanic as let's say the Vampire has a total of 9 [target], and the observer is 4d dice [7 less 3 obfuscate], it will take 9 rounds to locate the vamp! I had a player try to enforce this rule while attacking a single target surrounded by 8 body guards, he grappled the first and fed while surrounded by the others. He argues that they had to make the roles, I either gave them compounded bonuses each round or gave them perception - obfuscate vs stealth + obfuscate<br /> <br /> Anyway</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I reread the text and reformulated my question.<br /> <br /> I know the errata says someone else cloaked using Touch of Shadow through Cloak of the Night (Obfuscate 3) can still be detected with a simple Wits + Composure - Obfuscate roll, but the question is: does this person add Obfuscate to his surprise attack rolls?<br /> <br /> And am I correct in assuming that when someone is on the receiving end of a surprise attack, he/she rolls Wits + Composure - Obfuscate contested by the attacking vampire's Dexterity + Stealth + Obfuscate to decide if he/she notices the attack on time?<br /> <br /> Or to phrase it in another way:<br /> <br /> When Obfuscate 3 says that the vampire adds his Obfuscate dots to surprise attacks, I assume they are referring to this rule?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Surprise<br /> Characters who don\u2019t realize that they\u2019re about to be on the<br /> receiving end of bloody violence have a chance to notice the<br /> ambush by rolling Wits + Composure, contested by the attacker\u2019s<br /> Dexterity + Stealth. Any character who fails the roll cannot take<br /> an action in the first turn of combat, and can\u2019t apply Defense for<br /> that turn. Determine Initiative in the second turn as normal. </div> </div> </div>And am I assuming correctly that because of Obfuscate 1, the person on the receiving end gains a penalty equal to the vampire's Obfuscate?<br /> <br /> Do the respective bonus and penalty also apply to people obfuscated with Touch of Shadow through Cloak of the Night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","user":"Tomorrow's Nobody","date":". 03-05-2020, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T05:02:28-08:00","id":1372939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372925#post1372925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If so, then you should be able to use Dominate once you've applied Feral Whispers. The usability is limited since you already get the effects of the first two dots and will be limited by the animal's mind when using the third and fourth dots. Possession could be really rad, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feral Whisper allows you to be understood (and obeyed) only as long as you use it. And you can't use two discipline at once if not with a devotion. For that you need a devotion which is useless as you already have the same effect with feral Whisper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T05:15:47-08:00","id":1372941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372937#post1372937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I reread the text and reformulated my question.<br /> <br /> I know the errata says someone else cloaked using Touch of Shadow through Cloak of the Night (Obfuscate 3) can still be detected with a simple Wits + Composure - Obfuscate roll, but the question is: does this person add Obfuscate to his surprise attack rolls?<br /> <br /> And am I correct in assuming that when someone is on the receiving end of a surprise attack, he/she rolls Wits + Composure - Obfuscate contested by the attacking vampire's Dexterity + Stealth + Obfuscate to decide if he/she notices the attack on time?<br /> <br /> Or to phrase it in another way:<br /> <br /> When Obfuscate 3 says that the vampire adds his Obfuscate dots to surprise attacks, I assume they are referring to this rule?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And am I assuming correctly that because of Obfuscate 1, the person on the receiving end gains a penalty equal to the vampire's Obfuscate?<br /> <br /> Do the respective bonus and penalty also apply to people obfuscated with Touch of Shadow through Cloak of the Night?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sticking to the text, obfuscate 3 allows you to extend Obf. 2 to other people, rather than just objects or animals. Which means the person under touch of shadow now is under the effect of Obfuscate 1 itself which means: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [...] If he\u2019s doing something that would draw attention, including but not limited to being violent, everyone around him must make a reflexive Wits + Composure roll to notice the commotion, penalized by the vampire\u2019s Obfuscate dots. </div> </div> </div>.<br /> Seems pretty straightforward then: In case of a surprise attack the victim rolls wits+composure - Vampire obfuscate vs Dex+stealth (without obfuscate bonus as it is a normal mechanic)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372931#post1372931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here is a copy from Obfuscate 3<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was never a fan of this mechanic as let's say the Vampire has a total of 9 [target], and the observer is 4d dice [7 less 3 obfuscate], it will take 9 rounds to locate the vamp! I had a player try to enforce this rule while attacking a single target surrounded by 8 body guards, he grappled the first and fed while surrounded by the others. He argues that they had to make the roles, I either gave them compounded bonuses each round or gave them perception - obfuscate vs stealth + obfuscate<br /> <br /> Anyway</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that is a quite weirdly worded mechanic this one. I personally house rule this letting both the vampire and observer re-roll everytime the vampire moves. <br /> It is becuse indirect clues are like: water moving when vampire passes; smokes or curtains sliding away; heavy rain seems to not fall where the vampire is.<br /> <br /> I also give some environmental bonus for that roll as it become more a contexted rather than a prolonged roll but at my tables seems to work better.<br /> Obfuscate need to be hard to spot, but if you are smart, using e.g.: flour on the floor, fire extinguisher, fire sprinkler and so on you can have an edge.<br /> <br /> That's said, if you do not have Auspex to sense the aura to lash out against, you can be aware about the general position and also attempting a -5 attack, but you won't be able to lash out to let him get out from obfuscate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-05-2020, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T05:55:44-08:00","id":1372947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372925#post1372925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If so, then you should be able to use Dominate once you've applied Feral Whispers. The usability is limited since you already get the effects of the first two dots and will be limited by the animal's mind when using the third and fourth dots. <b>Possession could be really rad, though.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that exactly what the Subsume the Lesser Beast Devotion does? Allow you to possess an animal, that is. Which, perhaps not coincidentally, is an Animalism + Dominate Devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T07:57:51-08:00","id":1372967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372939#post1372939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you can't use two discipline at once if not with a devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't activate two Disciplines at once (provided both requires instant or extended actions to activate), but there's nothing stopping you from activating multiple Disciplines in consecutive turns, imposing multiple effects on the same victim. If a Discipline can be activated reflexively, you can do it the same turn you activate another Discipline that requires an instant action. That's one of the example uses for Celerity's active interrupt effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1372947#post1372947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that exactly what the Subsume the Lesser Beast Devotion does? Allow you to possess an animal, that is. Which, perhaps not coincidentally, is an Animalism + Dominate Devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. I just commented on Neos01's reason for why Dominate wouldn't work on animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T19:25:47-08:00","id":1373131,"title":"","content":"Tessie, would that mean a use of Majesty and Auspex at the same time not be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus","name":"Mateus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24020_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T19:56:56-08:00","id":1373136,"title":"","content":"how Potent is social maneuvering? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It says that a Blood Bond gives a Regnant a perfect impression<br /> <br /> how likely are a few social maneuvering attempts to help train a ghoul?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-05T21:17:33-08:00","id":1373150,"title":"","content":"A perfect impression merely means they can start the encounter to attempt to open doors with one roll per turn to open one door. A regnant can still fuck themself over acting like a shit, making it obvious that they're lying and/or manipulating the person, get a dramatic failure on the relevant social roll required or otherwise create an immediate hostile impression which prevents them from rolling further.<br /> <br /> Yes, it's certainly possible to make social maneuvering rolls to get someone to agree to train a ghoul, but they aren't forced to do it. (Do you really want someone training your ghoul when they actively dislike you or don't want to do it?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T03:26:52-08:00","id":1373169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1373136#post1373136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how likely are a few social maneuvering attempts to help train a ghoul?</div> </div> </div> </div>Social manoeuvring is for convincing someone to do a specific thing. It won't help you when training your ghoul because that's not a situation that social manoeuvring is supposed to cover. Besides, there's no rules for training a ghoul anyway so there's nothing for the social manoeuvring system to interact with.<br /> <br /> But when you do get into situations where social manoeuvring is appropriate (i.e. when convincing someone to do a specific thing, but the ST doesn't deem it to be too outrageous), then it can be really powerful for anyone who's good at it. With a perfect impression from a blood bond you also get to roll once per turn instead of once per hour/day/week/never.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T06:12:04-08:00","id":1373184,"title":"","content":"Ok fair points.<br /> <br /> if I tell a blood bound Capttive &quot;Do nothing to cause a disruption&quot; How longs that last for? Forever? <br /> <br /> I think its a fair point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T06:32:28-08:00","id":1373187,"title":"","content":"No it doesn't last forever. That's extremely ambiguous thus open to interpretation. It's perfectly fair for them to assume it's in reference to whatever you were discussing in their presence at the time of the directive and contingent on what they consider a disruption. If I were an ST and wanted to throw a monkey wrench in the face of a player trying to use a vinculum to exercise absolute control over every thought, action, and emotion over a character they're abusing, I'd have them interpret that to mean not to do anything that could be reasonably traced back to them as the source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T07:24:14-08:00","id":1373198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1373184#post1373184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok fair points.<br /> <br /> if I tell a blood bound Capttive &quot;Do nothing to cause a disruption&quot; How longs that last for? Forever?<br /> <br /> I think its a fair point.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no duration for these kinds of things. The blood bond is not something that compels the victim to act in any certain way. It changes the victim's emotions towards obsession, but how that expresses itself can vary wildly depending on the individuals, pre-existing relationships and circumstances. It's not like Dominate that forces someone to act according to your orders, or even like high level Majesty that dictates how the victim feels about you.<br /> <br /> A few examples:<br /> Alice might be so obsessed over every word her regnant says and never forgets it.<br /> Bob is more reasonable and assumes it's a contextual request.<br /> Charlie might forget about that request within the same scene because they're absent-minded despite wanting to follow it.<br /> Dennis actively ignores it because he think his meddling will be more beneficial.<br /> Eve might have a love/hate style relationship with her regnant and refuses even if it would cause her a breaking point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T07:41:56-08:00","id":1373201,"title":"","content":"Picture being helplessly, head-over-heels smitten with someone. They're amazing and you can't stop thinking about them, even if you're already in a committed relationship, even if you hate that you can't get them out of your head.<br /> <br /> That's what the blood bond does to you. No more and no less.<br /> <br /> If somebody you loved tied you up in the basement and told you to sit there and don't bother her would you do it?<br /> <br /> The Vinculum catches more flies with honey than vinegar. It's not Dominate and it doesn't prevent the victim from recognizing they are being unnaturally influenced. But if you can convince them you're their friend and on their side and what's good for you is good for them because you two are in this together, well, the Vinculum makes that sound very convincing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T03:57:28-08:00","id":1373351,"title":"","content":"oh an Idea?<br /> <br /> it says its Academicly possible to bind a mortal to an Invictus oath?<br /> <br /> Is a Hunter or one of their Family that's been Captured learning Oath of the Model Prisoner Valid then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T04:52:18-08:00","id":1373358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1373351#post1373351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh an Idea?<br /> <br /> it says its Academicly possible to bind a mortal to an Invictus oath?<br /> <br /> Is a Hunter or one of their Family that's been Captured learning Oath of the Model Prisoner Valid then?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the question? You've said it's possible to bind a mortal to an Invictus oath so why wouldn't it be valid?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T09:22:57-08:00","id":1373391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1373351#post1373351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh an Idea?<br /> <br /> it says its Academicly possible to bind a mortal to an Invictus oath?<br /> <br /> Is a Hunter or one of their Family that's been Captured learning Oath of the Model Prisoner Valid then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. They would need an Invictus member relaying such a thing even exists, which is uncharacteristic on it's face since we're talking about the only covenant dedicated to preserving the Masquerade as one of it's main tenets. And even if said Hunter or their family swears it, why would the kindred captors give a flying fuck? They use the prisoner to lure the Hunter into a trap and kill the prisoner as an unacceptable Masquerade breach and the city's prince eats some damage. Small price to pay in order to destroy a Masquerade breach and serial killer and the human who would otherwise join the kindred killing business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-07-2020, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T11:36:34-08:00","id":1373411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1373351#post1373351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh an Idea?<br /> <br /> it says its Academicly possible to bind a mortal to an Invictus oath?<br /> <br /> Is a Hunter or one of their Family that's been Captured learning Oath of the Model Prisoner Valid then?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like, rather than asking about individual mechanics, you're trying to find out whether it's possible to do a specific thing (supernaturally keep somebody prisoner somehow). Why don't you just tell us what it is you're trying to accomplish and we can answer that directly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-07T12:18:37-08:00","id":1373420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1373411#post1373411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds like, rather than asking about individual mechanics, you're trying to find out whether it's possible to do a specific thing (supernaturally keep somebody prisoner somehow). Why don't you just tell us what it is you're trying to accomplish and we can answer that directly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Im wanting to keep a hunters Family member a prisoner and want to stroke my ego by convincing myself that I m honorable and benign.<br /> <br /> have a better idea on how to keep a prisoner from escaping but to keep them safe and well treated?<br /> <br /> From earlier arguments about the Masquerade , taking them to a Notary might be a stupid thing, even one willing to consider officiating an oath from a Mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-08-2020, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T19:16:29-07:00","id":1374473,"title":"","content":"Could the Chimera Virus be used as a way to import Vicissitude 1-5 in a VtR chronicle? Or would it be too broken for the setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T22:34:28-07:00","id":1374504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1374473#post1374473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the Chimera Virus be used as a way to import Vicissitude 1-5 in a VtR chronicle? Or would it be too broken for the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but remember that basically all of Masquerade's Vicissitude could be represented by a single Devotion in Requiem\u2014Requiem disciplines are much more versatile, as a rule, and have tried to move away from multiple dots that do the same thing except more thoroughly (like Fleshcraft vs Bonecraft).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T05:23:07-07:00","id":1374546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1374504#post1374504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but remember that basically all of Masquerade's Vicissitude could be represented by a single Devotion in Requiem\u2014Requiem disciplines are much more versatile, as a rule, and have tried to move away from multiple dots that do the same thing except more thoroughly (like Fleshcraft vs Bonecraft).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the heads up. I used the first 5 Vicissitude dots as an example because the Chimera Virus, as presented in <i>Spilled Blood</i>, also progresses in similar stages that allow a gradual finer control of skin, muscle, cartilage, bone, e.t.c.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T09:03:11-07:00","id":1374930,"title":"","content":"Something I remember somewhere but cant find it anywhere looking...<br /> <br /> That a Revenant only wakes from torpor being fed a bit of Vitae.<br /> <br /> Is that anywhere? or did I imagine that or take as gospel someone impressing their head Cannon on me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T09:48:20-07:00","id":1374935,"title":"","content":"Is Riding the wave reflexive or what? <br /> I was wondering because, you are not allowed to interrupt any reflexive action with Celerity, which means that anyone could go for riding the wave to become immune to any mental discipline in a combat istance. I was thinking to give a celerity user, at least a chance to interrupt it with Celerity, being able to mesmerize/charm the enemy prior he could go in Freny, but seems that's not the case. <br /> How do you deal with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T11:09:18-07:00","id":1374943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1374935#post1374935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Riding the wave reflexive or what?<br /> I was wondering because, you are not allowed to interrupt any reflexive action with Celerity, which means that anyone could go for riding the wave to become immune to any mental discipline in a combat istance. I was thinking to give a celerity user, at least a chance to interrupt it with Celerity, being able to mesmerize/charm the enemy prior he could go in Freny, but seems that's not the case.<br /> How do you deal with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Riding the Wave is reflexive, but it's only done as a response to a Frenzy trigger so it doesn't cause any &quot;problem&quot; that isn't already caused by Frenzy. In fact, if you want to get the Frenzy semi-immunity to mind control as soon as possible, you're much better off taking the Frenzy check and hope you fail (or choose not to take the check and just enter Frenzy, if your group allows that). Unless your dice pool is insanely huge, failure on the Frenzy resist roll is much more likely than scoring all five required successes on the first roll when trying to Ride the Wave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T17:46:55-07:00","id":1374994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1374930#post1374930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I remember somewhere but cant find it anywhere looking...<br /> <br /> That a Revenant only wakes from torpor being fed a bit of Vitae.<br /> <br /> Is that anywhere? or did I imagine that or take as gospel someone impressing their head Cannon on me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's how you wake anyone who's in torpor from damage but there's nothing specific to Revenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T21:10:47-07:00","id":1375747,"title":"","content":"Could an elder Prince have Elysium or Court as their Touchstone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T22:30:20-07:00","id":1375757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Touchstone is part of the mortal world, usually a living,<br /> breathing person. Rarely, it can be a place or thing. The<br /> Touchstone tests a vampire\u2019s Requiem; and by her very<br /> existence, she asks challenging questions of the Kindred. She<br /> tests his values, his priorities, and his true nature. She touches<br /> his Requiem in a fundamentally positive way, even though her<br /> association might cause complications and tribulations for the<br /> vampire. </div> </div> </div>Anything related to vampire society is not 'part of the mortal world' and I would absolutely not allow it as ST. Though these things are always up to your ST, I feel like Elysium or the Court directly opposes the entire point of a Touchstone; to give the Vampire some connection to the mortal world and keep them from diving headfirst into becoming a monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T23:17:34-07:00","id":1375759,"title":"","content":"The prince from Greg Stolze's Chicago probably used the city itself as his touchstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T23:49:55-07:00","id":1375761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1375757#post1375757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything related to vampire society is not 'part of the mortal world' and I would absolutely not allow it as ST. Though these things are always up to your ST, I feel like Elysium or the Court directly opposes the entire point of a Touchstone; to give the Vampire some connection to the mortal world and keep them from diving headfirst into becoming a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am the ST. just trying to brainstorm how my Venture Prince gets willpower back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T23:50:40-07:00","id":1375762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1375759#post1375759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The prince from Greg Stolze's Chicago probably used the city itself as his touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should probably reread that soon. Love that trilogy so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T00:22:37-07:00","id":1375767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1375747#post1375747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could an elder Prince have Elysium or Court as their Touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not ecactly the same, but the merit noblesse oblige from secret of covenants allow you to take a political position in kindred society as a touchstone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T03:42:21-07:00","id":1375780,"title":"","content":"Can Abusive enough treatment still cause a bloodbond to snap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T04:02:18-07:00","id":1375782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeimosMasque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1375747#post1375747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could an elder Prince have Elysium or Court as their Touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>The locale itself, yes, but the concepts of kindred elysium or kindred court are antithetical to a touchstone\u2019s purpose. Keep in mind the fact that many of the more disgusting and misanthropic kindred schemes are plotted and the outright exercise of abuse of human beings take place at those gatherings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T04:13:41-07:00","id":1375785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1375780#post1375780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Abusive enough treatment still cause a bloodbond to snap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Technically asking them once to do something to erode their Humanity the first time may cause them to decide its better to take the hit to their Humanity from severing your head than killing someone they care about or the death by a thousand paper cuts that comes from being asked to do more and more acts of ever descending depravity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T04:41:19-07:00","id":1375789,"title":"","content":"Technically it's the killing of the regnant that breaks the bond in that case. The bond itself does not break unless a stage 3 bond is placed (provided the first bond isn't already) or through use of a Scale or other mystical methods. An abused thrall who knows of such methods could definitely seek them out (which wouldn't even be a breaking point) but that's akin to leaving an abusive relationship which many people unfortunately are hesitant to do despite the abuse they face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T07:42:16-07:00","id":1375809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1375780#post1375780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Abusive enough treatment still cause a bloodbond to snap?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bloodbond can only be broken by Regnant destruction.<br /> Non the less if the abuses are continued the thrall can decide to kill either himself or the the regnant eventually, as an act of complete desperation. But it will be done with an enourmos cost in willpower (not litterally, just metaphorically). Same way a complete desperate person would commit suicide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T10:30:16-07:00","id":1375830,"title":"","content":"I thought the vinculum could snap with enough pain or hatred? I thought there was a line about it in the corebook, but can't find it now. But I know there's an example in Spilled Blood, with the Parliamentarian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T11:16:37-07:00","id":1375836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1375830#post1375830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the vinculum could snap with enough pain or hatred? I thought there was a line about it in the corebook, but can't find it now. But I know there's an example in Spilled Blood, with the Parliamentarian.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Veilleux snapped along with her hold on him.&quot;<br /> <br /> The regnant's hold over a thrall servant is often made possible by the blood bond, but the blood bond alone doesn't force the thrall into service. It's fully possible for a thrall (especially if it's a ghoul who doesn't risk becoming a draugr, as in this example) to have an antagonistic relationship with their regnant despite the blood bond. As mentioned, it's even possible for a thrall to <i>kill</i> their regnant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T11:58:29-07:00","id":1375838,"title":"","content":"You cannot break the bond but, as Tessie pointed out, the thrall can reach a point when he decide to kill the regnant eventually. But I'd keep it for very rare and thematic cases","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T14:14:15-07:00","id":1375856,"title":"","content":"Thing is a Ghoul who was Coerced into his position Probaly will be fighting the blood bond every step of the Way.<br /> <br /> And if they overpower it long enough <br /> <br /> Their regnant could wind up staked...<br /> <br /> Reason why making it not too bad a situation is worthwhile I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T22:56:12-07:00","id":1376213,"title":"","content":"Is it safe to say, that in the covenants they probably have Approved teachers if you want to learn another Clans Signature Discipline<br /> <br /> Especialy the Invictus.<br /> <br /> In one game I ran on Rpol a Invictus Ventrue Traded the Rudiments of Dominate for the Rudiments of protean with a Unbound Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T04:02:38-07:00","id":1376238,"title":"","content":"It depends on the setting. If I\u2019m STing, my players and I don\u2019t permit too much clan and covenant proprietary power crossover because the clan specific powers, rituals, and mysteries, are, level by level, NOT equal in inherent utility or power and it devalues the respective clan or power if anyone can obtain them with an application of Majesty, Dominate, or Nightmare at level 1 or a stage 3 vinculum. If regulating clan specific disciplines is a necessary feature in the setting, (it was in a few because some players wanted to turn the chronicle into a Pok\u00e9mon tournament with their ghouls and childer in one, and another made it a goal to try and learn every discipline available in the game) I leave that to those with clan status, not covenant status.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T01:21:44-07:00","id":1376382,"title":"","content":"Id imagine in most domains The Ventrue probably have a member or two who have learned a dot or two of Majesty.<br /> <br /> and they'd probably prefer others in their clan develop partial blood bonds to them then the Daeva.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T02:43:59-07:00","id":1376384,"title":"","content":"Nope. It means said Ventrue allowed a Daeva to blood bond them. (Obviously you forgot that learning another clan's signature discipline entails consuming their blood.) and Majesty is a crutch for impotent attention whores that's broken by anyone capable of exercising a shred of mental fortitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T05:32:58-07:00","id":1376394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1376384#post1376384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. It means said Ventrue allowed a Daeva to blood bond them. (Obviously you forgot that learning another clan's signature discipline entails consuming their blood.) and Majesty is a crutch for impotent attention whores that's broken by anyone capable of exercising a shred of mental fortitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>partially blood bond them as it only ta kes one drink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T07:21:28-07:00","id":1376400,"title":"","content":"Point is, the typical Ventrue in most settings I play have enough self respect to NOT willingly volunteer to spend a year as the public ass licker of a Daeva whoremonger just for a variant of their own signature discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T07:36:35-07:00","id":1376401,"title":"","content":"Fair enough<br /> <br /> Those who would your suggesting would be looked down on enough by their clan to make them no more likable teachers? <br /> <br /> <br /> In the thing That happened in my game a Invictus Ventrue Fledgling Teaching The basics of Dominate to a Unbound Gangrel in return for the basics of Protean. Agree with me theyd not like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T11:03:49-07:00","id":1376416,"title":"","content":"In my game the secrets and blood of the unique clan disciplines are closely guarded and any clan member found to share them and the participants are brought before the prince and court, most likely for true death. This serves as a warning to others that gifts of Vecna are not bartered and traded like mortals coins with merchants.<br /> <br /> Anyone that runs causes the prince to smile as he enacts a Blood Hunt.<br /> <br /> By the way Vecna is the father of Vampires in my game. It's a Fantasy Requiem setting but with Vecna in a Caine position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T11:51:09-07:00","id":1376420,"title":"","content":"Your games seem to focus a lot on Clans as organisations, or at least as communities. In our game there's very little of that. Any such organisations or communities are almost always based around a single family and/or a Bloodline (which in turn is often member of the same Covenant as well). Other than that, Clans are the basis for a lot of prejudice regarding Clan stereotypes or a Clan's place in Kindred society, but the former isn't cause for any organisational structure, and the latter would either evolve into a Covenant or a Bloodline with time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T15:01:47-07:00","id":1376439,"title":"","content":"Still on the thing about Dealing with an unbound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T17:12:46-07:00","id":1376451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1376439#post1376439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still on the thing about Dealing with an unbound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clan stereotypes are descriptive, not prescriptive. Many Ventrue might certainly be too proud, but plenty of Ventrue could also just not give a shit about pride.<br /> They would only be punished if the other Kindred in the domain cares about that sort of thing. Most would not in my games. And they would only get punished if the deal would come to light. I mean, who would want to let such a deal become known in the first place? Access to a new Discipline is an advantage, and it's only more advantageous if it's not known by your enemies.<br /> A first stage blood bond isn't a particularly hefty price. Especially not if the character has access to one of several ways to protect against or outright break blood bonds. If it's a mutual exchange, a Voivode might even take advantage of it.<br /> Like most of your &quot;Do you think this could happen?&quot;-style questions, it's definitely possible but context determines how viable it is. No one could answer with more certainty without knowing a whole lot more about the context of the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T03:02:42-07:00","id":1376499,"title":"","content":"Is Dark Eras getting out this week? It's been in At Press since last week","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T10:55:38-07:00","id":1376729,"title":"","content":"It's out to backers. It will likely remain that way for a while as they gather errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T21:36:49-07:00","id":1376781,"title":"","content":"one thing on blood bound. Reasons I want it to be possible to break the blood bond if you feel enough resentment, Id prefer Their to be a reason other Then just because your a Kind master to Allow them to practice their religion, or Not to needlessly Humiliate a blood bound captured enemy. oh and reign in abuse of ghouls too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T03:00:59-07:00","id":1376797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1376781#post1376781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one thing on blood bound. Reasons I want it to be possible to break the blood bond if you feel enough resentment, Id prefer Their to be a reason other Then just because your a Kind master to Allow them to practice their religion, or Not to needlessly Humiliate a blood bound captured enemy. oh and reign in abuse of ghouls too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, a blood bond messes with you emotionally but isn't a compulsion that has to be followed. A thrall can practice their religion in secret regardless of what their regnant says (but may feel guilt over it).<br /> And it's not a carte blanche for abusing servants either, as explained before. Most ghoul servants are probably held in check through other means as well, like being their supplier for their Vitae addiction, being their supplier for superhuman powers, and, if the ghoul is relatively new, knowing where all their family members and friends live, alternatively if the ghoul is old enough, being the reason the ghoul doesn't run out of Vitae and die of old age. A combination of these might be just as effective as a blood bond to keep control over someone who faces abuse. Regardless, most vampires aren't abusive for the sake of being abusive. There's nothing to be gained from it and there's no compulsions from the Beast to abuse those around you for no reason (it does want you to respond to challenges, sure, but it should have no interest in antagonising anyone who isn't acting up against you unless you're hungry and even then it's about feeding rather than subjugating a rival). I'd mostly limit such behaviour to elders who have lost touch with human behaviour, with only the occasional sadistic jackass doing the same thing (and probably losing their ghoul servant in the process).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T09:34:53-07:00","id":1376817,"title":"","content":"Is Zmai the Worm from <i>Predators </i>(WtF) supposed/hinted to be a CofD version of an Antediluvian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T17:50:38-07:00","id":1376878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1376817#post1376817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Zmai the Worm from <i>Predators </i>(WtF) supposed/hinted to be a CofD version of an Antediluvian?</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly an open question.<br /> <br /> The entire chapter the Worm appears in is specifically optional, states outright that none of the stuff in it will be referenced in later supplements, and provides two equally non-official explanations for each creature detailed; one of the explanations presented for Zmai is that it's either a source of vampirism or a particularly inhuman creature that has been made a vampire or a vampire that has become particularly inhuman, and it doesn't settle on any one of those in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T18:04:59-07:00","id":1376880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1376817#post1376817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Zmai the Worm from <i>Predators </i>(WtF) supposed/hinted to be a CofD version of an Antediluvian?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. While they do say things won't be referenced in later supplements, the Nosferatu clan book describes something a lot like it.<br /> <br /> From p16, 'Then, they came, in search of the divine blood. A hunting party of five \u2014 a coterie we only now know as the Brothers Worm. They were dead men, yes, but men just the same; five brothers playing the same Requiem, hungry for blood, hungry for power. You know the legends \u2014 they were true then as they are now. Drink the blood of an ancient creature and you may know secret power. Drizzle the blood of a lycanthrope on a sponge of milk cake and consume it, or offer a debt to a dragon for a taste of what oozes through its veins. It may bring madness, but with that madness comes a flourish of promise, a grand revelation of pain.'<br /> <br /> It's one of the better Vampire books, strongly recommend it and the other clanbooks if you're interested in the setting. Though the Daeva and Ventrue ones can be a little dry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-28-2020, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T20:48:41-07:00","id":1376894,"title":"","content":"Curious if a Random Bum Gets Drained of Vitae and raises as a revenant, which trait needs to go up to show they've gotten more inner fire to Survive in the all night society<br /> <br /> Willpower? <br /> <br /> Resolve?<br /> <br /> Composure?<br /> <br /> If their to survive they must develop more Drive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T21:32:48-07:00","id":1376901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1376880#post1376880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably. While they do say things won't be referenced in later supplements, the Nosferatu clan book describes something a lot like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of Worms in Vampire. The Sta-Au deal with a Land of Worms that reads like some form of Wound or Scar or shoal, but that's got precious little in common with Zmai besides a single simple word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1376894#post1376894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious if a Random Bum Gets Drained of Vitae and raises as a revenant, which trait needs to go up to show they've gotten more inner fire to Survive in the all night society<br /> <br /> Willpower?<br /> <br /> Resolve?<br /> <br /> Composure?<br /> <br /> If their to survive they must develop more Drive.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to need to define terms if you want a solid answer to this question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T21:54:58-07:00","id":1376908,"title":"","content":"Drive Passion...<br /> <br /> A Desire to achieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-27T22:14:46-07:00","id":1376914,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T19:47:41-07:00","id":1377265,"title":"","content":"Curious What does the Charmed Or Enthralled Condition do to someone Who is actively hostile how will they remember it? <br /> <br /> If someone goes through a Ghetto or slum and is gulty of the Crimes of being well dressed and white and the gangster whod been going to accost them gets one of those conditions, does it make sense to him latter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T02:14:25-07:00","id":1377315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1377265#post1377265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious What does the Charmed Or Enthralled Condition do to someone Who is actively hostile how will they remember it?<br /> <br /> If someone goes through a Ghetto or slum and is gulty of the Crimes of being well dressed and white and the gangster whod been going to accost them gets one of those conditions, does it make sense to him latter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can understand this confusion actually. <br /> Book is specifying that once the condition ends the victim will remember the feeling he was having towards the Vampire. He simply do not feel the same anymore (I think same way you lose interest for a pretty girl/man when you get to know her better and understand she's not what you were expectin, somehow). So there are different cases:<br /> <br /> 1. The victim is aware abou Majesty and could get very angry (though I don't think it's the case in your example)<br /> 2. He could feel himself weird about what he was feeling, trying to get the distance from that person without hurting him (in memory of that confusing feeling - which it's still in his memory), to not risk to fall in that feeling back; just ignore it and treat the vampire as never happened; Trying to get close to him to be able to feel the same, amazing fashination he was having before.<br /> <br /> All these are lecit behavior because it pretty much depend on the personality of the victim (integrity as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T19:35:01-07:00","id":1378152,"title":"","content":"Something I asked WAY Back was what happens if I Ride the wave and select &quot;Protect&quot; This or that person as the desire.<br /> <br /> Whats the modifier for such a mortals integrity roll?<br /> <br /> Since the Obviously monstrous being is trying to protect him?<br /> <br /> But its probably still a bit of a shock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T06:46:50-07:00","id":1378743,"title":"","content":"Why would the mortal roll Integrity in the first place if they aren\u2019t the victim of an obviously supernatural attack? <br /> <br /> So a vampire slips into frenzy and opts to protect someone else.<br /> <br /> From what and how?<br /> <br /> Another single vampire intending to feed off the mortal?<br /> <br /> From a gang rape or brutal robbery by opportunistic criminals? <br /> <br /> From a car that just deliberately sideswiped him? <br /> <br /> None of those hypothetical situations would necessarily indicate the vampire\u2019s monstrous side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T16:31:45-07:00","id":1381132,"title":"","content":"I once encountered a Devotion in an official sourcebook (not fanmade) that used the Disciplines Dominate, Majesty, &amp; Nightmare.<br /> So with this in mind, I'm wondering how a kindred can use the signature Discipline of another Clan.<br /> Anyone capable of enlightening me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T16:59:21-07:00","id":1381140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1381132#post1381132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once encountered a Devotion in an official sourcebook (not fanmade) that used the Disciplines Dominate, Majesty, &amp; Nightmare.<br /> So with this in mind, I'm wondering how a kindred can use the signature Discipline of another Clan.<br /> Anyone capable of enlightening me?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they can get someone to teach them and would feed them blood. or if they diaberlize someone with the discipline. There are a few in the core book that require having two different signature disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:04:14-07:00","id":1381156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1381132#post1381132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once encountered a Devotion in an official sourcebook (not fanmade) that used the Disciplines Dominate, Majesty, &amp; Nightmare.<br /> So with this in mind, I'm wondering how a kindred can use the signature Discipline of another Clan.<br /> Anyone capable of enlightening me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Bloodline Disciplines are exclusive. The unique Clan Disciplines can be learned by anyone, provided they have someone who teaches it (or they can diablerise it from). Doesn't even have to be of the associated Clan. A Gangrel who knows Majesty can teach it to a Mekhet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:32:00-07:00","id":1381185,"title":"","content":"Thank you for enlightening me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T02:43:25-07:00","id":1381246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1381156#post1381156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only Bloodline Disciplines are exclusive. The unique Clan Disciplines can be learned by anyone, provided they have someone who teaches it (or they can diablerise it from). Doesn't even have to be of the associated Clan. A Gangrel who knows Majesty can teach it to a Mekhet.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not wrong also a point of vitae need to be shared, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T07:40:05-07:00","id":1381320,"title":"","content":"On question I asked earlier on Ventrue learning majesty? If a Ventrue has just enough conscience to want to sweeten his minions servitude a trifle, reasons to simply give them money versus to learn Majesty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T10:37:48-07:00","id":1381366,"title":"","content":"They can actually use money to obtain things they want or need, in essence the Ventrue is still paying for the services. Even if he really doesn\u2019t care about them at all, paying them for something that is known he could get for free implies he does value their services (and discretion in terms of memory alteration) and recognizes they have wants and needs independent of the Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T00:42:39-07:00","id":1381551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1381246#post1381246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I'm not wrong also a point of vitae need to be shared, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Less an &quot;also.&quot; Disciplines aren't &quot;taught,&quot; they manifest spontaneously. They can only manifest if they're already in your blood, so to manifest another clan's, you need to drink another clan's blood. You aren't taught, you drink the blood then your Beast can manifest it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many Kindred spontaneously manifest new Disciplines, as<br /> the Beast asserts itself in new and strange ways. The Blood<br /> makes strong connections between vampires, so most Kindred<br /> only display the Disciplines of their Clan. To learn another<br /> clan\u2019s unique Discipline, the vampire must first track down<br /> another vampire who possesses the Discipline and drink at least<br /> one point of his Vitae \u2014 with all of the attendant consequences. </div> </div> </div>So you can't &quot;teach&quot; Disciplines, only share blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T05:53:51-07:00","id":1381619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1381551#post1381551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Less an &quot;also.&quot; Disciplines aren't &quot;taught,&quot; they manifest spontaneously. They can only manifest if they're already in your blood, so to manifest another clan's, you need to drink another clan's blood. You aren't taught, you drink the blood then your Beast can manifest it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So you can't &quot;teach&quot; Disciplines, only share blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect.<br /> <br /> It is true that often vampires develop new Discipline dots seemingly at random or simply as a result of repeated exercise of lower dots, but you can (and sometimes <i>must</i>) be taught.<ul><li>In the VtR 2e Core rulebook (p. 83) it explicitly states that &quot;as well, Disciplines sometimes require teachers&quot;. You <i>may </i>develop Clan Disciplines and Common Disciplines without a teacher, but Uncommon Disciplines <i>require </i>a teacher.</li> <li>The merit <b>Tutelage </b>(Guide to the Night, p. 127) is about reducing costs of Disciplines and Devotions as part of an extended mentor-student relationship.</li> <li>The original Chicago-based Requiem novels have a character seek out tutelage to learn Obfuscate and it has a scene that covers a moment of said tutelage.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":". 04-15-2020, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T11:57:00-07:00","id":1381722,"title":"","content":"Hello to everyone,<br /> Do you think that daeva clan curse apply only to &quot;pure&quot; humans?<br /> Could it work for ghouls, wolf blooded and other minor splats?<br /> And for major splats like mages and geists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:04:24-07:00","id":1381725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1381722#post1381722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello to everyone,<br /> Do you think that daeva clan curse apply only to &quot;pure&quot; humans?<br /> Could it work for ghouls, wolf blooded and other minor splats?<br /> And for major splats like mages and geists?</div> </div> </div> </div>The book has a list on which ones counts as humans in terms of feeding and applying Swooning/Scarred. I'd just apply that to the Wanton Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:19:59-07:00","id":1381729,"title":"","content":"It applies to whatever mortal's blood that they consumed multiple times. Technically if they fed off Morris the Cat more than once, they'd roll a Humanity check each time and if they kept doing it eventually they'd develop the persistent Dependent Condition on an orange tabby cat that only goes away after the cat dies. Last time I checked, wolf blooded, ghouls, mages, and most other minor and major splats were mortal, so yes the curse would be applicable involving them as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T14:12:16-07:00","id":1382594,"title":"","content":"Hello, i have a simple question ! I can firstly say that english isn\u2019t my main language, i will try to be understandable, but as my question is simple that should not be a problem. :-) I\u2019m interested in Requiem only since a (full^^ ) week \u2013 i used to play Dark Age \u2013 and i found out about the lost/uncommon Dukhan clan here <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Clans_(2nd_Edition\" target=\"_blank\">http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Clans_(2nd_Edition</a>) . Before i came to ask here i carefully looked on the net but i could get almost no information about this clan. Is it <i>that</i> lost ? I could not find either to witch book refers \u00ab DE2 \u00bb. So, do you know about the Dukhan clan ? Who are those mysterious people ? Any thoughts about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26100,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26100-vita-brevis","user":"Vita Brevis","date":". 04-19-2020, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26100-vita-brevis","name":"Vita Brevis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:00:08-07:00","id":1382605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vita Brevis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1382594#post1382594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, i have a simple question ! I can firstly say that english isn\u2019t my main language, i will try to be understandable, but as my question is simple that should not be a problem. :-) I\u2019m interested in Requiem only since a (full^^ ) week \u2013 i used to play Dark Age \u2013 and i found out about the lost/uncommon Dukhan clan here <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Clans_(2nd_Edition\" target=\"_blank\">http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Clans_(2nd_Edition</a>) . Before i came to ask here i carefully looked on the net but i could get almost no information about this clan. Is it <i>that</i> lost ? I could not find either to witch book refers \u00ab DE2 \u00bb. So, do you know about the Dukhan clan ? Who are those mysterious people ? Any thoughts about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dukhan appear in Dark Eras 2 (that's what DE2 stands for), and are honestly more like a Mekhet bloodline than their own clan\u2014they qualify for Mekhet-specific merits, for example. I'm not really sure why they were implemented as a clan instead of a bloodline. They're designed for crossover with Beast: the Primordial, so they have powers based around dreams and nightmares.<br /> <br /> As for why you can't find much information, Dark Eras 2 is very new and hasn't existed for very long. More information will probably appear on the web once they've existed for longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:22:42-07:00","id":1382608,"title":"","content":"Thank you. Any light on what means &quot;dwelling within the Dream.&quot; ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26100-vita-brevis","name":"Vita Brevis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T16:27:56-07:00","id":1382631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1382605#post1382605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Dukhan appear in Dark Eras 2 (that's what DE2 stands for), and are honestly more like a Mekhet bloodline than their own clan\u2014they qualify for Mekhet-specific merits, for example. I'm not really sure why they were implemented as a clan instead of a bloodline. They're designed for crossover with Beast: the Primordial, so they have powers based around dreams and nightmares.<br /> <br /> As for why you can't find much information, Dark Eras 2 is very new and hasn't existed for very long. More information will probably appear on the web once they've existed for longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is dark eras 2 already out? I thought not yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T16:40:30-07:00","id":1382633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1382631#post1382631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is dark eras 2 already out? I thought not yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's out already yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T16:58:51-07:00","id":1382638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vita Brevis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1382608#post1382608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. Any light on what means &quot;dwelling within the Dream.&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dukhan have a strange relation with the part of the Astral where the nightmare-creatures known as the Begotten keep their Lairs, which is called the Primordial Dream; their bane applies when they spend too long without visiting the Astral, whose most accessible regions are the Dark Dream (another name for the Primordial Dream) and the Bright Dream (the mental worlds of humanity's collective unconscious and individual human souls).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T00:45:33-07:00","id":1382692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1382633#post1382633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's out already yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could you pls share the link. I'm not able to find it on Drive ThruRPG. Looking for Dark Eras 2 I can just find the first one.<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T02:27:26-07:00","id":1382699,"title":"","content":"It's not out. Only backers have access to an early version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:10:20-07:00","id":1382785,"title":"","content":"I believe you can pick it up <a href=\"https://chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-2.backerkit.com/hosted_preorders\" target=\"_blank\">on Backerkit</a>. Just choose &quot;PDF preorder&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T12:50:51-07:00","id":1383020,"title":"","content":"Curious how workable would working as a college professor be for a kindred? Night classes exist and you could get the haven merit centered on the campus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T15:37:33-07:00","id":1383042,"title":"","content":"Well, the concept of night classes is not exactly new, so I imagine any kindred with the temperament to work as a tutor, or is willing to teach vocational skills, elementary education or college supplemental courses could do it.<br /> I actually played a character who worked as a college professor. Teaching assistants (Herd, Retainers, occasionally partially vinculum bound victims) usually taught during daylight hours and she had very late office hours or would visit her students at their dorms if she found out they were struggling with their coursework and offer to help. With online courses and night classes becoming ubitiquitous, it would be easy for a kindred to get a job as a professor, what would not be easy would be getting tenure without heavy reliance on disciplines and vinculums. <br /> <br /> There is far too much incoming and outgoing traffic for an entire college campus to be a viable haven. Certainly select sections or even apply different merits to different facets of college existence but not haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T20:10:40-07:00","id":1383080,"title":"","content":"Greek houses anyone? On a viable haven?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T06:20:53-07:00","id":1383133,"title":"","content":"If you don't mind your haven routinely being plastered in the media because your chosen sorority or fraternity is the scene of police criminal investigations for things like prostitution, hazing assaults, rape/sexual assault, underage drinking, illegal drug use and distribution, grand theft auto, accidental deaths, cheating rings and other criminal conspiracies, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-22-2020, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T10:26:30-07:00","id":1383161,"title":"","content":"not best of ideas then.<br /> <br /> Was at a protest at OSU A year ago some brat from a frat tried stealing one of our signs and likely planned to deface it was told the signs are expensive. costing $100 each","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-22-2020, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T20:03:06-07:00","id":1384343,"title":"","content":"Hi. Can someone please help me understand how blood sorcery works in VtR 2e? There are a couple of things I don't get.<br /> <br /> 1) If a ritual is resisted, does this mean that every roll in the extended action gets the penalty, or the ritual is rolled as normal, and when it succeeds, there is a new roll that is resisted?<br /> <br /> 2) Same question for rituals that are contested.<br /> <br /> 3) If the target number of successes is met, but the ritualist still has rolls remaining, can they keep rolling to increase the ritual's potency, or does the ritual take effect immediately?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T04:48:25-07:00","id":1384391,"title":"","content":"1. Yes, the penalty is applicable to every roll made for the casting. Ritual dice pool + positive situational modifiers - target\u2019s relevant Resistance rating and other negative situational modifiers <br /> <br /> 2. Rituals aren\u2019t typically contested in a Ritual dice pool vs target\u2019s Resistance + Power Stat format. If the ritual has additional obstacles to be overcome, it will say so.<br /> <br /> 3. That\u2019s up to the storyteller. Personally I say the ritual takes effect at that time, unless they specified holding it for predeclared circumstances but it holds whatever potency was set on the activation turn, I don\u2019t usually allow rolling to continue jacking up the damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T06:46:55-07:00","id":1384404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1384343#post1384343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. Can someone please help me understand how blood sorcery works in VtR 2e? There are a couple of things I don't get.<br /> <br /> 1) If a ritual is resisted, does this mean that every roll in the extended action gets the penalty, or the ritual is rolled as normal, and when it succeeds, there is a new roll that is resisted?<br /> <br /> 2) Same question for rituals that are contested.<br /> <br /> 3) If the target number of successes is met, but the ritualist still has rolls remaining, can they keep rolling to increase the ritual's potency, or does the ritual take effect immediately?</div> </div> </div> </div>The blood sorcery supplement adress the third question, but i can t remember how","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T07:55:19-07:00","id":1384410,"title":"","content":"If we still use the Titles the Circle of the Crone is listed as having in the First edition<br /> <br /> Maiden Scarlet woman Mother Crone<br /> <br /> Fool, Trickster, Hero, Father, Hermit<br /> <br /> Would creating a Revenant by accident be considered an act that gains you the Father or Mother Titles? <br /> <br /> Or think based on the lack of nurturing on the &quot;Sires&quot; Part its seen as a technicality?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T09:07:35-07:00","id":1384424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1384343#post1384343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. Can someone please help me understand how blood sorcery works in VtR 2e? There are a couple of things I don't get.<br /> <br /> 1) If a ritual is resisted, does this mean that every roll in the extended action gets the penalty, or the ritual is rolled as normal, and when it succeeds, there is a new roll that is resisted?<br /> <br /> 2) Same question for rituals that are contested.<br /> <br /> 3) If the target number of successes is met, but the ritualist still has rolls remaining, can they keep rolling to increase the ritual's potency, or does the ritual take effect immediately?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The common interpretation of #3 has been that you must stop when you succeed. I could swear a dev has confirmed this at one point, but I can't find it right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T10:05:28-07:00","id":1384435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1384410#post1384410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would creating a Revenant by accident be considered an act that gains you the Father or Mother Titles?<br /> <br /> Or think based on the lack of nurturing on the &quot;Sires&quot; Part its seen as a technicality?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it depends what you do afterward. Do you take in and teach your new childe, or do you abandon them and cover up the problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T10:19:12-07:00","id":1384438,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies guys!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1384391#post1384391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. Rituals aren\u2019t typically contested in a Ritual dice pool vs target\u2019s Resistance + Power Stat format. If the ritual has additional obstacles to be overcome, it will say so.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some rituals specifically say &quot;Contested by Attribute + Blood Potency&quot;, but i can't find any further explanation on how this works.<br /> For instance &quot;Pangs of Proserpina&quot; says &quot;contested by Composure + Blood Potency&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T10:39:56-07:00","id":1384441,"title":"","content":"Prince of the Night: I suppose it depends on whether or not creating a revenant is viewed as similar to creating a ghoul or another kindred.<br /> <br /> Emerus: Then they would cast the ritual and if successful, the target has to equal or beat the activation roll results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-28-2020, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T21:20:47-07:00","id":1384565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1384343#post1384343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. Can someone please help me understand how blood sorcery works in VtR 2e? There are a couple of things I don't get.<br /> <br /> 1) If a ritual is resisted, does this mean that every roll in the extended action gets the penalty, or the ritual is rolled as normal, and when it succeeds, there is a new roll that is resisted?<br /> <br /> 2) Same question for rituals that are contested.<br /> <br /> 3) If the target number of successes is met, but the ritualist still has rolls remaining, can they keep rolling to increase the ritual's potency, or does the ritual take effect immediately?</div> </div> </div> </div>For number 3 based on the supplements<br /> <br /> Blasphemy &amp; Sacraments <br /> <br /> Once you hit your target successes and if it's a learned ritual (not improvised) you may add any extra successes to up a factor.<br /> <br /> In the new supplement Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation updated for 2nd edition it is now a single roll similar to Mage.<br /> <br /> I am going from memory so feel free to correct me if I have this is error.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:14:53-07:00","id":1384721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1384343#post1384343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. Can someone please help me understand how blood sorcery works in VtR 2e? There are a couple of things I don't get.<br /> <br /> 1) If a ritual is resisted, does this mean that every roll in the extended action gets the penalty, or the ritual is rolled as normal, and when it succeeds, there is a new roll that is resisted?<br /> <br /> 2) Same question for rituals that are contested.<br /> <br /> 3) If the target number of successes is met, but the ritualist still has rolls remaining, can they keep rolling to increase the ritual's potency, or does the ritual take effect immediately?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) As others have said, the penalty is taken on each roll casting the ritual.<br /> <br /> 2) This is the tricky one, and there really isn't a firm answer. You can <i>kind </i>of extrapolate from <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>, where contested rituals specify that the resistance roll happens under particular circumstances:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shed the Virulent Bowels, p. 185</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once the ritual is cast, the Acolyte may trigger it at any time in the course of the next lunar month. If the victim fails to contest the ritual<br /> at that time, his gullet splits wide, and his bowels eject from his body.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Curse of Aphrodite\u2019s Favor, p. 185</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The victim receives a contested roll against the Acolyte\u2019s final activation roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marian Apparition, p. 194</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred characters contest the caster\u2019s roll with Humanity. If they achieve fewer successes, add the caster\u2019s Theban Sorcery dots to their Humanity for the purpose of determining what constitutes detachment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, the spells in the core don't have these specific notes, so it can be hard to tell when and how to contest them. You could have it just be a one-roll pass or fail thing, but that makes sorcery a lot weaker. Or you could have the defender need to achieve the caster's successes on a single role, but that basically means it's impossible to defend against unless you have an enormous pool. I <i>think </i>the closest thing to RAI would be to have the victim contest the roll each turn, and try to achieve the ritual's successes before the caster, but that's a lot of dice rolling.<br /> <br /> My inclination has been to house rule it when this has come up: Unless a spell outlines how you contest it, make it resisted. Most powers (in general) that call for a specific number of successes are resisted, and there's not all that much of a rhyme or reason for which rituals are contested and which are resisted anyway.<br /> <br /> 3) &quot;If the target number of successes is met, the ritual\u2019s effect immediately takes place.&quot; VTR2E p. 151. But remember that excess successes add to Potency, and an exceptional success adds your Discipline dots to Potency, if applicable. If you're using <b>Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies</b>, it works differently, but I don't recall off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Edit: I dug through <b>Sacraments and Blasphemies</b> and found this: &quot;As rituals are always Extended in action, the casting is Contested each turn.&quot; So, yes, that's a 1e supplement, but it's also what was used to convert the rituals in the core. I'd probably still say make them resisted, but some spells are quite powerful, so contested rolls can even the playing field a bit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 04-29-2020, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:18:03-07:00","id":1384723,"title":"","content":"I believe if a ritual doesn't say otherwise it works like any extended, contested roll; both roll every time and whomever gets to the target successes first wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T03:06:59-07:00","id":1385566,"title":"","content":"In Spilled Blood the part for the Brood explains how casting Triadic Manifestations is an extended action that takes at least 15-30 minutes. Most Manifestations only seem to last an hour, some only for a scene. How can the Brood possibly know 15-30 minutes in advance that they need to prepare a Manifestation that only lasts for one scene? Is there something about the duration of Manifestations i'm missing? Can the effects of a Manifestation be held once cast to be triggered when needed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T08:01:30-07:00","id":1385604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1385566#post1385566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Spilled Blood the part for the Brood explains how casting Triadic Manifestations is an extended action that takes at least 15-30 minutes. Most Manifestations only seem to last an hour, some only for a scene. How can the Brood possibly know 15-30 minutes in advance that they need to prepare a Manifestation that only lasts for one scene? Is there something about the duration of Manifestations i'm missing? Can the effects of a Manifestation be held once cast to be triggered when needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that the writers have consistently underestimated the time it takes to perform blood sorcery in second edition, but this is by far the most egregious example of that. Even rituals with night-long durations are rarely used because most players tend to react to situations as they arise rather than acting proactively, and time constraints are one of the most common tools for a GM to put some pressure on their players.<br /> With the exception of Mantle of Amorous Fire, my character almost exclusively uses homebrewed five dot Cr\u00faac rituals (and rarely at that) because they are events unto themselves rather than preparations for future events. I generally either don't know whether any of my known rituals will be helpful or not for something I know is going to happen, or I couldn't have known I needed a ritual I'm already in the scene wherein it's useful.<br /> <br /> A scene is estimated in the books to be around one hour, though technically it could be anything from a few seconds to a whole night (or longer if the vampire resists daysleep). In practice, a scene is often over by the time you would've finished a ritual. The best way to handle scene long effects would be to have the ritual take place between scenes and have the effect be active the next scene, as long as there's not an overly long gap between the ritual and the coming scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T10:47:44-07:00","id":1385621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1385566#post1385566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Spilled Blood the part for the Brood explains how casting Triadic Manifestations is an extended action that takes at least 15-30 minutes. Most Manifestations only seem to last an hour, some only for a scene. How can the Brood possibly know 15-30 minutes in advance that they need to prepare a Manifestation that only lasts for one scene? Is there something about the duration of Manifestations i'm missing? Can the effects of a Manifestation be held once cast to be triggered when needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, a lot of aspects of the Brood don't really work mechanically. (Willpower being another one.) In my experience, you just have to house-rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T10:55:47-07:00","id":1385623,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think Blood Sorcery in general (including Belial's Brood's Triadic Manifestations) can easily be fixed by lowering the duration of sorcery rolls from 30/15/5 minutes per roll to 10/5/1 <i>turns</i> per roll.<br /> <br /> So one roll takes 10 turns (30 seconds) by default, can can be lowered to 5 turns (15 seconds) with an exceptional success or by casting a ritual below your level, or to 1 turn (3 seconds) when both of those factors apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T18:29:08-07:00","id":1386581,"title":"","content":"how to reconcile Belials Brood As a covenant with the Theban sorcery ritual &quot;Pledge to the Worthless one&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T13:03:36-07:00","id":1392649,"title":"","content":"Are the 1ed Covenant and Clan books still valid in 2ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T13:24:22-07:00","id":1392656,"title":"","content":"Not if you're using the default descriptions, mechanics, and background history of 2nd edition. You are free to mix and match but the powers and merits in 1st ed. materials were either made default (Carthian 9 again merits) or aren't relevant because of other mechanical changes. For example Invictus oaths in 1st edition were relatively difficult to activate, but due to mechanics changes in 2nd edition they're cheap, easy, available to non Invictus, and relatively uninspiring by comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T15:36:32-07:00","id":1392686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1392649#post1392649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the 1ed Covenant and Clan books still valid in 2ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Flavor-wise, though, a lot of the descriptions from the 1e books are still valid in 2e. The only thing to watch out for is that some 1e materials portray the Covenants as global monolithic conspiracies, which was a relic of Masquerade and was abandoned somewhere in the middle of the 1e line. So ignore anything that implies that specifically.<br /> <br /> (Alternately, if you do want the global monolithic conspiracies, check out the section of Danse Macabre on implementing that. Requiem is a toolbox more than a single pre-built world so you can change most aspects of it without breaking anything fundamental!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T07:36:05-07:00","id":1393422,"title":"","content":"How do I travel loong distances with Psychic projection<br /> <br /> did the authors just forget to put in a dice roll difficulty to hop across the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T09:09:14-07:00","id":1393450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1393422#post1393422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I travel loong distances with Psychic projection<br /> <br /> did the authors just forget to put in a dice roll difficulty to hop across the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Twilight Projection? They didn't forget because you can't. Just use the modified Speed if distance is an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T17:27:57-07:00","id":1393554,"title":"","content":"Vampires can't consume food still, correct? What about adding blood to coffee? If they can add blood to coffee, what is the blood to vitae conversion?<br /> <br /> My gut (lol) says vampires can't eat food and that drinks with blood would be liquid that needs to be violently expelled later, with the blood working like a blood bag mechanically. I just can't find any such ruling in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T01:00:37-07:00","id":1393589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1393554#post1393554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can't consume food still, correct? What about adding blood to coffee? If they can add blood to coffee, what is the blood to vitae conversion?<br /> <br /> My gut (lol) says vampires can't eat food and that drinks with blood would be liquid that needs to be violently expelled later, with the blood working like a blood bag mechanically. I just can't find any such ruling in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>See pag 90, blush of life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T03:51:23-07:00","id":1395987,"title":"","content":"The new Belial's Brood cannot Embrace childer and create ghouls. But can Claimed's feeding to death result in creating a revenant? And can they adopt ghoul created by common Kindred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T04:39:03-07:00","id":1395991,"title":"","content":"I don't know about revenants, but they can't adopt ghouls because that's not a thing. They can feed a ghoul if that's what you're asking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T09:40:58-07:00","id":1396035,"title":"","content":"I'd leave that in the realm of ST fiat. <br /> Re: ghouls, once created, the only thing a ghoul requires from a kindred is at least one vitae a month. There's no more willpower expenditure after initial creation. So it's up to the ST as to whether or not vitae from a Belial's Brood member is sufficient to maintain a ghoul. Personally I would say no, since the intention of the restriction is obvious that Belial's Brood is not meant to expand their ranks by natural (to kindred) means.<br /> <br /> Re: Revenant creation. I'd allow the possibility that they create revenants but such offspring don't get the usual benefits they normally enjoy in terms of locating their sire. Nor would it be something they could consciously arrange so they can effortlessly chain embrace their Humanity away by uplifting a horde of revenants they created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T09:45:41-07:00","id":1396036,"title":"","content":"Tessie, I mean feeding ghoul to form a full blood ties, becoming the new regnant and renewing the ghoul state. If it can be done then in case of the ghoul duying will that ghoul rise as revenant? It seems more probable then rising of feeding victim for in this case Blood Potency is rolled instead of Humanity+2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T07:37:57-07:00","id":1396165,"title":"","content":"Defense is calculated as (lowest of Dex or Wits) and Athletics. Does Defense suffer from the untrained penalty then? So that a Wits 3, Dex 2, Athletics 0 person would have defense 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T07:52:18-07:00","id":1396169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1396165#post1396165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defense is calculated as (lowest of Dex or Wits) and Athletics. Does Defense suffer from the untrained penalty then? So that a Wits 3, Dex 2, Athletics 0 person would have defense 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because it's not a Skill roll (or indeed rolled at all).<br /> <br /> (Dodge likewise doesn't have untrained penalties because it's just a roll of twice your Defense.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T08:03:37-07:00","id":1396173,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T04:13:55-07:00","id":1399557,"title":"","content":"Curious? Ideas how a child aged vampire Would go about playing and such to preserve their sense of normalacy?<br /> <br /> Kinda hard to have many playmates wwhen tour nocturnal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T11:08:20-07:00","id":1399625,"title":"","content":"They wouldn\u2019t develop a sense of normalcy with humans. They would need to quickly develop unparalleled skill at manipulation and deception or they\u2019ll end up meeting Final Death. And even that may not be enough. Anne Rice addressed the topic of child vampires and why their survivability depends on the sufferance of \u201cadult\u201d vampires and it\u2019s just as applicable in the Requiem setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T18:03:00-07:00","id":1399958,"title":"","content":"Meant a sense of normalcy with themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T06:15:55-07:00","id":1400297,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain to me how Coda Against Sorcery exactly works ( found on page 180 of Secrets of the Covenants)?<br /> <br /> It says the Merit can apply to non-Kindred magic, but what about Kindred magic that isn't sorcery? Can I use Coda Against Sorcery to shield myself against Disciplines like Dominate, Auspex, or Nightmare?<br /> <br /> Is Coda Against Sorcery tied to a specific domain or tied to a specific character? Do the &quot;rules of engagement&quot; count for my entire domain or just for me personally?<br /> <br /> Does the penalty provided by Coda Against Sorcery also apply to myself? For example, if use Coda Against Sorcery to prohibit Dominate usage, does that mean I myself then also gain a penalty on Dominate rolls equal to my dots in Coda Against Sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T08:15:44-07:00","id":1400316,"title":"","content":"It is supposed to work against a designated sorcery type or sorcerous ritual. Disciplines are not officially a type of sorcery, so no it wouldn't work as they are expressly distinct from a sorcery in terms of mechanics and resistance. However, if I am ST, I would entertain the suggestion that it could work against very specific applications of Animalism, Obfuscate, Dominate and Auspex. (The onus is on the player to make a logical argument to that effect outlining how said discipline rank use constitutes a sorcerous ritual.) And yes, I would say it levies the same penalty on you if you attempted to use said sorcery. You don't get to &quot;disbelieve&quot; &quot;renounce&quot; or &quot;reject&quot; magic use, get benefits from rejecting it, then turn around and use it without penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T08:47:48-07:00","id":1400322,"title":"","content":"That's a fair way of ruling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T13:38:44-07:00","id":1400385,"title":"","content":"Oh hows a vampire Justify taking Striking Looks Merit? Since they cant lose weight or such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-01T13:44:41-07:00","id":1400387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=