s supposed to be used about and can do with non-thralls: convince the target to do something they otherwise wouldn't do, within reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T18:18:03-07:00","id":1403603,"title":"","content":"But one successful roll will it Convince someone to be grateful for his position in life<br /> <br /> Make him feel valued.<br /> <br /> If I roll a successful social maneuvering &quot;Do not oppose me or seek to harm me&quot;&quot; Is that Ever, next night next week, as I Think eventualy it might come frayed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T03:29:02-07:00","id":1403636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1403603#post1403603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But one successful roll will it Convince someone to be grateful for his position in life<br /> <br /> Make him feel valued.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what the system is for, really, but you could easily modify it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I roll a successful social maneuvering &quot;Do not oppose me or seek to harm me&quot;&quot; Is that Ever, next night next week, as I Think eventualy it might come frayed... </div> </div> </div>Again, not really what the system is for. Social manoeuvering is about getting someone to do a favour for you. Most favours aren't for life. It's generally just a single, well defined thing. Just use some common sense if it comes up in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T05:11:45-07:00","id":1403647,"title":"","content":"On it's face those are all completely unrealistic requests using the Social Maneuvering rules. It doesn't matter what your impression level is. <br /> Why should anyone be eternally grateful for being a slave? Why would they not oppose an abusive slave master at a given opportunity?<br /> And even if the ST allowed such vague commands poorly masked as requests to stand due to specific circumstances, (because let's get real, the one making the demand is offering absolutely nothing in return) they don't last indefinitely. Whenever the specific influence that allowed such commands to take hold fades, that's when it ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T06:13:42-07:00","id":1403650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1403647#post1403647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On it's face those are all completely unrealistic requests using the Social Maneuvering rules. It doesn't matter what your impression level is. <br /> Why should anyone be eternally grateful for being a slave? Why would they not oppose an abusive slave master at a given opportunity?<br /> And even if the ST allowed such vague commands poorly masked as requests to stand due to specific circumstances, (because let's get real, the one making the demand is offering absolutely nothing in return) they don't last indefinitely. Whenever the specific influence that allowed such commands to take hold fades, that's when it ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are still talking about vinculum thralls, remember that they are forced to love the regnant.<br /> We see numerous examples in which someome abuse his loving companion, we call it toxic relationships, and it is much harder than most people think to oppose to this kind of non magic manipulation, so a magic imposed love should be even worse.<br /> <br /> BUT<br /> <br /> Let s remember that a social maneuvering require successful contested rolls, that are subjected to bonuses and maluses relevant to the used approach","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T13:12:37-07:00","id":1406320,"title":"","content":"What would a good relationship between the Lancea Et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone look like? I have trouble seeing what it could like, even more than that of one between the Invictus and Carthian Movement. Oh, and to be clear, I've had games where the Sancrified and Circle co-exist, but it's always been begrudging to covert undoing beneath amiable facades","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T14:13:17-07:00","id":1406328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1406320#post1406320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a good relationship between the Lancea Et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone look like? I have trouble seeing what it could like, even more than that of one between the Invictus and Carthian Movement. Oh, and to be clear, I've had games where the Sancrified and Circle co-exist, but it's always been begrudging to covert undoing beneath amiable facades</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it all depends on how competitive the two groups are or not about getting converts x doing some sort of esoteric/moral duty tied on their beliefs, actually.<br /> Not every religious leader has to be a televangelist/missionary/crusader type. Mormons, amish, some buddhist sects and jews tend to be more on the &quot;just leave us alone doing our own thing&quot; camp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-04-2020, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T16:46:55-07:00","id":1406351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1406328#post1406328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it all depends on how competitive the two groups are or not about getting converts x doing some sort of esoteric/moral duty tied on their beliefs, actually.<br /> Not every religious leader has to be a televangelist/missionary/crusader type. Mormons, amish, some buddhist sects and jews tend to be more on the &amp;quot;just leave us alone doing our own thing&amp;quot; camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be more specific, how would a good relationship between the 2 look? It seems like even the carthians and Invictus can have one (through Invictus willing to make concessions and carthians willing to help maintain peace with what laws are already there). I just really have trouble seeing one with the Circle and Sanctified<br /> <br /> Sorry i wasnt more specific earlier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T21:32:05-07:00","id":1406379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1406351#post1406351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be more specific, how would a good relationship between the 2 look? It seems like even the carthians and Invictus can have one (through Invictus willing to make concessions and carthians willing to help maintain peace with what laws are already there). I just really have trouble seeing one with the Circle and Sanctified<br /> <br /> Sorry i wasnt more specific earlier</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Never really explored hard the idea, but tolerance and.... a spiritual cold war of sorts, i think.<br /> <br /> Debates, discussions, as long as there's communication, each may learn more from the other, see conundrums, strengths, weaknesses, maybe find fracture points that lead into proving the other's belief wrong, a back &amp; forth between to groups trying to reveal a great truth, though they might be both blinding each other to what it actuallly is.<br /> <br /> A climate of tolerance and even sort of camaradie that obfuscates the reality of a deep-seated philosophical dispute over views of what the world is about and what kind of role is expected or not of the kindred in its undying hidden predatory existence, among other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-05-2020, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T08:04:10-07:00","id":1406442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1406320#post1406320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a good relationship between the Lancea Et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone look like? I have trouble seeing what it could like, even more than that of one between the Invictus and Carthian Movement. Oh, and to be clear, I've had games where the Sancrified and Circle co-exist, but it's always been begrudging to covert undoing beneath amiable facades</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps a relationship based on cordial debate and discussion of spiritual matters and their own experiences therein, and comparing the relative merits and evidences represented by their differing forms of magic.<br /> <br /> I presume that Kindred communities are small enough that the kind of relationship you're talking about is more on the level of individuals than organisations, in which I might expect it to be similar to the kind of friendship that a minister and an iman might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T12:38:06-07:00","id":1406490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1406442#post1406442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps a relationship based on cordial debate and discussion of spiritual matters and their own experiences therein, and comparing the relative merits and evidences represented by their differing forms of magic.<br /> <br /> I presume that Kindred communities are small enough that the kind of relationship you're talking about is more on the level of individuals than organisations, in which I might expect it to be similar to the kind of friendship that a minister and an iman might have.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quite true. Something to take in consideration is that the kindred population in most domains will not be a countless multitude - between a dozen to maybe the low hundreds (case of the Rio de Janeiro chronicle i last played) in certain metropolises - so kind of small when one thinks of cities as a whole <b>and </b>the membership of religious covenants an even smaller fraction of this total.<br /> <br /> So the whole following of the Church of Longinus or the Acolytes in any one city will generally be something that would fit in a single temple.<br /> He, a single high school classroom might have room to spare, depending on the domain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-05-2020, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T03:01:13-07:00","id":1406606,"title":"","content":"Not sure in which thread it would be better to post this...<br /> In dark eras 2 there is a Mage spell (fate 4, mind 1, + optional death 4) that allows a changeling to learn Goblin contract from the target creature as if it was a hobgoblin.<br /> Assuming that Strix are possible targets, i m wondering if there is a way to create a similar effect with a Cruac ritual.<br /> What themes should it use if possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T16:13:31-07:00","id":1407809,"title":"","content":"Is vampiric healing via vitae reflexive or is it an instant action? I'm having trouble finding anything in the books there. I understand it is limited by your ability to spend vitae. I guess the question is if it's an action type at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T16:24:33-07:00","id":1407810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1407809#post1407809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is vampiric healing via vitae reflexive or is it an instant action? I'm having trouble finding anything in the books there. I understand it is limited by your ability to spend vitae. I guess the question is if it's an action type at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the section on torpor: &quot;At the end of a vampire's turn, after any <u>reflexive healing</u>, if her last (rightmost) Health box is filled with lethal damage, she falls to torpor.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-13T04:56:30-07:00","id":1407894,"title":"","content":"Reflexive. Page 91 describes it as working within seconds, page 105 describes it as reflexive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T17:28:57-07:00","id":1411446,"title":"","content":"It's something I've been thinking about forever now, do Vampires have a true metaphysical effect on the environment, or is it pseudo-mystical? Like does a nosferatu hanging out in a park make that park creepy and disturbing BECAUSE that nosferatu is simply there, or is because the actions of the nosferatu, thus making it only SEEM like his presence is changing the area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T20:12:50-07:00","id":1411460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1411446#post1411446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something I've been thinking about forever now, do Vampires have a true metaphysical effect on the environment, or is it pseudo-mystical? Like does a nosferatu hanging out in a park make that park creepy and disturbing BECAUSE that nosferatu is simply there, or is because the actions of the nosferatu, thus making it only SEEM like his presence is changing the area?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. In a crossover game with Werewolf or Mage, this would likely be an explicit matter of Resonance, but in Vampire on its own, this is mostly the source of the bonuses the Feeding Grounds Merit provides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T04:29:38-07:00","id":1411628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1411446#post1411446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something I've been thinking about forever now, do Vampires have a true metaphysical effect on the environment, or is it pseudo-mystical? Like does a nosferatu hanging out in a park make that park creepy and disturbing BECAUSE that nosferatu is simply there, or is because the actions of the nosferatu, thus making it only SEEM like his presence is changing the area?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I play with &quot;Cacophony&quot; for Vampires the effect does not appear mystical but for mages / werewolfes the presence of a vampire especially if it\u00b4s brutal in hunting and it\u00b4s machinations will attract maybe spirits of violence, fear etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T06:58:20-07:00","id":1411634,"title":"","content":"What changes or breaks if the Fog of Eternity and its strangely vivid dreams touched upon an individual kindred's Oneiros?<br /> <br /> (A little something that nagged me from last time i read Mythologies. Yeah, i know it's essentially a 1e thing, but humor my anachronism....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T09:25:54-07:00","id":1411647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1411634#post1411634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What changes or breaks if the Fog of Eternity and its strangely vivid dreams touched upon an individual kindred's Oneiros?</div> </div> </div> </div>The assumption that nonhuman supernatural beings don't have an Oneiros, mainly. What were you expecting to have a problem with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T10:41:48-07:00","id":1411653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1411647#post1411647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The assumption that nonhuman supernatural beings don't have an Oneiros, mainly. What were you expecting to have a problem with?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More precisely, i guess my doubt might be &quot;how could vampires as a whole having a footing, even if unreliable and mostly unknowing, on the Astral Realms, particularly the Oneiros - maybe even interactions with something like goetic demons - affect either individuals or their society?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-03-2020, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T10:55:07-07:00","id":1411654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1411647#post1411647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The assumption that nonhuman supernatural beings don't have an Oneiros, mainly. What were you expecting to have a problem with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily the default assumption depending on which dev you ask and when you asked them.<br /> If we go by RAW, then vampires should have Oneiroi (because they're described as having souls according to Nameless &amp; Accursed) but they don't link up further to the Temenos that is exclusively the domain of mortals, mages and Beasts (from BtP, not the gestalt of a vampire's dark urges).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:27:25-07:00","id":1411668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1411654#post1411654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily the default assumption depending on which dev you ask and when you asked them.<br /> If we go by RAW, then vampires should have Oneiroi (because they're described as having souls according to Nameless &amp; Accursed) but they don't link up further to the Temenos that is exclusively the domain of mortals, mages and Beasts (from BtP, not the gestalt of a vampire's dark urges).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another question - is there any sort of connection/relation between the Beasts of BtP, the elusive other shaped inside every vampire and the changeling seeming of the same name? If so, which ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T12:37:45-07:00","id":1411677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1411668#post1411668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question - is there any sort of connection/relation between the Beasts of BtP, the elusive other shaped inside every vampire and the changeling seeming of the same name? If so, which ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from an identification with the wilderness, instinct, inhumanity, and the supernatural, it's just a shared evocative name. The Begotten are great Beasts built on pain and hunger and fear and revelation brought forth from the psychic landscape beyond human culture, whereas the Savage seeming of the Lost had their human minds taken from them while they were made to live as Beasts and developed an affinity for fae magics that let them come and go as they please.<br /> <br /> There's some conceptual alignment there with the Beast in Kindred thought, concerned as vampires are with self-control and humanity, but otherwise it's no more connected than 1e Geist and Promethean both having things called the Silent and the Wretched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T21:17:49-07:00","id":1412386,"title":"","content":"While in torpor could a vampire still convert blood to vitae, as long as it obeys the vampire's feeding restriction of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T23:11:01-07:00","id":1412396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412386#post1412386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While in torpor could a vampire still convert blood to vitae, as long as it obeys the vampire's feeding restriction of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think yes theoretically, but maybe his throat muscles are paralyzed, so it woul probably need a feeding tube","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T23:20:28-07:00","id":1412397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412396#post1412396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think yes theoretically, but maybe his throat muscles are paralyzed, so it woul probably need a feeding tube</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's a fair interpretation and honestly as this is basically for an ordo project a feeding tube is even thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T03:55:07-07:00","id":1412407,"title":"","content":"Core book says that partial cover from sunlight consider blood potency damage one step lower.<br /> Does this mean that a bp 1 vampire are considered bp 0 (no damage) if partially covered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T05:16:29-07:00","id":1412414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412386#post1412386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While in torpor could a vampire still convert blood to vitae, as long as it obeys the vampire's feeding restriction of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory deserves even the skin is able to absorb vitae. I don't thinknit's an hard rule but I recall it was written somewhere. I could be wrong though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T06:12:05-07:00","id":1412422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412397#post1412397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, that's a fair interpretation and honestly as this is basically for an ordo project a feeding tube is even thematic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Incidentally, i have done a setup somewhat like this in one of my games with an &quot;independent&quot; ghoul family feeding &amp; &quot;milking&quot; one or more (collected) kindred donors through decades or centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T13:20:15-07:00","id":1412468,"title":"","content":"Hey Vampire the Requiem peeps<br /> <br /> I would like to confirm what I think I understand about powers and feels...<br /> <br /> For example, I think i understand that if a vampire and a mage were in a crowded room, if the vampire uses a power the mage would feel the power. Not who, what or where but something.<br /> <br /> If the mage had passive? / active ? mage sight, was looking near the vampire and he used a power that falls into purview then he would see something.<br /> <br /> My final point is if obfuscte was used that it would not trigger a sense unless a specific arcana was fo used like mind vs obfuscate or an unveiling spell<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback<br /> <br /> (Also posting on Discord/Forum)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T13:30:05-07:00","id":1412470,"title":"","content":"These are all Mage questions much more than Vampire questions, but anyway:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412468#post1412468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Vampire the Requiem peeps<br /> <br /> I would like to confirm what I think I understand about powers and feels...<br /> <br /> For example, I think i understand that if a vampire and a mage were in a crowded room, if the vampire uses a power the mage would feel the power. Not who, what or where but something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how Passive Mage Sight works, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412468#post1412468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the mage had passive? / active ? mage sight, was looking near the vampire and he used a power that falls into purview then he would see something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how Active Mage Sight works, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412468#post1412468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My final point is if obfuscte was used that it would not trigger a sense unless a specific arcana was fo used like mind vs obfuscate or an unveiling spell<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback<br /> <br /> (Also posting on Discord/Forum)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T14:09:08-07:00","id":1412477,"title":"","content":"1. Assuming Obfuscate or some other power that works to conceal power usage is not also active, yes a mage would sense a supernatural power was used but no other specifics - being only slightly more useful than Detect Traps in D&amp;D 5e.<br /> <br /> 2. Again, assuming some other protective or illusionary power is not at work, active Mage Sight reveals whatever relevant detection it provides if he looks in the direction of the vampire using the relevant powers.<br /> <br /> 3. If Obfuscate or other power is at work, I would not allow a passive detection to provoke a Clash of Wills but I would allow an active detection attempt to do so. I have played with STs who do coin flip or percentage roll to see if a Mage passively senses &quot;something&quot; is at work but penalizes the attempt to identify anything else. Kind of like running a metal detector and having it go off briefly but when you backtrack you don't get anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T14:12:46-07:00","id":1412478,"title":"","content":"Great thank you, the Vampires are the players and the Mages are the NPCs. I waffled over posting to Vampire of Mage but wanted it very specifically from the vampires view.<br /> <br /> Great answers thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T22:05:34-07:00","id":1412542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412478#post1412478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great thank you, the Vampires are the players and the Mages are the NPCs. I waffled over posting to Vampire of Mage but wanted it very specifically from the vampires view.<br /> <br /> Great answers thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pag 25 of signs of sorcery clarify a lot mage sight.<br /> It can detect discipline usage qnd pinpoint the exact location if obfuscate is not in use","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T22:37:29-07:00","id":1412543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412542#post1412542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pag 25 of signs of sorcery clarify a lot mage sight.<br /> It can detect discipline usage qnd pinpoint the exact location if obfuscate is not in use</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice I will delve into SoS","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-09T07:12:01-07:00","id":1412716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1412407#post1412407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Core book says that partial cover from sunlight consider blood potency damage one step lower.<br /> Does this mean that a bp 1 vampire are considered bp 0 (no damage) if partially covered?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Been a couple days, so I think I can answer this: yes. A BP1 vampire wearing, for example, a burqa or niqab would not take any damage so long as they're almost completely covered. Note the book says &quot;If she only exposes her eyes ... consider her Blood Potency one step lower,&quot; so stuff like an umbrella or even normal heavy clothing and a hat probably wouldn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T14:02:31-07:00","id":1415595,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it's already been asked but...<br /> <br /> What are the Lost Clans ? or which are, I guess ?<br /> <br /> I know from A Thousand Years of Nights that the Julii and Akhud are still there, probably both numerous enough to be considered a small Clan, but an effective one, even if both have reasons to not reveal it (The Strix and the VII link, if I understood the references about the Akhud's past). The Pijavica are truly lost, with only one Elder who can't really create durable neonates. <br /> <br /> But are they really so few that no one notices anything ? I mean, I guess that if all the Bloodlines from 1ed are a thing it's easy for them to hide, but in 2nd they seem far less numerous (which i kind of dig, by the way!)<br /> <br /> Are there other Clans in the modern nights that I don't know off ? ANd what are their goals ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T14:12:28-07:00","id":1415598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1415595#post1415595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it's already been asked but...<br /> <br /> What are the Lost Clans ? or which are, I guess ?<br /> <br /> I know from A Thousand Years of Nights that the Julii and Akhud are still there, probably both numerous enough to be considered a small Clan, but an effective one, even if both have reasons to not reveal it (The Strix and the VII link, if I understood the references about the Akhud's past). The Pijavica are truly lost, with only one Elder who can't really create durable neonates.<br /> <br /> But are they really so few that no one notices anything ? I mean, I guess that if all the Bloodlines from 1ed are a thing it's easy for them to hide, but in 2nd they seem far less numerous (which i kind of dig, by the way!)<br /> <br /> Are there other Clans in the modern nights that I don't know off ? ANd what are their goals ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Spilled Blood has the Bekaak and the Nhang and Amari as well as hints of others. Second edition didn't really eliminate the first edition bloodlines but give you different rules for making them (as well as, for the most part, no interest in retreading them mechanically).<br /> <br /> You can create your own lost clans if you want, it seems basically encouraged by the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T16:06:36-07:00","id":1415618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1415595#post1415595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it's already been asked but...<br /> <br /> What are the Lost Clans ? or which are, I guess ?<br /> <br /> I know from A Thousand Years of Nights that the Julii and Akhud are still there, probably both numerous enough to be considered a small Clan, but an effective one, even if both have reasons to not reveal it (The Strix and the VII link, if I understood the references about the Akhud's past). The Pijavica are truly lost, with only one Elder who can't really create durable neonates.<br /> <br /> But are they really so few that no one notices anything ? I mean, I guess that if all the Bloodlines from 1ed are a thing it's easy for them to hide, but in 2nd they seem far less numerous (which i kind of dig, by the way!)<br /> <br /> Are there other Clans in the modern nights that I don't know off ? And what are their goals ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some groups i remembered on a spur of moment thing:<br /> <br /> - Ordo Dracul has the <i><b>Vedma </b></i>bloodline, that speaks of the Gangrel originating from them instead of the opposite.<br /> - Invictus has the <i><b>Annunaki</b></i>, a Gangrel/Ventrue (?) bloodline of lords of the land that predates the covenant by millenia, <i>making them <b>also </b>possibly older than the clans as we know them</i>.<br /> - Shadows of Mexico cites the <i><b>Xolotl </b></i>that while similar may <b>or not</b> be Nosferatu. Also, the <i><b>Cihuateteo</b></i>, who might be Daeva, Mekhet or something between.<br /> - Night Horrors: Wicked Dead has the <b><i>Formosae </i></b>and also the earlier &quot;<i><b>not </b>a clan, <b>not </b>even <b>kindred</b></i>&quot; first draft version of the Jiang Shi. And a blood-witch version of the <i><b>Cihuateteo</b></i>, too.<br /> - Shadows in the Dark: Mekhet cites in passing how the Norvegi bloodline originally came from a Clan <b><i>Grettir </i></b>in Iceland. It also has a variant form of Mekhet, the atavistic, haunted <b><i>Hollows</i></b>.<br /> - Requiem 2e, coincidentally (?) <b>also </b>cites Iceland as one of the places prone to spawning the clan more popularly known as <i><b>Jiang Shi</b></i>.<br /> - Dark Eras 2 has a new clan called Dukhan, or so i have heard.<br /> <br /> So, there are some indeed, but origins or veracity can be somewhat confusing &amp; dubious at times.<br /> <br /> Part of the matter to remember is - how many of those kindred actually <b>know </b>they are from one clan and not the other?<br /> For the Akhud, <b>not</b> knowing might be unusual, but Julii hiding out through ages, separated by generations and layers of half-truths &amp; secrets from the nemeses have a far from the insignificant chance of being themselves unaware of any origins or identity beside Ventrue (or Gangrel).<br /> Same could apply to any group of undead with discipline sets or dread powers awfully similar to the bag of tricks of one of the &quot;big five&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, what if the Akhud's tale is a lie, there's no demon and they are all the brood of some old, insane and alien ancient hollow Mekhet parasiting the souls of all its descendants through a mix of blood magic &amp; sympathy with something else? Or the Julii some independently spawned brood of what we know as Ventrue, and already existed in other, older, more distant lands without the knowledge of the arrogant roman kindred? History for the undead can be quite the unholy mess.<br /> <br /> Damn, even though presented now as a separate clan, there's a ridiculous degree of mix-up between Jiang Shi and Hollow Mekhet. While 2e gives us a peculiar context in the Triangle (Raleigh-Durham-Chapel Hill) community where the Jiang Shi grew numerous - <i>and in an organized enough manner</i> - to form into the local equivalent of a new clan, it could be that in some other domain in another country they simply join a larger community of local Mekhet as a sort of Hollow Shadow Cult instead.<br /> <br /> There was a time not too long ago the Jiang Shi were portrayed as <i>not even kindred</i> though similar in some ways, only for later on the writers to give us some special circunstances where these rare beings could thrive, to the point of joining and interacting with kindred to such a degree they evolved into a (local) clan, that might in time evolve into a global one. Or crash &amp; burn and be forgotten except for collectors of esoteric trivia of the undead.<br /> <br /> Who's to say the same could not happen - in the past, present or future - to any of the other things in Night Horrors: Wicked Dead or Spilled Blood? Damn, some of the beings in Wicked Dead have had previous iterations in older books if memory tricks me not (<i><b>Cihuateteo </b></i>in Shadows of Mexico &amp; Wicked Dead both, the <b><i>Aswang </i></b>may be found in Wicked Dead, the Antagonists bluebook and somewhere else i forget), so &quot;evolution of monsters&quot; may be played with in a number of forms.<br /> <br /> Things are far from clear cut and there are many ways for a ST to create and fit all kinds of weirdness, secret histories, mystery groups and lost secrets in their chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-04-2021, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T12:42:14-08:00","id":1424070,"title":"","content":"How would Vampires be affected during white nights? Would there be some exposure to the sun? I don't really have a clue how that looks, never experienced white nights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23530,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","user":"Dante[RU]","date":". 11-15-2020, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-15T23:40:27-08:00","id":1424186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1424070#post1424070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would Vampires be affected during white nights? Would there be some exposure to the sun? I don't really have a clue how that looks, never experienced white nights.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_sun#White_nights\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>wiki article should help with you deciding on it yourself for a game. There's a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/30_Days_of_Night\" target=\"_blank\">comic book</a> story - and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/30_Days_of_Night_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">film adaptation</a> - centered in the opposite phenomenon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-16-2020, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-16T00:57:12-08:00","id":1424198,"title":"","content":"There is no hard rule but, in my opinion, night is night and sunlight is sunlight hence you will suffer the normal damages during a white night whatever hour it is. On the contrary you could stay awake and active the whole time a night last. This is compensate by the fact that, such places with so extreme situations, are very sparsely populated and unattractive for kindred.<br /> Non the less there could be some lonely Gangrel/Nosferatu living and terrifying such places <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T16:36:10-08:00","id":1424625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1424070#post1424070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would Vampires be affected during white nights? Would there be some exposure to the sun? I don't really have a clue how that looks, never experienced white nights.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that Kindred wake at sundown, whenever that is, and that direct exposure to sunlight doesn't care if it's twilight or noon.<br /> <br /> Staying indoors, underground, or behind buildings would limit any potential for damage, but the same pressures that are likely to affect vampiric activity cycles in less equatorial climates get turned up several notches in places with white nights.<br /> <br /> High-Humanity Kindred will fare better, but otherwise you're looking at a much more pronounced cloistering of the All Night Society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T11:20:35-08:00","id":1426015,"title":"","content":"hows a member of one of the bloodlines that cant engage in any kind of social interaction with humanity without endangering the masquerade go about feeding?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T12:10:44-08:00","id":1426027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1426015#post1426015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hows a member of one of the bloodlines that cant engage in any kind of social interaction with humanity without endangering the masquerade go about feeding?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate. Other Disciplines. Blood dolls. Have your meals brought to you by ghouls and neonates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T05:18:09-08:00","id":1426119,"title":"","content":"one thing is I See no equilevent under nightmare of Masquerades paralyzing Stare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T09:17:07-08:00","id":1426133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1426119#post1426119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one thing is I See no equilevent under nightmare of Masquerades paralyzing Stare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dread Presence's quick illusions can be weaponized for the hunt. Aside from that, a literal &quot;Dread Gaze&quot; in Requiem could easily be a Nightmare Devotion based on Face of the Beast. A Devotion that simply turns the effect inflicted from Frightened to the Insensate Tilt (honestly, I would allow it to do that even without a Merit or Devotion, but not every ST might agree).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T12:19:08-08:00","id":1426156,"title":"","content":"So, you must have another book if you want to have decent Cruac and Sorcery rites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T12:54:13-08:00","id":1426164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1426156#post1426156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you must have another book if you want to have decent Cruac and Sorcery rites?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or devise your own. If you have access to Mage: the Awakening that might give you a grounding for how to make your own.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, the following 2e books have more Rites:<ul><li><b>Secrets of the Covenants</b></li> <li><b>Thousand Years of Night</b></li> </ul><br /> In the Storyteller's Vault, there are also:<ul><li><b>Rites of Damnation</b>, which translates 1e's system for Mage-like freeform Blood Sorcery to 2e</li> <li><b>Desecrated Rites</b>, which makes the regular casting less static and has some good ideas how to improve Blood Sorcery without making it Bloody Creative Thaumaturgy</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T13:00:24-08:00","id":1426165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1426156#post1426156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you must have another book if you want to have decent Cruac and Sorcery rites?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing you're referring to the Blood Sorcery book? Not exactly. It's a great tool for expanding on blood sorcery, if that's what you're after, but out of the two main problems with blood sorcery in the 2e core book, it only partly alleviates one of them.<br /> Due to word count we didn't get that many examples so there's a distinct lack of variety on various dot levels. In that regard any book that introduces additional rites helps. Secrets of the Covenants is probably the best second edition book for additional rites despite being mainly a fiction book. The Blood Sorcery book does not contain any additional rituals, but it can help by providing a few tools for designing new homebrew rites even if you don't use the expanded blood sorcery system.<br /> The second problem is the time necessary to carry out the rites. Players, like protagonists in most stories, are often reactive to whatever conflicts pop up even if they were the ones who caused the conflicts in the first place. That means by the time they realise they want to use a ritual, it's often too late to begin one due to how long it takes to activate. The only solution to this is house-ruling the time per roll to something a lot more manageable. I'd recommend one roll per minute unless you want to go back to 1e's one roll per turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-25T13:10:19-08:00","id":1426167,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> To any other book that isn't corebook, basically, yes.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar272_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"272\" data-vbnamecard=\"272\">saibot</a> I'll keep everything in mind, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T12:05:12-08:00","id":1427734,"title":"","content":"Does Obfuscate effect spirits (i.e. Uratha pack totems), or is there a caveat for ephemeral beings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25372-ssudd387","name":"Ssudd387","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T01:35:00-08:00","id":1427830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ssudd387</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1427734#post1427734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Obfuscate effect spirits (i.e. Uratha pack totems), or is there a caveat for ephemeral beings?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> None afaik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T03:26:07-08:00","id":1427833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ssudd387</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1427734#post1427734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Obfuscate effect spirits (i.e. Uratha pack totems), or is there a caveat for ephemeral beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no hard rule but I'd say yes. Obfuscate is not invisibility, it affects senses and not only living ones as it works on Vampires with dead brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T04:59:49-08:00","id":1427842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ssudd387</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1427734#post1427734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Obfuscate effect spirits (i.e. Uratha pack totems), or is there a caveat for ephemeral beings?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1427833#post1427833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no hard rule but I'd say yes. Obfuscate is not invisibility, it affects senses and not only living ones as it works on Vampires with dead brain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to mention some of the Hollow-connected devotions in the Mekhet clanbook do seem to imply at least some degree of interface with ephemeral beings, if memory tricks me not - and i admit it might, so i advise a look into the book if you can instead of just taking my word on it, as it may inspire further ideas on exploring the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-09-2020, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T15:57:00-08:00","id":1428812,"title":"","content":"About awakening a vampire from torpor<br /> The book says<br /> &quot;As well, any vampire with two more dots of Blood Potency than she has can feed her a point of Vitae to awaken her &quot;<br /> <br /> Does the phrasing imply that the Blood must be given freely? Or any Blood, despite how It was obtained, would do the trick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T17:06:15-08:00","id":1428816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1428812#post1428812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About awakening a vampire from torpor<br /> The book says<br /> &quot;As well, any vampire with two more dots of Blood Potency than she has can feed her a point of Vitae to awaken her &quot;<br /> <br /> Does the phrasing imply that the Blood must be given freely? Or any Blood, despite how It was obtained, would do the trick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any Vitae would do, but note that Vitae outside of a vampiric body loses its potency quickly and reverts to a wild mix of random blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T07:20:16-08:00","id":1430329,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I've been reading France by Night and L'H\u00e9r\u00e9sie Cathare (supplements in French for V<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />ark Ages 20y Edition) and it got me thinking...<br /> <br /> Do we know which clans were affiliated with the Romans, the Gauls, etc. in Europe ? As far as I can tell, no Clan is supposed to have their origin in Western Europe, save perhaps the Ventrues, who I guess could be the result of Roman Vampires Embracing natives of today's Northern France and thus changing their Blood, if they are indeed scions of the Julii.<br /> <br /> So, in those ancien territories, which clans would have led for centuries, before the coming of Rome and everything after. Or did Vampires never came before Rome in those parts ? It could be quite intruiguing in itself (and to an even larger degree, to the Americas - are the First Nations and Natives Vampires truly Ventrues, Tor\u00e9adors, etc. or is it just an easy way to classify them) ?<br /> <br /> Do we have any knowledge about it ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T09:18:51-08:00","id":1430339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1430329#post1430329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so I've been reading France by Night and L'H\u00e9r\u00e9sie Cathare (supplements in French for V<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />ark Ages 20y Edition) and it got me thinking...<br /> <br /> Do we know which clans were affiliated with the Romans, the Gauls, etc. in Europe ? As far as I can tell, no Clan is supposed to have their origin in Western Europe, save perhaps the Ventrues, who I guess could be the result of Roman Vampires Embracing natives of today's Northern France and thus changing their Blood, if they are indeed scions of the Julii.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing too definite or solid, but the Gangrel seem to have had a presence amidst the many celtic or celtic-influenced people. Nosferatu and Ventrue seem to have had a presence in the greek-speaking world, if one can rely on the myths of the bloodlines in the CoC (or any other covenant book for that matter) as fact, that is.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Requiem for Rome does give a short but punchy distribution of the foreign kindred across the roman world in the clans write-ups that can make a simple basis for historical games mixed fragments from the clanbooks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1430329#post1430329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in those ancien territories, which clans would have led for centuries, before the coming of Rome and everything after. Or did Vampires never came before Rome in those parts ? It could be quite intruiguing in itself (and to an even larger degree, to the Americas - are the First Nations and Natives Vampires truly Ventrues, Tor\u00e9adors, etc. or is it just an easy way to classify them) ?<br /> <br /> Do we have any knowledge about it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>More probably easy ways to classify them. Consider the Norvegi, who are classified as Mekhet even though they semi-openly claim descent from a norse vampire clan called Grettir, the Macellarii, a Ventrue bloodline even though its founder was apparently a Julii, or the Annunaki, who seem be both Gangrel <b>and </b>Ventrue while harkening to a civilization older than the Invictus they currently belong to by <i>millenia</i>.<br /> <br /> All clans historical references are only as reliable as the ST wants them to be, any ancient reference to a clan could actually be a different though similar (and now possibly extinct) one. Or in a contrarian note, any &quot;secret lost clan&quot; like the Akhud or Julii, just some insular group of Mekhet or Ventrue that developed an unique culture and mythology of its own.<br /> <br /> About vampires in the Americas, i really recommend you <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Shadows_of_Mexico\" target=\"_blank\">Shadows of Mexico</a> as a great showcase on the subject of precolumbian vampires and their blending with invading/migrating kindred in the centuries since. An early 1st edition book, but it has aged quite well imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-29-2020, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T10:39:32-08:00","id":1430346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1430339#post1430339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing too definite or solid, but the Gangrel seem to have had a presence amidst the many celtic or celtic-influenced people. Nosferatu and Ventrue seem to have had a presence in the greek-speaking world, if one can rely on the myths of the bloodlines in the CoC (or any other covenant book for that matter) as fact, that is.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Requiem for Rome does give a short but punchy distribution of the foreign kindred across the roman world in the clans write-ups that can make a simple basis for historical games mixed fragments from the clanbooks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> More probably easy ways to classify them. Consider the Norvegi, who are classified as Mekhet even though they semi-openly claim descent from a norse vampire clan called Grettir, the Macellarii, a Ventrue bloodline even though its founder was apparently a Julii, or the Annunaki, who seem be both Gangrel <b>and </b>Ventrue while harkening to a civilization older than the Invictus they currently belong to by <i>millenia</i>.<br /> <br /> All clans historical references are only as reliable as the ST wants them to be, any ancient reference to a clan could actually be a different though similar (and now possibly extinct) one. Or in a contrarian note, any &quot;secret lost clan&quot; like the Akhud or Julii, just some insular group of Mekhet or Ventrue that developed an unique culture and mythology of its own.<br /> <br /> About vampires in the Americas, i really recommend you <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Shadows_of_Mexico\" target=\"_blank\">Shadows of Mexico</a> as a great showcase on the subject of precolumbian vampires and their blending with invading/migrating kindred in the centuries since. An early 1st edition book, but it has aged quite well imho.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I need to get some of those books, but admitedly, reading them in English and not in French (my native language) makes it somewhat harder to understand at times !<br /> <br /> I thin one of Requiem's strength is how nebulous it is concerning the origin(s) of vampires, but it's also somewhat frustrating at times. Hopefully in a few years we'll see creators starting to push for more &quot;ancient&quot; settings in various countries to help cover some of those times (imagine a book about the rise of Dracula and the early days of his Ordo! it'd be crazy cool!). <br /> <br /> I know that the Five Clans led 1ed to be somewhat bloated with Bloodlines so I'm happy that 2nd seems to be avoiding it so far. Still, I wonder if it isn't frustrating for the writers sometimes XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-29T11:41:02-08:00","id":1430353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1430346#post1430346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, I need to get some of those books, but admitedly, reading them in English and not in French (my native language) makes it somewhat harder to understand at times !<br /> <br /> I thin one of Requiem's strength is how nebulous it is concerning the origin(s) of vampires, but it's also somewhat frustrating at times. Hopefully in a few years we'll see creators starting to push for more &quot;ancient&quot; settings in various countries to help cover some of those times (imagine a book about the rise of Dracula and the early days of his Ordo! it'd be crazy cool!).</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact, i do like the nebulousness exactly because it gives a ST immense freedom to reinterpret things in a number of ways or create utterly insane twists and run along with them.<br /> <br /> For example, how would you feel if i said one of the &quot;generic templates&quot; in the Ordo Dracul book hints about it either <i>making a cross through the pole</i> or <i>having witnessed the last glaciation</i>, if not both? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (And yeah, the PCs eventually found out she could transform into mammoth and other megafauna - to be more precise, the endgame partly involved her recovery of the capacity to do so through torpor)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1430346#post1430346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that the Five Clans led 1ed to be somewhat bloated with Bloodlines so I'm happy that 2nd seems to be avoiding it so far. Still, I wonder if it isn't frustrating for the writers sometimes XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters bloodlines are all pretty much optional and about as large or small as one wants them to be, so it doesn't really worry me.<br /> Unless i have some major plot going on for them, there's 50% chance the PC, its sire and 1-5 other kindred are the whole of it.<br /> <br /> For another, i have no problem with getting a bloodline - specially those available to multiple clans, with a origin myth harkening to antiquity, references to stuff that breaks from the normal rules or all of the above - and revealing they are actually remnants of a &quot;lost&quot; clan, some form of wicked dead or worse.<br /> Half the &quot;Mekhet&quot; bloodlines from Ancient Mysteries are actually Akhud infiltrators in my games, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-29-2020, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T01:44:36-08:00","id":1430849,"title":"","content":"I've read Thousand Years of Night, but I can't find a ruling on this and want to confirm: If a character's Vigor/Celerity/Resilience dots plus their dots in the corresponding Physical Attribute add up to more than ten, there's no rule that caps Attribute dice at ten, right? So if an elder has Vigor 5 with Strength 6 and Brawl 6, they can throw a punch at 17 dice before adding Willpower, Vitae expenditure, etc.?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T02:45:14-08:00","id":1430853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1430849#post1430849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read Thousand Years of Night, but I can't find a ruling on this and want to confirm: If a character's Vigor/Celerity/Resilience dots plus their dots in the corresponding Physical Attribute add up to more than ten, there's no rule that caps Attribute dice at ten, right? So if an elder has Vigor 5 with Strength 6 and Brawl 6, they can throw a punch at 17 dice before adding Willpower, Vitae expenditure, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly, Vigor doesn't count for the attribute's limit given by the BP. It's in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T09:11:19-08:00","id":1431293,"title":"","content":"How does a neonate Dukhan keeps his bane in check on a non-crossover session?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T11:44:45-08:00","id":1431306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1431293#post1431293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a neonate Dukhan keeps his bane in check on a non-crossover session?</div> </div> </div> </div>Holding off on dropping to Humanity 6 so it doesn't kick in, taking banes to remove torpor from the list of breaking points so repeated torpor is easier to manage, or getting ahold of &quot;some other method&quot; that allows them to access the Astral before they develop Nightmare Journey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T11:51:27-08:00","id":1431726,"title":"","content":"What has become of the Morbus with the 2e ? Their past rested a lot on the Fog of Eternity, but if I'm not mistaken, it has been removed in the 2nd Edition. I can't remember if they appeared again after Requiem for Rome or not (which i don't own).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T12:18:00-08:00","id":1431734,"title":"","content":"They popped up in the Dark Eras Companion, specifically the Black Plague era. Still operating in the shadows to keep their needs from alarming other Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T12:31:45-08:00","id":1431738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1431293#post1431293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a neonate Dukhan keeps his bane in check on a non-crossover session?</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to what Satchel said, if you are playing in Baghdad, I specifically wrote an Astral Iris into Baghdad's gates so Kindred can access the Astral without Beasts. I'd expect elder Dukhan have ways of bringing neonates into the Astral too, but such favours come with a price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T19:58:07-08:00","id":1431783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1431726#post1431726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What has become of the Morbus with the 2e ? Their past rested a lot on the Fog of Eternity, but if I'm not mistaken, it has been removed in the 2nd Edition. I can't remember if they appeared again after Requiem for Rome or not (which i don't own).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fog is gone, but keep in mind that vampires don't have perfect memory. I've used this comparison before, but think of it this way: I can't remember what I was doing last Tuesday, let alone three years ago. What hope is there for a centuries old being? Vampires have a tenuous grasp on their history, but they're also notorious liars, especially to themselves.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T21:48:15-08:00","id":1431787,"title":"","content":"Great ! So in theory, all I knew from Morbus in 1ed can be used - at least lorewise ? I'm not sure Cachexy works in the new edition as it was written down for the first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T22:12:43-08:00","id":1431792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1431787#post1431787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great ! So in theory, all I knew from Morbus in 1ed can be used - at least lorewise ? I'm not sure Cachexy works in the new edition as it was written down for the first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cachexy is also updated in the Dark Eras Companion. It\u2019s similar to the 1e version, but it had some quality of (un)life adjustments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T01:23:55-08:00","id":1431936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1431783#post1431783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Fog is gone, but keep in mind that vampires don't have perfect memory. I've used this comparison before, but think of it this way: I can't remember what I was doing last Tuesday, let alone three years ago. What hope is there for a centuries old being? Vampires have a tenuous grasp on their history, but they're also notorious liars, especially to themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought the fog still happens, its just not the default?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T02:11:49-08:00","id":1431938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1431936#post1431936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the fog still happens, its just not the default?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. In the torpor section it does mention that, on rare occasions, a vampire might wake up with a new personality or distorted recollections, but otherwise it's assumed the dreams you experience in torpor keep you sharp, and prepared for the future. The term &quot;fog of eternity&quot; is never used, and the idea that vampire history is unreliable <i>because </i>of torpor is gone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T05:57:59-08:00","id":1432187,"title":"","content":"I`m having a little trouble with animalism 3 numbers. Like, If a player summons a horde of rats(hundreds), how do I calculate its damage pool? Most humans could be killed by like, 2 or 3 rats biting them endlessly to feed on the vitae, but hundreds? Is there any way to calculate it or is animalism 3 that overpower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T06:29:13-08:00","id":1432193,"title":"","content":"Animalism 3 is something everyone appears to struggle with unless they're using it as a roleplaying tool rather than try to interact with it mechanically. I.e. it works as long as everyone simply reacts to it happening or the ST just narrates the effects of it being used. Anyone who wishes to interact with it mechanically is out of luck, and that's honestly a huge oversight, imo.<br /> <br /> If you do want to use it mechanically, you'd have to slap on some solution, either homebrew or from another book. DtD has a Swarm Tilt that could work for lesser animal swarms (maybe; I don't really recall how it works). CofD has a statted dog that, iirc, says it can stand in for a swarm of smaller animals (not what I'd recommend, but might as well mention it) as well as the Zombies! Tilt along with a statblock representing a horde that could work. The prerelease update of Deviant has optional rules for mass combat that can be used in tandem with the animal stat blocks in that one google document that's stickied on this forum.<br /> I personally think the best way to handle it with the tools given would be a variation of the Zombies! Tilt and simply do a simplified Horror statblock based on the type of animal. Just skip the Dread Powers and slap on whatever natural abilities the species should have. At least for smaller animals that are numerous enough to swarm. For large dogs and other animals that are not numerous enough and/or too dangerous to simplify to a single Environmental Tilt, I'd instead use the proper animal statblock combined with the new rules in Deviant if there's too many to roll for in a timely manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-14T06:33:08-08:00","id":1432195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1432187#post1432187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I`m having a little trouble with animalism 3 numbers. Like, If a player summons a horde of rats(hundreds), how do I calculate its damage pool? Most humans could be killed by like, 2 or 3 rats biting them endlessly to feed on the vitae, but hundreds? Is there any way to calculate it or is animalism 3 that overpower?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hi, Animalism 3 is very hard to modeling. I personally use Swarm rules you can find in Demon the Descent:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Animals of Size 1 are generally best represented by swarms, flocks and other groupings of the animals. Swarms are measured by their radius in yards. A swarm inflicts one point of bashing damage to anyone within its radius. A swarm can inflict more damage by condensing. Every time the swarm condenses to cover half of its full area, it inflicts one additional point of damage per turn.<br /> Therefore, a swarm of eight yards in radius inflicts two bashing damage per turn if it constricts down to a four yard radius, three bashing if it halves that again to a two-yard radius, and four bashing damage per turn it if condensed itself down to a one-yard radius. Though condensing doesn\u2019t usually happen all that often in nature (save in the case of creatures such as killer bees), it is an easy enough thing for a being with supernatural powers to command them to do so.<br /> Armor is effective against a swarm only if it covers one\u2019s full body, but even then it provides only half its rating. In addition, targets are distracted by the swarm, suffering \u20132 dice on all rolls while they are within the radius, even if they\u2019re not specifically attacked. </div> </div> </div>The point is:<br /> <br /> 1. Animalism 3 is not suddenly and instantly summoning all the swarm<br /> 2. Through Animalism 3 also bigger animals can come (dogs, cats....bears...)<br /> <br /> To address the timing issue I personally building up a damage value, 1 per turn, up to the cap of the successes rolled during the activation. This pool is following the above mentioned swarm's rules (no armor, -2 penality, etc).<br /> In case bigger animals, like dogs or bears, are fitting, I would have them arrive at the latest turn of the pool building up, and consider them separately (about the number of such animals this is actually your call).<br /> <br /> It might seem too powerful but consider that the damage is built up with time (4 turns to have 4 damages per turn in example), you might need to success in a first roll to spry the vitae directly on the target (against which I only allow a defense roll (defensex2) and action lost) otherwise you need an extra turn to command the swarm to attack after they had eaten the blood you did spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-14-2021, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T18:03:42-08:00","id":1432359,"title":"","content":"This happened to today session, at the Elysium:<br /> <br /> Premise: <br /> <br /> 1. PCs, got to London for the first time and not presented themeselves to the Prince, have been attacked through an Ambush because investigating on something they should not<br /> <br /> 2. PCs broke up the Masquerade several time to catch and hunt the assailants. They manage to kill one of them.<br /> <br /> 3. Few nights after OCs attacks the sheriff before he could speak thinking he was someone of the enemies of them. They are captured and taken to the Prince at rhe Elysium before all the kindred and Prinogens to be processed.<br /> <br /> One of the survived assiliant, legit member of that domain, enter accusing them to have attacked themeselves and killed one of its coterie while they were traing to investigate and catch the Masquerade violators. <br /> <br /> PCs said the truth, accusing him to try to cover something they don't want to be discovered. <br /> <br /> Several social rolls until one of the PC said: Prince, pls use your gift on bot me and himself forcing us tonsay the truth and you'll have your answer.<br /> <br /> How would you handle that? Why the Prince should refuse with a convincing argunent (convincing for the player)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T19:00:21-08:00","id":1432363,"title":"","content":"The foremost reason, the Prince doesn't know the PCs. They sneaked into town unannounced and immediately began shitting on the general order of the domain.<br /> 1. They arrive and pointedly did not present themselves.<br /> 2. The PCs interfered in an investigation being conducted by recognized kindred.<br /> 3. The PCs violated the Masquerade.<br /> 4. The PCs attacked and murdered a resident kindred.<br /> 5. The PCs attacked the sheriff.<br /> And finally, #6<br /> How in the holy hell do the PCs know the Prince has a power that can compel someone to speak the truth? Without knowing ANY relevant context to explain how they're aware of the Prince's power spread, I'd call that some massive metagaming bullshit and probably have the Prince order their execution on the spot.<br /> The PCs may well have evidence that convinces the Prince not to execute them or sentence them to a few centuries of torpor immediately, but I don't see any prince realistically holding praxis for long if they allow any wandering group of assholes stroll into the domain, violate the Masquerade, murder a resident, and assault the sheriff with impunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-15T19:41:43-08:00","id":1432366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1432363#post1432363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The foremost reason, the Prince doesn't know the PCs. They sneaked into town unannounced and immediately began shitting on the general order of the domain.<br /> 1. They arrive and pointedly did not present themselves.<br /> 2. The PCs interfered in an investigation being conducted by recognized kindred.<br /> 3. The PCs violated the Masquerade.<br /> 4. The PCs attacked and murdered a resident kindred.<br /> 5. The PCs attacked the sheriff.<br /> And finally, #6<br /> How in the holy hell do the PCs know the Prince has a power that can compel someone to speak the truth? Without knowing ANY relevant context to explain how they're aware of the Prince's power spread, I'd call that some massive metagaming bullshit and probably have the Prince order their execution on the spot.<br /> The PCs may well have evidence that convinces the Prince not to execute them or sentence them to a few centuries of torpor immediately, but I don't see any prince realistically holding praxis for long if they allow any wandering group of assholes stroll into the domain, violate the Masquerade, murder a resident, and assault the sheriff with impunity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Compelling the truth&quot; could be seen as a matter of Dominate or Majesty, both disciplines that are far from uncommon in the bag of tricks of princes in general, to pull a confession out of the target. So, kindred society being what it is, while completely an assumption on the PC's part, it's not a ludricous one in the least.<br /> <br /> That said, who's to say either the witness or the PCs haven't been preemptively tampered with, to <i>fabricate </i>a kind of truth, in the first place? That is also <b><i>definitely </i></b>something a reasonably experienced prince would be aware of the possibility of, making the whole argument less effective than the PC imagines it to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> The 2 big questions in the situation, as i see it at least, are:<br /> - Why would a coterie of kindred enter another city <b><i>unannounced </i></b>to do any sort of investigation in the first place? That can and should be seen as a foolish thing to do at best and brazen open flouting of the prince's authority by outsiders at worst.<br /> <br /> - Truth or not is <b><i>immaterial </i></b>to nocturnal politics! The PCs entered unnanounced the city, violated the masquerade and killed kindred residents (that were useful to it) - what can they offer as <i>compensation </i>for these acts in terms of information, resources or service that would be of value <i>towards the consolidation/preservation of its rule</i>?<br /> <br /> One does not sit in the throne to serve others or worry too much about the fictions of justice or truth, pshaw! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-15-2021, 10:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T02:22:17-08:00","id":1432391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1432363#post1432363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The foremost reason, the Prince doesn't know the PCs. They sneaked into town unannounced and immediately began shitting on the general order of the domain.<br /> 1. They arrive and pointedly did not present themselves.<br /> 2. The PCs interfered in an investigation being conducted by recognized kindred.<br /> 3. The PCs violated the Masquerade.<br /> 4. The PCs attacked and murdered a resident kindred.<br /> 5. The PCs attacked the sheriff.<br /> And finally, #6<br /> How in the holy hell do the PCs know the Prince has a power that can compel someone to speak the truth? Without knowing ANY relevant context to explain how they're aware of the Prince's power spread, I'd call that some massive metagaming bullshit and probably have the Prince order their execution on the spot.<br /> The PCs may well have evidence that convinces the Prince not to execute them or sentence them to a few centuries of torpor immediately, but I don't see any prince realistically holding praxis for long if they allow any wandering group of assholes stroll into the domain, violate the Masquerade, murder a resident, and assault the sheriff with impunity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Points 1 to 5 are exactly the reason they were risking their un-life indeed. Two of them (players) are new to Masquerade so I need to let them understand how things works and why but I prefer doing that in game, hence without to be TOO HARD <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. But still their execution was one option indeed.<br /> <br /> They knew Prince (or other in that court) had Dominate because, they know he's an elder Ventrue (thus is very unlikely he do not have one or 2 dots at least in dominate) and the prince itself used it to shut up one of them being way to much sarcastic, talking over to him (I know another reason to have them executed, but for the reason above I tried to be more patient - it actually worked indeed as the player couldn't speak for a good part of the speech and when the Prince freed him he was far more polite).<br /> By a story point of view, reason why Prince didn't kill them is because they spoke about something that attracted his attention (without getting into details, they reveled they found the blood of a long time disappeared elder of the Ordo, into a substance that was lastly spreading among the homeless of the city making them addicted and violent. Prince basically want to hear and know about that smelling something wrong. So he pretended to be generous giving the possibility to the 3 PCs to clean up their mess restoring the masquerade (warning them they would have been closely spied in case they intended to escape), while the Sheriff would have investigate on the two versions of the story. This is obviously only a story to feed to the primogens and other kindred to take time. He's also secretly summoned them privately to make the deal of continuing to investigate on that giving him any update.<br /> <br /> The point of my question remains though: I can see why Auspex can't be used as a proof in a judgment; only Auspex user knows the truth and he could turn the &quot;truth&quot; to its own convenience. But Dominate is quite different. You can command to say the truth to both parties, and you are compelled to say the truth (your truth) in front of the whole audience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1432366#post1432366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Compelling the truth&quot; could be seen as a matter of Dominate or Majesty, both disciplines that are far from uncommon in the bag of tricks of princes in general, to pull a confession out of the target. So, kindred society being what it is, while completely an assumption on the PC's part, it's not a ludricous one in the least.<br /> <br /> That said, who's to say either the witness or the PCs haven't been preemptively tampered with, to <i>fabricate </i>a kind of truth, in the first place? That is also <b><i>definitely </i></b>something a reasonably experienced prince would be aware of the possibility of, making the whole argument less effective than the PC imagines it to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> The 2 big questions in the situation, as i see it at least, are:<br /> - Why would a coterie of kindred enter another city <b><i>unannounced </i></b>to do any sort of investigation in the first place? That can and should be seen as a foolish thing to do at best and brazen open flouting of the prince's authority by outsiders at worst.<br /> <br /> - Truth or not is <b><i>immaterial </i></b>to nocturnal politics! The PCs entered unnanounced the city, violated the masquerade and killed kindred residents (that were useful to it) - what can they offer as <i>compensation </i>for these acts in terms of information, resources or service that would be of value <i>towards the consolidation/preservation of its rule</i>?<br /> <br /> One does not sit in the throne to serve others or worry too much about the fictions of justice or truth, pshaw! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You have a point here. Sure, the truth can be fabricated, sure, although it is for sure quite hard for some neonate to be able to modify their own memory and or the one of the accuser. Because their proposal was to actually dominate both the parties: the accuser (who was laying trying to revert their attempt to ambush them as a right act against themselves) and the players who were saying the truth indeed.<br /> <br /> The point is: it's hard to play these political lying game into Elysium, justifying to both players and PCs why not just using powers like Dominate, Auspex to know where dwell the truth.<br /> And as I said, yes, their crimes are enough to have them killed, non the less they justify themselves to be attacked and act to defend, which is making a huge difference if the Prince want to pretend to be fair and right in front of his court.<br /> <br /> EDIT: as a side note: I handled it having the prince asking the accuser to freely submit its supernatural inquisition. He obliviously politely declined saying that this is not custom in a &quot;civil&quot; domain to be mind controlled and that its word should count more than the one of parasites intruder. He will probably submit himself to this inquisition once he got prepared through dominate changing its memory (maybe through dominate 3 triggering the false memory to come out just for the inquiries)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-16-2021, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-16T05:53:26-08:00","id":1432400,"title":"","content":"The PCs maybe tweaking their memories shouldn't figure highly in the Prince or Sheriff's PoV actually - but they don't know the PCs in the first place, so how would one know they are not the brainwashed puppets of some 3rd party, in the city (the tale about them being from another city a completely memory edited fabrication) or outside it?<br /> <br /> Remember how it's implied in the clanbooks that Felix is a Khaibit ancient (if not a methuselah) that right out of torpor brainwashed a Daeva elder in believing Felix was his childe and presenting him to many other kindred as exactly so? Now consider that Felix is a kind of righteous and mostly well-meaning guy when compared to lots of other kindred and imagine what their degree of Dominate abuse on people around them can be... and how as a prince you might have to deal with variants of this kind of trickery <i>all the time</i>. So testimony, willing or coerced, is worth almost nothing.<br /> <br /> Evidence, obtained through mundane investigation, Auspex, blood magic, weird supernatural merits or whatever, <i>might </i>be of greater value. But again, <i>politics </i>comes first, if the prince does not have some particular reason to care about truth more than expediency.<br /> <br /> Because the PCs dropped the ball big time there - entering a city uninvited may not be such a big deal, as long as you present yourself <i>before being caught</i>. If you are, <i>everything </i>you say is unreliable (&quot;everything you say and do will be used against you&quot;, so to speak) and any other tradition break commited gets amped with a &quot;tried to avoid recognition/capture&quot; extra. They are screwed.<br /> <br /> Real questions are:<br /> - What can the prince or other kindred in power gain from sparing the PCs?<br /> - What kind of compensation can they offer - in information, favors &amp; services - to make up for their crimes?<br /> - And how will both things - the destruction of a local coterie and their continued presence in the city, now chained to either prince, sheriff, the mentors-patrons of the destroyed coterie or some other individual of power - change the dynamics of power in the domain from that point onward? Not to mention individuals with more personal ties to the destroyed kindred repositioning themselves (openly or in secret) in the factions' dance out of spite and/or a desire for revenge not adressed by whatever ruling comes out in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-16-2021, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T11:01:41-08:00","id":1432926,"title":"","content":"Would it be feasible to a vampire with Auspex 4 to develop something akin to &quot;Tactical Telepathy&quot; from Hurt Locker? Like, how close to the actual Telepathy merit is Auspex 4?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T11:36:12-08:00","id":1432933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1432926#post1432926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be feasible to a vampire with Auspex 4 to develop something akin to &quot;Tactical Telepathy&quot; from Hurt Locker? Like, how close to the actual Telepathy merit is Auspex 4?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, i would say compare their texts and decide for yourself how close the Telepathy merit and Auspex 4 power are and roll things from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T19:58:00-08:00","id":1433129,"title":"","content":"Is there a devotion or can Nightmare implant a fear into someone? like if someone isn't afraid of spiders can they be made afraid of spiders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T02:00:07-08:00","id":1433147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1433129#post1433129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a devotion or can Nightmare implant a fear into someone? like if someone isn't afraid of spiders can they be made afraid of spiders?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not.<br /> Nightmare 3, by default, make you able to inflict delusion which may lead to be scared of something: spiders are alien ans evil creatures.<br /> <br /> Buy also a devotion between Nightmare 3 + vigor 1 can let you implant new fears. Or Nightmare + dominate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T00:39:37-08:00","id":1433234,"title":"","content":"Hi,<br /> It's surely not the first time someone is asking, but I couldn't find any clear answer : <br /> <br /> - The Max Vitae/turn is an absolute limit ? (related to Tricks of the damned &amp; Disciplines). A BP1 Vampire using Predatory aspect (Protean**) to manifest his claws can no longer use one Vitae to heal damages on his turn ?<br /> - How could the same BP1 Vampire use Beast's skin (Protean***), who has a 2 Vitae cost ?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help !<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23555-falcina","name":"Falcina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23555_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T01:17:49-08:00","id":1433239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1433234#post1433234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi,<br /> It's surely not the first time someone is asking, but I couldn't find any clear answer : <br /> <br /> - The Max Vitae/turn is an absolute limit ? (related to Tricks of the damned &amp; Disciplines). A BP1 Vampire using Predatory aspect (Protean**) to manifest his claws can no longer use one Vitae to heal damages on his turn ?<br /> - How could the same BP1 Vampire use Beast's skin (Protean***), who has a 2 Vitae cost ?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your help !</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Bp gives you the limit. BP1 can use either protean 2 or healing himself, not both. <br /> To activate powers requiring more vitae he can spend the blood through 2 turns and the effect will take place only when the full price is paid. Which means a younger vampire takes more time to activate an effect that an older can in just one turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T03:49:20-08:00","id":1434102,"title":"","content":"Is there any official, in 1st or 2nd edition, way of transforming someone into a vampire by cursing them? Like, magically speaking. Akin to a witch or something cursing someone with vampirism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T05:43:43-08:00","id":1434111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434102#post1434102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any official, in 1st or 2nd edition, way of transforming someone into a vampire by cursing them? Like, magically speaking. Akin to a witch or something cursing someone with vampirism?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure there's nothing like that in 2e, and I don't recall seeing anything about it in 1e. The closest I can think of is tainting someone with Vitae to make them more likely to spontaneously Embrace, but it's not a sure thing and requires them dying somehow for it to even be relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-01T08:55:45-08:00","id":1434138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434102#post1434102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any official, in 1st or 2nd edition, way of transforming someone into a vampire by cursing them? Like, magically speaking. Akin to a witch or something cursing someone with vampirism?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434111#post1434111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure there's nothing like that in 2e, and I don't recall seeing anything about it in 1e. The closest I can think of is tainting someone with Vitae to make them more likely to spontaneously Embrace, but it's not a sure thing and requires them dying somehow for it to even be relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I might be mixing things a bit and would have to check the clanbooks for actual confirmation, but i remember it being implied that strong exposure to kindred mental powers or disciplines could also count as &quot;taint&quot; for matters of &quot;spontaneous embrace/rising&quot;.<br /> <br /> Someone ressurected through the use of the Worm Pipe (HtV: Night Stalkers, pgs. 146-148 and Nosferatu, pgs. 67-68) <i>definitely </i>would count as tainted in such a way, same for a person whose heart was taken by a Child of Phobos (Blood Sorcery, pgs. 55-59), i'd guess.<br /> <br /> edit: the last can count as <b><i>updated into </i></b><b><i>actual canon</i></b>, if the fragment on the Jiangshi in page 255 of 2nd edition is taken at face value.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, if one wants to explore the idea of witchcraft, hexing and vampirism mixing up i suggest a good look at Night Stalkers and Nosferatu &amp; Mekhet clanbooks. For beings that straddle the line between human blood witch and vampire i would also suggest Blood Sorcery (duh), Ordo Dracul (the Vedma bloodline, that claim to have created the Gangrel and not the opposite) and Night Horrors: Wicked Dead (for the Cihuateteo - at least one version, there's another in Shadows of Mexico, but i digress) for reference and ideas to mine and mix up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-01-2021, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T08:13:27-08:00","id":1434260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434102#post1434102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any official, in 1st or 2nd edition, way of transforming someone into a vampire by cursing them? Like, magically speaking. Akin to a witch or something cursing someone with vampirism?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're called dhampirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T10:13:24-08:00","id":1434269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434260#post1434260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're called dhampirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as i know someone must be born as a dhampir, as a byproduct of magic also but not on a born human","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T17:54:28-08:00","id":1434313,"title":"","content":"A child born with vampiric powers and bloodlust conceived only because vampire witchcraft enabled a vampire to be fertile when they rape someone IS cursing someone with vampirism.<br /> <br /> Technically the Tremere clan exists because a douchebag wizard and his asshole friends and cursed themselves after botching a spell. And in typical douchebag fashion they went out and cursed or murdered their followers.<br /> <br /> But no World of Darkness isn't competent enough to do justice to the story of Angelique Bouchard and Barnabas Collins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T20:21:52-08:00","id":1434343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434313#post1434313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A child born with vampiric powers and bloodlust conceived only because vampire witchcraft enabled a vampire to be fertile when they rape someone IS cursing someone with vampirism.<br /> <br /> Technically the Tremere clan exists because a douchebag wizard and his asshole friends and cursed themselves after botching a spell. And in typical douchebag fashion they went out and cursed or murdered their followers.<br /> <br /> But no World of Darkness isn't competent enough to do justice to the story of Angelique Bouchard and Barnabas Collins.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Vampire deals with mature subject matter and questionable consent by nature but a warning and request to be a bit more circumspect when discussing this particular topic.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-03-2021, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-02T23:24:17-08:00","id":1434350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434313#post1434313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A child born with vampiric powers and bloodlust conceived only because vampire witchcraft enabled a vampire to be fertile when they rape someone IS cursing someone with vampirism.<br /> <br /> Technically the Tremere clan exists because a douchebag wizard and his asshole friends and cursed themselves after botching a spell. And in typical douchebag fashion they went out and cursed or murdered their followers.<br /> <br /> But no World of Darkness isn't competent enough to do justice to the story of Angelique Bouchard and Barnabas Collins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but i think that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7210_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7210\" data-vbnamecard=\"7210\">Horodrigo</a> was asking if you can turn an adult human into a vampire with a curse.<br /> Thinking about it, an archmage could be able to use an imperial spell to apply the Vampire template","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T00:34:15-08:00","id":1434354,"title":"","content":"Am I wrong or is there a Strix's power which allow a kind of synthesis between the 2 being creating a new vampire?<br /> If yes, what should be the Clan's bane, if any?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T01:35:59-08:00","id":1434356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434354#post1434354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I wrong or is there a Strix's power which allow a kind of synthesis between the 2 being creating a new vampire?<br /> If yes, what should be the Clan's bane, if any?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Rank&quot; 6 Strix can turn humans that they are possessing into vampires (with a clan depending on several factors) sacrificing a part of themselves (ot totally in some cases).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T02:12:03-08:00","id":1434359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434354#post1434354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I wrong or is there a Strix's power which allow a kind of synthesis between the 2 being creating a new vampire?<br /> If yes, what should be the Clan's bane, if any?</div> </div> </div> </div>Synthesis between a Strix and a human, a revenant or a corpse just applies one of the preexisting Clan templates on the target.<br /> Synthesis between a Strix and a Kindred only grants dots of Blood Potency equal to how much Shadow Potency the Strix lost in the process.<br /> <br /> Available at Shadow Potency 6. Don't know why you say &quot;Rank&quot;. Yes, they were originally based on the ephemeral entity rules during the development of B&amp;S, but literally everything except the fact that they use three Attributes (something which isn't unique to ephemeral entities) has been rewritten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-03T02:25:39-08:00","id":1434360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434359#post1434359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Synthesis between a Strix and a human, a revenant or a corpse just applies one of the preexisting Clan templates on the target.<br /> Synthesis between a Strix and a Kindred only grants dots of Blood Potency equal to how much Shadow Potency the Strix lost in the process.<br /> <br /> Available at Shadow Potency 6. Don't know why you say &amp;quot;Rank&amp;quot;. Yes, they were originally based on the ephemeral entity rules during the development of B&amp;S, but literally everything except the fact that they use three Attributes (something which isn't unique to ephemeral entities) has been rewritten.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, i used &quot;Rank&quot; because i didn t remember how the power stat was named \ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T06:16:02-08:00","id":1434481,"title":"","content":"With predatory aura, Vampires recognize each others and their Clan appartenance, I\u2019m right ?<br /> Could they also determine Blood potency ? (considering they have to use a Willpower to lash out the Beast if adversary\u00b4s BP is higher)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23555-falcina","name":"Falcina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23555_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T06:30:04-08:00","id":1434483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434481#post1434481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With predatory aura, Vampires recognize each others and their Clan appartenance, I\u2019m right ?<br /> Could they also determine Blood potency ? (considering they have to use a Willpower to lash out the Beast if adversary\u00b4s BP is higher)</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires can sense Predatory Auras but gain no further information. They don't recognise whether it's a Clanmate or if they're even a vampire. It could be a Strix in the body of a mortal or a corpse.<br /> When Lashing Out they could get a vague measure of Blood Potency since they compare their strengths. The defender might figure out whether the aggressor has higher Blood Potency or not since they only have to spend WP to defend against those with higher BP. The aggressor always have to spend WP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T06:30:38-08:00","id":1434484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434481#post1434481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With predatory aura, Vampires recognize each others and their Clan appartenance, I\u2019m right ?<br /> Could they also determine Blood potency ? (considering they have to use a Willpower to lash out the Beast if adversary\u00b4s BP is higher)</div> </div> </div> </div>Predatory aura shows only if someone is a vampire or not.<br /> To discover a vampire clan you need to taste his blood and make a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T06:34:44-08:00","id":1434486,"title":"","content":"You can also recognise Clanmates through Blood Sympathy, but since you can't just choose to detect those within the same Clan it's quite unreliable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T12:23:59-08:00","id":1434773,"title":"","content":"Simple question about Resilience. Do the Active effects last against a single attack or for the entire turn? Also, can someone activate Resilience when they take damage, or do they have to declare it before the attack is rolled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25591-emerus","name":"Emerus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25591_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T13:17:47-08:00","id":1434780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434773#post1434773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple question about Resilience. Do the Active effects last against a single attack or for the entire turn? Also, can someone activate Resilience when they take damage, or do they have to declare it before the attack is rolled?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is for attack. Which is good because you can reflexively reduce the same amount of damage from multiple sources. <br /> You can activate it reflexively, hence also after the attack is rolled and after surprise attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T04:21:51-08:00","id":1434830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434780#post1434780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is for attack. Which is good because you can reflexively reduce the same amount of damage from multiple sources.<br /> You can activate it reflexively, hence also after the attack is rolled and after surprise attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does that mean that you can also activate celerity after your opponent rolls to see if they'd hit you at all and only then side step the atack? Similarly, can I look at how much damage my opponent is going to inflict to me before I decide if I'm going to heal? If I don't need to heal now, I can do some ability on my turn. <br /> <br /> <br /> Imo, rolling dice is resolving an action and you complete resolving one action before moving on (even if it's a reflexive action). <br /> <br /> However, in terms of Resilience, I housrule it that you may activate it after seeing damage, since it's a pretty... not exciting discipline otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T04:45:52-08:00","id":1434831,"title":"","content":"Resilience is for a turn, and affects every single attack of the bane/non-bane sort you activated it for within that whole turn. Thus the Duration entry of &quot;one turn&quot; for active effects and the entries going into &quot;all (Bane/non-bane) sources of damage.&quot; If you activate it and then 10 people attack you before your next turn, you subtract Resilience from the damage of all 10 of those attacks.<br /> <br /> By RAW they'd need to activate it before the damage is calculated, as such, but given Resilience is more about ignoring harm than preventing it, I tend to be lenient with that, myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434830#post1434830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, can I look at how much damage my opponent is going to inflict to me before I decide if I'm going to heal? If I don't need to heal now, I can do some ability on my turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the other examples are valid, you can heal whenever you want if you still have per-turn Vitae left, and it won't affect your next turn, because your per-turn limit resets on the start of your turn. You can ABSOLUTELY wait to see how much damage they did before healing, because healing is an 'after the fact' sorta thing, not preventing anything, like Resilience or Celerity would be.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T05:43:02-08:00","id":1434835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1434830#post1434830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that mean that you can also activate celerity after your opponent rolls to see if they'd hit you at all and only then side step the atack? Similarly, can I look at how much damage my opponent is going to inflict to me before I decide if I'm going to heal? If I don't need to heal now, I can do some ability on my turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> Imo, rolling dice is resolving an action and you complete resolving one action before moving on (even if it's a reflexive action).<br /> <br /> However, in terms of Resilience, I housrule it that you may activate it after seeing damage, since it's a pretty... not exciting discipline otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can definitely use Celerity (Interrupt) when the enemy perform the attack but before he roll for it as what you are doing is to anticipate the attack with your supernatural speed and reaction time. But if the attack is rolled and he hit, it already includes the damage, hence you cannot logically anticipate it unless you go back in time. In fact, if you decide to go first in initiative (not interruption), you must declare it before the actions are declared. <br /> you can heal whenever you want in the turn. You suffer damages and you can decide to heal them up if you like before the turn ends. If the damages would have led you in torpor but you are able to heal them up before end of the turn (meaning you have enough blood to spend), you can prevent torpor.<br /> <br /> About resilience, in my opinion is not a houserule as you are dealing with that: the active effect is reflexive and it subtract damages, which means that you can decide to subtract them also after they have been dealt as per healing them up. In fact there is no real distinction between resilience 1 and healing for one vitae when applied to bashing damages. The difference start to come up when dealing with lethal and/or aggravated damages (or when resilience exceed the first dot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-08-2021, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T06:27:27-08:00","id":1435065,"title":"","content":"I was re-reading the Coil of Zirnitra.<br /> &quot;Some Dragons have developed this Coil to regain the lost gifts granted to them by their heritage as part of a werewolf family. Some use it to recover the magics tied to their mortal bloodlines.&quot;<br /> Does this mean that it s possible to buy normal supernatural merits that was considered allowed by this heritage, or does this mean that even werewolf Tells, proximus spells and similar powers are included?<br /> I was thinking about a possible Hypathian ex alchemist character, and i m wondering if he could use the coil to re learn magnitude (1exp per dot) and distillations (1exp per level for each single one) without using the Grafting Unholy Flesh scale.<br /> Do you think it would be too overpowered?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 02-11-2021, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T18:23:36-08:00","id":1435257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1435065#post1435065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was re-reading the Coil of Zirnitra.<br /> &quot;Some Dragons have developed this Coil to regain the lost gifts granted to them by their heritage as part of a werewolf family. Some use it to recover the magics tied to their mortal bloodlines.&quot;<br /> Does this mean that it s possible to buy normal supernatural merits that was considered allowed by this heritage, or does this mean that even werewolf Tells, proximus spells and similar powers are included?<br /> I was thinking about a possible Hypathian ex alchemist character, and i m wondering if he could use the coil to re learn magnitude (1exp per dot) and distillations (1exp per level for each single one) without using the Grafting Unholy Flesh scale.<br /> Do you think it would be too overpowered?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that when development on 2e first started, the plan was that Tells, Proximus Blessings, and all sorts of other half-template abilities would be specialized Supernatural merits. SotC was written before werewolf/mage had definitively changed that.<br /> <br /> So, long story short, RAW no, but an ST could allow it and be within RAI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T03:46:19-08:00","id":1435282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1435257#post1435257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that when development on 2e first started, the plan was that Tells, Proximus Blessings, and all sorts of other half-template abilities would be specialized Supernatural merits. SotC was written before werewolf/mage had definitively changed that.<br /> <br /> So, long story short, RAW no, but an ST could allow it and be within RAI.</div> </div> </div> </div>SotC came out after both WtF 2e and MtA 2e. Also, Tells and Proximi Blessings <i>are</i> specialised Supernatural Merits. The only thing missing from the text of Zirnitra is an explicit confirmation that the vampire can ignore the &quot;half-template&quot; restrictions on those Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T06:34:41-08:00","id":1435291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1435282#post1435282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SotC came out after both WtF 2e and MtA 2e. Also, Tells and Proximi Blessings <i>are</i> specialised Supernatural Merits. The only thing missing from the text of Zirnitra is an explicit confirmation that the vampire can ignore the &quot;half-template&quot; restrictions on those Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, in fact my main dubt is about that missing explicit confirmation.<br /> What is your opinion about it?<br /> I m also worried about a possible game balance break...<br /> but i admit that the idea of an Hypatian vampire that uses a Coil to recover his former Alchemist s powers sounds so cool and badass in my mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 02-12-2021, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T08:00:33-08:00","id":1435298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1435291#post1435291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, in fact my main dubt is about that missing explicit confirmation.<br /> What is your opinion about it?<br /> I m also worried about a possible game balance break...<br /> but i admit that the idea of an Hypatian vampire that uses a Coil to recover his former Alchemist s powers sounds so cool and badass in my mind</div> </div> </div> </div>The flavour text is quite clear about the subject. At the very least, vampires who used to have another template should be able to buy Supernatural Merits that were available to their previous template. However, that means a former Proximus should still have to conform to the limitations to their previous state, which determines which Arcana they may buy Blessings from as well as how many dots' worth of Blessings they may purchase. For vampires that didn't belong to a different template, I'd suggest having a Merit with a Coil of Zirnitra prerequisite to count as being part of that template for purposes of template restrictions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T22:12:45-08:00","id":1435340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1435282#post1435282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SotC came out after both WtF 2e and MtA 2e. Also, Tells and Proximi Blessings <i>are</i> specialised Supernatural Merits. The only thing missing from the text of Zirnitra is an explicit confirmation that the vampire can ignore the &quot;half-template&quot; restrictions on those Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was <i>written</i> before they were out, was my wording. There's previews for SotC toys from beforehand, and it's not surprising that they didn't get changed, given the process for OPP stuff.<br /> <br /> And no, they are not specialized supernatural merits, they are a Wolf-Blood template feature and merit, and a proximus merit. Supernatural Merits are a special category of merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T16:25:32-08:00","id":1435493,"title":"","content":"Is vicissitude around in 2.0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3363-viridian-sun","name":"viridian sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T16:35:08-08:00","id":1435495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viridian sun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1435493#post1435493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is vicissitude around in 2.0?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from a different game, so I'm not sure why it would be, barring STV products or the Translation Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T19:19:06-08:00","id":1435500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viridian sun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1435493#post1435493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is vicissitude around in 2.0?</div> </div> </div> </div>Closest thing to it is the Chimera Virus from Spilled Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T19:21:47-08:00","id":1435501,"title":"","content":"What constitutes an apocryphal Coil for the Ordo Dracul? Would a Transhumanist Coil be considered apocryphal? Like, something that let's the vampire augment itself with cybernetics and artificial limbs, organs and stuff like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T19:36:13-08:00","id":1435502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1435501#post1435501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What constitutes an apocryphal Coil for the Ordo Dracul?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Ordo Dracul book, p176, &quot;Whereas the Coils of the Dragon are meant to overcome the curse laid upon Dracula and all Kindred, these apocryphal pseudo-Coils either subvert the power that was bestowed with the curse, or warp the nature of the curse without truly overcoming it.<br /> These philosophies are not officially welcome within the covenant. Knowledge of these powers is forbidden. Dragons found to have studied them should expect to be severely punished. Knowledge of these powers is one of the few ways for a Dragon to be driven out of the covenant \u2014 though most such Kindred are rendered into ash within a few nights thereafter.&quot;<br /> <br /> The covenant has changed a bit but it's a sound foundation to work off of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would a Transhumanist Coil be considered apocryphal? Like, something that let's the vampire augment itself with cybernetics and artificial limbs, organs and stuff like that? </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes, if only because that just shifts the arbiter of their immortality from something like God or Fate to whatever engineer made them. Plus technology is notoriously open to subversion, something the Ordo believe as a big no-no. One of the banned bloodlines among them is the Dragolescu, who can steal knowledge from the dead, but potentially open themselves to being taken over by ghosts. Unless you had some cutting edge, isolated technology that would always remain beyond the ability of someone with Computers 5 to just turn off, then you're sort of opening yourself to the same issue. Basically the same reason they don't make big human suits to walk around in while protecting them from sunlight, it's just sidestepping the issue and not improving the vampire.<br /> <br /> Plus artificial organs aren't quite necessary given the undead nature of the vampire, who can turn their flesh as hard as steel and doesn't need to really digest anything but blood.<br /> <br /> And of course, cybernetics don't really have to fit in a mystical Coil and can usually be something you craft without supernatural help. It might actually be something the Carthians embrace more than the Ordo Dracul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T09:17:00-08:00","id":1435857,"title":"","content":"Is there any rules for distributing Beats because of a mentor? Like, in an Ordo Dracul Mentor-Neonates group, is there any way for the Neonates to get more beats from studying, or for the mentor to distribute or gain Beats from teaching? I'm asking ruleswise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T16:56:42-08:00","id":1435914,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it\u2019s called awarding Beats for fulfilling Aspirations and awarding Beats after completing a game session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T00:43:30-08:00","id":1435975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1435857#post1435857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any rules for distributing Beats because of a mentor? Like, in an Ordo Dracul Mentor-Neonates group, is there any way for the Neonates to get more beats from studying, or for the mentor to distribute or gain Beats from teaching? I'm asking ruleswise.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also the Tutelage Merit in Guide to the Night, p. 127.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T12:18:07-08:00","id":1436258,"title":"","content":"Is it correct that you can wake without vitae after falling into torpor without someone rousing you?<br /> <br /> Per VTR 2.0, &quot;At the end of a vampire\u2019s turn, after any reflexive healing, if her last (rightmost) Health box is filled with lethal damage, she falls to torpor. If she\u2019s in daysleep, and has no blood with which to awaken, she instead drifts into the torpor. As well, a vampire can voluntarily fall into torpor, to shake off the feeding limitations imposed by her Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> During the first day of torpor, the vampire subconsciously spends as much Vitae as it takes to heal any wounds she may have. If, after spending all her Vitae, she still suffers a wound in her last three Health boxes, consider her Humanity one dot lower for determining how long she slumbers. For every twenty-five years a vampire remains in torpor, she loses a dot of Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> Use the following chart to determine how long a character must remain in torpor. Multiply the base duration (based on the vampire\u2019s Humanity dots) by her Blood Potency. After that amount of time in torpor, she can awaken.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3363-viridian-sun","name":"viridian sun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T13:04:29-08:00","id":1436268,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's true. You wake up with 0 vitae when the time has passed (probably in frenzy) and you have a full night to feed up before to fall into torpor again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T21:46:22-08:00","id":1436747,"title":"","content":"Merits like Crusader and Sorcerous Eunuch note that they protect against &quot;magic&quot;, but don't really elaborate on what &quot;magic&quot; means, and they don't specifically say Blood Magic. So, what forms of magic are they meant to apply to? is it just Blood Magic, or is it more than that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T04:13:45-08:00","id":1436777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1436747#post1436747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merits like Crusader and Sorcerous Eunuch note that they protect against &quot;magic&quot;, but don't really elaborate on what &quot;magic&quot; means, and they don't specifically say Blood Magic. So, what forms of magic are they meant to apply to? is it just Blood Magic, or is it more than that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's start with Crusader merit. There are 3 different powers here.<br /> Shield Against Sorcery (\u2022): There's a line that says &quot;Any magic targeting your character&quot;. It doesn't say what constitute magic, but it says any magic, wich is literally anything that is described as being magic, like supernal spells, Cru\u00e1c, Theban Sorcery, on sorcerous Eunuch this becomes a little more clear.<br /> Silence (\u2022\u2022): Says that &quot;If successful, the attack silences the enemy, which may prevent him from casting spells or using some Disciplines so long as the damage remains.&quot; wich means, anything that depends on voice, like some spells or issuing commands with the Dominate discipline will not work. Interesting to note that you can still be Mesmerized, but the Vampire will no be able to talk while the damage remains.<br /> A Hammer Against Witches (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Says that &quot;The victim must be casting a spell or ritual of some sort, or a Discipline using an extended action.&quot;, so, it considers extended actions to do supernatural things rituals and spells.<br /> <br /> Now, the other merit, Sorcerous Eunuch says that &quot;Any dice pool for a magical effect targeting your character suffers his Resolve as a penalty.&quot;, so, anything that the ST considers as magic, like Supernal spells, Cru\u00e1c, etc, receive this penalty. If you are not convinced about blood sorcery, the merit also says that &quot;As result of this, he can never learn Theban Sorcery, Cr\u00faac, or any other blood sorceries.&quot;, so it's safe to say that Theban Sorcery and Cru\u00e1c are considered like magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T14:44:41-08:00","id":1436877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1436777#post1436777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's start with Crusader merit. There are 3 different powers here.<br /> Shield Against Sorcery (\u2022): There's a line that says &quot;Any magic targeting your character&quot;. It doesn't say what constitute magic, but it says any magic, wich is literally anything that is described as being magic, like supernal spells, Cru\u00e1c, Theban Sorcery, on sorcerous Eunuch this becomes a little more clear.<br /> Silence (\u2022\u2022): Says that &quot;If successful, the attack silences the enemy, which may prevent him from casting spells or using some Disciplines so long as the damage remains.&quot; wich means, anything that depends on voice, like some spells or issuing commands with the Dominate discipline will not work. Interesting to note that you can still be Mesmerized, but the Vampire will no be able to talk while the damage remains.<br /> A Hammer Against Witches (\u2022\u2022\u2022): Says that &quot;The victim must be casting a spell or ritual of some sort, or a Discipline using an extended action.&quot;, so, it considers extended actions to do supernatural things rituals and spells.<br /> <br /> Now, the other merit, Sorcerous Eunuch says that &quot;Any dice pool for a magical effect targeting your character suffers his Resolve as a penalty.&quot;, so, anything that the ST considers as magic, like Supernal spells, Cru\u00e1c, etc, receive this penalty. If you are not convinced about blood sorcery, the merit also says that &quot;As result of this, he can never learn Theban Sorcery, Cr\u00faac, or any other blood sorceries.&quot;, so it's safe to say that Theban Sorcery and Cru\u00e1c are considered like magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, for Shield Against Sorcery and Sorcerous Eunuch things like disciplines, contracts, haunts, numena, etc would all count as magic? That's pretty amazing for something as cheap as a merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T15:33:56-08:00","id":1436885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1436877#post1436877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for Shield Against Sorcery and Sorcerous Eunuch things like disciplines, contracts, haunts, numena, etc would all count as magic? That's pretty amazing for something as cheap as a merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Within VtR &quot;sorcery&quot; should exclusively refer to blood sorcery, and it's specifically sorcery both Crusader and Sorcerous Eunuch focuses on. The two exceptions are Silence that affects any powers that requires speech (for completely mundane reasons) and A Hammer Against Witches which works against both sorcery <i>and</i> Disciplines using extended actions.<br /> <br /> When it comes to sorcery from other games, it's simply not specified so it's completely up to the ST to decide. But I would recommend this rule of thumb: Any category of powers that generally takes more than a turn to activate should be considered sorcery in this context. That means Mage spells, Ceremonies, Pack/Wolf Rites, and Obcasus Rites, but not Haunts, Gifts, or Atavisms/Nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-26T22:16:13-08:00","id":1437200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>viridian sun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1436258#post1436258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per VTR 2.0, &quot;At the end of a vampire\u2019s turn, after any reflexive healing, if her last (rightmost) Health box is filled with lethal damage, she falls to torpor. If she\u2019s in daysleep, and has no blood with which to awaken, she instead drifts into the torpor. As well, a vampire can voluntarily fall into torpor, to shake off the feeding limitations imposed by her Blood Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, I never read that close enough before - I always played it as you drop the second you fill your track up with lethal damage. But you get a full turn of action before you collapse eh?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T02:20:47-08:00","id":1437212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1437200#post1437200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damn, I never read that close enough before - I always played it as you drop the second you fill your track up with lethal damage. But you get a full turn of action before you collapse eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Healing up is reflexive. If, inside the same turn you fill out all your health boxes, you still have vitae to spend, yo can heal yourself up. <br /> <br /> E.g.: <br /> You are BP 5 vampire with 7 health fighting against a lonley and sad werewolf.<br /> The werewolf claws you for 16 bashing damages, which translate into 2 aggravated and 5 lethal damages. <br /> You can spend up to 5 vitae (although 1 would still be enough to save yourself from torpor), to heal up 5 lethal damages, ramaining at the end of this very turn, with only 2 aggravated damages.<br /> Let's say next turn the werewolf bites you for other 10 lethal damages (not bashing), as you only have 5 free health boxes, the 10 lethals are converted into 5 aggravated (for a total of 7 agg) which means you are destroyed as you cannot heal aggravated damages in a turn (you may only save yourself with Resilience).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 02-27-2021, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T03:59:11-08:00","id":1437220,"title":"","content":"We've always ignored that grace period because it can turn combat incredibly deadly. Beating someone to torpor (when a stake isn't at hand) is a good way to end a fight without killing the other part. But no one wants to go torpid at the hands of your enemies so anyone who has Vitae left to spend would want to heal at least one lethal damage to avoid torpor. That leads to them amassing more and more aggravated damage until they risk final death with another hit due to wrap around.<br /> In normal circumstances you'd try to surrender of flee before that but combat for Kindred tend to lead to Frenzy (if not started by someone Frenzying) and you can't change your goal during Frenzy, meaning anytime a Frenzying vampire is acting out of agression they'll continue until they've won (which doesn't necessarily mean killing the other part) or been beaten to torpor/death. Since the Frenzying vampire isn't allowed to act counter to their goal, allowing them to avoid torpor by healing during their turn means they'll always try to do that if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T19:29:09-08:00","id":1437313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1437220#post1437220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've always ignored that grace period because it can turn combat incredibly deadly. Beating someone to torpor (when a stake isn't at hand) is a good way to end a fight without killing the other part. But no one wants to go torpid at the hands of your enemies so anyone who has Vitae left to spend would want to heal at least one lethal damage to avoid torpor. That leads to them amassing more and more aggravated damage until they risk final death with another hit due to wrap around.<br /> In normal circumstances you'd try to surrender of flee before that but combat for Kindred tend to lead to Frenzy (if not started by someone Frenzying) and you can't change your goal during Frenzy, meaning anytime a Frenzying vampire is acting out of agression they'll continue until they've won (which doesn't necessarily mean killing the other part) or been beaten to torpor/death. Since the Frenzying vampire isn't allowed to act counter to their goal, allowing them to avoid torpor by healing during their turn means they'll always try to do that if possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I think the grace period works. It presents an interesting choice in combat for players - do I heal (or spend my blood on something else) now, or do I keep 1 vitae in reserve so that I can reflexively heal at the end of the turn and avoid torpor? Also, fights between Vampires should to some extent be battles of attrition. A Blood Potency 5 Vampire's main advantage over Blood Potency 1 is the larger pool of vitae and vitae per turn. Making them go torpid instantly when full of lethal negates this advantage to a certain extent - it makes it easy for a group of weak PCs to &quot;alpha strike&quot; a powerful NPC - taking them straight to full lethal in a single turn using celerity, willpower, blood buff, all-out attack and the like before the older Vampire can react.<br /> <br /> It feels right to me for a frenzying Vampire to just keep coming until their blood is exhausted. If you don't want to kill them for whatever reason, then it pays to be prepared - bring a stake or some restraints and a character who can reliably get the target in a grapple, or else be ready to fight very carefully. If all else fails, run away. I would also say that a kindred who is frenzying with the intent to murder other characters is likely to spend all their available blood towards that end (through Physical Intensity) rather than saving it for the purpose of healing.<br /> <br /> In many ways, beating an opponent into torpor is a much bigger victory than simply destroying them. They're now completely at your mercy - diablerie, burying your opponent in concrete, surgically removing their limbs, teeth, eyes etc. and then allowing them to wake from torpor - all of these are now on the table. With this in mind, it often makes sense for Vampires to fight to the last, welcoming final death over whatever else their attackers might have in store for them. On the other hand, a frenzing kindred who think that they might be treated leniently (e.g. if they're frenzying and attacking their coterie-mates) could spend the willpower to take control for a turn, opt <i>not </i>to heal, and therefore willingly put themselves into torpor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T21:50:58-08:00","id":1437325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1437212#post1437212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Healing up is reflexive. If, inside the same turn you fill out all your health boxes, you still have vitae to spend, yo can heal yourself up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I knew healing was reflexive, I just assumed that when your track filled with Lethal you were down.<br /> <br /> This is an interesting twist in that it makes Torpor more than just &quot;unconsciousness but for vampires&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T03:41:48-08:00","id":1437337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1437313#post1437313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I think the grace period works. It presents an interesting choice in combat for players - do I heal (or spend my blood on something else) now, or do I keep 1 vitae in reserve so that I can reflexively heal at the end of the turn and avoid torpor? Also, fights between Vampires should to some extent be battles of attrition. A Blood Potency 5 Vampire's main advantage over Blood Potency 1 is the larger pool of vitae and vitae per turn. Making them go torpid instantly when full of lethal negates this advantage to a certain extent - it makes it easy for a group of weak PCs to &amp;quot;alpha strike&amp;quot; a powerful NPC - taking them straight to full lethal in a single turn using celerity, willpower, blood buff, all-out attack and the like before the older Vampire can react.<br /> <br /> It feels right to me for a frenzying Vampire to just keep coming until their blood is exhausted. If you don't want to kill them for whatever reason, then it pays to be prepared - bring a stake or some restraints and a character who can reliably get the target in a grapple, or else be ready to fight very carefully. If all else fails, run away. I would also say that a kindred who is frenzying with the intent to murder other characters is likely to spend all their available blood towards that end (through Physical Intensity) rather than saving it for the purpose of healing.<br /> <br /> In many ways, beating an opponent into torpor is a much bigger victory than simply destroying them. They're now completely at your mercy - diablerie, burying your opponent in concrete, surgically removing their limbs, teeth, eyes etc. and then allowing them to wake from torpor - all of these are now on the table. With this in mind, it often makes sense for Vampires to fight to the last, welcoming final death over whatever else their attackers might have in store for them. On the other hand, a frenzing kindred who think that they might be treated leniently (e.g. if they're frenzying and attacking their coterie-mates) could spend the willpower to take control for a turn, opt <i>not </i>to heal, and therefore willingly put themselves into torpor</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the grace period is to the end of your own turn. Before your turn starts you have no reason to spend Vitae except for defensive purposes, and once your turn starts you're at almost no risk at taking an attack before it ends (basically only interrupts and counter attacks would pose a risk). That generally means you've either spent all Vitae per turn before your turn has even started (very unlikely above BP 1) or that you already know that you need to heal that last health box before you have any reason to spend your last Vitae on Physical Intensity or other offensive buffs.<br /> Funnily enough, a battle of attrition can very easily turn into the higher BP vampire's disadvantage because if they want to take advantage of their larger Vitae/turn and their much higher potential for force, they'll run out of Vitae much faster. (As long as no one's on Elder tier, I should add. The max Vitae pool starts adding up quick at BP 6+.)<br /> <br /> As for being at the mercy of your enemies, there's not much they can do to you that you can't recover from unless it's something that you simply won't wake up from (or immediately fall into torpor again from), which is a whole lot better than being assured you won't wake again up due to being dead.<br /> Besides, vampires generally don't meet where they're not observed by third parties (others at an Elysium, coterie mates, fellow Covenant members) because being one-on-one with another Kindred is deadly levels of stupid (considering the potential for violence and the multiple levels and types of mind control that are available). Rarely will anyone get away with doing anything to your torpid body without it being known to the whole domain within short.<br /> <br /> Good point about spending WP in Frenzy.<br /> But failing that, anyone who's winning against a vampire in Frenzy but without the means of restraining them still has no options if they can't subdue the vampire. It's either killing the opponent or fleeing a fight you're winning. And if ever two Kindred go Frenzy on each other, they're literally stuck in combat until one of them go down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T09:51:56-08:00","id":1437644,"title":"","content":"I have played with Lethal sending you to torpor immediately, and I'm planning to move to RAW soon. One thing htis ensures is, that people never consider whenever to fight or not, since the worst which will happen is torpor. Makes combat far less... risky, if the most you're doing to your opponent is torpor and you can't accidentally kill them. <br /> <br /> I'm imagining that people will be weary of fights, and conceding fights will become more common. Anyways,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-02T13:27:39-08:00","id":1437689,"title":"","content":"Well, this approach limits way too much the advantage of having high BP. I always had no issues with the standard rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T07:42:39-07:00","id":1440029,"title":"","content":"Quicken sight and aiming: &quot;...he can benefit from aiming instantly&quot;, does that mean the full maximum 3 dices bonus or only the first turn of aiming is applying in the same turn you use quicken sight?<br /> If aiming becomes reflexive while Quicken sight is active, I'd rather go for the 3 dices bonus, not sure though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T11:40:13-07:00","id":1440079,"title":"","content":"When you lose humanity to blood bond breaking point, can you take a Bane against it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-15T12:02:49-07:00","id":1440086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1440029#post1440029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quicken sight and aiming: &amp;quot;...he can benefit from aiming instantly&amp;quot;, does that mean the full maximum 3 dices bonus or only the first turn of aiming is applying in the same turn you use quicken sight?<br /> If aiming becomes reflexive while Quicken sight is active, I'd rather go for the 3 dices bonus, not sure though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes to the +3 bonus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-16T02:20:43-07:00","id":1440168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1440079#post1440079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you lose humanity to blood bond breaking point, can you take a Bane against it?</div> </div> </div> </div>So far the only Breaking Point that you can explicitly not take a Bane against is Diablerie.<br /> I think it would be legitimate to take a Bane against Breaking Points for harming your regent. The interesting question is whether you would need a different Bane for each step (i. e. a single Bane would not protect against going against your regent at every blood bond stage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T03:05:55-07:00","id":1440924,"title":"","content":"Ghouls have blood potency 0. Majesty Discipline 2: Electric Boogalo named Confidant gives its victims charmed condition, that expires after blood potency hours. <br /> Does that basically means that this discipline doesn't work when applied by a ghoul? Or does it mean that it can work for like a scene or some other smaller increment of time?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12764-zwinniak","name":"Zwinniak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T03:47:56-07:00","id":1440928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zwinniak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1440924#post1440924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls have blood potency 0. Majesty Discipline 2: Electric Boogalo named Confidant gives its victims charmed condition, that expires after blood potency hours.<br /> Does that basically means that this discipline doesn't work when applied by a ghoul? Or does it mean that it can work for like a scene or some other smaller increment of time?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it <b>stated </b>somewhere in the books ghouls have blood potency 0? Because though i'll admit to still tripping up in some 2e rules &amp; lore changes here and there, last i checked the term implies things like having a true blood pool and a bunch of other things ghouls were noteworthy for <b>not </b>possessing....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T04:02:26-07:00","id":1440930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1440928#post1440928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it <b>stated </b>somewhere in the books ghouls have blood potency 0? Because though i'll admit to still tripping up in some 2e rules &amp; lore changes here and there, last i checked the term implies things like having a true blood pool and a bunch of other things ghouls were noteworthy for <b>not </b>possessing....</div> </div> </div> </div>As per 297 of Vampire the Requiem 2ed in creating the ghoul:<br /> Blood Potency: Your character gains the Blood Potency trait at 0, allowing him to store and spend Vitae. This trait cannot be increased with Experiences or time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zwinniak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1440924#post1440924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls have blood potency 0. Majesty Discipline 2: Electric Boogalo named Confidant gives its victims charmed condition, that expires after blood potency hours.<br /> Does that basically means that this discipline doesn't work when applied by a ghoul? Or does it mean that it can work for like a scene or some other smaller increment of time?</div> </div> </div> </div>This question is also relevant to mortals on which the devotion &quot;The Wish&quot; was used. They recieve 3 levels of majesty where they have no blood potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12764-zwinniak","name":"Zwinniak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-22T06:21:18-07:00","id":1440938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zwinniak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1440930#post1440930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As per 297 of Vampire the Requiem 2ed in creating the ghoul:<br /> Blood Potency: Your character gains the Blood Potency trait at 0, allowing him to store and spend Vitae. This trait cannot be increased with Experiences or time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This question is also relevant to mortals on which the devotion &amp;quot;The Wish&amp;quot; was used. They recieve 3 levels of majesty where they have no blood potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's indeed a lack of the system in my opinion. I'd rule it work for a scene although I'm usually traying to not give Clan disciplines to Ghoul. But this is not a hard rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T11:11:35-07:00","id":1441783,"title":"","content":"Does recovery of Humanity come with any explicit conditions or prerequisites, or is it technically enough to spell the Experience?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T11:32:30-07:00","id":1441786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1441783#post1441783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does recovery of Humanity come with any explicit conditions or prerequisites, or is it technically enough to spell the Experience?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally I do not allow to buy humanity back without roleplaying it. But I don't think there are hard rules about that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T16:25:49-07:00","id":1441825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1441783#post1441783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does recovery of Humanity come with any explicit conditions or prerequisites, or is it technically enough to spell the Experience?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's up to your ST. If every Experience expenditure requires role-playing then it has to be roleplayed out. If your ST allows Experience expenditure between scenes, sessions or chronicles without role-playing the minutiae then it doesn't require being roleplayed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T17:38:53-07:00","id":1441833,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking as comparisons to Mage: the Awakening, which specifically requires a journey of contemplation before getting dots back. For vampires I kind of like the idea that the only thing keeping them from feeling more human again for a while is just not wanting to try enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-28T20:27:14-07:00","id":1441849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1441833#post1441833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking as comparisons to Mage: the Awakening, which specifically requires a journey of contemplation before getting dots back. For vampires I kind of like the idea that the only thing keeping them from feeling more human again for a while is just not wanting to try enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's about the size of it; Touchstones are where the main complication arises, because they're attached in descending order, getting new ones only requires buying another dot in the Merit, and replacing lost or dead ones requires buying Humanity back up.<br /> <br /> Humanity's comparatively cheap to buy, but it's relatively easy to lose once you've detached all your available Touchstones, and it's easier to cling to your latest significant relationship than scramble to keep the plates spinning at the higher levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T01:30:14-07:00","id":1441867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1441833#post1441833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking as comparisons to Mage: the Awakening, which specifically requires a journey of contemplation before getting dots back. For vampires I kind of like the idea that the only thing keeping them from feeling more human again for a while is just not wanting to try enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion is the other way around. Vampire aren't human any longer, so their normal status would rather be without humanity with the Beast taking over the control. Thus would rather be the vampire doing efforts to gather back pieces of lost humanity in an eternal struggle with the Beast (which is a metaphoric rather than real entity -as it was in Masquerade) which has the advantage of time and that everything get corrupted at some point, piece by piece.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T16:33:50-07:00","id":1441969,"title":"","content":"The reason Mage has a specific, onerous process you have to go through before buying Wisdom is because it\u2019s the game that most doesn\u2019t actually want you to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-29T18:15:08-07:00","id":1441986,"title":"","content":"Does the Blush of Life allow vampires to actually taste food and drink, or does it merely upgrade &quot;so disgusting you gag and spit it up immediately&quot; to bland?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1441969#post1441969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason Mage has a specific, onerous process you have to go through before buying Wisdom is because it\u2019s the game that most doesn\u2019t actually want you to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Acts of Hubris and the Conditions inflicted by failed rolls grant the Arcane Beats that are integral to buying it back, as does the very act of pursuing the necessary Obsession, as does going on adventures in its custom built &quot;literally go through a sojourn of discovery in your own soul and your connection to humanity and the universe&quot; corner of the setting. Also, using spells to inflict further Conditions on yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T01:38:38-07:00","id":1442016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1441969#post1441969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason Mage has a specific, onerous process you have to go through before buying Wisdom is because it\u2019s the game that most doesn\u2019t actually want you to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You very much are intended to buy up Wisdom if that's what you want for your character, and the games provides in-game mechanics for how to go about it since Wisdom is a stat that's relatively known in-game (even if not directly quantifiable by the characters). I actually like the concept of it.<br /> <br /> But I do think it's a badly implemented concept since most groups have very limited playing times and this forces some of that time to be dedicated to a thing only relevant to a single player who might not be that interested in playing it out in the first place. Not to mention that the time (on top of the XP) you invest into this can be nullified by a single roll the very next session if you're unlucky.<br /> When it comes to Humanity we do require the character to make an actual effort (just like how it works with Integrity) but that effort can either take place during a session if it's interesting, between sessions if it's not that interesting, or during downtime if we have a timeskip in the game. What makes Wisdom recovery bad is that you're forced into the first of these three options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-30-2021, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T17:31:04-07:00","id":1442108,"title":"","content":"Anyway, vampires eating, how does that work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T18:25:16-07:00","id":1442116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442108#post1442108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, vampires eating, how does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>how so? the act of eating like a cake? or the act of feeding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-30T20:43:58-07:00","id":1442129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442116#post1442116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how so? the act of eating like a cake? or the act of feeding?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were just asking if they can taste real food or drink.<br /> <br /> I don't know if there's a canon answer. I don't allow it, everything tasting like ash or dust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T04:46:54-07:00","id":1442163,"title":"","content":"I was imagining a Prince meeting some important human figure over tea, and wondering if that would be a case where he partakes just to be social or actually could get something out of it (even if blood is better and he would pay for it later).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T05:11:27-07:00","id":1442165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442163#post1442163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was imagining a Prince meeting some important human figure over tea, and wondering if that would be a case where he partakes just to be social or actually could get something out of it (even if blood is better and he would pay for it later).</div> </div> </div> </div>I allow to enjoy also the food under blush of life effect. But I can't recall any hard rule in that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T06:39:02-07:00","id":1442169,"title":"","content":"The sidebar on Solace mentions that &quot;the food has taste&quot; and the section on the Blush of Life's adjustments to its statement of &quot;Food and drink taste terrible, and immediately cause violent, bloody vomiting&quot; only specifies that you can keep it down until later in the night. The section on Humanity says that Humane Kindred &quot;remember the way food tasted.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd say that all aggregates to &quot;no.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T13:27:08-07:00","id":1442299,"title":"","content":"So, the implication I get from the settings chapter of the core book is that the five &quot;main&quot; Covenants are mostly just the ones that are really big in the Western world (with the likes of the Lancea et Sanctum and Ordo Dracul having some agendas to proselytize), and that other parts of the world have entirely different Covenants emerging from their cultural context which are just as big.<br /> <br /> Is that on the money? Is there a more direct reference to that in a later book? Or even in a part of the core which I've missed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T16:55:01-07:00","id":1442335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442299#post1442299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the implication I get from the settings chapter of the core book is that the five &quot;main&quot; Covenants are mostly just the ones that are really big in the Western world (with the likes of the Lancea et Sanctum and Ordo Dracul having some agendas to proselytize), and that other parts of the world have entirely different Covenants emerging from their cultural context which are just as big.<br /> <br /> Is that on the money? Is there a more direct reference to that in a later book? Or even in a part of the core which I've missed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is an interesting question with nebulous answers i'd guess.<br /> <br /> According to Rites of the Dragon, some of the first kindred Dracula met were a pair of turkish women of the Invictus that took over his castle and would learn more of the group by traveling to Adrianople, then ottoman capital. And the first time he heard about acolytes of the Crone was as &quot;a band of pagans <i>in the steppes who terrorized even the fearsome Tatars</i> and whose blasphemies against God had lured demons to give them worldly power&quot;, so it also depends on one's definition of &quot;Western world&quot; one might say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-01-2021, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T17:21:22-07:00","id":1442340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442335#post1442335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is an interesting question with nebulous answers i'd guess.<br /> <br /> According to Rites of the Dragon, some of the first kindred Dracula met were a pair of turkish women of the Invictus that took over his castle and would learn more of the group by traveling to Adrianople, then ottoman capital. And the first time he heard about acolytes of the Crone was as &quot;a band of pagans <i>in the steppes who terrorized even the fearsome Tatars</i> and whose blasphemies against God had lured demons to give them worldly power&quot;, so it also depends on one's definition of &quot;Western world&quot; one might say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though that information might be superseded a bit when we've got descriptions of covenants in Kindred Beijing with names such as Bureaus of Childer and Silence and they've got two covenants influenced by Rites of the Dragon but are not properly part of the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> That said, the point about the global West is well made when I had forgotten how Athens is stated to be home to numerous uniquely Greek Covenants (such as the combination Appolonian-Byzantine Christian cult) in addition to the Circle, Lancea and Ordo, with no mention of Invictus or Carthians. Or how in Berlin, a covenant from the communist half of the city absorbed most of the Carthians upon unification. It kind of seems like only North American cities are presented as having the vanilla Covenants.<br /> <br /> I suppose what I'm getting at is that while I find this presentation extremely intriguing and inviting for world building purposes, I'm a tad frustrated that the book's overall presentation precludes having set it up or giving it context. At least as far as I can tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T17:35:25-07:00","id":1442342,"title":"","content":"I think you would use the trappings of the main 5 to fill out any other type of covenant.That Appolonian-Byzantine cult might be able to use Theban Sorcery but doesn't have the same type of deep seated cathoclism that the Lancea have. They still are a cult that uses some christian trappings and can use some of the same merits that the Lancea can use but are not the Lancea.<br /> <br /> I guess what I am getting at is that you can use the main 5 covenants and file the serial numbers off and can be used to make Covenants outside the western world. Or you can mix and match different aspects to make a Covenant that isn't western based.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T17:42:15-07:00","id":1442343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442340#post1442340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though that information might be superseded a bit when we've got descriptions of covenants in Kindred Beijing with names such as Bureaus of Childer and Silence and they've got two covenants influenced by Rites of the Dragon but are not properly part of the Ordo Dracul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uncertain. There being a presence of the &quot;core five&quot; in places beyond the Americas or Western Europe does not on itself preclude the existence of other covenants as local, regional or continental powers. Who's to say the Circle of Crone does not draw support from undead patrons of a thousand sects across eastern asia, africa, oceania and parts of south &amp; central americas?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442340#post1442340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the point about the global West is well made when I had forgotten how Athens is stated to be home to numerous uniquely Greek Covenants (such as the combination Appolonian-Byzantine Christian cult) in addition to the Circle, Lancea and Ordo, with no mention of Invictus or Carthians. Or how in Berlin, a covenant from the communist half of the city absorbed most of the Carthians upon unification. It kind of seems like only North American cities are presented as having the vanilla Covenants.<br /> <br /> I suppose what I'm getting at is that while I find this presentation extremely intriguing and inviting for world building purposes, I'm a tad frustrated that the book's overall presentation precludes having set it up or giving it context. At least as far as I can tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few years ago i shared ST duties in a game centered on Rio de Janeiro, a city that (in our fragmented, personal, patchwork take of its history) while dominated by disputes between Crone, Sanctfied and to a lesser degree dragons, has, much to the chagrin of both religious covenants, a quite thriving underground of shadow cults &amp; bloodlines of a syncretic character where sometimes the teaching of Cruac, Theban Sorcery and stranger things will mix and meld in a strange melange of manners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-07-2021, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-01T19:14:36-07:00","id":1442347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442299#post1442299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the implication I get from the settings chapter of the core book is that the five &quot;main&quot; Covenants are mostly just the ones that are really big in the Western world (with the likes of the Lancea et Sanctum and Ordo Dracul having some agendas to proselytize), and that other parts of the world have entirely different Covenants emerging from their cultural context which are just as big.<br /> <br /> Is that on the money? Is there a more direct reference to that in a later book? Or even in a part of the core which I've missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on who you ask and when you ask you're going to get answers that vary quite q bit because the role of the main five Covenants have been developed and reinterpreted several times by various devs and writers during the production of VtR and both of its editions.<br /> They were created as five archetypal organisations that could be applied literally anywhere without necessarily having anything to do with their equivalents in other domains. Then the Covenant books introduced the concept of local/regional variations within the Covenants while also cementing them as discrete organisations with histories. Later first edition supplements and various Dark Eras for second edition expand upon their origins as well as describing preceeding Covenants, which heavily informs how they could have spread (though with modern travel and communication it's become much easier to spread them further, potentially globally). <br /> How other Covenants relate to the main five still varies quite dramatically. Sometimes they're basically carbon copies with a cultural twist (closely following the idea of the five main Covenants as archetypes) while others are completely new with their own ideologies, roles and advantages.<br /> <br /> What can be said for sure is that the big five originated in Europe and naturally spread to the Americas, and that other regions (and earlier historical periods) have/had their own Covenants. But in modern times when the main five can spread much easier it's fully up to the creator of the setting (be it a writer for a supplement or the ST of a campaign) to either create whole new Covenants, use the main five as blueprints, and/or just straight up use the main five. All approaches are supported.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T20:59:27-07:00","id":1442800,"title":"","content":"What happens to someone suffering the Soul Loss condition if they get Embraced?<br /> Also, since it's possible to posthumous Embrace someone, is the soul a necessity for the Embrace to happen in the first place?<br /> Final question, what happens to the Soul (the disembodied one) after the Embrace?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T22:33:52-07:00","id":1442803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442800#post1442800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to someone suffering the Soul Loss condition if they get Embraced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming it takes, they've traded a theoretically reversible condition for a largely irreversible one.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, since it's possible to posthumous Embrace someone, is the soul a necessity for the Embrace to happen in the first place? </div> </div> </div>Open question, but probably not. Vampires have souls as the setting's primary experts on souls recognize them, blood can do a lot in this horror setting, starting Humanity explicitly doesn't map to former Integrity, and the Strix can Synthesize a corpse into a Kindred vampire that does possess Humanity.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Final question, what happens to the Soul (the disembodied one) after the Embrace? </div> </div> </div>Whatever is most interesting for your game. Normally it's gone at the moment of death, which doesn't seem to stop post-mortem Embraces from producing largely normal vampires who have souls that can be stolen by Tremere or consumed through diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T01:51:52-07:00","id":1442815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442800#post1442800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to someone suffering the Soul Loss condition if they get Embraced?<br /> Also, since it's possible to posthumous Embrace someone, is the soul a necessity for the Embrace to happen in the first place?<br /> Final question, what happens to the Soul (the disembodied one) after the Embrace?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Tremere doesn't say vampires have souls. Tremere says vampires have something which fills the same functions as a soul, but unlike mortals, mages and deviants, they do not call it a soul.<br /> The mention of deviants is especially noteworthy in this. The sidebar in Nameless &amp; Accursed is written to explain what Tremere could feed on so it would be easy to assume it would either call everything the Tremere could feed on souls, or everything they could feed on that aren't mortal/Awakened souls (since those two are special for ideological reasons) functional substitutes. Instead, vampires have functional substitutes the Tremere can feed on while deviants have actual souls but so broken they <i>can't</i> be fed on, strongly implying that whatever vampires have is the soul twisted to being unrecognisable (moreso than the souls of deviants), or they gain something else entirely.<br /> <br /> Considering that killing the victim is the first step of the Embrace (feeding the corpse some Vitae being the second) as well as the prevalence of Posthumous Embraces (i.e. where the second step simply takes place after some time, I've always argued that vampires don't have souls. With the news in Nameless &amp; Accursed I revised this stance to assume that whatever they have is not the original soul transformed by the Embrace but something new. Hence, Embracing someone without a soul should be completely possible.<br /> <br /> But as a last note I want to add that, while I'm pretty sure my interpretation on CofD soul metaphysics is the most reasonable interpretation, it's all still based on information from MtA rather than what makes for an interesting VtR game, and thus it's only relevant in your game if you're highly invested in adhereing closely to the &quot;canon setting&quot; as much as CofD can be said to have one. In our current vampire game the soul is absolutely necessary for the Embrace because it provides &quot;fuel&quot; for the transformation and the development of the first dot of Blood Potency. Someone who's soulless would probably become a Revenant or possibly even a larval if they can get Embraced at all. (The soul is also what transforms into ghosts in our game, which is absolutely not how it works in CofD as GtSE is quite explicit about. Hence a human can either leave a ghost or be Embraced, but not both barring exceptional circumstances.)<br /> What I mean is, fuck the canon unlesd you're just theorycrafting, and do what's best for your game.<br /> <br /> Edit: Almost forgot about diablerie. The thing is, the fluff around diablerie is written fully from the perspective of the characters. It says <i>diablerists</i> are convinced of the existence of the soul, but the truth is that the effects of the diablerie doesn't really align with what is known about souls in general. Maybe diablerie is the consumption of the vampire's soul substitue (see N&amp;A), or maybe it's something else entirely. I mean the primary effect is getting special XP based on Blood Potency and a Discipline dot. The equivalents of a mage would be Gnosis and Arcana, neither of which is part of their souls. The soul is necessary for using the Arcana, but pop in a human's soul and the mage will still regain their original powers. If the same is true for vampires (about where the BP/Disciplines are located, I mean, not the part about popping in a human soul although that is an interesting question), then you'd be able to perform diablerie on soulless (or soul-equivalent-less) vampires (perhaps after a Tremere has stolen it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-06-2021, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T07:16:18-07:00","id":1442833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442815#post1442815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that Tremere doesn't say vampires have souls. Tremere says vampires have something which fills the same functions as a soul, but unlike mortals, mages and deviants, they do not call it a soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this from somewhere other than Nameless and Accursed? I can't find anything making a distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T09:37:23-07:00","id":1442851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1442833#post1442833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this from somewhere other than Nameless and Accursed? I can't find anything making a distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot. Dave Brookshaw wrote a whole list on Discord, but the wording in N&amp;A is completely different.<br /> Here's the post (if I can get this to work on this forum):<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/cm1mOcE.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T17:07:44-07:00","id":1443190,"title":"","content":"Does a souless person still produces Vitae normally for Kindred?<br /> I'm asking because for a Strix, a Souless person does not produces Vitae from Breath Drinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":7210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","user":"Horodrigo","date":". 04-08-2021, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T17:21:15-07:00","id":1443196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1443190#post1443190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does a souless person still produces Vitae normally for Kindred?<br /> I'm asking because for a Strix, a Souless person does not produces Vitae from Breath Drinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say so, given the other differences between blood-bound Vitae and the stuff the Strix are made of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T00:22:51-07:00","id":1443221,"title":"","content":"I'd say no because both Kindred and Strix drain Vitae that is interchangible for all purposes where its medium isn't relevant (i.e. non-blood Vitae can't be spillt; this logistical difficulty is shared with ghouls who have blood Vitae but no means of spilling it themselves). I assume that since both fuel traits share the exact same name and are used for the same stuff at the same rates, etc, actually is the same stuff, and the text about blood Vitae is pretty clear that the blood is only a medium for the Vitae rather than being what Vitae consists of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T02:21:44-07:00","id":1443230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1443221#post1443221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say no because both Kindred and Strix drain Vitae that is interchangible for all purposes where its medium isn't relevant (i.e. non-blood Vitae can't be spillt; this logistical difficulty is shared with ghouls who have blood Vitae but no means of spilling it themselves). I assume that since both fuel traits share the exact same name and are used for the same stuff at the same rates, etc, actually is the same stuff, and the text about blood Vitae is pretty clear that the blood is only a medium for the Vitae rather than being what Vitae consists of.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this way, it would also explain why blood created with magic and powers is inert.<br /> Probably the vitae sacrificed for cruac rites is turned into this kind of &quot;soulless&quot; blood in the aftermath","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T16:27:30-07:00","id":1443532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1443221#post1443221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say no because both Kindred and Strix drain Vitae that is interchangible for all purposes where its medium isn't relevant (i.e. non-blood Vitae can't be spillt; this logistical difficulty is shared with ghouls who have blood Vitae but no means of spilling it themselves).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would view the limits of Strix Vitae in Cr\u00faac as an indicator of ways in which they are not interchangeable; that if there's a difference based on how they can exit the corpus, there can also be a difference based in how it enters. The lack of a soul fails to produce the particular kind of vital breath that the Strix convert into Vitae, but the gratifying sensation of warm blood straight from the vein suffusing the undead tissues is a converter for the vampire.<br /> <br /> I would see this as a dichotomy that reflects their distinct natures; the Strix is a more insubstantial being and feeds through a more ephemeral medium, while the Kindred are distinctly, viscerally physical, and the physical is what their Beast engages with. I'd see that in the references to the physical sensations and motions underlying a lot of what vampires do supernaturally, as well as how the Strix that embodies itself in something physical switches over to the physical diet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T18:06:54-07:00","id":1443544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1443532#post1443532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would view the limits of Strix Vitae in Cr\u00faac as an indicator of ways in which they are not interchangeable; that if there's a difference based on how they can exit the corpus, there can also be a difference based in how it enters. The lack of a soul fails to produce the particular kind of vital breath that the Strix convert into Vitae, but the gratifying sensation of warm blood straight from the vein suffusing the undead tissues is a converter for the vampire.<br /> <br /> I would see this as a dichotomy that reflects their distinct natures; the Strix is a more insubstantial being and feeds through a more ephemeral medium, while the Kindred are distinctly, viscerally physical, and the physical is what their Beast engages with. I'd see that in the references to the physical sensations and motions underlying a lot of what vampires do supernaturally, as well as how the Strix that embodies itself in something physical switches over to the physical diet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also worth pointing out: Within the text of Vampire, the Strix are the only source of the Soulless Condition, and through a power that lets them create Vitae-generating phylacteries, at that.<br /> <br /> &quot;Soulless victims produce no Vitae&quot; is firmly contained within the sidebar on the Breath Drinking move, rather than in the sidebar on the Feed move or in the text of the Soulless Condition (which, despite the only source of the Condition in the book being restricted to living mortal targets, <i>does</i> have altered text relevant to Vampire), and Unnatural Affinity outright names several things that don't have souls as viable subjects whose only complication is managing to feed on them.<br /> <br /> Stored blood and animal blood are thinner fare and hard to stomach at higher Blood Potency, but they <i>are</i> technically always viable sources of Vitae for Kindred, and the Strix reject Humanity and outright don't have feeding restrictions otherwise and hail from stranger spheres than vampires of mortal stock, so there's pretty strong odds for Blood-based Vitae being able to cobble together a semblance of a mortal-adjacent soul through the Embrace being an extension of a generally more worldly-connected medium for vital essence compared to the soul-harvesting smoke-monsters that give rise to the undead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T08:24:41-07:00","id":1443748,"title":"","content":"Hey, if a vampire is standing somewhere out in the open where it would be death for them to fall asleep, do they even need to make a roll to stay awake? Or do they just get to remain alert by default, but forfeiting the potential to roll the exceptional success that would allow them to operate during the day without being Lethargic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T10:24:28-07:00","id":1443756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1443748#post1443748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, if a vampire is standing somewhere out in the open where it would be death for them to fall asleep, do they even need to make a roll to stay awake? Or do they just get to remain alert by default, but forfeiting the potential to roll the exceptional success that would allow them to operate during the day without being Lethargic?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do need to roll eventually rolling to wake up in case of danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T02:46:23-07:00","id":1444315,"title":"","content":"So, who really Donovan &quot;Gage&quot; from New Orleans setting is?<br /> Gage is his &quot;secret&quot; false surname which was hiding his real, uncanny, surname. <br /> Any idea, official or even unofficial, about that topic?<br /> <br /> How could his darkest secret be kept as such in front of a simple Auspex 2 question: what's his deepest secret?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-17-2021, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T07:11:08-07:00","id":1444326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1444315#post1444315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, who really Donovan &quot;Gage&quot; from New Orleans setting is?<br /> Gage is his &quot;secret&quot; false surname which was hiding his real, uncanny, surname.<br /> Any idea, official or even unofficial, about that topic?<br /> <br /> How could his darkest secret be kept as such in front of a simple Auspex 2 question: what's his deepest secret?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's complicated. AFAIK, whoever came up with that plot thread in NO didn't leave us much in the way of clues about his &quot;true&quot; identity - supposing the writer even though of one and the whole point wasn't for a ST to insert whoever he or she felt might be interesting for one's specific chronicle.<br /> <br /> To boot, it's a 1e book, when Auspex 2 worked different and wasn't something that could insta-pop this like a balloon.<br /> So, in all honesty, no real idea of answers nor if it's worth the effort to adapting it to a 2e game in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T07:11:53-07:00","id":1444327,"title":"","content":"He was supposedly John Wilkes Booth. His dark secret was that, despite appearances, he was really not a devout adherent to Vidal's perverse interpretation of the Sanctified as Roman Catholicism for undead bloodsuckers and STs should probably manufacture specifics. However, why that constitutes a &quot;dark secret&quot; is beyond me since none of the listed Sanctified NPCs were truly devout to the idea of post mortem Roman Catholicism or the concept of vampires being chosen by God to test humanity's faith, up to and including Vidal. <br /> <br /> It's rather easy to hide any &quot;deepest secret&quot; from Auspex mind rapists. Simply say Dominate was used to remove or alter the specifics from his memory with a big middle finger to Auspex users that Donovan &quot;knows&quot; it was removed or changed and doesn't care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-18-2021, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T13:36:03-07:00","id":1444540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1444326#post1444326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To boot, it's a 1e book, when Auspex 2 worked different and wasn't something that could insta-pop this like a balloon.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So, in all honesty, no real idea of answers nor if it's worth the effort to adapting it to a 2e game in the first place.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, I do think Second Edition does lean more into the idea that vampires are less likely to meet with one another in person (and you have to be looking at the subject to use it), and using Auspex on another vampire in Elysium seems like it should be a significant faux pas.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Besides that, I think it's reasonable to say that when vampires are aware of the existence of a fairly basic power to uncover their secrets, somebody with a secret that they're dead set on keeping might develop a Devotion capable of contesting or deceiving Uncanny Perception and similar powers (presuming none of the sample Devotions do so already).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1444327#post1444327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's rather easy to hide any &quot;deepest secret&quot; from Auspex mind rapists. Simply say Dominate was used to remove or alter the specifics from his memory with a big middle finger to Auspex users that Donovan &quot;knows&quot; it was removed or changed and doesn't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside a term I think should be retired in this day and age, I don't think this idea would work against the power as written. Uncanny Perception doesn't seem to be based on mind reading, but on a more extrasensory level. I mean, an example is given of how it can detect a subject being under the control of another, that's probably not often a thing they're consciously aware of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T14:51:17-07:00","id":1444552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1444540#post1444540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, I do think Second Edition does lean more into the idea that vampires are less likely to meet with one another in person (and you have to be looking at the subject to use it), and using Auspex on another vampire in Elysium seems like it should be a significant faux pas.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Besides that, I think it's reasonable to say that when vampires are aware of the existence of a fairly basic power to uncover their secrets, somebody with a secret that they're dead set on keeping might develop a Devotion capable of contesting or deceiving Uncanny Perception and similar powers (presuming none of the sample Devotions do so already).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>True on all aspects, but the real question, at least in my point of view - is the (undefined/undeveloped) plot hook of Donovan Gage's true identity/dark secret worth the effort of updating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T06:35:34-07:00","id":1444819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1444552#post1444552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True on all aspects, but the real question, at least in my point of view - is the (undefined/undeveloped) plot hook of Donovan Gage's true identity/dark secret worth the effort of updating?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if your players would actually care. Donovan being the highest on the list of who takes over from Vidal might make it worthwhile finding his dark secret, but if its just he was JWB, who cares...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T08:11:07-07:00","id":1444827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1444819#post1444819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if your players would actually care. Donovan being the highest on the list of who takes over from Vidal might make it worthwhile finding his dark secret, but if its just he was JWB, who cares...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's partly my issue - &quot;Donovan has a big, bad secret&quot; - well, <b><i>what kindred doesn't</i></b>, so it's pretty much a non-issue as a hook, on itself sparks nothing.<br /> About <i>his mortal identity</i> being a big, bad secret - at first brush it sparks some curiosity &quot;ok, what could be so weird about his mortal past that might bother other kindred and damage his status if revealed?&quot;<br /> <br /> But then comes the matter of there being <i>almost nothing</i> on that identity or <b><i>why would kindred care</i></b>, meaning <i>the ST has to do the grunt work of fleshing it out</i> for it to start being useful in the first place. And then worry about setting x gameplay issues related to cross-edition changes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally too much of a hassle imho - specially considering far more juicy bits like <b><i>how did <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane_Katrina\" target=\"_blank\">Katrina</a> (or the much more recent <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane_Harvey\" target=\"_blank\">Harvey</a>) and the rebuilding process in the years since, affect the local balance of power</i></b> to consider - but then i have barely touched NO: City of Damned in more than a decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-20-2021, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T05:14:28-07:00","id":1445024,"title":"","content":"cool topic! it's good that you created it! found many answers useful for myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26776-cornelgo","name":"cornelGo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T07:39:49-07:00","id":1445819,"title":"","content":"Can a grappled Kindred use Protean 1 to merge with the ground and escape the grapple?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T08:39:02-07:00","id":1445826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1445819#post1445819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a grappled Kindred use Protean 1 to merge with the ground and escape the grapple?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say no as you are litterally between your opponent hands. Other than that, I'd allow to use discipline (which requieres an action) only if you are owning the edge in the grapple in that turn. This is true also for Dominate. Otherwise Mental's disciplines become too strong in my opinion. <br /> I might allow, maybe, to use Majesty (which does not require eyes contact) and Protean 5, only if the PC declares to not fight back for the grapple advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T23:30:42-07:00","id":1445935,"title":"","content":"It might be worth borrowing mage's rule for casting in a grapple for other powers that don't require hand movements or something similarly impossible. Which is to say, if it needs a roll, it's done at a -3 penalty if you lost the grapple roll.<br /> <br /> I'd allow Protean 1 so long as they're already touching the surface, myself. Not needing a roll, you'd be able to use it either way.<br /> <br /> Reflexive stuff, of course, should always be available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-26T15:34:52-07:00","id":1445997,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know who was Prince before Maxwell was the first time in Chicago by Night? I can only find references to Maxwell and the Matriarch and not much about Chicago before 1965 or so.<br /> <br /> I could do a detailed re-read myself, but my guess is that if the information is in there someone in here already knows it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T16:51:46-07:00","id":1446521,"title":"","content":"Question: If the Carthians use Mandate of the Masses and the vampire they target with it is possessed by a Strix, what happens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T06:53:18-07:00","id":1446594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1446521#post1446521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: If the Carthians use Mandate of the Masses and the vampire they target with it is possessed by a Strix, what happens?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Laughs in yellow eyes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, I think that the Kindred still suffers the consequences, but the Strix will probably be unharmed. But the problems of low Blood Potency will probably be a minor nuisance for the Strix if she was using this Kindred because of the high Blood Potency. I think that the Strix can use a Draurg just fine, but just because I don't remember any special ruling for Draurgs possessed by Strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T00:59:56-07:00","id":1447367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1444827#post1444827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's partly my issue - &quot;Donovan has a big, bad secret&quot; - well, <b><i>what kindred doesn't</i></b>, so it's pretty much a non-issue as a hook, on itself sparks nothing.<br /> About <i>his mortal identity</i> being a big, bad secret - at first brush it sparks some curiosity &quot;ok, what could be so weird about his mortal past that might bother other kindred and damage his status if revealed?&quot;<br /> <br /> But then comes the matter of there being <i>almost nothing</i> on that identity or <b><i>why would kindred care</i></b>, meaning <i>the ST has to do the grunt work of fleshing it out</i> for it to start being useful in the first place. And then worry about setting x gameplay issues related to cross-edition changes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally too much of a hassle imho - specially considering far more juicy bits like <b><i>how did <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane_Katrina\" target=\"_blank\">Katrina</a> (or the much more recent <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane_Harvey\" target=\"_blank\">Harvey</a>) and the rebuilding process in the years since, affect the local balance of power</i></b> to consider - but then i have barely touched NO: City of Damned in more than a decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a lot of this in nwod or chronicles. Another example is the Secret Accord in Mages Boston's book. I wish they would just reveal the mysteries/secrets and then I can just ignore them if I come up with something better rather than not describing them and making me do all the work when i have no idea what the original writer was intending","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T06:24:18-07:00","id":1447394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447367#post1447367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a lot of this in nwod or chronicles. Another example is the Secret Accord in Mages Boston's book. I wish they would just reveal the mysteries/secrets and then I can just ignore them if I come up with something better rather than not describing them and making me do all the work when i have no idea what the original writer was intending</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Though i can definitely relate to the issue of the occasional hook that on itself is a little too vague to spark inspiration on the ST, must admit that i never paid much attention to the Accord. The one thing i got serious milleage of in Mage's Boston book was the Prince of 10.000 Leaves, connecting Wicked Dead's ghouls with them among other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-04-2021, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T13:48:17-07:00","id":1447442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447367#post1447367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a lot of this in nwod or chronicles. Another example is the Secret Accord in Mages Boston's book. I wish they would just reveal the mysteries/secrets and then I can just ignore them if I come up with something better rather than not describing them and making me do all the work when i have no idea what the original writer was intending</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do not rule out the possibility that there <i>is no intended secret</i>. The writer may have just been like &quot;here's a cool plot thread to fill in&quot; and not actually have anything they firmly intended.<br /> <br /> I strongly suspect that's the case with the Nameless in the Montreal setting for Requiem, for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T14:38:24-07:00","id":1447448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447442#post1447442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do not rule out the possibility that there <i>is no intended secret</i>. The writer may have just been like &amp;quot;here's a cool plot thread to fill in&amp;quot; and not actually have anything they firmly intended.<br /> <br /> I strongly suspect that's the case with the Nameless in the Montreal setting for Requiem, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could invent a &quot;cool&quot; plot for whatever NPC in the setting without wirter pointing me out a specific character with no further details. If I pay for a premade setting I'd like a bit more tips. Then up to me whether use them as they are, modify them or ignore these at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T14:53:03-07:00","id":1447452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447442#post1447442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do not rule out the possibility that there <i>is no intended secret</i>. The writer may have just been like &quot;here's a cool plot thread to fill in&quot; and not actually have anything they firmly intended.<br /> <br /> I strongly suspect that's the case with the Nameless in the Montreal setting for Requiem, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sometimes you don't need answers per se, as long as there's enough detail and specifity to paint a vibrant image that a ST can improvise its own crazy from.<br /> Unfortunately some hooks are more generic and perfunctory or unfinished in presentation than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T16:12:45-07:00","id":1447478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447442#post1447442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not rule out the possibility that there <i>is no intended secret</i>. The writer may have just been like &quot;here's a cool plot thread to fill in&quot; and not actually have anything they firmly intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as the one guy who knows the full contents of the Secret Concord is a signature character with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/509469-boston-unveiled-what-have-you-done-with-it?p=521804#post521804\">a narrative threading across multiple books</a>, I don't think that's one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I strongly suspect that's the case with the Nameless in the Montreal setting for Requiem, for instance. </div> </div> </div>You suspect wrong, unless Liv was fucking with us <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76737#post76737\">seven years ago on these very forums</a> when the Nameless was less than two years new.<br /> <br /> <br /> It may never go to print, but storyhooks bigger than a single bullet point in a sidebar <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1046759-the-flayer-insatiable?p=1047085#post1047085\">tend to be written with something in mind</a>, as I can assure you from spending the last three years sporadically trying to pin down a mystery-figure for my own setting well enough to drop hints in power descriptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T23:35:42-07:00","id":1447528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447478#post1447478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You suspect wrong, unless Liv was fucking with us <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/36324-tell-me-about-your-nameless?p=76737#post76737&amp;quot;]seven</a> years ago on these very forums[/URL] when the Nameless was less than two years new.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that whole thread <i>is</i> Olivia just fucking with the fans. I get your point that she probably did have something more specific in mind for the Nameless, but she's also upfront about not caring to reveal it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like, I get that a mystery can excite fans and possibly even generate some buzz draw in more people, but as a gaming resource it's just as good or bad as a plot hook without any underlying thoughts. Sometimes that's enough to get the creative juices flowing, but often it's just a ton of work for the ST to come up with content that fits both this mysterious frame <i>and</i> the game they're running.<br /> To paraphrase a coplayer of mine: Coming up with cool plot hooks is the easy part. I can do that myself. If I buy a book that contains setting materials I expect actually useable setting materials, not just questions that takes as much time and effort to fill in as a campaign setting I planned from scratch.<br /> That's almost exactly what Marcus said above so it's hardly a unique sentiment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T02:32:30-07:00","id":1447552,"title":"","content":"What's considered a magical effect as per the Sorcerous Eunuch merit? Are disciplines magical effects? Werewolf gifts/rites? Supernal magic? Depending on interpretation, this merit is either really very extra good, or just decent, and I'm not entirely sure what was intended with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T04:27:52-07:00","id":1447560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447552#post1447552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's considered a magical effect as per the Sorcerous Eunuch merit? Are disciplines magical effects? Werewolf gifts/rites? Supernal magic? Depending on interpretation, this merit is either really very extra good, or just decent, and I'm not entirely sure what was intended with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been discussed a few times. The consensus is that among vampiric powers it's definitely only Blood Sorcery that is affected, hence why Blood Sorcery specifically can't be used by the character.<br /> <br /> It's less clear about other games since each game is designed primarily for itself with mostly just the system allowing for crossovers. Anyway, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1436885\">here's</a> my unofficial rule of thumb:<br /> &quot;Any category of powers that generally takes more than a turn to activate should be considered sorcery in this context. That means Mage spells, Ceremonies, Pack/Wolf Rites, and Obcasus Rites, but not Haunts, Gifts, or Atavisms/Nightmares.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:13:49-07:00","id":1447640,"title":"","content":"What does the Divination/Destruction/Transmutation/etc signify for the Blood Sorcery in the Secrets of the Covenants book? I couldn't find anything about it elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:25:18-07:00","id":1447641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447640#post1447640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the Divination/Destruction/Transmutation/etc signify for the Blood Sorcery in the Secrets of the Covenants book? I couldn't find anything about it elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>A separate \u201c1.5 edition\u201d book, called Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies, detailed Blood Sorcery as \u2018free-form\u2019 magic. I think it came from there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:37:50-07:00","id":1447644,"title":"","content":"It's a late first edition book but still first edition. The second edition corebook has a small sidebar about using the themes from BS:S&amp;B in second edition as an optional rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:39:13-07:00","id":1447645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447641#post1447641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A separate \u201c1.5 edition\u201d book, called Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies, detailed Blood Sorcery as \u2018free-form\u2019 magic. I think it came from there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup! It's <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a>. One of my favourite books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:43:34-07:00","id":1447647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447394#post1447394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Though i can definitely relate to the issue of the occasional hook that on itself is a little too vague to spark inspiration on the ST, must admit that i never paid much attention to the Accord. The one thing i got serious milleage of in Mage's Boston book was the Prince of 10.000 Leaves, connecting Wicked Dead's ghouls with them among other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too connected the Prince to Wicked deads Ghuls wasn't it? I made them the actual residents of the princes' dimension (minor nobility being cannibals) and they swapped places with anybody devoured at the main temple. Bringing the ghul to this world where the red world cult revered them and started slowly kidnapping important people and replacing them with Ghul clones. (most of the time the devoured person just vanished as normal, but if there was a double in the abyss then it could come over once the soul of the original/whatever was gone) Also abused the Vampire/Spirit rider people blood tenebrous figuring in the world of the prince, carrion or cannibal spirits would use vampires as sock puppets. Vampires who committed diablerie being royalty in the prince timeline others being just above mortals. Allowed one of the kings of the princes realm to power up and reach his final form as a spirit-possessed vampire badass vs mages with White phos and portals/bans and whatever, it didn't go well even with all that lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-05-2021, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T16:46:47-07:00","id":1447658,"title":"","content":"Feral Infection questions:<br /> <br /> If the vampire doesn't specify a target (or a supernatural victim spends willpower to ignore such), &quot;her victims turn upon one another&quot;. Does this mean that the frenzied creatures will only attack other people who have been affected by the power? Will they <i>not</i> attack the vampire who used the power(since they are not one of the &quot;victims&quot;)? What happens when there's only one person left who is affected by the power(or only one person failed their resistance roll)? Do they come out of frenzy? Or do they attack other non-frenzied people in the vicinity?<br /> <br /> What does the beast &quot;want&quot; during the Feral Infection frenzy? I'm assuming &quot;attack other victims&quot;? How far will they go in that attack - just beat people unconscious? Kill them? Feed upon their flesh like the animals affected do?<br /> <br /> Am I correct in assuming Indomitable would probably add its bonus to the pool to resist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T06:27:45-07:00","id":1447708,"title":"","content":"I would allow Indomitable to be used to resist Feral Infection.<br /> <br /> As far as the user not giving any directions... I have the infected destroy anything that that has the user's blood, then turn on non infected, ignoring the user's ghouls or undead familiar(s) - seeing them as fellow infected, then turn on each other for the duration. Animals kill and eat. Other sentient beings would just kill and move to the next target, going on to hacking corpses if there's nothing to kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-06-2021, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T07:09:50-07:00","id":1447709,"title":"","content":"Not sure what do you mean with: &quot;...anything that has user's blood&quot;. If I'm not wrong people only need to smell the blood spilled out on the ground to be affected by the power.<br /> <br /> I rule Feral Infection as a riot (much more &quot;feral&quot; though): anyone affected, if not directed through someone specific, is being destroying the most close to him, either he's afflicted by the same power or not.<br /> <br /> People affected by the power lash out to their primitive and most violent instincts and they should not care if whoever is around them is in the same mood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 05-06-2021, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T07:37:26-07:00","id":1447711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447709#post1447709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what do you mean with: &amp;quot;...anything that has user's blood&amp;quot;. If I'm not wrong people only need to smell the blood spilled out on the ground to be affected by the power.<br /> <br /> I rule Feral Infection has a riot (much more &amp;quot;feral&amp;quot; though): anyone affected, if not directed through someone specific, is being destroying the most close to him, either he's afflicted by the same power or not.<br /> <br /> People affected by the power lash out to their primitive and most violent instincts and they should not care if whoever is around them is in the same mood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and if they're affected by the power and aren't directed against a target, they're going to destroy or shred the object or section of ground where the blood was spilled. <br /> <br /> One of my characters flung some of her blood on the car and Halloween haunted house of a Carthian who swindled her sire and &quot;incidentally destroyed&quot; one of her touchstones to attract poisonous snakes, birds, rodents, and vermin to destroy his car.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T08:27:01-07:00","id":1447714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447711#post1447711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and if they're affected by the power and aren't directed against a target, they're going to destroy or shred the object or section of ground where the blood was spilled.<br /> <br /> One of my characters flung some of her blood on the car and Halloween haunted house of a Carthian who swindled her sire and &quot;incidentally destroyed&quot; one of her touchstones to attract poisonous snakes, birds, rodents, and vermin to destroy his car.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any animal that can smell the vampire\u2019s blood enters a state of feral rage. It lashes out, attacking the nearest victim without a thought for its own safety </div> </div> </div>It says animals (Humans and other creatures included even though they have to make a roll to resist) that can SMELL, not taste. Whoever smell the blood, falls into this state where they are forced to attack each other (if not directed).<br /> I think you are confusing with Summon the Hunt (Animalism 3), where animals must devour the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 05-06-2021, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T09:22:56-07:00","id":1447720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447709#post1447709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rule Feral Infection as a riot (much more &quot;feral&quot; though): anyone affected, if not directed through someone specific, is being destroying the most close to him, either he's afflicted by the same power or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it you don't read any real meaning into &quot;her victims turn upon one another&quot; other than just the most likely &quot;closest target&quot; is probably going to be another victim of the power, but they do not have to be?<br /> <br /> Do you have victims target the vampire triggering the power if they happen to be close (which the probably will be, giving the blood-spilling requirement)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T13:36:45-07:00","id":1447728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447720#post1447720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take it you don't read any real meaning into &quot;her victims turn upon one another&quot; other than just the most likely &quot;closest target&quot; is probably going to be another victim of the power, but they do not have to be?<br /> <br /> Do you have victims target the vampire triggering the power if they happen to be close (which the probably will be, giving the blood-spilling requirement)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. I mean, if not pointed to anyone specific it's totally lecit for you to have them turning on another which is affected cause &quot;violence calls violence&quot;. But if he's sourronded by people not affected, or the closest affected is a bit too far, it doesn't matter and he'll turn on the closest one.<br /> <br /> About the second question, no. The vampire who has triggered the power won't be attacked (while his friends can be attacked - which is the main drawback of this power already mentioned in previous post about this topic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T22:07:06-07:00","id":1447764,"title":"","content":"So. Maybe I'm just bad with game mechanics, but how exactly does the active part of Vigor work? It adds vigor dots as a weapon bonus to attacks. Does that mean +vigor as damage, or +vigor as attack rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-06T23:19:30-07:00","id":1447772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447764#post1447764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So. Maybe I'm just bad with game mechanics, but how exactly does the active part of Vigor work? It adds vigor dots as a weapon bonus to attacks. Does that mean +vigor as damage, or +vigor as attack rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>As extra damage on successful attack rolls, just like how weapon damage is added on top of your rolled successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-07T05:18:11-07:00","id":1447794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1447647#post1447647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I too connected the Prince to Wicked deads Ghuls wasn't it? I made them the actual residents of the princes' dimension (minor nobility being cannibals) and they swapped places with anybody devoured at the main temple. Bringing the ghul to this world where the red world cult revered them and started slowly kidnapping important people and replacing them with Ghul clones. (most of the time the devoured person just vanished as normal, but if there was a double in the abyss then it could come over once the soul of the original/whatever was gone) Also abused the Vampire/Spirit rider people blood tenebrous figuring in the world of the prince, carrion or cannibal spirits would use vampires as sock puppets. Vampires who committed diablerie being royalty in the prince timeline others being just above mortals. Allowed one of the kings of the princes realm to power up and reach his final form as a spirit-possessed vampire badass vs mages with White phos and portals/bans and whatever, it didn't go well even with all that lol.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I never quite make a whole unified storyline out of it, but messed with bits and pieces here and there across several games, like:<br /> <br /> - An occult ritual based on liver-eating (from Mythologies, pgs 62-67) that not only eased blood potency requirements for kindred, but allowed ghouls and mortals to harvest vitae on their own.<br /> <br /> - Tried to extrapolated from the &quot;Temple Hounds&quot; of Howard's Rock, making the stages of the Hunger (see World of Darkness: Antagonists, pp. 118\u2013121) into a set of forms somewhat mirroring/mocking the Uratha. I think i mixed it with the Thief (Antagonists 124-126) to ramp it up into an actual match of their battle forms.<br /> <br /> - A family of filipino-american models/socialites vaguely inspired in the Kardashians into one version of the Aswang (originated with the Drama of the Outcast Erinye branch of the entity), with members peppered in the Cheiron Group &amp; Abbey Road both.<br /> <br /> - A private isle in the Fillipines that served as ancestral holding/invite only nightlife center/cult community of sorts, a cross between Howard's Rock and Ibiza so to speak. Or Wickerman festival crossed with the films (the owners <i>might </i>be the family cited above, but could also be an independent piece of scripture, depending on ST's preferences).<br /> <br /> - Wicked Dead Ghuls i would explain as a debased form of the priesthood of the Blasphemous Scribe (Red Word), if memory tricks me not. Those who transcended their curse by &quot;awakening&quot; to their destiny as prophets of the Secret Branch of the Red Word develop the merit-based magic with powers like the Sons of Phobos (from Blood Sorcery &amp; Requiem 2nd ed).<br /> <br /> - Oh yeah, adapted Eaters of Sin (Mythologies, pgs 54-60) and Hamartiaphage as another Prince of 100.000 Leaves-related mortal group, main difference being they devoured people in the proccess, the objective being purifying the soul of the departed of the sins of the flesh through consumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-07-2021, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T02:29:49-07:00","id":1448573,"title":"","content":"I can remember, time ago, I've found a nice stat set for Vhozd (War ghoul) which perfectly fit to Requiem system. <br /> What I'm interested to is not too much the stat themselves if the peculiar attack types.<br /> Something like he could strike multiple enemies with a single blow, etc. Can't find it anymore though. I found somenthing online but it's not what I was looking for. Can anyone either help me finding it out or resuming the mechanics in here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T09:52:42-07:00","id":1448595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1448573#post1448573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can remember, time ago, I've found a nice stat set for Vhozd (War ghoul) which perfectly fit to Requiem system. <br /> What I'm interested to is not too much the stat themselves if the peculiar attack types.<br /> Something like he could strike multiple enemies with a single blow, etc. Can't find it anymore though. I found somenthing online but it's not what I was looking for. Can anyone either help me finding it out or resuming the mechanics in here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know anything about this homebrew, but attacking multiple opponents generally use the autofire rules: Roll one attack roll per target (with their Defense if applicable), with each attack taking a penalty equal to the total number of targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T00:06:12-07:00","id":1448661,"title":"","content":"Does the Carthian Law <b>Right of Return</b> void the limitation of no Covenant status higher than your primary organization's? Could I be a member of the Carthian Movement and have 3 dots of Carthian Status and 3 dots of Invictus status, for example? Could I be a member of the Carthian Movement and have 2 dots of Carthian Status and 4 dots of Circle of the Crone status?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T19:46:21-07:00","id":1448745,"title":"","content":"No. It doesn't void it, since acquisition of covenant unique doesn't require you to pledge sole membership to get the relevant merit or magic, just the relevant status rank. And in many cases, that can be ignored. Your &quot;primary covenant&quot; is the one with the most status dots. Obviously if your character's primary covenant is for example, the Circle of the Crone, your character wouldn't be trying to obtain higher status in the Carthian Movement than whatever their Acolyte status is. <br /> <br /> Right of Return does not count your Carthian Movement covenant status for purposes of determining the maximum allowable status in other covenants when holding status across multiple covenants is a thing. And it allows you a slightly higher impression than a suspected spy would normally hold.<br /> <br /> A 3 Carthian / 3 Invictus character is normally not allowed because you can't have equal or scattered through all of highest covenants. <br /> <br /> A 2 Carthian / 4 Circle of the Crone status is sort of the scenario the merit is meant for, a highly influential Acolyte dabbling in the Carthian Movement who has Right of Return is less likely to be stripped of their position than a 3 Circle of the Crone 1 Invictus member.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 05-16-2021, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T01:19:35-07:00","id":1449329,"title":"","content":"How does falling damage work for vampires? The book says 1 bashing per meter fallen, then at 30 meters it's a flat 10 lethal. But, vampires convert mundane lethal damage to bashing, so at terminal velocity they would only takes 10 bashing damage, the equivalent of a 10 meter fall? Or do you ignore the flip to 10 lethal and just stick to 1 bashing per meter up to a max of 30 bashing at 30+ meters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T02:36:15-07:00","id":1449332,"title":"","content":"10 bashing, letting it go higher would imply that vampires somehow have a higher terminal velocity than the living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T07:57:19-07:00","id":1449347,"title":"","content":"I personally do not like fall damages mechanic. Too few damages even for mortal. I mean: 10 meters fall for a man is only 3 damages. <br /> I personally double such damages when the fall is not on his feet. <br /> Meaning that if you fall on your feet it's 3 bashing, while if you fall on your back it's pretty much losing concsciousness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T15:28:39-07:00","id":1449387,"title":"","content":"Does the 2.0 Invictus use the same titles as the 1.0 Invictus? Blood and Smoke doesn't really go into the covenants' structures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T18:22:17-07:00","id":1449407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1449347#post1449347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally do not like fall damages mechanic. Too few damages even for mortal. I mean: 10 meters fall for a man is only 3 damages.<br /> I personally double such damages when the fall is not on his feet.<br /> Meaning that if you fall on your feet it's 3 bashing, while if you fall on your back it's pretty much losing concsciousness</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ?? It's 1 bashing per meter fallen, so falling 10 meters would be 10 bashing. At least in core CoD it is, not sure if it's different elsewhere or I missed an faq or something. That typically enough to fill a human's health track with bashing and wrap a few points over into lethal. It is a bit strange that the damage goes from 29 bashing at 29 meters to 10 lethal at 30. 10 lethal seems less than it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T18:28:10-07:00","id":1449408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1449387#post1449387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the 2.0 Invictus use the same titles as the 1.0 Invictus? Blood and Smoke doesn't really go into the covenants' structures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> General assumption is that unless something in 2E specifically mentions a change, 1E stuff continues to work. So yes, the structure from 1E should still work, unless I've missed something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T19:13:34-07:00","id":1449411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1449408#post1449408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> General assumption is that unless something in 2E specifically mentions a change, 1E stuff continues to work. So yes, the structure from 1E should still work, unless I've missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only big thing that has changed with Invictus IIRC is that they aren't technophobic in 2e anymore. The world changes, but the people in it stay mostly the same, just with new tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T00:51:22-07:00","id":1449434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1449407#post1449407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">?? It's 1 bashing per meter fallen, so falling 10 meters would be 10 bashing. At least in core CoD it is, not sure if it's different elsewhere or I missed an faq or something. That typically enough to fill a human's health track with bashing and wrap a few points over into lethal. It is a bit strange that the damage goes from 29 bashing at 29 meters to 10 lethal at 30. 10 lethal seems less than it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Falling inflicts one point of damage per three meters <br /> fallen.&quot;<br /> <br /> Copied directly from the CofD core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T00:58:16-07:00","id":1449435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1449407#post1449407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ?? It's 1 bashing per meter fallen, so falling 10 meters would be 10 bashing. At least in core CoD it is, not sure if it's different elsewhere or I missed an faq or something. That typically enough to fill a human's health track with bashing and wrap a few points over into lethal. It is a bit strange that the damage goes from 29 bashing at 29 meters to 10 lethal at 30. 10 lethal seems less than it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just read back the page in CoD book. It's 1 bashing every three meters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T03:19:56-07:00","id":1449443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1449434#post1449434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Falling inflicts one point of damage per three meters<br /> fallen.&quot;<br /> <br /> Copied directly from the CofD core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, don't know why my copy says differently. That doesn't seem like nearly enough damage then. Anything less than 30 meters just won't do enough damage to ever be able to kill a human, which is absurd. I think I prefer the 1 bashing damage per meter version.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T03:40:11-07:00","id":1449445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1449443#post1449443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, don't know why my copy says differently. That doesn't seem like nearly enough damage then. Anything less than 30 meters just won't do enough damage to ever be able to kill a human, which is absurd. I think I prefer the 1 bashing damage per meter version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to bet it's just an outdated copy. Redownload and you'll get the print version.<br /> <br /> Edit: As for house ruling falling damage to 1B per m; you also need to change what happens at terminal velocity. 29B to 10L is not a good conversion rate since the former will outright kill the vast majority of mortals by wrapping around and filling the Health track with aggravated damage, while the latter can be survived by every single non-Small-Framed adult as long as they're at full health and get some treatment to be stabilised after the fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-24-2021, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T04:02:03-07:00","id":1449447,"title":"","content":"Do you plan to make a translation guide between VtR and V5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T16:51:01-07:00","id":1449730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1449447#post1449447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you plan to make a translation guide between VtR and V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not gonna happen, but judging on how close VtR 2e and V5 are mechanics-wise, it should probably be easier than ever to convert things yourself. If you wish to translate things from V5 to VtR, I highly recommend Rose Bailey's book 'Bloody Dots', which is her guide to designing Vampire the Requiem Disciplines and bloodlines. Rose Bailey was one of the lead designers on Vampire the Requiem, so her opinion is quite valuable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/280672/BLOODY-DOTS-The-Writers-Guide-to-Disciplines\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/280672.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/280672/BLOODY-DOTS-The-Writers-Guide-to-Disciplines\" target=\"_blank\"> BLOODY DOTS: The Writer's Guide to Disciplines - White Wolf | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/280672/BLOODY-DOTS-The-Writers-Guide-to-Disciplines\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/280672/BLOODY-DOTS-The-Writers-Guide-to-Disciplines </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> BLOODY DOTS: The Writer's Guide to Disciplines - Vampires are defined by power. Carmilla invaded dreams and turned trust to murder. Dracula commanded and became the chil </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T02:34:46-07:00","id":1450792,"title":"","content":"I was hoping for some quick clarification on how the last dot of Riding the Wave style works:<br /> <br /> <i>Animal Grace (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Your character dodges and strikes as fluidly as an animal, with confidence and awareness. When spending Willpower to attack or defend, gain both benefits. Add a +2 die bonus to Defense, and a +3 die bonus to attack rolls.</i><br /> <br /> There are no 'both' benefits to spending WP naturally, unless they mean adding the +2 to a Resistance trait. Additionally, defense isn't a die pool (unless they mean Dodging?), so a +2 die bonus just seems like a typo or something. Is this merit meant to give +2 defense and +3 to an attack roll? If you do two attacks during your round (attacking two separate target via fighting style or whatever), do you then get +4 to defense if you spend WP to augment both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T04:32:40-07:00","id":1450797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1450792#post1450792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was hoping for some quick clarification on how the last dot of Riding the Wave style works:<br /> <br /> <i>Animal Grace (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): Your character dodges and strikes as fluidly as an animal, with confidence and awareness. When spending Willpower to attack or defend, gain both benefits. Add a +2 die bonus to Defense, and a +3 die bonus to attack rolls.</i><br /> <br /> There are no 'both' benefits to spending WP naturally, unless they mean adding the +2 to a Resistance trait. Additionally, defense isn't a die pool (unless they mean Dodging?), so a +2 die bonus just seems like a typo or something. Is this merit meant to give +2 defense and +3 to an attack roll? If you do two attacks during your round (attacking two separate target via fighting style or whatever), do you then get +4 to defense if you spend WP to augment both?</div> </div> </div> </div>When attacking, you can spend a WP for +3. When you're applying your Defense, you can spend a WP for +2. That's how it normally works. This Merit makes it so that when you spend WP on either of these benefits, you also get to use the other benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T21:23:14-07:00","id":1450910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1450797#post1450797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When attacking, you can spend a WP for +3. When you're applying your Defense, you can spend a WP for +2. That's how it normally works. This Merit makes it so that when you spend WP on either of these benefits, you also get to use the other benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must be blind because I didn't see anything about WP giving +defense anywhere. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T23:08:29-07:00","id":1450915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1450910#post1450910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I must be blind because I didn't see anything about WP giving +defense anywhere. Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>From Chronicle of darkness core pag 88 and Vampire 2ed core pag 176<br /> &quot;Spending a point of Willpower increases his Defense by 2, but only against one attacker.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T23:15:49-07:00","id":1450917,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was looking in thr section about Willpower. Thank you so much for the help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T01:42:07-07:00","id":1450927,"title":"","content":"What's the closest equivalent to Mask of Tranquility in 2E? Or barring that, what other ways can a vampire hide/mask their predator aura/Beast? I'm sure I missed it because I should be sleeping but I can't find the Discipline that does this now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26808-katieplays","name":"KatiePlays","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26808_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T02:14:01-07:00","id":1450933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KatiePlays</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1450927#post1450927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the closest equivalent to Mask of Tranquility in 2E? Or barring that, what other ways can a vampire hide/mask their predator aura/Beast? I'm sure I missed it because I should be sleeping but I can't find the Discipline that does this now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate 1 is also about that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T09:06:01-07:00","id":1450963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1450933#post1450933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obfuscate 1 is also about that</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, thanks! It felt a little heavy handed for what I was looking for (the character doesn't want to be socially invisible, just doesn't want it to be so clear to people in the know that he's a vampire), but maybe I was just reading too much into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26808-katieplays","name":"KatiePlays","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26808_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T11:50:47-07:00","id":1450975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KatiePlays</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1450963#post1450963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, thanks! It felt a little heavy handed for what I was looking for (the character doesn't want to be socially invisible, just doesn't want it to be so clear to people in the know that he's a vampire), but maybe I was just reading too much into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it violates the spirit of the rules if a player wants to selectively use that aspect of the power while choosing not to access the other. If that works for the game, go for it. Some of the Disciplines have little additional effects like that, and they're definitely written with the expectation that players will want to get creative with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T13:20:30-07:00","id":1450977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KatiePlays</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1450963#post1450963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, thanks! It felt a little heavy handed for what I was looking for (the character doesn't want to be socially invisible, just doesn't want it to be so clear to people in the know that he's a vampire), but maybe I was just reading too much into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you can chose to only hide your aura without being also socially invisible. And also, Obfuscate 1 does not hide you in areas where you are not suppose to be, while it still suppress your nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 06-05-2021, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T17:01:23-07:00","id":1450995,"title":"","content":"And if the ST insists on applying the full effect, a simple one dot Merit or one XP Devotion should allow you to only suppress the Predatory Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T03:26:27-07:00","id":1451033,"title":"","content":"Two things:<br /> <br /> First, was the Other Frenzy option ever updated for 2nd edition? And if not, what book was it found in again?<br /> <br /> Second, I was trying to find a way with the Hurt Locker rules to weaponize mockery or condemnation of hypocrisies to the point of inflicting the Broken condition, or even encouraging suicide. The options given for Intimidation, Socialize, and Expression weren't appropriate, Empathy focused on Breaking Points, and Persuasion just... didn't seem quite right, somehow. <br /> <br /> Suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T10:46:59-07:00","id":1451236,"title":"","content":"How does the Iron Skin merit interact with Kindred taking bashing damage from weapons? If someone tries to hit me with a sword, and the sword deals bashing damage to vampires, would Iron Skin count as armor against it? Or is 'bashing attacks' just if someone punches me in the face?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T12:30:08-07:00","id":1451242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451236#post1451236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Iron Skin merit interact with Kindred taking bashing damage from weapons? If someone tries to hit me with a sword, and the sword deals bashing damage to vampires, would Iron Skin count as armor against it? Or is 'bashing attacks' just if someone punches me in the face?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the latter. Vampires are more sturdy than humans because their bodies don't operate under the normal rules of biology, not because their skin is hardened or resistant to cutting; they can keep going despite the fact that they've lost pieces that would end a human life. So, I'd argue it only applies to things that would deal bashing inherently, not things that deal lethal to humans but bashing to vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:08:03-07:00","id":1451695,"title":"","content":"Does using obfuscates &quot;Cloak of Night&quot; power to vanish completely use 2 blood. 1 for &quot;Cloak of Night&quot; &amp; 1 as part of &quot;Face in the Crowd&quot;. Also, it says that using CoN with &quot;Touch of Shadows&quot; you can now affect other people, since ToS requires 1 blood, then using it with CoN which also requires 1 blood would mean you need to use 2 blood for CoN + ToN also? <br /> <br /> CoN + FitC = 2 blood (1 for CoN + 1 for Fitc (mentioned in CoN)) &amp; CoN + ToS = 2 blood also<br /> <br /> How does this work for BP 1 vampires only being able to spend 1 blood a turn....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:35:23-07:00","id":1451707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451695#post1451695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does using obfuscates &amp;quot;Cloak of Night&amp;quot; power to vanish completely use 2 blood. 1 for &amp;quot;Cloak of Night&amp;quot; &amp; 1 as part of &amp;quot;Face in the Crowd&amp;quot;. Also, it says that using CoN with &amp;quot;Touch of Shadows&amp;quot; you can now affect other people, since ToS requires 1 blood, then using it with CoN which also requires 1 blood would mean you need to use 2 blood for CoN + ToN also? <br /> <br /> CoN + FitC = 2 blood (1 for CoN + 1 for Fitc (mentioned in CoN)) &amp; CoN + ToS = 2 blood also<br /> <br /> How does this work for BP 1 vampires only being able to spend 1 blood a turn....</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not wrong, face in the crowd doesn't cost anything. So It would be 1 vitae to vanish through Cloak of Night and 2 vitae to have someone else affected by touch of Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T11:36:53-07:00","id":1451709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451707#post1451707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I'm not wrong, face in the crowd doesn't cost anything. So It would be 1 vitae to vanish through Cloak of Night and 2 vitae to have someone else affected by touch of Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Normally, it doesn't but the CoN text adds, &quot;The vampire can also spend a point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd to vanish completely.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is confusing. Either it's already considered in the cost of the power (the 1 blood cost in CoN) or it isn't and CoN's 1 blood cost is in addition to the FitC's extra cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-11-2021, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T14:30:02-07:00","id":1451750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451709#post1451709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Normally, it doesn't but the CoN text adds, &quot;The vampire can also spend a point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd to vanish completely.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is confusing. Either it's already considered in the cost of the power (the 1 blood cost in CoN) or it isn't and CoN's 1 blood cost is in addition to the FitC's extra cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>that because CoN isn't an action. You do not activate CoN, you activate Face in the Crowd boosting the effect with the vitae required by CoN. So it's still 1 vitae in total. Same way for ToS which, on the other hand, cost already 1 vitae, which bring the overall cost to 2 vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T14:49:30-07:00","id":1451757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451750#post1451750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that because CoN isn't an action. You do not activate CoN, you activate Face in the Crowd boosting the effect with the vitae required by CoN. So it's still 1 vitae in total. Same way for ToS which, on the other hand, cost already 1 vitae, which bring the overall cost to 2 vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it's not an action but it does still have a cost of 1 blood. The text that then says you &quot;can also spend a point of vitae&quot; would then be redundant since your spending blood on the cost of CoN anyway (and have to combine with ToS)<br /> <br /> You spend 1 blood using CoN, that's in its cost, this expenditure is separate blood from the one needed for ToS. Using CoN then always costs 1 blood, the text then says you can ALSO spend 1 blood and combine it with FitC to vanish completely.<br /> <br /> 2 blood per turn is outside the reach of a BP 1 vampire so even using CoN + ToS together cant be done, unless there was a rule saying vampires can expend blood over multiple turns that got removed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-11-2021, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T15:23:43-07:00","id":1451762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451757#post1451757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure it's not an action but it does still have a cost of 1 blood. The text that then says you &quot;can also spend a point of vitae&quot; would then be redundant since your spending blood on the cost of CoN anyway (and have to combine with ToS)<br /> <br /> You spend 1 blood using CoN, that's in its cost, this expenditure is separate blood from the one needed for ToS. Using CoN then always costs 1 blood, the text then says you can ALSO spend 1 blood and combine it with FitC to vanish completely.<br /> <br /> 2 blood per turn is outside the reach of a BP 1 vampire so even using CoN + ToS together cant be done, unless there was a rule saying vampires can expend blood over multiple turns that got removed...</div> </div> </div> </div>The way it's phrased may be no the best one and yet I don't see too much reasons to be confused. The price of CoN is 1 vitae, stop. It's not an action so you can't act\u00edvate it by itself. You are using it to boost the effect of either FitC or ToS, adding its cost to the one related to whichever you're using as basis. <br /> <br /> It indeed says: when activating FitC (0 cost) you can also spend 1 Vitae (the cost of CoN) to vanish completely. It's not saying ...you can also spend 1 Vitae in addition to CoN to vanish completely.<br /> Wouldn't make too much sense to me.<br /> <br /> And I'd say, even if not specified, you can spend the vitae over more turns as you do for many others powers. But this is just my call though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 06-11-2021, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-11T20:04:08-07:00","id":1451797,"title":"","content":"Marcus is right. Order of operations is: Activate Face in the Crowd as an instant action, spending a Vitae as you do to enhance it with the effect of Cloak of Night. As noted, not having an action means it's not really a discrete effect so much as an add-on to other powers. The &quot;also&quot; in &quot;...can also spend a point of Vitae...&quot; is in relation to the previous paragraph, which outlines using Cloak of Night to enhance Touch of Shadow so it can affect other people, as opposed to just animals and objects. It also says <u>a</u> point of Vitae, which doesn't really make sense if it really means &quot;spend 2 Vitae.&quot; I guess the phrasing is a little imprecise, but it's definitely not meant to indicate turning on Cloak of Night requires spending 2 Vitae when using Face in the Crowd. It would say 2 Vitae in the cost if that were so. You <i>do </i>have to spend 2 Vitae to use Touch of Shadow on another person/vampire, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T07:06:34-07:00","id":1451844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451797#post1451797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marcus is right. Order of operations is: Activate Face in the Crowd as an instant action, spending a Vitae as you do to enhance it with the effect of Cloak of Night. As noted, not having an action means it's not really a discrete effect so much as an add-on to other powers. The &amp;quot;also&amp;quot; in &amp;quot;...can also spend a point of Vitae...&amp;quot; is in relation to the previous paragraph, which outlines using Cloak of Night to enhance Touch of Shadow so it can affect other people, as opposed to just animals and objects. It also says <u>a</u> point of Vitae, which doesn't really make sense if it really means &amp;quot;spend 2 Vitae.&amp;quot; I guess the phrasing is a little imprecise, but it's definitely not meant to indicate turning on Cloak of Night requires spending 2 Vitae when using Face in the Crowd. It would say 2 Vitae in the cost if that were so. You <i>do </i>have to spend 2 Vitae to use Touch of Shadow on another person/vampire, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>No such thing as order of operations in chronicles, the system is just not that precise. I think we can all agree on how it's intended and that the text is badly written and makes the mention of spending blood for fitc redundant. Not being able to use ToS with CoN at blood potency 1 though is still a issue and while it's easy to just assume vampires can spend blood over multiple turns (which would explain some devotions with a high cost) unless I've missed it, this isnt stated as possible anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T07:28:39-07:00","id":1451848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451844#post1451844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No such thing as order of operations in chronicles, the system is just not that precise. I think we can all agree on how it's intended and that the text is badly written and makes the mention of spending blood for fitc redundant. Not being able to use ToS with CoN at blood potency 1 though is still a issue and while it's easy to just assume vampires can spend blood over multiple turns (which would explain some devotions with a high cost) unless I've missed it, this isnt stated as possible anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in this specific case, but there are plenty of devotions and powers specificaly stating you can spend Vitae over multiple turns. As it's not specified here I guess it's your call though. I personally would allow it. Manuals are written by human being which makes oversights possibile. So I try to figure out what would make more sense.<br /> Having a power which can't be used by kindred younger than 50 years old, which only apply ToS effects on others (not even full vanish), doesn't seems the intention of developers in this case as they allow much extreme effects to, potentially, even BP 1 vampires (see Juggernaut Gait, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 06-12-2021, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T07:46:29-07:00","id":1451851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451848#post1451848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in this specific case, but there are plenty of devotions and powers specificaly stating you can spend Vitae over multiple turns. As it's not specified here I guess it's your call though. I personally would allow it. Manuals are written by human being which makes oversights possibile. So I try to figure out what would make more sense.<br /> Having a power which can't be used by kindred younger than 50 years old, which only apply ToS effects on others (not even full vanish), doesn't seems the intention of developers in this case as they allows much extreme powers to, potentially, even BP 1 vampires (see Force of Nature, Primeval Miasma, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Force of Nature doesn't state that you can spend the blood cost over multiple turns and as for &quot;plenty of devotions/powers that specifically state you can&quot; which ones are they?<br /> <br /> Cloak the Gathering says for 4 blood you can vanish from sight AND use it on a number of people equal to his BP. So let's see, 2 blood for Cloak of Gathering, 1 Blood for Cloak of Night, the last blood must come from the extra cost for Face in the Crowd?<br /> <br /> Evidence then that FitC + CoN requires 2 blood. Cloak the Gathering adding an additional 2 cost to use on multiple people.<br /> <br /> Now is being Blood Potency 4 before you can use Cloak the Gathering to conceal multiple people at all intended? I have no idea which is annoying.<br /> <br /> Cult of Personality needing 10 points makes it basically unusable though which suggests you should be able to spend blood over multiple turns but then when does the discipline or devotion start? when you begin to spend blood or only after you have spent the entire cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-12-2021, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T08:38:52-07:00","id":1451861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451851#post1451851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Force of Nature doesn't state that you can spend the blood cost over multiple turns and as for &amp;quot;plenty of devotions/powers that specifically state you can&amp;quot; which ones are they?<br /> <br /> Cloak the Gathering says for 4 blood you can vanish from sight AND use it on a number of people equal to his BP. So let's see, 2 blood for Cloak of Gathering, 1 Blood for Cloak of Night, the last blood must come from the extra cost for Face in the Crowd?<br /> <br /> Evidence then that FitC + CoN requires 2 blood. Cloak the Gathering adding an additional 2 cost to use on multiple people.<br /> <br /> Now is being Blood Potency 4 before you can use Cloak the Gathering to conceal multiple people at all intended? I have no idea which is annoying.<br /> <br /> Cult of Personality needing 10 points makes it basically unusable though which suggests you should be able to spend blood over multiple turns but then when does the discipline or devotion start? when you begin to spend blood or only after you have spent the entire cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>It starts when you spend the last vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T08:41:03-07:00","id":1451862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451844#post1451844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[..] while it's easy to just assume vampires can spend blood over multiple turns (which would explain some devotions with a high cost) unless I've missed it, this isnt stated as possible anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it was missed in VtR, but the base rule is that any splat with conventional fuel traits (aka not Mummies, Beasts and Deviants) can spend it over several turns if they can't spend it all during a single turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T09:39:45-07:00","id":1451868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451862#post1451862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it was missed in VtR, but the base rule is that any splat with conventional fuel traits (aka not Mummies, Beasts and Deviants) can spend it over several turns if they can't spend it all during a single turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sure, Mage, Demon, and Promethean all mention being able to spend fuel over multiple turns and I hope that it has just been missed from Vampire. But then again regaining willpower from a full nights sleep is a base rule missing from Vampire, it could be a similar thing here.<br /> <br /> If one was entirely new to Chronicles knowing this fuel trait &quot;base&quot; rule would be very hard to find (honestly ive not read the horror/ephemeral sections of the blue book). One would need to read the other splats to see that they could and then apply it to vampires.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's more a common rule than a base rule in this case which was mistakenly missed out in vampire meaning a blood potency 1 vampire wanting to use CoN + FitC to vanish himself needs to spend 2 blood over 2 turns from the evidence that the cost of Cloak the Gathering to vanish multiple peoplt being 4 blood.<br /> <br /> Yossarian &amp; Marcus<br /> If it was only 1 blood to use both CoN with FitC to vanish completely then the example in the Cloak the Gathering devotion should cost only 3 blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-12-2021, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T11:20:53-07:00","id":1451879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451868#post1451868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yossarian &amp; Marcus<br /> If it was only 1 blood to use both CoN with FitC to vanish completely then the example in the Cloak the Gathering devotion should cost only 3 blood?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s 4 Vitae because (as the Devotion notes explicitly), you\u2019re using the following four effects at once:<br /> <br /> Face in the Crowd to make yourself forgettable. (0 Vitae)<br /> <br /> Cloak the Gathering to use Touch of Shadow on multiple characters at once (2 Vitae)<br /> <br /> Touch of Shadow to extend Face in the Crowd over others. (1 Vitae)<br /> <br /> Cloak of Night to enhance Face in the Crowd to make yourself and everyone else invisible. (1 Vitae)<br /> <br /> If you did have to spend 2 to use Cloak of Night on yourself, it would be 5 Vitae, not 4.<br /> <br /> <b>First Edit: </b>Always better to have examples. Emphases and explanatory text mine:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire, p. 142</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cloak the Gathering enhances the effect of <b>Touch of Shadow </b>[1 Vitae] and <b>Cloak of Night</b> [1 Vitae]. By paying <b>two extra points of Vitae</b> [Cloak the Gathering costs 2 in and of itself], the vampire can expand the effect of Touch of Shadow to encompass a number of people equal to his Blood Potency, though subject to the normal Size modifiers of Touch of Shadow. He can also opt to activate <b>Face in the Crowd </b>[0 Vitae] at the same time. If he also pays the extra cost for Cloak of Night to vanish completely rather than fading into the background, the effect applies to everyone masked by Cloak the Gathering \u2014 so for four points of Vitae total he can vanish from sight along with a number of people equal to his Blood Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Second Edit: </b>You can spend Vitae over several turns to use powers you don't have high enough Blood Potency to use in one. I've freelanced on <b>Vampire </b>and know this to be true. It's a rule from First Edition that just isn't noted in Second; it's an oversight, not a change (unlike the Willpower thing, which <i>was </i>intentional). It works like all the other monster types with fuel traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-12-2021, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T12:15:26-07:00","id":1451893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451879#post1451879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s 4 Vitae because (as the Devotion notes explicitly), you\u2019re using the following four effects at once:<br /> <br /> Face in the Crowd to make yourself forgettable. (0 Vitae)<br /> <br /> Cloak the Gathering to use Touch of Shadow on multiple characters at once (2 Vitae)<br /> <br /> Touch of Shadow to extend Face in the Crowd over others. (1 Vitae)<br /> <br /> Cloak of Night to enhance Face in the Crowd to make yourself and everyone else invisible. (1 Vitae)<br /> <br /> If you did have to spend 2 to use Cloak of Night on yourself, it would be 5 Vitae, not 4.<br /> <br /> Edit: Always better to have examples. Emphases mine:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Touch of Shadow cost (1 Vitae).<br /> Cloak the Gathering upgrading Touch of Shadows to include multiple people. (2 Vitae)<br /> Spending the extra cost for (the text in Cloak of Night's extra cost) FitC to vanish completely (1 vitae)<br /> <br /> Note your not activating CoN itself, just paying the extra (note it says extra cost not normal cost) cost to upgrade FitC, CtG is the power.allowing you to use the extra CoN cost to upgrade FitC to others. Which is still evidence that the 1 blood to vanish completely with CoN is an extra cost ontop of the normal 1 for CoN because CtG allows you to pay the extra (but not the normal cost) to upgrade FitC to others.<br /> <br /> (at no point does touch of shadow extend FitC over others, rather CtG allows you to pay extra via CoN (without paying for CoN) to extend FitC to yourself and others.<br /> <br /> why does it say to pay the extra cost to vanish completely instead of normal cost for Cloak on Night? Because you aren't actually using CoN, your just taking advantage of its extra 1 blood cost to upgrade FitC to vanish completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 06-12-2021, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-12T13:46:08-07:00","id":1451900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1451893#post1451893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (at no point does touch of shadow extend FitC over others, rather CtG allows you to pay extra via CoN (without paying for CoN) to extend FitC to yourself and others.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;With just a touch, the vampire can extend the muted attentions of Face in the Crowd to an object or animal, rather than himself.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's quite literally what Touch of Shadow does. That's from the text of Touch of Shadow. It's what Cloak the Gathering even says it does: &quot;...the vampire can expand the effect of Touch of Shadow to encompass a number of people equal to his Blood Potency.&quot; Touch of Shadow is the same effect as Face in the Crowd, just on other people.<br /> <br /> However, I <i>was </i>a tad imprecise there, because the Devotion text does just say you're using Face in the Crowd for the Cloak of Night effect. So, the most accurate way to express it is:<br /> <br /> Cloak the Gathering to expand the effect of Touch of Shadow so you can use it on multiple characters at once. (2 Vitae)<br /> <br /> Touch of Shadow to use the <i>effect </i>of Face in the Crowd on other people. (1 Vitae)<br /> <br /> Face in the Crowd to make yourself forgettable as well. (0 Vitae)<br /> <br /> Cloak of Night to enhance Face in the Crowd and Touch of Shadow to make yourself and everyone else invisible. (1 Vitae)<br /> <br /> I'm struggling to understand what isn't clear here. I understand your logic, but you're coming at it from a false premise: i.e., that there's normally a 2 Vitae cost to use Cloak of Shadow on yourself, but then for some reason it only costs 1 Vitae when you use it in conjunction with Cloak the Gathering.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm not trying to be snippy with you, but the word &quot;extra&quot; really isn't as significant as you think it is, and I don't want to get into a drawn out semantic argument over it. I promise you, it's 1 Vitae to use Cloak of Night. If you don't see it that way, cool, but let's just drop this then, because it's not the point of the thread.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay, so I did a bit of digging, because I remembered there were some errata changes to the way Cloak of Night works. In the very first release of <b>Blood &amp; Smoke </b>(<i>not </i><b>Vampire: The Requiem Second Edition</b>), Cloak of Night automatically enhanced the effect of Touch of Shadow so you could use it on other people. You didn't have to spend a Vitae. If you wanted to make a victim disappear completely as opposed to just making them harder to notice, you had to spend an <i>extra </i>blood on top of the cost of Touch of Shadow. However, after some errata, this was changed so you always have to spend a Vitae when combining Touch of Shadow with Cloak of Night, though the text implies you can be selective about how deep the invisibility is.<br /> <br /> As for Face in the Crowd, here's the relevant text from the alpha of <b>B&amp;S</b>:<br /> <br /> &quot;The vampire can also spend an <i><u><b>extra</b></u></i> point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd or Touch of Shadow to vanish completely.&quot;<br /> <br /> Presumably, that extra was the cost listed in the power, which was indeed 1 Vitae. Now here's the same text from <b>VTR2E</b>:<br /> <br /> &quot;The vampire can also spend a point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd to vanish completely.&quot;<br /> <br /> Specifically, the word &quot;extra&quot; is removed so that it doesn't seem like you have to spend two blood to disappear. In short, the reason it says <b><i><u>&quot;extra&quot;</u></i></b> in Cloak the Gathering is because it's referring to the way the system worked in the first place; that is, it was free to use Cloak of Night in some circumstances, but you had to pay a Vitae to totally disappear other people or yourself. You <i>never </i>had to spend two Vitae to disappear yourself, however. The change doesn't really affect Cloak the Gathering, it just makes the wording a little odd.<br /> <br /> Alright, if that's not enough, I don't know what is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 06-12-2021, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T19:34:16-07:00","id":1454258,"title":"","content":"English is not my mother tongue, but Google Translate. <br /> <br /> 1) Does a child become kiss addicted when Embraced by a vampire with a Kiss of the Succubus? <br /> <br /> 2) Is the blood addiction and blood bond the same even if the ghoul is Embraced? Invictus and Ventrue have vampires from Ghoul, are they the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25958-veiros","name":"veiros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25958_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T16:13:55-07:00","id":1454309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>veiros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1454258#post1454258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Does a child become kiss addicted when Embraced by a vampire with a Kiss of the Succubus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kiss of the Succubus specifies that it causes Addiction in mortals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>veiros</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Is the blood addiction and blood bond the same even if the ghoul is Embraced? Invictus and Ventrue have vampires from Ghoul, are they the same?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't seem to find anything that says that death and rising as a vampire causes pre-existing bond and addiction to end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T01:09:04-07:00","id":1454333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>veiros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1454258#post1454258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">English is not my mother tongue, but Google Translate.<br /> <br /> 1) Does a child become kiss addicted when Embraced by a vampire with a Kiss of the Succubus?<br /> <br /> 2) Is the blood addiction and blood bond the same even if the ghoul is Embraced? Invictus and Ventrue have vampires from Ghoul, are they the same?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are no specifications on these points. I personally see that as the Embrace being a reset. The Embrace pass through the death. This should be enough to justify the end of any pre-existing condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T06:03:15-07:00","id":1454344,"title":"","content":"Thank you. It was very helpful\uff1a)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25958-veiros","name":"veiros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25958_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T10:30:34-07:00","id":1455661,"title":"","content":"How likely is A revenant to Rise before or after a funeral?<br /> <br /> also how to you think kindred society would feel about revenants with the fertile blood merit<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T10:37:35-07:00","id":1455662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1455661#post1455661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How likely is A revenant to Rise before or after a funeral?<br /> <br /> also how to you think kindred society would feel about revenants with the fertile blood merit</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> About as likely as a post-mortem embrace, i guess? Honestly no idea whatsoever, but definitely a reason for kindred to be <b>quite</b> watchful of their feeding habits and frenzies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T12:37:24-07:00","id":1455676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1455661#post1455661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How likely is A revenant to Rise before or after a funeral?</div> </div> </div> </div>How long does it take to prepare and hold a funeral in your culture? Considering Revenants rises within a week, that's going to determine whether they do so more often before or after a planned funeral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T12:49:41-07:00","id":1456548,"title":"","content":"if I Want to learn disciplines that do not naturally resonate with my clan is it probaly worthwhile to behold myself to a member of a bloodline of my clan rather then to another clan entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T13:49:46-07:00","id":1456550,"title":"","content":"The motives and personality of the individual vampire whose tutelage and blood you are submitting to matters much more than what clan or bloodline they descend from. Pick someone you are very sure is not inclined to take advantage of you (much).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T08:35:16-07:00","id":1456602,"title":"","content":"when vampires make social maneuvering against one blood bound to them they always have a perfect impression<br /> <br /> hows this likely to translate?<br /> <br /> how longs the effect of social maneuvering going to hold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T13:13:08-07:00","id":1456615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1456602#post1456602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">when vampires make social maneuvering against one blood bound to them they always have a perfect impression<br /> <br /> hows this likely to translate?<br /> <br /> how longs the effect of social maneuvering going to hold.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I got your question.<br /> You use social maneuvering when you want something from someone else who does not want to give you; may it be an object, a favor or an alliance. If you win you get it and it last until the favor, Alliance is supposed to last. Or until something happens to change the conditions.<br /> <br /> Specifically, blood Bond lasts one year or so. After it expires, if not prolonged, conditions can be considered as changed. The bonded could feel himself used, cheated or simply repenting to have accepted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-12-2021, 05:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T02:34:56-07:00","id":1456642,"title":"","content":"Oh a crossover issue Im not comfortable with the idea of a hunter with deprogramming being able to remove the enslaved condition in a few hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-18T07:31:45-07:00","id":1457101,"title":"","content":"Oh I vaguely remember it saying a revenant has to receive vitae to awaken from torpor Anyone have a page number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T17:18:42-07:00","id":1457661,"title":"","content":"So, for Obfuscate 1, if the vampire does something violent or attention grabbing then people can make a perception roll (penalised by their Obfuscate) to notice them.<br /> <br /> Does noticing them include noticing what they look like, etc? Does it see through the &quot;some guy&quot; effect so you could recognise the vampire and describe them later, or do you notice the commotion but just that &quot;some guy&quot; is doing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T18:51:42-07:00","id":1457668,"title":"","content":"if a revenant wants to hunt animal blood is animal ken or survival better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T00:48:23-07:00","id":1457696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1457668#post1457668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if a revenant wants to hunt animal blood is animal ken or survival better?</div> </div> </div> </div>To literally hunt for animals would be Survival. However, the hunting process involves a lot of different steps and distilling it down to a single dice pool generally means you get to pick which step to roll for. The last step could be Presence/Manipulation + Animal Ken to dominate or manipulate an animal into getting close enough, if the ST glosses over how to find an animal in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T05:05:54-07:00","id":1457701,"title":"","content":"&quot;So, for Obfuscate 1, if the vampire does something violent or attention grabbing then people can make a perception roll (penalised by their Obfuscate) to notice them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Does noticing them include noticing what they look like, etc? Does it see through the &quot;some guy&quot; effect so you could recognise the vampire and describe them later, or do you notice the commotion but just that &quot;some guy&quot; is doing it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes. If they make the penalized check, it means they see through the Obfuscate attempt. They see the character as they are. In that instant, Obfuscate isn't broken (others may not notice the Obfuscated character) but for that individual who passed the check, they're either unaffected by the power, or something actually stands out about the character who tried and failed to Obfuscate. If they know them or are familiar with them, yes, they recognize them immediately. Outside that you're getting into the individual's mental acuity. If it's a pick out in a line up later, I give them a bonus to the check to recall seeing them with other relevant modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-26-2021, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T13:33:17-07:00","id":1457920,"title":"","content":"Is it safe to say a Revenant with the Fertile Vitae merit would be wise NOT to make an issue of someone 'usurping' them as someones sire <br /> <br /> instead they should be rejoicing to see them receiving a proper embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T10:43:15-07:00","id":1458067,"title":"","content":"I think that depends on the circumstances. If for instance said revenant is in the business of grooming candidates as childer for &quot;proper&quot; kindred society, they may take issue with a Ventrue uplifting their childe they were hired to prep for an influential Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T17:16:39-07:00","id":1458090,"title":"","content":"thats a pretty specific situation<br /> <br /> Say some random revenant who managed to buy the merit as a sign of his blood thickening ever so slightly.think hed be advised not to object to a ventrue scion of the invictus deciding to uplift his childe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T20:21:25-07:00","id":1458101,"title":"","content":"Not really. In kindred society humans are viewed as commodities through a lens of suitable or unsuitable for herd cultivation, ghoul creation, or the embrace. Permission and acquisition of herds is a privilege kindred betray and kill each other over, and ghoul ownership or permission to embrace is a status symbol in kindred society. I don't see kindred finding anyone poaching from them to be acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T07:32:06-07:00","id":1458829,"title":"","content":"Revenants arent Kindred it needs to be mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T22:02:17-07:00","id":1459097,"title":"","content":"Neither are humans. That doesn't change the fact that they're part of kindred society. If revenants are in the setting, so are they.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T03:27:28-07:00","id":1459532,"title":"","content":"How would you write Nomads in a more urbanized region ? As far as I can tell, Nomads as described in the books work best in large countries (US, Russia, even China, Canada, etc.) with vast regions largely uninhabited/scarcely inhabited between towns.<br /> <br /> But how to make the Nomads truly distinct from settled vampires in regions where large-ish cities give way to smaller town and then village and then smaller town and then large-ish cities ? Where distance isn't so great nowadays that it wouldn't be difficult for a Vampire to say, drive 300 km up a road to hit another large town, and where it'd be easy for vampires to congregate in a large city while actually nestling in the smaller towns around during the day.<br /> <br /> Would it be possible for Nomads to truly develop a distinct approach to unlife in those conditions instead of just being &quot;settled vampires on the road because reason?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T03:55:24-07:00","id":1459537,"title":"","content":"Driving 300 km up the road is, if you're using an interstate road system, around 4.5 hours driving without stopping, one way. Much longer if you're not. For creatures that can only be effectively active after sundown to sunrise, that's still a lot of travel time one way. Add in the possibility of 1 to 5 vampires that may congregate around rest stops or popular gas stations and restaurants located within a half mile radius of an interstate exit are very likely to be considered racks to the kindred population of the town or district and/or considered standard patrol area for the local sheriff or hounds. Suddenly sneaking around unnoticed may not be so easy. The kindred nomad culture is likely to be the kindred who know which towns are safe to stop in and which ones are better to avoid, which motels and YMCAs are Lancea Sanctum safe spots, or what Cacophony signs to listen for vs. clueless city dwelling kindred on a road trip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-10T04:33:18-07:00","id":1459540,"title":"","content":"I wasn't particularly thinking about sneaking somewhere, but I guess it makes sense yeah. I guess it'd also be possible for Vampires in such regions to be even more territorial than elsewhere, since drifting Vampires can appears into town much easier than elsewhere, so having that &quot;I'm a real Nomad&quot; vibe could actually help one moving around, instead of being targeted because the Kindred here don't want newcomers since the last four hundred years or something.<br /> <br /> In which case, real hardened nomads would be possibly even more important because, yeah, they know what to do and say and where to not go, at all, and newbies believe that it's as simple as moving to the next town down the road.<br /> <br /> So perhaps I could do with a distinction between Old and New World's Nomads. The former are more like a guild of guides and travelers while the latter are closer to the roving gang vibe they have in my mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 09-10-2021, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T07:37:57-07:00","id":1459650,"title":"","content":"To uplify a revenant Do I need to drain their blood or just give them a drop of my vitae and invest a humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-11T11:22:17-07:00","id":1459672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1459650#post1459650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To uplify a revenant Do I need to drain their blood or just give them a drop of my vitae and invest a humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know just Vitae with humanity investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-16T21:20:15-07:00","id":1460175,"title":"","content":"Can Chary be added to feeding rolls?<br /> <br /> If a former ghoul joins a Revenant Coterie Any reasons he wouldnt Teach any clan disciplines h e was taught to h is new comrades?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-17-2021, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T00:36:26-07:00","id":1460622,"title":"","content":"1st Edition question:<br /> If you use Dominate 5 - Possession on a ghoul, can you use disciplines during that time? If so, yours or the ghouls? Do you use your vitae or theirs? Can you use their vitae to blood buff or heal? Do you project your predator's taint? Do you contest disciplines with your blood potency and mental stats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T01:07:27-07:00","id":1460624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1460622#post1460622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st Edition question:<br /> If you use Dominate 5 - Possession on a ghoul, can you use disciplines during that time? If so, yours or the ghouls? Do you use your vitae or theirs? Can you use their vitae to blood buff or heal? Do you project your predator's taint? Do you contest disciplines with your blood potency and mental stats?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about 1st edition as I've been not taking it back for so many years but I think you can't use discipline (neither yours nor his), you use your mental (probably also social?) attributes but his physical, can't blood buff and I believe you can resist discipline with your blood potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T05:02:20-07:00","id":1460632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1460622#post1460622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1st Edition question:<br /> If you use Dominate 5 - Possession on a ghoul, can you use disciplines during that time? If so, yours or the ghouls? Do you use your vitae or theirs? Can you use their vitae to blood buff or heal? Do you project your predator's taint? Do you contest disciplines with your blood potency and mental stats?</div> </div> </div> </div>The power as written in 1st edition and indicated it worked only on mortals. It specifically said it didn't work on kindred but did not mention whether or not mortals included ghouls, mages, werewolves, changelings, as they tended to fall under the &quot;mortals&quot; classification in other references. Using the power was described as a psychic duel (Resolve + Composure + power stat vs the other's pool) over a few turns between the vampire and prospective victim until a victor emerged. That said, It's up to the ST to decide whether or not the power worked. <br /> My group allowed it to work on mages, changelings, werewolves, kinfolk, ghouls, but not prometheans, demons, sin eaters and you could use Dominate or any nonphysical discipline you knew provided you had the vitae in your new body. You could also use the attendant powers of your victim 'if' you know what powers they have. (This was to ensure werewolves and mage players didn't proceed to behave as if the Veil will protect them or Paradox was inapplicable when supernatural powers were flung around in full view of normal people. You never know who all is watching.) <br /> It was rare but not unheard of for high level mages or werewolves to contract a vampire to possess troublesome members, have them burn through their mystic fuels, alienate their allies and strand them in a legal quagmire before returning control.<br /> No predator's taint only registered if a ghoul was possessed (0 BP) mages have spells to detect possession, which would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-21-2021, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T22:29:08-07:00","id":1460790,"title":"","content":"So basically there's no FAQ or stated intent anywhere and it's just up to your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T00:40:14-07:00","id":1460802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1460790#post1460790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically there's no FAQ or stated intent anywhere and it's just up to your ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlike Onyx Path, White Wolf did publish an errata document for VtR. Unfortunately it doesn't say anything about your questions. It says that the line giving a +2 bonus against those whose share a blood tie should be removed, presumably because it could never be applied since vampires are always immune.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T09:19:16-07:00","id":1460853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1460790#post1460790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically there's no FAQ or stated intent anywhere and it's just up to your ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>No not using the 1st edition version. The next closest power one could reference for guidance would be the 4th level of Animalism (1st edition) as it allowed the user to possess an animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-22-2021, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T18:51:41-07:00","id":1461900,"title":"","content":"Few questions on touchstones? Does a website or a friend you onlly knoow olnline Count as a touchstone?<br /> <br /> With object Touch stones what counts as a scene of significant interaction with a touch stone<br /> <br /> sharpening a sword Reading the bible The prince or Uncle toms Cabin. Praying at a Kamidana<br /> <br /> Not sure what youd do with a Maneki Neko. Ideas?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If its a janitor you see on the way when going back to your own domicile. Is saying 'hello&quot; Enough?<br /> Cam a vampire with no touchstones left regain them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T19:27:45-07:00","id":1461905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1461900#post1461900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Few questions on touchstones? Does a website or a friend you onlly knoow olnline Count as a touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the requisite emotional investment, sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With object Touch stones what counts as a scene of significant interaction with a touch stone </div> </div> </div>Something you could build a scene around. As points of vulnerability and storyhook generators, an object or place that reminds you of your humanity should be engaged with enough that something could conceivably come up to endanger that relationship you have with it, whether it's your Gutenberg Bible needing rebound or the city planning to bulldoze your childhood home.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If its a janitor you see on the way when going back to your own domicile. Is saying 'hello&quot; Enough? </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cam a vampire with no touchstones left regain them. </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","a