erid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T08:08:27-07:00","id":1463314,"title":"","content":"Does it say anywhere that a Revenant doesnt &quot;Un-Natturally&quot; wake from torpor They have to be fed Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T08:33:42-07:00","id":1465143,"title":"","content":"I created an account just to get satisfaction for this one question:<br /> <br /> What is the Yagnatia logo supposed to be? I see a face with a sharp chin, a big mustache, and bushy eyebrows. I showed it to my girlfriend, though, and she saw uterine imagery - the eyebrows were ovaries. What was the intention? Does anyone know?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Second question: is it possible, without using any disciplines, to feed from a sleeping person and not wake them up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27139,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27139-chevaliermalfet","user":"ChevalierMalFet","date":".  I had a second question I wanted to ask and didn't want to make another post. 10-24-2021, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27139-chevaliermalfet","name":"ChevalierMalFet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T10:08:48-07:00","id":1465153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1461961#post1461961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just praying at a kamidana or playing a video game syst em probaly isnt enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the action, but how much time and effort you dedicate to it. If you spend hours praying/playing, cleaning, making maintenance, etc, then sure, it counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T21:54:38-07:00","id":1465242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChevalierMalFet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1465143#post1465143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I created an account just to get satisfaction for this one question:<br /> <br /> What is the Yagnatia logo supposed to be? I see a face with a sharp chin, a big mustache, and bushy eyebrows. I showed it to my girlfriend, though, and she saw uterine imagery - the eyebrows were ovaries. What was the intention? Does anyone know?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked the original author about this once, and he was as baffled as you are. The mustache face is almost impossible not to see, but I think your GF's theory is pretty good. It would kind of make sense considering their weakness was infertility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChevalierMalFet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1465143#post1465143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: Second question: is it possible, without using any disciplines, to feed from a sleeping person and not wake them up?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the underlying assumption is that the Kiss is pleasurable enough that your victim won't just bolt up and start screaming, but it's more a narrative choice than a mechanics one. At worst, they dismiss anything they might remember as a weird, sexy dream. That said, with enough sudden blood loss, you probably won't really feel like waking up anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 10-25-2021, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T00:08:03-07:00","id":1465246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1465242#post1465242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I asked the original author about this once, and he was as baffled as you are. The mustache face is almost impossible not to see, but I think your GF's theory is pretty good. It would kind of make sense considering their weakness was infertility.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense, actually, along with their female leadership.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1465242#post1465242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the underlying assumption is that the Kiss is pleasurable enough that your victim won't just bolt up and start screaming, but it's more a narrative choice than a mechanics one. At worst, they dismiss anything they might remember is a weird, sexy dream. That said, with enough sudden blood loss, you probably won't really feel like waking up anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see! I'm trying to put together a one-shot for a few of my friends and relations, none of whom have played Vampire before and need pre-made characters, and I was brainstorming about different ways of regular feeding. (To me, &quot;how do you keep on top of your blood needs&quot; is a really important question.) Someone had the idea of owning a hotel, or having a ghoul that owns a hotel, and you go from room to room at night with the skeleton key. The goal would be a perfect sneak-feed, without needing to use Dominate to cover it up afterwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27139-chevaliermalfet","name":"ChevalierMalFet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T03:11:33-07:00","id":1465258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChevalierMalFet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1465246#post1465246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes a lot of sense, actually, along with their female leadership.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I see! I'm trying to put together a one-shot for a few of my friends and relations, none of whom have played Vampire before and need pre-made characters, and I was brainstorming about different ways of regular feeding. (To me, &amp;quot;how do you keep on top of your blood needs&amp;quot; is a really important question.) Someone had the idea of owning a hotel, or having a ghoul that owns a hotel, and you go from room to room at night with the skeleton key. The goal would be a perfect sneak-feed, without needing to use Dominate to cover it up afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a really solid concept! Honestly, I find the best way to approach these things as an ST is to just let them work\u2026until they don\u2019t. Then the dice come out. Presumably the hotel system is tried and true, but tonight, somehow, something goes very wrong.<br /> <br /> And of course, if someone\u2019s got a few dots of Herd, that\u2019s a great mechanical justification for why the hotel method works so well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T10:51:31-07:00","id":1465297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChevalierMalFet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1465246#post1465246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see! I'm trying to put together a one-shot for a few of my friends and relations, none of whom have played Vampire before and need pre-made characters, and I was brainstorming about different ways of regular feeding. (To me, &quot;how do you keep on top of your blood needs&quot; is a really important question.) Someone had the idea of owning a hotel, or having a ghoul that owns a hotel, and you go from room to room at night with the skeleton key. The goal would be a perfect sneak-feed, without needing to use Dominate to cover it up afterwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fine concept, but I think it should be kept in mind that Requiem's general concept runs on the idea that vampires don't need to be super elaborate about covering up their feeding so long as they aren't really obvious and public about it.<br /> <br /> If a vampire feeds on somebody with sufficient privacy and intimacy, they can rely on something between &quot;the person doesn't fully recognise that the skin has been broken and blood is being drawn (helped by no visible wound afterwards)&quot; and &quot;the person does recognise it, but pretends that they don't, because this is too much of a good thing even if it is a bit messed up, and hey, vampires don't exist, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't need memory erasing magic, just a context in which people can have plausible deniability or a bit of rationalisation to avoid acknowledging that they're in a dysfunctional situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T15:53:59-07:00","id":1465445,"title":"","content":"The way celerity is written has me confused for dodging. Id have assumed since it adds to your defense that you would just dodge as if your defense was one higher and therefore grant two dice to the dodge. However, the way it is written sounds like it adds only 1 to your defense per dot, but when you dodge, it doesnt multiply by two the defense granted by celerity. Essentially a guy with 3 defense and 2 celerity would have 5 defense against normal attacks, 2 defense against firearm attacks, and only 8 dice on a dodge since it would be (3x2)+2. Is this correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T16:48:49-07:00","id":1465450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1465297#post1465297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]<br /> If a vampire feeds on somebody with sufficient privacy and intimacy, they can rely on something between &quot;the person doesn't fully recognise that the skin has been broken and blood is being drawn (helped by no visible wound afterwards)&quot; and &quot;the person does recognise it, but pretends that they don't, because this is too much of a good thing even if it is a bit messed up, and hey, vampires don't exist, right?&quot;<br /> [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the privacy that I'm going for. The idea is that if the vampire only takes a single Vitae from the victim, then the victim doesn't have to rely on rationalizations and can deny it entirely - it'd be easy enough to simply think, &quot;I was alone and asleep the whole night, and that's the end of it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27139-chevaliermalfet","name":"ChevalierMalFet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T17:28:10-07:00","id":1465453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1465445#post1465445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way celerity is written has me confused for dodging. Id have assumed since it adds to your defense that you would just dodge as if your defense was one higher and therefore grant two dice to the dodge. However, the way it is written sounds like it adds only 1 to your defense per dot, but when you dodge, it doesnt multiply by two the defense granted by celerity. Essentially a guy with 3 defense and 2 celerity would have 5 defense against normal attacks, 2 defense against firearm attacks, and only 8 dice on a dodge since it would be (3x2)+2. Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire Rules FAQ</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How are Defense and Dodge calculated with Celerity?</b><br /> <br /> <b>Defense: \u200b</b>((lower of Wits or Dexterity) + Athletics + Celerity)<br /> <br /> <b>Dodge: </b>\u200b(2 * ((lower of Wits or Dexterity) + Athletics + Celerity))<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You do indeed double it. The book just uses some poor phrasing. In your scenario, you'd have 10 dice to dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T03:50:27-08:00","id":1467037,"title":"","content":"In half damned it mentions that biological ghoul families age slower, have blood bonds and don't require the same &quot;constant&quot; supply of vitae to maintain their limited immortality.<br /> <br /> My question is, is this expanded on or defined at all? How much slower do they age? Do they start with a stage 3 blood bond? Do they need less than the standard 1 per month of vitae to maintain themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T08:14:12-08:00","id":1467051,"title":"","content":"I don't think it was developped in the pages properly ? I've read it recently and I'm pretty sure it was left to the appreciation of the GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T12:39:24-08:00","id":1467090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1467051#post1467051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it was developped in the pages properly ? I've read it recently and I'm pretty sure it was left to the appreciation of the GM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, darn at least that explains why I can't track down more than a offhand mention","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T12:46:42-08:00","id":1467094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1467090#post1467090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, darn at least that explains why I can't track down more than a offhand mention</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you have to read between the lines for this info, and it's scattered between the core and <b>Half-Damned</b>, but basically, bio ghoul families operate like this:<br /> <br /> They have a max natural lifespan of 150 years, and tend to age about half as fast once they hit adulthood (that last bit is based on some first edition material, but it holds true for the current edition's descriptions).<br /> <br /> They don't rapidly age when they lose their Vitae sources<br /> <br /> They can buy and use Disciplines without Kindred aid, but only the common ones (Animalism, Obfuscate, and the physical powers) unless they have special access to a clan Discipline as their benefit or have a regnant.<br /> <br /> They get Unseen Sense: Vampires for free.<br /> <br /> They have an inherent addiction to vampire blood, and if their family has a regnant, they're born with a full blood bond to her.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, they work like normal ghouls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-07-2021, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T00:10:22-08:00","id":1467238,"title":"","content":"When a vampire loses his Touchstone by losing a dot of Humanity (from 6 to 5), must he buy a Touchstone merit dot to be able to establish a new Touchstone, or he may just find another one by roleplay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 11-09-2021, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T00:36:33-08:00","id":1467241,"title":"","content":"There are <i>two</i> separate things that can happen to disrupt a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> One is that the Touchstone can be <i>detached.</i> This is what happens when your Humanity drops below the Touchstone rating. It's still your Touchstone, can still restore Willpower, but no longer provides a bonus to resist Humanity detachment. This is merely the point where your relationship is not sufficient to stem your growing alienation. In your example scenario, you are at Humanity 5, but you still have a Humanity 6 Touchstone. If your Humanity increases back to 6, your Humanity 6 Touchstone reattaches and once again provides its bonus to resist breaking points.<br /> <br /> The other is that the Touchstone can be <i>lost.</i> This is what happens when the person dies or you have a desperate argument bad enough to entirely destroy the relationship. When this occurs, the Touchstone is removed from your Humanity track. If the Touchstone was an additional one added by the Touchstone Merit, that Merit dot is refunded per Sanctity of Merits.<br /> <br /> If the lost Touchstone was the <i>last</i> Touchstone remaining on your Humanity track, you approach a crisis as detailed on page 88 of the corebook. You may either suffer a loss of Humanity, in which case you have a month in which to develop a new relationship into a replacement Touchstone. This is separate from the Touchstone Merit, which is for having two or more Touchstones. If you refuse the loss of Humanity or can't find a new Touchstone within a month, you fall Languid and will soon enter torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T02:11:36-08:00","id":1467246,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much! Cool!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T12:30:58-08:00","id":1467279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1467241#post1467241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are <i>two</i> separate things that can happen to disrupt a Touchstone.<br /> <br /> One is that the Touchstone can be <i>detached.</i> This is what happens when your Humanity drops below the Touchstone rating. It's still your Touchstone, can still restore Willpower</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that for certain? I always assumed you can't regain Willpower from detached Touchstones because of this wording:<br /> <br /> &quot;Any time the vampire defends her <i>attachment </i>to her Touchstone...&quot;<br /> <br /> That and because you can have multiple ones, you can always get more if you lose access to that Willpower source. However, that Touchstone section is a famously opaque with its phrasing, so I'm more than happy to be wrong on this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T13:41:18-08:00","id":1467288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1467279#post1467279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that for certain? I always assumed you can't regain Willpower from detached Touchstones because of this wording:<br /> <br /> &quot;Any time the vampire defends her <i>attachment </i>to her Touchstone...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I simply took it to be the more coherent reading to assume &quot;attachment&quot; here is not the mechanical term but the plain language for connection or relationship. That's not ironclad, of course, but your mechanical &quot;attachment&quot; to a Touchstone is just how high your Humanity is, so if it meant mechanically attached I assumed it would use different language than &quot;defend your attachment.&quot; There are a number of other benefits to interacting with a Touchstone that don't care whether it's mechanically attached, and knowing that Requiem was written on the assumption that vampires don't regain Willpower from sleep, linking falling Humanity to loss of Willpower Anchors strikes me as extra harsh.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T13:46:27-08:00","id":1467289,"title":"","content":"Here I'm with Yossarin. I've alsways interpreted that detachment from a Touchstone means it doesn't means for you too much. You can still love, caring (although a Touchstone can also be your worst enemy) of her/it but it is nothing more than another beloved mortal/object.<br /> <br /> Touchstone is not what you love, but what keep you bound to your humanity. Losing the attachment to me means you lose all the benefits (and malus as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-09-2021, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T13:53:20-08:00","id":1467291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1467288#post1467288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I simply took it to be the more coherent reading to assume &quot;attachment&quot; here is not the mechanical term but the plain language for connection or relationship. That's not ironclad, of course, but your mechanical &quot;attachment&quot; to a Touchstone is just how high your Humanity is, so if it meant mechanically attached I assumed it would use different language than &quot;defend your attachment.&quot; There are a number of other benefits to interacting with a Touchstone that don't care whether it's mechanically attached, and knowing that Requiem was written on the assumption that vampires don't regain Willpower from sleep, linking falling Humanity to loss of Willpower Anchors strikes me as extra harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it both ways, honestly. I think you're <i>probably </i>right, because usually the book will specify in cases like that, but that Touchstone section really is hard to parse if you don't read it carefully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T15:19:53-08:00","id":1467294,"title":"","content":"For comparison's sake, I'll point to\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2022 Werewolf. whose section on regaining Willpower from Touchstones doesn't use the word &quot;attachment&quot; at all, but whose Touchstones are much more firmly attached;<br /> \u2022 Changeling, where detached Touchstones specifically can't provide Willpower but reattaching Touchstones is a matter of spending enough scenes of meaningful interaction to unmark severe damage from the relevant Clarity box;<br /> \u2022 Hunter, which specifies defending the character's relationship to an attached Touchstone;<br /> \u2022 and Deviant's closest equivalent, affirming a Wavering Touchstone, doesn't say if it's a choice you can opt out of, but you specifically don't get Willpower from doing the sort of thing that would get you Willpower if you do affirm a Wavering Touchstone.<br /> <br /> I think it's just down to Vampire being the first line to use Touchstones and having the Predatory Aura available to farm mortals for Willpower through the Inspired Condition to supplement their Masks and Dirges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T19:00:49-08:00","id":1467844,"title":"","content":"How does arthmoic surgery (False Gods: Ventrue) apply to your Retainers/ghouls etc...<br /> <br /> It says the merits for arthmoic surgery, are purchased by the victim:<br /> <br /> &quot;The patient must purchase the Procedure Merit to gain its advantages; the doctor does not&quot;<br /> <br /> So, if you as a kindred surgically improve your retainer, how does the NPC pay the cost? Or do you just get the benefit of a retainer, enhanced by your surgery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24946-mr_stick","user":"Mr_Stick","date":". 11-14-2021, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24946-mr_stick","name":"Mr_Stick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T23:45:06-08:00","id":1467974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr_Stick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1467844#post1467844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does arthmoic surgery (False Gods: Ventrue) apply to your Retainers/ghouls etc...<br /> <br /> It says the merits for arthmoic surgery, are purchased by the victim:<br /> <br /> &quot;The patient must purchase the Procedure Merit to gain its advantages; the doctor does not&quot;<br /> <br /> So, if you as a kindred surgically improve your retainer, how does the NPC pay the cost? Or do you just get the benefit of a retainer, enhanced by your surgery?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because NPCs don't track Experiences, they just have it, unless the Storyteller wants to add a barrier of entry. Arthmoic Procedures work similar to Invictus Oaths, in that the cost for the Surgeon (i.e., the liege) is largely a role-playing one. You go out and convince / coerce a subject into undergoing a procedure, and you reap a benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-16-2021, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T00:12:45-08:00","id":1468239,"title":"","content":"The answer is probably no but,<br /> could an Invictus Notary be the witness of an oath in which he is also the vassal or liege?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T05:26:10-08:00","id":1468257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468239#post1468239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer is probably no but,<br /> could an Invictus Notary be the witness of an oath in which he is also the vassal or liege?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the notary is the witness. And if they are the only notary in the domain, that's likely to be inevitable. Invictus oaths don't automatically require the voluntary consent of participants or even the presence of a notary but if you're talking about the stereotypical description of an Invictus member dedicated to protocols and projecting the illusion that such contracts are above board, there is likely to be a rule requiring an uninvolved 3rd party to ensure the contract doesn't entail a non-Invictus supernaturally coercing the Invictus member into a vassal role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T05:48:19-08:00","id":1468259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468257#post1468257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically the notary is the witness. And if they are the only notary in the domain, that's likely to be inevitable. Invictus oaths don't automatically require the voluntary consent of participants or even the presence of a notary but if you're talking about the stereotypical description of an Invictus member dedicated to protocols and projecting the illusion that such contracts are above board, there is likely to be a rule requiring an uninvolved 3rd party to ensure the contract doesn't entail a non-Invictus supernaturally coercing the Invictus member into a vassal role.</div> </div> </div> </div>My doubts are mostly about an Invictus prince who is also a Notary.<br /> The next available Notary is a vassal of him, but she lives in a distant city.<br /> It s allowed for the Prince to take Oaths with himself as the liege and also the Notary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T06:11:21-08:00","id":1468262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468259#post1468259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My doubts are mostly about an Invictus prince who is also a Notary.<br /> The next available Notary is a vassal of him, but she lives in a distant city.<br /> It s allowed for the Prince to take Oaths with himself as the liege and also the Notary?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's not prohibited. The only thing that's expressly prohibited is an Invictus member cannot be cosigned into the vassal role in an oath where the liege is a non Invictus member or the inclusion of non-kindred as a participants in any capacity. However, there is no opposed roll or check or &quot;the oath automatically fails if those prohibitions are ignored&quot; feature. The consequences are purely in-game only. An Invictus notary who includes non- Kindred or binds an Invictus member as vassal to a non-Invictus member may be stripped of their position or killed. An Invictus prince who abuses the notary position will inevitably lose the support of his covenant and thus his praxis. Alternatively, if the Invictus functions as a regional power bloc he may be subject to Final Death reprisal from the Invictus in another domain.<br /> <br /> I imagine in such a scenario, the Prince probably has his seneschal act as witness and the prospective vassal brings one as well, just for the sake of public formality. But they could just as easily meet, just the two of them in some back alley, swear it and it's done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 11-18-2021, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T09:23:22-08:00","id":1468352,"title":"","content":"I have a question regarding vampire healing, I have never found myself into a situation where an opponent managed to fill my last dot with lethal but still I would like to know, what happens in that case? The vampire gets to reflexively spend blood to heal (if he has any) or he fall straight into torpor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T09:53:35-08:00","id":1468354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468352#post1468352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question regarding vampire healing, I have never found myself into a situation where an opponent managed to fill my last dot with lethal but still I would like to know, what happens in that case? The vampire gets to reflexively spend blood to heal (if he has any) or he fall straight into torpor?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<b>At the end of a vampire\u2019s turn</b>, after any reflexive healing,<br /> if her last (rightmost) Health box is filled with lethal damage,<br /> she falls to torpor.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T11:04:59-08:00","id":1468357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468352#post1468352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question regarding vampire healing, I have never found myself into a situation where an opponent managed to fill my last dot with lethal but still I would like to know, what happens in that case? The vampire gets to reflexively spend blood to heal (if he has any) or he fall straight into torpor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. If, before your turn is over, you can't use blood to heal up at least one health box, the vampire fall in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T11:16:41-08:00","id":1468358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468357#post1468357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. If, before your turn is over, you can't use blood to heal up at least one health box, the vampire fall in torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So the fact that healing is a reflexive action means that I could do it even if my turn has passed? like if I acted in my turn and then the opponend filled me to lethal on his turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T11:30:41-08:00","id":1468359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468358#post1468358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So the fact that healing is a reflexive action means that I could do it even if my turn has passed? like if I acted in my turn and then the opponend filled me to lethal on his turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you see a turn as including all the actions from each involved actor, then yes, you can act, being damaged, and then healing up (if you still can spend blood), as healing up is reflexive. You can do whatever amount of reflexive actions in a same turn and at any time of that turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T11:37:07-08:00","id":1468361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468359#post1468359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you see a turn as including all the actions from each involved actor, then yes, you can act, being damaged, and then healing up (if you still can spend blood), as healing up is reflexive. You can do whatever amount of reflexive actions in a same turn and at any time of that turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T19:25:27-08:00","id":1468379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468358#post1468358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the fact that healing is a reflexive action means that I could do it even if my turn has passed? like if I acted in my turn and then the opponend filled me to lethal on his turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you pay attention to the RAW posted by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> it is actually a delayed effect, which makes some sense for an undead.<br /> <br /> Lethal doesn't cause instant torpor, it <i>only happens at the end of the vampire's turn</i>. So if the vampire suffers this damage outside its own turn, by RAW it has an action still before falling into torpor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T06:25:19-08:00","id":1468395,"title":"","content":"Which unfortunately leads to the situation where a vampire either needs to have no more Vitae in their Vitae pool, or have hit their Vitae per turn limit, to be forced into torpor and not keep on fighting. Considering that torpor from violence almost always means you're at the mercy of your enemies (which, in-character, should be extremely feared even if the players knows the ST won't off the PCs like that), a lot of fights between BP3+ vampires (who're less likely to hit their per turn cap) are to the death. If the attack is after the vampire's initiative in the global turn order, you can't even force torpor from the per turn limit since they refresh that limit before their personal turn has started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T06:37:33-08:00","id":1468396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468395#post1468395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which unfortunately leads to the situation where a vampire either needs to have no more Vitae in their Vitae pool, or have hit their Vitae per turn limit, to be forced into torpor and not keep on fighting. Considering that torpor from violence almost always means you're at the mercy of your enemies (which, in-character, should be extremely feared even if the players knows the ST won't off the PCs like that), a lot of fights between BP3+ vampires (who're less likely to hit their per turn cap) are to the death. If the attack is after the vampire's initiative in the global turn order, you can't even force torpor from the per turn limit since they refresh that limit before their personal turn has started.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right but it also depends on how many lethal damages it deals. Cause you might also not have enough capacity to spend blood to heal up all the damages exceding the last health box. <br /> Dealing 4-5 damages in a hit is not so hard to acomplish and if you are already almost at the limit of your health's boxes it becomes difficult to survive.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I said a bullshit: receiving more lethal/damages then your health bar converts lethal into aggravated so that you still need healing up the rightmost health box to survive (unless you are not being filled with aggravated in one unique hit, which, unless resilience, means death).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-20-2021, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T07:38:31-08:00","id":1468399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468396#post1468396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's right but it also depends on how many lethal damages it deals. Cause you might also not have enough capacity to spend blood to heal up all the damages exceding the last health box.<br /> Dealing 4-5 damages in a hit is not so hard to acomplish and if you are already almost at the limit of your health's boxes it becomes difficult to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As an aside, i'm now immagining someone with a Obfuscate+Resilience &quot;better play dead&quot; devotion that allows them to fake falling in torpor, healing damage but <i><b>not</b> </i>seeming to do so when they &quot;drop&quot; down in apparent incapacitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T07:42:52-08:00","id":1468401,"title":"","content":"Let's say you have quite a few vanilla strategies to gain time to heal up, such us Protean 1 and Primeval miasma.<br /> If you play smart you can find a workaround to survive enough.<br /> <br /> Edit: by the way I said a bullshit in my previous post: receiving more lethal/damages then your health bar converts lethal into aggravated so that you still need healing up the rightmost health box to survive (unless you are not being filled with aggravated in one unique hit, which, unless resilience, means death).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-20-2021, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T07:51:16-08:00","id":1468403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468395#post1468395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which unfortunately leads to the situation where a vampire either needs to have no more Vitae in their Vitae pool, or have hit their Vitae per turn limit, to be forced into torpor and not keep on fighting. Considering that torpor from violence almost always means you're at the mercy of your enemies (which, in-character, should be extremely feared even if the players knows the ST won't off the PCs like that), a lot of fights between BP3+ vampires (who're less likely to hit their per turn cap) are to the death.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're to the death if the intent is to kill someone, but the mechanics for Beaten Down and surrender are applicable to any vampire with Humanity over 2 who hasn't taken a Bane to remove murder as a breaking point. The violence rules start with intent for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T08:02:06-08:00","id":1468404,"title":"","content":"I played a game of werewolf once where the prey was a daeva cult leader that was encroaching in the pack territory, it was the only werewolf game (and one of the most difficult) I had where the prey was a vampire. long story short, after killing all of her followers, we found out that the daeva wasn't the smoking hot blonde that was giving the orders but her right hand man who ended up dealing 3 aggravated to our Ithaeur with an assault rifle before being flung out of a window. The ST told us that he went into torpor but none of us ever figured that he was a vampire until the survivor of the cult took him and got away, I think that for torpor to be really dangerous, the ones who put you into it have to be aware that you are a vampire otherwise you would just look like a corpse (especially with blush of life) which is not a given since vampires are very apt at hiding their nature, I mean werewolves could have find out but since not all of them even met a vampire in the first place (an excuse for us not doing our homework really), thats not a given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T09:21:11-08:00","id":1468406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468403#post1468403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're to the death if the intent is to kill someone, but the mechanics for Beaten Down and surrender are applicable to any vampire with Humanity over 2 who hasn't taken a Bane to remove murder as a breaking point. The violence rules start with intent for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an optional system so not something that I think should be considered to be in use by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468404#post1468404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that for torpor to be really dangerous, the ones who put you into it have to be aware that you are a vampire otherwise you would just look like a corpse (especially with blush of life)</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, vampires mostly faces other vampires or humans in combat. Humans who don't know much about vampires or even that vampires exist are going to have a really a tough time putting the vampire in a losing position in the first place. Vampires are the second most resilient and second most combat proficient splat after werewolves in terms of both innate abilities and commonly developed abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T09:49:33-08:00","id":1468407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468406#post1468406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an optional system so not something that I think should be considered to be in use by default.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, vampires mostly faces other vampires or humans in combat. Humans who don't know much about vampires or even that vampires exist are going to have a really a tough time putting the vampire in a losing position in the first place. Vampires are the second most resilient and second most combat proficient splat after werewolves in terms of both innate abilities and commonly developed abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lucky roll is always a possibility and also the fact that some splats (like werewolves) are capable of dealing a lot of lethal damage in a turn, If I were a storyteller I would justify my players surviving torpor with the excuse that their opponent didn't know that they were a vampire or weren't knoleadgeable enough about them to know about torpor, afterall, If you manage to tear a vampire in half or blow their head off and it stopped moving, you would assume that they were death, unless you knew how vampires functions, which is again not a given even for werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T13:37:23-08:00","id":1468421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468406#post1468406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an optional system so not something that I think should be considered to be in use by default.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Beaten Down and Surrender is optional. Intent is not. Intent should not always include murder, and making Intent clear on both sides can help encourage surrender/fleeing over fights to the death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T15:06:35-08:00","id":1468429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468421#post1468421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beaten Down and Surrender is optional. Intent is not. Intent should not always include murder, and making Intent clear on both sides can help encourage surrender/fleeing over fights to the death.</div> </div> </div> </div>That.<br /> <br /> Intent should be the first consideration at the beginning of combat in any RPG, because the idea that every combat is to the death just because the opponent must stop moving is dumb. Defeat isn't that.<br /> <br /> Any vampire who start their turn having to heal to avoid torpor knows that things aren't ok. Why burn more resources in a fight you already knows you're likely to loose and risk death? No rule is needed for the character to accept this is a good time for surrender, and other gracefully accept it.<br /> <br /> Even more if you play the social aspect of it. People who push the envelope on violence get a reputation for it, nut this is frequently just a reputation as a dangerous asshole. Even in ancient warfare this was actually an attitude to avoid, not to indulge, and the few occasions of indulgence are historically relevant precisely because of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T08:37:00-08:00","id":1468501,"title":"","content":"Isn't it a mistake that Enfeebling Aura being the Devotion of 2 dots of Disciplines total costs 3 Experiences instead of 1? For it doesn't look overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","user":"Aleksay","date":". 11-21-2021, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T12:18:03-08:00","id":1468515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468501#post1468501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it a mistake that Enfeebling Aura being the Devotion of 2 dots of Disciplines total costs 3 Experiences instead of 1? For it doesn't look overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the rule of thumb at the start of the section, it should be 2 Experiences at most (you can bump up the price by one if the effect is broadly useful). Honestly, 2 seems about right for that one; it's very good inherently, but you need to have decent stats for it to be really effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T19:52:44-08:00","id":1468886,"title":"","content":"Do you actually have to take blood in order to use the Kiss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T04:02:59-08:00","id":1468966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468886#post1468886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you actually have to take blood in order to use the Kiss?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the impression I got at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T05:56:55-08:00","id":1468976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dragon must know of a <b>supernatural ability</b> possessed by the subject, and choose a body part symbolic of that skill. </div> </div> </div>Are there any limits on kinds of supernatual abilities which can be taken by this Scale of Zirnitra? Because the wording is <b>extremely</b> vague, and I've seen people argue that, for example, Werewolf Gifts or Mage's Arcana is one &quot;ability&quot; for the purposes of this ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T14:42:43-08:00","id":1469021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1468976#post1468976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any limits on kinds of supernatual abilities which can be taken by this Scale of Zirnitra? Because the wording is <b>extremely</b> vague, and I've seen people argue that, for example, Werewolf Gifts or Mage's Arcana is one &quot;ability&quot; for the purposes of this ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's mostly meant to be Supernatural Merits that only humans can take, but I believe any quality that apply to &quot;minor&quot; templates also count, if applicable. So, you could take Wolf-Blooded and Proxima powers (<i>if </i>your character had those things in her lineage), but you couldn't take Changeling Contracts or Promethean Transmutations. You couldn't learn Arcana because you don't have Gnosis, for instance, though a Proximus could learn a &quot;spell.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T14:47:09-08:00","id":1469023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1469021#post1469021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mostly meant to be Supernatural Merits that only humans can take, but I believe any quality that apply to &quot;minor&quot; templates also count, if applicable. So, you could take Wolf-Blooded and Proxima powers (<i>if </i>your character had those things in her lineage), but you couldn't take Changeling Contracts or Promethean Transmutations. You couldn't learn Arcana because you don't have Gnosis, for instance, though a Proximus could learn a &quot;spell.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking about the base Coil. Dark Archon is talking about the Scale, Grafting Unholy Flesh, which <b>specifically</b> works on other supers, and even has a way to handle fuel traits other than WP and Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T18:13:26-08:00","id":1469053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1469023#post1469023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're talking about the base Coil. Dark Archon is talking about the Scale, Grafting Unholy Flesh, which <b>specifically</b> works on other supers, and even has a way to handle fuel traits other than WP and Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Serves me right for skimming.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T06:32:02-08:00","id":1470845,"title":"","content":"Animalism 2 allows the vampire to have a loyal animal companion (as long as the vampire continues paying the vitae cost).<br /> <br /> If a player would decide that he wishes to have the same 2 dogs (animal companions) by his side using animalism 2 through the campaign, how would you define it through a character sheet ?<br /> <br /> Would you ask the player to have a few dots in retainer (although looking by the rules, each dog would be a 4-5 dot retainer), or would simply asking additional vitae tax at the beginning of a session suffice (the upkeep price) ?<br /> <br /> <br /> My main concern is that the retainer merit (as described in the core book of 2nd edition) does not suit well for pets, or in this case blood infused zombie pets.<br /> <br /> <br /> I personally would just make a custom merit Pack at a single dot, and ask the player to get 2 dots in it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T08:42:51-08:00","id":1470858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1470845#post1470845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a player would decide that he wishes to have the same 2 dogs (animal companions) by his side using animalism 2 through the campaign, how would you define it through a character sheet ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing at all barring it from Animalism alone, and it is the whole effect of a level two Discipline, why does you want to ask for more?<br /> <br /> As it stand, the Discipline upkeep alone is more than enough to cover your bases, it already cost as much as a level 5 Merit, IIRC. If the player <i>wants</i> more benefits, then you could have a custom Merit to represent those dogs and increase their effectiveness/protection.<br /> <br /> One idea is to have a 1-dot Merit for the specific Familiar to be able to raise easier and get 1 more dot in a Mental attribute of your choice. Raising easier could be an ability to spend the upkeep eve from a distance, willing the animal back to life. That will make those dogs far more reliable without being far more powerful, and at the very least protect them with the Sanctity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T12:48:51-08:00","id":1470874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1470858#post1470858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing at all barring it from Animalism alone, and it is the whole effect of a level two Discipline, why does you want to ask for more?<br /> <br /> As it stand, the Discipline upkeep alone is more than enough to cover your bases, it already cost as much as a level 5 Merit, IIRC. If the player <i>wants</i> more benefits, then you could have a custom Merit to represent those dogs and increase their effectiveness/protection.<br /> <br /> One idea is to have a 1-dot Merit for the specific Familiar to be able to raise easier and get 1 more dot in a Mental attribute of your choice. Raising easier could be an ability to spend the upkeep eve from a distance, willing the animal back to life. That will make those dogs far more reliable without being far more powerful, and at the very least protect them with the Sanctity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, thanks for the reply !<br /> <br /> I do agree with you on this, that the discipline itself gives you that benefit. What made me doubt my self was an idea of vinculum. If I would have a tier 3 vinculum on a mortal I would probably want to get a retainer merit at some point, or if I would use dominate 4 devotion (I think it's called dementation) to create a few servants. My trail of though was the powers allow me to have access to these things, but by spending experience I want to ensure that these NPCS are part of my character and will be available when I need them instead of just being a one ofs.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand I am spending a big pile experience just on the discipline, I might as well get it's bonuses.<br /> <br /> I hope I expressed my thought process clear. And I do personally think that not having a merit but I also want to make sure that rules are applied here correctly.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Just to add another example. If a player would use majesty 2 on a cop to help him out, there would be no need for any additional exp cost. But if the player would call the same cop over and over again and use majesty, maybe at some point he should get an allies/retainer merit .<br /> <br /> A same example with the dogs. If when the problem rises a player would just find a dog and use Animalism 2, all is well. But if he wishes to keep those animals by his side, maybe they should be represented some how.<br /> <br /> I would like to hear more of your opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I could be in a totally wrong here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1013,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","user":"Stralos","date":". 12-19-2021, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T13:31:10-08:00","id":1470876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1470874#post1470874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, thanks for the reply !<br /> <br /> I do agree with you on this, that the discipline itself gives you that benefit. What made me doubt my self was an idea of vinculum. If I would have a tier 3 vinculum on a mortal I would probably want to get a retainer merit at some point, or if I would use dominate 4 devotion (I think it's called dementation) to create a few servants. My trail of though was the powers allow me to have access to these things, but by spending experience I want to ensure that these NPCS are part of my character and will be available when I need them instead of just being a one ofs.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand I am spending a big pile experience just on the discipline, I might as well get it's bonuses.<br /> <br /> I hope I expressed my thought process clear. And I do personally think that not having a merit but I also want to make sure that rules are applied here correctly.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Just to add another example. If a player would use majesty 2 on a cop to help him out, there would be no need for any additional exp cost. But if the player would call the same cop over and over again and use majesty, maybe at some point he should get an allies/retainer merit .<br /> <br /> A same example with the dogs. If when the problem rises a player would just find a dog and use Animalism 2, all is well. But if he wishes to keep those animals by his side, maybe they should be represented some how.<br /> <br /> I would like to hear more of your opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I could be in a totally wrong here</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Merits are fluid. A representation of what you could or can achieve by roleplaying most of the time.<br /> Disciplines allow you to obtain something and that's should suffice to obtain the effect they describe without investing more xp. <br /> As per your examples:<br /> <br /> you raise 2 dogs with animalism 2, you have them as long you can pay the cost. This would lead the player to also consider them as a duty not only as an advantage. You must be there for them when needed.<br /> <br /> Dominate 4 changes memories so not sure what you are talking about. Might you mean the devotion which inflict the subservient condition?<br /> <br /> Majesty 2 make a cop cooperate with you for a defined amount of time. Then you need to either place a more durable bound (Vinculum) or to always recall him with the possibility the cop become aware about something wrong with you.<br /> <br /> I personally track acquired servant as MERIT* with no XP cost. You create a full bond with the cop? The you can write down Ally* 1 or 2. The * mean this merit has been acquired by pure roleplaying with no XP investment, hence it's not covered by the Santicity of merit - when you lose it you lose it. Otherwise the player can invest XP to buy Ally 2, describing how, and then the merit is &quot;santified&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T14:34:35-08:00","id":1470883,"title":"","content":"Merits, to me, are about providing a specific mechanical effect attached to a specific narrative. Allies lets you get favors of a particular severity from a particular group every particular amount of time without a roll. This is not the same as Majesty or Dominate letting you get one specific cop to do something for you when you use your powers on them. It is an advantage over and above having this option.<br /> <br /> A Merit does not need to exist where it does not provide any given mechanical effect attached to a specific narrative; they do not have to exist only to bookmark something as important. If you are getting all the mechanical benefit you need out of something without a Merit, then a Merit is just an XP tax. This isn't fun or useful.<br /> <br /> More specific to this example:<br /> <br /> Merit to make your ghouled beasts better or cost you less in upkeep: Good. This is what stuff like Swarm Form or Claws of the Unholy do.<br /> Merit that says you have ghouled beasts: Not interesting or helpful. I wouldn't bother. The fact that the player keeps them around and gives them screen time is all they need to be important to the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-19T14:38:35-08:00","id":1470885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1470874#post1470874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, thanks for the reply !</div> </div> </div> </div>Be welcome!<br /> <br /> I understand your worries and they're not completely off, but let me explain this further.<br /> <br /> Despite how we present them, Social Merits actually do not represent a character's relationships and ties to other entities, people and organizations. <b><i>They represent a Player's agency and power over those ties</i></b>. They're about making the tie something the Player can explore in a expected manner and consistently, giving mechanics to the relationship the <u>player</u> can use reliably. That's why they have the Sanctity.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean a relationship can only exist, or endure, if it is a stat in a sheet. It means non-stated relationships aren't under Player control in that same reliable way, <u>unless another rule gives this to them</u>.<br /> <br /> What if a PC controls the same person over and over through the same power? There's nothing wrong with it. <b>The player is still getting out of it what the power gives, but can't expect much beyond that consistently and reliably</b>. This can work very well one night and backfire horribly another, because the only guarantee is whatever the power gave them.<br /> <br /> So yeah, buying the Merits would make this relationship more stable, and would also give the player the degree of agency predicted in the Merit proper, preferably beyond what the power itself gives. Maybe the PC doesn't need to use the power anymore o that person, in character because some twist of fate made the effect permanent on that person, out of character because they're now a Merit.<br /> <br /> Looking now at Animalism 2, the thing is that dogs are extremely simple as characters, standing somewhere in between characters and equipment for our purposes. No matter how much personality you give them, what would their benefit be as Merits? They have good stats, but can't interact with most things as a human can, can't follow complex instructions, can't have their own social connections, can be killed without much repercussion and you can simply buy another one for what their stats are worth. You have a personal attachment to them, but as stats on a sheet they're not much, really.<br /> <br /> On the other hand the power already covers it all. It makes the animal loyal, hard, competent and whatnot. The entire description of what you could want from a stable, permanent connection the power already gives you. What reliable, mechanical benefit can be taken from this relationship that isn't already built in? The only thing missing is the Sanctity, but it isn't worth your sweat over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T06:20:19-08:00","id":1471274,"title":"","content":"I have a question regarding Majesty 1 (Awe).<br /> It states in its description, that: <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">For the rest of the scene, he suffers no penalties to Social rolls from his actions or appearance \u2014 even if he\u2019s just beaten another man to death or waved a gun in a crowded nightclub. Given a chance, he can talk his way out of minor criminal offenses and almost any social faux pas. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does this include the penalties you receive from lower humanity ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T06:59:56-08:00","id":1471276,"title":"","content":"No. It also wouldn't apply to impressions created by prior interactions. But arguably the Humanity penalty wouldn't be applicable because if you're using Majesty, it's no longer a mundane social interaction, which is what Humanity caps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T11:36:17-08:00","id":1471290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471274#post1471274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question regarding Majesty 1 (Awe).<br /> It states in its description, that: <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">For the rest of the scene, he suffers no penalties to Social rolls from his actions or appearance \u2014 even if he\u2019s just beaten another man to death or waved a gun in a crowded nightclub. Given a chance, he can talk his way out of minor criminal offenses and almost any social faux pas. </span><br /> <br /> Does this include the penalties you receive from lower humanity ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, at least as they apply to rolls to relate to humans that are outward-facing \u2014 it won't fix Empathy rolls to read social cues, but it'll definitely ease the process of just making conversation.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu benefit greatly from this if they can get a blood donor for the Discipline, but Awe draws attention and their Curse still makes any Social failures go extra badly regardless of the scale of penalty in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T13:12:55-08:00","id":1471295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471276#post1471276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. It also wouldn't apply to impressions created by prior interactions. But arguably the Humanity penalty wouldn't be applicable because if you're using Majesty, it's no longer a mundane social interaction, which is what Humanity caps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate a bit more, on what do you mean by using Majesy you make it no longer a mundane social interaction ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471290#post1471290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, at least as they apply to rolls to relate to humans that are outward-facing \u2014 it won't fix Empathy rolls to read social cues, but it'll definitely ease the process of just making conversation.<br /> <br /> The Nosferatu benefit greatly from this if they can get a blood donor for the Discipline, but Awe draws attention and their Curse still makes any Social failures go extra badly regardless of the scale of penalty in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought so as well at first, but I imagine if you would use Awe but you would insult someone and try asking for a favour you would still get penalties. After reading this discipline, the initial fluff text looks like an interpretation of how awe works, not part of it's effect. Thoughts ? I'm just trying to figure it out if having 1 dot of majesty is intended game design to reverses all humanity penalties. Thoughts ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T13:48:34-08:00","id":1471298,"title":"","content":"The penalty for lower Humanity is described as follows: &quot;Take a \u2013(whatever) die penalty on any roll to relate to humans.&quot; Guidelines are provided on p. 106:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These modifiers apply to rolls relating to humans. Manipulating humans for food with Subterfuge or frightening them with Intimidation are not affected; but trying to understand a human\u2019s emotional cues with the Empathy Skill would be affected. </div> </div> </div>Humanity penalties aren't inflicted by your &quot;actions or appearance&quot; except in the broadest possible interpretation. They're not external or circumstantial, but internal. They're you not being able to relate to the kine as people and therefore not quite getting the right cues. Awe is circumstantial. It lets you break social mores with impunity, but that doesn't mean you know the right words to successfully relate to people.<br /> I'm voting that Awe doesn't automatically remove the social penalty from low Humanity. The caveat applies that the social penalty is not universal, and a lot of the things you might be doing during Awe are things that wouldn't suffer the penalty in the first place. The penalty is about genuinely connecting with and understanding people. If you're just treating them like tools and food then you often don't really <i>need</i> to connect with or understand them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T14:00:10-08:00","id":1471299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471295#post1471295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought so as well at first, but I imagine if you would use Awe but you would insult someone and try asking for a favour you would still get penalties. After reading this discipline, the initial fluff text looks like an interpretation of how awe works, not part of it's effect. Thoughts ? I'm just trying to figure it out if having 1 dot of majesty is intended game design to reverses all humanity penalties. Thoughts ?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Penalties to Social rolls&quot; are a mechanical effect that the Discipline explicitly negates; Social rolls are rolls made using a Social Attribute and this is the signature Discipline of the &quot;vampire as glamorous and compelling figure&quot; clan.<br /> <br /> The basic power attracts attention \u2014 the Discipline name is <i>Majesty</i> for a reason. The three effects that aren't the penalty negator combine to indicate that the descriptive text is the basis for the mechanical effects; nobody cares what you're doing <i>and</i> you're at the center of attention, meaning you add your Majesty dots to Presence rolls to talk to people around you, subtract them from rolls to notice anything else, can call anyone in the room to you, and ignore penalties for social faux pas. For most characters with a single dot in Majesty, that's the same difference made as in picking up a dot in a Skill you didn't have before, except it only goes that far for Presence rolls where an inability to relate to your food would matter.<br /> <br /> For most vampires that's sufficient for a survival strategy based around having lots of people around paying attention to you instead of keeping yourself out of the public eye, and basically anyone who isn't a Daeva needs a teacher to develop it and probably risks being blood-bonded to learn it. Most vampires whose Curse isn't built around keeping extensive Herds or being a guided missile for your regular meals either put the effort into maintaining their Humanity or make their peace with the price of detachment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-26-2021, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T16:23:17-08:00","id":1471305,"title":"","content":"I'm with Satchel here.<br /> Low Humanity makes the Vampire more alien to humans because he's less inclined to deal with them and more a monster in nature. Penalties related to Humanity are also based on appearance, which is something Awe specifically neglect.<br /> Being a psycho with an ashen pallor, to me seems to be similar - if not better - than beating down someone in front of an audience with the face &quot;caked in shit&quot;, which is exactly what Awe is described to be applicable to.<br /> <br /> Also, there's no order to activate Awe. You can do a deplorable action and then activate Awe to talk your way out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T14:19:00-08:00","id":1471357,"title":"","content":"&quot;Could you elaborate a bit more, on what do you mean by using Majesy you make it no longer a mundane social interaction ?&quot;<br /> <br /> When a vampire activates different levels of Majesty, they are actively impairing others' ability to make basic judgements about how others are permitted to react regardless of visible cues and cripples their ability to discern lies. As the power progresses to higher levels, it further inhibits the victim's ability to make character decisions, forces false impressions upon the victim, makes them susceptible to demands placed on them and at its apex compels subservience. It's a vampire power designed to twist social interactions to the advantage of the user, there's nothing mundane about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 12-27-2021, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T02:13:46-08:00","id":1471481,"title":"","content":"Will Strix take damage in his shadow form, if he is attacked by weapon made out of fire or sunlight, or weapon using fire, like incendiary bullets or flamethrowers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T03:08:44-08:00","id":1471485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471481#post1471481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Strix take damage in his shadow form, if he is attacked by weapon made out of fire or sunlight, or weapon using fire, like incendiary bullets or flamethrowers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the weapon engulfs the strix so that it can't escape, so maybe from the flamethrower, but other weapons would just push them back. Note that it takes a <i>minute</i> of exposure to damage the strix, so you'd need a syncronised squad of people with flamethrowers to keep it up.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how it works by the book. Personally, I think that weaponised banes should be damaging on the level of attacks that normally deals aggravated damage (i.e. successes+mod damage that is downgraded to bashing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T12:11:10-08:00","id":1471551,"title":"","content":"I have a doubt regarding the first level of the nightmare discipline, the book says that you can conjure reflexively small illusions, is this just fluff or it has a mechanical effect like a bonus to intimidate? I thought about this when in the last game I was, one of the nosferatu used nightmare to make it appear that a gun held by a gangbanger was a sneak and the ST ruled that, not only would the guy drop the gun but the player would get a plus 3 bonus to his intimidation roll because the guy would be scared shitless at that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T12:58:27-08:00","id":1471553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471551#post1471551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a doubt regarding the first level of the nightmare discipline, the book says that you can conjure reflexively small illusions, is this just fluff or it has a mechanical effect like a bonus to intimidate? I thought about this when in the last game I was, one of the nosferatu used nightmare to make it appear that a gun held by a gangbanger was a sneak and the ST ruled that, not only would the guy drop the gun but the player would get a plus 3 bonus to his intimidation roll because the guy would be scared shitless at that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is not strict mechanic to handle hallucination so I'd have nothing to complain if you want to just use it as flavour to get the bonus on intimidation.<br /> I personally tend to prize good idea/description. Nightmare can be (with a bit of fantasy) one of the most funny discipline. <br /> In my opinion, if someone is not aware about the existence of these kind of mind tricks, I would let the gangbanger drop the gun. Otherwise I would still require a composure roll to resist the urge to drop the gun. <br /> And yes, the bonus on intimidation rolls is always applicable as it is the effect of Dread Presence which last for a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T13:14:56-08:00","id":1471554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471553#post1471553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, there is not strict mechanic to handle hallucination so I'd have nothing to complain if you want to just use it as flavour to get the bonus on intimidation.<br /> I personally tend to prize good idea/description. Nightmare can be (with a bit of fantasy) one of the most funny discipline.<br /> In my opinion, if someone is not aware about the existence of these kind of mind tricks, I would let the gangbanger drop the gun. Otherwise I would still require a composure roll to resist the urge to drop the gun.<br /> And yes, the bonus on intimidation rolls is always applicable as it is the effect of Dread Presence which last for a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bonus he got was on top of his +2 that comes with his level of nightmare, we asked the ST what was the point of even rolling for that if the guy was this scared and he said that in case of failure, the guy would have just made a run for it out of sheer terror, the roll wasn't for scaring him further but to focalize the dude fear into giving the player what he wanted, personally I thought it was a bit excessive but since it would make sense that the totally normal human gangbanger would be scared out of his mind, I guess the uber bonus was appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T13:40:17-08:00","id":1471555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471554#post1471554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> The bonus he got was on top of his +2 that comes with his level of nightmare, we asked the ST what was the point of even rolling for that if the guy was this scared and he said that in case of failure, the guy would have just made a run for it out of sheer terror, the roll wasn't for scaring him further but to focalize the dude fear into giving the player what he wanted, personally I thought it was a bit excessive but since it would make sense that the totally normal human gangbanger would be scared out of his mind, I guess the uber bonus was appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with you. In this case I wouldn't had the PC roll with another +3. I'm not a fan of rolling everything. 99% of normal ppl would throw the gun away. I would give a chance to resist to the urge only to other kindred or ppl aware of this with a roll. For example: wits+composure penalized by Nightmare","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-31-2021, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T14:16:25-08:00","id":1471558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471555#post1471555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd agree with you. In this case I wouldn't had the PC roll woth another +3. I'm not a fan of rolling everything. 99% of normal ppl would throw the gun away. I would give a chance to resist to the urge only to other kindred or ppl aware of this with a roll. For example: wits+composure penalized by Nightmare</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that most rolls concerning humans would be superflous in most cases when it comes to supernatural templates, I am of the idea that what would logically work for a scene, like interrogating a drug dealer after you tore his muscle apart bare handed, shouldn't require rolls (unless it is for detecting lies), in this particular case I told the ST that at that point, he might just have had the gangbanger spill the beans but his game, his rules.<br /> <br /> I think though that hallucinations should definitely apply modifiers when appropriate, for example during a car chase, if you can have the driver hallucinate cockroaches running allover him, you would definitely put a negative modifier or even cause a composure roll to avoid crashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T14:56:56-08:00","id":1471559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471558#post1471558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that most rolls concerning humans would be superflous in most cases when it comes to supernatural templates, I am of the idea that what would logically work for a scene, like interrogating a drug dealer after you tore his muscle apart bare handed, shouldn't require rolls (unless it is for detecting lies), in this particular case I told the ST that at that point, he might just have had the gangbanger spill the beans but his game, his rules.<br /> <br /> I think though that hallucinations should definitely apply modifiers when appropriate, for example during a car chase, if you can have the driver hallucinate cockroaches running allover him, you would definitely put a negative modifier or even cause a composure roll to avoid crashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. This is how I see that and what I was indeed suggesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T15:19:48-08:00","id":1471560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471559#post1471559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. This is how I see that and what I was indeed suggesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-31T22:22:13-08:00","id":1471578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471558#post1471558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that most rolls concerning humans would be superflous in most cases when it comes to supernatural templates, I am of the idea that what would logically work for a scene, like interrogating a drug dealer after you tore his muscle apart bare handed, shouldn't require rolls (unless it is for detecting lies), in this particular case I told the ST that at that point, he might just have had the gangbanger spill the beans but his game, his rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree on principle, the point is precisely the disagreement on the specifics.<br /> <br /> For you, the logical conclusion of such interrogation is that the dealer spill the beans. For me, the logical conclusion is that the dealer enters shock and is afterwards too traumatized by the experience to be able to talk anything that makes sense. There <b>is</b> such a thing as too much pressure.<br /> <br /> And it seems to me that this ST had the same idea.<br /> <br /> The purpose of a roll isn't to decide if a character does what they describe, but to see if the character gets the desired results. While they achieving the described action is beyond doubt, getting the desired result from a frankly excessive action isn't so guaranteed, and failure may still have interesting dramatic consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T01:50:19-08:00","id":1471583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471578#post1471578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree on principle, the point is precisely the disagreement on the specifics.<br /> <br /> For you, the logical conclusion of such interrogation is that the dealer spill the beans. For me, the logical conclusion is that the dealer enters shock and is afterwards too traumatized by the experience to be able to talk anything that makes sense. There <b>is</b> such a thing as too much pressure.<br /> <br /> And it seems to me that this ST had the same idea.<br /> <br /> The purpose of a roll isn't to decide if a character does what they describe, but to see if the character gets the desired results. While they achieving the described action is beyond doubt, getting the desired result from a frankly excessive action isn't so guaranteed, and failure may still have interesting dramatic consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What you're saying is for sure a possibility in a realistic scenario but when you are rolling - let's say for an interrogation - you roll a contested: presence/manipulation + intimidation + Nightmare vs. Resolve+Composure.<br /> Failing the roll usually means the opponent got more successes which means he's able to maintain control. That doesn't mean he's not scared. It mean he can keep the control of his actions, which, in my opinion, exclude the scenario where he's too much traumatized to get a reasonable answer, simply he can decide whether to give it or not.<br /> <br /> Your proposed scenario, for me, would be an outcome for a critical failure: you got the shit out of him and now he's completely useless for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> What I was suggesting not to roll for, was for simpler and more sudden actions though. Like seeing the gun you are holding as a nightmarish snake. If the subject is not used to these kind of tricks, I really find no sense to delay the game rolling, giving him an almost unexplanable reason to keep the gun in his hand. It might be different in the case of an interrogation though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-01-2022, 05:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T05:35:04-08:00","id":1471585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471578#post1471578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree on principle, the point is precisely the disagreement on the specifics.<br /> <br /> For you, the logical conclusion of such interrogation is that the dealer spill the beans. For me, the logical conclusion is that the dealer enters shock and is afterwards too traumatized by the experience to be able to talk anything that makes sense. There <b>is</b> such a thing as too much pressure.<br /> <br /> And it seems to me that this ST had the same idea.<br /> <br /> The purpose of a roll isn't to decide if a character does what they describe, but to see if the character gets the desired results. While they achieving the described action is beyond doubt, getting the desired result from a frankly excessive action isn't so guaranteed, and failure may still have interesting dramatic consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree on the principle and I'm not saying that the ST was wrong but a split second hallucination of you holding a snake, while undoubtedly scary as fuck, wouldn't in my opinion be such a traumatizing experience, especially for an hardened gang banger who I guess would require a lot more to be traumatized on the level you suggest, besides in such a situation, the easiest path for survival and getting away from the creepy guy with black scleras would be to simply tell him what he wants to know, thats basic self preservation.<br /> <br /> I think that blatant displays of power shouldn't require rolls for simple things like getting info out of mortals (with plenty of exceptions of course), lets use the gangbanger example, instead of nightmare the nos could have just tanked whatever bullet the ganger managed to fire before using vigor to snatch the gun away and tear it apart in front of him, into such a situation, anyone with a minimum of brain would just surrender and do what the creepy bulletproof guy told him to do, sure you could roll for detecting lies but having an intimidation roll in such situations would be just crunch for the sake of it in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Rolls in my opinion should be meaningful, supernatural splats have plenty of ways to get around common things like getting informations and rolls should be used for those cases where it would be thematically appropriate to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T11:07:01-08:00","id":1471606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471583#post1471583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your proposed scenario, for me, would be an outcome for a critical failure: you got the shit out of him and now he's completely useless for the rest of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>My comment was on the specific context. As was described, the ST decided that the NPC would let go the gun regardless (they <b>were</b> that convinced the gun was a snake). The ST was specifically rolling to see if the gangbanger would flee the scene or not. I do agree it is a kind of distorted use of the rules, but it was an on-the-fly improvisation to decide upon two possible, interesting, dramatically relevant but unpredictable outcomes.<br /> <br /> The principle behind this decision, given how I understood this, is what I'm defending. I'm not saying this should be used all the time or something like that, I'm against stalling the game with unnecessary dice rolls, too, but when the idea strikes you sometimes have to jump to the opportunity to create a more interesting game.<br /> <br /> And I'm personally all in favor of making the PCs feel when their decisions aren't the smartest ones, but not simply bashing them with default failure despite their characters' skills. When my PCs use <b>excessive force</b>, this is exactly the kind of thing I pull out, because it gives them a chance to still succeed, but also a hint that they should thing through some ideas before executing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471585#post1471585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree on the principle and I'm not saying that the ST was wrong but a split second hallucination of you holding a snake, while undoubtedly scary as fuck, wouldn't in my opinion be such a traumatizing experience, especially for an hardened gang banger who I guess would require a lot more to be traumatized on the level you suggest</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things. First, my exact suggestion was for the example of tearing the muscles off of an awaken person with your bare hands. I don't disagree that the gang banger wouldn't be mentally scarred for life just because of an illusory snake that lasted a couple moments.<br /> <br /> But your take on how people react is extremely puerile if you think that being battle hardened equates to always acting with the smartest decision for self-preservation. People under sudden stress in situations they're not used to make stupid decisions. That's why you see so many stories about people reacting to danger with stupidity.<br /> <br /> And human experience isn't binary, sheltered vs hardened. This is a mortal. They may have seen a lot of violence in their lives, but they probably never held a venomous snake in their hands or dealt with sudden perfect illusions. This is, by definition, outside this person's experiences. Someone with experience dealing with snakes would be far more likely to react cool-ish in tis situation, for example, or even a magician or someone used to tricks and special effects. Even then, not because they really know what they're doing, but simply because the sudden vision is more familiar and so less likely to trigger an instant panic reaction.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why this person should do something so thoughtful as stopping, listening to the stranger, thinking through an answer and giving it, instead of just running away from this shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471585#post1471585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rolls in my opinion should be meaningful, supernatural splats have plenty of ways to get around common things like getting informations and rolls should be used for those cases where it would be thematically appropriate to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>The crux of the matter is a difference on what you consider thematically appropriate, that's what you're not getting. For you mortals aren't a meaningful interaction in the game, and there's nothing wrong with this thinking, but for others the relationship between supernatural and plain natural is a core theme, and there's also nothing wrong with it.<br /> <br /> Your ST (probably) didn't did this because they think every uncertainty demands a roll. They did this precisely because they though this was thematically appropriate to showcase how this power can get out of hand when dealing with common mortals, no matter how used they are to mundane violence. That's just a matter of two people having different perspectives on the themes of the fiction, which is fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T12:08:16-08:00","id":1471610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471606#post1471606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My comment was on the specific context. As was described, the ST decided that the NPC would let go the gun regardless (they <b>were</b> that convinced the gun was a snake). The ST was specifically rolling to see if the gangbanger would flee the scene or not. I do agree it is a kind of distorted use of the rules, but it was an on-the-fly improvisation to decide upon two possible, interesting, dramatically relevant but unpredictable outcomes.<br /> <br /> The principle behind this decision, given how I understood this, is what I'm defending. I'm not saying this should be used all the time or something like that, I'm against stalling the game with unnecessary dice rolls, too, but when the idea strikes you sometimes have to jump to the opportunity to create a more interesting game.<br /> <br /> And I'm personally all in favor of making the PCs feel when their decisions aren't the smartest ones, but not simply bashing them with default failure despite their characters' skills. When my PCs use <b>excessive force</b>, this is exactly the kind of thing I pull out, because it gives them a chance to still succeed, but also a hint that they should thing through some ideas before executing them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Two things. First, my exact suggestion was for the example of tearing the muscles off of an awaken person with your bare hands. I don't disagree that the gang banger wouldn't be mentally scarred for life just because of an illusory snake that lasted a couple moments.<br /> <br /> But your take on how people react is extremely puerile if you think that being battle hardened equates to always acting with the smartest decision for self-preservation. People under sudden stress in situations they're not used to make stupid decisions. That's why you see so many stories about people reacting to danger with stupidity.<br /> <br /> And human experience isn't binary, sheltered vs hardened. This is a mortal. They may have seen a lot of violence in their lives, but they probably never held a venomous snake in their hands or dealt with sudden perfect illusions. This is, by definition, outside this person's experiences. Someone with experience dealing with snakes would be far more likely to react cool-ish in tis situation, for example, or even a magician or someone used to tricks and special effects. Even then, not because they really know what they're doing, but simply because the sudden vision is more familiar and so less likely to trigger an instant panic reaction.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why this person should do something so thoughtful as stopping, listening to the stranger, thinking through an answer and giving it, instead of just running away from this shit.<br /> <br /> <br /> The crux of the matter is a difference on what you consider thematically appropriate, that's what you're not getting. For you mortals aren't a meaningful interaction in the game, and there's nothing wrong with this thinking, but for others the relationship between supernatural and plain natural is a core theme, and there's also nothing wrong with it.<br /> <br /> Your ST (probably) didn't did this because they think every uncertainty demands a roll. They did this precisely because they though this was thematically appropriate to showcase how this power can get out of hand when dealing with common mortals, no matter how used they are to mundane violence. That's just a matter of two people having different perspectives on the themes of the fiction, which is fine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't take it the wrong way but I think you are exagerating way too much how a person would react or not in the specific situation I presented, this is a guy who was cornered into an alley and just saw his gun turn into a cobra, the reason why he would spill the beans is because he has no other options beside attacking empty handed, the black eyed monster in front of him.<br /> <br /> Just because you get scared it doesn't mean you turn into a moron all of a sudden, yes some people panic and do stupid things but its very different from, for example, having a gun pointed at you and being asked to hand over your money, in this kind of situations most people would either do as they are told or freeze and force the mugger to take the wallet himself, in this specific situation the only reasonable things the guy could have done is to either answer the nos questions or try and flee, since he was lucid enough to understand he wasn't going to escape this, he would have reasonably answered any question he was being asked because, when you take out the snake thing, this wasn't so different from having a gun pointed at his head and being asked things, something that an hardened criminal would most definitely be familiar with.<br /> <br /> Regarding the ST he said that he did it because in case of failure he would have had the guy shit his pants and cry for his mommy, forcing the nos into an extended emphaty roll to calm him down, yes it was a mostly light hearted game after so many dark ones we had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T15:49:41-08:00","id":1471623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471610#post1471610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't take it the wrong way but I think you are exagerating way too much how a person would react or not in the specific situation I presented, this is a guy who was cornered into an alley and just saw his gun turn into a cobra, the reason why he would spill the beans is because he has no other options beside attacking empty handed, the black eyed monster in front of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think you're not familiar with how people react before they have time to think. First reaction to an unfamiliar situation is reflexive, the more overcome with emotion you are, the less you're able to process before you react. Also, there's nothing similar to a cobra on your hand and a gun to your head, except how you can compare things with a clear, calm mind and draw logical conclusions, but I'm talking about reflexive reactions, not logical conclusions.<br /> <br /> But this is way out of topic now. We have irreconcilable differences in thought about the matter and lets stay at this. I see no problem with the ST's decision and reasoning, at all, and I think the roll was a good call through and through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T16:39:30-08:00","id":1471691,"title":"","content":"It s stated in the core book that blood sorcery can summon strix.<br /> I was wondering if it would also be capable of manipulate them in other ways, like sealing strix in items or directly damage them.<br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-02T22:46:55-08:00","id":1471718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1471691#post1471691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It s stated in the core book that blood sorcery can summon strix.<br /> I was wondering if it would also be capable of manipulate them in other ways, like sealing strix in items or directly damage them.<br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing specific already existing, as far as I know, but why not with a custom spell - unless there's already somenthing somewhere. Blood Sorcery is quite useless in terms of gameplay, let have it be useful as a plot tool at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 01-07-2022, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-07T15:28:52-08:00","id":1472025,"title":"","content":"I have a doubt regarding blood bonds and werewolves, the rules states that vampires don't lose vitae unless they suffer truly horrible injuries that maim the flesh or even remove limbs (like the ones werewolves do) and any release of vitae is done purposefully, now, what if a werewolf bites a vampire (the only way they can deal lethal without using gifts or fire) and the vampire want to reflexively spend vitae to blood bond the wolf, would it be possible? I have been skimming both books for a while and I didn't find anything that specifically says that it wouldn't work (I would rule that werewolves get to use their primal urge to resist it like vampires of course), by logic if you bite someone, you are bound to injest at least a small quantity of it even if you don't want to so how would you deal with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T09:12:43-08:00","id":1472059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472025#post1472025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a doubt regarding blood bonds and werewolves, the rules states that vampires don't lose vitae unless they suffer truly horrible injuries that maim the flesh or even remove limbs (like the ones werewolves do) and any release of vitae is done purposefully, now, what if a werewolf bites a vampire (the only way they can deal lethal without using gifts or fire) and the vampire want to reflexively spend vitae to blood bond the wolf, would it be possible? I have been skimming both books for a while and I didn't find anything that specifically says that it wouldn't work (I would rule that werewolves get to use their primal urge to resist it like vampires of course), by logic if you bite someone, you are bound to injest at least a small quantity of it even if you don't want to so how would you deal with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Core book says &quot;Any time a character imbibes a point or more of Vitae, it creates or reinforces a blood bond&quot;.<br /> So a simple bite would not be enough, but if the werewolf decides to inflict aggravated by eating the flesh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T09:42:03-08:00","id":1472062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472059#post1472059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Core book says &quot;Any time a character imbibes a point or more of Vitae, it creates or reinforces a blood bond&quot;.<br /> So a simple bite would not be enough, but if the werewolf decides to inflict aggravated by eating the flesh...</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought werewolves could only inflict aggravated on mortals and other werewolves, vampires are neither but still, if you are biting and rending something, you are getting some blood into your mouth, I don't mean this as any times a werewolves bites a vampire, he should get blood bonded (vampires don't lose vitae even when they bleed with blush of life, expending vitae is almost always a choice), I mean that if a vampire purposefully lets itself be bitten by one with the explicit purpose of blood bonding the werewolf, I can't see how a 3 meters tall killing machine with razor sharp teeths capable of destroying steel, wouldn't find itself with a snootful of vamp blood containing at least a point of vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T12:39:51-08:00","id":1472069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472062#post1472062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought werewolves could only inflict aggravated on mortals and other werewolves, vampires are neither but still, if you are biting and rending something, you are getting some blood into your mouth, I don't mean this as any times a werewolves bites a vampire, he should get blood bonded (vampires don't lose vitae even when they bleed with blush of life, expending vitae is almost always a choice), I mean that if a vampire purposefully lets itself be bitten by one with the explicit purpose of blood bonding the werewolf, I can't see how a 3 meters tall killing machine with razor sharp teeths capable of destroying steel, wouldn't find itself with a snootful of vamp blood containing at least a point of vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your idea.<br /> Probably i would require at least an instant action for the vampire to force its blood to exit from a wound, and only if he know exactly where he would be bitten.<br /> Else the vitae would simply remain in his body, unless as the core book states &quot; if the vampire loses a chunk of flesh or a limb, the blood will remain with the lost part, and pour out as the tissue and bone decays. Only in these terrible cases would blood loss equate with Vitae loss.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T13:42:51-08:00","id":1472073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472069#post1472069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand your idea.<br /> Probably i would require at least an instant action for the vampire to force its blood to exit from a wound, and only if he know exactly where he would be bitten.<br /> Else the vitae would simply remain in his body, unless as the core book states &quot; if the vampire loses a chunk of flesh or a limb, the blood will remain with the lost part, and pour out as the tissue and bone decays. Only in these terrible cases would blood loss equate with Vitae loss.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since werewolves in Gauru establish grapples when they attack, weather with claws or jaws, I figure that a vampire wouldn't need to know where he would be bitten since he would most likely still be in the wolf jaws from that turn onward also, I don't think a wound as in an health level would be necessary for this to work, a vampire with resilience would still be able to absorb any damage and still bleed some vitae into the wolf (the book also mention that vampires using resilience, still suffer visual wounds). I don't know if it should be an instant action since, unless you are using disciplines, spending vitae is a reflexive action by default but I understand the balance reasons for this, as both a werewolf and a vampire player I always found it strange that woofs would chomp on creatures whose blood is an highly addictive and mind altering substance so easily and without consequences, especially because they have plenty of other ways to easily destroy leeches without risking stuff like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 01-08-2022, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T14:12:41-08:00","id":1472078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472073#post1472073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as both a werewolf and a vampire player I always found it strange that woofs would chomp on creatures whose blood is an highly addictive and mind altering substance so easily and without consequences, especially because they have plenty of other ways to easily destroy leeches without risking stuff like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>A highly addictive and mind-altering substance <i>that is also the stuff they need to not be functionally dead for an extended period of time</i>.<br /> <br /> Even assuming that the breaking points apply to Harmony, the effects of a first-stage Vinculum are negligible as a deterrent for a werewolf trying to destroy a vampire by biting it. Likewise, Vitae addiction is contingent upon failing a roll and don't really serve much immediate disincentive to keep attacking the vampire. On a long enough timescale, perhaps, but in the situation where you've hunted down a specific vampire and are biting it because you are trying to permanently destroy it, the fact that it stores and bleeds a finite amount of heroin is not intrinsically damning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T14:20:43-08:00","id":1472080,"title":"","content":"I'd personally discuss this with the players if needed.<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind bleeding Vitae on purpose is sound. The balance issue also is relevant. But that's ultimately not a question of what makes more sense or is more supported by RAW, instead it is a question of which of two splats should have the upper hand in this particular in a conflict.<br /> <br /> So that means the best answer depends too much on the specific chronicle. Making it work on a Werewolf game will highlight vampires as dangerous foes. Making it work on a Vampire game would justify the Uratha avoiding open conflict with Vampires. For a crossover game with players on both sides, it helps define the balance of power between the two splats, so it has to be carefully considered.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think the best default answer would be actually to have it work for two reasons. First, so you tone down conflict between the two of them. Second, because in a direct fight the Uratha already have the upper hand. But in the end the chronicle can mess a lot with those assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T14:29:12-08:00","id":1472083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472078#post1472078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A highly addictive and mind-altering substance <i>that is also the stuff they need to not be functionally dead for an extended period of time</i>.<br /> <br /> Even assuming that the breaking points apply to Harmony, the effects of a first-stage Vinculum are negligible as a deterrent for a werewolf trying to destroy a vampire by biting it. Likewise, Vitae addiction is contingent upon failing a roll and don't really serve much immediate disincentive to keep attacking the vampire. On a long enough timescale, perhaps, but in the situation where you've hunted down a specific vampire and are biting it because you are trying to permanently destroy it, the fact that it stores and bleeds a finite amount of heroin is not intrinsically damning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I needed this for my chronicle so it was more for a narrative standpoint but I figured I would try to understand how this would mechanically work as well, my doubts come from how the bond would affect harmony as well, werewolves are not psychos, they can feel love and other deeper emotional connections but the harmony system doesn't really support this so I'm stuck as to how a vinculum, of any level, would actually deal with the breaking point, the bonus to disciplines would still apply but urathas don't really get breaking points for hurting those who they love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T14:41:08-08:00","id":1472085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472080#post1472080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally discuss this with the players if needed.<br /> <br /> The reasoning behind bleeding Vitae on purpose is sound. The balance issue also is relevant. But that's ultimately not a question of what makes more sense or is more supported by RAW, instead it is a question of which of two splats should have the upper hand in this particular in a conflict.<br /> <br /> So that means the best answer depends too much on the specific chronicle. Making it work on a Werewolf game will highlight vampires as dangerous foes. Making it work on a Vampire game would justify the Uratha avoiding open conflict with Vampires. For a crossover game with players on both sides, it helps define the balance of power between the two splats, so it has to be carefully considered.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think the best default answer would be actually to have it work for two reasons. First, so you tone down conflict between the two of them. Second, because in a direct fight the Uratha already have the upper hand. But in the end the chronicle can mess a lot with those assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The campaign is a human one so this is not a splat war or anything, the blood bond was to introduce a vampire character and to make the campaign more varied, I like to think of it as a second season to a tv series, in the first one the protagonists were dealing with a werewolf and now they would deal with a vampire.<br /> <br /> The blood bond was to show how the vamp (an ancillae Daeva) would establish a foothold in a small town that is a werewolf territory, since she can't fight them directly, she would have started blood bonding their wolf blooded and human members of the pack (easy enough) but would have had to deal with the uratha at some point, so the idea was to lure one of them in an isolated spot (stupid I know but the pack took an hit in the &quot;first season&quot; so there is only one uratha in the pack at the moment), let the woof chomp on her a little and then use her maxed majesty with the bonus that comes from the bond to charm it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T14:41:41-08:00","id":1472086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472083#post1472083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but urathas don't really get breaking points for hurting those who they love.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Vinculum I think it can be done in three ways, depending on the chronicle. It could be a Breaking Point towards Flesh, Spirit, or whatever is more pronounced (so it always unbalance).<br /> <br /> Unbalance would work well with the idea that this is a powerful unnatural emotion that messes with you no matter what. Flesh would work with the notion that this emotion is itself kind of a ban, a spiritual urge, and you're denying it. And Spirit would be the notion that complex emotions are a human trait and keep you from living your spiritual nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T14:50:26-08:00","id":1472088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472086#post1472086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Vinculum I think it can be done in three ways, depending on the chronicle. It could be a Breaking Point towards Flesh, Spirit, or whatever is more pronounced (so it always unbalance).<br /> <br /> Unbalance would work well with the idea that this is a powerful unnatural emotion that messes with you no matter what. Flesh would work with the notion that this emotion is itself kind of a ban, a spiritual urge, and you're denying it. And Spirit would be the notion that complex emotions are a human trait and keep you from living your spiritual nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this but how would it mechanically work? how would the breaking point affect the fight and the uratha especially and what condition would it give? a first level vinculum wouldn't even make an uratha esitate I guess but a second definitely would since at that point, you are starting to get stronger feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T15:15:21-08:00","id":1472089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472059#post1472059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Core book says &amp;quot;Any time a character imbibes a point or more of Vitae, it creates or reinforces a blood bond&amp;quot;.<br /> So a simple bite would not be enough, but if the werewolf decides to inflict aggravated by eating the flesh...</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves can't inflict aggravated by default. They need some gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T15:27:44-08:00","id":1472090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472089#post1472089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves can't inflict aggravated by default. They need some gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves consuming the flesh of a human or wolf inflict aggravated damage. Your mileage may vary, but in general Kindred still have human flesh \u2014 vampirism negates some of its maintenance requirements, but it <i>is</i> a human body for at least as far forward from the Embrace as it would have held together without the Cleansing resetting the timer on attached pieces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T15:39:23-08:00","id":1472091,"title":"","content":"I feel like, if your intent is to discuss an answer rather than just take what you are given, it is best to start a new thread so it can be more easily found and referenced by people with similar questions in the future and so it doesn't clog the 'simple answers' thread. Page-long discussion doesn't seem on-topic for a 'simple question/simple answer' thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T15:44:01-08:00","id":1472093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472090#post1472090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves consuming the flesh of a human or wolf inflict aggravated damage. Your mileage may vary, but in general Kindred still have human flesh \u2014 vampirism negates some of its maintenance requirements, but it <i>is</i> a human body for at least as far forward from the Embrace as it would have held together without the Cleansing resetting the timer on attached pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest, I always thought that dealing lethal by default (they even specified vampires) because &quot;father wolf blah blah blah&quot; was stupid and a bit given to Apocalypse players to appease them for werewolves not causing aggravated by default, vampires are supposed to be durable, hell they even have trouble killing eachother, also a werewolf dealing bashing would still dust a vampire in a couple of rounds, crippled defense and plus 3 from gauru plus any brawl dots you have, with a specialty for using claws that deals +2 and immediately allow you to grapple, you are going to fuck up a vampire anyway, add spirits and gifts that only makes you better and killing and you wouldn't see that much of a difference.<br /> <br /> Rergarding eating flesh causing aggravated, I think it has to do with the fact that vampires don't really have any essence to talk about, it would make sense since they can't interact with spirits in any way, shape or form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T15:45:56-08:00","id":1472095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472091#post1472091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like, if your intent is to discuss an answer rather than just take what you are given, it is best to start a new thread so it can be more easily found and referenced by people with similar questions in the future and so it doesn't clog the 'simple answers' thread. Page-long discussion doesn't seem on-topic for a 'simple question/simple answer' thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My apologies, I didn't think this would spark a long discussion, still I feel it would be useful to know such tidbits so I posted them here but I will stop anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T16:15:22-08:00","id":1472097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472090#post1472090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves consuming the flesh of a human or wolf inflict aggravated damage. Your mileage may vary, but in general Kindred still have human flesh \u2014 vampirism negates some of its maintenance requirements, but it <i>is</i> a human body for at least as far forward from the Embrace as it would have held together without the Cleansing resetting the timer on attached pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says, flesh of an human. Kindred are not humans and they, by default, downgrade aggravated to lethals (and lethals to bashing) and, in fact, werewolf bite deal lethals to kindred","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T16:22:01-08:00","id":1472098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472097#post1472097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It says, flesh of an human. Kindred are not humans and they, by default, downgrade aggravated to lethals (and lethals to bashing) and, in fact, werewolf bite deal lethals to kindred</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, vampires don't downgrade aggravated by default, they downgrade the lethal damage from common sources, werewolves jaws are not natural and so they deal lethal but I agree that them dealing aggravated wouldn't really fit since werewolves do so by absorbing essence and vampires don't have any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T17:03:30-08:00","id":1472101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472097#post1472097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says, flesh of an human. Kindred are not humans and they, by default, downgrade aggravated to lethals (and lethals to bashing) and, in fact, werewolf bite deal lethals to kindred</div> </div> </div> </div>Per both corebooks:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR2e Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Few rare perversions of nature \u2014 Disciplines, Devotions, and sorceries \u2014 cause aggravated wounds to Kindred.</b> Some masters of the Protean Discipline hone their claws and fangs to such vicious ends; this breeds a healthy fear and respect of clan Gangrel within most courts.<br /> <br /> Aggravated wounds look completely unnatural. They\u2019re perversions of nature that tax the Masquerade. Each vampire wounds differently. Flesh may become brittle and burn like paper. Tissue may bubble and stink. Blackened veins may streak across the victim\u2019s body. Foamy pustules may taint the area around the injury. <b>Whatever the method, aggravated wounds appear as manifestations of the natural world violently eliminating something that <u>does not belong</u>.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF2e Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Uratha] can eat the flesh of wolves and humans [to gain Essence]. For every point of damage caused by an Uratha\u2019s bite, they can choose to ingest the flesh and gain a point of Essence. <b>This is a stark violation of the Oath of the Moon, and always a Harmony breaking point toward the spirit. When devouring flesh for Essence, the Uratha causes aggravated wounds</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472098#post1472098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, vampires don't downgrade aggravated by default, they downgrade the lethal damage from common sources, werewolves jaws are not natural and so they deal lethal but I agree that them dealing aggravated wouldn't really fit since werewolves do so by absorbing essence and vampires don't have any.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves get Essence by absorbing Essence <i>in the case of drawing it from loci or from downed spirits who were the target of the Sacred Hunt.</i> Wolves, humans, and the auspice moon don't have Essence stores the werewolf is pulling from (barring the extra Essence generated by the Reception Lunacy Condition).<br /> <br /> There is likewise nothing to actually suggest that vampires do not have Essence at the same sort of level as wolves and humans for the magical purposes of the Great Hunter's descendants tapping into the force of consumption undergirding their branch of the metaphysics. They have flesh. It comes from a human body. It can be eaten. The ones doing the eating are magical beings whose jaws are suffused with the resonance of predation to such a degree that their human bite attack does more severe damage than normal. The act is taboo for the ones doing the biting, but offers power and sustenance.<br /> <br /> Separated vampire flesh generally sticks around at least as long as a piece of a corpse as old as the vampire would have, which means most neonates and some ancillae (at the very least) won't be giving werewolves a mouthful of ashes for their trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T17:15:30-08:00","id":1472102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472101#post1472101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per both corebooks:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolves get Essence by absorbing Essence <i>in the case of drawing it from loci or from downed spirits who were the target of the Sacred Hunt.</i> Wolves, humans, and the auspice moon don't have Essence stores the werewolf is pulling from (barring the extra Essence generated by the Reception Lunacy Condition).<br /> <br /> There is likewise nothing to actually suggest that vampires do not have Essence at the same sort of level as wolves and humans for the magical purposes of the Great Hunter's descendants tapping into the force of consumption undergirding their branch of the metaphysics. They have flesh. It comes from a human body. It can be eaten. The ones doing the eating are magical beings whose jaws are suffused with the resonance of predation to such a degree that their human bite attack does more severe damage than normal. The act is taboo for the ones doing the biting, but offers power and sustenance.<br /> <br /> Separated vampire flesh generally sticks around at least as long as a piece of a corpse as old as the vampire would have, which means most neonates and some ancillae (at the very least) won't be giving werewolves a mouthful of ashes for their trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is one of the many things we won't be getting an answer unless an author clarify it, the Wtf2e book specify that its either wolves or humans, vampires are not humans and werewolves jaws do not cause aggravated to them by default, the kind of thing that cause aggravated to vampires are either banes or some truly horryfing magic and werewolves jaws are neither.<br /> <br /> Personally I think that the aggravated damage is due to the fact that werewolves are physically removing chunk of important shit out of someone's body, this might be a problem for mortals or werewolves since even with their regenaration, massive physical trauma can still do a werewolf in, a vampire is a walking corpse who doesn't need to be whole to function hence them not getting aggravated damage from the wolves jaws.<br /> <br /> There is also nothing that suggest vampires have any essence either so I would guess that its up to the story teller unless we get some official clarification on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T17:18:36-08:00","id":1472104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472093#post1472093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be honest, I always thought that dealing lethal by default (they even specified vampires) because &quot;father wolf blah blah blah&quot; was stupid and a bit given to Apocalypse players to appease them for werewolves not causing aggravated by default, vampires are supposed to be durable, hell they even have trouble killing eachother, also a werewolf dealing bashing would still dust a vampire in a couple of rounds, crippled defense and plus 3 from gauru plus any brawl dots you have, with a specialty for using claws that deals +2 and immediately allow you to grapple, you are going to fuck up a vampire anyway, add spirits and gifts that only makes you better and killing and you wouldn't see that much of a difference.<br /> <br /> Rergarding eating flesh causing aggravated, I think it has to do with the fact that vampires don't really have any essence to talk about, it would make sense since they can't interact with spirits in any way, shape or form.</div> </div> </div> </div>The themes and moods of a game that has a theme and conflict in the form of &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot; that empahsizes the alienation that comes with inherently being an apex predator in a world where even monsters might not want to commit that far is something of a far stretch from &quot;father wolf blah blah blah.&quot; Werewolf is owed to be the sort of thing you always have to wonder about being lunch to.<br /> <br /> That said, I feel like you've somehow still managed to over read the advantages a werewolf has, and I really can't shake the feeling that you have a misapprehension about how violent conflict in Chronicles works (which is not a thing to feel bad, because it seems like a lot of people don't properly grok it) or how werewolf operates in relationship to it, particularly given how there's a lot of design deliberately being done to distance from Apocalypse's more direct warrior take on the subject. The stack of unsourced benefits do in fact specific things that work better in some contexts and not in others, and it's not like CHronicles plays out like a game of Dungeons and Dragons where everyone stands around just trying to kill each other.<br /> <br /> In relationship to that structure, though, vampires as a general rule are fixers and arrangers, their durability itself being a thing that has direct costs that demand immediate payments. I wouldn't be quick to discount any vampire who did dedicate themselves to a apex predator way of life, even in comparison to the Uratha, but that requires being about that, and most vampires (even the Gangrel) have more to gain playing a game of &quot;board control&quot; than the more direct apex predator approach. There are ways the Kindred, in this way, are still going to be more prey animal than not.<br /> <br /> Finally I think there's a context being ignored on the whole &quot;Agg damage bite for Essence&quot;, which is namely that one assumes taking giant fucking bites out of someone requires similar conditions to which a werewolf hunts down a spirit to submission-namely, the Aggravated argument needs you hunt a thing to submission. That said though, even if you don't account for anything about essence bearing, the context of that being a scenario where you take a Big Honking Bite out of a prey animal you hunted down to submission is going to lends itself to Aggravated damage. I don't how dead you are, a wolf mauling my shoulder, upper arm, and upper chest/back enough to fit that context is probably going to qualify for aggravated damage as much as shoving an arm into a wood chipper would qualify for aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> But mostly I popped it to say &quot;Hi! Has anyone mentioned how abrasive you come off with even your more reasonable commentary? Because dear god, you manage to find ways to shit on things unnecessarily that doesn't help you address the problems in as helpful a way as you might like, and I feel like someone should point it out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, &quot;father wolf blah blah blah&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T18:06:25-08:00","id":1472109,"title":"","content":"As a clarification, in my opinion forcing vitae out of the body and &quot;burning&quot; vitae reflexively are two different things.<br /> The latter is described as a &quot;natural&quot; thing for vampires and dilutes the &quot;power density&quot; of the blood.<br /> The first instead is described as a thing that the Beast doesn t like to do, so i think it requires some sort of concentration for the vampire, at least an instant action.<br /> For werewolf bites, even if part of the blood enter in their throat the core books specify that it would not contain vitae, the vampire should be able to concentrate while being bitten to direct its vitae to the mouth, and only if the werewolf holds the mouth on the flesh for at least one turn.<br /> Also i don t know if werewolf eating vampire s flesh should gain Essence or deal aggravated, but i m sure that in this case (as the core book states) the ingested chunks of flesh would contain a lot of true Vitae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T18:58:00-08:00","id":1472111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472104#post1472104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The themes and moods of a game that has a theme and conflict in the form of &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot; that empahsizes the alienation that comes with inherently being an apex predator in a world where even monsters might not want to commit that far is something of a far stretch from &quot;father wolf blah blah blah.&quot; Werewolf is owed to be the sort of thing you always have to wonder about being lunch to.<br /> <br /> That said, I feel like you've somehow still managed to over read the advantages a werewolf has, and I really can't shake the feeling that you have a misapprehension about how violent conflict in Chronicles works (which is not a thing to feel bad, because it seems like a lot of people don't properly grok it) or how werewolf operates in relationship to it, particularly given how there's a lot of design deliberately being done to distance from Apocalypse's more direct warrior take on the subject. The stack of unsourced benefits do in fact specific things that work better in some contexts and not in others, and it's not like CHronicles plays out like a game of Dungeons and Dragons where everyone stands around just trying to kill each other.<br /> <br /> In relationship to that structure, though, vampires as a general rule are fixers and arrangers, their durability itself being a thing that has direct costs that demand immediate payments. I wouldn't be quick to discount any vampire who did dedicate themselves to a apex predator way of life, even in comparison to the Uratha, but that requires being about that, and most vampires (even the Gangrel) have more to gain playing a game of &quot;board control&quot; than the more direct apex predator approach. There are ways the Kindred, in this way, are still going to be more prey animal than not.<br /> <br /> Finally I think there's a context being ignored on the whole &quot;Agg damage bite for Essence&quot;, which is namely that one assumes taking giant fucking bites out of someone requires similar conditions to which a werewolf hunts down a spirit to submission-namely, the Aggravated argument needs you hunt a thing to submission. That said though, even if you don't account for anything about essence bearing, the context of that being a scenario where you take a Big Honking Bite out of a prey animal you hunted down to submission is going to lends itself to Aggravated damage. I don't how dead you are, a wolf mauling my shoulder, upper arm, and upper chest/back enough to fit that context is probably going to qualify for aggravated damage as much as shoving an arm into a wood chipper would qualify for aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> But mostly I popped it to say &quot;Hi! Has anyone mentioned how abrasive you come off with even your more reasonable commentary? Because dear god, you manage to find ways to shit on things unnecessarily that doesn't help you address the problems in as helpful a way as you might like, and I feel like someone should point it out.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, &quot;father wolf blah blah blah&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This isn't about splat wars, I have absolutely no problem with werewolves being the big bananas of the lower splats and will keep playing the game and buy any supplement that comes out (when they decide to publish them anyway) even If I don't care about the lore (there is plenty about vampire that I find ridiculous rest assured), what I object is nerfing a splat in favour of another, a werewolf rolling 15 attack dices against an opponent who can't use his full defense because he is fighting a 3 meters tall killing machine? sure, this is kinda the werewolves whole shtick (although having werewolves losing the skill part of their defense against eachother is kinda stupid), what I object is purposefully nerfing one of the other splats core abilities in favour of another (hell they even pinpointed vampires in the manual when talking about predators jaws), this was basically akin to say that mages can stop a werewolf regeneration cuz magic blah blah blah, hence my father wolf comment but whatever.<br /> <br /> I have been in enough werewolf games to know exactly how combat works, short, bloody and with a satisfying crunch with the irraka striking the first (and hopefully last) blow and the rahu finishing the rest, at least if the pack has done its homework and don't end up fighting a rank 5 spirit with plenty of backup and without knowing about its bane. Unlike apocalypse you actually study your prey and stack all the advantages you can, striking it when it least expects it and when it can't defend itself, you find out where the prey lives so you can prepare the field, you find out what are its allies so you can isolate him, you find out about its enemies so you can ally with them, you find out what are its defences to better neautralize them, you find out what scares it so you can exploit it, you find out what it wants so you can bait it and after all of that you declare the hunt, you remove layer upon layer of the prey defences, you drive it out of its den and chase it until it drops and at that point the killing becomes trivial, this is why I love werewolf not the mythology but this, werewolves are not just monsters but highly skilled operators that surgically strike their targets from the shadows and vanish without leaving any trace, they are basically a furry seal team 6 and I love them for it.<br /> <br /> Regarding vampires I agree on everything you said and like I have wrote before, I don't have any problems with vampires being weaker than werewolves since combat is not part of what makes the game fun but downplaying their durability was not a good way to portray it and that is just my opinion.<br /> <br /> Regarding aggravated damage, I like to stick to what is written in the core books (which is also why I get pissed everytime I read one since, more often than not, I end up more confused than before) and the book specifically refers to mortals and werewolves, vampires are not mortals and since they took the time and space to specify that werewolves jaws deal lethal to them, I think they would have also pointed out if this would have worked on them too since vampires are, again, not mortals, like not even close. The part about removing pieces of vampires is moot because they can easily regenerate this kind of injuries, you can chop a vamp's arm off with an axe, its still going to do bashing damage and its still going to reattach it or regrow another one reflexively for one point of vitae.<br /> <br /> Regarding you getting aggravated by my commentary, thats on you, I've never insulted nor acted aggressively against anyone (who the fuck does that over a game anyway?) so while I may come off as an asshole (and I kinda am a little I admit), I would never purposefully attack anyone over their opinion nor will I change my tone when criticizing a piece of fictional literature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 01-09-2022, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T19:44:23-08:00","id":1472114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472111#post1472111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding you getting aggravated by my commentary, thats on you,</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sprinkling contentious language into ordinary posts, which is a pain to filter past and adds nothing to this conversation that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472095#post1472095\">you said you would stop clogging the Simple Questions thread with</a> and then proceeded to immediately jump back into.<br /> <br /> If you have a question, great, ask it, but nobody is asking for your capital-O Opinion about how stupid you think some element of the game is in this thread for checking how the lore and mechanics work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Simple question: Does accessing a Haven through Carthian Pull also give you access to a dot of Safe Place, or are the temporary digs an exception to the requirement that a Haven be tied to a Safe Place? Similarly, does losing the temporary Haven at the end of the month count as a breaking point for characters whose Humanity is high enough for it to matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T20:06:55-08:00","id":1472115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472111#post1472111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding you getting aggravated by my commentary, thats on you, I've never insulted nor acted aggressively against anyone (who the fuck does that over a game anyway?) so while I may come off as an asshole (and I kinda am a little I admit), I would never purposefully attack anyone over their opinion nor will I change my tone when criticizing a fictional piece of literature.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's completely on you. You don't have to openly insult someone or be aggressive to anyone to still come off as rude as rude and condescending, particularly with unrelated asides that have no purpose asides from shitting on something, particularly something that people in reasonably have a good chance of enjoying.<br /> <br /> That you admit to coming off as an asshole but staunchly state you'll do nothing about it does not help your case. I realize you're still relatively new around here, but the days where that's a reasonable defense for various faux pas, be they games understanding or social, eventually run out, and things like the above shit show of an opinion on Forsaken only devour that good will all the faster.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, good will towards writing intention and good faith in questioning go a long way. Chronicles is not a game where context is blanked out, and and trying to bend the game in ways that don't adhere to the narrative employed will ultimately fail to work.<br /> <br /> I might returned to get more into the details, but I've got a clock to beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-08T20:27:10-08:00","id":1472118,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Please desist all arguments and move onto other topics. The next argument will get this thread shut down. This is the first and final warning.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-09T01:59:31-08:00","id":1472125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472114#post1472114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple question: Does accessing a Haven through Carthian Pull also give you access to a dot of Safe Place, or are the temporary digs an exception to the requirement that a Haven be tied to a Safe Place? Similarly, does losing the temporary Haven at the end of the month count as a breaking point for characters whose Humanity is high enough for it to matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that the Haven dots would constitute an exception. The only thing the player is really benefiting from are the sunproofing and subtle, comfortable nuances of staying in the home of another Kindred. A Safe Place rating should still exist, but that would be at the discretion of the ST. Just because you're crashing on the couch doesn't mean the Haven's owner will batten down the hatches if someone comes looking for you.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I'd say no to the Breaking Point. The Haven doesn't belong to the character, and their departure was an understood inevitability. They aren't able to personalize and memorialize their Requiems in that space, which are the sort of investments whose loss would cause the Breaking Point to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25372-ssudd387","name":"Ssudd387","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T18:42:34-08:00","id":1472835,"title":"","content":"Whats it seem like if a hideous kindred Uses Majesty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T03:15:07-08:00","id":1472864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472835#post1472835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whats it seem like if a hideous kindred Uses Majesty?</div> </div> </div> </div>Majesty doesn't make you pretty it just improve your presence/charisma. There's plenty of example of &quot;ugly&quot; (for esthetic standards) people which are much more charismatic and &quot;attractive&quot; then pretty men. Think to politician, or VIP, they may be ugly and yet moving masses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T17:42:47-08:00","id":1472916,"title":"","content":"Yet to a nosferatu who learns majesty it can be a relief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T00:27:16-08:00","id":1472941,"title":"","content":"It is indeed. He will still be ugly (although in 2ed Nosderatu are not ugly by default, they can also be beautiful and yet making humans feel awkard) but will be seen with &quot;other eyes&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T03:22:40-08:00","id":1472947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472941#post1472941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is indeed. He will still be ugly (although in 2ed Nosderatu are not ugly by default, they can also be beautiful and yet making humans feel awkard) but will be seen with &quot;other eyes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're already not ugly by default in 1st ed, this is strictly a Masquerade thing, not Requiem. In Requiem they only cause unease, any appearance feature is optional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T05:18:38-08:00","id":1472958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1472941#post1472941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is indeed. He will still be ugly (although in 2ed Nosderatu are not ugly by default, they can also be beautiful and yet making humans feel awkard) but will be seen with &quot;other eyes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like others said, the horrible appearance is a masquerade thing, you can make a nosferatu with striking looks whose incredible beauty makes humans uneasy, they are not scary because they are ugly (although they can obviously be), they are scary because people can tell that there is something terribly wrong about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T10:30:04-08:00","id":1473476,"title":"","content":"I was reading about animalism and saw the description of the 5th dot: &quot;As the undisputed master of her territory, a frenzying creature cannot attack the vampire, nor may they spend Willpower to resist her commands delivered through Feral Infection&quot;, does this refers to animals only or also humans, kindreds, werewolves and other supernaturals like with feral infection? also what does it mean that they can't attack it? a frenzying creature would leave the vampire alone or attack only to defend itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 01-28-2022, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T11:13:59-08:00","id":1473481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1473476#post1473476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was reading about animalism and saw the description of the 5th dot: &quot;As the undisputed master of her territory, a frenzying creature cannot attack the vampire, nor may they spend Willpower to resist her commands delivered through Feral Infection&quot;, does this refers to animals only or also humans, kindreds, werewolves and other supernaturals like with feral infection? also what does it mean that they can't attack it? a frenzying creature would leave the vampire alone or attack only to defend itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing here gives any indication of not affecting humans and supernaturals, and <i>Feral Infection</i> itself doesn't even let animal spend Willpower, so it clearly refers to humans and supernaturals affected.<br /> <br /> For the second question, given how the rest of the power works, I think the creature would leave the vampire completely alone (except under their command, of course). Only if another supernatural power compelled the creature to attack the vampire, or somehow helped it to fight in self-defense, would I let a Clash of Wills define the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T11:39:08-08:00","id":1473483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1473481#post1473481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing here gives any indication of not affecting humans and supernaturals, and <i>Feral Infection</i> itself doesn't even let animal spend Willpower, so it clearly refers to humans and supernaturals affected.<br /> <br /> For the second question, given how the rest of the power works, I think the creature would leave the vampire completely alone (except under their command, of course). Only if another supernatural power compelled the creature to attack the vampire, or somehow helped it to fight in self-defense, would I let a Clash of Wills define the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, so humans or supernaturals that aren't in kuruth or equivalent can attack normally right? I'm thinking particualrly about vampires riding the wave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T11:50:22-08:00","id":1473485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1473483#post1473483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, so humans or supernaturals that aren't in kuruth or equivalent can attack normally right? I'm thinking particualrly about vampires riding the wave.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another question altogether.<br /> <br /> It says lowercase frenzy, which isn't exactly a thing in the rules, except the very rules of <i>Feral Infection</i>. So it is clearly meant actually for victims of that power, which can affect anyone and isn't necessarily cancelled by other Frenzy states.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, ST's call, the book certainly should be clearer about that. As written it isn't impossible to cause a Frenzied character to become also frenzied by Animalism 4, but otherwise does it affects other Frenzy rules than Animalism-induced? If it does, I don't think a character Riding the Wave would be exempt, as it is still under the grasp of a Frenzy even if in some control over it.<br /> <br /> Either way, keep that in mind. Humans and other supernaturals at first can attack normally except by the penalties already defined by the level 5 power, but the level 4 power is <b>meant</b> to induce frenzy and so exert that control over them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T12:09:10-08:00","id":1473487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1473485#post1473485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's another question altogether.<br /> <br /> It says lowercase frenzy, which isn't exactly a thing in the rules, except the very rules of <i>Feral Infection</i>. So it is clearly meant actually for victims of that power, which can affect anyone and isn't necessarily cancelled by other Frenzy states.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, ST's call, the book certainly should be clearer about that. As written it isn't impossible to cause a Frenzied character to become also frenzied by Animalism 4, but otherwise does it affects other Frenzy rules than Animalism-induced? If it does, I don't think a character Riding the Wave would be exempt, as it is still under the grasp of a Frenzy even if in some control over it.<br /> <br /> Either way, keep that in mind. Humans and other supernaturals at first can attack normally except by the penalties already defined by the level 5 power, but the level 4 power is <b>meant</b> to induce frenzy and so exert that control over them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, from what I gather from this <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/my-slow-descent-into-animalism/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/my-slow-descent-into-animalism/</a>, feral infection is not supposed to induce a different kind of frenzy as it refers to &quot;frenzy or similar states&quot;, so my take is that if a vampire or another supernatural succumb to frenzy or another equivalent (I'm only aware of kuruth so I guess other splats just go nuts like humans do) weather through feral infection or other means, they still can't attack the vampire, this would include also vampires who are riding the frenzy, am I right in my reasoning? Also, how would a clash of wills work in this case? you don't have to roll anything for the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 01-28-2022, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T15:21:32-08:00","id":1473505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1473487#post1473487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">am I right in my reasoning?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so. About the Clash, other posters have a better grasp than me on that rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T17:45:44-08:00","id":1473509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1473487#post1473487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'm only aware of kuruth so I guess other splats just go nuts like humans do)</div> </div> </div> </div>The sentence after the one describing how Feral Infection affects vampires and werewolves is &quot;Humans and other supernatural creatures fall into an atavistic state where they must attack the target, or move towards it if they can't reach it,&quot; so yes, other splats explicitly go nuts like humans do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how would a clash of wills work in this case? you don't have to roll anything for the power. </div> </div> </div>&quot;All characters using conflicting powers enter a contested roll-off, each using a pool of his Blood Potency plus his dots in the Discipline.&quot; Doesn't matter that the normal use of the power doesn't involve a roll, Clash of Wills has defined dicepools for Disciplines, Devotions, and blood sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T18:21:53-08:00","id":1473510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1473505#post1473505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think so. About the Clash, other posters have a better grasp than me on that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T18:28:02-08:00","id":1473511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1473509#post1473509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sentence after the one describing how Feral Infection affects vampires and werewolves is &quot;Humans and other supernatural creatures fall into an atavistic state where they must attack the target, or move towards it if they can't reach it,&quot; so yes, other splats explicitly go nuts like humans do.<br /> <br /> &quot;All characters using conflicting powers enter a contested roll-off, each using a pool of his Blood Potency plus his dots in the Discipline.&quot; Doesn't matter that the normal use of the power doesn't involve a roll, Clash of Wills has defined dicepools for Disciplines, Devotions, and blood sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T17:28:07-08:00","id":1473614,"title":"","content":"Can Family ghouls be captured blood bound then sold on a auction block?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T17:34:47-08:00","id":1473615,"title":"","content":"Yes, they can be captured and sold if the setting permits it.<br /> But if they're a member of a ghoul family they're probably already blood bound to the vampire progenitor or his house/ dynasty or alternatively immune/resistant to vinculums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T23:16:35-08:00","id":1473633,"title":"","content":"I mean, yes, you can capture a person and sell them on an auction block if you're capable of subduing and imprisoning them (and are a horrible, evil bastard). The Vinculum isn't necessarily going to make it that much easier to do so. It makes you obsessively <i>love</i> someone. If you loved someone, would you let them sell you into slavery without resisting? Not to mention a vampire purchasing human slaves probably doesn't want one who obsessively loves not you, but <i>the guy who ran the slave auction.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T08:56:09-08:00","id":1474203,"title":"","content":"So I was building a Strix Antagonist and..... this section confused the hell out of me.<br /> <br /> &quot;All Strix begin with two dots in Brawl, Athletics, and Occult. The Strix learn skills by absorbing them during feeding or by reading the mind of a host. A Strix may have up to its Attribute dot maximum in Skill dots, and no Skill may be raised above 5. If a Strix gains a new Skill dot when already at its maximum, it may choose to replace one of its existing dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> So... A shadow potency 1 Stix has a maximum attribute of 5 and starts with 6 dots of skills. Breaking it's own rules right off the bat. So what gives?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T15:09:09-08:00","id":1474232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1474203#post1474203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was building a Strix Antagonist and..... this section confused the hell out of me.<br /> <br /> &quot;All Strix begin with two dots in Brawl, Athletics, and Occult. The Strix learn skills by absorbing them during feeding or by reading the mind of a host. A Strix may have up to its Attribute dot maximum in Skill dots, and no Skill may be raised above 5. If a Strix gains a new Skill dot when already at its maximum, it may choose to replace one of its existing dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> So... A shadow potency 1 Stix has a maximum attribute of 5 and starts with 6 dots of skills. Breaking it's own rules right off the bat. So what gives?</div> </div> </div> </div>What gives is that it's talking about the maximum number in the range provided in the Attribute Dots column of the Shadow Potency chart, not the Attribute Maximum column of same.<br /> <br /> A Shadow Potency 1 Strix starts with six dots of Skills and has four to six Attribute dots. A Shadow Potency 2-3 Strix may have up to ten dots of Skills, because it has eight to ten Attribute dots. Shadow Potency 4-5 Strix may have up to fifteen dots of Skills, because they have ten to fifteen Attribute dots. Continue down the chart accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T09:08:15-07:00","id":1478576,"title":"","content":"Does Awe interact at all with Courtoisie? Specifically, Value of the Spoken Word. Awe gives a bonus to Presence roll when talking to people, and Value of the Spoken Word comes with the following wording: 'Your character can leverage taunts, teasing, goading, threatening, and otherwise speaking to create openings to harm her opponent.'<br /> <br /> My first assumption is as written Awe would contribute to Value of the Spoken Word dice pools (if replacing Strength with Presence), but I am was wondering if anyone else had any rulings/insights on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T18:27:34-07:00","id":1478630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478576#post1478576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Awe interact at all with Courtoisie? Specifically, Value of the Spoken Word. Awe gives a bonus to Presence roll when talking to people, and Value of the Spoken Word comes with the following wording: 'Your character can leverage taunts, teasing, goading, threatening, and otherwise speaking to create openings to harm her opponent.'<br /> <br /> My first assumption is as written Awe would contribute to Value of the Spoken Word dice pools (if replacing Strength with Presence), but I am was wondering if anyone else had any rulings/insights on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>My instinct would be yes. Courtoisie is at least somewhat mystical, and Majesty bolsters that trait supernaturally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T07:32:32-07:00","id":1478687,"title":"","content":"No, Awe does not stack with activation rolls of other disciplines. <br /> Courtiose augments Manipulation, not Presence. <br /> Yes you could have them both active simultaneously, but not both at the same time since you don't normally roll two Attributes with a skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-12-2022, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T07:38:29-07:00","id":1478688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478687#post1478687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, Awe does not stack with activation rolls of other disciplines.<br /> Courtiose augments Manipulation, not Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question isn't about the 1e bloodline Discipline Courtoisie, but the 2e Invictus Fighting Style Merit Courtoisie.<br /> <br /> I lean loosely in the same direction as Yossarian.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T09:14:18-07:00","id":1478696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478688#post1478688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question isn't about the 1e bloodline Discipline Courtoisie, but the 2e Invictus Fighting Style Merit Courtoisie.<br /> <br /> I lean loosely in the same direction as Yossarian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm well aware it's referencing the fighting style, though it also exists as a discipline that does the same as the merit. The merit chain allows you to switch Intimidation, Expression, Socialize, and Subterfuge for Weaponry or Brawl, Presence for Strength and Manipulation for Dexterity. The merit also expressly says it's for use in hand-to-hand or weaponry combat, not social exchanges, and gives your character taunt and a damage shield just like numerous video games characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T10:19:28-07:00","id":1478700,"title":"","content":"The merit I was asking specifically about says the following:<br /> <br /> <b>Your character can leverage taunts, teasing, goading, threatening, and otherwise speaking to create openings to harm her opponent. If she engages her opponent socially</b>, she may substitute her Expression, Intimidation, Socialize, or Subterfuge Skills for either her Athletics or Weaponry in combat, or her Presence for her Strength, her Manipulation for her Dexterity.<br /> <br /> While Awe itself adds to any Presence rolls while you're talking to people. It seemed like there was an overlap, but I wasn't sure if that was by intent or accident, or if people generally allowed this sort of interaction or not.<br /> <br /> I wasn't asking about any Disciplines; I'm perfectly aware Awe does not contribute to those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T08:56:19-07:00","id":1478767,"title":"","content":"Then you should also know that Awe specifically states that it adds Presence to rolls only when you're talking normally to people. <br /> That would mean that it doesn't work when you're drawing weapons and kicking people in the crotch and screaming obscenities while using a supernatural power like Courtoisie to enable you to substitute social Skills and Attributes for physical Skills and Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T09:11:19-07:00","id":1478768,"title":"","content":"Does anybody know any cruac rituals that can be casted in turns instead of minutes? I'm thinking of making a crone character but the way ritual casting works, most of them would be highly situational and basically useless in an unforseen combat situation (the ST already said that the game might become fairly combat heavy depending on our actions), I read somewhere that there a was a supplement that brought back instant casting or something similar to 2ed but I don't know which one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T12:47:39-07:00","id":1478786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478767#post1478767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you should also know that Awe specifically states that it adds Presence to rolls only when you're talking normally to people.<br /> That would mean that it doesn't work when you're drawing weapons and kicking people in the crotch and screaming obscenities while using a supernatural power like Courtoisie to enable you to substitute social Skills and Attributes for physical Skills and Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but the Courtoisie style isn't supernatural though? Nothing about the way it is written suggests it relies on the supernatural. And Awe doesn't say you have to be talking normally to people, it says you have to be talking to them: goading and taunting counts as talking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T16:54:22-07:00","id":1478805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478768#post1478768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody know any cruac rituals that can be casted in turns instead of minutes? I'm thinking of making a crone character but the way ritual casting works, most of them would be highly situational and basically useless in an unforseen combat situation (the ST already said that the game might become fairly combat heavy depending on our actions), I read somewhere that there a was a supplement that brought back instant casting or something similar to 2ed but I don't know which one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t quite remember it it had instant casting, but the book you\u2019re looking for is likely <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T17:17:48-07:00","id":1478807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478805#post1478805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t quite remember it it had instant casting, but the book you\u2019re looking for is likely <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, I knew about that but my understanding is that the mechanics in there have been superseeded by the 2nd ed core extended casting, Isn't there anything similar for 2nd ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T17:25:50-07:00","id":1478808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478807#post1478807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks, I knew about that but my understanding is that the mechanics in there have been superseeded by the 2nd ed core extended casting, Isn't there anything similar for 2nd ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing purely 2E then, IIRC, I\u2019m afraid.<br /> <br /> Maybe there was something in <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>\u2026? Though this is less a suggestion and more a I\u2019m-clueless-either confession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T17:45:33-07:00","id":1478810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478808#post1478808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing purely 2E then, IIRC, I\u2019m afraid.<br /> <br /> Maybe there was something in <b>Secrets of the Covenants</b>\u2026? Though this is less a suggestion and more a I\u2019m-clueless-either confession.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T17:48:20-07:00","id":1478811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478768#post1478768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody know any cruac rituals that can be casted in turns instead of minutes? I'm thinking of making a crone character but the way ritual casting works, most of them would be highly situational and basically useless in an unforseen combat situation (the ST already said that the game might become fairly combat heavy depending on our actions), I read somewhere that there a was a supplement that brought back instant casting or something similar to 2ed but I don't know which one.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of like asking if there are any knives that are good for pounding in stakes.<br /> <br /> Secrets of the Covenants' Mantle of the Glorious Dervish provides a fairly solid couple of combat boosts for the lowest number of successes typically required of an extended action, and you can devise rituals with similar sorts of effects, but performing ritual magic in ChroD is generally incompatible with direct combat as an overlapping activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T23:11:13-07:00","id":1478822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478807#post1478807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks, I knew about that but my understanding is that the mechanics in there have been superseeded by the 2nd ed core extended casting, Isn't there anything similar for 2nd ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules in Blood Sorcery could be considered 1.5 ed.<br /> They are almost compatible with 2ed.<br /> If you decide to apply them, the Divination theme offers a solution to the problem.<br /> You can cast in advance rituals with the activation postponed, and set a fast activation condition like a password.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T01:11:37-07:00","id":1478826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vintervalpen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478786#post1478786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, but the Courtoisie style isn't supernatural though? Nothing about the way it is written suggests it relies on the supernatural. And Awe doesn't say you have to be talking normally to people, it says you have to be talking to them: goading and taunting counts as talking?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing natural about being able to use a Social Skill or Attribute in place of a Physical Attribute or Skill to do weapon damage. Courtiosie also is not a Social merit either, it's a Fighting Style. <br /> And no, flinging insults and doing obscene hand gestures in order to be able to do extra physical damage is not engaging in a normal conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T01:54:33-07:00","id":1478832,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T05:17:48-07:00","id":1478840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478826#post1478826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, flinging insults and doing obscene hand gestures in order to be able to do extra physical damage is not engaging in a normal conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The line in Awe about talking normally is very clearly about it not providing the bonus to dicepools for supernatural effects, because the same note on Majesty exists in the rules for Lashing Out.<br /> <br /> Courtoisie is explicitly about making your opponent make mistakes through social engagement and being &quot;polite&quot; \u2014 this isn't &quot;flinging insults and doing obscene hand gestures,&quot; it's the exact sort of misdirection that Majesty benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T07:50:24-07:00","id":1478843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478840#post1478840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The line in Awe about talking normally is very clearly about it not providing the bonus to dicepools for supernatural effects, because the same note on Majesty exists in the rules for Lashing Out.<br /> <br /> Courtoisie is explicitly about making your opponent make mistakes through social engagement and being &quot;polite&quot; \u2014 this isn't &quot;flinging insults and doing obscene hand gestures,&quot; it's the exact sort of misdirection that Majesty benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah as in the book literally spells out in English that you DON'T add Majesty or Vigor ratings to your dice rolls for Lashing Out. And that Awe affects Presence rolls, not Manipulation rolls, which is what goading someone into doing something classifies as.<br /> And it also classifies Courtoisie as a Fighting Style for using weapons and hand to hand, not a Social merit for Social maneuvering like Etiquette or Fast Talking. But continue ignoring what the rules say about Awe use since following it means you have to use 15 dice instead of 20 dice to beat someone to Final Death in a social encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-14-2022, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T17:59:07-07:00","id":1478878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478843#post1478843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah as in the book literally spells out in English that you DON'T add Majesty or Vigor ratings to your dice rolls for Lashing Out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The supernatural power. Which Courtoisie isn't, it being a highly social fighting style where the most mechanically unusual element relies on your doing Expression, Intimidation, Socialize, or Subterfuge and/or leveraging your Presence or Manipulation by being sufficiently performative/evocative in the societal theater of A Polite Duel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that Awe affects Presence rolls, not Manipulation rolls, which is what goading someone into doing something classifies as. </div> </div> </div>How unfortunate, then, that the Style doesn't mention any other form of social engagement, the Condition imposed by the second dot of Majesty doesn't specifically benefit Manipulation rolls, and the VtR2e corebook's general rules chapter's section on Presence doesn't describe that Attribute as &quot;assertiveness, gravitas, and raw appeal&quot; or &quot;a strong bearing that changes moods and minds.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it also classifies Courtoisie as a Fighting Style for using weapons and hand to hand, not a Social merit for Social maneuvering like Etiquette or Fast Talking. </div> </div> </div>It is a Style Merit built for engaging in socially-enforced one-on-one fights with weapons. The first dot is for preventing other characters from cutting in, the third dot is for forcing your opposition to engage with you, and the second dot is for allowing you to use your Social Attributes and Skills offensively and defensively.<br /> <br /> These effects define and apply within the context of &quot;the duel,&quot; which is a narrow enough circumstance that being able to Dodge with Manipulation + Socialize or strike with Presence + Intimidation and get a couple of extra bonus dice as long as you're keeping up an appropriate form of banter while you do so is not an overwhelming bonus to have from something as particular as a clan Discipline coupled with a covenant-specific Style Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But continue ignoring what the rules say about Awe use since following it means you have to use 15 dice instead of 20 dice to beat someone to Final Death in a social encounter. </div> </div> </div>What the rules say about Awe use is that it's for talking normally, <i>not for other uses of Majesty</i>, which is a supernatural power whose second dot is rolled with Presence, as are roughly half the Majesty-based Devotions in the core rulebook.<br /> <br /> It's similarly called out as not boosting Presence for the purposes of Lashing Out, which is an extension of the vampire's supernatural qualities that specifically doesn't get bonus dice from Disciplines unless they individually say otherwise.<br /> <br /> Neither of these implies that the basic Be Good At Social Stuff power should not apply to a maneuver premised around using the fact that you're Good At Social Stuff to fare better in a formal duel with weapons than you would in an informal punch-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-14-2022, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T18:16:39-07:00","id":1478880,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>I think the question has been asked and answered. Time to move on.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T04:40:51-07:00","id":1478943,"title":"","content":"why Auspex can't spot out a strix possessing a kindred? Why the questions: is this kindred being possessed? By which creature? should be not valid ones<br /> It seems a weak way to make striges unnoticeable.<br /> <br /> Here the piece of the core I'm referring to which surprised me - Pag 98:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Princes consult Mekhet sages, hoping to find some easier way of telling the Strix apart by scrutinizing suspected hosts with Auspex, but no such method exists \u2014 to the Mekhet<br /> Discipline, the aura of a Strix in a vampire host is exactly \u2014 disturbingly \u2014 like that of a vampire who has committed diablerie. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T05:20:54-07:00","id":1478944,"title":"","content":"A vampire with Auspex isn't literally asking the GM questions and getting answers. The Beast's knowledge comes to mind through sensory impressions and hallucinations: &quot;a pall of grey smoke hanging in the air,&quot; &quot;the smell of brimstone and clotted blood.&quot; It just so happens that the Beast returns the same sensory information for &quot;is this vampire Strix-ridden&quot; as it does &quot;is this vampire a diablerist.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T05:48:45-07:00","id":1478945,"title":"","content":"Don't know. I'm not convinced. &quot;Is this person a diablerist?&quot; is one of the sample questions proposed by the very core book and thus I'm expecting an answer which is different from: What creature is controlling him (given that the kindred is aware about Striges). If I'm asking what creature is controlling someone I'm not expecting to notice he's a diablerist. Also, the text refers to an Aura, like it's a heritage of the 1st edition where Aura's reading was still an Auspex's thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T06:05:35-07:00","id":1478946,"title":"","content":"As the book says, the question you asked was &quot;is this person a diablerist?&quot; and the answer you got was &quot;the smell of brimstone and clotted blood.&quot; The Beast does not speak English and, on this particular point, it doesn't seem to draw a distinction between a vampire who's swallowed a soul and a strix who's drowned the will of a vampire. They're both &quot;the smell of brimstone and clotted blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the answer to your question. We both know the real reason is that strix possession wouldn't be particularly worth being paranoid over if any old Mekhet could reliably spot them. If your objection is just that you don't think the narrative justification for this restriction is satisfying, you're free to feel that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 04-16-2022, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T06:18:06-07:00","id":1478947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478946#post1478946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the book says, the question you asked was &quot;is this person a diablerist?&quot; and the answer you got was &quot;the smell of brimstone and clotted blood.&quot; The Beast does not speak English and, on this particular point, it doesn't seem to draw a distinction between a vampire who's swallowed a soul and a strix who's drowned the will of a vampire. They're both &quot;the smell of brimstone and clotted blood.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the answer to your question. We both know the real reason is that strix possession wouldn't be particularly worth being paranoid over if any old Mekhet could reliably spot them. If your objection is just that you don't think the narrative justification for this restriction is satisfying, you're free to feel that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>you're missing my point. I'm not saying the answer should be verbal or not, no matter the language etc. I'm fine that the answer is provided through conjured imagery. What I'm saying is: If I'm asking whether that guy is a diablerist, and I receive the appropriate imagery, this will answer to the very question related to whether he's Diablerist or not. No matter if he's being possessed by a Strix. On the other end, if I'm asking what creature is possessing him. I'm expecting that the imagery conjured will answer to that question, no matter if it's a diablerist.<br /> Let's say we are facing a strix's possessed kindred which strix never diablerized anyone. Asking: <br /> <br /> - Is this person a diablerist? no answer<br /> - What creature is being possessing this person: a pall of grey smoke hanging the air.<br /> <br /> Which lead me to know that this person is being possessed by a strix, not that it may be a diablerist (if I'm not specifically asking for that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-16-2022, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T06:45:49-07:00","id":1478949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478947#post1478947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026\u2026<br /> Let's say we are facing a strix's possessed kindred which strix never diablerized anyone. Asking: <br /> <br /> - <b> Is this person a diablerist? no answer</b><br /> <br /> \u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Which lead me to know that this person is being possessed by a strix, not that it may be a diablerist (if I'm not specifically asking for that).</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Bold emphases mine.<br /> <br /> IMO, it feels like the intended answer to the first bolded part is actually \u201cYes, he\u2019s a diablerist.\u201d Which would null the second bolded part \u2014 you can never be sure.<br /> (I\u2019m gonna have to reread the book more though)<br /> <br /> Kinda like how normal humans can\u2019t <i>entirely</i> rely on thermometers and digital cameras to ferret out vampires (though some vampire hunters may do). I at least read it in a way that the Strix are to vampires what vampires are to humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Clarity 04-16-2022, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T07:29:38-07:00","id":1478950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478947#post1478947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other end, if I'm asking what creature is possessing him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you asking what creature is possessing him?<br /> <br /> Vampires are routinely at risk of entering a state where they do the sort of things on bad nights that Strix could cause them to do and the Strix are cultural bogey-birds to the vast majority of Kindred who've heard of them. It would be like asking if the Illuminati had replaced a known cocaine addict because you saw them snorting coke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T07:43:07-07:00","id":1478951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478947#post1478947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> you're missing my point. I'm not saying the answer should be verbal or not, no matter the language etc. I'm fine that the answer is provided through conjured imagery. What I'm saying is: If I'm asking whether that guy is a diablerist, and I receive the appropriate imagery, this will answer to the very question related to whether he's Diablerist or not. No matter if he's being possessed by a Strix. On the other end, if I'm asking what creature is possessing him. I'm expecting that the imagery conjured will answer to that question, no matter if it's a diablerist.<br /> Let's say we are facing a strix's possessed kindred which strix never diablerized anyone. Asking: <br /> <br /> - Is this person a diablerist? no answer<br /> - What creature is being possessing this person: a pall of grey smoke hanging the air.<br /> <br /> Which lead me to know that this person is being possessed by a strix, not that it may be a diablerist (if I'm not specifically asking for that).</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, auspex register the Strix as the predatory aura of a vampire.<br /> So if a vampire is possessed by a strix, the beast would feel:<br /> &quot;There is an aura of a different vampire inside this vampire, it must be a diablerist&quot; instead of &quot;there is an aura of something strange inside this vampire, it must be possessed&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T07:44:54-07:00","id":1478952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478950#post1478950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you asking what creature is possessing him?<br /> <br /> Vampires are routinely at risk of entering a state where they do the sort of things on bad nights that Strix could cause them to do and the Strix are cultural bogey-birds to the vast majority of Kindred who've heard of them. It would be like asking if the Illuminati had replaced a known cocaine addict because you saw them snorting coke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if someone is asking, for any reason, whether this kindred is being controlled, the following question would most probably be: by who.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T07:59:22-07:00","id":1478953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478952#post1478952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if someone is asking, for any reason, whether this kindred is being controlled, the following question would most probably be: by who.</div> </div> </div> </div>When Requiem's main forms of supernatural control are not possession-based and the &quot;person&quot; being engaged with is not the person whose body is being possessed, it would seem reasonable to conclude that &quot;Is this person being controlled by someone else?&quot; comes back &quot;no&quot; when turned on a possessing influence.<br /> <br /> Vampires do not routinely and knowingly deal with ghosts and spirits, the Ventrue's ability to possess others is either the pinnacle of Dominate or a high-level Devotion that only works on animals, and basically all of the mechanics of Strix possession treat the Strix as a separate individual for the purposes of effects connected to the host. The Strix is not being controlled, but the embodied Strix is who the questions are being asked about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T09:53:51-07:00","id":1478962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478947#post1478947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying the answer should be verbal or not, no matter the language etc. I'm fine that the answer is provided through conjured imagery. What I'm saying is: If I'm asking whether that guy is a diablerist, and I receive the appropriate imagery,</div> </div> </div> </div>Will you?<br /> <br /> I think you're focusing too much on the mechanics still, for one, and second you're unwilling to accept what the game explicitly declares as an exception to normal rules.<br /> <br /> The <b><i>setting</i></b> defines that a Strix possession can't be distinguished from Diablerie. Just roll with it instead of trying to game it out of existence. If you ask &quot;did this person commit Diablerie?&quot;, the answer will be yes, because that's how Strix possession works. If you ask &quot;Is this person possessed?&quot;, the answer will be no, because that's still how Strix possession works. If you don't like Strix possession working like that, change it in your game.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the power isn't obliged to only answer the specific question you made just because the mechanics posits it in terms of questions and answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T11:13:35-07:00","id":1478965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478947#post1478947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Is this person a diablerist? no answer<br /> - What creature is being possessing this person: a pall of grey smoke hanging the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>21C has it: the Beast cannot distinguish the difference between &quot;is a diablerist&quot; and &quot;is strix-possessed.&quot; If you ask &quot;is this person a diablerist?&quot; the answer is <i>yes</i> when the person is strix-possessed. And conversely, if you ask &quot;is this person strix-possessed?&quot; the answer is <i>yes</i> when the person is a diablerist who is not strix-possessed. Other questions, I think, don't twig: &quot;is this person being controlled by someone else?&quot; is more aimed at powers like Dominate, whereas I'm not sure I would allow &quot;what creature is possessing this person?&quot; as a valid Auspex question in the first place. Narratively, say, the Beast is probably interpreting &quot;this person&quot; to mean the strix and not the comatose body it's riding.<br /> <br /> In general, answer Auspex questions on the assumption that you can't use Auspex to detect strix possession. It's just an in-built inability of Auspex, an exception case to its reliability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T11:26:31-07:00","id":1478966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1478965#post1478965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 21C has it: the Beast cannot distinguish the difference between &amp;quot;is a diablerist&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;is strix-possessed.&amp;quot; If you ask &amp;quot;is this person a diablerist?&amp;quot; the answer is <i>yes</i> when the person is strix-possessed. And conversely, if you ask &amp;quot;is this person strix-possessed?&amp;quot; the answer is <i>yes</i> when the person is a diablerist who is not strix-possessed. Other questions, I think, don't twig: &amp;quot;is this person being controlled by someone else?&amp;quot; is more aimed at powers like Dominate, whereas I'm not sure I would allow &amp;quot;what creature is possessing this person?&amp;quot; as a valid Auspex question in the first place. Narratively, say, the Beast is probably interpreting &amp;quot;this person&amp;quot; to mean the strix and not the comatose body it's riding.<br /> <br /> In general, answer Auspex questions on the assumption that you can't use Auspex to detect strix possession. It's just an in-built inability of Auspex, an exception case to its reliability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's sounds quite fair if we consider it as a specific exception of Auspex. I can live with that, I'm only sorry I didn't know at the time my players made that question to me \ud83d\ude05.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T07:09:41-07:00","id":1479295,"title":"","content":"Hello everybody,<br /> <br /> a little context first. Im getting ready to run a chronicle using requiem for rome. I'm using first edition Requiem. One thing that bugs me about first edition is how &quot;squishy&quot; the Kindred feel due to taking lethal from blades. I liked that 2E made it so that they take only bashing from &quot;mundane&quot; sources of DMG.<br /> <br /> So my question is, would it break anything, mechanics-wise, if I used 2E Ruling regarding bashing/lethal dmg ? Because I can't think of anything but I wanted to make sure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We are using VTR 1E, Requiem for Rome, Fall of the Camarilla and maybe WOD Armory.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T07:18:17-07:00","id":1479296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacedigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1479295#post1479295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everybody,<br /> <br /> a little context first. Im getting ready to run a chronicle using requiem for rome. I'm using first edition Requiem. One thing that bugs me about first edition is how &quot;squishy&quot; the Kindred feel due to taking lethal from blades. I liked that 2E made it so that they take only bashing from &quot;mundane&quot; sources of DMG.<br /> <br /> So my question is, would it break anything, mechanics-wise, if I used 2E Ruling regarding bashing/lethal dmg ? Because I can't think of anything but I wanted to make sure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We are using VTR 1E, Requiem for Rome, Fall of the Camarilla and maybe WOD Armory.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, kindred do take bashing from any mundane weapon in 1st ed. Also. What led you to think differently? I may have lost something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T07:23:05-07:00","id":1479297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1479296#post1479296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know, kindred do take bashing from any mundane weapon in 1st ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be misremembering from the fact that 1e Kindred take bashing damage from <i>f</i><i>irearms.</i> Melee weapons still dealt lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T07:58:56-07:00","id":1479299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1479296#post1479296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know, kindred do take bashing from any mundane weapon in 1st ed. Also. What led you to think differently? I may have lost something</div> </div> </div> </div>I only have the printed german version of the VTR 1E Corebook. But it states under the description of Lethal DMG that blade do inflict Lethal DMG to kindred. Since blades will be very relevant in the roman setting, appart from the occasional club maybe, I wanted to make my players a little bit more resilient, and really show that they do not need really need their insides anymore ^^' Apart from brain and heart I guess...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T08:04:42-07:00","id":1479300,"title":"","content":"Yes, you are right indeed. Well, 1st ed had a lot of issues in my view. I personally run fall of Camarilla Chronicle (which is supposely created for 1st ed) using 2ed rules and it worked just fine. So you should not have issues having blades dealing bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T18:22:23-07:00","id":1479321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacedigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1479299#post1479299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only have the printed german version of the VTR 1E Corebook. But it states under the description of Lethal DMG that blade do inflict Lethal DMG to kindred. Since blades will be very relevant in the roman setting, appart from the occasional club maybe, I wanted to make my players a little bit more resilient, and really show that they do not need really need their insides anymore ^^' Apart from brain and heart I guess...</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't break anything as you're applying it to all Kindred, although it may be reasonable to consider porting over to 2nd ed entirely.<br /> <br /> And you don't need your brains, either, this is a common misconception, but vampires only really need their hearts and their <b>heads</b>, and for mystical reasons that do not link to any organ or amount of mass in particular. It is the symbolic idea of a head that counts, and in a society that attributes advanced thought and emotions to the stomach, this symbolic head is probably more face than nervous system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T20:48:47-07:00","id":1479324,"title":"","content":"How long does it take, roughly, for a Kindred to develop their discipline abilities after the embrace?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T22:41:42-07:00","id":1479326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1479324#post1479324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does it take, roughly, for a Kindred to develop their discipline abilities after the embrace?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t remember anything from the books, other than how Disciplines tend to rise spontaneously, or via violence.<br /> <br /> For neonates, I\u2019d personally go for \u201cas long as it takes for the fledgeling to recognize and wholeheartedly accept that she will need to violate others just to survive\u201d. For some people, that\u2019ll take awhile. For some, nigh none.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T23:11:10-07:00","id":1479327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1479324#post1479324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does it take, roughly, for a Kindred to develop their discipline abilities after the embrace?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not only undisclosed on the books, but hard to define.<br /> <br /> My own rule of thumb is about 6 months to 1 year for the average Fledgling, as far as you can define such a vampire. That assumes that this initial development happens some time after learning the basics of your new condition and attaining self-control, but once you're ready it is kind of instinctive and builds up on this recent experience. It is probably also non-linear, with fleeting, uncontrolled and incomplete effects of what will be those first three dots manifesting sometimes until the Fledgling learns to control them in quick succession.<br /> <br /> But this rule may vary wildly depending on too may factors. The Kindred condition is only superficially similar, and the mortal source of this new vampire also matters. The context of the Embrace, the particulars of the Sire, everything may play a role. This rule also assumes that the first three dots have the same general nature and effort of any other, but maybe they're aren't metaphysically the same. Maybe they're more innate, or maybe less, something with a barrier for gain that needs to be surpassed to then unlock the ability to learn Disciplines.<br /> <br /> So in the end they may have taken the entire backstory of a character, maybe even decades to learn. And maybe they'd been there from the moment of the Embrace, as natural as walking, eating and not breathing. And maybe a single character may have the three cases, with each of the first dots being learned with huge spams of time between them.<br /> <br /> Whatever makes for a good story or serves as the baseline for a chronicle that starts right after the Embrace. There's not many hard facts about the Kindred in Requiem, the time for development of the first Disciplines isn't one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T03:19:11-07:00","id":1479330,"title":"","content":"I would assume the Embrace straight up grants one or two dots. The question is how long until they realise they actually have those powers, which could vary wildly depending on whether someone's there to explain shit for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T04:47:34-07:00","id":1479332,"title":"","content":"I'm on the idea that the first 3 dots are coming with the embrace and the new kindred would discover theme in case of need or dangerous situation (if not instructed)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T08:39:19-07:00","id":1479339,"title":"","content":"I wrote one to two dots because only two dots have to be from in-Clan Disciplines. The third can even be of a Covenant Discipline. The text even says that the player should consider how the vampire learned the third dot if it's not in-Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T10:36:01-07:00","id":1479347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1479339#post1479339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote one to two dots because only two dots have to be from in-Clan Disciplines. The third can even be of a Covenant Discipline. The text even says that the player should consider how the vampire learned the third dot if it's not in-Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't mean this third dot can't be innate too, as long as it isn't a Covenant Discipline. The Curse is fickle, spontaneously developing the first dot of a random Discipline, even at the very Embrace, isn't out of the table, either as a response to your specific Sire's curse or an effect of your own unique circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T17:05:13-07:00","id":1479381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1479347#post1479347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't mean this third dot can't be innate too, as long as it isn't a Covenant Discipline. The Curse is fickle, spontaneously developing the first dot of a random Discipline, even at the very Embrace, isn't out of the table, either as a response to your specific Sire's curse or an effect of your own unique circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, very much this. First Requiem PC i made, a nosferatu car theft boss, happened to start with Auspex, something his mind would later on associate with vague recollections of seeing his soon to be sire looming over him in a pale aura crisscrossed in black veins, while he bled on the sidewalk on his last moments as a living, breathing man on earth. Flashes that would later on led into some hefty curiosity tinged with paranoia as he learned more of kindred nature and his own powers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> But anyway, a probable mix of sire vitae tainted through diablerie with a natural aptitude awakened while on the edge of death, could be said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-23-2022, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 