atar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T16:08:15-07:00","id":1481793,"title":"","content":"if a revenant is left out right before dawn with a lockpicking kit think its a fair test??<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T16:49:34-07:00","id":1481802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1481793#post1481793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if a revenant is left out right before dawn with a lockpicking kit think its a fair test??</div> </div> </div> </div>At a fixed BP of 1 they're taking damage every ten minutes and rolling to resist frenzy with a -1 penalty unless they're hurt or hungry or especially inhuman. What is the test here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T20:41:06-07:00","id":1481814,"title":"","content":"thought the mention of a lockpicking kit made it obvious? To pick the lock into a house or utility shed To avoid being killed by the sun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T21:09:00-07:00","id":1481818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1481814#post1481814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thought the mention of a lockpicking kit made it obvious? To pick the lock into a house or utility shed To avoid being killed by the sun.</div> </div> </div> </div>To make the question more obvious: What is being tested by specifically putting a character in a situation where they will assuredly suffer an atavistic panic response and take a path of lesser resistance like hiding behind the shed or battering down the door or breaking into a nearby house or going literally any other route that doesn't require them to manage precision tools in a time-sensitive situation that is more tremendously uncomfortable than deadly for a starting character, and by what metric are we being asked to say if it is or is not &quot;fair&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T11:33:49-07:00","id":1481853,"title":"","content":"whats being tested is their ability to think clearly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T13:49:39-07:00","id":1481950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1481853#post1481853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">whats being tested is their ability to think clearly.</div> </div> </div> </div>They won't.<br /> <br /> At the first signs of coming dawn Frenzy will kick in, and even in the absence of frenzy panic will ensue. Not to say that the tool itself means nothing if the character doesn't have some experience and skill with it. This is a setup meant for unavoidable failure.<br /> <br /> If you want to measure a Revenant's ability to think clearly, you need a situation that doesn't require a particular skill, either by being simple if focus demanding, or by being open to several solutions, and you must not pressure with imminent Frenzy-inducing stimuli.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T12:40:42-07:00","id":1482960,"title":"","content":"Will there be any more books for the second edition? <br /> <br /> I would like to see:<br /> - A book about the Strix<br /> - Once upon a midnight darkly: A \u201cDark Fairy Tales\u201d theme book based on the origins of the clans <br /> - More updates of the first edition books","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T12:47:35-07:00","id":1482962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1482960#post1482960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be any more books for the second edition?<br /> <br /> I would like to see:<br /> - A book about the Strix<br /> - Once upon a midnight darkly: A \u201cDark Fairy Tales\u201d theme book based on the origins of the clans<br /> - More updates of the first edition books</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think there was a supplement about a broken masquerade that was supposed to come out but so far no news...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T13:20:25-07:00","id":1482964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elythia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1482960#post1482960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be any more books for the second edition?<br /> <br /> I would like to see:<br /> (...)<br /> - More updates of the first edition books</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no official books on the horizon, but some of the CofD freelancers took to writing books for the Storytellers Vault under the name <i>None More Dark Publishing</i>. That includes expansions for Clanbooks and updates for old Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T06:33:22-07:00","id":1484350,"title":"","content":"Sort of the opposite of that Carthian Pull question from a while back: Can Safe Places tied to an Attach\u00e9 be made Havens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T02:11:06-07:00","id":1484489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1484350#post1484350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of the opposite of that Carthian Pull question from a while back: Can Safe Places tied to an Attach\u00e9 be made Havens?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. By the rules as written, nothing prevents it, and I don't think it violates the spirit of the rules. The drawback of Attach\u00e9 would still apply, so it wouldn't be the most convenient-to-access haven in the world, but I think it makes sense that a character could develop a personal attachment to it, even if it doesn't expressly belong to her (what are vampires if not parasites, after all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T19:31:47-07:00","id":1484569,"title":"","content":"This one is awkward. I know (or at least I <i>think</i> I know) that when making a character the fifth rank in attributes costs two points, or dots.<br /> <br /> I swear I remember this <i>somewhere</i>, but I can't find <i>where</i>. I have both the ChoD and VtR pdfs open and I'm skimming through them (using the search function for Attributes and dots) but I'm not finding them. <br /> <br /> Is this a relic from the First Edition books, or am I just blind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T21:12:49-07:00","id":1484575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1484569#post1484569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one is awkward. I know (or at least I <i>think</i> I know) that when making a character the fifth rank in attributes costs two points, or dots.<br /> <br /> I swear I remember this <i>somewhere</i>, but I can't find <i>where</i>. I have both the ChoD and VtR pdfs open and I'm skimming through them (using the search function for Attributes and dots) but I'm not finding them. <br /> <br /> Is this a relic from the First Edition books, or am I just blind?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is indeed a 1e thing. 2e does not have this limitation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T21:19:30-07:00","id":1484576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lorekeeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1484575#post1484575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is indeed a 1e thing. 2e does not have this limitation</div> </div> </div> </div>So If I put an Attribute in my Primary right up to Five, I STILL have one dot left?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T22:14:11-07:00","id":1484577,"title":"","content":"If Physical is your primary set, Strength \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf Dexterity \u25cf Stamina \u25cf\u25cf is a valid spread, even before applying the Favored Attribute from the Kindred template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T19:14:33-07:00","id":1484924,"title":"","content":"The Devotion &quot;Conditioning&quot; (2E Requiem, Pg 143) is written to only use one Discipline Dominate. Aren't Devotions supposed to be a combination of Disciplines?<br /> <br /> Is there a required Discipline not mentioned? And if there isn't, why is Conditioning listed as a Devotion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T19:31:40-07:00","id":1484927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1484924#post1484924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devotion &quot;Conditioning&quot; (2E Requiem, Pg 143) is written to only use one Discipline Dominate. Aren't Devotions supposed to be a combination of Disciplines?<br /> <br /> Is there a required Discipline not mentioned? And if there isn't, why is Conditioning listed as a Devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Disciplines are the cemented (or metaphysically more mainstream at the moment) forms of the expressions of the Beast's(/Curse's/Blood's/etc.) power, practiced and cultivated enough that it becomes a norm. Devotions are mutagens and strange iterations of viral curses, cancerous memetics, and fractally warped legacies-deviations from that now established strain of power which denote things that were, things to come, or things sideways to....well, not the sun.<br /> <br /> The most <i>common</i> way for such to develop and otherwise express is &quot;This power is the unholy love child of this Discipline and that Discipline&quot;, but any given growing/rotting tendril of the Beast's/Curse's/Blood's power has enough muscle and sinew to writhe and wriggle in different ways. All it takes is someone looking at their inner eye* expressed by Auspex and wondering &quot;Okay, but what if I rip it out and leave it on the bannister, can I still <i>see</i> what's happening underneath the skin of reality at that point?&quot; to realize what might be done.<br /> <br /> As an idea, it's a personal microcosm of the dread barbarians at the gate leave Requiem Kindred-not so much that they <i>invade</i>, so much as they <i>infect, change</i>, and <i>become part of the family/self</i>.<br /> <br /> *&quot;<i>i f y o u r a j n a i s n o t a n e y e, t h e n w h y i t c a l l i t s u c h? A l u m p o f v i t r e o u s b o d y a n d a q u e o u s h u m o r s h a l l s e e j u s t a s c l e a r.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-24-2022, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-24T23:19:05-07:00","id":1484944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1484924#post1484924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devotion &quot;Conditioning&quot; (2E Requiem, Pg 143) is written to only use one Discipline Dominate. Aren't Devotions supposed to be a combination of Disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer, no, they're not. They can have any requirement including at least 1 Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T00:06:20-07:00","id":1484947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1484924#post1484924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devotion &quot;Conditioning&quot; (2E Requiem, Pg 143) is written to only use one Discipline Dominate. Aren't Devotions supposed to be a combination of Disciplines?<br /> <br /> Is there a required Discipline not mentioned? And if there isn't, why is Conditioning listed as a Devotion?</div> </div> </div> </div>As it has been said above. I just want to add that Conditioning is not even the only 1 discipline example, e.g.: summoming. But there are others also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T00:29:58-07:00","id":1484948,"title":"","content":"The need for two or more Disciplines <i>was</i> a thing in Masquerade, where the only thing similar to Devotions are Combo Disciplines, and they indeed work with at least two Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T04:55:58-07:00","id":1485617,"title":"","content":"I was wondering something about the active effect of vigor that let's you grab and use big objects like cars and boulders as weapons, the book states that you can't grab objects with size greater than a character's strength, this effectively means that, going by the book sizes examples at pag. 182, you are likely never going to be able to lift items like cars and boulders since they could get size 10+. Meanwhile I just bought the revised version of reap the whrilwind whose rules for vigor states that you can simply lift and use whatever you can get your hands on, now, given that the revised edition of reap the whirlwind came after the requiem 2nd ed corebook, should I consider the rullings in it as an errata of sort?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T05:37:07-07:00","id":1485619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1485617#post1485617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering something about the active effect of vigor that let's you grab and use big objects like cars and boulders as weapons, the book states that you can't grab objects with size greater than a character's strength, this effectively means that, going by the book sizes examples at pag. 182, you are likely never going to be able to lift items like cars and boulders since they could get size 10+. Meanwhile I just bought the revised version of reap the whrilwind whose rules for vigor states that you can simply lift and use whatever you can get your hands on, now, given that the revised edition of reap the whirlwind came after the requiem 2nd ed corebook, should I consider the rullings in it as an errata of sort?</div> </div> </div> </div>By the way by boosting your strength with blood you can easy use a car as a weapon. Let's consider strength 4 Vigor 3, with 2 vitae it's totally feasible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T06:34:19-07:00","id":1485621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1485619#post1485619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way by boosting your strength with blood you can easy use a car as a weapon. Let's consider strength 4 Vigor 3, with 2 vitae it's totally feasible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Physical Intensity only adds to rolls, not Traits. More concretely, vampires whose Blood Potency used to be high enough to support baseline Traits above 5 still benefit from those Traits.<br /> <br /> IIRC, back in 1e the Strength + Stamina roll for lifting objects explicitly added to your Strength for that purpose, and per Deviant's expanded version of the Size chart a sports car is Size 10 and an SUV is Size 15; a character with Strength 4 and Vigor 4 could lift a compact car (Size 8) easily enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T06:40:57-07:00","id":1485622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1485621#post1485621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical Intensity only adds to rolls, not Traits. More concretely, vampires whose Blood Potency used to be high enough to support baseline Traits above 5 still benefit from those Traits.<br /> <br /> IIRC, back in 1e the Strength + Stamina roll for lifting objects explicitly added to your Strength for that purpose, and per Deviant's expanded version of the Size chart a sports car is Size 10 and an SUV is Size 15; a character with Strength 4 and Vigor 4 could lift a compact car (Size 8) easily enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer, I think I will use the rules in reap the whirlwind at this point, the book is pretty unclear also on how this objects would work as improvised weapons like saying that objects size 5 deal lethal to mortal while by raw, basically all items used as weapons would deal lethal regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T06:43:40-07:00","id":1485623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1485621#post1485621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical Intensity only adds to rolls, not Traits. More concretely, vampires whose Blood Potency used to be high enough to support baseline Traits above 5 still benefit from those Traits.<br /> <br /> IIRC, back in 1e the Strength + Stamina roll for lifting objects explicitly added to your Strength for that purpose, and per Deviant's expanded version of the Size chart a sports car is Size 10 and an SUV is Size 15; a character with Strength 4 and Vigor 4 could lift a compact car (Size 8) easily enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer, I think I will use the rules in reap the whirlwind at this point, the core is pretty unclear on this and the rules for using big items as improvised weapons are similarly confusing (items size 5 deal lethal but by raw, all items used as weapons deal lethal regardless).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T13:05:46-07:00","id":1485641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1485622#post1485622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I will use the rules in reap the whirlwind at this point</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules in Reap the Whirlwind are the same in the revised version as in the original. It says that you can use any object you can lift as an improvised melee or throwing weapon, and the book's section on Attributes describes Strength as &quot;How much your character can lift, and how hard he hits.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given that the text did not change at all between publishings and &quot;getting hit by a truck&quot; is specifically given as an example of the sort of massive bodily destruction that vampires still suffer lethal damage from, we can safely conclude that they did not put a stealth erratum in the second publishing of the quickstart book for VtR2e just because the wording was less precise.<br /> <br /> This is a &quot;book was designed before they were allowed to do a formalized Second Edition&quot; artifact, kind of like how the rules for Fatigue weren't in every book and a couple of slightly different Conditions filled the role instead. Vampires throwing cars is still an impressive feat rather than something any schmuck with Vigor 1 can pull off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-02-2022, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T14:07:21-07:00","id":1485646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1485641#post1485641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules in Reap the Whirlwind are the same in the revised version as in the original. It says that you can use any object you can lift as an improvised melee or throwing weapon, and the book's section on Attributes describes Strength as &quot;How much your character can lift, and how hard he hits.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given that the text did not change at all between publishings and &quot;getting hit by a truck&quot; is specifically given as an example of the sort of massive bodily destruction that vampires still suffer lethal damage from, we can safely conclude that they did not put a stealth erratum in the second publishing of the quickstart book for VtR2e just because the wording was less precise.<br /> <br /> This is a &quot;book was designed before they were allowed to do a formalized Second Edition&quot; artifact, kind of like how the rules for Fatigue weren't in every book and a couple of slightly different Conditions filled the role instead. Vampires throwing cars is still an impressive feat rather than something any schmuck with Vigor 1 can pull off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T01:23:25-07:00","id":1485683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1485621#post1485621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical Intensity only adds to rolls, not Traits. More concretely, vampires whose Blood Potency used to be high enough to support baseline Traits above 5 still benefit from those Traits.<br /> <br /> IIRC, back in 1e the Strength + Stamina roll for lifting objects explicitly added to your Strength for that purpose, and per Deviant's expanded version of the Size chart a sports car is Size 10 and an SUV is Size 15; a character with Strength 4 and Vigor 4 could lift a compact car (Size 8) easily enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does not add specifically to DERIVED traits. Strength it's not a derived trait so I still consider physical intensity as adding to strength for the purpose of lifting obiect since the very description talks about impressive, short, physical feats, which lifting a car is indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T05:38:07-07:00","id":1486333,"title":"","content":"Hi<br /> <br /> My question is rather simple. After reading the Dominate discipline, it is my understanding that any vampire can attempt to dominate any other vampire regardless of their respective Blood Potency (unlike in Masquerade) and Blood Potency only helps know in the contested roll to defend against the effects of the discipline. Did I get that right?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5712-daraexus","name":"Daraexus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5712_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T05:46:31-07:00","id":1486335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daraexus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1486333#post1486333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi<br /> <br /> My question is rather simple. After reading the Dominate discipline, it is my understanding that any vampire can attempt to dominate any other vampire regardless of their respective Blood Potency (unlike in Masquerade) and Blood Potency only helps know in the contested roll to defend against the effects of the discipline. Did I get that right?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!</div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T05:57:32-07:00","id":1486336,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5712-daraexus","name":"Daraexus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5712_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T04:37:27-07:00","id":1486861,"title":"","content":"Is the whole &quot;vampires are blurry on camera&quot; thing still canon in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T04:39:52-07:00","id":1486862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1486861#post1486861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the whole &amp;quot;vampires are blurry on camera&amp;quot; thing still canon in 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc, the Lost Visage works as a string of coincidences that helps the vampire avoid getting properly filmed, as opposed to brute-forcing the result via blurring the image. It\u2019s not a conscious thing, but a vampire can willingly shut it down I believe. Gonna have to look again for the exact wordings, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T04:46:41-07:00","id":1486863,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T06:46:28-07:00","id":1486877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1486862#post1486862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc, the Lost Visage works as a string of coincidences that helps the vampire avoid getting properly filmed, as opposed to brute-forcing the result via blurring the image. It\u2019s not a conscious thing, but a vampire can willingly shut it down I believe. Gonna have to look again for the exact wordings, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right. Unless there is more information in one of the supplements, the only information I can find on it in 2ed core is on page 60 where it is described as part of the First Tradition fluff without any sort of mechanical details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T16:54:35-07:00","id":1489168,"title":"","content":"Can a victim be reduced to zero Composure through Mortal Terror? If so, what happens if that threshold is hit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-04T17:39:12-07:00","id":1489172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1489168#post1489168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a victim be reduced to zero Composure through Mortal Terror? If so, what happens if that threshold is hit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely recall reading mechanics somewhere in 1e that an Attribute reduced to 0 prevented you from performing any tasks that required that Attribute, but I don't remember where I saw that, I wouldn't know where to begin looking, and it might have been unofficial content.<br /> <br /> In the context of 2e, since no mechanics are provided for Attribute ratings below 1 besides the Strix's rules for decaying corpse hosts, a rating of 1 represents below-average talent in an Attribute, and Mortal Terror already applies a Condition that also penalizes Resolve, I think it's safe to run the Dread bonus as capped at reducing the victim to Composure 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T00:13:32-07:00","id":1489196,"title":"","content":"Primary and long story short, &quot;make a great story&quot;. For those more structure-types like me, any dice pool reduced to 0 is a chance roll...so let them roll 1d10, and everyone can lose their shit when they roll a 0 (=10) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Remember your primary goal is to make great memories for your players. No one 'wins' or 'loses' in the eternity of the WoD, we just draw out the drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27517-theran","name":"Theran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T10:35:43-07:00","id":1489245,"title":"","content":"I tried seeing if this was already asked/answered, but couldn't find it. The section for 'Resisting Frenzy' mentions earning a Beat when entering a Frenzy where there is a dramatic situation and consequences. Does a Player still earn a beat if they Ride the Wave with the same narrative weight for dramatics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11410-mclugh","name":"McLugh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-05T12:15:46-07:00","id":1489256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>McLugh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1489245#post1489245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried seeing if this was already asked/answered, but couldn't find it. The section for 'Resisting Frenzy' mentions earning a Beat when entering a Frenzy where there is a dramatic situation and consequences. Does a Player still earn a beat if they Ride the Wave with the same narrative weight for dramatics?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say nope!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T05:23:12-07:00","id":1489470,"title":"","content":"How much Vitae can be possibly taken from a mortal?<br /> <br /> The Corebook establishes that a kindred deals one lethal damage per Vitae to a mortal vessel, be it by using The Kiss or by assaulting them. So, assuming that an average mortal would have Stamina 2 and therefore Health 7, what is the maximum amount of Vitae that can be taken from this typical mortal? Is it 7, equal to the number of Health boxes that they would have? Or is it 14, allowing vampire to first fill mortal's Health track with lethal damage and then with aggravated, getting two times worth of Vitae in return?<br /> <br /> If so, how would that correspond with the rule that states:<i>&quot;When mortal's rightmost Health box has lethal damage, she takes another point of damage each minute (upgrading existing lethal damage to aggravated) until she receives medical attention or dies&quot;? </i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27533-vargock","name":"Vargock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T06:42:22-07:00","id":1489476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vargock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1489470#post1489470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much Vitae can be possibly taken from a mortal?<br /> <br /> The Corebook establishes that a kindred deals one lethal damage per Vitae to a mortal vessel, be it by using The Kiss or by assaulting them. So, assuming that an average mortal would have Stamina 2 and therefore Health 7, what is the maximum amount of Vitae that can be taken from this typical mortal? Is it 7, equal to the number of Health boxes that they would have? Or is it 14, allowing vampire to first fill mortal's Health track with lethal damage and then with aggravated, getting two times worth of Vitae in return?<br /> <br /> If so, how would that correspond with the rule that states:<i>&quot;When mortal's rightmost Health box has lethal damage, she takes another point of damage each minute (upgrading existing lethal damage to aggravated) until she receives medical attention or dies&quot;? </i></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Kindred can pull a number of Vitae from a mortal equal to the mortal\u2019s unmodified Health dots.&quot;<br /> p.95","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T07:52:13-07:00","id":1489483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1489476#post1489476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Kindred can pull a number of Vitae from a mortal equal to the mortal\u2019s unmodified Health dots.&quot;<br /> p.95</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's embarrassing xD I read this paragraph so many times, but somehow my eyes slipped past this statement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27533-vargock","name":"Vargock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T03:12:18-07:00","id":1490237,"title":"","content":"Is it possibile to speak being still under the effect of Obfuscate 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T14:55:11-07:00","id":1490444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1490237#post1490237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possibile to speak being still under the effect of Obfuscate 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VTR2E, p. 137</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obfuscate tricks the victim\u2019s mind directly, removing traces of the vampire from the sensory information reaching her brain, rather than fooling her senses directly. Obfuscate affects smell and taste as much as sight or <b>hearing</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, Obfuscate covers all the senses; it removes you from other people's <i>perceptions</i>, not just their sight.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T16:04:04-07:00","id":1490449,"title":"","content":"Speaking of obfuscate, the book mention tracking the vampire while obfuscated with an extended action but does this actually break obfuscate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T01:26:37-07:00","id":1490493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1490444#post1490444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Basically, Obfuscate covers all the senses; it removes you from other people's <i>perceptions</i>, not just their sight.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, I was actually asking if it's possible to speak to a subject remaining invisible although heard by himself. I think that, strictly sticking to mechanics, it is a kind of interaction with the subject so that would have you being visible for himself.<br /> <br /> And more over: being invisible trying to carry a dead (or also alive) body how that would be seen by people around him? Would it be seen as a flying corps/man? How big can be the object which an invisible kindred can carry without having anyone notice that? A pistol for sure, a rifle maybe..?!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1490449#post1490449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of obfuscate, the book mention tracking the vampire while obfuscated with an extended action but does this actually break obfuscate?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit unclear but I think that you can UNDERSTAND where he's staying and then, perceiving him, you can Lash Out against him to break obfuscate or, if you are not a kindred, trying a &quot;Blind&quot; attack (-5 - defense) to try catching him.<br /> <br /> Normally this would be a prolonged roll for the seeker against the successes rolled by the first roll of who is hiding, but I don't like this mechanic to much as, after several attempts it's pretty normal to spot an obfuscate being so what I personally do is:<br /> <br /> - if the vampire remain still i adopt the normal rule with the prolonged roll<br /> - if the vampire is changing position for me it's either a you catch him on the first roll or not, rolling on every new area/room.<br /> <br /> But I think this can be refined honestly as I'm not very happy with that also!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-17-2022, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T03:29:30-07:00","id":1490502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1490493#post1490493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks, I was actually asking if it's possible to speak to a subject remaining invisible although heard by himself. I think that, strictly sticking to mechanics, it is a kind of interaction with the subject so that would have you being visible for himself.<br /> <br /> And more over: being invisible trying to carry a dead (or also alive) body how that would be seen by people around him? Would it be seen as a flying corps/man? How big can be the object which an invisible kindred can carry without having anyone notice that? A pistol for sure, a rifle maybe..?!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's a bit unclear but I think that you can UNDERSTAND where he's staying and then, perceiving him, you can Lash Out against him to break obfuscate or, if you are not a kindred, trying a &quot;Blind&quot; attack (-5 - defense) to try catching him.<br /> <br /> Normally this would be a prolonged roll for the seeker against the successes rolled by the first roll of who is hiding, but I don't like this mechanic to much as, after several attempts it's pretty normal to spot an obfuscate being so what I personally do is:<br /> <br /> - if the vampire remain still i adopt the normal rule with the prolonged roll<br /> - if the vampire is changing position for me it's either a you catch him on the first roll or no, rolling on every new area/room.<br /> <br /> But I think this can be refined honestly as I'm not very happy with that also!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the answer, I'm running a vampire game now and made a mortal with very high tracking skills and professional training in it so I was unsure if adding him to the game would have been too much since he is most likely going to track an obfuscate user in one turn, a blind attack makes perfect sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T00:30:25-07:00","id":1490969,"title":"","content":"About waking in case of danger book says: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The dead heart shoves Vitae through the body once, hard. When something disturbs the vampire\u2019s slumber or puts her at risk, make a Humanity roll. Success allows her to remain awake for a number of turns equal to her Humanity. Failure means she remains asleep. Once those turns are over, she falls back to sleep without an additional Humanity roll. Once she\u2019s exceeded 5 + her Blood Potency successes during her waking turns, she can remain awake indefinitely, as if she never went to sleep in the first place. </div> </div> </div>It's not clear to me how such 5+BP successes are supposed to be accumulated; Supposing that the humanity roll is successful and - let's say - having humanity 6 the vampire is able to act for 6 turns, is he supposed to roll Stamina+Resolve every turn hoping to reach the 5+BP successes within these 6 turns?<br /> Text also says: as if she never went to sleep in the first place. Is the lethargic condition still applicable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T09:55:19-07:00","id":1491102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1490969#post1490969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About waking in case of danger book says:<br /> <br /> It's not clear to me how such 5+BP successes are supposed to be accumulated; Supposing that the humanity roll is successful and - let's say - having humanity 6 the vampire is able to act for 6 turns, is he supposed to roll Stamina+Resolve every turn hoping to reach the 5+BP successes within these 6 turns?<br /> Text also says: as if she never went to sleep in the first place. Is the lethargic condition still applicable?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the condition, but otherwise I think what would happen is this: at the end of the 6 turns awake, if the vampire still wanted to stay awake they would have to make another Humanity roll. If successful they can stay awake another Humanity turns (6 in this case). This keeps repeating every Humanity turns as long as the vampire wants to stay awake until the total successes on all the Humanity rolls exceeds 5+Blood Potency at which point they no longer have to roll and can just stay awake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T11:04:01-07:00","id":1491106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brennanhawkwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1491102#post1491102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know about the condition, but otherwise I think what would happen is this: at the end of the 6 turns awake, if the vampire still wanted to stay awake they would have to make another Humanity roll. If successful they can stay awake another Humanity turns (6 in this case). This keeps repeating every Humanity turns as long as the vampire wants to stay awake until the total successes on all the Humanity rolls exceeds 5+Blood Potency at which point they no longer have to roll and can just stay awake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, that makes sense. I misinterpreted the text saying: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once those turns are over, she falls back to sleep without an additional Humanity roll </div> </div> </div> as if it was stating that NO further humanity rolls were allowed, but I was wrong!!<br /> Thanks!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T19:21:07-07:00","id":1491389,"title":"","content":"curious on feeding<br /> <br /> <br /> if I'm hunting animals' ideas when animal ken or survival is appropriate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T01:47:33-07:00","id":1491403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1491389#post1491389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">curious on feeding<br /> <br /> <br /> if I'm hunting animals' ideas when animal ken or survival is appropriate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Survival is to find out animals: where they could possibly hide, what kind in a specific area or how to lure them.<br /> <br /> Animal ken is for when you meet them and want to approach without having them fleeing or attacking you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-01T09:52:32-07:00","id":1494095,"title":"","content":"can a ghoul make a feeding roll to assist his master?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T02:26:37-07:00","id":1494125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1494095#post1494095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can a ghoul make a feeding roll to assist his master?</div> </div> </div> </div>Using teamwork rules, why not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T06:59:59-07:00","id":1494727,"title":"","content":"Does lava(molten rock) count as a source for aggravated damage for Vampires?<br /> <br /> While lava can burn things with relative ease, lava is not fire. Does the vampire takes aggavated damage from burns of any kind, like electrical burns, lava, etc, or only fire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T07:56:56-07:00","id":1494730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1494727#post1494727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does lava(molten rock) count as a source for aggravated damage for Vampires?<br /> <br /> While lava can burn things with relative ease, lava is not fire. Does the vampire takes aggavated damage from burns of any kind, like electrical burns, lava, etc, or only fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lava is the sort of thing that sets flammable things on fire upon contact, including human bodies. That part would deal aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Burns from other sources should be downgraded. They're not fire, and generally causes burns without igniting the victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T08:32:34-07:00","id":1494732,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure human body can be set on fire though. It can be burnt but it shouldn't be flamable (except for hair). I may be wrong though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-10T09:00:36-07:00","id":1494735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1494732#post1494732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure human body can be set on fire though. It can be burnt but it shouldn't be flamable (except for hair). I may be wrong though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything containing carbon is flammable, more carbon density generally means that less heat is required to ignite the item.<br /> But human body is also full of water, then it s technically flammable, but it requires very high temperatures (lava for example, or a crematorium) to ignite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 10-10-2022, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-30T21:35:19-07:00","id":1495941,"title":"","content":"Except, carbon dioxide; lava is as hot or hotter than fire. It should do aggravated-damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-31T06:07:23-07:00","id":1495968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1495941#post1495941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, carbon dioxide; lava is as hot or hotter than fire. It should do aggravated-damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is not the hotness itself. A vampire in a 2000\u00b0 oven is not having the same effects than with a flame of 900\u00b0.<br /> It's the fire as mistical element which deal aggravated.<br /> <br /> But if the skin can be but on fire instead to be carbonized than I'm fine with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-31-2022, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T06:56:16-08:00","id":1496307,"title":"","content":"Are the Tsihstekeri mentioned anywhere else other than the 2e corebook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/560-obsidian-pharaoh","name":"Obsidian Pharaoh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar560_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-07T15:39:21-08:00","id":1496414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obsidian Pharaoh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1496307#post1496307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Tsihstekeri mentioned anywhere else other than the 2e corebook?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were meant to be mentioned in <b>Spilled Blood</b>, but the section got cut. Otherwise, I don't believe they are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T16:30:06-08:00","id":1496558,"title":"","content":"Book of the Dead has rules for vampires eating ghosts for vitae, and even being unable to sustain themselves in the blood of the living... The ghost eater merit.<br /> <br /> Is there a rule to apply high blood potency feeding restrictions to vampires who can only feed on essence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T19:01:19-08:00","id":1496569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1496558#post1496558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of the Dead has rules for vampires eating ghosts for vitae, and even being unable to sustain themselves in the blood of the living... The ghost eater merit.<br /> <br /> Is there a rule to apply high blood potency feeding restrictions to vampires who can only feed on essence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires use the Unnatural Affinity Merit (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 114) to feed on ghosts in Second Edition, which was intended as a way for high-Blood Potency vampires to feed on things other than other Kindred. So, effectively, vampires are restricted to their Blood Potency restrictions unless they have that Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T09:01:07-08:00","id":1496597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1496569#post1496569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires use the Unnatural Affinity Merit (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 114) to feed on ghosts in Second Edition, which was intended as a way for high-Blood Potency vampires to feed on things other than other Kindred. So, effectively, vampires are restricted to their Blood Potency restrictions unless they have that Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> I think at my table i will just have high BP ghost eating vampires (that merit had the drawback of risking losing the ability to eat the living) forced to eat from Geists. Which shouldn't be too hard in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, without any merits, can vampires in the Underworld just drink a Ghost's blood (as opposed to converting essence into vitae like the 1e merit, or however Unnatural Affinity works) trading lethal damage for vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 11-09-2022, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T10:17:53-08:00","id":1496609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1496597#post1496597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of which, without any merits, can vampires in the Underworld just drink a Ghost's blood (as opposed to converting essence into vitae like the 1e merit, or however Unnatural Affinity works) trading lethal damage for vitae?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t see why not. If it\u2019s solid (relatively speaking) and has blood, a vampire can typically eat it. Assuming their Blood Potency doesn\u2019t require Kindred blood, though in that case, you\u2019d still be able to pay Willpower to process each point, like one would a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-09-2022, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T18:34:38-08:00","id":1496766,"title":"","content":"Did I read it right?<br /> <br /> The Sears Catalog Philips Screw-Driver of Vampire Slaying: so, is it technically possible to stab a vampire enough with a screw-driver, (does Lethal), that they experience the Final-Death?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T18:53:08-08:00","id":1496769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1496766#post1496766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I read it right?<br /> <br /> The Sears Catalog Philips Screw-Driver of Vampire Slaying: so, is it technically possible to stab a vampire enough with a screw-driver, (does Lethal), that they experience the Final-Death?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you'd have to do it a <i>lot</i>, but sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T22:15:15-08:00","id":1496777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1496766#post1496766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I read it right?<br /> <br /> The Sears Catalog Philips Screw-Driver of Vampire Slaying: so, is it technically possible to stab a vampire enough with a screw-driver, (does Lethal), that they experience the Final-Death?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Arc says, yes, with the additional caveat that the way vampires are affected by damage means this will take as long as you would take to punch a normal person to death \u2014 unless there's something special about that screwdriver, it's dealing bashing damage to vampires like almost everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T03:39:03-08:00","id":1496787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1496766#post1496766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I read it right?<br /> <br /> The Sears Catalog Philips Screw-Driver of Vampire Slaying: so, is it technically possible to stab a vampire enough with a screw-driver, (does Lethal), that they experience the Final-Death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any weapon deals bashing to vampire, so yes, technically you can beat to final death any vampire with any weapon or even ny punching him, you just need to deal much more damages to fill out the health bar at least twice to send him in torpor and a third one to destroy him. <br /> That ignoring reflexive regeneration or resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T05:55:56-08:00","id":1496792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1496766#post1496766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I read it right?<br /> <br /> The Sears Catalog Philips Screw-Driver of Vampire Slaying: so, is it technically possible to stab a vampire enough with a screw-driver, (does Lethal), that they experience the Final-Death?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well yes, vampires take bashing from anything that isn't fire, sun or magic in nature (and the last one also depends since the books don't give a clear answer to that), in theory you could stomp on a torpid vampire's head and turn it into mush so yeah, a screwdriver could definitely do the job, of course that is in theory, in practice things are likely to go different...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T18:12:48-08:00","id":1500411,"title":"","content":"To what extent is this considered poaching or an attack?<br /> <br /> 1: Entering your Domain for the purpose of passing through.<br /> 2: Walking around your Domain.<br /> 3: Walking in your Domain with [Obfuscate/Protean].<br /> 4: Refueling at a gas station in your Domain.<br /> 5: Talk to a human in your Domain.<br /> 6: [Majesty/Dominate] to a human in your Domain.<br /> 7: Go to a secret room with your Domain's human.<br /> 8: Take your Domain's person out of the map","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25958-veiros","name":"veiros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25958_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T02:45:37-08:00","id":1500443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>veiros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1500411#post1500411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what extent is this considered poaching or an attack?<br /> <br /> 1: Entering your Domain for the purpose of passing through.<br /> 2: Walking around your Domain.<br /> 3: Walking in your Domain with [Obfuscate/Protean].<br /> 4: Refueling at a gas station in your Domain.<br /> 5: Talk to a human in your Domain.<br /> 6: [Majesty/Dominate] to a human in your Domain.<br /> 7: Go to a secret room with your Domain's human.<br /> 8: Take your Domain's person out of the map</div> </div> </div> </div>This pretty much depends on the landlord and on the generic law given by the Prince. Personally I would go like that:<br /> <br /> 1. Nope. It would be very annoying and too strict not even been allowed to cross a road. Plus, if there are several domain next to each other with this proibition it may become impossibile to move from A to B without violating it.<br /> <br /> 2. A landlord very strict could complain with that if you do not ask for his permission, at least once<br /> <br /> 3. Protean? You mean as a rat, dog or bat, not like a monstruos hulk or quadrupedal right? In such case I don't see differences with point 2 unless the landlord considers it a subtle attempt to spy or dealing some non lecit activity. <br /> <br /> 4. As point 1<br /> <br /> 5. If you are allowed to enter (point 1) or to walking around (point 2) I don't see how a conversation could be seen as a crime<br /> <br /> 6. Depends. If you have not received permission for hunting probably yes.<br /> <br /> 7. Probably yes. If you get spotted...as it's a secret room<br /> <br /> 8. It again depends. Humans walk around freely. If it's not an human linked to the landlord probably not if done in a discrete way.<br /> <br /> The question is: how much you want to bother your player with this? The risk is they feel like they cannot do anyting anywhere if you use too strict rules for each domain in a city where there are several of those. I see it can work if you have a specific, unique, area strictly forbidden by the landlord. You know, everyone knows, so up to you violating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-23-2022, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T06:07:01-08:00","id":1500449,"title":"","content":"Thank you.<br /> I understand that\uff1a)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25958-veiros","name":"veiros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25958_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T13:52:35-08:00","id":1500521,"title":"","content":"What happens when BP lowers and attributes and skills are beyond 5? I know you <b>keep </b>the attributes, but can you <b>use </b>them? I see two options:<br /> <br /> 1. Use up to 5.<br /> 2. Use the real value.<br /> <br /> What is the case?<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-17T14:43:46-08:00","id":1500530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/818754-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-vampire?p=1500521#post1500521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when BP lowers and attributes and skills are beyond 5? I know you <b>keep </b>the attributes, but can you <b>use </b>them? I see two options:<br /> <br /> 1. Use up to 5.<br /> 2. Use the real value.<br /> <br /> What is the case?<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep and use your full stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}